(congenital factor IX deficiency or Christmas disease), including control and prevention of bleeding in surgical settings. Nonacog alfa (BeneFIX), is not indicated for the treatment of other factor deficiencies (e.g., factors II, VII and X), nor for the treatment of hemophilia A patients with inhibitors to factor VIII, nor for the reversal of coumarin-induced anticoagulation, nor for the treatment of bleeding due to low levels of liver-dependent coagulation factors.",2,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T13:52:08.450968+00:00
