PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,BR-572,Bacillus Calmette-Guerin (BCG) Vaccine,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Xh2vekgo1TndVqoRQnpd0sAyGHTAjWrS/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/BR-572_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Xh2vekgo1TndVqoRQnpd0sAyGHTAjWrS_view_usp_drivesdk_1c9f42c8aa.pdf,page_text/BR-572_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Xh2vekgo1TndVqoRQnpd0sAyGHTAjWrS_view_usp_drivesdk_1c9f42c8aa.json,1da25221818cfcdf6ee81aa56225d4b7cc357d4065586b2699db23b79c651917,750928,1,ocr,"antibodies has been detected up to 14 months). It is therefore necessary to wait until the child has been BCG Vaccine is a live freeze-dried vaccine derived from attenuated strain of Mycobacterium bovis found to be seronegative, as determined by immuno-transfer (Western Blot) with the support, if necessary, of techniques for detecting the viral genome, before confirming that the child is not (Bacillus Calmette Guerin Moscow strain 361- I) used for the prevention of tuberculosis. The freeze- infected. dried vaccine is white and crystalline in appearance. It contains Sodium Glutamate as stabilizer. The vaccine meets the requirements of W.H.O. when tested by the methods outlined in W.H.O., If the child is infected BCG vaccine is contraindicated irrespective of the child’s condition, given the potential risk of development of “BCG-itis” in the vaccinated child. The advice of a specialized medical",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"DO NOT USE BCG vaccine should be given routinely to all infants at risk of early exposure to tuberculosis. This vaccine should be given soon after the child is born. BCG administered early in life provides high level of a EE Ee A protection particularly against severe forms of childhood tuberculosis and tubercular meningitis. In Square is Square Square is lighter than matches darker than countries with low prevalance of tuberculosis, BCG vaccination should be restricted to high risk groups 0 outer circle io outer circle © outer circle such as hospital personnel and tuberculin negative contacts of known cases of tuberculosis. The vaccine ‘The colour of the inner square of the WMs Once a vaccine has reached or exceeded the discard point, can be given simultaneously with DTP, DT, TT, Measles, Polio, Hepatitis B, Haemophilus influenzae type begins with a shade that is lighter than the DISCARD POINT the colour of the inner square will be the same colo outer circle and continues to darken with or darker than the outer circle. b, yellow fever vaccines and vitamin A supplementation, but at a separate site. time and/or exposure to heat. Inform your supervisor",1,1,INDICATIONS AND IMMUNIZATION SCHEDULE,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T13:59:18.149555+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,BR-599,Human Tetanus Immunoglobulin,Tetagam P,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IfqZYUbt1HT15wQlIyy5dUbgBpdkL1fq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/BR-599_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IfqZYUbt1HT15wQlIyy5dUbgBpdkL1fq_view_usp_drivesdk_bfeb1c6376.pdf,page_text/BR-599_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IfqZYUbt1HT15wQlIyy5dUbgBpdkL1fq_view_usp_drivesdk_bfeb1c6376.json,40a373ee65eb945c1a7c39f611ae042340dfbb4cf598dc729bd0411f42539a11,280613,4,digital_text,Pharmaceutical form Solution for injection for intramuscular use. Tetagam P is a clear solution. The colour can vary from colourless to pale-yellow up to light brown during shelf life. Presentations Pack with 1 prefilled syringe with 1 ml Pack with 10 prefilled syringes with 1 ml Pack with 1 prefilled syringe with 2 ml Not all pack sizes may be marketed. NAME AND ADDRESS OF THE MARKETING AUTHORISATION HOLDER CSL Behring GmbH Emil-von-Behring-Str. 76 35041 Marburg Germany DATE OF LAST REVISION September 2024 REG-11303-01 DMC DMC 1 2 3 4 5 6 Material Number | Component Description: REG-11303-01_LFT TETAGAM P 1 ML UNE_D3 Artwork Author: Tamara Hillgärtner Technical Datasheet: n/a GLAMS Part Number: REG-11303-01 Additional comments: 640 x 210 mm Colours: Black Technical Colours (indication only – not to be printed): Die Cut REG-11303-01_LFT TETAGAM P 1 ML UNE_D3.indd 1REG-11303-01_LFT TETAGAM P 1 ML UNE_D3.indd 1 25.08.2025 10:16:2525.08.2025 10:16:25 [Page 4] REG-11303-01_LFT TETAGAM P 1 ML UNE_D3.indd 2REG-11303-01_LFT TETAGAM P 1 ML UNE_D3.indd 2 25.08.2025 10:16:2525.08.2025 10:16:25 [Page 5],3,4,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM AND PRESENTATIONS,Postexposure prophylaxis Immediate prophylaxis after tetanus prone injuries in patients • not adequately vaccinated • whose immunisation status is not known with certainty • with severe deficiency in antibody production Therapy of clinically manifest tetanus Tetanus immunoglobulin should always be administered in conjunction with an active tetanus vaccination unless there are contraindications or confirmation of adequate vaccination. WHO guidelines and other official guidance regarding the use of human tetanus immunoglobulin for intramuscular use should be observed.,3,3,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T13:59:21.317839+00:00
