PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,BR-940,Epoetin alfa (Recombinant Human Erythropoietin),Renogen,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LKEaAQggPIYv34Wni7VuyWF1kKEtIN69/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/BR-940_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LKEaAQggPIYv34Wni7VuyWF1kKEtIN69_view_usp_drivesdk_912c1de970.pdf,page_text/BR-940_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LKEaAQggPIYv34Wni7VuyWF1kKEtIN69_view_usp_drivesdk_912c1de970.json,17ae7f1f41e134e938bfa1ccffb3b043f8f3fa6ea985a604e528da16d1b1767f,12162780,2,digital_text_and_ocr,,,,,Units SC once in a week. Baseline endogenous serum erythropoietin levels varied among Erythropoietin is contraindicated in patients with: patients with cancer related anemia. Treatment of patients with grossly elevated serum erythropoietin levels (eg. > 200 mUnits/mL) is not recommended. The hematocrit should 1. Uncontrolled hypertension. 2. Known hypersensitivity to mammalian cell-derived products be monitored on a weekly basis in patients receiving erythropoietin therapy until 3. Known hypersensitivity to Albumin (Human). hematocrit becomes stable. 2. Zidovudine-treated HIV-infected Patients.,2,2,CONTRAINDICATIONS,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T14:10:16.973624+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,BR-948,Insulin Human (rDNA),Humulin N Kwikpen,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1C2Ipt5RMg0xb_ixD7Qsctml1CutMmdlc/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/BR-948_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1C2Ipt5RMg0xb_ixD7Qsctml1CutMmdlc_view_usp_drivesdk_e7d7993bfe.pdf,page_text/BR-948_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1C2Ipt5RMg0xb_ixD7Qsctml1CutMmdlc_view_usp_drivesdk_e7d7993bfe.json,a410bdd0d1d87bd7e199c70ed1bb2ab80e8d20dd0208b3a68b7bfeee781e1feb,1174852,2,digital_text,"Insulin Human (Humulin® N KwikPen) is a sterile suspension of a white, crystalline precipitate of isophane human insulin in an isotonic phosphate buffer. 5. CLI NICAL PARTICULARS 5.1 Ther apeutic Indication For the treatment of patients with diabetes mellitus who require insulin for the maintenance of glucose homeostasis. 5.2 Poso logy and method of administration The dosage should be determined by the physician, according to the requirement of the patient. Insulin Human (Humulin ® N KwikPen) should be given by subcutaneous injection. This formulation should not be administered intravenously. Subcutaneous administration should be in the upper arms, thighs, buttocks or abdomen. Use of injection sites should be rotated so that the same site is not used more than approximately once a month. Care should be taken when injecting any Humulin ® insulin preparations to ensure that a blood vessel has not been entered. After any insulin injection, the injection site should not be massaged. Patients must be educated to use proper injection techniques. 5.3 Con",1,1,4. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Hypoglycemia. Hypersensitivity to Humulin® or to the formulation excipients, unless used as part of a desensitization program. Under no circumstances should any Humulin ® formulation, other than Humulin® R (Soluble), be given intravenously. 5.4 Speci",1,1,traindications,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T14:10:20.896001+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,BR-950,Insulin Human (rDNA),Humulin 70/30 Kwikpen,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1OFJt4eARFoPfqY1Sitvr3ZqWT9bbF_cf/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/BR-950_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OFJt4eARFoPfqY1Sitvr3ZqWT9bbF_cf_view_usp_drivesdk_a814a44026.pdf,page_text/BR-950_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OFJt4eARFoPfqY1Sitvr3ZqWT9bbF_cf_view_usp_drivesdk_a814a44026.json,32dfe2861b2405a789a70fc0df51c0af769fcf4a1f2898dba1748376d09c81a5,970120,2,digital_text,"A suspension for injection in a prefilled pen. Insulin Human (Humulin® 70/30 KwikPen) is a sterile suspension of human insulin in the proportion of 30% soluble insulin to 70% isophane insulin. 5. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 5.1 Therapeutic Indication For the treatment of patients with diabetes mellitus who require insulin for the maintenance of glucose homeostasis. 5.2 P osology and method of administration Posology The dosage should be determined by the physician, according to the requirement of the patient. Pediatric population No data are available Method of administration Insulin Human Humulin ® 70/30 ( KwikPen) in prefilled pen is only suitable for subcutaneous injection. This formulation should not be administered intravenously. Subcutaneous administration should be in the upper arms, thighs, buttocks or abdomen. Use of injection sites should be rotated so that the same site is not used more than approximately once a month in order to reduce the risk of lipodystrophy and cutaneous amyloidosis (see section 5.4 Special warnings and precautions for use and 5.8 Undesirable effects). Care should be taken when injecting any Humulin ® insulin preparations to ensure that a blood vessel has not been entered. After any insulin injection, the injection site should not be massaged. Patients must be educated to use proper injection techniques. Humulin ® Mixture formulation is a ready‑m ade defined mixture of soluble and isophane insulin designed to avoid the need for the patient to mix insulin preparations. A patient’s treatment regimen should be based on their individual metabolic requirements. 5.3",1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,For the treatment of patients with diabetes mellitus who require insulin for the maintenance of glucose homeostasis. 5.2 P,1,1,Therapeutic Indication,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:10:24.545640+00:00
