PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-10256,Prednisolone (as acetate),Pred Forte,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BTFVrqmqDlg9BomNNr_l9xPe0XBDmeFo/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-10256_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1BTFVrqmqDlg9BomNNr_l9xPe0XBDmeFo_view_usp_drivesdk_1d93533df6.pdf,page_text/DR-10256_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1BTFVrqmqDlg9BomNNr_l9xPe0XBDmeFo_view_usp_drivesdk_1d93533df6.json,043bb78e44700e3e910c555310dfccc7f6245a51bfe7e307e4952690573ede33,247677,4,digital_text,Prednisolone acetate is a synthetic corticosteroid. It is a white crystalline substance with a melting point at about 235°C with some decomposition and an empirical formula of C 23H30O6. It has a characteristic ultraviolet absorption maximum of 242 millimicrons in methanol. STRUCTURAL FORMULA,1,1,DESCRIPTION,"For steroid responsive inflammation of the palpebral and bulbar conjunctiva, cornea and anterior segment of the globe.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:33:47.880320+00:00
