PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-1168,Sodium Fusidate,FUCIDIN,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1kqBSM0jIl_sP2pe6Mpf3lNAkLqn9EUL0/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-1168_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kqBSM0jIl_sP2pe6Mpf3lNAkLqn9EUL0_view_usp_drivesdk_d326d2fe90.pdf,page_text/DR-1168_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kqBSM0jIl_sP2pe6Mpf3lNAkLqn9EUL0_view_usp_drivesdk_d326d2fe90.json,4110b7773c0f58a29d404bbdcc7af8aa9ff2abea2f56df5f4725df2620178341,1020060,2,digital_text,The tablet is an approximately 7.8 x 16.0 mm white to off-white greyish marbled film-coated oval biconvex tablet without embossing.,1,1,Product Description,"Sodium fusidate (Fucidin®) tablets are indicated for the treatment of infections caused by susceptible organisms, especially staphylococci, e.g. osteomyelitis, septicaemia, endocarditis, superinfected cystic fibrosis, pneumonia, skin and soft tissue infections, surgical and traumatic wound infections.",1,1,Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:33:58.652868+00:00
