PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-2350,Aspirin,Aspilets,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1eel3Mgee5Z3SEY59rcr3kADcWl_jq2Lf/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-2350_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eel3Mgee5Z3SEY59rcr3kADcWl_jq2Lf_view_usp_drivesdk_a3480a2418.pdf,page_text/DR-2350_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eel3Mgee5Z3SEY59rcr3kADcWl_jq2Lf_view_usp_drivesdk_a3480a2418.json,047f136fac1070957896597e01eea497c00d5fca3aac529d8d9c384234e6f47b,4453920,1,digital_text,".. ............................................... BO mg CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY Pharmacodynamics Aspirin is a nonsteroidal anti-inBammatory agent. Tl7e antithrombotic activity of aspirin is due to its inhibitory effect on platelets which is mediated via irre\/ersible acetylation of platelet cyclooxygenase with subsequent blockade of platelet lhromboxane synthesis. The inhibitory effect of aspirin on platelet lhromboxane production persists for the lifespan of the plale.il, arour<l 7 to 10 days. As a resull, acelylatk>n of platelet cyclooxygenase and consequenl inhibition of thromboxane formation is cumulative on repeated dosing. Low doses of aspirin inhibit platelet aggregation and may be more effective than higher doses. Larger doses inhibit cyclooxygenase in artenal walls. interfenng with prostacyclin production, a potent vasodilator and inhibitor of plalelet aggregation. Pharmacokinetics",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,• For primary pre-vention of thromboembolic disorders and cardiovascular events: - lschemic stroke • Transient iscflemic attack (TIA) - Prevention of recurrent Ml • Unstab~ angina pectoris • Chronic stat>le angina pectoris,1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:34:17.526946+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-262,Digoxin,Lanoxin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ua1elpNpgvqYLtzwcKFV1Y43cmn9IV2X/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-262_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ua1elpNpgvqYLtzwcKFV1Y43cmn9IV2X_view_usp_drivesdk_4e503edbf9.pdf,page_text/DR-262_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ua1elpNpgvqYLtzwcKFV1Y43cmn9IV2X_view_usp_drivesdk_4e503edbf9.json,59ee759066864493e9c885d4dcfe440d2b95bcc0d41dce5eda61df0f91dcc786,214910,2,digital_text,"Digoxin (Lanoxin) Tablet: White, round, biconvex tablets each containing 250 micrograms (0.250 mg) Digoxin, EP. Digoxin (Lanoxin) Solution for Injection : A clear, colourless, sterile aqueous solution containing 250 micrograms (0.250 mg) Digoxin, EP per mL and supplied in a 2 mL ampoule. Digoxin (Lanoxin) (Pediatric /Geriatric) Elixir : A clear, yellow, lime flavoured solution containing 50 micrograms (0.050 mg) Digoxin, EP in each 1mL of sweetened, aqueous-alcoholic elixir.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Cardiac failure Digoxin (Lanoxin) is indicated in the management of chronic cardiac failure where the dominant problem is systolic dysfunction. Its therapeutic benefit is greatest in those patients with ventricular d ilatation. Digoxin (Lanoxin) is specifically indicated where cardiac failure is accompanied by atrial fibrillation. Supraventricular Arrhythmias Digoxin (Lanoxin) is indicated in the management of certain supraventricular arrhythmias, particularly chronic atrial flutter and fibrillation.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:34:20.893998+00:00
