PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-4113,Betamethasone (As Valerate),Betnovate,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1a5jRDC5pFtyF3_JvQ4DunrnC8dXoD4E4/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-4113_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1a5jRDC5pFtyF3_JvQ4DunrnC8dXoD4E4_view_usp_drivesdk_d5ccb1354e.pdf,page_text/DR-4113_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1a5jRDC5pFtyF3_JvQ4DunrnC8dXoD4E4_view_usp_drivesdk_d5ccb1354e.json,9d74c374393ffc9d1b88a6cb204e1ebd77832d4b20282ed247d843214bde3329,104659,4,digital_text,Each gram of Betamethasone valerate (Betnovate) Cream contains 1 milligram of betamethasone (as valerate). Each gram of Betamethasone valerate (Betnovate) Ointment contains 1 milligram of betamethasone (as valerate). Each milliliter of Betamethasone valerate (Betnovate) Lotion contains 1 milligram of betamethasone (as valerate).,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Betamethasone valerate (Betnovate) is a potent topical corticosteroid indicated for adults, elderly and children over 1 year for the relief of the inflammatory and pruritic manifestations of steroid responsive dermatoses. These include the following: • Atopic dermatitis (including infantile atopic dermatitis) • Nummular dermatitis (discoid eczema) • Prurigo nodularis • Psoriasis (excluding widespread plaque psoriasis) • Lichen simplex chronicus (neurodermatitis) and lichen planus • Seborrhoeic dermatitis • Irritant or allergic contact dermatitis • Discoid lupus erythematosus • Adjunct to systemic steroid therapy in generalised erythroderma • Insect bite reactions • Miliaria (prickly heat)",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:34:26.851965+00:00
