PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-4464,Atropine (as sulfate),None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/17k9RzBGusnBqr-ZEdusXj4_3sUo7mkfh/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-4464_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17k9RzBGusnBqr-ZEdusXj4_3sUo7mkfh_view_usp_drivesdk_3face95b22.pdf,page_text/DR-4464_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17k9RzBGusnBqr-ZEdusXj4_3sUo7mkfh_view_usp_drivesdk_3face95b22.json,6fd5b9589c51f1b9adaf43823119f196cb30d45ec7da507087bea8b8580f8fc6,2792590,1,ocr,"Atropine sulfate 500 mcg/ mL Solution for Injection is a clear, colorless solution, free from visible foreign matter. Atropine sulfate 1 mg/mL Solution for Injection is a clear, colorless solution, free from visible foreign matter.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"As mydriatic and cycloplegic for thorough examination of retina and optic disc. As a treatment of iridocyclitis and choroiditis following cataract surgery. Premedication (during anesthesia) to inhibit salivary and respiratory secretions and to reduce incidence of laryngospasm. Acute myocardial infarction to decrease vagal tone. Antispasmodic in renal colic. Antidote for acute poisoning with anticholinesterase, organop! hosphorous in pesticides, rapid type of mushroom poisoning.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T18:35:58.646504+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-4465,Calcium gluconate,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1tZHTr4D3l5Jqws0d6nQJ4qYlwQTGYyRa/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-4465_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1tZHTr4D3l5Jqws0d6nQJ4qYlwQTGYyRa_view_usp_drivesdk_9cae95fb95.pdf,page_text/DR-4465_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1tZHTr4D3l5Jqws0d6nQJ4qYlwQTGYyRa_view_usp_drivesdk_9cae95fb95.json,5c1554bdddc573dd738fd66b983fe87afb84f219f081f5eb254801d9e73f7b2c,1937694,2,ocr,"Calcium gluconate 100 mg / mL Solution for Injection is a clear, colorless solution, free from foreign matter.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Calcium gluconate is administered when therapy with Calcium is needed. It is necessary for the proper functioning of the nerves and muscles, for the clotting of blood, for normal cardiac function, and for the maintenance of the body skeleton. It is a source of Calcium ion specific in the treatment of hypocalcemic tetany or hyperkalemia and parathyroid tetany. It is also used for magnesium intoxication to counteract respiratory paralysis.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T18:36:07.871594+00:00
