PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-5054,Brewer's Yeast,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fcY3UZkYNODMI4D_g_oVUdDm5jGXiL9C/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-5054_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1fcY3UZkYNODMI4D_g_oVUdDm5jGXiL9C_view_usp_drivesdk_81d4760c94.pdf,page_text/DR-5054_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1fcY3UZkYNODMI4D_g_oVUdDm5jGXiL9C_view_usp_drivesdk_81d4760c94.json,35e7dadef2c269c32efc1f170ba3e086eb77ac0c2c172553f1e666d7f6e2408b,583062,1,ocr,"ADVERSE DRUG REACTION REPORTING For suspected Adverse Drug Reaction (ADR), report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph or Brewer's Yeast 500 mg is a brown, round, biconvex tablet, plain on both sides. drug.safety@philusa.com.ph. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of ADR. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This product contains Brewer's yeast, a nutritional supplement rich in minerals such as AVAILABILITY Amber Glass Bottle x 100’s vitamin B-complex, selenium, protein; and chromium, an essential trace mineral used by the body in maintaining normal blood sugar levels. STRENGTH OF MEDICINE Please see formulation. Manufactured by: Marketing Authorization Holder: Amherst Laboratories, Inc. Philusa Corporation WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? For the prevention and treatment of Vitamin B deficiency, UNILAB Pharma Campus, 28 Shaw Bivd., Kapitotyo, Brgy Mamplasan, Bifian, Pasig City Laguna, Philippines HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? As dietary supplement: Infants — 1 to 2.5 g dally in milk Children - 4 to6g REGISTRATION NUMBER: DR-5054 Adults —6 to8g In condition of severe vitamin B deficiency, adults may be given doses up to 30g daily. DATE OF RENEWAL OF THE AUTHORIZATION: 19 February 2019 WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? DATE OF REVISION OF PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET (PIL): 13 November 2020 Do not take this product if you have allergies to any of its contents. Consult your doctor before taking this sup t Pp ially if you have di frequent yeast infections, gout, and Crohn's disease, UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Brewer's yeast may cause gas (flatulence). WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? This product may interact with medications for depression specifically monoamine oxidase inhibitors (MAOIs). brewer'syeast-1120 [Page 2]",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T18:36:44.554893+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-5056,Iron (as ferrous sulfate heptahydrate),Unbranded,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1nrKNWPCncvQ19WiJMknmZomWxgpHpGlc/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-5056_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1nrKNWPCncvQ19WiJMknmZomWxgpHpGlc_view_usp_drivesdk_facfa777ef.pdf,page_text/DR-5056_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1nrKNWPCncvQ19WiJMknmZomWxgpHpGlc_view_usp_drivesdk_facfa777ef.json,6be7d750c9fa4b1a96137ff179b444acd206e97c1ad72b11cc91eb94e88ffdaa,634815,1,ocr,"if the patient has taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor immediately or contact a Poison Control Center. Iron (as Ferrous sulfate heptahydrate) is a chocolate brown, round, biconvex, sugar-coated tablet, plain on both sides. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Keep container tightly closed and protect from light. Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This product contains ferrous sulfate, an iron salt. Iron salts are used to treat or prevent iron deficiency anemia. Iron is an essential element as it is used by the body for a variety of processes WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? such as metabolic processes which includes oxygen transport and DNA synthesis. If your symptoms persist or worsen, or if you are experiencing an adverse reaction from this medicine, consult a physician. STRENGTH OF MEDICINE Please see formulation, ADVERSE DRUG REACTION REPORTING For suspected Adverse Drug Reaction (ADR), report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph or WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? drug.safety@philusa.com.ph. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of ADR. For the prophylaxis and treatment of simple iron deficiency disorders and iron deficiency anemia. AVAILABILITY HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Iron (as ferrous sulfate heptahydrate) tablet in amber glass bottle x 100's. For iron supplementation: REGISTRATION NUMBER: DR-5056 Adults: 1 to 2 tablets 3 times a day after meals. DATE OF RENEWAL OF THE AUTHORIZATION: 27 May 2019 For therapy: as prescribed by the physician. DATE OF REVISION OF PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET (PIL): 13 November 2020 WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you have allergies to any iron products, do not take this medicine. Manufactured by: Amherst Laboratories, Inc. UNILAB Pharma Campus, Barangay Mamplasan, Bifian, Laguna, Philippines CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE Consult your doctor first before taking iron supplements if you have certain blood diseases like Marketing Authorization Holder: hemolytic anemia; or if you have a history of gastric ulcers or bleeding. PHILUSA CORPORATION 28 Shaw Bivd., Kapitotyo, Pasig, Metro Manila UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Ferrous sulfate may cause gastrointestinal disorders such as gastric irritation, nausea, vomiting, epigastric pain, diarrhea, and constipation. It can also cause tooth discoloration and blackening of stool. iron-1120 [Page 2]",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T18:36:50.888138+00:00
