PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-X1716,Betamethasone (As Valerate),Betnovate,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N8NQmhJezEMvcr1qcSSdiiamXbhqInGh/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-X1716_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1N8NQmhJezEMvcr1qcSSdiiamXbhqInGh_view_usp_drivesdk_da4558e153.pdf,page_text/DR-X1716_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1N8NQmhJezEMvcr1qcSSdiiamXbhqInGh_view_usp_drivesdk_da4558e153.json,9d74c374393ffc9d1b88a6cb204e1ebd77832d4b20282ed247d843214bde3329,104659,4,digital_text,Each gram of Betamethasone valerate (Betnovate) Cream contains 1 milligram of betamethasone (as valerate). Each gram of Betamethasone valerate (Betnovate) Ointment contains 1 milligram of betamethasone (as valerate). Each milliliter of Betamethasone valerate (Betnovate) Lotion contains 1 milligram of betamethasone (as valerate).,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Betamethasone valerate (Betnovate) is a potent topical corticosteroid indicated for adults, elderly and children over 1 year for the relief of the inflammatory and pruritic manifestations of steroid responsive dermatoses. These include the following: • Atopic dermatitis (including infantile atopic dermatitis) • Nummular dermatitis (discoid eczema) • Prurigo nodularis • Psoriasis (excluding widespread plaque psoriasis) • Lichen simplex chronicus (neurodermatitis) and lichen planus • Seborrhoeic dermatitis • Irritant or allergic contact dermatitis • Discoid lupus erythematosus • Adjunct to systemic steroid therapy in generalised erythroderma • Insect bite reactions • Miliaria (prickly heat)",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:41:57.729453+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-X1740,Diclofenac Sodium,Voltaren,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1m_7BwSCaRWY5YJOS4iaFFQcpCx3X3eGp/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-X1740_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1m_7BwSCaRWY5YJOS4iaFFQcpCx3X3eGp_view_usp_drivesdk_469c80301e.pdf,page_text/DR-X1740_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1m_7BwSCaRWY5YJOS4iaFFQcpCx3X3eGp_view_usp_drivesdk_469c80301e.json,294f61d974a1bc5ee7e27c1a83ca4d7d6963c5b72444633bcc0e36aecba2c158,203817,16,digital_text,Solution for injection. Active substance The active substance is diclofenac sodium. Each ampoule (3 mL) contains 75 mg of diclofenac sodium. Active moiety Diclofenac Excipients Mannitol; sodium metabisulphite (E223); benzyl alcohol; propylene glycol; water for injection; sodium hydroxide. Pharmaceutical formulations may vary between countries.,1,1,Pharmaceutical form,"Intramuscular injection Treatment of: • Exacerbations of inflammatory and degenerative forms of rheumatism: rheumatoid arthritis, ankylosing spondylitis, osteoarthritis, spondylarthritis, painful syndromes of the vertebral column, non-articular rheumatism. • Acute attacks of gout. • Renal colic and biliary colic. • Post-traumatic and post-operative pain, inflammation and swelling. • Severe migraine attacks. Intravenous infusion Treatment or prevention of post-operative pain in a hospital setting. Diclofenac sodium [Page 2]",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:42:01.182726+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-X1812,Metoprolol Tartrate,BetalocÂ®,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FXllkL7u63DKvYULkvTVIQNFzsaba0hT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-X1812_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FXllkL7u63DKvYULkvTVIQNFzsaba0hT_view_usp_drivesdk_7087b8852a.pdf,page_text/DR-X1812_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FXllkL7u63DKvYULkvTVIQNFzsaba0hT_view_usp_drivesdk_7087b8852a.json,8b340bc2fd4ad9992fc01cadebfdc665d33d7b8f061b2bb03f0fb1690953a66b,138978,13,digital_text,"Tablets of 50 mg and 100 mg. The metoprolol tartrate 50 mg tablet is white to off-white, circular with a diameter of 8 mm, scored and marked A/BB on one side. The score line is only to facilitate breaking for ease of swallowing and not to divide into equal doses. The metoprolol tartrate 100 mg tablet is white to off-white, circular with a diameter of 10 mm, scored and marked A/ME on one side. The tablet can be divided into equal halves by breaking along the score lines. 4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 4.1 Therapeutic indications Hypertension: to reduce blood pressure and to reduce the risk of cardiovascular and coronary mortality (including sudden death), and morbidity. [Page 2] Angina pectoris. Disturbances of cardiac rhythm including especially supraventricular tachycardia. Maintenance treatment after myocardial infarction. Functional heart disorders with palpitations. Migraine prophylaxis. Hyperthyroidism. 4.2 Dosage and method of administration The tablets should be taken on an empty stomach. Hypertension The recommended dosage in patients with hypertension is 100-200 mg daily, given as a single dose in the morning or in divided doses (morning and evening). If needed, other antihypertensive agents may be added. Long-term antihypertensive treatment with metoprolol in daily doses of 100-200 mg has been shown to reduce total mortality, including sudden cardiovascular death, stroke and coronary events in hypertensive patients. Angina pectoris The recommended dosage is 100-200 mg daily, given in divided doses (morning and evening). If needed, other antianginal agents may be added. Cardiac arrhythmias The recommended dosage is 100-200 mg daily given in divided doses (morning and evening). If needed, other antiarrhythmic agents may be added. Maintenance treatment after myocardial infarction Long-term o ral treatment with metoprolol in doses of 2 00 mg daily, given in divided doses (morning and evening) has been shown to reduce the risk of death (including sudden death), and to reduce the risk of reinfarction (also in patients with diabetes mellitus). Functional heart disorders with palpitations [Page 3] The recommended dosage is 100 mg once daily, given as a single dose in the morning. If needed, the dose can be increased to 200 mg. Migraine prophylaxis The recommended dosage is 100-200 mg daily, given in divided doses morning and evening. Hyperthyroidism The recommended dosage is 150-200 mg daily, divided in 3-4 doses. If needed, the dose can be increased. Impaired renal function Dose adjustment is not needed in patients with impaired renal function. Impaired hepatic function Dose adjustment i s normally not needed in patients suffering from liver cirrhosis because metoprolol has a low protein binding (5-10 %). When there are signs of serious impairment of liver function (e.g. shunt-operated patients) a dose reduction should be considered. Elderly Dose adjustment is not needed in the elderly. Children There is limited experience with metoprolol treatment in children.",1,3,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Hypertension: to reduce blood pressure and to reduce the risk of cardiovascular and coronary mortality (including sudden death), and morbidity. [Page 2] Angina pectoris. Disturbances of cardiac rhythm including especially supraventricular tachycardia. Maintenance treatment after myocardial infarction. Functional heart disorders with palpitations. Migraine prophylaxis. Hyperthyroidism.",1,2,4.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:42:04.137873+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-X1824,Phenobarbital,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GVkP9ox7o7fONZVyouiDIoqKc2cOodCu/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-X1824_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GVkP9ox7o7fONZVyouiDIoqKc2cOodCu_view_usp_drivesdk_36afd35be7.pdf,page_text/DR-X1824_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GVkP9ox7o7fONZVyouiDIoqKc2cOodCu_view_usp_drivesdk_36afd35be7.json,2b8013ff1d190dd76b81d5ab58a95a345f7afe44ad4e6ffe76a62e9c4bb1b7d8,1718066,1,ocr,"Phenobarbital 15, 60 and 90 mg is a white, round, biconvex tablet, plain on both sides. WARNING; May be habit forming Phenobarbital 30 mg is a white, round, flat beveled-edge tablet, bisected on one side and plain on the other. CAUTION: “DDB Regulation requires prescription and dispensing through a Special orm 1s Drugs by a current PDEA S2-licensed medical PHARMACODYNAMICS practitioner.” Pher isa in which the basic structure is barbituric acid, a used for its ai Ss in AVAILABILITY management of tonic-clonic o- mal) and | partial (focal) seizures. Phenobarbital is Hacti as oral "" Phenobarbital 15 mg, 30 mg, 60 mg, 90 mg Tablet: Amber Glass Bottle x 100's YP REGISTRATION NUMBER PHARMACOKINETICS Phenobarbital 15 mg Tablet: DR-X1824 ; Phenobarbital 30 mg Tablet: DR-5056 Phenobarbital 60 mg Tablet: DR-X2017; Phenobarbital 90 mg Tablet: DR-XY21882 Phenobarbital is classified as a long-acting barbiturate when taken orally. Its onset of action is 1 hour or longer, and its duration of action ranges from 10 to 12 hours. DATE OF RENEWAL OF AUTHORIZATION Phenobarbital 15 mg Tablet: 04 Jan 2019 Distribution, Phenobarbital 30 mg Tablet: 04 Jan 2019 Barbiturates are weak acids that are absorbed and rapidly distributed to all tissues and fluids, Phenobarbital 60 mg Tablet: 04 Jan 2019 with high concentrations in the brain, liver, and kidneys. Phenobarbital 90 mg Tablet: 04 Jan 2019 Phenobarbital has the lowest lipid solubility, lowest plasma binding, lowest brain protein binding, the longest delay in onset activity, and the longest duration of action. The plasma DATE OF REVISION OF PACKAGE INSERT half-life for phenobarbital in adults ranges between 53 and 118 hours with a mean of 79 hours. 13 November 2020 The plasma half-life for p (less than 48 hours old) ranges between 60 to 180 hours with a mean of 110 hours. Manufactured by Amherst Laboratories, Inc. Metabolism: ali 4 UNILAB Pharma Campus, Barangay Mamplasan, Binafi, Laguna, Philippines are by the hepatic microsomal enzyme system, and the p are ed in the urine and, less commonly, in the feces. Marketing Authorization Holder: Elimination. PHILUSA CORPORATION 28 Shaw Boulevard, Pasig City Approximately 25% to 50% of a dose of phenobarbital is eliminated unchanged in the urine. The excretion of unmetabolized barbiturate is one feature that distinguishes the long-acting category from those belonging to other seen te which are almost entirely metabolized. The RPBOO of the as vy of g! acid,",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Phenobarbital is used as an anti-epileptic agent to control tonic-clonic (grand mal) and partial (focal) seizures.,1,1,INDICATION(S),medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T18:42:12.836398+00:00
