VIER Manufactured by: Frequency not known: abdominal pain, isolated Les Laboratoires Servier Industrie face, lip, eyelid edema (swelling). Exceptionally, 905 route de Saran Quincke’s edema (rapid swelling of tissues such 45520 Gidy, France as the face, lips, mouth, tongue or throat that may result in breathing difficulty). Imported by:",1,2,prescription.,"in pregnant women. Daflon 500 is recommended for treating venous Animal studies do not indicate reproductive circulation disorders (swollen legs, pain, nocturnal toxicity. cramps) and for treating symptoms due to acute As a precautionary measure, it is preferable hemorrhoidal attack. to avoid the use of Diosmin + Hesperidin (Daflon 500) during pregnancy.",1,1,Indication,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T18:46:12.711295+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY13021,Morphine Sulfate,Mst Continus,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XGtmXDfGoQ1DH2VO6nSEL4LdVEw1y_XZ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY13021_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1XGtmXDfGoQ1DH2VO6nSEL4LdVEw1y_XZ_view_usp_drivesdk_6be83a46ca.pdf,page_text/DR-XY13021_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1XGtmXDfGoQ1DH2VO6nSEL4LdVEw1y_XZ_view_usp_drivesdk_6be83a46ca.json,c42bebaa8248c7ebc4deafdf34228490413c8f290c7b0c0edbfd05f5bf1a2af2,421278,2,digital_text,"Modified-release, film-coated, biconvex tablets, marked with the NAPP logo on one side and the strength of the preparation on the other. 10 mg: golden brown 30 mg: purple 60 mg: orange 4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 4.1 Therapeutic indications For the relief of moderate to severe pain. 4.2 Posology and method of administration Route of administration: oral MORPHINE SULPHATE (MST CONTINUS ®) tablets should be used at 12-hourly intervals. The dosage is dependent upon the severity of the pain, the patient’s age and previous history of analgesic requirements. Adults A patient presenting with severe pain, uncontrolled by weaker opioids (e.g. tramadol) should normally be started on 30 mg 12-hourly. Patients previously on normal release oral morphine should be given the same total daily dose as MORPHINE SULPHATE (MST CONTINUS®) tablets but in divided doses at 12-hourly intervals. Increasing severity of pain will require an increased dosage of the tablets. Increase incrementally by 30-50% as required. The correct dosage for any individual patient is that which is sufficient to control pain with no, or tolerable side-effects for a full 12 hours. It is recommended that the higher strengths be reserved for patients who have already been titrated to a stable analgesic dose using lower strengths of morphine or other opioid preparations. Patients receiving MORPHINE SULPHATE (MST CONTINUS®) tablets in place of parenteral morphine should be given a sufficiently increased dosage to compensate for any reduction in analgesic effects associated with oral administration. Usually, such increased requirement is of the order of 100%. In such patients individual dose adjustments are required. Children with severe cancer pain Starting dose in the range of 0.2 to 0.8 mg morphine per kg bodyweight 12-hourly is recommended. Doses should then be titrated according to the dosage prescribed to adults. Post-operative pain MORPHINE SULPHATE (MST CONTINUS ®) tablets are not recommended in the first 24 hours post-operatively or until normal bowel function has returned; thereafter it is suggested that the following dosage schedule be observed at the physician’s discretion: (a) MORPHINE SULPHATE (MST CONTINUS ®) tablets 20 mg 12 hourly to patients under 70 kg (b) MORPHINE SULPHATE (MST CONTINUS ®) tablets 30 mg 12 hourly to patients over 70 kg (c) Elderly - a reduction in dosage may be advisable in the elderly (d) Children - not recommended Supplemental parenteral morphine may be given if required but with careful attention to the total dosages of morphine, and bearing in mind the prolonged effects of morphine in this modified release formulation.",1,1,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,For the relief of moderate to severe pain.,1,1,4.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:46:15.714466+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY1329,Multivitamins + Buclizine hydrochloride + Lysine hydrochloride,Appetite Plus,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1kvhF4V5XOvdG3sqQUzPsjbNRW3vemP5t/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY1329_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kvhF4V5XOvdG3sqQUzPsjbNRW3vemP5t_view_usp_drivesdk_bffd634066.pdf,page_text/DR-XY1329_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kvhF4V5XOvdG3sqQUzPsjbNRW3vemP5t_view_usp_drivesdk_bffd634066.json,6473bc854bcd01c65e974c9ed70c9759dcc0d368370e57cd3bd945e1be82e7c1,734096,1,digital_text,Orange syrup with orange /f_lavor and sweet to bitter aftertaste.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"As a nutritional supplement to improve appetite and weight gain, and to support immune system function. For the prevention and treatment of de/f_iciencies in vitamin C and vitamin B-complex.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:46:18.692212+00:00
