PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY13465,Dexamethasone + Neomycin Sulfate (Equivalent To Neomycin) + Polymyxin B Sulfate,Maxitrol,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1v9f1GMl2yi40vqu29TBG4q4B3VPsoC0j/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY13465_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1v9f1GMl2yi40vqu29TBG4q4B3VPsoC0j_view_usp_drivesdk_ac30b6893b.pdf,page_text/DR-XY13465_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1v9f1GMl2yi40vqu29TBG4q4B3VPsoC0j_view_usp_drivesdk_ac30b6893b.json,5af2f7a2f3c7c558435ce7008c6b65d644a491c73712bb9ff8462068ef5b3713,148925,10,digital_text,"Dexamethasone, Polymyxin B, Neomycin (Maxitrol®) Ophthalmic Suspension: Sterile ophthalmic suspension Opaque, white to pale yellow suspension, no agglomerates Dexamethasone, Polymyxin B, Neomycin (Maxitrol®) Ophthalmic Ointment: Sterile ophthalmic ointment A greasy, translucent to opaque and white to light yellow, homogeneous ointment, free of lumps 3. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 3.1 Therapeutic Indications General: • For the short term treatment of steroid responsive inflammatory conditions of the eye for which a corticosteroid is indicated and where a bacterial infection or a risk of bacterial ocular infection exists. • The use of a combination drug with an anti-infective component is indicated where the risk of infection is high or where there is an expectation that potentially dangerous numbers of bacteria will be present in the eye. • Two particular anti-infective drugs in this product are active in combination against common bacterial eye pathogens including Staphylococcus aureus, Haemophilus influenzae, Klebsiella/Enterobacter species, and Pseudomonas aeruginosa • This product does not provide adequate coverage against: streptococci, including Streptococcus pneumoniae. Inflammatory conditions of the palpebral and bulbar conjunctiva, cornea, and anterior segment of the globe where the inherent risk of corticosteroids use in certain DEXAMETHASONE POLYMYXIN B SO4 NEOMYCIN SO4 [Page 2] infective conjunctivitis is accepted to obtain a diminution in edema and inflammation. Also indicated in chronic anterior uveitis and corneal injury from chemical, radiation or thermal burns; or penetration of foreign bodies. Eye Suspension (Drops) • Following surgery and injuries where an antibiotic effect is desired and where a reduction of the inflammatory reaction is also required. • Eye infections requiring simultaneous antibacterial treatment and anti-inflammatory treatment with a glucocorticosteroid. Eye Ointment • Eye inflammations, which are sensitive to glucocorticoids, are accompanied by bacterial infection, or are at risk of bacterial infection of the eye, such as conjunctivitis, inflammation of the eyelids/eyeball, inflammation of the cornea and anterior portion of the eye, chronic inflammation of the anterior iris. Dexamethasone 0.1%, Polymyxin B sulfate, Neomycin sulfate (Maxitrol®) Sterile Ophthalmic Suspension and Ointment are indicated in ocular inflammation when concurrent use of an antimicrobial is judged necessary 3.2 Posology and Method of Administration Dexamethasone, Polymyxin B, Neomycin (Maxitrol®) Ophthalmic Suspension: Posology 1 to 2 drops topically in the conjunctival sac(s). In mild disease, drops may be used up to 4 to 6 times daily. In severe disease, drops may be used hourly, being tapered to discontinuation as the inflammation subsides. Use in children The safety and efficacy of Dexamethasone, Polymyxin B and Neomycin (Maxitrol ®) ophthalmic suspension in children have not been established. Use in geriatric population No dosage adjustment is needed. Use in patients with hepatic or renal impairment Dexamethasone, Polymyxin B and Neomycin (Maxitrol ®) ophthalmic suspension has not been studied in patients with hepatic or renal impairment. However, due to low systemic absorption of the active substances after topical administration of MAXITROL ophthalmic suspension, dose adjustment is not necessary. Method of administration For ocular use. Shake well before use. After cap is removed, if tamper evident snap collar is loose, remove before using product. To prevent contamination of the dropper tip and suspension, care must be taken not to touch the eyelids, surrounding areas or other surfaces with the dropper tip. Keep the bottle tightly closed when not in use. Nasolacrimal occlusion or gently closing the eyelid after administration is recommended. This may reduce the systemic absorption of medicinal products administered via the ocular route and result in a decrease in systemic adverse reactions. If more than one topical ophthalmic product is being used, the products must be administered at least 5 minutes apart. Eye ointments should be administered last. [Page 3] Dexamethasone, Polymyxin B, Neomycin (Maxitrol®) Ophthalmic Ointment: Posology Apply a small amount into the conjunctival sac(s) up to 3 or 4 times daily or, may be used adjunctively with drops at bedtime. Use in children The safety and efficacy of the ophthalmic ointment in children have not been established. Use in geriatric population No dosage adjustment is needed. Use in patients with hepatic or renal impairment Ophthalmic Ointment has not been studied in patients with hepatic or renal impairment. However, due to low systemic absorption of the active substances after topical administration of ophthalmic ointment, dose adjustment is not necessary. Method of administration For ocular use. To prevent contamination of the tube tip and ointment, care must be taken not to touch the eyelids, surrounding areas or other surfaces with the tube tip. Keep the tube tightly closed when not in use. If more than one topical ophthalmic product is being used, the products must be administered at least 5 minutes apart. Eye ointments should be administered last.",1,3,2. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"General: • For the short term treatment of steroid responsive inflammatory conditions of the eye for which a corticosteroid is indicated and where a bacterial infection or a risk of bacterial ocular infection exists. • The use of a combination drug with an anti-infective component is indicated where the risk of infection is high or where there is an expectation that potentially dangerous numbers of bacteria will be present in the eye. • Two particular anti-infective drugs in this product are active in combination against common bacterial eye pathogens including Staphylococcus aureus, Haemophilus influenzae, Klebsiella/Enterobacter species, and Pseudomonas aeruginosa • This product does not provide adequate coverage against: streptococci, including Streptococcus pneumoniae. Inflammatory conditions of the palpebral and bulbar conjunctiva, cornea, and anterior segment of the globe where the inherent risk of corticosteroids use in certain DEXAMETHASONE POLYMYXIN B SO4 NEOMYCIN SO4 [Page 2] infective conjunctivitis is accepted to obtain a diminution in edema and inflammation. Also indicated in chronic anterior uveitis and corneal injury from chemical, radiation or thermal burns; or penetration of foreign bodies. Eye Suspension (Drops) • Following surgery and injuries where an antibiotic effect is desired and where a reduction of the inflammatory reaction is also required. • Eye infections requiring simultaneous antibacterial treatment and anti-inflammatory treatment with a glucocorticosteroid. Eye Ointment • Eye inflammations, which are sensitive to glucocorticoids, are accompanied by bacterial infection, or are at risk of bacterial infection of the eye, such as conjunctivitis, inflammation of the eyelids/eyeball, inflammation of the cornea and anterior portion of the eye, chronic inflammation of the anterior iris. Dexamethasone 0.1%, Polymyxin B sulfate, Neomycin sulfate (Maxitrol®) Sterile Ophthalmic Suspension and Ointment are indicated in ocular inflammation when concurrent use of an antimicrobial is judged necessary",1,2,3.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:46:47.398418+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY13480,Fluorometholone Acetate,Flarex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oz0cETquO8iU9GHzKAlvIV9PkRm9z2-_/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY13480_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oz0cETquO8iU9GHzKAlvIV9PkRm9z2-__view_usp_drivesdk_84e015907e.pdf,page_text/DR-XY13480_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oz0cETquO8iU9GHzKAlvIV9PkRm9z2-__view_usp_drivesdk_84e015907e.json,dcd4151afc7664b27b43151628dc7b9bb80183d69197f415311fe969a79840d2,181136,8,digital_text,"Pharmaceutical form White to off white Sterile Ophthalmic Suspen sion. The reference monograph for this drug product is USP. Active substance Each mL of the suspension contains: Fluorometholone Acetate, USP...........1.0 mg Excipients Sodium chloride, monobasic sodium phosphate (monohydrat e), disodium edetate, hydroxyethylcellulose, tyloxapol, benzalkoniu m chloride, hydrochloric acid, sodium hydroxide, purified water.",1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,"Fluorometholone Acetate (Flare x®) Sterile Ophthalmic Suspen sion is indicated for the treatment of steroid-responsiv e, non-infectious inflammations of the eyes, such as inflammations of palpebral and bulbar conjunctiva, cornea, and anterior segment of the eye.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:46:50.308615+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY13767,Tropicamide,Mydriacyl,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oPOi8naOglD7R3gyKQ7YnWpiyQZTz8bS/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY13767_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oPOi8naOglD7R3gyKQ7YnWpiyQZTz8bS_view_usp_drivesdk_b44e18adfb.pdf,page_text/DR-XY13767_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oPOi8naOglD7R3gyKQ7YnWpiyQZTz8bS_view_usp_drivesdk_b44e18adfb.json,845fb404e12fe2a20a8335582a8e7e9158225f1eefca39857617e72085383ef7,636792,2,digital_text,"Eye drops, solution. 4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 4.1 Therapeutic indications TROPICAMIDE (MYDRIACYL) Ophthalmic Solution contains tropicamide, which is pharmacologically related to the parasympatholytic (anticholinergic) group. It is a mydriatic and cycloplegic. TROPICAMIDE (MYDRIACYL) Ophthalmic Solution is indicated for mydriasis and cycloplegia for diagnostic purposes. The 0.5% solution is recommended where mydriasis only is desired. 4.2 Posology and method of administration Posology • For examination of the fundus: 1 or 2 drops of the 0.5% solution in the eye(s), 15 or 20 minutes prior to examination. Use in children Do not use in a concentration greater than 0.5% in small infants (See section 4.4, Section 4.8 and Section 4.9). Use in patients with hepatic or renal impairment The safety and efﬁcacy of TROPICAMIDE (MYDRIACYL) Ophthalmic Solution in patients with hepatic and renal impairment have not been established. Method of administration For topical ophthalmic use only. To prevent contamination of the dropper tip and solution, care must be taken not to touch the eyelids, surrounding areas or other surfaces with the dropper tip. Keep the bottle tightly closed when not in use. If more than one topical ophthalmic product is being used, the products must be administered at least 5 minutes apart. Eye ointments should be administered last.",1,1,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"775740 1. NAME OF THE MEDICINAL PRODUCT TROPICAMIDE (MYDRIACYLTM) 5 mg/ml (0.5%) Ophthalmic Solution 2. QUALITATIVE AND QUANTITATIVE COMPOSITION 1 ml of solution contains 5 mg tropicamide [Tropic acid-N-ethyl-N-(γ-picolyl) amide). Preservative: 1ml of solution contains 0.1 mg benzalkonium chloride. Tropicamide is a white crystalline solid melting at 96° to 96.5°C. It is slightly soluble in water. For the full list of excipients, see section 6.1. 3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM Eye drops, solution. 4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 4.1 Therapeutic indications TROPICAMIDE (MYDRIACYL) Ophthalmic Solution contains tropicamide, which is pharmacologically related to the parasympatholytic (anticholinergic) group. It is a mydriatic and cycloplegic. TROPICAMIDE (MYDRIACYL) Ophthalmic Solution is indicated for mydriasis and cycloplegia for diagnostic purposes. The 0.5% solution is recommended where mydriasis only is desired.",1,1,= Indication of text order1-4,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:46:53.653229+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY13867,Budesonide,BudecortÂ®,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1s6jufLIhQMDZUItGXbJnzn__hqwKKt84/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY13867_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1s6jufLIhQMDZUItGXbJnzn__hqwKKt84_view_usp_drivesdk_e2c37964dc.pdf,page_text/DR-XY13867_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1s6jufLIhQMDZUItGXbJnzn__hqwKKt84_view_usp_drivesdk_e2c37964dc.json,c75e5f55783c8cfbc9cf4c3d6961888e30fb4eef8f0d5ced22b34649107e174c,287410,9,digital_text,"Inhalation powder 3. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 3.1 Therapeutic indication Bronchial asthma 3.2 Dosage and method of administration The dosage of Budesonide (BUDECORT Turbuhaler) is individual. Initially, at the beginning of inhaled corticosteroid therapy, for therapy during periods of severe asthma or when scaling down or withdrawing oral corticosteroids the dosage should be: Children aged 6 years and older: 100-800 micrograms per day, divided into 2-4 inhalations. With daily doses up to 400 micrograms the full dose may be given in one administration. Adults: The normal dose range is 200-800 micrograms per day, divided into 2-4 inhalations. In more severe cases daily doses of up to 1600 micrograms may be needed. With daily doses up to 400 micrograms the full dose may be given in one administration. The maintenance dose should be the lowest possible. Following a single dose an effect may be expected after a few hours. The full therapeutic effect is only achieved after a few weeks of treatment. Treatment with Budesonide (BUDECORT Turbuhaler) is prophylactic therapy with no demonstrated effect on acute disorders. Clinical trials indicate that a larger amount of budesonide is deposited in the lungs when administered with Budesonide (BUDECORT Turbuhaler), compared with Budesonide (BUDECORT pMDI). If a patient in a stable phase is transferred from Budesonide [Page 2] (BUDECORT pMDI) to Budesonide (BUDECORT Turbuhaler) a reduction in dose may therefore be appropriate. In patients in whom an increased therapeutic effect is desired, in general an increase of the Budesonide (BUDECORT Turbuhaler) dose is to be recommended in preference to combination treatment with oral corticosteroids because of the lower risk of systemic side effects. Patients dependent on oral steroids: When transfer from oral steroids is initiated the patient must be in a relatively stable condition. A high dose of Budesonide (BUDECORT) is given in combination with the previously used oral steroid dose for 10 days. After that, the oral dose should be gradually reduced by e.g. 2.5 mg prednisolone or equivalent per month to the lowest possible level. The oral steroid can often be discontinued entirely. There is no experience of treatment of patients with impaired hepatic or renal function. Since budesonide is predominantly eliminated through hepatic metabolism, increased exposure may be expected in patients with severe cirrhosis of the liver. Instructions for correct use of Turbuhaler Turbuhaler is inspiratory flow-driven which means that, when the patient inhales through the mouthpiece, the substance will follow the inspired air into the airways. Note: It is important to instruct the patient • To carefully read the instructions for use: “How to use Budesonide (BUDECORT Turbuhaler) • To breathe in forcefully and deeply through the mouthpiece to ensure that an optimal dose is delivered to the lungs • Never to breath out through the mouthpiece • To rinse the mouth out with water after inhaling the prescribed dose to minimise the risk of oropharyngeal thrush It is possible that the patient will not taste or perceive any medicine when Budesonide (BUDECORT Turbuhaler) is used; this is because such a small amount of substance is dispensed.",1,2,2. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,Bronchial asthma,1,1,3.1 Therapeutic indication,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:46:56.754785+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY14048,Tamoxifen (as citrate),Nolvadex-D,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZAHPQR2I-KIQQ8XInMqZJxZMbh4-VU9W/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY14048_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZAHPQR2I-KIQQ8XInMqZJxZMbh4-VU9W_view_usp_drivesdk_caf99d9947.pdf,page_text/DR-XY14048_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZAHPQR2I-KIQQ8XInMqZJxZMbh4-VU9W_view_usp_drivesdk_caf99d9947.json,0b9484891cbf57be250a97c2ea644c402294c23a5eed631816d2466659771408,178791,10,digital_text,"White to off-white, octagonal, biconvex, film-coated tablets, intagliated with NOLVADEX D on one face and plain on the reverse. 4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 4.1 Therapeutic indications Tamoxifen (NOLVADEX-D) is indicated for the treatment of breast cancer. 4.2 Dosage and method of administration Breast Cancer Adults The recommended daily dose of tamoxifen is normally 20 mg. No additional benefit, in terms of delayed recurrence or improved survival i n patients, has been demonstrated with higher doses. Substantive evidence supporting the use of t reatment with 30-40 mg per day i s not available, although these doses have been used in some patients with advanced disease. Older people Similar dosing regimens of Tamoxifen (NOLVADEX-D) have beenused in older people with breast cancer and in some of these patients it has been used as sole therapy. Paediatric population The use of Tamoxifen (NOLVADEX-D) is not recommended in children. The safety and efficacy of Tamoxifen (NOLVADEX-D) in children has not yet been established (see 5.1 Pharmacodynamic and 5.2 Pharmacokinetic properties). Method of administration For administration by the oral route.",1,1,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,Tamoxifen (NOLVADEX-D) is indicated for the treatment of breast cancer.,1,1,4.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:46:59.697321+00:00
