PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY14481,Tobradex + Dexamethasone,Tobradex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WIsSKjr-hhp1rMfWHgoPzmRkrx-gBax9/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY14481_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WIsSKjr-hhp1rMfWHgoPzmRkrx-gBax9_view_usp_drivesdk_dc2b8dee87.pdf,page_text/DR-XY14481_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WIsSKjr-hhp1rMfWHgoPzmRkrx-gBax9_view_usp_drivesdk_dc2b8dee87.json,cbea0bcb38758803a989ce1880d1dff035b9e5f399fbdadd69324a43220cfa31,277525,13,digital_text,"Pharmaceutical form(s) Tobramycin + Dexamethasone (Tobradex®) Sterile Ophthalmic Suspension: white to off-white suspension. The reference monograph for this drug product is Ph. Eur. Tobramycin + Dexamethasone (Tobradex®) Sterile Ophthalmic Ointment: white to off-white homogeneous ointment. The reference monograph for this drug product is Ph. Eur. Certain dosage strengths and dosage forms may not be available in all countries. Active substance(s) Tobramycin + Dexamethasone (Tobradex®) Sterile Ophthalmic Suspension: Each mL of suspension contains: Tobramycin, Ph. Eur.....................3 mg Dexamethasone, Ph. Eur................1 mg Tobramycin + Dexamethasone (Tobradex®) Sterile Ophthalmic Ointment: Each gram of ointment contains: Tobramycin, Ph. Eur......................3 mg Dexamethasone, Ph. Eur................1 mg Excipients Tobramycin + Dexamethasone (Tobradex®) Sterile Ophthalmic Suspension: Excipient with known effect: 1 mL of the eye drops suspension contains 0.1 mg of benzalkonium chloride. Other excipients: tyloxapol, disodium edetate, sodium chloride, hydroxyethylcellulose, sodium sulphate anhydrous, sulphuric acid and/or sodium hydroxide (to adjust pH) and purified water. Tobramycin + Dexamethasone (Tobradex®) Sterile Ophthalmic Ointment: Other excipients: chlorobutanol anhydrous, liquid paraffin and white soft paraffin. [Page 2] Pharmaceutical formulations may vary between countries",1,2,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,"Tobramycin/Dexamethasone (TOBRADEX®) Sterile Ophthalmic Suspension and Ointment are indicated for steroid-responsive inflammatory ocular conditions for which a corticosteroid is indicated and where superficial bacterial ocular infection or a risk of bacterial ocular infection exists. Ocular steroids are indicated in inflammatory conditions of the palpebral and bulbar conjunctiva, cornea and anterior segment of the globe where the inherent risk of steroid use in certain infective conjunctivitises is accepted to obtain a diminution in edema and inflammation. They are also indicated in chronic anterior uveitis and corneal injury from chemical, radiation or thermal burns, or penetration of foreign bodies. The use of a combination drug with an anti-infect ive component is indicated where the risk of superficial ocular infection is high or where th ere is an expectation that potentially dangerous numbers of bacteria will be present in the eye.",2,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:47:27.712320+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY14715,Fluorouracil,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1tgAo9uXYvqFqDD4vP5pdYLBHbTiqirO2/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY14715_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1tgAo9uXYvqFqDD4vP5pdYLBHbTiqirO2_view_usp_drivesdk_fa16179036.pdf,page_text/DR-XY14715_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1tgAo9uXYvqFqDD4vP5pdYLBHbTiqirO2_view_usp_drivesdk_fa16179036.json,c6421394aea6cab818a5d1c829b778ffc99f954bc4e5c876d24355079e15eaac,285105,13,digital_text,"The chemical structure of fluorouracil is shown below: The CAS registry number is 51-21-8. The chemical formula of fluorouracil is C4H3FN2O2. Its molecular weight is 130.1. Fluorouracil is a white to almost white, practically odorless, crystalline powder. It is sparingly soluble in water, slightly soluble in alcohol, and practically insoluble in chloroform and ether. Fluorouracil Injection is a sterile, colorless, preservative free solution containing 5-Fluorouracil in Water for Injections, prepared with the aid of sodium hydroxide. The pH of the solution is approximately 8.9. Fluorouracil Injection is a clear, colorless to slightly yellow solution. It is available as a solution containing 50 milligrams/mL of fluorouracil.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Fluorouracil is indicated alone or in combination for the palliative treatment of malignant tumors, particularly o f the breast, colon or rectum; and in the treatment of gastric, primary hepatic, pancreatic, uterine (cervical particularly), ovarian and bladder carcinomas. Fluorouracil should only b e used when other proven measures have failed or are considered impractical.",1,1,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:47:30.687067+00:00
