PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY18115,Mefenamic Acid,Ponser,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1jhDN4JJ1N6UFeihmuMmnEGdK4jSiFzqu/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY18115_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jhDN4JJ1N6UFeihmuMmnEGdK4jSiFzqu_view_usp_drivesdk_ea17c58f25.pdf,page_text/DR-XY18115_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jhDN4JJ1N6UFeihmuMmnEGdK4jSiFzqu_view_usp_drivesdk_ea17c58f25.json,1652426b8ef7e9d6d36b2ffa26724f94b8f458336ba78236f9c0f60987bcecbc,104439,2,digital_text,"Ponser 500 mg capsule is a oﬀ-white microcrystalline powder encapsulated in empty gelatin capsule size #0 with light blue cap and white body. Ponser 500 mg tablet is a oﬀ-white, capsule form tablet. Ponser 50 mg per 5 mL is a white to oﬀ-white suspension.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Mefenamic Acid is indicated in the relief of mild to moderately severe somatic and neuritic pains such as headache, migraine, traumatic pain, postpartum pain, postoperative pain, dental pain and pain conditions: dysmenorrheal, hemorralgia, accompanied by spasm or hypogastric pain.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:51:12.258722+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY18126-B,Amoxicillin (as trihydrate),Termox,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/19_o2-yPpIyE6DqCW4SnQ6s2gUtl1IoBg/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY18126-B_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19_o2-yPpIyE6DqCW4SnQ6s2gUtl1IoBg_view_usp_drivesdk_0369163beb.pdf,page_text/DR-XY18126-B_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19_o2-yPpIyE6DqCW4SnQ6s2gUtl1IoBg_view_usp_drivesdk_0369163beb.json,fe8c078072fb25df16c15e50629ff6701cfee3df05b112cfd3421d183630eeb6,262473,1,digital_text,"Amoxicillin is a semi-synthetic antibiotic, an analog on ampicillin with a broad-spectrum of bactericidal activity against many gram-positive and gram-negative microorganism. Amoxicillin is D(-)-a-amino-p-hydroxybenzyl penicillin trihydrate.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,For the treatment of infections caused by susceptible strains of gram-positive and gram-negative microorganisms.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:51:14.944797+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY18187,CARBOCISTEINE,GUIAMAR,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RnsPTH1693nJlrhsd0bbLqSdKSrc5RM9/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY18187_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RnsPTH1693nJlrhsd0bbLqSdKSrc5RM9_view_usp_drivesdk_1e7b3b5a33.pdf,page_text/DR-XY18187_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RnsPTH1693nJlrhsd0bbLqSdKSrc5RM9_view_usp_drivesdk_1e7b3b5a33.json,46e2c2b47e0cc0b29176ef20d1573de47d53de7dfed523c92fd87847c26e2e7a,255534,2,digital_text_and_ocr,"Carbociseine ( Guiamar)100 mg/5 mL is a clear orange syrup with orange flavor. What is in the Medicine? This medicine contains Carbocisteine, a mucolytic that causes phlegm to be less thick and sticky , th us making it easier to cough up and expel through the mouth. Strength of the Medicine: Each 5 mL (1 teaspoonful) syrup contains: Carbocisteine ………………………………………………….. 100 mg What is this medicine used for? This medicine is used for its mucolytic activity in respiratory disorders associated with productive cough. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Children: To be taken three to four times a day 8 - 12 years: 10 mL – 15 mL 4 - 7 years : 7.5 mL- 10 mL 2 - 3 years : 5 mL - 7.5 mL Or as prescribed by the physician. When should you NOT take this medicine? * If you are allergic to the product and to any of its ingredients. * If you have a history of peptic ulcer and should be avoided if you have an active ulceration Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: *This medicine should be given with care in patents with history of peptic ulcer and be avoided in patients with active ulceration. *Take this medicine exactly as directed on the label or as prescribed by your doctor. *Do not use this medicine in larger amounts or for more than recommended. *Tell your doctor that you are taking other medicines known to caus bleeding in the stomach. *Do not use this medicine after the expiry date on the label. *Ask your doctor if you are pregnant or breastfeeding before taking this medicine. What are the undesirable effects of this medicine? Nausea and gastric discomfort, gastro -intestinal bleeding and skin rash have occasionally occurred with carbocisteine. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Tell your doctor about all medicines you are using and medicines you start or stop using. Other drugs may interact with carbocisteine, including prescription and over-the-counter drugs, vitamins and herbal products. What should you do if you miss a dose of this medicine? Take the missed dose as soon as you remember. Skip the missed dose if it is almost time for your next scheduled dose . Do not double the dose. If you have any further questions about these oral syrup, ask your doctor or pharmacist. What are the signs and symptoms of overdose? Gastro-intestinal disturbance What should you do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? Contact your doctor, or hospital immediately. Bring the container or label with you to help doctors with necessary information. How should you keep/ store Carbocisteine? Keep out of the reach and sight of children. Do not use Carbocisteine syrup after the expiry date wh ich is stated on the label. It should be stored at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Keep or store it away from direct heat and light. Medicines should not be disposed of via wastewater or household waste. Ask your pharmacist how to dispose of medicines no longer required. These measures will help to protect the environment When should you consult your doctor? *Before taking this medicine, consult your doctor if you are pregnant and breastfeeding. *If symptoms do not improve or new symptoms appear. Name and Address of the Manufacturer and Marketing Authorization Holder: St. Martin Pharm Lab Co. 55 Lakandula Street, Parang, Marikina City, Philippines Registration Number: DR-XY18187 Date of First Authorization/ Renewal of the Authorization: 12/27/2012 / 12/27/2024 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: 9/16/2019 “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph” Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. CARBOCISTEINE [Page 2] [Page 3]",1,1,Description of the Product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T18:51:39.237083+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY18227,Omeprazole,Losec,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1jdjC1Wb_o9ly3wkNSz7k5ficXNE9sG0Z/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY18227_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jdjC1Wb_o9ly3wkNSz7k5ficXNE9sG0Z_view_usp_drivesdk_e3707eb939.pdf,page_text/DR-XY18227_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jdjC1Wb_o9ly3wkNSz7k5ficXNE9sG0Z_view_usp_drivesdk_e3707eb939.json,8efdca72bb29f83e22d0b695fadb48e0f9502932d409177f18497e24c90f38b5,203478,3,digital_text,"Omeprazole (Losec) capsule 10 mg: hard gelatin capsule with an opaque pink body, marked 10 and an opaque pink cap marked A/OS. Each capsule contains omeprazole 10 mg as enteric coated pellets. Omeprazole (Losec) capsule 20 mg: hard gelatin capsule with an opaque pink body, marked 20 and an opaque reddish-brown cap marked A/OM. Each capsule contains omeprazole 20 mg as enteric coated pellets. 4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 4.1 Therapeutic indications Omeprazole (Losec) is indicated for the treatment of – Duodenal ulcer – Gastric ulcer – NSAID associated gastric and duodenal ulcers or erosions – Helicobacter pylori eradication in peptic ulcer disease – Reflux esophagitis – Symptomatic gastro-esophageal reflux disease – Acid related dyspepsia – Zollinger-Ellison syndrome – Patients considered to be at risk of aspiration of gastric contents during general anesthesia/Acid aspiration prophylaxis. 4.2 Dosage and method of administration Omeprazole (Losec) capsules are recommended to be given in the morning and swallowed whole with half a glass of water. The capsules must not be chewed or crushed. For patients with swallowing difficulties and for children who can drink or swallow semi-solid food The capsule can be opened and the contents swallowed directly with half a glass of water or after mixing the contents in a slightly acidic fluid eg, fruit juice or applesauce, or in non-carbonated water. The dispersion should be taken immediately (or within 30 minutes). Always stir just before drinking. Rinse it down with half a glass of water. Alternatively, patients can suck the capsule and swallow the pellets with half a glass of water. Ingest without chewing the enteric-coated pellets. Duodenal ulcer The recommended dosage in patients with an active duodenal ulcer is Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg once daily. Symptom resolution is rapid and in most patients healing occurs within 2 weeks. For those patients who may not be fully healed after the initial course, healing usually occurs during a further 2-week treatment period. In patients with poorly responsive duodenal ulcer, 2 capsules of Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg once daily is recommended and healing is usually achieved within 4 weeks. For the prevention of relapse in patients with duodenal ulcer disease, the recommended dose is Omeprazole (Losec) 10 mg once daily. If needed the dose can be increased to 1 to 2 capsules of Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg once daily. For NSAID associated duodenal ulcers, see NSAID associated gastroduodenal lesions. For eradication of Helicobacter pylori, see Helicobacter pylori (Hp) eradication regimens in peptic ulcer disease. Gastric ulcer The recommended dosage is Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg once daily. Symptom resolution is rapid and in most patients healing occurs within 4 weeks. For those patients who may not be fully healed after the initial course, healing usually occurs during a further 4-week treatment period. In patients with poorly responsive gastric ulcer, 2 capsules of Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg once daily is recommended and healing is usually achieved within 8 weeks. For the prevention of relapse of patients with poorly responsive gastric ulcer, the recommended dose is Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg once daily. If needed, the dose can be increased to 2 capsules of Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg once daily. For eradication of Helicobacter pylori, see Helicobacter pylori (Hp) eradication regimens in peptic ulcer disease. For NSAID associated gastric ulcers, duodenal ulcers or gastroduodenal erosions in patients with or without continued NSAID treatment the recommended dosage of Omeprazole (Losec) is 20 mg once daily. Symptom resolution is rapid and in most patients healing occurs within 4 weeks. For those patients who may not be fully healed after the initial course, healing usually occurs during a further 4-week treatment period. For the prevention of NSAID associated gastric ulcers, duodenal ulcers, gastroduodenal erosions and dyspeptic symptoms the recommended dosage of Omeprazole (Losec) is 20 mg once daily. Helicobacter pylori (Hp) eradication regimens in peptic ulcer disease: Triple therapy regimens: Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg, amoxicillin 1 g and clarithromycin 500 mg, all twice a day for one week or Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg, metronidazole 400 mg (or tinidazole 500 mg) and clarithromycin 250 mg, all twice a day for one week. or Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg 2 capsules once daily with amoxicillin 500 mg and metronidazole 400 mg both three times a day for one week. Dual therapy regimens: Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg 2-4 capsules daily with amoxicillin 1.5 g daily in divided doses for two weeks. In clinical studies, daily doses of 1.5-3 g of amoxicillin have been used or Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg 2 capsules once daily and clarithromycin 500 mg three times a day for two weeks. To ensure healing in patients with active peptic ulcer disease, see further dosage recommendations for Duodenal and Gastric ulcer. In each regimen if the patient is still Hp positive, therapy may be repeated. Reflux esophagitis The recommended dosage is Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg once daily. Symptom resolution is rapid and in most patients healing occurs within 4 weeks. For those patients who may not be fully healed after the initial course, healing usually occurs during a further 4-week treatment period. In patients with severe reflux esophagitis 2 capsules of Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg once daily is recommended and healing is usually achieved within 8 weeks. For the long-term management of patients with healed reflux esophagitis the recommended dose is Omeprazole (Losec) 10 mg once daily. If needed, the dose can be increased to 1-2 capsules of Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg once daily. Symptomatic gastro-esophageal reflux disease The recommended dosage is Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg daily. Symptom relief is rapid. Patients may respond adequately to 10 mg daily, and therefore individual dose adjustment should be considered. If symptom control has not been achieved after 4 weeks of treatment with Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg daily, further investigation is recommended. Acid-related dyspepsia In the relief of symptoms in patients with epigastric pain/discomfort with or without heartburn the recommended dosage is Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg once daily. Patients may respond adequately to 10 mg daily and therefore this dose could be considered as a starting dose. If symptom control has not been achieved after 4 weeks of treatment with Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg daily, further investigation is recommended. Zollinger-Ellison syndrome In patients with Zollinger-Ellison syndrome, the dosage should be individually adjusted and treatment continued as long as is clinically indicated. The recommended initial dosage is 3 capsules of Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg daily. All patients with severe disease and inadequate response to other therapies have been effectively controlled and more than 90% of the patients maintained on doses of Omeprazole (Losec) 20-120 mg daily. When doses exceed Omeprazole (Losec) 80 mg daily, the dose should be divided and given twice daily. Acid aspiration prophylaxis The recommended dosage is 2 capsules of Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg in the evening before surgery, followed by 2 capsules of Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg on the morning after surgery. Impaired renal function Dose adjustment is not needed in patients with impaired renal function. Impaired hepatic function As bioavailability and plasma half-life of omeprazole are increased in patients with impaired hepatic function a daily dose of 10-20 mg may be sufficient. Elderly Dose adjustment is not needed in the elderly. Children For use in children 2 years and older the recommended dose is: Weight Dosage 10-20 kg Omeprazole (Losec) 10 mg once daily >20 kg Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg once daily If needed the dose may be increased to 20 mg and 40 mg respectively. For use in children 0-24 months the recommended dose is: Weight Dosage 10-20 kg Omeprazole (Losec) 10 mg once daily If needed the dose may be increased to 20 mg <10 kg 1 mg/kg/day For children 0-3 months a dose of 0.5 mg/kg/day may be sufficient Helicobacter pylori eradication for children from 4 years Weight Dosage 15-30 kg Omeprazole (Losec) 10 mg, amoxicillin 25 mg/kg, and clarithromycin 7.5 mg/kg, all twice a day for one week. 30-40 kg Omeprazole (Losec) 20 mg, amoxicillin 750 mg and clarithromycin 7.5 mg/kg, all twice a day for one week. >40 kg Dosage as in adults",1,1,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,Omeprazole (Losec) is indicated for the treatment of – Duodenal ulcer – Gastric ulcer – NSAID associated gastric and duodenal ulcers or erosions – Helicobacter pylori eradication in peptic ulcer disease – Reflux esophagitis – Symptomatic gastro-esophageal reflux disease – Acid related dyspepsia – Zollinger-Ellison syndrome – Patients considered to be at risk of aspiration of gastric contents during general anesthesia/Acid aspiration prophylaxis.,1,1,4.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:51:41.973796+00:00
