PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY19608,Cefalexin (As Monohydrate),Airex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1u_mL6sUv3no0iIYC6juGuZMETv7awRZm/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY19608_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1u_mL6sUv3no0iIYC6juGuZMETv7awRZm_view_usp_drivesdk_54aff95933.pdf,page_text/DR-XY19608_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1u_mL6sUv3no0iIYC6juGuZMETv7awRZm_view_usp_drivesdk_54aff95933.json,210cdc8b2e46b21c2588c2ceff074ec60517e4384ebae8d2f518df6ac0d25d8a,113420,2,digital_text,"Airex 250 mg is almost white, semi granular powder encapsulated in empty gelatin capsule size # 1 with gray cap and yellow body. Airex 500 mg is a white, semi granular powder encapsulated in empty gelatin capsule size # 0 with scarlet cap and ivory body. Airex 250 mg suspension is an orange granule. Airex 125 mg suspension is an off-white powder. Airex 100 mg per mL suspension (oral drops) is a white powder.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of urinary tract infection and respiratory tract infection, otitis media, skin and other infections due to sensitive organisms.",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:54:18.360526+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY19867,Meclizine Hydrochloride,Bonamine,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/16PqnBAIcxe1Neg5-aB37fNfAKZfL5o8l/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY19867_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_16PqnBAIcxe1Neg5-aB37fNfAKZfL5o8l_view_usp_drivesdk_cb28a33e18.pdf,page_text/DR-XY19867_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_16PqnBAIcxe1Neg5-aB37fNfAKZfL5o8l_view_usp_drivesdk_cb28a33e18.json,7f4050a49f9046c09b94cd0b4034533d9c79b5e29fc205542ad96eea0f4030e8,220276,1,digital_text,"Meclizine Hydrochloride (Bonamine®) Chewable Tablet is a pale orange, mottled, round, biconvex tablet, plain on one side and scored on the other side with characteristic sweet yogurt-like flavor. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Active Pharmaceutical Ingredient (API): Meclizine Hydrochloride Excipients used are: . . Glycine, Corn Starch, Carmellose Calcium, Flavor, Magnesium Stearate, Sodium Saccharin, Colorant, Sodium Lauryl Sulfate, and Purified Water. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Meclizine Hydrochloride (Bonamine®) Chewable_Tablet for Kids: . Each chewable tablet contains 12.5 mg of MeclIzme Hydrochloride. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Meclizine Hydrochloride (Bonamine®) Chewable Tablet i_s used_ for _the prevention and treatment of nausea, vomiting, or dizziness associated with motion sickness. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? A daily dose should be taken one hour before travel starts for 24-hour protection. . The tablet may be chewed and swallowed with or without water or swallowed whole with water. MECLIZINE HYDROCHLORIDE (BONAMINE®) 12.5 MG CHEWABLE TABLET FOR KIDS Age Recommended Dose Children > 11 yrs. old 2 tablets 5 to 10 yrs. old 1 tablet Or, as prescribed by a physician. If additional dose is needed, interval should be 4 hours or longer. Children 5-15 yrs old should be limited to two single doses only. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? • A known hypersensitivity to Meclizine or any ingredient in this product. • Patients taking monoamine oxidase inhibitor antidepressant. • Pregnant or breastfeeding mothers. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE • This drug may cause drowsiness. Take due precautions against driving a car or operating dangerous machinery. • A doctor must always be consulted before giving Meclizine especially if the patient is taking other medications (antidepressant) and patients who are alcoholics or who regularly ingest alcohol in excess before giving this drug. • It is also wise to remember to check the expiration date on the package or label of this product. Do not use after expiry date. FRONT 75 x 160 mm Dimensions are in millimeters unless otherwise noted Tolerances are + 1 mm Revision Date: Supplier: Color Used: Graphics Artist: ■ Black 75 mm UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Drowsiness, fatigue, dry mouth, constipation, headache, stomach upset, and rarely blurred vision have been reported with the use of Meclizine. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Avoid alcohol, sedatives, anti-allergic drugs and tranquilizers while taking Meclizine as this may increase the drowsiness effect. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Do not double the dose. If you miss a dose, just take the next dose as scheduled_ (i.e., once a day) if needed to prevent and treat nausea, vomiting, or dizziness associated with motion sickness. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE Overdose of Meclizine may manifest as follows: • Drowsiness • Dry mouth • Fatigue • Rarely, blurred vision WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If more than the recommended dose has been given, consult a health professional immediately. Do not exceed recommended dosage. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Keep out of reach of children. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? Pregnant or breastfeeding mothers, patients with increased pressure in the e_ye, asthma, emphysema, chronic pulmonary disease, difficulty in breathing and th_ose with difficulty in urination due to enlargement of the prostate gland and those taking sedatives and tranquilizers should take Meclizine only under the direction of a doctor. HOW SUPPLIED? Meclizine Hydrochloride (Bonamine®) 12.5 mg Chewable Tablet for Kids: Alu/PVC Blister Pack x 1 O's (Box of 120's) NAME AND ADDRESS OF MARKETING AUTHORIZATION HOLDER Taisho Pharmaceuticals (Philippines), Inc. 8th Floor CLIPP Center Building, 11th Avenue corner 39th Street, Bonifacio Global City, Taguig 1634, Philippines Under Authority of: Taisho Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd., Tokyo, Japan Trademark Owner NAME AND ADDRESS OF MANUFACTURER lnterphil Laboratories, Inc. Canlubang Industrial Estate, Bo. Pittland, Cabuyao, Laguna, Philippines ADR REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adverse drug reaction, report_ to FDA: www.fda.gov.ph Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. REGISTRATION NUMBER Meclizine Hydrochloride (Bonamine®) 12.5 mg Chewable Tablet for Kids: DR-XY19867 RENEWAL OF THE AUTHORIZATION Meclizine Hydrochloride (Bonamine®) 12.5 mg Chewable Tablet for Kids: 21 October 2029 DATE OF REVISION OF THE PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET (PIL) May 2024 @-1 0524 BACK r-' O'I 0 [Page 2]",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T18:54:21.186149+00:00
