ions susceptible to Metronidazole: described in the indications. - Amoebiasis - Urogenital trichomoniasis - Nonspecific vaginalis PRECAUTION - Giardiasis Patients should be warned not to take any alcohol during treatment due to possible occurrence of disulfiram-tike - Curative treatment of medico-surgical infections due to susceptible anaerobic pathogens. reactions. - Prophylaxis against infections caused by susceptible anaerobic pathogens in high risk surgical contents - Conversion from prophylactic or curative injectable treatment of infections due to susceptible PREGNANCY AND LACTATION anaerobic pathogens Metronidazole crosses the placental barrier and its effects on the human fetal organogenesis are not known; tts Metronidazole is also indicated in the treatment of trichomoniasis in both male and female patients when the use in pregnancy should be carefully evaluated. Metronidazole is present in human milk when administered to presence of trichomonas has been demonstrated by wet smear or culture and for sexual partners of those nursing mothers; unnecessary exposure to the drug should be avoided. ients who have recurrence of infections. Trichomonal infection is demonstrated for other protozoa including Entamoeba hysfolytica, giardiasis and liver abscess. [Page 2]",1,1,INDICATION,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T18:55:08.430552+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY19897,Cefuroxime (As Sodium),Profurex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GIVv_UFh4IZPf3yR_DBMgM8kspcRD2T6/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY19897_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GIVv_UFh4IZPf3yR_DBMgM8kspcRD2T6_view_usp_drivesdk_87a2b7dd48.pdf,page_text/DR-XY19897_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GIVv_UFh4IZPf3yR_DBMgM8kspcRD2T6_view_usp_drivesdk_87a2b7dd48.json,597eb8c5b03d0af7bef30015dbf39175dbed8af6f07edd0f03d9b816cccc1daf,7030489,1,ocr,"diuretics such as furosemide as these combinations are suspected of adversely affecting renal function. Clinical experience with Cefuroxime (Profurex) is a white to faintly powder to which appropriate amount of water is added to prepare a suspension for Cefuroxime has shown that this is not likely to be a problem at the recommended dose levels. There is no experimental evidence of intramuscular use or a solution for intravenous administration. embryonic or teratogenic effects attributable to Cefuroxime, but as with all drugs, it should be administered with caution during the early months of pregnancy. Freshly prepared solutions of Cefuroxime (Profurex) are yellowish in color, variations in the intensity of this color do not indicate any change in either the efficacy or safety of the product. Cefuroxime does not interfere in the enzyme-based tests for glycosuria. Slight interference with copper reduction methods PHARMACODYNAM (Benedict's, Fehlings, Clinitest) may be observed. However, this should not lead to false-positive results, as may be experienced Cefuroxime is a bactericidal cephalosporin antibiotic which is resistant to most B-lactamases and is active against a wide range with some other cephalosporins. of gram-positive and gram-negative organisms. It is indicated for the treatment of infections caused by sensitive bacteria. Cefuroxime may cause false-negative reactions in the ferricyanide test. Some cephalosporins can cause a falsely high reading In addition, it is an effective prophylactic agent against post-operative infection in a variety of operations. Usually, it will be in the alkaline picrate assay for creatinine, although the degree of elevation is unlikely to be of clinical importance. It is possible that Cefuroxime may also interfere with this determination. As with other antibiotics, prolonged use may result in effective alone, but when appropriate, it may be used in combination with an aminoglycoside antibiotic or in conjunction with metronidazole, orally or by suppository or injection especially for prophylaxis in colonic surgery. (see Pharmaceutical Precautions) the over-growth of non-susceptible organisms. PHARMACOKINETICS PREGNANCY AND LACTATION Absorption Cefuroxime is pregnancy category B, duing pregnancy, mean plasma concentrations of Cefuroxime are 50% lower, the AUC is After IM injection the peak serum level occurs after about 15-60 minutes and range from 26-34.9 mcg/mL. After IV infusion 25% lower, and the plasma half-life is shorter than nonpregnant values. Cefuroxime is one of the antibiotics recommended for prophylactic use prior to cesarean delivery. over 30 minutes of single 750 mg dose of Cefuroxime results in peak serum concentrations of the drug averaging 51.1 mcg/mL. Distribution ADVERSE DRUG REACTIONS Cefuroxime is excreted in breast milk. Caution should be exercised if Cefuroxime is given to nursing mother. The apparent volume of distribution of Cefuroxime in healthy adults ranges from 9.3-15.8 L/1.73m2. Cefuroxime can be found in bone, synovial fluid and aqueous humour above the minimum inhibitory levels for common pathogens. Adverse reactions to Cefuroxime have occurred relatively infrequent and have been generally mild and transient in nature. The blood-brain barrier can be passed by Cefuroxime when the meninges are inflamed. Effects reported include rashes, gastrointestinal disturbances and candida intertrigo. The principal changes in hematological The plasma protein binding of Cefuroxime is about 33-50%. parameters seen in some patients are decreased hemoglobin concentration and eosinophilia. Metabolism and excretion A positive Coomb's test has been found in some patients treated with Cefuroxime this phenomenon can interfere Cefuroxime is not metabolized and is excreted unchanged principally in urine by both glomerular filtration and tubular secretion. with the crossmatching of blood. In adults with normal renal function, 90-100% of a single IM or IV dose of Cefuroxime is excreted unchanged in urine within Although there are sometimes transient increases in serum liver enzymes and serum bilirubin, particularly in patients with 24 hours, most being. pre-existing liver disease, there is no evidence of hepatic involvement. BACTERIOLOGY There may also be some variation in the results of biochemical tests of renal function, but these do not appear to be of clinical Cefuroxime is highly active against Staphylococcus aureus, including strains which are resistant to penicillin (but not the rare importance. As a precaution, renal functions should be monitored if this is already impaired. Transient pain may be experienced at the site of intramuscular injection. This is more likely to occur with higher doses. However, methicillin-resistant strains) ; Staphylococcus epidermidis, Haemophilus influenzae, Klebsiella spp., Enterobacter spp., Streptococcus pyogenes, Escherichia coli, Streptococcus mitis (viridans group), Clostridium spp., Proteus mirabilis, Proteus rettgeri, Salmonella typhi, it is unlikely to be a cause for discontinuation of treatment. Salmonella typhimurium, and other Salmonella spp., Shigella spp., Neisseria spp., (including B-lactamase producing strains DRUG INTERACTIONS of N. gonorrheae) and Bordetella pertussis. It is also moderately active against strains of Proteus vulgaris, Proteus morgani, Concurrent administration of probenecid prolongs the excretion of Cefuroxime and produces an elevated peak serum level. and Bacteroides fragilis. Concurrent administration of potent diuretics, aminoglycosides, estrogens or progestins may adversely affect renal function. OVERDOSAGE In vitro, the activity of Cefuroxime and aminoglycoside antibiotics in combination have been shown to be at least additive with occasional evidence of synergy. PHARMACEUTICAL PRECAUTION Serum levels of Cefuroxime are reduced by dialysis.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Cefuroxime (Profurex) is indicated for (1) prophylaxis against infection to abdominal, pelvic, orthopedic, cardiac, pulmonary, The dry powder in vials should be stored at temperatures not exceeding 25°C and protected from light. Cefuroxime (Profurex) esophageal, and vascular surgery where there is increased risk of infection ; (2) respiratory tract infections, e.g.acute and chronic should not be mixed in the syringe with aminoglycoside antibiotics. Suspension of Cefuroxime (Profurex) for intramuscular bronchitis, infected bronchiectasis, bacterial pneumonia, lung abscesses, and post-operative chest infections ; (3) ear, nose injection and aqueous solutions for direct intravenous injection retain their potency for 5 hours if kept at temperature not exceeding 25°C and for 48 hours if refrigerated. More diluted solutions, i.e. 1.5 g plus 50 mL Water for Injection, retain their potency for 24 hours and throat infections, e.g. sinusitis, tonsilitis, and pharyngitis ; (4) urinary tract infections like acute or chronic pyelonephritis, cystitis ; (5) soft tissue infections like cellulitis, erysipelas, peritonitis ; (6) bone and joint infections like osteomyelitis and septic if kept at temperature not exceeding 25°C and for 72 hours if refrigerated. The color of prepared solution and suspension of arthritis ; (7) obstetric and gynecologic infection, pelvic inflammatory diseases ; (8) gonorrhea particularly when penicillin is Cefuroxime (Profurex) may darken on storage. unsuitable ; (9) other infections including septicemia and meningitis. Cefuroxime (Profurex) is compatible with the more commonly used intravenous infusion fluids. It will retain potency for up",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T18:55:25.803364+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY19929,,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1iCsgCPrA7NsupKcmHTqPYK_ZJe4D31G5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY19929_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1iCsgCPrA7NsupKcmHTqPYK_ZJe4D31G5_view_usp_drivesdk_aea0cfc98d.pdf,page_text/DR-XY19929_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1iCsgCPrA7NsupKcmHTqPYK_ZJe4D31G5_view_usp_drivesdk_aea0cfc98d.json,f58a09accd2dae5e81636e1ad7ac7b2c8e516ed4c86c68054c111ae0e5bf7b55,973661,1,ocr,"Infuse only after diluting with large-volume parenteral solution. Potassium Chloride 2 mEq/mL Solution for Injection (IV) is a sterile, non-pyrogenic, hypertonic solution of Administer only if solutionis clear andthe sealis intact. Discard any unused portion. Potassium Chloridein Water for Injection. Regular laboratory determinations must be done to monitor fluid and electrolyte, and acid-base balance. pH: 4.0to8.0 Incompatib es: Pharmacology: Potassium Chloride should not be added to mannitol, blood or blood products, or amino-acid or lipid- Potassium is a predominant intracellular cation which plays a vital role in the maintenance of electrical containing solutions because it may precipitate these substances from solution or cause lysis of infused excitability of nerve and muscle. It also plays an important role in the genesis and correction of red blood cells. imbalances in acid-base metabolism. Improperly used, potassium salts are extremely dangerous. Storage Condition: Pharmacokinetics: Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. A high gradient of potassium (K') across cell membranes is maintained by active ion transport Protect from freezing. systems. Intracellular concentration is approximately 150 mmol while the plasma concentration is 4 to mmol. Caution: Potassium (K’) is freely filtered at the glomerulus and is almost completely reabsorbed in the proximal Foods, Drugs, Devices, and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription. tubule. About 10% of the amount filtered isexcreted in theurine. For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph",1,1,Description:,"Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. For the treatment of hypokalemia of all causes, including hypokalemic periodic paralysis and diabetic ketoacidosis. Presentation: In cases of metabolic alkalosis with potassium (K*) depletion resistant to Sodium Chloride. 20 mL vials of lowdensity polyethylene plasticin boxes of 20’s For acute or chronic disorders of acid-base imbalance. Potassium (K') supplementation should be considered if: Date of First Authorization: 16 May 1995 1 Plasma potassium (K’) concentration is repeatedly less than 2.5 mmol even if asymptomatic. = 2. Plasma potassium (K*) concentration is between 2.5 and 3.0 mmol with symptoms or EKG Renewalof the Authorization: 25 May 2025 findings suggestive of hypokalemia. 3. Plasma _ potassium (K*) concentration is consistently between 3.0 and 3.5 mmol with clear-cut Date of Revision of Package Insert: 29 August 2020 symptoms or EKG signs of hypokalemia. DR-XY19929",1,1,Indications:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T18:55:33.573731+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY20042,Fluticasone Propionate,Cultivate,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_0G2RN2fCoXxuJDHhF9dqLBDNMJJM7Rt/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY20042_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_0G2RN2fCoXxuJDHhF9dqLBDNMJJM7Rt_view_usp_drivesdk_256777fed7.pdf,page_text/DR-XY20042_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_0G2RN2fCoXxuJDHhF9dqLBDNMJJM7Rt_view_usp_drivesdk_256777fed7.json,e5daa5b55a2970d443ee99877495f0b5744b304f7fe9292a432027e3dc8faefb,119810,4,digital_text,Each gram of Fluticasone propionate (Cutivate) Cream contains 500 microgram s of fluticasone propionate (micronised).,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"TREATMENT OF INFLAMMATORY DERMATOSES Fluticasone propionate (Cutivate) Cream is a potent topical corticosteroid indicated for adults, children and infants aged 3 months and over for the relief of the inflammatory and pruritic manifestations of corticosteroid-responsive dermatoses. These include: the following: − Atopic dermatitis (including infantile atopic dermatitis) − Nummular dermatitis (discoid eczemas) − Prurigo nodularis [Page 2] − Psoriasis (excluding wi despread plaque psoriasis) − Lichen simplex chronicus ( neurodermatitis) and lichen planus − Seborrhoeic dermatitis − Irritant or allergic contact dermatitis − Discoid lupus erythematosus − An adjunct to systemic steroid therapy in generalised erythroderma − Insect bite reactions − Miliaria REDUCTION OF RISK OF RELAPSE Fluticasone propionate (Cutivate) Cream is indicated for the reduction of the risk of relapse of chronic recurrent atopic dermatitis once an acute episode has been treated effectively.",1,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:55:36.233608+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY2013,Acyclovir,Zovirax,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/10Vo5q_jmYgBPpKH38IPoIrm9M2JecSxt/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY2013_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_10Vo5q_jmYgBPpKH38IPoIrm9M2JecSxt_view_usp_drivesdk_f12e027234.pdf,page_text/DR-XY2013_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_10Vo5q_jmYgBPpKH38IPoIrm9M2JecSxt_view_usp_drivesdk_f12e027234.json,ca125d1919d15b525fa6550ae8cb2650d991f4f110a24a91cc66b210979d3549,118953,5,digital_text,"Acyclovir (Zovirax) 200mg Tablet: Each white, round, biconvex tablet, engraved with ‘GXCL3” on one side and plain on the other contains 200mg acyclovir. Acyclovir (Zovirax) 400mg Tablet: Each whi te, shield shaped tablet, engraved with ‘GXCM1” on one side and plain on the other contains 400mg acyclovir. Acyclovir (Zovirax) 800mg Tablet: Each white, biconvex, oval tablet engraved with ‘GXCX5” on one side and plain on the other contains 800mg acyclovir.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Acyclovir (Zovirax) oral formulations are indicated for the treatment of herpes simplex virus infections of the skin and mucous membranes including initial and recurrent genital herpes. Acyclovir (Zovirax) oral formulations are indicated for the suppression (prevention of recurrences) of recurrent herpes simplex infections in immune-competent patients. Acyclovir (Zovirax) oral formulations are indicated for the prophyl axis of herpes si mplex infections in immune- compromised patients. Acyclovir (Zovirax) oral formulations are indicated for the treatment of varicella infections (chicken- pox) and herpes zoster (shingles). Studies have shown that early treatment of shingles with Acyclovir (Zovirax) has a beneficial effect on pain and can reduce the incidence of post-herpetic neuralgia (zoster-associated pain). Acyclovir (Zovirax) oral formulations are indicated for the management of certain severely immunocompromised patients, namely those with advanced HIV disease (CD4+ counts <200/mm 3, including patients with AIDS or severe ARC) or following bone marrow transplantation. Studies have shown that oral Acyclovir (Zovirax) given in conjunction with antiretroviral therapy (mainly oral RETROVIR) reduced mortality in patients with advanced HIV disease and that oral Acyclovir (Zovirax) preceded by one month's treatment with intravenous Acyclovir (Zovirax) reduced mortality in bone marrow transplant recipients. In addition, oral Acyclovir (Zovirax) provided effective prophylaxis for herpes virus disease.",2,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:55:39.020437+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY20150,Amoxicillin (as trihydrate),Valzimox,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-pUHzhzmarI9ypk8X30IgYbECVTyai0e/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY20150_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-pUHzhzmarI9ypk8X30IgYbECVTyai0e_view_usp_drivesdk_7b418e4308.pdf,page_text/DR-XY20150_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-pUHzhzmarI9ypk8X30IgYbECVTyai0e_view_usp_drivesdk_7b418e4308.json,282167c64bdb3bc7dd08fe8a1ed624ab2ecc84c7c66ce63d31456b1c22f59066,520742,1,ocr,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-29T18:55:44.010747+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY20237-B,Benzathine Benzylpenicillin,Zalpen,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FFN1egr3oHcZy6iaD1geduhq4YHJoAxH/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY20237-B_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FFN1egr3oHcZy6iaD1geduhq4YHJoAxH_view_usp_drivesdk_403e5d23a8.pdf,page_text/DR-XY20237-B_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FFN1egr3oHcZy6iaD1geduhq4YHJoAxH_view_usp_drivesdk_403e5d23a8.json,123c83b87373005a61ae71f2d695fb3060f4dbcb3d31324424fc12880a077154,4491842,2,ocr,"Benzathine benzylpenicillin (Zalpen) is a white, crystalline powder, supplied in a clear and colorless glass vial with rubber stopper and silver aluminum seal. CHARACTERISTICS Benzathine benzylpenicillin (Zalpen) is a white, crystalline semisynthetic antibiotic powder which is very slightly soluble in water. The chemical name of Benzathine benzylpenicillin is 4-Thia-1-azabicyclo [3,2,0] heptane-2-carboxylic acid, 3, 3-dimethyl-7oxo-6- [(phenylacetyl)amino]-[2S-(2 ,5 ,68)] compounded with N.N’bis(phenylmethyl)-1,2-ethanediamine (2:1), tetrahydrate.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Benzathine benzylpenicillin (Zalpen) has the same antimicrobial action as benzylpenicillin, but because of the relatively low blood concentrations of benzylpenicillin produced, its use should be restricted to microorganisms that are highly susceptible to benzylpenicillin. In acute infections and when bacteremia is present, the initial treatment should be with benzylpenicillin by injection. Infections treated with Benzathine benzylpenicillin (Zalpen) include diphtheria (asymptomatic carriers); pharyngitis (Streptococcus pyogenes); Arcanobacterium (Corynebacterium hemolyticum); rheumatic fever (primary and secondary prophylaxis); spleen disorders (pneumococcal infection prophylaxis) and syphilis (including non-venereal treponematoses). The most important indication of Benzathine benzylpenicillin (Zalpen) is in the treatment of syphilis and the prophylaxis against streptococcal pharyngitis and rheumatic fever.",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T18:56:04.679507+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY20263,Valaciclovir (as Hydrochloride),Valtrex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1e28H8Ahd4ke4YNe1kigcF1Kpq6FNGQ3u/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY20263_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1e28H8Ahd4ke4YNe1kigcF1Kpq6FNGQ3u_view_usp_drivesdk_149767af95.pdf,page_text/DR-XY20263_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1e28H8Ahd4ke4YNe1kigcF1Kpq6FNGQ3u_view_usp_drivesdk_149767af95.json,73340d3435598d2cbea98015172cc9d7e3a3a88774a7043cf3dcbb46a71299e6,107066,6,digital_text,"Each white to off-white, biconvex, elongated, unscored, film-coated tablet branded with “GX CF1” contains 500mg of Valaciclovir.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Valaciclovir (Valtrex) is indicated for the treatment of herpes zos ter (shingles). Valaciclovir ( Valtrex) accelerates the resolution of pain: it reduces the duration of and the proportion of patients with zoster -associated pain, which includes acute and post -herpetic neuralgia. Valaciclovir (Valtrex) is indicated for the treatment of herpes simplex infections of the skin and mucous membranes, including initial and recurrent genital herpes. Valaciclovir (Valtrex) is indicated for the treatment of herpes labialis (cold sores). Valaciclovir (Valtrex) is indicated for the prev ention (suppression) of recurrent herpes simplex infections of the skin and mucous membranes, including genital herpes. Valaciclovir (Valtrex) can reduce transmission of genital herpes when taken as suppressive therapy and combined with safer sex practices. Valaciclovir ( Valtrex) is indicated for the prophylaxis of cytomegalovirus (CMV) infection and disease, following organ transplantation. CMV prophylaxis with Valaciclovir ( Valtrex) reduces acute graft rejection (renal transplant patients), opportunistic infections and other herpes virus infections (herpes simplex virus (HSV), varicella zoster virus (VZV)).",2,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:56:07.658145+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY20266,Guaifenesin,Guiamed,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1o3Zi6OmqEGtAJJqDWqg5q0sDaUgAlCU6/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY20266_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1o3Zi6OmqEGtAJJqDWqg5q0sDaUgAlCU6_view_usp_drivesdk_077c0d4885.pdf,page_text/DR-XY20266_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1o3Zi6OmqEGtAJJqDWqg5q0sDaUgAlCU6_view_usp_drivesdk_077c0d4885.json,26c61c17b53aecaa2239dcee636471ceb8b9168a4cff16970cfb17c4dc1b645e,157869,2,digital_text_and_ocr,"Guiamed is a red clear syrup with sweet taste cherry flavored. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Guaifenesin is an expectorant. It helps loosen congestion in your chest and throat, making it easier to cough out through your mouth. Guaifenesin is well absorbed from gastrointestinal tract. It is metabolized and then excreted in the urine.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T18:56:11.301000+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY20446,Tramadol Hydrochloride,Siverol,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZksQns00CRbd0zxkIys84i1VTJznYlTh/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY20446_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZksQns00CRbd0zxkIys84i1VTJznYlTh_view_usp_drivesdk_8357c1b20e.pdf,page_text/DR-XY20446_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZksQns00CRbd0zxkIys84i1VTJznYlTh_view_usp_drivesdk_8357c1b20e.json,5b7d9c5d97fb7773d15251cf234cb682fcb0b58da18abfbae5eaf3661975ab72,520656,2,digital_text,"Tramadol HCl (Siverol) 50mg Capsule: Hard gelatin capsule with a green opaque cap and an ivory opaque body Tramadol HCl (Siverol) 50 mg/1 mL Solution for Injection: Clear, sterile, colorless solution, free from extraneous matter, filled in a 2 mL clear ampule with blue dot Tramadol HCl (Siverol) 100 mg/2 mL Solution for Injection: Clear, sterile, colorless solution, free from extraneous matter, filled in a 2 mL clear ampule with blue dot CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY PHARMACODYNAMICS Tramadol is a synthetic opioid analgesic that acts on the central nervous system. It is a pure non-selective agonist of the µ, δ, and  opioid receptors with a higher affinity for the µ receptors. Other mechanisms which contribute to its analgesic effect are inhibition of neuronal uptake of noradrenaline and enhancement of serotonin release. PHARMACOKINETICS After oral administration of a single 50 mg capsule, tramadol is rapidly and almost completely absorbed with a mean absorption delay of approximately 30 minutes. Food does not significantly affect the rate or extent of absorption. The absorption half-life is 23 ± 11 minutes. Tramadol has a high tissue affinity with a volume of distribution of 2 to 3 L/kg in young adults. The volume of distribution is reduced by about 25% in those over 75 years old. Plasma protein binding is about 20% and is independent of concentration up to 10 mcg/mL. Saturation of plasma protein binding occurs only at concentrations outside the clinically relevant range. After oral administration of two 50 mg capsules, the mean absolute bioavailability is 68 to 72%, while the mean absolute bioavailability of a single oral 100 mg dose is approximately 75%. Peak serum level (C ) of tramadol is reached approximately two hours after oral administration. C is approximately 280 ng/mL after oral administration max max (100 mg), while the mean serum concentration after intravenous (IV) administration is 410 ng/mL (1.46 times higher). After repeated oral administration of 50 mg and 100 mg tramadol capsules every six hours, steady state is reached 30 to 36 hours after the first administration and bioavailability is greater than 90%. After intramuscular (IM) injection of 50 mg tramadol, bioavailability is approximately 100% and peak serum level is attained after 45 minutes. The peak concentrations of the M1 metabolite (major metabolite) occur three hours after tramadol administration. Tramadol crosses the placental and blood-brain barriers. The mean ratio of serum tramadol in the umbilical veins compared to maternal veins was 0.83 for 40 women given tramadol during labor. The cumulative excretion in breastmilk within 16 hours post-dose was 100 mcg of tramadol (0.1% of the maternal dose) and 27 mcg (0.02% of the maternal dose) of M1 after a single 100 mg IV dose of tramadol. Tramadol is extensively metabolized in the liver. The major metabolic pathways appear to be N- and O-demethylation and glucuronidation or sulfation. Only M1 is pharmacologically active. Production of M1 is dependent on the cytochrome P (CYP) 2D6 isoenzyme of CYP450. Patients who metabolize drugs poorly via CYP2D6 may obtain reduced benefit from tramadol, due to reduced formation of M1. N-demethylation is catalyzed by the CYP3A4 isoenzyme of CYP450. The inhibition of one or both types of the isoenzymes CYP3A4 and CYP2D6 involved in the biotransformation of tramadol may affect the plasma concentrations of tramadol or its active metabolite. Tramadol and its metabolites are excreted mainly by the kidneys with a cumulative renal excretion (tramadol and metabolites) of approximately 95%. In young adults, approximately 15 to 19% of an administered dose is excreted in the urine as unchanged drug. Biliary excretion is of little importance. The half-life of tramadol is five to seven hours and the half-life of M1 is six to eight hours. Total clearance is approximately 430 to 610 mL/min. Special Populations: Renal Impairment: Elimination of tramadol and M1 is diminished in patients with renal impairment. In patients with renal failure (creatinine clearance < 5 mL/min), the half-life of tramadol was 11 hours and that of M1 was 17 hours. Hepatic Impairment: Elimination of tramadol and M1 is diminished in patients with hepatic impairment, the mean half-life of tramadol was 13 hours and the mean half-life of M1 was 19 hours. Elderly: In the elderly (>75 years old), tramadol's volume of distribution is decreased by 25% and clearance is decreased by 40%. As a result, tramadol's C and total max exposure are increased by 30% and 50%, respectively. However, the half-life of tramadol is only slightly prolonged by 15%.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,> Relief of moderate to severe pain,1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:56:14.118814+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY20557,Desferrioxamine mesilate,Desferal,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/19io4woiY_KvoIh62MMhlw0AEGB3MeYSR/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY20557_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19io4woiY_KvoIh62MMhlw0AEGB3MeYSR_view_usp_drivesdk_68af819bd3.pdf,page_text/DR-XY20557_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19io4woiY_KvoIh62MMhlw0AEGB3MeYSR_view_usp_drivesdk_68af819bd3.json,906b074541e6dcc2d399414bc26087fc841c8c6c627f8e0610a4c52a58626136,524480,14,digital_text,Pharmaceutical form(s) Vials containing 500 mg powder for solution for injection. Active substance(s) One vial contains 500 mg desferrioxamine methane sulphonate. Certain dosage strengths may not be available in all countries. Excipients Not applicable.,1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,"Therapeutic Monotherapy iron chelation treatment for chronic iron overload, e.g.  transfusional hemosiderosis, as seen in thalassemia major, sideroblastic anemia, auto- immune hemolytic anemia, and other chronic anemias.  idiopathic (primary) hemochromatosis in patients in whom concomitant disorders (e.g. severe anemia, cardiac disease, hypoproteinemia) preclude phlebotomy.  iron overload associated with porphyria cutanea tarda in patients unable to tolerate phlebotomy. Treatment for acute iron poisoning. Treatment for chronic aluminum overload in patients with end-stage renal failure (under maintenance dialysis) with  aluminum-related bone disease,  dialysis encephalopathy or  aluminum-related anemia. Diagnostic Diagnosis of iron or aluminum overload.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:56:18.737659+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY20944,Sumatriptan,Imigran,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uCeaFQJo47B9Bm2r0bt2X83ul3nzDfbq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY20944_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uCeaFQJo47B9Bm2r0bt2X83ul3nzDfbq_view_usp_drivesdk_af8a6091bd.pdf,page_text/DR-XY20944_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uCeaFQJo47B9Bm2r0bt2X83ul3nzDfbq_view_usp_drivesdk_af8a6091bd.json,2f666e08ce6fe5c4b12c233b8d18a45cac005431720f01121f9ea9f3842dbaf6,198715,4,digital_text,"Sumatriptan (Imigran) 50 mg tablet : Pink film-coated, capsule- shaped biconvex tablets (of nominal dimensions 12 x 6.5 mm) engraved ‘50’ on one face and plain on the other. Each tablet contains 50 mg sumatriptan base as the succinate salt",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Sumatriptan (Imigran) tablets are indicated for the acute relief of migrai ne attacks with or without aura, including the acute treatment of migraine attacks associated with the menstrual period in women.",2,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:56:21.584828+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY20977,Lamotrigine,Lamictal,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FhVt_tMzlMebjVxQZ_5eUTmlOGIgRIIo/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY20977_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FhVt_tMzlMebjVxQZ_5eUTmlOGIgRIIo_view_usp_drivesdk_6ca498caa8.pdf,page_text/DR-XY20977_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FhVt_tMzlMebjVxQZ_5eUTmlOGIgRIIo_view_usp_drivesdk_6ca498caa8.json,f3ddfe6940e35ae9b8def9de3652a8a0d11bbe4929f841fbc64d031070864068,353564,17,digital_text,"Lamotrigine (Lamictal) 50 mg Tablet: Each pale yellowish brown, unscor ed, multifaceted, superelliptical tablet, branded ‘GSEE1’ on one side, with ‘50’ on the reverse, contains 50mg of Lamotrigine. Lamotrigine (Lamictal) 100 mg Tablet: Each pale yellowish brown, unscor ed, multifaceted, superelliptical tablet, branded ‘GSEE5’ on one side, with ‘100’ on the reverse, contains 100mg of Lamotrigine. Lamotrigine (Lamictal) 25 mg Dispersible/Chewable Tablet: Each white to off-white, multi-facet ed, superelliptical tablet, branded with “GSCL5” on one side and “25” on the other, contains 25mg Lamotrigine. The tablet has a black currant odour, unscored and may be slightly mottled.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"EPILEPSY  Adults and Adolescents (over 12 years of age) Lamotrigine (Lamictal) is indicated for use as adjunctive or monotherapy in the treatment of epilepsy, for partial seizures and generalised seizures, including tonic-clonic seizures and the seizures associated with Lennox-Gastaut Syndrome.  Children (2 to 12 years of age) Lamotrigine (Lamictal) is indicated as adjunctive therapy in the treatm ent of epilepsy, for partial seizures and generalised seizures including tonic-clonic seizures and the seizures associated with Lennox-Gastaut syndrome. After epileptic control has been achiev ed during adjunctive therapy, concomitant anti-epileptic drugs (AEDs) may be withdrawn and patients continued on Lamotrigine (Lamictal) monotherapy. Lamotrigine (Lamictal) is indicated as monotherapy in the treatment of typical absence seizures. If Lamotrigine (Lamictal) 2 mg dispersible/chewable tablet is not available and the calculat ed dose in children is less than 2.5 mg daily, then Lamotrigine (Lamictal) cannot be used. DO NOT attempt to administer partial quantities of the dispersible/chewable tablets. BIPOLAR DISORDER  Adults (18 years of age and over) Lamotrigine (Lamictal) is indicated for the prevention of mood episodes in patients with bipolar disorder, predominantly by preventing depressive episodes.",3,3,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:56:24.519566+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY21182,Ferrous Fumarate (49.5mg elemental iron) + Thiamine Mononitrate (Vit. B) + Pyridoxine Hydrochloride (Vit. B6) + Cyanocobalamin (Vit. B12),Trev-Iron,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1OWRb1U4A0TrWriiB6Hv6_EKS2SqcmrZq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY21182_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OWRb1U4A0TrWriiB6Hv6_EKS2SqcmrZq_view_usp_drivesdk_46b0ad431e.pdf,page_text/DR-XY21182_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OWRb1U4A0TrWriiB6Hv6_EKS2SqcmrZq_view_usp_drivesdk_46b0ad431e.json,18adcf1b115d8c055f9245ab08a8a9334a8125ba24160f7f2a3cfb090d738b2c,358997,1,ocr,,1,1,prescription.,"Trev-iron is a well balanced hematinic formula that provides more than just iron to correct and prevent anemia. It also provides the necessary B-complex vitamins to stimulate appetite, promote growth and weight gain, build up energy and increase overall resistance to stress and infections.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T18:56:30.184388+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY21335,L-Ornithine-L-Aspartate,Hepa-Merz,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Pfn7Ra5-vjHbhU3jumWuPZ1G7ow9kfQ4/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY21335_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Pfn7Ra5-vjHbhU3jumWuPZ1G7ow9kfQ4_view_usp_drivesdk_b9a34958f3.pdf,page_text/DR-XY21335_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Pfn7Ra5-vjHbhU3jumWuPZ1G7ow9kfQ4_view_usp_drivesdk_b9a34958f3.json,c5083ba9c07baf5146f1bedb9a8f5a5991ac80f088ccdbe0925ca2995649ad14,610486,2,digital_text,,,,,For the treatment of concomitant disease and sequelae due to impaired hepatic detoxification activity (e. g. in cirrhosis of the liver) with the symptoms of latent and manifest hepatic encephalopathy.,1,1,Therapeutic indications,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T18:56:33.492561+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY21352,Mesalazine,Salofalk,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1l0cQEWTCITshO2NnzpqqgLlwKKWMbqIO/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY21352_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1l0cQEWTCITshO2NnzpqqgLlwKKWMbqIO_view_usp_drivesdk_26b6182a24.pdf,page_text/DR-XY21352_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1l0cQEWTCITshO2NnzpqqgLlwKKWMbqIO_view_usp_drivesdk_26b6182a24.json,54be0985ddc6aea03082e3badd1be991f5d459808df2750a500c26728ca2e328,865721,8,digital_text,"Butter-yellow to ochre gastro-resistant oblong formed tablets, lustreless with smooth surface",1,1,Product Description:,Salofalk® is used for the treatment of: - Ulcerative colitis and proctitis (treatment of acute attack or to prevent relapse) - Crohn’s disease (treatment of acute attack),1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:56:36.756712+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY21447,Ofloxacin,Inoflox,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Z-0u7Im8E-4523Kz94gOmk4tluCtLCQ3/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY21447_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Z-0u7Im8E-4523Kz94gOmk4tluCtLCQ3_view_usp_drivesdk_23412daa0a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY21447_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Z-0u7Im8E-4523Kz94gOmk4tluCtLCQ3_view_usp_drivesdk_23412daa0a.json,243097ffbea39070819d577628a26106b3a9d0ef45e0c17b3d89ed9abb99422a,463233,1,digital_text,"Ofloxacin (Inoflox) Otic Solution is a sterile, clear, pale yellow liquid. PHARMACODYNAMICS Ofloxacin is a synthetic broad-spectrum antimicrobial agent which inhibits DNAtopoisomerase, more commonly referred to as the DNA gyrase. DNA gyrase is necessary for bacterial DNA replication and some aspects of transcription, repair, recombination, and transposition. Inhibition of DNA gyrase in susceptible microorganisms results in the inhibition of ATP-dependent negative supercoiling of DNA, inhibition of ATP-independent relaxation of supercoiled DNA, and promotion of double-stranded DNA breakage resulting in bacterial cell death. ANTIMICROBIAL SPECTRUM OF ACTIVITY Ofloxacin is active in vitro and clinically in otic infections against most strains of the following microorganisms: Staphylococcus aureusGram-positive Aerobic and Facultative Microorganisms Streptococcus pneumoniae Escherichia coli Haemophilus influenzae Moraxella catarrhalis Proteus mirabilis Gram-negative Aerobic and Facultative Microorganisms Pseudomonas aeruginosa 3mg/mL Otic Drops Topical Antibacterial PHARMACOKINETICS The extent of otic and systemic absorption of Ofloxacin after topical application to the ear has not been fully elucidated. Serum concentrations achieved after topical application to the ear are minimal relative to those produced by oral or parenteral doses of the drug. Topical application of Ofloxacin to the ear is associated with minimal penetration into the middle ear when the tympanic membrane is intact; however, Ofloxacin penetration is enhanced when the tympanic membrane is perforated. Some systemic absorption of Ofloxacin occurs after topical application to the ear. After single administration of 10 drops of Ofloxacin 0.3% otic solution in adult patients with tympanostomy tubes with or without otorrhea, serum Ofloxacin concentrations averaged 4.1 or 5.4 ng/mL, respectively. Peak serum concentration of 10 ng/mL is achieved after topical application of Ofloxacin 0.3% otic solution in adults with perforated tympanic membranes . Ofloxacin concentrations in middle ear mucosa showed considerable interindividual variation and ranged from undetectable to 602 mcg/g after administration of Ofloxacin 0.3% otic solution in adults with perforated tympanic membranes.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"DOSE OF OFLOXACIN OTIC SOLUTION DURATION OF TREATMENT Children 6 months to 13 years 5 drops instilled into the affected ear once daily 7 daysOtitis externa Adults and children over 13 years 10 drops instilled into the affected ear once daily 7 days Acute otitis media with tympanostomy tubes Children 1 to 12 years 5 drops instilled into the affected ear twice daily 10 days Chronic suppurative otitis media with perforated tympanic membranes Adults and children 12 years or older 10 drops instilled into the affected ear twice daily 14 days Or, as prescribed by a physician. Directions for Use: Turn the cap clockwise until the cap comes in contact with the shoulder of the container. This punctures the inner seal. The solution is now ready for use. For Patients with Otitis Externa: 1. Incline the head sideways with the affected ear upwards 2. Instill the recommended dose of Ofloxacin Otic Drops into the affected ear 3. Keep the head inclined sideways for five minutes to facilitate penetration of the drops into the ear 4. Wipe off excess solution with clean cotton 5. Repeat for the opposite ear if needed For patients with Acute Otitis Media and Chronic Suppurative Otitis Media: 1. Refer to steps 1 to 2 in the Directions for Use for Patients with Otitis Externa 2. Pump the tragus of the ear ( a small cartilaginous flap in front of the external opening of the ear) four times by pushing inward to facilitate penetration of the drops into the middle ear 3. Refer to steps 3 to 5 in the Directions for Use for Patients with Otitis Externa Information for Patients: Avoid contaminating the applicator tip with material from the finger or other sources to preserve the sterility of the drops.",1,1,INDICATIONS AGE GROUP,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:56:39.854211+00:00
