PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY22028,Meclizine Hydrochloride,Bonamine,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cmQGJdB0wRZiOZUKiTtT_dNxazpRGIQ2/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY22028_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cmQGJdB0wRZiOZUKiTtT_dNxazpRGIQ2_view_usp_drivesdk_d8f83b39f5.pdf,page_text/DR-XY22028_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cmQGJdB0wRZiOZUKiTtT_dNxazpRGIQ2_view_usp_drivesdk_d8f83b39f5.json,217a706ee46a5119c92d6d71df1c17e27adea59edc6c58549576f64f68e8bef0,193796,1,digital_text,"Meclizine Hydrochloride (Bonamine®) Chewable Tablet is a pale orange, mottled, round, biconvex tablet, plain on one side and scored on the other side with characteristic sweet yogurt-like flavor. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Active Pharmaceutical Ingredient (API): Meclizine Hydrochloride Excipients used are: Glycine, Corn Starch, Carmellose Calcium, Flavor, Magnesium Stearate, Sodium Saccharin, Colorant, Sodium Lauryl Sulfate, and Water. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Meclizine Hydrochloride (Bonamine®) Chewable Tablet for Adults: Each chewable tablet contains 25 mg of Meclizine Hydrochloride. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Meclizine Hydrochloride (Bonamine®) Chewable Tablet is used for the prevention and treatment of nausea, vomiting, or dizziness associated with motion sickness. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? A daily dose should be taken one hour before travel starts for 24-hr protection. The tablet may be chewed and swallowed with or without water or swallowed whole with water. MECLIZINE HYDROCHLORIDE (BONAMINE®) 25 MG CHEWABLE TABLET FOR ADULTS Age I Recommended Dose Adults and Children ;e 11 yrs. old I 1 to 2 tablets Or, as prescribed by a physician. If additional dose is needed, interval should be 4 hours or longer. Children 5-15 yrs old should be limited to two single doses only. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? • A known hypersensitivity to Meclizine or any ingredient in this product. • Patients taking monoamine oxidase inhibitor antidepressant • Pregnant or breastfeeding mothers CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE • This drug may cause drowsiness. Take due precautions against driving a car or operating dangerous machinery. • A doctor must always be consulted before giving Meclizine especially if the patient is taking other medications (antidepressant) and patients who are alcoholics or who regularly ingest alcohol in excess before giving this drug. • It is also wise to remember to check the expiration date on the package or label of this product. Do not use after expiry date. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Drowsiness, fatigue, dry mouth, constipation, headache, stomach upset, and rarely blurred vision have been reported with the use of Meclizine. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Avoid alcohol, sedatives, anti-allergic drugs and tranquilizers while taking Meclizine as this may increase the drowsiness effect. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Do not double the dose. If you miss a dose, just take the next dose as scheduled (i.e., once a day) if needed to prevent and treat nausea, vomiting, or dizziness associated with motion sickness. FRONT CX) <:I' .-I Supplier: Revision Date: _j,&.CJl)I� Printing Corp. Tel. No.: 532-5870 • 532-0721 • 532-7645 Color Used: Graphics Artist: ■ Black 148 mm SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE Overdose of Meclizine may manifest as follows: Drowsiness Dry mouth Fatigue Rarely, blurred vision WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If more than the recommended dose has been given, consult a health professional immediately. Do not exceed recommended dosage. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Keep out of reach of children. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? Pregnant or breastfeeding mothers, patients with increased pressure in the eye, asthma, emphysema, chronic pulmonary disease, difficulty in breathing and those with difficulty in urination due to enlargement of the prostate gland and those taking sedatives and tranquilizers should take Meclizine only under the direction of a doctor. HOW SUPPLIED? Meclizine Hydrochloride (Bonamine®) 25 mg Chewable Tablet for Adult: Box of 240's NAME AND ADDRESS OF MARKETING AUTHORIZATION HOLDER Taisho Pharmaceuticals (Philippines), Inc. 8th Floor CLIPP Center Building, 11th Avenue corner 39th Street, Bonifacio Global City, Taguig 1634, Philippines Under Authority of: Taisho Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd., Tokyo, Japan Trademark Owner NAME AND ADDRESS OF MANUFA CTURER lnterphil Laboratories, Inc. Canlubang Industrial Estate, Bo. Pittland, Cabuyao, Laguna ADR REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to FDA: www.fda.gov.ph Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction . REGISTRATION NUMBER Meclizine Hydrochloride (Bonamine®) 25 mg Chewable Tablet for Adult: DR-XY22028 RENEWAL OF THE AUTHORIZATION Meclizine Hydrochloride (Bonamine®) 25 mg Chewable Tablet for Adult: 11 September 2023 DATE OF REVISION OF THE PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET (PIL) September 2023 @-1 1023 BACK ►I [Page 2]",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T18:57:36.957452+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY22121-B,Cefalexin (As Monohydrate),Cefax,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1P2liaTOe9MjlbXSMfc4KBrOTqOP2Hzr8/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY22121-B_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1P2liaTOe9MjlbXSMfc4KBrOTqOP2Hzr8_view_usp_drivesdk_35089c0e76.pdf,page_text/DR-XY22121-B_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1P2liaTOe9MjlbXSMfc4KBrOTqOP2Hzr8_view_usp_drivesdk_35089c0e76.json,e8a2b7cfa019c9d3ac1564a55e227e15ab1895eeda1dab81825378507fa12ae9,1201392,2,ocr,n (Oral Drops) is a white to off-white powd ler when dry and a white to off-white Cefax 100 mg/mL Powd er For Oral Suspensio suspension when recons'! tituted with a sweet frui it cherry/orange flavor taste.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTI,"tractinfections, otitis media, skin and other infections due to sensitive organisms. For the treatment of urinary",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T18:57:51.459484+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY22130,Carvedilol,Dilatrend,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XCw40CFnvykxM-DdC2lJK597lU4FZZoy/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY22130_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1XCw40CFnvykxM-DdC2lJK597lU4FZZoy_view_usp_drivesdk_335d3b5a73.pdf,page_text/DR-XY22130_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1XCw40CFnvykxM-DdC2lJK597lU4FZZoy_view_usp_drivesdk_335d3b5a73.json,f4644bf9f2f7b401d1340f62f445140c9d1270a4fc3abdc66d763faa1a4353f1,275142,16,digital_text,"1.1 Therapeutic / Pharmacologic Class of Drug Alpha (α) and beta (β) adrenergic receptor blocking agents ATC code: C07AG02 1.2 Type of Dosage Form Tablets. The tablets are round with a bilateral score, and either yellow (6.25 mg) or white to pale yellowish- white (25 mg). The tablet(s) can be divided into equal doses. 1.3 Route of Administration Oral 1.4 Sterile / Radioactive Statement Not applicable",1,1,1. DESCRIPTION,"Hypertension Carvedilol is indicated for the management of essential hypertension. It can be used alone or in combination with other anti-hypertensive agents (e.g. calcium channel blockers, diuretics). Coronary Heart Disease Carvedilol has demonstrated clinical efficacy in coronary heart disease. Preliminary data shows efficacy and safety in patients with unstable angina and silent myocardial ischaemia. Chronic Heart Failure Unless a contraindication exists, carvedilol is indicated for the treatment of all patients with stable and symptomatic mild, moderate and severe chronic heart failure of ischaemic or non -ischaemic aetiology in combination with standard therapy (including ACE inhibitors and diuretics with or without digitalis). Left ventricular dysfunction following acute myocardial infarction Long term treatment following myocardial infarction complicated by left ventricular dysfunction (left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) ≤ 40% or wall motion index ≤ 1.3), in combination with ACE inhibitors and other treatments recommended in the management of patients after myocardial infarction.",1,1,2.1 Therapeutic Indication(s),high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:57:55.447058+00:00
