PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY24538,Phenylpropanolamine Hydrochloride + Brompheniramine Maleate,Nasatapp,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UqTOtRam8Mr60rXXO7l_Ta_pzQgRcBeF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY24538_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UqTOtRam8Mr60rXXO7l_Ta_pzQgRcBeF_view_usp_drivesdk_9ab358ad25.pdf,page_text/DR-XY24538_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UqTOtRam8Mr60rXXO7l_Ta_pzQgRcBeF_view_usp_drivesdk_9ab358ad25.json,332be9c9912d8397730bb3891db10c4b3956b80f1ffbab5947c7b714191407b9,451990,1,ocr,"goiter, benign prostatic hypertrophy, heart rate irregularity, glaucoma and to those receiving antidepressant Nasatapp is a combination of the decongestant, Phenylpropanolamine Hydrochloride, and the therapy. Patients with heart disease and uncontrolled or untreated high blood pressure should consult a antihistamine, Brompheniramine Maleate. This combination reduces excessive nasopharyngeal secretion doctor prior to taking PPA. and diminishes inflammatory mucosal edema and congestion in the upper respiratory tract. The antihistamine action of Brompheniramine Maleate reduces or diminishes the allergic response of nasal tissues. It is complemented by the mild vasoconstrictor action of Phen",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,Drops - In bottle of 145 mL Indicated for allergic and vasomotor or other hyperactive nasal disorders and acute coryza; relief of nasal,1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T19:00:46.055422+00:00
