(Vitamin B6) + Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12)""",Neuro B's 500,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Qu3rKNXkY-F_VQFISvKWY_RhyRNYfvNP/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY24942_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Qu3rKNXkY-F_VQFISvKWY_RhyRNYfvNP_view_usp_drivesdk_1519d65058.pdf,page_text/DR-XY24942_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Qu3rKNXkY-F_VQFISvKWY_RhyRNYfvNP_view_usp_drivesdk_1519d65058.json,fe7381a182eabde199a9ac5652b33d908393d8e4e411cf58fe70b0070928da99,513013,1,ocr,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-29T19:01:14.297162+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY2508,Phytomenadione,Konakion MM,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZpzPapUpbMY53-3Yvjmmjzbsee0vJyNM/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY2508_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZpzPapUpbMY53-3Yvjmmjzbsee0vJyNM_view_usp_drivesdk_535396a1df.pdf,page_text/DR-XY2508_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZpzPapUpbMY53-3Yvjmmjzbsee0vJyNM_view_usp_drivesdk_535396a1df.json,27c8478773110bf368e46d01af26b956fe4a08f1c9bf61d002e06b00728ad094,655867,2,digital_text,,,,,"Hemorrhage or risk of hemorrhage as a result of severe ‘hypoprothrombinemia’ (i.e. deficiency of clotting factors II, VII, IX and X) of various etiologies, including overdosage of coumarin-type anticoagulants, their combination with phenylbutazone and other forms of hypovitaminoses K (e.g. in obstructive jaundice as well as liver and intestinal disorders, and after prolonged treatment with antibiotics, sulfonamides or salicylates). For prophylaxis and treatment of hemorrhagic disease in the newborn, Phytomenadione (Konakion®) MM pediatric ampoules (2 mg/ 0.2 mL) should be used.",1,1,Indications and usage,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T19:01:17.493236+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY2509,Propylthiouracil,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/12phVG58hZXE-wBXPqzCDoaPps27FlEJU/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY2509_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_12phVG58hZXE-wBXPqzCDoaPps27FlEJU_view_usp_drivesdk_8ff7cc3374.pdf,page_text/DR-XY2509_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_12phVG58hZXE-wBXPqzCDoaPps27FlEJU_view_usp_drivesdk_8ff7cc3374.json,0bc2bbf5af63d4d9416c55f72576e0d2892e29d6050872185d86dfecdf2dfbe6,122904,1,ocr,,,,,"picture should be controlled in 8 days intervals. For the treatment of hyperthyroidism. Application fields: Properties: All forms of thyrotoxicosis, basedow, iodothyroidism, preoperative treatment of Propylthlouracil inhibits the integration of iodine into the thyroglobulin and with that the basedowfield goiter, completion of radioiodine therapy. thyroxine production, The thyroid effect results from the inhibition of the intrathyroidal peroxidase-system. Caution: Propylthiouracil is well absorbed after oral dose, maximum serum levels wil) be achieved Foods, Drugs, Devices and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription, after 1-2 hours. - Keep drugs out of reach of children.",1,1,Indication:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T19:01:24.075123+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY25101,Dopamine hydrochloride,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vDxHSB0M26ZO92d10Y1bkR4aOihJOvNY/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY25101_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vDxHSB0M26ZO92d10Y1bkR4aOihJOvNY_view_usp_drivesdk_52c460329c.pdf,page_text/DR-XY25101_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vDxHSB0M26ZO92d10Y1bkR4aOihJOvNY_view_usp_drivesdk_52c460329c.json,d78d8d7db01b3c1da09df5f68726c6fd11e23d0e5360eae79ab7869651bc8082,289462,14,digital_text,"Dopamine hydrochloride is a naturally o ccurring biochemical catecholamine precursor of noradrenaline and adrenaline. The chemical name of dopamine hydrochloride is 4-(2- aminoethyl) benzene-1,2-diol hydrochloride and has the chemical formula C8H11NO2.HCl. Excipient with known effect Sodium metabisulfite Chemical structure The chemical structure is: HO HO CH2CH2NH2 DOPAMINE HYDROCHLORIDE . HCl MW 189.6 CAS number CAS 51-61-6",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"For the correction of hemodynamic imbalance present in: Acute hypotension or shock associated with myocardial infarction, endotoxic septicemia, trauma and renal failure. Viewed on: Thursday, January 4, 2024 - 9:43:08 PM Eastern Time [Page 2] 2 As an adjunct after open heart surgery, where there is persistent hypotension after correction of hypovolemia. In chronic cardiac decompensation as in congestive failure.",1,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:01:27.103047+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY25188,Amisulpride,Solian,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ddwrQNk4vMHzvUgdSCYk3M5pbJz4VFxa/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY25188_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ddwrQNk4vMHzvUgdSCYk3M5pbJz4VFxa_view_usp_drivesdk_3ce1cc1025.pdf,page_text/DR-XY25188_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ddwrQNk4vMHzvUgdSCYk3M5pbJz4VFxa_view_usp_drivesdk_3ce1cc1025.json,d14091091f9cd1c5bc8be6ec0538c0b63a66a3cc292b29de8d55cbe642f49e84,929004,1,digital_text,"200 mg Tablet: Round, /f_lat scored tablets with “SMI 200” engraved on one side and a score line on the other side 400 mg Film-coated Tablet: Scored /f_ilm-coated tablets",1,1,Pharmaceutical Form,Treatment of schizophrenia.,1,1,Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:01:30.479709+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY25228,Loperamide Hydrochloride,Lorban,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1244H19scqWVDPTzdPJJJWv4LPWdBOvYK/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY25228_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1244H19scqWVDPTzdPJJJWv4LPWdBOvYK_view_usp_drivesdk_5600765225.pdf,page_text/DR-XY25228_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1244H19scqWVDPTzdPJJJWv4LPWdBOvYK_view_usp_drivesdk_5600765225.json,95998f33644c298cce1b38b2e710c05c3f4770db0ce86b64a491cecde95bf3af,78309,2,digital_text,"White to slightly-yellow powder encapsulated in empty gelatin capsule size #3 with Light green cap and white body. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This medicine contains loperamide, an antidiarrheal agent which slows intestinal movement and reduced fluid and salt loss in the intestines, resulting in improved stool consistency.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T19:01:33.660165+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY25423,Doxurubicin Hydrochloride,Ebedoxo,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/13ePpMJ6Ie04JTtIc0xFmarsEG4U0D6Bc/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY25423_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13ePpMJ6Ie04JTtIc0xFmarsEG4U0D6Bc_view_usp_drivesdk_1ec9550305.pdf,page_text/DR-XY25423_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13ePpMJ6Ie04JTtIc0xFmarsEG4U0D6Bc_view_usp_drivesdk_1ec9550305.json,b45d96a85f70390c43e91669d58a517786372d90dc1cece92884b5a05ac08828,355180,20,digital_text,"Clear, blood-red solution for injection CLINICAL PARTICULARS Therapeutic indications - Small-cell lung cancer (SCLC) - Advanced or recurrent endometrial carcinoma - Ewing's sarcoma - For systemic treatment of locally advanced or metastatic urocystic carcinoma - Early stage of Hodgkin's lymphoma (stage I-II) in bad prognosis - Advanced Hodgkin's lymphoma (stage III-IV) - Induction of remission in acute lymphatic leukaemia - Induction of remission in acute myeloid leukaemia - Metastatic mammary carcinoma - Advanced neuroblastoma - Highly malignant non-Hodgkin's lymphoma - Neo-adjuvant and adjuvant therapy of osteosarcoma - Advanced ovarian carcinoma - Advanced soft tissue sarcoma in adult age - Wilms' tumour (in stage II in highly malignant variants, all advanced stages (III-IV)) - Advanced multiple myeloma - Advanced or recurrent papillary/follicular thyroid cancer - Anaplastic thyroid cancer In addition for doxorubicin 50 mg solution for injection - For intravesical relapse prophylaxis of superficial urocystic tumours after TUR in patients with high risk of relapse Dosage and method of administration For strict intravenous and intravesical use. Allow the vial to come to room temperature before inserting a needle. Doxorubicin hydrochloride [Page 2] CLEAN TEXT FILE Doxorubicin hydrochloride 2 mg/mL (10 mg/mL and 50 mg/25 mL) Solution for Injection Doxorubicin must only be administered under the supervision of a qualified physicians experienced in the use of cytostatics. Furthermore, during treatment patients should be kept under close and frequent supervision. Due to the risk of a lethal cardiomyopathy, the risks and benefits to the individual patient should be weighted before each application. It is recommended that an evaluation of hepatic function be carried out prior to individual dosing, using conventional clinical laboratory tests such as AST, ALT, alkaline phosphatase, bilirubin as well as renal function (see Special warnings and precautions for use). Analysis of LVEF by ultrasound examination or myocardial scintigraphy should be carried out to assess the patient’s cardiac function prior to treatment start and following each cumulative dose of approximately 100 mg/m 2 (see Special warnings and precautions for use). Intravenous (i.v.) administration of doxorubicin must be performed with special caution. Inject doxorubicin slowly via the tubing of a freely running intravenous infusion of sodium chloride 0.9% w/v intravenous injection or glucose intravenous injection 5% w/v. This will minimize the risk of thrombosis and perivenous extravasation, which can lead to severe cellulitis, blistering and tissue necrosis. A direct intravenous injection is not recommended due to the risk of extravasation, which may occur even in the presence of adequate blood return upon needle aspiration; or administer doxorubicin as an infusion diluted in sodium chloride 0.9% w/v intravenous injection or glucose intravenous injection 5% w/v. Doxorubicin may be administered intravenously as bolus injection within minutes, as short-term infusion up to one hour or as continuous infusion up to 24 hours. Doxorubicin must NOT be administered by intramuscular subcutaneous, oral or intrathecal route. Intravenous administration The recommended dose is usually calculated on the basis of body surface area (mg/m²). The dose scheme of doxorubicin administration vary depending on the indication (solid tumour or acute leukaemia) and in relation to its use in specific treatment regimens (as a single agent or in combination with other chemotherapeutics or as part of a multidisciplinary approach consisting of a combination of chemotherapy, surgical procedure and radiotherapy, and hormonal treatment). Monotherapy The recommended dose is 60-75 mg/m² as single dose i.v. or as separate doses for 2-3 consecutive days, [Page 3] CLEAN TEXT FILE Doxorubicin hydrochloride 2 mg/mL (10 mg/mL and 50 mg/25 mL) Solution for Injection administered intravenously at intervals of 21 days. Dose scheme and dose can be adapted according to the protocol. For detailed information please refer to current protocols. Combination therapy If doxorubicin is used in combination with other cytostatic agents dose should be reduced to 30-60 mg/m2 every 3 to 4 weeks. Maximum cumulative dose The maximum cumulative dose of 450-550 mg/m² should not be exceeded (including administration of related active substances like daunorubicin). If patients with concomitant heart disease receive mediastinal and/or heart irradiation, prior treatment with alkylating and high-risk patients (e.g. patients with preexisting arterial hypertension >5 years, with prior coronary, valvular or myocardial heart damage or patients aged >70 years) a maximum total dose of 400 mg/m 2 body surface area should not be exceeded and the cardiac function of these patients should be monitored (see Special warnings and precautions for use). Special patient groups Immunosuppressed patients In case of immunosuppression the dose must be reduced, an alternative dose is 15-20 mg/m2 body surface per week. Patients with hepatic impairment In impaired hepatic function dose should be reduced according to the following table: Serum bilirubin Recommended dose 20–50 μmol/L ½ normal dose >50–85 μmol/L ¼ normal dose Doxorubicin is contraindicated in patients with severe hepatic impairment (see Contraindications). Patients with renal impairment In patients with renal impairment (GFR <10 mL/min), 75% of the calculated dose should be administered. Patients at risk for cardiac impairment Patients at increased risk for cardiotoxicity should be considered for treatment with a 24 hours continuous infusion of a single dose, rather than bolus injection. In this way, cardiotoxicity may be less frequent, without a reduction in therapeutic efficacy. In these patients, the ejection fraction should be measured before each course. [Page 4] CLEAN TEXT FILE Doxorubicin hydrochloride 2 mg/mL (10 mg/mL and 50 mg/25 mL) Solution for Injection Patients with reduced myeloid reserve In patients with myelosuppressive treatment in their medical history doses may be reduced as their myeloid reserve may be inadequate. Obese patients A reduced starting dose or prolonged dose interval might need to be considered in obese patients (see Special warnings and precautions for use). Older patients (≥65 years) Doses may be reduced in elderly patients. Paediatric population In view of a substantial risk for doxorubicin-induced cardiotoxicity in childhood specific cumulative maximum doses depending on the youth of the patient should be installed. For children (<12 years) the usual maximum cumulative dose is 300 mg/m2, whereas for adolescents (>12 years) maximum cumulative dose is 450 mg/m2. For infants the maximum cumulative dose is still undetermined, a much lower tolerability is expected. Dose for children should be reduced since they have an increased risk of cardiotoxicity especially delayed cardiotoxicity. Myelotoxicity should be anticipated, with nadirs at 10 to 14 days after start of treatment. Please refer to current treatment protocols and expert literature. Intravesical administration Doxorubicin can be given by intravesical instillation for treatment of superficial bladder carcinoma and to prevent relapse after transurethral resection (T.U.R). The recommended dose for intravesical treatment of superficial bladder carcinoma is 30-50 mg in 25-50 mL of physiological saline per instillation. The optimal concentration is about 1 mg/mL. The solution should remain in the bladder for 1-2 hours. During this period the patient should be turned 90° every 15 minutes. To avoid undesired dilution with urine the patient should be informed not to drink anything for a period of 12 hours before the instillation (this should reduce the production of urine to about 50 mL/h). The instillation may be repeated with an interval of 1 week to 1 month, dependent on whether the treatment is therapeutic or prophylactic.",1,4,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"- Small-cell lung cancer (SCLC) - Advanced or recurrent endometrial carcinoma - Ewing's sarcoma - For systemic treatment of locally advanced or metastatic urocystic carcinoma - Early stage of Hodgkin's lymphoma (stage I-II) in bad prognosis - Advanced Hodgkin's lymphoma (stage III-IV) - Induction of remission in acute lymphatic leukaemia - Induction of remission in acute myeloid leukaemia - Metastatic mammary carcinoma - Advanced neuroblastoma - Highly malignant non-Hodgkin's lymphoma - Neo-adjuvant and adjuvant therapy of osteosarcoma - Advanced ovarian carcinoma - Advanced soft tissue sarcoma in adult age - Wilms' tumour (in stage II in highly malignant variants, all advanced stages (III-IV)) - Advanced multiple myeloma - Advanced or recurrent papillary/follicular thyroid cancer - Anaplastic thyroid cancer In addition for doxorubicin 50 mg solution for injection - For intravesical relapse prophylaxis of superficial urocystic tumours after TUR in patients with high risk of relapse",1,1,Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:01:37.562729+00:00
