titis media, mastoiditis, sinusitis, follicular tonsillitis, and pharyngitis  Dental infections Note: Penicillin is the usual drug of choice in the treatment and prevention of streptococcal infections, including the prophylaxis of rheumatic fever. Cefalexin is generally effective in the eradication of streptococci from the nasophar- are not available at present.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:02:11.755329+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY26041,Goserelin Acetate (Equivalent To Goserelin Base),ZoladexÂ® LA,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/19n9aWj7qLQPZEUj1joUyseYpzhc7RMI5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY26041_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19n9aWj7qLQPZEUj1joUyseYpzhc7RMI5_view_usp_drivesdk_a468077964.pdf,page_text/DR-XY26041_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19n9aWj7qLQPZEUj1joUyseYpzhc7RMI5_view_usp_drivesdk_a468077964.json,4fcb70fabd495d52de5b05bbdd7a3192efdaa13833965c56e2ee9ab2fe6030fc,672883,11,digital_text,"Depot, pre-filled syringe 4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 4.1 Therapeutic indications Prostate cancer: Goserelin (ZOLADEX® LA) 10.8 mg is indicated in the management of prostate cancer suitable for hormonal manipulation. Endometriosis: Goserelin (ZOLADEX® LA) 10.8 mg is indicated in the management of endometriosis including alleviation of symptoms, such as pain, and reduction in the size and number of endometrial lesions. Uterine fibroids: Goserelin (ZOLADEX® LA) 10.8 mg is indicated in the management of fibroids including shrinkage of lesions, improvement in the patient's haematological status and reduction of symptoms, such as pain. It can be used as an adjunct to surgery to facilitate the operative technique and reduce operative blood loss. Breast cancer: Goserelin (ZOLADEX® LA) 10.8 mg is indicated in the management of estrogen-receptor-positive breast cancer in premenopausal women. [Page 2] 4.2 Dosage and method of administration Caution should be taken while inserting Goserelin (ZOLADEX® LA) into the anterior abdominal wall due to the proximity of underlying inferior epigastric artery and its branches. Use extra care when administering Goserelin (ZOLADEX® LA) to patients with a low BMI and/or who are receiving full anticoagulation medication (see section 4.4 Special warnings and special precautions for use). For correct administration of Goserelin (ZOLADEX® LA), see instructions on the instruction card (see section 6.6 Instructions for use, handling and disposal). Adult men: One depot of Goserelin (ZOLADEX® LA) 10.8 mg injected subcutaneously into the anterior abdominal wall, every 3 months (see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). Adult women: One depot of Goserelin (ZOLADEX® LA) 10.8 mg injected subcutaneously into the anterior abdominal wall, every 12 weeks. Elderly: No dosage adjustment is necessary in the elderly. Renal Impairment: No dosage adjustment is necessary for patients with renal impairment. Hepatic Impairment: No dosage adjustment is necessary for patients with hepatic impairment. Children: Not indicated for use in children.",1,2,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Prostate cancer: Goserelin (ZOLADEX® LA) 10.8 mg is indicated in the management of prostate cancer suitable for hormonal manipulation. Endometriosis: Goserelin (ZOLADEX® LA) 10.8 mg is indicated in the management of endometriosis including alleviation of symptoms, such as pain, and reduction in the size and number of endometrial lesions. Uterine fibroids: Goserelin (ZOLADEX® LA) 10.8 mg is indicated in the management of fibroids including shrinkage of lesions, improvement in the patient's haematological status and reduction of symptoms, such as pain. It can be used as an adjunct to surgery to facilitate the operative technique and reduce operative blood loss. Breast cancer: Goserelin (ZOLADEX® LA) 10.8 mg is indicated in the management of estrogen-receptor-positive breast cancer in premenopausal women. [Page 2]",1,1,4.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:02:14.966731+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY26102,Fusidic Acid + Hydrocortisone,Fucidin H,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mt41VDtY5hzMiNO4StrB-yqaJTDpX0Hi/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY26102_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mt41VDtY5hzMiNO4StrB-yqaJTDpX0Hi_view_usp_drivesdk_c673f48073.pdf,page_text/DR-XY26102_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mt41VDtY5hzMiNO4StrB-yqaJTDpX0Hi_view_usp_drivesdk_c673f48073.json,9668eba83b37aa914fa91f21b86d9382dfa19675ec1873979edf9af03d98e266,1035131,2,digital_text,"Fucidin® H cream is a topical cream preparation containing 20 mg/g of fusidic acid and 10 mg/g of hydrocortisone acetate in the form of micro crystals, suspended in the cream vehicle. The product appears as a white homogeneous cream in aluminium tubes with cap.",1,1,Product Description,"Fusidic acid and hydrocortisone acetate (Fucidin® H) Cream is indicated for the treatment of dermatitis, including atopic dermatitis and contact dermatitis, where an infection with bacteria sensitive to fusidic acid is suspected or confirmed. Because of its hydrocortisone content, Fucidin® H Cream is particularly appropriate in cases where a milder corticosteroid is indicated, including milder inflammatory dermatoses - on the face and on children’s skin. Fucidin® H Cream is cosmetically acceptable for use on the face and hands and convenient for use in the groin area and armpits.",1,1,Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:02:18.400007+00:00
