PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY27497,Metoprolol Tartrate,Neobloc,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1nGijcgkoRLx7E7ZYd6Zq3Zx8bO2facfF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY27497_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1nGijcgkoRLx7E7ZYd6Zq3Zx8bO2facfF_view_usp_drivesdk_a67c08ac96.pdf,page_text/DR-XY27497_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1nGijcgkoRLx7E7ZYd6Zq3Zx8bO2facfF_view_usp_drivesdk_a67c08ac96.json,652643f391588d4f90d179c9a7a675a65240b6bf9d8b2a41fb7174b92e33cbfb,298144,2,ocr,"METOPROLOL tartrate (NEOBLOC®) 50mg is a round, biconvex, white tablet coded with GX! MT5 on one side, METOPROLOL tartrate (NEOBLOC®) 100mg is a round, biconvex, white tablet coded with GXI MT1 on one side, NEOBLOC® is a brand of METOPROLOL tartrate, a beta-adrenergic receptor blocking agent which acts preferentially on &1-receptors. This 81-blocking activity of METOPROLOL tartrate (NEOBLOC®) is manifested by a reduction in heart rate and cardiac output, and control of blood pressure both at rest and during exercise.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"It is used in the of jon, angina pectoris, cardiac arrhythmias, jal infarction, and heart failure. It is also used in the management of hyperthyroidism and in the prophylactic treatment of migraine.",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T19:07:32.247361+00:00
