PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY28626,Pimecrolimus,Elidel,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GDYFh2Y8_ZPXOUclZHKvu8_eKegtWJwy/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY28626_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GDYFh2Y8_ZPXOUclZHKvu8_eKegtWJwy_view_usp_drivesdk_8d3c7f6b26.pdf,page_text/DR-XY28626_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GDYFh2Y8_ZPXOUclZHKvu8_eKegtWJwy_view_usp_drivesdk_8d3c7f6b26.json,c68c92bd875663600d914b58e9fdd31c19a6e6cadee4ea9d63d6e21f92edcd7a,612950,3,digital_text,"Pimecrolimus (Elidel) 1% cream is whitish, odorless, non-staining and easily spreadable.",1,1,DESCRIPTION,Pimecrolimus (Elidel) 1% cream is indicated for the short-term treatment of the signs and symptoms of atopic dermatitis (eczema) and intermittent long-term treatment to prevent progression to flares in patients 3 months of age and above. Treatment with Pimecrolimus (Elidel) is indicated in patients whom the use of conventional topical corticosteroid therapy is deemed inadvisable because of potential risks or in patients who are not adequately responsive to or intolerant of conventional topical corticosteroid therapy.,1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:11:40.260374+00:00
