PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY29934,Levetiracetam,Keppra,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Mp_y8573sz9BdDCN6FJzqiJVg6ldKTOS/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY29934_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Mp_y8573sz9BdDCN6FJzqiJVg6ldKTOS_view_usp_drivesdk_17c6b046c4.pdf,page_text/DR-XY29934_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Mp_y8573sz9BdDCN6FJzqiJVg6ldKTOS_view_usp_drivesdk_17c6b046c4.json,d5aec24f78d6215e5c1cbad0386dde95365a9c678d3bd9d4008880813cc64779,178893,9,digital_text,"Levetiracetam (Keppra) 250 mg Film-Coated Tablet: Each blue, oblong, debossed with code ‘ucb’ and ‘250’ on one side, film coated tablet contains 250 mg of levetiracetam. The score li ne is only to facilitate breaking for ease of swallowing and not to divide into equal doses. Levetiracetam (Keppra) 500 mg Film-Coated Tablet: Each yellow, oblong, debossed with code ‘ucb’ and ‘500’ on one side, film coated tablet contains 500 mg of levetiracetam. The score li ne is only to facilitate breaking for ease of swallowing and not to divide into equal doses. Levetiracetam (Keppra) 1 g Film-Coated Tablet: Each white, scored, oblong, debossed with code ‘ucb’ and ‘1000’ on one side, film coated tablet contains 1 g of levetiracetam. The score line is only to facilitate breaking for ease of swallowing and not to divide into equal doses. Levetiracetam (Keppra) 100 mg/mL Oral Solution: Each mL of clear liquid oral solution contains 100 mg of levetiracetam. Levetiracetam (Keppra) 500 mg/5 mL Concentrate for Solution for IV Infusion: Each mL contains 100 mg Levetiracetam. The 5 mL vial contains 500 mg of Levetiracetam.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Levetiracetam is indicated as monotherapy in the treatment of:  partial onset seizures with or without secondary generalisation in adults and adolescents from 16 years of age with newly diagnosed epilepsy. Levetiracetam is indicated as adjunctive therapy in the treatment of:  partial onset seizures with or without secondary generalisation in adults, adolescents and children from 4 years of age with epilepsy  myoclonic seizures in adults and adolescents from 12 years of age with juvenile myoclonic epilepsy,  primary generalised tonic-clonic seizures in adults and adolescents from 4 years of age with idiopathic generalised epilepsy. Levetiracetam concentrate is an alternative for patients (adults and children from 4 years of age) when oral administration is temporarily not feasible.",3,3,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:16:40.759996+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY29937,Cefalexin (as monohydrate),Airex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1AWSvh6p-ge-286-fnF41OnQC-bGpxL4N/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY29937_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1AWSvh6p-ge-286-fnF41OnQC-bGpxL4N_view_usp_drivesdk_1dfcbce646.pdf,page_text/DR-XY29937_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1AWSvh6p-ge-286-fnF41OnQC-bGpxL4N_view_usp_drivesdk_1dfcbce646.json,210cdc8b2e46b21c2588c2ceff074ec60517e4384ebae8d2f518df6ac0d25d8a,113420,2,digital_text,"Airex 250 mg is almost white, semi granular powder encapsulated in empty gelatin capsule size # 1 with gray cap and yellow body. Airex 500 mg is a white, semi granular powder encapsulated in empty gelatin capsule size # 0 with scarlet cap and ivory body. Airex 250 mg suspension is an orange granule. Airex 125 mg suspension is an off-white powder. Airex 100 mg per mL suspension (oral drops) is a white powder.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of urinary tract infection and respiratory tract infection, otitis media, skin and other infections due to sensitive organisms.",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:16:43.429754+00:00
