sodium / Sulbactam sodium (Silgram), peak serum concentrations of ampicillin and sulbactam are obtained. Ampicillin serum levels are similar to those produced by the administration of equivalent amounts of ampicillin alone. The mean serum half-life of both drug is approximately 1 hour in healthy volunteers. Approximately 75 to 85% of both ampicillin and sulbactam are excreted unchanged in the urine during the first 8 hours after administration of Ampicillin sodium / Sulbactam sodium (Silgram) to individuals with normal renal function.",1,1,DESCRIPTION,Ampicillin sodium/ Sulbactam sodium (Silgram) is indicated in the treatment of the following: ! Community acquired pneumonia ! Upper urinary tract infection ! Intra-abdominal infections ! Gynecological infections ! Skin and soft tissue infections ! Prophylaxis against infections associated with abdominal surgery,1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:18:21.974989+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY30368,Amantadine sulphate,PK-Merz,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gJNdpZIbNFjXoLzrpitH6IPIoCiJCrjj/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY30368_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gJNdpZIbNFjXoLzrpitH6IPIoCiJCrjj_view_usp_drivesdk_cd43601b57.pdf,page_text/DR-XY30368_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gJNdpZIbNFjXoLzrpitH6IPIoCiJCrjj_view_usp_drivesdk_cd43601b57.json,260e541b4bb32c87acd465d4d20a3aa4cc04e99faa7916cce508473412669f4f,384356,2,digital_text,"Amantadine Sulphate (PK-Merz) film-coated tablets 1 00 mg ar e orange, round, biconvex film-coated tablets with a groove on one side. The tablets have a diamet er of 10.0 to 10.3 mm and ar e 3.8 to 4.3 mm in height. PHARMA",1,1,Product Description:,"F or the treatment of symptoms of Parkinson's disease, e.g. stiffness (rigor), trembling (tremor) and diminished movement or motionlessness (hypokinesia or akinesia) as well as movement disorders similar to Parkinson's disease caused by certain medicinal products (neuroleptics and medicinal products with a similar mechanism of action) (extrapyramidal symptoms such as early dyskinesia, akathisia and parkinsonism).",1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:18:25.434512+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY30375,Methimazole,Methazol,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1B0gp6Z3Mcr89x0DuJJSE3ue-vpUG_8xV/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY30375_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1B0gp6Z3Mcr89x0DuJJSE3ue-vpUG_8xV_view_usp_drivesdk_ab05add228.pdf,page_text/DR-XY30375_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1B0gp6Z3Mcr89x0DuJJSE3ue-vpUG_8xV_view_usp_drivesdk_ab05add228.json,7b4fda66446b628ab4b0fac14861213ba30df5bd1809aa288edd8a295a1276d5,2629031,1,ocr,"Methimazole 5 mg Tablet (Methazol) is a white to off-white, 9.5 mm round tablet, hexabeveled on one side and beveled-edged, scored",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Methimazole (Methazol) is used in the management of hyperthyroidism, including the treatment of Graves’ disease, used in the preparation of hyperthyroid patients for thyroidectomy, as an adjunct to radio-iodine therapy and the treatment of thyroid storm.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T19:18:34.585179+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY30395,Salbutamol (as sulfate),Asmalin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cgTd6ppDW0Gj6ny3te9JPRliPDRj0oth/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY30395_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cgTd6ppDW0Gj6ny3te9JPRliPDRj0oth_view_usp_drivesdk_9248e6ee0b.pdf,page_text/DR-XY30395_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cgTd6ppDW0Gj6ny3te9JPRliPDRj0oth_view_usp_drivesdk_9248e6ee0b.json,b7424bbae0d94d61685926dfa3408b0531a0b8b2eb25091d27b433dee6053776,4264512,1,digital_text,"Salbutamol (Asmalin®) 100 mcg/dose metered-dose inhaler (CFC/ODS-Free) is a suspension aerosol for oral inhalation supplied in a pressurized container. Asmalin uses hydrofluoroalkane (HFA) as propellant. This does not change the efficacy of salbutamol at the same nominal dose. PHARMACODYNAMICS Salbutamol is a selective short-acting beta2-agonist with a preferential effect on beta2-receptors found in the respiratory tract. It stimulates adenyl cyclase, the enzyme which catalyzes the conversion of adenosine triphosphate (ATP) to cyclic-3’,5’-adenosine monophosphate (cAMP). cAMP mediates cellular responses such as bronchial smooth muscle relaxation resulting in bronchodilation. PHARMACOKINETICS Salbutamol is readily absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract after oral administration. When given by inhalation, 10% to 20% of the dose reaches the lower airways. The remainder is retained in the delivery system or is deposited in the oropharynx from where it is swallowed. Plasma protein binding is around 10%. Salbutamol undergoes first-pass metabolism in the liver, being converted to salbutamol 4’-O-sulfate. The plasma half-life of salbutamol has been estimated to range from 4 to 6 hours. Salbutamol is rapidly excreted, mainly in the urine, as metabolites and unchanged drug; a smaller proportion is excreted in the feces. Majority of a salbutamol dose given orally or by inhalation is excreted within 72 hours. Bronchodilation begins within 5 to 15 minutes after oral inhalation of salbutamol and peaks in 0.5 to 3 hours. The mean duration of effect persists for at least 4 hours. In some patients, bronchodilation may persist up to 6 hours.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,• For the relief of bronchospasm associated with reversible obstructive airway diseases such as bronchial asthma and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease • For the prevention of exercise-induced bronchospasm if the drug is to be given before exertion,1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:18:38.772859+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY30458,Deferiprone,Ferriprox,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1c0oOGFaN9nRksizMjJZ4RLLWyw-v3rNV/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY30458_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1c0oOGFaN9nRksizMjJZ4RLLWyw-v3rNV_view_usp_drivesdk_66af13275b.pdf,page_text/DR-XY30458_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1c0oOGFaN9nRksizMjJZ4RLLWyw-v3rNV_view_usp_drivesdk_66af13275b.json,05d67f983116b2c619a94bfd20e7b01c272d4b7625e28d3698dce2cce4b59509,9664653,1,ocr,The most serious is the of avery,1,1,prescription.,"your first dose in the morning. Take your son dose et Take your third Deferiprone (Ferriprox™) is used ir in the treatment of it iron overload in patients dose in the evening. It is not y to with with for whom is food. However, you may find it easier to ‘eraser to take your medication, if you take it with your meals. Deferiprone (Ferriprox™) will be most effective",1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T19:18:48.519014+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY30494,Ipratropium bromide + Salbutamol (as sulfate),Duavent,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WY5vYbjvgh1zGaRf7mchMNVB-3ccAF8h/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY30494_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WY5vYbjvgh1zGaRf7mchMNVB-3ccAF8h_view_usp_drivesdk_42a4f84883.pdf,page_text/DR-XY30494_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WY5vYbjvgh1zGaRf7mchMNVB-3ccAF8h_view_usp_drivesdk_42a4f84883.json,237798c3b02bdd21d2d9daff2f9eb1103e1890981008c8e47f223e3dc37d0d99,545004,1,digital_text,"Ipratropium bromide-Salbutamol is a sterile, clear colorless aqueous solution filled in a 2.5 mL pulmoneb. PHARMACODYNAMICS Ipratropium bromide is an anticholinergic bronchodilator that reduces the formation of cyclic guanosine monophosphate (cGMP), a mediator of bronchospasm, thereby relaxing the smooth muscles of the bronchi and bronchioles. It is a potent bronchodilator, particularly in large bronchial airway; some evidence suggests that Ipratropium bromide also has bronchodilator activity in small airways. Salbutamol is a selective short-acting beta -adrenergic agonist with preferential effect on beta -adrenergic receptors found in the respiratory tract. It stimulates adenyl cyclase, the 2 2 enzyme which catalyzes the conversion of adenosine triphosphate (ATP) to cyclic-3',5'-adenosine monophosphate (cAMP). cAMP mediates cellular responses such as bronchial smooth muscle relaxation resulting in bronchodilation. Ipratropium bromide-Salbutamol combination maximizes the response to treatment in patients with bronchial asthma and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) by increasing bronchodilation through two distinctly different mechanisms, i.e., anticholinergic (parasympatholytic) and beta -agonist (sympathomimetic) effects. Simultaneous administration of both 2 an anticholinergic (Ipratropium bromide) and a beta -agonist (Salbutamol) produces a greater bronchodilator effect than when either drug is used alone.2 Bronchodilation occurs within 15 to 30 minutes with peak effect seen approximately 1 to 2 hours after oral inhalation via nebulization of 400 to 600 mcg of Ipratropium bromide. Bronchodilation generally persists for 4 to 5 hours, but may last up to 7 to 8 hours in some patients. After concomitant administration via nebulization of Salbutamol and Ipratropium in patients with COPD, bronchodilation persists for 5 to 7 hours compared with 3 to 4 hours in patients given Salbutamol alone. PHARMACOKINETICS Only a small amount of Ipratropium reaches the systemic circulation after inhalation. Some Ipratropium is inadvertently swallowed but it is poorly absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract. Pharmacokinetic studies in asthmatic patients receiving Salbutamol inhalation solution indicate that less than 20% of a single dose of the drug is absorbed when administered by nebulization. The remainder of the dose was recovered from the nebulizer and expired air. Ipratropium is 0 to 9% bound to plasma albumin and α -acid glycoproteins in vitro. It is partially metabolized to N-isopropylnortropium methobromide, an inactive ester hydrolysis product.1 Salbutamol is metabolized in the liver, being converted to Salbutamol 4'-O-sulfate which has little or no beta-adrenergic stimulating effect and no beta-adrenergic blocking effect. Animal studies show that Salbutamol can cross the blood-brain barrier and the placenta. It may be secreted in breast milk, but the concentrations are not known.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"·M anagement of reversible bronchospasm associated with obstructive airway diseases (e.g., bronchial asthma) ·F or use in patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) on a regular inhaled bronchodilator who continue to have evidence of bronchospasm and who require a second bronchodilator",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:18:51.632376+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY30590,Aceclofenac,Clanza,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BV_fe3u-Hd4pcfRdxtMbImz_gYOHGlR6/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY30590_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1BV_fe3u-Hd4pcfRdxtMbImz_gYOHGlR6_view_usp_drivesdk_b71a1c617d.pdf,page_text/DR-XY30590_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1BV_fe3u-Hd4pcfRdxtMbImz_gYOHGlR6_view_usp_drivesdk_b71a1c617d.json,6e79afdab5b25f9659b4a9ade085ca429e40ee1eab6e13e8c548016926d40dda,99236,1,digital_text,"White, round, biconvex film-coated tablet, engraved with “A” on one side, “UT” on the other side.",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Aceclofenac is indicated for the relief of pain and inflammation in toothache, trauma, lumbago, osteoarthritis, rheumatoid arthritis and ankylosing spondylitis.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:18:54.526435+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY30659,Methylphenidate Hydrochloride,Concerta,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1f45WIoaJik_lR3Msq1gWiiZT7Ju-vX96/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY30659_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1f45WIoaJik_lR3Msq1gWiiZT7Ju-vX96_view_usp_drivesdk_01b981985b.pdf,page_text/DR-XY30659_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1f45WIoaJik_lR3Msq1gWiiZT7Ju-vX96_view_usp_drivesdk_01b981985b.json,0caf85b3989933985fd45080b5d987f887a8f9a1ba3308745a839216263fb1c4,398959,21,digital_text,,,,,"Methylphenidate hydrochloride (Concerta®) is indicated for the treatment of Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD). The efficacy of methylphenidate hydrochloride (Concerta®) in the treatment of ADHD was established in controlled trials of children and adolescents aged 6 to 17 and adults aged 18 to 65 who met DSM -IV criteria for ADHD. Methylphenidate hydrochloride (Concerta®) should be used as a par t of a comprehen sive treat ment program where remedial measures alone prove insufficient. A comprehensive treatment program for the treatment of ADHD may include other measures (psychological, educational, social) for patients with this disorder. Diagnosis must be made according to DSM criteria or ICD guidelines. Methylphenidate hydrochloride (Concerta®) treatment is not indicated in all patients with ADHD and the decision to use the drug must be based on a very thorough assessment of the severity of the patient’s symptoms. Stimu lants are not inte nded for use in the patient who exhibits symptoms secondary to environmental factors and/or other primary psychiatric disorders, including psychosis. Appropriate educational placement is essential, and psychosocial intervention is often helpful. Specific etiology of this syndrome is unknown, and there is no single diagnostic test. Adequate diagnosis requires the use of medical and special psychological, educational, and social resources. Learn ing may or may not be impaired.",8,8,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T19:18:57.748504+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY30665,Folic Acid,Folinc,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1eAjulW6QjIHpc-b0Y6qkqn2VQuqpe4EB/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY30665_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eAjulW6QjIHpc-b0Y6qkqn2VQuqpe4EB_view_usp_drivesdk_616fc5f269.pdf,page_text/DR-XY30665_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eAjulW6QjIHpc-b0Y6qkqn2VQuqpe4EB_view_usp_drivesdk_616fc5f269.json,cb9524a962e2bd7f8f8fc5067262f93b14a9c7db86983ea3e02b5e4c6d7068c3,1129746,2,ocr,"Folinc is a light yellow to yellow to yellowish-orange powder encapsulated in empty gelatin capsule size #3 with light green cap and light green body. Folic Acid is a member of the vitamin B group. Folic Acid is reduced in the body to tetrahydrofolate, which is a coenzyme for various metabolic processes including the synthesis of purine and pyrimidine nucleotides, and hence in the synthesis of DNA, it is also involved in some amino-acid conversions, and in the formation and utilization of formate. Deficiency, which can result in megaloblastic anemia develops when the dietary intake is inadequate (as in malnutrition), when there is malabsorption (as in sprue), increased utilization (as in pregnancy or conditions such as hemolytic anemia), increased loss (as in hemodialysis), or as a result of the administration of folate antagonists and other drugs that interfere with normal folate metabolism.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Folic acid is used in the treatment and prevention of the folate deficiency state. It is also used in women of child- bearing potential and pregnant women to protect against neural tube defects in their offspring.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T19:19:09.555980+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY30701,RANITIDINE (AS HYDROCHLORIDE),RAXIDE,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Pme5cfYsFhB0QLrxZK18fW91Z-IgGIz9/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY30701_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Pme5cfYsFhB0QLrxZK18fW91Z-IgGIz9_view_usp_drivesdk_f6037b4056.pdf,page_text/DR-XY30701_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Pme5cfYsFhB0QLrxZK18fW91Z-IgGIz9_view_usp_drivesdk_f6037b4056.json,451af5d51831dd6b8189df0ae9326af48359370a4c20238dcb69367515b6cd08,871228,2,ocr,"white to cream, round, biconvex film-coated tablet. RANITIDINE (Raxide”) 150mg or 300mg Tablet is a RAXIDE® is a brand of Ranitidine, a rapidly-acting histamine H, receptor antagonist used in conditions where eficial, such as gastric and duodenal ulcers. inhibition of gastric acid secretion may be ben! It inhibits basal and stimulated secretion of gas! tric acid, reducing both the volume and the acid and pepsin content of the secretion. It has relatively long duration of action and so a single 150mg dose effectively suppresses gastric acid secretion for 12 hours.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"luding that associated with H. pylori, NSAID-associated peptic ulcer, Treatment of duodenal and gastric ulcer, inc! chronic episodic dyspepsia, post-operative ulcer, acute reflux esophagitis, Zollinger-Ellison syndrome, symptomatic relief in g »hageal reflux di: and prophylaxis of Mendelson’s syndrome.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T19:19:22.263989+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY30798,FOLIC ACID,FOLICARD,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mOmSk6H1LTlQ07-8eAWwmRHPu3jYVCao/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY30798_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mOmSk6H1LTlQ07-8eAWwmRHPu3jYVCao_view_usp_drivesdk_9ae16feb6a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY30798_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mOmSk6H1LTlQ07-8eAWwmRHPu3jYVCao_view_usp_drivesdk_9ae16feb6a.json,29e3b205dbe82afaa983e3139ec06d6665b054b3a5ed9fb2e00224b3343a2efb,723789,2,ocr,"Folic Acid (Folicard*) 5 mg capsule is a scarlet and white hard gelatin capsule printed with the logo of Gruppo Medica, Inc. in black ink on both cap and body.",1,1,Product Description,"Folic Acidis used in the treatment and prevention of folate deficiency state. As a prophylactic in instances in which the Folic Acid requirement is increased, especially during pregnancy, to prevent and reduce incidence of neural tube defects. Used in the treatment of megaloblastic anemias which may result from malabsorption syndromes such as sprue, idiopathic steatorrhea, celiac disease, intestinal reticulosis, regional jejunitis, jejunal diverticulosis, blind loop syndrome, and gastroenterostomy. Folic Acid is also indicated for chronic hemolytic anemia, exfoliative skin disease, gingivitis, anorectic cancer, cervical dysplasia and cardiovascular disease.",1,1,Indication,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T19:19:32.739266+00:00
