PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY30956,Moxifloxacin (as hydrochloride),Vigamox,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VzvfP059U3s9ccnuyVhMcJtZMoZdE6lv/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY30956_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VzvfP059U3s9ccnuyVhMcJtZMoZdE6lv_view_usp_drivesdk_92e8d7833f.pdf,page_text/DR-XY30956_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VzvfP059U3s9ccnuyVhMcJtZMoZdE6lv_view_usp_drivesdk_92e8d7833f.json,56c32c6bad2c6f64aa8318562744482e1798a2b11cf4e3d1f2dbffcc96ddb4fa,360678,12,digital_text,"Pharmaceutical form Moxifloxacin Hydrochloride (Vigamox) 0.5% Sterile Ophthalmic Solution is a sterile, stable ophthalmic solution containing 0.545% w/v Moxifloxacin Hydrochloride, equivalent to 0.5% Moxifloxacin base. The product is greenish yellow in color, which originates from the active ingredient. The reference monograph for this drug product is Ph. Eur. Active substance Excipients Sodium chloride, boric acid, sodium hydroxide and/or hydrochloric acid (for pH adjustment) and purified water.",1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,"Moxifloxacin (as hydrochloride) (Vigamox®) Sterile Ophthalmic Solution is indicated for the treatment of bacterial conjunctivitis caused by bacteria susceptible to moxifloxacin. Moxifloxacin (as hydrochloride) (Vigamox®) Sterile Ophthalmic Solution is indicated in adults and pediatric patients including neonates, infants, children and adolescents aged 0 to 18 years.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:21:56.325697+00:00
