PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY31312,Clindamycin (As Phosphate)  + Benzoyl Peroxide,Duac,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1EpjvApkdJXntLNsP2afKr3L33Oai8g-1/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY31312_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1EpjvApkdJXntLNsP2afKr3L33Oai8g-1_view_usp_drivesdk_97ccc60df2.pdf,page_text/DR-XY31312_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1EpjvApkdJXntLNsP2afKr3L33Oai8g-1_view_usp_drivesdk_97ccc60df2.json,110a8a635a2efa80db1b2845dedcb8e6163fc1c246f1440a2c5a790b5b1d887f,188983,6,digital_text,Clindamycin (as phosphate) + Benzoyl peroxid e (Duac) is a white to slightly ye llow coloured topical gel containing clindamycin (1.2% clindamycin phosphate) at a concentration equivalent to 1% w/w (10mg/g) and benzoyl peroxide 5% w/w (50mg/g).,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Clindamycin (as phosphate) + Benzoyl peroxide (Duac) Gel is indicated for the topical treatment of acne vulgaris.,3,3,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:23:22.004572+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY31313,Clarithromycin,Clariget,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1P0dRBBy7rHdlxhJ7p9FzU7mLJR9vrf5r/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY31313_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1P0dRBBy7rHdlxhJ7p9FzU7mLJR9vrf5r_view_usp_drivesdk_e718d6e988.pdf,page_text/DR-XY31313_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1P0dRBBy7rHdlxhJ7p9FzU7mLJR9vrf5r_view_usp_drivesdk_e718d6e988.json,5106c4a525f941f3122e1af949c747d3e1a38c0eba26685b6d7887eb2a0026e9,14561487,16,digital_text,"Clarithromycin (Clariget ®) 250mg film-coated tablet is available as white colored, round film-coated tablets, engraved “CLARI 250” on one side and plain on the other side. Clarithromycin (Clariget ®) 500mg film-coated tablet is available as white colored, oblong film coated tablets, engraved “GETZ” on one side and “CLARI 500” on the other side. Clarithromycin (Clariget®) 125mg/5mL granules for suspension is available as white to off-white granular powder.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Clarithromycin (Clariget ®) is indicated for treatment of infections due to susceptible organisms. Such infections include: - Lower respiratory tract infections (e.g., bronchitis, pneumonia) - Upper respiratory tract infections (e.g., pharyngitis, sinusitis) - Acute otitis media in children - Skin and soft tissue infections (e.g., folliculitis, cellulitis, erysipelas) - Leprosy - Disseminated or localized mycobacterial infections due to Mycobacterium avium or Mycobacterium intracellulare. Localized infections due to Mycobacterium chelonae, Mycobacterium fortuitum, or Mycobacterium kansasii - Clarithromycin (Clariget ®) tablets and granules for oral suspension are indicated for the prevention of disseminated Mycobacterium avium complex (MAC) disease in patients with advanced HIV infection - Clarithromycin (Clariget ®) in the presence of acid suppression is also indicated for the eradication of H. pylori resulting in decreased recurrence of duodenal ulcer - Treatment odontogenic infections",1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:23:34.060762+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY31326,Prednisolone Phosphate (As Sodium),Romamed,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-44YKUbC_3PPiCncx7WE8o2G-iH97168/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY31326_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-44YKUbC_3PPiCncx7WE8o2G-iH97168_view_usp_drivesdk_d1a3f12875.pdf,page_text/DR-XY31326_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-44YKUbC_3PPiCncx7WE8o2G-iH97168_view_usp_drivesdk_d1a3f12875.json,8092916b028caef2129e35b2667e9e82118d44eb04f85a0bef58708d5277e785,1441958,2,ocr,"Prednisolone (Romamed) is a glucocorticoid given, as the free alcohol or in esterified form, orally or parenterally, in the treatment of various disorders in which corticosteroids are indicated, except adrenal deficiency states. It is also given by local injection, applied rectally and applied topically as eye drops or ear drops. Adverse effects are those of corticoster- oids in general. It has relatively slight mineralocorticoid effects. Prednisolone (Romamed) is a clear colorless to yellowish to light orange syrup in grape flavor with a sweet fruit taste.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,For replacement therapy in adrenal insufficiency.,1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T19:24:34.554390+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY31354,Rosuvastatin (as calcium),Crestor,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1QE2s8HpARZVMbveooVKDpJTqohK77nc5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY31354_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QE2s8HpARZVMbveooVKDpJTqohK77nc5_view_usp_drivesdk_13094fad4f.pdf,page_text/DR-XY31354_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QE2s8HpARZVMbveooVKDpJTqohK77nc5_view_usp_drivesdk_13094fad4f.json,4fd13496504e9b43619997e5a4bd77e95095470b80c63f4cac4f076608ae79f8,336468,21,digital_text,"5 mg film-coated tablet – round, biconvex, 7 mm, yellow coloured. 10 mg film-coated tablet - round, biconvex, 7 mm, pink coloured. 20 mg film-coated tablet - round, biconvex, 9 mm, pink coloured. 40 mg film-coated tablet - oval, biconvex, 11.4 x 6.9 mm, pink coloured. Tablets are impressed with ‘ZD4522’ and the tablet strength. 4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 4.1 Therapeutic indications Rosuvastatin (CRESTOR) should be used as an adjunct to diet when the response to diet and exercise is inadequate. ROSUVASTATIN [Page 2] Prevention of Cardiovascular Events In adult patients with an increased risk of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease based on the presence of cardiovascular disease risk markers such as an elevated hsC RP level, age, hypertension, low HDL -C, smoking or a family history of premature coronary heart disease, Rosuvastatin (CRESTOR) is indicated to reduce total mortality and the risk of major cardiovascular events (cardiovascular death, stroke, MI, unstable a ngina, or arterial revascularization). In adult patients with hypercholesterolaemia Rosuvastatin (CRESTOR) is indicated to: • reduce elevated LDL-C, Total Cholesterol, triglycerides and to increase HDL -cholesterol in patients with primary hypercholesterol aemia (heterozygous familial and non familial) and mixed dyslipidaemia (Fredrickson Types IIa and IIb). Rosuvastatin (CRESTOR) also lowers ApoB, nonHDL-C, VLDL-C, VLDL-TG, the LDL-C/HDL-C, total C/HDL-C, nonHDL-C/HDL- C, ApoB/ApoA-I ratios and increases ApoA-I in these populations. • treat patients with primary dysbetalipoproteinaemia (Fredrickson Type III hyper lipoproteinaemia). • treat isolated hypertriglyceridaemia (Fredrickson Type IV hyperlipidaemia). • reduce Total Cholesterol and LDL -C in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia (HoFH), as an adjunct to diet and other lipid lowering treatments (e.g. LDL apheresis) or alone if such treatments are unavailable. • slow or delay the progression of atherosclerosis. Children and adolescents 6 to 17 years of age: Rosuvastatin (CRESTOR) is indicated to reduce the Total Cholesterol, LDL -C and Apo B in patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia (HeFH). 4.2 Dosage and method of administration The usual dose range is 10-40 mg orally once a day. The dosage of Rosuvastatin (CRESTOR) should be individualised according to the goal of therapy and patient response. The majority of patients are controlled at the start dose. However, if necessary, dose adjustment can be made at 2 to 4 week intervals. (See Section 5.1",1,2,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Rosuvastatin (CRESTOR) should be used as an adjunct to diet when the response to diet and exercise is inadequate. ROSUVASTATIN [Page 2] Prevention of Cardiovascular Events In adult patients with an increased risk of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease based on the presence of cardiovascular disease risk markers such as an elevated hsC RP level, age, hypertension, low HDL -C, smoking or a family history of premature coronary heart disease, Rosuvastatin (CRESTOR) is indicated to reduce total mortality and the risk of major cardiovascular events (cardiovascular death, stroke, MI, unstable a ngina, or arterial revascularization). In adult patients with hypercholesterolaemia Rosuvastatin (CRESTOR) is indicated to: • reduce elevated LDL-C, Total Cholesterol, triglycerides and to increase HDL -cholesterol in patients with primary hypercholesterol aemia (heterozygous familial and non familial) and mixed dyslipidaemia (Fredrickson Types IIa and IIb). Rosuvastatin (CRESTOR) also lowers ApoB, nonHDL-C, VLDL-C, VLDL-TG, the LDL-C/HDL-C, total C/HDL-C, nonHDL-C/HDL- C, ApoB/ApoA-I ratios and increases ApoA-I in these populations. • treat patients with primary dysbetalipoproteinaemia (Fredrickson Type III hyper lipoproteinaemia). • treat isolated hypertriglyceridaemia (Fredrickson Type IV hyperlipidaemia). • reduce Total Cholesterol and LDL -C in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia (HoFH), as an adjunct to diet and other lipid lowering treatments (e.g. LDL apheresis) or alone if such treatments are unavailable. • slow or delay the progression of atherosclerosis. Children and adolescents 6 to 17 years of age: Rosuvastatin (CRESTOR) is indicated to reduce the Total Cholesterol, LDL -C and Apo B in patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia (HeFH).",1,2,4.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T19:24:37.860903+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY31516,Tigecycline,Tygacil,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cMS7c1fvCadrG4qB9l8w19Oll5-wtrYF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY31516_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cMS7c1fvCadrG4qB9l8w19Oll5-wtrYF_view_usp_drivesdk_3ff7e86b44.pdf,page_text/DR-XY31516_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cMS7c1fvCadrG4qB9l8w19Oll5-wtrYF_view_usp_drivesdk_3ff7e86b44.json,fa554c7d94d2fd446026a31d80bd836fee16a307592e09f04378759dffef76f7,404328,28,digital_text,"Tigecycline (Tygacil) is a glycylcycline antibacterial for intravenous infusion. The chemical name of tigecycline (4S,4aS,5aR,12aS)-9-[2-(tert-butylamino)acetamido]-4,7- bis(dimethylamino)-1,4,4a,5,5a,6,11,12a-octahydro-3,10,12,12a-tetrahydroxy-1,11-dioxo-2- naphthacenecarboxamide. The molecular formula is C29H39N5O8 and the molecular weight is 585.65. The structural formula is represented below: Tigecycline is an orange lyophilized powder or cake.",1,1,2. DESCRIPTION,"Adults Tigecycline is indicated for treatment of the following infections in adults: N N H3C H3C H3C O OH N CH3H3C O H OH H OH N CH3H3C OH O NH2 O H H TIGECYCLINE Viewed on: Sunday, July 7, 2024 - 10:06:35 PM Eastern Time [Page 2]  Complicated skin and skin structure infections (cSSSI), including those with methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA). Tigecycline is not indicated for the treatment of diabetic foot infections (DFI) (see Section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties).  Complicated intra-abdominal infections (cIAI).  Community-acquired pneumonia (CAP). Tigecycline is not indicated for the treatment of hospital-acquired or ventilator-associated pneumonia (see Section 4.4 Special warnings and precautions for use). Pediatrics Tigecycline is indicated in children from the age of eight years for treatment of the following infections only in situations where other alternative antibiotics are not suitable:  Complicated skin and skin structure infections (cSSSI), including those with methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA) Tigecycline is not indicated for the treatment of diabetic foot infections (DFI). (see Section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties)  Complicated intra-abdominal infections (cIAI)",1,2,4.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T20:12:49.245379+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY31530,Omeprazole (as sodium),Risek,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Pa3j6-o2OsUyR1p_NSU0Y2YFSdqJl-1y/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY31530_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Pa3j6-o2OsUyR1p_NSU0Y2YFSdqJl-1y_view_usp_drivesdk_9beda04e65.pdf,page_text/DR-XY31530_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Pa3j6-o2OsUyR1p_NSU0Y2YFSdqJl-1y_view_usp_drivesdk_9beda04e65.json,8c46c72bdfaafadf8721c889e7b21533cd0d358c8db1567cec7828564de0a104,464156,2,digital_text,Omeprazole (Risek®) Lyophilized Powder for Intravenous Injection and Infusion is available as white to off-white hygroscopic powder filled in amber glass USP type II vial with a red color flip-off seal having FLIP-OFF embossed with a grey color rubber stopper.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Omeprazole for intravenous use is indicated as an alternative to oral therapy for the following indications i.e. Adults - Treatment of duodenal ulcers. - Prevention of relapse of duodenal ulcers. - Treatment of gastric ulcers. - Prevention of relapse of gastric ulcers. - In combination with appropriate antibiotics, Helicobacter pylori (H. pylori) eradication in peptic ulcer disease. - Treatment of NSAID-associated gastric and duodenal ulcers. - Prevention of NSAID-associated gastric and duodenal ulcers in patients at risk. - Treatment of reflux oesophagitis. - Long-term management of patients with healed reflux oesophagitis. - Treatment of symptomatic gastro-oesophageal reflux disease. - Treatment of Zollinger-Ellison syndrome.",1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T20:12:52.593069+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY31603,Gadobutrol,Gadovist,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zLf3HYXdl6TlsM2rBR6sU0p9H7hxzqLx/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY31603_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zLf3HYXdl6TlsM2rBR6sU0p9H7hxzqLx_view_usp_drivesdk_167536aa15.pdf,page_text/DR-XY31603_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zLf3HYXdl6TlsM2rBR6sU0p9H7hxzqLx_view_usp_drivesdk_167536aa15.json,795f0a378ab5c0004e36d7b989a83891012552a61ba7d045a9b024bb5ba6748b,77630,2,digital_text,"Solution for injection. Clear, colorless to pale yellow solution. The physico-chemical properties of the 1.0 mmol/ml solution for injection Gadobutrol (Gadovist) listed below are: Osmolarity at 37 °C: 1117 mOsm/l solution Osmolality at 37°C: 1603 mOsm/kg H 2O pH of the solution: 6.6 – 8.0 Viscosity at 37°C: 4.96 mPa•s 4. CLINICAL P ARTICULARS",1,1,3. PHARMA CEUTICAL FORM,"T1-weighted scanning sequences are particularly suitable for contrast- enhanced examinations. The usual safety rules for magnetic resonance imaging must be observed, e.g. exclusion of cardiac pacemakers and ferromagnetic implants. 4.2.2 Dosage regimen Adults: A single intravenous injection of 0.1 mmol gadobutrol per kg body weight (equivalent to 0.1 ml Gadobutrol (Gadovist) per kg body weight) is recommended. A total amount of 0.3 mmol gadobutrol per kg body weight (equivalent to 0.3 ml Gadobutrol (Gadovist) per kg body weight) may be administered at maximum for the central nervous system (CNS) and CE-MRA. A dose of 0.075 mmol gadobutrol per kg body weight (equivalent to 0.075 ml Gadobutrol (Gadovist) per kg body weight) may be administered at minimum for imaging of the CNS (see section ‘Clinical Efficacy’). R Whole Body MRI (except MRA) In general, the administration of 0.1 ml Gadobutrol (Gadovist) per kg body weight is sufficient to answer the clinical question. P Additional dosage recommendation for cranial and spinal MRI If a strong clinical suspicion of a lesion persists despite a normal contrast-enhanced MRI or when more accurate information on the number, size or extent of lesions might influence management or therapy of the patient, a further injection of 0.1 ml Gadobutrol (Gadovist) per kg body weight up to 0.2 ml Gadobutrol (Gadovist) per kg body weight within 30 minutes of the first injection may increase the diagnostic yield of the examination. For the exclusion of metastases or recurrent tumors the injection of 0.3 ml Gadobutrol (Gadovist) per kg body weight often leads to higher diagnostic confidence. This applies to lesions with poor vascularization and/or small extracellular space or when relatively less heavily T1-weighted scanning sequences are used. For brain perfusion studies the use of an injector is recommended: 0.1 - 0.3 ml Gadobutrol (Gadovist) per kg body weight (3 - 5 ml/sec). R CE-MRA Imaging of one field of view: 7.5 ml for body weight less than 75 kg 10 ml for body weight of 75 kg or more (corresponding to 0.1-0.15 mmol per kg body weight) Imaging of more than one field of view: 15 ml for body weight less than 75 kg 20 ml for body weight of 75 kg or more (corresponding to 0.2-0.3 mmol per kg body weight) 4.2.3 Special patient populations 4.2.3.1 Pediatric patients For children of all ages including full-term newborns the recommended dose is 0.1 mmol gadobutrol per kg body weight (equivalent to 0.1 ml Gadobutrol (Gadovist) per kg body weight) for all indications, see section ‘Indication(s)’. 4.2.3.2 Geriatric patients In clinical studies, no overall differences in safety or effectiveness were observed between elderly (aged 65 years and above) and younger patients, and other reported clinical experience has not identified differences in responses between the elderly and younger patients. No dosage adjustment is considered necessary. 4.2.3.3 P atients with hepatic impairment Since Gadobutrol is exclusively eliminated in an unchanged form via the kidneys, no dosage adjustment is considered necessary (see also section ‘Pharmacokinetic properties’). 4.2.3.4 P atients with renal impairment The elimination of gadobutrol is prolonged in patients with renal impairment. However, to ensure diagnostically useful images no dosage adjustment is recommended (see also section ‘Special warnings and precautions for use’ and section ‘Pharmacokinetic properties’). 4.3 C",1,1,indications (time depending on type of lesion/tissue).,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T20:12:55.660792+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY31634,Paracetamol,Anaseran,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1772t4S2IHELnDpQy48EQh0c69hgqD37C/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY31634_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1772t4S2IHELnDpQy48EQh0c69hgqD37C_view_usp_drivesdk_0fe095ddcf.pdf,page_text/DR-XY31634_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1772t4S2IHELnDpQy48EQh0c69hgqD37C_view_usp_drivesdk_0fe095ddcf.json,0559c0b287be92d2f8ee4565ec770f55bd8b666f1de433f18101a6a824987441,179013,2,digital_text,"Paracetamol (Anaseran) 500 mg is peach-colored tablet, round, flat, beveled edge and scored on one side. Paracetamol (Anaseran) 125 mg/ 5 mL syrup is an orange-colored syrup with banana flavor and sweet fruit taste. Paracetamol (Anaseran) 100 mg/ mL is a pink suspension with tutti-frutti flavor and sweet fruit taste. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This product contains paracetamol, a fever reducer and pain reliever.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T20:12:58.313639+00:00
