PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY31693,Multivitamins,Beetab,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ihhyfC5qwXQd7KdNjLSNLPBgXFuZAEHy/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY31693_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ihhyfC5qwXQd7KdNjLSNLPBgXFuZAEHy_view_usp_drivesdk_9db92456c1.pdf,page_text/DR-XY31693_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ihhyfC5qwXQd7KdNjLSNLPBgXFuZAEHy_view_usp_drivesdk_9db92456c1.json,2f2ac0d29ae38d33ccc5d2d48b8394d2fe4cb8fc56297ae2c3865f4b15b569bd,1133503,2,ocr,"Vitamin B Complex + Vitamin E (Beetab) is light-pink to pink, capsule shaped, biconvex, scored film coated tablet. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Each film coated tablet contains a high potency formulation of the three neurotropic vitamin Bl, B6, B12 which. is scientifically-based. This pharmacodynamic and neurotropic concentration of Thiamine, Pyridoxine and Cyanocobalamin precisely works in providing etiologic and symptomatic therapy of painful neurological conditions. Vitamin E, a fat-soluble vitamin, prevents the oxidation of polyunsatu- rated fatty acids. It reacts with free radicals, which are the cause of oxidative damage to all membranes, without the formation of another free radical in the process. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? 1-3 tablets a day or as prescribed by the physician. WHEN YOU SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you are allergic to any component of the product. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Do not take more than the recommended dose. Do not use after the expiry date on the label.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T20:13:14.757579+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY31693,Multivitamins,Beetab,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vraSndpqxsW9pWqgjIglYfPyXLtsb4b1/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY31693_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vraSndpqxsW9pWqgjIglYfPyXLtsb4b1_view_usp_drivesdk_4a93c078da.pdf,page_text/DR-XY31693_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vraSndpqxsW9pWqgjIglYfPyXLtsb4b1_view_usp_drivesdk_4a93c078da.json,8e6c2d79f9c2c2b855de4918b73b0a80751d489ea5fe40083edfa241c74581cd,145078,1,digital_text,"Vitamin B Complex + Vitamin E (Beetab) is light-pink to pink, capsule shaped, biconvex, scored film coated tablet. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Each film coated tablet contains a high potency formulation of the three neurotropic vitamin B1, B6, B12 which is scientifically-based. This pharma codynamic and neurotropic concentration of Thiamine, Pyridoxine and Cyanocobalamin precisely works in providing etiologic and symptomatic therapy of painful neurological conditions. Vitamin E, a fat -soluble vitamin, prevents the oxidation of polyunsaturate d fatty acids. It reacts with free radicals, which are the cause of oxidative damage to all membranes, without the formation of another free radical in the process. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? 1-3 tablets a day or as prescribed by the physician. WHEN YOU SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you are allergic to any component of the product. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Do not take more than the recommended dose. Do not use after the expiry date on the label.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T20:13:17.759341+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY31774,Dequalinium Chloride,Fluomizin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MvlsQ2qB2RWXZ3Ytv18NKWD9b90qtnY1/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY31774_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MvlsQ2qB2RWXZ3Ytv18NKWD9b90qtnY1_view_usp_drivesdk_1de7f2574e.pdf,page_text/DR-XY31774_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MvlsQ2qB2RWXZ3Ytv18NKWD9b90qtnY1_view_usp_drivesdk_1de7f2574e.json,ab773c29efb5dc48be6111ff0d460a115d66b5b603bbb703be1135f3f3fefccf,2475012,2,digital_text,"Dequalinium chloride are white or almost white, oval, biconvex vaginal tablets. CLINICAL PARTICULARS Therapeutic indications Fluomizin_PHILLIPINEN_PH_380852_148x210_Version5_110117.indd 1 11.01.17 11:33Fluomizin_PHILLIPINEN_PH_380233_148x210_Version3_171221.indd 1Fluomizin_PHILLIPINEN_PH_380233_148x210_Version3_171221.indd 1 17.12.21 14:0817.12.21 14:08 [Page 2] new article-no.: 380233 / 317482 – old article-no.: 380112 / 313167 –Code: dDDddDDd – Plant: Rottendorf Format 148 x 210 mm – Font: Helvetica Cyr – Font-Size: 6.75 pt – Creation-Date: 17.12.2021 – Version 3 : yb de r u t ca f una M :m o r f esnec i l r edn U Caution: Foods, Drugs, Devices and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription. Do not use the medicine after the expiry date stated on the package. Keep medicines out of the reach of children. Special precautions for storage Store at temperatures not exceeding 30 oC Shelf-life 36 months Incompatibilities Dequalinium chloride vaginal tablet is incompatible with soaps and other anionic surfactants, with phenol and with chlorocresol List of excipients Lactose monohydrate, Cellulose microcrystalline, Magnesium stearate PHARMACEUTICAL PARTICULARS Local tolerance A study in rabbits showed the good vaginal tolerance of Dequalinium chloride vaginal tablets. No reproduction toxicity studies have been conducted with Dequalinium chloride vaginal tablets. However, developmental toxicity studies with quarternary ammonium compounds did not reveal evidence of embryofoetal toxicity. In view of the negligible vaginal absorption, there are no human pharmacokinetic data for dequalinium chloride available. Preclinical safety data Considering the minimal vaginal absorption of dequalinium chloride, no acute or chronic toxicity is to be expected. Overdose Application of more than 1 vaginal tablet will not increase the efficacy of Dequalinium chloride vaginal tablets. This will rather result in an increase of side effects. However, no severe side effects after using an overdose of Dequalinium chloride vaginal tablets have been reported. In the case of an overdose, a vaginal lavage should be performed to remove rest of the tablets.",1,2,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Fluomizin_PHILLIPINEN_PH_380852_148x210_Version5_110117.indd 1 11.01.17 11:33Fluomizin_PHILLIPINEN_PH_380233_148x210_Version3_171221.indd 1Fluomizin_PHILLIPINEN_PH_380233_148x210_Version3_171221.indd 1 17.12.21 14:0817.12.21 14:08 [Page 2] new article-no.: 380233 / 317482 – old article-no.: 380112 / 313167 –Code: dDDddDDd – Plant: Rottendorf Format 148 x 210 mm – Font: Helvetica Cyr – Font-Size: 6.75 pt – Creation-Date: 17.12.2021 – Version 3 : yb de r u t ca f una M :m o r f esnec i l r edn U Caution: Foods, Drugs, Devices and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription. Do not use the medicine after the expiry date stated on the package. Keep medicines out of the reach of children. Special precautions for storage Store at temperatures not exceeding 30 oC Shelf-life 36 months Incompatibilities Dequalinium chloride vaginal tablet is incompatible with soaps and other anionic surfactants, with phenol and with chlorocresol List of excipients Lactose monohydrate, Cellulose microcrystalline, Magnesium stearate PHARMACEUTICAL PARTICULARS Local tolerance A study in rabbits showed the good vaginal tolerance of Dequalinium chloride vaginal tablets. No reproduction toxicity studies have been conducted with Dequalinium chloride vaginal tablets. However, developmental toxicity studies with quarternary ammonium compounds did not reveal evidence of embryofoetal toxicity. In view of the negligible vaginal absorption, there are no human pharmacokinetic data for dequalinium chloride available. Preclinical safety data Considering the minimal vaginal absorption of dequalinium chloride, no acute or chronic toxicity is to be expected. Overdose Application of more than 1 vaginal tablet will not increase the efficacy of Dequalinium chloride vaginal tablets. This will rather result in an increase of side effects. However, no severe side effects after using an overdose of Dequalinium chloride vaginal tablets have been reported. In the case of an overdose, a vaginal lavage should be performed to remove rest of the tablets. PHARMACOLOGICAL PROPERTIES Pharmacodynamic properties Pharmacotherapeutic group: Gynaecological anti-infective and antiseptic ATC code: G01A C05 Dequalinium chloride vaginal tablets contains dequalinium chloride, a quaternary ammonium compound with a broad antimicrobial spectrum against different Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria, fungi, and protozoa (Trichomonas vaginalis). The in vit ro activity of dequalinium chloride against the following vaginally important microorganisms was established and expressed as Minimum Inhibition Concentration (MIC). )l / gm ( CIMM IC (mg/l) Gram-positive bacteria Gram-negative bacteria Group B streptococci 2 – 8 Fusobacteria 32 – 64 Staphylococcus aureus 0.2 – 10 Gardnerella vaginalis 2.0 – 256 Group A streptococci 0.25 – 20 E. coli 1 – 400 Listeria sp. 4 – 32 Serratia sp. 3.1 – 400 Peptostreptococci 1 – 32 Klebsiella sp. 3.1 – 400 Group D streptococci 0.2 – 64 Pseudomonas sp. 5 – 400 Fungi Bacteroides Prevotella sp. 64 – 512 Candida tropicalis 0.2 – 50 Proteus sp. 20 - >1024 Candida albicans 0.2 – 200 Protozoa Candida glabrata 0.2 – 256 Trichomonas vaginalis28.8 – 400 Candida krusei 128 After dissolution of a Dequalinium chloride vaginal tablet (10 mg dequalinium chloride) in an estimated 2.5 to 5 ml of vaginal fluid, the dequalinium chloride concentration in the vaginal fluid is 4000 to 2000 mg/l, which is higher as the MIC 90 of all tested pathogenic microrganisms. Development of resistance of microorganisms to dequalinium chloride has not been reported. As for other surface-active compounds, the primary mode of action of dequalinium chloride is the enhancement of cell permeability and the subsequent loss of enzymatic activity, causing cell death. Dequalinium chloride in vaginal tablets exerts its action locally within the vagina. Marked relief of discharge and inflammation generally occurs within 24 to 72 hours. The efficacy of Dequalinium chloride vaginal tablets in the treatment of vaginal infections of various genesis has been shown by an active controlled, double-blind clinical study. Pharmacokinetic properties Preclinical data from rabbits indicate that dequalinium chloride is absorbed only to a very small amount after vaginal application. Distribution is observed into the liver, kidney, and lung. Dequalinium chloride seems to be metabolised to the 2,2’- dicarboxylic acid derivate and excreted in the non- conjugated form via faeces. sp. / Rottendorf Pharma GmbH Ostenfelder Strasse 51-61 59320 Ennigerloh Germany Fluomizin_PHILLIPINEN_PH_380852_148x210_Version5_110117.indd 2 11.01.17 11:33 Renewal of Authorization 16 September 2021 For suspected drug adverse reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. and to DKSH Market Expansion Services Philippines, Inc. Pharmacovigilance at pharmacovigilance.ph@dksh.com or hotline +63 9989654158. The patient should seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Nature and contents of container PVP/PE/PVDC Blister pack by 6's (Box of 6's) 380233 / 317482 Imported & Distributed by: DKSH Market Expansion Services Philippines, Inc. 3rd Floor, Science Hub Tower 2, Campus Avenue, McKinley Hill Cyberpark, Pinagsama, Taguig City, Metro Manila DATE OF REVISION OF THE TEXT January 2024 Reg. No.: DR-XY31774 Fluomizin_PHILLIPINEN_PH_380233_148x210_Version3_171221.indd 2Fluomizin_PHILLIPINEN_PH_380233_148x210_Version3_171221.indd 2 17.12.21 14:0817.12.21 14:08 [Page 3]",1,2,Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T20:13:22.156573+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY31781,Gliperide,Glimepiride,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1T2yVBgdldN2gJR-LHCvYLiufUz82d30D/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY31781_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1T2yVBgdldN2gJR-LHCvYLiufUz82d30D_view_usp_drivesdk_fda1f6db45.pdf,page_text/DR-XY31781_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1T2yVBgdldN2gJR-LHCvYLiufUz82d30D_view_usp_drivesdk_fda1f6db45.json,b60fd2aab303d5ad8f0db9faa388d8e4ce8c586fa0ddb3e7c3df7498450c77b7,171885,2,digital_text,"Glimepiride (Gliperide) 2mg tablet is a White to off-white tablet, round, biconvex, bisected on one side and plain on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Used in the Management of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus (DM).,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T20:13:25.483791+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY31819,Roximed,Roxithromycin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1OaUOCTWStRVdqvJbTIhnq9lUAhXuXL6v/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY31819_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OaUOCTWStRVdqvJbTIhnq9lUAhXuXL6v_view_usp_drivesdk_585f82fc86.pdf,page_text/DR-XY31819_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OaUOCTWStRVdqvJbTIhnq9lUAhXuXL6v_view_usp_drivesdk_585f82fc86.json,790bb84d4029fd19a44dd1e468fb9832cbae3ca1fa90ca7addd5ea0b42026986,133057,2,digital_text,"Roximed 150 film-coated tablet is a old-rose to dark-pink, film coated tablet, capsule-shaped, bisected on one side and plain on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Roxithromycin like erythromycin is used in the treatment of a wide variety of infections caused by susceptible organism. Its uses have included bronchitis, severe campylobacter enteritis, chancroid, diphtheria, legionnaire's disease and other Legionella infections, neonatal conjunctivitis, pertussis, pneumonia (as well as streptococcal), sinusitis and combined with neomycin, for the prophylaxis of surgical infection in patients undergoing bowel surgery.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T20:13:28.673005+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY31826,Sevoflurane,Sevorane,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1irI-06KREueff0RHNeA9zTGPjBBysaWy/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY31826_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1irI-06KREueff0RHNeA9zTGPjBBysaWy_view_usp_drivesdk_1a8fbb3cb7.pdf,page_text/DR-XY31826_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1irI-06KREueff0RHNeA9zTGPjBBysaWy_view_usp_drivesdk_1a8fbb3cb7.json,aba9dd5522c03e55a70431c1a483877c0450c8e2eeabed09258c06c9214bbb20,3698769,15,ocr,"Sevoflurane is a nonflammable liquid anesthetic agent administered by vaporization. It is a fluorinated derivative of methyl isopropyl ether. Sevoflurane is identified chemically as fluoromethyl 2, 2, 2-trifluoro-1- (trifluoromethyl) ethyl ether and has a molecular weight of 200.05. Sevoflurane has the following physical and chemical properties: Table 1. Physical And Chemical Properties of Sevoflurane Physical/Chemical Property Value Boiling Point at 760 mm Hg 58.6°C Specific Gravity at 20°C 1.520 - 1.525 Vapor pressure (calculated) in mm Hg* 157 mm Hg at 20°C 197 mm Hg at 25°C 317 mm Hg at 36°C Distribution Partition Coefficients at 37°C: Blood/Gas 0.63-0.69 Water/Gas 0.36 Olive Oil/Gas 47.2-53.9 Brain/Gas 1.15 “Equation for vapor pressure (calculated), mm Hg: Log,,.P vap =A+B/T, where: A = 8.086; B = -1726.68; T = °C+273.16°K (Kelvin) [Page 2] Table 2. Mean Component/Gas Partition Coefficients at 25°C for Polymers Used Commonly in Medical Applications: Polymer Mean Component/Gas Partition Coefficients at 25°C Conductive rubber | 14.0 Butyl rubber 7.7 Polyvinyl chloride 17.4 1.3 Polyethylene Sevoflurane is nonflammable and non-explosive as defined by the requirements of International Electrotechnical Commission 601-2-13. Sevoflurane is a clear, colorless, liquid. Sevoflurane is nonpungent. It is miscible with ethanol, ether, chloroform and petroleum benzene, and it is slightly soluble in water. Sevoflurane Degradation Sevoflurane is stable when stored under normal room lighting conditions. No discernible degradation of sevoflurane occurs in the presence of strong acids or heat. Sevoflurane is not corrosive to stainless steel, brass, aluminum, nickel-plated brass, chrome-plated brass, or copper beryllium alloy. Chemical degradation can occur upon exposure of inhaled anesthetics to CO9 absorbent within the anesthesia machine. When used as directed with fresh absorbents, degradation of sevoflurane is minimal, and degradants are undetectable or non-toxic. Sevoflurane degradation and subsequent degradant formation are enhanced by increasing absorbent temperature, desiccated CO absorbent (especially potassium hydroxide-containing), increased sevoflurane concentration and decreased fresh gas flow. Sevoflurane can undergo alkaline degradation by two pathways. The first results from the loss of hydrogen fluoride with the formation of pentafluoroisopropany! fluoromethy! ether (PIFE or more commonly known as Compound A). The second pathway for degradation of sevoflurane occurs only in the presence of desiccated CO9 absorbents and leads to the dissociation of sevoflurane into hexafluoroisopropanol (HFIP) and formaldehyde. HFIP is inactive, non-genotoxic, rapidly glucoronidated, cleared, and has toxicity comparable to sevoflurane. Formaldehyde is present during normal metabolic processes. Upon exposure to a highly desiccated absorbent, formaldehyde can further degrade into methanol and formate. Formate can contribute to the formation of carbon monoxide, in the presence of high temperature. Methanol can react with Compound A to form the methoxy addition product Compound B. Compound B can undergo further HF elimination to form Compounds C, D, and E. With highly desiccated absorbents, especially those containing potassium hydroxide, the formation of formaldehyde, methanol, carbon monoxide, Compound A and perhaps some of it’s degradants, Compounds B, C, and D may occur. [Page 3] Lewis Acid Degradation At least 300 ppm of water is added as a Lewis Acid inhibitor. No other additives or chemical stabilizers are utilized.",1,3,DESCRIPTION,Sevoflurane may be used for induction and maintenance of general anesthesia in adult and pediatric patients for inpatient and outpatient surgery.,3,3,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T21:17:44.771002+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY31855,Cefalexin (as Monohydrate),Lemaflex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1l6nw6xzXv-pOXsekc1_3TVaCWVpYjRUu/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY31855_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1l6nw6xzXv-pOXsekc1_3TVaCWVpYjRUu_view_usp_drivesdk_fa8b00ede9.pdf,page_text/DR-XY31855_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1l6nw6xzXv-pOXsekc1_3TVaCWVpYjRUu_view_usp_drivesdk_fa8b00ede9.json,313eb839f73596cf77adcc6b9434e847bec97b0429b24b7d5873e277a0b6a348,1738060,1,ocr,"**KLCA PRINTING PRESS WATERMARK LOGOS ARE NOT INCLUDED OR PART OF THE ARTWORK DESIGN** DIRECTIONS FOR RECONSTITUTION For 250 mg/5 mL Powder for Suspension and 125 mg/5 mL Powder for Suspension. |CEFALEXIN| ke the bottle to loosen the powder. To make a 60 mL reconstituted LEMAFLEX” suspension, mix thoroughly the contents with 43 mL water and shake well Until the powder is evenly suspended. Antibacterial For 100 mg/mL Powder for Suspension (Oral Drops Shake the bottle to loosen the powder. To make a 10 mL reconstituted (Cephalospo! ) suspension, mix thoroughly the contents with 7.0 mL water and shake well 500 mg Capsule until the powder is evenly suspended. 250 mg/5 mL Powder for Suspension The reconstituted suspension is stable for 7 days at temperatures not exceeding 30°C and 14 days when refrigerated (2°C - 8°C). Shake well 125 mg/5 mL Powder for Suspension before use. 100 mg/mL Powder for Suspension (Oral Drops)",1,1,DESCRIPTION: GO ML INSERT (FOR NOTIFICATION),"eee pioerpeet cystine ocd pte with Treatment of infections caused by side-chain, including in respiratory tract, urinary tract, gynecologic obstetric, skin, soft tissue and bone infections, gonorrhea, syphilis and dental ctive : cefamandole against strains of Staphylococcus aureus that are insensitive to Penicillin + cefmenoxime and against the majority ofAmpicillin resistant E. coli + cefmetazole + cefonicid PHARMACOKINETICS * cefoperazone + ceforanide Cefalexin is almost completely absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract and produces a peak plasma concentration of about 18 micrograms/mL 1 hour + cefotetan after a 500- mg oral dose. If cefalexin is taken with food, absorption may be * cefpiramide + latamoxef. delayed, but the total amount absorbed is not appreciably altered. Up to 15% of a dose is bound to plasma proteins. The plasma half-life is about 1 hour; INTERACTIONS it increases with reduced renal function. Cefalexin is widely distributed in the body but does not enter the CSF in significant quantities. It crosses the The renal excretion of cefalexin, and many other cephalosporins, is delayed placenta and small quantities are found in breast milk. Cefalexin is not by probenecid. metabolised. About /% or more of a dose is excreted unchanged in the OVERDOSAGE AND TREATMENT urine in the first 6 hours by glomerular filtration and tubular secretion; urinary concentrations greater than 1 mg/mL have been achieved after a dose of Overdosage: Symptoms of oral overdose may include nausea, vomiting, 500 mg. Probenecid delays urinary excretion. Therapeutically effective epigastric distress, diarrhea and haematuri concentrations may be found in the bile and some may be excreted by this Treatment: General management consist of close, clinical and laboratory route. Cefalexin is removed by haemodialysis and peritoneal dialysis monitoring of haematological, renal and hepatic functions and coagulation",1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T21:22:01.230355+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY31926,,,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vmLJhlILAYGoMmkHJ0egRcsWweJVddjo/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY31926_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vmLJhlILAYGoMmkHJ0egRcsWweJVddjo_view_usp_drivesdk_ca26c2d866.pdf,page_text/DR-XY31926_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vmLJhlILAYGoMmkHJ0egRcsWweJVddjo_view_usp_drivesdk_ca26c2d866.json,08933d7f227f87aa38c4224cb527d1c8ffda4abe964d925d1c4e5370d9c175b5,331094,2,digital_text,,,,,"Treatment-resistant schizophrenia Clozapine is indicated in treatment -resistant schizophrenic patients and in schizophrenia patients who have severe, untreatable neurological adverse reactions to other antipsychotic agents, including atypical antipsychotics. Treatment resistance is defined as a lack of satisfactory clinical improvement despite the use of adequate doses of at least two different antipsychotic agents, including an atypical antipsychotic agent, prescribed for adequate duration. Psychosis during the course of Parkinson's disease Clozapine is also indicated in psychotic disorders occurring during the course of Parkinson's disease, in cases where standard treatment has failed.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T21:22:04.361605+00:00
