PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32026,INDAPAMIDE,VAZAMIDE SR,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1o8hcNl8-Asu1G5oJDq4T1VBViPAEFS9z/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32026_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1o8hcNl8-Asu1G5oJDq4T1VBViPAEFS9z_view_usp_drivesdk_19b9a7b5e0.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32026_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1o8hcNl8-Asu1G5oJDq4T1VBViPAEFS9z_view_usp_drivesdk_19b9a7b5e0.json,c7af3b0f9618bc3b1d8be55476dacc6d430e46cd83d9869fb5f770e558960b16,349547,1,digital_text,Indapamide (Vazamide SR) 1.5mg Sustained-Release Tablet is a white to off white round biconvex film coated tablet.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Indapamide is indicated in the management of mild to moderate hypertension and also for edema, including that associated with heart failure.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T21:22:35.211448+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32027,Piperacillin (As Sodium) + Tazobactam (As Sodium),Vigocid,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1H-Kg3rJulDVkuhI2aCG7MewPCKVd-xfq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32027_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1H-Kg3rJulDVkuhI2aCG7MewPCKVd-xfq_view_usp_drivesdk_c8da065bdc.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32027_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1H-Kg3rJulDVkuhI2aCG7MewPCKVd-xfq_view_usp_drivesdk_c8da065bdc.json,d69a4bce28fc2cb9e48822feba9831e7ec3e60ccb0ffbb6cb8e6351bebfd510c,667755,2,digital_text,"Piperacillin/Tazobactam are antibacterial combination for intravenous administration which consists of semi synthetic antibiotic piperacillin and a β-lactamase inhibitor tazobactam. Piperacillin/Tazobactam (Vigocid) parenteral combination is a white powder consisting of piperacillin and tazobactam as their sodium salts. Piperacillin/Tazobactam (Vigocid) 4 g/500 mg Lyophilized Sterile Powder for Injection is a white to oﬀ-white powder, supplied in a Type III clear and colorless glass vial with rubber stopper and silver aluminum seal. Chemical formula : C H N NaO S23 26 5 7 Chemical structure : Chemical name : sodium (2S, 5R, 6R)-6-[(R)-2-(4-ethyl-2,3-dioxo-1-piperazine- carboxamido)-2-phenylacetamido]-3,3-dimethyl-7-oxo-4-thia-1- Piperacillin/Tazobactam (Vigocid) 2 g/250 mg Lyophilized Sterile Powder for Injection is a white to oﬀ-white powder, supplied in a Type III clear and colorless glass vial with rubber stopper and green aluminum seal. Tazobactam (as sodium) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 500 mg CHARACTERISTICS Piperacillin is a ureidopenicillin, derived from D(-)-α-aminobenzyl-penicillin. Molecular weight : 539.54 Piperacillin is bactericidal in action by inhibiting septum formulation and cell wall synthesis of susceptible bacteria. In vitro, piperacillin is active against a variety of gram-positive and gram-negative aerobic and anaerobic bacteria with an extended spectrum of activity against gram-negative bacteria. Its spectrum of activity is widened by administration with the beta-lactamase inhibitor tazobactam. Tazobactam has the potential to extend the spectrum of activity of beta-lactam antibiotics against beta-lactamase-producing bacteria. It has little clinically relevant in vitro activity against bacteria due to its reduced aﬃnity to penicillin-binding proteins. PHARMACODYNAMICS Clostridia spp. (C. diﬃcile, C. perfringens) Gram-positive anaerobes Enterococci (E. faecalis, E. faecium) Nocardia spp. Piperacillin/Tazobactam has been shown to be active against most strains of the following microorganisms: Staphylococcus aureus (excluding methicillin and oxacillin-resistant isolates) Staphylococcus (S. Pneumoniae, S. pyogenes, S. bovis, S. agalactiae, viridans group streptococci) Listeria monocytogenes Corynebacteria Gram-positive aerobes Peptostreptococcus spp. Gram-negative aerobes Neisseria gonorrhea Citrobacter spp. Eubacterium group Enterobacter spp. Gardnerella vaginalis Escherichia coli Actinomyces spp. Neisseria meningitidis Moraxella catarrhalis Klebsiella spp. Chemical structure : ylmethyl)-4-thia-1-azabicyclo[3.2.0]heptane-2-carboxylate-4,4- Tazobactam is a penicillanic acid sulphone derivative Chemical name : sodium (2S,3S, 5R)-3-methyl-7-oxo-3-(1H-1,2,3-triazol-1- dioxide Chemical formula : C H N NaO S10 11 4 5 Molecular weight : 322.3 • Biliary tract infections (cholangitis) • Skin infections (burns, ecthyma gangrenosum, ulceration) • Immunocompromised patients (neutropenic patients) in combination with an aminoglycoside Piperacillin/Tazobactam (Vigocid) is indicated for the treatment of infections caused by Pseudomonas aeruginosa, and also infections due to other susceptible bacteria: • Gynecological infections including postpartum endometritis and pelvic inﬂammatory disease (PID) • Lower respiratory tract infections (cystic ﬁbrosis) • Bone and joint infections • Septicemia Metabolism Distribution Piperacillin is metabolized to a minor microbiologically active desethyl metabolite. T azobactam is metabolized to a single metabolite that lacks pharmacological and antibacterial activities. Excretion Piperacillin and tazobactam are widely distributed in body tissues and ﬂuids. There is little diﬀusion into the CSF except when the meninges are inﬂamed. Both piperacillin and tazobactam are eliminated via the kidney by glomerular ﬁltration and tubular secretion. About 60 to 80% of dose is excreted unchanged in the urine within 24 hours, achieving high concentrations. Piperacillin and tazobactam are also secreted into the bile, high concentrations are also found and about 20% of a dose may be excreted by this route. Plasma concentrations are enhanced if probenecid is administered concomitantly. Piperacillin and tazobactam are removed by hemodialysis.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"• Upper respiratory tract infections (otitis media) • Surgical infection prophylaxis • Urinary tract infection • Intra-abdominal infections (peritonitis) Piperacillin/Tazobactam (Vigocid) is commonly given with an aminoglycoside for the treatment of serious infections, they should be administered separately because of possible incompatibility. For mild or uncomplicated infections: Piperacillin/Tazobactam (Vigocid) is given intravenously in a ratio of piperacillin (as the sodium salt) 8 parts to 1 part of tazobactam (as the sodium salt). May be administered by slow intravenous injection over 3 to 5 minutes by intravenous infusion over 20 to 40 minutes. Doses should generally be reduced in moderate to severe renal impairment. For the treatment of serious or complicated infections: In life - threatening infections particularly caused by Klebsiella spp. or Pseudomonas: Prophylaxis of infection during surgery:",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T21:22:38.772073+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY321,Sodiumcitrate+Dextromethorphan+Chlorphenamine Maleate,Pleuragex-DM,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WeyQX5jw6R_H56EWTjkigl3eldKQiow7/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY321_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WeyQX5jw6R_H56EWTjkigl3eldKQiow7_view_usp_drivesdk_f74ffdcdf6.pdf,page_text/DR-XY321_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WeyQX5jw6R_H56EWTjkigl3eldKQiow7_view_usp_drivesdk_f74ffdcdf6.json,15a1ff30139bc1081116771d17a317581ed7eadb03f9a9fd2fe0eb8dda411d8c,1180794,1,digital_text,,1,1,prescriptron.,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-29T21:22:42.187156+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32202,Dexmedetomidine (as hydrochloride),Precedex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/10VWErx791x5DgXSPy3mwmXWx3ssuKokf/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32202_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_10VWErx791x5DgXSPy3mwmXWx3ssuKokf_view_usp_drivesdk_48e5b85983.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32202_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_10VWErx791x5DgXSPy3mwmXWx3ssuKokf_view_usp_drivesdk_48e5b85983.json,b8e17757ffec7c205264cdd252993f78065df19e696422243cfe3c59f150432e,223588,23,digital_text,"Dexmedetomidine (Precedex) Concentrate for Intravenous Infusion is a sterile, nonpyrogenic solution suitable for intravenous infusion following dilution. Dexmedetomidine in 0.9% Sodium Chloride (Precedex Premix) Solution for Intravenous Infusion is a sterile, nonpyrogenic ready to use solution suitable for intravenous infusion. Dexmedetomidine hydrochloride is a central alpha2-adrenergic agonist. Dexmedetomidine is the S-enantiomer of medetomidine. Dexmedetomidine hydrochloride chemical name is 1H-Imidazole, 4-[1-(2,3- dimethylphenyl)ethyl]-, monohydrochloride, (S). Dexmedetomidine has a molecular weight of 236.7 and the empirical formula is C13H16N2•HCl and the structural",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"ICU Sedation Dexmedetomidine is indicated for sedation of initially intubated and mechanically ventilated patients during treatment in an intensive care setting. Dexmedetomidine should be administered by continuous infusion not to exceed 24 hours. Dexmedetomidine has been continuously infused in mechanically ventilated patients prior to extubation, during extubation, and post-extubation. It i s not necessary t o discontinue dexmedetomidine prior to extubation. Procedural Sedation Dexmedetomidine is indicated for sedation/anxiolysis of non-intubated patients prior to and/or during surgical and other procedures.",2,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T21:55:11.627455+00:00
