ns • Septicemia Metabolism Distribution Piperacillin is metabolized to a minor microbiologically active desethyl metabolite. T azobactam is metabolized to a single metabolite that lacks pharmacological and antibacterial activities. Excretion Piperacillin and tazobactam are widely distributed in body tissues and ﬂuids. There is little diﬀusion into the CSF except when the meninges are inﬂamed. Both piperacillin and tazobactam are eliminated via the kidney by glomerular ﬁltration and tubular secretion. About 60 to 80% of dose is excreted unchanged in the urine within 24 hours, achieving high concentrations. Piperacillin and tazobactam are also secreted into the bile, high concentrations are also found and about 20% of a dose may be excreted by this route. Plasma concentrations are enhanced if probenecid is administered concomitantly. Piperacillin and tazobactam are removed by hemodialysis.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"• Upper respiratory tract infections (otitis media) • Surgical infection prophylaxis • Urinary tract infection • Intra-abdominal infections (peritonitis) Piperacillin/Tazobactam (Vigocid) is commonly given with an aminoglycoside for the treatment of serious infections, they should be administered separately because of possible incompatibility. For mild or uncomplicated infections: Piperacillin/Tazobactam (Vigocid) is given intravenously in a ratio of piperacillin (as the sodium salt) 8 parts to 1 part of tazobactam (as the sodium salt). May be administered by slow intravenous injection over 3 to 5 minutes by intravenous infusion over 20 to 40 minutes. Doses should generally be reduced in moderate to severe renal impairment. For the treatment of serious or complicated infections: In life - threatening infections particularly caused by Klebsiella spp. or Pseudomonas: Prophylaxis of infection during surgery:",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T21:55:14.867609+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32292,Nepafenac,Nevanac,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1o_rMoP-Jy8RyeKKOc1HoKa0Tp_MyIRQq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32292_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1o_rMoP-Jy8RyeKKOc1HoKa0Tp_MyIRQq_view_usp_drivesdk_75e872c95b.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32292_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1o_rMoP-Jy8RyeKKOc1HoKa0Tp_MyIRQq_view_usp_drivesdk_75e872c95b.json,629d1c99c5a39b4dfb38f2f3ef3b1e028e1e22b389133f93863c86cf83932680,205438,7,digital_text,"Nepafenac (Nevanac ®) Sterile Ophthalmic Suspension 0.1% is a sterile, topical, non- steroidal anti - inflammatory (NSAID) prodrug for ophthalmic use. Each mL of nepafenac (Nevanac ®) Sterile Ophthalmic Suspension contains 1 mg of nepafenac. Nepafenac is designated chemically as 2- amino-3- benzoylbenezenacetamide with an empirical formul a of C15H14N2O2. The structural formula of nepafenac is: Nepafenac is a yellow crystalline powder. The molecular weight of nepafenac is 254.28. Nepafenac (Nevanac ®) Sterile Ophthalmic Suspension is supplied as a sterile, aqueous 0.1% suspension with a pH approximately of 7.4. The osmolality of n epafenac (Nevanac ®) Sterile Ophthalmic Suspension is approximately 305 mOsmol/kg.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,Nepafenac (Nevanac ®) Sterile Ophthalmic Suspension is indicated for the treatment of pain and inflammation associated with cataract surgery.,3,3,INDICATIONS AND USAGE:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T21:55:18.179366+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32295,Co-Amoxiclav,Augmentin Es,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1myaZszGG1_FbB4jejyCoStXLsTSPfYIl/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32295_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1myaZszGG1_FbB4jejyCoStXLsTSPfYIl_view_usp_drivesdk_41ba6b6eea.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32295_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1myaZszGG1_FbB4jejyCoStXLsTSPfYIl_view_usp_drivesdk_41ba6b6eea.json,4caf5e475eed276b5220b2ca11c13d850edf0b6d065709295454b4fb302db3bd,578366,8,digital_text,,,,,"Amoxicillin-clavulanate should be used in accordance with local official antibiotic-prescribing guidelines and local susceptibility data.  Adult formulations Co-amoxiclav is indicated for short term treatment of bacterial infections at the following sites when caused by amoxicillin-clavulanate-susceptible organisms: - Upper respiratory tract infections (including ENT) e.g. recurrent tonsillitis, sinusitis, otitis media, typically caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae, Haemophilus influenzae#, Moraxella catarrhalis# and Streptococcus pyogenes. - Lower respiratory tract infections e.g. acute exacerbations of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (AEOCPD)/acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis (AECB), lobar and bronchopneumonia, typically caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae, Haemophilus influenzae# and Moraxella catarrhalis#. - Genito-urinary tract infections e.g. cystitis, urethritis, pyelonephritis, female genital infections typically caused by Enterobacteriaceae* (mainly Escherichia coli#), Staphylococcus saprophyticus and Enterococcus species and gonorrhoea caused by Neisseria gonorrhoeae#. - Skin and soft tissue infections typically caused by Staphylococcus aureus#, Streptococcus pyogenes and Bacteroides species#. - Bone and joint infections e.g. osteomyelitis typically caused by Staphylococcus aureus#, where more prolonged therapy may be appropriate. - Dental infections e.g. dentoalveolar abscess - Other Infections e.g. septic abortion, puerperal sepsis, intra-abdominal sepsis.  Paediatric formulations Co-amoxiclav is indicated for short term treatment of bacterial infections at the following sites when caused by amoxicillin-clavulanate sensitive organisms: - Upper respiratory tract infections (including ENT) e.g. recurrent tonsillitis, sinusitis, otitis media typically caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae, Haemophilus influenzae#, Moraxella catarrhalis# and Streptococcus pyogenes. - Lower respiratory tract infections e.g. acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis, lobar and bronchopneumonia typically caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae, Haemophilus influenzae# and Moraxella catarrhalis#. - Genito-urinary tract infections e.g. cystitis, urethritis, pyelonephritis, female genital infections typically caused by Enterobacteriaceae# (mainly Escherichia coli#) Staphylococcus saprophyticus and Enterococcus species, and gonorrhoea caused by Neisseria gonorrhoeae#. - Skin and soft tissue infections typically caused by Staphylococcus aureus#, Streptococcus pyogenes and Bacteroides species#. Amoxicillin-clavulanate Paediatric three times daily The paediatric three times daily dosing regimen is also indicated for the following infections: - Bone and joint infections e.g. osteomyelitis typically caused by Staphylococcus aureus#, where more prolonged therapy may be appropriate. - Other infections e.g. septic abortion, puerperal sepsis, intra-abdominal sepsis. [Page 4]  All formulations #Some members of these species of bacteria produce beta-lactamase, rendering them insensitive to amoxicillin alone. (see Clinical Pharmacology, Pharmacodynamic effects for further information). Susceptibility to amoxicillin-clavulanate will vary with geography and time. Local susceptibility data should be consulted where available, and microbiological sampling and susceptibility testing performed where necessary. Infections caused by amoxicillin-susceptible organisms are amenable to co-amoxiclav treatment due to its amoxicillin content. Mixed infections caused by amoxicillin-susceptible organisms in conjunction with amoxicillin-clavulanate- susceptible beta-lactamase-producing organisms may therefore be treated by co-amoxiclav.",3,4,INDICATIONS,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T21:55:21.472175+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32295,Co-Amoxiclav,Augmentin Es,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1opqmFwWdQIG4q_euH3-CzVXmmmLnmXAe/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32295_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1opqmFwWdQIG4q_euH3-CzVXmmmLnmXAe_view_usp_drivesdk_259f1c442b.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32295_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1opqmFwWdQIG4q_euH3-CzVXmmmLnmXAe_view_usp_drivesdk_259f1c442b.json,15637e1d5d54559e002f6dee096c2ccb476d6e0d8cc7adeb1014ea8d86171a7d,247572,6,digital_text,"Co-amoxiclav (Augmentin ES) 642.9mg/5mL Powder for Suspension: Bottles of off-white powder which, when reconstituted, yields an off-white to tan coloured, strawberry flavoured suspension. Each 5mL of reconstituted suspension contains 600mg amoxicillin and 42.9mg clavulanic acid. The amoxicillin is present as amoxicillin trihydrate and the clavulanic acid is present as potassium clavulanate in a ratio of 14:1.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Co-amoxiclav (Augmentin) should be used in accordance with local official antibiotic-prescribing guidelines and local susceptibility data. Co-amoxiclav (Augmentin ES) is indicated for short-term treatment of bacterial infections in paediatric patients at the following sites when caused by Co-amoxiclav (Augmentin) -susceptible organisms: Upper respiratory tract infections (including ENT) e.g. Acute otitis media (AOM), persistent AOM, or recurrent AOM, typically caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae*, Haemophilus influenzae# and Moraxella catarrhalis#. Tonsillo-pharyngitis and sinusitis, typically caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae*, Haemophilus influenzae#, Moraxella catarrhalis# and Streptococcus pyogenes. Lower respiratory tract infections e.g. lobar and bronchopneumonia typically caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae*, Haemophilus influenzae# and Moraxella catarrhalis#. Skin and soft tissue infections typically caused by Staphylococcus aureus# and Streptococcus pyogenes. *Penicillin minimum inhibitory concentration (MIC) less than or equal to 4 micrograms/mL. [Page 3] #Some members of these species of bacteria produce beta-lactamase, rendering them insensitive to amoxicillin alone (see Pharmacological Properties, Pharmacodynamics for further information). Susceptibility to Co-amoxiclav (Augmentin) will vary with geography and time. Local susceptibility data should be consulted where available, and microbiological sampling and susceptibility testing performed where necessary.",2,3,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T22:43:36.084948+00:00
