PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32444,Deferasirox,Exjade,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1z972Ourtml5fZeCfMJS6eJ-TtnGXo950/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32444_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1z972Ourtml5fZeCfMJS6eJ-TtnGXo950_view_usp_drivesdk_4c14971d7a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32444_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1z972Ourtml5fZeCfMJS6eJ-TtnGXo950_view_usp_drivesdk_4c14971d7a.json,26ca283430ac2b2a80ab66b4bfb2700aa98517325e357eaa2afe2c646d57899b,449778,24,digital_text,Pharmaceutical form(s) Dispersible tablets. Active substance(s) Each dispersible tablet contains 125 mg / 250 mg deferasirox as active substance. Certain dosage strengths may not be available in all countries. Excipients Lactose monohydrate; crospovidone; microcrystalline cellulose; povidone (K30); s odium lauryl sulphate; silicon dioxide; magnesium stearate,1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,Deferasirox (Exjade ®) is i ndicated for the treatment of chronic iron overload due to blood transfusions (transfusional hemosiderosis) in adult and pediatric patients (aged 2 years and over). Deferasirox (Exjade®) is also indicated for the treatment of chronic iron overload in patie nts with non-transfusion-dependent thalassemia syndromes aged 10 years and older.,1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T23:16:06.616996+00:00
