PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32448,Everolimus,Certican,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oTS862Kmq0mvgU7lMAx9kPBvkqoiMKP5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32448_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oTS862Kmq0mvgU7lMAx9kPBvkqoiMKP5_view_usp_drivesdk_0c0b3efe70.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32448_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oTS862Kmq0mvgU7lMAx9kPBvkqoiMKP5_view_usp_drivesdk_0c0b3efe70.json,d9361ac78c494139aaed77320f6f7949285639148f452b50e5ea36b21b918484,569227,31,digital_text,"Pharmaceutical forms White to yellowish tablets, marbled, round, flat with a bevelled edge. Active substance Each tablet contains 250 mcg or 500 mcg everolimus. Certain dosage strengths and dosage forms may not be available in all countries. Active moiety Everolimus Excipients Butylated hydroxytoluene (E321), magnesium stearate, lactose monohydrate, hypromellose, crospovidone, lactose anhydrous. Pharmaceutical formulations may vary between countries.",1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,"Kidney and heart transplantation Everolimus (Certican ®) is indicated for the prophylaxis of organ rejection in adult patients at low to moderate immunological risk receiving an allogeneic rena l or cardiac transplant. In kidney and heart transplantation, everolimus (Certican ®) should be used in combination with ciclosporin for microemulsion and corticosteroids. Liver transplantation Everolimus (Certican ®) is indicated for the prophylaxis of orga n rejection in adult patients receiving a hepatic transplant. In liver transplantation, everolimus (Certican ®) should be used in combination with tacrolimus and corticosteroids.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T23:16:13.735604+00:00
