Glaucoma (increased eye pressure) (dizziness) due to motion sickness. - Breathing problem such as asthma, chronic pulmonary disease, emphysema HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? (excessive air in the lungs), or chronic bronchitis - Anenlarged prostate gland or difficulty in urinating This medicine should be taken orally (by mouth), once a day, one hour before travel starts. ¢ If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, consult a doctor before use. Dose may be repeated every 24 hours if necessary. * If symptoms do not improve or new symptoms appear. Tablets may be chewed then swallowed without water or swallowed whole with water. For suspected adverse drug reaction, seek medical attention immediately and Age Group Recommended Dose: report to the FDA at www.fda.gov.ph AND Unilab at (+632) 858-1000 or to be given once a day, one hour before travel Adults and children: productsafety@unilab.com.ph. By reporting undesirable effects, you can help 1 to 2 tablets provide more information on the safety of this medicine. 12 years and older 6 to 12 years Ye tablet AVAILABILITY Or, as prescribed by a doctor. Box of 100 (in blister strip x 10's) WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? DATE OF REVISION OF PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET (PIL): June 2018 ¢ If you are allergic to Meclizine or any ingredient in this product DATE OF FIRST AUTHORIZATION: 05 October 2007 « Ifyou need to perform activities requiring mental alertness or physical coordination (e.g., operating a machine or driving a motor vehicle) since drowsiness may occur with use of Meclizine hydrochloride Manufactured by Amherst Laboratories, Inc. ¢ If you are pregnant or breastfeeding UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS UNILAB Pharma Campus, Barangay Mamplasan, Bifian, Laguna, Philippines for UNILAB, Inc. Drowsiness, fatigue, dry mouth, constipation, headache, stomach upset, and rarely, blurred No. 66 United Street, Mandaluyong City, Metro Manila, Philippines vision have been reported with the use of Meclizine. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Medicines that depress the nervous system, barbiturates (e.g., Phenobarbital), tranquilizers (e.g., Diazepam), and alcohol should not be taken together with Meclizine P300000021908 DR-XY32470 Reg.IPOPHIL because of the potential for increased toxicity Trusted Quality Healthcare L FRONT BACK P 072 [Page 2]",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T16:16:26.576154+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32479,Lactobacillus Acidophilus + Estriol,Gynoflor,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1h3Wr-b3GtcvdD24eMiKHoxBnHbO0Fqfi/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32479_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1h3Wr-b3GtcvdD24eMiKHoxBnHbO0Fqfi_view_usp_drivesdk_d66a6618d8.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32479_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1h3Wr-b3GtcvdD24eMiKHoxBnHbO0Fqfi_view_usp_drivesdk_d66a6618d8.json,f2404d12104215142837ca5e308d7ef2a4d9cef4c4add3f28abcbf03d0b7c80c,235197,2,digital_text,"Vaginal tablets The vaginal tablets are slightly beige, spotted, oval and biconvex. CLINICAL PARTICULARS Therapeutic indications • restoration of the Lactobacillus flora after local and/or sys - temic treatment with anti-infective or chemotherapeutic agents; • atrophic vaginitis due to estrogen deficiency during meno - pause and post-menopause, or as co-medication to syste - mic hormone replacement therapy; • vaginal discharge of unknown origin or mild to intermediate cases of bacterial vaginosis and candidiasis, where use of anti-infective therapy is not absolutelynecessary. Posology and method of administration Restoration therapy, vaginal discharge of unknown origin, mild tointermediate vaginal infections: 1 – 2 vaginal tablets daily for 6 – 12 days. The vaginal tablets should be inserted deeply into the vagina in the evenings before retiring. This is best performed in a recli - ning position with the legs slightlybent. Treatment should be interrupted during menstruation and re - sumed afterwards. Atrophic vaginitis: In cases of atrophic vaginitis, a dose of 1 vaginal tablet daily is recommended for 6 – 12 days, followed by a maintenance dose of 1 vaginal tablet at 1 – 2 days per week. Instructions for use / handling Lactobacillus acidophilus + Estriol vaginal tablet contains ex - cipients which do not dissolve completely, such that remains of the tablet are occasionally found in the panties. This is of no importance for the efficacy of Lactobacillus acidophilus + Estriol vaginaltablets. In rare cases of a very dry vagina, it is possible that the vaginal tablet does not dissolve and is discharged by the vagina as intact tablet. As consequence, the treatment is not optimal. However, this is not harmful to the vagina. For prevention, the vaginal tablet can be moistened with a drop of water before insertion into a very dry vagina. Patients should use a sanitary towel or panty liner. Patients should not use vaginal douches or rinses during treat- ment with Lactobacillus acidophilus + Estriol vaginal tablets.",1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"• restoration of the Lactobacillus flora after local and/or sys - temic treatment with anti-infective or chemotherapeutic agents; • atrophic vaginitis due to estrogen deficiency during meno - pause and post-menopause, or as co-medication to syste - mic hormone replacement therapy; • vaginal discharge of unknown origin or mild to intermediate cases of bacterial vaginosis and candidiasis, where use of anti-infective therapy is not absolutelynecessary.",1,1,Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T00:24:17.312893+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32505,Pregabalin,Lyrica,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/14QroJS5bVK3egTdS-zeRI3Ls857j6S0f/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32505_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14QroJS5bVK3egTdS-zeRI3Ls857j6S0f_view_usp_drivesdk_28e30b390a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32505_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14QroJS5bVK3egTdS-zeRI3Ls857j6S0f_view_usp_drivesdk_28e30b390a.json,d72cc9073d8697d190729b81a4cdfd8a82d029c2cfb2c481f379a0b9ac89becb,115631,2,digital_text,"Component Type Superseded Afﬁliate Item Code TrackWise/GLAMS Job No. MA No. Superseded Supplier Code Sign-offs Afﬁliate Item Code 3D Render IDNew Supplier Code Supplier SAP No. Packing Site/Printer Keyline/Drawing No. Lyrica_50mg_75mg_150mg_56_PP LYRICA 25/50/75/150mg PH Leaflet 400564714;400564221; 400564222 109762935/0020 1 Philippines N/A N/A Helvetica Neue LT W1G 6 pt 6 pt180 x 420 mm 003000009449_3_420x180mm_horizontal_v1_FVID1449922 1 1 of 2 3380426 N/A 3380426 DRP-6121|DRP- 6119|DRP-6120 N/A PAA220855 PAA191455 Pfizer Manufacturing Freiburg (Freiburg - DE) 29 Jan 24 19:00 Keyline DataMatrix 1944 PMS 541 PREGABALIN L YRICA™ 25 mg, 50 mg, 75 mg, 150 mg Capsule 1.0 PHARMACOLOGIC CATEGORY Anti-epileptic 2.0 DESCRIPTION Pregabalin is a gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA) analogue (S)-3-(aminomethyl)- 5-methylhexanoic acid) with an empirical formula of C 8H17NO2 and molecular weight of 159.23. The molecular structure of pregabalin is:",1,1,Description,"Neuropathic Pain Pregabalin is indicated for the treatment of neuropathic pain in adults, including neuropathic pain associated with spinal cord injury. Epilepsy Pregabalin is indicated as adjunctive therapy in adults with partial seizures, with or without secondary generalization. Generalized Anxiety Disorder Pregabalin is indicated for the treatment of Generalized Anxiety Disorder (GAD) in adults. Fibromyalgia Pregabalin is indicated for the management of fibromyalgia.",1,1,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T00:24:20.655868+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32516,Cefradine (as Monohydrate),Solphride,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1I-mHZTBitIs8f6vugRwHNV38r9isrLvL/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32516_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1I-mHZTBitIs8f6vugRwHNV38r9isrLvL_view_usp_drivesdk_be8c9375d0.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32516_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1I-mHZTBitIs8f6vugRwHNV38r9isrLvL_view_usp_drivesdk_be8c9375d0.json,d6b0c88bded915a1820fd0a656a5b63797295ce0ca533d5674336dbf2bd7f823,425601,1,digital_text,Cefradine (Solphride) is a white to off-white to pinkish white powder. CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"It is used in the treatment of susceptible infections caused by strains of Staphylococci, Streptococci, Streptococcus pneumonia, Haemophilus influenza, Eschirichia coli, Proteus mirabilis, Klebsiella sp. Streptococci including those of the biliary, respiratory and urinary tract and of the skin. For severe infections, treatment with parenteral cephalosporins is to be preferred.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T00:24:23.513363+00:00
