dverse changes in plasma lipids have also been noted but their clinical partly due to a reduction in peripheral resistance; they also enhance the effects of other significance is unclear. antihypertensives. Signs of electrolyte imbalance include dry mouth, thirst, weakness, lethargy, drowsiness, restlessness, muscle pain and cramps, seizures, oliguria, hypotension, and gastrointestinal disturbances. Hydrochlorothiazide is a diuretic and antihypertensive. It is the 3,4-dihydro derivative of chlorothiazide. Other side effects include anorexia, gastric irritation, nausea, vomiting, constipation, diarrhea, its chemical name is 6-chloro-3,4-dihydro-2H-1,2,4 benzothiadiazine-7-sulfonamide 1,1 dioxide. Its sialadenitis, headache, dizziness, photosensitivity reactions, orthostatic hypotension, paraesthesia, empirical formula is C;HgCIN30,S>. impotence, and yellow vision. Hypersensitivity reactions include skin rashes, fever, pulmonary edema, Hydrochlorothiazide is fairly rapidly absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract. It is reported to have a pneumonitis, anaphylaxis, and toxic epidermal necrolysis. Cholestatic jaundice, pancreatitis, and blood bioavailability of about 65% to 70%. It has been estimated to have a plasma half-life of between about dyscrasias including thrombocytopenia, and more rarely, granulocytopenia, leucopenia, and aplastic 5 and 15 hours and appears to be preferentially bound to red blood cells. It is excreted mainly and haemolytic anemia have been reported. unchanged in the urine. Hydrochlorothiazide crosses the placental barrier and is distributed into breast milk.",1,1,DESCRIPTION AND PHARMACOKINETICS:,"(hypokalemia, hypochloremia, hyponatremia) and dehydration resulting from excessive diuresis. Hydrochlorothiazide is used in the treatment of edema associated with heart failure and with renal and In massive overdosage, treatment should be symptomatic and directed at fluid and electrolyte hepatic disorders. It is also used in the treatment of hypertension, either alone or together with other replacement. Use of activated charcoal should be considered if the patient presents within 1 hour of antihypertensives such as ACE inhibitors and beta blockers. ingestion. Hydrochlorothiazide is also indicated in the treatment of edema accompanying premenstrual syndrome, prevention of water retention associated with corticosteroids and estrogens, treatment of diabetes",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T00:24:37.329558+00:00
