Tazobactam (As Sodium)""",Piptaz,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1EG-LqR4wk_JIpKpPG9QNBGcPmr2Dl5OS/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32669_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1EG-LqR4wk_JIpKpPG9QNBGcPmr2Dl5OS_view_usp_drivesdk_179eaa7edb.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32669_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1EG-LqR4wk_JIpKpPG9QNBGcPmr2Dl5OS_view_usp_drivesdk_179eaa7edb.json,8e0edb8e45cf04373daa741e93f3afb1166917e5d2b93dd669abb63d0df96c5e,7476079,2,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T00:40:21.370013+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32673,Clopidogrel (as bisulfate),Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qFD0ijbrzN4IwRbS7lOsBBeaL8x5DERb/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32673_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qFD0ijbrzN4IwRbS7lOsBBeaL8x5DERb_view_usp_drivesdk_67c2aef65b.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32673_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qFD0ijbrzN4IwRbS7lOsBBeaL8x5DERb_view_usp_drivesdk_67c2aef65b.json,9cae71fc9ba8862a8cdf3ca2dea92022c7455d53804bc0c83655839ef5f05e80,347698,11,digital_text,,,,,"Clopidogrel is indicated in adults for the secondary prevention of atherothrombotic events in: Recent MI, Recent Stroke or Established Peripheral Arterial Disease For patients with a history of recent myocardial infarction (MI), recent stroke, or established peripheral arterial disease, clopidogrel has been shown to reduce the rate of a combined endpoint of new ischemic stroke (fatal or not), new MI (fatal or not), and other vascular death. Acute Coronary Syndrome - For patients with non -ST-segment elevation acute coronary syndrome (unstable ang ina/non-Q-wave myocardial infarction [MI]) including patients who are to be managed medically and those who are to be managed with percutaneous coronary intervention (with or without stent) or CABG, clopidogrel has been shown to decrease the rate of a comb ined endpoint of cardiovascular death, MI, or stroke as well as the rate of a combined endpoint of cardiovascular death, MI, stroke, or refractory ischemia. - For patients with ST -segment elevation acute myocardial infarction, clopidogrel has been shown t o reduce the rate of death from any cause and the rate of a combined endpoint of death, re -infarction or stroke. In patients with moderate to high-risk Transient Ischemic Attack (TIA) or minor Ischemic Stroke (IS) Clopidogrel in combination with ASA is indicated in: - Adult patients with moderate to high-risk TIA (ABCD21 score ≥4) or minor IS (NIHSS2 ≤3) within 24 hours of either the TIA or IS event. Clopidogrel is indicated in adults for the prevention of atherothrombotic and thromboembolic events in: Atrial Fibrillation In patients with atrial fibrillation (AF) at increased risk of vascular events who can take vitamin K antagonist (VKA) therapy, VKA has been shown to be associated with a better clinical benefit than acetylsalicylic acid (ASA) alone or the combination of clopidogrel and ASA for the reduction of stroke. In patients with atrial fibrillation who have at least one risk factor for vascular events and who cannot take VKA therapy (e.g., specific risk of bleeding, physician assessment that pat ient is unable to comply with INR (international normalised ratio) monitoring or that VKA use is inappropriate), clopidogrel is indicated in combination with ASA for the prevention of atherothrombotic and thromboembolic events, including stroke. Clopidogre l in combination with ASA has been shown to reduce the rate of the combined endpoint of stroke, myocardial infarction (MI), non-CNS systemic embolism, or vascular death, largely through a reduction in stroke.",1,1,Indications,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T00:56:57.209370+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32695,Montelukast (as Sodium),Montiget,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1pPPdoPPtjXqGwGfqN8O6gP8nmcFP76fE/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32695_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1pPPdoPPtjXqGwGfqN8O6gP8nmcFP76fE_view_usp_drivesdk_82b66bc7f7.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32695_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1pPPdoPPtjXqGwGfqN8O6gP8nmcFP76fE_view_usp_drivesdk_82b66bc7f7.json,42ffc70f1d73d4506470fdb6893f12c798e74507ce8278c08924aaa71fbf4bec,5965891,8,digital_text,"Montelukast (Montiget®) 4mg Pediatric Granules are available as white to off-white granular powder filled in a printed sachet. Montelukast (Montiget ®) 4mg Chewable Tablet is available as light pink to pink round biconvex shaped tablet engraved ""GETZ"" on one side and plain on other side. Montelukast (Montiget ®) 5mg Chewable Tablet is available as white round biconvex shaped tablet engraved ""GETZ"" on one side and plain on other side. Montelukast (Montiget ®) 10mg Film-Coated Tablet is available as cream to light yellow colored square shaped film-coated tablet having bisect line on one side and plain on other side.",3,3,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"- Montelukast (Montiget ®) is indicated for the prophylaxis and chronic treatment of asthma including: - The prevention of day and night time symptoms. - The treatment of aspirin-sensitive asthmatic patients. - The prevention of exercise-induced bronchoconstriction. - Montelukast (Montiget ®) is effective alone or in combination with other agents used in the maintenance treatment of chronic asthma. Montelukast (Montiget ®) and inhaled corticosteroids may be used concomitantly with additive effects to control asthma or to reduce the inhaled corticosteroid dose while maintaining clinical stability. - Montelukast (Montiget ®) is also indicated for the relief of symptoms of seasonal allergic rhinitis in adults and pediatric patients 2 years of age and older, and perennial allergic rhinitis in adults and pediatric patients 6 months of age and older, including nasal congestion, rhinorrhea, nasal itching, sneezing, nasal congestion upon awakening, difficulty going to sleep, and nighttime awakenings; tearing, itchy, red, and puffy eyes.",3,3,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T00:57:06.133442+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32719,Fexofenadine Hydrochloride,Allerfen,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/148a8GMJAplLVQ4G6wEWOh_anaoB6rDcu/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32719_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_148a8GMJAplLVQ4G6wEWOh_anaoB6rDcu_view_usp_drivesdk_d5f0499bbc.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32719_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_148a8GMJAplLVQ4G6wEWOh_anaoB6rDcu_view_usp_drivesdk_d5f0499bbc.json,098d224fbb1b6bb768a7f055574ec55567f329f43c8d21af0db8feb472ad7d84,583373,1,digital_text,"Fexofenadine HCl is a histamine H1-receptor antagonist with the chemical name (±)-4 -[1 hydroxy-4-[4-(hydroxydiphenylmethyl)-1- piperidinyl]-butyl]-α, α-dimethyl benzeneacetic acid hydrochloride. The empirical formula is C32H39NO4HCl. Fexofenadine HCL is an off-white crystalline powder. It is freely soluble in methanol and ethanol, slightly soluble in chloroform and water, and insoluble in hexane. Fexofenadine HCl is a racemate and exists as a zwitterion in aqueous media at physiological pH. Fexofenadine HCl (Allerfen) 120 mg is a brick red film-coated tablet, round, biconvex, bisected on one side and plain on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Fexofenadine is indicated in seasonal and perennial allergic rhinitis and chronic idiophatic urticaria. An active metabolite of terfenadine, is a non-sedating antihistamine. It does not possess significant sedative or antimuscarinic actions.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T01:41:50.469084+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32723,Clobetasol Propionate,Clobex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1O7DoWRecwWgESsNS0gB3dEvBNask6-aa/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32723_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1O7DoWRecwWgESsNS0gB3dEvBNask6-aa_view_usp_drivesdk_6606516a23.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32723_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1O7DoWRecwWgESsNS0gB3dEvBNask6-aa_view_usp_drivesdk_6606516a23.json,ee405c4758a5618e36d50d9886ccc0f479761e12fc8e2a034fd1e32cc310cff7,1202017,7,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T02:26:21.445565+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32734,ASPIRIN,ASTHROMED,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MfbLfZLGIvpz3wBU7RrfUwjr32NtyM85/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32734_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MfbLfZLGIvpz3wBU7RrfUwjr32NtyM85_view_usp_drivesdk_f9da829429.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32734_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MfbLfZLGIvpz3wBU7RrfUwjr32NtyM85_view_usp_drivesdk_f9da829429.json,c3db567d007be032ad47cb802cd7ed6f91e910d0d5b6a4e6c1f6473c22e2f151,163263,2,digital_text,"Aspirin (Asthromed) 100 mg is old-rose to dark-pink enteric coated tablet, round, biconvex and plain on both sides.. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This product contains aspirin with 100 mg Acetylsalicylic acid. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Each enteric-coated tablet contains: Aspirin, USP………………………………………………………………………. 100mg WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? For the prophylaxis of cerebrovascular disease or myocardial infarction or for the secondary prevention of thrombotic cerebrovascular or cardiovascular disease. It is also used for pain, in musculoskeletal conditions, headache, dysmenorrhea, pyrexia, and fever. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Prevention of Myocardial Infarction and stroke: 75 mg to 100 mg daily. Take immediately after meals. Swallow whole. Do not chew/crush. As Analgesic/Antipyretic: 300 mg to 900 mg every 4 to 6 hours when necessary to a maximum of 4 g daily or as prescribed by the physician. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE?  Children and adolescents under 16 years of age  Breast-feeding mothers because of risk of Reye’s syndrome.  With previous or active peptic ulceration.  Hemophilia  Not for treatment of gout  With history of hypersensitivity to aspirin or any other",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T02:26:24.645171+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32773,Itopride Hydrochloride,Ganaton,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1D-M6xVZoFzFOWztfZSM1vZcnmU-CvHOR/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32773_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1D-M6xVZoFzFOWztfZSM1vZcnmU-CvHOR_view_usp_drivesdk_debf0eed6c.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32773_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1D-M6xVZoFzFOWztfZSM1vZcnmU-CvHOR_view_usp_drivesdk_debf0eed6c.json,0e1fa9bfd745208fa006dc67ab22014b52435af9cc3de9ca1ee3719ff08015cf,544336,2,digital_text,"Itopride hydrochloride is a white to pale yellowish white crystal or crystalline powder. It is odorless and has a bitter taste. It is very soluble in water, freely soluble in methanol or in glacial acetic acid, sparingly soluble in ethanol and practically insoluble in acetic anhydride or in ether. The pH of the solution is 4.0 to 5.0. The melting point is 193 to198°C. CLINICAL PARTICULARS Therapeutic Indications Treatment of gastrointestinal symptoms caused by gastric dysmotility and delayed gastric emptying, like sensation of bloating, early satiety, postprandial fullness, upper abdominal pain or discomfort, anorexia, heartburn, nausea and vomiting; functional (non-ulcer) dyspepsia or chronic gastritis. Posology and Method of Administration Adults The recommended dose of itopride hydrochloride for adult patients is one tablet (50 mg) taken orally three times a day before meals. The dose may be reduced according to the patient’s age and symptoms (see PRECAUTIONS). Duration of Treatment In clinical studies, itopride hydrochloride has been administered up to 8 weeks.",1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Treatment of gastrointestinal symptoms caused by gastric dysmotility and delayed gastric emptying, like sensation of bloating, early satiety, postprandial fullness, upper abdominal pain or discomfort, anorexia, heartburn, nausea and vomiting; functional (non-ulcer) dyspepsia or chronic gastritis.",1,1,Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T02:26:27.868978+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32858,Methotrexate,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1s8aOte6OpzZ-4PNaoulRDtxGZTDuwj5G/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32858_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1s8aOte6OpzZ-4PNaoulRDtxGZTDuwj5G_view_usp_drivesdk_db8f504c20.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32858_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1s8aOte6OpzZ-4PNaoulRDtxGZTDuwj5G_view_usp_drivesdk_db8f504c20.json,b78304c21c74717efa9566fd85c7cfe1c2c4e00faf25c809720bc129530be04b,263516,29,digital_text,Methotrexate Solution for Injection is a clear yellow solution. Methotrexate Solution for Injection is preservative-free. Methotrexate Solution for Injection has a pH of 7.5 to 9.0.,3,3,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Antineoplastic chemotherapy Methotrexate has a broad spectrum of antineoplastic activity. It is indicated for the treatment of breast cancer, gestational choriocarcinoma, and in patients with chorioadenoma destruens and hydatidiform mole. Methotrexate may be used in combination with other chemotherapeutic agents for the palliative treatment of acute leukemia, particularly acute lymphoblastic leukemia. It may also be used in the treatment of Burkitt's lymphoma, advanced stages (III and IV, Peters' Staging System) of lymphosarcoma, especially in children, and in advanced cases of mycosis fungoides. High dose therapy [Page 4] 4 In high-dose schedules, methotrexate may be effective alone or in combination therapy, in the treatment of epidermoid cancers of the head and neck, osteogenic sarcoma and bronchogenic carcinoma. Calcium folinate (leucovorin calcium) must be used in conjunction with high dose methotrexate therapy. Psoriasis chemotherapy (see WARNINGS box) Methotrexate may b e of value in the symptomatic control of severe, recalcitrant, disabling psoriasis which is not adequately responsive to other forms of treatment. However, due to the high risk associated with its use, methotrexate should be used after the diagnosis has been definitely established, as by biopsy and/or after dermatologic consultation. Rheumatoid arthritis chemotherapy (see WARNINGS box) Management of severe, recalcitrant, active rheumatoid arthritis in adults not responding to, or intolerant of, an adequate trial of NSAIDs and one or more disease modifying drugs. Aspirin, NSAIDs and/or low dose steroids may b e continued, although the possibility o f increased toxicity w ith concomitant use of NSAIDs including salicylate has not been fully explored. Steroids may be reduced gradually in patients who respond to methotrexate. Combined use of methotrexate with gold, penicillamine, hydroxychloroquine, sulfasalazine or cytotoxic agents has not been studied and may increase the incidence of adverse effects. Rest and physiotherapy as indicated should be continued.",3,4,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T02:26:31.460473+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32859,Methotrexate,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1h2Vqsa8XnUhqEsRlLm_n8zongENNCXUR/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32859_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1h2Vqsa8XnUhqEsRlLm_n8zongENNCXUR_view_usp_drivesdk_c4ec1dada9.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32859_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1h2Vqsa8XnUhqEsRlLm_n8zongENNCXUR_view_usp_drivesdk_c4ec1dada9.json,b78304c21c74717efa9566fd85c7cfe1c2c4e00faf25c809720bc129530be04b,263516,29,digital_text,Methotrexate Solution for Injection is a clear yellow solution. Methotrexate Solution for Injection is preservative-free. Methotrexate Solution for Injection has a pH of 7.5 to 9.0.,3,3,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Antineoplastic chemotherapy Methotrexate has a broad spectrum of antineoplastic activity. It is indicated for the treatment of breast cancer, gestational choriocarcinoma, and in patients with chorioadenoma destruens and hydatidiform mole. Methotrexate may be used in combination with other chemotherapeutic agents for the palliative treatment of acute leukemia, particularly acute lymphoblastic leukemia. It may also be used in the treatment of Burkitt's lymphoma, advanced stages (III and IV, Peters' Staging System) of lymphosarcoma, especially in children, and in advanced cases of mycosis fungoides. High dose therapy [Page 4] 4 In high-dose schedules, methotrexate may be effective alone or in combination therapy, in the treatment of epidermoid cancers of the head and neck, osteogenic sarcoma and bronchogenic carcinoma. Calcium folinate (leucovorin calcium) must be used in conjunction with high dose methotrexate therapy. Psoriasis chemotherapy (see WARNINGS box) Methotrexate may b e of value in the symptomatic control of severe, recalcitrant, disabling psoriasis which is not adequately responsive to other forms of treatment. However, due to the high risk associated with its use, methotrexate should be used after the diagnosis has been definitely established, as by biopsy and/or after dermatologic consultation. Rheumatoid arthritis chemotherapy (see WARNINGS box) Management of severe, recalcitrant, active rheumatoid arthritis in adults not responding to, or intolerant of, an adequate trial of NSAIDs and one or more disease modifying drugs. Aspirin, NSAIDs and/or low dose steroids may b e continued, although the possibility o f increased toxicity w ith concomitant use of NSAIDs including salicylate has not been fully explored. Steroids may be reduced gradually in patients who respond to methotrexate. Combined use of methotrexate with gold, penicillamine, hydroxychloroquine, sulfasalazine or cytotoxic agents has not been studied and may increase the incidence of adverse effects. Rest and physiotherapy as indicated should be continued.",3,4,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T02:26:35.009485+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32871,Fentanyl (as Citrate),None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MY4Q3pPc_anVhsoJ0vekyg7UIbBP_kME/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32871_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MY4Q3pPc_anVhsoJ0vekyg7UIbBP_kME_view_usp_drivesdk_44bf5fa905.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32871_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MY4Q3pPc_anVhsoJ0vekyg7UIbBP_kME_view_usp_drivesdk_44bf5fa905.json,5b80b106334b6c29e643b0dd3a690c1ecf8c147ed7e3d4a0f9bb6c9a5f06915d,386767,21,digital_text,"Chemical structure FENTANYL Viewed on: Thursday, May 16, 2024 - 11:04:21 PM Eastern Time [Page 2] Page 2 of 21 The chemical formula of fentanyl citrate is C22H28N2O.C6H8O7 and its molecular weight is 528.6. The chemical structure of fentanyl citrate is shown below: CAS number 990-73-8 Fentanyl c itrate is a sterile solution of fentanyl c itrate and sodium chloride in Water for Injections. It is presented in ampoules and containing 2 mL or 10 mL of a 50 micrograms per mL s olution of fentanyl present as fentanyl c itrate. The solution does not contain any preservative. The pH of the solution is adjusted with sodium hydroxide or hydrochloric acid to 5.0 to 7.5, if necessary. Fentanyl citrate is a white or almost white powder, soluble in water, freely soluble in methanol, sparingly soluble in alcohol. For the full list of excipients, see Section 6.1 List of Excipients.",1,2,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Fentanyl is indicated for analgesic action of short duration during premedication, induction and maintenance of anesthesia and in the immediate post-operative periods. It may be used as an opioid analgesic supplement in general and regional anesthesia. Fentanyl m ay b e used in combination with neuroleptic agents such as droperidol as an anesthetic premedication, for the induction of anesthesia and as an adjunct in the maintenance of general and regional anesthesia. The state of neurolept analgesia may b e converted to neurolept anesthesia by the concurrent administration of 65% nitrous oxide in oxygen.",2,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T02:26:38.230700+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32877,Silymarin,Legalon,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1p1v_5mHofcz_MtPVNKDCD4QXqH404g0V/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32877_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1p1v_5mHofcz_MtPVNKDCD4QXqH404g0V_view_usp_drivesdk_c664c1a892.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32877_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1p1v_5mHofcz_MtPVNKDCD4QXqH404g0V_view_usp_drivesdk_c664c1a892.json,8b472f8b45b9872b4ca1faa9cd924fa8ac650a8791c461ffe58f641913d555e5,152090,4,digital_text,"The liver has several vital functions in the human body; it plays a major role in metabolism (sugar, proteins and fats), in digestion (bile secret ion) and in the detoxification of metabolic wastes. Any form of damage to the liver affects the membranes of the liver cells, hence, impairs functional capacity. Silymarin, the active substance of Legalon is of plant origin. It acts as a stabilizer of cel l membranes and is hence capable of protecting the liver from noxious influences and of restoring or revitalizing liver cells which have previously been damaged. Its effects are reflected in improvement in general condition, lessening of digestive symptoms , and increase in appetite and body weight in patients whose general condition and nutritional state have been impaired by liver disease. It also ameliorates the signs of liver disease and normalizes laboratory tests of liver function",1,1,4. Production Description,Supportive treatment of chronic inflammatory diseases of the liver and cirrhosis.,2,2,7. Indication,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T02:26:41.722462+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32882,Voriconazole,Vfend,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1k-2NAMD6rGpiqHmhv0O31BsNTSpA2Tfg/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32882_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1k-2NAMD6rGpiqHmhv0O31BsNTSpA2Tfg_view_usp_drivesdk_c1a05db604.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32882_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1k-2NAMD6rGpiqHmhv0O31BsNTSpA2Tfg_view_usp_drivesdk_c1a05db604.json,b4c9c0324a409b4ecf68a5d1f5c1dcf69174a39283dfea1a8b022db7aaecf1d3,572254,43,digital_text,"Voriconazole (Vfend®), a triazole antifungal agent, is available as a lyophilized powder for solution for intravenous infusion and film-coated tablets for oral administration. The structural formula is: Voriconazole is designated chemically as (2R, 3S)-2-(2,4-difluorophenyl)-3-(5-fluoro-4- pyrimidinyl)-1-(1H-1,2,4-triazol-1-yl)-2-butanol with an empirical formula of C16H14F3N5O and a molecular weight of 349.3. Voriconazole drug substance is a white to light-colored powder.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Voriconazole is a broad spectrum, triazole antifungal agent and is indicated as follows:  Treatment of invasive aspergillosis; ℞ Viewed on: Friday, May 17, 2024 - 3:03:24 AM Eastern Time [Page 2] Page 2 of 43  Treatment of candidemia in non-neutropenic patients;  Treatment of serious invasive Candida infections (including C. krusei);  Treatment of esophageal candidiasis;  Treatment of serious fungal infections caused by Scedosporium spp. and Fusarium spp.;  Treatment of other serious fungal infections in patients intolerant of, or refractory to, other therapy;  Prevention of breakthrough of fungal infections in febrile high-risk patients (allogeneic bone marrow transplants, relapsed leukemia patients);  Prophylaxis in patients who are at high risk of developing invasive fungal infections, such as hematopoietic stem cell transplant (HSCT) recipients.",1,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T02:26:45.633032+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32914,Flucloxacillin (as sodium),Coxafen,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PjJUMdPc8NhJadjZE54XhB9ZNuYFQTT-/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32914_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PjJUMdPc8NhJadjZE54XhB9ZNuYFQTT-_view_usp_drivesdk_d4a5ae00fc.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32914_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PjJUMdPc8NhJadjZE54XhB9ZNuYFQTT-_view_usp_drivesdk_d4a5ae00fc.json,3d3d6e03f744898cc5c34263314096dde44e034434b3a72b64aa034eda98e98d,338322,1,digital_text,Each capsule contains:,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Flucloxacillin like dicloxacillin, is about twice as well absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract as cloxacillin, but absorption is also reduced by the presence of food in the stomach. After an oral dose of 250 mg to 1 g in fasting subjects, peak plasma concentrations in about 1 hour are usually in the range of 5 to 15 ug per mL. Plasma concentrations following the intramuscular injection of flucloxacillin sodium are similar, but peak concentrations are achieved in about 30 minutes. Doubling the dose can double the plasma concentrations. About 95% of flucloxacillin in the circulation is bound to plasma proteins. Flucloxacillin has been reported to have a plasma half-life of approximately 1 hour. The half-life is prolonged in neonates. Patients with a previous history of flucloxacillin-associated jaundice/hepatic dysfunction. Warnings Serious and occasionally fatal hypersensitivity reactions (anaphylaxis) have been reported in patients receiving beta-lactam antibiotics. Anaphylaxis has occurred in patients on oral therapy. Cross-sensitivity between penicillins and cephalosporins is well documented. Before commencing therapy with any penicillin, careful enquiry should be made concerning previous hypersensitivity reactions to penicillins, cephalosporins or other allergens. If an allergic reaction occurs, appropriate therapy should be instituted and Flucloxacillin (Coxafen) therapy discontinued.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T02:26:48.570468+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32985,Fenofibrate,Inofib,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1tDN35BA42e_3YX5Uw0VuJyUgQTiDC2gA/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32985_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1tDN35BA42e_3YX5Uw0VuJyUgQTiDC2gA_view_usp_drivesdk_67dd1dd0e4.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32985_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1tDN35BA42e_3YX5Uw0VuJyUgQTiDC2gA_view_usp_drivesdk_67dd1dd0e4.json,3b25ed6ac624ad5a9e77b3d6141150fab9c5e0e0d726b49ca017d33457c4948c,1224510,1,digital_text,"Capsule with orange cap and body, filled with white to off-white powder*** Fenofibrate, a fibric acid derivative, is a lipid regulating drug with actions on plasma lipids.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"It is used in the treatment of type IIa, type IIB, type III, type IV and type V hyperlipoproteinaemias.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T03:17:30.460030+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY32998,Oxaliplatin,Eloxatin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZQ5N-l5JBuS81cwEQd5SVTSzvTBPxvkb/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY32998_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZQ5N-l5JBuS81cwEQd5SVTSzvTBPxvkb_view_usp_drivesdk_e905b436be.pdf,page_text/DR-XY32998_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZQ5N-l5JBuS81cwEQd5SVTSzvTBPxvkb_view_usp_drivesdk_e905b436be.json,638b1e049b0bebaeef48c79137140953e60b95a402da8d3f053e0a6a4bfe0fed,815972,17,digital_text,"ONLY USE the recommended solvents. Any reconstituted solution showing traces of precipitation must not be administered and must be disposed of in compliance with regulatory requirements relating to the disposal of toxic waste Reconstitution of the solution • Water for injections or a 5% glucose solution (50 mg/ml) should be used to reconstitute the solution. • For a 20-mg vial: add 4 ml of solvent to yield a concentration of 5 mg/ml. • For a 50-mg vial: add 10 ml of solvent to yield a concentration of 5 mg/ml. • For a 100-mg vial: add 20 ml of solvent to yield a concentration of 5 mg/ml. From a microbiological and chemical perspective, the reconstituted solution should be immediately diluted in a 5% glucose solution (50 mg/ml). Inspect visually before use. Only clear solutions with no particles can be used. The medicinal product is for single use only. Any unused solution must be discarded. Dilution for intravenous infusion Withdraw the required amount of concentrate from the vial and then dilute with 250 to 500 ml of 5% glucose solution (50 mg/ml) to obtain an oxaliplatin concentration of between 0.2 mg/ml and 0.7 mg/ml. The concentration range for which the physical and chemical stability of oxaliplatin have been demonstrated is between 0.2 mg/ml and 2.0 mg/ml. Administer by intravenous infusion. After dilution in a 5% glucose solution, physical and chemical stability have been demonstrated for 24 hours between +2°C and +8°C. From a microbiological point of view, the solution for infusion must be used immediately. If the drug is not used immediately, the duration and conditions of storage before use are the sole responsibility of the user and should not normally exceed 24 hours at a temperature between +2°C and +8°C, unless the dilution was performed in duly controlled and validated aseptic conditions. Inspect visually before use. Only clear solutions with no particles can be used. The medicinal product is for single use only. Any unused solution must be disposed of (see Section on Waste disposal below). NEVER use solutions containing chloride or sodium chloride for reconstitution or dilution. The compatibility of the oxaliplatin solution for infusion has been tested with standard PVC -based administration sets. Infusion The administration of oxaliplatin does not require prehydration. Oxaliplatin diluted in 250 to 500 ml of a 5% glucose solution (50 mg/ml), to obtain a concentration not less than 0.2 mg/ml must be infused either by peripheral vein or a central venous line over 2 to 6 hours. [Page 17] 17 When oxaliplatin is administered with 5-fluorouracil (5-FU), the oxaliplatin infusion must be given before 5- fluorouracil (5-FU). Waste disposal Any unused product, as well as all materials that have been used for reconstitution, dilution and administration, must be destroyed according to standard hospital procedures relative to cytotoxic agents as per current laws related to the disposal of hazardous waste. Caution Foods, Drugs, Devices and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription. Manufactured by Sanofi-Aventis Deutschland GmbH Brüningstrasse 50 D-65926 Frankfurt am Main Germany Imported by sanofi-aventis Philippines, Inc. 21st and 22nd Floors, One World Place Corporate Offices, 32nd Street, Bonifacio Global City, Taguig City If you experience any side effects with the use of this product, you are advised to seek medical attention. You are also encouraged to report any side effects to Sanofi Philippines Pharmacovigilance Unit via email at PV.Philippines@sanofi.com. By reporting side effects, you can help provide more information on the safety of this product. For suspected adverse reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph Reg. No.: DR-XY32998 Date of first authorization: 15 Feb 2007 CCDS version 15 Date of leaflet revision: January 2020 [Page 18]",16,17,Product Characteristics.,"Oxaliplatin, in combination with 5-fluorouracil (5-FU) and folinic acid (FA), is indicated for: - adjuvant treatment of stage III (Dukes’ C) colon cancer after complete resection of the primary tumor - treatment of metastatic colorectal cancer.",1,1,Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T03:17:34.645390+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY33009,Montelukast (as Sodium),Montiget,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1w5Ot5JDTTb_zDY9ZRNhZAiAndS2373yr/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY33009_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1w5Ot5JDTTb_zDY9ZRNhZAiAndS2373yr_view_usp_drivesdk_3da2383eff.pdf,page_text/DR-XY33009_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1w5Ot5JDTTb_zDY9ZRNhZAiAndS2373yr_view_usp_drivesdk_3da2383eff.json,7b9d7df903720b8013ebfac85cade4587361afcdc3dc2efe468aaf5039bd0609,5962612,8,digital_text,"Montelukast (Montiget®) 4mg Pediatric Granules are available as white to off-white granular powder filled in a printed sachet. Montelukast (Montiget ®) 4mg Chewable Tablet is available as light pink to pink round biconvex shaped tablet engraved ""GETZ"" on one side and plain on other side. Montelukast (Montiget ®) 5mg Chewable Tablet is available as white round biconvex shaped tablet engraved ""GETZ"" on one side and plain on other side. Montelukast (Montiget ®) 10mg Film-Coated Tablet is available as cream to light yellow colored square shaped film-coated tablet having bisect line on one side and plain on other side.",3,3,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"- Montelukast (Montiget ®) is indicated for the prophylaxis and chronic treatment of asthma including: - The prevention of day and night time symptoms. - The treatment of aspirin-sensitive asthmatic patients. - The prevention of exercise-induced bronchoconstriction. - Montelukast (Montiget ®) is effective alone or in combination with other agents used in the maintenance treatment of chronic asthma. Montelukast (Montiget ®) and inhaled corticosteroids may be used concomitantly with additive effects to control asthma or to reduce the inhaled corticosteroid dose while maintaining clinical stability. - Montelukast (Montiget ®) is also indicated for the relief of symptoms of seasonal allergic rhinitis in adults and pediatric patients 2 years of age and older, and perennial allergic rhinitis in adults and pediatric patients 6 months of age and older, including nasal congestion, rhinorrhea, nasal itching, sneezing, nasal congestion upon awakening, difficulty going to sleep, and nighttime awakenings; tearing, itchy, red, and puffy eyes.",3,3,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T03:18:17.040455+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY33087,Iron (as Ferrous Fumarate) + Vitamin b12+Folic Acid,Ferrovit,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uydymV3hisyMqLbSd5U5b4WuewSLIWx0/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY33087_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uydymV3hisyMqLbSd5U5b4WuewSLIWx0_view_usp_drivesdk_94b7bd9c73.pdf,page_text/DR-XY33087_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uydymV3hisyMqLbSd5U5b4WuewSLIWx0_view_usp_drivesdk_94b7bd9c73.json,bb6c6264e594a137eb7588ae207e34e73bb7669ee0c5474479c7016f4ead61b2,2314848,1,ocr,"Brown color, oily suspension, filled in 10 minim, oblong, red, opaque, soft gelatin shell capsule *Keep out of reach of children «Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C in a dry place, away from direct sunlight. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This medicine contains Iron, Folic Acid and Vitamin B12 WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If you are allergic (hypersensitive) to active substances or any of the other ingredients STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE *lf any undesirable effect occurs",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T03:18:28.700978+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY33089,Cefixime (As Trihydrate),Trifixime,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1c1ezP7Bo8hpB2VeQNqUHiCs7TpgpkoqD/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY33089_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1c1ezP7Bo8hpB2VeQNqUHiCs7TpgpkoqD_view_usp_drivesdk_09dc5694b9.pdf,page_text/DR-XY33089_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1c1ezP7Bo8hpB2VeQNqUHiCs7TpgpkoqD_view_usp_drivesdk_09dc5694b9.json,bfc507c76e448dafe1fb8ac3652aab4e6b873f813fc4fa7a34401cf2c38a7827,3551384,1,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T03:18:33.313645+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY33112,Ambroxol Hydrochloride,Broxitrol,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo4Lh312akW9H2S8tIoyFNzleyLP_1_y/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY33112_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xo4Lh312akW9H2S8tIoyFNzleyLP_1_y_view_usp_drivesdk_7736431fb9.pdf,page_text/DR-XY33112_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xo4Lh312akW9H2S8tIoyFNzleyLP_1_y_view_usp_drivesdk_7736431fb9.json,c3d305c92ba97d2328123cfcb251aab61c21f56c0ca790f7ddf9a3f2c6cd5f6e,460063,2,ocr,"Broxitrol Syrup is a clear straw, slightly viscous liquid with bitter-sweet taste cola flavor Broxitrol Syrup (oral drops) is a clear straw, slightly viscous liquid with bitter-sweet taste and banana flavor. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This medicines contain Ambroxol , which stimulates fluid secretion in the respiratory tract and breaks down mucus resulting in the production of less thick and less sticky mucus/phlegm. Ambroxol improves mucocilliary clearance (mucus flow and transport) making phlegm easier to cough and expel. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE See formulation above WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? For the treatment of respiratory disorder associated with productive cough. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THE MEDICINE? This medication should be taken orally (by mouth). The recommendations for children are based on a total dose of 1.2 — 1.6 mg Ambroxol per kg bodyweight. The dose is best taken after meals. Ambroxol hydrochloride oral drops may be diluted to milk, juice or water. Ambroxol 15 mg/5 mL Syrup: Ambroxol 6 mg/mL Syrup (Oral drops): Children: Children: 5 to 10 years old: 5 mL 3 times a day 13 to 24 months: 1.25 mL 2 times a day 2 to 5 years old: 2.5 mL 3 times a day 7 to 12 months: 1 mL 2 times a day 1 to 2 years old: 2.5 mL 2 times a day Infant under 6 months: 0.5 mL 2 times a day For long-term treatment, the dose may be reduced or as prescribed by the physician. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you are allergic to any ingredient of the product. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS Ambroxol is generally well tolerated. Mild stomach disturbances such as pyrosis (heartburn), dyspepsia, diarrhea, nausea and vomiting may occur. Rash/urticaria, angioedema (rapid swelling of the skin), anaphylactic reactions (rare, life-threatening allergic reaction) and other allergic reactions have been reported. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOODS SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? There are no reports of adverse drug reactions with other medications. Administration of Ambroxo! with antibiotics (e.g. Amoxicillin, Cefuroxime, Erythromycin) leads to higher antibiotic concentration in bronchopulmonary secretions and in sputum, [Page 2] Tell your doctor about other medicines you are taking, and allergy. especially other medicines for cough, cold WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, just take the next dose if still needed for the condition being treated, and the subsequent doses at the recommended time or schedule exceed recommended dose. (e.g every . or 12 hours). Do not HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THE MEDICINE? * Keep the product out of reach and sight of children. * Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE Symptoms of Ambroxol overdose include extensions of the diarrhea, dyspepsia, pyrosis, nausea, vomiting and skin rash es). common undesirable effects (e.g. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE USED MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE * Severe skin lesions such as Stevens-Johnson syndrome and Lyell'e syndrome have been reported rarely with the administration of mucolytics such as Ambroxol. These may be due to the severity of the underlying disease or concomitant medication. If new skin or mucosal lesions occur, discontinue Ambroxol and consult a physician immediately. * Do not use after the expiry date on the label. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If symptoms do not improve or new symptoms appear and if undesirable effects develops AVAILABILITY Syrup: Amber glass bottle x 60mL (Box of 1's) Drops: 15mL Amber bottle with medicine dropper (Box of 1's) DATE OF REVISION OF PATIENT INFORMATION LEAF LET (PIL): March 22, 2018 Ambroxol (Broxitrol) Syrup Oral Dro ps Registration no. DR-XY33561 Valid until July 10, 2024 Ambroxol (Broxitrol) Syrup Registrati on no. DR-XY33112 Valid until March 15, 2024 ADR Reporting Statement “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph Patient must seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction.” Manufactured by Manufactured for:",1,2,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T03:18:45.488678+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY33116,,,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1b-upGPf0xUXpUJx_dy2kTdUUrfjGC_03/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY33116_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1b-upGPf0xUXpUJx_dy2kTdUUrfjGC_03_view_usp_drivesdk_5573348aae.pdf,page_text/DR-XY33116_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1b-upGPf0xUXpUJx_dy2kTdUUrfjGC_03_view_usp_drivesdk_5573348aae.json,08933d7f227f87aa38c4224cb527d1c8ffda4abe964d925d1c4e5370d9c175b5,331094,2,digital_text,,,,,"Treatment-resistant schizophrenia Clozapine is indicated in treatment -resistant schizophrenic patients and in schizophrenia patients who have severe, untreatable neurological adverse reactions to other antipsychotic agents, including atypical antipsychotics. Treatment resistance is defined as a lack of satisfactory clinical improvement despite the use of adequate doses of at least two different antipsychotic agents, including an atypical antipsychotic agent, prescribed for adequate duration. Psychosis during the course of Parkinson's disease Clozapine is also indicated in psychotic disorders occurring during the course of Parkinson's disease, in cases where standard treatment has failed.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T03:18:48.519756+00:00
