lying disease (e.g. dyslipidemia in diabetes mellitus). Appropriate dietary measures initiated before therapy should be continued. Additional indication: Fenofibrate (Lipanthyl® NT) 145 mg is indicated for the reduction in the progression of diabetic retinopathy in patients with type 2 diabetes and existing diabetic retinopathy. Fenofibrate (Lipanthyl® NT) 145 mg does not replace the appropriate control of blood pressure, blood glucose and blood lipids in reducing the progression of diabetic retinopathy.",1,1,Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T03:31:58.484728+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY33322,Morphine Sulfate,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Z1WfuqevuPDBqkzsvoqktobhXNmOGLV5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY33322_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Z1WfuqevuPDBqkzsvoqktobhXNmOGLV5_view_usp_drivesdk_3bff80cde5.pdf,page_text/DR-XY33322_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Z1WfuqevuPDBqkzsvoqktobhXNmOGLV5_view_usp_drivesdk_3bff80cde5.json,d63c7d1ee4bf1b0f9c4e5a83d4830434d72eabba94b037f6c1837fd009a8ce5f,446245,21,digital_text,"The structural formula of morphine sulfate is shown below: CAS number: 6211-15-0 Morphine Sulfate Injection is a clear colorless to slightly yellow, sterile solution. The solution does not contain any antioxidant or preservative.",2,2,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Morphine Sulfate Injection is indicated for the short-term management of severe pain for which other treatment options have failed, are contradicted, not tolerated or are otherwise inappropriate to provide sufficient management of pain. Morphine Sulfate Injection may also be used as a pre-operative medication and as an analgesic adjunct in general anaesthesia. OHO H H CH 2 CH 2 CH3 OH N . H2SO4 . 5H2O 2 Viewed on: Thursday, May 16, 2024 - 11:13:06 PM Eastern Time [Page 3] 3",2,3,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T03:32:05.756409+00:00
