PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY33473,Varenicline Tartrate,Champix,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1b_t2rquMl6LouPXMSMGEasrH-7Smv-LB/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY33473_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1b_t2rquMl6LouPXMSMGEasrH-7Smv-LB_view_usp_drivesdk_9a09962378.pdf,page_text/DR-XY33473_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1b_t2rquMl6LouPXMSMGEasrH-7Smv-LB_view_usp_drivesdk_9a09962378.json,ec67b1a3d78b8fe9ccc33fe103b37df13b28589bcd9f7233447a6d7b3b451602,421525,33,digital_text,"Varenicline tartrate (Champix) film-coated tablets contain the active ingredient, varenicline (as the tartrate salt), which is a partial agonist selective for α4β2 nicotinic acetylcholine receptor subtypes. Varenicline, as the tartrate salt, is a powder which is a white to off-white to slightly yellow solid with the following chemical name: 7,8,9,10-tetrahydro- 6,10-methano-6H-pyrazino[2,3-h][3] benzazepine, (2R,3R)-2,3- dihydroxybutanedioate (1:1). It is highly soluble in water. Varenicline tartrate (Champix) has a molecular weight of 361.35 Daltons, and a molecular formula of C13H13N3•C4H6O6. The chemical structure is: HO O C C O O O H O H H 2 N N N R R",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,Varenicline tartrate (Champix) is indicated as an aid to smoking cessation treatment.,2,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:05:15.832136+00:00
