PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY34655,Tamsulosin Hydrochloride,Prozelax,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Anq9BTidkWlEHInGQj_UfIfP9ot67kCQ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY34655_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Anq9BTidkWlEHInGQj_UfIfP9ot67kCQ_view_usp_drivesdk_e3d76fe4df.pdf,page_text/DR-XY34655_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Anq9BTidkWlEHInGQj_UfIfP9ot67kCQ_view_usp_drivesdk_e3d76fe4df.json,876c67678dd304fe13b95b3a0993736c37bb9b5f5aaab018b393d1e870850235,487863,1,digital_text,"Tamsulosin (Prozelax )200 mcg capsule: white to off-white pellets in a capsule with a slightly pink cap and off white body PHARMACOLOGY Pharmacodynamics Tamsulosin HCl is a sulfamoylphenethylamine derivative alpha -adrenergic blocking agent (alpha -adrenoceptor antagonist). It binds selectively and 1 1 competitively to postsynaptic alpha -adrenoceptors, in particular to subtypes alpha and alpha About 70% of alpha -receptors in human prostate are 1 1A 1D. 1 of the alpha subtype. Tamsulosin brings about relaxation of prostatic and urethral smooth muscles resulting in improved urinary flow rate and a 1A reduction in symptoms of benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH). It also improves the irritative symptoms in which bladder instability plays an important role. Tamsulosin's ability to decrease intra-ureteral pressure and increase fluid passage has also been shown to be effective in medical expulsive therapy in increasing the rate of spontaneous stone passage. Alpha -blockers can reduce blood pressure by lowering peripheral resistance. Selectivity of tamsulosin for alpha -receptors which are mainly located 1 1A in nonvascular smooth muscle (e.g., prostate) may result in a reduced incidence of adverse cardiovascular effects (e.g., syncope, dizziness, hypotension). Pharmacokinetics The plasma levels of tamsulosin HCl gradually increases reaching peak concentrations (Cmax) at a median time of 6 hours after a single dose of tamsulosin 400 mcg extended release in the fasted state. At steady state (reached by day 4 of multiple dosing), plasma concentrations of tamsulosin peak at 4 to 6 hours under fasting and fed conditions. An increase in peak plasma concentrations is observed from approximately 6 ng/mL after the first dose to 11 ng/mL in steady state. The plasma concentration decreases after the Cmax is reached; however, at approximately 16 to 24 hours post-dose, a small increase or second plateau is observed. The absolute bioavailability of tamsulosin is estimated to be 55 to 59%. Absorption of tamsulosin is reduced by a recent meal. Tamsulosin's mean steady-state apparent volume of distribution after intravenous (IV) administration is 16 L, which suggests distribution into extracellular fluids. Tamsulosin is 94 to 99% bound to plasma proteins primarily alpha acid glycoproteins. It is extensively metabolized by cytochrome P450 enzymes 1 (CYP3A4 and CYP2D6 isoenzymes) in the liver; less than 10% of the dose is excreted in the urine unchanged. The metabolites of tamsulosin undergo extensive conjugation to glucuronide or sulfate prior to renal excretion. Tamsulosin's pharmacokinetic profile in humans has not been fully established, thus, possible interactions with other cytochrome P450 metabolized compounds cannot be predicted. Tamsulosin is primarily excreted through the urine with approximately 9% of the dose excreted as unchanged drug. Because of the absorption rate- controlled pharmacokinetics of tamsulosin capsule, the apparent half-life of tamsulosin increases to about 12 to 15 hours in healthy volunteers.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION®),Treatment of the signs and symptoms of benign prostatic hyperplasia/hypertrophy (BPH) including bladder outlet obstruction,1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:13:58.309682+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY3467,Sodium Chloride,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yfgBkGn7Df6SnvIzrW0iokmAu9-unpaO/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY3467_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1yfgBkGn7Df6SnvIzrW0iokmAu9-unpaO_view_usp_drivesdk_2ba7a96197.pdf,page_text/DR-XY3467_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1yfgBkGn7Df6SnvIzrW0iokmAu9-unpaO_view_usp_drivesdk_2ba7a96197.json,cf67ab6000ac0b5eb72aae1a9df46b1faf9d8cfd7af0a8738cad75b8665b086c,3779224,2,ocr,"Sodium Chloride 2.5 mEq/ mL Solution for I.V. Infusion is a clear, colorless solution; free from visible foreign matter.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Maintenance Therapy - In patients Who are not able to ta Kia food and fluids orally but who have normal renal function, with no abnormal fluid and electrolyte losses, and no pre-existing deficits or excesses. Usually, about 70 mEq sodium per day will be sufficient to correct the mild sodium deficit. Replacement Therapy - In patients with water and electrolyte losses resulting in hyponatremia as in: 4 Syndrome of Inappropriate Anti-Diuretic Hormone (SIADH) 2. Water Intoxication - iatrogenic 3. Decrease ECF volume due to: a) Renal causes: 4. Osmotic diuresis 2. Diuretic therapy 3. Hypoaldosteronism 4. Salt-losing nephropathy, etc. b) Extra renal causes 4. Diarrhea 2. Vomiting 3. Burns 4. Wound drainage, etc.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T04:14:09.083690+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY34671,Aceclofenac,Clanza S,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RMYKvwoNVTaLaiemMOuDf3rrt-XtQgyA/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY34671_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RMYKvwoNVTaLaiemMOuDf3rrt-XtQgyA_view_usp_drivesdk_1e5756dd7a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY34671_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RMYKvwoNVTaLaiemMOuDf3rrt-XtQgyA_view_usp_drivesdk_1e5756dd7a.json,7c7b090a7a9f79024c1eecbd4ad8385ad907853a4f8509e5310b0a9173f5f03c,100908,1,digital_text,"Each red, oval softgel capsule is printed with “CLS” and filled with mucous liquid.",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Aceclofenac is indicated for the relief of pain and inflammation in toothache, trauma, lumbago, osteoarthritis, rheumatoid arthritis and ankylosing spondylitis.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:14:12.058525+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY34709,Levetiracetam,Keppra,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1QsQs9Chl-IChrxcNSsef3_IuYPlb2dLE/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY34709_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QsQs9Chl-IChrxcNSsef3_IuYPlb2dLE_view_usp_drivesdk_2794c92da8.pdf,page_text/DR-XY34709_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QsQs9Chl-IChrxcNSsef3_IuYPlb2dLE_view_usp_drivesdk_2794c92da8.json,d5aec24f78d6215e5c1cbad0386dde95365a9c678d3bd9d4008880813cc64779,178893,9,digital_text,"Levetiracetam (Keppra) 250 mg Film-Coated Tablet: Each blue, oblong, debossed with code ‘ucb’ and ‘250’ on one side, film coated tablet contains 250 mg of levetiracetam. The score li ne is only to facilitate breaking for ease of swallowing and not to divide into equal doses. Levetiracetam (Keppra) 500 mg Film-Coated Tablet: Each yellow, oblong, debossed with code ‘ucb’ and ‘500’ on one side, film coated tablet contains 500 mg of levetiracetam. The score li ne is only to facilitate breaking for ease of swallowing and not to divide into equal doses. Levetiracetam (Keppra) 1 g Film-Coated Tablet: Each white, scored, oblong, debossed with code ‘ucb’ and ‘1000’ on one side, film coated tablet contains 1 g of levetiracetam. The score line is only to facilitate breaking for ease of swallowing and not to divide into equal doses. Levetiracetam (Keppra) 100 mg/mL Oral Solution: Each mL of clear liquid oral solution contains 100 mg of levetiracetam. Levetiracetam (Keppra) 500 mg/5 mL Concentrate for Solution for IV Infusion: Each mL contains 100 mg Levetiracetam. The 5 mL vial contains 500 mg of Levetiracetam.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Levetiracetam is indicated as monotherapy in the treatment of:  partial onset seizures with or without secondary generalisation in adults and adolescents from 16 years of age with newly diagnosed epilepsy. Levetiracetam is indicated as adjunctive therapy in the treatment of:  partial onset seizures with or without secondary generalisation in adults, adolescents and children from 4 years of age with epilepsy  myoclonic seizures in adults and adolescents from 12 years of age with juvenile myoclonic epilepsy,  primary generalised tonic-clonic seizures in adults and adolescents from 4 years of age with idiopathic generalised epilepsy. Levetiracetam concentrate is an alternative for patients (adults and children from 4 years of age) when oral administration is temporarily not feasible.",3,3,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:14:15.720746+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY34729,Everolimus,Certican,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rmWgckAUGT0aJ0gAea-WFAQAWWQyhNkH/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY34729_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rmWgckAUGT0aJ0gAea-WFAQAWWQyhNkH_view_usp_drivesdk_7ca423382a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY34729_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rmWgckAUGT0aJ0gAea-WFAQAWWQyhNkH_view_usp_drivesdk_7ca423382a.json,d9361ac78c494139aaed77320f6f7949285639148f452b50e5ea36b21b918484,569227,31,digital_text,"Pharmaceutical forms White to yellowish tablets, marbled, round, flat with a bevelled edge. Active substance Each tablet contains 250 mcg or 500 mcg everolimus. Certain dosage strengths and dosage forms may not be available in all countries. Active moiety Everolimus Excipients Butylated hydroxytoluene (E321), magnesium stearate, lactose monohydrate, hypromellose, crospovidone, lactose anhydrous. Pharmaceutical formulations may vary between countries.",1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,"Kidney and heart transplantation Everolimus (Certican ®) is indicated for the prophylaxis of organ rejection in adult patients at low to moderate immunological risk receiving an allogeneic rena l or cardiac transplant. In kidney and heart transplantation, everolimus (Certican ®) should be used in combination with ciclosporin for microemulsion and corticosteroids. Liver transplantation Everolimus (Certican ®) is indicated for the prophylaxis of orga n rejection in adult patients receiving a hepatic transplant. In liver transplantation, everolimus (Certican ®) should be used in combination with tacrolimus and corticosteroids.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:14:19.881154+00:00
