PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY34973,"Gadoxetic acid, disodium",Primovist,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sCkbkpadXoni4DrUnLM5BrGvP1ZPp0SH/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY34973_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1sCkbkpadXoni4DrUnLM5BrGvP1ZPp0SH_view_usp_drivesdk_486104cd70.pdf,page_text/DR-XY34973_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1sCkbkpadXoni4DrUnLM5BrGvP1ZPp0SH_view_usp_drivesdk_486104cd70.json,c9a7e8df4546a45145ce55f10d50a0610dc600ece83f8f66eb8384262427dc13,568518,2,digital_text,Solution for injection. 4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS,1,1,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"This medicinal product is for diagnostic use only. Gadoxetic acid, disodium (Primovist) is a gadolinium-based contrast agent for T1-weighted magnetic resonance imaging of the liver. In dynamic and delayed imaging, Gadoxetic acid, disodium (Primovist) improves the detection of liver lesions (e.g. number, size, segmental distribution and visualization) and provides additional information regarding classification and characterization of focal liver lesions, thereby increasing diagnostic confidence.",1,1,4.1 Indication(s),high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:16:02.899302+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY34979,Paracetamol + Phenylephrine Hydrochloride + Dextromethorphan Hydrobromide,Tusedex,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PKJ2ErA6WGHpb3rYUb-kgsO4078h0jMu/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY34979_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PKJ2ErA6WGHpb3rYUb-kgsO4078h0jMu_view_usp_drivesdk_a7ca37cc6a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY34979_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PKJ2ErA6WGHpb3rYUb-kgsO4078h0jMu_view_usp_drivesdk_a7ca37cc6a.json,04c6196436c095f373d8cf242b6aee5a77e0387b786a66a7f0e9c553581cc3b6,150176,2,digital_text,"Appeared as white to off-white free flowing powder encapsulated in Empty Gelatin Capsule, size # 0 with scarlet cap and yellow body. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This product contains: Dextromethorphan Hydrobromide: acts centrally to elevate the threshold for coughing. It has no analgesic or additive properties. The onset of antitussive action occurs in 15 to 30 minutes after administration and is of long duration. Paracetamol: the analgesic action of Paracetamol involves peripheral and central influence, but the specific mechanism is as yet undetermined. Antipyretic activity is mediated through hypothalamic heat regulating centers. Paracetamol inhibits prostaglandin synthetase. Therapeutic doses of Paracetamol have negligible effects on the cardiovascular or respiratory systems; however, toxic doses may cause circulatory failure and rapid, shallow breathing. Phenylephrine Hydrochloride: is a sympathomimetic which acts predominantly on alpha receptors and has little action on beta receptors. It therefore functions as an oral nasal decongestant with minimal Central nervous system (CNS) stimulation.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T04:16:06.334879+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY35002,Pioglitazone (As Hydrochloride) + Metformin (as Hydrochloride),Actosmet,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vtE9CiA9RKj-ISUmSRpN7QnHquZ7H3R4/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY35002_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vtE9CiA9RKj-ISUmSRpN7QnHquZ7H3R4_view_usp_drivesdk_e160f3b54f.pdf,page_text/DR-XY35002_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vtE9CiA9RKj-ISUmSRpN7QnHquZ7H3R4_view_usp_drivesdk_e160f3b54f.json,6c653e2cfb7b5818d0700a2bc0f90b2e95fbf6b617431ed877e191d8e5c17031,5258341,1,digital_text,White to off-white oblong convex film coated tablet embossed 15/850 on one face CLR on the other.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Pioglitazone HCl and Metformin HCl (Actosmet) is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes who are already treated with a combination of pioglitazone and metformin or whose diabetes is not adequately controlled with metformin alone, or for those patients who have initially responded to pioglitazone alone and require additional glycemic control. Management of type 2 diabetes should also include nutritional counseling, weight reduction as needed, and exercise. These efforts are important not only in the primary treatment of type 2 diabetes, but also to maintain the efficacy of drug therapy. Important Limitations of Use Pioglitazone exerts its antihyperglycemic effect only in the presence of endogenous insulin. Pioglitazone HCl and Metformin HCl (Actosmet) should not be used to treat type 1 diabetes or diabetic ketoacidosis, as it would not be effective in these settings. Use caution in patients with liver disease [see Warnings and Precautions].",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:16:11.972652+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY3501,Sucralfate,Iselpin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Bhek4vVAfw1MaU7mJrJJOpSnb_zfJjuI/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY3501_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Bhek4vVAfw1MaU7mJrJJOpSnb_zfJjuI_view_usp_drivesdk_7f8ec9d230.pdf,page_text/DR-XY3501_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Bhek4vVAfw1MaU7mJrJJOpSnb_zfJjuI_view_usp_drivesdk_7f8ec9d230.json,dc8058fc004a3e410caf27b4669b282395b242c6730e605edf3e802a534b4ad6,168647,7,digital_text,"Sucralfate is a white, amorphous powder which is soluble in strong acids and in alkalis but practically insoluble in water and in alcohol. It is a basic, aluminum complex of sucrose octasulfate. Sucralfate has the chemical name, α-D-Glucopyranoside β-D-fructofuranosyl, octakis (hydrogen sulfate), aluminum complex. Its molecular formula is C 12HmAll6OnS8 (m and n are approximately 54 and 75 respectively, resulting in an average molecular weight of about 2086 daltons). Its chemical structure is:",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Sucralfate is indicated for the treatment of gastric and duodenal ulcer and chronic gastritis It is also indicated for the relapse prophylaxis of gastric and duodenal ulce r, and treatment of reflux oesophagitis, and the prophylaxis of stress ulcer.",1,1,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:16:15.023926+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY35026,Rosuvastatin (as calcium),Rovista,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/13omw8NLUTJ-3jZOJhSCBlcyUNzbGQvrn/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY35026_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13omw8NLUTJ-3jZOJhSCBlcyUNzbGQvrn_view_usp_drivesdk_274e1bdbc8.pdf,page_text/DR-XY35026_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13omw8NLUTJ-3jZOJhSCBlcyUNzbGQvrn_view_usp_drivesdk_274e1bdbc8.json,27a90e0f788deaf6232c312c50a036dbc85d1a3dd89f8e08b985691e896b70c3,252542,2,digital_text,"Rosuvastatin (Rovista®) 5 mg Film-Coated Tablet is available as Oval shaped biconvex Light blue color tablet, engraved “GETZ” on one side & “5” on other side. Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) 10 mg Film-Coated Tablet is available as Oval shaped purple colored biconvex tablet, engraved “GETZ” on one side & “10” on other side. Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) 20 mg Film-Coated Tablet is available as Green colored oval shaped biconvex film coated tablet, engraved “GETZ” on one side & “20” on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) should be used as an adjunct to diet when the response to diet and exercise is inadequate: Prevention of Cardiovascular Events In adult patients with an increased risk of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease based on the presence of cardiovascular disease risk markers such as an elevated hsCRP level, age, hypertension, low HCL-C, smoking or a family history of premature coronary heart disease, Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) is indicated to reduce total mortality and the risk of major cardiovascular events (cardiovascular death, stroke, MI, unstable angina, or arterial revascularization). In adult patients with hypercholesterolaemia Rosvastatin (Rovista ®) is indicated to: - reduce elevated LDL-C, total cholesterol, triglycerides and to increase HDL-cholesterol in patients with primary hypercholesterolaemia (heterozygous familial and non familial) and mixed dyslipidemia (Fredrickson Types IIa and IIb). Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) also lowers ApoB, nonHDL-C, VLDL-C, VLDL-TG, the LDL-C/ HDL-C, total C/HDL-C, nonHDL-C/ HDL-C, ApoB/ ApoA-I ratios and increases ApoA-I in these populations. Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) also lowers ApoB, nonHDL-C, VLDL-C, VLDL-TG, the LDL-C/ HDL-C, total C/HDL-C, nonHDL-C/ HDL-C, ApoB/ ApoA-1 ratios and increases ApoA-1 in these populations. - treat patient with primary dysbetalipoproteinaemia (Fredrickson Type III hyper lipoproteinaemia) - treat isolated hypertriglyceridaemia (Fredrickson Type IV hyper hyperlipidaemia). - reduce Total Cholesterol and LDL-C in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, as an adjunct to diet and other lipid lowering treatments (e.g. LDL apheresis) or alone if such treatments are unavailable. - slow or delay the progression of atherosclerosis. Children and adolescents 6 to 17 years of age: Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) is indicated to reduce the total cholesterol, LDL-C and Apo B in patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia (HeFH).",1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:16:18.129147+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY35027,,Rovista,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1kGf2QcHM2BUFWtsFUmVAYpzmQ5_UZC4s/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY35027_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kGf2QcHM2BUFWtsFUmVAYpzmQ5_UZC4s_view_usp_drivesdk_155c872c16.pdf,page_text/DR-XY35027_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kGf2QcHM2BUFWtsFUmVAYpzmQ5_UZC4s_view_usp_drivesdk_155c872c16.json,27a90e0f788deaf6232c312c50a036dbc85d1a3dd89f8e08b985691e896b70c3,252542,2,digital_text,"Rosuvastatin (Rovista®) 5 mg Film-Coated Tablet is available as Oval shaped biconvex Light blue color tablet, engraved “GETZ” on one side & “5” on other side. Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) 10 mg Film-Coated Tablet is available as Oval shaped purple colored biconvex tablet, engraved “GETZ” on one side & “10” on other side. Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) 20 mg Film-Coated Tablet is available as Green colored oval shaped biconvex film coated tablet, engraved “GETZ” on one side & “20” on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) should be used as an adjunct to diet when the response to diet and exercise is inadequate: Prevention of Cardiovascular Events In adult patients with an increased risk of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease based on the presence of cardiovascular disease risk markers such as an elevated hsCRP level, age, hypertension, low HCL-C, smoking or a family history of premature coronary heart disease, Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) is indicated to reduce total mortality and the risk of major cardiovascular events (cardiovascular death, stroke, MI, unstable angina, or arterial revascularization). In adult patients with hypercholesterolaemia Rosvastatin (Rovista ®) is indicated to: - reduce elevated LDL-C, total cholesterol, triglycerides and to increase HDL-cholesterol in patients with primary hypercholesterolaemia (heterozygous familial and non familial) and mixed dyslipidemia (Fredrickson Types IIa and IIb). Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) also lowers ApoB, nonHDL-C, VLDL-C, VLDL-TG, the LDL-C/ HDL-C, total C/HDL-C, nonHDL-C/ HDL-C, ApoB/ ApoA-I ratios and increases ApoA-I in these populations. Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) also lowers ApoB, nonHDL-C, VLDL-C, VLDL-TG, the LDL-C/ HDL-C, total C/HDL-C, nonHDL-C/ HDL-C, ApoB/ ApoA-1 ratios and increases ApoA-1 in these populations. - treat patient with primary dysbetalipoproteinaemia (Fredrickson Type III hyper lipoproteinaemia) - treat isolated hypertriglyceridaemia (Fredrickson Type IV hyper hyperlipidaemia). - reduce Total Cholesterol and LDL-C in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, as an adjunct to diet and other lipid lowering treatments (e.g. LDL apheresis) or alone if such treatments are unavailable. - slow or delay the progression of atherosclerosis. Children and adolescents 6 to 17 years of age: Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) is indicated to reduce the total cholesterol, LDL-C and Apo B in patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia (HeFH).",1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:16:21.172349+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY35028,Rosuvastatin (as calcium),Rovista,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LgU-No2fL7x4SeyhY4U7Ic7Szuoa6z3h/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY35028_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LgU-No2fL7x4SeyhY4U7Ic7Szuoa6z3h_view_usp_drivesdk_b039fbc1d0.pdf,page_text/DR-XY35028_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LgU-No2fL7x4SeyhY4U7Ic7Szuoa6z3h_view_usp_drivesdk_b039fbc1d0.json,27a90e0f788deaf6232c312c50a036dbc85d1a3dd89f8e08b985691e896b70c3,252542,2,digital_text,"Rosuvastatin (Rovista®) 5 mg Film-Coated Tablet is available as Oval shaped biconvex Light blue color tablet, engraved “GETZ” on one side & “5” on other side. Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) 10 mg Film-Coated Tablet is available as Oval shaped purple colored biconvex tablet, engraved “GETZ” on one side & “10” on other side. Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) 20 mg Film-Coated Tablet is available as Green colored oval shaped biconvex film coated tablet, engraved “GETZ” on one side & “20” on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) should be used as an adjunct to diet when the response to diet and exercise is inadequate: Prevention of Cardiovascular Events In adult patients with an increased risk of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease based on the presence of cardiovascular disease risk markers such as an elevated hsCRP level, age, hypertension, low HCL-C, smoking or a family history of premature coronary heart disease, Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) is indicated to reduce total mortality and the risk of major cardiovascular events (cardiovascular death, stroke, MI, unstable angina, or arterial revascularization). In adult patients with hypercholesterolaemia Rosvastatin (Rovista ®) is indicated to: - reduce elevated LDL-C, total cholesterol, triglycerides and to increase HDL-cholesterol in patients with primary hypercholesterolaemia (heterozygous familial and non familial) and mixed dyslipidemia (Fredrickson Types IIa and IIb). Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) also lowers ApoB, nonHDL-C, VLDL-C, VLDL-TG, the LDL-C/ HDL-C, total C/HDL-C, nonHDL-C/ HDL-C, ApoB/ ApoA-I ratios and increases ApoA-I in these populations. Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) also lowers ApoB, nonHDL-C, VLDL-C, VLDL-TG, the LDL-C/ HDL-C, total C/HDL-C, nonHDL-C/ HDL-C, ApoB/ ApoA-1 ratios and increases ApoA-1 in these populations. - treat patient with primary dysbetalipoproteinaemia (Fredrickson Type III hyper lipoproteinaemia) - treat isolated hypertriglyceridaemia (Fredrickson Type IV hyper hyperlipidaemia). - reduce Total Cholesterol and LDL-C in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, as an adjunct to diet and other lipid lowering treatments (e.g. LDL apheresis) or alone if such treatments are unavailable. - slow or delay the progression of atherosclerosis. Children and adolescents 6 to 17 years of age: Rosuvastatin (Rovista ®) is indicated to reduce the total cholesterol, LDL-C and Apo B in patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia (HeFH).",1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:16:23.923849+00:00
