PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY35140,Amphotericin B,Ampholip,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KK6uTAsExqJpbHISQ5MsmIYK1SkcRd0B/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY35140_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1KK6uTAsExqJpbHISQ5MsmIYK1SkcRd0B_view_usp_drivesdk_3ae4e417b5.pdf,page_text/DR-XY35140_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1KK6uTAsExqJpbHISQ5MsmIYK1SkcRd0B_view_usp_drivesdk_3ae4e417b5.json,87fc0c964774288169ffe767e3f9385b12e5875879583c6750b66bae26497620,210733,2,digital_text,"Amphotericin B (Ampholip) is a sterile, isotonic, pyrogen-free suspension, yellow and opaque in appearance.",1,1,Description:,"Amphotericin B (Ampholip) is indicated for the treatment of invasive fungal infections in patients who are refractory to or intolerant of conventional Amphotericin B therapy. Used for the treatment of severe systemic fungal infections including aspergillosis, blastomycosis, candidiasis, coccidioidomycosis, cryptococcosis, histoplasmosis, mucormycosis, paracoccidioidomycosis and sporotrichosis and is the usual treatment of choice in fungal endocarditis, meningitis, peritonitis, or severe respiratory tract infections.",1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:16:46.753616+00:00
