PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY35166,Lysozyme hydrochloride,Flemizyme,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LrOFjN-rx50oKM0N1VrEfAtBpf7hBcAR/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY35166_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LrOFjN-rx50oKM0N1VrEfAtBpf7hBcAR_view_usp_drivesdk_cbe7e30864.pdf,page_text/DR-XY35166_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LrOFjN-rx50oKM0N1VrEfAtBpf7hBcAR_view_usp_drivesdk_cbe7e30864.json,300b8c7600002663ede55a7e7b5fd269f635e5e8369068704ce20391fa22cc25,1069838,1,ocr,"Lysozyme hydrochloride belongs to Pregnancy Category B, meaning Flemizyme 30 mg Tablet either animal reproduction studies have not demonstrated a fetal risk White, round tablet, bisected on one side, with engraved “PL 30” on but there are no controlled studies in pregnant women; or animal the other side. reproduction studies have shown an adverse effect (other than a Flemizyme 60 mg Tablet decrease in fertility) that was not confirmed in controlled studies in women in the 1st trimester (and there is no evidence of a risk in later White to off-white round tablet, bisected on one side, with engraved ""PL 60"" on the other side. trimesters). Drugs in this category should be used in pregnancy only when clearly needed.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: FLEMIZYME (30 mg Tablet) in inflammation of the oto-rhino-laryngeal www.fda.gov.ph or email to pharmacovigilance@pascuallab.com area as what occurs in sinusitis, allergic rhinitis, pharyngitis, Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse laryngitis, tracheitis, otitis, gingivitis, pyorrhea, etc. drug reaction. FLEMIZYME (60 mg Tablet) as potentiator and synergist to antibiotics REGISTRATION NUMBER during antibiotic therapy. Flemizyme 30mg Tablet: DR-XY35166 FLEMIZYME in high doses as antiviral, in hepatitis, herpes zoster, Flemizyme 60mg Tablet: DR-XY33707 herpes simplex, chicken pox and warts. Date of First Authorization",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T04:17:00.573786+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY35200,Fluticasone furoate,Avamys,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sXsA9X8uvhS8Tl7yM-gsjre6vaFskx1X/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY35200_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1sXsA9X8uvhS8Tl7yM-gsjre6vaFskx1X_view_usp_drivesdk_2bb9bc065d.pdf,page_text/DR-XY35200_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1sXsA9X8uvhS8Tl7yM-gsjre6vaFskx1X_view_usp_drivesdk_2bb9bc065d.json,9fecb93f06b89839a51133ce3042f21d2b7c3dd1a2607c2f937d82eb0929a8c4,1250829,7,digital_text,"Fluticasone furoate (Avamys) Nasal Spray is a white, uniform suspension contained in an amber glass bottle, fitted with a metering (50 microliters) atomising spray pump. This inner pack is incorporated within a predominantly offwhite plastic device with a blue side-actuated lever and a lid which contains a stopper. Each spray of the suspension delivers approximately 27.5 micrograms of micronised Fluticasone furoate as an exdevice dose.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Adults and Adolescents (12 years and older) Treatment of the nasal symptoms (rhinorrhea, nasal congestion, nasal itching and sneezing) and ocular symptoms (itching/burning, tearing/watering, and redness of the eye) of seasonal allergic rhinitis. Treatment of the nasal symptoms (rhinorrhea, nasal congestion, nasal itching and sneezing) of perennial allergic rhinitis Children (2 to 11 years) Treatment of the nasal symptoms (rhinorrhea, nasal congestion, nasal itching and sneezing) of seasonal and perennial allergic rhinitis.",3,3,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:17:05.041586+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY35220,Ascorbic Acid (as Sodium Ascorbate),Carezee,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GXZMd_8BlGI5btELAG3j-wprs5wTaSHq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY35220_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GXZMd_8BlGI5btELAG3j-wprs5wTaSHq_view_usp_drivesdk_29a694b29e.pdf,page_text/DR-XY35220_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GXZMd_8BlGI5btELAG3j-wprs5wTaSHq_view_usp_drivesdk_29a694b29e.json,5b823d99502ce0d3f366ae229da619a8aa3daf2b33b6e10abc2e430d232e4a28,284441,1,ocr,"Carezee syrup is a clear, orange to brown orange syrup with lemon odor and flavor. Carezee drops is a clear, orange to brown orange syrup has sweet, slightly salty taste with lemon flavor and odor. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This product contains Vitamin C. Vitamin C helps the body’s natural defense against damaging free radicals. Free radicals are highly reactive and unstable chemicals generated during normal body activities that require oxygen and after exposure to UV light, cigarette smoke and various pollutants, Vitamin C forms part of the body's natural immune system and stimulates the activity. of specialized white blood cells which inhibit harmful bacteria and viruses. Vitamin C also needed for the formation of the protein, collagen. It is important in the formation of bones, teeth f cartilage and skin and promotes faster healing. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE See formulation above WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? For the treatment and prevention of Vitamin C deficiency. For body resistance against stress, common colds and other infections HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THE MEDICINE? Orally, once a day or as prescribed by the physician For Carezee syrup: Children - % to 1 teaspoon (2.5mL - SmL. Adults - 2 to 4 teaspoonfuls (10mL - 20mL) For Carezee drops: Infants - 0.6m (60mg) daily WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you are allergic to any-ingredient of the product UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS Prolonged intake of Vitamin C in excess of 2 g/day may /ead to nausea, abdominal cramps, diarrhea and nose bleeds. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOODS SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? The amount of Vitamin C in the product is not expected to interact with food or medicines. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, just give the next dose and the subsequent doses at the usual recommended schedule. Da not double the dose unless recommended by a doctor HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THE MEDICINE? * Keep the product out of reach and sight of children * Store at temperatures not exceeding 30° * Protect from light * Always keep container tightly closed SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE There is no information regarding overdosage of Vitamin C WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE USED MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE ¢ Should be given with care to patients with hyperoxaluria ¢ Do not use after the expiry date on the labe * Do not give more than the recommended dose WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? if any undesirable effect occurs AVAILABILITY Syrup: Boston round amber glass bottle x 120ml (Box of 1's} Drops: Amber Bottle x 30 mt with Aluminum Cap, Medicine Dropper. DATE OF REVISION OF PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET (PIL); February 12, 2018 Carezee Oral Drops: Registration no. DR-XY35220 Valid until] December 10, 2021 Carezee Syrup: Registration no. DRHR-881 Valid until October 8, 2019. ADR Reporting Statement “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph” Patient must seek medical attention immediately at the = sign of any adverse drug reaction Manufactured for: PHARMACARE PRODUCTS CORPORATION SB Residences Unit 2&3 302 P. Dela Cruz St., San Bartolome, Novaliches Quezon City Manufactured by: LA CROSEUS PHARMA INC Brgy. Sto. Tomas Bifian, Laguna [Page 2]",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T04:17:11.803392+00:00
