PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY35911,Omeprazole,Zefxon,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RNe_oga1WjB6BRthmjecSnAcM9ZE-l0a/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY35911_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RNe_oga1WjB6BRthmjecSnAcM9ZE-l0a_view_usp_drivesdk_942bf863b4.pdf,page_text/DR-XY35911_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RNe_oga1WjB6BRthmjecSnAcM9ZE-l0a_view_usp_drivesdk_942bf863b4.json,f959da91b603b7aef155365a2f657ee2e109a3b0c5c5874f477c491c7b9528db,102326,1,digital_text,"Dry Product Dry, white lyophilized cake or powder, filled in colorless vial Reconstituted Product Clear and free from visible particle PHARMACODYNAMICS Omeprazole injection is a proton acid pump inhibitor which reduces gastric acid secretion by specific action; inhibition of the enzyme H+, K+-ATPase (The proton pump) in the parietal cell, the final step of acid secretion; thus inhibition of acid secretion occurs. PHARMACOKINETICS Absorption Maximum plasma concentration is reached 0.5 to 3.5 hours after administration. Distribution The apparent volume of distribution in healthy subjects is approximately 0.3 Ukg and a similar value is also seen in patients with renal insufficiency. In the elderly and in patients with hepatic insufficiency, the volume of distribution is slightly decreased. The plasma protein binding of omeprazole is about 95%. Metabolism Omeprazole is completely metabolised by the cytochrome P450 system, mainly in the liver. No metabolite has been found to have any effect on gastric acid secretion. Almost 80% of an intravenously given dose is excreted as metabolites in the urine, and the remainder is found in the faeces, primarily originating from biliary secretion. Excretion The average half-life of the terminal phase of the plasma concentration-time curve following IV 0.6 Umin. There is no change in half-life during treatment. Elimination of omeprazole is unchanged in patients with reduced renal function. The elimination half-life is increased in patients with impaired liver function, but omeprazole has not shown any accumulation with once daily oral dosing.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Omeprazole (Zefxon) injection is indicated for alternative use to oral medication in - Duodenal ulcer - Gastric ulcer - Reflux oesophagitis - Zollinger-Ellison syndrome - Aspiration prophylaxis,1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:19:22.018677+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY35916,Methimazole,Methazol,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1m1VlRVkTX7E-7N9nTd786tgtaqbAJEHq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY35916_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1m1VlRVkTX7E-7N9nTd786tgtaqbAJEHq_view_usp_drivesdk_faf8605b3a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY35916_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1m1VlRVkTX7E-7N9nTd786tgtaqbAJEHq_view_usp_drivesdk_faf8605b3a.json,7b4fda66446b628ab4b0fac14861213ba30df5bd1809aa288edd8a295a1276d5,2629031,1,ocr,"Methimazole 5 mg Tablet (Methazol) is a white to off-white, 9.5 mm round tablet, hexabeveled on one side and beveled-edged, scored",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Methimazole (Methazol) is used in the management of hyperthyroidism, including the treatment of Graves’ disease, used in the preparation of hyperthyroid patients for thyroidectomy, as an adjunct to radio-iodine therapy and the treatment of thyroid storm.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T04:19:31.145481+00:00
