PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY36586,Cetirizine Dihydrochloride + Phenylephrine Hydrochloride,Alnix Plus,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1G6qNPZZ9SriYH7jZ2APY2UOX4S9VfgmY/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY36586_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1G6qNPZZ9SriYH7jZ2APY2UOX4S9VfgmY_view_usp_drivesdk_7020db561f.pdf,page_text/DR-XY36586_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1G6qNPZZ9SriYH7jZ2APY2UOX4S9VfgmY_view_usp_drivesdk_7020db561f.json,958a9127347969d7b1f7dfc7c02fe198038aaa4f65ba409ac60c35ebdd295ca2,200615,1,digital_text,"A white, round, biconvex, film-coated tablet, plain on both sides. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This medicine contains cetirizine dihydrochloride and phenylephrine HCl. Cetirizine Dihydrochloride, an antiallergy, blocks the action of histamine, a substance that causes allergic symptoms. Cetirizine Dihydrochloride is less likely to cause drowsiness and dizziness than the older class of anti-allergy medicines. Phenylephrine HCl, a nasal decongestant, clears obstructed air passages and nasal sinuses due to congestion making breathing easier. It also reduces postnasal drip. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T04:24:55.804991+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY36620,Phenylephrine hydrochloride + Brompheniramine maleate,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/19rfPKO7yywOm4QcxvHS8J0WDye3nBU5w/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY36620_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19rfPKO7yywOm4QcxvHS8J0WDye3nBU5w_view_usp_drivesdk_f058b6e77b.pdf,page_text/DR-XY36620_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19rfPKO7yywOm4QcxvHS8J0WDye3nBU5w_view_usp_drivesdk_f058b6e77b.json,8ec7cf84dfa4946619ae22e2a194cc67d7c1fdb5885ab3eb7b33665c7169d2da,862892,1,ocr,"and "" hi use of like ‘a dopamine receptor agonist bromocriptine, Light-green, round, biconvex tablet, bisected on one side and plain on the other side id may reduce y beta-blocking dr 198. The risk of ind other side effects may be increased. Clear orange colored syrup with orange flavor and sweet fruit taste Syrup for oral An isolated report describes a fatal reaction in a pal gi lol J but concurrent ly to be uneventful. Clear orange colored syrup with orange flavor and sweet fruit taste er t alkaloid: h "" r nd effects of \d other with",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTIONS,"Foods, Drugs, Devices, and fa imeem prohibits pensing ain deeweNpHaCEEoes means pcmeeesesecnn: Hypertension i adver dru action, con: It ur doctor immediately and e il us at customerrelations@dynadrug.com Us Concurrent use or use within 2 weeks of monoamine oxidase inhibitors (MAO!) For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to FOA wow. fda.gov.ph Premature infants and neonates",1,1,CONTRAINDICATIONS,low,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T04:25:05.040688+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY36632,Levetiracetam,Keppra,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1naAhZJXW2Kknk_xF_FXG1mNOBeUYfr7v/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY36632_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1naAhZJXW2Kknk_xF_FXG1mNOBeUYfr7v_view_usp_drivesdk_68996b7302.pdf,page_text/DR-XY36632_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1naAhZJXW2Kknk_xF_FXG1mNOBeUYfr7v_view_usp_drivesdk_68996b7302.json,d5aec24f78d6215e5c1cbad0386dde95365a9c678d3bd9d4008880813cc64779,178893,9,digital_text,"Levetiracetam (Keppra) 250 mg Film-Coated Tablet: Each blue, oblong, debossed with code ‘ucb’ and ‘250’ on one side, film coated tablet contains 250 mg of levetiracetam. The score li ne is only to facilitate breaking for ease of swallowing and not to divide into equal doses. Levetiracetam (Keppra) 500 mg Film-Coated Tablet: Each yellow, oblong, debossed with code ‘ucb’ and ‘500’ on one side, film coated tablet contains 500 mg of levetiracetam. The score li ne is only to facilitate breaking for ease of swallowing and not to divide into equal doses. Levetiracetam (Keppra) 1 g Film-Coated Tablet: Each white, scored, oblong, debossed with code ‘ucb’ and ‘1000’ on one side, film coated tablet contains 1 g of levetiracetam. The score line is only to facilitate breaking for ease of swallowing and not to divide into equal doses. Levetiracetam (Keppra) 100 mg/mL Oral Solution: Each mL of clear liquid oral solution contains 100 mg of levetiracetam. Levetiracetam (Keppra) 500 mg/5 mL Concentrate for Solution for IV Infusion: Each mL contains 100 mg Levetiracetam. The 5 mL vial contains 500 mg of Levetiracetam.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Levetiracetam is indicated as monotherapy in the treatment of:  partial onset seizures with or without secondary generalisation in adults and adolescents from 16 years of age with newly diagnosed epilepsy. Levetiracetam is indicated as adjunctive therapy in the treatment of:  partial onset seizures with or without secondary generalisation in adults, adolescents and children from 4 years of age with epilepsy  myoclonic seizures in adults and adolescents from 12 years of age with juvenile myoclonic epilepsy,  primary generalised tonic-clonic seizures in adults and adolescents from 4 years of age with idiopathic generalised epilepsy. Levetiracetam concentrate is an alternative for patients (adults and children from 4 years of age) when oral administration is temporarily not feasible.",3,3,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:25:08.502697+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY36639,Paracetamol + Propyphenazone + Caffeine,Saridon Triple Action,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Hfq5y_oT1hSau0Hh0uc6BxB0-1SFW-6Z/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY36639_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Hfq5y_oT1hSau0Hh0uc6BxB0-1SFW-6Z_view_usp_drivesdk_85de082b78.pdf,page_text/DR-XY36639_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Hfq5y_oT1hSau0Hh0uc6BxB0-1SFW-6Z_view_usp_drivesdk_85de082b78.json,c70d337ee35647b9369cde92185661c113f4482366acbe2f68542d687d5f62ed,702236,1,digital_text,"Paracetamol / Propyphenazone / Caﬀeine (Saridon Triple Action) is an analgesic/antipyretic. 3. What is in the Medicine? 450 mg tablet: Each tablet contains Paracetamol.............................250 mg Propyphenazone...................150 mg Caﬀeine.......................................50 mg 4. Strength of the Medicine Paracetamol 250 mg / Propyphenazone 150 mg / Caﬀeine 50 mg 5. What is the Medicine used for? • For fast and eﬀective relief of mild to severe headaches • For the relief of pain such as headache, toothache, menstrual discomfort, postoperative and rheumatic pain • For the relief of pain and fever associated with colds and /f_lu 6. How much and how often should you use this Medicine? Single dose. Adults: 1-2 tablets Adolescents aged 12-16 years: 1 tablet If necessary, up to three single doses may be taken within 24 hours. The tablets should be taken with ample water or other /f_luid. Should not be taken for more than one week or at dose higher than those recommended, except as directed by a doctor. Patients with hepatic impairment: Paracetamol is contraindicated in patients with severe hepatic insuﬃciency (Child-Pugh>9). Paracetamol should be used with caution in patients with mild to moderate hepatic insuﬃciency (Child-Pugh <9). Patients with renal impairment: Paracetamol should be used with particular caution in patients with severe renal failure. Dose adjustment may be necessary in patients with impaired renal function. 7. When should you not take this Medicine? Saridon Triple Action should not be used if any of the following conditions is present: • Allergy to pyrazolones or related compounds (hypersensitivity to phenazone, propyphenazone, aminophenazone, metamizole-containing products) • Allergy to phenylbutazone-containing products • Known hypersensitivity to paracetamol, acetylsalicylic acid or proven allergy to caﬀeine • Inherited de/f_iciency of glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase (evidenced by hemolytic anemia) • Acute hepatic porphyria Special caution should be taken (lowering of the dosage and/or spacing out of the doses) in the following conditions: • Impaired hepatic function (e.g. in cases of chronic alcohol abuse or hepatitis) • Impaired renal function • Gilbert’s syndrome (/f_luctuating benign jaundice secondary to glucoronyl-transferase de/f_iciency) • Hematopoetic dysfunction Saridon Triple Action should not be given to infants or children under 12 years of age. Pregnancy and Lactation: • Category C • It is recommended that Saridon Triple Action should not be used during pregnancy, particularly in the /f_irst trimester and in the /f_inal six weeks. • Saridon Triple Action should not be used by nursing women. 8. Care that should be taken when taking this Medicine? • Should not be taken regularly for a prolonged period, except as directed by a doctor. • Prolonged intake of paracetamol-containing analgesics resulting in high cumulative doses may in rare instances lead to analgesic nephropathy and largely irreversible renal insuﬃciency. • Very rare cases of serious skin reactions have been reported. In the event of skin reddening, rash blisters or peeling, discontinue paracetamol use and seek medical attention immediately. • Continual use of analgesics for the treatment of headache may itself lead to chronic headaches. • Special caution for patients with asthma, chronic rhinitis or chronic urticaria, particularly those hypersensitive to other anti-in/f_lammatory agents. • There have been isolated reports of asthma attacks and anaphylactic reaction associated with propyphenazone and paracetamol-containing preparations in susceptible individuals. • Should not be used after the expiry date shown in the pack. • Ability to Drive: Unlikely to produce an impairment of driving performance or performance related to driving. 9. Undesirable Eﬀects of this Medicine • Allergic reactions such as skin rash and urticaria – occasional • Hypersensitivity reactions with symptoms such as pruritus, erythema, urticaria, angioedema, dyspnea or asthma – very rare • Isolated reports of anaphylactoid reactions or anaphylactic shocks • Isolated cases of thrombocytopenia, leucopenia, agranulocytosis and pancytopenia associated with paracetamol and propyphenazone have been reported. 10. What other Medicine or Food should be avoided while taking this Medicine? Hypnotics, Anti-epileptic drugs (phenobarbital, phenytoin, carbamazepine), Rifampicin, Propanthelin, Metoclopropamide, Chloramphenicol, Zidovudine, Barbiturates, Antihistaminics, Benzodiazepines, Oral contraceptives, Cimetidine, Disul/f_iram, Theophylline, Ephedrine, Smoking, Alcohol. 11. What should you do if you miss a dose? No available information. 12. Signs and Symptoms of Overdose Following overdose, symptoms of paracetamol poisoning often appear within 24-48 hours, but may be delayed beyond this time. Symptoms: Poisoning is more likely to occur in the presence of alcohol. Liver damage (hepatocellular necrosis) and impairment of liver function may occur and may progress to hepatic coma. Clinical indications of liver damage may not manifest until 24 days following overdose. Hypokalemia and metabolic acidosis (including lactic acidosis) may also develop in the setting of acute and/or chronic overdose. There have been isolated reports of acute renal failure following paracetamol overdose. 13. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? Management of overdose: The cytotoxic eﬀects can be lessened by intravenous administration of sulfhydryl compounds such as cysteamine or N-acetylcysteine, if possible within eight hours of ingestion of the overdose. 14. How should you keep this Medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 25oC. 15. When should you consult your doctor? If symptoms persist, consult your doctor. Instructions for Use/Handling: The tablets should be taken with ample water or other /f_luid. Manufacturer: PT. Bayer Indonesia Jalan Raya Jakarta Bogor KM 32, Cisalak, Kec. Sukmajaya, Kota Depok, Jawa Barat, Indonesia Marketing Authorization Holder: Bayer Philippines, Inc. 8th Floor, Science Hub, Tower 1, Campus Avenue Corner Turin Street, McKinley Hill Cyberpark, Pinagsama, Taguig City At the /f_irst sign of any adverse drug reaction, patient must seek medical attention immediately. Report any suspected adverse drug reaction or product complaint to MedInfoCH-PH@bayer.com or drugsafety.philippines@bayer.com or to the Philippines FDA at adr@fda.gov.ph. If you want to report a product complaint or side eﬀect, please contact your health care professional or the Philippines FDA at adr@fda.gov.ph. Inquiries can also be directed to: Bayer Philippines, Inc. Taguig City, Philippines E-mail: MedInfoCH-PH@bayer.com drugsafety.philippines@bayer.com Registration Number: DR-XY36639 Date of First Authorization: 11 September 2009 Date of Revision of Patient Information Lea/f_let: July 2024 (Based on Paracetamol CCDS version 3 dated 22 May 2020) 117 117 117 117 PT. BAYER INDONESIA ARTWORK DEVELOPMENT COMMERCIAL Material Information Component Type : LFL T Material Number : 91141250 Pharmacode : 117 Pack-Mat Supplier : GPI/PURA Artwork Agency : AGP History 00 / 08/07/24 : TL032620, Revise as per comment from country 01 / 11/07/24 : Revise as per comment from country 02 / 11/07/24 : Adding period after “/f_luid” and “overdose”, adding comma after “Street” Material Speci/f_ication Dimension : 140 x 190 mm Material : HVS 60 gsm Product Information Product Name : Saridon Dossage Form (EFF, FCT, Others) : Plain tablet Pack Size : 120 s ; 10s Market : PH SKU : 80483660; 87426327 Change Request : TL032620 Replacement Artwork (for TL) : 89955874 Coating Type : WB Varnish Color 1 Black UV Varnish Matt Varnish Calendering Embossing : Yes No Hot Stamp/Hot Foil : Braille Yes No Yes No FOLDED Remark : Cut, B1-B2 Vertical 2x (Folded) UNFOLDED Non Coating Color 2 N/A Color 3 N/A Color 4 N/A Color 5 N/A N/A Color 6 N/A Color 7 N/A Color 8 N/A Carton Finishing: Technical & Non Printing Items: Lea/f_let Type : [Page 2]",1,1,2. Description of the Product,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T04:25:11.589463+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY36674,Cefepime (As Hydrochloride),Zepime,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mnr0djPPR5xAqydcX78BCj7nHclV92YQ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY36674_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mnr0djPPR5xAqydcX78BCj7nHclV92YQ_view_usp_drivesdk_995dbe7580.pdf,page_text/DR-XY36674_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mnr0djPPR5xAqydcX78BCj7nHclV92YQ_view_usp_drivesdk_995dbe7580.json,71c8a3199c79068a3618575359cfd57fc5adcd57cca1d989a432532a9705aea1,506184,4,digital_text,"Cefepime is a white to oﬀ-white, non-hygroscopic, crystalline powder. Freely soluble in water. Store in airtight containers and protect from light.",3,3,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Cefepime is a fourth-generation cephalosporin antibiotic used in the treatment of infections due to susceptible organisms. They include infections of the urinary tract, respiratory tract, and skin.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:25:15.429960+00:00
