PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY36685,Zylet,Loteprednol Etabonate /Tobramycin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1q3TtN1fkua_Fx8cxRH47Y_EGXYjRfU1D/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY36685_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1q3TtN1fkua_Fx8cxRH47Y_EGXYjRfU1D_view_usp_drivesdk_bb14b0e0c7.pdf,page_text/DR-XY36685_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1q3TtN1fkua_Fx8cxRH47Y_EGXYjRfU1D_view_usp_drivesdk_bb14b0e0c7.json,f22c921e7f744e250cbaae6abd6f8164706e42445de76859d00cc7a1a6fd699f,280319,2,digital_text,"Loteprednol etabonate + Tobramycin (Zylet) Ophthalmic Suspension is a sterile, multiple dose topical anti-inflammatory cortico - steroid and antibiotic combination for ophthalmic use. Loteprednol etabonate + Tobramycin (Zylet) is a white to off-white milky suspension. The chemical structures of loteprednol etabonate and tobramycin are shown below.Loteprednol etabonate: C24H31ClO7 Mol. Wt. 466.96 Chemical name: chloromethyl 17 α-[(ethoxycarbonyl)oxy]-11 β-hydroxy-3-oxoandrosta-1,4-diene-17 β -carboxylate Tobramycin: C18H37N5O9 Mol. Wt. 467.52 Chemical Name: O-3-Amino-3-deoxy-α-D-glucopyranosy1-(1→ 4)-O- [2,6-diamino-2,3,6-trideoxy-α-D-ribo-hexopyranosyl- (1→ 6)] -2-deoxystreptamine",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"Loteprednol etabonate + Tobramycin (Zylet) is indicated for steroid-responsive inflammatory ocular conditions for which a corti - costeroid is indicated and where superficial bacterial ocular infection or a risk of bacterial ocular infection exists. Ocular steroids are indicated in inflammatory conditions of the palpebral and bulbar conjunctiva, cornea and anterior segment of the globe such as allergic conjunctivitis, acne rosacea, superficial punctate keratitis, herpes zoster keratitis, iritis, cyclitis, and where the inherent risk of steroid use in certain infective conjunctivitides is accepted to obtain a diminution in edema and inflammation. They are also indicated in chronic anterior uveitis and corneal injury from chemical, radiation or thermal burns, or penetration of foreign bodies. The use of a combination drug with an anti-infective component is indicated where the risk of superficial ocular infection is high or where there is an expectation that potentially dangerous numbers of bacteria will be present in the eye. The particular anti-infective drug in this product (tobramycin) is active against the following common bacterial eye pathogens: Staphylococci, including S. aureus and S. epidermidis (coagulase-positive and coagulase-negative), including penicillin-resistant strains. Streptococci, including some of the Group A-beta-hemolytic species, some nonhemolytic species, and some Streptococcus pneumoniae. Pseudomonas aeruginosa, Escherichia coli, Klebsiella pneumoniae, Enterobacter aerogenes, Proteus mirabilis, Morganella morganii, most Proteus vulgaris strains , Haemophilus influenzae, and H. aegyptius, Moraxella lacunata, Acinetobacter calcoaceticus and some Neisseria species.",1,1,INDICATIONS AND USAGE:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:25:21.692265+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY36700,Montelukast (as sodium),Airokast,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Ug39u04Bw2NWenM8ZD8P7hV-LnVbgdGO/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY36700_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Ug39u04Bw2NWenM8ZD8P7hV-LnVbgdGO_view_usp_drivesdk_9ab2e7cf96.pdf,page_text/DR-XY36700_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Ug39u04Bw2NWenM8ZD8P7hV-LnVbgdGO_view_usp_drivesdk_9ab2e7cf96.json,3303ec650b6487251ce33233fae8ce2533abe75b1f9b07a13baef65a668ee30e,429292,2,digital_text,"MONTELUKAST (Airokast) is a selective and orally active leukotriene receptor antagonist that specifically inhibits the cysteinyl leukotriene CysLT1 receptor. MONTELUKAST (Airokast) is described chemically as [R-(E)]-1-[[[1-[3-[2-(7-chloro-2-quinolinyl)ethenyl]phenyl]-3-[2-(1-hydroxy-1- methylethyl)phenyl]propyl]thio]methyl]cyclopropane acetic acid, monosodium salt. The empirical formula is C35H35ClNNaO3S, and its molecular weight is 608.18. Montelukast sodium is a hygroscopic, optically active, white to off-white powder. Montelukast sodium is freely soluble in ethanol, methanol, and water and practically insoluble in acetonitrile. Montelukast (Airokast) is pink with mottling, round, biconvex, plain on one side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Used in the management of chronic asthma.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:25:24.993906+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY36702,Montelukast (as sodium),Airokast,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/13-0_RM21s3nAL7AC__xuB_i7Nr0FRUjr/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY36702_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13-0_RM21s3nAL7AC__xuB_i7Nr0FRUjr_view_usp_drivesdk_0784a77dfd.pdf,page_text/DR-XY36702_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13-0_RM21s3nAL7AC__xuB_i7Nr0FRUjr_view_usp_drivesdk_0784a77dfd.json,e4305dfa831551e43e2967fd849700df3dece538c29097ad86e8e088fee245aa,430818,2,digital_text,"MONTELUKAST (Airokast) is a selective and orally active leukotriene receptor antagonist that specifically inhibits the cysteinyl leukotriene CysLT1 receptor. MONTELUKAST (Airokast) is described chemically as [R-(E)]-1-[[[1-[3-[2-(7-chloro-2-quinolinyl)ethenyl]phenyl]-3-[2-(1-hydroxy-1- methylethyl)phenyl]propyl]thio]methyl]cyclopropane acetic acid, monosodium salt. The empirical formula is C35H35ClNNaO3S, and its molecular weight is 608.18. Montelukast sodium is a hygroscopic, optically active, white to off-white powder. Montelukast sodium is freely soluble in ethanol, methanol, and water and practically insoluble in acetonitrile. Montelukast (Airokast) ia brownish-yellow film-coated tablet, round, biconvex, plain on one side and bisected on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Uesd in the management of chronic asthma.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:25:27.816489+00:00
