PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY36722,Amlodipine (as besilate),Amlocare,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/14Ang89COJYrZI2FCllMvFfSX3AD49MUy/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY36722_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14Ang89COJYrZI2FCllMvFfSX3AD49MUy_view_usp_drivesdk_78eefce599.pdf,page_text/DR-XY36722_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14Ang89COJYrZI2FCllMvFfSX3AD49MUy_view_usp_drivesdk_78eefce599.json,cf508f620ac58289117c0fe5a7aafa98b6a153f8811edf87dcbea2f6b8e75d9d,804888,1,digital_text,"A white or almost white powder. Slightly soluble in water and in isopropyl alcohol; sparingly soluble in dehydrated alcohol; freely soluble in methyl alcohol. Store in airtight containers. Protect from light. Amlodipine (as Besilate), USP ..........................10 mg Amlodipine is a dihydropyridine blocker. It is a peripheral and coronary vasodilator but unlike the blockers Verapamil or Diltiazem, has little or no effect on cardiac conduction and negative inotropic activity is rarely seen at therapeutic doses. Administration results primarily in vasodilation, with reduced peripheral resistance, blood pressure, and afterload, increased coronary blood , and a increase in heart rate. This in turn results in an increase in myocardial oxygen supply and cardiac output. It has no antiarrhythmic activity. Amlodipine maybe even more selective than Nifedipine for vascular smooth muscle. Most of the dihydropyridine blockers are chiral compounds used as racemic mixtures. Each ablet contains:",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Increased Angina or Myocardial Infarction Amlodipine (Amlocare) is contraindicated in patients with known sensitivity to Amlodipine. Hypotension,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:25:59.406970+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY36724,Levofloxacin (as hemihydrate),Quiflox,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/18jkmfdzN9h59NgMwT_NrUG7-0Zv7n-xO/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY36724_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18jkmfdzN9h59NgMwT_NrUG7-0Zv7n-xO_view_usp_drivesdk_69b48066bb.pdf,page_text/DR-XY36724_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18jkmfdzN9h59NgMwT_NrUG7-0Zv7n-xO_view_usp_drivesdk_69b48066bb.json,effc1135121161e60e5db996930649679ca6d0813e2c1d8b1835fe49c9c3d977,499773,1,digital_text,,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"*Levofloxacin has been shown to be active against Bacillus anthracis both in vitro and by use of plasma levels as a surrogate marker in a rhesus monkey for anthrax (post- exposure). Treatment of wide range of infection caused by Gram-positive and Gram-negative Levofloxacin is rapidly and almost completely absorbed following oral administration with peak plasma concentrations achieved within an hour of a dose. It is distributed into body tissues including the bronchial mucosa and lungs, but penetration into Cerebrospinal Fluid is relatively poor. Levofloxacin is approximately 30 to 40% bound to plasma proteins. It is only metabolized to a small degree to inactive metabolites. The elimination half-life of levofloxacin is 6 to 8 hours, although this may be prolonged in patients with renal impairment. Levofloxacin is excreted largely unchanged, primarily in the urine. It is not removed by hemodialysis or peritoneal dialysis. organism e.g., lower respiratory tract and skin infection, typhoid and paratyphoid fever and urinary tract infection, prophylaxis for meningococcal meningitis and surgical infections. Known hypersensitivity to levofloxacin, other quinolones or to any component of the product.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T04:26:02.319896+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY36725,Levofloxacin (as hemihydrate),Quiflox,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MW4903yzH18tIjJippd_eXS-lqBR30xv/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY36725_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MW4903yzH18tIjJippd_eXS-lqBR30xv_view_usp_drivesdk_0de238a2b8.pdf,page_text/DR-XY36725_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MW4903yzH18tIjJippd_eXS-lqBR30xv_view_usp_drivesdk_0de238a2b8.json,c3bd965e15f5482010d1b917902d57bf184c1812d86e1a9d8d2afecb9993fa63,499772,1,digital_text,,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"*Levofloxacin has been shown to be active against Bacillus anthracis both in vitro and by use of plasma levels as a surrogate marker in a rhesus monkey for anthrax (post- exposure). Treatment of wide range of infection caused by Gram-positive and Gram-negative Levofloxacin is rapidly and almost completely absorbed following oral administration with peak plasma concentrations achieved within an hour of a dose. It is distributed into body tissues including the bronchial mucosa and lungs, but penetration into Cerebrospinal Fluid is relatively poor. Levofloxacin is approximately 30 to 40% bound to plasma proteins. It is only metabolized to a small degree to inactive metabolites. The elimination half-life of levofloxacin is 6 to 8 hours, although this may be prolonged in patients with renal impairment. Levofloxacin is excreted largely unchanged, primarily in the urine. It is not removed by hemodialysis or peritoneal dialysis. organism e.g., lower respiratory tract and skin infection, typhoid and paratyphoid fever and urinary tract infection, prophylaxis for meningococcal meningitis and surgical infections. Known hypersensitivity to levofloxacin, other quinolones or to any component of the product.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T04:26:05.544150+00:00
