PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY37522,Levocetirizine Dihydrochloride,Xyzal,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bOZ5visf6q167E-duJ-YfJDUHydpXRA8/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY37522_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bOZ5visf6q167E-duJ-YfJDUHydpXRA8_view_usp_drivesdk_8757eb9c03.pdf,page_text/DR-XY37522_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bOZ5visf6q167E-duJ-YfJDUHydpXRA8_view_usp_drivesdk_8757eb9c03.json,17acffd1628731b51dbb356e391f8604307e78376d8d0ff3dc2ad0f1ea00b84d,242164,9,digital_text_and_ocr,"Levocetirizine dihydrochloride (Xyzal) 5 mg Tablet: Each white to off-white, oval, film-coated tablet with a Y logo on one side, contains 5 mg of levocetirizine as dihydrochloride. Levocetirizine dihydrochloride (Xyzal) 5 mg/mL Solution (Oral Drops): Each mL of clear and colourless liquid solution contains 5 mg of levocetirizine as dihydrochloride. Levocetirizine dihydrochloride (Xyzal) 500 mcg/mL Oral Solution: Each mL of clear and colourless liquid solution contains 500mcg of levocetirizine as dihydrochloride. EXCIPIENTS Levocetirizine dihydrochloride, 5 mg, film-coated tablet Microcrystalline cellulose, Lactose monohydrate, Colloidal anhydrous silica, Magnesium stearate, Hypromellose, Titanium dioxide, Macrogol 400 Levocetirizine dihydrochloride, 5 mg/ml, oral drops, solution Sodium acetate, Acetic acid, Propylene glycol, Glycerol 85%, Methyl parahydroxybenzoate, Propyl parahydroxybenzoate, Saccharin sodium, Purified water Levocetirizine dihydrochloride, 500 mcg/mL, oral solution Sodium acetate, Acetic acid, Methyl parahydroxybenzoate (E218), Propyl parahydroxybenzoate (E216), Glycerol 85%, Maltitol, Saccharin sodium, Tutti frutti flavour, Purified water",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,For the symptomatic treatment of: • allergic rhinitis (including persistent allergic rhinitis) • urticaria,3,3,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T04:33:12.962105+00:00
