PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY37948,Cefotaxime As Sodium,Cefogram,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1k0XDKQ45HTBsaN2L9wIwyHwECDi90jda/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY37948_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1k0XDKQ45HTBsaN2L9wIwyHwECDi90jda_view_usp_drivesdk_0366454d82.pdf,page_text/DR-XY37948_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1k0XDKQ45HTBsaN2L9wIwyHwECDi90jda_view_usp_drivesdk_0366454d82.json,7ded52659c6e050a50a309dd031ef3657162800fc213a9cf7a67f765f08f7da3,450035,1,digital_text,"An off-white pale yellowish powder 1.05 of monograph substance is approximately equivalent to 1G of Cefotaxime. Freely soluble in water, particularly insoluble In organic solvents. Cefotaxime is a third generation cephalosporins antibiotic with an extended spectrum of activity and increased potency against Gram-negative bacteria including the Enterobacteriaceae, Haemophilus influenza, Morella (Brahamella) catarrhalis, and Neissena spp. But only moderate activity against Pseudomonas spp. Its active metabolite desacylacefotaxime is given by injections the sodium salt. Adverse effects are similar to those for all cephalosporins, including hypersensitivity reactions. There is some risk of colonization and superinfection with resistant organism.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"Cefotaxime is indicated in the treatment of serious infections, either before the infecting organism has been identified or when caused by bacteria of established sensitivity, including osteomyelitis, septicemia, bacterial endocarditis, meningitis, and peritonitis and other serious bacterial infections suitable for parenteral antibiotic therapy.",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:36:47.765777+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY37962,Nebivolol (as hydrochloride),Toricard-5,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1jhyL7EXWAUggkkrpCUb3UTkTByZKxie-/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY37962_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jhyL7EXWAUggkkrpCUb3UTkTByZKxie-_view_usp_drivesdk_a3d8b437f5.pdf,page_text/DR-XY37962_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jhyL7EXWAUggkkrpCUb3UTkTByZKxie-_view_usp_drivesdk_a3d8b437f5.json,2ddb17c64567c9604be9a164b77ba392f9d55749e246a847f05ca1ae88a49dd0,533848,1,digital_text,"Nebivolol (as Hydrochloride) (Toricard-5) 5 mg Tablet is a white to off-white, round, biconvex, uncoated tablet with cross break line on one side and plain on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,It is indicated in the treatment of essential hypertension. Treatment of stable mild and moderate chronic heart failure in addition to standard therapies in elderly patients.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:36:50.800944+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY37979,"""Pioglitazone (as hydrochloride) + Metformin
hydrochloride""",Zolid Plus,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PwEO1lfLm6d0b4nRtCvgByKdz7zHiBCo/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY37979_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PwEO1lfLm6d0b4nRtCvgByKdz7zHiBCo_view_usp_drivesdk_d137a100a1.pdf,page_text/DR-XY37979_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PwEO1lfLm6d0b4nRtCvgByKdz7zHiBCo_view_usp_drivesdk_d137a100a1.json,d4b1dd5f26fcfaabb9a54a02f9b34b4855f343925baef907bf2464e977bdfa57,203484,2,digital_text,"Pioglitazone + Metformin HCl (Zolid ® Plus) 15mg / 500mg Tablet is available as green, oblong shaped, film-coated tablet, engraved ""Getz"" on one side and plain on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Pioglitazone + Metformin HCl (Zolid ® Plus) is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus particularly overweight patients, who are unable to achieve sufficient glycaemic control at their maximally tolerated dose of oral metformin alone.",1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:36:53.875190+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY38014,Onglyza,Saxagliptin (As Hydrochloride),PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UkDzUaO0yfNwyFA9PUm5QqSQAlQWEMWQ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY38014_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UkDzUaO0yfNwyFA9PUm5QqSQAlQWEMWQ_view_usp_drivesdk_6bb911b145.pdf,page_text/DR-XY38014_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UkDzUaO0yfNwyFA9PUm5QqSQAlQWEMWQ_view_usp_drivesdk_6bb911b145.json,16d7e5ff5e9ec93618592ee9ed29f34f3a6c67a5571b97b37c880e8881002413,908464,46,digital_text,"Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) 5 mg tablets are pink, biconvex, round, film -coated tablets with “5” printed on one side and “4215” printed on the reverse side, in blue ink. Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) 2.5 mg tablets are pale yellow to light yellow, biconvex, round, film -coated tablets with “2.5” printed on one side and “4214” printed on the reverse side, in blue ink. 4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 4.1 Therapeutic indications Monotherapy: Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus. Combination therapy: Add-on combination: Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) is indicated in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus to improve glycemic control in combination with metformin, a thiazolidinedione (TZD), a sulfonylurea (SU), metformin with an SGLT2 inhibitor, metformin with a sulfonylurea, or insulin (with or without metformin) when the single agent alone, with diet and exercise, does not provide adequate glycemic control. Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) is indicated in patients wit h type 2 diabetes mellitus to improve glycemic control in triple combination with metformin plus a sulfonylurea when the two agents, with diet and exercise, do not provide adequate glycemic control. Initial combination: Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) is indicated for use as initial combination therapy with metformin, as an adjunct to diet and exercise, to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus when dual saxagliptin and metformin therapy is appropriate. Limitation of Use: Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) should not be used in patients with type 1 diabetes or for the treatment of diabetic ketoacidosis. 4.2 Dosage and method of administration Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) tablets must not be split or cut. [Page 3] 4.2.1 Recommended dosage Monotherapy and add-on combination therapy The recommended dose of Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) is 5 mg once daily as monotherapy or as add -on combination therapy with metformin (with or without a sulfonylurea), a thiazolidinedione, a sulfonylurea, metformin with an SGLT2 inhibitor, or insulin (with or without metformin). Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) can be taken with or without food. Initial combination therapy The recommended starting doses of Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) and metformin when used as initial combination therapy is 5 mg Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) plus 500 m g metformin once daily. Patients with inadequate glycemic control on this starting dose should further have their metformin dose increased according to approved local label guidelines. 4.2.2 Renal impairment Assessment of renal function is recommended prior to i nitiation of Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) and periodically thereafter (see 4.4 Special warnings and special precautions for use, Use in patients with renal impairment and 5.3 Pharmacokinetic properties, Renal impairment). Mild renal impairment No dosage adjustment is required for patients with mild renal impairment (eGFR 60-89 mL/min/1.73 m 2 (by Modified Diet in Renal Disease [MDRD] eGFR equation). Moderate renal impairment No dosage adjustment is required for patients with eGFR ≥ 45 mL/min/1.73 m2. For patients w ith moderate renal impairment with eGFR < 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2, the dose is 2.5 mg once daily. Severe renal impairment For patients with severe renal impairment (eGFR < 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2), or with end -stage renal disease (ESRD) requiring hemodialysis , the dos e is 2.5 mg once daily. Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) should be administered following hemodialysis. Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) has not been studied in patients undergoing peritoneal dialysis. 4.2.3 Hepatic impairment No dosage adjustment for Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) is necessa ry for patients with mild, moderate, or severe hepatic impairment. 4.2.4 Pediatric and adolescent Safety and effectiveness of Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) in pediatric and adolescent patients have not been established. [Page 4] 4.2.5 Geriatric No dosage adjustment for Saxagliptin (O NGLYZA) is required based solely on age. Because elderly patients are more likely to have decreased renal function, care should be taken in dose selection in the elderly based on renal function. (See 4.4.8 Geriatric use)",2,4,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Monotherapy: Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus. Combination therapy: Add-on combination: Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) is indicated in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus to improve glycemic control in combination with metformin, a thiazolidinedione (TZD), a sulfonylurea (SU), metformin with an SGLT2 inhibitor, metformin with a sulfonylurea, or insulin (with or without metformin) when the single agent alone, with diet and exercise, does not provide adequate glycemic control. Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) is indicated in patients wit h type 2 diabetes mellitus to improve glycemic control in triple combination with metformin plus a sulfonylurea when the two agents, with diet and exercise, do not provide adequate glycemic control. Initial combination: Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) is indicated for use as initial combination therapy with metformin, as an adjunct to diet and exercise, to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus when dual saxagliptin and metformin therapy is appropriate. Limitation of Use: Saxagliptin (ONGLYZA) should not be used in patients with type 1 diabetes or for the treatment of diabetic ketoacidosis.",2,2,4.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:36:57.777556+00:00
