PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY38089,Capecitabine,Xeloda,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/11Cgv80LOxfXMZ3tO3vkTbX1IglaVMUiH/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY38089_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11Cgv80LOxfXMZ3tO3vkTbX1IglaVMUiH_view_usp_drivesdk_d1943ea013.pdf,page_text/DR-XY38089_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11Cgv80LOxfXMZ3tO3vkTbX1IglaVMUiH_view_usp_drivesdk_d1943ea013.json,a92d137038f248603e2546bb9d2f73b71a54ed65f8bfce9a6a5d76ce960c52f8,777925,2,digital_text,1.1 Therapeutic / Pharmacologic Class of Drug Cytostatic agent 1.2 Type of Dosage Form 500 mg Film-coated tablet 1.3 Route of Administration Oral 1.4 Sterile / Radioactive Statement Not applicable,1,1,1. DESCRIPTION,"Breast Cancer: Capecitabine (Xeloda) in combination with docetaxel is indicated for the treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic breast cancer after failure of cytotoxic chemotherapy. Previous therapy should have included an anthracycline. Capecitabine (Xeloda) is also indicated as monotherapy for the treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic breast cancer after failure of a taxane and an anthracycline-containing chemotherapy regimen or for whom further anthracycline therapy is not indicated. Colon, colorectal cancer: Capecitabine (Xeloda) is indicated as adjuvant treatment of patients with colon cancer. Capecitabine (Xeloda) is indicated for the treatment of patients with metastatic colorectal cancer. Oesophagogastric cancer: Capecitabine (Xeloda) is indicated as first-line treatment of patients with advanced oesophagogastric cancer. Gastric cancer: Capecitabine (Xeloda) in combination with oxaliplatin is indicated as adjuvant treatment of patients following complete resection of stage II and III gastric adenocarcinoma.",1,1,2.1 Therapeutic Indication(s),high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:37:32.362527+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY38119,Tamsulosin hydrochloride,Tamsolin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-67cGFA_Jtg9LSQcjWXDqSLQjlmh9CSe/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY38119_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-67cGFA_Jtg9LSQcjWXDqSLQjlmh9CSe_view_usp_drivesdk_2b8f604b32.pdf,page_text/DR-XY38119_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-67cGFA_Jtg9LSQcjWXDqSLQjlmh9CSe_view_usp_drivesdk_2b8f604b32.json,fdaba748e0fed9d74952ed19627e1d563c1808a4439f9a639194bd33a94eabe3,2150363,2,ocr,Pediatric Use Tamsulosin hydrochloride (Tamsolin®) 400 mcg Modified-Release Capsule is available Tamsulosin hydrochloride capsules are not indicated for use in pediatric populations. as hard gelatin capsules having standard grey opaque cap and caramel opaque body printed Getz logo and 0.4 on shell containing white to off-white spherical pellets. Hepatic Impairment Patients with moderate hepatic impairment do not require dose adjustment.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Tamsulosin hydrochloride (Tamsolin®) capsules are available for oral administration as: Tamsulosin hydrochloride (Tamsolin®) capsules are indicated for the treatment of the Each modified-release capsule contains: signs and symptoms of benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH). Tamsulosin hydrochloride... 400mcg (as modified release pellets),1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS.,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T04:37:48.634462+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY38148,Thiamine Hydrochloride + Pyridoxine Hydrochloride + Cyanocobalamin,Bee-All,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1blqRlHmq99B8EpwVhDhqOr5cuM9mOzEV/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY38148_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1blqRlHmq99B8EpwVhDhqOr5cuM9mOzEV_view_usp_drivesdk_4b5c4b03d7.pdf,page_text/DR-XY38148_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1blqRlHmq99B8EpwVhDhqOr5cuM9mOzEV_view_usp_drivesdk_4b5c4b03d7.json,d53588789ba38722c64cc93f1dd0411299e74bd5a569a9ab4340249d26493d32,108742,1,digital_text,LABORATORIES Healthcare Inc. LFT/02/609 BEE-ALL ® THIAMINE HYDROCHLORIDE + PYRIDOXINE HYDROCHLORIDE + CYANOCOBALAMIN,1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL,"For the treatment of neuritis, neuralgia, shoulder-arm syndrome, facial paresis, pregnancy neuritis, drug-induced and alcoholic neuropathy, diabetic neuropathy, sciatica, lumbago-lumbalgia, intercostals neuralgia, trigeminal neuralgia, optic neuritis, numbness of extremities, hyperemesis, gravidarum and Vitamin B deficiency. - Deficiency of vitamin B1 (as in Beri Beri Syndrome, Wernicke-Korsakoff Syndrome) - Deficiency of vitamin B6 (as in anemia, dermatitis, cheilosis and neurological symptoms such as peripheral neuritis, and convulsions) - Deficiency of vitamin B12 (as in megalobastic anemias and demyelination, and other neurological damage).",1,1,INDICATIONS :,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T04:37:51.320957+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY38183,Amlodipine (as besilate),Aforbes,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vtCaG0BGwHQVRlVOBImu5WR0j2uMg3Vm/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY38183_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vtCaG0BGwHQVRlVOBImu5WR0j2uMg3Vm_view_usp_drivesdk_26d94df3ae.pdf,page_text/DR-XY38183_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vtCaG0BGwHQVRlVOBImu5WR0j2uMg3Vm_view_usp_drivesdk_26d94df3ae.json,90ec0bbc353762e752a882a313789436d46ff96f0cbc8143e0412e024c81b602,819907,1,digital_text,,,,,"Amlodipine (Aforbes) is indicated for the treatment of hypertension and can be used as the sole agent to control blood pressure in the majority of patients. Patients not adequately controlled on a single antihypertensive agent may beneﬁt from the addition of amlodipine (Aforbes) which has been used in combination with a thiazide diuretic, beta-adrenoceptor blocking agent, or an angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor. Amlodipine (Aforbes) is indicated for the ﬁrst-line treatment of myocardial ischemia, whether due to ﬁxed obstruction (stable angina) and/or vasospasm/vasoconstriction (Prinzmetal’s or variant angina) of the coronary vasculature. Amlodipine (Aforbes) may be used where the clinical presentation suggests a possible vasospastic/vasoconstrictiv e component but where vasospasm/vasoconstriction has not been conﬁrmed. Amlodipine (Aforbes) may be used alone, as monotherapy, or in combination with other anti-anginal drugs in patients with angina that is refractory to nitrates and/or adequate doses of beta-blockers.",1,1,INDICATIONS,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T04:37:54.984932+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY38190,Ropinirole hydrochloride,Requip PD,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BGshRK2lH4_ChgFqv6mv7yK9SOuMwBkk/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY38190_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1BGshRK2lH4_ChgFqv6mv7yK9SOuMwBkk_view_usp_drivesdk_8f99031293.pdf,page_text/DR-XY38190_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1BGshRK2lH4_ChgFqv6mv7yK9SOuMwBkk_view_usp_drivesdk_8f99031293.json,10d3b9b8eaa213f764d6ae843d467e56dbe0e6cfc3d5430c9481485ec4bc2d2b,491776,6,digital_text,"Each prolonged release tablet contains ropinirole hydrochloride equivalent to 2 mg, 4 mg or 8 mg ropinirole free base.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION," Ropinirole HCl (Requip PD) is indicated for the treatment of Parkinson's disease.  Ropinirole HCl (Requip PD) is effective as early therapy in patients requiring dopaminergic therapy.  As adjunctive treatment to L-dopa, Ropinirole HCl (Requip PD) enhances the efficacy of L-dopa, including control of ""on-off"" fluctuations and ""end of dose"" effects associated with chronic L-dopa therapy and permits reduction in daily L- dopa dose.",2,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:37:58.315305+00:00
