PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY38195,Norepinephrine (as bitartrate),Levophed SF (Sulfite-Free),PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vSW0PdLBD-sTl4cWrTezxcEX5A3wMop-/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY38195_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vSW0PdLBD-sTl4cWrTezxcEX5A3wMop-_view_usp_drivesdk_3385fc5041.pdf,page_text/DR-XY38195_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vSW0PdLBD-sTl4cWrTezxcEX5A3wMop-_view_usp_drivesdk_3385fc5041.json,fa89361bad1de580455759d00ef3873c1151c75e9ced1c16bfb19ca595a71dba,213481,8,digital_text,"Norepinephrine (LEVOPHED® SF) is a sterile concentrated solution for injection with a clear, colorless or yellowish solution. It has two volumes: 2 mL and 4 mL filled in 2 mL and 5 mL glass ampoules respectively.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,Indicated for use as an emergency measure in the restoration of blood pressure in cases of acute hypotension.,1,1,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:38:07.757080+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY38258,Itraconazole,Sporanox,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rgFhYpB38tkNakkJa1mMz3eODRqDR5iu/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY38258_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rgFhYpB38tkNakkJa1mMz3eODRqDR5iu_view_usp_drivesdk_365d83a416.pdf,page_text/DR-XY38258_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rgFhYpB38tkNakkJa1mMz3eODRqDR5iu_view_usp_drivesdk_365d83a416.json,e16e50fa1993d160af89e0e6580d11f87f8fa4dd7871491f739ff4461a65b4f7,490731,32,digital_text,,,,,"Itraconazole (Sporanox®) capsules are indicated for the following conditions: • Gynecological indications: - Treatment of vulvovaginal candidosis. • Dermatological / mucosal / ophthalmological indications: - Treatment of dermatomycosis, including highly keratinized regions as in plantar tinea pedis and palmar tinea manus; - Treatment of pityriasis versicolor; - Treatment of oral candidosis; - Treatment of fungal keratitis. • Treatment of onychomycosis, caused by dermatophytes and/or yeasts. • Systemic mycoses, only in the following fungal infections: - Treatment of systemic aspergillosis and candidosis; - Cryptococcosis (including cryptococcal meningitis): - Treatment of immunocompromised patients with cryptococcosis and in all patients with cryptococcosis of the central nervous system, only when first line treatment is considered inappropriate or has proven ineffective; - Treatment of histoplasmosis; - Treatment of blastomycosis; - Treatment of sporotrichosis, including lymphocutaneous/cutaneous and extracutaneous; - Treatment of paracoccidioidomycosis; - Treatment of chromomycosis.",5,5,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T04:38:11.648428+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY38276,Everolimus,Afinitor,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1m7jsSjy1EYLJAZXZ6qEPpdubENs8TLQS/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY38276_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1m7jsSjy1EYLJAZXZ6qEPpdubENs8TLQS_view_usp_drivesdk_02eb1c952c.pdf,page_text/DR-XY38276_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1m7jsSjy1EYLJAZXZ6qEPpdubENs8TLQS_view_usp_drivesdk_02eb1c952c.json,2c58706fe85796ff891093fccc92e4ddf4f84956bd1103deaf23eb16dfe6f441,1008882,51,digital_text,"Pharmaceutical form(s) Tablets White to slightly yellow, elongated tablets with a bevelled edge and no score. • 2.5 mg: The tablets are engraved with “LCL” on one side and “NVR” on the other. • 5 mg: The tablets are engraved with “5” on one side and “NVR” on the other. • 10 mg: The tablets are engraved with “UHE” on one side and “NVR” on the other. Dispersible Tablets White to slightly yellowish, round, flat tablets with a bevelled edge and no score. • 2 mg: The tablets are engraved with “D2” on one side and “NVR” on the other. • 3 mg: The tablets are engraved with “D3” on one side and “NVR” on the other. • 5 mg: The tablets are engraved with “D5” on one side and “NVR” on the other. Active substance Tablets • 2.5 mg: Each tablet contains 2.5 mg everolimus. • 5 mg: Each tablet contains 5 mg everolimus. • 10 mg: Each tablet contains 10 mg everolimus. Dispersible Tablets • 2 mg: Each dispersible tablet contains 2 mg everolimus. • 3 mg: Each dispersible tablet contains 3 mg everolimus. • 5 mg: Each dispersible tablet contains 5 mg everolimus. Certain dosage strengths and dosage forms may not be available in all countries. Excipients Tablet: Butylated hydroxytoluene (E321), magnesium stearate, lactose monohydrate, hypromellose, crospovidone and lactose anhydrous. Dispersible Tablet: Butylated hydroxytoluene (E321), magnesium stearate, lactose monohydrate, hypromellose, crospovidone, mannitol, cellulose microcrystalline, and silica colloidal anhydrous. Information might differ in some countries. [Page 2]",1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,"Afinitor Tablets are indicated for the treatment of: • Postmenopausal women with hormone receptor -positive advanced breast cancer in combination with an aromatase inhibitor, after prior endocrine therapy. • Patients with adva nced neuroendocrine tumors of gastrointestinal, lung or pancreatic origin • Patients with advanced renal cell carcinoma • Patients with tuberous sclerosis complex (TSC) who have renal angiomyolipoma not requiring immediate surgery. Afinitor Dispersible Tablets are indicated for the adjunctive treatment of • Patients aged 2 years and older whose refractory partial- onset seizures, wit h or without secondary generalization, are associated with tuberous sclerosis complex (TSC ). Afinitor Tablets and Afinitor Dispersible Tablets are indicated for the treatment of: • Patients with TSC who have subependymal giant cell astrocytoma (SEGA) not requiring immediate surgery.",2,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:38:16.511966+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY38297,Levonorgestrel + Ethinylestradiol; Ferrous Fumarate,Protec,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1jsFq9OE4G-obfSh-8TXvHY1wS7C3q9vl/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY38297_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jsFq9OE4G-obfSh-8TXvHY1wS7C3q9vl_view_usp_drivesdk_5de1f09437.pdf,page_text/DR-XY38297_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jsFq9OE4G-obfSh-8TXvHY1wS7C3q9vl_view_usp_drivesdk_5de1f09437.json,1a58411b38366a8a023755ce13044b68a6c0b019793a767cae67a44844b3455f,552645,9,digital_text,"Ethinyl Estradiol + Levonorgestrel + Ferrous fumarate (PROTEC) is a safe and easy to use contraceptive pill. It is also used in the treatment of menstrual disorders such as painful menstruation, menstrual cycle symptoms, and excessive uterine bleeding. It contains iron that helps improve the hemoglobin level of blood during menstruation. Ethinyl Estradiol + Levonorgestrel + Ferrous fumarate (PROTEC) does not delay the return of fertility after discontinuing its use. Generally, your bleeding pattern before taking Ethinyl Estradiol + Levonorgestrel + Ferrous fumarate (PROTEC) will return after you discontinue taking it. Some women, However, may have to wait a few months before their usual bleeding pattern returns.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Ethinyl Estradiol + Levonorgestrel + Ferrous fumarate (PROTEC) is indicated for contraception and treatment of menstrual disorders such as dysmennorhea, premenstrual syndrome, and menorrhagia.",1,1,INDICATION,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:38:19.792229+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY38299,Guaifenesin,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Ed5SLTNBCfItm3AJmozgYn_xDYrlWziS/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY38299_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Ed5SLTNBCfItm3AJmozgYn_xDYrlWziS_view_usp_drivesdk_b34bea8c1a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY38299_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Ed5SLTNBCfItm3AJmozgYn_xDYrlWziS_view_usp_drivesdk_b34bea8c1a.json,40f842fcebe8bbd6e816b25b2376a453031fc583ba31915d3e4e4f8bb961b122,227550,1,digital_text,"Dark, red, oblong shaped, soft gelatin capsule containing clear oily liquid.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Expectorant action to help loosen phlegm and thin bronchial secretions to make cough more productive.,1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:38:22.551199+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY38376,Mesalazine,Pentasa,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PZlVnxD09IBPK6821jQHZL4XeUfwCozj/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY38376_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PZlVnxD09IBPK6821jQHZL4XeUfwCozj_view_usp_drivesdk_9a201c9178.pdf,page_text/DR-XY38376_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PZlVnxD09IBPK6821jQHZL4XeUfwCozj_view_usp_drivesdk_9a201c9178.json,ca40eaa04d0463acf9ab1f0441c0c4ea36be602e35e0372f398cdc3f2c677248,324597,4,digital_text,"Suppositories 1g Apper ance of Mesalazine (Pentasa ®) suppositories 1g: White to tan, spotted, oblong suppositories. THERAPEUTIC INDI CATIONS Treatment of acute mild to moderate ulcerative colitis that is limited to the rectum (ulcerative proctitis). POSOLOGY AND METHOD OF ADMINISTRATION 1 suppository 1 -2 times daily. Paediatric population: There is little experience and only limited documentation for an effect in children. Method of administration A visit to the toilet is recommended before administration of suppositories. INSTRUCTION FOR USE (For rectal administration only) 1. Place one of the finger protectors on one finger. 2. Insert the suppository as far up as possible into your rectum. 3. Insertion may be easier if you moisten the suppository with water or moisturising cream first. 4. If it slips out within 10 minutes, a new one may be inserted. 5. Discard the used finger protector. Should be inserted into the back passage (rectum) only. It is intended to be left in place for as long as possible and is therefore best inserted before going to sleep.",1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,Treatment of acute mild to moderate ulcerative colitis that is limited to the rectum (ulcerative proctitis).,1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDI CATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:38:25.909423+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY38472,Perindopril Arginine / Indapamide,Coversyl Plus,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hXA4DGIJgJsySQpHR0_H6Oi2l8l1BUsU/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY38472_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hXA4DGIJgJsySQpHR0_H6Oi2l8l1BUsU_view_usp_drivesdk_768c9d3d37.pdf,page_text/DR-XY38472_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hXA4DGIJgJsySQpHR0_H6Oi2l8l1BUsU_view_usp_drivesdk_768c9d3d37.json,8523410b3a9fa739e8c058ed3281c55e6eaf115a921a588373fcf3af10c516d3,6209648,6,ocr,"The peak plasma level is reached in humans approximately White, round film-coated tablet. one hour after oral administration of the product.",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"converting enzyme inhibitor, and indapamide, a chloro- sulphamoyl diuretic. Its pharmacological properties are derived Substitution therapy for the treatment of essential hyper- from those of each of the components taken separately, tension, in patients already controlled with Perindopril and in addition to those due to the additive synergic action of the Indapamide given concurrently at the same dose level. two products when combined.",1,1,INDICATION,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T04:40:08.616712+00:00
