PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY38648,Pyrazinamide,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LOZ6NdJ2QacQW03mvAqFU5yWQYXIMJ0O/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY38648_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LOZ6NdJ2QacQW03mvAqFU5yWQYXIMJ0O_view_usp_drivesdk_6afd3b7f7e.pdf,page_text/DR-XY38648_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LOZ6NdJ2QacQW03mvAqFU5yWQYXIMJ0O_view_usp_drivesdk_6afd3b7f7e.json,b79fcc7adea338999cdba1332fa582ea7462ff697ffd39c8a6d8a6aa9b03da1a,291002,1,digital_text,White to off-white suspension with orange flavor.,1,1,Description:,"All forms of pulmonary and extrapulmonary tuberculosis due to strains of Mycobacterium tuberculosis sensitive to Pyrazinamide. When treating all forms of tuberculosis, Pyrazinamide is used as part of multi -drug regimens for the treatment of tuberculosis, primarily in the initial 8 -week phase of short -course treatment.",1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:40:57.885092+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY38668,Clopidogrel (as bisulfate),Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/17f94omQq-D781RpKqOsViafOVeXSpa99/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY38668_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17f94omQq-D781RpKqOsViafOVeXSpa99_view_usp_drivesdk_b79e7c81e3.pdf,page_text/DR-XY38668_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17f94omQq-D781RpKqOsViafOVeXSpa99_view_usp_drivesdk_b79e7c81e3.json,01e053636bcda5854f548cabaf37576b4cfb9adb7cc68987e69dfb66749c86f2,69918,1,digital_text,"Clopidogrel 75 mg film-coated tablet is a baby pink to light pink in color, round, biconvex and plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"It is used as an alternative to aspirin to prevent thromboembolic events in patients at risk of thromboembolic disorders such as myocardial infarction, peripheral arterial disease and ischemic stroke. It is also used in combination with aspirin for the prevention of subacute stent occlusion after intracoronary stenting. It prevents platelet loss during extracorporeal circulatory procedures. It is used as part of the treatment for acute coronary syndromes, including unstable angina and non-Q-wave myocardial infarction.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:41:02.033530+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY38677,Cinnarizine,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1P9mLLKvBLFzrCfHoZ1cxnJnhZQSgszBx/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY38677_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1P9mLLKvBLFzrCfHoZ1cxnJnhZQSgszBx_view_usp_drivesdk_673c8ffd03.pdf,page_text/DR-XY38677_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1P9mLLKvBLFzrCfHoZ1cxnJnhZQSgszBx_view_usp_drivesdk_673c8ffd03.json,006aaeb8f762bd2ae0515e94597e55a3912bd307ae8807211f122bc7fb6f4f73,870475,2,digital_text,"RiteMED® Cinnarizine 25 mg is a white, round, biconvex tablet, bisected on one side RiteMED® Cinnarizine 75 mg is a size #4 capsule with light green opaque cap and white opaque body PHARMACODYNAMICS Cinnarizine’s action in the treatment of peripheral vascular disease is due to its anti-vasoconstrictor properties, its action on blood hyperviscosity, and its anti-ischemic effect. Cinnarizine has been shown to be a non-competitive antagonist of the smooth muscle contractions caused by various vasoactive agents, including histamine. Anti-vasoconstriction is thought to be through a calcium blocker mechanism and is evident selectively in vascular smooth muscle. In addition to this direct calcium antagonism, cinnarizine decreases the contractile activity of vasoactive substances, such as norepinephrine and serotonin, by blocking receptor-operated calcium channels. Blockade of the cellular influx of calcium is tissue-selective, and results in anti-vasoconstrictor properties without effect on blood pressure and heart rate. Increased peripheral muscle blood flow may be mediated by prevention of calcium entry into ischemic erythrocytes, thereby preserving flexibility. Cinnarizine may further improve deficient microcirculation by increasing erythrocyte deformability and decreasing blood viscosity. Cellular resistance to hypoxia is increased. Cinnarizine inhibits stimulation of the vestibular system, which results in suppression of nystagmus and other autonomic disturbances. PHARMACOKINETICS After oral administration, absorption is relatively slow. Peak serum concentrations occur 1 to 3 hours after intake. The plasma protein binding of cinnarizine is 91%. Cinnarizine is extensively metabolized mainly via CYP2D6, but there is considerable inter-individual variation in the extent of metabolism. The reported elimination half-life for cinnarizine ranges from 4 to 24 hours. The elimination of metabolites is about 1/3 in the urine (unchanged as metabolites and glucuronide conjugates) and 2/3 in the feces. Plasma elimination half-life is about 3 to 4 hours. Hepatobiliary Disorders: Cholestatic jaundice Skin and Subcutaneous Tissue Disorders: Hyperhidrosis, lichenoid keratosis, lichens planus, subacute cutaneous lupus erythematosus Musculoskeletal and Connective Tissue Disorders: Muscle rigidity General Disorders and Administration Site Conditions: Lethargy, fatigue Investigations: Weight increased OVERDOSE AND TREATMENT Acute cinnarizine overdoses have been reported with doses ranging from 90 to 2,250 mg. The signs and symptoms of cinnarizine overdose are mainly due to the anticholinergic (atropine-like) activity of the drug. The most commonly reported signs and symptoms include: alterations in consciousness ranging from somnolence to stupor and coma, vomiting, extrapyramidal symptoms, and hypotonia. In a small number of young children, seizures developed. Clinical consequences were not severe in most cases, but deaths have bee n reported after single and polydrug overdoses involving cinnarizine. There is no specific antidote. Treatment is symptomatic and supportive care. Activated charcoal should only be considered in patients presenting within one hour of taking a potentially toxic overdose (i.e., more than 15 mg/kg). STORAGE CONDITIONS Keep the product out of reach and sight of children. Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. AVAILABILITY RiteMED ® Cinnarizin e 25 mg Tablet RiteMED® Cinnarizin e 75 mg Capsule Pantone 2756 U COLOR GUIDE Spread size: 140 mm x 196 mm Folded size: 140 mm x 98 mm RM - CINNARIZINE Line Insert (Front Spread) V.3 ADVERSE DRUG REACTION REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adverse drug reaction, seek medical attention immediately and report to the FDA at www. fda.gov.ph AND RiteMED at (+632) 8-726-0835 or e-mail productsafety@ritemed.com.ph. By rep orting undesirable effects, you can help ptovide more information on the safety of this medicine. CAUTION Foods, Drugs, Devices, and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription. Manufactured by UNILAB, Inc. No. 66 United Street, Mandaluyong City For RiteMED Phils., Inc. 56 EDSA, Mandaluyong, Metro Manila Date of First Authorization: December 18, 2009 Date of Revision: October 2021 25 mg Tablet : DR-XY37211 75 mg Capsule: DR-XY38677 Reg. IPOPHIL • F .A. Revision Date: 19 October 2021 , in Alu/PCTFE Blister Pack x 10’s (Box of 30’s) , in Alu/PCTFE Blister Pack x 10’s (Box of 30 capsules) [Page 2] WARNINGS AND PRECAUTIONS As with other antihistamines, cinnarizine may cause epigastric discomfort; taking it after meals may diminish gastric irritation. Cinnarizine is a vasodilator. While it has not been found to reduce blood pressure significantly, it should be used with caution in those with coronary artery disease or in patients with hypotension. In patients with Parkinson’s disease, cinnarizine should only be given if the advantages outweigh the possible risk of aggravating this disease. There have been rare reports of extrapyramidal symptoms after taking cinnarizine, sometimes associated with depressive feelings. Cinnarizine may cause somnolence, particularly at the start of treatment. Therefore, caution should be taken when alcohol or central nervous system depressants or tricyclic antidepressants are used concomitantly. Use of cinnarizine should be avoided in porphyria. Cinnarizine may cause drowsiness, particularly at the start of treatment; caution should be taken during activities such as driving or operating machinery. INTERACTIONS WITH OTHER MEDICAMENTS • Concomitant use of alcohol, CNS depressants or tricyclic antidepressants may potentiate the sedative effects of either these drugs or of cinnarizine. Alcoholic drink should be avoided. Diagnostic interference • Cinnarizine may prevent an otherwise positive reaction to dermal reactivity indicators if used within four days prior to testing because of its antihistamine effect. STATEMENT ON USAGE FOR HIGH RISK GROUPS PREGNANCY AND LACTATION Pregnancy The safety of cinnarizine in pregnancy has not been established. Therefore, it is not recommended to administer cinnarizine during pregnancy. Lactation There are no data on the excretion of cinnarizine in breast milk. Therefore, it is not recommended in breastfeeding mothers. RENAL AND HEPATIC IMPAIRMENT Cinnarizine should be used with care in patients with hepatic or renal insufficiency. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS Immune System Disorders: Hypersensitivity Psychiatric Disorders: Somnolence, hypersomnia Nervous System Disorders: Dyskinesia, extrapyramidal disorder, parkinsonism, tremor, headache Gastrointestinal Disorders: Nausea, stomach discomfort, vomiting, upper abdominal pain, dyspepsia, dry mouth",1,2,PRODUCT DESCRIPTIONS,,2,2,INDICATIONS,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T04:41:05.378607+00:00
