"Metoprolol succinate + Hypertension: As monotherapy or in combination with other antihypertensive agents patients with bronchospastic disease who do not respond to, or cannot tolerate, other Lactation: Since metoprolol is excreted in breast milk, the drug should be used with caution antihypertensive treatment. Since beta; selectivity is not absolute, coadminister a in breastfeeding mothers. * Pediatric hypertension vis. betay-stimulating agent, and use the lowest possible metoprolol dose. Bronchodilators, Cardiosel-0D including betag-agonists, should be readily available or administered concomitantly. Children: The safety and efficacy in children < 6 years old have not been established. R Cardiac arrhythmias: Disturbances of cardiac rhythm, including supraventricular tachycardia, . mg Extendea-helease lable reduction of ventricular rate in atrial fibrillation and ventricular extrasystoles Pheochromocytoma: If metoprolol is used in the setting of pheochromocytoma, it should Elderly: Clinical experience in hypertensive patients has not identified differences in * Myocardial intarction (MI): Maintenance treatment atter MI always be given in combination with an alpha-blocker, and only after the alpha-blocker has responses between elderly and younger patients. In general, dose selection for an elderly BETA BLOCKING AGENT + Functional heart disorders with palpitations been initiated. Administration of beta-blockers alone in the setting of pheochromocytoma has patient should be cautious, usually starting at the low end of the dosing range, reflecting the been associated with a paradoxical increase in blood pressure due to the attenuation of greater frequency of decreased hepatic, renal or cardiac function, and of concomitant disease + Hyperthyroidism beta-mediated vasodilatation in skeletal muscle. FORMULATIONS + Prophylaxis of migraine headache or other drug therapy. Each film-coated extended release tablet contains:",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T