PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY39418,Tobramycin,Tobrex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uDJKXHjdIjAgh0Cz9o0fZQclBoskjyiB/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY39418_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uDJKXHjdIjAgh0Cz9o0fZQclBoskjyiB_view_usp_drivesdk_8e2c5bfe47.pdf,page_text/DR-XY39418_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uDJKXHjdIjAgh0Cz9o0fZQclBoskjyiB_view_usp_drivesdk_8e2c5bfe47.json,c64e743f6d61e68581959c5f294d34558f5ed8f868efdf2606ce0b55c21d9e00,268365,11,digital_text,"Pharmaceutical form(s) Sterile Ophthalmic Ointment. White to off-white homogeneous ointment. The reference monograph for this drug product is Ph. Eur. Active substance(s) Tobramycin (Tobrex®) Sterile Ophthalmic Ointment: Each gram of ointment contains: Tobramycin, Ph. Eur......................3 mg Excipients Tobramycin (Tobrex®) Sterile Ophthalmic Ointment: Excipients: chlorobutanol, liquid paraffin, white soft paraffin. Pharmaceutical formulations may vary between countries.",1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,"Tobramycin (Tobrex®) 3 mg/g (0.3%) Sterile Ophthalmic Ointment is a topical antibiotic indicated in the treatment of external infections of the eye and its adnexa caused by susceptible bacteria. Appropriate monitoring of bacterial response to topical antibiotic therapy should accompany the use of Tobramycin (Tobrex®) 3 mg/g (0.3%) Sterile Ophthalmic Ointment. Clinical studies have shown tobramycin to be safe and effective for use in children. As with other antibiotics, appropriate monitori ng of bacterial response to treatment should be performed. [Page 2]",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:47:54.466717+00:00
