PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY39441,Piperacillin (as Sodium ) + Tazobactam (as Sodium),Tazocin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Ja5k9-jDtokeobY_UBZz4ouzsVDGBIqX/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY39441_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Ja5k9-jDtokeobY_UBZz4ouzsVDGBIqX_view_usp_drivesdk_7878243375.pdf,page_text/DR-XY39441_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Ja5k9-jDtokeobY_UBZz4ouzsVDGBIqX_view_usp_drivesdk_7878243375.json,67d96ac7043b095961b8449adfa36e701121815c99c4f9d289a882bc1677e3d9,429588,19,digital_text,"Piperacillin/tazobactam is an injectable antibacterial combination consisting of the semisynthetic antibiotic piperacillin sodium and the β-lactamase inhibitor tazobactam sodium for intravenous administration. Piperacillin sodium is derived from D(-)-a-aminobenzylpenicillin. The chemical name of piperacillin sodium is sodium (2S, 5R, 6R)-6-[(R)-2-(4-ethyl-2,3-dioxo-1-piperazinecarboxamido)- 2-phenylacetamido] –3,3 – dimethyl-7-oxo-4-thia-1-azabicyclo [3.2.0]heptane – 2 – carboxylate. Piperacillin sodium is a white, crystalline powder. It is freely soluble in water, alcohol, and methyl alcohol but is practically insoluble in ethyl acetate. Its structural formula is: Tazobactam sodium is a derivative of the penicillin nucleus. Chemically, tazobactam is a penicillanic acid sulfone. Its chemical name is sodium(2S-,3S-,5R) – 3 – methyl-7-oxo-3-(1H-1,2,3- triazol-1-ylmethyl)-4-thia-1-azabicyclo[3.2.0]heptane-2-carboxylate,4,4-dioxide. Tazobactam sodium is a white to pale yellow non-hydroscopic crystalline powder. The chemical structure of tazobactam sodium is:",1,1,2. DESCRIPTION,"Piperacillin/tazobactam (Tazocin) is indicated for the treatment of the following systemic and/or local bacterial infections caused by gram-positive and gram-negative aerobic and anaerobic organisms susceptible to piperacillin/tazobactam or piperacillin: Adults o Lower respiratory tract infections o Urinary tract infections o Intra-abdominal infections o Skin and skin structure infections o Bacterial septicemia o Gynecological infections, including post-partum endometritis and pelvic inflammatory disease (PID) o Febrile neutropenic infections. Combination treatment with an aminoglycoside is recommended. o Bone and joint infections o Polymicrobial infections (gram-positive/gram-negative aerobes and anaerobes) Children (2 years of age or older) o Febrile neutropenic infections. Combination treatment with an aminoglycoside is recommended o Intra-abdominal infections In serious infections, empiric therapy with piperacillin/tazobactam may be initiated before susceptibility test results are available. Note: For associated bacteremia due to extended-beta-lactamase (ESBL) producing organisms, see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic Properties.",2,2,4.1. Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:48:30.435342+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY39444,Tigecycline,Tygacil,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NqUtzAWjoLzxuF_Q2K70WQjAtiy5JJmX/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY39444_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1NqUtzAWjoLzxuF_Q2K70WQjAtiy5JJmX_view_usp_drivesdk_052a1bc111.pdf,page_text/DR-XY39444_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1NqUtzAWjoLzxuF_Q2K70WQjAtiy5JJmX_view_usp_drivesdk_052a1bc111.json,717aa996a4e7a0c33ee21e685952663948adcc5e917c44bebce49e0863f06b0e,414671,28,digital_text,"Tigecycline (Tygacil) is a glycylcycline antibacterial for intravenous infusion. The chemical name of tigecycline (4S,4aS,5aR,12aS)-9-[2-(tert-butylamino)acetamido]-4,7- bis(dimethylamino)-1,4,4a,5,5a,6,11,12a-octahydro-3,10,12,12a-tetrahydroxy-1,11-dioxo-2- naphthacenecarboxamide. The molecular formula is C29H39N5O8 and the molecular weight is 585.65. The structural formula is represented below: Tigecycline is an orange lyophilized powder or cake.",1,1,2. DESCRIPTION,"Adults Tigecycline is indicated for treatment of the following infections in adults: o Complicated skin and skin structure infections (cSSSI), including those with methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA). N N H3C H3C H3C O OH N CH3H3C O H OH H OH N CH3H3C OH O NH2 O H H TIGECYCLINE Viewed on: Sunday, July 7, 2024 - 10:10:26 PM Eastern Time [Page 2] Tigecycline is not indicated for the treatment of diabetic foot infections (DFI) (see Section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). o Complicated intra-abdominal infections (cIAI). o Community acquired pneumonia (CAP). Tigecycline is not indicated for the treatment of hospital-acquired or ventilator-associated",1,2,4.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:48:33.840114+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY3945,Flupentixol Decanoate,Fluanxol Depot,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1icfSdTL5Ry-MKpXktuEY5sfxy6qEUdl9/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY3945_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1icfSdTL5Ry-MKpXktuEY5sfxy6qEUdl9_view_usp_drivesdk_3dc45b90c8.pdf,page_text/DR-XY3945_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1icfSdTL5Ry-MKpXktuEY5sfxy6qEUdl9_view_usp_drivesdk_3dc45b90c8.json,4baa9d81d15da485f220bb1c310ecb1ecce58dd7007829ee39315b5fbc4173b2,182816,2,digital_text,"For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA:www.fda.gov.ph. Patient is advised to seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction that shall appear. 7. MARKETING A UTHORISATION HOLDER Manufactured by: H. Lundbeck A/S Ottiliavej 9, Valby, 2500, Denmark Imported and distributed by:",2,2,prescription.,"Schizophrenia and allied psychoses, especially with symptoms such as hallucinations, paranoid delusions and thought disturbances along with apathy, energy and withdrawal. 4.2 Do sage regimen Adults: Flupentixol decanoate is administered by intramuscular injection into the upper outer quadrant of the buttock. Local tolerability is good. Dosage and interval between injections should be individually adjusted according to the therapeutic response. In the maintenance treatment, the dosage range would normally be 20 ‑ 40 mg (1 ‑ 2 mL) every 2 ‑ 4 weeks. Some patients may need higher doses or shorter intervals between doses. Injection volumes exceeding 2 mL should be distributed between two injection sites. Those not previously treated with long ‑acting antip sychotic injections should continue with oral neuroleptic drugs but in diminishing dosage. 4.3",1,1,apeutic indications,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T04:48:37.125269+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY39468,Citicoline (as sodium),Neuropse,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Yayi8K2_KB49SOCQhHFmrfy6gCcpDxj-/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY39468_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Yayi8K2_KB49SOCQhHFmrfy6gCcpDxj-_view_usp_drivesdk_6d4b9bed78.pdf,page_text/DR-XY39468_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Yayi8K2_KB49SOCQhHFmrfy6gCcpDxj-_view_usp_drivesdk_6d4b9bed78.json,c9693b2dd0aeb7fdc9dabbaf556091b8904d9c87217a17c3bb3e8ce427e6cc73,1679368,2,ocr,Citicoline Sodium is an off-whi cap and scarlet body. ite granular powder encapsulated in empty gelatin capsule size #00 with scarlet,1,1,PRODUCTDESCRIPTION:,"Used in the management of Cerebrov. injuries. ascular disorders including ischaemic stroke, parkinsonism and head",1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T04:49:12.522374+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY39482,Warfedin,Warfarin (As Sodium),PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Q4HvUOFD7e6XS8-pWlilCCTAETzMx7IL/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY39482_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Q4HvUOFD7e6XS8-pWlilCCTAETzMx7IL_view_usp_drivesdk_d9400db73b.pdf,page_text/DR-XY39482_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Q4HvUOFD7e6XS8-pWlilCCTAETzMx7IL_view_usp_drivesdk_d9400db73b.json,25671e6eb41855e3317a5cb2554b7ec8483ef60dbdb942c9faa73b91df8ed871,43623,2,digital_text,"5 mg Tablet - Light orange to orange tablet , round, biconvex, plain on one side and bisected on the other side. 2.5 mg Tablet - Light green to mint green tablet , round, biconvex , plain on one side and bisected on the other side. Warfarin is a coumarin anticoagulant used in the treatment and prophylaxis of thromboembolic disorders. It acts by depressing the hepatic vitamin K -dependent synthesis of coagulation factors II (prothrombin), VII, IX, X and of the coagulation protein C and its cofactor protein S.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Warfarin is used in the prevention and treatment of venous thromboembolism (deep-vein thrombosis and pulmonary embolism). It is also used for the prevention of systemic thromboembolism and ischemic stroke in patients with atrial fibrillation, prosthetic heart valves, or who have suffered myocardial infar ction and in the management of stroke or transient ischemic attacks.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:49:15.820083+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY39483,Warfedin,Warfarin (As Sodium),PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1emR5sA-MWNNJXhakR4XBgnlh_9kyoeUB/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY39483_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1emR5sA-MWNNJXhakR4XBgnlh_9kyoeUB_view_usp_drivesdk_cc7a6a72d0.pdf,page_text/DR-XY39483_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1emR5sA-MWNNJXhakR4XBgnlh_9kyoeUB_view_usp_drivesdk_cc7a6a72d0.json,25671e6eb41855e3317a5cb2554b7ec8483ef60dbdb942c9faa73b91df8ed871,43623,2,digital_text,"5 mg Tablet - Light orange to orange tablet , round, biconvex, plain on one side and bisected on the other side. 2.5 mg Tablet - Light green to mint green tablet , round, biconvex , plain on one side and bisected on the other side. Warfarin is a coumarin anticoagulant used in the treatment and prophylaxis of thromboembolic disorders. It acts by depressing the hepatic vitamin K -dependent synthesis of coagulation factors II (prothrombin), VII, IX, X and of the coagulation protein C and its cofactor protein S.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Warfarin is used in the prevention and treatment of venous thromboembolism (deep-vein thrombosis and pulmonary embolism). It is also used for the prevention of systemic thromboembolism and ischemic stroke in patients with atrial fibrillation, prosthetic heart valves, or who have suffered myocardial infar ction and in the management of stroke or transient ischemic attacks.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:49:18.635357+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY39592,Escitalopram ( as oxalate ),S-Celepra,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UWutBYh-GpddgZTmmTpkD393FrlieHNA/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY39592_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UWutBYh-GpddgZTmmTpkD393FrlieHNA_view_usp_drivesdk_94956057a9.pdf,page_text/DR-XY39592_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UWutBYh-GpddgZTmmTpkD393FrlieHNA_view_usp_drivesdk_94956057a9.json,69a1d89e2dc7315918e7ea016376715bc29b7df0c26f8f117c42be508df36ef5,2110543,3,digital_text,"Escitalopram Tablets 5 mg : Light yellow coloured, circular, biconvex film-coated tablets with a breakline on one surface. Escitalopram Tablets 10 mg : Light pink colored,circular, biconvex film-coated tablets. Escitalopram Tablets 20 mg : Orange colored, circular, biconvex film-coated tablets.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION :,Treatment of major depressive episodes Treatment of panic disorder with or without agoraphobia Treatment of social anxiety disorder (social phobia) Treatment of generalized anxiety disorder Treatment of obsessive-compulsive disorder,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:49:22.654358+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY39607,Rosuvastatin (as calcium),Rosucol,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fVXH4DB4unXi8tzd3Vw_Z8ROm5QW1Jxv/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY39607_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1fVXH4DB4unXi8tzd3Vw_Z8ROm5QW1Jxv_view_usp_drivesdk_5b88e6ce1e.pdf,page_text/DR-XY39607_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1fVXH4DB4unXi8tzd3Vw_Z8ROm5QW1Jxv_view_usp_drivesdk_5b88e6ce1e.json,9aa34667170b8948c1583d12003e8b42722e0f22b681ec7b080cc9915af93ff7,1957670,2,digital_text,"5mg - White to off-white coloured, circular, biconvex, film-coated tablets, plain on both sides. 10mg - Light pink to pink coloured, circular, biconvex, film-coated tablets, plain on both sides. 20mg - White to off-white coloured, circular, biconvex, film-coated tablets, plain on both sides. s. Pregnant and nursing women. PHARMACODYNAMICS PHARMACOKINETICS Each film-coated tablet contains: As As radio-labeled dose is in vitro CrCl2 CrCl > 80 mL/min/1.73m semi-annually ≥ 65 Front Size: 150 x 160 mm 5mg Film-Coated Tablet 10mg Film-Coated Tablet 20mg Film-Coated Tablet HMG CoA Reductase Inhibitor",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Rosuvastatin is indicated: a.) As an adjunct to diet to reduce elevated total-C, LDL-C, ApoB, non-HDL-C, and TG levels and to increase HDL-C in patients with primary hypercholesterolemia (excluding heterozygous familial and nonfamilial hypercholesterolemia) and mixed dyslipidemia (Fredrickson Type IIa and IIb). b.) As an adjunct to diet for the treatment of patients with elevated serum TG levels (Fredrickson Type IV). c.) To reduce LDL-C, total-C, and ApoB in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia as an adjunct to other lipid-lowering treatments (e.g., LDL apheresis) or if such treatments are unavailable.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T04:49:27.696717+00:00
