PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY39755,Co-Amoxiclav,Bactiv 1 g,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1olrd0v_8zIEFzB21jD6BGUNBZlaMa3xa/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY39755_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1olrd0v_8zIEFzB21jD6BGUNBZlaMa3xa_view_usp_drivesdk_b8566f1190.pdf,page_text/DR-XY39755_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1olrd0v_8zIEFzB21jD6BGUNBZlaMa3xa_view_usp_drivesdk_b8566f1190.json,1a407f2bb2c8e125a4bade99a4f6a7db596525ac548bca07e78d75c3b4eebfb5,2084186,2,ocr,"Bactiv625: Whiteovalshapedfilm-coated, debossedwith“A” ononesideand“64"" ontheother side. Bactiv1g: Whitecoloredcapsuleshapedfilm-coated, debossedwith*A” ononesideandwithascorelinebetween“6""and*5"" ontheotherside.",1,1,PHARMACEUTICALFORM,"Co-Amoxiclavis an antibiotic agentwitha broad spectrum of activity againstthe commonly occurring bacterial pathogens in general practice and hospital. TheB-lactamase inhibitory action of clavulanate extendsthespectrumofamoxicillintoembraceawiderrangeof organisms, includingmanyresistanttootherB-actam antibiotics. Co-Amoxiclav oral preparations are indicated for short-term treatmentof bacterial infections atthe following sites when amoxicillin resistant Bactamase-producing strains are suspected as the cause. In . othersituations, amoxicillinaloneshouldbeconsidered Upper Respiratory Tract Infections (including ENT) in particular sinusitis, otitis media, recurrent tonsillitis. These infections are often caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae, Haemophilus influenzae*, Moraxella catarrhalis* and Streptococcus pyogenes. Lower Repiratory Tract Infections in particular acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis (especially if considered severe), bronchopneumonia. These infections are often caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae, Haemophilus influenzae"", Moraxella catarrhalis"". Genito-urinary Tract and Abdominal Infections in particular cystitis (especially when recurrent or complicated — excluding prostatitis), septic abortion, pelvic or puerperal sepsis and intra- . abdominal sepsis. These infections are often caused by Enterobacteriaceae* (mainly Escherichia coli*), Staphylococcus saprophyticus, Enterococcus species.* Skin and Soft Tissue Infections in particular cellulitis, animal bites and severe dental abscess with spreading cellulitis. These infections are often caused by Sfapylococcus aureus Streptococcus yogenes and Bacteroides * Some members of fi ese species of bacteria produ ee tactamase, rendering them insensitive to amoxicillin alone. Mixed infections caused by amoxicillin-susce ptible organisms in conjunction with Co-Amoxiclav-susceptible B4actamase-producing organisms may be treated with Co-Amoxiclav. These infections should not require the addition of another antibioticresistant to B-lactamases.",1,1,Therapeuticindications,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T04:51:02.851964+00:00
