itis), septic abortion, pelvic or puerperal sepsis and intra- . abdominal sepsis. These infections are often caused by Enterobacteriaceae* (mainly Escherichia coli*), Staphylococcus saprophyticus, Enterococcus species.* Skin and Soft Tissue Infections in particular cellulitis, animal bites and severe dental abscess with spreading cellulitis. These infections are often caused by Sfapylococcus aureus Streptococcus yogenes and Bacteroides * Some members of fi ese species of bacteria produ ee tactamase, rendering them insensitive to amoxicillin alone. Mixed infections caused by amoxicillin-susce ptible organisms in conjunction with Co-Amoxiclav-susceptible B4actamase-producing organisms may be treated with Co-Amoxiclav. These infections should not require the addition of another antibioticresistant to B-lactamases.",1,1,Therapeuticindications,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T04:51:33.612334+00:00
