PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY40320,,Foligen,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/11dLV8dfyxd7heasW-kHURpnOBOhigg0C/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY40320_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11dLV8dfyxd7heasW-kHURpnOBOhigg0C_view_usp_drivesdk_cc86b9abea.pdf,page_text/DR-XY40320_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11dLV8dfyxd7heasW-kHURpnOBOhigg0C_view_usp_drivesdk_cc86b9abea.json,7f352395d0f862d35e86e15e7814f0a1278211100560d70a2fff2f1d76041ee8,97412,1,ocr,Foligen 5mg tablet is a round biconvex with score at one side and plain on the other side pink coated tablet.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Folic acid is indicated in the treatment and prevention of folate deficiency state. it is also used in women of child bearing potential and pregnant women to protect againts neural tube defects in their offspring.,1,1,INDICATION,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T05:01:30.311349+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY40364,Gemcitabine (as hydrochloride),Gemzar,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1o8qmuhkCHVZLZOWIn7v-IwADVKZVPXP7/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY40364_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1o8qmuhkCHVZLZOWIn7v-IwADVKZVPXP7_view_usp_drivesdk_e0790ac0b1.pdf,page_text/DR-XY40364_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1o8qmuhkCHVZLZOWIn7v-IwADVKZVPXP7_view_usp_drivesdk_e0790ac0b1.json,8b9b89d2726e8a9c4273993c2fec9dff8e1fe0d2356e808f33b8bd49039cfa1c,132381,2,digital_text,"Powder for solution for infusion. White to off-white plug or powder. 5. CLINICAL INFORMATION 5.1 Therapeutic Indications • Non-small cell lung cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) alone, or in combination with cisplatin, is indicated for the first line treatment of locally advanced or metastatic non-small cell lung cancer. • Pancreatic Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is indicated for treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic adenocarcinoma of the pancreas. Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) also is indicated for patients with 5-FU refractory pancreatic cancer. • Bladder Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is indicated for treatment of patients with bladder cancer. • Breast Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is indicated for the treatment of patients with advanced breast cancer. Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is indicated for the treatment of patients with unresectable, locally recurrent or metastatic breast cancer who have relapsed following adjuvant/neoadjuvant chemotherapy (gemcitabine in combination with paclitaxel) or following chemotherapy for metastatic disease (gemcitabine in monotherapy). Prior chemotherapy should have included an anthracycline unless clinically contraindicated. • Cervical Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®), in combination with cisplatin, is indicated for the first line treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic cervical cancer. • Ovarian Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®), in combination with carboplatin, is indicated for locally advanced or metastatic epithelial ovarian carcinoma in patients with relapsed disease following a recurrence-free interval of at least 6 months after platinum-based, first line therapy. Other Therapeutic Activity: Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) alone or in combination has shown activity in renal cancer. Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) has shown some activity in advanced small cell lung cancer and advanced refractory testicular cancer. 5.2 Dosage and Administration 1. Standard Dosing • Non-small cell lung cancer Single drug chemotherapy Adults: The recommended dose of Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is 1000 mg/m2, given by 30 minute intravenous infusion. This should be repeated once weekly for three weeks, followed by a one week rest period. This four week cycle is then repeated. Dosage reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. In combination Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) in combination with cisplatin can be administered according to two dosage schedules; one based on a three-week cycle, the other based on a four-week cycle. The three week cycle is the usual schedule; the three-week cycle includes the administration of 1250 mg/m2 of Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) by intravenous infusion of 30 minutes on days 1 and 8, followed by a one-week rest period. This three-week cycle is then repeated. Dosage reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. The four-week cycle includes the administration of 1000 mg/m2 of Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) by intravenous infusion of 30 minutes on days 1, 8 and 15, followed by a one-week rest period. This four-week cycle is then repeated. Dosage reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. Adults: Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) in combination with carboplatin is recommended using Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) 1000 mg/m2 or 1200 mg/m2, given by 30-minute infusion administered on Days 1 and 8 of each 21-day cycle. After Gemcitabine (Gemzar®), carboplatin will be given on Day 1, consistent with a target AUC of 5 mg/mL•min. Dosage reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. • Pancreatic cancer Adults: The recommended dose of Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is 1000 mg/m2, given by 30 minute intravenous infusion. This should be repeated once weekly for up to 7 weeks followed by a week of rest. Subsequent cycles should consist of injections once weekly for 3 consecutive weeks out of every 4 weeks. Dosage reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. • Bladder Cancer Single Drug Chemotherapy The recommended dose of Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is 1250 mg/m2, given by 30 minute intravenous infusion. The dose should be given on days 1, 8, and 15 of each 28 day cycle. This four week cycle is then repeated. Dosage reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. In combination: The recommended dose of Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) in combination with cisplatin is 1000 mg/m2, administered by intravenous infusion of 30 minutes on days 1, 8 and 15, followed by a one-week rest period for a 28 day cycle. The recommended dose of cisplatin is 70 mg/m2 given at day 2. This four-week cycle is then repeated. Decrease or postponement of the dosage before each administration of the chemotherapy can be considered according to the individual safety response of the patients. In a clinical trial, in combination with cisplatin given at the dose of 100 mg/m2, bone marrow suppression has been more important. Dosage reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. • Breast Cancer Combination Use: Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) in combination with paclitaxel: paclitaxel (175 mg/m2) administered on Day 1 over approximately 3 hours as an intravenous infusion, followed by Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) (1250 mg/m2) as a 30-minute intravenous infusion on Days 1 and 8 of each 21-day cycle. Dose reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. Patients should have an absolute granulocyte count of at least 1,500 (x106/L) prior to initiation of gemcitabine + paclitaxel combination. • Cervical Cancer Combination use Adult Neoadjuvant Treatment and Metastatic Disease: Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) in combination with cisplatin is recommended using cisplatin 70 mg/m2 administered on Day 1 followed by Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) 1250 mg/m2 administered on Days 1 and 8 every 21 days. This three week cycle is then repeated. Dose reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. Adult Combination Therapy Using Radiation: Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) in combination with cisplatin is recommended using 40 mg/m2 followed immediately by Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) 125 mg/m2 by intravenous infusion once weekly for 6 weeks (Days 1, 8, 15, 22, 29, and 36), 1 to 2 hours before concurrent pelvic radiation therapy. Radiation therapy should be 50.4 Gy external beam radiation delivered to the entire field of radiation in 28 fractions, 1.8 Gy/day, 5 days/week, over the 6 weeks of chemotherapy. • Ovarian Cancer Adults: Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) in combination with carboplatin is recommended using Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) 1000 mg/m2 administered in Days 1 and 8 of each 21-day cycle as a 30-minute intravenous infusion. After Gemcitabine (Gemzar®), carboplatin should be given on Day 1 to attain a target AUC of 4.0 mg/mL·min. Dosage reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. 2. Monitoring, Dose Adjustments or Titration, Methods of Terminating Treatment Patients receiving Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) should be monitored prior to each dose for platelet, leukocyte and granulocyte counts and, if necessary, the dose of Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) may be either reduced or withheld in the presence of hematologic toxicity, according to the following scale: Absolute count granulocyte (x 106/L) Platelet Count (x 106/L) % of full dose >1,000 and >100,000 100 500 -1000 or 50,000 -100,000 75 <500 or <50,000 hold Periodic checks of renal and hepatic function, including transaminases and serum creatinine, should also be performed periodically in patients receiving gemcitabine. Elderly patients There is no evidence to suggest that dose adjustments, other than those already recommended for all patients, are necessary in the elderly, although Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) clearance and half-life are affected by age. Patients with hepatic or renal impairment Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) should be used with caution in patients with hepatic insufficiency or with impaired renal function as there is insufficient information from clinical studies to allow clear dose recommendation for this patient population. Mild to moderate renal insufficiency (GFR from 30 mL/min to 80 mL/min) has no consistent, significant effect on gemcitabine pharmacokinetics. Children Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) has been studied in limited Phase I and II trials in children in a variety of tumor types. These studies did not provide sufficient data to establish the efficacy and safety of gemcitabine in children.",1,1,4. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"• Non-small cell lung cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) alone, or in combination with cisplatin, is indicated for the first line treatment of locally advanced or metastatic non-small cell lung cancer. • Pancreatic Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is indicated for treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic adenocarcinoma of the pancreas. Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) also is indicated for patients with 5-FU refractory pancreatic cancer. • Bladder Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is indicated for treatment of patients with bladder cancer. • Breast Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is indicated for the treatment of patients with advanced breast cancer. Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is indicated for the treatment of patients with unresectable, locally recurrent or metastatic breast cancer who have relapsed following adjuvant/neoadjuvant chemotherapy (gemcitabine in combination with paclitaxel) or following chemotherapy for metastatic disease (gemcitabine in monotherapy). Prior chemotherapy should have included an anthracycline unless clinically contraindicated. • Cervical Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®), in combination with cisplatin, is indicated for the first line treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic cervical cancer. • Ovarian Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®), in combination with carboplatin, is indicated for locally advanced or metastatic epithelial ovarian carcinoma in patients with relapsed disease following a recurrence-free interval of at least 6 months after platinum-based, first line therapy. Other Therapeutic Activity: Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) alone or in combination has shown activity in renal cancer. Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) has shown some activity in advanced small cell lung cancer and advanced refractory testicular cancer.",1,1,5.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:01:41.440797+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY40393,Levocetirizine Dihydrochloride,Allercet -L,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MPi9unforyAnH1Tw2PKInoaN9TBnYart/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY40393_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MPi9unforyAnH1Tw2PKInoaN9TBnYart_view_usp_drivesdk_4bc92c5e5c.pdf,page_text/DR-XY40393_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MPi9unforyAnH1Tw2PKInoaN9TBnYart_view_usp_drivesdk_4bc92c5e5c.json,4456c55c0d610ed8b05685703c538979f1758280838aef72296e5d3c07c7ddec,7785787,2,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T05:01:52.590980+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY40409,Medroxyprogesterone Acetate,Depofemme,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/13DPizuyLQnAE9PUR0BmLUfg6u-BewkOA/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY40409_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13DPizuyLQnAE9PUR0BmLUfg6u-BewkOA_view_usp_drivesdk_a08445b36d.pdf,page_text/DR-XY40409_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13DPizuyLQnAE9PUR0BmLUfg6u-BewkOA_view_usp_drivesdk_a08445b36d.json,c1950a37e44d11ab7b13ccf846782532978ca3d6e63187bfd6d4fbde7f6a1c88,1376564,1,digital_text,"Medroxyprogesterone acetate (Depofemme) is a long-acting reversible hormonal contraceptive birth control drug that is injected every three months. It is a progestin-only contraceptive. 3. What is in the medicine? Each mL of aqueous sterile suspension contains Medroxyprogesterone acetate. 4. Strength of the medicine Each mL of aqueous sterile suspension contains: Medroxyprogesterone acetate USP………..150 mg Excipient: Polyethylene Glycol 3350, Polysorbate 80, Sodium Chloride, Methyl Paraben, Propyl Paraben, Water for Injection ad 1 mL 5. What is this medicine used for? Medroxyprogesterone acetate (Depofemme) is used as contraceptive injection for a period of three (3) months. 6. What does this medicine do to the body? Medroxyprogesterone acetate (Depofemme) administered parenterally as an intramuscular injection provides long acting progestational eﬀect by inhibiting gonadotropin production, which in turn prevents follicular maturation and ovulation. This will cause a long term unovulation in women of reproductive age. Medroxyprogesterone acetate (Depofemme) causes progestational changes in the cervical mucus in which it becomes more viscous, inhibiting sperm penetration into uterus. This steroid also produces morphological changes in the endometrium. 7. How much and how often should you use this medicine? One vial containing 150 mg Medroxyprogesterone acetate for every 3 months, given deep intramuscularly. It should be certain that the recipient is not pregnant on the ﬁrst injection. For this purpose, it is recommended to give the injection during the ﬁrst 5 days after the onset of a normal menstrual period or within 6 weeks postpartum. 8. When should you not take this medicine? a. Vaginal bleeding of unknown cause b. Mammary pathologic changes of unknown cause c. Pregnancy (either for diagnosis or treatment) d. Active thrombophlebitis or has history of thromboembolic disorder or cerebrovascular disease e. Liver function disorder 9. Undesirable eﬀects: ─ Anaphylactic reaction. ─ Local reaction; discoloration at injection site ─ It is recommended to directly inform the recipient at the start of treatment that menstrual cycle changes like irregular bleeding, and spotting might occur. Also, for some time excessive bleeding occurs especially at the start of treatment. This can be overcome by administration of Ethinyl Estradiol 0.05-0.10 mg daily for 7-21 days. ─ After repeated injections, amenorrhea and unovulation can last for up to 18 months or some time longer. 10. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Drug-Drug Interactions A mi no g lu teth im id e: A m in o g l u t e t h i m i d e a d m i n i s t e re d c o n c o m i t an t l y wi t h Medroxyprogesterone acetate (Depofemme) may signiﬁcantly depress the serum concentration of medroxyprogesterone acetate. Users of Medroxyprogesterone acetate (Depofemme) should be warned of the possibility of decreased eﬃcacy with the use of this or any related drugs. Rifampin: Rifampin can increase the metabolism of exogenously administered progestational agents. Norethindrone has speciﬁcally been aﬀected; a reduction of plasma concentrations has occurred. The extent to which Rifampin may alter the metabolism of other progestogens remains to be determined; the possibility of an interaction should be considered. Drug-Laboratory Test Interactions The following laboratory tests may be aﬀected by the use of Medroxyprogesterone acetate (Depofemme): a. Gonadotrophin level b. Plasma progesterone level c. Urinary pregnanediol level d. Plasma testosterone level (in male) Supplier Code o 180 mm 190 mm For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to FDA : www.fda.gov.ph If you suspect any adverse drug reaction, consult your doctor immediately and e-mail us at customerrelations@nurturemed.ph MEDROXYPROGESTERONE ACETATE (DEPOFEMME) Patient Information Leaﬂet (PIL) mga sumusunod na panglaboratoryang pagsusuri : a. Level ng gonadotrophin b. Level ng plasma progesterone c. Level ng urinary pregnanediol d. Level ng plasma testosterone (sa mga lalaki) e. Level ng plasma estrogen (sa mga babae) f. Level ng plasma cortisol g. Glucose tolerance test h. Metyrapone test 11. Ano ang mga dapat gawin kapag nakaligtaan ang pag-inom ng gamot na ito? Kumunsulta sa agad sa doktor. 12. Paano ang tamang paraan para itago ang gamot? Itago ito sa lugar na may temperaturang hindi lalagpas sa 30ºC. Itago sa hindi maaabot ng mga bata. 13. Mga senyales at sintomas ng overdose: Maaring magresulta sa panahon ng amenorrhea na may iba’t ibang haba at maaring sundan ng iregular na pagreregla ng ilang beses ang pag-inom ng labis na dosis. Ang sobrang taas na dosis (500 mg araw-araw o higit pa) ng Medroxyprogesterone acetate (Depofemme) ay naiugnay sa corticoid-like activity at sa sintomas ng Cushingoid (hal. moon faces at pagtaas ng presyon ng dugo). Walang alam na paggamot para sa pag-inom ng labis na dosis. 14. Ano ang dapat gawin kapag nakainom ng sobra? Kailangang kumunsulta ka sa iyong doktor o pumunta sa pinakamalapit na ospital kapag nakakaranas ka ng mga sintomas ng overdose. 15. Mga pag-iingat sa paggamit ng gamot:",1,1,2. Description of Product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T05:01:55.830969+00:00
