PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY40440,Bromazepam,Lexotan,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JWye9QXEzKBIKe5OZCL7WKIqCXvm8uHF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY40440_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1JWye9QXEzKBIKe5OZCL7WKIqCXvm8uHF_view_usp_drivesdk_f1891484b3.pdf,page_text/DR-XY40440_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1JWye9QXEzKBIKe5OZCL7WKIqCXvm8uHF_view_usp_drivesdk_f1891484b3.json,491838ba2959aea9c97756eba375878924c67000627059d0e9cc40c1206973ee,1669747,4,digital_text,"1.1 Therapeutic/Pharmacologic Class of Drug Anxiolytic. ATC code: N05BA08 1.2 Product Description Bromazepam (Lexotan) 1.5 mg tablets are max. slightly yellowish, cylindrical biplane tablets with the imprint “/1.5” on the upper side and a break score on the lower side. 1.3 Route of Administration Oral.",1,1,1. DESCRIPTION,"of the product, effects on the neonate can be expected, such as hypothermia, hypotonia and moderate respiratory depression. Moreover, infants born to mothers who took benzodiazepines chronically during the latter stages of pregnancy may have developed physical dependence and may be at some risk for developing withdrawal symptoms in the postnatal period. 2.5.2 Labor and Delivery See 2.5.1 Pregnancy. 2.5.3 Lactation As benzodiazepines pass into breast milk, nursing mothers should not take Bromazepam (Lexotan). 2.5.4 Pediatric Use See 2.2.1 Special Dosage Instructions. 2.5.5 Geriatric Use See also 2.2.1 Special Dosage Instructions, 2.6 Undesirable Effects and 3.2.5 Pharmacokinetics in Special Populations. The pharmacological effects of benzodiazepines appear to be greater in elderly patients than in younger patients, even at similar plasma benzodiazepine concentrations, possibly because of age-related changes in drug–receptor interactions, post-receptor mechanisms and organ function. A reduction in dose for patients above 50 years is recommended. 2.5.6 Hepatic Impairment See 2.2.1 Special Dosage Instructions, 2.3",2,2,"indication as, due to the pharmacological action",high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:02:35.706986+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY40446,METFORMIN (AS HYDROCHLORIDE),None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1varaKzjHMe12owDXEbJGgQ5UdnIHc2Rr/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY40446_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1varaKzjHMe12owDXEbJGgQ5UdnIHc2Rr_view_usp_drivesdk_f90145e173.pdf,page_text/DR-XY40446_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1varaKzjHMe12owDXEbJGgQ5UdnIHc2Rr_view_usp_drivesdk_f90145e173.json,330267cb47480271b4980cb5bb83efd88940b1634073524ec2fe21c74c12945f,1220800,1,ocr,,,,,"before treatment initiation and regularly thereafter. less of a problem with metformin than with the suifonylureas. Lactic acidosis, Alcohol intoxication is associated with an increased risk of lactic acidosis, the use of Treatment of Type 2 (non-insulin dependent) Diabetes Mellitus although rare, usually occur in patients whose condition Metformin is contraindicated in patients with GFR <30 mUmin and should be in case of fasting, or hepatic i metformin particularly those with renal impairment. LLOYD LABORATORIES, temporarily discontinued in the presence of conditions that alter renal function.",1,1,INDICATION:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T05:02:50.614040+00:00
