PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY40563,Linezolid,Zyvox,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1a20nG--YRoJi5K7Ltbh4lMxKEwb8lF7U/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY40563_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1a20nG--YRoJi5K7Ltbh4lMxKEwb8lF7U_view_usp_drivesdk_57a58d8afe.pdf,page_text/DR-XY40563_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1a20nG--YRoJi5K7Ltbh4lMxKEwb8lF7U_view_usp_drivesdk_57a58d8afe.json,61767a5bcdae7df9dfacf3014f39ebb41582885155423ee0e6669e5253519f49,328597,29,digital_text,"ZYVOX Solution for Infusion (IV), ZYVOX Film Coated Tablets, ZYVOX Powder for Oral Suspension contain Linezolid, which is a synthetic antibacterial agent of the oxazolidinone class. The chemical name for linezolid is (S)-N-[[3-[3-Fluoro-4-(4-morpholinyl) phenyl]-2-oxo-5- oxazolidinyl] methyl]-acetamide. The empirical formula is C16H20FN3O4. Its molecular weight is 337.35, and its chemical structure is represented below: O N C 3H F O H C N O O N Linezolid (ZYVOX) Solution for Infusion (IV) is supplied as a ready-to-use sterile isotonic solution for intravenous infusion. Each mL contains 2 mg of linezolid. Inactive ingredients are dextrose monohydrate 50.24 mg/mL in an aqueous vehicle for intravenous administration, sodium citrate dihydrate 1.64 mg/mL and citric acid anhydrous 0.85 mg/mL. Sodium hydroxide NF and/or hydrochloric acid NF are used to adjust the pH. The sodium (Na+) content is 0.38 mg/mL (5 mEq/300-mL bag). Linezolid (ZYVOX) Film Coated Tablet for oral administration contains 600 mg linezolid as a film-coated compressed tablet. Inactive ingredients are carnauba wax, corn starch hydroxypropylcellulose, hypromellose, magnesium stearate, microcrystalline cellulose, polyethylene glycol, sodium starch glycolate and titanium dioxide. The sodium (Na+) content is 2.92 mg per 600-mg tablet (0.1 mEq/tablet). Linezolid (ZYVOX) Powder for Oral Suspension is supplied as an orange-flavored granule/powder for constitution into a suspension for oral administration. Following constitution, each 5 mL contains 100 mg of linezolid. Inactive ingredients are aspartame, citric acid, colloidal silicon dioxide, flavors, mannitol, microcrystalline cellulose and carboxymethylcellulose sodium, sodium benzoate, sodium chloride, sodium citrate, sucrose and xanthan gum (see section 6.5 Patient Counseling Information). The sodium (Na+) content is 8.52 mg/5 mL (0.4 mEq/5 mL).",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Nosocomial Pneumonia Linezolid (ZYVOX) is indicated for the treatment of nosocomial pneumonia caused by Staphylococcus aureus (methicillin-susceptible and resistant isolates) or Streptococcus pneumoniae (see section 5.3 Preclinical Safety Data – Clinical Studies). Community-acquired Pneumonia Linezolid (ZYVOX) is indicated for the treatment of community-acquired pneumonia caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae, including cases with concurrent bacteremia, or Staphylococcus aureus (methicillin-susceptible isolates only) (see section 5.3 Preclinical Safety Data – Clinical Studies). Complicated Skin and Skin Structure Infections Linezolid (ZYVOX) is indicated for the treatment of complicated skin and skin structure infections, including diabetic foot infections, without concomitant osteomyelitis, caused by Staphylococcus aureus (methicillin-susceptible and -resistant isolates), Streptococcus pyogenes, or Streptococcus agalactiae. Linezolid (ZYVOX) has not been studied in the treatment of decubitus ulcers (see section 5.3 Preclinical Safety Data – Clinical Studies). Uncomplicated Skin and Skin Structure Infections Linezolid (ZYVOX) is indicated for the treatment of uncomplicated skin and skin structure infections caused by Staphylococcus aureus (methicillin-susceptible isolates only) or Streptococcus pyogenes (see section 5.3 Preclinical Safety Data – Clinical Studies). Vancomycin-resistant Enterococcus faecium Infections Linezolid (ZYVOX) is indicated for the treatment of vancomycin-resistant Enterococcus faecium infections, including cases with concurrent bacteremia (see section 5.3 Preclinical Safety Data – Clinical Studies). Limitations of Use • Linezolid (ZYVOX) is not indicated for the treatment of Gram-negative infections. It is critical that specific Gram-negative therapy be initiated immediately if a concomitant Gram-negative pathogen is documented or suspected (see section 4.4 Special Warnings and Precautions for Use). • The safety and efficacy of linezolid (ZYVOX) formulations given for longer than 28 days have not been evaluated in controlled clinical trials (see section 5.3 Preclinical Safety Data – Clinical Studies). Usage To reduce the development of drug-resistant bacteria and maintain the effectiveness of linezolid (ZYVOX) and other antibacterial drugs, linezolid (ZYVOX) should be used only to treat or prevent infections that are proven or strongly suspected to be caused by susceptible bacteria. When culture and susceptibility information are available, they should be considered in selecting or modifying antibacterial therapy. In the absence of such data, local epidemiology and susceptibility patterns may contribute to the empiric selection of therapy.",2,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:02:59.202804+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY40595,Montelukast (as Sodium),Montiget,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PGRrs4bb_Rvts5Um2c50cLPJy9Hrq5ZM/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY40595_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PGRrs4bb_Rvts5Um2c50cLPJy9Hrq5ZM_view_usp_drivesdk_9e3159bdac.pdf,page_text/DR-XY40595_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PGRrs4bb_Rvts5Um2c50cLPJy9Hrq5ZM_view_usp_drivesdk_9e3159bdac.json,d1b74a954d64bed73300f8a05b961923ec42db025d4e3495954639eedb0ca872,5889310,8,digital_text,"Montelukast (Montiget®) 4mg Pediatric Granules are available as white to off-white granular powder filled in a printed sachet. Montelukast (Montiget ®) 4mg Chewable Tablet is available as light pink to pink round biconvex shaped tablet engraved ""GETZ"" on one side and plain on other side. Montelukast (Montiget ®) 5mg Chewable Tablet is available as white round biconvex shaped tablet engraved ""GETZ"" on one side and plain on other side. Montelukast (Montiget ®) 10mg Film-Coated Tablet is available as cream to light yellow colored square shaped film-coated tablet having bisect line on one side and plain on other side.",3,3,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"- Montelukast (Montiget ®) is indicated for the prophylaxis and chronic treatment of asthma including: - The prevention of day and night time symptoms. - The treatment of aspirin-sensitive asthmatic patients. - The prevention of exercise-induced bronchoconstriction. - Montelukast (Montiget ®) is effective alone or in combination with other agents used in the maintenance treatment of chronic asthma. Montelukast (Montiget ®) and inhaled corticosteroids may be used concomitantly with additive effects to control asthma or to reduce the inhaled corticosteroid dose while maintaining clinical stability. - Montelukast (Montiget ®) is also indicated for the relief of symptoms of seasonal allergic rhinitis in adults and pediatric patients 2 years of age and older, and perennial allergic rhinitis in adults and pediatric patients 6 months of age and older, including nasal congestion, rhinorrhea, nasal itching, sneezing, nasal congestion upon awakening, difficulty going to sleep, and nighttime awakenings; tearing, itchy, red, and puffy eyes.",3,3,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:03:07.941595+00:00
