PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41127,Minerals + Cholecalciferol (Vitamin D3),Calciumade,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1AMhdh6fd2ALIWD7Lc8z2gy-mlxPZJbnV/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41127_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1AMhdh6fd2ALIWD7Lc8z2gy-mlxPZJbnV_view_usp_drivesdk_69a4778f1d.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41127_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1AMhdh6fd2ALIWD7Lc8z2gy-mlxPZJbnV_view_usp_drivesdk_69a4778f1d.json,ce3e258b8855020ab3da8c13e388a9a12cb82a38d2f5a70276eac7429d2b9152,113536,1,digital_text,"This product is an orange, biconvex, elliptical-shaped coated tablet with product name on one side and plain on the other side. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This medicine contains a combination of Calcium, Vitamin D, Magnesium, Zinc, and Manganese which are nutrients known to help protect against osteoporosis and promote optimum bone health. BONE-BUILDING NUTRIENTS BIOCHEMICAL AND PHYSIOLOGIC FUNCTIONS Calcium • The most important structural component of bones and teeth • A key factor in the normal transmission of nerve impulses • Essential for the formation of fibrin, the fibrous protein that makes up the structure of blood clots. • Key player in the regulation of cellular metabolism and may regulate a variety of enzymatic processes that affect cell secretions, ciliary action, cell division, and cell proliferation. Vitamin D 3 • Acts to maintain normal concentrations of calcium and phosphorus in plasma, mainly by facilitating calcium absorption from the small intestine and by enhancing the parathyroid hormone (PTH)-mediated mobilization of calcium and phosphorus from bone • The active form of vitamin D increases the production of calcium-binding proteins in the lining of the small intestine Magnesium • Essential for enzymes needed to incorporate calcium in bones • Involved in reactions that convert vitamin D into its active form; the presence of the active form of vitamin D results in a 10-30% increase in calcium absorption allowing more calcium to be deposited in bones • Important for the electrical stability of cells, the maintenance of membrane integrity, muscle contraction, blood clotting, nerve conduction, and the regulation of vascular tone Reg. IPOPHIL DR-XY41127 P300000036095 BONE-BUILDING NUTRIENTS BIOCHEMICAL AND PHYSIOLOGIC FUNCTIONS Zinc • A cofactor for various enzymes required for normal bone development • Required for proper calcium absorption, enhances the activity of vitamin D • Necessary for proper osteoblast activity and bone collagen",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T05:05:13.106048+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41127,Minerals + Cholecalciferol (Vitamin D3),Calciumade,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1e59YHrD-8mo09s6a6fWXBfI84Nq1SARA/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41127_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1e59YHrD-8mo09s6a6fWXBfI84Nq1SARA_view_usp_drivesdk_81f86de194.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41127_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1e59YHrD-8mo09s6a6fWXBfI84Nq1SARA_view_usp_drivesdk_81f86de194.json,ce3e258b8855020ab3da8c13e388a9a12cb82a38d2f5a70276eac7429d2b9152,113536,1,digital_text,"This product is an orange, biconvex, elliptical-shaped coated tablet with product name on one side and plain on the other side. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This medicine contains a combination of Calcium, Vitamin D, Magnesium, Zinc, and Manganese which are nutrients known to help protect against osteoporosis and promote optimum bone health. BONE-BUILDING NUTRIENTS BIOCHEMICAL AND PHYSIOLOGIC FUNCTIONS Calcium • The most important structural component of bones and teeth • A key factor in the normal transmission of nerve impulses • Essential for the formation of fibrin, the fibrous protein that makes up the structure of blood clots. • Key player in the regulation of cellular metabolism and may regulate a variety of enzymatic processes that affect cell secretions, ciliary action, cell division, and cell proliferation. Vitamin D 3 • Acts to maintain normal concentrations of calcium and phosphorus in plasma, mainly by facilitating calcium absorption from the small intestine and by enhancing the parathyroid hormone (PTH)-mediated mobilization of calcium and phosphorus from bone • The active form of vitamin D increases the production of calcium-binding proteins in the lining of the small intestine Magnesium • Essential for enzymes needed to incorporate calcium in bones • Involved in reactions that convert vitamin D into its active form; the presence of the active form of vitamin D results in a 10-30% increase in calcium absorption allowing more calcium to be deposited in bones • Important for the electrical stability of cells, the maintenance of membrane integrity, muscle contraction, blood clotting, nerve conduction, and the regulation of vascular tone Reg. IPOPHIL DR-XY41127 P300000036095 BONE-BUILDING NUTRIENTS BIOCHEMICAL AND PHYSIOLOGIC FUNCTIONS Zinc • A cofactor for various enzymes required for normal bone development • Required for proper calcium absorption, enhances the activity of vitamin D • Necessary for proper osteoblast activity and bone collagen",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T05:05:16.032744+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41226,Nilotinib (as hydrochloride monohydrate),Tasigna,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/11Ie0bF1RtrOTkZSXX_0hjBIJiHzrrEQ5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41226_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11Ie0bF1RtrOTkZSXX_0hjBIJiHzrrEQ5_view_usp_drivesdk_d9a98bd0a3.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41226_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11Ie0bF1RtrOTkZSXX_0hjBIJiHzrrEQ5_view_usp_drivesdk_d9a98bd0a3.json,2ec4c4780a8e414ca2b5000b95955e9ec23cb0824e092a25077d2fad114fff38,710316,44,digital_text,"Pharmaceutical form Hard capsules. 150 mg hard capsules White to yellowish powder in red opaque hard gelatin capsules, size 1 with black axial imprint “NVR/BCR”. 200 mg hard capsules White to yellowish powder in light yellow opaque hard gelatin capsules, size 0 with red axial imprint “NVR/TKI”. Active substances 150 mg hard capsules Each capsule contains 150 mg nilotinib base (as hydrochloride, monohydrate). 200 mg hard capsules Each capsule contains 200 mg nilotinib base (as hydrochloride, monohydrate) Certain dosage strengths and dosage forms may not be available in all countries. Excipients 150 mg hard capsules Capsule content: Lactose monohydrate; Crospov idone; Poloxamer 188; Silica colloidal, anhydrous/Colloidal silicon dioxide; Magnesium stearate Capsule shell: Gelatin; Titanium dioxide (E 171); Iron oxide, red (E 172), Iron oxide, yellow (E 172) Nilotinib [Page 2] Printing ink: Shellac; Iron oxide, black (E 172); n-Butyl alcohol; Propylene glycol; Dehydrated ethanol; Isopropyl alcohol; Ammonium hydroxide 200 mg hard capsules Capsule content: Lactose monohydrate; Crospov idone; Poloxamer 188; Silica colloidal, anhydrous/Colloidal silicon dioxide; Magnesium stearate Capsule shell: Gelatin; Titanium dioxide (E 171); Iron oxide, yellow (E 172) Printing ink: Shellac; Dehydrated alcohol; Isopropyl alcohol; Butyl alcohol; Propylene glycol; Strong ammonia solution; Potassium hydroxide; Titanium dioxide; Industrial methylated spirit; Iron oxide, red (E 172), Iron oxide, black (E172) Pharmaceutical formulations may vary between countries.",1,2,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION, Treatment of adult pati ents with newly diagnosed Philadelphia chromosome positive chronic myeloid leukemia (Ph+ CML) in chronic phase. Patients who have been treated with nilotinib (Tasigna ®) for at least 3 years and have achieved a sustained deep molecular response may be elig ible for treatment discontinuation (see sections DOSAGE REGIMEN AND ADMINISTRATION and CLINICAL,2,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:05:19.755159+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41252,Esomeprazole (As Magnesium),Nexpro-40,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/11BgR0UlJ7xbfBokFNWXNROv0ThRdVHOT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41252_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11BgR0UlJ7xbfBokFNWXNROv0ThRdVHOT_view_usp_drivesdk_c53e6e7329.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41252_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11BgR0UlJ7xbfBokFNWXNROv0ThRdVHOT_view_usp_drivesdk_c53e6e7329.json,0454e97b6ee779a99185ec5807c3ec538daf4c002e221de74169e42c59b0fbc3,312163,1,digital_text,"Esomeprazole (Nexpro-20) 20 mg Enteric-Coated Tablet is a brick red colored, round shape, biconvex, film coated tablet, imprinted with ""20"" on one side with black ink and plain on other side. Esomeprazole (Nexpro-40) 40 mg Enteric-Coated Tablet is a brick red colored, round shape, biconvex, film coated tablet, imprinted with ""40"" on one side with black ink and plain on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Esomeprazole is indicated in the following conditions: Gastro-esophageal Reflux Disease (GERD): - treatment of erosive reflux esophagitis - long-term management of patients with healed esophagitis to prevent relapse - symptomatic treatment of gastro-esophageal reflux disease (GERD) Patients requiring continued NSAID therapy: - prevention of gastric and duodenal ulcers associated with non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) therapy in patients at risk In combination with appropriate antibacterial therapeutic regimens for the eradication of Helicobacter pylori: - healing of Helicobacter pylori associated duodenal ulcer - prevention of relapse of peptic ulcers in patients with Helicobacter pylori associated ulcer disease.,1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:05:23.107862+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41262,Naftazone,Mediaven Forte,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hbAWdVN7qn2j0JtMcdZqwvyJ_v-ZlIEI/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41262_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hbAWdVN7qn2j0JtMcdZqwvyJ_v-ZlIEI_view_usp_drivesdk_bd40ee14f8.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41262_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hbAWdVN7qn2j0JtMcdZqwvyJ_v-ZlIEI_view_usp_drivesdk_bd40ee14f8.json,7f30b30324644887a9b12e474b1d78060c11d7a81ce4a74956d189779ec8d1de,275416,2,digital_text,"“For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph” Patient to seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Distribution Naftazone does not bind to plasma proteins. Elimination/Metabolism Approximately 90% of the asministered dose is excreted in the urine, and the elimination half-life equals 1.5 hours. Naftazone excreted by the kidneys appears almost completely as sulfo-and glucuro-conjugates. Kinetics for Special Patient Groups Renal insufficiency No data are available for renal insufficiency. [Page 3]",2,2,prescription.,"All forms of venous insufficiency: pre-varicose conditions (heavy legs, intermittent ankle oedema, nocturnal leg cramps, etc.). Painful varices. Secondary venous insufficiency (post thrombotic syndrome, leg complaints with ovulation inhibitors). Diabetic retinopathy. Dosage/Application 1 x 1 film-coated tablet daily, for one month or longer. The use and safety of Naftazone (Mediaven forte) in children and adolescents has not been examinated to date.",1,1,Indications/Possible Applications,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T05:05:26.048953+00:00
