PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41520,Paclitaxel,Paclitex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cBvYVD85ZH-Y5f-itpqRuRNecjEwHEcT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41520_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cBvYVD85ZH-Y5f-itpqRuRNecjEwHEcT_view_usp_drivesdk_ebe4f0b6c0.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41520_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cBvYVD85ZH-Y5f-itpqRuRNecjEwHEcT_view_usp_drivesdk_ebe4f0b6c0.json,a4fdb95a58c594e48fd44ae6d60bc2eb389f70b2535999dbf1c1693e5bf2ff32,139676,2,digital_text,"Paclitaxel is an antineoplastic agent from the taxane class of drugs. The chemical name of paclitaxel is: (2 S,5 R,7 S,10 R,13 S)-10,20-bis(acetoxy)-2-benzoyloxy-1,7- dihydroxy-9-oxo-5,20- epoxytax- 11-en-13-yl (3 S) -3-benzoylamino-3-phenyl-D- lactate. 11-en-13-yl (3 S) -3-benzoylamino-3-phenyl-D- lactate. Injectable paclitaxel is supplied as a non aqueous solution to be previously diluted in a suitable parenteral fluid prior to intravenous infusion. A white to off -white powder. Insoluble in water; soluble in alcohol. PHARMACOLOGY Paclitaxel’s antineoplastic action arises from induction of microtubule formation and stabilization of microtubules, thereby disrupting normal cell division in the G2 and M phases of the cell cycle.",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Paclitaxel is used for the primary treatment of advanced ovarian cancer with cisplatin or carboplatin, and for secondary treatment. In the treatment of node- positive breast cancer, paclitaxel is used for primary adjuvant therapy after anthracycline-containing chemotherapy. In locally advanced or metastatic breast cancer, it is used first -line with an anthracycline, or as a second- line single-agent, usually after failure of anthracycline-based therapy. In patients with metastatic disease who over express HER2 (human epidermal growth receptor 2) it may be used with trastuzumab as initial therapy. Paclitaxel is used with cisplatin or carboplatin, for the primary treatment of advanced non-small cell lung cancer. It may be used for the second- line treatment of AIDS-related Kaposi’s sarcoma, and has been tried in other neoplasms including cancers of the head and neck, and relapsed germ-cell tumours. PHARMACOKINETICS Intravenous paclitaxel exhibits a biphasic decline in plasma concentrations, with a mean terminal half -life of anywhere between about 3 and 50 hours. The pharmacokinetics are non- linear. The steady -state volume of distribution is reported to range from 200 to 700 litres/m 2, indicating extensive extravascular distribution, tissue binding, or both. Paclitaxel is 89% or more bound to plasma protein in vitro. The elimination of paclitaxel has not been fully elucidated; only about 1 to 12% of a dose is reported to be excreted in urine, as unchanged drug, indicating extensive non-renal clearance. Paclitaxel is metabolized in the liver, with the major metabolic pathway apparently mediated by the cytochrome P450 isoenzyme CYP2C8, although CYP3A4 may play a minor role. Metabolites are excreted in the faeces via the bile, the primary metabolite being 6α-hydroxypaclitaxel.",1,1,INDICATION,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:06:58.506105+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41586,Rosuvastatin (As Calcium),Turbovas -5,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NvuaRMgKBSGFukNkF8KhbIce55imH-x6/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41586_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1NvuaRMgKBSGFukNkF8KhbIce55imH-x6_view_usp_drivesdk_79b8d520db.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41586_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1NvuaRMgKBSGFukNkF8KhbIce55imH-x6_view_usp_drivesdk_79b8d520db.json,af7a0f84f0d087b11255e0590176f866ef99d7b258d4e9eca58046582e9959f8,7424434,3,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T05:07:08.539563+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41615,Ascorbic Acid,Mightee-Cee,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gbLc5WckC_zWGZIpBzozxckfKk2wwzY9/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41615_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gbLc5WckC_zWGZIpBzozxckfKk2wwzY9_view_usp_drivesdk_68d24c2fdb.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41615_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gbLc5WckC_zWGZIpBzozxckfKk2wwzY9_view_usp_drivesdk_68d24c2fdb.json,0b9e158585dea2b2a1160fcbc3c98ce04ff3cf30ad6778778406021c48c39741,704314,1,ocr,"ACID Vitamin Cis a water-soluble vitamin which is necessary for the body to form collagen in bones, cartilage, muscle, and blood vessels and aids in the absorption of iron which is needed for red blood cell production Sodium Ascorbate is a natural non-acidic form of Vitamin C. It is neutralized with sodium for persons that MIGHTEE-CEE have sensitive stomach, preventing gastric irritation due to acidity. It is also essential for the proper healing of wounds and enhances the defensive mechanisms of the body against bacterial infections. Sodium Ascorbate offers many health benefits, which includes boosting of the immune system and 200 mg / 5 mL Syrup energy levels. It is more bioavailable than other forms of Vitamin C. VITAMIN",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"Ascorbic Acid(as Sodium Ascorbate)(Mightee-Cee) may be taken or the treatment and prevention of Vitamin C deficiency. It enhances body resistance from infectious diseases and common colds. It also boosts our body’s immune system. Sodium Ascorbate speeds up healing of wounds, recovery from ilnesses and maintenance of healthy bones, teeth and gums.",1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T05:07:13.943474+00:00
