PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41645,Theophylline,Nuelin SR 250,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/172AM2ttJw7Sf3LsRGuHjQC9Pb2KvCtA6/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41645_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_172AM2ttJw7Sf3LsRGuHjQC9Pb2KvCtA6_view_usp_drivesdk_2af65fb6c4.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41645_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_172AM2ttJw7Sf3LsRGuHjQC9Pb2KvCtA6_view_usp_drivesdk_2af65fb6c4.json,9871e2238533f8dc5ac3e5399c3caa7c93e12c824ba4c66c5d678a30b327104b,438655,2,digital_text,,,,,"For the relief and prophylaxis of reversible bronchospasm associated with bronchial asthma, bronchitis, emphysema and related conditions.",1,1,INDICATIONS,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T05:07:27.366048+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41647,Calcium (as carbonate),Unbranded,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1nDSqzK1zUZpc3Z7j19MU1uKnlSNCjBOQ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41647_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1nDSqzK1zUZpc3Z7j19MU1uKnlSNCjBOQ_view_usp_drivesdk_c182d16e36.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41647_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1nDSqzK1zUZpc3Z7j19MU1uKnlSNCjBOQ_view_usp_drivesdk_c182d16e36.json,1661da9f88f36e287987774732b76e07974a7b96402aeed0ac97504470d25268,346400,2,ocr,"Calcium carbonate 1250 mg Tablet is a white to off-white, oblong, biconvex, film-coated tablet, bisected on one side, plain on the other side. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This medicine contains Calcium, a nutrient known to help protect against osteoporosis and promote optimum bone health. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Please see Formulation WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? For the prevention and treatment of calcium deficiency states in individuals with inadequate levels of calcium in their diet, calcium malabsorption and malnutrition. For prevention and treatment of osteoporosis. Increased calcium requirement in children and adolescent and during pregnancy and lactation. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Calcium Supplement 1-3 tablet(s) daily. Average daily consumption should not exceed 8 tablets. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOTTAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you are allergic to any component in the product. If you have hypercalcemia (excess calcium in the blood), kidney impairment, or any disease associated with hypercalcemia. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Do not take more than 8 tablets in a 24-hour period nor use the maximum dosage of this product, except under the advice and supervision of a physician. It can cause flatulence, diarrhea or constipation. Hypercalcemia and alkalosis may occur with large doses. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS Hypercalcemia, hypercalciuria (excess calcium in the urine), vascular and soft tissue calcification (deposition of calcium in blood vessels and soft tissue) and nephrolithiasis (kidney stones) have been reported with high doses of calcium. Minor gastrointestinal disturbances such as bloating, constipation, flatulence, and nausea have also been reported with calcium supplements. [Page 2] WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOODS SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? May interact with certain prescription drugs (i.e. tetracyclines, digitalis). If you are presently taking a prescription drug, do not take this product without checking with your physician or other health professionals. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO WHEN YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, just take the next dose and the subsequent doses at the usual recommended schedule, i.e., once a day. Do not double the dose unless recommended by a doctor. WHAT ARE THE SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE? No data available on overdosage when taken in the recommended dose. However, in particularly susceptible individuals (i.e. patients with kidney failure), doses greater than 2 g elemental calcium per day may cause high levels of calcium in the urine and lead to kidney stones, which may result to kidney damage. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from light. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT A DOCTOR? - If any undesirable effect occurs. -Women who are pregnant should have regular prenatal check-up with their doctor. AVAILABILITY Alu Strip foil x 4's (Box of 100's) ADR REPORTING For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph Patient should seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. REGISTRATION NUMBER DR-XY41647 DATE OF FIRST AUTHORIZATION 05 February 2013 Manufactured by:",1,2,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T05:07:33.684862+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41657,Midazolam,Dormicum,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CS9sURmCnnIKDbMEpGmBDCKWoTgO6Sum/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41657_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1CS9sURmCnnIKDbMEpGmBDCKWoTgO6Sum_view_usp_drivesdk_eb35cd80a0.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41657_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1CS9sURmCnnIKDbMEpGmBDCKWoTgO6Sum_view_usp_drivesdk_eb35cd80a0.json,b85a299b417b9404f774fb1b5e95e619e061ce721d20afe11a0d97425a1ac856,740215,4,digital_text,"1.1 Therapeutic / Pharmacologic Class of Drug Midazolam (Dormicum®) Tablet is a sleep-inducing agent belonging to the benzodiazepines. ATC code: N05CD08. 1.2 Type of Dosage Form Tablets. Midazolam (Dormicum®) 15 mg film-coated tablets are oval, cylindrical, biconvex, grey-blue tablets with ”15” engraved on one side and a break-mark on the other side. 1.3 Route of Administration Oral use. 1.4 Sterile / Radioactive Statement Not applicable.",1,1,1. DESCRIPTION,"- Short-term treatment of insomnia. Benzodiazepines are only indicated when the disorder is severe, disabling or subjecting the individual to extreme distress. - Sedation in premedication before surgical or diagnostic procedures.",1,1,2.1 Therapeutic Indication(s),high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:07:36.905894+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41692,Glucose + Amino Acids + Electrolytes + Vitamin B1,Bfluid,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Ic_Ughiolnkc9HlDXefQULhEF8D3F79Q/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41692_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Ic_Ughiolnkc9HlDXefQULhEF8D3F79Q_view_usp_drivesdk_909a96438f.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41692_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Ic_Ughiolnkc9HlDXefQULhEF8D3F79Q_view_usp_drivesdk_909a96438f.json,409cd00a23313a1ccc5ac70d8240d0e2e63964617657d032fc0bd47831a9fc87,1021942,2,digital_text,,1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Provision of amino acids, electrolytes, vitamin B , and water via a peripheral vein to patients with 1 mild hypoproteinemia or mild malnutrition due to inadequate oral intake, and before and after surgery.",1,1,INDICATIONS,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T05:07:41.318469+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41696,Abiraterone Acetate,Zytiga,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1amQv8T8kRtqaLgfp9TzKMeMQ4dRZmOEu/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41696_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1amQv8T8kRtqaLgfp9TzKMeMQ4dRZmOEu_view_usp_drivesdk_20b4498628.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41696_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1amQv8T8kRtqaLgfp9TzKMeMQ4dRZmOEu_view_usp_drivesdk_20b4498628.json,081a10e9aaebaa4b2f7057415bb07b7d9b9b041822909e68d03cd790e59b1b03,836975,21,digital_text,"Cardiovascular reactions The three Phase 3 studies excluded patients with uncontrolled hypertension, clinically significant heart disease as evidenced by myocardial infarction, arterial thrombotic events in the past 6 months, severe or unstable angina, NYHA Class III or IV heart failure (study 301) or Class II to IV heart failure (studies 3011 and 302) or cardiac ejection fraction measurement of < 50%. All p atients enrolled (both active and placebo-treated patients) w ere concomitantly treated with androgen deprivation therapy, predominantly with the use of LHRH analogues, which has been associated with diabetes, myocardial infarction, cerebrovascular accident and sudden cardiac death. The incidence of cardiovascular adverse reactions in the Phase 3 studies in patients taking abiraterone acetate versus patients taking placebo were as follows: atrial fibrillation 2.6% vs 2.0%, tachycardia 1.9% vs. 1.0%, angina pectoris 1.7% vs. 0.8%, cardiac failure 0.7% vs. 0.2% and arrhythmia 0.7% vs. 0.5%. Hepatotoxicity Hepatotoxicity with elevated ALT, AST and total bilirubin has been reported in patients treated with abiraterone acetate. Across Phase 3 clinical studies, hepatotoxicity grades 3 and 4 (e.g., ALT or AST increases of > 5X ULN or bilirubin increases > 1.5X ULN) were reported in approximately 6% of patients who received abiraterone acetate, typically during the first 3 months after starting treatment. In Study 3011, grade 3 or 4 hepatotoxicity was observed in 8.4% of patients treated with abiraterone acetate (Zytiga®). Ten patients who received abiraterone acetate (Zytiga®) were discontinued because of hepatotoxicity; two had Grade 2 hepatotoxicity, six had Grade 3 hepatotoxicity, and two had Grade 4 hepatotoxicity. No patient died of hepatotoxicity in Study 3011. In the Phase 3 clinical studies, patients whose baseline ALT or AST were elevated were more likely to experience liver function test e levations th an those beginning with normal values. When elevations of either ALT or AST > 5 x ULN, or elevations in bilirubin > 3 x ULN were observed, abiraterone acetate was withheld or discontinued. In two instances marked increases in liver function tests occurred (see Special Warnings and Special Precautions for Use). These two patients with normal baseline hepatic function, experienced ALT or AST elevations 15 to 40 x ULN and bilirubin elevations 2 to 6 x ULN. Upon discontinuation of treatment, both patients had normalization of their liver function tests and one patient was re-treated with without recurrence of the elevations. In study 302, Grade 3 or 4 ALT or AST elevations were observed in 35 (6.5%) patients treated with abiraterone acetate. Aminotransferase elevations resolved in all but 3 patients (2 with new multiple liver metastases and 1 with AST elevation approximately 3 weeks after the last dose of abiraterone acetate). In Phase 3 clinical studies, treatment discontinuations due to ALT and AST increases or abnormal hepatic function were reported in 1.1% of patients treated with abiraterone acetate and 0.6% of patients treated with placebo; no deaths were reported due to hepatotoxicity events. In clinical trials, the risk for hepatotoxicity was mitigated by exclusion of patients with baseline hepatitis or significant abnormalities of liver function tests. In the 3011 trial, patients with baseline ALT and AST > 2.5 X ULN, bilirubin > 1.5 X ULN or those with active or symptomatic viral hepatitis or chronic liver disease; ascites or bleeding disorders secondary to hepatic dysfunction were excluded. In the 301 trial, patients with baseline ALT and AST ≥ 2.5 X ULN in the absence of liver metastases and > 5 X ULN in the presence of liver metastases were excluded. In the 302 trial, patients with liver metastases were not eligible and patients with baseline ALT and AST ≥ 2.5 X ULN were excluded. Abnormal liver function tests developing in patients participating in clinical trials were vigorously managed by requiring treatment interruption and permitting re-treatment only after return of liver function tests to the patient’s baseline (see Dosage and Method of Administration). Patients with elevations of ALT or AST > 20 x ULN were not re-treated. The safety of re-treatment in such patients is unknown. The mechanism for hepatotoxicity is not understood. [Page 20] Approved package insert – EU SmPC 30 April 2021 OVERDOSE Human experience of overdose with abiraterone acetate (Zytiga®) is limited. There is no specific antidote. In the event of an overdose, administration should be withheld and general supportive measures undertaken, including monitoring for arrhythmias, hypokalemia and for signs and symptoms of fluid retention. Liver function also should be assessed. INCOMPATIBILITIES Not applicable. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS FOR DISPOSAL AND HANDLING Based on its mechanism of action, this medicinal product may harm a developing fetus; therefore, women who are pregnant or may be pregnant should not handle it without protection, e.g., gloves. Any unused medicinal product or waste material should be disposed of in accordance with local requirements. This medicinal product may pose a risk to the aquatic environment (see Preclinical Safety Data). SPECIAL PRECAUTIONS FOR STORAGE Store at temperatures not exceeding 30oC. Keep out of the sight and reach of children. AVAILABILITY 250 mg tablet: HDPE Bottle of 120’s/Box of 1’s 500 mg film-coated tablet: PVdC/PE/PVC/aluminum blister x 12 film-coated tablets in carton wallet, 5 wallets in a box/Box of 60’s CAUTION Foods, Drugs, Devices and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription. Patient must seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. Questions or comments? Email us at Janssendrugsafety_Phil@its.jnj.com. REGISTRATION NUMBER 250 mg tablet: DR-XY41696 500 mg film-coated tablet: DR-XY46839 DATE OF FIRST AUTHORIZATION 250 mg tablet: 15 February 2013 500 mg film-coated tablet: 09 March 2020 250 mg tablet: Manufactured by: Patheon Inc. 2100 Syntex Court Mississauga, Ontario, L5N 7K9, Canada Packed by: Janssen-Cilag S.p.A. Via C. Janssen Borgo San Michele Latina, Italy 500 mg film-coated tablet: [Page 21] Approved package insert – EU SmPC 30 April 2021 Manufactured by: Patheon S.A.S. 40 Boulevard de Champaret 38300 Bourgoin-Jallieu France Packed by: Janssen-Cilag S.p.A. Via C. Janssen Borgo San Michele Latina, Italy Imported by: KM 14 Edison Road, Merville, Parañaque City Revision date: 20 September 2021 (based on 30 April 2021 EU SmPC) [Page 22]",19,21,Description of selected adverse reactions,Abiraterone acetate (Zytiga®) is indicated with prednisone or prednisolone for: • the treatment of newly diagnosed high risk metastatic hormone sensitive prostate cancer (mHSPC) in adult men in combination with androgen deprivation therapy (ADT) (see Pharmacodynamic Properties) • the treatment of metastatic castration resistant prostate cancer (mCRPC) in adult men who are asymptomatic or mildly symptomatic after failure of androgen deprivation therapy in whom chemotherapy is not yet clinically indicated (see Pharmacodynamic Properties) • the treatment of metastatic castration resistant prostate cancer (mCRPC) in adult men whose disease has progressed on or after a docetaxel-based chemotherapy regimen.,12,12,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:07:47.071565+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41729,Clarithromycin,Macromycin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wGdIi4NS3-_jOjsFsReYYJBWT42Zb9xj/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41729_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wGdIi4NS3-_jOjsFsReYYJBWT42Zb9xj_view_usp_drivesdk_84021d1880.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41729_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wGdIi4NS3-_jOjsFsReYYJBWT42Zb9xj_view_usp_drivesdk_84021d1880.json,f6c45de1a658808adbe9f61ab6134ecf23c10c8880363b6063e0b74285fbc26e,8528993,1,digital_text,"Clarithromycin is semi synthetic macrolide antibiotic obtained by substitution of the hydroxyl group in position 6 by a CH3O group of the lactone ring of erythromycin. Clarithromycin is 6-0 methyl erythromycin A. Characterized by white to off-white, round, biconvex ﬁlm-coated tablet, plain on both sides. The white to off-white antibiotic powder is bitter, practically odorless, essentially insoluble in water, and slightly soluble in ethanol, methanol and acetonitrile. Its molecular weight is 747.96.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,It is used in the treatment of respiratory-tract infections (including otitis media) and in skin and soft-tissue infections. It is also used for the prophylaxis and treatment of nontuberculous mycobacterial infections.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:07:53.558878+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41743,L-Ornithine-L-Aspartate,Hepa-Merz,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/15tbQMPJn5J04at9Ij1xQ8Y0PPSYQMcIO/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41743_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15tbQMPJn5J04at9Ij1xQ8Y0PPSYQMcIO_view_usp_drivesdk_11db13a2f5.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41743_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15tbQMPJn5J04at9Ij1xQ8Y0PPSYQMcIO_view_usp_drivesdk_11db13a2f5.json,e8c657b7dd31b184d128ffba216d40b673db0826c2f6cf17aa32f2a2e61abe5a,349264,2,digital_text,Concentrate for solution for infusion. L-Ornithine-L-Aspartate (Hepa-Merz) infusion concentrate is a clear solution.,1,1,Pharmaceutical Form:,"For the treatment of hyperammonemia as a result of acute and chronic liver disease such as liver cirrhosis, fatty liver, hepatitis, especially for the treatment of incipient disturbances of consciousness (precoma) or neurological complications (hepatic encephalopathy).",1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:07:56.727210+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41745,Calcipotriol (as Monohydrate) + Betamethasone (as dipropionate),DAIVOBET,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/101AgKxmpR5Gv_zBPvcM4-T5P6ulmZrMs/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41745_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_101AgKxmpR5Gv_zBPvcM4-T5P6ulmZrMs_view_usp_drivesdk_7ecdd83da6.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41745_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_101AgKxmpR5Gv_zBPvcM4-T5P6ulmZrMs_view_usp_drivesdk_7ecdd83da6.json,f496f7dae0ab26afaba3869afea5935632c816de183ec117edf26f92cdc6edc5,1079764,2,digital_text,"Gel. Almost clear, colourless to slightly off-white gel.",1,1,Product Description,Topical treatment of scalp psoriasis. Topical treatment of mild to moderate “non-scalp” plaque psoriasis vulgaris.,1,1,Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:08:00.583823+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41780,Everolimus,Afinitor,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1j5fo2jAST0k5fSn5YZ0ZG4ldrrEus-JX/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41780_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1j5fo2jAST0k5fSn5YZ0ZG4ldrrEus-JX_view_usp_drivesdk_a88c2de43b.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41780_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1j5fo2jAST0k5fSn5YZ0ZG4ldrrEus-JX_view_usp_drivesdk_a88c2de43b.json,2c58706fe85796ff891093fccc92e4ddf4f84956bd1103deaf23eb16dfe6f441,1008882,51,digital_text,"Pharmaceutical form(s) Tablets White to slightly yellow, elongated tablets with a bevelled edge and no score. • 2.5 mg: The tablets are engraved with “LCL” on one side and “NVR” on the other. • 5 mg: The tablets are engraved with “5” on one side and “NVR” on the other. • 10 mg: The tablets are engraved with “UHE” on one side and “NVR” on the other. Dispersible Tablets White to slightly yellowish, round, flat tablets with a bevelled edge and no score. • 2 mg: The tablets are engraved with “D2” on one side and “NVR” on the other. • 3 mg: The tablets are engraved with “D3” on one side and “NVR” on the other. • 5 mg: The tablets are engraved with “D5” on one side and “NVR” on the other. Active substance Tablets • 2.5 mg: Each tablet contains 2.5 mg everolimus. • 5 mg: Each tablet contains 5 mg everolimus. • 10 mg: Each tablet contains 10 mg everolimus. Dispersible Tablets • 2 mg: Each dispersible tablet contains 2 mg everolimus. • 3 mg: Each dispersible tablet contains 3 mg everolimus. • 5 mg: Each dispersible tablet contains 5 mg everolimus. Certain dosage strengths and dosage forms may not be available in all countries. Excipients Tablet: Butylated hydroxytoluene (E321), magnesium stearate, lactose monohydrate, hypromellose, crospovidone and lactose anhydrous. Dispersible Tablet: Butylated hydroxytoluene (E321), magnesium stearate, lactose monohydrate, hypromellose, crospovidone, mannitol, cellulose microcrystalline, and silica colloidal anhydrous. Information might differ in some countries. [Page 2]",1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,"Afinitor Tablets are indicated for the treatment of: • Postmenopausal women with hormone receptor -positive advanced breast cancer in combination with an aromatase inhibitor, after prior endocrine therapy. • Patients with adva nced neuroendocrine tumors of gastrointestinal, lung or pancreatic origin • Patients with advanced renal cell carcinoma • Patients with tuberous sclerosis complex (TSC) who have renal angiomyolipoma not requiring immediate surgery. Afinitor Dispersible Tablets are indicated for the adjunctive treatment of • Patients aged 2 years and older whose refractory partial- onset seizures, wit h or without secondary generalization, are associated with tuberous sclerosis complex (TSC ). Afinitor Tablets and Afinitor Dispersible Tablets are indicated for the treatment of: • Patients with TSC who have subependymal giant cell astrocytoma (SEGA) not requiring immediate surgery.",2,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:08:05.639554+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41845,Glutamic Acid + Calcium + Thiamine Mononitrate + Cyanocobalamin,Glutabion,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N76iZNURVb-ep4-nwIgyawWsfl76aPEH/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41845_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1N76iZNURVb-ep4-nwIgyawWsfl76aPEH_view_usp_drivesdk_7fed2485c5.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41845_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1N76iZNURVb-ep4-nwIgyawWsfl76aPEH_view_usp_drivesdk_7fed2485c5.json,7ff794e062bbeff9f42935eb3f684d8b907fd5699fbc71859c8429de1a68628a,60508,3,digital_text,"Pink to old-rose film-coated tablet, round, biconvex, plain on both sides What is in the medicine? Glutamic Acid-also called glutamirate , is an extraordinary neurotransmitter that increases the firing of neurons in the central nervous system. It is a major excitatory neurotransmitter in the brain and spinal cord. It is converted into either Glutamine or Gamma- Aminobutyric Acid (GABA), two other amino acids that help pass messages to the brain. Glutamic acid is aliphatic, acidic amino acid which is degraded really in the body to form glutamate and is used in dietary supplements. Glutamic Acid is important in the metabolism of sugar and fats , an old in the transportation of potassium into the spinal fluid and across blood - brain barrier. Although it does not pass the blood-brain barrier as readily as glutamine does, it is found at high levels in the blood and may infiltrate the brain in smal l amounts. The brain can use Glutamic acid as fuel. Glutamic Acid also helps to correct personality disorders and is useful in treating childhood behavioral disorders. It is used to treat epilepsy, mental retardation, muscular dystrophy, ulcers and hypogl ycemia coma, a complication of insulin treatment for diabetes. It is a component of folate (folic acid), a B vitamin that helps the body break down amino acids. Di Calcium Phosphate- It is important for the formation of steady bones, normal functioning of energy and for reproduction, Oral calcium salts can cause gastrointestinal irritation. Excessive amounts of calcium salts may lead to hypercalcemia usually in patients with renal failure or taking also vitamin . Symptoms of hypocalcaemia are: anorexia, nausea, vomiting, constipation, abdominal pain, muscle weakness, mental disturbances, polydipsia, polyurea, nephrocalcinosis, renal calculi and in severe cases arrhythmias and edema. Thiamine mononitrate (Vitamin B1 )-It plays an important role in helping t he body metabolize carbohydrate and fat to produce energy. It is essential for normal growth and development and helps to maintain proper functioning of the heart and the nervous digestive systems. Thiamine is rapidly absorbed form the gastrointestinal t ract with a limit of 5 mg. It is widely distributed to the most body tissues and appears in breast milk 0.9-1.5 mg is recommended for healthy men and 0.8-1.1 mg for healthy women. It is a water-soluble vitamin and is essential in carbohydrate metabolism. T hiamine deficiency leads to beri- beri.It is characterized by the peripheral neuropathy, muscle wasting and weakness and paralysis (chronic “dry” beri-beri). Cardiac failure and edema are the characteristics for acute “wet” beri-beri. Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12 )-Its main function in the formation of red blood cells and in the maintenance of healthy nervous system. Vitamin B12 is a specially important vitamin for maintaining healthy nerve cells and it aids in the production of DNA and RNA, the body’s gene tic material. Cyanocobalamin works to promote normal growth and development, helps with certain types of nerve damage, and treats pernicious anemia. It is also essential for the proper production of blood platelets for cell function, and the metabolism of nutrients necessary for cell growth. Vitamin B12 substances bind to intrinsic factor, a glycoprotein secretes by the gastric mucosa and are then actively absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract. It is stored in the liver and excreted in the bile. It diffuses in the placenta and appears in breast milk. [Page 2] Cyanocobalamin should not be given to patients with suspected Vitamin B12 deficiency without first confirming the diagnosis. Adults requirement 1-2 mcg vitamin B12 only occurs in animal products (meat, liver, kidney, milk, eggs, dairy products, fish and does not found in vegetables. Strength of the medicine Each film-coated tablet contains: Glutamic acid ………………………… ............................ 325 mg Calcium (as Dibasic Calcium Phosphate)........................... 58.91 mg Vitamin B1( ThiamineMononitrate)………………….…….5 mg Vitamin B12( Cyanocobalamin)………………….…………..10 mcg What is this medicine used for? Enhances mental faculties, productivity, concentration, alacity, memory; refreshes dull and sluggish system in cases of mental and physical fatigue. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Daily Supplement: 1 tablet daily Long and Strenuous mental activity: 1-2 tablets after meal Or as prescribed by physician When should you not take this medicine? If you are allergic to any component in the product. Care that should be taken when taking medicine? Do not take more than the recommended dose. Consult a physician if any adverse effects occurs. Do not use after the expiry date. Undesirable effects of this medicine Glutamic acid is generally free of side effects for vast majority of people who take it, however, people with kidney or liver dis ease should not consume high intakes of amino acids without consulting a healthcare professional. Because over stimulation of glutamate receptors is thought to be a possible cause of certain neurological disease (e.g., amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (Lo u Gehrig’s disease) and epilepsy) , people with a neurological disease should consult of physician before supplementing with glutamate. Nausea, vomiting, loss of appetite, constipation, stomach pain, thirst, dry mouth, increased urination. Supplementation with purified Glutamic acid on an empty stomach of 3 grams or more has resulted in intestinal disturbances. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Tetracycline, quinolone antibiotics (e.g. ciprofloxacin) gallium nitrate, cellulose sodium phosphate, etidronate, magnesium sulfate, calcium channel blockers (e.g., diltiazem, verapamil), phenytoin. Do not eat large amounts of bran or whole grain cereals and brads. They may reduce absorption of calcium. Also, consuming alcohol, large amounts caffeine, and tobacco smoking may affect absorption of calcium. What should you do if you miss a dose? If you miss the dose for the day just take the next dose and subs equent doses at the usual recommended schedule, i.e., once a day. Do not double the dose unless recommended by a physician. Signs and symptoms of overdose: Glutamic acid: Excessive consumption puts more strain on the kidneys since they have to excrete more urea than normal. It can also acidify the blood. Dicalcium phosphate: Overdose symptoms may include nausea, vomiting, decreased appetite, constipation, confusion, delirium, stupor and coma. Thiamine mononitrate (Vitamin B1): Mild overdose of Vitamin B can cause problems like headache, upset stomach, and weakness of the body. Acute overdose can cause symptoms like cardiac arrhythmia i.e, irregular heartbeats, hypotension, convolutions, a key symptom for thiamine overdose is lips turning blue. Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12): Overdose has not been observed. However, administration in doses greater than 10 mcg daily may produce a hematological response in patients with folate deficiency. [Page 3] What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a physician. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from light When should you consult your doctor? If any undesirable effect occurs. Availability Alu Foil Strip x 10’s (Box of 100’s) Manufactured by:",1,3,Description of the product,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T05:08:08.913114+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY41845,Glutamic Acid + Calcium + Thiamine Mononitrate + Cyanocobalamin,Glutabion,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XIyDy7piWo6i37GRziYJU8ZWBDdEKGTk/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY41845_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1XIyDy7piWo6i37GRziYJU8ZWBDdEKGTk_view_usp_drivesdk_c44b2a226b.pdf,page_text/DR-XY41845_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1XIyDy7piWo6i37GRziYJU8ZWBDdEKGTk_view_usp_drivesdk_c44b2a226b.json,1313ee121b96efe10330df0b7d42934d533afa93b69d561ad083117a9e418be6,1232899,2,ocr,"White to off-white sustained-release tablet, oval shaped and plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,For the treatment of type 2 diabetes mellitus.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T05:08:30.910752+00:00
