PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY42100,Gemcitabine (as hydrochloride),Gemzar,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1jSVnUlfCjepR0ujKsCxcHHsMI4DMqxZE/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY42100_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jSVnUlfCjepR0ujKsCxcHHsMI4DMqxZE_view_usp_drivesdk_7ff98386f4.pdf,page_text/DR-XY42100_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jSVnUlfCjepR0ujKsCxcHHsMI4DMqxZE_view_usp_drivesdk_7ff98386f4.json,8b9b89d2726e8a9c4273993c2fec9dff8e1fe0d2356e808f33b8bd49039cfa1c,132381,2,digital_text,"Powder for solution for infusion. White to off-white plug or powder. 5. CLINICAL INFORMATION 5.1 Therapeutic Indications • Non-small cell lung cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) alone, or in combination with cisplatin, is indicated for the first line treatment of locally advanced or metastatic non-small cell lung cancer. • Pancreatic Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is indicated for treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic adenocarcinoma of the pancreas. Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) also is indicated for patients with 5-FU refractory pancreatic cancer. • Bladder Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is indicated for treatment of patients with bladder cancer. • Breast Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is indicated for the treatment of patients with advanced breast cancer. Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is indicated for the treatment of patients with unresectable, locally recurrent or metastatic breast cancer who have relapsed following adjuvant/neoadjuvant chemotherapy (gemcitabine in combination with paclitaxel) or following chemotherapy for metastatic disease (gemcitabine in monotherapy). Prior chemotherapy should have included an anthracycline unless clinically contraindicated. • Cervical Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®), in combination with cisplatin, is indicated for the first line treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic cervical cancer. • Ovarian Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®), in combination with carboplatin, is indicated for locally advanced or metastatic epithelial ovarian carcinoma in patients with relapsed disease following a recurrence-free interval of at least 6 months after platinum-based, first line therapy. Other Therapeutic Activity: Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) alone or in combination has shown activity in renal cancer. Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) has shown some activity in advanced small cell lung cancer and advanced refractory testicular cancer. 5.2 Dosage and Administration 1. Standard Dosing • Non-small cell lung cancer Single drug chemotherapy Adults: The recommended dose of Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is 1000 mg/m2, given by 30 minute intravenous infusion. This should be repeated once weekly for three weeks, followed by a one week rest period. This four week cycle is then repeated. Dosage reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. In combination Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) in combination with cisplatin can be administered according to two dosage schedules; one based on a three-week cycle, the other based on a four-week cycle. The three week cycle is the usual schedule; the three-week cycle includes the administration of 1250 mg/m2 of Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) by intravenous infusion of 30 minutes on days 1 and 8, followed by a one-week rest period. This three-week cycle is then repeated. Dosage reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. The four-week cycle includes the administration of 1000 mg/m2 of Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) by intravenous infusion of 30 minutes on days 1, 8 and 15, followed by a one-week rest period. This four-week cycle is then repeated. Dosage reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. Adults: Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) in combination with carboplatin is recommended using Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) 1000 mg/m2 or 1200 mg/m2, given by 30-minute infusion administered on Days 1 and 8 of each 21-day cycle. After Gemcitabine (Gemzar®), carboplatin will be given on Day 1, consistent with a target AUC of 5 mg/mL•min. Dosage reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. • Pancreatic cancer Adults: The recommended dose of Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is 1000 mg/m2, given by 30 minute intravenous infusion. This should be repeated once weekly for up to 7 weeks followed by a week of rest. Subsequent cycles should consist of injections once weekly for 3 consecutive weeks out of every 4 weeks. Dosage reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. • Bladder Cancer Single Drug Chemotherapy The recommended dose of Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is 1250 mg/m2, given by 30 minute intravenous infusion. The dose should be given on days 1, 8, and 15 of each 28 day cycle. This four week cycle is then repeated. Dosage reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. In combination: The recommended dose of Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) in combination with cisplatin is 1000 mg/m2, administered by intravenous infusion of 30 minutes on days 1, 8 and 15, followed by a one-week rest period for a 28 day cycle. The recommended dose of cisplatin is 70 mg/m2 given at day 2. This four-week cycle is then repeated. Decrease or postponement of the dosage before each administration of the chemotherapy can be considered according to the individual safety response of the patients. In a clinical trial, in combination with cisplatin given at the dose of 100 mg/m2, bone marrow suppression has been more important. Dosage reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. • Breast Cancer Combination Use: Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) in combination with paclitaxel: paclitaxel (175 mg/m2) administered on Day 1 over approximately 3 hours as an intravenous infusion, followed by Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) (1250 mg/m2) as a 30-minute intravenous infusion on Days 1 and 8 of each 21-day cycle. Dose reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. Patients should have an absolute granulocyte count of at least 1,500 (x106/L) prior to initiation of gemcitabine + paclitaxel combination. • Cervical Cancer Combination use Adult Neoadjuvant Treatment and Metastatic Disease: Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) in combination with cisplatin is recommended using cisplatin 70 mg/m2 administered on Day 1 followed by Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) 1250 mg/m2 administered on Days 1 and 8 every 21 days. This three week cycle is then repeated. Dose reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. Adult Combination Therapy Using Radiation: Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) in combination with cisplatin is recommended using 40 mg/m2 followed immediately by Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) 125 mg/m2 by intravenous infusion once weekly for 6 weeks (Days 1, 8, 15, 22, 29, and 36), 1 to 2 hours before concurrent pelvic radiation therapy. Radiation therapy should be 50.4 Gy external beam radiation delivered to the entire field of radiation in 28 fractions, 1.8 Gy/day, 5 days/week, over the 6 weeks of chemotherapy. • Ovarian Cancer Adults: Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) in combination with carboplatin is recommended using Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) 1000 mg/m2 administered in Days 1 and 8 of each 21-day cycle as a 30-minute intravenous infusion. After Gemcitabine (Gemzar®), carboplatin should be given on Day 1 to attain a target AUC of 4.0 mg/mL·min. Dosage reduction with each cycle or within a cycle may be applied based upon the amount of toxicity experienced by the patient. 2. Monitoring, Dose Adjustments or Titration, Methods of Terminating Treatment Patients receiving Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) should be monitored prior to each dose for platelet, leukocyte and granulocyte counts and, if necessary, the dose of Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) may be either reduced or withheld in the presence of hematologic toxicity, according to the following scale: Absolute count granulocyte (x 106/L) Platelet Count (x 106/L) % of full dose >1,000 and >100,000 100 500 -1000 or 50,000 -100,000 75 <500 or <50,000 hold Periodic checks of renal and hepatic function, including transaminases and serum creatinine, should also be performed periodically in patients receiving gemcitabine. Elderly patients There is no evidence to suggest that dose adjustments, other than those already recommended for all patients, are necessary in the elderly, although Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) clearance and half-life are affected by age. Patients with hepatic or renal impairment Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) should be used with caution in patients with hepatic insufficiency or with impaired renal function as there is insufficient information from clinical studies to allow clear dose recommendation for this patient population. Mild to moderate renal insufficiency (GFR from 30 mL/min to 80 mL/min) has no consistent, significant effect on gemcitabine pharmacokinetics. Children Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) has been studied in limited Phase I and II trials in children in a variety of tumor types. These studies did not provide sufficient data to establish the efficacy and safety of gemcitabine in children.",1,1,4. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"• Non-small cell lung cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) alone, or in combination with cisplatin, is indicated for the first line treatment of locally advanced or metastatic non-small cell lung cancer. • Pancreatic Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is indicated for treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic adenocarcinoma of the pancreas. Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) also is indicated for patients with 5-FU refractory pancreatic cancer. • Bladder Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is indicated for treatment of patients with bladder cancer. • Breast Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is indicated for the treatment of patients with advanced breast cancer. Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) is indicated for the treatment of patients with unresectable, locally recurrent or metastatic breast cancer who have relapsed following adjuvant/neoadjuvant chemotherapy (gemcitabine in combination with paclitaxel) or following chemotherapy for metastatic disease (gemcitabine in monotherapy). Prior chemotherapy should have included an anthracycline unless clinically contraindicated. • Cervical Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®), in combination with cisplatin, is indicated for the first line treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic cervical cancer. • Ovarian Cancer Gemcitabine (Gemzar®), in combination with carboplatin, is indicated for locally advanced or metastatic epithelial ovarian carcinoma in patients with relapsed disease following a recurrence-free interval of at least 6 months after platinum-based, first line therapy. Other Therapeutic Activity: Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) alone or in combination has shown activity in renal cancer. Gemcitabine (Gemzar®) has shown some activity in advanced small cell lung cancer and advanced refractory testicular cancer.",1,1,5.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:10:11.213787+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY42110,Piracetam,Neurocetam,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Yc0nZG_PTeeMDToNafiTj4bOVV3CJvM4/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY42110_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Yc0nZG_PTeeMDToNafiTj4bOVV3CJvM4_view_usp_drivesdk_615a53a83e.pdf,page_text/DR-XY42110_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Yc0nZG_PTeeMDToNafiTj4bOVV3CJvM4_view_usp_drivesdk_615a53a83e.json,c8edaffd88d24f987f2e2af55acd5f6de4dc05e83bd58c63d24e4c2a65ef59e3,1510700,3,digital_text,"Light Pink colored, oblong shaped, biconvex, film coated tablets, plain on both surfaces",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Piracetam is indicated in adult patients suffering from myoclonus of cortical origin, irrespective of aetiology, and should be used in combination with other anti-myoclonic therapies.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:10:14.590817+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY42115,Lapatinib (as ditosylate),Tykerb,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Dj57x8DU9_rnTo1BlqxE6mkm7PVQUFT4/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY42115_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Dj57x8DU9_rnTo1BlqxE6mkm7PVQUFT4_view_usp_drivesdk_a4d7ac9d5e.pdf,page_text/DR-XY42115_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Dj57x8DU9_rnTo1BlqxE6mkm7PVQUFT4_view_usp_drivesdk_a4d7ac9d5e.json,f0a176337c41d9842fa03a0651b2ae44c51f179bad0daa3bff3f6fa00e525cce,529609,29,digital_text,"Pharmaceutical form Film-coated tablets Oval, biconvex, yellow film-coated tablets, with one side plain and the opposite side debossed with GS XJG. Active substance Lapatinib ditosylate monohydrate. The 250 mg film-coated tablet contains 405 mg of lapatinib ditosylate monohydrate, equivalent to 250 mg lapatinib free base. Excipients Microcrystalline cellulose Povidone Sodium starch glycolate Magnesium stearate Yellow tablet film-coat Hypromellose Titanium dioxide Macrogol/PEG 400 Polysorbate 80 Iron oxide yellow Iron oxide red Pharmaceutical formulations may vary between countries. LAPATINIB [Page 2]",1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,"HER2 overexpressing metastatic breast cancer Lapatinib (Tykerb®), in combination with capecitabine, is indicated for the treatment of patients with advanced or metastatic breast cancer, whose tumo rs overexpress HER2/neu (ErbB2) and who have progressed on prior trastuzumab therapy in the metastatic setting (see section CLINICAL STUDIES). Lapatinib ( Tykerb®), in combination with trastuzumab, is indicated for the treatment of patients with hormone receptor -negative metastatic breast cancer whose tumo rs overexpress HER2/neu (ErbB2) and w ho have progressed on prior trastuzumab therapy in com bination with chemotherapy in the metastatic setting (see section CLINICAL STUDIES). Lapatinib (Tykerb®), in combination with paclitaxel, is indicated for the first line treatment of patients with me tastatic breast cancer whose tu mors overexpress HER2 /neu (ErbB2) and for whom trastuzumab is not appropriate (see section CLINICAL STUDIES). Lapatinib ( Tykerb®), in combination with an aromatase inhibitor, is indicated for the treatment of postmenopausal women with hormone receptor -positive, HER2/neu (ErbB2) overexpressing advanced or metastatic breast cancer, and for whom endocrine therapy is indicated (see section CLINICAL STUDIES). No data are available on the efficacy of this combination relative to tr astuzumab in combination with an aromatase inhibitor or chemotherapy in this patient population.",2,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:10:18.699602+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY42155,Candesartan Cilexetil,Atasart,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UZdSIM7cuQIjkY1youkPiw0aG8yV407M/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY42155_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UZdSIM7cuQIjkY1youkPiw0aG8yV407M_view_usp_drivesdk_cb1026a5f1.pdf,page_text/DR-XY42155_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UZdSIM7cuQIjkY1youkPiw0aG8yV407M_view_usp_drivesdk_cb1026a5f1.json,a769c4756c4ad4ab4c1768875be8f71601153a4f440baec1872926ec57501a06,423854,2,digital_text,"Candesartan Cilexetil (ATASART®) 8mg tablet is available as off-white to cream colored, square shaped, biconvex tablet, marked bisect line on one side and plain on other side. Candesartan Cilexetil (ATASART®) 16mg tablet is available as white colored, square shaped, biconvex tablet, marked bisect line on one side and plain on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Candesartan Cilexetil (ATASART ®) is indicated for the treatment of hypertension. It may be used alone or in combination with other antihypertensive agents and for the treatment of heart failure in patients with impaired left ventricle systolic function (left ventricular ejection fraction 40%) to reduce cardiovascular death and to reduce heart failure hospitalizations.,1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:10:22.081265+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY42156,Candesartan Cilexetil,Atasart,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LdUxacQOX1hZsAxFIDy-6Wg65nsVdLO_/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY42156_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LdUxacQOX1hZsAxFIDy-6Wg65nsVdLO__view_usp_drivesdk_e4e8ff145a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY42156_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LdUxacQOX1hZsAxFIDy-6Wg65nsVdLO__view_usp_drivesdk_e4e8ff145a.json,8039ca8d1e8daa9e055fd2faf3776e14d23617329d03d710221268d258847238,423854,2,digital_text,"Candesartan Cilexetil (ATASART®) 8mg tablet is available as off-white to cream colored, square shaped, biconvex tablet, marked bisect line on one side and plain on other side. Candesartan Cilexetil (ATASART®) 16mg tablet is available as white colored, square shaped, biconvex tablet, marked bisect line on one side and plain on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Candesartan Cilexetil (ATASART ®) is indicated for the treatment of hypertension. It may be used alone or in combination with other antihypertensive agents and for the treatment of heart failure in patients with impaired left ventricle systolic function (left ventricular ejection fraction 40%) to reduce cardiovascular death and to reduce heart failure hospitalizations.,1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:10:25.559362+00:00
