PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY42164,Atorvastatin (as calcium),Onestatin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qljqfleHG96x1FCWExx4mP_WQ1g5cKMI/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY42164_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qljqfleHG96x1FCWExx4mP_WQ1g5cKMI_view_usp_drivesdk_661959fb81.pdf,page_text/DR-XY42164_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qljqfleHG96x1FCWExx4mP_WQ1g5cKMI_view_usp_drivesdk_661959fb81.json,be83f9e1f7d0fe1fa572002c9a10f09c9a1eb5ec09e547ec6759a61e862a0209,1537890,2,ocr,"Atorvastatin 10 mg Tablet is a white to off-white, oblong, biconvex, film-coated tablet, plain on both sides. Atorvastatin 40 mg Film-Coated Tablet is a white to off-white, oval, biconvex, film-coated tablet, plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"It is used to reduce LDL-Cholesterol, apolipoprotein B, and triglycerides and to increase HDL-Cholesterol in the treatment of hyperlipidaemias (type lla or Ib hyperlipoproteinaemias), hypertriglyceridaemia (type IV), and dysbetalipoproteinaemia (type Il).",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T05:10:48.491726+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY42169,Ondansetron (as Hydrochloride Dihydrate),Onsia,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/16xugWKaj4ZYUCeYhoqQKoBBC_D-ZYvks/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY42169_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_16xugWKaj4ZYUCeYhoqQKoBBC_D-ZYvks_view_usp_drivesdk_c3ff300575.pdf,page_text/DR-XY42169_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_16xugWKaj4ZYUCeYhoqQKoBBC_D-ZYvks_view_usp_drivesdk_c3ff300575.json,56d736b9aed73073df8252135608c2523dc095abe3a6396159f5c536a6c109f0,66149,2,digital_text,"Clear, colorless to slightly pale yellow sterile solution. PHARMACOLOGIC CATEGORY : Antiemetic. Pharmacodynamics Ondansetron HCl dihydrate (Onsia) is a selective first-generation inhibitor of type 3 serotonin (5-HT3) receptors, is an antiemetic. The antiemetic activity of Ondansetron HCl dihydrate (Onsia) appears to be mediated both centrally and peripherally via inhibition of 5-HT3 receptor. Serotonin receptors of the 5-HT3 are located in peripherally on vagal nerve terminal, enteric neurons in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract and centrally in the chemoreceptor trigger zone. During chemotherapy, mucosal enterochromaffin cells from the small intestine release serotonin, which stimulates the 5-HT3 receptors. This evokes vagal afferent discharge, inducing vomiting. Activation of vagal afferents may also cause a release of 5-HT in the area postrema (the locus of the chemotherapy trigger zone), located on the floor of the fourth ventricle, and this may also promote emesis through a central mechanism. Thus, the effect of Ondansetron HCl dihydrate (Onsia) in the management of the nausea and vomiting induced by cytotoxic chemotherapy and radiotherapy is probably due to antagonism of 5-HT3 receptors on neurons located both in the peripheral and central nervous system. Pharmacokinetics The pharmacokinetic properties of Ondansetron HCl dihydrate (Onsia) are unchanged on repeat dosing. Absorption : Equivalent systemic exposure is achieved after IV administration of Ondansetron HCl dihydrate (Onsia). Distribution : Ondansetron HCl dihydrate (Onsia) is extensively distributed in the body, about 70-75% of the drug in plasma is protein bound. Metabolism : Ondansetron HCl dihydrate (Onsia) is metabolized in the liver through multiple enzymatic pathways; Ondansetron HCl dihydrate (Onsia) is a substrate for cytochrome P450 isoenzymes, primarily CYP3A4, but also CYP1A2 and CYP2D6. Elimination : Ondansetron HCl dihydrate (Onsia) is cleared from the systemic circulation predominantly by hepatic metabolism. Less than 5% of the absorbed dose is excreted unchanged in the urine. Elimination half-life is 2 to 7 hours (children younger than 15 years) and 3 to 6 hours (adults).",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION :,1. For the management of nausea and vomiting induced by cytotoxic chemotherapy and radiotherapy 2. For the prevention and treatment of postoperative nausea and vomiting,1,1,INDICATIONS :,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:10:51.418574+00:00
