PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY43438,Gabapentin,Epiven,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ph5K7v3QP8uAxIjpnGDF6hLEJPlzcoXd/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY43438_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ph5K7v3QP8uAxIjpnGDF6hLEJPlzcoXd_view_usp_drivesdk_58c934ff5d.pdf,page_text/DR-XY43438_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ph5K7v3QP8uAxIjpnGDF6hLEJPlzcoXd_view_usp_drivesdk_58c934ff5d.json,b4c3be71244b4b3d627b6564508ae6dc737e7fce930e0458ba05f20d11872abb,5145209,2,ocr,"In clinical trials, the effective dosing range was 900 to 3600 mg/day. Therapy may be initiated by titrating the dose as described in Table 1 or by administering 300 mg three EPIVEN 300 mg hard capsules: A two-piece, yellow opaque hard gelatin capsule and containing white granules. times a day (TID) on Day 1. Thereafter, based on individual patient response and tolerability, the dose can be further increased in 300 mg/day increments every 2-3 days It also contains the following excipients: Microcrystalline cellulose, Sodium starch glycollate, Polyvidone, Magnesium stearate, Talc, Ethanol, and Purified water. up to a maximum dose of 3600 mg/day. Slower titration of gabapentin dosage may be appropriate for individual patients. The minimum time to reach a dose of 1800 mg/day is one week, to reach 2400 mg/day is a total of 2 weeks, and to reach 3600 mg/day is a total of 3 weeks. Dosages up to 4800 mg/day have been well tolerated in",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Seizures,1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T05:23:05.914479+00:00
