PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY43610,Ondansetron (as hydrochloride),Ondavell,PI_04,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Pm38ir150ZDjM1dt3Ewmb7J3O-HjD95Z/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY43610_PI_04_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Pm38ir150ZDjM1dt3Ewmb7J3O-HjD95Z_view_usp_drivesdk_0128409734.pdf,page_text/DR-XY43610_PI_04_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Pm38ir150ZDjM1dt3Ewmb7J3O-HjD95Z_view_usp_drivesdk_0128409734.json,156a1ae936f1343efad05014516e3521bce5f76a7057c2698446d9a9f838e825,174237,2,digital_text,LABORATORIES Healthcare Inc. [Page 3],2,2,PHARMACEUTICAL,"Adults : Ondansetron (Ondavell) Film-Coated Tablet is indicated for the management of nausea and vomiting induced by cytotoxic chemotherapy and radiotherapy. Ondansetron (Ondavell) Film-Coated Tablet is indicated for the prevention of post-operative nausea and vomiting (PONV). For treatment of established PONV, administration by injection is recommended. Paediatric Population : Ondansetron (Ondavell) Film-Coated Tablet is indicated for the management of chemotherapy-induced nausea and vomiting (CINV) in children aged ≥6 months. No studies have been conducted on the use of orally administered ondansetron in the prevention and treatment of PONV in children aged ≥1 month, administration by IV injection is recommended for this purpose.",1,1,INDICATIONS :,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T05:23:46.722595+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY43611,Ondansetron (as hydrochloride dihydrate),Ondavell,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oSohtrAahHsYYfJFWdsLpWDuW1rTP6Kw/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY43611_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oSohtrAahHsYYfJFWdsLpWDuW1rTP6Kw_view_usp_drivesdk_53eb276df8.pdf,page_text/DR-XY43611_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oSohtrAahHsYYfJFWdsLpWDuW1rTP6Kw_view_usp_drivesdk_53eb276df8.json,e3497fb4a491ac9317cea21e0311bc6078ca2e44d05ea0b6ba0f7a3c22458c4c,183071,2,digital_text,LABORATORIES Healthcare Inc. [Page 3],2,2,PHARMACEUTICAL,"Adults : Ondansetron (Ondavell) 2 mg/mL Solution for Injection is indicated for the management of nausea and vomiting induced by cytotoxic chemotherapy and radiotherapy. Ondansetron (Ondavell) 2 mg/mL Solution for Injection is indicated for the prevention and treatment of post-operative nausea and vomiting (PONV). Paediatric Population : Ondansetron (Ondavell) 2 mg/mL Solution for Injection is indicated for the management of chemotherapy-induced nausea and vomiting (CINV) in children aged ≥6 months, and for the prevention and treatment of PONV in children aged ≥1 month.",1,1,INDICATIONS :,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T05:23:49.931898+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY4362,Iopromide,Ultravist,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/11Asc5hwPTewZomziqMnT-ndtKdgKhzfU/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY4362_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11Asc5hwPTewZomziqMnT-ndtKdgKhzfU_view_usp_drivesdk_dc5fc8b0f4.pdf,page_text/DR-XY4362_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11Asc5hwPTewZomziqMnT-ndtKdgKhzfU_view_usp_drivesdk_dc5fc8b0f4.json,77627d5a044d617fcec0cbbbeaea73bae26b79b3baedbcf70c09d6a2c48de39d,573625,2,digital_text,"Solution for injection / infusion. Clear, colorless to pale yellow solution. The physico-chemical properties of Iopromide (Ultravist) at the concentrations listed below are: Iodine concentration (mg/ml) 300 370 Osmolality (osm/kg H2O) at 37 °C 0.59 0.77 Viscosity (mPa•s) at 20 °C at 37 °C 8.9 4.7 22.0 10.0 Density (g/ml) at 20 °C at 37 °C 1.328 1.322 1.409 1.399 pH-value 6.5-8.0 6.5-8.0 4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS",1,1,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"This medicinal product is for diagnostic use only. Iopromide (Ultravist) 300/370: For intravascular use and use in body cavities. Contrast enhancement in computerized tomography (CT), arteriography and venography, intravenous/intraarterial digital subtraction angiography (DSA); intravenous urography, use for ERCP, arthrography and examination of other body cavities. Iopromide (Ultravist) 370: especially for angiocardiography Iopromide (Ultravist) 300/370: not for intrathecal use.",1,1,4.1 Indication(s),high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:23:53.544599+00:00
