PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY43630,Prulifloxacin,Prulibact,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-f-ohdsQtUH7pbQZxgoBn1oW-zo6rPeV/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY43630_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-f-ohdsQtUH7pbQZxgoBn1oW-zo6rPeV_view_usp_drivesdk_b241922a13.pdf,page_text/DR-XY43630_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-f-ohdsQtUH7pbQZxgoBn1oW-zo6rPeV_view_usp_drivesdk_b241922a13.json,e7aa8f33b6bbe61962746a3a05606de4c8567f0ee3067164f61e8d1e98d9a058,1443376,2,digital_text,"Brownish pink coloured, oval shaped film coated tablets with a breakline on one surface.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Treatment of hypercholesterolemia It is indicated in the treatment of infections caused by susceptible organisms, in the following conditions: ! Acute uncomplicated lower urinary tract infections (simple cystitis); ! Complicated lower urinary tract infections; ! Acute exacerbation of chronic bronchitis. The local antibiotic susceptibility pattern should be considered in the treatment of patients with infectious diseases.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:24:15.025455+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY43632,Cefixime ( as trihydrate),Supixime -400,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RF5fVZxwMG3MSmo6vIt_KyQ_xRJo5jx6/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY43632_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RF5fVZxwMG3MSmo6vIt_KyQ_xRJo5jx6_view_usp_drivesdk_36d5a3ed4f.pdf,page_text/DR-XY43632_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RF5fVZxwMG3MSmo6vIt_KyQ_xRJo5jx6_view_usp_drivesdk_36d5a3ed4f.json,530f74568c807fd581bd0935e3787a7a723090ea93210e7c563c50e93dc7db86,2020823,3,digital_text,Cefixime (as trihydrate) capsules 100 mg: Blue/Red Coloured '4' Size capsules with MICRO/MICRO printed containing white to light yellow granular powder. Cefixime (as trihydrate) capsules 200 mg: Light Green/Dark Green coloured '2' size capsules with MICRO/MICRO printed containing white to yellow granular powder. Cefixime (as Trihydrate) capsules 400 mg: Purple/White coloured '0' size capsules plain capsules containing white to light yellow granular powder,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Cefixime is an orally active cephalosporin antibiotic which has marked in vitro bactericidal activity against a wide variety of Gram-positive and Gram-negative organisms. It is indicated for the treatment of the following acute infections when caused by susceptible micro-organisms: Upper Respiratory Tract Infections (URTI): e.g. otitis media; and other URTI where the causative organism is known or suspected to be resistant to other commonly used antibiotics, or where treatment failure may carry significant risk. Lower Respiratory Tract Infection: e.g. bronchitis. Urinary Tract Infections: e.g. cystitis, cystourethritis, uncomplicated pyelonephritis. Clinical efficacy has been demonstrated in infections caused by commonly occurring pathogens including Streptococcus pneumoniae, Streptococcus pyogenes, Escherichia coli, Proteus mirabilis, Kliebsiella species, Haemophilus influenzae (beta-lactamase positive and negative), Branhamella catarrhalis (beta-lactamase positive and negative) and Enterobacter species. Cefixime is highly stable in the presence of beta-lactamase enzymes. Most strains of enterococci (Streptococcus faecalis, group D Streptococci) and Staphylococci (including coagulase positive and negative strains and meticillin-resistant strains) are resistant to Cefixime. In addition, most strains of Pseudomonas, Bacteriodes fragalis, Listeria monocytogenes and Clostridia are resistant to Cefixime.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:24:18.806321+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY43655,Ondansetron (as hydrochloride dihydrate),Ondavell,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cHRL8m_TC6n5c80BmceFTjuPbvIU3ykI/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY43655_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cHRL8m_TC6n5c80BmceFTjuPbvIU3ykI_view_usp_drivesdk_791bd8577a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY43655_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cHRL8m_TC6n5c80BmceFTjuPbvIU3ykI_view_usp_drivesdk_791bd8577a.json,e3497fb4a491ac9317cea21e0311bc6078ca2e44d05ea0b6ba0f7a3c22458c4c,183071,2,digital_text,LABORATORIES Healthcare Inc. [Page 3],2,2,PHARMACEUTICAL,"Adults : Ondansetron (Ondavell) 2 mg/mL Solution for Injection is indicated for the management of nausea and vomiting induced by cytotoxic chemotherapy and radiotherapy. Ondansetron (Ondavell) 2 mg/mL Solution for Injection is indicated for the prevention and treatment of post-operative nausea and vomiting (PONV). Paediatric Population : Ondansetron (Ondavell) 2 mg/mL Solution for Injection is indicated for the management of chemotherapy-induced nausea and vomiting (CINV) in children aged ≥6 months, and for the prevention and treatment of PONV in children aged ≥1 month.",1,1,INDICATIONS :,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T05:24:22.018667+00:00
