PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY43764,Axitinib,Inlyta,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HSrZTHsTUAL18e-H-CvwFi90VR5j4sJ5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY43764_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HSrZTHsTUAL18e-H-CvwFi90VR5j4sJ5_view_usp_drivesdk_a09e02ef5d.pdf,page_text/DR-XY43764_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HSrZTHsTUAL18e-H-CvwFi90VR5j4sJ5_view_usp_drivesdk_a09e02ef5d.json,309f106049d4764777da9d445d4ace02fdac2a417636f56c29f0946cb3bb2cd7,2432111,19,digital_text,"Axitinib has the chemical name N-methyl-2-[3-((E)2-pyridin-2-yl-vinyl)-1H-indazol-6- ylsulfanyl]-benzamide. The molecular formula is C22H18N4OS and the molecular weight is 386.47 Daltons. The chemical structure is: Axitinib is a white to light-yellow powder with a pKa of 4.8. The solubility of axitinib in aqueous media over the range pH 1.1 to pH 7.8 is in excess of 0.2 μg/mL. The partition coefficient (noctanol/water) is 3.5. In addition to the active ingredient Axitinib, the tablet contains inactive ingredients: microcrystalline cellulose, lactose monohydrate, croscarmellose sodium, magnesium stearate, and Opadry II.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,Axitinib (Inlyta) is indicated for the treatment of advanced renal cell carcinoma (RCC) after failure of one prior systemic therapy. (see also Section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic Properties). [Page 2] Page 2 of 19,1,2,4.1. Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:26:08.592584+00:00
