PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY43829,Canagliflozin (as hemihydrate),Invokana,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1InOjdnPNRCuIiGGEbkQDTNt2bC1ZMWh1/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY43829_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1InOjdnPNRCuIiGGEbkQDTNt2bC1ZMWh1_view_usp_drivesdk_2ff52cf636.pdf,page_text/DR-XY43829_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1InOjdnPNRCuIiGGEbkQDTNt2bC1ZMWh1_view_usp_drivesdk_2ff52cf636.json,2129e56cce90ac189c5d73ccce982b2ce4d42db86dcf2f0c94bf308eca5cb87f,1802736,47,digital_text,"• Canagliflozin (Invokana®) 100 mg tablets are yellow, capsule-shaped, immediate-release, and film-coated, with “CFZ” on one side and “100” on the other side. • Canagliflozin (Invokana®) 300 mg tablets are white, capsule-shaped, immediate-release, and film- coated, with “CFZ” on one side and “300” on the other side. THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus. Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is indicated to reduce the risk of major adverse cardiovascular events (cardiovascular death, nonfatal myocardial infarction and nonfatal stroke) in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus who have established cardiovascular disease (CVD) or at least two risk factors for CVD. Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is indicated for the treatment of diabetic kidney disease with albuminuria in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus. In this population, Canagliflozin (Invokana®) reduces the risk of end -stage kidney disease (ESKD), doubling of serum creatinine, renal or cardiovascular (CV) death, and hospitalization for heart failure. Limitation of Use Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is not recommended in patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus or for the treatment of diabetic ketoacidosis. POSOLOGY AND METHOD OF ADMINISTRATION Dosage – Adults 18 years of age and older The recommended dose of Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is 100 mg or 300 mg once daily. See Table 1 for dosage recommendations based on estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR). The 300 mg dose may be considered for patients with an eGFR ≥ 60 mL/min/1.73 m2 [ CrCl ≥ 60 mL/min], who need tighter glycemic control and who have a low risk of adverse reactions associated with reduced intravascular volume with Canagliflozin (Invokana®) treatment (see below and Special Warnings and Special Precautions for Use). A starting dose of 100 mg once daily should be used in patients on loop diuretics and patients ≥ 75 years of age. In patients with evidence of reduced intravascular volume, correcting this condition prior to initiation of Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is recommended. For those patients who are tolerating Canagliflozin (Invokana®) 100 mg and who need tighter glycemic control, the dose can be increased to Canagliflozin (Invokana®) 300 mg (see Special Warnings and Special Precautions for Use). When Canagliflozin ( Invokana®) is used as add-on therapy with insulin or an insulin secretagogue (e.g. sulfonylurea), a lower dose of insulin or the insulin secretagogue may be considered to reduce the risk of hypoglycemia (see Special Warnings and Special Precautions for Use and Undesirable Effects). [Page 2] Approved Package Insert – CCDS v18, 27 June 2022 Table 1: Dosage recommendation by eGFR eGFR (mL/min/1.73 m2) or CrCl (mL/min) Dosage Recommendation ≥ 60 100 mg orally once daily, taken before the first meal of the day. Dose can be increased to 300 mg once daily for additional glycemic control. 30 to < 60 100 mg once daily. <30 Initiation is not recommended; however patients with albuminuria greater than 300 mg/day may continue 100 mg once daily to reduce the risk of ESKD, doubling of serum creatinine, CV death, and hospitalization for heart failure.* * In CREDENCE, treatment with Canagliflozin (Invokana®) 100 mg was continued in patients until the initiation of dialysis or in the event of renal transplantation. Administration Canagliflozin (Invokana®) should be taken orally once a day, preferably before the first meal of the day (see Pharmacokinetic Properties). Tablets are to be swallowed whole. Missed dose If a dose is missed, it should be taken as soon as the patient remembers; however, a double dose should not be taken on the same day. Special populations Pediatrics (< 18 years of age) The safety and efficacy of Canagliflozin (Invokana®) have not been established in pediatric patients. Elderly In patients ≥ 75 years of age, the starting dose of Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is 100 mg once daily. Renal function and risk of volume depletion should be taken into account (see Special Warnings and Special Precautions for Use and Undesirable Effects).",1,2,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus. Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is indicated to reduce the risk of major adverse cardiovascular events (cardiovascular death, nonfatal myocardial infarction and nonfatal stroke) in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus who have established cardiovascular disease (CVD) or at least two risk factors for CVD. Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is indicated for the treatment of diabetic kidney disease with albuminuria in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus. In this population, Canagliflozin (Invokana®) reduces the risk of end -stage kidney disease (ESKD), doubling of serum creatinine, renal or cardiovascular (CV) death, and hospitalization for heart failure. Limitation of Use Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is not recommended in patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus or for the treatment of diabetic ketoacidosis.",1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:26:33.607552+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY43829,Canagliflozin (as hemihydrate),Invokana,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wZodgQSZxbjkgB0aSvBmxaGDGzpUJAiX/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY43829_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wZodgQSZxbjkgB0aSvBmxaGDGzpUJAiX_view_usp_drivesdk_bd70422628.pdf,page_text/DR-XY43829_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wZodgQSZxbjkgB0aSvBmxaGDGzpUJAiX_view_usp_drivesdk_bd70422628.json,9670bdc4c953eb4393d6563c6f083448dd12c179fba6ff942ca5a21359616dfd,1519393,48,digital_text,"• Canagliflozin (Invokana®) 100 mg tablets are yellow, capsule-shaped, immediate-release, and film-coated, with “CFZ” on one side and “100” on the other side. • Canagliflozin (Invokana®) 300 mg tablets are white, capsule-shaped, immediate-release, and film- coated, with “CFZ” on one side and “300” on the other side. THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus. Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is indicated to reduce the risk of major adverse cardiovascular events (cardiovascular death, nonfatal myocardial infarction and nonfatal stroke) in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus who have established cardiovascular disease (CVD) or at least two risk factors for CVD. Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is indicated for the treatment of diabetic kidney disease with albuminuria in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus. In this population, Canagliflozin (Invokana®) reduces the risk of end -stage kidney disease (ESKD), doubling of serum creatinine, renal or cardiovascular (CV) death, and hospitalization for heart failure. Limitation of Use Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is not recommended in patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus or for the treatment of diabetic ketoacidosis. POSOLOGY AND METHOD OF ADMINISTRATION Dosage – Adults 18 years of age and older The recommended dose of Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is 100 mg or 300 mg once daily. See Table 1 for dosage recommendations based on estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR). The 300 mg dose may be considered for patients with an eGFR ≥ 60 mL/min/1.73 m2 [CrCl ≥ 60 mL/min], who need tighter glycemic control and who have a lo w risk of adverse reactions associated with reduced intravascular volume with Canagliflozin (Invokana®) treatment (see below and Special Warnings and Special Precautions for Use). A starting dose of 100 mg once daily should be used in patients on loop diuretics and patients ≥ 75 years of age. In patients with evidence of reduced intravascular volume, correcting this condition prior to initiation of Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is recommended. For those patients who are tolerating Canagliflozin (Invokana®) 100 mg and who need tighter glycemic control, the dose can be increased to Canagliflozin (Invokana®) 300 mg (see Special Warnings and Special Precautions for Use). When Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is used as add -on therapy with insulin or an insulin secreta gogue (e.g. sulfonylurea), a lower dose of insulin or the insulin secretagogue may be considered to reduce the risk of hypoglycemia (see Special Warnings and Special Precautions for Use and Undesirable Effects). Canagliflozin [Page 2] Proposed Package Insert – CCDS v19, 07 November 2022 Table 1: Dosage recommendation by eGFR eGFR (mL/min/1.73 m2) or CrCl (mL/min) Dosage Recommendation ≥ 60 100 mg orally once daily, taken before the first meal of the day. Dose can be increased to 300 mg once daily for additional glycemic control. 30 to < 60 100 mg once daily. <30 Initiation is not recommended; however patients with albuminuria greater than 300 mg/day may continue 100 mg once daily to reduce the risk of ESKD, doubling of serum creatinine, CV death, and hospitalization for heart failure.* * In CREDENCE, treatment with Canagliflozin (Invokana®) 100 mg was continued in patients until the initiation of dialysis or in the event of renal transplantation. Administration Canagliflozin (Invokana®) should be taken orally once a day, preferably before the first meal of the day (see Pharmacokinetic Properties). Tablets are to be swallowed whole. Missed dose If a dose is missed, it should be taken as soon as the patient remembers; however, a double dose should not be taken on the same day. Special populations Pediatrics (< 18 years of age) The safety and efficacy of Canagliflozin (Invokana®) have not been established in pediatric patients. Elderly In patients ≥ 75 years of age, the starting dose of Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is 100 mg once daily. Renal function and risk of volume depletion should be taken into account (see Special Warnings and Special Precautions for Use and Undesirable Effects).",1,2,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus. Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is indicated to reduce the risk of major adverse cardiovascular events (cardiovascular death, nonfatal myocardial infarction and nonfatal stroke) in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus who have established cardiovascular disease (CVD) or at least two risk factors for CVD. Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is indicated for the treatment of diabetic kidney disease with albuminuria in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus. In this population, Canagliflozin (Invokana®) reduces the risk of end -stage kidney disease (ESKD), doubling of serum creatinine, renal or cardiovascular (CV) death, and hospitalization for heart failure. Limitation of Use Canagliflozin (Invokana®) is not recommended in patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus or for the treatment of diabetic ketoacidosis.",1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:26:39.986348+00:00
