PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY43863,Tadalafil,Cialis,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1G9OHJ_EmYB6Wq7yj33V9nsfF-Y28XENI/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY43863_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1G9OHJ_EmYB6Wq7yj33V9nsfF-Y28XENI_view_usp_drivesdk_7b09d20174.pdf,page_text/DR-XY43863_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1G9OHJ_EmYB6Wq7yj33V9nsfF-Y28XENI_view_usp_drivesdk_7b09d20174.json,d15423a1d5032b40d2987bb87993b22c1567a40220ea2c9e038a87bf33f2549b,786966,2,digital_text,Tadalafil (Cialis ®) is available as film-coated tablets for oral administration. Tadalafil (Cialis ®) is available as a yellow almond-shaped tablet debossed with “C5”. 4. PHARMACOLOGIC CATEGORY Phosphodiesterase Type-5 Inhibitor 5. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 5.1 Therapeutic indications Erectile Dysfunction Tadalafil (Cialis ®) indicated for the treatment of erectile dysfunction (ED). Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia Tadalafil (Cialis ®) is indicated for the treatment of the signs and symptoms of benign prostatic hyperplasia,1,1,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,Erectile Dysfunction Tadalafil (Cialis ®) indicated for the treatment of erectile dysfunction (ED). Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia Tadalafil (Cialis ®) is indicated for the treatment of the signs and symptoms of benign prostatic hyperplasia,1,1,5.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:27:07.660049+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY43865,Indacaterol (as maleate)/Glycopyrronium (as bromide),Ultibro Breezhaler,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xMFrSZBHoJbWV1XvfcC6h_7BcpLh7oFG/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY43865_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xMFrSZBHoJbWV1XvfcC6h_7BcpLh7oFG_view_usp_drivesdk_70ed394b46.pdf,page_text/DR-XY43865_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xMFrSZBHoJbWV1XvfcC6h_7BcpLh7oFG_view_usp_drivesdk_70ed394b46.json,ace19697984c0cccd112ff5cf76112b276d1ca55e808364701cb688d8c6c08ca,856902,29,digital_text_and_ocr,"Pharmaceutical form Indacaterol/glycopyrronium 110/50 microgram, inhalation powder in hard capsules. Transparent yellow cap and transparent body capsules containing a white to practically white powder, with the product code “IGP110.50” pri nted in blue under two blue bars on the body and the company logo ) printed in black on the cap. Active substance Each capsule contains 143 micrograms indacaterol maleate equivalent to 110 micrograms indacaterol and 63 micrograms glycopyrronium bromide equivalent to 50 micrograms glycopyrronium. The delivered dose (the dose that leaves the mouthpiece of the inhaler) is equivalent to 85 micrograms indacaterol and 43 micrograms glycopyrronium. Excipients Capsule fill: Lactose monohydrate, magnesium stearate. Capsule shell components: Hypromellose, purified water, carrageenan, potassium chloride, FD&C Yellow5/Tartrazine.",1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,Once-daily maintenance bronchodilator treatment to relieve symptoms and reduce exacerbations in adult patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD).,1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T05:27:20.155809+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY43892,Mesalazine,Pentasa,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ywjUdC_9hkxebT2NdtQlGZrSIrpowK5Y/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY43892_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ywjUdC_9hkxebT2NdtQlGZrSIrpowK5Y_view_usp_drivesdk_162ee5c28d.pdf,page_text/DR-XY43892_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ywjUdC_9hkxebT2NdtQlGZrSIrpowK5Y_view_usp_drivesdk_162ee5c28d.json,f4008ec108d9f2a1fd92f06649c270fb5dd3bdc5978c803fe81fcb752be18283,219065,3,digital_text,"Prolonged-release tablet 1g. A PPEARANCE White-grey to pale brown, speckled, oval tablets. Embossing on both sides: PENTASA. T HERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS Treatment of mild to moderate ulcerative colitis and Crohn’s disease. DOSAGE AND ADMINISTRATION Treatment of Ulcerative colitis Active disease: Adults: Individual dosage, up to 4 g daily in divided doses. Children (≥ 6 years of age): Individual dosage, starting with 30-50 mg/kg/day in divided doses. Maximum dose: 75 mg/kg/day in divided doses. The total dose should not exceed 4 g/day (maximum adult dose). Maintenance treatment: Adults: Individual dosage. Recommended dosage, 2 g once daily. Can also be taken in divided doses. Children (≥ 6 years of age): Individual dosage, starting with 15-30 mg/kg/day in divided doses. The total dose should not exceed 2 g/day (recommended adult dose). T reatment of Crohn’s disease Active disease: Adults: Individual dosage, up to 4 g daily in divided doses. Children (≥ 6 years of age): Individual dosage, starting with 30-50 mg/kg/day in divided doses. Maximum dose: 75 mg/kg/day in divided doses. The total dose should not exceed 4 g/day (maximum adult dose). Maintenance treatment: Adults: Individual dosage, up to 4 g daily in divided doses. Children (≥ 6 years of age): Individual dosage, starting with 15-30 mg/kg/day in divided doses. The to tal dose should not exceed 4 g/day (recommended adult dose). There is only limited documentation for an effect in children (age 6-18 years). It is generally recommended that half the adult dose may be given to children up to a body weight of 40 kg; and the normal adult dose to those above 40 kg. Method of Administration Mesalazine (PENTASA®) tablets must not be chewed. To facilitate swallowing the tablets may be dispersed in 50 ml of cold water. Stir and drink immediately.",1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,Treatment of mild to moderate ulcerative colitis and Crohn’s disease.,1,1,HERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:27:23.264875+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY43902,Aceclofenac + Paracetamol,Dolowin Plus,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XmiCJHN00VsNWRvJTwUf8bvDqCOLs9dM/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY43902_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1XmiCJHN00VsNWRvJTwUf8bvDqCOLs9dM_view_usp_drivesdk_4dfa7d8fe3.pdf,page_text/DR-XY43902_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1XmiCJHN00VsNWRvJTwUf8bvDqCOLs9dM_view_usp_drivesdk_4dfa7d8fe3.json,212643f291f2ffc8db74fec53af5e6fb0eb58bf212b4ddfbda312e600a9a68e0,6509965,3,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T05:27:31.854630+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY43909,Verapamil Hydrochloride,Isoptin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UXXMTd7tqUXA-YyK--MWEVkBh64tSfaX/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY43909_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UXXMTd7tqUXA-YyK--MWEVkBh64tSfaX_view_usp_drivesdk_e776d973ab.pdf,page_text/DR-XY43909_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UXXMTd7tqUXA-YyK--MWEVkBh64tSfaX_view_usp_drivesdk_e776d973ab.json,c9f273b5ee14f813b2a035ceee9001b5232571b755bcb1cfe6fdeef7794d7de3,423860,16,digital_text,"Verapamil hydrochloride is a calcium ion influx inhibitor (slow channel blocker or calcium ion antagonist). Verapamil hydrochloride is an almost white, crystalline powder, practically free of odor, with a bitter taste. It is soluble in water, freely soluble in chloroform, sparingly soluble in alcohol and practically insoluble in ether. Verapamil Hydrochloride (Isoptin®) Solution for I.V. Injection Verapamil hydrochloride injection is a sterile, nonpyrogenic solution and contains no bacteriostat or antimicrobial agent and is intended for single-dose intravenous administration. It may contain hydrochloric acid for pH adjustment; pH is 4.9. CLINICAL PARTICULARS Therapeutic indications Verapamil Hydrochloride (Isoptin®) Solution for I.V. Injection Verapamil hydrochloride injection is indicated in adults, neonates, infants, children, and adolescents for the treatment of supraventricular tachyarrhythmias, which includes the following: 1. Rapid conversion to sinus rhythm of paroxysmal supraventricular tachycardias, including those associated with accessory bypass tracts (Wolff-Parkinson-White [W-P-W] or Lown- [Page 2] Ganong-Levine [L-G-L] syndromes). When clinically advisable, appropriate vagal maneuvers (e.g., Valsalva maneuver) should be attempted prior to administration of verapamil hydrochloride. 2. Temporary control of rapid ventricular rate in atrial flutter or atrial fibrillation except when the atrial flutter and/or atrial fibrillation are associated with accessory bypass tracts (Wolff- Parkinson-White (W-P-W) or Lown-Ganong-Levine (L-G-L) syndromes). Posology and method of administration Posology – Verapamil Hydrochloride (Isoptin ®) Solution for I.V. Injection Adults The recommended intravenous doses of verapamil hydrochloride are as follows: Initial dose: 5 to 10 mg (0.075 to 0.15 mg/kg body weight) given as an intravenous bolus over at least two minutes. Repeat dose: 10 mg (0.15 mg/kg body weight) 30 minutes after the first dose if the initial response is not adequate. Special Populations Pediatric population The safety and efficacy of verapamil hydrochloride injection have been established in neonates, infants, children and adolescents: Initial Dose 0 to 1 year: 0.1 to 0.2 mg/kg body weight (usual single dose range: 0.75 to 2 mg) should be administered as an intravenous bolus over at least two minutes under continuous ECG monitoring. 1 to 15 years: 0.1 to 0.3 mg/kg body weight (usual single dose range: 2 to 5 mg) should be administered as an intravenous bolus over at least two minutes. Do not exceed 5 mg. Repeat Dose 0 to 1 year: 0.1 to 0.2 mg/kg body weight (usual single dose range: 0.75 to 2 mg) 30 minutes after the first dose if the initial response is not adequate. 1 to 15 years: 0.1 to 0.3 mg/kg body weight (usual single dose range: 2 to 5 mg) 30 minutes after the first dose if the initial response is not adequate. Do not exceed 10 mg as a single dose. Elderly patients The dose should be administered over at least three minutes to minimize the risk of untoward drug effects. Method of administration For intravenous use only. Verapamil hydrochloride should be given as a slow intravenous injection over at least a two minute period of time under continuous electrocardiographic and blood pressure monitoring. Parenteral drug products should be inspected visually for particulate matter and discoloration prior to administration, whenever solution and container permit. Verapamil hydrochloride is physically compatible and chemically stable for at least 24 hours at 25°C protected from light in most common large volume parenteral solutions. Use only if solution is clear and vial seal is intact. [Page 3] Unused amount of solution should be discarded immediately following withdrawal of any portion of contents. For stability reasons this product is not recommended for dilution with sodium lactate injection, USP in polyvinyl chloride bags. Admixing intravenous verapamil hydrochloride with albumin, amphotericin B, hydralazine hydrochloride or trimethoprim and sulfamethoxazole should be avoided. Verapamil hydrochloride will precipitate in any solution with a pH above 6.0.",1,3,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Verapamil Hydrochloride (Isoptin®) Solution for I.V. Injection Verapamil hydrochloride injection is indicated in adults, neonates, infants, children, and adolescents for the treatment of supraventricular tachyarrhythmias, which includes the following: 1. Rapid conversion to sinus rhythm of paroxysmal supraventricular tachycardias, including those associated with accessory bypass tracts (Wolff-Parkinson-White [W-P-W] or Lown- [Page 2] Ganong-Levine [L-G-L] syndromes). When clinically advisable, appropriate vagal maneuvers (e.g., Valsalva maneuver) should be attempted prior to administration of verapamil hydrochloride. 2. Temporary control of rapid ventricular rate in atrial flutter or atrial fibrillation except when the atrial flutter and/or atrial fibrillation are associated with accessory bypass tracts (Wolff- Parkinson-White (W-P-W) or Lown-Ganong-Levine (L-G-L) syndromes).",1,2,Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:27:35.307695+00:00
