PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY44086,,,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1jqAPNUePgqPBwdJ7prr2UcJMqVOz1JBf/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY44086_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jqAPNUePgqPBwdJ7prr2UcJMqVOz1JBf_view_usp_drivesdk_10ce529a64.pdf,page_text/DR-XY44086_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jqAPNUePgqPBwdJ7prr2UcJMqVOz1JBf_view_usp_drivesdk_10ce529a64.json,90848272002a12ad0c1df78ff42dbd6f45f821618a9195f86fd9b5e20edf473e,206914,1,digital_text,"10 mg: White to off-white film-coated tablet, oval-shaped, biconvex, plain on both sides. 20 mg: White to off-white film-coated tablet, oval-shaped, biconvex, plain on one side and bisected on the other side. 40 mg: White to off-white film-coated tablet, oval-shaped, biconvex, plain on one side and bisected on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Atorvastatin is used to reduce LDL-cholesterol, apolipoprotein B, and triglycerides, and to increase HDL-cholesterol in the treatment of hyperlipidaemias, including hypercholesterolaemias and combined (mixed) hyperlipidaemias (type IIa or IIb hyperlipoproteinaemias), hypertriglyceridaemia (type IV), and dysbetalipoproteinaemia (type III). It is also used for primary and secondary prophylaxis of cardiovascular events in patients with multiple risk factors, including diabetes mellitus.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:29:42.578306+00:00
