PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY44173,Co-Amoxiclav,Cavumox,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1I47_ywwfoW58jAeltbFAAC1LgsS_ca-8/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY44173_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1I47_ywwfoW58jAeltbFAAC1LgsS_ca-8_view_usp_drivesdk_b126e31b6a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY44173_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1I47_ywwfoW58jAeltbFAAC1LgsS_ca-8_view_usp_drivesdk_b126e31b6a.json,3d2c1fb334013e02642e02894f84800d8c4071eca7fd848ae53fa9949815dbfb,498858,1,digital_text,A white sterile powder for IV injection and IV infusion,1,1,PROdUCT dESCRIPTION:,"Amoxicillin-clavulanate should be used in accordance with local official antibiotic-prescribing guidelines and local susceptibility data. CAvUMOx ® intravenous is indicated for short term treatment of bacterial infections and Amoxicillin resistant with b-lactamase production in bacterial strains such as: - Upper Respiratory Tract Infections (including ENT) e.g. recurrent tonsillitis, sinusitis, otitis media, typically caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae, Haemophilus influenzae#, Moraxella catarrhalis# and Streptococcus pyogenes. - Lower Respiratory Tract Infections e.g. acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis, lobar and bronchopneumonia, typically caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae, Haemophilus influenzae# and Moraxella catarrhalis#. - Genito-urinary Tract Infections e.g. cystitis, urethritis, pyelonephritis, female genital infections typically caused by Enterobacteriaceae# (mainly Escherichia coli#), Staphylococcus saprophyticus and Enterococcus species, and gonorrhoea caused by Neisseria gonorrhoeae# - Skin and Soft Tissue Infections typically caused by Staphylococcus aureus#, Streptococcus pyogenes and Bacteroides species#. - Bone and Joint Infections e.g. osteomyelitis typically caused by Staphylococcus aureus #, where more prolonged therapy may be appropriate - Other Infections e.g. septic abortion, puerperal sepsis, intra-abdominal sepsis. Co-amoxiclav intravenous injection is indicated for prophylaxis against infection which may be associated with major surgical procedures e.g. gastrointestinal, pelvic, head and neck, cardiac, renal, joint replacement and biliary tract. A comprehensive list of sensitive organisms is provided in Pharmacodynamics. #Some members of these species of bacteria produce b-lactamase, rendering them insensitive to Amoxicillin alone. Local susceptibility data should be consulted where available, and microbiological sampling and susceptibility testing performed where necessary. Infections caused by Amoxicillin-susceptible organisms are amenable to CAvUMOx ® treatment due to its Amoxicillin content. Mixed infections caused by Amoxicillin-susceptible organisms in conjunction with CAvUMOx ® susceptible b-lactamase-producing organisms may therefore be treated by CAvUMOx®.",1,1,INdICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T05:30:18.988920+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY44194,Rosuvastatin Calcium,Torros,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ke4h0RXab_UaDlizMOi-CapmdrA_8hF-/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY44194_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ke4h0RXab_UaDlizMOi-CapmdrA_8hF-_view_usp_drivesdk_6e28f7489f.pdf,page_text/DR-XY44194_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ke4h0RXab_UaDlizMOi-CapmdrA_8hF-_view_usp_drivesdk_6e28f7489f.json,7b900d0db28bd538c6d71524e8ce6a3d248da728b98d9faf6b6680e109d541e7,1013782,9,digital_text_and_ocr,"10mg Film-Coated Tablet is a salmon pink to light orange film- coated tablet round, biconvex, plain on one side and bisected on the other side. 20mg Film-Coated Tablet is a salmon pink to light orange film- coated tablet round, biconvex, plain on one side and bisected on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Used to reduce LDL-cholesterol, apolipoprotein B, and triglycerides, and to increase HDL-cholesterol in the management of hyperlipidemias including primary hypercholesterolemia (type lla), mixed dyslipidemia (type llb), and hypertriglyceridemia (type lV), as well as in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia. It is also used to reduce the progression of atherosclerosis.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T05:30:39.013165+00:00
