PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY44523,Salbutamol (As Sulfate),Provexel,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/19OCMEv2KH94JLkeshBOLAnpzOLXF-cxQ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY44523_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19OCMEv2KH94JLkeshBOLAnpzOLXF-cxQ_view_usp_drivesdk_9848604484.pdf,page_text/DR-XY44523_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19OCMEv2KH94JLkeshBOLAnpzOLXF-cxQ_view_usp_drivesdk_9848604484.json,5423b0d6ffae7bf99b506a935a55412bbc8bb632d9b8d0bf875073505f83598a,1106863,1,digital_text,"Salbutamol 100 mcg/ actuation Metered-Dose Inhaler is a metered dose pressurized inhalation aerosol. The container is made of PHARMACODYNAMICS: the respiratory tract. It stimulates adenyl cyclase, the enzyme which catalyzes the conversion of adenosine triphosphate (ATP) to cyclic-3’ ,5’-adenosine monophosphate (cAMP). CAMP mediates cellular responses such as bronchial smooth muscle relaxation resulting in bronchodilation.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,For the relief of bronchospasm associated with reversible obstructive airway diseases such as bronchial asthma and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. For the prevention of exercise-induced bronchospasm if the drug is given before exertion.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T06:04:04.070754+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY44546,,,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J9MYg7uMhYwJilyKzLqCJu8K7y2Ul0lO/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY44546_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1J9MYg7uMhYwJilyKzLqCJu8K7y2Ul0lO_view_usp_drivesdk_3be9f08ec8.pdf,page_text/DR-XY44546_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1J9MYg7uMhYwJilyKzLqCJu8K7y2Ul0lO_view_usp_drivesdk_3be9f08ec8.json,8b48289eb6726df5b7fe05c6183daaae0bb204645adbfaf2bc66923c3c8cec08,353829,14,digital_text,"The active constituents of Bimatoprost + Timolol Maleate (GANFORT® PF) eye drops are bimatoprost 0.3 mg/mL and timolol 5.0 mg/mL (with timolol present as timolol maleate). Chemical structure: (structure of bimatoprost) CAS Registry No. 155206-00-1 (structure of timolol maleate) CAS Registry No. 26921-17-5 Bimatoprost is a synthetic prostamide analogue for ophthalmic use. It is a white to off-white powder and is very soluble in ethyl alcohol, methyl alcohol and slightly soluble in water. Chemical name: (Z)-7-[(1R,2R,3R,5S)-3,5-Dihydroxy-2-[(1E,3S)-3-hydroxy-5-phenyl-1- pentenyl]cyclopentyl]-N-ethyl-5-heptenamide Empirical formula: C25H37NO4 Timolol maleate is a non -selective beta -adrenergic receptor blocking agent. It is a white, odourless , crystalline powder which is soluble in water, methanol and alcohol. BIMATOPROST + TIMOLOL MALEATE [Page 2] Chemical name: (S)-1-(tert-butylamino)-3- [(4-morpholino-1,2,5-thiadiazol-3-yl) oxy] - 2-propanol maleate (1:1) (salt) Molecular weight: 432.50 as the maleate salt Empirical formula: C13H24N4O3S.C4H4O4",1,2,DESCRIPTION,Bimatoprost + Timolol Maleate (GANFORT® PF) eye drops are indicated for the reduction of intraocular pressure (IOP) in patients with open-angle glaucoma or ocular hypertension who are insufficiently responsive to topical beta-blockers or prostaglandin analogues.,5,5,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T06:04:07.457109+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY44609,Citicoline (as sodium),Cholinerv,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1e3n-iPvi8lyALpNzzMQt1kak5SOrkjqH/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY44609_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1e3n-iPvi8lyALpNzzMQt1kak5SOrkjqH_view_usp_drivesdk_97f8070554.pdf,page_text/DR-XY44609_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1e3n-iPvi8lyALpNzzMQt1kak5SOrkjqH_view_usp_drivesdk_97f8070554.json,6fac2c189fc695746b2a3c3b8b6bc9302a162addb0df3c9d03007dc89a5a5745,3730688,1,ocr,"Citicoline Sodium (Cholinerv®) 500 mg Film-Coated Tablet: Purple, capsule-shaped, film-coated tablet Citicoline Sodium (Cholinerv®) 1 g Film-Coated Tablet: Purple, elliptical, film-coated tablet Citicoline Sodium (Cholinerv®) 100 mg/mL Adult Solution (Oral Drops): Clear, light purple-colored fruit-flavored liquid Citicoline Sodium (Cholinerv®) 125 mg/mL or 250 mg/mL Solution for Injection: Clear, colorless, sterile aqueous solution filled in 5 mL clear Type | glass ampules with a fill volume of 4 mL CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY PHARMACODYNAMICS Citicoline is a complex organic molecule that functions as an intermediate in the biosynthesis of cell membrane phospholipids. Citicoline is also known as CDP-choline or cytidine diphosphate choline (cytidine 5-'diphosphocholine). CDP-choline belongs to the group of biomolecules in living systems known as nucleotides that play important roles in cellular metabolism. The pharmacologic action of citicoline appears to involve mechanisms that extend beyond phospholipid metabolism. Citicoline metabolites - choline, methionine, betaine, and cytidine-derived nucleotides - enter a number of metabolic pathways. DXXXN Biochemical markers of cholinergic nerve transmission are known to be deficient in conditions characterized by degeneration of cholinergic neurons, such as Alzheimer's disease. Citicoline modestly improves cognitive function in Alzheimer's disease by serving as an acetylcholine precursor. The brain uses choline preferentially for acetylcholine synthesis, which can limit the amount of choline available for phosphatidylcholine production. Citicoline has been investigated as a therapy for stroke patients. Three mechanisms are postulated: (1) repair of the neuronal membrane via increased synthesis of phosphatidylcholine; (2) repair of damaged cholinergic neurons via potentiation of acetylcholine production; and (3) reduction of free fatty acid build-up at the site of stroke-induced nerve damage. Citicoline protects cholinergic neurons from autocannibalism, a process in which membrane phospholipids are catabolized to provide choline for the synthesis of acetylcholine. This occurs when choline supplies are depleted, necessitating sacrifice of membrane phospholipids to maintain neurotransmission. As an exogenous source of choline for acetylcholine production, citicoline thus spares membrane phospholipids (in particular, phosphatidylcholine) and prevents neuronal cell death. PHARMACOKINETICS Citicoline is a water-soluble compound with greater than 90% bioavailability. Pharmacokinetic studies in healthy adults have shown oral doses of citicoline to be rapidly absorbed, with less than 1% excreted in the feces. Plasma levels peak in a biphasic manner, at 1 hour after ingestion followed by a second larger peak at 24 hours post-dosing. Citicoline is metabolized in the gut wall and liver. The byproducts of exogenous citicoline formed by hydrolysis in the intestinal wall are choline and cytidine. After absorption, choline and cytidine are dispersed throughout the body, enter systemic circulation for utilization in various biosynthetic pathways and cross the blood-brain barrier for re-synthesis into citicoline in the brain. Pharmacokinetic studies using “C citicoline show citicoline elimination occurs mainly via respiratory CO, and urinary excretion, in two phases, mirroring the biphasic plasma peaks. The initial peak in plasma concentration is followed by a sharp decline, which then slows over the next 4 to 10 hours. In the second phase, an initially rapid decline after the 24-hour plasma peak is similarly followed by a slower elimination rate. The elimination half-life is 56 hours for CO, and 71 hours for urinary excretion.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTIONS,"* Acute and recovery phase of cerebral infarction (e.g., ischemia due to stroke) * Cognitive dysfunction due to degenerative (i.e., Alzheimer's disease) and cerebrovascular disease * Cerebral insufficiency (e.g., dizziness, memory loss, poor concentration, disorientation) due to head trauma or brain injury * Parkinson's disease",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T06:04:20.173462+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY44618,Rocuronium Bromide,Kabiroc,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ATKVnEWIvDIobCsgwR1bjCObZJ2u3VLe/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY44618_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ATKVnEWIvDIobCsgwR1bjCObZJ2u3VLe_view_usp_drivesdk_93c3147d61.pdf,page_text/DR-XY44618_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ATKVnEWIvDIobCsgwR1bjCObZJ2u3VLe_view_usp_drivesdk_93c3147d61.json,377fc3b00b19104d12307efc38a9fd82737737373b0fcef15f60a02b55108564,687735,16,digital_text,"Solution for injection / infusion Clear, colourless to pale brownish-yellow solution",1,1,1.0 PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated in adult and paediatric patients (from term neonates to adolescents (0 to < 18 years) as an adjunct to general anaesthesia to facilitate tracheal intubation during routine sequence induction and to provide skeletal muscle relaxation, during surgery. Also indicated in adults to facilitate tracheal intubation during rapid sequence induction and as an adjunct in the intensive care unit (ICU) (e.g. to facilitate intubation), for short term use.",5,5,4.0 INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T06:04:24.040532+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY44622,Potassium Citrate,Tascit BID,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WcIHQCprEAsfm7FOR1ZgvQyxzO_zB_FP/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY44622_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WcIHQCprEAsfm7FOR1ZgvQyxzO_zB_FP_view_usp_drivesdk_6c7d09c86a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY44622_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WcIHQCprEAsfm7FOR1ZgvQyxzO_zB_FP_view_usp_drivesdk_6c7d09c86a.json,561ca08fece070fec28a6427c5247b0c8c4a6242eb741a29ba9835de9b067d81,1254015,1,digital_text,"® Potassium Citrate (Tascit ) 1080 mg (10 mEq) Extended-Release Tablet: Cream-mottled, elliptical tablet, plain on both sides ® Potassium Citrate (Tascit BID) 1620 mg (15 mEq) Extended-Release Tablet: Cream-mottled, modified oval tablet, plain on both sides PHARMACODYNAMICS Metabolism of absorbed potassium citrate produces an alkaline load, raising urinary pH and increasing urinary citrate by augmenting citrate clearance. Thus, potassium citrate therapy appears to increase urinary citrate mainly by changing the renal handling of citrate, and, to a smaller extent, by increasing the filterable load of citrate. Increased urinary citrate and pH decrease calcium ion activity by increasing calcium complexation to dissociated anions and thus decreasing the saturation of calcium oxalate. Potassium citrate also inhibits the crystallization and spontaneous nucleation of calcium oxalate and calcium phosphate in hypocitraturic calcium nephrolithiasis. However, potassium citrate does not alter the urinary saturation of calcium phosphate, because the effect of increased citrate complexation of calcium is antagonized by the rise in pH-dependent dissociation of phosphate. Calcium phosphate stones are more stable in alkaline urine. PHARMACOKINETICS Potassium citrate is oxidized in the body to form potassium bicarbonate. Oxidation is virtually complete. Less than 5% of the citrate is excreted unchanged in the urine.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTIONS,• For the management of:  Renal tubular acidosis (RTA) with calcium stones  Hypocitraturic calcium oxalate nephrolithiasis of any etiology  Uric acid lithiasis with or without calcium stones • For the prevention of stone relapse after extracorporeal shock wave lithotripsy (ESWL) or lithotomy,1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T06:04:28.824392+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY44643,Losartan Potassium,Bepsar,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mSmPTi7wD6GgFCDnoKpFjjlLhUp85yuc/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY44643_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mSmPTi7wD6GgFCDnoKpFjjlLhUp85yuc_view_usp_drivesdk_b993faf51f.pdf,page_text/DR-XY44643_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mSmPTi7wD6GgFCDnoKpFjjlLhUp85yuc_view_usp_drivesdk_b993faf51f.json,ec27ada388d82d37424e4a6a1ecf2cff724ba036e7c5c26dc4ac0eb5075e3a44,2881319,1,ocr,,,,,"the active metabolite can be removed by haemodialysis. It is used in the management of hypertension, particularly in patients who develop cough with Angiotensin Converting",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T06:04:42.178159+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY44670,Zinc Sulfate Monohydrate,Unbranded,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1X36levgCEs2UQlAJXm6jPbgg0HHPvDjv/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY44670_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1X36levgCEs2UQlAJXm6jPbgg0HHPvDjv_view_usp_drivesdk_c65e1e3b8f.pdf,page_text/DR-XY44670_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1X36levgCEs2UQlAJXm6jPbgg0HHPvDjv_view_usp_drivesdk_c65e1e3b8f.json,8df22733a8703b1b5e4e8774a2fd5c5ce85e240ea71aae39a473a628cf965e01,317820,1,ocr,"Zinc Sulfate Monohydrate 27 mg/mL Syrup (Oral Drops) is a turbid, orange syrup with orange flavor. Zinc Sulfate Monohydrate 55 mg/5 mL Syrup is a turbid, viscous, orange syrup with orange flavor. WHATIS IN THE MEDICINE? This product contains Zinc. Zinc helps the body’s natural defense against damaging free radical (antioxidant effect) and helps boost immune function. Free radicals are highly reactive and unstable chemicals generated during normal body activities that require oxygen (e.g., respiration, digestion, blood circulation, immune system response, etc.) and after exposure to UV light, cigarette smoke and various pollutants. One major effect of zinc is onthe ability of cells to properly replicate the DNA which is required for cells to multiply. Hence, zinc is needed for normal growth. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTIONS,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T06:04:47.790949+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY44672,Esomeprazole (As Magnesium Trihydrate),Eso 40,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/15YHCm2E3TXQnmGjeTanAZcaoHC4UwjK4/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY44672_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15YHCm2E3TXQnmGjeTanAZcaoHC4UwjK4_view_usp_drivesdk_a4f70ae36d.pdf,page_text/DR-XY44672_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15YHCm2E3TXQnmGjeTanAZcaoHC4UwjK4_view_usp_drivesdk_a4f70ae36d.json,274291b4b4d9ab026372a2bbc610dc21337cd3d6536da5d9e808b89c89dc3c4b,425410,1,digital_text,,,,,"For the treatment of gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD) and erosive esophagitis. Prevention of stomach ulcers in people taking nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs), such as Ibuprofen, treatment of Helicobacter pylori (H. Pylori) infections, treatment of pathological hypersecretory conditions, in which stomach acid is greatly overproduced, such as Zollinger-Ellison syndrome.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T06:04:50.642255+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY44686,Carboprost (as tromethamine),Endoprost,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1T_sqvMG57rhG9w4ojc9DaJ1S80tAz91Q/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY44686_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1T_sqvMG57rhG9w4ojc9DaJ1S80tAz91Q_view_usp_drivesdk_4a82629dca.pdf,page_text/DR-XY44686_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1T_sqvMG57rhG9w4ojc9DaJ1S80tAz91Q_view_usp_drivesdk_4a82629dca.json,1bbac33b0fd7c6519aa9c38a60d7f5eb60830cdb10a6fb4357942f28ff5799fb,1455348,1,digital_text,"Endoprost is a clear colourless sterile aqueous solution of Carboprost Tromethamine for intramuscular injection. Carboprost is a synthetic 15 methyl analogue of naturally occurring prostaglandin F2a. Carboprost Tromethamine is chemically a salt of (5Z, 13E)-(8R,9S,11R,15S)-9,11,15-trihydroxy-15- methyl-5, 13-prostadien-1-oic acid with 2-amino-2-hydroxymethyl-1,3-propanediol. The molecular formula is C H O N and has molecular weight of 489.64. It is a white to lightly off-white crystalline 25 48 8 powder and is soluble in water.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,Carboprost Tromethamine (Endoprost) is indicated for the treatment of post partum haemorrhage especially due to uterine atony which has not responded to conventional methods of management. Carboprost Tromethamine (Endoprost) may be used prophylactically by intramuscular injection at the birth of anterior shoulder in patients with following risks: § Grand multipara. § Pre-eclampsia. § Rapid or prolonged labour. § Placental abnormalities. § Previous uterine surgery. § History of PPH. § History of retained placenta. § Over distention of uterus.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T06:04:54.391106+00:00
