PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY44879,Brinzolamide + Brimonidine tartrate,Simbrinza,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/18pMT5CyGtA8niI6037mtb-aVMwW3NS2P/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY44879_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18pMT5CyGtA8niI6037mtb-aVMwW3NS2P_view_usp_drivesdk_cc5fd3c133.pdf,page_text/DR-XY44879_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18pMT5CyGtA8niI6037mtb-aVMwW3NS2P_view_usp_drivesdk_cc5fd3c133.json,7a818d6ad15a816f2f1e61b5247502e9a765a52331ca4c0cf292d7a380b0ab0f,163416,14,digital_text,"Pharmaceutical form Sterile Ophthalmic Suspension Active substance(s) One mL of the sterile ophthalmic suspension contains 10 mg of brinzolamide, and 2 mg brimonidine tartrate corresponding to 1.3 mg of brimonidine tartrate. Excipients Excipient with known effect: 1 mL of the sterile ophthalmic suspension contains 0.03 mg of benzalkonium chloride. Other excipients: propylene glycol, carbomer 974P, boric acid, mannitol, sodium chloride, tyloxapol, hydrochloric acid and/or sodium hydroxide and purified water. Pharmaceutical formulations may vary between countries.",1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,Brinzolamide/ Brimonidine tartrate (Simbrinza) Sterile Ophthalmic Suspension is indicated for the reduction of elevated intraocular pressure (IOP) in adult patients with open angle glaucoma or ocular hypertension.,1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T06:13:45.919351+00:00
