PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY44898,Aprepitant,Emend,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/15e--lAyaYamVe9rkHTqXFN9X5l9hasTD/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY44898_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15e--lAyaYamVe9rkHTqXFN9X5l9hasTD_view_usp_drivesdk_01fce80c00.pdf,page_text/DR-XY44898_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15e--lAyaYamVe9rkHTqXFN9X5l9hasTD_view_usp_drivesdk_01fce80c00.json,e26e7c2cbfb6c446d12b975da969367dde0640d932b323f4f3bc42c5cfd29bca,221301,23,digital_text,"APREPITANT (EMEND), is a substance P neurokinin 1 (NK1) receptor antagonist. Aprepitant is a structurally novel substance P neurokinin 1 (NK1) receptor antagonist, chemically described as 5 -[[(2R,3S)-2-[(1R)-1-[3,5-bis(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]ethoxy]- 3-(4-fluorophenyl)-4-morpholinyl]methyl]-1,2-dihydro-3H-1,2,4-triazol-3-one. Its empirical formula is C23H21F7N4O3, and its structural formula is: APREPITANT N O O CF3 CF3 F NNH NH O CH3 [Page 2] 2 Aprepitant is a white to off-white crystalline solid, with a molecular weight of 534.43. It is practically insoluble in water. Aprepitant is sparingly soluble in ethanol and isopropyl acetate and slightly soluble in acetonitrile.",1,2,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"APREPITANT (EMEND), in combination with other antiemetic agents, is indicated for the prevention of acute and delayed nausea and vomiting associated with initial and repeat courses of: • highly emetogenic cancer chemotherapy (see RECOMMENDED DOSE). • moderately emetogenic cancer chemother apy (see RECOMMENDED",2,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T06:14:22.649391+00:00
