PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY45014,D-Alpha Tocopherol (Vitamin E),None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/173fav4SmG5mt_5biDyC6j1BAGprgvZpX/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY45014_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_173fav4SmG5mt_5biDyC6j1BAGprgvZpX_view_usp_drivesdk_a1ce897906.pdf,page_text/DR-XY45014_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_173fav4SmG5mt_5biDyC6j1BAGprgvZpX_view_usp_drivesdk_a1ce897906.json,9cc0769f676b18107be73e5fd7340498b400e822c7a6fbff2e88c4be7768c087,3132650,2,ocr,"d-Alpha Tocopherol 400 |.U. Scftgel Capsule is a galden yellow to brownish yellow oily liquid, with characteristic odor contained in a clear, oblong, yellowish soft gelatin capsule. Whatisin the Medicine? Each softgel capsule contains 400 IU of d-Alpha Tocopherol (Vitamin E) as the active ingredient. Gelatin Capsule: Methyl Paraben, Propy! Paraben, Gelatin Powder, Glycerin and Purified Water. Strength of the Medicine: 4001.U. Softgel Capsule Whatis this Medicine used for? itis usedin the treatment and prevention of Vitamin E deficiency. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Take an oral dose of 1 capsule once or twice daily with food or as prescribed by a physician. When should you not take this medicine? Ask a doctor or pharmacist if it is safe for you to use Vitamin E if you have other nditions, especially: ae apd anemia (lowred blaed celts} . ableeding or blood clotting disorder suchas hemaphilia liver disease kidney disease any allergies an eye disorder called retinitis pigmentosa avitamin K deficiency high cholesterol or triglycerides (a type of fat inthe blood} ahistory of cancer ahistory of stroke or alood clot if you need surgery, cr have recently had surgery. Donat use this medicine without doctor’s advice if you are breast-feeding.a baby. Care that should be taken wher taking this medicine? - Swallow capsules whole; do not crush or chew. ~ Use vitamin E exactly as directed on the label, or as prescribed by your doctor. Do not use in larger or smaller amounts or for longer than recommended. Undesirable Effects: ing may be associated with the use of d-alpha Tocapherol: The oe blurred vision diarrhea dizziness headache nausea or stomach cramps unusual tiredness or weakness [Page 2] What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Avoid taking other , mineral Ld ,ornutritional products without your doctor’s advice. Tell your doctor about all medicines you use, and those you start or stop using during your treatment, especially: cholestyramine minerat oif orlistat (alli, Xenical} warfarin (Coumadin, Jantoven} What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the missed dose as soon as you remember. Skip the missed dose if it is alrnost time for your next scheduled dose. Da not take extra medicine to make up the missed dose. Signs and symptoms of overdose: Symptoms of overdose may include: stomach pain, nausea, diarrhea, dizziness, headache, blurred vision, or tiredness. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage: In case of accidental overdose, discontinue use and seek professional assistance immediately. Howshould you keep this Medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from light. Keep out reach of children. When should you consult your Doctor? When you take more d-Alpha Tocopherol than you should, talk to a doctor. If you get any side effects, talk to your doctor. Availability: Alu/Clear PVDC Blister Pack x 10’s (Box of 100’s}. ADR Reporting: For suspected adverse drug reaction, report tothe FDA: www.fda.gov.ph Patient should seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration Number: DRP-XY45014 Date of First Authorization: 26 January 2016 Revision Date: September 2021 Manufactured by:",1,2,Description of the Product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T06:36:35.815439+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY45022,Ondansetron (as hydrochloride dehydrate),Ondavell,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_j3r2tswCsWzBfRypr6bgqFjCBqL-JxM/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY45022_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_j3r2tswCsWzBfRypr6bgqFjCBqL-JxM_view_usp_drivesdk_e304903edc.pdf,page_text/DR-XY45022_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_j3r2tswCsWzBfRypr6bgqFjCBqL-JxM_view_usp_drivesdk_e304903edc.json,156a1ae936f1343efad05014516e3521bce5f76a7057c2698446d9a9f838e825,174237,2,digital_text,LABORATORIES Healthcare Inc. [Page 3],2,2,PHARMACEUTICAL,"Adults : Ondansetron (Ondavell) Film-Coated Tablet is indicated for the management of nausea and vomiting induced by cytotoxic chemotherapy and radiotherapy. Ondansetron (Ondavell) Film-Coated Tablet is indicated for the prevention of post-operative nausea and vomiting (PONV). For treatment of established PONV, administration by injection is recommended. Paediatric Population : Ondansetron (Ondavell) Film-Coated Tablet is indicated for the management of chemotherapy-induced nausea and vomiting (CINV) in children aged ≥6 months. No studies have been conducted on the use of orally administered ondansetron in the prevention and treatment of PONV in children aged ≥1 month, administration by IV injection is recommended for this purpose.",1,1,INDICATIONS :,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T06:36:39.116323+00:00
