PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY45385,Multivitamins + Minerals (see formulation on reverse side),Dibavit,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1SUCPKJ9lxeg1jaTbSF1uKfD8r2KeqJtd/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY45385_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1SUCPKJ9lxeg1jaTbSF1uKfD8r2KeqJtd_view_usp_drivesdk_13ed4444c4.pdf,page_text/DR-XY45385_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1SUCPKJ9lxeg1jaTbSF1uKfD8r2KeqJtd_view_usp_drivesdk_13ed4444c4.json,8b30f4c754b6364b98a2c83c1a908b8ba1c0a11fa4280067fb20ceb732f9e593,2734249,1,ocr,"WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Orange color, oily suspension, filled in 20 minim, oblong, green opaque, soft gelatin shell capsule Take the missed dose as soon as you remember it. However, if it is almost time for the next dose, skip the dose you missed and use your WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? next dose when you are meant to. Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten dose. Multivitamins + Minerals (Dibavit) contains Vitamin D3, Vitamin E, Vitamin B6, Vitamin B1, Zinc, Vitamin A, Copper, Vitamin B12, Vitamin WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? B9 & Chromium. If you (or someone else) accidentally taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor or contact the nearest accident and emergency department. VITAMIN 03 Vitamin D is absorbed with the aid of bile salts from the small intestine. Vitamin D is converted to its major circulating form and is transported to the kidney to form the metabolically active form. Vitamin D is HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? transported in the plasma bound to a specific vitamin D-binding protein, which is its main storage form. * Keep out of reach of children. Small amounts are stored in the liver, and also in adipose tissue. * Store at temperatures not exceeding 25°C in a dry place & away from direct sunlight. VITAMIN E Absorption of vitamin E is relatively inefficient (20-80%); the efficiency of absorption falls as the dose WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? increases. Vitamin E is taken up principally via the lymphatic system and is transported in the blood bound * If you are allergic (hypersensitive) to active substances or any of the other ingredients to lipoproteins. It is stored in all fatty tissues, in particular adipose tissue, liver and muscle. The major route of elimination is the feces. * If any undesirable effect occurs * If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, consult a doctor before using this product VITAMIN Bs Vitamin Bs are all water-soluble and are absorbed in the small intestine, converted to their active forms PACKAGING and transported in the blood-stream throughout the body. The excesses of vitamin Bs, as well as their * PVC/PVDC/Alu Blister Pack x 10's (Box of 30's) metabolites, are largely excreted in the urine. ZINC Absorption occurs throughout the length of the small intestine, mostly in the jejunum. Zinc is transported Manufactured by: MEGA LIFESCIENCES Public Company Limited 384 Moo 4, Soi 6, Bangpoo Industrial Estate, Pattana 3 Road, in association with albumin, amino acids and a 2-macroglobulin. Zinc is principally an intracellular ion and Phraeksa, Mueang, Samutprakarn 10280, Thailand approximately 95% is found within the cells. Elimination of zinc is mainly in the feces; smaller amounts are excreted in the urine and via the skin. Manufactured under license from:",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T06:46:04.290946+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY45399,Teicoplanin,Brutio 200,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vvBkhVY1X8DIpGZXCjpmWRqir0kZYlVb/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY45399_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vvBkhVY1X8DIpGZXCjpmWRqir0kZYlVb_view_usp_drivesdk_6c0d6dc7f4.pdf,page_text/DR-XY45399_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vvBkhVY1X8DIpGZXCjpmWRqir0kZYlVb_view_usp_drivesdk_6c0d6dc7f4.json,994dd9ca725b9002892042bb4dd1af25efe4c8bccdcb5016af2639a178401da1,4961267,1,digital_text,Off white to yellowish lyophilized mass filled in clear glass tubular vials. Teicoplanin belongs to a group of antibiotics called glycopeptides. Bacteria have an external cell wall that is reinforced by molecules called peptidoglycans. The cell wall is vital for protection against the normal environment of the body in which the bacteria live. Teicoplanin works by blocking the formation of these peptidoglycans. By doing this the walls of the bacteria become weak and this results in the death of the bacteria. TeicopIanin is used to treat serious infections of the heart and blood. It is not absorbed from the gut and is therefore only given by injection or infusion.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Teicoplanin is indicated in potentially serious Gram-positive infections, including and osteomyelitis, respiratory infections, skin and",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T06:46:09.216563+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY45400,Teicoplanin,Brutio 400,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Vq7sB2Y-YlEV4JVq04uycS4ROBXqidSz/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY45400_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Vq7sB2Y-YlEV4JVq04uycS4ROBXqidSz_view_usp_drivesdk_1591e76e0c.pdf,page_text/DR-XY45400_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Vq7sB2Y-YlEV4JVq04uycS4ROBXqidSz_view_usp_drivesdk_1591e76e0c.json,e12fce6040edf90b7888652e378f6c2a39ffc910351d0753f566508949e05253,3050829,1,digital_text,"Off white to yellowish lyophilized mass filled in clear glass tubular vials. Teicoplanin belongs to a group of antibiotics called glycopeptides. Bacteria have an external cell wall that is reinforced by molecules called peptidoglycans. The cell wall is vital for protection against the normal environment of the body in which the bacteria live. Teicoplanin works by blocking the formation of these peptidoglycans. By doing this the walls of the bacteria become weak and this results in the death of the bacteria. TeicopIanin is used to treat serious infections of the heart and blood. It is not absorbed from the gut and is therefore only given by injection or infusion. vitro against both aerobic and anaerobic Gram-positive and peptococci. Species usually resistant: Nocardia asteroides, lactobacillus spp., Leuconostoc and all Gram-negative bacteria. Bactericidal synergy has been demonstrated in vitro, in combination with aminoglycosides, against group 0 streptococci and staphylococci. In vitro combinations of Teicoplanin with rifampicin or fluorinated quinolones show primarily additive effects and sometimes synergy. One-step resistance to Teicoplanin could not be obtained in vitro, and multi-step resistance was only reached in vitro after 11 to 14 passages. Teicoplanin does not show cross-resistance with other classes of antibiotics. Following intravenous and intramuscular administration, Teicoplanin is widely distributed in body tissues. It is slowly eliminated with a plasma half-life of 70 to 100 hours; the excretory route is renal. Teicoplanin is not absorbed when administered orally. Teicoplanin does not penetrate through the blood-brain barrier.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Teicoplanin is indicated in potentially serious Gram-positive infections, including those which cannot be treated with other antimicrobial drugs. The effectiveness of Teicoplanin has been documented in the following infections caused by organisms sensitive to Teicoplanin: endocarditis. septicaemia and osteomyelitis, respiratory infections, skin and soft tissue infections, urinary tract infections and peritonitis associated with chronic ambulatory peritoneal dialysis (CAPD).",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T06:46:13.955536+00:00
