PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY46194,Irbesartan Hydrochlorothiazide,Co-Alvoprel,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xTgXLyPzFTHZ0qCawzbgZil1UlLhg16D/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY46194_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xTgXLyPzFTHZ0qCawzbgZil1UlLhg16D_view_usp_drivesdk_9b0886798e.pdf,page_text/DR-XY46194_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xTgXLyPzFTHZ0qCawzbgZil1UlLhg16D_view_usp_drivesdk_9b0886798e.json,2150c272a013c1e57181df57d58441719445ae4125f4e6ef681f907143f7b354,581102,3,digital_text,"Irbesartan + Hydrochlorothiazide (Co-Alvoprel) 150 mg/ 12.5 mg Film coated tablet: Light pink, oblong, biconvex film-coated tablets. Irbesartan + Hydrochlorothiazide (Co-Alvoprel) 300 mg/ 12.5 mg Film-coated tablet: Light pink, oblong, biconvex film-coated tablets.",2,2,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Treatment of essential hypertension. This fixed dose combination is indicated in adult patients whose blood pressure is not adequately controlled on irbesartan or hydrochlorothiazide alone (see Pharmacodynamic properties).,2,2,INDICATION,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T07:33:17.203573+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY46203,Lactulose,Duphalac Mom,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dnM_-z_zEkJTs2dvw0auSOMqQDDm63IE/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY46203_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dnM_-z_zEkJTs2dvw0auSOMqQDDm63IE_view_usp_drivesdk_123cfa5594.pdf,page_text/DR-XY46203_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dnM_-z_zEkJTs2dvw0auSOMqQDDm63IE_view_usp_drivesdk_123cfa5594.json,47e6ea7e62efdbda818ab908f614ea859dd5f1092208172d52c5008c2e9c3646,453432,2,digital_text,"Oral solution flavored with fruit aroma. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM Oral solution. A clear, viscous liquid, colorless to brownish yellow. CLINICAL PARTICULARS What is the medicine used for? • Constipation: regulation of the physiological rhythm of the colon • Where a soft stool is considered of medical benefit (hemorrhoids, post colonic/anal surgery) • Hepatic encephalopathy (HE): treatment and prevention of hepatic coma or precoma (adults) • As a prebiotic, which helps create and maintain a healthy intestinal balance and stimulates the intestinal absorption of minerals like calcium and magnesium (adults) How much and how often should you use this medicine? A single dose of lactulose should be swallowed in one and should not be kept in the mouth for an extended period of time. The posology should be adjusted according to the individual needs of the patient. In case of single daily dose, this should be taken at the same time, e.g., during breakfast. During the therapy with laxatives, it is recommended to drink sufficient amounts of fluids (1.5 – 2 liters, equal to 6-8 glasses) during the day. The lactulose solution may be administered diluted or undiluted. Lactulose (Duphalac ® Mom) in bottles the measuring cup may be used. Dosing in constipation or where a soft stool is considered of medical benefit Lactulose may be given as a single dose or in two divided doses. After a few days the starting dosage may be adjusted to the maintenance dose based upon treatment response. Several days (2-3 days) of treatment may be needed before treatment effect occurs. Starting dose daily Maintenance dose daily Adults and adolescents 15 – 45 ml 15 – 30 ml Dosing in Hepatic Encephalopathy (for adults only) For oral administration: Starting dose: 3 to 4 times daily 20-30 g or 30-45 ml. This dose may be adjusted to the maintenance dose to achieve 2 to 3 soft stools per day. Dosing in Prebiotic Indication (for adults only) Daily dose of 7.5 ml -15 ml lactulose (corresponding to 5g to 10g/day) exerts the prebiotic effects. Pediatric population The safety and efficacy in children (newborn to 18 years of age) have not been established. No data are available. Elderly patients and patients with renal or hepatic insufficiency No special dosage recommendations exist, since systemic exposure to lactulose is negligible. When should you not take this medicine? • Hypersensitivity to the active substance or to any of the ingredients. • Galactosemia • Gastrointestinal obstruction, digestive perforation or risk of digestive perforation When should you consult your doctor? Consultation of a physician is advised in case of: - Painful abdominal symptoms of undetermined cause before the treatment is started - Insufficient therapeutic effect after several days. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine Chronic use of unadjusted doses and misuse can lead to diarrhea and disturbance of the electrolyte balance. The dose normally used in constipation should not pose a problem for diabetics. Pediatric population Use of laxatives in children should be exceptional and under medical supervision. It should be taken into account that the defecation reflex could be disturbed during the treatment. The dose used in the treatment of HE is usually much higher and may need to be taken into consideration for diabetics. This product contains lactose, galactose and fructose from the route of production. Therefore, patients with rare hereditary problems of galactose or fructose intolerance, total lactase deficiency or glucose-galactose malabsorption should not take this medicine. Lactulose should be administered with care to patients who are intolerant to lactose. Lactulose should be administered with care to patients who are intolerant to lactose. (see section ‘List of excipients’). What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this Medicine? No interaction studies have been performed. Pregnancy and lactation Pregnancy No effects during pregnancy are anticipated, since systemic exposure to lactulose is negligible. Lactulose (Duphalac ® Mom) can be used during pregnancy. Lactation No effects on the breastfed newborn/infant are anticipated, since the systemic exposure of the breast-feeding woman to lactulose is negligible. Lactulose (Duphalac ® Mom) can be used during breast-feeding. Fertility No effects are to be expected, since systemic exposure to lactulose is negligible. Effects on ability to drive and use machines Lactulose (Duphalac ® Mom) has no or negligible influence on the ability to drive and use machines. Undesirable effects Summary of the safety profile Flatulence may occur during the first few days of treatment. As a rule, it disappears after a few days. When dosages higher than instructed are used, abdominal pain and diarrhea may occur. In such a case the dosage should be decreased. If high doses (normally only associated with hepatic encephalopathy, HE) are used for an extended period of time, the patient may experience an electrolyte imbalance due to diarrhea. Hypersensitivity reactions mainly limited to the skin have been observed and identified as potential adverse reactions during post- 1137748 pharma code pharma code FRONTBlack 1137748_d1 [Page 2] pharma code pharma code BACKBlack 1137748_d1 1137748 approval use. Because these reactions were reported spontaneously from a population of uncertain size, it is not possible to reliably estimate their frequency.* Tabulated list of adverse reactions The following undesirable effects have been experienced with the below indicated frequencies in lactulose-treated patients in placebo- controlled clinical trials [very common (≥1/10); common (≥1/100, to <1/10); uncommon (≥1/1,000 to <1/100); rare (≥1/10,000 to <1/1,000); very rare (<1/10,000)] or have been reported spontaneously during postapproval use [frequency not known (a precise frequency cannot be estimated from the available data)]. System/ organ class Frequency category Very common Common Uncommon *Frequency not known Immune system dis- orders Hypersensi - tivity Gastrointes - tinal disor- ders Diarrhea Flatulence abdom- inal pain nausea, vomiting Skin and subcutane - ous tissue disorders Rash, pruri- tus, urticaria, erythema Investiga- tions Electrolyte imbalance due to diarrhea Pediatric population The safety profile in children is expected to be similar as in adults. Signs and Symptoms of Overdose If the dose is too high, the following may occur: Symptom: diarrhea and abdominal pain. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? Treatment: cessation of treatment or dose reduction. Extensive fluid loss by diarrhea or vomiting may require correction of electrolyte disturbances.",1,2,Description of the Product,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T07:33:20.036063+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY46204,Ascorbic Acid (As Calcium Ascorbate) + Lemon Bioflavonoids,Nat-C Ester,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1SjR5qPLLcodyo7t_qbXpOWR5bF4tutBt/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY46204_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1SjR5qPLLcodyo7t_qbXpOWR5bF4tutBt_view_usp_drivesdk_5d15155ce7.pdf,page_text/DR-XY46204_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1SjR5qPLLcodyo7t_qbXpOWR5bF4tutBt_view_usp_drivesdk_5d15155ce7.json,a0d299f86bae9310aa5f7672b0f5bdf9f870fc63abf3e5e478c05c5745686290,2310945,1,ocr,"Light brown colour, powder filled in aluminium foil sachet OR-XY46204 WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph This medicine contains Ascorbic Acid & Citrus Bioflavonoid Manufactured by: STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE MEGA LIFESCIENCES Public Company Limited",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T07:33:28.958331+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY46214,Choline Alfoscerate,Glicetile,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vLTMeQnB0bqWWpWmkxgNc_WuNUY3y1TY/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY46214_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vLTMeQnB0bqWWpWmkxgNc_WuNUY3y1TY_view_usp_drivesdk_65113eaf92.pdf,page_text/DR-XY46214_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vLTMeQnB0bqWWpWmkxgNc_WuNUY3y1TY_view_usp_drivesdk_65113eaf92.json,612aae1ababedc341cc3385c0f637e8ca531371e6478d960034697361aa3cebc,590148,1,ocr,"EFFECTS ON ABILITY TO DRIVE AND USE MACHINES Each light yellow-colored, oval, soft capsule is filled with colorless, transparent liquid No data available",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"or to Degenerative brain syndromes psicoorganiche-involutional secondary cerebrovascular insufficiency, or cognitive disorders of the elderly characterized by primary or secondary memory deficits, confusion and disorientation, loss of motivation and initiative from and reduction of attentional capacity. Alterations in the affective sphere and senile behavior: emotional lability, irritability, indifference to its surroundings. Senile pseudodepression",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T07:33:36.048424+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY46226,Pyridoxine Hydrochloride + Folic Acid + Cyanocobalamin,Acumen,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Yw6xSC3_NcSnOpZKZeat23NXVeevc7_A/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY46226_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Yw6xSC3_NcSnOpZKZeat23NXVeevc7_A_view_usp_drivesdk_f68579f40f.pdf,page_text/DR-XY46226_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Yw6xSC3_NcSnOpZKZeat23NXVeevc7_A_view_usp_drivesdk_f68579f40f.json,c6a8ae910a88926cc3531b8f8566d71d24cc1cbb37633f9af6b4a880b978eacf,438732,1,digital_text,"Acumen is a red, capsule-shaped, biconvex, ﬁlm-coated tablet, plain in both sides. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? TM Pyridoxine HCl + Folic Acid + Cyanocobalamin (Acumen ) Film-coated Tablet has Vitamin B6, a nutrient that helps sustain mental performance. Vitamin B6 helps maintain activity, memory, and perception of the environment, particularly in the elderly. Vitamin B6 helps promote mental concentration and stimulate mental capacities. TM Pyridoxine HCl + Folic Acid + Cyanocobalamin (Acumen ) Film-coated Tablet contains Folic Acid, a nutrient that is essential for mental function and performance. Folic Acid helps maintain cognitive function. TM Pyridoxine HCl + Folic Acid + Cyanocobalamin (Acumen ) Film-coated Tablet also contains Vitamin B12, a nutrient that supports cognitive performance. Vitamin B12 helps maintain cognitive performance and perception of the environment in the elderly. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Please see formulation. WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? This drug helps support memory performance and mental vitality. TM Pyridoxine HCl + Folic Acid + Cyanocobalamin (Acumen ) Film-coated Tablet contains high doses of 3 essential B vitamins: B12, B6 and folic acid. (These doses are higher than in many standard vitamin B capsules). Scientiﬁc studies have proven these B vitamins to have the following health beneﬁts:  Help support memory function and mental vitality;  Help maintain memory and cognitive performance;  Help promote concentration and stimulate mental capacity;  Help maintain cognitive function and help with mental aptitude and performance. Vitamin B6 , Folic Acid, and Vitamin B12 also reduce levels of homocysteine, an amino acid which, if present in the body, has been identiﬁed as a risk factor for memory loss and cognitive decline. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Orally, one tablet daily, or as prescribed by the physician. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you are allergic to any component of the product. INSERT VITAMINS Pyridoxine HCl + Folic Acid Cyanocobalamin 20mg / 800 mcg / 500 mcg Film-coated Tablet TM Acumen VITAMINS Manufactured by:",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:TM,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T07:33:38.994065+00:00
