PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY46261,Fimasartan potassium (as trihydrate),Kanarb,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Bhz6vp7SYZ9ZVJ_gwY753AVoKmh53Frq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY46261_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Bhz6vp7SYZ9ZVJ_gwY753AVoKmh53Frq_view_usp_drivesdk_01ffcb430a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY46261_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Bhz6vp7SYZ9ZVJ_gwY753AVoKmh53Frq_view_usp_drivesdk_01ffcb430a.json,599788f56e80b98891b6e281db95a3da5c1e23a878cd38042d8bc1d881ff0918,1319422,1,digital_text,"Fimasartan potassium trihydrate (Kanarb®) 60 mg is a yellow /f_ilm-coated hexagonal tablet, the front side of which is engraved with “FMS6” Fimasartan potassium trihydrate (Kanarb®) 120 mg is an orange /f_ilm-coated hexagonal tablet, the front side of which is engraved with “FMS12”. The back side for /f_imasartan potassium (Kanarb®) tablets (60 and 120 mg) are engraved with “BR” and there is a split line in the middle.",1,1,Product Description,"Fimasartan potassium trihydrate (Kanarb®) /f_ilm-coated tablet is indicated for the treatment of essential hypertension. Recommended Dosage Adult Hypertension The recommended initial dose of /f_imasartan potassium trihydrate (Kanarb ®) /f_ilm-coated tablets is 60 mg once daily with or without food. If blood pressure is not adequately controlled at 60 mg, the dosage of /f_imasartan potassium trihydrate (Kanarb®) /f_ilm-coated tablets may be increased to 120 mg once daily. Whenever possible, it is recommended that /f_imasartan potassium trihydrate (Kanarb®) /f_ilm-coated tablets be taken at the same time during the day (e.g., morning). The blood pressure lowering effect of /f_imasartan potassium trihydrate (Kanarb®) /f_ilm-coated tablets is substantially present within 2 weeks, and maximal reduction is generally attained after 8 to 12 weeks of treatment. Geriatric Use No initial dosage adjustment is required for elderly patients (age ≤ 70 years) Renal Impairment No initial dosage adjustment is required for patients with mild to moderate renal impairment (creatinine clearance 30 - 80 mL/min). For severe renal impairment (creatinine clearance < 30 mL/min), the recommended initial dose is 30 mg once daily and the dose should not exceed 60 mg. Hepatic Impairment No initial dosage adjustment is required for patients with mild hepatic impairment. Fimasartan potassium trihydrate (Kanarb®) /f_ilm-coated tablets is not recommended to patients with moderate to severe hepatic impairment. Pediatric Use The ef/f_icacy and safety of Fimasartan potassium trihydrate (Kanarb®) /f_ilm-coated tablets has not been established in patients18 years or younger. Intravascular Volume-Depleted Patients (e.g., Patients receiving high doses of diuretics) For patients whose intravascular volume is depleted, at risk for symptomatic hypotension, the initial dose of 30 mg once daily is recommended. Mode/Route of Administration To be taken orally",1,1,Indication,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T07:33:59.725415+00:00
