PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY46398,Tofacitinib (as citrate),Xeljanz XR,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Umt3p4SJnpBdpEHdfPUBpLzv5xuQYlmJ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY46398_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Umt3p4SJnpBdpEHdfPUBpLzv5xuQYlmJ_view_usp_drivesdk_7fabb9a41d.pdf,page_text/DR-XY46398_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Umt3p4SJnpBdpEHdfPUBpLzv5xuQYlmJ_view_usp_drivesdk_7fabb9a41d.json,eb60dee3a5c141f32f5422624ea839c1ef2b3ec776871d9e11f9cf92db0571e0,554212,47,digital_text,"Tofacitinib citrate (CP-690,550-10) has a molecular weight of 504.5 Daltons, or 312.4 Daltons, for tofacitinib free base (CP-690,550). The molecular formula of Tofacitinib citrate is C16H20N6O•C6H8O7 and its chemical structure is provided below: NN Me Me N N N H O N HO2C CO2H HO2C OH • Tofacitinib citrate (Xeljanz®) is a white round film-coated tablet with “Pfizer” on one side and “JKI 5” on the other side and is available for oral administration in 5 mg dosage strength. Tofacitinib citrate (Xeljanz® XR) is pink oval tablet with a drilled hole at one end of the tablet band and “JKI 11” printed on one side of the tablet and is available for oral administration in 11 mg dosage strength. Excipients with known effect: Each Tofacitinib citrate (Xeljanz®) 5 mg tablet also contains 62.567 mg lactose monohydrate. Each Tofacitinib citrate (Xeljanz® XR) 11 mg tablet also contains 152.229 mg sorbitol.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Tofacitinib (Xeljanz®/Xeljanz® XR) are indicated for the treatment of adult patients with moderately to severely active rheumatoid arthritis (RA), who have had an inadequate response to one or more disease-modifying anti-rheumatic drugs (DMARDs).",2,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T07:43:23.632258+00:00
