PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY46688,Paracetamol,Pyrex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1kP6tAxCDbWaL0BQRc1nyTw2CsrSiNaWh/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY46688_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kP6tAxCDbWaL0BQRc1nyTw2CsrSiNaWh_view_usp_drivesdk_a7acf9f670.pdf,page_text/DR-XY46688_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kP6tAxCDbWaL0BQRc1nyTw2CsrSiNaWh_view_usp_drivesdk_a7acf9f670.json,cb75c55390529cb5d1ed802c953d23d89b9c01668bdfafb0eea3bdca804c47dd,723900,1,digital_text,"Paracetamol 1 g/100 mL Solution for IV Infusion is a clear, colorless to faint yellow or pale yellow solution with no precipitate.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT :,"Paracetamol is given by intravenous infusion when clinically justified and/or when other route is not possible for the short-term treatment of moderate pain, particularly after surgery, and for short treatment of fever or hyperthermia.",1,1,INDICATION :,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T07:49:40.264104+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY46695,Naproxen Sodium,Flanax,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1z8gqd63aGKBVn9Wemtbns5Ws39L94f7f/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY46695_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1z8gqd63aGKBVn9Wemtbns5Ws39L94f7f_view_usp_drivesdk_f31201598b.pdf,page_text/DR-XY46695_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1z8gqd63aGKBVn9Wemtbns5Ws39L94f7f_view_usp_drivesdk_f31201598b.json,d4191c19283b9e51a0d95706666f2d620ec9f4ad2073026fd2216cd954440209,2499618,1,ocr,"pI can increase the risk of GIT bleeding Naproxen Sodium (Flanax®) is a blue, opaque film-coated, modified oval-shaped tablet. 0. What should you do if you miss a dose? If you skip or miss a dose, take the next dose particularly if there is still pain and inflammation and continue with 2. What is in the Medicine? This product contains Naproxen Sodium which belongs to a group of medicines called non-steroidal your regular dosing schedule of every 8 to 12 hours. Do not take a double dose to make up for a missed one. anti-inflammatory drugs (also known as NSAIDs). Like other NSAIDs, Naproxen Sodium works by changing the 11 Signs and Symptoms of Overdose body's chemical response to pain, swelling and fever resulting in relief of symptoms of inflammation (e.g. Drowsiness, heart bum, indigestion, nausea or vomiting swelling, redness) and relief of pain and/or fever. 3. 12. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? Strength of the Medicine Should a patient ingest more than a large quantity of Naproxen Sodium (Flanax) accidentally or purposefully, One tablet contains 220 mg of the active ingredient, Naproxen sodium (or the sodium salt of naproxen) — made seek medical attention immediately. The stomach may be emptied, and usual supportive measures from a combination of Naproxen 200 mg and 20 mg sodium (of low content, equating to a slice of wheat bread). employed 4. What is this Medicine used for? 13, How should you keep this Medicine? Naproxen sodium (Flanax®) can be used to relieve headache, toothache, muscular ache and backache, pain of Naproxen Sodium (Flanax®) should be kept out of reach of children. menstrual cramps (i.e., period pain), minor pain of arthritis, minor aches and pains associated with the common Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. cold, and fever. Do not use Naproxen Sodium (Flanax®) after the expiry date shown on the carton or blister strip. 5. How much and how often should you use this Medicine? When should you consult your doctor? Each dose should be taken with water on full stomach after eating. Adults: 1 tablet every 12 hours while For further information, consult your doctor or pharmacist who has detailed scientific information. symptoms persist. Elderly (>65): 1 tablet per day and no more than 2 tablets per day. Take Naproxen only if with pain and stop when pain is gone. 15. What are the Do not give this drug to children under 12 years old, except under the advice and supervision of a doctor. Naproxen Sodium (Flanax®) 220 mg Film Coated Tablet - PAPC a Pack x 10's (Box of 100's and 500's) 6. When should you not take this Medicine? 16, Stomach and intestinal pain should not be treated with Naproxen Sodium (Flanax®). ADR Reporting Statement For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. Naproxen Sodium (Flanax®) should not be taken by patients with: a) history of disease of the stomach or of the Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. intestines (ulcer), b) blood coagulation disorders or are receiving drug therapy that interferes with blood coagulation; c) kidney impairment; d) allergy to Naproxen; e) allergy to aspirin or other anti-inflammatory and pain relieving drugs, f) history of Cardiovascular Arrest, Myocardial Infarction, Coronary Artery Bypass Graft, Registration Number",1,1,Description of the Product,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T07:49:51.501303+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY46728,Nicardipine hydrochloride,Nicarpin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lmmWJxvNT0iU5ahrt_-iWf71JWhL241W/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY46728_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1lmmWJxvNT0iU5ahrt_-iWf71JWhL241W_view_usp_drivesdk_b4ee772007.pdf,page_text/DR-XY46728_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1lmmWJxvNT0iU5ahrt_-iWf71JWhL241W_view_usp_drivesdk_b4ee772007.json,f8af42c7690d28b157586a9c460e148588e77c941d99ec6ef89c3769f3962224,265743,2,digital_text,"Nicardipine (Nicarpin®) 1 mg/mL (10 mg/10 mL) is a clear, pale yellow colored solution; supplied in a 10 mL one point cut (OPC), type I brown glass ampoule. PHARMACODYNAMICS Pharmacotherapeutic group: SELECTIVE CALCIUM INHIBITORS WITH V ASCULAR EFFECTS ATC code: C08CA04 (cardiovascular system). Mechanism of action Nicardipine is a second generation slow calcium channel inhibitor, and belongs to the phenyl-dihydropyridine group. Nicardipine has a greater selectivity for L-type calcium channels in vascular smooth muscle than cardiac myocytes. At very low concentrations it inhibits the influx of calcium into the cell. Its action is produced mainly on arterial smooth muscle. This is reflected in relatively large and rapid changes in blood pressure, with minimal inotropic changes in cardiac function (baroreflex effect). Pharmacodynamic effects Administered by systemic route, nicardipine is a potent vasodilator which diminishes total peripheral resistance and lowers blood pressure. Heart rate is temporarily increased; as a result of a decrease in after-load, cardiac output is markedly and durably increased. In humans, the vasodilator action also occurs in both acute and chronic administration in the large and small arteries, increasing blood flow and improving arterial compliance. Renal vascular resistance is decreased. PHARMACOKINETICS Distribution Nicardipine is highly bound to plasma proteins over a wide concentration range. Biotransformation Nicardipine is metabolised by cytochrome P450 3A4. Studies involving either a single dose, or repeated administration 3 times daily for 3 days, have shown that less than 0.03% of unchanged nicardipine is recovered in the urine in humans after oral or intravenous administration. The most abundant metabolite in human urine is the glucuronide of the hydroxy form, which is formed by the oxidative cleaving of the N-methylbenzyl moiety and the oxidation of the pyridine ring. Elimination After co-administration of a radioactive intravenous dose of nicardipine with an oral 30 mg dose given every 8 hours, 49% of the radioactivity was recovered in the urine and 43% in the faeces within 96 hours. None of the products administered was recovered as unchanged nicardipine in the urine. The elimination profile of the medicinal product following an intravenous dose consists of three phases, with corresponding half-lives: alpha 6.4 min, beta 1.5 hours, gamma 7.9 hours. Renal failure The pharmacokinetics of intravenously administered nicardipine was studied in subjects with severe renal failure requiring haemodialysis (creatinine clearance <10 ml/min), mild/moderate renal failure (creatinine clearance 10−50 ml/min) and normal renal function (creatinine clearance >50 ml/min). At steady state, Cmax and AUC were significantly higher and clearance significantly lower in subjects with mild/moderate renal failure compared to subjects with normal renal function. There were no significant differences in the principal pharmacokinetic parameters between severe renal dysfunction and normal renal function.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Intravenous nicardipine (Nicarpin®) is indicated for the treatment of acute life-threatening hypertension, particularly in the event of: • Malignant arterial hypertension/Hypertensive encephalopathy; • Aortic dissection, when short acting beta-blocker therapy is not suitable, or in combination with a beta-blocker when beta-blockade alone is not ef fective; • Severe pre-eclampsia, when other intravenous antihypertensive agents are not recommended or are contra-indicated. Nicardipine is also indicated for the treatment of post-operative hypertension.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T07:49:54.597265+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY46737,Pantoprazole (as sodium sesquihydrate),Panvell,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DlHa4m-1oQG1BHR42FyrPGbhUCLahq9f/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY46737_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1DlHa4m-1oQG1BHR42FyrPGbhUCLahq9f_view_usp_drivesdk_8ba64eaa7a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY46737_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1DlHa4m-1oQG1BHR42FyrPGbhUCLahq9f_view_usp_drivesdk_8ba64eaa7a.json,7b9b86c67d6368310a7133e35ce2df14a9392c4f0fb1ee06bf7d4745bc6d69ef,3213291,2,ocr,"— Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome and other pathological hypersecretory conditions. Pantoprazole Sodium Sesquihydrate (Panvell®) 40 mg Lyophilized Powder for Injection is a hygroscopic, white and clear powder. After reconstitution, the solution is colorless to yellowish. DOSAGE AND ROUTE OF ADMINISTRATION Dosag",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Proton Pump Inhibitor Pantoprazole is indicated for : — Reflux oesophagitis. — Gastric and duodenal ulcer. PRODUCT DESCRIPTION — Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome and other pathological hypersecretory conditions. Pantoprazole Sodium Sesquihydrate (Panvell®) 40 mg Lyophilized Powder for Injection is a hygroscopic, white and clear powder. After reconstitution, the solution is colorless to yellowish.",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T07:50:27.928938+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY46740,Bortezomib,Myborte,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/14_mH-mQcoHhs-lA0B2Ujdv0E5uyWSpNV/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY46740_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14_mH-mQcoHhs-lA0B2Ujdv0E5uyWSpNV_view_usp_drivesdk_cb75c9b2ff.pdf,page_text/DR-XY46740_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14_mH-mQcoHhs-lA0B2Ujdv0E5uyWSpNV_view_usp_drivesdk_cb75c9b2ff.json,418e5ee2bb0de369ac5afb377d9763330b7f6c47f8bfe62a164df15cc61616ab,1598412,2,digital_text,Bortezomib for Injection 3.5 mg is a white to off white cake or powder ﬁlled in 10 mL single-use USP Type-I tubular glass vial stoppered with 13 mm two leg slotted bromobutyl rubber stopper and sealed with 13 mm aluminium ﬂip- off seal. The reconstituted solution is a clear colorless solution free from extraneous visible matter.,1,1,Product Description,"Bortezomib as monotherapy or in combination with pegylated liposomal doxorubicin or dexamethasone is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with progressive multiple myeloma who have received at least 1 prior therapy and who have already undergone or are unsuitable for haematopoietic stem cell transplantation. Bortezomib in combination with melphalan and prednisone is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with previously untreated multiple myeloma who are not eligible for high-dose chemotherapy with haematopoietic stem cell transplantation. Bortezomib in combination with dexamethasone, or with dexamethasone and thalidomide, is indicated for the induction treatment of adult patients with previously untreated multiple myeloma who are eligible for high-dose chemotherapy with haematopoietic stem cell transplantation. Bortezomib in combination with rituximab, cyclophosphamide, doxorubicin and prednisone is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with previously untreated mantle cell lymphoma who are unsuitable for haematopoietic stem cell transplantation.",1,1,Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T07:50:32.212718+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY46743,Zinc,E-Zinc EZTab,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZXiEglLhanBbmnQpkxGuKPgYzndYmFBG/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY46743_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZXiEglLhanBbmnQpkxGuKPgYzndYmFBG_view_usp_drivesdk_80e6b1c0b1.pdf,page_text/DR-XY46743_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZXiEglLhanBbmnQpkxGuKPgYzndYmFBG_view_usp_drivesdk_80e6b1c0b1.json,2e3003837afab435a8aa6a41bf30488ff8e8c4d2690480a932057502f8116dd9,485248,1,digital_text,"White, apple-flavored, round tablet bisected on one side and plain on the other side. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This nutritional supplement contains zinc. Zinc has several known functions/ef- fects: • Zinc is recommended as an adjunct in the management of acute diarrhea together with reduced osmolarity oral rehydration salt (ORS). Zinc given during an episode of acute diarrhea has been shown to reduce the duration and severity of diarrhea and reduces the incidence of future diarrhea episodes in the next 2-3 months. • Zinc is required for the normal development and maintenance of the immune system by helping regulate the activity of cells involved in the immune function. • Zinc is a cofactor for many enzymes involved in cell division and growth. Since zinc stores are low during periods of rapid growth, adequate zinc supplementation is needed for optimum physical growth and development. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Each chewable tablet contains 20 mg of elemental zinc. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? This nutritional supplement is used for the following conditions: • As an adjunct in the management of acute diarrhea • To help boost immune function • To help support optimum physical growth and development HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you are allergic to any ingredient in the product. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS Psychiatric disorders: Drowsiness Nervous system disorders: Headache, metallic taste Gastrointestinal disorders: Abdominal pain/cramps, diarrhea, dyspepsia, gastritis, gastrointestinal discomfort/irritation, nausea, vomiting Metabolism and nutrition disorders: Loss of appetite WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? The following interactions should be considered before giving this medicine. • Bisphosphonates (alendronate, etidronate, risedronate): Concomitant intake of a bisphosphonate and zinc may decrease the absorption of both the bisphosphonate and zinc. • Cholesterol medicines: Additive effects are possible with concomitant administration; use with caution. • Copper or iron: Concomitant administration with zinc inhibits the absorption of copper and iron. Administer zinc and copper or iron as far apart as possible. • Penicillamine: Concomitant administration reduces zinc absorption. • Quinolones: Zinc decreases absorption of quinolone antibiotics (e.g., ciprofloxacin, levofloxacin, ofloxacin). Zinc salts or vitamins containing zinc should be given 2 hours after or 6 hours before antibiotics. • Tetracycline: Concomitant administration results in decreased tetracycline effectiveness. Administer tetracycline at least 2 hours before or 3 hours after zinc. • Food: Concomitant intake of caffeine or tea and zinc reduces zinc absorption. Food containing high amounts of phosphorus, calcium (dairy), or phytates (e.g., bran, brown bread) may also reduce its absorption. Tell the doctor about other medicines the patient is taking, including supplements and herbal products. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If the patient misses a dose, just give the next dose and the subsequent doses at the usual recommended schedule, i.e., once a day. Do not double the dose unless recommended by a doctor. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Keep the product out of sight and reach of children. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSAGE Signs of acute zinc toxicity (doses >200 mg/day) include gastrointestinal pain/cramps, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, loss of appetite, headache, lethargy (sleepiness), muscle pain and fever. Prolonged zinc supplementation may cause impairment of copper and iron status, and anemia at doses >50 mg/day; immune deficiency, reduced blood high-density lipoprotein (HDL) levels, and gastric erosion at doses >150 mg/day. Long term (average 6.3 years) ingestion of supplemental zinc (80 mg/day) has also been linked to a significant increase in hospitalizations for urinary tract infections and kidney stones. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE • Zinc should be used with caution in patients with kidney disease. • Do not take more than the recommended dose. • Do not use after the expiry date on the label. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If any undesirable effect occurs. ADVERSE DRUG REACTION REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adverse drug reaction, seek medical attention immediately and report to the FDA at www.fda.gov.ph AND PHAREX HEALTH CORPORATION at (+632) 7-971-3333 or productsafety@pharexhealth.com.ph. By reporting undesirable effects, you can help provide more information on the safety of this medicine.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T07:50:35.623961+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY46747,Paracetamol + Caffeine,Brainergy,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cmE-8qfXzvETq-pV-vKhH1xbx5y6mCUK/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY46747_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cmE-8qfXzvETq-pV-vKhH1xbx5y6mCUK_view_usp_drivesdk_73fb6584f0.pdf,page_text/DR-XY46747_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cmE-8qfXzvETq-pV-vKhH1xbx5y6mCUK_view_usp_drivesdk_73fb6584f0.json,84a889296beefc4586da27f05c086d6c3b3ceae4f544b1fa8b3143e2b8c20c42,917503,1,digital_text,"Vitamin C 100 mg + Zinc 10 mg per 5 mL (Ceelin® Plus) is a yellow-green, apple-ﬂavored syrup. Vitamin C 40 mg + Zinc 5 mg per mL (Ceelin® Plus) oral drops is a yellow-green to yellow- orange, apple-ﬂavored syrup. These products use the ZincPlus® technology of Pediatech® that ensures a stabilized combination of Vitamin C and Zinc and provides a delicious tasting syrup without the astringent taste of Zinc. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? These nutritional supplements contain vitamin C and zinc. Young children are growing rapidly and their immune system may not yet be fully developed. Hence, supplementation with vitamin C and zinc may be beneﬁcial. Vitamin C and zinc together help the body’s natural defense against damaging free radicals (antioxidant effect) and help boost immune function. Free radicals are highly reactive and unstable chemicals generated during normal body activities that require oxygen (e.g., respiration, digestion, blood circulation, immune system response, etc.) and after exposure to UV light, cigarette smoke and various pollutants. One major effect of zinc is on the ability of cells to properly replicate their DNA, which is required for cells to multiply. Hence, zinc is needed for normal growth of infants and young children, cell renewal and cell repair. 100 mg 27.44 mg Each mL syrup (oral drops) contains: Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C) ………….………..…...…..… Zinc Sulfate Monohydrate………………………….. (equivalent to 5 mg elemental Zinc) 40 mg 13.72 mg STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Vitamin C and zinc have other important functions: Please see formulations. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THE MEDICINE? HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? If the child is allergic to any component of the product. The amounts of nutrients in the product are not expected to interact with food or medicines. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOODS SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THE MEDICINE? If the child misses the dose for the day, just give the next dose and the subsequent doses at the usual recommended schedule, i.e., once a day. Do not double the dose unless recommended by a doctor. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS Vitamin C • Vitamin C is usually well tolerated. However, nausea, vomiting, heartburn, abdominal cramps, fatigue, ﬂushing, insomnia, and sleepiness have been reported with high doses (i.e., 1 g or more daily). Zinc • Gastrointestinal side effects such as nausea and vomiting are seen with doses of elemental zinc greater than 30 mg. WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? These nutritional supplements are used for the prevention and treatment of deﬁciencies of vitamin C and zinc. NUTRIENTS Vitamin C Zinc FUNCTIONS The body’s major water-soluble antioxidant which acts as ﬁrst defense against free radicals in the aqueous (water) phase including blood, plasma and other intracellular and extracellular ﬂuids A cofactor of enzymes involved in the formation of collagen, the most abundant protein essential in the formation of bones, teeth, cartilage and skin. Collagen provides strength and elasticity to the skin and helps promote faster wound healing Forms part of the body’s natural immune system; it stimulates the activity of antibodies and immune cells which inhibit foreign antigens such as bacteria and viruses that are harmful to the body • Cofactor of various enzymes involved in cell division and growth• Required for the normal development and maintenance of the immune system; helps regulate the activity of cells involved in immune function • Functions as an antioxidant by being a cofactor of the enzyme superoxide dismutase which is involved in the removal of harmful free radicals • Essential for skin integrity and wound healing; it promotes tissue repair by stimulating cell division through proper connective tissue formation • • • Age Group Vitamin C + Zinc (Ceelin® Plus) 100 mg/10 mg per 5mL Syrup Orally, once a day. 2.5 mL (1/2 teaspoonful)1-3 years 5 mL (1 teaspoonful)4-8 years 5-10 mL (1 to 2 teaspoonsful) Or, as directed by a doctor. 9-13 years Age Group Vitamin C + Zinc (Ceelin® Plus) 40 mg/5 mg per mL Syrup (Oral Drops) Orally, once a day. 0.5 mLBirth to <6 months 0.5 to 1 mL6-11 months 1 mL Or, as directed by a doctor. 1-2 years HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THE MEDICINE? Vitamin C 100 mg + Zinc 10 mg per 5 mL (Ceelin® Plus) Syrup: Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Vitamin C 40 mg + Zinc 5 mg per mL (Ceelin® Plus) Syrup (oral drops): Store at temperatures not exceeding 25°C. • Keep the product out of reach and sight of children. • Keep container tightly closed. • Do not take more than the recommended dose. • Do not use after the expiry date on the label. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSAGE Vitamin C • Prolonged intake of ascorbic acid (Vitamin C) in excess of 2 g/day may lead to nausea, abdominal cramps, diarrhea, and nose bleeds.Zinc • Rare occurrences of acute zinc poisoning have been reported. The toxicity signs observed after ingestion of high zinc doses (4 to 8 grams elemental zinc) include nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, fever, metallic taste, and lethargy (sleepiness). WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE USED MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If the child has taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor or contact a Poison Center right away. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THE MEDICINE • If any undesirable effect occurs. • If the child is taking other vitamin-mineral supplement. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? DATE 