PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY46860,Multivitamins,Renal Vite Plus,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Yqil1t6eigRDcwWmHawRoZGj6YzOUM5_/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY46860_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Yqil1t6eigRDcwWmHawRoZGj6YzOUM5__view_usp_drivesdk_3b6bae1eb7.pdf,page_text/DR-XY46860_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Yqil1t6eigRDcwWmHawRoZGj6YzOUM5__view_usp_drivesdk_3b6bae1eb7.json,78458384818dc0e7b1e04114f78ce4b9db255013316be27a660ca17827bf775a,75997,1,digital_text,"Renal Vite Plus is a yellowish powder inside a caramel-brown capsule EGC #1, blister pack by I O's box of 30 Capsules. What is in the medicine? Renal Vite Plus contains vitamins which are organic substances required for various metabolic processes. Strength of the medicine: Each capsule contains: Ascorbic acid (Vit. C), USP Niacinamide (Vit. B3) Pyridoxine Hydrochloride (Vit. B6) Calcium Pantothenate (Vit. B5) Thiamine Mononitrate (Vit. Bl) Riboflavin (Vit. B2) Folic Acid (Vit. B9) Cyanocobalamin (Vit. B12) Biotin (Vit. B7) What is this medicine used for? For the treatment and prevention of Vitamin C and B complex deficiency. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Take one (1) capsule daily, or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? If you are allergic to any of the components in the product. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: .................................................................................................. 60mg ....................................................................................................... 20mg .................................................................................. 10mg .......................................................................................5 mg ................................................................................... 3 mg ............................................................................................... 1.70 mg ..................................................................................................................... lm g ...................................................................................... 500 mcg ........................................................................................................ 300 mcg - Doses ofCyanocobalamin greater than 10 mcg may produce hematological response in patients with folate deficiency. - Do not take more that recommended doses. - Do not use after the expiry date stated on the label. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Generally, if taken with recommended dose, this medicine is well tolerated but in some cases the following may be seen: Ascorbic acid is usually well tolerated. Large doses are repo1ted to cause dianhea, hyperoxaluria and other gastrointestinal disturbances. Prolonged or excessive use of chewable vitamin C preparations may cause erosion of tooth enamel. Riboflavin (Vitamin B2) - Large doses may result to bright yellow discoloration in mine. Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12) - Allergic hypersensitivity reactions have occuned rarely that includes rash, itching, anaphylaxis. Niacinamide - It has a vasodilating action that causes flushing, sensation of heat, faintness, pounding in the head. Biotin- nausea, cramping, dianhea What other medicine or food should be avoided? Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C) - Omeprazole Pyiidoxine HCl (Vitamin B6) - Pyridoxine reduces the effects of Levodopa and Altretamine. Vitamin B6 decreases concentration of Phenobarbital and Phenytoin. Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12) - Neomycin, Aminosalicylic Acid, Histamine H2 Antagonist, Omeprazole, Colchicine reduce the absorption of Vitamin B12. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: The following symptoms might be seen in large doses: Pyiidoxine HCl (Vitamin B6) - Long te1m use of large doses is associated with the development of severe peripheral neuropathies. Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12) - gastrointestinal disturbances, fever, chills, hot flushing, dizziness, malaise, acnefonn, emptions, tremor Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C) - Large doses may cause dianhea, abdominal pain and disturbances. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? If any undesirable effect occurs. ""For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: ,vww.fda.gov.ph"". Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration No.: DR-XY46860 Date of Authorization: March 26, 2020 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: April 15, 2020 {i:t�\ £ Manufactured by:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T07:53:04.454000+00:00
