PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY47359,Salbutamol (as sulfate),Salbo,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1l9KeKQS7x4ODq4sf2FXPrkxUJ8rxBrwL/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY47359_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1l9KeKQS7x4ODq4sf2FXPrkxUJ8rxBrwL_view_usp_drivesdk_fe7147eb64.pdf,page_text/DR-XY47359_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1l9KeKQS7x4ODq4sf2FXPrkxUJ8rxBrwL_view_usp_drivesdk_fe7147eb64.json,c998d7d83c9b2d5408f67ccc34125393efc339c80464f84a12ff9b7128391b90,243687,2,digital_text,"Salbutamol (Salbo) 100mcg is a pressurized metered dose inhaler consisting of an aluminum canister with metering valve containing pressurized liquid, fitted over a bluish green color actuator along with a dark bluish green color cap. Upon spraying on black sheet white smear will appear. Each canister contains at least 200 actuations.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Salbutamol (Salbo) inhaler is indicated in adults, adolescents and children aged 4 to 11 years. Salbutamol (Salbo) inhaler provides short-acting (4-6 hours) bronchodilation with fast onset (within 5 minutes) in reversible airways obstruction. It is particularly suitable for the relief and prevention of asthma symptoms. It should be used to relieve symptoms when they occur and to prevent them in those circumstances recognized by the patient to precipitate an asthma attack (e.g., before exercise or unavoidable allergen exposure). Salbutamol (Salbo) inhaler is particularly valuable as relief medication in mild, moderate or severe asthma, provided that reliance on it does not delay the introduction and use of regular inhaled corticosteroid therapy.",1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T08:29:26.438107+00:00
