PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY47366,"""Fluticasone furoate + Umeclidinium (as bromide) +
Vilanterol (as trifenatate)""",Trelegy Ellipta,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Nnw5xDWG5BnNjCRWQofUV_r-piLwBSq4/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY47366_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Nnw5xDWG5BnNjCRWQofUV_r-piLwBSq4_view_usp_drivesdk_fb0ce692a2.pdf,page_text/DR-XY47366_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Nnw5xDWG5BnNjCRWQofUV_r-piLwBSq4_view_usp_drivesdk_fb0ce692a2.json,0ee4241f97ad23399d448c1cf0df4ad10e16718379a77b371b89538da026fd96,1158834,22,digital_text,"Each pre-dispensed dose contains 100 micrograms fluticasone furoate, 62.5 micrograms umeclidinium and 25 micrograms vilanterol. Each single inhalation provides a delivered dose (the dose leaving the mouthpiece of the inhaler) of 92 micrograms fluticasone furoate, 55 micrograms umeclidinium and 22 micrograms vilanterol. The plastic Ellipta inhaler consists of a light grey body, a beige mouthpiece cover and a dose counter, packed into a foil laminate tray containing a desiccant sachet. The tray is sealed with a pee lable foil lid. The inhaler contains 30 regularly dist ributed blisters, each containing a white powder.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Fluticasone furoate + Umeclidinium + Vilanterol (Trelegy Ellipta) is indicated for maintenance treatment to prevent and relieve symptoms associated with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD).,8,8,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T08:30:08.746639+00:00
