PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY47705,Rosuvastatin (As Zinc) + Ezetimibe,Rozuor,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/129pTx9U3sKPaiUy296WxPeyRN2F5jBWg/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY47705_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_129pTx9U3sKPaiUy296WxPeyRN2F5jBWg_view_usp_drivesdk_75105148b2.pdf,page_text/DR-XY47705_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_129pTx9U3sKPaiUy296WxPeyRN2F5jBWg_view_usp_drivesdk_75105148b2.json,b335b4c83f52357757d59c5d95d87d8bd797d8a3ac45edc54111b13e118d844e,6083121,2,ocr,"is adequately controlled with separately administered monocomponent preparations of the Rosuvastatin/ezetimibe (Rozuor®) 10 mg/10 mg hard capsules: Unmarked self-closing Coni same doses as the recommended combination. Snap type, size 0, hard gelatin capsule with yellow colored cap and yellow colored body filled The patient should be on an appropriate lipid-lowering diet and should continue on this diet with two tablets. The length of the capsule is about 21.7 mm (+ 0.5 mm). during treatment with rosuvastatin/ezetimibe (Rozuor®). Rosuvastatin/ezetimibe (Rozuor®) 20 mg/10 mg hard capsules: Unmarked self-closing Coni The recommended daily dose is one capsule of the given strength with or without food. Snap type, size 0, hard gelatin capsule with caramel colored cap and yellow colored body filled with two tablets. The length of the capsule is about 21.7 mm (+ 0.5 mm). Rosuvastatin/ezetimibe (Rozuor®) is not suitable for initial therapy. Treatment initiation or dose adjustment if necessary should only be done with the monocomponents and after setting the",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"10mg/10mg capsule Rosuvastatin/ezetimibe (Rozuor®) is indicated as adjunct to diet for treatment of primary hypercholesterolemia as substitution therapy in adult patients adequately controlled with the 20mg/10mg capsule individual substances given concurrently at the same dose level as in the fixed dose Lipid Modifying Agent Combination combination, but as separate products.",1,1,INDICATION,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T08:46:31.499862+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY47709,Cefoperazone (as sodium) + Sulbactam (as sodium),Fosular,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PEz1QbzUKvQdaZkDlQUoXkIYMWvli4xc/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY47709_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PEz1QbzUKvQdaZkDlQUoXkIYMWvli4xc_view_usp_drivesdk_4736a0a66d.pdf,page_text/DR-XY47709_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PEz1QbzUKvQdaZkDlQUoXkIYMWvli4xc_view_usp_drivesdk_4736a0a66d.json,add54fa0588b4f30e41fd2cdb42b8dba015d9ecf4c6d9501e1012ac4734202ad,646191,2,digital_text,Cefoperazone + Sulbactam (Fosular) 500 mg/500 mg Powder for Injection (IM/IV) is a dry white powder for reconstitution in a 1:1 ratio in terms of Sulbactam/Cefoperazone.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Mono-therapy Sulbactam/cefoperazone is indicated for the treatment of the following infections when caused by susceptible organisms: • Respiratory Tract Infections • Urinary Tract Infections (Upper and Lower) • Intra-abdominal Infections • Septicemia • Meningitis • Skin and Soft Tissue Infections • Bone and Joint Infections • Endometritis • Other Infections of the Genital Tract Concomitant Use: Because of the broad-spectrum of activity of sulbactam/cefoperazone, most infections can be treated adequately with this antibiotic alone. However, sulbactam/cefoperazone may be used concomitantly with other antibiotics if such combinations are indicated. If an aminoglycoside is used (see section Incompatibilities, Aminoglycosides), renal function should be monitored during the course of therapy (see section Dosage and Method of Administration, Use in Renal Dysfunction).",1,1,INDICATION :,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T08:46:35.085906+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY47720,Zinc (as gluconate),None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1I3k5cq2HWBaZCfheTJuZYqknZwi05g3a/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY47720_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1I3k5cq2HWBaZCfheTJuZYqknZwi05g3a_view_usp_drivesdk_d90decc1ab.pdf,page_text/DR-XY47720_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1I3k5cq2HWBaZCfheTJuZYqknZwi05g3a_view_usp_drivesdk_d90decc1ab.json,799eaf2251b4743c41070ed7d259b7e35b917d7b7ac42b7365f6c79927099155,70543,2,digital_text,"Concentrate for solution for infusion. Clear colourless solution. Osmolarity: between 25 and 45 mosmol/l. Osmolality: between 25 and 45 mosmol/kg. Density: 1.006 g/cm3 (at 25°C) pH: between 5.0 and 7.0 4 CLINICAL PARTICULARS 4.1 Therapeutic indications Supplementation solution in prolonged parenteral nutrition and in situations where a pronounced deficiency may occur: e.g. severe malnutrition, hypercatabolism, digestive fistula, chronic diarrhoea. 4.2 Posology and method of administration Posology The dosage must be adapted to each patient, taking into account losses and zinc status. The solution is a supplementation additive for parenteral nutrition intended to be used in mixtures for parenteral nutrition or diluted in isotonic solutions. Recommended basal requirements by intravenous route are the following. Higher doses may be needed to compensate abnormally high losses. Adults: - 2.5 to 5 mg/day Paediatric population: - premature: 0.45 to 0.50 mg/kg/day, - infants younger than 3 months: 0.25 mg/kg/day, - infants older than 3 months: 0.1 mg/kg/day, - children: 0.05 mg/kg/day to a maximum of 5 mg/day. Method of administration Recommended administration: intravenous route after dilution with a slow infusion rate. For instructions on dilution of the medicinal product before administration, see section 6.6.",1,1,3 PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Supplementation solution in prolonged parenteral nutrition and in situations where a pronounced deficiency may occur: e.g. severe malnutrition, hypercatabolism, digestive fistula, chronic diarrhoea.",1,1,4.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T08:46:37.925086+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY47721,Teicoplanin,Vellanin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1YIArB3r77BAHiIEOeKavUTypvpZNkS5p/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY47721_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YIArB3r77BAHiIEOeKavUTypvpZNkS5p_view_usp_drivesdk_7f2c306e90.pdf,page_text/DR-XY47721_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YIArB3r77BAHiIEOeKavUTypvpZNkS5p_view_usp_drivesdk_7f2c306e90.json,1e80e5e7105a73b3508dd24aeb3160f87b6876fb75b7a50d3ecb062ccab306e5,843787,2,digital_text,"Teicoplanin (Vellanin®) 400 mg Powder for Injection is a sterile, yellowish powder for reconstitution with water for injections. On reconstitution gives a clear (colorless to yellowish) solution.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Teicoplanin (Vellanin ®) 400 mg Powder for Injection is indicated in adults and in children from birth for the parenteral treatment of the following infections: • complicated skin and soft tissue infections, • bone and joint infections, • hospital acquired pneumonia, • community acquired pneumonia, • complicated urinary tract infections, • infective endocarditis, • peritonitis associated with continuous ambulatory peritoneal dialysis (CAPD), • bacteraemia that occurs in association with any of the indications listed above. Teicoplanin (Vellanin ®) 400 mg Powder for Injection is also indicated as an alternative oral treatment for Clostridium difficile infection-associated diarrhoea and colitis. Where appropriate, teicoplanin should be administered in combination with other antibacterial agents. Consideration should be given to official guidance on the appropri - ate use of antibacterial agents.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T08:46:41.097504+00:00
