PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY47742,Abemaciclib,Yulareb,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/10DVBo-dyJy9jOy3c4mcSR6s9X6GecTVr/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY47742_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_10DVBo-dyJy9jOy3c4mcSR6s9X6GecTVr_view_usp_drivesdk_cb0263662a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY47742_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_10DVBo-dyJy9jOy3c4mcSR6s9X6GecTVr_view_usp_drivesdk_cb0263662a.json,680bcde0ab919a2aa40d2a9852188ccbfe6576fffd3f707ef94acace4fdb7459,712815,30,digital_text_and_ocr,50 mg Film-coated Tablet Oval beige tablet with “Lilly” debossed on one side and “50” on the other side 100 mg Film-coated Tablet Oval white to practically white tablet with “Lilly” debossed on one side and “100” on the other side 150 mg Film-coated Tablet Oval yellow tablet with “Lilly” debossed on one side and “150” on the other side 200 mg Film-coated Tablet Oval beige tablet with “Lilly” debossed on one side and “200” on the other side,1,1,4. PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"6.1 Early Breast Cancer Abemaciclib (Yulareb®) is indicated: ▪ in combination with endocrine therapy for the adjuvant treatment of adult patients with hormone receptor (HR) -positive, human epidermal growth factor receptor 2 (HER2)-negative, node-positive early breast cancer at high risk of recurrence. In pre- or perimenopausal women, aromatase inhibitor endocrine therapy should be combined with a luteinising hormone-releasing hormone (LHRH) agonist. 6.2 Advanced or Metastatic Breast Cancer Abemaciclib (Yulareb®) is indicated: ▪ in combination with an aromatase inhibitor as initial endocrine-based therapy for the treatment of postmenopausal women, and men, with hormone receptor (HR) - positive, human epidermal growth factor receptor 2 (HER2) -negative advanced or metastatic breast cancer. ▪ in combination with fulvestrant for the treatment of adult patients with hormone receptor (HR)-positive, human epidermal growth factor receptor 2 Abemaciclib [Page 2] USPI Mar 2020, USPI Oct 2021 EMA SmPC 01 Apr 2022 (HER2)-negative advanced or metastatic breast cancer with disease progression following endocrine therapy. ▪ as monotherapy for the treatment of adult patients with HR-positive, HER2- negative advanced or metastatic breast cancer with disease progression following endocrine therapy and prior chemotherapy in the metastatic setting.",1,2,6. INDICATIONS AND USAGE,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T08:47:44.356227+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY47743,Abemaciclib,Yulareb,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1otaTQoZZd8K7vCRaS4Qs1mTcgs0tX6vR/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY47743_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1otaTQoZZd8K7vCRaS4Qs1mTcgs0tX6vR_view_usp_drivesdk_b3af192310.pdf,page_text/DR-XY47743_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1otaTQoZZd8K7vCRaS4Qs1mTcgs0tX6vR_view_usp_drivesdk_b3af192310.json,680bcde0ab919a2aa40d2a9852188ccbfe6576fffd3f707ef94acace4fdb7459,712815,30,digital_text_and_ocr,50 mg Film-coated Tablet Oval beige tablet with “Lilly” debossed on one side and “50” on the other side 100 mg Film-coated Tablet Oval white to practically white tablet with “Lilly” debossed on one side and “100” on the other side 150 mg Film-coated Tablet Oval yellow tablet with “Lilly” debossed on one side and “150” on the other side 200 mg Film-coated Tablet Oval beige tablet with “Lilly” debossed on one side and “200” on the other side,1,1,4. PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"6.1 Early Breast Cancer Abemaciclib (Yulareb®) is indicated: ▪ in combination with endocrine therapy for the adjuvant treatment of adult patients with hormone receptor (HR) -positive, human epidermal growth factor receptor 2 (HER2)-negative, node-positive early breast cancer at high risk of recurrence. In pre- or perimenopausal women, aromatase inhibitor endocrine therapy should be combined with a luteinising hormone-releasing hormone (LHRH) agonist. 6.2 Advanced or Metastatic Breast Cancer Abemaciclib (Yulareb®) is indicated: ▪ in combination with an aromatase inhibitor as initial endocrine-based therapy for the treatment of postmenopausal women, and men, with hormone receptor (HR) - positive, human epidermal growth factor receptor 2 (HER2) -negative advanced or metastatic breast cancer. ▪ in combination with fulvestrant for the treatment of adult patients with hormone receptor (HR)-positive, human epidermal growth factor receptor 2 Abemaciclib [Pag