PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY47758,Tirofiban (as hydrochloride monohydrate),Aggrastat,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUoIm9XSMkrUC8IJnmO3YcjCzKyBoSyZ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY47758_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1BUoIm9XSMkrUC8IJnmO3YcjCzKyBoSyZ_view_usp_drivesdk_e8f21a7945.pdf,page_text/DR-XY47758_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1BUoIm9XSMkrUC8IJnmO3YcjCzKyBoSyZ_view_usp_drivesdk_e8f21a7945.json,d9e9c10112794da26cccf59b6a285a8a63eb9e84de16a0847ba96869e26a5e72,211310,10,digital_text,Tirofiban (Aggrastat) is a clear and colourless concentrate solution for infusion.,1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Tirofiban (Aggrastat) is indicated for the prevention of an imminent myocardial infarction in adult patients with acute coronary syndrome without ST stretch elevation (NSTE -ACS) in whom the last episode of chest pain occurred during the last 12 hours and ECG changes and/or increased myocardial enzymes are present. Tirofiban (Aggrastat) therapy particularly benefits patients who are highly at risk of developing myocardial infarction within the first 3 -4 days after the onset of symptoms of acute angina, including, for example, those patients who are likely to have early percuta neous coronary artery intervention (PCI). Tirofiban (Aggrastat) is also indicated for the reduction of severe cardiovascular events in patients with acute myocardial infarction (STEMI) in whom primary PCI is envisaged (see Posology and Method of Administration and Pharmacodynamic Properties). Tirofiban (Aggrastat) should be used together with acetylsalicylic acid and unfractionated heparin.",1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T08:49:02.949295+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY47770,Macitentan,Opsumit,PI_02,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/18uKQhxju4QMtZfv0sM4HBYEIk22gO5Ca/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY47770_PI_02_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18uKQhxju4QMtZfv0sM4HBYEIk22gO5Ca_view_usp_drivesdk_c73f814a10.pdf,page_text/DR-XY47770_PI_02_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18uKQhxju4QMtZfv0sM4HBYEIk22gO5Ca_view_usp_drivesdk_c73f814a10.json,375a776a832cb5753547e8c7c0afae8626e26171cc9af1da4ae98b871f7a0723,249655,15,digital_text_and_ocr,"Film-coated tablet (tablet). 5.5 mm, round, biconvex, white to off-white film-coated tablets, debossed with “10” on one side. 4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 4.1 Therapeutic indications Macitentan (Opsumit®), as monotherapy or in combination, is indicated for the long-term treatment of pulmonary arterial hypertension (PAH) in adult patients of WHO Functional Class (FC) II to III. Efficacy has been shown in a PAH population including idiopathic and heritable PAH, PAH associated with connective tissue disorders, and PAH associated with corrected simple congenital heart disease (see section 5.1). 4.2 Posology and method of administration Treatment should only be initiated and monitored by a physician experienced in the treatment of PAH. Posology The recommended dose is 10 mg once daily. Special populations Elderly No dose adjustment is required in patients over the age of 65 years (see section 5.2). Macitentan [Page 2] 2 Hepatic impairment Based on pharmacokinetic (PK) data, no dose adjustment is required in patients with mild, moderate or severe hepatic impairment (see sections 4.4 and 5.2). However, there is no clinical experience with the use of macitentan in PAH patients with moderate or severe hepatic impairment. Macitentan (Opsumit®) must not be initiated in patients with severe hepatic impairment, or clinically significant elevated hepatic aminotransferases (greater than 3 times the Upper Limit of Normal (> 3 × ULN); see sections 4.3 and 4.4). Renal impairment Based on PK data, no dose adjustment is required in patients with renal impairment. There is no clinical experience with the use of macitentan in PAH patients with severe renal impairment. The use of macitentan (Opsumit®) is not recommended in patients undergoing dialysis (see sections 4.4 and 5.2). Paediatric population The safety and efficacy of macitentan in children and adolescents below 18 years have not yet been established. No data are available. Method of administration The film-coated tablets are not breakable and are to be swallowed whole, with water. They may be taken with or without food. Macitentan (Opsumit®) should be taken every day at about the same time. If the patient misses a dose of Macitentan (Opsumit®), the patient should be told to take it as soon as possible and then take the next dose at the regularly scheduled time. The patient should be told not to take two doses at the same time if a dose has been missed.",1,2,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Macitentan (Opsumit®), as monotherapy or in combination, is indicated for the long-term treatment of pulmonary arterial hypertension (PAH) in adult patients of WHO Functional Class (FC) II to III. Efficacy has been shown in a PAH population including idiopathic and heritable PAH, PAH associated with connective tissue disorders, and PAH associated with corrected simple congenital heart disease (see section 5.1).",1,1,4.1 Therapeutic indications,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T08:49:08.952954+00:00
