PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY47821,Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12),B 12 Ankermann,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1tolkGxMNtxz6okhV9rWgmxxt-Auo8fAF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY47821_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1tolkGxMNtxz6okhV9rWgmxxt-Auo8fAF_view_usp_drivesdk_62545a8d73.pdf,page_text/DR-XY47821_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1tolkGxMNtxz6okhV9rWgmxxt-Auo8fAF_view_usp_drivesdk_62545a8d73.json,cebb8b4b6f0aec2ae8193ae006d7a79c0ba3dffcc1e868cc0de046515c02131e,1520685,2,digital_text,"Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) film- coated tablets are round, biconvex, white coated tablet. 2. What is in the medicine and strength of the medicine? Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) contains cobalamin in the form of cyanocobalamin (a synthetic form of vitamin B12), which is known as vitamin B12. Each tablet contains: Active substance: Cyanocobalamin ...............................1.00 mg Excipients: Lactose monohydrate..................258.70 mg Povidone K 30..................................10.07 mg Croscarmellose sodium...................2.75 mg Stearic acid.........................................5.00 mg Aquapolish® P white........................14.70 mg Sucrose.............................................58.87 mg Talc.....................................................13.73 mg Kaolin, heavy......................................6.06 mg Calcium carbonate............................8.88 mg Titanium dioxide................................6.06 mg Acacia, dried dispersion...................4.00 mg Macrogol 6000...................................0.40 mg Macrogolglycerol hydroxystearate.................................0.07 mg Sodium laurilsulfate.........................0.06 mg Montan glycol wax.............................0.50 mg Availability: Original packs (blister packs) with 10 coated tablets, 50 coated tablets and 100 coated tablets 3. What is Cyanocobalamin (B12 Anker- mann®) used for? Most people absorb enough vitamin B12 through their diet, but if you have had stomach surgery, suﬀer from certain disorders of the digestive tract or have to follow a strict diet, or if you use certain medicinal products, your body may not absorb enough vitamin B12. Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) is used in adults in the following situations: • In case of haematological and neurolog- ical symptoms of a vitamin B12 deficien- cy, where these cannot be corrected by nutrition alone. • For the treatment of vitamin B12 defi- ciency, which can manifest as haema- topoietic disorders such as pernicious anaemia (idiopathic or following gastrec- tomy); atrophic gastritis, sprue, celiac disease, funicular spinal disease and other symptoms associated with vitamin B12 deficiency, which can arise, for example, due to malabsorption following partial intestinal ventricle resection to treat blind-loop syndrome, and certain rare forms of anaemia in pregnancy. • To support treatment with amino salicylic acid and other pharmaceutical products (e.g. long-term treatments with active substances that inhibit gastric acid production) that can lead to reduced vitamin B12 levels. 4. How much and how often should you use Cyanocobalamin (B12 Anker- mann®)? Always take this medicine exactly as your doctor or pharmacist has told you. Check with your doctor or pharmacist if you are not sure. Individual and Daily Doses Use in adults The recommended daily dose is 1 tablet Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®). This corresponds to 1 mg cyanocobalamin per day. Use in children and adolescents Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) is not suitable for use by children and adolescents under the age of 18. Cyanocobalamin Use in elderly patients The same dose as for other adults applies. If you have kidney problems In patients with moderate kidney problems, Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) can be used in the normal dosage. In cases of severe kidney problems, a dose reduction is recommended. In addition, the amount of vitamin B12 in your blood serum should be checked regularly. If you have liver problems It is not known if you can safely take this medicine if you are having liver problems. Please inform your doctor if you have any liver problems. Method and Length of Administration The coated tablet should be swallowed whole with some fluid, preferably in the morning on an empty stomach. The treatment duration is determined by the therapeutic response. A targeted diagnostics and therapy control should adjust the patient to an optimal dose of cyanocobalamin. Parenteral treatment should be given for haematological and neurological symptoms until blood values have returned to normal. As long as Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) is well tolerated, the duration of use is not limited. Oral vitamin B12 tablets can be substituted for life as long as the cause of the vitamin B12 deficiency persists and sufficient vitamin uptake from intestines is proven. You should contact your doctor regularly to monitor treatment response. 5. When you should not take Cyanocobala- min (B12 Ankermann®)? • If you are allergic to cobalamin or vita- min B12 or any of the other ingredients of this medicine listed in section 2. • If you have a disorder that requires the excretion of cyanide from your body (de- toxification) (in cases of pernicious anae- mia that is associated with, for example, tobacco-related visual impairment (amblyopia) or inflammation of the optic nerve (optic neuritis). In this situation, other vitamin B12 preparations should be used. • If you have vitamin B12 deficiency and suﬀer from a certain hereditary disease of the eye (Leber‘s optic atrophy) 6. Care should be taken when taking Cya- nocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) Warnings and precautions Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before taking Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®). At the beginning of treatment, your clinical condition should be diagnosed by your physician to clarify the underlying reason of the deficiency, including the assessment of your gastrointestinal tract function. Your doctor will decide if vitamin B12 absorption from food is insufficient and if the oral supplementation with Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) is necessary. Due to the serious nature of the disease, your doctor will probably want to monitor your response to this medicine within the first 3 months. This will probably involve examination of your blood. If you adhere well to the treatment plan, the treatment may be lifelong, depending on your underlying disease. If you are in need of periodic renal dialyses, your doctor should perform regular blood examinations and the dosage of Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) may need to be reduced. If you have a folic acid deficiency, this may weaken your response to therapy. Read all of this leaﬂet carefully before you start taking this medicine, because it contains important information for you. - Keep this leaflet, you may need to read it again. - If you have any further questions, ask your treating doctor or pharmacist. - This medicine has been prescribed for you only. Do not pass it on to others. It may harm them, even if their signs of illness are the same as yours. - If you get any side eﬀects, talk to your doctor or pharmacist. This includes any possible side eﬀects not listed in this lea flet. See section 7. 24194 24194 LF_B12_Ankermann_148x420_PH_Artesan_20240807.indd 1LF_B12_Ankermann_148x420_PH_Artesan_20240807.indd 1 07.08.2024 08:02:0707.08.2024 08:02:07 [Page 2] VNr. 02-0824-00 / 602126 / PH 148 x 420 mm / PC 24194 10021277 Wörwag Pharma GmbH & Co. KG Flugfeld-Allee 24, 71034 Böblingen In this case, the use of Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) should be accompanied by folic acid supplementation. Children and adolescents Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) is not suitable for children and adolescent below the age of 18 as there is insufficient clinical data and the dose is unsuitable. Patients with rare hereditary galactose intolerance, lactase deficiency, glucose- galactose malabsorption, rare hereditary fructose intolerance or sucrase-isomaltase deficiency should not take Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®). Pregnancy and breast-feeding If you are pregnant, think you may be pregnant or are planning to have a baby, ask your doctor or pharmacist for advice before taking this medicine. If necessary, the use of Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) during pregnancy may be taken into consideration. Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) can be used during breastfeeding. Driving and using machines Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) is not expected to aﬀect the ability to drive or use machines. 7. Undesirable effects of Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) Like all medicines, this medicine can cause side eﬀects, although not everybody gets them. If the side eﬀects listed below occurs, consult your doctor or pharmacist immediately as you may need medical treatment. In the assessment of side eﬀects the following frequency categories are used: Very common (≥1/10) Common (≥1/100 to <1/10) Uncommon (≥1/1,000 to < 1/100) Rare (≥1/10,000 to <1/1,000) Very rare (<1/10,000) Not known (cannot be estimated from the available data) Uncommon: may affect up to 1 in 100 people - Severe hypersensitivity reactions which can manifest as hives, skin rash or itch- ing of large areas of the body. Not known (frequency cannot be estimated from the available data): - acne like and blister eruptions; - fever. Reporting of side effects If you get any side eﬀects, talk to your doctor or pharmacist. This includes any possible side eﬀects not listed in this leaflet. By reporting side eﬀects, you can help provide more information on the safety of this medicine. 8. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®)? Tell your doctor or pharmacist if you are taking, have recently taken or might take any other medicines, including medicines obtained without a prescription. Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) can be influenced by the following substances: • Proton pump inhibitors (e.g. omeprazole), histamine H2-antagonists (e.g. cimeti- dine), both of which are used to treat excess acid in the stomach that causes digestive disorders or ulcers • Colchicine, an active ingredient used to treat gout • Neomycin and chloramphenicol, which are antibiotics • Biguanides, e.g. metformin, which is used to treat diabetes mellitus • Amino salicylic acid, which is used for the treatment of inflammatory diseases of the digestive tract • Oral contraceptives • Glucocorticoids, e.g. prednisone, which are used to treat inflammation • Prolonged use of nitrous oxide (a gas used during anesthesia) 9. What should you do if you miss a dose? If you forget to take a dose, you should take it as soon as you remember unless it is time to take your next dose. If this happens, do not take the forgotten dose but take your usual dose at the correct time. Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten dose. 10. Signs and Symptoms of Overdose Vitamin B12 has a large therapeutic range. Poisonings or overdose symptoms are not known. Cases of accidental overdose should be treated symptomatically, if necessary. 11. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you take more Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®) than you should, talk to your doctor who will decide about required measures. No case of intoxication has been reported. There is no known antidote for overdose. In the case of overdose, symptomatic treatment should be initiated. 12. How should you keep Cyanocobalamin (B12 Ankermann®)? Keep this medicine out of the sight and reach of children. Do not use this medicine after the expiry date which is stated on the carton and the blister. Do not throw away any medicines via wastewater or household waste. Ask your pharmacist how to throw away medicines you no longer use. These measures will help to protect the environment. Storage Condition: Store below 30 °C 13. When should you consult your doctor? You should always consult your doctor before stopping treatment. If you have any further questions on the use of this medicine, ask your doctor or pharmacist. 14. ADR Reporting Statement For suspected adverse drug reaction, please report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. 15. Marketing Authorization Holder Imported & Distributed by: Metro Drug, Inc. Sta. Rosa Estate, Barangay Macabling, Sta. Rosa, Laguna, Philippines 16. Manufacturer Manufactured by: Artesan Pharma GmbH & Co. KG Wendlandstraße 1, 29439 Lüchow, Germany For: Wörwag Pharma GmbH & Co. KG Flugfeld-Allee 24, 71034 Böblingen, Germany Registration Number: DR-XY47821 Date of First Authorization: 15 March 2022 Date of Revision of Package Insert: June 2024 LF_B12_Ankermann_148x420_PH_Artesan_20240807.indd 2LF_B12_Ankermann_148x420_PH_Artesan_20240807.indd 2 07.08.2024 08:02:0807.08.2024 08:02:08 [Page 3]",1,2,1. Description of the Product,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T08:51:05.835036+00:00
