ubcutaneous Rash’ the incidence of hypoglycaemia was slightly higher than placebo and was not dose-related. Rates of adverse tissue disorders events including dehydration or hypotension were similar to placebo, and there were no clinically meaningful dose-related changes in laboratory parameters, including serum electrolytes and biomarkers of renal Musculoskeletal . function. and connective Back pain tissue disorders a In the event of an overdose, appropriate supportive treatment should be initiated as dictated by the patient's Renal and urinary Nocturia Clinical status. The removal of dapaglifiozin by hemodialysis has not been studied. disorders Polyuria”’ Renal impairment™” Vulvovaginal system and breast pruritus” STORAGE CONDITION: Store at a temperatures not exceeding 30°C. disorders Pruritus genital” Haematocrit DOSAGE FORMS AND PACKAGING AVAILABLE Blood creatinine Dosage Form: Tablet. increased* increased~* Investigations Creatinine renal Blood urea Dapaglifiozin Tablets 5 mg/10 mg: Alu/Alu Blister Pack of 3 x 10's (Box of 30's) Clearance increased” decreased” Weight decreased”",2,2,infections “**,low,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T08:51:42.536043+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY47831,Isavuconazonium Sulfate,Cresemba,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hGcVZnHhvlJuzZX1CeFwd2yAW782Ow3-/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY47831_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hGcVZnHhvlJuzZX1CeFwd2yAW782Ow3-_view_usp_drivesdk_81e5b45b05.pdf,page_text/DR-XY47831_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hGcVZnHhvlJuzZX1CeFwd2yAW782Ow3-_view_usp_drivesdk_81e5b45b05.json,c2d3fd9adfb79a785b0957006cee1e3c9b522d0748b95ecdcb707b2ef1304866,472795,21,digital_text,"Isavuconazonium Sulfate is a white to yellow powder chemically described as [2-[1-[1-[(2R,3R)-3-[4-(4- cyanophenyl)-1,3-thiazol-2-yl]-2-(2,5-difluorophenyl)-2-hydroxybutyl]-1,2,4-triazol-4-ium-4- yl]ethoxycarbonyl-methylamino]pyridin-3-yl]methyl 2-(methylamino)acetate;hydrogen sulfate. Its structural formula is Isavuconazonium Sulfate is the sulfate ester form of isavuconazonium, a prodrug of the triazole antifungal agent isavuconazole, with broad-spectrum antifungal activity. Upon administration, isavuconazonium sulfate is hydrolyzed by plasma esterases to yield the active moiety isavuconazole. Isavuconazole binds to and inhibits the fungal cytochrome P450 family enzyme lanosterol14-alpha- demethylase (CYP51), which catalyzes the demethylation of lanosterol to yield ergosterol, an important component of the fungal cell membrane. Inhibition of CYP51 leads to a decrease in fungal ergosterol production and disrupts synthesis of the fungal cell membrane, which decreases membrane integrity, increases cell membrane permeability and promotes the loss of essential intracellular elements. This results in fungal cell lysis and death.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,Isavuconazonium sulfate (Cresemba) is indicated in adults for the treatment of • invasive aspergillosis • mucormycosis in patients for whom amphotericin B is inappropriate (see sections 4.4 Special,1,1,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T08:51:45.931922+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY47832,Isavuconazonium Sulfate,Cresemba,PI_02,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1D1hXV_MCFVP9JgM7WWXESrnvOeZJEZE9/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY47832_PI_02_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1D1hXV_MCFVP9JgM7WWXESrnvOeZJEZE9_view_usp_drivesdk_59f0f8d3c9.pdf,page_text/DR-XY47832_PI_02_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1D1hXV_MCFVP9JgM7WWXESrnvOeZJEZE9_view_usp_drivesdk_59f0f8d3c9.json,76d337ee7a024e93e107c0efbd002f81dc56305d6dc09ff60b780575aece4e1b,290896,20,digital_text,"Isavuconazonium Sulfate is a white to yellow powder chemically described as [2-[1-[1-[(2R,3R)-3-[4- (4-cyanophenyl)-1,3-thiazol-2-yl]-2-(2,5-difluorophenyl)-2-hydroxybutyl]-1,2,4-triazol-4-ium-4- yl]ethoxycarbonyl-methylamino]pyridin-3-yl]methyl 2-(methylamino)acetate;hydrogen sulfate. Its structural formula is Isavuconazonium Sulfate is the sulfate ester form of isavuconazonium, a prodrug of the triazole antifungal agent isavuconazole, with broad-spectrum antifungal activity. Upon administration, isavuconazonium sulfate is hydrolyzed by plasma esterases to yield the active moiety isavuconazole. Isavuconazole binds to and inhibits the fungal cytochrome P450 family enzyme lanosterol14-alpha- demethylase (CYP51), which catalyzes the demethylation of lanosterol to yield ergosterol, an important component of the fungal cell membrane. Inhibition of CYP51 leads to a decrease in fungal ergosterol production and disrupts synthesis of the fungal cell membrane, which decreases membrane integrity, increases cell membrane permeability and promotes the loss of essential intracellular elements. This results in fungal cell lysis and death.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,Isavuconazonium sulfate (Cresemba) is indicated in adults for the treatment of • invasive aspergillosis • mucormycosis in patients for whom amphotericin B is inappropriate (see sections 4.4 Special,1,1,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T08:51:49.266720+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY47832,Isavuconazonium Sulfate,Cresemba,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RGEU-AiJv2IuCGQLPrdhaoiioSUz1iR0/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY47832_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RGEU-AiJv2IuCGQLPrdhaoiioSUz1iR0_view_usp_drivesdk_fff5cef5d9.pdf,page_text/DR-XY47832_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RGEU-AiJv2IuCGQLPrdhaoiioSUz1iR0_view_usp_drivesdk_fff5cef5d9.json,bc421ebba6d766706f217005dad8eb4f62a10d48aa375d3027bd942cfda557f7,458670,20,digital_text,"Isavuconazonium Sulfate is a white to yellow powder chemically described as [2-[1-[1-[(2R,3R)-3-[4- (4-cyanophenyl)-1,3-thiazol-2-yl]-2-(2,5-difluorophenyl)-2-hydroxybutyl]-1,2,4-triazol-4-ium-4- yl]ethoxycarbonyl-methylamino]pyridin-3-yl]methyl 2-(methylamino)acetate;hydrogen sulfate. Its structural formula is Isavuconazonium Sulfate is the sulfate ester form of isavuconazonium, a prodrug of the triazole antifungal agent isavuconazole, with broad-spectrum antifungal activity. Upon administration, isavuconazonium sulfate is hydrolyzed by plasma esterases to yield the active moiety isavuconazole. Isavuconazole binds to and inhibits the fungal cytochrome P450 family enzyme lanosterol14-alpha- demethylase (CYP51), which catalyzes the demethylation of lanosterol to yield ergosterol, an important component of the fungal cell membrane. Inhibition of CYP51 leads to a decrease in fungal ergosterol production and disrupts synthesis of the fungal cell membrane, which decreases membrane integrity, increases cell membrane permeability and promotes the loss of essential intracellular elements. This results in fungal cell lysis and death.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,Isavuconazonium sulfate (Cresemba) is indicated in adults for the treatment of • invasive aspergillosis • mucormycosis in patients for whom amphotericin B is inappropriate (see sections 4.4 Special,1,1,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T08:51:52.493837+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY47833,Montelukast (as sodium) + Levocetirizine Hydrochloride,Co-Altria,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WqB3GyfGKNyK8bELL88uSDYclM8AdjtT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY47833_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WqB3GyfGKNyK8bELL88uSDYclM8AdjtT_view_usp_drivesdk_0db7cf11cc.pdf,page_text/DR-XY47833_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WqB3GyfGKNyK8bELL88uSDYclM8AdjtT_view_usp_drivesdk_0db7cf11cc.json,bdc381357e9990ad485de3072a3034f625627d28d44761fc2f8d8c2f360b5a66,6545938,2,ocr,"on the activities of CYP isoenzymes 1A2, 2C9, 2C19, 2D6, 2E1 and 3A4 at concentrations well above peak concentrations achieved following a 5 mg oral dose. Due to its low metabolism and absence of metabolic inhibition potential, the interaction of levocetirizine with other substances, or vice-versa, is unlikely. Circular, flat, beveled edge, plain, uncoated bilayered tablets, of which one layer is light yellow to creamish yellow and the other layer is light pink to pink coloured, with slight mottled appearance on both the layers. Elimination",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"The plasma half-life in adults is 7.9 + 1.9 hours. The half-life is shorter in small children. The mean apparent total body clearance in adults is 0.63 mL/min/kg. The major route of excretion of levocetirizine and metabolites is via urine, accounting for a Indicated for the relief of symptoms associated with seasonal and perennial allergic rhinitis. mean of 85.4% of the dose. Excretion via feces accounts for only 12.9% of the dose. Levocetirizine is excreted both by glomerular filtration and active tubular",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T08:52:52.436382+00:00
