PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48029,Loxoprofen (as Sodium dihydrate),Loxotop PAP,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/18-_TSWBi_UrPwbJR98rbIJpTzEdOB_Qq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48029_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18-_TSWBi_UrPwbJR98rbIJpTzEdOB_Qq_view_usp_drivesdk_cb32eb7ad9.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48029_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18-_TSWBi_UrPwbJR98rbIJpTzEdOB_Qq_view_usp_drivesdk_cb32eb7ad9.json,cb9c375aa4485b85c67c81a9e95b815830c28962b8b61a442c35d13b1a4e2762,904083,2,digital_text,"Patch preparation comprising ointment, uniformly spread over a support with the surface of the ointment covered by a liner. The ointment surface is white to light yellow in color. The ointment has a fragrance of mentha oil.",1,1,Product Description,"Loxoprofen ( LOXOTOPTM PAP) is indicated for anti-inﬂammation and analgesia in the following diseases and symptoms: Osteoarthritis, myalgia, posttraumatic swelling and pain.",1,1,1. Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:10:56.560512+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48030,Esflurbiprofen,Locoa,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PtsrVyJ3JzbX28MyzmMtegicg6PF0rly/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48030_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PtsrVyJ3JzbX28MyzmMtegicg6PF0rly_view_usp_drivesdk_82d6748a98.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48030_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PtsrVyJ3JzbX28MyzmMtegicg6PF0rly_view_usp_drivesdk_82d6748a98.json,94ab8081857198f217f1cc23b9536cf39fe04482c9edf1276bc8a251caf7a916,213848,7,digital_text,"Colorless to light yellow plaster patch with a characteristic odor. The plaster, with its top covered by a liner, is spread on a support. 4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 4.1 Therapeutic indications For the relief of pain and inflammation associated with osteoarthritis. 4.2 Posology and method of administration Posology Esflurbiprofen (LOCOA) should be applied to the affected area once daily in adults. Maximum number of patches of Esflurbiprofen (LOCOA) to be used per day is two (2) patches. Esflurbiprofen (LOCOA) is a topical patch with improved transdermal absorption and enhanced penetration into affected tissues; therefore the maximum number which is two (2) patches per day will be sufficient. Moreover, the safety of 2 patches per day has been examined in clinical studies. The use of Esflurbiprofen (LOCOA) with any other anti-inflammatory agent with expected systemic effects should be avoided wherever possible. If such use is deemed necessary, it should be limited to a minimal level and the condition of the patient should be carefully monitored. Elderly Since elderly patients are more susceptible to adverse reactions, their condition should be carefully monitored during treatment. Paediatric population Safety has not been established in low -birth-weight babies, neonates, nursing infants , infants and children. [Clinical studies have only been performed in adults and there is no experience in the use for the above patients.] Method of administration Esflurbiprofen (LOCOA) is applied to the affected area. Esflurbiprofen (LOCOA) cannot be applied to the damaged skin or membrane and to the area of eczema or rash. Careful administration is required with attention to the skin condition of the application site. [Page 2] 2 Esflurbiprofen (LOCOA) should be detached slowly and carefully to prevent any damage to the skin.",1,2,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,For the relief of pain and inflammation associated with osteoarthritis.,1,1,4.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:11:01.261406+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48040,,,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/153v2LeHPz-RdkElXG0W-80vA_2XwK8ah/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48040_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_153v2LeHPz-RdkElXG0W-80vA_2XwK8ah_view_usp_drivesdk_8e410b1d5c.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48040_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_153v2LeHPz-RdkElXG0W-80vA_2XwK8ah_view_usp_drivesdk_8e410b1d5c.json,87d4f59505de76a1bd93c8580deb20605b7d8698ab72fb0df83201765a63485c,193635,10,digital_text,Dexmedetomidine (as hydrochloride) (Icunes) 100 micrograms/mL Concentrate for Solution for Intravenous Infusion is supplied as clear and colorless solution with a pH of 4.5 to 7.0. Dexmedetomidine (as hydrochloride) (Icunes) 100 micrograms/mL is presented in 2 mL vial and must be diluted prior to use.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Intensive Care Unit (ICU) Sedation: For sedation of initially intubated patients during treatment in an intensive care setting. The use of Dexmedetomidine infusion by continuous infusion in these patients should not exceed 24 hours. Procedural Sedation: For sedation of non-intubated patients prior to and/or during surgical and other procedures.,4,4,INDICATION,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:11:05.857666+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48049,Ascorbic Acid + Zinc,Doctri-Cee Plus,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Ofdj4IwQyjBEGE6k-urBI6Gq2u9YQpSN/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48049_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Ofdj4IwQyjBEGE6k-urBI6Gq2u9YQpSN_view_usp_drivesdk_42c3655ac8.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48049_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Ofdj4IwQyjBEGE6k-urBI6Gq2u9YQpSN_view_usp_drivesdk_42c3655ac8.json,6496c6fcf67d29199f1510f8781a35d3c126aec72eb40af91e67414461ebc914,579281,1,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T09:11:09.199300+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48054,Lidocaine Hydrochloride,Lignovell,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XAVfq2lsMH-vwbXk-vwTlo8k0_RStilo/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48054_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1XAVfq2lsMH-vwbXk-vwTlo8k0_RStilo_view_usp_drivesdk_59efbb0133.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48054_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1XAVfq2lsMH-vwbXk-vwTlo8k0_RStilo_view_usp_drivesdk_59efbb0133.json,16daff621160bdd1ad78b87dde8cf1b9cab8773a969c9e83362f12e9d023c308,628366,2,digital_text,Lidocaine Hydrochloride (Lignovell®) Solution for Injection is a clear and colorless sterile injection solution.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Adults (>18 years of age) Lidocaine Solution for Injection is indicated for production of local or regional anesthesia by : • Infiltration techniques including percutaneous injection, • Peripheral nerve block techniques such as brachial plexus and intercostal blocks, and • Central neural techniques including epidural and caudal blocks, when the accepted procedures for these techniques, as described in standard textbooks, are observed. Geriatrics (> 65 years of age) Elderly patients should be given reduced doses commensurate with their age and physical condition. Pediatrics (<18 years of age) Children should be given reduced doses commensurate with their age, weight and physical condition. Lidocaine Solution for Injection should be used with caution in children younger than two years of age as there are insufficient data to support the safety and efficacy of this product in this patient population at this time.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:11:14.415400+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48063,Atorvastatin (as calcium) + Fenofibrate,Fenostat,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Cfe66bfRyPW0UGZDFVsM2DpQ3muBZssu/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48063_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Cfe66bfRyPW0UGZDFVsM2DpQ3muBZssu_view_usp_drivesdk_8cc7da42b4.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48063_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Cfe66bfRyPW0UGZDFVsM2DpQ3muBZssu_view_usp_drivesdk_8cc7da42b4.json,708dde7b0f2f175ab36d2676b7f9f423b9f55c66ce403653373b45d0609416e0,10788910,2,digital_text,"10mg / 160mg - White to off white coloured, circular, biconvex, film coated tablets, plain on both sides. 20mg / 160mg - Light yellow to yellow coloured, circular, biconvex, film coated tablets, plain on both sides. 40mg / 160mg - Light pink to pink coloured, circular, biconvex, film coated tablets, plain on both sides. PHARMACODYNAMICS Atorvastatin Atorvastatin is a selective, competitive inhibitor of HMG-CoA reductase, the rate-limiting enzyme responsible for the conversion of 3-hydroxy-3-methyl-glutaryl-coenzyme A to mevalonate, a precursor of sterols, including cholesterol. Triglycerides and cholesterol in the liver are incorporated into very low-density lipoproteins (VLDL) and released into the plasma for delivery to peripheral tissues. Low-density lipoprotein (LDL) is formed from VLDL and is catabolised primarily through the receptor with high affinity to LDL (LDL receptor). Atorvastatin lowers plasma cholesterol and lipoprotein serum concentrations by inhibiting HMG-CoA reductase and subsequently cholesterol biosynthesis in the liver and increases the number of hepatic LDL receptors on the cell surface for enhanced uptake and catabolism of LDL. Atorvastatin reduces LDL production and the number of LDL particles. Atorvastatin produces a profound and sustained increase in LDL receptor activity coupled with a beneficial change in the quality of circulating LDL particles. Atorvastatin is effective in reducing LDL-C in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia, a population that has not usually responded to lipid-lowering medicinal products. Reductions in total-C, LDL-C, and apolipoprotein B have been proven to reduce risk for cardiovascular events and cardiovascular mortality. Fenofibrate Fenofibrate is a fibric acid derivative whose lipid modifying effects reported in humans are mediated via activation of Peroxisome Proliferator Activated Receptor type alpha",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Mixed Dyslipidemia Fenostat is indicated as an adjunct to diet to reduce elevated total-C, LDL-C, apoB, and TG levels and to increase HDLC in adult patients with mixed dyslipidemia. Hypercholesterolemia Fenostat is indicated as an adjunct to diet to reduce elevated total-C, LDL-C, apoB and to increase HDL-C in adult patients with primary hypercholesterolemia. Lipid altering agents should be used in addition to diet restricted in saturated fat and cholesterol only when the response to diet and other non-pharmacological measures has been inadequate. NCEP Guidelines for Lipid Management *CHD = coronary heart disease **Almost all people with 0-1 risk factor have 10-year risk < 10%; thus, 10-year risk assessment in people with 0-1 risk factor is not necessary. After the LDL-C goal has been achieved, if the TG level is still ≥ 200 mg/dL, non-HDL-C (TC minus HDL-C) becomes a secondary target of therapy. Non-HDL-C goals are set 30 mg/dL higher than LDL-C goals for each risk category.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:11:23.209276+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48064,Atorvastatin (as calcium) + Fenofibrate,Fenostat,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gXaYEEKmxNBU9SH9-tgC5EC61PknB4aB/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48064_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gXaYEEKmxNBU9SH9-tgC5EC61PknB4aB_view_usp_drivesdk_c210677c12.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48064_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gXaYEEKmxNBU9SH9-tgC5EC61PknB4aB_view_usp_drivesdk_c210677c12.json,f3c30a8bf61b4c1f061ffc0835d873e844b12597c69b63c3137ab7a37e179f97,10788910,2,digital_text,"10mg / 160mg - White to off white coloured, circular, biconvex, film coated tablets, plain on both sides. 20mg / 160mg - Light yellow to yellow coloured, circular, biconvex, film coated tablets, plain on both sides. 40mg / 160mg - Light pink to pink coloured, circular, biconvex, film coated tablets, plain on both sides. PHARMACODYNAMICS Atorvastatin Atorvastatin is a selective, competitive inhibitor of HMG-CoA reductase, the rate-limiting enzyme responsible for the conversion of 3-hydroxy-3-methyl-glutaryl-coenzyme A to mevalonate, a precursor of sterols, including cholesterol. Triglycerides and cholesterol in the liver are incorporated into very low-density lipoproteins (VLDL) and released into the plasma for delivery to peripheral tissues. Low-density lipoprotein (LDL) is formed from VLDL and is catabolised primarily through the receptor with high affinity to LDL (LDL receptor). Atorvastatin lowers plasma cholesterol and lipoprotein serum concentrations by inhibiting HMG-CoA reductase and subsequently cholesterol biosynthesis in the liver and increases the number of hepatic LDL receptors on the cell surface for enhanced uptake and catabolism of LDL. Atorvastatin reduces LDL production and the number of LDL particles. Atorvastatin produces a profound and sustained increase in LDL receptor activity coupled with a beneficial change in the quality of circulating LDL particles. Atorvastatin is effective in reducing LDL-C in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia, a population that has not usually responded to lipid-lowering medicinal products. Reductions in total-C, LDL-C, and apolipoprotein B have been proven to reduce risk for cardiovascular events and cardiovascular mortality. Fenofibrate Fenofibrate is a fibric acid derivative whose lipid modifying effects reported in humans are mediated via activation of Peroxisome Proliferator Activated Receptor type alpha",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Mixed Dyslipidemia Fenostat is indicated as an adjunct to diet to reduce elevated total-C, LDL-C, apoB, and TG levels and to increase HDLC in adult patients with mixed dyslipidemia. Hypercholesterolemia Fenostat is indicated as an adjunct to diet to reduce elevated total-C, LDL-C, apoB and to increase HDL-C in adult patients with primary hypercholesterolemia. Lipid altering agents should be used in addition to diet restricted in saturated fat and cholesterol only when the response to diet and other non-pharmacological measures has been inadequate. NCEP Guidelines for Lipid Management *CHD = coronary heart disease **Almost all people with 0-1 risk factor have 10-year risk < 10%; thus, 10-year risk assessment in people with 0-1 risk factor is not necessary. After the LDL-C goal has been achieved, if the TG level is still ≥ 200 mg/dL, non-HDL-C (TC minus HDL-C) becomes a secondary target of therapy. Non-HDL-C goals are set 30 mg/dL higher than LDL-C goals for each risk category.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:11:31.752216+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48074,,,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ft3lqWR3bRPx7f8qptdrxhE14EnKu5JC/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48074_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ft3lqWR3bRPx7f8qptdrxhE14EnKu5JC_view_usp_drivesdk_58986f7688.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48074_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ft3lqWR3bRPx7f8qptdrxhE14EnKu5JC_view_usp_drivesdk_58986f7688.json,6a2eabee6aa014345055c229d431d45cc1a9fa269a429a63e0f943be4a72d2bb,108962,6,digital_text,"Brimonidine tartrate (ALPHAGAN®P) 0.1% ophthalmic solution is a relatively selective alpha-2 adrenergic agonist for ophthalmic use. The chemical name of brimonidine tartrate is 5-bromo-6-(2- imidazolidinylideneamino) quinoxaline L-tartrate. It has a molecular weight of 442.24 as the tartrate salt. The structural formula is: Formula: C11H10BrN5 • C4H6O6 CAS Number: 70359-46-5 In solution, brimonidine tartrate (ALPHAGAN®P) 0.1% ophthalmic solution has a clear, greenish- yellow color. It has an osmolality of 250-350 mOsmol/kg and a pH of 7.4-8.0. Each mL of brimonidine tartrate (ALPHAGAN®P) 0.1% ophthalmic solution contains: Active Ingredient: brimonidine tartrate 0.1% (1 mg/mL) Preservative: PURITE® 0.005% (0.05 mg/mL) CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY Mechanism of Action: Brimonidine tartrate (ALPHAGAN®P) 0.1% ophthalmic solution is an alpha-adrenergic receptor agonist. It has a peak ocular hypotensive effect occurring at two hours post-dosing. Fluorophotometric studies in animals and humans suggest that brimonidine tartrate has a dual mechanism of action by reducing aqueous humor production and increasing uveoscleral outflow. Brimonidine tartrate [Page 2] Pharmacokinetics: After ocular administration of either a 0.1% or 0.2% solution, plasma concentrations peaked within 0.5 to 2.5 hours and declined with a systemic half-life of approximately 2 hours. In humans, systemic metabolism of brimonidine is extensive. It is metabolized primarily by the liver. Urinary excretion is the major route of elimination of the drug and its metabolites. Approximately 87% of an orally administered radioactive dose was eliminated within 120 hours, with 74% found in the urine. Clinical Evaluation: Elevated IOP presents a major risk factor in glaucomatous field loss. The higher the level of IOP, the greater the likelihood of optic nerve damage and visual field loss. Brimonidine tartrate has the action of lowering intraocular pressure with minimal effect on cardiovascular and pulmonary parameters. A 3-month (with a double-masked extension to 1 year) clinical study (N=433) was conducted to evaluate the safety, efficacy, and acceptability of brimonidine tartrate (ALPHAGAN P ®) 0.1% ophthalmic solution compared with brimonidine tartrate (ALPHAGAN P®) 0.2% ophthalmic solution administered 3 times daily in patients with glaucoma or ocular hypertension. A 3-month analysis of the pivotal study indicated brimonidine tartrate (ALPHAGAN P ®) 0.1% ophthalmic solution is equivalent in IOP-lowering effect to brimonidine tartrate (ALPHAGAN P®) 0.2% ophthalmic solution and effectively lowers IOP in patients with glaucoma or ocular hypertension (mean change from baseline IOP -3.3 to -5.4mmHg). Additionally, 12-month analysis of the pivotal study indicated brimonidine tartrate (ALPHAGAN P®) 0.1% ophthalmic solution continued to be equivalent to brimonidine tartrate (ALPHAGAN P®) 0.2% ophthalmic solution and effectively lowered IOP in patients with glaucoma or ocular hypertension (mean change from baseline IOP at hours 0, 2, and 8 ranged from -2.7 to -5.4 mmHg). Brimonidine tartrate (ALPHAGAN P®) 0.1% ophthalmic solution is well-tolerated and provides a superior safety profile when compared with brimonidine tartrate (ALPHAGAN P ®) 0.1% ophthalmic solution. Brimonidine tartrate (ALPHAGAN P ®) 0.1% ophthalmic solution is the lowest effective dose of brimonidine tartrate that combines the IOP lowering efficacy with the most favorable safety and tolerability profile.",1,2,DESCRIPTION,Brimonidine tartrate (ALPHAGAN®P) 0.1% ophthalmic solution is indicated for the lowering of intraocular pressure in patients with open-angle glaucoma or ocular hypertension.,2,2,INDICATIONS AND USAGE,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:11:35.579901+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48077,Dexketoprofen (as trometamol),Voxib,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yVppQ_Albi4OiAt5x3RxBaoJkXFvLSSS/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48077_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1yVppQ_Albi4OiAt5x3RxBaoJkXFvLSSS_view_usp_drivesdk_16bfb96f34.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48077_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1yVppQ_Albi4OiAt5x3RxBaoJkXFvLSSS_view_usp_drivesdk_16bfb96f34.json,2d0a166586ee313c8bbeb37fa7c0fac37f7c4bd2504a163ae9886714cccd458b,503742,2,digital_text,Voxib (dexketoprofen) 25 mg/mL Solution for Injection (I.M./I.V.) or Concentrate for Solution for I.V. Infusion is supplied as clear and colorless solution with a pH of 6.5 to 8.5.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Symptomatic treatment of acute pain of moderate to severe intensity, when oral administration is not appropriate such as post-operative pain, renal colic and low back pain.",1,1,INDICATIONS :,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:11:39.536634+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48078,Azacitidine,Azacytin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XnkzUt9DogFEiypVyzZEjaljS9qeu5mh/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48078_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1XnkzUt9DogFEiypVyzZEjaljS9qeu5mh_view_usp_drivesdk_2b6502ef3e.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48078_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1XnkzUt9DogFEiypVyzZEjaljS9qeu5mh_view_usp_drivesdk_2b6502ef3e.json,b267b640005ef953ee745637defb7b1c0d220058fd4da516bd726058960456d9,1626825,2,digital_text,White to off white lyophilized powder for reconstitution. The reconstituted solution is a colorless solution free from visible extraneous matter.,1,1,Product description:,"Azacitidine is indicated for the treatment of adult patients who are not eligible for haematopoietic stem cell transplantation (HSCT) with: · intermediate-2 and high-risk myelodysplastic syndromes (MDS) according to the International Prognostic Scoring System (IPSS), · chronic myelomonocytic leukaemia (CMML) with 10-29 % marrow blasts without myeloproliferative disorder, · acute myeloid leukaemia (AML) with 20-30 % blasts and multi-lineage dysplasia, according to World Health Organisation (WHO) classification, · AML with >30% marrow blasts according to the WHO classification.",1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:11:46.025681+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48085,Bilastine,Bilaxten,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wkYyBk5yG03jqOmJj3-x5n84ETiFi6-j/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48085_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wkYyBk5yG03jqOmJj3-x5n84ETiFi6-j_view_usp_drivesdk_06d658d703.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48085_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wkYyBk5yG03jqOmJj3-x5n84ETiFi6-j_view_usp_drivesdk_06d658d703.json,bf18a4b96db4d6cf93a518ba5a99adf03a538b730a8ee8ea6fba8a462f172704,190469,8,digital_text,"Somnolence, headache, dizziness and fatigue were observed either in patients treated with bilastine 20 mg or with placebo. The frequency reported was 3.06% vs 2.86% for somnolence; 4.01% vs. 3.38% for headache; 0.83% vs. 0.59% for dizziness, and 0.83% vs. 1.32% for fatigue. The information collected during the post-marketing surveillance has confirmed the safety profile observed during the clinical development. Reporting of suspected adverse reactions Reporting suspected adverse reactions after authorization of the medicinal products is important. It allows continued monitoring of the benefit/risk balance of the medicinal product. For suspected adverse drug reactions, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph Please seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. OVERDOSE There are no data for overdose in children. Information regarding acute overdose of bilastine is retrieved from the experience of clinical trials conducted during the development in adults and the post-marketing surveillance. I n clinical trials, after admi nistration of bilastine at doses 10 to 11 times the therapeutic dose (220 mg as single dose or 200 mg/day for 7 days) to 26 adult healthy volunteers, frequency of treatment emergent adverse events was two times hi gher than with placebo. The adverse reactions mos t frequently reported were di zziness, headache and nausea. No serious adverse events and no significant prolongation in the QTc interval were reported. The information collected in the post-marketing surveillance is consistent wit h that reported in clinical trials. Critical evaluation of bilastine’s multiple dose (100 mg x4 day s) effect on ventricular repolarization by a “thorough QT/QTc c ross-over study” involving 30 healthy adult volunteers did not show significant QTc prolongation. In the event of overdose symptomatic and supportive treatment is recommended. There is no known specific antidote to bilastine.",6,6,Description of selected adverse reactions in adult and adolescent patients,Symptomatic treatment of allergic rhino-conjunctivitis (seasonal and perennial) and urticaria. Bilastine (Bilaxten) is indicated in children aged 6 to 11 years with a body weight of at least 20 kg.,1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:11:50.135735+00:00
