PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48145,Ritonavir,Tonavir,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JRYBupEyVlH6JWkm7pzIuZuG1ualUta6/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48145_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1JRYBupEyVlH6JWkm7pzIuZuG1ualUta6_view_usp_drivesdk_d3b16b6cfe.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48145_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1JRYBupEyVlH6JWkm7pzIuZuG1ualUta6_view_usp_drivesdk_d3b16b6cfe.json,11f88013edbd0776a352f9628578aebd2ccf7a115d06eb40476b938e2ede210f,2524881,2,digital_text,For older children it may be feasible to substitute tablets for the maintenance dose of the oral solution. Dosage conversion from oral solution to tablets for children Ritonavir is not recommended in children below 2 years of age due to lack of data on safety and efficacy. Special populations Elderly Pharmacokinetic data indicated that no dose adjustment is necessary for elderly patients (see,1,1,Product Characteristics).,Ritonavir is indicated in combination with other antiretroviral agents for the treatment of HIV-1 infected patients (adults and children of 2 years of age and older).,1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:13:19.060248+00:00
