PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48184,Trifarotene,Aklief,PI_02,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CNWatyZVwmfAepKceiYRPY2YHOpblroI/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48184_PI_02_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1CNWatyZVwmfAepKceiYRPY2YHOpblroI_view_usp_drivesdk_b5ffd5df0a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48184_PI_02_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1CNWatyZVwmfAepKceiYRPY2YHOpblroI_view_usp_drivesdk_b5ffd5df0a.json,687259b1170f0491511c9dedc6d558dcd4cf57b3ad9b6dd7d3afff11037fa25a,666519,1,digital_text,"White and homogeneous preparation • One pump actuation should be enough to cover the face (i.e., forehead, cheeks, nose, and chin). • Two actuations of the pump should be enough to cover the upper trunk (i.e., reachable upper back, shoulders and chest). One additional pump actuation may be used for middle and lower back if acne is present.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Trifarotene (Aklief) Cream is a retinoid indicated for the topical treatment of Acne Vulgaris in patients 9 years of age and older. Trifarotene (Aklief) is indicated for the cutaneous treatment of Acne Vulgaris of the face and/or the trunk in patients from 12 years of age and older, when many comedones, papules, and pustules are present. Pharmacological Properties Mechanism of Action Trifarotene is an agonist of retinoic acid receptors (RAR), with particular activity at the gamma subtype of RAR. Stimulation of RAR results in modulation of targets genes which are associated with various processes, including cell differentiation and mediation of in ammation. The exact process by which trifarotene ameliorates acne is unknown.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:14:45.976343+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48184,Trifarotene,Aklief,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RV8yLzc7S-HGTLV3MUpZUX23mGv3ewu1/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48184_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RV8yLzc7S-HGTLV3MUpZUX23mGv3ewu1_view_usp_drivesdk_bee0af8224.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48184_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RV8yLzc7S-HGTLV3MUpZUX23mGv3ewu1_view_usp_drivesdk_bee0af8224.json,1c778d34b85895d9bf385675830ecb74c6abb74ab07be80cc0de8a44c37618ff,2203256,1,digital_text,White and homogeneous preparation,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Trifarotene (Aklief) Cream is a retinoid indicated for the topical treatment of Acne Vulgaris in patients 9 years of age and older. Trifarotene (Aklief) is indicated for the cutaneous treatment of Acne Vulgaris of the face and/or the trunk in patients from 12 years of age and older, when many comedones, papules, and pustules are present. Pharmacological Properties Mechanism of Action Trifarotene is an agonist of retinoic acid receptors (RAR), with particular activity at the gamma subtype of RAR. Stimulation of RAR results in modulation of target genes which are associated with various processes, including cell differentiation and mediation of inﬂammation. The exact process by which trifarotene ameliorates acne is unknown.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:14:51.554086+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48185,Anagrelide (as hydrochloride),Anator,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VWQ9Xuoclepl-YwoUbI7LS8wpu7vVrqm/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48185_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VWQ9Xuoclepl-YwoUbI7LS8wpu7vVrqm_view_usp_drivesdk_dd276666e6.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48185_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VWQ9Xuoclepl-YwoUbI7LS8wpu7vVrqm_view_usp_drivesdk_dd276666e6.json,9877b79192c9811ee119d3b7ffacf3aea6271661ed27f44060210796d64511a5,373689,1,digital_text,"Anagrelide (Anator) 500mcg Capsule is a size ‘4’ hard gelatin capsule having gray opaque cap and white opaque body, imprinted ‘1453’ on cap and ‘0.5mg’ on body with black ink containing white to off-white powder.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Anagrelide Capsules 0.5 mg is indicated for the reduction of elevated platelet counts in at risk essential thrombocythemia (ET) patients who are intolerant to their current therapy or whose elevated platelet counts are not reduced to an acceptable level by their current therapy. An at risk essential thrombocythemia patient is defined by one or more of the following features: • > 60 years of age or • a platelet count > 1000 X 109/1 or • a history of thrombo-haemorrhagic events. Or as prescribed by the physician.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:14:54.619787+00:00
