PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48220,Budesonide + Formoterol Fumarate Dihydrate,Fortra,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1AyQRIpYGfdgYpRsvVVI0YuCnDy02gTTB/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48220_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1AyQRIpYGfdgYpRsvVVI0YuCnDy02gTTB_view_usp_drivesdk_9b75a9ec6b.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48220_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1AyQRIpYGfdgYpRsvVVI0YuCnDy02gTTB_view_usp_drivesdk_9b75a9ec6b.json,6639064ef1cdbeed339ab9de5f34547b7fef13b2a4649f6a49ff9276263e2c98,59430,2,digital_text,Budesonide + Formoterol fumarate dihydrate (Fortra) 200mcg/ 6mcg is a metered dose pressurized inhalation suspension consisting of an Aluminum canister fitted over a red color actuator along with a light brown color cap. The inhaler also contains the CFC-free propellant HFA 134a. Upon spraying on black sheet white smear will appear. Each canister contains at least 120 actuations.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Budesonide + Formoterol fumarate dihydrate (Fortra) is indicated for: Treatment of Asthma Budesonide + Formoterol fumarate dihydrate (Fortra) is indicated for the treatment of asthma in patients 12 years of age and older. Maintenance Treatment of Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) Budesonide + Formoterol fumarate dihydrate (Fortra) is indicated for the twice daily maintenance treatment of airflow obstruction in patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) including chronic bronchitis and emphysema.,1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:24:15.393988+00:00
