he first 3 months of pregnancy. Do not use Cetirizine Hydrochloride (Simtec) if you are breastfeeding. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE Do not use Cetirizine Hydrochloride (Simtec) in children less than 3 years Storage: Store Cetirizine Hydrochloride (Simtec) tablets at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from light and excessive moisture. old. Do not take this medicine after the expiry date printed on the pack or if the packaging is torn or shows signs of tampering. If you are not sure Shelf Life: 3 years WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR whether you should start taking Cetirizine Hydrochloride (Simtec), talk to your doctor or pharmacist. If unusual symptoms or allergy occur, the product should be stopped and a healthcare professional consulted. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE NAME AND ADDRESS OF MARKETING AUTHORIZATION HOLDER You should only take the dose of Cetirizine Hydrochloride (Simtec) that is DB (Philippines), Inc. directed by the doctor or pharmacist. Company Registeration No: CS200719600 Tell your doctor if, for any reason, you have not taken your medicine Unit 2802, Level 28, Atlanta Centre 31 Annapolis Street Greenhills, San exactly as directed. Juan City, 1502 Metro Manila, Philippines Tell any other doctors, dentists and pharmacists who are treating you that NAME AND ADDRESS OF MANUFACTURER you are taking Cetirizine Hydrochloride (Simtec). Duopharma Manufacturing (Bangi) Sdn Bhd. If you are about to be started on any new medicines, tell your doctor, Lot No. 2 & 4, Jalan P/7, Section 13, Bangi Industrial Estate, 43650 Bandar Baru Bangi, Selangor, Malaysia. dentist or pharmacist that you are taking Cetirizine Hydrochloride (Simtec). REGISTRATION NUMBER DR-XY48304 If you plan to have surgery that needs a general anaesthetic, tell your doctor or dentist that you are taking Cetirizine Hydrochloride (Simtec). DATE OF FIRST AUTHORIZATION Somnolence effects (drowsiness) has been reported in some patients 19 August 2022 taking Cetir