PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48365,Tolvaptan,Jinarc,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wiAQpf5nhKtog6KeKGcG8YsF6euOfTL0/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48365_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wiAQpf5nhKtog6KeKGcG8YsF6euOfTL0_view_usp_drivesdk_705a450539.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48365_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wiAQpf5nhKtog6KeKGcG8YsF6euOfTL0_view_usp_drivesdk_705a450539.json,a23ce741165221e4ccb64f77729febe779a6f5d44fb0059b466b14eda3903d73,234028,14,digital_text,"Tolvaptan (Jinarc®) 15 mg tablets Blue, triangular (major axis: 6.58 mm, minor axis: 6.20 mm), shallow-convex, debossed with “OTSUKA” and “15” on one side. Tolvaptan (Jinarc®) 30 mg tablets Blue, round (diameter: 8 mm), shallow-convex, debossed with “OTSUKA” and “30” on one side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Tolvaptan (Jinarc ®) is indicated to slow the progression of cyst development and renal insufficiency of autosomal dominant polycystic kidney disease (ADPKD) in adults with chronic kidney disease (CKD) stage 1 to 4 at initiation of treatment with evidence of rapidly progressing disease (see Pharmacodynamics) .,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:28:56.967427+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48371,Nilotinib (as hydrochloride dihydrate),Nicmel 200,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Rd0mtE4nO1jMYUZhMRjUK6-k6O9DfeMF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48371_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Rd0mtE4nO1jMYUZhMRjUK6-k6O9DfeMF_view_usp_drivesdk_b3b638fc94.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48371_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Rd0mtE4nO1jMYUZhMRjUK6-k6O9DfeMF_view_usp_drivesdk_b3b638fc94.json,f30b32680310fc00887c72ed782e60d461fb4f1930e66ae0d932ff7830582e52,1506537,2,digital_text,"8.8 Renal Impairment 7.2 Drugs that Inhibit or Induce Cytochrome P450 3A4 Enzymes 7.5 Drugs that May Prolong the QT Interval 8.3 Nursing Mothers 8.4 Pediatric Use 12 CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY 7 DRUG INTERACTIONS 8 USE IN SPECIFIC POPULATIONS 7.1 Eﬀects of Nilotinib on Drug Metabolizing Enzymes and Drug Transport Systems Newly Diagnosed Ph+ CML-CP 2. DOSAGE AND ADMINISTRATION 1.2 Resistant or Intolerant Ph+ CML-CP and CML-AP Ÿ Avoid food 2 hours before and 1 hour after taking the dose (5.9). Nilotinib (Niltib) is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with newly diagnosed Philadelphia chromosome positive chronic myelogenous leukemia (Ph+ CML) in chronic phase. The effectiveness of Nilotinib is based on major molecular response and cytogenetic response rates See full prescribing information for complete boxed warning. 2.1 Recommended Dosing Nilotinib should be taken twice daily at approximately 12-hour intervals and must be taken on an empty stomach. No food should be consumed for at least 2 hours before the dose is taken and for at least 1 hour after the dose is taken. Advise patients to swallow the capsules whole with water. Nilotinib may be given in combination with hematopoietic growth factors such as erythropoietin or G-CSF if clinically indicated. Nilotinib may be given with hydroxyurea or anagrelide if clinically indicated. Ÿ Nilotinib prolongs the QT interval. Prior to Nilotinib administration and periodically, monitor for hypokalemia or hypomagnesemia and correct deficiencies (5.2). Obtain ECGs to monitor the QTc at baseline, seven days after initiation, and periodically thereafter, and following any dose adjustments (5.2, 5.3, 5.7, 5.15). Ÿ Sudden deaths have been reported in patients receiving nilotinib (5.3). Do not administer Nilotinib to patients with hypokalemia, hypomagnesemia, or long QT syndrome (4, 5.2). For patients who are unable to swallow capsules, the contents of each capsule may be dispersed in 1 teaspoon of applesauce (puréed apple). The mixture should be taken immediately (within 15 minutes) and should not be stored for future use. Ÿ Avoid use of concomitant drugs known to prolong the QT interval and strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (5.8). FULL PRESCRIBING INFORMATIONWARNING: QT PROLONGATION and SUDDEN DEATHS",1,1,11 DESCRIPTION,1.2 Resistant or Intolerant Ph+ CML-CP and CML-AP 2.1 Recommended Dosing 3 DOSAGE FORMS AND STRENGTHS,1,1,1 INDICATIONS AND USAGE,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:31:27.502507+00:00
