ministration and periodically, monitor for hypokalemia or hypomagnesemia and correct deficiencies (5.2). Obtain ECGs to monitor the QTc at baseline, seven days after initiation, and periodically thereafter, and following any dose adjustments (5.2, 5.3, 5.7, 5.15). Ÿ Sudden deaths have been reported in patients receiving nilotinib (5.3). Do not administer Nilotinib to patients with hypokalemia, hypomagnesemia, or long QT syndrome (4, 5.2). For patients who are unable to swallow capsules, the contents of each capsule may be dispersed in 1 teaspoon of applesauce (puréed apple). The mixture should be taken immediately (within 15 minutes) and should not be stored for future use. Ÿ Avoid use of concomitant drugs known to prolong the QT interval and strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (5.8). FULL PRESCRIBING INFORMATIONWARNING: QT PROLONGATION and SUDDEN DEATHS",1,1,11 DESCRIPTION,1.2 Resistant or Intolerant Ph+ CML-CP and CML-AP 2.1 Recommended Dosing 3 DOSAGE FORMS AND STRENGTHS,1,1,1 INDICATIONS AND USAGE,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:31:30.654089+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48381,Abrocitinib,Cibinqo,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CSX-QDZGqdSd8C7PagFK0_fRnoi7Gib5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48381_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1CSX-QDZGqdSd8C7PagFK0_fRnoi7Gib5_view_usp_drivesdk_df8664081a.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48381_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1CSX-QDZGqdSd8C7PagFK0_fRnoi7Gib5_view_usp_drivesdk_df8664081a.json,09b8c8fa83427891bd27c0faa46804f8e93c6eaab2792afad97da2ec3fbdbd22,543092,30,digital_text,"Structure of Abrocitinib: N N N H N H N S OO Abrocitinib (Cibinqo) 50 mg film-coated tablets: Pink, oval tablet 10.50 mm long and 4.75 mm wide, debossed with “PFE” on one side and “ABR 50” on the other. Abrocitinib (Cibinqo) 100 mg film-coated tablets: Pink, round tablet 9.00 mm in diameter, debossed with “PFE” on one side and “ABR 100” on the other. Abrocitinib (Cibinqo) 200 mg film-coated tablets: Pink, oval tablet 18.42 mm long and 8.00 mm wide debossed with “PFE” on one side and “ABR 200” on the other.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Abrocitinib (Cibinqo) is indicated for the treatment of patients 12 years of age and older with moderate to severe atopic dermatitis, including the relief of pruritus, who have had an inadequate response to prescribed topical therapy or for whom these treatments are not advisable. Abrocitinib (Cibinqo) can be used with or without medicated topical therapies for atopic dermatitis.",2,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:31:34.240632+00:00
