hydrochloride""",Zemimet SR,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZZB6MFgfEhU9htGO4aSv5_a1Wve1eJJU/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48388_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZZB6MFgfEhU9htGO4aSv5_a1Wve1eJJU_view_usp_drivesdk_d712191401.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48388_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZZB6MFgfEhU9htGO4aSv5_a1Wve1eJJU_view_usp_drivesdk_d712191401.json,432d35da2ab4aecd5b5e57e31f6055d58d940fb70d4135658b722b5ab2c6a591,9698061,2,ocr,"Lipase increased 5(357) 6(426) (019% to <5%) Gemigl liptin/ Metformin HCl SOmg/g is oblong shaped, brown colored, flm-coated tablet _Pyrexia_ 3(214) 214) \n addition, the unexpected adverse events regardless of causality and the unexpected",1,1,"[Pharmaceutical Form,","at ‘The 24-week add-on combination therapy was extended thr week with gemigliptin rug reactions for which the causality could not be excluded are listed in the table Gemigliptin/Metformin HCl is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve 50 mg once daily added on to stable dose of metformin. The ee events that increased ir glycemic control in adults with type 2 diabetes tus. more than 1% during the latter 28 weeks when compared with the first 24 weeks, U ted Adverse Unexpected Adverse - As initial therapy for treatment naive patients with inadequate glycemic control by diet of assessment of causality, were diarrhea (071 % vs 27%), urinary tract infection (071% vs Events ts 366% (11/3036 pect Reactions 010% (3): and exercise alone. 18%), hypoglycemia (071% vs 2796), dizziness (0719 vs 36%) and nausea (143% vs 279). Incidence oan en subjects, 144 cases) subjects, 3 cases) ients with inadequate glycemic control with the maximal tolerated dose of events reported in more than 2 patients (18%) during the latter 28 weeks were ae in alone. asthenia (18%) and gia (18%), Gastro- intestinal Flatulence, Pancreatitis - In combination with sulfonylurea in No clinically meanit | changes in vital