PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48418,Vericiguat,Verquvo,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rdH4IGbsL8t3KTH_cRMdnFL0qAWiM1ju/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48418_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rdH4IGbsL8t3KTH_cRMdnFL0qAWiM1ju_view_usp_drivesdk_e4fd67a34e.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48418_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rdH4IGbsL8t3KTH_cRMdnFL0qAWiM1ju_view_usp_drivesdk_e4fd67a34e.json,e1eb61694f931092b910fd42d1bd1a5617d6ace5a25ad931d799ab6858f3980a,1585350,2,digital_text,"Film-coated tablets. Vericiguat (Verquvo™) 2.5 mg Film-coated Tablet Round, biconvex, white film-coated tablet with a diameter of 7 mm, debossed with “2.5” on one side and “VC” on the other side. Vericiguat (Verquvo™) 5 mg Film-coated Tablet Round, biconvex, brown-red film-coated tablet with a diameter of 7 mm, debossed with “5” on one side and “VC” on the other side. Vericiguat (Verquvo™) 10 mg Film-coated Tablet Round, biconvex, yellow-orange film-coated tablet with a diameter of 9 mm, debossed with “10” on one side and “VC” on the other side. 14. PHARMACEUTICAL PARTICULARS 14.1 Chemistry The chemical name of vericiguat is methyl {4,6-diamino-2-[5-fluoro-1-(2-fluorobenzyl)-1Hpyrazolo[3,4-b] pyridin-3-yl] pyrimidin-5-yl} carbamate. The molecular formula is C19H16F2N8O2 and the molecular weight is 426.39 g/mol. The chemical structure is: N NN N N H 2 H 2 N C H 3 N H N O O F F Vericiguat is a white to yellowish powder that is freely soluble in dimethyl sulfoxide, slightly soluble in acetone, very slightly soluble in ethanol, acetonitrile, methanol, ethyl acetate, and practically insoluble in 2-propanol.",2,2,13. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Vericiguat (Verquvo™) is indicated to reduce the risk of cardiovascular death and heart failure (HF) hospitalization following a worsening HF event, in adults with symptomatic chronic HF and ejection fraction less than 45%, in combination with other HF therapies.",1,1,1. INDICATIONS AND USAGE,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T09:37:33.025249+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48419,Vericiguat,Verquvo,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1d7_Qp_LxGI9VfcHu6NhLLywPIZGULVbj/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48419_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1d7_Qp_LxGI9VfcHu6NhLLywPIZGULVbj_view_usp_drivesdk_04b4495644.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48419_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1d7_Qp_LxGI9VfcHu6NhLLywPIZGULVbj_view_usp_drivesdk_04b4495644.json,e1eb61694f931092b910fd42d1bd1a5617d6ace5a25ad931d799ab6858f3980a,1585350,2,digital_text,"Film-coated tablets. Vericiguat (Verquvo™) 2.5 mg Film-coated Tablet Round, biconvex, white film-coated tablet with a diameter of 7 mm, debossed with “2.5” on one side and “VC” on the other side. Vericiguat (Verquvo™) 5 mg Film-coated Tablet Round, biconvex, brown-red film-coated tablet with a diameter of 7 mm, debossed with “5” on one side and “VC” on the other side. Vericiguat (Verquvo™) 10 mg Film-coated Tablet Round, biconvex, yellow-orange film-coated tablet with a diameter of 9 mm, debossed with “10” on one side and “VC” on the other side. 14. PHARMACEUTICAL PARTICULARS 14.1 Chemistry The chemical name of vericiguat is methyl {4,6-diamino-2-[5-fluoro-1-(2-fluorobenzyl)-1Hpyrazolo[3,4-b] pyridin-3-yl] pyrimidin-5-yl} carbamate. The molecular formula is C19H16F2N8O2 and the molecular weight is 426.39 g/mol. The chemical structure is: N NN N N H 2 H 2 N C H 3 N H N O O F F Vericiguat is a white to yellowish powder that is freely soluble in dimethyl sulfoxide, slightly soluble in acetone, very slightly soluble in ethanol, acetonitrile, methanol, ethyl acetate, and practically insoluble in 2-propanol.",2,2,13. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Vericiguat (Verquvo™) is indicated to reduce the risk of cardiovascular death and heart failure (HF) hospitalization following a worsening HF event, in adults with symptomatic chronic HF and ejection fraction less than 45%, in combination with other HF therapies.",1,1,1. INDICATIONS AND USAGE,