PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48906,Palbociclib,Ibrance,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1QbhMjB3hHgDj9lgGjJfGGoy3qtD_0cqU/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48906_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QbhMjB3hHgDj9lgGjJfGGoy3qtD_0cqU_view_usp_drivesdk_eb276cdece.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48906_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QbhMjB3hHgDj9lgGjJfGGoy3qtD_0cqU_view_usp_drivesdk_eb276cdece.json,1b9f3900363ea59b195bdf44fac0757f48232fbc0de8c01e5eef474a2383debc,1054228,37,digital_text,"75 mg strength: Round, light purple, film-coated tablet debossed with “Pfizer” on one side and “PBC 75” on the other side. 100 mg strength: Oval, green, film-coated tablet debossed with “Pfizer” on one side and “PBC 100” on the other side. 125 mg strength: Oval, light purple, film-coated tablet debossed with “Pfizer” on one side and “PBC 125” on the other side.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Palbociclib (Ibrance) is indicated for the treatment of hormone receptor (HR)-positive, human epidermal growth factor receptor 2 (HER2)-negative advanced or metastatic breast cancer in combination with:  an aromatase inhibitor as initial endocrine-based therapy  fulvestrant in patients who have received prior therapy.",1,1,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:10:06.163659+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY48906,Palbociclib,Ibrance,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cWUZhvgwHljS-O_AgN__0ANxuNU_JhOr/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY48906_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cWUZhvgwHljS-O_AgN__0ANxuNU_JhOr_view_usp_drivesdk_5e05afb577.pdf,page_text/DR-XY48906_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cWUZhvgwHljS-O_AgN__0ANxuNU_JhOr_view_usp_drivesdk_5e05afb577.json,b2a6d3feef370bbbd2a1a5178c8be327cc193b7f3142f56eff7412f9b6e5e804,1246660,36,digital_text,"Palbociclib (Ibrance) of Palbociclibis 6-acetyl-8-cyclopentyl-5-methyl-2- {[5 (piperazin-1-yl) pyridin-2-yl]amino}pyrido[2,3-d]pyrimidin-7(8H)-one. Its molecular formula is C24H29N7O2 which corresponds to a molecular weight of 447.54 Daltons. Chemical structure N N N Me O N H N N HN O Me Palbociclib is a yellow to orange powder with a pKa of 7.4 (secondary piperazine nitrogen) and 3.9 (pyridine nitrogen). The solubility of Palbociclib in aqueous media decreases over the range pH 4.3 to pH 9.0 from greater than 0.7 mg/mL to less than 0.002 mg/mL. At or below pH 4, Palbociclib behaves like a high-solubility compound. Above pH 4, the solubility of the drug substance reduces significantly. The partition coefficient (1-octanol /water) at pH 7.4 is 0.99. Palbociclib (Ibrance) is supplied as film-coated tablets for oral administration: 75 mg strength: Round, light purple, film-coated tablet debossed with “Pfizer” on one side and “PBC 75” on the other side. 100 mg strength: Oval, green, film-coated tablet debossed with “Pfizer” on one side and “PBC 100” on the other side. [Page 2] 2 125 mg strength: Oval, light purple, film-coated tablet debossed with “Pfizer” on one side and “PBC 125” on the other side.",1,2,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Palbociclib (Ibrance) is indicated for the treatment of hormone receptor (HR) positive, human epidermal growth factor receptor 2 (HER2)-negative advanced or metastatic breast cancer in combination with:  an aromatase inhibitor as initial endocrine-based therapy  fulvestrant in patients who have received prior therapy.",2,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:10:02.297683+00:00
