PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY49083,Atogepant,Aquipta,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Pz6kxaS10QFEmchcZsPilJO6yXCv_766/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY49083_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Pz6kxaS10QFEmchcZsPilJO6yXCv_766_view_usp_drivesdk_3066730d29.pdf,page_text/DR-XY49083_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Pz6kxaS10QFEmchcZsPilJO6yXCv_766_view_usp_drivesdk_3066730d29.json,b8c6d3e40a8b47ff8c0b3239857ac4277446c6c367c919c0444d5c0f16ffb332,182423,11,digital_text,"Tablet 10 mg tablets White to off-white, round biconvex tablet, diameter 6 mm, and debossed with “A” and “10” on one side. 60 mg tablets White to off-white, oval biconvex tablet, 16 mm x 9 mm, and debossed with “A60” on one side. 3. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 3.1 Therapeutic indications Atogepant (Aquipta™) is indicated for prophylaxis of migraine in adults who have at least 4 migraine days per month. 3.2 Posology and method of administration Posology The recommended dose is 60 mg atogepant once daily. The tablets can be taken with or without meals. Missed dose Atogepant [Page 2] A missed dose should be taken as soon as it is remembered. If it is forgotten for an entire day, the missed dose should be skipped and the next dose taken as scheduled. Dose modifications Dosing modifications for concomitant use of specific medicinal products are provided in Table 1 (see section 3.5). Table 1: Dose modifications for interactions Dose modifications Recommended once daily dose Strong CYP3A4 inhibitors 10 mg Strong OATP inhibitors 10 mg Special populations Elderly Population pharmacokinetic modelling suggests no clinically significant pharmacokinetic differences between elderly and younger subjects. No dose adjustment is needed in elderly patients. Renal impairment No dose adjustment is recommended for patients wit h mild or moderate renal impairment (see section 4.2). In patients with severe renal impairment (creatinine clearance [CLcr] 15-29 mL/min), and in patients with end-stage renal disease (ESRD) (CLcr < 15 mL/min), the recommended dose is 10 mg once daily. For patients with ESRD undergoing intermittent dialysis, AQUIPTA should preferably be taken after dialysis. Hepatic impairment No dose adjustment is recommended for patients with mild or moderate hepatic impairment (see section 4.2). Atogepant should be avoided in patients with severe hepatic impairment. Pediatric population The safety and efficacy of atogepant in children (< 18 years of age) have not yet been established. No data are available. Method of administration Atogepant (Aquipta™) is for oral use. Tablets should be swallowed whole and should not be split, crushed, or chewed.",1,2,2. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,Atogepant (Aquipta™) is indicated for prophylaxis of migraine in adults who have at least 4 migraine days per month.,1,1,3.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:11:19.406773+00:00
