PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY49320,Meropenem (as trihydrate),Meronash-500,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1jS6QsM0H0HwZWVhwXgiTNfP7TgqTfHC_/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY49320_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jS6QsM0H0HwZWVhwXgiTNfP7TgqTfHC__view_usp_drivesdk_e081db479c.pdf,page_text/DR-XY49320_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jS6QsM0H0HwZWVhwXgiTNfP7TgqTfHC__view_usp_drivesdk_e081db479c.json,5eea2529796165e9a87c8c50c026435a60488cff78a950c8b9cfbd11f8c526ca,2674608,2,digital_text,,,,,"Refer to the latest labelling materials of the innovator (locally available); however intellectual property matter should be considered. Kindly indicate all mandatory information following AO 2016-0008. Kindly indicate in the package insert the following: -Pharmacodynamics -Registration number -Date of first of authorization -Date of revision of package insert Antibacterial (Carbapenem) [Page 2] Refer to the latest labelling materials of the innovator (locally available); however intellectual property matter should be considered. Kindly indicate all mandatory information following AO 2016-0008. Overdose and Treatment Reconcile with the information indicated on the first page of the PI Statement for compatibility/in-use must be based on the In-use stability study submitted during compliance. Caution statement: Foods, Drugs, Devices and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription [Page 3]",1,2,Indications: Separate Dosage and Mode of Administration,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:13:11.058080+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY49396,"""Dapagliflozin (as propanediol monohydrate) +
Sitagliptin (as phosphate monohydrate)""",Sidapvia,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_Am94Tx_VlFFEuxP7A2gD6nvpEdJPo9s/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY49396_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_Am94Tx_VlFFEuxP7A2gD6nvpEdJPo9s_view_usp_drivesdk_9c3d5fa6aa.pdf,page_text/DR-XY49396_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_Am94Tx_VlFFEuxP7A2gD6nvpEdJPo9s_view_usp_drivesdk_9c3d5fa6aa.json,a693e0d1e8e69811d1c2d7075fa023ed9b85b2bafb7cfa784c8d84cf974b10a7,589395,44,digital_text,"Film-coated tablets. Dapagliflozin/sitagliptin (Sidapvia) 10 mg/100 mg tablets are yellow, oval shaped, approximately 8 mm x 15 mm, biconvex, film-coated tablets with “F M” debossed on one side and plain on the other side. 4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 4.1 Therapeutic indications Dapagliflozin/sitagliptin (Sidapvia) is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycaemic control in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus when treatment with both dapagliflozin and sitagliptin is appropriate. 4.2 Posology and method of administration Posology The recommended dose of Dapagliflozin/sitagliptin (Sidapvia) is one dapagliflozin 10 mg/sitagliptin 100 mg tablet taken orally once daily at any time of the day, with or without food. DAPAGLIFLOZIN/SITAGLIPTIN [Page 2] CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY 2 of 44 The tablet is to be swallowed whole. Special Populations Renal impairment Dapagliflozin/sitagliptin (Sidapvia) should not be used in patients with an estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) <45 mL/min/1.73 m2 (see section 5.2). Renal function should be evaluated prior to initiation of Dapagliflozin/sitagliptin (Sidapvia) and periodically thereafter. Hepatic impairment Dapagliflozin/sitagliptin (Sidapvia) may be used in patients with mild to moderate hepatic impairment. There is limited experience in patients with severe hepatic impairment, therefore, care should be exercised when Dapagliflozin/sitagliptin (Sidapvia) is used in this population (see section 5.2). Paediatric and adolescent patients Dapagliflozin/sitagliptin (Sidapvia) is not indicated for use in paediatric and adolescent patients. Dapagliflozin and sitagliptin have not been studied in paediatric patients under 10 years of age. Sitagliptin should not be used in children and adolescents 10 to 17 years of age because of insufficient efficacy. Elderly patients Dapagliflozin/sitagliptin (Sidapvia) may be used in elderly patients. However, older patients are more likely to have impaired renal function. The renal function recommendations provided for all patients also apply to elderly patients (see section 4.4).",1,2,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,Dapagliflozin/sitagliptin (Sidapvia) is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycaemic control in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus when treatment with both dapagliflozin and sitagliptin is appropriate.,1,1,4.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:13:15.510662+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY49504,Tirzepatide,Mounjaro KwikPen,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1O1W78WAf_XmHv1C5fZ9d4-UZQq-j-nnQ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY49504_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1O1W78WAf_XmHv1C5fZ9d4-UZQq-j-nnQ_view_usp_drivesdk_0ad9db725b.pdf,page_text/DR-XY49504_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1O1W78WAf_XmHv1C5fZ9d4-UZQq-j-nnQ_view_usp_drivesdk_0ad9db725b.json,82ae4097b86c24da365e9d1931d7f2d336e7ae61be4c4d809d5342e720418972,953151,34,digital_text,"Solution for injection (injection). Clear, colourless to slightly yellow solution. 4. Pharmacologic Category Pharmacotherapeutic group: Drugs used in diabetes, blood glucose lowering drugs, excl. insulins. ATC code: A10BX16 5. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 5.1 Therapeutic indications Type 2 diabetes mellitus Tirzepatide (Mounjaro) is indicated for the treatment of adults with insufficiently controlled type 2 diabetes mellitus as an adjunct to diet and exercise • as monotherapy when metformin is considered inappropriate due to intolerance or contraindications • in addition to other medicinal products for the treatment of diabetes. For study results with respect to combinations, effects on glycaemic control and the populations studied, see sections 5.4, 5.5 and 6.1. Weight management Tirzepatide (Mounjaro) is indicated as an adjunct to a reduced-calorie diet and increased physical activity for weight management, including weight loss and weight maintenance, in adults with an initial Body Mass Index (BMI) of • ≥ 30 kg/m 2 (obesity) or • ≥ 27 kg/m2 to < 30 kg/m2 (overweight) in the presence of at least one weight -related comorbid condition (e.g., hypertension, dyslipidaemia, obstructive sleep apnoea, cardiovascular disease, prediabetes, or type 2 diabetes mellitus). 5.2 Posology and method of administration Posology The starting dose of tirzepatide is 2.5 mg once weekly. After 4 weeks, the dose should be increased to 5 mg once weekly. If needed, dose increases can be made in 2.5 mg increments after a minimum of 4 weeks on the current dose. The recommended maintenance doses are 5 mg, 10 mg and 15 mg. The maximum dose is 15 mg once weekly. When tirzepatide is added to existing metformin and/or sodium-glucose co-transporter 2 inhibitor (SGLT2i) therapy, the current dose of metformin and/or SGLT2i can be continued. [Page 3] When tirzepatide is added to existing therapy of a sulphonylurea and/or insulin, a reduction in the dose of sulphonylurea or insulin may be considered to reduce the risk of hypoglycaemia. Blood glucose self - monitoring is necessary to adjust the dose of sulphonylurea and insulin. A stepwise approach to insulin reduction is recommended (see sections 5.4 and 5.8). Missed doses If a dose is missed, it should be administered as soon as possible within 4 days after the missed dose. If more than 4 days have passed, skip the missed dose and administer the next dose on the regularly scheduled day. In each case, patients can then resume their regular once weekly dosing schedule. Changing the dosing schedule The day of weekly administration can be changed, if necessary, as long as the time between two doses is at least 3 days. Special populations Elderly, gender, race, ethnicity or body weight No dose adjustment is needed based on age, gender, race, ethnicity or body weight (see sections 6.1 and 6.2). Only very limited data are available from patients aged ≥ 85 years. Renal impairment No dose adjustment is required for patients with renal impairment including end stage renal disease (ESRD). Experience with the use of tirzepatide in patients with severe renal impairment and ESRD is limited. Caution should be exercised when treating these patients with tirzepatide (see section 6.2). Hepatic impairment No dose adjustment is required for patients with hepatic impairment. Experience with the use of tirzepatide in patients with severe hepatic impairment is limited. Caution should be exercised when treating these patients with tirzepatide (see section 6.2). Paediatric population The safety and efficacy of tirzepatide in children aged less than 18 years have not yet been established. No data are available. Method of administration Tirzepatide (Mounjaro) is to be injected subcutaneously in the abdomen, thigh or upper arm. The dose can be administered at any time of day, with or without meals. Injection sites should be rotated with each dose. If a patient also injects insulin, t hey should inject Tirzepatide (Mounjaro) into a different injection site. Patients should be advised to carefully read the instructions for use included with the package leaflet before administering the medicinal product. [Page 4]",2,3,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Type 2 diabetes mellitus Tirzepatide (Mounjaro) is indicated for the treatment of adults with insufficiently controlled type 2 diabetes mellitus as an adjunct to diet and exercise • as monotherapy when metformin is considered inappropriate due to intolerance or contraindications • in addition to other medicinal products for the treatment of diabetes. For study results with respect to combinations, effects on glycaemic control and the populations studied, see sections 5.4, 5.5 and 6.1. Weight management Tirzepatide (Mounjaro) is indicated as an adjunct to a reduced-calorie diet and increased physical activity for weight management, including weight loss and weight maintenance, in adults with an initial Body Mass Index (BMI) of • ≥ 30 kg/m 2 (obesity) or • ≥ 27 kg/m2 to < 30 kg/m2 (overweight) in the presence of at least one weight -related comorbid condition (e.g., hypertension, dyslipidaemia, obstructive sleep apnoea, cardiovascular disease, prediabetes, or type 2 diabetes mellitus).",2,2,5.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:13:20.130560+00:00
