PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY7761,Multivitamins + Minerals,Usanatal,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1p5Pp4DUvUo2NDemPIVQak5CUEsiimSzo/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY7761_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1p5Pp4DUvUo2NDemPIVQak5CUEsiimSzo_view_usp_drivesdk_c7e954b3d0.pdf,page_text/DR-XY7761_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1p5Pp4DUvUo2NDemPIVQak5CUEsiimSzo_view_usp_drivesdk_c7e954b3d0.json,9c4f20e3d31e0ae5111c99aba68380009c0ffafd2592362ca1b922965453387b,1922618,2,ocr,"Nic is readily in the tract. Red, capsule-shaped, sugar-coated tablet Calcium is absorbed mainly in the small intestine through active transport and passive diffusion. Intestinal absorption v varies ue on dietary states and physiological needs but about 30% to 40% of dietary intake",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"mins to 6 hours post ingestion. Clinical presentation results from direct injury to the gastrointestinal mucosa and Hyper retinoid or vitamin D thera may include abdominal pain, vomiting, diarrhea, hematemesis, melena and lethargy. The next phase is the Distrbances in calcium metabolism such as hypercalcemia and hypercalciuria xaluria latent phase or the relative stability phase which occurs after 6 to 24 hours. The third phase is characterized by is shock and metabolic acidosis and typically occur within 6 to 72 hours post ingestion. Shock may be due to its with renal failure given aluminum antacids hypovolemia or direct cardiotoxicity. The fourth phase is hepatotoxicity or hepatic necrosis which may be Hemochromatosis and other iron storage disorders ected within 12 to 96 hours. Hepatocellular necrosis should be suspected when jaundice, bleeding lronsoadi major, anemia, chronic hemolytic anemias) hypoglycemia, encephal and positive anion gap metabolic acidosis are evident. Renal failure may Chronic liver disease ensue with tissue sion. The fifth is bowel obstruction which can present 2 to 8 weeks after Active gas