PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY8460,Paracetamol,Higestic,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MCxi_kR8gnoqaeQ9a2mXx9uW098NkVQ9/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY8460_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MCxi_kR8gnoqaeQ9a2mXx9uW098NkVQ9_view_usp_drivesdk_4b04ec1519.pdf,page_text/DR-XY8460_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MCxi_kR8gnoqaeQ9a2mXx9uW098NkVQ9_view_usp_drivesdk_4b04ec1519.json,df778f628ea5448ac76d10a9b8ef7f175b1e17ac18882bf8c4fd7a9357d1d2b1,423855,1,ocr,"Paracetamol 125 mg/5 mL Syrup is a clear, red, lemon-strawberry flavored syrup. Paracetamol 250 mg/5 mL Suspension is a white suspension with strawberry flavor. Paracetamol 500 mg Tabletis a white, round, flat, bisected, uncoated tablet. Whatis in the Medicine? This medicine contains Paracetamol, a para-aminophenol derivative, has analgesic and antipyretic properties and weak anti- inflammatory activity. It is often the analgesic or antipyretic of choice, especially in the elderly and in patients in whom salicytates or other NSAIDS are contraindicated. Such patients include asthmatics, those with the history of peptic ulcer and children. Strength of the Medicine",1,1,Product Description,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:15:43.634539+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DR-XY9450,Azathioprine,Imuran,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/12CF4ufxhN0OfqNuLpmZtVxdjuDg4I7Pb/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DR-XY9450_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_12CF4ufxhN0OfqNuLpmZtVxdjuDg4I7Pb_view_usp_drivesdk_21087b5361.pdf,page_text/DR-XY9450_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_12CF4ufxhN0OfqNuLpmZtVxdjuDg4I7Pb_view_usp_drivesdk_21087b5361.json,bd6345ff5d8c292be8878a87d637726a3c127e6f1f6d294097230bded9c6b0e3,205243,2,digital_text,"Each yellow , r ound, biconvex, film-coated scor ed tablet contains 50 mg of the active ingr edient azathioprine br anded with ‘GX",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Azathioprine (Imur an) is used as an immunosuppr essant antimetabolite either alone or , mor e commonly , in combination with other agents (usually corticoster oids) and pr ocedures which influence the immune r esponse. Ther apeutic effect may be evident only after weeks or months and can include a steroid- sparing effect, ther eby r educing the toxicity associated with high dosage and pr olonged usage of corticosteroids. Azathioprine (Imur an), in combination with corticoster oids and/or other immunosuppr essive agents and pr ocedures, is indicated to enhance the survival of or gan tr ansplants, such as r enal tr ansplants, car diac tr ansplants and hepatic tr ansplants. It also r educes the corticoster oid r equirements of renal transplant recipients. Azathioprine (Imur an) is indicated for the tr eatment of moder ate to sever e inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) (Cr ohn’s disease or ulcer ative colitis) in patients in whom corticoster oid ther apy is r equired, in patients who cannot toler ate corticoster oid ther apy, or in patients whose disease is refractory to other standard first line therapy. Azathioprine (Imur an), either alone or mor e usually in combination with corticoster oids and/or other drugs and pr ocedures, has been used with clinical benefit (which may include r eduction of dosage or discontinuation of corticoster oids) in a proportion of patients suffering fr om the following: - Sever e rheumatoid arthritis - Systemic lupus erythematosus - Dermatomyositis and polymyositis - Auto-immune chronic active hepatitis - P emphigus vulgaris - P olyarteritis nodosa - Auto-immune haemolytic anaemia - Chr onic r efractory idiopathic thr ombocytopenic purpur a - Relapsing remittent multiple sclerosis",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:15:47.390004+00:00
