PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRHR-1112,ORAL REHYDRATION SALTS,Sodalite-75,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hrC0CwKxBykckP_nA8dySnS95lUz_5Ri/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRHR-1112_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hrC0CwKxBykckP_nA8dySnS95lUz_5Ri_view_usp_drivesdk_90cdd53194.pdf,page_text/DRHR-1112_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hrC0CwKxBykckP_nA8dySnS95lUz_5Ri_view_usp_drivesdk_90cdd53194.json,eab2b70e16182378e0921abf8dac2c6da70e23c1ca788439aa4bf6505b4c8725,324514,1,ocr,"* Oral Rehydration Salts may be used in severe dehydration SODALITE?-75 ts an ORS’ which appears as white crystalline only if intravenous fluid is not available. powder in a sachet. when reconstituted it ts colorless liquid in «This reduced osmolarity ORS gtanules in sachet should be orange flavor. made into solution immediately before use If not refrigerated discard any remaining solution an hour after constitution. If WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? refrigerated. the constituted solution can be kept for 24 hours This medicine conforms with the WHO reduced osmolarity glucose- after which it should no longer be used based oral rehydration salts (ORS), the prefered method for treating + Use only cooled boiled/clean drinking water to constitute this dehydration product. The constituted solution should never be boiled * This product gives a cloudy solution when reconstituted STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Shake or stir well before feeding, See formulation above *Do not use more than the recommended dose unless recommended by a doctor WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? + Do not use after the expiry date on the label. This product ts used for the treatment of dehydration due to diarrhea WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If any undesirable effect occurs or dehydration worsen. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THE MEDICINE? AVAILABILITY For Children Less than 2 years cld — % glass (50 to 100 mL) Aluminum Sachet of 4 34 g (Box of 30