PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRHR-1203,Carbocisteine,Nivicof,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/15_uysCqsLpi327bDAP2c9TeurAoY1dcX/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRHR-1203_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15_uysCqsLpi327bDAP2c9TeurAoY1dcX_view_usp_drivesdk_c33507e3f9.pdf,page_text/DRHR-1203_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15_uysCqsLpi327bDAP2c9TeurAoY1dcX_view_usp_drivesdk_c33507e3f9.json,38373d89c39f466b725ae06fd93e6802edd747acc781a977041aa18386d7035d,147094,2,digital_text,"50 mg per 5 ml Suspension (Oral Drops) is a pinkish-red colored with tutti-frutti flavor. 100 mg per 5 ml Syrup is a clear, yellow syrup with fruit taste. 500 mg Capsule is a white to off -white compacted powder encapsulated in empty gelatin capsule, size #0 with green cap and yellow body. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Carbocisteine is a mucolytic agent used to relieve the chest congestion caused by thick and sticky mucus in the airways. This may be associated with lung diseases such as chronic obstructive pulmonary disorder (COPD), bronchitis, emphysema, etc.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:16:27.538795+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRHR-1295,Ascorbic Acid,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VI0PnCPtUrYnwVUdO9F5HDfo_BjTdakA/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRHR-1295_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VI0PnCPtUrYnwVUdO9F5HDfo_BjTdakA_view_usp_drivesdk_3064f8836b.pdf,page_text/DRHR-1295_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VI0PnCPtUrYnwVUdO9F5HDfo_BjTdakA_view_usp_drivesdk_3064f8836b.json,cd31cad09561bd218ebfdd4717d15e43f643d4edc02ab67b8125103e4f0ae4d8,3622645,2,ocr,"Ascorbic Acid 500 mg Tablet: Ascorbic Acid is a white, round, 7/16” in diameter, beveled edge tablet, flat bisected on one side, and flat plain on the other side. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Please see formulation. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? For the prevention and treatment of Vitamin C deficiency. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Ascorbic Acid 500 mg Tablet: Children 6-12 years: % tablet a day. Adult: 1 tablet a day or as prescribed by the physician. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Do not take more than the recommended dose. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Ascorbic Acid should be given with care to patients with hyperoxaluria and glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase (G6PD) deficiency. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Ascorbic Acid is generally well tolerated. However, large doses are reported to cause diarrhea and other gastrointestinal disturbances, hyperoxaluria and formation of renal calcium oxalate calculi. Tolerance may be induced with prolonged used of large doses. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? It should not be given for the first month after desferrioxamin treatmment. Giving ascorbic acid for vitamin C deficiency to patient receiving fluphenazine for bipolar disorder was associated with decreased in serum concentrations of fluphenazine and deterioration of behavior. Omeprazole may affect the bioavailabiloty of vitamin C. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Take the missed dose as soon as you remember. If it is almost time for your next dose, skip the missed dose and return to your normal dosing schedule. Do not double a dose under any circumstances. [Page 2] SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE Gastrointestinal disturbances (e.g., diarrnea), hyperoxaluria, formation of renal calcium oxalate calculi and tolerance may be induced with prolonged use of large doses. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED USAGE? If the patient has taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor immediately. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Preserve in tight light resistant container. Keep container tightly closed and protected from light. Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C.Prolonged exposure to heat, light and moisture may lead to discoloration of tablet which does not affect the efficacy and safety of the product. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If the patient experience any of the above-mentioned undesirable effects or any signs and symptoms of overdose. For suspected Adverse Drug Reaction (ADR), report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph or drug.safety@philusa.com.ph. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of ADR. AVAILABILITY Ascorbic Acid 500 mg Tablet: Amber Glass Bottle x 100’s REGISTRATION NUMBER Ascorbic Acid 500 mg Tablet: DRHR-1295 DATE OF RENEWAL OF THE AUTHORIZATION Ascorbic Acid 500 mg Tablet: 19 March 2028 DATE OF REVISION OF PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET November 2024 Manufactured by: Amherst Laboratories, Inc. UNILAB Pharma Campus, Barangay Mamplasan, Bifian, Laguna Marketing Authorization Holder: PHILUSA CORPORATION 28 Shaw Blvd., Kapitolyo, Pasig, Metro Manila ascorbicacid-1124 [Page 3]",1,2,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:16:36.782777+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRHR-1319,,,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1YrFf7VihnZcvWoxQOwDTX83FffmW15l-/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRHR-1319_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YrFf7VihnZcvWoxQOwDTX83FffmW15l-_view_usp_drivesdk_05dd6f2b97.pdf,page_text/DRHR-1319_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YrFf7VihnZcvWoxQOwDTX83FffmW15l-_view_usp_drivesdk_05dd6f2b97.json,66947a20639113816b41fe1f9d87874afd452c573d10d479ffde026ca304547d,64723,1,ocr,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T12:16:41.640647+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRHR-1335,Oral Rehydration Salts (ORS-75 Replacement),Olrite,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/19UC9Ji8cNHojlypzXCCZvDBI9uudDY0k/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRHR-1335_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19UC9Ji8cNHojlypzXCCZvDBI9uudDY0k_view_usp_drivesdk_1f0e12ea29.pdf,page_text/DRHR-1335_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19UC9Ji8cNHojlypzXCCZvDBI9uudDY0k_view_usp_drivesdk_1f0e12ea29.json,7a4a42fa581d46187345275b617c71b359cb05e9194c19096f169d6aa8d2a4fb,1713389,1,ocr,"Oral Rehydration Salts ORS-75 Replacement (OLRITE) is a fine, white powder contained in an aluminum foil sachet (5.575 g Box of 25's and 30's / 22.30 g Box of 10's) What is in the medicine? The medicine contains new formulation-low osmolarity oral rehydration salts that conforms with the WHO/UNICEF, the prefered method for the treatment of dehydration due to diarrhea Strength of the medicine Each Sachet contains: 250 mL 1 Liter Glucose anhydrous Food Grade, BP 3.375 g 13.5g Trisodium Citrate Dihydrate 725 mg 2.99 Sodium Chloride 650 mg 26g Potassium Chloride 375 mg 1.59 FD & C Yellow #5 (Tartrazine) 2.5 mg 10 mg Equivalent in mmol/L Sodium 75 mmol Glucose 75 mmol Chloride 65 mmol Potassium 10 mmol Citrate 10 mmol What is this medicine used for? Used for the replacement of fluid and electrolyte losses in mild to moderate dehydration due to diarrhea or vomiting How much and how often should you use this medicine for? The 2005 WHO Manual for the treatment of diarrhea provides the following information on the assessment and treatment of dehydration 1. HOW TOASSESS THE DEGREE OF DEHYDRATIONAND CHOOSEATREATMENTPLAN USE TREATMENT USE TREATMENT PATIENT REQUIRES (Can be treated at home) (Consult a doctor or HOSPITALIZATION ith CLINICAL, NO DEHYRATION ‘MILD TO MODERATE @ SEVEREDEHYRATION MARK! @ Use ORS to prevent dehydration © Use 0! at e@Requires rapid aration intravenous rehydration 4. LOOK AT Condition ‘