PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRHR-1545,Ascorbic Acid,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1QPx-wLN8wttdqqC0565DSCP-9LP6leSq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRHR-1545_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QPx-wLN8wttdqqC0565DSCP-9LP6leSq_view_usp_drivesdk_657030b5ba.pdf,page_text/DRHR-1545_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QPx-wLN8wttdqqC0565DSCP-9LP6leSq_view_usp_drivesdk_657030b5ba.json,b62c1fe36dd0360c563f85317c67129bcc36b7a614a8f9a29399b3738dbf3b8d,124677,1,digital_text,"Ascorbic Acid 100 mg/5 mL syrup is a clear orange syrup. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This medicine contains Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C), a water-soluble antioxidant vitamin which helps protect the body from the damaging eﬀects of free readicals. Free radicals are highly reactive and unstable chemicals generated during normal body activities that require oxygen (e.g. respiration, digestion, blood circulation, Immune system response, etc.) and after exposure to UV light, cigarette smoke and various pollutants. Vitamin C forms part of the body’s natural immune system and stimulates the activity of specialized white blood cells which inhibit harmful bacteria and viruses. Vitamin C is also needed for the formation of the protein, collagen. Collagen is important in the formation of bones, teeth, cartilage, and skin and helps promote faster wound healing.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:17:07.093505+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRHR-1549,Carbocisteine,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wvRhYG3G2kkbTOohyTiJItMYunHR6bqq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRHR-1549_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wvRhYG3G2kkbTOohyTiJItMYunHR6bqq_view_usp_drivesdk_7e52c060be.pdf,page_text/DRHR-1549_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wvRhYG3G2kkbTOohyTiJItMYunHR6bqq_view_usp_drivesdk_7e52c060be.json,29e241ba9d143631c3a3d733b354ddffd23e1dab25f489c6ab58699fbf8a7c90,1152457,1,digital_text,"White, crystalline powder contained in a white body/orange cap capsule #0. BOIE What is in the medicine? Each capsule contains Carbocisteine 500mg Strength of the medicine 500mg What is this medicine used for? Carbocisteine is indicated in acute and chronic disorders of the upper and lower respiratory tract characterized by excessive or viscous mucus such as acute and chronic bronchitis, bronchopneumonia, pulmonary emphysema, bronchiectasis and bronchial asthma. It is also used as adjunctive therapy in otitis, sinusitis, nasopharyngitis, tubal otorrhea and in reducing hypersecretion prior to surgery. How much and how often should you use this medicine? For adults: 1 capsule 3 times a day or as prescribed by the physician When should you not take this medicine? Do not take this medicine if you are known to be allergic (hypersensitive) to Carbo- cisteine. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine? Administer with caution to patients with history of peptic ulcer disease because of the risk that mucolytics may disrupt the gastric mucosal barrier. Undesirable eﬀects of this medicine Nausea, gastric discomfort and gastrointestinal bleeding have occasionally occured with Carbocisteine. Skin rashes have also been reported. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Please tell your doctor or pharmacist if you are taking or have recently taken any other medicines, including medicines obtained without a prescription. Currently, Carbocisteine is not known to aﬀect or be aﬀected by any other medicines you may be taking. What should you do if you miss a dose? If you forget to take Carbocisteine 500mg capsule, take the missed dose as soon as you remember. If it is almost time for your next dose, do not take the missed dose but simply take your next dose at the normal time. Do not take a double dose to make up for the one you missed. Signs and symptoms of overdose Gastrointestinal disturbance is the most likely symptom of Carbocisteine overdosage. Tell your doctor immediately if you develop any of the following symptoms: blood in your vomit or black tarry stools. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? Consult a doctor if you have taken more than the recommended dose. How should you keep this medicine? When should you consult your doctor? Consult your doctor or go to the nearest hospital immediately if any of the following happen after taking your medicine: • Wheezing, diﬃculty breathing or swallowing, dizziness • Swelling of the eyelids, face, lips, tongue or throat • Skin rashes • Bleeding from the stomach or intestine (which may be seen as black, tar-like stools). FRONT Manufactured for: BOIE INCORPORATED 6/F Sycamore Prime Building, Alabang-Zapote Road cor. Buencamino St., Cupang, Muntinlupa City Manufactured by:",1,1,Description of the product,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:17:10.948163+00:00
