PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRHR-2007,Ascorbic Acid,Cecon Junior,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1C5BJxKh5FLHgmWDqIb6hB_OAHsF0CmWy/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRHR-2007_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1C5BJxKh5FLHgmWDqIb6hB_OAHsF0CmWy_view_usp_drivesdk_a94a2925fd.pdf,page_text/DRHR-2007_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1C5BJxKh5FLHgmWDqIb6hB_OAHsF0CmWy_view_usp_drivesdk_a94a2925fd.json,a8e686cc9efca9b5f70da58821189c03a54d00ae67f1855aaefff83ba0895758,161068,3,digital_text,"Orange to brownish-orange, mottled, ellipse, plain, bioconvex tablet. What is in the Medicine? Each chewable tablet contains Sodium Ascorbate ……………………………………………………….. 92.81 mg (Equivalent to Ascorbic Acid 75 mg) (Vitamin C) Ascorbic Acid 90% Gran ……………………………………………… 30.56 mg (Equivalent to Ascorbic Acid 25 mg) (Vitamin C) Total Equivalent Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C): 100 mg Strength of the Medicine The strength of the medicine is 100 mg. What is this medicine used for? Vitamin C for the treatment and prevention of Vitamin C deficiency. Strengthens immune system Vitamin C stimulates the activity of specialized white blood cells which inhibit harmful bacteria and viruses. It helps increase body resistance to stress, common colds, viral and other types of",1,1,Description of the Product,"Antioxidant Vitamin C is an antioxidant which helps protect the body from harmful effects of free radicals, toxic chemicals and pollutants. Stimulates collagen synthesis Vitamin C is needed for the formation of collagen, an important protein used to make skin, scar tissue, tendons, ligaments, and blood vessels. Helps in wound healing and regeneration process Vitamin C hastens wound healing and increases body resistance from infectious diseases; helps in the repair and maintenance of healthy gums, teeth, bones and connective tissues. Helps in absorption of iron Vitamin C is a co-factor in iron metabolism which enhances absorption of iron. How much and how often should you use this Medicine? The chewable tablet should be taken orally. For children 7-12 years: 1-2 tablet daily For children 4-6 years old: 1 tablet daily Or it may be taken as directed by a doctor. When should you not take this Medicine? [Page 2] You should not take this medicine if you have hypersensitivity to Vitamin C or to any of the excipients. Care that should be taken when taking this Medicine? Ascorbic acid is usually well tolerated. Large doses may cause diarrhea and the formation of renal calcium oxalate calculi. Doses of 600 mg or more daily have a diuretic action. Ascorbic acid should be given with care to patients with hyperoxaluria. Tolerance may be induced in patients with prolonged use of taking high doses, resulting in symptoms of deficiency when intake is reduced to normal. Undesirable effects of this Medicine Prolonged or excessive use of chewable vitamin C preparations may cause erosion of tooth enamel. Large doses of ascorbic acid have resulted in hemolysis in patients with G6PD deficiency. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Ascorbic acid may increase the absorption of iron on iron-deficiency states. Omeprazole may affect the bioavailability of dietary vitamin C. Ascorbic acid is often given in addition to patients with iron overload to achieve better iron excretion. However, early on in treatment when there is excessive tissue iron there is some evidence that ascorbic acid may worsen the iron toxicity, particularly to the heart. Thus, ascorbic acid should not be given for the first month of deferoxamine treatment. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the next dose if you missed a dose. Pregnancy and Lactation: Ascorbic acid in doses greater than 1 g daily should not be taken during pregnancy since the effect of large doses on the fetus was unknown. Ascorbic acid crosses the placenta and is distributed into breast milk. Signs and Symptoms of Overdose: Ascorbic acid in excess of body’s needs is also rapidly eliminated unchanged in the urine. It is removed by hemodialysis. Prolonged or excessive use of Vitamin C preparations may cause erosion of tooth enamel. Large doses of ascorbic acid have resulted in hemolysis in patients with G6PD Deficiency. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Keep this and other medications out of reach of children. Keep away from heat and direct sunlight. Exposure to these conditions may lead to slight discoloration. When should you consult your doctor? Consult your doctor for any signs of adverse drug reaction. “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph”. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration Number: DRHR-2007 Date of First Authorization: 25 Nov 2020 Availability: Aluminum Strip Foil x 6's (Box of 30's) Manufactured by: [Page 3]",1,2,infections.,low,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T12:22:36.445706+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRHR-2096,Carbocisteine,Solmux,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HgxSLuw28oXgBXmMOA2s7Q6YI511b0pu/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRHR-2096_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HgxSLuw28oXgBXmMOA2s7Q6YI511b0pu_view_usp_drivesdk_f49c97b68b.pdf,page_text/DRHR-2096_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HgxSLuw28oXgBXmMOA2s7Q6YI511b0pu_view_usp_drivesdk_f49c97b68b.json,31f45f5fde6d22adf2244e5a5c2f286a3ba65b015e99adb8d8252f810bd06e20,854304,1,ocr,"HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THESE MEDICINES? Carbocisteine (Solmux®) 40 mg/mL Syrup (Oral Drops), 100 mg/5 mL Pediatric Syrup, are red, clear syrups Keep the product out of reach and sight of children. Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. with strawberry odor and sweet strawberry taste using the TasteRite® technolo y. TasteRite® technology is a unique system p for liquid dosage forms to improve sins AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSAGE the taste of the medicine. is usually with stomach or intestinal discomfort. WHAT TO DO IF YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? Carbocisteine (Solmux® Forte) 500 mg/5 mL Adult is a pink, thick with fruity y odor, and strawberry taste; it uses sorbitol as sweetener and does not contain sucrose or table sugar. If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor or contact a poison control center right away. Carbocisteine (Solmux®) 500 mg Capsule is a hard gelatin capsule with ivory opaque cap and rich yellow opaque CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THESE MEDICINES? These medicines should be given with care in patients with a history of stomach or intestinal ulcer and WHAT ARE IN THE MEDICINES? gastrointestinal bleeding. © Do not take more than the recommended dose. These contain car! a that causes phlegm to be less thick and sticky and thus easier © Do not use after the expiry date on the label to cough up and expel. Carbocisteine, in an in vitro study (outside the living organism), was shown to have WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? significantly reduced the ability of bacteria to adhere to human pharyngeal cells. If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, consult your doctor before using this product STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINES Stop taking the medicine and consult your doctor immediately if you develop any of the following",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTIONS,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:22:43.978110+00:00
