PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRHR-305,Methyl Salicylate + Menthol,Begesic,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UVXNnMqgK8y-NZvWWahzD-8IHdvWtSmy/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRHR-305_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UVXNnMqgK8y-NZvWWahzD-8IHdvWtSmy_view_usp_drivesdk_83692a11f0.pdf,page_text/DRHR-305_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UVXNnMqgK8y-NZvWWahzD-8IHdvWtSmy_view_usp_drivesdk_83692a11f0.json,e71875ed58630fd84dc88913c1db3f38b83f7c7ab8b3e13b5dfdd8f5896da094,489039,1,ocr,"Methyl Salicylate + Menthol (Begesic) is a topically-applied pain-relieving cream that is greaseless, non-staining, and pleasant smelling. Applied on the skin, it produces a warm sensation. Methyl Salicylate + Menthol (Begesic) is hypo-allergenic and extremely soothing. Methyl Salicylate + Menthol (Begesic) is a white cream. What is this medicine used for? For the relief of sores, aches, strained muscles, minor arthritis and stiffness. What in the medicine? It contains Methy] salicylate and Menthol work by causing the skin to feel cool and warm. Known as counterirritants. Strength of the medicine? Each 100 g of cream contains: Methyl salicylate, USP. 10g Menthol, USP. 56g How much and how often should you use this medicine? Apply generously on the affected area, 2 to 3 times daily or whenever necessary Use in children Methyl salicylate + Menthol (Begesic) is not intended for use under 2 years or consult the physician When should you not take this medicine? If you are allergic to Methyl salicylate and Menthol or any of the other ingredients of this medicine. Care that should be taken when taking medicine? - When using other drugs for anticoagulants. - Ifyou are pregnant or breastfeeding. - Ifyou have asthma. Avoid eye area contact. If this occurs accidentally wash away with plenty of clean water. Do not apply to abrasion or open wound, mucous areas, broken or irritated skin Do not use hot compression to the affected area which is applied. Do not bandage tightly Do not swallow. Undesirable effects of this medicine If Methyl Salicylate + Menthol (Begesic) cream is topically applied a large amount it might cause a mild salicylism It might cause skin irritation in sensitive skin patients What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Aspirin Warfarin Ibuprofen Non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDS) What should you do if you miss a dose? Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten dose Signs and symptoms of overdose ‘The signs nd symptoms of Methyl licylate overdose are the following: - Tinnitus. - Diarrhea - Difficulty in hearing Dizziness Nausea Sweating Headache - Mental Confusion What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a physician or pharmacist, you should stop Methyl salicylate + Menthol (Begesic) cream If you accidentally swallow the cream contact your doctor or hospital immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°. Keep out reach of children. When should you consult your doctor? If any undesirable effect occurs. Availability: Aluminum Collapsible Tube x 30 g FOR EXTERNAL USE ONLY Manufactured by: Berlin Pharmaceutical Industry Co., Ltd. Berlin 222 Romklao Road, Klongsampravet, Latkrabang, Bangkok 10520, Thailand Imported and Distributed by: Littman Drug Corporation 3rd Flr., No.3 Jaime Cardinal Sin St... Brgy. Pleasant Hills, Mandaluyong City, Metro Manila ADR Reporting Statemement “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www,fda.gov.ph”. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration number",1,1,Description of the product,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:23:10.249043+00:00
