PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRHR-720,Carbocisteine,Solmux Forte,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N374noExmBzyiOM1Ovw7SKmGV50_sfmd/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRHR-720_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1N374noExmBzyiOM1Ovw7SKmGV50_sfmd_view_usp_drivesdk_9408d6462c.pdf,page_text/DRHR-720_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1N374noExmBzyiOM1Ovw7SKmGV50_sfmd_view_usp_drivesdk_9408d6462c.json,36e1829f25d61d8d165227e96f531a39fd4e47607664c4d96693165e0a249ed4,2049789,1,ocr,"CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE Carbocisteine (Solmux Forte) 500 mg/5 mL adult suspension is a pink, thick suspension with fruity strawberry ¢ This medicine should be given with care in patients with a history of stomach or intestinal ulcer and odor, and strawberry taste; it uses sorbitol as sweetener and does not contain sucrose or table sugar. gastrointestinal bleeding. ¢ Do not use with other medicines containing carbocisteine. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? © Do not take more than the recommended dose. This medicine contains carbocisteine, a medicine that causes phlegm to be less thick and sticky and thus © Do not use after the expiry date on the label. easier to cough up and expel. Carbocisteine, in an in vitro study (outside the living organism), was shown to have significantly reduced the ability of bacteria to adhere to human pharyngeal cells. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? Ask a doctor before use if: STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE - You are pregnant or breastfeeding",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:23:56.999523+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRHR-881,Ascorbic Acid,Carezee,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1aKUlOXEAqY8PurcJxt5vZIuUrMiBtuqG/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRHR-881_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1aKUlOXEAqY8PurcJxt5vZIuUrMiBtuqG_view_usp_drivesdk_a8fdcccb39.pdf,page_text/DRHR-881_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1aKUlOXEAqY8PurcJxt5vZIuUrMiBtuqG_view_usp_drivesdk_a8fdcccb39.json,5b823d99502ce0d3f366ae229da619a8aa3daf2b33b6e10abc2e430d232e4a28,284441,1,ocr,"Carezee syrup is a clear, orange to brown orange syrup with lemon odor and flavor. Carezee drops is a clear, orange to brown orange syrup has sweet, slightly salty taste with lemon flavor and odor. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This product contains Vitamin C. Vitamin C helps the body’s natural defense against damaging free radicals. Free radicals are highly reactive and unstable chemicals generated during normal body activities that require oxygen and after exposure to UV light, cigarette smoke and various pollutants, Vitamin C forms part of the body's natural immune system and stimulates the activity. of specialized white blood cells which inhibit harmful bacteria and viruses. Vitamin C also needed for the formation of the protein, collagen. It is important in the formation of bones, teeth f cartilage and skin and promotes faster healing. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE See formulation above WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? For the treatment and prevention of Vitamin C deficiency. For body resistance against stress, common colds and other infections HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THE MEDICINE? Orally, once a day or as prescribed by the physician For Carezee syrup: Children - % to 1 teaspoon (2.5mL - SmL. Adults - 2 to 4 teaspoonfuls (10mL - 20mL) For Carezee drops: Infants - 0.6m (60mg) daily WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you are allergic to any-ingredient of the product UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS Prolonged intake of Vitamin C in excess of 2 g/day may /ead to nausea, abdominal cramps, diarrhea and nose bleeds. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOODS SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? The amount of Vitamin C in the product is not expected to interact with food or medicines. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, just give the next dose and the subsequent doses at the usual recommended schedule. Da not double the dose unless recommended by a doctor HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THE MEDICINE? * Keep the product out of reach and sight of children * Store at temperatures not exceeding 30° * Protect from light * Always keep container tightly closed SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE There is no information regarding overdosage of Vitamin C WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE USED MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE ¢ Should be given with care to patients with hyperoxaluria ¢ Do not use after the expiry date on the labe * Do not give more than the recommended dose WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? if any undesirable effect occurs AVAILABILITY Syrup: Boston round amber glass bottle x 120ml (Box of 1's} Drops: Amber Bottle x 30 mt with Aluminum Cap, Medicine Dropper. DATE OF REVISION OF PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET (PIL); February 12, 2018 Carezee Oral Drops: Registration no. DR-XY35220 Valid until] December 10, 2021 Carezee Syrup: Registration no. DRHR-881 Valid until October 8, 2019. ADR Reporting Statement “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph” Patient must seek medical attention immediately at the = sign of any adverse drug reaction Manufactured for: PHARMACARE PRODUCTS CORPORATION SB Residences Unit 2&3 302 P. Dela Cruz St., San Bartolome, Novaliches Quezon City Manufactured by: LA CROSEUS PHARMA INC Brgy. Sto. Tomas Bifian, Laguna [Page 2]",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:24:04.397693+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-001,Irbesartan/Hydrochlorothiazide,Co-Aprovel,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zXdjclrRZ-CCml9dhh-cVe3m-e0pkE0l/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-001_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zXdjclrRZ-CCml9dhh-cVe3m-e0pkE0l_view_usp_drivesdk_a880fb9e24.pdf,page_text/DRP-001_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zXdjclrRZ-CCml9dhh-cVe3m-e0pkE0l_view_usp_drivesdk_a880fb9e24.json,885d00c3927bb4b0ea7300ea47f2c28c8e12f97fa209e4c3f8f4d50ba8c47710,220266,13,digital_text,"Irbesartan / Hydrochlorothiazide (CoAprovel) 150 mg / 12.5 mg film-coated tablets Peach, biconvex, oval-shaped, with a heart debossed on one side and the number 2875 engraved on the other side. Irbesartan / Hydrochlorothiazide (CoAprovel) 300 mg / 12.5 mg film-coated tablets Peach, biconvex, oval-shaped, with a heart debossed on one side and the number 2876 engraved on the other side. Irbesartan / Hydrochlorothiazide (CoAprovel) 300 mg / 25 mg film-coated tablets Pink, biconvex, oval-shaped, with a heart debossed on one side and the number 2788 engraved on the other side.",1,1,Pharmaceutical Form,"Irbesartan / Hydrochlorothiazide (CoAprovel) is indicated for the treatment of hypertension. It may be used either alone or in combination with other antihypertensive agents (e.g., beta-adrenergic blocking agent, long-acting calcium-channel blocking agent). Irbesartan / Hydrochlorothiazide ( CoAprovel) may also be used as initial therapy in patients who are likely to need multiple drugs to achieve their blood pressure goals.",1,1,Indication,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:11:24.396836+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-002,Irbesartan + Hydrochlorothiazide,Co-Aprovel,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GptLDakXFzbYm4hJPYxpKQTFtTerQ8Fp/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-002_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GptLDakXFzbYm4hJPYxpKQTFtTerQ8Fp_view_usp_drivesdk_ea4ec6645b.pdf,page_text/DRP-002_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GptLDakXFzbYm4hJPYxpKQTFtTerQ8Fp_view_usp_drivesdk_ea4ec6645b.json,885d00c3927bb4b0ea7300ea47f2c28c8e12f97fa209e4c3f8f4d50ba8c47710,220266,13,digital_text,"Irbesartan / Hydrochlorothiazide (CoAprovel) 150 mg / 12.5 mg film-coated tablets Peach, biconvex, oval-shaped, with a heart debossed on one side and the number 2875 engraved on the other side. Irbesartan / Hydrochlorothiazide (CoAprovel) 300 mg / 12.5 mg film-coated tablets Peach, biconvex, oval-shaped, with a heart debossed on one side and the number 2876 engraved on the other side. Irbesartan / Hydrochlorothiazide (CoAprovel) 300 mg / 25 mg film-coated tablets Pink, biconvex, oval-shaped, with a heart debossed on one side and the number 2788 engraved on the other side.",1,1,Pharmaceutical Form,"Irbesartan / Hydrochlorothiazide (CoAprovel) is indicated for the treatment of hypertension. It may be used either alone or in combination with other antihypertensive agents (e.g., beta-adrenergic blocking agent, long-acting calcium-channel blocking agent). Irbesartan / Hydrochlorothiazide ( CoAprovel) may also be used as initial therapy in patients who are likely to need multiple drugs to achieve their blood pressure goals.",1,1,Indication,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:11:27.980013+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-006,Glimepiride,Solosa,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZnxRQhZCTuE6HqfqqEJWY5AKEv5Tm7Ru/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-006_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZnxRQhZCTuE6HqfqqEJWY5AKEv5Tm7Ru_view_usp_drivesdk_a19ab5484b.pdf,page_text/DRP-006_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZnxRQhZCTuE6HqfqqEJWY5AKEv5Tm7Ru_view_usp_drivesdk_a19ab5484b.json,36d3f304f323aa4a63c8385ebd477003412629ed376cd09285abb6a3bc302556,350441,4,digital_text,"In healthy persons, the minimum effective oral dose is approx. 0.6 mg. The effect of glimepiride is dose-dependent and reproducible. The physiological response to acute physical exercise, i.e., reduction of insulin secretion, is still present under glimepiride. There was no significant difference in effect regardless of whether the drug was given 30 minutes or immediately before a meal. In diabetic patients, good metabolic control over 24 hours can be achieved with one single dose. Moreover, in a clinical study, good metabolic control was even achieved in 12 out of 16 patients with renal insufficiency (creatinine clearance 4 to 79 ml/min). Although the hydroxy metabolite of glimepiride caused a small but significant decrease in serum glucose in healthy persons, it accounts for only a minor part of the total drug effect. Combination therapy with metformin: In patients not adequately controlled with the maximum dosage of either glimepiride or metformin, combination therapy with both oral antidiabetic agents can be initiated. The improvement in metabolic control in conjunction with combination treatment as compared to treatment with either medicinal product alone has been verified in two studies. Combination therapy with insulin: In patients not adequately controlled with the maximum dosage of glimepiride, concomitant insulin therapy can be initiated. In two studies, the combination achieved the same improvement in metabolic control as insulin alone; however, a lower average dose of insulin was required in combination therapy. [Page 3] 27/05/2022 15:10 - VISTAlink folder 4206689 - Page 2/3 848449 2/4 848449 3/4",2,3,Pharmacodynamic Characteristics,"Non-insulin-dependent (type 2) diabetes mellitus, whenever blood glucose levels cannot be controlled adequately by diet, physical exercise and weight reduction alone.",1,1,Indications,low,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T14:11:31.423112+00:00
