PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-072,Alfuzosin Hydrochloride,Xatral OD,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_o7bn0T1_pTVFuZfi6p-mFFap7gDY_P0/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-072_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_o7bn0T1_pTVFuZfi6p-mFFap7gDY_P0_view_usp_drivesdk_7f10125886.pdf,page_text/DRP-072_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_o7bn0T1_pTVFuZfi6p-mFFap7gDY_P0_view_usp_drivesdk_7f10125886.json,141c3600c1f7bccecc15a7beadfe72d2f744b511cb7f5c63144cb8570c8a3e64,3191793,2,ocr,,,,,section Adverse Reactions). - Treatment of the functional symptoms of benign prostatic Precautions hypertrophy. - Adjunctive treatment for vesical catheterization in acute urinary - Care should be taken when Alfuzosin Hydrochloride (Xatral OD) retention associated with benign prostatic hypertrophy is administered to patients who have had a pronounced hypotensive response to another alpha-1-blocker.,1,1,Indications,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T14:12:28.850522+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-073,CEFACLOR (AS MONOHYDRATE),XEZTRON,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1kxuGg7gzOMpwj4fUZZJldMmLqvmOTHbQ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-073_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kxuGg7gzOMpwj4fUZZJldMmLqvmOTHbQ_view_usp_drivesdk_0306d89676.pdf,page_text/DRP-073_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kxuGg7gzOMpwj4fUZZJldMmLqvmOTHbQ_view_usp_drivesdk_0306d89676.json,941fe97fefc93e38f3d1dab2abd0c4957f48504685d84958e23dfb2f08764677,444664,1,digital_text,"CEFACLOR (as monohydrate), USP…………….........………………250 mg Each 5 mL (1 teaspoonful) contains:",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"plasma half-life of 0.5 to 1 hour has been reported; it may be slightly prolonged in patients with renal impairment. About 25% is bound to plasma proteins. Cefaclor appears to be widely distributed in the body; it crosses the placenta and low concentrations have been detected in breast milk. It is rapidly excreted by the kidneys; up to 85% of a dose appears unchanged in the urine within 8 hours, the greater part within 2 hours. High concentrations of cefaclor are achieved in the urine within 8 hours of a dose; peak concentrations of 600, 900, and 1900 micrograms/mL have been reported after doses of 0.25, 0.5,and 1 g respectively. Probenecid delays excretion. Some cefaclor is removed by haemodialysis. Cefaclor is well absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract. Oral doses of 250 mg, 500 mg, and 1 g produce peak plasma concentrations of about 7, 13, and 23 micrograms/mL respectively after 0.5 to 1 hour. The presence of food may delay the absorption of cefaclor, but the total amount absorbed is unchanged. A PHARMACOKINETICS",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:12:31.716995+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-075,CEFACLOR (AS MONOHYDRATE),XEZTRON,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rC_UBFh_WXPQKujRjXv-eTnpgvgPGu4W/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-075_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rC_UBFh_WXPQKujRjXv-eTnpgvgPGu4W_view_usp_drivesdk_cf73ac9b67.pdf,page_text/DRP-075_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rC_UBFh_WXPQKujRjXv-eTnpgvgPGu4W_view_usp_drivesdk_cf73ac9b67.json,9e5c9494b78012688810440f967a626235fc5a2208583bb459a6dd4975e4374a,444645,1,digital_text,"A white to off-white crystalline powder. Slightly soluble in water; practically insoluble in chloroform, in methyl alcohol, and in benzene. pH of a 2.5% suspension in water is between 3.0 and 4.5. Store in airtight containers. ANTIMICROBIAL ACTION Cefaclor is bactericidal and has antimicrobial activity similar to that of cefalexin but is reported to be more active against Gram-negative bacteria including Escherichia coli, Klebsiella pneumoniae, Neisseria gonorrhoeae, and Proteus mirabilis, and especially against Haemophilus inﬂuenzae. It is active against some beta-lactamase-producing strains of H. inﬂuenzae. It may be less resistant to staphylococcal penicillinase than cefalexin or cefradine and a marked inoculum effect has been reported in vitro. PHARMACOKINETICS Cefaclor is well absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract. Oral doses of 250 mg, 500 mg, and 1 g produce peak plasma concentrations of about 7, 13, and 23 micrograms/mL respectively after 0.5 to 1 hour. The presence of food may delay the absorption of cefaclor, but the total amount absorbed is unchanged. A plasma half-life of 0.5 to 1 hour has been reported; it may be slightly prolonged in patients with renal impairment. About 25% is bound to plasma proteins. Cefaclor appears to be widely distributed in the body; it crosses the placenta and low concentrations have been detected in breast milk. It is rapidly excreted by the kidneys; up to 85% of a dose appears unchanged in the urine within 8 hours, the greater part within 2 hours. High concentrations of cefaclor are achieved in the urine within 8 hours of a dose; peak concentrations of 600, 900, and 1900 micrograms/mL have been reported after doses of 0.25, 0.5,and 1 g respectively. Probenecid delays excretion. Some cefaclor is removed by haemodialysis.",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"For the treatment of susceptible infections including upper and lower respiratory-tract infections, skin infections, and urinary-tract infections.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:12:34.409793+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-078,Cimetidine,Lemecit,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vaGRLfXBtpf8n3WKw2mEfoDJUF0xflU3/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-078_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vaGRLfXBtpf8n3WKw2mEfoDJUF0xflU3_view_usp_drivesdk_96fcaf4f60.pdf,page_text/DRP-078_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vaGRLfXBtpf8n3WKw2mEfoDJUF0xflU3_view_usp_drivesdk_96fcaf4f60.json,ecf295b6ee430caa89a8bca3778a69568ecc5a93f4196b921a6ee6dd441308ca,2096454,1,ocr,"Tell your doctor if you are breasfeeding or plan to breastfeed. Cimetidine (LEMECIT) is a white to off-white round biconvex tablet with score on one side and company logo engraved on Cimetidine has been detected in human breast milk. Because of the possibility for adverse reaction in nursing infants from the other side. cimetidine, a choice should be made whether to stop nursing or to stop use this medication. The importance of the drug to the mother should be considered.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"high pulse rate, dilated pupils, speech disturbance, agitation and disorientation in one patient and respiratory depression in Treatment of duodenal ulcer, benign gastric ulcer, post-operative ulcer, reflux esophagitis, Zollinger-Ellison syndrome and another patient who had chronic schizophenia and was also taking trifluoperazine and hydroxyzine. Also, fatal bradycardia condition where reduction of gastric secretion and acid is desirable, prophylaxis or recurrent hemorrhage from stress has been reported after overdosage with an unknown amount of cimetidine and diazepam. Seek emergency medical attetion right away if you take to much cimetidine. ulceration in patients with bleeding peptic ulcers, prophylaxis of gastrointestinal haemorrhage and before general anesthesia _ in patients at risk of acid aspiration, particularly obstetric patients during labor. Dyspepsia",1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T14:12:44.667345+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-079,Diphenhydramine Hydrochloride,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cbxZ1LHazqNfQRcGSJ1ZWqvgCTTdYVzv/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-079_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cbxZ1LHazqNfQRcGSJ1ZWqvgCTTdYVzv_view_usp_drivesdk_fc1e20c567.pdf,page_text/DRP-079_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cbxZ1LHazqNfQRcGSJ1ZWqvgCTTdYVzv_view_usp_drivesdk_fc1e20c567.json,c59bb63e86dc8c87fc49f24d875c48e18ab9ba45196c39ff7ae58a24c3cee0d4,1483795,1,ocr,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-29T14:13:08.550315+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-079-02,Diphenhydramine Hydrochloride,Hydrafen,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cv9_DJPPpuIC5itCrQMC6_z-8Rs7CLNm/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-079-02_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cv9_DJPPpuIC5itCrQMC6_z-8Rs7CLNm_view_usp_drivesdk_5c6470844b.pdf,page_text/DRP-079-02_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cv9_DJPPpuIC5itCrQMC6_z-8Rs7CLNm_view_usp_drivesdk_5c6470844b.json,2f784b36c3eee8fb2cb23d2963079bf4ba18589875815b98e5bbfce1a628430e,1541783,1,ocr,"Diphenhydramine Hydrochloride (HYDRAFEN) is a clear red syrup with cherry flavor contained ina 60 mL amber round bottle What is in the medicine? This medicine contains Diphenhydramine as hydrochloride which belongs to the sedating class of antihistamines. It reduces the effects of natural chemical histamine in the body. Histamine can produce symptoms of sneezing itching, watery eyes, and runny nose. It acts as a cough suppressant through its effect on the cough center in the brain, likewise as an antiemetic, it acts by suppressing the vomiting center in the brain Strength of the medicine Each 5 milliliter (1 teaspoonful) of the syrup contains 12.5 m Diphenhydramine HCI, USP Ethyl Alcohol 0.89% What is this medicine used fo: Diphenhydramine Hydrochloride is used for control of vasomotor rhinitis, hay fever, urticaria, angioneurotic edema, drug sensitization, serum and penicillin reaction, contact dermatitis, atopic eczema and other allergic states responsive to antihistamines. Also indicated for the active treatment of motion sickness (it should be given at least 30 minutes before travelling), and in the treatment of vertigo. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Children (over 9 kgs of body weight! 1 Adu mL (1-2 teaspoonfuls), 3-4 times daily, maximum dose not to exceed 300 mg 20 mL (4 teaspoonfuls), 3-4 times daily Or as prescribed by the physician When should you not take this medicine? -Should not be given to patients with allergy to any ingredient in the product -It should not be given to infants and nursing mothers (pregnant or breastfeeding) -Patient taking medicines for depression Care that should be taken when taking this medicine -Care must take place to patient that requires mental alertness (e.g. driving or operating machines). -Do not take more than the recommended dose. -Should be used with care in conditions such as angle-closure glaucoma, urinary retention, prostatic hyperplasia, or pyloroduodenal obstruction. Undesirable effects of this medicine Undesirable effect with sedating antihistamine including Diphenhydramine HCI is CNS depression, with effects varying from slight drowsiness to deep sleep, and including lassitude, dizziness, and incoordination Other undesirable effects include muscle weakness, gastrointestinal discomfort, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea or constipation, dryness of the mouth, nose, throat, ringing in the ears, visual disturbances, blurred vision, insomnia tremor, nervousness, dizziness, headache, irritability, chest tightness, increased or decreased blood pressure, palpitation, tachycardia (rapid heart rate), arrhythmia (irregular heart beat), and photosensitivity. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Diphenhydramine HCI may enhance the sedative effects of CNS depressants including alcohol, barbiturates, hypnotics, opioid analgesics, anxiolytic sedatives, and antipsychotics. It also has an additive antimuscarinic action with other antimuscarinic drugs, such as atropine and some antidepressants (both tricyclics and MAOIs). What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose Overdosage is associated with antimuscarinic, extrapyramidal and CNS effects. When CNS stimulation predominates over CNS depression, which is more likely in children or the elderly, it causes ataxia, excitement, tremors, psychoses, hallucinations and convulsions; hyperpyrexia may also occur. Deepening coma and cardiorespiratory collapse may follow. In adults, CNS depression is more common with drowsiness, coma, and convulsion, progressing to respiratory failure and cardiovascular collapse What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? If symptoms persist or any undesirable effects occur, consult your doctor. Rags suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph.” See ly at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration No.: DRP-079-02 Date of Renewal Authorization: February 15, 2022 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: March 16, 2022 Manufactured by the oe: Distributed by Marketing Authorization Holder: FULL HEALTH INTERNATIONAL PHARMA",1,1,Description of the product,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T14:12:53.028380+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-079-02,Diphenhydramine Hydrochloride,Hydrafen,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1tR86rHoxJk-eNbUuWKKeIKMPIXcBYXt_/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-079-02_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1tR86rHoxJk-eNbUuWKKeIKMPIXcBYXt__view_usp_drivesdk_526fb2ca33.pdf,page_text/DRP-079-02_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1tR86rHoxJk-eNbUuWKKeIKMPIXcBYXt__view_usp_drivesdk_526fb2ca33.json,2f784b36c3eee8fb2cb23d2963079bf4ba18589875815b98e5bbfce1a628430e,1541783,1,ocr,"Diphenhydramine Hydrochloride (HYDRAFEN) is a clear red syrup with cherry flavor contained ina 60 mL amber round bottle What is in the medicine? This medicine contains Diphenhydramine as hydrochloride which belongs to the sedating class of antihistamines. It reduces the effects of natural chemical histamine in the body. Histamine can produce symptoms of sneezing itching, watery eyes, and runny nose. It acts as a cough suppressant through its effect on the cough center in the brain, likewise as an antiemetic, it acts by suppressing the vomiting center in the brain Strength of the medicine Each 5 milliliter (1 teaspoonful) of the syrup contains 12.5 m Diphenhydramine HCI, USP Ethyl Alcohol 0.89% What is this medicine used fo: Diphenhydramine Hydrochloride is used for control of vasomotor rhinitis, hay fever, urticaria, angioneurotic edema, drug sensitization, serum and penicillin reaction, contact dermatitis, atopic eczema and other allergic states responsive to antihistamines. Also indicated for the active treatment of motion sickness (it should be given at least 30 minutes before travelling), and in the treatment of vertigo. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Children (over 9 kgs of body weight! 1 Adu mL (1-2 teaspoonfuls), 3-4 times daily, maximum dose not to exceed 300 mg 20 mL (4 teaspoonfuls), 3-4 times daily Or as prescribed by the physician When should you not take this medicine? -Should not be given to patients with allergy to any ingredient in the product -It should not be given to infants and nursing mothers (pregnant or breastfeeding) -Patient taking medicines for depression Care that should be taken when taking this medicine -Care must take place to patient that requires mental alertness (e.g. driving or operating machines). -Do not take more than the recommended dose. -Should be used with care in conditions such as angle-closure glaucoma, urinary retention, prostatic hyperplasia, or pyloroduodenal obstruction. Undesirable effects of this medicine Undesirable effect with sedating antihistamine including Diphenhydramine HCI is CNS depression, with effects varying from slight drowsiness to deep sleep, and including lassitude, dizziness, and incoordination Other undesirable effects include muscle weakness, gastrointestinal discomfort, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea or constipation, dryness of the mouth, nose, throat, ringing in the ears, visual disturbances, blurred vision, insomnia tremor, nervousness, dizziness, headache, irritability, chest tightness, increased or decreased blood pressure, palpitation, tachycardia (rapid heart rate), arrhythmia (irregular heart beat), and photosensitivity. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Diphenhydramine HCI may enhance the sedative effects of CNS depressants including alcohol, barbiturates, hypnotics, opioid analgesics, anxiolytic sedatives, and antipsychotics. It also has an additive antimuscarinic action with other antimuscarinic drugs, such as atropine and some antidepressants (both tricyclics and MAOIs). What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose Overdosage is associated with antimuscarinic, extrapyramidal and CNS effects. When CNS stimulation predominates over CNS depression, which is more likely in children or the elderly, it causes ataxia, excitement, tremors, psychoses, hallucinations and convulsions; hyperpyrexia may also occur. Deepening coma and cardiorespiratory collapse may follow. In adults, CNS depression is more common with drowsiness, coma, and convulsion, progressing to respiratory failure and cardiovascular collapse What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? If symptoms persist or any undesirable effects occur, consult your doctor. Rags suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph.” See ly at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration No.: DRP-079-02 Date of Renewal Authorization: February 15, 2022 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: March 16, 2022 Manufactured by the oe: Distributed by Marketing Authorization Holder: FULL HEALTH INTERNATIONAL PHARMA",1,1,Description of the product,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T14:13:00.935851+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-086,Cefaclor (As Monohydrate),Cefmed,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vjq2nWwZL6aa9hj97eHYZzTruYF1Qiou/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-086_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vjq2nWwZL6aa9hj97eHYZzTruYF1Qiou_view_usp_drivesdk_fb70d2f3e5.pdf,page_text/DRP-086_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vjq2nWwZL6aa9hj97eHYZzTruYF1Qiou_view_usp_drivesdk_fb70d2f3e5.json,c551567174495922a42cd89d911003d12d0cf31913f3083ea014824a10e078ab,427577,1,digital_text,"Cefaclor is white to off-white, strawberry flavored granules for suspension. Reconstituted suspension is pinkish-red in color. CEFMED (cefaclor monohydrate) is a semisynthetic cephalosporin antibiotic for oral administration. Like other cephalosporins is an inhibitor of bacterial cell wall synthesis. It acylates membrane-bound transpeptidase enzymes thus preventing the cross- linking of peptidoglycan necessary for bacterial cell wall strength and rigidity. The chemical formula for Cefaclor is C15H14ClN3O4S.H2O and the molecular weight is 385.82. Cefaclor monohydrate is a white to off white crystalline powder, slightly soluble in water, but is insoluble in alcohol and chloroform.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Treatment of susceptible infections including upper and lower respiratory tract infections, skin infections and urinary tract infections. Upper respiratory infections, including pharyngitis, tonsillitis and otitis media. Skin and skin structure infections. Urinary tract infections, including pyelonephritis and cystitis.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:13:17.380123+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-086-02,Cefaclor (as Monohydrate),Aclor,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/17d3GlGZ2FXS0zRo2S0YAX2SUC0asgQQq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-086-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17d3GlGZ2FXS0zRo2S0YAX2SUC0asgQQq_view_usp_drivesdk_e1f12034a3.pdf,page_text/DRP-086-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17d3GlGZ2FXS0zRo2S0YAX2SUC0asgQQq_view_usp_drivesdk_e1f12034a3.json,5b8e6d2634cbb46815662aad9bd06b46ab2efd0ea85c9e57684e153a977d5d1d,617836,1,digital_text,"Cefaclor is off-white to pinkish white, free flowing strawberry flavored granules for suspension. Reconstituted product is a pink suspension.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Treatment of susceptible infections including upper and lower respiratory tract infections, skin infections and urinary tract infections. Upper respiratory infections, including pharyngitis, tonsillitis and otitis media. Skin and skin structure infections. Urinary tract infections, including pyelonephritis and cystitis.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:13:11.132221+00:00
