PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-094,Amoxicillin (as trihydrate),Axmel,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NUO0y5prW6FZqCNTBglLeCdTvjnPEURA/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-094_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1NUO0y5prW6FZqCNTBglLeCdTvjnPEURA_view_usp_drivesdk_57b7503390.pdf,page_text/DRP-094_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1NUO0y5prW6FZqCNTBglLeCdTvjnPEURA_view_usp_drivesdk_57b7503390.json,8d882cda85d7c4fc2f314325fd328f540c1f0d6505faeb535a3e74e69d63c051,483882,1,digital_text,Amoxicillin (Axmel) 500 mg Capsule is a white to yellowish white powder contained in a red/white hard gelatin capsule. Amoxicillin (Axmel) 250 mg Capsule is a white to yellowish white powder contained in a red/white hard gelatin capsule. Amoxicillin (Axmel) 250 mg/5 mL Powder for Suspension is a white to yellowish white powder and light yellow suspension upon reconstitution with characteristic of pineapple ﬂavor. Amoxicillin (Axmel) 125 mg/5 mL Powder for Suspension is a white to yellowish white powder and light yellow to yellow suspension upon reconstitution with characteristic of pineapple ﬂavor. Amoxicillin (Axmel) 100 mg/mL Powder for Suspension (Oral Drops) is a white to yellowish white powder and a very light yellow to light yellow suspension upon reconstitution with characteristic of pineapple ﬂavor.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,For the treatment of infections caused by susceptible strains of Gram-positive and Gram-negative microorganisms. • Acute bacterial sinusitis • Acute otitis media • Acute streptococcal tonsillitis and pharyngitis • Acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis • Community acquired pneumonia • Acute cystitis • Asymptomatic bacteriuria in pregnancy • Acute pyelonephritis • Typhoid and paratyphoid fever • Dental abscess with spreading cellulitis • Prosthetic joint infections • Helicobacter pylori eradication,1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:13:56.991307+00:00
