PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-096,Cefalexin (as monohydrate),Exel,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1G3HZ8jqJ7yMzhDLmzCa_htcCpzPFXl60/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-096_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1G3HZ8jqJ7yMzhDLmzCa_htcCpzPFXl60_view_usp_drivesdk_10faff1484.pdf,page_text/DRP-096_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1G3HZ8jqJ7yMzhDLmzCa_htcCpzPFXl60_view_usp_drivesdk_10faff1484.json,85acfc9bbbdd00a7f1a47637f4e18af3b678d3b8f6cb8135db334a0764a16aa3,79358,1,digital_text,"Cefalexin (Exel) 500 mg Capsule is a white to oﬀ-white crystalline powder contained in gray/yellow rich hard gelatin capsule. Cefalexin (Exel) 250 mg Capsule is a white to oﬀ-white powder contained in scarlet/gray hard gelatin capsule. Cefalexin (Exel) 250 mg/5 mL Powder for Suspension is a white to oﬀ-white powder, and very light to light orange suspension upon reconstitution, orange ﬂavored, and with characteristic odor. Cefalexin (Exel) 125 mg/5 mL Powder for Suspension is a white to white-cream powder, and light orange to orange suspension upon reconstitution, orange ﬂavored and with characteristic odor. Cefalexin (Exel) 100 mg/mL Powder for Suspension (Oral Drops) is a white to oﬀ- white powder, peach to light orange suspension upon reconstitution, orange ﬂavored and with characteristic odor.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"the following conditions, when caused by susceptible bacteria. Respiratory tract infections, Acute and chronic bronchitis and infected bronchiectasis. Ear, nose and throat infections: Otitis media, mastoiditis, sinusitis, follicular tonsillitis and pharyngitis. Urinary tract infections: Acute and chronic pyelonephritis, cystitis and prostatitis. Prophylaxis of recurrent urinary tract infection. Gynaecological and obstetric infections Skin, soft -tissue and bone infections. DOSAGE AND MODE OF",1,1,INDICATION: It is indicated for treatment of,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:14:03.698030+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-097,Amoxicillin (as trihydrate),Axmel,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Q32UbVwCIG6H7bWJyP_l0RIfM848HXlV/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-097_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Q32UbVwCIG6H7bWJyP_l0RIfM848HXlV_view_usp_drivesdk_6269a7b49c.pdf,page_text/DRP-097_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Q32UbVwCIG6H7bWJyP_l0RIfM848HXlV_view_usp_drivesdk_6269a7b49c.json,8d882cda85d7c4fc2f314325fd328f540c1f0d6505faeb535a3e74e69d63c051,483882,1,digital_text,Amoxicillin (Axmel) 500 mg Capsule is a white to yellowish white powder contained in a red/white hard gelatin capsule. Amoxicillin (Axmel) 250 mg Capsule is a white to yellowish white powder contained in a red/white hard gelatin capsule. Amoxicillin (Axmel) 250 mg/5 mL Powder for Suspension is a white to yellowish white powder and light yellow suspension upon reconstitution with characteristic of pineapple ﬂavor. Amoxicillin (Axmel) 125 mg/5 mL Powder for Suspension is a white to yellowish white powder and light yellow to yellow suspension upon reconstitution with characteristic of pineapple ﬂavor. Amoxicillin (Axmel) 100 mg/mL Powder for Suspension (Oral Drops) is a white to yellowish white powder and a very light yellow to light yellow suspension upon reconstitution with characteristic of pineapple ﬂavor.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,For the treatment of infections caused by susceptible strains of Gram-positive and Gram-negative microorganisms. • Acute bacterial sinusitis • Acute otitis media • Acute streptococcal tonsillitis and pharyngitis • Acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis • Community acquired pneumonia • Acute cystitis • Asymptomatic bacteriuria in pregnancy • Acute pyelonephritis • Typhoid and paratyphoid fever • Dental abscess with spreading cellulitis • Prosthetic joint infections • Helicobacter pylori eradication,1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:14:08.109279+00:00
