PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10046,Pantoprazole (as sodium sesquihydrate) + Domperidone,Pantec-DSR,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1t05FIntUrIqeUn2SF9pWyaGh2ct1hXPo/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10046_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1t05FIntUrIqeUn2SF9pWyaGh2ct1hXPo_view_usp_drivesdk_f7e9dbb45d.pdf,page_text/DRP-10046_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1t05FIntUrIqeUn2SF9pWyaGh2ct1hXPo_view_usp_drivesdk_f7e9dbb45d.json,e6189450623569e469062e0249584862b3a37533b665c304ed76d619afcce3d1,1472932,1,digital_text,"Pantoprazole Sodium is a white to off - white crystalline powder and is racemic. Pantoprazole has weakly basic and acidic properties. Pantoprazole sodium is freely soluble in water, very slightly soluble in phosphate buffer at pH 7.4 and practically insoluble in n-hexane. Domperidone is almost a white powder; practically insoluble in water, slightly soluble in alcohol and methyl alcohol and solubl e in dimethylformamide. Clinical Pharmacology: Pantoprazole is a proton pump inhibitor (PPI). It suppresses the terminal step in gastric acis production by covalently binding to the (H+,K+)-ATPase enzyme system at the sectary surface of the gastric parietal cell. This leads to inhibition of both basal and stimulated gastric acid secretion, irrespective of stimulus. It is a weak base and it is highly ionized at low pH. Domperidone is a benzimidazole derivative. It acts by selectively antagonizing the peripheal dopaminergic D2 receptors in the gastrointestinal wall, thereby enhancing gastrointestinal peristalsis and motility and increasing lower esophageal sphincter (LES) tone.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"Symptomatic management of burning in various acid peptic disorders associated with nausea and vomiting; GERO, reflux esophagitis, non-ulcer dyspepsia, gastroparesis and idiopathic hiccup or any other peptic disease accompanied by nausea and/or vomiting (e.g. acute gastritis including that induced by NSAIDs).",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:14:33.437350+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10051,Ketorolac Trometamol,Ketorz,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oRNnevr70cw9t7X7rWjTpn2gNV_lnKYM/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10051_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oRNnevr70cw9t7X7rWjTpn2gNV_lnKYM_view_usp_drivesdk_f25e9d4838.pdf,page_text/DRP-10051_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oRNnevr70cw9t7X7rWjTpn2gNV_lnKYM_view_usp_drivesdk_f25e9d4838.json,9ffdee06fca346be608e0eb06491b8a9ed50d897a9b9114eba5ae2b51f7110e1,1446845,2,digital_text,"Ketorolac trometamol injection USP is a member of the pyrrolo-pyrrole group of nonsteroidal anti-inﬂammatory drugs (NSAIDs). The chemical name for ketorolac trometamol is (±)-5-benzoyl-2,3-dihydro-IH-pyrrolizine- 1-carboxylic acid, compound with 2-amino-2-(hydroxymethyl)-1 ,3-propanediol (I: I), and the chemical Structure is: Ketorolac trometamol is a racemic mixture of [-]S and [+]R ketorolac trometamol. Ketorolac trometamol may exist in three crystal forms. All forms are equally soluble in water. Ketorolac trometamol has a pKa of 3.5 and an n-octanol/water partition coeﬃcient of 0.26. The molecular weight of Ketorolac trometamol is 376.41. Its molecular formula is C H N O .19 24 2 6 Ketorolac trometamol Injection USP is available for intravenous (IV) or intramuscular (IM) administration as: 15 mg in 1 mL (1.5%) and 30 mg in I mL (3%) in sterile solution; 60 mg in 2 mL(3%) of ketorolac trometamol in sterile solution is available for IM administration only. The solutions contain 0.1% citric acid, I 0% (w/v) Ethanol absolute, USP, and 6.68 mg, 4.35 mg and 8.70 mg, respectively, of sodium chloride in sterile water. The pH is adjusted with sodium hydroxide or hydrochloric acid. The sterile solutions are clear and slightly yellow in colour.",1,1,DRUG DESCRIPTION,"Indications: Ketorolac Injection is indicated for the short-term management of moderate to severe acute post-operative pain. Acute Pain in Adult Patients Ketorolac trometamol is indicated for the short-term (≤5 days) management of moderately severe acute pain that requires analgesia at the opioid level, usually in a postoperative setting. Therapy should always be initiated with intravenous or intramuscular dosing of ketorolac trometamol, and oral ketorolac trometamol is to be used only as continuation treatment, if necessary. The total combined duration of use of ketorolac trometamol injection and oral ketorolac trometamol is not to exceed 5 days of use because of the potential of increasing the frequency and the severity of adverse reactions associated with the recommended doses Patients should be switched to alternative analgesics as soon as possible, but ketorolac trometamol therapy is not to exceed 5 days. Ketorolac trometamol injection has been used concomitantly with morphine and meperidine and has shown an opioid- sparing eﬀect. For breakthrough pain, it is recommended to supplement the lower end of the ketorolac trometamol injection dosage range with low doses of narcotics when necessary, unless otherwise contraindicated. Ketorolac trometamol injection and narcotics should not be administered in the same syringe.",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T14:14:37.165510+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10052,Ketorolac Trometamol,Ketorz,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1A14eRd7qRyZHG41tTyi3YltRxydjCe_t/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10052_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1A14eRd7qRyZHG41tTyi3YltRxydjCe_t_view_usp_drivesdk_6e848a0d7e.pdf,page_text/DRP-10052_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1A14eRd7qRyZHG41tTyi3YltRxydjCe_t_view_usp_drivesdk_6e848a0d7e.json,9ffdee06fca346be608e0eb06491b8a9ed50d897a9b9114eba5ae2b51f7110e1,1446845,2,digital_text,"Ketorolac trometamol injection USP is a member of the pyrrolo-pyrrole group of nonsteroidal anti-inﬂammatory drugs (NSAIDs). The chemical name for ketorolac trometamol is (±)-5-benzoyl-2,3-dihydro-IH-pyrrolizine- 1-carboxylic acid, compound with 2-amino-2-(hydroxymethyl)-1 ,3-propanediol (I: I), and the chemical Structure is: Ketorolac trometamol is a racemic mixture of [-]S and [+]R ketorolac trometamol. Ketorolac trometamol may exist in three crystal forms. All forms are equally soluble in water. Ketorolac trometamol has a pKa of 3.5 and an n-octanol/water partition coeﬃcient of 0.26. The molecular weight of Ketorolac trometamol is 376.41. Its molecular formula is C H N O .19 24 2 6 Ketorolac trometamol Injection USP is available for intravenous (IV) or intramuscular (IM) administration as: 15 mg in 1 mL (1.5%) and 30 mg in I mL (3%) in sterile solution; 60 mg in 2 mL(3%) of ketorolac trometamol in sterile solution is available for IM administration only. The solutions contain 0.1% citric acid, I 0% (w/v) Ethanol absolute, USP, and 6.68 mg, 4.35 mg and 8.70 mg, respectively, of sodium chloride in sterile water. The pH is adjusted with sodium hydroxide or hydrochloric acid. The sterile solutions are clear and slightly yellow in colour.",1,1,DRUG DESCRIPTION,"Indications: Ketorolac Injection is indicated for the short-term management of moderate to severe acute post-operative pain. Acute Pain in Adult Patients Ketorolac trometamol is indicated for the short-term (≤5 days) management of moderately severe acute pain that requires analgesia at the opioid level, usually in a postoperative setting. Therapy should always be initiated with intravenous or intramuscular dosing of ketorolac trometamol, and oral ketorolac trometamol is to be used only as continuation treatment, if necessary. The total combined duration of use of ketorolac trometamol injection and oral ketorolac trometamol is not to exceed 5 days of use because of the potential of increasing the frequency and the severity of adverse reactions associated with the recommended doses Patients should be switched to alternative analgesics as soon as possible, but ketorolac trometamol therapy is not to exceed 5 days. Ketorolac trometamol injection has been used concomitantly with morphine and meperidine and has shown an opioid- sparing eﬀect. For breakthrough pain, it is recommended to supplement the lower end of the ketorolac trometamol injection dosage range with low doses of narcotics when necessary, unless otherwise contraindicated. Ketorolac trometamol injection and narcotics should not be administered in the same syringe.",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T14:14:40.407606+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10053,Ketorolac Trometamol,Ketorz,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/125Vu1LobWQrPYGfWX0A04ta6pD2CIXxl/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10053_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_125Vu1LobWQrPYGfWX0A04ta6pD2CIXxl_view_usp_drivesdk_aa13dca448.pdf,page_text/DRP-10053_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_125Vu1LobWQrPYGfWX0A04ta6pD2CIXxl_view_usp_drivesdk_aa13dca448.json,9ffdee06fca346be608e0eb06491b8a9ed50d897a9b9114eba5ae2b51f7110e1,1446845,2,digital_text,"Ketorolac trometamol injection USP is a member of the pyrrolo-pyrrole group of nonsteroidal anti-inﬂammatory drugs (NSAIDs). The chemical name for ketorolac trometamol is (±)-5-benzoyl-2,3-dihydro-IH-pyrrolizine- 1-carboxylic acid, compound with 2-amino-2-(hydroxymethyl)-1 ,3-propanediol (I: I), and the chemical Structure is: Ketorolac trometamol is a racemic mixture of [-]S and [+]R ketorolac trometamol. Ketorolac trometamol may exist in three crystal forms. All forms are equally soluble in water. Ketorolac trometamol has a pKa of 3.5 and an n-octanol/water partition coeﬃcient of 0.26. The molecular weight of Ketorolac trometamol is 376.41. Its molecular formula is C H N O .19 24 2 6 Ketorolac trometamol Injection USP is available for intravenous (IV) or intramuscular (IM) administration as: 15 mg in 1 mL (1.5%) and 30 mg in I mL (3%) in sterile solution; 60 mg in 2 mL(3%) of ketorolac trometamol in sterile solution is available for IM administration only. The solutions contain 0.1% citric acid, I 0% (w/v) Ethanol absolute, USP, and 6.68 mg, 4.35 mg and 8.70 mg, respectively, of sodium chloride in sterile water. The pH is adjusted with sodium hydroxide or hydrochloric acid. The sterile solutions are clear and slightly yellow in colour.",1,1,DRUG DESCRIPTION,"Indications: Ketorolac Injection is indicated for the short-term management of moderate to severe acute post-operative pain. Acute Pain in Adult Patients Ketorolac trometamol is indicated for the short-term (≤5 days) management of moderately severe acute pain that requires analgesia at the opioid level, usually in a postoperative setting. Therapy should always be initiated with intravenous or intramuscular dosing of ketorolac trometamol, and oral ketorolac trometamol is to be used only as continuation treatment, if necessary. The total combined duration of use of ketorolac trometamol injection and oral ketorolac trometamol is not to exceed 5 days of use because of the potential of increasing the frequency and the severity of adverse reactions associated with the recommended doses Patients should be switched to alternative analgesics as soon as possible, but ketorolac trometamol therapy is not to exceed 5 days. Ketorolac trometamol injection has been used concomitantly with morphine and meperidine and has shown an opioid- sparing eﬀect. For breakthrough pain, it is recommended to supplement the lower end of the ketorolac trometamol injection dosage range with low doses of narcotics when necessary, unless otherwise contraindicated. Ketorolac trometamol injection and narcotics should not be administered in the same syringe.",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T14:14:43.746236+00:00
