PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10062,Bicalutamide,Casodex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Qs5jX-ccmdA4OM-uukU-6u8SfspJ8-7E/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10062_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Qs5jX-ccmdA4OM-uukU-6u8SfspJ8-7E_view_usp_drivesdk_0fd3d95080.pdf,page_text/DRP-10062_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Qs5jX-ccmdA4OM-uukU-6u8SfspJ8-7E_view_usp_drivesdk_0fd3d95080.json,77cabca715853a94ecc3769d375fbd5f202cee99bfce408455bf8388df7e8af5,189099,9,digital_text,"White film-coated tablet. 4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 4.1 Therapeutic indications Treatment of advanced prostate cancer in combination with luteinizing-hormone releasing hormone (LHRH) analogue therapy or surgical castration. 4.2 Dosage and method of administration Adult males including the elderly: one tablet (50 mg) once a day. Treatment with Bicalutamide (CASODEX) should be started at least 3 days before commencing treatment with an LHRH analogue, or at t he same time as surgical castration. Renal impairment: no dosage adjustment i s necessary for patients with renal impairment. Hepatic impairment: no dosage adjustment i s necessary f or patients with mild hepatic impairment. Increased accumulation may occur in patients with moderate to severe hepatic impairment (see section 4.4 Special warnings and precautions for use). Paediatric population: Bicalutamide (CASODEX) is contraindicated for use in children (see section 4.3 Contraindications). [Page 2]",1,1,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,Treatment of advanced prostate cancer in combination with luteinizing-hormone releasing hormone (LHRH) analogue therapy or surgical castration.,1,1,4.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:15:27.603711+00:00
