PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10183,Ascorbic Acid (As Sodium Ascorbate) + Zinc (As Sulfate Monohydrate),Vitcee Plus,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1q9zxzNpW_GDYLagnL7wacTFhf3LJK4tW/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10183_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1q9zxzNpW_GDYLagnL7wacTFhf3LJK4tW_view_usp_drivesdk_ffd671bd45.pdf,page_text/DRP-10183_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1q9zxzNpW_GDYLagnL7wacTFhf3LJK4tW_view_usp_drivesdk_ffd671bd45.json,53bb99db5592dedb35102220bbb156d098848677c87801671283fa1ca3d8eab1,530362,1,ocr,"The medicine is a white crystalline powder contained in a Brown/Brown size #0, blister pack by 10’s, box of 30 Capsules / blister pack by 10’s, box of 100 Capsules. What is in the medicine? This medicine contains a combination of Ascorbic Acid and Zinc Sulfate. Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C) is a water soluble vitamin which is essential for the synthesis of collagen and intercellular material. Zinc Sulfate helps regulate the activity of cells involved in immune function. Strength of the medicine: Sodium Ascorbate ....... Each capsule contains: e sessseeeeeees 962.40 mg quivalent to 500 mg Ascorbic Acid) ~ 2 inc Sulfate Monohydrate 55 mg (equivalent to 20 mg elemental Zinc) What is this medicine used for? It is used for the prevention and treatment of Vitamin C and Zinc deficiencies. How much and how often should you use this medicine for? Take 1 — 2 capsules a day, or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? If you are allergic to any components of the medicine. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: recommended dose. It should be given care to patients with excessive calcium oxalate kidney stones (hyperoxaluria). Do not take more than the Undesirable effects of this medicine: Vitamin C is usually well tolerated, however when given in high doses greater than 1g or more daily it causes diarrhea and gastrointestinal disturbances. Zinc may cause gastrointestinal disturbance that includes abdominal pain, dyspepsia, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, gastric irritation, and gastritis. This may be reduced by giving them meals before taking the medicine. What other medicine or food should be avoided? The amount of nutrients in the product is not expected to interact with food of medicine. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: Prolonged intake of Vitamin C greater than 2g daily may lead to nausea, abdominal cramps, diarrhea and nose bleeding. Prolonged use of hi h zinc doses (4-8 grams elemental zinc) may cause nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, metallic taste, fever, and lethargy (sleepiness). ) What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? Treatment with zinc overdosa includes of ving milk or alkali carbonates and activated charcoal. The use of emetics or gastric lavage should be avoi ded . Generally, gi you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C Protect from direct sunlight When should ou consult your doctor? If any undesiral 4 le effects occur, consult your doctor. “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph.” Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration number: DRP-10183 Date of Renewal Authorization: August 3, 2021 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: October 20, 2021 Manufactured by the Distributed by: Marketing Authorization Holder:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T14:17:46.226449+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10183,Ascorbic Acid (As Sodium Ascorbate) + Zinc (As Sulfate Monohydrate),Vitcee Plus,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vV5jMy2Y9a3NzE5ZdGSCti-7lEbYB54D/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10183_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vV5jMy2Y9a3NzE5ZdGSCti-7lEbYB54D_view_usp_drivesdk_d8094fc8a5.pdf,page_text/DRP-10183_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vV5jMy2Y9a3NzE5ZdGSCti-7lEbYB54D_view_usp_drivesdk_d8094fc8a5.json,53bb99db5592dedb35102220bbb156d098848677c87801671283fa1ca3d8eab1,530362,1,ocr,"The medicine is a white crystalline powder contained in a Brown/Brown size #0, blister pack by 10’s, box of 30 Capsules / blister pack by 10’s, box of 100 Capsules. What is in the medicine? This medicine contains a combination of Ascorbic Acid and Zinc Sulfate. Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C) is a water soluble vitamin which is essential for the synthesis of collagen and intercellular material. Zinc Sulfate helps regulate the activity of cells involved in immune function. Strength of the medicine: Sodium Ascorbate ....... Each capsule contains: e sessseeeeeees 962.40 mg quivalent to 500 mg Ascorbic Acid) ~ 2 inc Sulfate Monohydrate 55 mg (equivalent to 20 mg elemental Zinc) What is this medicine used for? It is used for the prevention and treatment of Vitamin C and Zinc deficiencies. How much and how often should you use this medicine for? Take 1 — 2 capsules a day, or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? If you are allergic to any components of the medicine. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: recommended dose. It should be given care to patients with excessive calcium oxalate kidney stones (hyperoxaluria). Do not take more than the Undesirable effects of this medicine: Vitamin C is usually well tolerated, however when given in high doses greater than 1g or more daily it causes diarrhea and gastrointestinal disturbances. Zinc may cause gastrointestinal disturbance that includes abdominal pain, dyspepsia, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, gastric irritation, and gastritis. This may be reduced by giving them meals before taking the medicine. What other medicine or food should be avoided? The amount of nutrients in the product is not expected to interact with food of medicine. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: Prolonged intake of Vitamin C greater than 2g daily may lead to nausea, abdominal cramps, diarrhea and nose bleeding. Prolonged use of hi h zinc doses (4-8 grams elemental zinc) may cause nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, metallic taste, fever, and lethargy (sleepiness). ) What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? Treatment with zinc overdosa includes of ving milk or alkali carbonates and activated charcoal. The use of emetics or gastric lavage should be avoi ded . Generally, gi you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C Protect from direct sunlight When should ou consult your doctor? If any undesiral 4 le effects occur, consult your doctor. “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph.” Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration number: DRP-10183 Date of Renewal Authorization: August 3, 2021 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: October 20, 2021 Manufactured by the Distributed by: Marketing Authorization Holder:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T14:17:54.111983+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10192,Gemcitabine (as Hydrochloride),Gempower,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Fom6YHhO_Sikh0ng0-meY-mK5LrszJNL/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10192_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Fom6YHhO_Sikh0ng0-meY-mK5LrszJNL_view_usp_drivesdk_74996a7361.pdf,page_text/DRP-10192_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Fom6YHhO_Sikh0ng0-meY-mK5LrszJNL_view_usp_drivesdk_74996a7361.json,0748add4fac314e7a2e8c3f91c212233834635ec360f15bf2ccb1a301d8122b8,1356158,2,digital_text,Gemcitabine HCI is a novel nucleoside (deoxycytidine) analogue. monohydrochloride (b-isomer). 9 11 2 3 4 Molecular weight : 299.66 C H F N O HCI Date of Authorization: 03 AUG 2021 Date of leaﬂet revision: 10 AUG 2021 22945-2 MEI-GG242023 [Page 2] Gemcitabine is contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to the drug.,1,2,DESCRIPTION :,"Dilution : Diluent for reconstitution of gemcitabine is 0.9% Sodium chloride injection without preservatives. Because of solubility considerations, the maximum concentration for gemcitabine upon reconstitution is 40mg/mL, avoid reconstitutions at concentrations > 40mg/mL. This may lead to incomplete reconstitution. Chloride injection to the 1-g vial. Shake to dissolve. These dilutions each yield a gemcitabine concentration of 40mg/mL. The appropriate amount of drug may be administered as prepared by further diluting with 0.9% sodium chloride injection to concentration as low as 0.1mg/mL. [Page 3]",2,2,used.,low,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T14:17:58.233346+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10193,Gemcitabine (as Hydrochloride),Gempower,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1g8XRJF4o6hg2VDvS6scmNeTYA4AOzAJ1/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10193_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1g8XRJF4o6hg2VDvS6scmNeTYA4AOzAJ1_view_usp_drivesdk_8ff546135b.pdf,page_text/DRP-10193_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1g8XRJF4o6hg2VDvS6scmNeTYA4AOzAJ1_view_usp_drivesdk_8ff546135b.json,0748add4fac314e7a2e8c3f91c212233834635ec360f15bf2ccb1a301d8122b8,1356158,2,digital_text,Gemcitabine HCI is a novel nucleoside (deoxycytidine) analogue. monohydrochloride (b-isomer). 9 11 2 3 4 Molecular weight : 299.66 C H F N O HCI Date of Authorization: 03 AUG 2021 Date of leaﬂet revision: 10 AUG 2021 22945-2 MEI-GG242023 [Page 2] Gemcitabine is contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to the drug.,1,2,DESCRIPTION :,"Dilution : Diluent for reconstitution of gemcitabine is 0.9% Sodium chloride injection without preservatives. Because of solubility considerations, the maximum concentration for gemcitabine upon reconstitution is 40mg/mL, avoid reconstitutions at concentrations > 40mg/mL. This may lead to incomplete reconstitution. Chloride injection to the 1-g vial. Shake to dissolve. These dilutions each yield a gemcitabine concentration of 40mg/mL. The appropriate amount of drug may be administered as prepared by further diluting with 0.9% sodium chloride injection to concentration as low as 0.1mg/mL. [Page 3]",2,2,used.,low,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T14:18:01.553434+00:00
