PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10199-09,Trimetazidine Hydrochloride,Amtaz,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/18sB-Yy3XEkDdmYWyKsIaApqwOCweGvTo/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10199-09_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18sB-Yy3XEkDdmYWyKsIaApqwOCweGvTo_view_usp_drivesdk_07011d425d.pdf,page_text/DRP-10199-09_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18sB-Yy3XEkDdmYWyKsIaApqwOCweGvTo_view_usp_drivesdk_07011d425d.json,49ac482912da97bf21334f5eda63c462519ef0f811404a76087e5268ea701d3a,503910,1,digital_text,,1,1,"PRODUCT DESCRIPTION: White, circular, biconvex tablet plain on both sides.","angina pectoris (chest pain caused by coronary disease). DOSAGE AND MODE/ROUTE OF ADMINISTRATION: The dose is one tablet of 35mg of Trimetazidine twice daily during meals. The benefit of the treatment should be assessed after three months and trimetazidine should be discontinued if there is no treatment response. Special populations Patients with renal impairment: In patients with moderate renal impairment (creatinine clearance [30-60] ml/min), the recommended dose is 1 tablet of 35 mg in morning during breakfast. Elderly patients: Elderly patients may have increased trimetazidine exposure due to age-related decrease in renal function. In patients with moderate renal impairment (creatinine clearance [30-60] ml/min), the recommended dose is 1 tablet of 35mg in the morning during breakfast. Dose titration in elderly patients should be exercised with caution. Pediatric population: The safety and efficacy of trimetazidine in children aged below 18 years have not been established. Mode of Administration: For oral use. Tablets must be taken orally twice daily, i.e., one in the morning and one in the evening during meals.",1,1,"INDICATIONS: Used in adult patient, in combination with other medicines to treat",low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T14:18:11.662019+00:00
