PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10262,Diosmin + Hesperidin,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xy-rfNEgNMaBNVP7aL5odZtPHK25xUz-/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10262_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xy-rfNEgNMaBNVP7aL5odZtPHK25xUz-_view_usp_drivesdk_8cc1aad2cc.pdf,page_text/DRP-10262_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xy-rfNEgNMaBNVP7aL5odZtPHK25xUz-_view_usp_drivesdk_8cc1aad2cc.json,f8f989dc674144f25a131896ed1d721cbd672a17a49fec759255ab003d6c3949,586090,1,ocr,"A light brown color film coated elliptical tablet. "" Cc > CD "" WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? RiteMED® Diosmin + Hesperidin Film-Coated Tablet contains 450 mg of Diosmin and 50 mg of Hesperidin as active ingredients, Diosmin and Hesperidin are flavonoid compounds. When used together, they prolong the vasoconstriction effect of noradrenaline on the venous wall, thus increasing venous return and reducing venous hyperpressure present in patients with chronic venous disease and haemorrhoidal disease. WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? RiteMED® Diosmin + Hesperidin Film-Coated Tablet is used for treatment of organic and functional chronic venous insufficiency of the lower limbs with the following symptoms: heavy legs, pain and nocturnal cramps. Treatment of chronic hemorrhoids and acute hemorrhoidal attacks. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Usual dose in chronic venous insufficiency: 1 tablet 2 times daily. In acute hemorrhoidal attacks: 3 tablets 2 times daily for 4 days followed by 2 tablets 2 times daily for 3 days, then 2 tablets daily. In chronic hemorrhoidal disease: 2 tablets daily. Tablets are to be taken after meals. WHEN NOT TO TAKE THIS MEDICINE? © Do not take this medicine if you are allergic to Diosmin or Hesperidin or to any ingredients of this medicine. e Avoid taking this medicine if you are breastfeeding. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE 260mm No harmful effect has so far been reported for pregnancy in human. You are not recommended to breastfeed during treatment. (+2mm) UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Some cases of minor gastrointestinal and neurovegetative disorders have been reported which never required cessation of treatment. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Please tell your pharmacist if you are taking or have recently taken any other medicines, including medicines obtained without a prescription. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose of RiteMED™ Diosmin + Hesperidin Film-Coated Tablet and you are taking it regularly, take it as soon as possible. If it is approaching time for the next dose, do not double the dose to make up for the forgotten dose, unless advised by your health care provider. Do not take 2 doses at once. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE None have been mentioned. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? Seek for medical attention if you have taken more than the recommended dosage. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from light and moisture. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? ® If you are allergic to the medicine e If you have any other health related problems e If symptoms do not improve or new symptoms appear e If undesirable effects develop ADVERSE DRUG REACTION REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adverse drug reaction, seek medical attention immediately and report to the FDA at www.fda.gov.ph AND RiteMED at (+632) 8-726-0835 or e-mail productsafety@ritemed.com.ph. By reporting undesirable effects, you can help provide more information on the safety of this medicine. AVAILABILITY RiteMED® Diosmin + Hesperidin 450 mg/ 50 mg Film-Coated Tablet, in Alu/PVC Blister Pack x 10's (Box of 30's) Manufactured by Y.S.P. Industries (M) SDN. BHD. Lot 3, 5 & 7, Jalan P/7, Section 13 Kawasan Perindustrian Bandar Baru Bangi 43000 Kajang, Selangor, Malaysia Imported and distributed by RiteMED Phils., Inc. 56 Epifanio Delos Santos Ave., Mandaluyong Metro Manila Date of First Authorization: August 26, 2021 Date of Revision: December 2021 DRP-10262 RTM7008461INO1 Reg. IPOPHIL + __ W 110mm (+2mm) [Page 2]",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T14:19:15.164954+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10269,Ascorbic Acid,Vforci,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vb7w3zkg6Xb9cfeVyc6MECVaR6wXbkq5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10269_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vb7w3zkg6Xb9cfeVyc6MECVaR6wXbkq5_view_usp_drivesdk_9258f02eb5.pdf,page_text/DRP-10269_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vb7w3zkg6Xb9cfeVyc6MECVaR6wXbkq5_view_usp_drivesdk_9258f02eb5.json,766ffb1f02b934988c3599b60854f331f07a11b3619e2c1ca31a67c1d8d9417d,411354,1,digital_text,"Orange coloured, round shaped, ﬂat, one side break line and other side plain uncoated chewable tablet 3. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This medicine contains Ascorbic Acid or Vitamin C. Vitamin C is a water-soluble vitamin that is necessary for normal growth and development. This vitamin is required for the growth and repair of tissues in all parts of the body. It is necessary to form collagen- an important protein used to make skin, scar tissue, tendons, ligaments, and blood vessels. Vitamin C is essential for wound healing and for the repair and maintenance of cartilages, bones and teeth. Vitamins C is also one of the many antioxidants – nutrients that block some of the damage caused by free radicals. Antioxidants also help reduce the damage to the body caused by toxic chemicals and pollutants such as cigarette smoke, food preservatives, etc., Vitamins C is also a co-factor in many biological processes especially in iron metabolism, resistance to infection, and in cellular respiration. Excipients: Sucrose, Colour supra sunset yellow, Sodium saccharin, Puriﬁed water, Essence dry orange special, Magnesium stearate and Puriﬁed talc. 4. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE?",1,1,2. DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T14:19:18.014208+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10275-01,Febuxostat,Goutfree 40,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1380xEzwJzpD4pPpH-LI1TZ3mzCAgFsgp/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10275-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1380xEzwJzpD4pPpH-LI1TZ3mzCAgFsgp_view_usp_drivesdk_14db44a8b6.pdf,page_text/DRP-10275-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1380xEzwJzpD4pPpH-LI1TZ3mzCAgFsgp_view_usp_drivesdk_14db44a8b6.json,442a8ff827573b2497a5c1c8f10d2fe35806aeefc12962289c08ae973e8bc63f,1504228,1,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-29T14:19:24.542855+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10280,Latanoprost,Latanopta,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1x8ZWPdopxrVQSZ3wPFoTfemWWh7ltSjl/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10280_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1x8ZWPdopxrVQSZ3wPFoTfemWWh7ltSjl_view_usp_drivesdk_4386608c67.pdf,page_text/DRP-10280_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1x8ZWPdopxrVQSZ3wPFoTfemWWh7ltSjl_view_usp_drivesdk_4386608c67.json,dae48e240f3588504edfda47d4e7207909f438d518b8b0e8bbd2c5504db85d9b,438167,2,digital_text,"Latanoprost (Latanopta) is a prostaglandin F2α analogue. Latanoprost (Latanopta) is a prostanoid selective prostaglandin F receptor agonist that is believed to reduce the intraocular pressure (IOP) by increasing the outflow of aqueous humor. Studies in animals and man suggest that the main mechanism of action is increased uveoscleral outflow. Elevated IOP represents a major risk factor for glaucomatous field loss. The higher the level of IOP, the greater the likelihood of optic nerve damage and visual field loss.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,For the reduction of elevated intraocular pressure in patients with open-angle glaucoma or ocular hypertension.,2,2,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:19:27.583703+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10281,Domperidone (as maleate),Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1U03llUEbCXvsZm5zGbj6RCllaTGLDTuG/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10281_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1U03llUEbCXvsZm5zGbj6RCllaTGLDTuG_view_usp_drivesdk_0431ebb82a.pdf,page_text/DRP-10281_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1U03llUEbCXvsZm5zGbj6RCllaTGLDTuG_view_usp_drivesdk_0431ebb82a.json,3e20484fec455893063e096119b156029a412b75dea85d32bb44743fb94a72f4,1042840,1,digital_text,"In accordance with ICH-E14 guidelines, a thorough QT study was performed. This study included a placebo, an active comparator and a positive control and was conducted in healthy subjects with up to 80 mg per day 10 or 20 mg administered 4 times a day of domperidone. However, two previous drug-drug interaction studies showed some evidence of QTc prolongation when domperidone was administered as monotherapy (10 mg 4 times a day). The largest time-matched mean difference of QTcF between domperidone and placebo was 5.4 msec (95 % CI: -1.7 to 12.4) and 7.5msec (95 % CI: 0.6 to 14.4), respectively. Eq. to Domperidone............10 mg The low absolute bioavailability of oral domperidone (approximately 15%) is due to an extensive first-pass metabolism in the gut wall and liver. Although domperidone's bioavailability is enhanced in normal subjects when taken after a meal, patients with gastrointestinal complaints should take domperidone 15-30 minutes before a meal. Reduced gastric acidity impairs the absorption of domperidone. Oral bioavailability is decreased by prior concomitant administration of cimetidine and sodium bicarbonate. The time of peak absorption is slightly delayed and the AUC somewhat increased when the oral drug is taken after a meal.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Domperidone is indicated for the relief of the symptoms of nausea and vomiting.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:19:31.065653+00:00
