PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10306-01,Tranexamic Acid,Gentranex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PEZEAzylHiZlAvFN3jwRj-laij3wiXSw/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10306-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PEZEAzylHiZlAvFN3jwRj-laij3wiXSw_view_usp_drivesdk_7235614b46.pdf,page_text/DRP-10306-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PEZEAzylHiZlAvFN3jwRj-laij3wiXSw_view_usp_drivesdk_7235614b46.json,8576e3c76a17b0193127cd1d4bb27202de169bb072671b78a8e5ee46a5063a79,402332,2,digital_text,"Yellow coloured, capsule shaped, biconvex, film coated tablets, plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Indicated for short term use for haemorrhage or risk of haemorrhage in those with increased fibrinolysis or fibrinogenolysis. Local fibrinolysis as occurs in the following conditions: 1. a) Prostatectomy and bladder surgery b) Menorrhagia c) Epistaxis d) Conisation of the cervix e) Traumatic hyphaema 2. Management of dental extraction in haemophiliacs 3. Hereditary angioneurothic edema,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:19:37.601344+00:00
