PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10396,Docetaxel (As Trihydrate),Taceedo 20,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1R4iPd6jeYutgFo6XsnjCEjeV7jUmhC06/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10396_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1R4iPd6jeYutgFo6XsnjCEjeV7jUmhC06_view_usp_drivesdk_f5345a77eb.pdf,page_text/DRP-10396_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1R4iPd6jeYutgFo6XsnjCEjeV7jUmhC06_view_usp_drivesdk_f5345a77eb.json,0542cee7064ad1fdee108a04123ef4d7027449a5c01d908c7b1972c8fce94256,893321,2,digital_text,"Each Single Dose Vial (0.5 mL) contains: Absorption A population pharmacokinetic analysis has been performed with docetaxel in 577 patients. Pharmacokinetic parameters estimated by the model were very close to those estimated from phase I studies. The pharmacokinetics of docetaxel were not altered by the age or sex of the patient. Docetaxel (as Trihydrate), USP ....................... 80 mg",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"TACEEDO in combination with doxorubicin and cyclophosphamide is indicated for the adjuvant treatment of patients with: Docetaxel clearance was not modified in patients with mild to moderate fluid retention and there are no data available in patients with severe fluid retention. • operable node-positive breast cancer • operable node-negative breast cancer Breast cancer For patients with operable node-negative breast cancer, adjuvant treatment should be restricted to patients eligible to receive chemotherapy according to internationally established criteria for primary therapy of early breast cancer. TACEEDO in combination with doxorubicin is indicated for the treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic breast cancer who have not previously received cytotoxic therapy for this condition. Combination therapy Prednisone TACEEDO in combination with trastuzumab is indicated for the treatment of patients with metastatic breast cancer whose tumours over express HER2 and who previously have not received chemotherapy for metastatic disease. The combined administration of docetaxel, cisplatin and 5-fluorouracil in 12 patients with solid tumours had no influence on the pharmacokinetics of each individual medicinal product. haematological toxicities. All patients on the docetaxel-containing arm of the TAX 323 and TAX 324 studies, received prophylactic antibiotics. • Induction chemotherapy followed by chemoradiotherapy (TAX 324) For the induction treatment of patients with locally advanced (technically unresectable, low probability of surgical cure, and aiming at organ preservation) squamous cell carcinoma of the head and neck (SCCHN), the recommended dose of docetaxel is 75 2 2 mg/m as a 1 hour intravenous infusion on day 1, followed by cisplatin 100 mg/m administered as a 30-minute to 3-hour infusion, followed by 5-fluorouracil 1000 2 mg/m /day as a continuous infusion from day 1 to day 4. This regimen is administered every 3 weeks for 3 cycles. Following chemotherapy, patients should receive chemoradiotherapy. For cisplatin and 5-fluorouracil dose modifications, see the corresponding summary of product characteristics. General Dose adjustments during treatment • Induction chemotherapy followed by radiotherapy (TAX 323) For the induction treatment of inoperable locally advanced squamous cell carcinoma of 2 the head and neck (SCCHN), the recommended dose of docetaxel is 75 mg/m as a 2 1-hour infusion followed by cisplatin 75 mg/m over 1 hour, on day one, followed by 5- 2 fluorouracil as a continuous infusion at 750 mg/m per day for five days. This regimen is administered every 3 weeks for 4 cycles. Following chemotherapy, patients should receive radiotherapy. Based on pharmacokinetic data with docetaxel at 100 mg/m² as single agent, patients who have both elevations of transaminase (ALT and/or AST) greater than 1.5 times the upper limit of the normal range (ULN) and alkaline phosphatase greater than 2.5 times the 2 ULN, the recommended dose of docetaxel is 75 mg/m . For those patients with serum bilirubin > ULN and/or AL T and AST > 3.5 times the ULN associated with alkaline phosphatase > 6 times the ULN, no dose-reduction can be recommended, and docetaxel should not be used unless strictly indicated. In combination with cisplatin and 5- fluorouracil for the treatment of patients with gastric adenocarcinoma, the pivotal clinical study excluded patients with AL T and/or AST > 1.5 × ULN associated with alkaline phosphatase > 2.5 × ULN, and bilirubin > 1 x ULN; for these patients, no dose- reductions can be recommended and docetaxel should not be used unless strictly indicated. No data are available in patients with hepatic impairment treated by docetaxel in combination in the other indications. Older people",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:20:50.689039+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10397,Olanzapine,Olzadin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1pF5q_oQY81xU0umzkdBaxLC21MzqVpZx/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10397_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1pF5q_oQY81xU0umzkdBaxLC21MzqVpZx_view_usp_drivesdk_4bcbc172b9.pdf,page_text/DRP-10397_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1pF5q_oQY81xU0umzkdBaxLC21MzqVpZx_view_usp_drivesdk_4bcbc172b9.json,0c4886015e692496273a4e4cb79fc4c166b1d2f8b682bad39731b7903b30dbce,4061577,1,ocr,"Olanzapine 5 mg and 10 mg (Olzadin) are white, oval-shaped, biconvex film-coated tablets, scored on one side and plain on the other side. in humans, but potential benefits may warrant use of the drug in pregnant women despite potential risks. Nursing mothers receiving Olanzapine Film-Coated Tablet (Olzadin) should discontinue breastfeeding because it is excreted in breast milk.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Itis used in the management of schizophrenia and for short-term treatment of mania associated with bipolar disorder.,1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T14:21:02.949441+00:00
