PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10464,Olapatadine (as Hydrochloride),Opadinex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1eawN1g_jebPiki8_T3tJ_O3_NhOToyrm/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10464_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eawN1g_jebPiki8_T3tJ_O3_NhOToyrm_view_usp_drivesdk_3c4f158ec3.pdf,page_text/DRP-10464_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eawN1g_jebPiki8_T3tJ_O3_NhOToyrm_view_usp_drivesdk_3c4f158ec3.json,5ce94c5954d42e8b401cdc2a4b6b2ebd0ce0b7bd06eafa0c84434b5d9422b1dd,467818,1,digital_text,Olopatadine Hydrochloride (Opadinex) Eye Drops are a sterile solution of Olopatadine Hydrochloride in water for injection. It contains not less than 90.0% and not more than 110% of the labeled amount of Olopatadine C H No ).21 23 3 The product is available in 5 mL plastic container containing 2 mg of Olopatadine per mL of ophthalmic solution.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Olopatadine Hydrochloride is indicated for the treatment of ocular itching associated with seasonal allergic conjunctivitis. Geriatrics: No overall differences in safety and effectiveness have been observed between elderly and other adult patients. Pediatrics (<18 years): The effectiveness of Olopatadine Hydrochloride has not been established in pediatric patients <18 years of age. No overall difference in safety has been observed between pediatric and adult patients.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:22:17.905298+00:00
