PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10500,Cefixime (as trihydrate),Cefixime (as trihydrate),PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1QToRsBMpDrujARvH4hEHjHxYJ7ooeOVh/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10500_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QToRsBMpDrujARvH4hEHjHxYJ7ooeOVh_view_usp_drivesdk_ed3390a53f.pdf,page_text/DRP-10500_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QToRsBMpDrujARvH4hEHjHxYJ7ooeOVh_view_usp_drivesdk_ed3390a53f.json,c13633a5c16e5030f3c9f62100b28bed42982ec928fae164f268e65082f99dcd,1982478,2,digital_text,Cefixime 100 mg/5 mL Granules for Oral Suspension: Off-white to yellowish-white suspension with orange flavor packed in 60 mL white translucent HDPE bottle with white LDPE flip top cap and measuring cap (Box of 1’s).,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of the following infections due to susceptible microorganisms:  Acute bronchitis, acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis, bronchiectasis with infection, secondary infections in chronic respiratory tract diseases, pneumonia  Urinary tract infec tions including pyelonephritis and cystitis  Gonococcal urethritis  Cholecystitis, cholangitis  Scarlet fever  Sinusitis, tonsilitis, pharyngitis, otitis media  Typhoid fever (enteric fever) including multi-drug resistant typhoid fever",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:23:39.028426+00:00
