PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10519-01,Butamirate Citrate,Coptamed,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1TxynfWKLsVFXN3-_Pu-_iaiVra0Ww7AT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10519-01_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1TxynfWKLsVFXN3-_Pu-_iaiVra0Ww7AT_view_usp_drivesdk_f6560aa09a.pdf,page_text/DRP-10519-01_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1TxynfWKLsVFXN3-_Pu-_iaiVra0Ww7AT_view_usp_drivesdk_f6560aa09a.json,e4f307a8d55db51122d66022453da12d49a183a4f81deab1a3c628b2269ebbc8,556677,1,digital_text,"Butamirate Citrate (COPTAMED) syrup is a clear, colorless syrup with vanilla /f_lavor. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Butamirate Citrate contains the active ingredient Butamirate Citrate which belongs to a group of medicines called antitussive. Butamirate Citrate is a non-narcotic antitussive which presents non-speci/f_ic anticholinergic and antispasmodic eﬀects, fa cilitating respiration. It acts centrally by di minishing the tussigenic re/f_lex, and pe ripherally via a bronchospasmolytic ac tivity enhanced by an anti-in/f_lammatory action. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T14:25:48.176101+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10520-01,Paracetamol + Hyoscine N-Butylbromide,Teracyn,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/12IyEqV_2auVVBgF8HlOLFsNj1VBjgJAn/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10520-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_12IyEqV_2auVVBgF8HlOLFsNj1VBjgJAn_view_usp_drivesdk_61bbc9a416.pdf,page_text/DRP-10520-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_12IyEqV_2auVVBgF8HlOLFsNj1VBjgJAn_view_usp_drivesdk_61bbc9a416.json,5042108397d3ef9ccf16d964fc86407d0d95686935e59f123cd5ea47fe0cee08,471934,1,digital_text,"White /f_ilm-coated, capsule-shaped tablet.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T14:25:50.808778+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10523,Multivitamins,Multilem PNF,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1scpV6TEbbEBTwDulk7shyp-9Aj0q3u7o/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10523_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1scpV6TEbbEBTwDulk7shyp-9Aj0q3u7o_view_usp_drivesdk_74de1f67e6.pdf,page_text/DRP-10523_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1scpV6TEbbEBTwDulk7shyp-9Aj0q3u7o_view_usp_drivesdk_74de1f67e6.json,89bf8c162857257eae2c24f8a963d2b9f14382a6943457f58534a7fa6d21dbd9,1205707,1,ocr,"A yellow to brown colored powder contained in a scarlet/brown capsule size #1. Blister pack by 10's, box of 30 and 100 capsules. What is in the medicine? Multilem PNF Capsule contains vitamins which are organic substances required for various metabolic processes. Strength of the medicine: Each capsule contains: 2500 IU Retinol Acetate (Vitamin A), USP 400 IU Cholecalcifero! (Vitamin D,) Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C) 80 mg Nicotinic Acid 23 mg d-a- Tocopheryl Acid Succinate (Vitamin E). 10 mg Pyridoxine Hydrochloride (Vitamin B,)......... 2mg Thiamine Mononitrate (Vitamin B,) 1.7 mg Riboflavin (Vitamin B.) 1.3mg Folic Acid 400 mcg Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin 12 6 mcg What is this medicine used for? General nutritional supplementation of daily diet for prevention of vitamin deficiency especially in case of inadequate nutrition, growth, strenuous physical activity, convalescence and for maintenance of body resistance. These are also used to provide nutritional balance necessary for proper physical growth and mental development. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Take one capsule daily, or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? If you are allergic to any of the components in the product. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: -Do not take more than the recommended dose. -Do not use after the expiry date stated on the label. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Generally, if taken with recommended dose, this medicine is well tolerated but in some cases the following may be seen: Retinol Acetate (Vitamin A)- Hypervitaminosis A due to intake of very high doses can cause fatigue, irritability, anorexia, loss of weight, vomiting, sedation, dizziness, confusion and diarrhea. Cholecalciferol (Vitamin D3) - Excessive intake may lead to hypercalcemia or hyperphosphatemia. d-a-Tocophery! Acid Succinate (Vitamin E)- A higher incidence of necrotizing enterocolitis has been noted in premature infants weighing less than 1.5 kg treated with Vitamin E. Riboflavin (Vitamin B2)- Large doses may result to bright yellow discoloration in urine. Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12)- Allergic hypersensitivity reactions have occurred rarely that includes rash, itching and anaphylaxis. Nicotinic Acid- It has a vasodilating action that causes flushing, sensation of heat, faintness and pounding in the head. What other medicine or food should be avoided? Retinol Acetate (Vitamin A)- Neomycin, Cholestyramine or Liquid paraffin may reduce the absorption of Vitamin A. Increase risk of hypervitaminosis A if given with retinoids such as isotretinoin and tretinoin. Cholecalciferol (Vitamin D3)- Increased risk of hypercalcemia if Vitamin D is given with Thiazide diuretics, Calcium and Phosphate. d-a-Tocopheryl Acid Succinate (Vitamin E)- Cholestyramine, Colestipol and Orlistat may interfere with the absorption of Vitamin E. High doses of Vitamin E may increase the effects of anti-coagulants. Pyridoxine HCI (Vitamin B6)- Pyridoxine reduces the effects of Levodopa and Altretamine. Vitamin B6 decreases concentration of Phenobarbital and Phenytoin. Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12)- Neomycin, Aminosalicylic Acid, Histamine H2 Antagonist, Omeprazole and Colchicine reduce the absorption of Vitamin B12. Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C)- Omeprazole What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: The following symptoms might be seen in large doses: Retinol Acetate (Vitamin A)- Intake in excess of 10,000 IU daily or weekly intakes in excess of 25,000 IU have resulted to hypervitaminosis A (fatigue, irritability, anorexia, loss of weight, vomiting, sedation, dizziness, confusion and diarrhea). Cholecalciferol (Vitamin D3)- Anorexia, lassitude, nausea, vomiting, constipation, diarrhea, polyuria, nocturia, sweating, headache, thirst, somnolence and vertigo. d-a-Tocophery! Acid Succinate (Vitamin E)- Large doses may cause diarrhea, abdominal pain and disturbances, blurred vision, dizziness, fatigue and weakness. Pyridoxine HCI (Vitamin B6)- Long term use of large doses is associated with the development of severe peripheral neuropathies. Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12)- gastrointestinal disturbances, fever, chills, hot flushing, dizziness, malaise, acneform, eruptions and tremor. Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C)- Large doses may cause diarrhea, abdominal pain and disturbances. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? If any undesirable effect occurs. “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph.” Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration number: DRP-10523 Date of Authorization: October 08, 2021 Patient Information Leaflet Date of Revision: November 15, 2022 Manufactured by the Distributed by: Marketing Authorization Holder:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T14:26:00.056654+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10525,Cefoperazone (as sodium) + Sulbactam (as sodium),Cefriotam,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FzRx7eBF3uY0JqDRpM5TPINA4gserRZb/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10525_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FzRx7eBF3uY0JqDRpM5TPINA4gserRZb_view_usp_drivesdk_14294995ba.pdf,page_text/DRP-10525_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FzRx7eBF3uY0JqDRpM5TPINA4gserRZb_view_usp_drivesdk_14294995ba.json,424a2150c15db15396f5e61c799af794d955e13e26685796e52ae7bb00d7fe7a,1544293,1,digital_text,White to almost white powder,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Monotherapy Cefoperazone + sulbactam is Indicated for the treatment of the following infections when caused by susceptible organisms: • Respiratory Tract Infections (Upper and Lower); • Urinary Tract Infections (Upper and Lower); • Peritonitis, Cholecystitis, Cholangitis, and other Intra-abdominal Infections; • Septicemia; • Meningitis; • Skin and Soft Tissue Infections; • Bone and Joint Infections; • Pelvic Inflammator y Disease, Endometritis, Gonorrhea, and other Infections of the Genital Tract. Combination Therapy Because of the broad spectrum of activity of cefoperazone + sulbactam, most infections can be treated adequately with this antibiotic alone. However, cefoperazone + sulbactam may be used concomitantly with other antibiotics if such combinations are indicated. If an aminoglycoside is used, renal function should be monitored during the course of therapy.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:26:07.137753+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10525-02,Cefoperazone (as sodium) + Sulbactam (as sodium),Winpersul,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/16I0eUeToMpk5KJnAPkNzLqFCubMlt_fz/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10525-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_16I0eUeToMpk5KJnAPkNzLqFCubMlt_fz_view_usp_drivesdk_46a838f57d.pdf,page_text/DRP-10525-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_16I0eUeToMpk5KJnAPkNzLqFCubMlt_fz_view_usp_drivesdk_46a838f57d.json,45cd33c11b55bcba30201492073e4c3ed28106c18d1b8dd476dfdd8d6c41d35a,1112016,1,digital_text,White to almost white powder,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Monotherapy Cefoperazone + sulbactam is indicated for the treatment of the following infections when caused by susceptible organisms: • Respiratory Tract Infections (Upper and Lower); • Urinary Tract Infections (Upper and Lower); • Peritonitis, Cholecystitis, Cholangitis, and other Intra-abdominal Infections; • Septicemia; • Meningitis; • Skin and Soft Tissue Infections; • Bone and Joint Infections; • Pelvic Inflammator y Disease, Endometritis, Gonorrhea, and other Infections of the Genital Tract. Combination Therapy Because of the broad spectrum of activity of cefoperazone + sulbactam, most infections can be treated adequately with this antibiotic alone. However, cefoperazone + sulbactam may be used concomitantly with other antibiotics if such combinations are indicated. If an aminoglycoside is used, renal function should be monitored during the course of therapy.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:26:03.713349+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10530-03,Linezolid,Lizod,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mvxHh5_1LhchUXWFK_gq90q2OPgcu0n0/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10530-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mvxHh5_1LhchUXWFK_gq90q2OPgcu0n0_view_usp_drivesdk_8116ce438a.pdf,page_text/DRP-10530-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mvxHh5_1LhchUXWFK_gq90q2OPgcu0n0_view_usp_drivesdk_8116ce438a.json,b557825c7a2e1a7f48a9b399dfdf24ca471c490143428cc8ff0211e3c2713a8a,10200034,2,ocr,Clear colourless to slightly brown or yellowish-brown color solution.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"«Nosocomial pneumonia * Community acquired pneumonia Linezolid is indicated in adults for the treatment of community acquired pneumonia and nosocomial pneumonia when known or suspected to be caused by susceptible Gram-positive bacteria. In determining whether Linezolid 2 mg/mL Solution for Infusion is an appropriate treatment, the results of microbiological tests or information on the prevalence of resistance to antibacterial agents among Gram-positive bacteria should be taken into consideration. Linezolid is not active against infections caused by Gram-negative pathogens. Specific therapy against Gram-negative organisms must be initiated concomitantly ifa Gram-negative pathogen is documented or suspected. ¢ Complicated skin and soft tissue infections. Linezolid is indicated in adults for the treatment of complicated skin and soft tissue infections only when microbiological testing has established that the infection is known to be caused by susceptible Gram-positive bacteria. Linezolid is not active against infections caused by Gram-negative pathogens. Linezolid should only be used in patients with complicated skin and soft tissue infections with known or possible co-infection with Gram-negative organisms if there are no alternative treatment options available. In these circumstances treatment against Gram-negative organisms must be initiated concomitantly. Treatment with linezolid should only be initiated in a hospital environment and after consultation with a relevant specialist such as a microbiologist or an infectious diseases specialist. Consideration should be given to official guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T14:26:46.698877+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10530-04,Linezolid,Loxenil IV,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Mwc0m_xqT2RtoUW_dsx6NpdKnT6jJuOg/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10530-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Mwc0m_xqT2RtoUW_dsx6NpdKnT6jJuOg_view_usp_drivesdk_47ca2096fb.pdf,page_text/DRP-10530-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Mwc0m_xqT2RtoUW_dsx6NpdKnT6jJuOg_view_usp_drivesdk_47ca2096fb.json,e9c134740e5a041156834dd445c1855d4eec03e0def7e9b440cfdb3580afcd79,822434,3,digital_text,Clear colourless to slightly brown or yellowish-brown color solution.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"• Nosocomial pneumonia • Community acquired pneumonia Linezolid is indicated in adults for the treatment of community acquired pneumonia and nosocomial pneumonia when known or suspected to be caused by susceptible Gram-positive bacteria. In determining whether Linezolid 2 mg/ml Solution for Infusion is an appropriate treatment, the results of microbiological tests or information on the prevalence of resistance to antibacterial agents among Gram-positive bacteria should be taken into consideration. Linezolid is not active against infections caused by Gram-negative pathogens. Specific therapy against Gram-negative organisms must be initiated concomitantly if a Gramnegative pathogen is documented or suspected. • Complicated skin and soft tissue infections. Linezolid is indicated in adults for the treatment of complicated skin and soft tissue infections only when microbiological testing has established that the infection is known to be caused by susceptible Gram-positive bacteria. Linezolid is not active against infections caused by Gram-negative pathogens. Linezolid should only be used in patients with complicated skin and soft tissue infections with known or possible co-infection with Gram-negative organisms if there are no alternative treatment options available. In these circumstances treatment against Gram-negative organisms must be initiated concomitantly. Treatment with linezolid should only be initiated in a hospital environment and after consultation with a relevant specialist such as a microbiologist or an infectious diseases specialist. Consideration should be given to official guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:26:50.019782+00:00
