PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10596,Morphine Hydrochloride,Morphina,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/155Eqp8Rgra4fZ6vteKKqohMg9j6ehntx/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10596_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_155Eqp8Rgra4fZ6vteKKqohMg9j6ehntx_view_usp_drivesdk_c9c7957ca3.pdf,page_text/DRP-10596_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_155Eqp8Rgra4fZ6vteKKqohMg9j6ehntx_view_usp_drivesdk_c9c7957ca3.json,b26738c7636b2cf9f1fbaca90d8181a81303e5f1a3f5e67d7014ca3c9fa8cecc,3627844,2,ocr,Clear colourless or yellowish liquid.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Morphine hydrochloride is prescribed: - toreverse severe, acute pain after severe injuries, fractures of bones, burns, surgery; - to prevent acute and chronic pain in the case of myocardial infarction, as well as in the case of acute pancreatitis; - torelieve severe chronic pain in the case of malignant tumour and to relive colicky pain arising from movements of renal and gall stones; - for premedication before anesthesia.",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T14:29:49.525302+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10597,Rosuvastatin (as calcium),Fusovast,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_wtjHYohj2yvT-kODlp5ULS5y4lGwWZF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10597_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_wtjHYohj2yvT-kODlp5ULS5y4lGwWZF_view_usp_drivesdk_810e68883a.pdf,page_text/DRP-10597_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_wtjHYohj2yvT-kODlp5ULS5y4lGwWZF_view_usp_drivesdk_810e68883a.json,321cfeb2337d02839475eb8a1e6bb14aaf21e51de636796a7861c8070644e008,543158,1,digital_text,Light pink colored lm-coated oval shape tablet “20” engraved on one side and breakline on another side.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Treatment of hypercholesterolaemia Adults, adolescents and children aged 6 years or older with primary hypercholesterolaemia (type IIa including heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia) or mixed dyslipidaemia (type IIb) as an adjunct to diet when response to diet and other non-pharmacological treatments (e.g. exercise, weight reduction) is inadequate. Adults, adolescents and children aged 6 years or older with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia as an adjunct to diet and other lipid lowering treatments (e.g. LDL apheresis) or if such treatments are not appropriate. Prevention of Cardiovascular Events Prevention of major cardiovascular events in patients who are estimated to have a high risk for a rst cardiovascular event, as an adjunct to correction of other risk factors.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:29:52.617673+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10598,Baclofen,Baclisolv,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZJmQTc7lvaqB8CzLbF4Kkjmo5reXL2TZ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10598_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZJmQTc7lvaqB8CzLbF4Kkjmo5reXL2TZ_view_usp_drivesdk_feed642380.pdf,page_text/DRP-10598_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZJmQTc7lvaqB8CzLbF4Kkjmo5reXL2TZ_view_usp_drivesdk_feed642380.json,f28e5be1baf724d3de1de8b6a63c21d612161c54071f26d6d06541449c3a5c00,520181,1,digital_text,Light yellow coloured round shaped uncoated tablet having breakline on one side and plain on other side.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Baclofen is indicated for the relief of spasticity of voluntary muscle resulting from such disorders as multiple sclerosis, and other spinal lesions, e.g. tumors of the spinal cord, syringomyelia, motor neurone disease, transverse myelitis, a traumatic partial section of the cord. Baclofen is also indicated in adults and children for the relief of spasticity of voluntary muscle arising from e.g. cerebrovascular accidents, cerebral palsy, meningitis, and traumatic head injury. Patient selection is important when initiating Baclofen therapy; it is likely to be of most benefit in patients whose spasticity constitutes a handicap to activities and/or physiotherapy. Treatment should not be commenced until the spastic state has become stabilized. Pediatric population Baclofen is indicated in patients 0 to <18 years for the symptomatic treatment of spasticity of cerebral origin, especially where due to infantile cerebral palsy, as well as following cerebrovascular accidents or in the presence of neoplastic or degenerative brain disease. Baclofen is also indicated for the symptomatic treatment of muscle spasms occurring in spinal cord diseases of infectious, degenerative, traumatic, neoplastic, or unknown origin such as multiple sclerosis, spastic spinal paralysis, amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, syringomyelia, transverse myelitis, traumatic paraplegia or paraparesis, and compression of the spinal cord.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:29:55.670633+00:00
