PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10710-03,Piperacillin (As Sodium) + Tazobactam (As Sodium),Rytam,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1a9uF_DR4QYEpRE_wB8qjix_4DBYbPfrE/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10710-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1a9uF_DR4QYEpRE_wB8qjix_4DBYbPfrE_view_usp_drivesdk_530bc945c8.pdf,page_text/DRP-10710-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1a9uF_DR4QYEpRE_wB8qjix_4DBYbPfrE_view_usp_drivesdk_530bc945c8.json,be20715112f1b8e304c2d97c497fcc01c4be257fb613c3b4ce269ef8ae203af2,351798,2,digital_text,Powder: White to almost white powder Sterile Water: Clear and colorless solution,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for the treatment of the following infections in adults and children o ver 2 years of age Adults and Adolescents - Severe pneumonia including hospital -acquired and ventilator-associated pneumonia - Complicated urinary tract infections (including pyelonephritis) - Complicated intra-abdominal infections - Complicated skin and soft tissue infections (including diabetic foot infections) Treatment of patients with bacteremia that occurs in association with, or is suspected to be associated with, any of the infections listed above. Piperacillin/Tazobactam may be used in the management of neutropenic patients with fever suspected to be due to a bacterial infection. Children 2 to 12 years of age - Complicated intra-abdominal infections Piperacillin/Tazobactam may be used in the management of neutropenic children with fever suspected to be due to a bacterial infection. Consideration should be given to official guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:33:58.385514+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10721-02,Dapagliflozin,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hT1XGfSl5FghLzLoKjq80SP8KO4xW9Gj/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10721-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hT1XGfSl5FghLzLoKjq80SP8KO4xW9Gj_view_usp_drivesdk_8f306c1c7d.pdf,page_text/DRP-10721-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hT1XGfSl5FghLzLoKjq80SP8KO4xW9Gj_view_usp_drivesdk_8f306c1c7d.json,7a81c2d32b4a672c4ebe087d13a476a4e88fece6ea495f579cb6fd2ab9f6e506,8100205,2,digital_text,"Dapagliflozin 10 mg Film-Coated Tablet is pale yellow to yellow film-coated tablet, oval-shaped, biconvex, with brea k line on one side and plain on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Type 2 diabetes mellitus Dapagliflozin is indicated in adults for the treatment of insufficiently controlled type 2 diabetes mellitus as an adjunct to diet and exercise as monotherapy when metformin is considered inappropriate due to intolerance. in addition to other medicinal products for the treatment of type 2 diabetes. For study results with respect to combination of therapies, effects on glycaemic control, cardiovascular and renal events, and the populations studied. Dapagliflozin is indicated in adults for the treatment of symptomatic chronic heart failure with reduced ejection fraction. Chronic kidney disease Dapagliflozin is indicated in adults for the treatment of chronic kidney disease.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:34:07.764202+00:00
