PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10838,Fulvestrant,Eranfu,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MFS0V5ro1guTT1g5NVa_jJ2B5F3mEwMK/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10838_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MFS0V5ro1guTT1g5NVa_jJ2B5F3mEwMK_view_usp_drivesdk_2ca7b8746f.pdf,page_text/DRP-10838_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MFS0V5ro1guTT1g5NVa_jJ2B5F3mEwMK_view_usp_drivesdk_2ca7b8746f.json,a4231cd1e7dd4b7ba2b8beda025e4294e79cf22700d61aeeccd1725dc2643c94,2720474,2,digital_text,"Clear, colorless to yellow, viscous liquid free from visible particulate matter. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM Solution for injection Fulvestrant Injection is a clear, colorless to yellow, viscous liquid free from visible particulate matter, presented in 5.0 mL Type-I glass syringe with OVS tip cap. CLINICAL PARTICULARS",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Fulvestrant is indicated for the: - Treatment of hormone receptor (HR)-positive, human epidermal growth receptor 2 (HER2)-negative advanced breast cancer in postmenopausal women not previously treated with endocrine therapy. - Treatment of HR-positive advanced breast cancer in postmenopausal women with disease progression following endocrine therapy. - Treatment of HR-positive, HER2-negative advanced or metastatic breast cancer in combination with palbociclib in women with disease progression after endocrine therapy.",1,1,Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:38:04.612232+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10864,Ambroxol hydrochloride,Expel OD,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1u3-oXIysvshXTOLTIDggwfG3jx8mHNey/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10864_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1u3-oXIysvshXTOLTIDggwfG3jx8mHNey_view_usp_drivesdk_c9740f266d.pdf,page_text/DRP-10864_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1u3-oXIysvshXTOLTIDggwfG3jx8mHNey_view_usp_drivesdk_c9740f266d.json,bdbad7115184b77f75f55a9ea53bf9d185e6476f3a019ee0360362e7627a77f8,698721,2,digital_text,"Ambroxol HCI 75 mg sustained-release capsule comes in a hard gelatin capsule with scarlet red opaque cap and clear transparent body. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This medicine contains ambroxol, a mucolytic, which stimulates fluid secretion in the respiratory tract and breaks down mucus resulting in the production of less thick and less sticky mucus/phlegm. Ambroxol improves mucociliary clearance (mucus flow and transport) making phlegm easier to cough up and expel. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T14:38:09.587417+00:00
