ug is excreted in human milk. Because many drugs are excreted in human milk and because of the potential for serious adverse reactions in nursing infants from Clopidogrel, a decision should be made Clopidogrel bisulfate is a white to off-white powder. It is freely soluble in water and in methanol; whether to discontinue nursing or to discontinue the drug, taking into account the importance of the drug to practically insoluble in ether. the mother. Clopidogrel bisulfate (TIMIBEST) for oral administration is provided as brick red colour, round shape Pediatric Use biconvex, film-coated tablets plain on both side containing 99.812 mg of clopidogrel bisulfate which is the Safety and effectiveness in pediatric populations have not been established. molar equivalent of 75 mg of clopidogrel base. Geriatric Use Each tablet contains magnesium stearate, Colloidal Anhydrous Silica, Maize Starch , Crospovidone, There is no need of dosage adjustment in geriatric patients. Magnesium Stereate, Polyethyline glycol, Isopropyl Alcohol*,Lactose. The brick red colour film coating DRUGINTERACTIONS contains Titanium Dioxide, Red oxide of iron, Ready mix film coat , Coating Material Purified Talc, Clopidogrel should be used with caution in patients receiving other drugs that increase the risk of bleeding, Methylene Dichloride. including anticoagulants, other antiplatelets, and NSAIDs. Clopidogrel may inhibit the cytochrome P450 CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY - Mechanism of Action isoenzyme CYP2C9 and interactions with drugs metabolised by this isoenzyme are theoretically possible; it Clopidogrel is an inhibitor of platelet activation and aggregation through the irreversible binding of its active may also inhibit CYP2B6. metabolite to the P2Y12 class of adenosine diphosphate(ADP) receptors on platelets thus inhibiting ADP- ADVERSE DRUG REACTIONS mediated platelet aggregation. The incidence of adverse effects, particularly blood dyscrasias, is lower with Clopidogrel, although Pharmacodynamics fatalit