PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10946-05,Gentamicin (as sulfate),Neogenta,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zU-g6aD432zANGYoPPCTyUlHUM1tuSgw/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10946-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zU-g6aD432zANGYoPPCTyUlHUM1tuSgw_view_usp_drivesdk_60ad6f402f.pdf,page_text/DRP-10946-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zU-g6aD432zANGYoPPCTyUlHUM1tuSgw_view_usp_drivesdk_60ad6f402f.json,e8a6f50b972e3787b844039abdac8cb96f7cb87833171689c6c4dc9d103f512e,664982,1,digital_text,A clear colorless to slightly yellowish solution.,1,1,Product Description:,"hearing loss. Renal damage is reversible. Other aminoglycosides side effects include: localized ocular toxicity and hypersensitivity, lid itching, lid swelling and conjunctival erythema; bacterial/fungal corneal ulcers, nonspecic conjunctivitis; conjunctival epithelial defects; or hyperemia. Overdose and Treatment: Symptoms The oral ingestion of the contents of one bottle is unlikely to cause any signicant adverse effect. Management Haemodialysis and peritoneal dialysis will aid the removal from blood but the former is probably more efcient. Calcium salts given intravenously have been used to counter the neuromuscular blockade cause by gentamicin. Shelf-life: 3 years Caution: Foods, Drug, Devices, and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription. For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. Seek medical attention immediately at the rst sign of any adverse drug reaction. Storage Condition: Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from light. Do not refrigerate or freeze. KEEP ALL MEDICINES OUT OF REACH OF",1,1,indications of vestibular damage and impending,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:45:39.237588+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10957,Dexamethasone phosphate (as sodium),Ocubidex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1A8Rs1V-w-Wsz5UTsbPHeaQlG0CGo3LLS/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10957_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1A8Rs1V-w-Wsz5UTsbPHeaQlG0CGo3LLS_view_usp_drivesdk_ecfc959f49.pdf,page_text/DRP-10957_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1A8Rs1V-w-Wsz5UTsbPHeaQlG0CGo3LLS_view_usp_drivesdk_ecfc959f49.json,6655c6460ec48cac6554dfe7c287a6080a08c1fc84fc32ad92973ea47aa3a8c2,760211,1,digital_text,Clear colourless to pale yellow solution.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for treatment of steroid responsive inﬂammatory conditions of the palpebral and bulbar conjunctiva, cornea, and anterior segment of the globe such as allergic conjunctivitis, acne rosacea, superﬁcial punctate keratitis, herpes zoster keratitis, iritis, cyclitis, selected infective conjunctivitides when the inherent hazard of steroid use is accepted to obtain an advisable diminution in edema and inﬂammation; corneal injury from chemical, radiation, or thermal burns, or penetration of foreign bodies.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:46:07.673656+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-10960-02,Ceftriaxone (Sodium),Eurotrix,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/17P4mfoMBe-SKH_A56MlDU92uhLoDzyci/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-10960-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17P4mfoMBe-SKH_A56MlDU92uhLoDzyci_view_usp_drivesdk_6610f7c341.pdf,page_text/DRP-10960-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17P4mfoMBe-SKH_A56MlDU92uhLoDzyci_view_usp_drivesdk_6610f7c341.json,3b719cdc2c4ac53ad0a187758ea88b77929f359ff7399e650daa422e28095864,270494,4,digital_text,"White to yellowish-orange crystalline powder. When powder is reconstituted with sterile water for injection, it gives a light yellow to amber coloured solution.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated in the treatment of the following infections in adults and children including term neonates (from birth): Bacterial Meningitis Community acquired pneumonia Hospital acquired pneumonia Acute otitis media Intra-abdominal infections Complicated urinary tract infections (including pyelonephritis) Infections of bones and joints Complicated skin and soft tissue infections Gonorrhoea Syphilis Bacterial endocarditis Ceftriaxone may be used: For treatment of acute exacerbations of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease in adults For treatment of disseminated Lyme borreliosis (early (stage II) and late (stage III)) in adults and children including neonates from 15 days of age. For Pre-operative prophylaxis of surgical site infections In the management of neutropenic patients with fever that is suspected to be due to a bacterial infection In the treatment of patients with bacteraemia that occurs in association with, or is suspected to be associated with, any of the infections listed above Ceftriaxone should be co-administered with other antibacterial agents whenever the possible range of causative bacteria would not fall within its spectrum. Consideration should be given to official guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:46:10.850613+00:00
