PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11154-15,Nicardipine Hydrochloride,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1OU1-WBeQsKiK7NMESdK9wd6FKGVeHs1_/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11154-15_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OU1-WBeQsKiK7NMESdK9wd6FKGVeHs1__view_usp_drivesdk_78435a0fa2.pdf,page_text/DRP-11154-15_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OU1-WBeQsKiK7NMESdK9wd6FKGVeHs1__view_usp_drivesdk_78435a0fa2.json,a6b674f7362b1d65d2371d13735e54b4e79293fceec68db4a24cb65103af8dbd,3477547,1,digital_text,Yellow Coloured Clear Solution.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Nicardipine hydrochloride is indicated for the treatment of acute life-threatening hypertension, particularly in the event of: Malignant arterial hypertension/hypertensive encephalopathy; Aortic dissection, when short acting beta-blocker therapy is not suitable, or in combination with a beta-blocker when beta-blockade alone is not effective; Severe pre-eclampsia, when other intravenous antihypertensive agents are not recommended or are contraindicated; Nicardipine hydrochloride is also indicated for the treatment of post-operative hypertension.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:54:27.923213+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11154-16,Nicardipine Hydrochloride,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wD0QSxTY0V-S4B0XIMoS9fNwuLAE_xOe/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11154-16_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wD0QSxTY0V-S4B0XIMoS9fNwuLAE_xOe_view_usp_drivesdk_c372760bda.pdf,page_text/DRP-11154-16_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wD0QSxTY0V-S4B0XIMoS9fNwuLAE_xOe_view_usp_drivesdk_c372760bda.json,3516da6e56246080d9ac810f27a1ed350f18c549466bc6b758cf95973f1bf7a2,1264785,1,digital_text,Yellow Coloured Clear Solution.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Nicardipine hydrochloride is indicated for the treatment of acute life-threatening hypertension, particularly in the event of: Malignant arterial hypertension/hypertensive encephalopathy; Aortic dissection, when short acting beta-blocker therapy is not suitable, or in combination with a beta-blocker when beta-blockade alone is not effective; Severe pre-eclampsia, when other intravenous antihypertensive agents are not recommended or are contraindicated; Nicardipine hydrochloride is also indicated for the treatment of post-operative hypertension.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:54:31.275582+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11155,Octreotide (as acetate),Otide 50,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/11QmCNQsJ0BsY6JaErC2LYdKANV0b4KQ9/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11155_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11QmCNQsJ0BsY6JaErC2LYdKANV0b4KQ9_view_usp_drivesdk_a3351fb8f1.pdf,page_text/DRP-11155_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11QmCNQsJ0BsY6JaErC2LYdKANV0b4KQ9_view_usp_drivesdk_a3351fb8f1.json,8d4d006e17e84a872bab58392c6da0d13802cc258513d864efba2ef3f02515fc,679784,2,digital_text,OTIDE 50: 1 mL clear and colorles solution filled in 1 mL clear glass ampoule. OTIDE 100: 1 mL clear and colorles solution filled in 1 mL clear glass ampoule.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Symptomatic control and reduction of growth hormone (GH) and IGF-1 plasma levels in patients with acromegaly who are inadequately controlled by surgery or radiotherapy. Octreotide acetate treatment is also indicated foracromegalic patients unfit or unwilling to undergo surgery, or in the interim period until radiotherapy becomes fully effective. Relief of symptoms associated with functional gastroenteropancreatic (GEP) endocrine tumors: Carcinoid tumors with features of the carcinoid syndrome; VIPomas; Glucagonomas; Gastrinomas/Zollinger-Ellison syndrome, usually in conjunction with proton-pump inhibitors or H2-antagonist therapy; Insulinomas, for pre-operative control of hypoglycemia and for maintenance therapy; GRFomas. Octreotide acetate is not an anti-tumor therapy and is not curative in these patients. Prevention of complications following pancreatic surgery. Emergency management to stop bleeding and to protect from re-bleeding owing to gastro-esophageal varices in patients with cirrhosis. Octreotide acetate is to be used in association with specific treatment such as endoscopic sclerotherapy.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:54:34.781210+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11157,Sitagliptin (as phosphate monohydrate),None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1AeT8TRwxlom30o117atu_VSqkus2nkdM/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11157_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1AeT8TRwxlom30o117atu_VSqkus2nkdM_view_usp_drivesdk_2f95ebf234.pdf,page_text/DRP-11157_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1AeT8TRwxlom30o117atu_VSqkus2nkdM_view_usp_drivesdk_2f95ebf234.json,aa80612d18a92e224dfaf523f3b5ea5e62171bb92997be5e9e8f0e8bee927450,450643,3,digital_text,"Sitagliptin 25 mg Film -Coated Tablet is available as peach to light orange, circular, biconvex film -coated tablet , plain on both sides packed in Alu/Alu Blister Pack x 10’s (Box of 30’s). Sitagliptin 50 mg Film -Coated Tablet is available as light beige to beige , circular, bicon vex film -coated tablet, with “50” embossed on one side and with break line on the other side packed in Alu/Alu Blister Pack x 10’s (Box of 30’s). Sitagliptin 100 mg Film-Coated Tablet is available as light beige to beige , circular, bicon vex film -coated tablet, with “100” embossed on one side and with break line on the other side packed in Alu/Alu Blister Pack x 1 0’s (Box of 30’s).",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Monotherapy SITAGLIPTIN PHOSPHATE is indicated as an adjunct to diet a nd exercise to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus. Combination with Metformin SITAGLIPTIN PHOSPHATE is indicated in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus to improve glycemic control in combination with metformin as initial therapy or when the single agent alone, with diet and exercise, does not provide adequate glycemic control. Combination with a Sulfonylurea SITAGLIPTIN PHOSPHATE is indicated in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus to improve glycemic control in combination with a sulfonylurea when treatment with the single agent alone, with diet and exercise, does not provide adequate glycemic control. Combination with a PPARγ agonist SITAGLIPTIN PHOSPHATE is indicated in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus to impr ove glycemic control in combination with a PPARγ agonist (i.e., thiazolidinediones) as initial therapy or when the single agent alone, with diet and exercise, does not provide adequate glycemic control. Combination with Metformin and a Sulfonylurea SITAGLIPTIN PHOSPHATE is indicated in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus to improve glycemic control in combination with metformin and a sulfonylurea when dual therapy with these agents, with diet and exercise, does not provide adequate glycemic control. Combination with Metformin and a PPARγ agonist SITAGLIPTIN PHOSPHATE is indicated in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus to improve glycemic control in combination with metformin and a PPARγ agonist (i.e., thiazolidinediones) when dual therapy with these agents, with diet and exercise, does not provide adequate glycemic control. Combination with Insulin SITAGLIPTIN PHOSPHATE is indicated in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in combi nation with insulin (with or without metformin).",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T14:54:38.267596+00:00
