PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11247,Ascorbic Acid,Imilion C-Plus,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/15aBzwxdsVYmkPVofIxsvzKLx8E1hmTz7/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11247_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15aBzwxdsVYmkPVofIxsvzKLx8E1hmTz7_view_usp_drivesdk_c4dc7115cd.pdf,page_text/DRP-11247_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15aBzwxdsVYmkPVofIxsvzKLx8E1hmTz7_view_usp_drivesdk_c4dc7115cd.json,3e32c0e297fc95300a6c259ffbc60f349c9b8f4d2f4fed61fe4ec25028f69dad,417293,1,digital_text,"Vitamin C (Imilion C-Plus) 500mg Chewable Tablet is an orange yellow disc. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE This product contains Ascorbic Acid, a Vitamin. Ascorbic Acid is also known as Vitamin C. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Each tablet contains Vitamin C 200 mg, Sodium Ascorbate 300 mg WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? This medicine is used for treatment and prevention of Vitamin C deficiency. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? These tablets are to be taken by mouth. Chew Vitamin C Chewable Tablet before swallowing. Adults (including elderly) For the treatment of Vitamin C deficiency: 250mg- 100mg daily in divided doses. For the prevention of Vitamin C deficiency: 25mg- 75mg daily Children (aged 4 to 12 years) For the treatment of Vitamin C deficiency: 125mg- 500mg daily in divided doses. For the prevention of Vitamin C deficiency: 25mg- 75mg daily Children under 4 years Vitamin C chewable tablets 500mg are not suitable for children under 4 years of age. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Do not take Vitamin C (Imilion C-Plus): · If you have an allergic reaction to Vitamin C or any component if the preparation. · If you suffer form hyperoxaluria (excretion of urine containing large amounts of calcium oxalate crystals) CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Before taking Vitamin C (Imilion C-Plus) Chewable Tablet, tell your doctor: · If you are to undergo any blood or urine test as ascorbic acid can interfere with some blood and urine tests · If you are a regular smoker · If you have kidney failure as Vitamin C enhances aluminum absorption (present in antacids) which may reach toxic levels. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE As with all medicines, Vitamin C (Imilion C-Plus) Chewable Tablet can cause unwanted side effects in some patients. Stop taking this medicine immediately and consult your doctor if you suffer an allergic reaction after taking this medicine. An allergic reaction may include itching, a rash, swelling of the face, lips, tongue and/or throat with difficulty in swallowing or breathing. If you experience any of the following you should see your doctor of pharmacist: · Diarrhea, stomach cramps, nausea (feeling sick), vomiting (being sick) · Flushing or redness of the skin · Hemolytic anemia (where the body's immune system attacks its own red blood cells), signs may include fatigue and paleness · Diuretic effect (increased urine flow) due to increased intake of ascorbic acid taken is prolonged period. High doses of over 600mg daily can have a diuretic effect in some patients. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Vitamin C (Imilion C-Plus) Chewable Tablets may interfere with other medicines that you may be taking. This includes medicine you can buy without a prescription, including herbal medicines. In particular, tell your doctor if you are taking any of the following: · Amphetamines · Contraceptives · Iron-containing medicines · Antacids · Amygdalin (Vitamin B17) – can cause cyanide toxicity WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten dose, just resume your schedule and go on as before. If you are not sure what to do, ask you pharmacist. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE Ascorbic Acid may cause acidosis or hemolytic anemia in certain individuals with a deficiency of glucose 6-phosphate dehydrogenase. Renal failure can occur with massive ascorbic acid overdosage. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSE? If too many tablets are taken, consult your doctor or go to your nearest hospital IMMEDIATELY. Take the tablets or this leaflet with you so the doctor knows what has been taken HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Do not store above 25°C. Store in the original container. Keep away from heat and direct sunlight. Exposure to these conditions may lead to slight discoloration. Keep out of reach and sight of children. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? Tell your doctor or pharmacist if you think you may experience any of the symptoms or experience other problems with your medicine not mentioned above. He or she will have more information about it and will tell you what to do. ADR REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. AVAILABILITY PVC/Aluminum Blister Pack X 10's (Box of 100's) REGISTRATION NUMBER: DRP-11247 DATE OF FIRST AUTHORIZATION/RENEWAL OF THE AUTHORIZATION: FEB. 17, 2022 DATE OF REVISION OF PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET: JUN. 25, 2024 Manufactured by:",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T14:57:11.076538+00:00
