PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11451-01,Montelukast (as sodium),Gokast-10,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/17cg2mbPQg-Koa8ObOyuDY-gs0zEVl2Sv/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11451-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17cg2mbPQg-Koa8ObOyuDY-gs0zEVl2Sv_view_usp_drivesdk_d0920a82f5.pdf,page_text/DRP-11451-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17cg2mbPQg-Koa8ObOyuDY-gs0zEVl2Sv_view_usp_drivesdk_d0920a82f5.json,5e62374df3caedaad264953be05f8d1be482bc069267b3685f3d23b556c9ee1d,159681,2,digital_text,"Yellow colour, round shape, biconvex, film coated tablets, plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for the treatment of asthma as add -on therapy in those patientswith mild to moderate persistent asthma who are inadequately controlled on inhaled corticosteroids and in whom “as -needed” short acting β -agonists provide inadequate clinical control of asthma. In those asthmatic patients in whom Montelukast 10 mg film -coated tablets is indicated in asthma, Montelukast 10 mg film -coated tablets can also provide symptomatic relief of seasonal allergic rhinitis. Montelukast 10 mg film -coated tablets is also indicated in the prophylaxis of asthma in which the predominant component is exercise-induced bronchoconstriction.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:00:20.905565+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11452-01,Montelukast (as sodium),Gentakast 5,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cFuiHV4K_9QfapnK81WpBQyNcxJrhjsz/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11452-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cFuiHV4K_9QfapnK81WpBQyNcxJrhjsz_view_usp_drivesdk_2728920eec.pdf,page_text/DRP-11452-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cFuiHV4K_9QfapnK81WpBQyNcxJrhjsz_view_usp_drivesdk_2728920eec.json,7e147052aa3285f30426a80d095c561be6a1a30c5938ea34c06a7bfa9bdaedc0,161690,2,digital_text,Light pink coloured round shaped uncoated tablet plain on both sides.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for the treatment of asthma as add-on therapy in those patients with mild to moderate persistent asthma who are inadequately controlled on inhaled corticosteroids and in whom 'as -needed' short-acting β-agonists provide inadequate clinical control of asthma. Montelukast may also be an alternative treatment option to low -dose inhaled corticosteroids for patients with mild persistent asthma who do not have a recent history of serious asthma attacks that required oral corticosteroid use, and who have demonstrated that they are not capable of using inhaled corticosteroids. Montelukast is also indicated in the prophylaxis of asthma from in which the predominant component is exercise-induced bronchoconstriction.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:00:24.184513+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11453-01,Montelukast (as sodium),Gokast-4,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1o_xBH5jgffHBD-DcDFcXLMkNKD2FuQUq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11453-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1o_xBH5jgffHBD-DcDFcXLMkNKD2FuQUq_view_usp_drivesdk_894328e42d.pdf,page_text/DRP-11453-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1o_xBH5jgffHBD-DcDFcXLMkNKD2FuQUq_view_usp_drivesdk_894328e42d.json,c43c9e753745808532457ef4a176e94e65cf705d601e47ab11f5bc4a9ed85d97,162629,2,digital_text,White to off white coloured round shaped uncoated tablet plain on both sides.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for the treatment of asthma as add-on therapy in those patients with mild to moderate persistent asthma who are inadequately controlled on inhaled corticosteroids and in whom 'as -needed' short-acting β-agonists provide inadequate clinical control of asthma. Montelukast may also be an alternative treatment option to low -dose inhaled corticosteroids for patients with mild persistent asthma who do not have a recent history of serious asthma attacks that required oral corticosteroid use, and who have demonstrated that they are not capable of using inhaled corticosteroids. Montelukast is also indicated in the prophylaxis of asthma from in which the predominant component is exercise-induced bronchoconstriction.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:00:27.481093+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11454,Silver Sulfadiazine,Silvakhriz,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NEDyBCQjjmZh35AXb7e5ZkfXPtfw6UeN/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11454_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1NEDyBCQjjmZh35AXb7e5ZkfXPtfw6UeN_view_usp_drivesdk_e430f9bc2b.pdf,page_text/DRP-11454_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1NEDyBCQjjmZh35AXb7e5ZkfXPtfw6UeN_view_usp_drivesdk_e430f9bc2b.json,e9e53a987e1126bdd708518d029b05ee1f0aa468e23866bc368dc519a799f26a,93920,2,digital_text,"White, soft, thick mass cream",1,1,Product Description:,"-treatment of infected burn wounds -prevention of infection of burn wounds -treatment of infected skin lesions Mode of Application: Silver Sulfadiazine can be applied directly to the wound in a layer of at least 2-3 mm. Silver Sulfadiazine can also be applied using a sterile gauze dressing. At least every 24 hours the cream should be reapplied after the removal of the old cream. Application is easy and painless. Discoloration of linen and bedclothes does not occur. Side-effects: Leucopenia has been reported in a restricted number of patients (incidence 0.4%). In most of these patients, the white blood cell count (WBC) returned to normal in spite of prolonged treatment. In case signs or symptoms possibly related to leucopenia appear or when the patient is known to be hypersensitive to sulfonamides, a WBC count is recommended. Skin rash has been reported in a small number of patients (incidence 0.3%), but appears to be related to excipients propylene glycol and cetyl alcohol. Silver Sulfadiazine has not been shown to alter electrolyte balance.",1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:00:30.716558+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11456,Telmisartan + Amlodipine,Telmilop,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ePwa84jXEKP6Fl4E4TynktRMS5yKUq-2/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11456_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ePwa84jXEKP6Fl4E4TynktRMS5yKUq-2_view_usp_drivesdk_f0ce1da0d5.pdf,page_text/DRP-11456_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ePwa84jXEKP6Fl4E4TynktRMS5yKUq-2_view_usp_drivesdk_f0ce1da0d5.json,821a9c5e6545980cc8645e687c54fa5ebd4feaa2b8a4cad6ceabd00df5f160b9,698185,1,digital_text,"White to off white, oblong, uncoated bilayered tablet with debossed 'C7' on one side and blue plain on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Treatment of essential hypertension. Replacement Therapy: Patients receiving Telmisartan and Amlodipine besilate from separate tablets may instead receive Telmisartan + Amlodipine besilate containing the same component doses. Add-on therapy: Telmisartan + Amlodipine besilate is indicated in patients whose blood pressure is not adequately controlled on Telmisartan or Amlodipine monotherapy. Initial therapy: Telmisartan + Amlodipine besilate may also be used as initial therapy in patients who are likely to need multiple drugs to achieve their blood pressure goals. The choice of Telmisartan + Amlodipine besilate as initial therapy for hypertension should be based on an assessment of potential benefits and risks.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:00:34.734946+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11457-01,,,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/13Bi_CpS50chlcC5mrfY9VMI3QjG6g75H/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11457-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13Bi_CpS50chlcC5mrfY9VMI3QjG6g75H_view_usp_drivesdk_25ff69c16c.pdf,page_text/DRP-11457-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13Bi_CpS50chlcC5mrfY9VMI3QjG6g75H_view_usp_drivesdk_25ff69c16c.json,bc1081039d7ab8f17e8750dfa0f544c09ac09d4ff904d74b761b45b8c53a614b,627720,1,digital_text,"Sitagliptin 100 mg is a white to off-white colored, round shaped, biconvex, film-coated tablet, plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Sitagliptin is indicated for the treatment of diabetes mellitus type 2 in persons 18 years of age and older who have failed dietary measures and exercise: - as monotherapy, as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus, when metformin cannot be used. - as dual combination therapy, with metformin, or with a sulfonylurea, or with a thiazolidinedione where the use of a thiazolidinedione is considered appropriate. - as triple combination therapy with metformin and a sulfonylurea when combination therapy with both agents does not provide adequate glycemic control. - as add-on combination therapy with insulin (with or without metformin).",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:00:37.621037+00:00
