PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11585,Ibandronic Acid (as sodium monohydrate),Ibanox,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1SxYgZ9R9xxPjfatji1UV-_wFgVJVaPPJ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11585_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1SxYgZ9R9xxPjfatji1UV-_wFgVJVaPPJ_view_usp_drivesdk_7c629314bc.pdf,page_text/DRP-11585_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1SxYgZ9R9xxPjfatji1UV-_wFgVJVaPPJ_view_usp_drivesdk_7c629314bc.json,ae358ca998ecd07637a92bec82f08078b1e115c480dc9ba44a3d8776173cc6d7,4687926,2,ocr,"Film-coated tablet. White, round biconvex tablets. CLINICAL PARTICULARS Therapeutic indications Treatment of osteoporosis in postmenopausal women at increased risk of fracture (see Pharmacodynamic properties). A reduction in the risk of vertebral fractures has been demonstrated, efficacy on femoral neck fractures has not been established. woe",1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Treatment of osteoporosis in postmenopausal women at increased risk of fracture (see Pharmacodynamic properties). A reduction in the risk of vertebral fractures has been demonstrated, efficacy on femoral neck fractures has not been established. woe",1,1,Therapeutic indications,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T15:03:39.832112+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11595,Capecitabine,Capnorm-500,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZjwcZLPSwMdhRkHbaDrGbEkcXnkFLqYt/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11595_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZjwcZLPSwMdhRkHbaDrGbEkcXnkFLqYt_view_usp_drivesdk_9663b7b86f.pdf,page_text/DRP-11595_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZjwcZLPSwMdhRkHbaDrGbEkcXnkFLqYt_view_usp_drivesdk_9663b7b86f.json,8ae38ff2687757ed5f924e2442725bce38028905020a59bf1413e2c66f020913,1434217,1,digital_text,A light pink-colored elongated biconvex film-coated tablets.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Capecitabine is indicated for the treatment of: - for the adjuvant treatment of patients following surgery for stage III (Dukes' stage C) colon cancer. - metastatic colorectal cancer. - first-line treatment of advanced gastric cancer in combination with a platinum-based regimen. - in combination with docetaxel for the treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic breast cancer after failure of cytotoxic chemotherapy. Previous therapy should have included an anthracycline. - as monotherapy for the treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic breast cancer after failure of taxanes and an anthracycline-containing chemotherapy regimen or for whom further anthracycline therapy is not indicated.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:03:43.512026+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11601-01,Ceftazidime (As Pentahydrate),Zefadime,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JJwOI_eTQAiA70jif-RlSUjO6cU8_zcC/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11601-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1JJwOI_eTQAiA70jif-RlSUjO6cU8_zcC_view_usp_drivesdk_ce8a67f69c.pdf,page_text/DRP-11601-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1JJwOI_eTQAiA70jif-RlSUjO6cU8_zcC_view_usp_drivesdk_ce8a67f69c.json,b6607c3685ebf1f0fe79e45721e04c0eda33deac9b03d043536d62eeb4b495f0,415999,4,digital_text,White to cream colored crystalline powder,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for the treatment of the infections listed below in adults and children including neonates (from birth). • Nosocomial pneumonia • Broncho-pulmonary infections in cystic fibrosis • Bacterial meningitis • Chronic suppurative otitis media • Malignant otitis externa • Complicated urinary tract infections • Complicated skin and soft tissue infections • Complicated intra-abdominal infections • Bone and joint infections • Peritonitis associated with dialysis in patients on CAPD. Treatment of patients with bacteraemia that occurs in association with, or is suspected to be associated with, any of the infections listed above. Ceftazidime may be used in the management of neutropenic patients with fever that is suspected to be due to a bacterial infection. Ceftazidime may be used in the peri -operative prophylaxis of urinary tract infections for patients undergoing trans -urethral resection of the prostate",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:03:46.709636+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11606,Nicardipine Hydrochloride,Nicarsaph,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mQ67dVj8Mhl3TvOd_LlwKl_Aprrjs43P/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11606_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mQ67dVj8Mhl3TvOd_LlwKl_Aprrjs43P_view_usp_drivesdk_3a5bcf8fab.pdf,page_text/DRP-11606_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mQ67dVj8Mhl3TvOd_LlwKl_Aprrjs43P_view_usp_drivesdk_3a5bcf8fab.json,e35a90374ee0abc37178b4d6450369e429685b0277d34f7992a489674d01d63b,5510663,1,digital_text,Pale yellow to yellow coloured clear solution.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Nicardipine solution for injection is indicated for the treatment of acute life-threatening hypertension, particularly in the event of: • Malignant arterial hypertension/hypertensive encephalopathy • Aortic dissection, when short acting beta-blocker therapy is not suitable, or in combination with a beta-blocker when beta-blockade alone is not eﬀective • Severe pre-eclampsia, when other intravenous antihypertensive agents are not recommended or are contra-indicated • Nicardipine is also indicated for the treatment of post-operative hypertension",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:03:51.473299+00:00
