PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11623,Norepinephrine (as bitartrate),Norepinsaph-1,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ppME9NgR0VDlw76zmYsWBb_BDsGQhpGN/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11623_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ppME9NgR0VDlw76zmYsWBb_BDsGQhpGN_view_usp_drivesdk_acabac7960.pdf,page_text/DRP-11623_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ppME9NgR0VDlw76zmYsWBb_BDsGQhpGN_view_usp_drivesdk_acabac7960.json,73fced7c4c7cee87e965e1d3dde3151c0a0854aa389ea4f09ac7127076b62114,8625515,1,ocr,"rrine base (which is t to 80 mglliter tartrate). Dilutions other than Aclear, colourless solution. 40 mgfliter Norepinephrine base may also be used. If dilutions other than 40 mg/liter Norepinephrine base are used, check the infusion rate calculation carefully before starting treatment.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,risks to the fetus should therefore be weighed against the potential benefit to the mother. Breastfeeding Indicated for use as an emergency measure in the restoration of blood pressure in cases of acute lo labl the use of hypotension pi phrine in lactation.,1,1,INDICATION,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T15:04:14.453183+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11624,Colecalciferol (Vitamin D3),None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bdDA1lWz8KBDBJV-JWEysdLzmw_Eb59Z/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11624_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bdDA1lWz8KBDBJV-JWEysdLzmw_Eb59Z_view_usp_drivesdk_8dc9555810.pdf,page_text/DRP-11624_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bdDA1lWz8KBDBJV-JWEysdLzmw_Eb59Z_view_usp_drivesdk_8dc9555810.json,0eb5726b2a22ced0f8f73731862928c9e469098c4a46c44c5a789c9428837b84,291792,1,digital_text,"Pale yellow to yellow film-coated tablet, oval shaped, biconvex, with break line on one side and plain on the other side. What is in the medicine? It contains Vitamin D3 which regulates the uptake and metabolism of calcium as well as the incorporation of calcium in bone tissue. Strength of the medicine Each fim-coated tablet contains: Vitamin D3…………………………… 2,000 IU. What is this medicine used for? It is used for the treatment and prevention of Vitamin D deficiencies as well as maintenance and support of immune system function. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Adult Dose 1 tablet daily or as prescribed by physician. Use in Children Vitamin D3 is not intended for use in children under 12 years due to lack of study data. When should you not take this medicine? If you are allergic to colecalciferol or any of the other ingredients of this medicine. If you have hypercalcaemia (increased levels of calcium in the blood) or hypercalciuria (increased levels of calcium in urine). If you have hypervitaminosis D (increased levels of Vitamin D in the blood). If you have kidney stones. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine? If you suffer from sarcoidosis (a special type of connective tissue disease that af fects the lungs, skin and joints). When using other drugs containing Vitamin D. If you have kidney problems or have had kidney stones. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Like all medicines, this medicine can cause side effects, although not everybody gets them. Stop taking Vitamin D3 and seek immediate medicinal help if you experience symptoms of serious allergic reactions, such as: · Swollen face, lips, tongue or throat · Difficult to swallow · Hives and difficulty in breathing Uncommon: Hypercalcaemia and hypercalciuria. Rare: pruritis, rash and urticaria What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? · Cholestyramine (used to treat high cholesterol). · Phenytoin or barbiturates (used to treat epilepsy). · Laxatives which contain paraffin oil. · Thiazide diuretics (to treat high blood pressure). · Glucocorticoids (to treat infalmmation). · Cardiac glycosides (to treat heart conditions, e.g. digoxin) What should you do if you miss a dose? Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten dose. Signs and symptoms of overdose The signs and symptoms of Vitamin D3 are the following: · Getting sick or infected often · Fatigue or tiredness · Bone and back pain · Depression · Impaired wound healing · Bone less · Hair loss · Muscle pain What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a physician. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from light and moisture. When should you consult your doctor? If any undesirable effect occurs. Availability: Alu/Amber PVC-PVDC Blister Pack x 10’s (Box of 100’s) Name and address of Manufacturer:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T15:04:17.787165+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11631,Tadalafil,Tadafil 20,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Q2kB1c_o3l-Q-tM0HDeNQsd3gayj6bLn/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11631_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Q2kB1c_o3l-Q-tM0HDeNQsd3gayj6bLn_view_usp_drivesdk_5cf19ff4d2.pdf,page_text/DRP-11631_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Q2kB1c_o3l-Q-tM0HDeNQsd3gayj6bLn_view_usp_drivesdk_5cf19ff4d2.json,524f54b810878f508401cc5a1ff5e0683461a26338299ee2b14a1993faa47a17,182542,2,digital_text,"Tadalafil Tablets USP 2.5 mg: Blue colour, round shaped, biconvex, film coated tablets debossed with ‘T18’ on one side and ‘H’ on the other side. Tadalafil Tablets USP 5 mg: White colour, round shaped, biconvex, film coated tablets debossed with ‘T17’ on one side and ‘H’ on the other side. Tadalafil Tablets USP 10 mg: White colour, capsule shaped, biconvex, film coated tablets debossed with ‘T16’ on one side and ‘H’ on the other side. Tadalafil Tablets USP 20 mg: White colour, capsule shaped, biconvex, film coated tablets debossed with ‘T15’ on one side and ‘H’ on the other side. Tadalafil is (6 R-12aR)-6-(1,3-Benzodioxol-5-yl)-2-methyl- 2, 3, 6, 7, 12, 12a-hexahydro-2- methylpyrazino[1’,2’: 1,6]pyrido[3,4-b]indole-1,4-dione. The molecular formula is C22H19N3O4 and the molecular weight is 389.41. The chemical structure of Tadalafil is: Tadalafil is white or almost white crystalline powder. Sample was slightly hygroscopic. Freely Soluble in dimethyl sulfoxide, dimethylformamide, slightly soluble in methylene chloride and practically insoluble in water. Tadalafil contain the following inactive ingredients: Lactose Monohydrate, Copovidone, Colloidal Silicon Dioxide, (Aerosil 200), Polyoxyl 40 hydrogenated castor oil (Kolliphor RH 40), Lactose Monohydrate, (Super Tab 11 SD), Micro crystalline cellulose, (Avicel PH 1 02), Croscarmellose sodium {Ac-disol), Colloidal Silicon Dioxide, (Aerosil 200), Magnesium stearate (Ligarned MF-2-V), Opadry II White 32K580001, Purified water THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS Erectile Dysfunction Tadalafil is indicated for the treatment of erectile dysfunction (ED). Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia TADALAFIL is indicated for the treatment of the signs and symptoms of benign prostatic hyperplasia",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Erectile Dysfunction Tadalafil is indicated for the treatment of erectile dysfunction (ED). Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia TADALAFIL is indicated for the treatment of the signs and symptoms of benign prostatic hyperplasia,1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:04:20.946901+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11632-01,Levodropropizine,Extusiv,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ou3pcoEAg20XQG_SNRorAUbp1i93W7HY/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11632-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ou3pcoEAg20XQG_SNRorAUbp1i93W7HY_view_usp_drivesdk_a8331c8b6f.pdf,page_text/DRP-11632-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ou3pcoEAg20XQG_SNRorAUbp1i93W7HY_view_usp_drivesdk_a8331c8b6f.json,1996794aae7be95225d1a54056cfa9c688a5c5e2e5822058390975d1180cc65f,1426145,1,ocr,"Central nervous system Almostcolorless, clear orange-flavored syrup. ° Exhaustion, faintness ° Somnolence, clouding ofconsciousness (stupor)",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Cardiovascular system Forthe symptomaticrelief of cough © Palpitations . Hypersensitivity reactions may occur in predisposed patients because levodropropizine PHARMACODYNAMICS contains parabens Ac . Allergic skin reactions were observed in very rare cases. Levodropropizine, the (-)-(S)-isomer of dropropizine, is a cough suppressant with peripheral action. It . Consult your physician or pharmacist in the event other side effects appear. decreases the excitability of tracheobronchial receptors thus suppressing the cough reflex.",1,1,INDICATION,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T15:04:28.192538+00:00
