he total adult anaerobes Gardnerella vaginalis and Helicobacter pylori and against some spirochetes. The mode of action of daily dose; aged 7 to 10 years one-half the tota 4 . | adult daily do: se; alternatively 35 to 50 mg/kg daily in divided doses. In balantidiasis and Bi ystis h - 750 mg (1 % tablets) three times daily for 5 and 10 days, metronidazole involves reduction by bacterial ‘nitroreductases’ to an unstable intermediate which interacts with DNA, respectivel effectively preventing further replication. A number of factors affect the sensitivity of microorganisms to metronidazole in In giardiasis - 2 g (4 tablets) once daily for 3 successive days, or 400 mg three times daily for 5 days, or 500 mg (1 tablet) vitro. Anaerobic conditions are important for optimal activity. twice daily for 7 to 10 days dental infections. In acute necrotizing ulcerative gingivitis — 200 mg three times daily is given for 3 days; similar doses are used in acute PHARMACOKINETICS h +i di ta Holi, h Metronidazole is readily and almost completely absorbed after oral doses. Peak plasma concentrations of about 6 and 12 In peptic ulcer disease in therapy t F ter pylori - 400 mg twice daily except when given with omeprazole and amoxicillin, metronidazole 400 mg is used three times daily; continued for 1 week. micrograms/mL are achieved, usually within 1 to 2 hours, after single doses of 250 and 500 mg respectively. Some For leg ulcers and pressure sores infected with anaerobic bacteria - 400 mg may be given three times daily for 7 days. accumulation occurs and consequently there are higher concentrations when multiple doses are given. Absorption may Metronidazole (Sydenzole) should be given with caution and at reduced doses to patients with severe hepatic impairment, be delayed, but is not reduced overall by food. Metronidazole is widely distributed. It appears in most body tissues and and especially hepatic encephalopathy. In patients with renal impairment, metronidazole need to be given immediately after fluids including bile, bone, breast milk, cerebral abscesses, CSF, liver and liver abscesses, saliva, seminal fluid, and vaginal secretions, and achieves concentrations similar to those in plasma. It also crosses the placenta and rapidly hemodialysis. enters the fetal circulation. No more than 20% is bound to plasma proteins. Metronidazole is metabolised in the liver by Or as prescribed by a physician. side-chain oxidation and glucuronide",4,4,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"INTERACTIONS Metronidazole (Sydenzole) is a 5-nitroimidazole derivative used in the treatment of susceptible protozoal infections such as amoebiasis, balantidiasis, Blastocystis hominis infections, giardiasis, and trichomoniasis. It is also used in the When given with alcohol, metronidazole (Sydenzole) may provoke a disulfiram-like reaction in some patients. Acute psychoses or confusion have been associated with the use of metronidazole (Sydenzole) and disulfiram together. treatment and prophylaxis of anaerobic bacterial infections which include bacterial vaginosis, acute necrotizing ulcerative Metronidazole (Sydenzole) is reported to impair the metabolism or excretion of several drugs including warfarin, phenytoin, gingivitis, pelvic inflammatory disease, tetanus, and antibiotic associated colitis. It is used to eradicate Helicobacter pylori lithium, ciclosporin, and fluorouracil, with the consequent potential for an increased incidence of adverse effects. There is in peptic ulcer disease (with other antimicrobials, and either bismuth compounds or proton pump inhibitors) and in the some evidence that phenytoin might accelerate the metabolism of metronidazole (Sydenzole). Plasma concentrations of metronidazole (Sydenzole) are decreased by phenobarbital, with a consequent reduction in the effectiveness of management of malodorous tumors and ulcers where there is anaerobic infection. metronidazole (Sydenzole). Cimetidine has increased plasma concentrations of metronidazole (Sydenzole) and might increase the risk of neurological adverse effects. [Page 5]",4,4,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T15:04:44.794460+00:00
