PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11713,Omeprazole,Mepracid 40Â®,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1AA84GutaBQ-ayRDfIhY53EJhBbnGTbxr/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11713_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1AA84GutaBQ-ayRDfIhY53EJhBbnGTbxr_view_usp_drivesdk_b8bb94bd2b.pdf,page_text/DRP-11713_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1AA84GutaBQ-ayRDfIhY53EJhBbnGTbxr_view_usp_drivesdk_b8bb94bd2b.json,267d50e2da6cadb31ec8fd76cbcab5b5530edaef1b95bf8ab69ff6f8f7401873,440634,1,digital_text,"Omeprazole belongs to a class of antisecretory compounds, the substituted Benzimidazoles, that do not exhibit anticholinergic or H2 histamine antagonistic properties, but that suppress gastric acid secretion by specific inhibition of the H/K ATPase enzyme system at the secretory surface of the gastric parietal cell. Because this enzyme is the ""acid (proton) pump"" within the gastric mucosa, Omeprazole has been characterized as a gastric acid pump inhibitor: It blocks the final step of acid production. The effect is dose related & inhibit both basal & stimulated acid secretion regardless of the stimulus.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"It is used to treat peptic ulcer disease, gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD), heartburn and other symptoms associated with GERD, severe erosive esophagitis and approved for combination use in the eradication of H. Pylori in patients with active duodenal ulcer.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:08:20.533747+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11720-01,Moxifloxacin (as hydrochloride),Moxidin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dndp4mp3W6QsygUmyl7xi9EA_L43bZlR/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11720-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dndp4mp3W6QsygUmyl7xi9EA_L43bZlR_view_usp_drivesdk_08ad196262.pdf,page_text/DRP-11720-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dndp4mp3W6QsygUmyl7xi9EA_L43bZlR_view_usp_drivesdk_08ad196262.json,31c1e87148aad6ca019df4297492e83c1dd524a3baf4e80918bbf0d50e58277c,3010955,1,digital_text,Pale green-yellow solution in a transparent plastic bottle.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"The treatment of bacterial conjunctivitis, tarsadenitis, keratitis (including corneal ulcer), caused by susceptible strains of the following organisms, aseptic therapy after ophthalmic surgery: Staphylococcus aureus, Streptococcus, Streptococcus pneumoniae, Enterococcus, Micrococcus, Moraxella, Corynebacterium, Citrobacter, Klebsiella, Enterobacter, Serratia, Proteus, Morganella morganii, Haemophilus influenzae, Pseudomonas, Burkholderia cepacia, Stenotrophomonas maltophilia, Acinetobacter.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:08:25.001906+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11723,Salbutamol (As Sulfate),Ventolin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZvHiva3TLPkyOqg4KrYNfzvy0NjmM2_s/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11723_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZvHiva3TLPkyOqg4KrYNfzvy0NjmM2_s_view_usp_drivesdk_939443f14f.pdf,page_text/DRP-11723_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZvHiva3TLPkyOqg4KrYNfzvy0NjmM2_s_view_usp_drivesdk_939443f14f.json,77b010438cf993032cb52ee7edd83237a7dbaa3f770e55acb94e5fe6e0d1d007,1375516,2,digital_text,"Salbutamol (Ventolin) 2mg/5mL Syrup, orange flavour: Each 5mL of orange flavoured syrup contains Salbutamol sulfate equivalent to 2mg Salbutamol.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Salbutamol (Ventolin) is a selective beta- 2 adrenoceptor agonist indicated for the treatment or prevention of bronchospasm. It provides short acting bronchodilation in reversible airways obstruction due to asthma, chronic bronchitis and emphysema. Bronchodilators should not be the only or main treatment in patients with persistent asthma. In patients with persistent asthma unresponsive to Salbutamol (Ventolin), treatment with inhaled corticosteroids is recommended to achieve and maintain control. Failing to respond to treatment with Salbutamol (Ventolin) may signal a need for urgent medical advice or treatment. Salbutamol (Ventolin) syrup is indicated for the relief of bronchospasm in bronchial asthma of all types, chronic bronchitis and emphysema. Salbutamol (Ventolin) Syrup is suitable oral therapy for children or those adults who prefer liquid medicines.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:08:28.793352+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11726-01,Ciprofloxacin (as Hydrochloride),Cirok,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_3KEHkv-XNVUveXNmzWUp2teDHZXaVra/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11726-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_3KEHkv-XNVUveXNmzWUp2teDHZXaVra_view_usp_drivesdk_727855b5cb.pdf,page_text/DRP-11726-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_3KEHkv-XNVUveXNmzWUp2teDHZXaVra_view_usp_drivesdk_727855b5cb.json,46971cdc5330fd0cf1c22727d2d1eb752a0bc677b5a7d88e5661a656a5d17f16,4470193,2,digital_text,"White to off-white coloured, capsule-shaped, film-coated tablet. Break-line on one side and plain on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Indicated for the treatment of the following infections. Special attention should be paid to available information on resistance to ciprofloxacin before commencing therapy. Consideration should be given to official guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents. Adults Lower respiratory tract infections due to Gram-negative bacteria - exacerbations of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease - broncho-pulmonary infections in cystic fibrosis or in bronchiectasis - pneumonia Chronic suppurative otitis media Acute exacerbation of chronic sinusitis especially if these are caused by Gram-negative bacteria Urinary tract infections Genital tract infections Gonococcal uretritis and cervicitis due to susceptible Neisseria gonarrhoeae Epididymo-orchitis including cases due to susceptible Neisseria gonorrhoeae Pelvic inflammatory disease including cases due to susceptible Neisseria gonorrhoeae In the above genital tract infections when thought or known to be due to Neisseria gonorrhoeae it is particularly important to obtain local information on the prevalence of resistance to ciprofloxacin and to confirm susceptibility based on laboratory testing. Infections of the gastro-intestinal tract (e.g. travellers' diarrhoea) Intra-abdominal infections Infections of the skin and soft tissue caused by Gram-negative bacteria Malignant external otitis Infections of the bones and joints Treatment of infections in neutropenic patients Prophylaxis of infections in neutropenic patients Prophylaxis of invasive infections due to Neisseria meningitides Inhalation anthrax (post-exposure prophylaxis and curative treatment) Ciprofloxacin may be used in the management of neutropenic patients with fever that is suspected to be due to a bacterial infection. Paediatric population Broncho-pulmonary infections in cystic fibrosis caused by Pseudomonas aeruginosa. Complicated urinary tract infections and pyelonephritis Inhalation anthrax (post-exposure prophylaxis and curative treatment) Ciprofloxacin may also be used to treat severe infections in children and adolescents when this is considered to be necessary. Treatment should be initiated only by physicians who are experienced in the treatment of cystic fibrosis and/or severe infections in children and adolescents.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:08:34.606487+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11728-01,Co-Amoxiclav,ALCLAV NEO,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xwGO5vbcNSj0f7OXDw5yYFkFNI7_5ggm/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11728-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xwGO5vbcNSj0f7OXDw5yYFkFNI7_5ggm_view_usp_drivesdk_cc806d9eb5.pdf,page_text/DRP-11728-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xwGO5vbcNSj0f7OXDw5yYFkFNI7_5ggm_view_usp_drivesdk_cc806d9eb5.json,083840ba874288132bcb2d0dbaa51ad108c279f2616a244a706ba9d7ab9c7ef3,1439238,2,digital_text,"White to off white oval shaped, biconvex film coated tablets with scoring on one side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Co-Amoxiclav is indicated for the treatment of the following infections in adults and children: - Acute bacterial sinusitis (adequately diagnosed) - Acute otitis media - Acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis (adequately diagnosed) - Community acquired pneumonia - Cystitis - Pyelonephritis - Skin and soft tissue infections in particular cellulitis, animal bites, severe dental abscess with spreading cellulitis. - Bone and joint infections, in particular osteomyelitis. Consideration should be given to official guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:08:38.226017+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11729,Mometasone Furoate,Mmfred,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WOAvswHYQH-Jrbf60OwlPIXbjRDQF7PT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11729_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WOAvswHYQH-Jrbf60OwlPIXbjRDQF7PT_view_usp_drivesdk_21a29e2ba1.pdf,page_text/DRP-11729_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WOAvswHYQH-Jrbf60OwlPIXbjRDQF7PT_view_usp_drivesdk_21a29e2ba1.json,ee0ea7df186da5246beff49487ea8309e5812481c3b0ab9221d3814396ce1dc6,818161,1,digital_text,MMFRED (MOMETASONE Furoate) 1 mg/g (0.1% w/w) Topical Cream is white semi-solid mass filled in printed laminated tube.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Mometasone Furoate 0.1% w/w Cream is indicated for the treatment of inflammatory pruritic manifestations of and psoriasis (excluding widespread plaque psoriasis) and atopic dermatitis in adults and children aged 2 to 18 years.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:08:40.994196+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11731,Clobetasol Propionate,Clobfred,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fP11DiA5u_y02vnzlrgX95ZyZVoWwiBo/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11731_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1fP11DiA5u_y02vnzlrgX95ZyZVoWwiBo_view_usp_drivesdk_5f097bea1f.pdf,page_text/DRP-11731_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1fP11DiA5u_y02vnzlrgX95ZyZVoWwiBo_view_usp_drivesdk_5f097bea1f.json,5eb0822a7e3f38140aa2d2e5ae9141151d53057d84ddc980a5c0c944e4c668d6,738176,2,digital_text,"Manufactured by: Fredun Pharmaceuticals Limited Plot No. 14, 15, 16, Zorabian Industrial Complex Village Veoor, Tal. Palghar, Thane 401404, Maharashtra, India Imported and Distributed by:",2,2,prescription.,"Clobetasol is a very potent topical corticosteroid indicated for adults, elderly and children over 1 year for the short-term treatment only of more resistant inflammatory and pruritic manifestations of steroid responsive dermatoses unresponsive to less potent corticosteroids. These include the following: - Psoriasis (excluding widespread plaque psoriasis) - Recalcitrant dermatoses - Lichen planus - Discoid lupus erythematosus - Other skin conditions which do not respond satisfactorily to less potent steroids.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T15:08:44.048588+00:00
