PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11805-06,Co - Amoxiclav,Bacticox 625,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uwi0SF-igFt9fiEf0W9EvQqsSb_blQzP/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11805-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uwi0SF-igFt9fiEf0W9EvQqsSb_blQzP_view_usp_drivesdk_75d51937d1.pdf,page_text/DRP-11805-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uwi0SF-igFt9fiEf0W9EvQqsSb_blQzP_view_usp_drivesdk_75d51937d1.json,8c432e5e183a3734697731b02042737873d968bfe94ea89f4b7134cda799c1a2,749708,3,digital_text,White to off-white coloured oval shaped elongated film-coated tablet,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for the treatment of the following infections in adults and children • Acute bacterial sinusitis (adequately diagnosed) • Acute otitis media • Acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis (adequately diagnosed) • Community acquired pneumonia • Cystitis • Pyelonephritis • Skin and soft tissue infections in particular cellulitis, animal bites, severe dental abscess with spreading cellulitis. • Bone and joint infections, in particular osteomyelitis. Consideration should be give n to official guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:10:25.648084+00:00
