PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-11979,Salbutamol (as sulfate),None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1V49OmeS0LWiJD3k7kQ7clMr5qvLarrRv/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-11979_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1V49OmeS0LWiJD3k7kQ7clMr5qvLarrRv_view_usp_drivesdk_629540491e.pdf,page_text/DRP-11979_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1V49OmeS0LWiJD3k7kQ7clMr5qvLarrRv_view_usp_drivesdk_629540491e.json,12c0af54b16c43b46c0c86e4d99551684293293a46cb5cbb779398c3e5de308f,521169,1,digital_text,"White coloured, round shaped, flat, break line on one side and other side plain uncoated tablet.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Salbutamol is a selective beta2-adrenoceptor agonist indicated for the treatment or prevention of bronchospasm. It provides short acting (four hours) bronchodilation in reversible airways obstruction due to asthma, chronic bronchitis and emphysema. Bronchodilators should not be the only or main treatment in patients with persistent asthma. In patients with persistent asthma unresponsive to Salbutamol, treatment with inhaled corticosteroids is recommended to achieve and maintain control. Failing to respond to treatment with Salbutamol may signal a need for urgent medical advice or treatment. Salbutamol tablets are indicated for the relief of bronchospasm in bronchial asthma of all types, chronic bronchitis and emphysema.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:25:42.581437+00:00
