PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12076,Cefuroxime (As Sodium),Furoximed,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mzXSPp1jGLniN91BN_2hLYpEOi0RhAIu/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12076_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mzXSPp1jGLniN91BN_2hLYpEOi0RhAIu_view_usp_drivesdk_882a129743.pdf,page_text/DRP-12076_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mzXSPp1jGLniN91BN_2hLYpEOi0RhAIu_view_usp_drivesdk_882a129743.json,a7b2f7b2e7b6f6c21030af24fa13ad7b89dd7148c232fc5f5d050882677ea78b,761096,4,digital_text,White or faintly yellow powder,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for the treatment of infections listed below in adults and children, including neonates (from birth) • Community acquired pneumonia • Acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis • Complicated urinary tract infections, including pyelonephritis • Soft -tissue infections: cellulitis, erysipelas and wound infections • Intra-abdominal infections • Prophylaxis against infection in gastrointestinal (in cluding oesophageal), orthopaedic, cardiovascular, and gynaecological surgery (including caesarean section) In the treatment and prevention of infections in which it is very likely that anaerobic organisms will be encountered, cefuroxime should be administ ered with additional appropriate antibacterial agents. Consideration should be given to official guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:27:26.941175+00:00
