PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12139,Palonosetron (as hydrochloride),Paloset,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Hf4BUfxF-YomKD4VJC0B0RfIefOwJWKI/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12139_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Hf4BUfxF-YomKD4VJC0B0RfIefOwJWKI_view_usp_drivesdk_04866f1494.pdf,page_text/DRP-12139_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Hf4BUfxF-YomKD4VJC0B0RfIefOwJWKI_view_usp_drivesdk_04866f1494.json,3569bc4e76908b89f1a280e13eb0cb8b5db11a9a235c01346a287cf546454cf6,8948921,2,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-29T15:29:30.490871+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12142-01,Potassium Chloride,Poklor,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZxumX04ww3o-YOBlqoLB793T8C0LHT9b/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12142-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZxumX04ww3o-YOBlqoLB793T8C0LHT9b_view_usp_drivesdk_4fc4d08db3.pdf,page_text/DRP-12142-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZxumX04ww3o-YOBlqoLB793T8C0LHT9b_view_usp_drivesdk_4fc4d08db3.json,42f9792bdf50daf36b13df37ba3b8ec3d14c4f82186b89d594c4acf8d8811988,441926,1,digital_text,"The Potassium Chloride Extended-Release Tablets, USP 10 mEq product is an immediately dispersing extended-release oral dosage form of potassium chloride containing 750 mg of microencapsulated potassium chloride, USP equivalent to 10 mEq of potassium in a tablet. These formulations are intended to slow the release of potassium so that the likelihood of a high localized concentration of potassium chloride within the gastrointestinal tract is reduced. Potassium chloride is an electrolyte replenisher. The chemical name of the active ingredient is potassium chloride, and the structural formula is KCl. Potassium chloride, USP occurs as a white, granular powder or as colorless crystals. It is odorless and has a saline taste. Its solutions are neutral to litmus. It is freely soluble in water and insoluble in alcohol. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM Brown color, caplet shaped ﬁlm coated tablet. Having one side Break line & other side plain",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Potassium chloride extended-release tablets are indicated for the treatment and prophylaxis of hypokalemia with or without metabolic alkalosis, in patients for whom dietary management with potassium-rich food or diuretic dose reduction is insuﬃcient.",1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATION,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:29:33.223582+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12150,Cefoxitin (As Sodium),One-Cefoxcel,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Q69UpA5k611KEcP2izI6BUqsNyt4OWu5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12150_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Q69UpA5k611KEcP2izI6BUqsNyt4OWu5_view_usp_drivesdk_046f7b2527.pdf,page_text/DRP-12150_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Q69UpA5k611KEcP2izI6BUqsNyt4OWu5_view_usp_drivesdk_046f7b2527.json,2af5eba16512ef360cd31b25dae6e9a89e8912c6d8283e5febb3ccff0658a6ff,120866,1,digital_text,"White to off-white granules or powder, having a characteristic odor.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Cefoxitin for injection is indicated for the treatment of serious infections caused by susceptible strains of the designated microorganisms in the diseases listed as follows: •Lower respiratory tract infections •Urinary tract infections •Intra-abdominal infections •Gynecological infections •Septicemia •Bone and joint infections •Skin and skin structure infections ADMINISTRATION OF DOSE Cefoxitin for Injection may be administered intravenously or intramuscularly (see reconstitution directions for each route below). Dosage and route of administration are determined by severity of infection, susceptibility of the causative organisms, and condition of the patient. Adults The usual adult dosage is 1 g or 2 g of cefoxitin sodium every 8 hours. In adults with renal insufficiency, an initial loading dose of 1 g to 2 g may be given. After a loading dose, the recommendations for maintenance dosage may be used as a guide. In severe infections, the total daily dosage should not exceed 12 g per day. Children (Over 3 months) 20 to 40 mg/kg every 6 hours or every 8 hours. Cefoxitin sodium is not recommended for the therapy of meningitis. If meningitis is suspected, an appropriate antibiotic should be used. In children with renal insufficiency, the dosage frequency should be reduced as indicated for adults. Intravenous administration Warning For Neonates Solutions containing preservatives should not be used for injection or for flushing catheters in treating neonates. Benzyl alcohol as a preservative in Bacteriostatic Water for Injections has been associated with toxicity in neonates. Intramuscular administration Cefoxitin for Injection 1 g with 2 ml of 0.5% or 1 % lignocaine hydrochloride (without adrenaline) solution. Some patients may be hypersensitive to lignocaine. If lignocaine cannot be used, Cefoxitin for Injection may be reconstituted with 2 ml of Sterile Water for Injections.",1,1,INDICATION,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:29:36.601217+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12155,Atorvastatin(as Calcium Trihydrate),Atormed-20,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HAI_v_x7EheGDAc2amiT8E4GnpntplZ9/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12155_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HAI_v_x7EheGDAc2amiT8E4GnpntplZ9_view_usp_drivesdk_bc70356a57.pdf,page_text/DRP-12155_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HAI_v_x7EheGDAc2amiT8E4GnpntplZ9_view_usp_drivesdk_bc70356a57.json,57e76e873397b1022c34395adddc743c8de546e89432aa28cd956a287489982a,202277,4,digital_text,"White coloured, round shaped, biconvex, film coated tablets, plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Hypercholesterolaemia Atorvastatin 20mg Film coated Tablets is indicated as an adjunct to diet for reduction of elevated total cholesterol (total -C), LDL -cholesterol (LDL -C), apolipoprotein B, and triglycerides in adults, adolescents and children aged 10 years or older with primary hypercholesterolaemia including familial hypercholesterolaemia (heterozygous variant) or combined (mixed) hyperlipidaemia (Corresponding to Types IIa and IIb of the Fredrickson classification) when response to diet and other nonpharmacological measures is inadequate. Atorvastatin 20mg Film coated Tablets is also indicated to reduce total -C and LDL -C in adults with homozygo us familial hypercholesterolaemia as an adjunct to other lipid - lowering treatments (e.g. LDL apheresis) or if such treatments are unavailable. Prevention of cardiovascular disease Prevention of cardiovascular events in adults estimated to have a high risk for a first cardiovascular event, as an adjunct to correction of other risk factors.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:29:50.501617+00:00
