PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12252-04,Ampicillin (As Sodium) + Sulbactam (As Sodium),Bactamed,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-9RkSBmBBtzwTu0jAkWjmCnmPiUIjMGJ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12252-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-9RkSBmBBtzwTu0jAkWjmCnmPiUIjMGJ_view_usp_drivesdk_4ded2f86f2.pdf,page_text/DRP-12252-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-9RkSBmBBtzwTu0jAkWjmCnmPiUIjMGJ_view_usp_drivesdk_4ded2f86f2.json,6e60e2f192cf42ccf718d7fee0b31385379767eb739a48460daaba5d5f28a984,677481,2,digital_text,White or almost white powder.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for infections caused by susceptible microorganisms. Typical indications are upper and lower respiratory tract infections including sinusitis, otitis media and epiglottitis; bacterial pneumonias; urinary tract infections and pyelonephritis; intra-abdominal infections including peritonitis, cholecystitis, endometritis and pelvic cellulitis; bacterial septicemia; skin, soft tissue, bone and joint infections and gonococcal infections. Ampicillin/Sulbactam IV/IM may also be administered peri-operatively to reduce the incidence of post-operative wound infections in patients undergoing abdominal or pelvic surgery, in which peritoneal contamination may be present. In termination of pregnancy or cesarean section, Ampicillin sodium/Sulbactam sodium IV/IM may be used prophylactically to reduce post- operative sepsis.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:33:48.290115+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12257,Fenofibrate,Fenosaph-160,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1v-Dca8SrMrQYc37mH5amq1e421zoUgON/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12257_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1v-Dca8SrMrQYc37mH5amq1e421zoUgON_view_usp_drivesdk_29abcf5d39.pdf,page_text/DRP-12257_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1v-Dca8SrMrQYc37mH5amq1e421zoUgON_view_usp_drivesdk_29abcf5d39.json,9906896b7e05105d1879810ee9f9ab979ada86baf00876142a881b594122855f,1880235,1,digital_text,"Hard gelatin capsule of size 0 having yellow color cap & red color body, containing white powder.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Fenoﬁbrate 160 mg capsule are indicated as an adjunct to diet and other non-pharmacological treatment (e.g., exercise, weight reduction) for the following: • Treatment of severe hypertriglyceridemia with or without low HDL cholesterol. • Mixed hyperlipidemia when a statin is contraindicated or not tolerated. • Mixed hyperlipidemia in patients at high cardiovascular risk in addition to a statin when triglycerides and HDLcholesterol are not adequately controlled.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:34:02.814300+00:00
