ld be considered when serum liver DH function tests increase to a level considered clinically significant. Caution has to be exercised to maintain the bile flow of the patients taking UDCA. INTERACTION WITH OTHER MEDICAMENTS AND OTHER FORMS OF INTERACTION Ursodeoxycholic acid should not be administered concomitantly with colestyramine, colestipol or antacids containing aluminium hydroxide and/or smectite (aluminium oxide), because these preparations bind ursodeoxycholic acid in the PHARMACEUTICAL FORM intestine and thereby inhibit its absorption and efficacy. Should the use of a preparation containing one of these substances be necessary, it must be taken at least 2 hours before or after Ursodeoxycholic acid. Ursodeoxycholic acid White to off white colored caplet shaped film-coated having break-line on one side and other side plain. can affect the absorption of ciclosporin from the intestine. In patients receiving ciclosporin treatment, blood concentrations",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"OVERDOSAGE AND TREATMENT Lupibile, also known as ursodeoxycholic acid (UDCA) is indicated for: Accidental or intentional overdosage with ursodiol has not been reported. The most severe manifestation of overdosage janagement of cholestatic liver diseases, such as primary biliary cirrhosis (PB! would likely consist of diarrhea that should be treated symptomatically. Cholestatic liver diseases are characterized by a decrease in bile secretion an bile flow. Caution has to be exercised to maintain the bile flow of the patients taking Symptoms of acute toxicity in animal studies were salivation and vomiting in dogs, and ataxia, dyspnea, ptosis, agonal The diagnosis of cholestatic liver diseases i is based on the biochemical signs of cholestasis (such as an increase in convulsions and coma in hamsters. alkaline phosphatase, y-GT, bilirubin), and also an increase in IgM levels and the presence of antimitochondrial antibodies STORAGE CONDITION The monitoring of Lupibile in the management of cholestatic liver diseases should be based on the biochemical Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. parameters of cholestasis, as described above, as well as on signs of hepatic cytolysis (such as AST, ALT) which are very often associated with cholestasis during the progression of the diseases. CAUTION Foods, Drugs, Devices, and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription. Serum liver function tests (y-GT, alkaline phosphatase, AST, ALT) and bilirubin level should be monitored every month for three months after start of therapy, and e six months thereafter. ADR REPORTING STATEMENT Improved serum liver function tests (e.g. AS, ALT) do not always correlate with improved disease status. In addition to For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph identifying responsive and non-responsive patients, this monitoring will allow the early detection of a possible deterioration Seek medical attention right away if any of the adverse reaction occurs. of the hepatic function. For patients who have a recent history of adequate biochemical response to the treatment, UDCA discontinuation should be considered when serum liver function tests increase to a level considered clinically significant, aseline AVAILABILITY generally increase in ALT, AST levels three times the baseline value and increase in total bilirubin to twice the value, confirmed by repeated tests. Alu/Alu Blister Pack x 10’s (Box of 100’s) Ursodeoxycholic acid is not indicated for the treatment of decompensated cirrhosis. FDA REG. NO.: DRP-12263-02 Geriatrics: Appropriate studies Ursodeoxycholic acid have not been performed in the geriatric population. However, geriatric-specific problems that would limit the use or usefulness of Ursodeoxycholic acid in the elderly are not expected. DATE OF FIRST AUTHORIZATION: December 13, 2023 Pediatrics: The safety and ress of U holic acid in children have not been established. DATE OF REVISION OF PACKAGE INSERT: January 24, 2024",1,1,THERAPEUTI