PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12279,Sitagliptin (as phosphate) + Metformin HCl,Metsaphtin-50/1000,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1740SV9HnbH_hjUkQknIWx3LGp6SdPAbh/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12279_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1740SV9HnbH_hjUkQknIWx3LGp6SdPAbh_view_usp_drivesdk_9ac1bef659.pdf,page_text/DRP-12279_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1740SV9HnbH_hjUkQknIWx3LGp6SdPAbh_view_usp_drivesdk_9ac1bef659.json,c78d1f2b7e82d996974a1d56a2b26032b475b2fd2a714368371d2307f779a088,3721405,2,digital_text,"Brown coloured, elongated, biconvex, ﬁlm-coated tablet having breakline on one side and plain on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Indicated as initial therapy in patients with type 2 Diabetes mellitus to improve glycemic control when diet and exercise do not provide adequate glycemic control. Indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus inadequately controlled on Metformin or Sitagliptin alone or in patients already being treated with the combination of Sitagliptin and Metformin. Indicated as part of triple combination therapy with a sulfonylurea as an adjunct to diet and exercise in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus inadequately controlled with any two of the three agents: Metformin, Sitagliptin, or a sulfonylurea. Indicated as part of triple combination therapy with a PPARγ agonist (i.e., thiazolidinediones) as an adjunct to diet and exercise in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus inadequately controlled with any two of the three agents: Metformin, Sitagliptin, or a PPARγ agonist. Indicated in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in combination with insulin.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T15:34:30.641284+00:00
