PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12308-01,DL-Alpha-Tocopherol (Vitamin E),None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dbPSpXFwxBfST4Fzrsn1t-pyOBrl2XoO/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12308-01_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dbPSpXFwxBfST4Fzrsn1t-pyOBrl2XoO_view_usp_drivesdk_4af9f6eb28.pdf,page_text/DRP-12308-01_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dbPSpXFwxBfST4Fzrsn1t-pyOBrl2XoO_view_usp_drivesdk_4af9f6eb28.json,62ec6ada665323586861bf6cd6270edb9c6c3c0fc823b6bf5979fcbca24aa8d9,437272,1,digital_text,"Green colored transparent oblong shaped soft gelatin capsules contain clear transparent liquid. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Antioxidants function as scavengers to detoxify free radicals. Free radicals are highly reactive and unstable chemicals formed in the body during normal physiological and biochemical processes such as respiration, metabolism and immune system response. This product contains dl-Alpha-Tocopherol, the natural form of vitamin E which has higher biologic activity, stays longer in the blood and is preferentially resecreted by the liver to be utilized by body tissues compared to the synthetic form. Moreover, it can be recycled to its active unionized form, which can be used again by the body. Vitamin E helps maintain membrane integrity in all cells of the body including the nerve tissues by acting as the body's fat-soluble antioxidant which acts as the first defense against free radicals in the lipid (fat) phase of cells. It promotes cell and tissue renewal of the skin, heart, lungs, muscles, and liver. It modulates the synthesis of prostaglandins important for the body's immune response. Vitamin E is also involved in the metabolism of nucleic acid and the functioning of the mitochondria which is the main site of energy production in cells.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T15:36:43.768814+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1232,Atorvastatin (as calcium),Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Xpyc9Mjxmta-72JiD5Dj7w5ANggDxG7A/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1232_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Xpyc9Mjxmta-72JiD5Dj7w5ANggDxG7A_view_usp_drivesdk_a3d3b99563.pdf,page_text/DRP-1232_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Xpyc9Mjxmta-72JiD5Dj7w5ANggDxG7A_view_usp_drivesdk_a3d3b99563.json,b6da4f9ab7d9967fe40ffd2a868467a924bd15199ba62942c15a5dc5d9532659,4803190,2,digital_text_and_ocr,,,,,"Nervous System: Insomnia, dizziness, paresthesia, somnolence, amnesia, abnormal dreams, libido Active liver disease or unexplained persistent elevations of serum transaminases. decreased, emotional lability, incoordination, peripheral neuropathy, torticollis, facial paralysis, Hypersensitivity to any component of this medication. hyperkinesia, depression, hypesthesia, hypertonia. Pregnant, breast-feeding, or of childbearing potential who are not using adequate contraceptive measures. Musculoskeletal System: Arthritis, leg cramps, bursitis, tenosynovitis, myasthenia, tendinous contracture, myositis « Drug Interactions The risk of myopathy during treatment with other drugs in this class is increased with concurrent Skin and Appendages: Pruritus, contact dermatitis, alopecia, dry skin, sweating, acne, urticaria, eczema, administration of cyclosporine, fibric acid derivatives, erythromycin, azole antifungals, or niacin. This seborrhea, skin ulcer. increase in risk may also occur when combining these drugs with atorvastatin. Urogenital System: Urinary tract infection, hematuria, albuminuria, urinary frequency, cystitis, impotence, Phenazone (antipyrine) is a non-specific model for evaluation of drug metabolism by the hepatic dysuria, kidney calculus, nocturia, epididymitis, fibrocystic breast, vaginal hemorrhage, breast microsomal enzyme system. Administration of multiple doses of atorvastatin with phen