etabolic acidosis USP Type | clear glass ampoule x 20 mL in plastic tray (Box of 10's) * Tricyclic antidepressant overdose. INSTRUCTIONS AND SPECIAL PRECAUTION FOR HANDLING AND DISPOSAL Sodium bicarbonate should only be used after other resuscitative measures such as cardiac compression, Discard any unused solution. ventilation, adrenaline and antiarrythmic agents have been attempted. Any unused product or waste material should be disposed of in accordance with local requirements In neonates, Sodium bicarbonate is indicated for: CAUTION * Correction of metabolic acidosis associated with cardiac arrest in patients with pre-existing metabolic acidosis Foods, Drugs, Devices and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription. + Cardiac arrest associated with hyperkalaemia with pre-existing metabolic acidosis ADR REPORTING STATEMENT + Life threatening hyperkalaemia with pre-existing metabolic acidosis. No benefits have been demonstrated from the routine use of Sodium bicarbonate in resuscitation of For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. neonates. In neonates, Sodium bicarbonate is recommended in resuscitation only in cases of prolonged cardiac arrest, irresponsive to other therapy, after establishment of adequate ventilation and circulation. DRP-12382 - 04 Date of First Authorization : February 2023",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T15:58:13.589595+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12388,Benzydamine(As Hydrochloride),Mediflam,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1622YQaojA0Q8s6Vl4oJkFOcseOxIXQdK/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12388_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1622YQaojA0Q8s6Vl4oJkFOcseOxIXQdK_view_usp_drivesdk_f5023c7802.pdf,page_text/DRP-12388_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1622YQaojA0Q8s6Vl4oJkFOcseOxIXQdK_view_usp_drivesdk_f5023c7802.json,e06ed6619e94dd118757f0d2bfad8fb84c32d9cac754edbb1dd33576e865cae9,581206,1,digital_text,"Clear solution with mint flavor. Clear solution with lemon flavor. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Each mL contains: Benzydamine (as Hydrochloride) ……………………………………………. 3 mg WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Benzydamine hydrochloride spray works by stopping pain and swelling (inflammation). It is used to treat many painful conditions of the mouth or throat including: - Mouth ulcers - Teething - Sore throat - Sore tongue or gums - Discomfort associated with dentures or dental work HOW MUCH & HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Always use Benzydamine hydrochloride exactly as instructed by your doctor or pharmacist. Check with your doctor or pharmacist if you are not sure. Adults and children over 12 years of age Spray 2-4 puffs, repeat every 2 to 3 hours if necessary but not more than stated. Children 6-12 years of age Spray 2 puffs to the sore area every 2 to 3 hours if necessary but not more than stated. Children under 6 years of age Spray 1 puff for every 4 kg of body weight, up to a maximum of 4 puffs, to the sore area every 1 ½ to 3 hours. Contact your doctor if your symptoms worsen or they do not improve. How to use the spray - Open the cap. Twist the spray-tube until pointed to your mouth. - Spray into sore/inflamed area of your mouth or throat. - After spraying the desired number of puff, wipe the nozzle cleanly to prevent blockage. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Do not use if: - You are allergic to Benzydamine hydrochloride - You are allergic to any of the other ingredients of this product",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T15:58:27.574746+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12389,Benzydamine(As Hydrochloride),Mediflam,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LefP_A_ImJQz3PxxoHCfAz-UaItocRiZ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12389_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LefP_A_ImJQz3PxxoHCfAz-UaItocRiZ_view_usp_drivesdk_50abcec8e0.pdf,page_text/DRP-12389_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LefP_A_ImJQz3PxxoHCfAz-UaItocRiZ_view_usp_drivesdk_50abcec8e0.json,8a6dc81a3cc2e1476beaa45a21aaa11eda46418337e09b8308a9489cceb8482a,824286,1,digital_text,"Clear solution with mint flavor. Clear solution with lemon flavor. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Each mL contains: Benzydamine (as Hydrochloride) ……………………………………………. 3 mg WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Benzydamine hydrochloride spray works by stopping pain and swelling (inflammation). It is used to treat many painful conditions of the mouth or throat including: - Mouth ulcers - Teething - Sore throat - Sore tongue or gums - Discomfort associated with dentures or dental work HOW MUCH & HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Always use Benzydamine hydrochloride exactly as instructed by your doctor or pharmacist. Check with your doctor or pharmacist if you are not sure. Adults and children over 12 years of age Spray 2-4 puffs, repeat every 2 to 3 hours if necessary but not more than stated. Children 6-12 years of age Spray 2 puffs to the sore area every 2 to 3 hours if necessary but not more than stated. Children under 6 years of age Spray 1 puff for every 4 kg of body weight, up to a maximum of 4 puffs, to the sore area every 1 ½ to 3 hours. Contact your doctor if your symptoms worsen or they do not improve. How to use the spray - Open the cap. Twist the spray-tube until pointed to your mouth. - Spray into sore/inflamed area of your mouth or throat. - After spraying the desired number of puff, wipe the nozzle cleanly to prevent blockage. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Do not use if: - You are allergic to Benzydamine hydrochloride - You are allergic to any of the other ingredients of this product",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T15:58:30.584319+00:00
