PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12488,Amlodipine (As Besilate),Dipinew,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rxtzNrFYDQ62CJCqB8Rkdl8MGpMRZGed/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12488_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rxtzNrFYDQ62CJCqB8Rkdl8MGpMRZGed_view_usp_drivesdk_4b2815df99.pdf,page_text/DRP-12488_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rxtzNrFYDQ62CJCqB8Rkdl8MGpMRZGed_view_usp_drivesdk_4b2815df99.json,5e381bfd9c1493a0adc3018c1445d2dac7e03c5ee418cfd08254f8c84bb2ab0e,5442022,1,digital_text,"White coloured, round shaped, flat, uncoated tablet having break line on one side plain on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Hypertension: Amlodipine besilate is indicated for the first-line treatment of hypertension and can be used as the sole agent to control blood pressure in the majority of patients. Patients not adequately controlled on a single antihypertensive agent (other than amlodipine) may benefit from the addition of amlodipine, which has been used in combination with a thiazide diuretic, alpha blockers, beta adrenoceptor blocking agent or an angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitor. Amlodipine besilate is also indicated to reduce the risk of fatal coronary heart disease (CHD) and non-fatal myocardial infarction (MI), and to reduce the risk of stroke. Coronary Artery Disease: Amlodipine besilate is indicated to reduce the risk of coronary revascularization and the need for hospitalization due to angina in patients with coronary artery disease (CAD). Chronic Stable Angina: Amlodipine besilate is indicated for the first-line treatment of myocardial ischemia, whether due to fixed obstruction (stable angina) and/or vasospasm/vasoconstriction (Prinzmetal's or variant angina) of coronary vasculature. Amlodipine besilate may be used where the clinical presentation suggests a possible vasospastic/vasoconstrictive component but where vasospasm/vasoconstriction has not been confirmed. Amlodipine may be used alone, as monotherapy or in combination with other anti-anginal drugs in patients with angina that is refractory to nitrates and/or adequate doses of beta-blockers.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:00:40.074408+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12488,Amlodipine (As Besilate),Dipinew,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1z1HKoNihSmsPdVIAQ0Yb_7m1KY1Lx2NP/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12488_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1z1HKoNihSmsPdVIAQ0Yb_7m1KY1Lx2NP_view_usp_drivesdk_3f886d52e0.pdf,page_text/DRP-12488_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1z1HKoNihSmsPdVIAQ0Yb_7m1KY1Lx2NP_view_usp_drivesdk_3f886d52e0.json,5e381bfd9c1493a0adc3018c1445d2dac7e03c5ee418cfd08254f8c84bb2ab0e,5442022,1,digital_text,"White coloured, round shaped, flat, uncoated tablet having break line on one side plain on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Hypertension: Amlodipine besilate is indicated for the first-line treatment of hypertension and can be used as the sole agent to control blood pressure in the majority of patients. Patients not adequately controlled on a single antihypertensive agent (other than amlodipine) may benefit from the addition of amlodipine, which has been used in combination with a thiazide diuretic, alpha blockers, beta adrenoceptor blocking agent or an angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitor. Amlodipine besilate is also indicated to reduce the risk of fatal coronary heart disease (CHD) and non-fatal myocardial infarction (MI), and to reduce the risk of stroke. Coronary Artery Disease: Amlodipine besilate is indicated to reduce the risk of coronary revascularization and the need for hospitalization due to angina in patients with coronary artery disease (CAD). Chronic Stable Angina: Amlodipine besilate is indicated for the first-line treatment of myocardial ischemia, whether due to fixed obstruction (stable angina) and/or vasospasm/vasoconstriction (Prinzmetal's or variant angina) of coronary vasculature. Amlodipine besilate may be used where the clinical presentation suggests a possible vasospastic/vasoconstrictive component but where vasospasm/vasoconstriction has not been confirmed. Amlodipine may be used alone, as monotherapy or in combination with other anti-anginal drugs in patients with angina that is refractory to nitrates and/or adequate doses of beta-blockers.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:00:45.215869+00:00
