PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12596-01,Oxaliplatin,Genplatin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/14bpfOd5cWEbKGBkJXl519eIkoz98utaJ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12596-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14bpfOd5cWEbKGBkJXl519eIkoz98utaJ_view_usp_drivesdk_85a818a98c.pdf,page_text/DRP-12596-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14bpfOd5cWEbKGBkJXl519eIkoz98utaJ_view_usp_drivesdk_85a818a98c.json,72e8c1a610c874a69fd677ec895eb88a8bf3cc6f07b3e0bb7a2b27359b48b42b,314162,5,digital_text,White to slightly white lyophilized drying powder injection.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Used in combination with infusional 5-fluorouracil/leucovorin, is indicated for: • adjuvant treatment of stage III colon cancer in patients who have undergone complete re-section of the primary tumor. • treatment of advanced colorectal cancer.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:07:39.566525+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1260,Clarithromycin,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1l4s38oPc0NyqLwbyg9nq6SybhF9lagdp/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1260_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1l4s38oPc0NyqLwbyg9nq6SybhF9lagdp_view_usp_drivesdk_0ac24e3c19.pdf,page_text/DRP-1260_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1l4s38oPc0NyqLwbyg9nq6SybhF9lagdp_view_usp_drivesdk_0ac24e3c19.json,3728ed224a5a6a19a99777121a6349c897fae84b5f34726ae8460abd0bd12aaa,46303,1,digital_text,,,,,"Clarithromycin is indicated for the treatment of upper and lower respiratory tract infections, pharyngitis/ tonsilitis, acute maxillary sinusitis, acute bacter ial exacer bation of chronic br onchitis, bacter ial pneumonia, uncomplicated skin and skin structure infections, and acute otitis media. MECHANISM OF ACTION s 0 5 e h t o t g n i d n i b y b n o i t c a l a i r e t c a b i t n a s t i s t r e x e t I . c i t o i b i t n a e d i l o r c a m c i t e h t n y s - i m e s a s i n i c y m o r h t i r a l C ribosomal subunit of susceptible organism and and inhibiting protein synthesis. ANTIMICROBIAL ACTION Clarithromycin is active in vitro against a variety of aerobic and anaerobic Gram-positive and Gram-negative organism as well as most Mycobacterium avium complex (MAC) organisms. Gram-positive aerobes: Staphylococcus aureus, Str eptococcus pneumoniae, Str eptococcus pyogenes, Listeria monocytogenes and some strains of Corynebacter ium. Gram-negative aerobes: Haemophilus influenzae, Moraxella (Branhamella) catarrhalis, Neiserria gonorrhea, H elicobacter pylori. Other aerobes: Mycoplasma pneumoniae, Mycobacterium avium complex (MAC) consisting of Microbacterium avium and Mycobacterium intracellure. PHARMACOKINETICS Clarithromycin is r apidly absorbed fr om the gastrointestinal tr act after or al administr ation. T he absolute bioavailability of 250 mg C larithromycin tablet w as approximately 50%. F ood slightly delays both the onset of Clarithromycin absorption and the formation of antimicrobial active metabolite, 14-hydroxy- clarithromycin, but does not af fect the bioavailability. T herefore, Clarithromycin tablets may be given w ithout regard to food.",1,1,INDICATIONS,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T16:07:42.379071+00:00
