PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12681,Lysozyme Hydrochloride + Cetylpyridinium Chloride,Lysobact Spray,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Kx_CTzHhSOdYEJp4zl9DlTH05wcpvK-S/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12681_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Kx_CTzHhSOdYEJp4zl9DlTH05wcpvK-S_view_usp_drivesdk_5f296aef12.pdf,page_text/DRP-12681_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Kx_CTzHhSOdYEJp4zl9DlTH05wcpvK-S_view_usp_drivesdk_5f296aef12.json,eb8d7e1b74bd0d9f4f204f06fe0ecd93071052ca1278d813af7ade073fece0d6,2334069,2,digital_text_and_ocr,,,,,"5 days, because the balance of normal microflora (natural ¢ The applicator can be moved sideways and ensures proper application of the spray into the oral cavity. protective barrier) in the oral cavity could be disrupted witha risk of fungal or bacterial growth. ¢ Turn the applicator upwards, under the right angle in relation to the bottle. * Before the first application of the spray, press the spray If your symptoms last longer than 5 days and/or high body temperature occurs at the same time, you need to contact pump several times in order to accomplish an equal spraying. your doctor. * Open your mouth completely, direct the applicator [Page 2] towards the diseased site and press the spray pump as many times as it is directed in drug dosage. • Hold your breath during the spraying. Do not swallow. • After applying the medicine, turn the applicator downwards, which will block the further spraying. Dosage For a single dose, it is necessary to press the spray pump five times. The procedure can be repeated 3-6 times a day, with minimal intervals of 2 h between the dosing. LYSOBACT SPRAY is not intended for children aged below 6 years. Duration of treatment It is recommended not to use this product longer than 5 days. If you apply more LYSOBACT Spray than you should If you applied more spray than you should, contact your doctor or pharmacist straight away! If you apply more spray than you should, contact your doctor,and he will provide you with assistance. If you forget to apply LVSOBACT Spray If you forget to use this medicine, do not use the double dose afterwards, but continue the usage according to the usual schedule. If you forget to apply LYSOBACT Spray, use it as soon as you remember. After that, continue with usage at the usual schedule and in the recommended way. If you stop using LVSOBACT Spray Use this medicine for as long as your doctor has prescribed you. If you suddenly stop using this medicine, no harmful effects on your organism are expected. If you have any further questions on the use of LYSOBACT Spray, or if you are not sure, consult your doctor or pharmacist. 4.Possible side effects Like other medicines, LYSOBACT Spray can cause side effects, although not everyone gets them. Side effects associated with the use of LYSOBACT Spray are very rare (they affect less than 1 in 10.000 patients) or their frequency is unknown (it cannot be estimated based on the available data). The following side effects can appear: Immune system disorder Very rarely: hypersensitivity reactions including anaphylactic reaction, angioedema (Quincke's oedema), and anaphylactic shock. These reactions are characterised by swelling of the face, lips, mouth, tongue or throat, and they may be followed by difficulty breathing and shortness of breath (bronchoconstriction), as well as a drop in blood pressure and feeling weakness (circulatory complications). Skin and subcutaneous tissue disorders Unknown:skin rash, itching, urticaria (hives). In addition, isolated (individual) cases of severe skin reactions have been reported, such as erythema multiforme and Stevens-Johnson syndrome, out of which some may be life-threatening. These reactions are followed by severe redness, skin blistering and/or peeling off. FOR SUSPECTED ADVERSE DRUG REACTION, REPORT TO THE FDA:www.fda.gov.ph Patient should seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. 5.How to store LVSOBACT Spray Keep LYSOBACT Spray out of the reach and sight of children. Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Do not freeze. LYSOBACT Spray must not be used after the expiry date given on the pack. Shelflife: 36 months. 6.Further information What LVSOBACT Spray contains Each 1 ml ofLYSOBACTSpray contains: 20.00 mg of Lysozyme Hydrochloride (corresponding to 800000 FIP U),and 1.50 mg ofCetylpyridinium Chloride. One pressure onto the spray pump will release 0.20 ml of the solution which contains 4 mg of lysozyme, and 0.3 mg ofcetylpyridinium. LYSOBACT Spray with peppermint flavour, (20 + 1.5) mg/mI oromucosal spray, solution contains the following excipients: Glycerol 85%, Propylene Glycol, Methyl Parahydroxybenzoate, Sac charin Sodium, Propyl Parahydroxybenzoate, Peppermint Flavour, Sodium Hydroxide, Purified Water. What LVSOBACT Spray looks like and contents of the pack LYSOBACT Spray with peppermint flavour, (20 + 1.5) mg/m I oromucosal spray, solution is colourless to slightly yellow solution with peppermint odour. Contents of the pack: 30 ml of the solution in amber glass bottle with a spray pump and applicatorforthe spray. Imported and Distributed by:",1,2,Therapeutic indications do not justify usage for more than,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T16:10:34.528371+00:00
