PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12693,Metformin hydrochloride,Glucomin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1eE1Nu_4oO4QoiW0P50IBSGE9Tu_P504u/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12693_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eE1Nu_4oO4QoiW0P50IBSGE9Tu_P504u_view_usp_drivesdk_6b09a89a52.pdf,page_text/DRP-12693_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eE1Nu_4oO4QoiW0P50IBSGE9Tu_P504u_view_usp_drivesdk_6b09a89a52.json,9776575cb608c17e7168fab2a7e506845e9fe3e1cc4018b49d406880cb287957,266460,1,digital_text,"Metformin hydrochloride Tablets are oral hypoglycemic drugs used in the management of type 2 diabetes. Metformin hydrochloride (N,N-dimethylimidodicarbonimidicdiamide hydrochloride) is not chemically or pharmacologically related to any other classes of oral hypoglycemic agents. Metformin hydrochloride is a white to off-white crystalline compound with a molecular formula of C4H11N5.HCl and a molecular weight of 165.63. Metformin hydrochloride is freely soluble in water and is practically insoluble in acetone, ether, and chloroform. The pKa of metformin is 12.4. The pH of a 1% aqueous solution of metformin hydrochloride is 6.68.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Metformin hydrochloride (Glucomin) is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in adults and children with type 2 diabetes mellitus.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:10:55.229168+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12693-01,Metformin Hydrochloride,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-huaJomgLpYx9gRIlWedorX3mgmWqyUE/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12693-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-huaJomgLpYx9gRIlWedorX3mgmWqyUE_view_usp_drivesdk_eaf22ed17f.pdf,page_text/DRP-12693-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-huaJomgLpYx9gRIlWedorX3mgmWqyUE_view_usp_drivesdk_eaf22ed17f.json,35b26c0fc0759fbc5e5bdb88be78775521c950dcae0b4f340bdeecab306c43a4,201315,1,digital_text,"Metformin hydrochloride Tablets are oral hypoglycemic drugs used in the management of type 2 diabetes. Metformin hydrochloride (N,N-dimethylimidodicarbonimidicdiamide hydrochloride) is not chemically or pharmacologically related to any other classes of oral hypoglycemic agents. Metformin Hydrochloride is a white to off-white crystalline compound with a molecular formula of C4H11N5.HCl and a molecular weight of 165.63. Metformin hydrochloride is freely soluble in water and is practically insoluble in acetone, ether, and chloroform. The pKa of metformin is 12.4. The pH of a 1% aqueous solution of metformin hydrochloride is 6.68. Metformin Hydrochloride 500 mg is a white to off-white film-coated tablet, round, biconvex and plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Metformin hydrochloride is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in adults and children with type 2 diabetes mellitus.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:10:52.358928+00:00
