PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12704,Losartan Potassium + Hydrochlorothiazide,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1itw04BjJWrJNZGvMPyhE-QWZl0Jz7zVa/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12704_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1itw04BjJWrJNZGvMPyhE-QWZl0Jz7zVa_view_usp_drivesdk_cc1fa40e69.pdf,page_text/DRP-12704_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1itw04BjJWrJNZGvMPyhE-QWZl0Jz7zVa_view_usp_drivesdk_cc1fa40e69.json,fcec8383f882a74aab02f8c9d5c403a2bfbdcd183c2e13084dc0dae722148f84,505376,1,digital_text,"Yellow coloured, round shaped, biconvex both side plain lm coated tablet.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Hypertension: Losartan Potassium + Hydrochlorothiazide is indicated for the treatment of hypertension, for patients in whom combination therapy is appropriate. Reduction in the Risk of Cardiovascular Morbidity and Mortality in Hypertensive Patients with Left Ventricular Hypertrophy: Losartan Potassium + Hydrochlorothiazide is a combination of losartan and hydrochlorothiazide. In patients with hypertension and left ventricular hypertrophy, losartan, often in combination with hydrochlorothiazide, reduces the risk of cardiovascular morbidity and mortality as measured by the combined incidence of cardiovascular death, stroke, and myocardial infarction in hypertensive patients with left ventricular hypertrophy.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:11:07.630571+00:00
