PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12812,Sertaconazole (As Nitrate),Sertatop,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1pCce2htjl4OqGVJUtJgMSnQvtbb4yB9O/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12812_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1pCce2htjl4OqGVJUtJgMSnQvtbb4yB9O_view_usp_drivesdk_cbe40bc302.pdf,page_text/DRP-12812_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1pCce2htjl4OqGVJUtJgMSnQvtbb4yB9O_view_usp_drivesdk_cbe40bc302.json,a015a1bcd584db7433c2fe503f106285a18af9bb1dbd338d8fe8536008ad3850,549127,1,digital_text,"White colored homogenous soft mass cream. Pharmacologic Category: Antifungal (imidazole and triazole derivatives) for topical use. Pharmacodynamics: Sertaconazole is an antifungal that belongs to the imidazole class of antifungals and exhibits activity similar to that of other imidazoles. It is believed that they act primarily by inhibiting the cytochrome P450-dependent synthesis of ergosterol. Ergosterol is a key component of the cell membrane of fungi, and lack of this component leads to fungal cell injury, primarily by leakage of key constituents in the cytoplasm from the cell. Sertaconazole has been shown to be active against isolates of dermatophytes (e.g. Trichophyton rubrum, Trichophyton mentagro - phytes, and Epidermophyton ﬂoccosum). Additionally, Sertaconazole has demonstrated broad spectrum of antifungal activity both in vitro and in experimental in vivo models, which includes opportunistic ﬁlamentous fungi (e.g. Aspergillus, Alternaria, Scopulariopsis, Fusarium), and pathogenic yeasts such as Malassezia furfur, Candida albicans, Candida tropicalis, Torulopsis, and trichosporon. Activity has also been observed against Trichomonas and some gram-positive organisms (staphylococci, streptococci). Pharmacokinetics: Sertaconazole achieves high epidermal concentrations following cutaneous application. Cutaneous absorption was 64% of the dose at 12 hours and 72% at 24 hours following topical application of 2% cream. Systemic absorption is minimal to undetectable. The drug was undetectable in serum or urine samples from healthy subjects for up to 24 hours with 16 g of Sertaconazole 2% cream.",1,1,cription:,Sertaconazole is indicated for the topical treatment of superﬁcial fungal infections of skin including tinea pedis.,1,1,Indication:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T16:16:15.425198+00:00
