PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12817-01,Sitagliptin (as phosphate monohydrate) + Metformin hydrochloride,Lupigliptin Plus,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Iu6P54Lpx8i9pNHVgIuNBol5P7KRnPvv/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12817-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Iu6P54Lpx8i9pNHVgIuNBol5P7KRnPvv_view_usp_drivesdk_3caeb2869c.pdf,page_text/DRP-12817-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Iu6P54Lpx8i9pNHVgIuNBol5P7KRnPvv_view_usp_drivesdk_3caeb2869c.json,c2d0ed3221f3303e62c67647d3eac7dea82d9d968c925ccfa56f231c9235bfb7,1877516,1,digital_text,"Lupigliptin Plus 50 mg/500 mg is available as w hite to off-white, oblong shaped film-coated tablet, biconvex plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Sitagliptin + Metformin HCl is indicated as initial therapy in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus to improve glycemic control when diet and exercise do not provide adequate glycemic control. Sitagliptin + Metformin HCl is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus inadequately controlled on metformin or sitagliptin alone or in patients already being treated with the combination of sitagliptin and metformin. Sitagliptin + Metformin HCl is indicated as part of triple combination therapy with a sulfonylurea as an adjunct to diet and exercise in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus inadequately controlled with any two of the three agents: sitagliptin, metformin, or sulfonylurea. Sitagliptin + Metformin HCl is indicated as part of triple combination therapy with a PPARγ agonist (i.e., thiazolidinediones) as an adjunct to diet exercise in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus inadequately controlled with any two of the three agents: sitagliptin, metformin, or a PPARγ agonist. Sitagliptin + Metformin HCl is indicated in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus as adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in combination with insulin.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:16:34.862833+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12818,Silver Sulfadiazine,Argyrex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1btuW5vd6_yPwYv5RXtIDbNROXzul-WaU/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12818_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1btuW5vd6_yPwYv5RXtIDbNROXzul-WaU_view_usp_drivesdk_dcfc9f4676.pdf,page_text/DRP-12818_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1btuW5vd6_yPwYv5RXtIDbNROXzul-WaU_view_usp_drivesdk_dcfc9f4676.json,e7fcf93bc90ddeb9ea31c6f7d248de0cd663872ac74df576b8c0927b68b9f5c6,531453,3,digital_text,"White colored smooth cream. PHARMACODYNAMICS Pharmacotherapeutic group: Antibacterial (Sulfonamide) for topical use. ATC Code: D06BA01. Silver sulfadiazine has broad antimicrobial activity against Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria including Pseudomonas aeruginosa, and some yeasts and fungi. Silver sulfadiazine has a bactericidal action; in contrast to sulfadiazine, the silver salt acts primarily on the cell membrane and cell wall and its action is not antagonized by p-aminobenzoic acid (PABA). PHARMACOKINETICS Silver sulfadiazine slowly releases sulfadiazine when in contact with wound exudates. Up to about 10% of the sulfadiazine may be absorbed; concentrations in blood of 10 to 20 mcg per mL have been reported, although higher concentrations may be achieved when extensive areas of the body are treated. Some silver may also be absorbed.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Silver sulfadiazine is an antibacterial agent for topical use. It is a sulfonamide that is used in conjunction with debridement, as a 1% w/w cream it is used for the prevention and treatment of infection in severe burns. Silver sulfadiazine is also used in other skin conditions, such as leg ulcers, where infection may prevent healing and for the prophylaxis of infection in skin grafting. It is used for the prevention and treatment of Pseudomonas and Staphylococcus infections in all kinds of wounds and ulcers, especially burns.",1,1,INDICATION,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:16:37.889484+00:00
