PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-12881,Sitagliptin (as phosphate) + Metformin Hydrochloride,Sitanova Plus 50/500,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/17dLJJ0NclVRs-anp71yEPrqcvuz3etyY/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-12881_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17dLJJ0NclVRs-anp71yEPrqcvuz3etyY_view_usp_drivesdk_121c27af7d.pdf,page_text/DRP-12881_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17dLJJ0NclVRs-anp71yEPrqcvuz3etyY_view_usp_drivesdk_121c27af7d.json,df3182a6f5efe122d07077e9b2453fb1151a17fa45841392a0d96a6c80e0a6fa,809523,4,digital_text,"Light orange caplet deep biconvex film-coated tablet, one score on one side",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For adult patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus: Indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycaemic control in patients inadequately controlled on their maximal tolerated d ose of metformin alone or those already being treated with the combination of sitagliptin and metformin. Sitagliptin Phosphate + Metformin Hydrochloride is indicated in combination with a sulphonylurea (i.e., triple combination therapy) as an adjunct to di et and exercise in patients inadequately controlled on their maximal tolerated dose of metformin and a sulphonylurea. Sitagliptin Phosphate + Metformin Hydrochloride is indicated as triple combination therapy with a peroxisome proliferator -activated recept or gamma (PPARγ) agonist (i.e., a thiazolidinedione) as an adjunct to diet and exercise in patients inadequately controlled on their maximal tolerated dose of metformin and a PPARγ agonist. Sitagliptin Phosphate + Metformin Hydrochloride is also indicated as add-on to insulin (i.e., triple combination therapy) as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycaemic control in patients when stable dose of insulin and metformin alone do not provide adequate glycaemic control.",2,2,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:19:32.072860+00:00
