PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-131,CEFALEXIN (AS MONOHYDRATE),LONAREL,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1iwt8qfo0Vq0QIzhT3jfJKb0nSnnofbn2/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-131_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1iwt8qfo0Vq0QIzhT3jfJKb0nSnnofbn2_view_usp_drivesdk_a80fa4c073.pdf,page_text/DRP-131_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1iwt8qfo0Vq0QIzhT3jfJKb0nSnnofbn2_view_usp_drivesdk_a80fa4c073.json,bcf9d6ab03711bc9fd378fc5d1540714d332074ab34bf6ee1069e92631596679,892280,1,digital_text,"Prepared by adding water to the powder to give 60 mL ﬂavored and colored suspension containing 250 mg of Cefalexin (as monohydrate) in each 5 mL. It complies with the USP speciﬁcations for Cefalexin mixture. DESCRIPTION Cefalexin is a semisynthetic cephalosporin antibacterial drug intended for oral administration. It is 7-(D-α-Amino- α-phenylacetamido)-3-methyl-3-cephem-4-carboxylic acid monohydrate. Cephalexin has the molecular formula C16H17N3O4SH2O and the molecular weight is 365.41. Cephalexin has the following structural formula: Cefalexin is a white to off-white crystalline powder. Slightly soluble in water, practically soluble in water, practically insoluble in alcohol, in chloroform, and in ether.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"For the treatment of urinary tract infections, infections of the respiratory tract, otitis media, skin and other infections due to sensitive organisms. PHARMACOKINETICS Cefalexin is almost completely absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract and produces a peak plasma concentration of about 18 micrograms/mL 1 hour after a 500- mg oral dose. If cefalexin is taken with food, absorption may be delayed, but the total amount absorbed is not appreciably altered. Up to 15% of a dose is bound to plasma proteins. The plasma half-life is about 1 hour; it increases with reduced renal function. Cefalexin is widely distributed in the body but does not enter the CSF in signiﬁcant quantities. It crosses the placenta and small quantities are found in breast milk. Cefalexin is not metabolised. About 80% or more of a dose is excreted unchanged in the urine in the ﬁrst 6 hours by glomerular ﬁltration and tubular secretion; urinary concentrations greater than 1 mg/mL have been achieved after a dose of 500 mg. Probenecid delays urinary excretion. Therapeutically effective concentrations may be found in the bile and some may be excreted by this route. Cefalexin is removed by haemodialysis and peritoneal dialysis.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:24:59.100675+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13113,Miconazole,Medonazole,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1eLXZIY3gSn75afe_KBuJyInY6v3B5vRI/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13113_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eLXZIY3gSn75afe_KBuJyInY6v3B5vRI_view_usp_drivesdk_eddabd07ee.pdf,page_text/DRP-13113_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eLXZIY3gSn75afe_KBuJyInY6v3B5vRI_view_usp_drivesdk_eddabd07ee.json,d238b7a2296cec3eef8bc8a8e095a7754390bfbf768586216da35b601fd9faae,532620,1,digital_text,White soft cream,1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T16:25:02.748748+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13122,Levetiracetam,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1tlTcHKK6siNiQfloCnjlUdxMF85Mblax/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13122_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1tlTcHKK6siNiQfloCnjlUdxMF85Mblax_view_usp_drivesdk_bc7773cbee.pdf,page_text/DRP-13122_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1tlTcHKK6siNiQfloCnjlUdxMF85Mblax_view_usp_drivesdk_bc7773cbee.json,52d1498de0b3e1e3487923453bc8f603d8a31f41aa8f6d8ba8ec049fd998fba7,477691,2,digital_text,"Clear, colourless sterile solution, free from foreign particles.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Levetiracetam is indicated as monotherapy in the treatment of partial onset seizures with or without secondary generalisation in adults and adolescents from 16 years of age with newly diagnosed epilepsy. Levetiracetam is indicated as adjunctive therapy • in the treatment of partial onset seizures with or without secondary generalisation in adults, adolescents and children from 4 years of age with epilepsy. · in the treatment of myoclonic seizures in adults and adolescents from 12 years of age with Juvenile Myoclonic Epilepsy. · in the treatment of primary generalised tonic-clonic seizures in adults and adolescents from 12 years of age with Idiopathic Generalised Epilepsy. Levetiracetam concentrate solution for infusion is an alternative for patients when oral administration is temporarily not feasible.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:25:05.784343+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1313,Omeprazole,Hycid-20,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sozCJlUray-qSahdLKWgn7rOm7ahj3V3/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1313_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1sozCJlUray-qSahdLKWgn7rOm7ahj3V3_view_usp_drivesdk_efeae3cedd.pdf,page_text/DRP-1313_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1sozCJlUray-qSahdLKWgn7rOm7ahj3V3_view_usp_drivesdk_efeae3cedd.json,8fdaea9c73b34feead7a6498ebb9cee0761e9ff5795840218c8b25e96131aae8,676318,1,digital_text,Pink transparent cap and clear transparent body hard gelatin capsules containing white enteric-coated pellets.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Omeprazole is used in the treatment of peptic ulcer disease, and other conditions where inhibition of gastric acid secretion may be beneficial, including aspiration syndrome, dyspepsia, gastroesophageal reflux disease, and Zollinger Ellison Syndrome.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:25:11.703113+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1313-02,Omeprazole,Obax,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hhaTVJcH4gfC8C23kGYuldchqN9yfOpW/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1313-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hhaTVJcH4gfC8C23kGYuldchqN9yfOpW_view_usp_drivesdk_f8df5f47ab.pdf,page_text/DRP-1313-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hhaTVJcH4gfC8C23kGYuldchqN9yfOpW_view_usp_drivesdk_f8df5f47ab.json,cb63570cd280fcc7629c11764f5d15b33d0ca8b04d32583e224a4229d4f850a8,534777,1,digital_text,Pink transparent cap and clear transparent body hard gelatin capsules containing white enteric-coated pellets.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Omeprazole is used in the treatment of peptic ulcer disease, and other conditions where inhibition of gastric acid secretion may be beneficial, including aspiration syndrome, dyspepsia, gastroesophageal reflux disease, and Zollinger Ellison Syndrome.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:25:08.706969+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13131,Tacrolimus,Tacrohab,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GlWZFiOHodBfCbd4Dbip126taTozgMsu/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13131_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GlWZFiOHodBfCbd4Dbip126taTozgMsu_view_usp_drivesdk_1f0cd9f959.pdf,page_text/DRP-13131_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GlWZFiOHodBfCbd4Dbip126taTozgMsu_view_usp_drivesdk_1f0cd9f959.json,ceeb6850235beb272c7e4ac49f3b9b7c2b6a2a48679cf9fc6a93d53bfbda13d6,2090113,2,digital_text,"A white to slightly yellowish ointment. Pharmacodynamics The mechanism of action of Tacrolimus in atopic dermatitis is not fully understood. While the following have been cytoplasmic immunophilin (FKBP12), Tacrolimus inhibits calcium-dependent signal transduction pathways in T cells, thereby preventing the transcription and synthesis of IL-2,IL-3, IL-4, IL-5 and other cytokines such as GM-CSF, TNF-a and IFN-y. In vitro, Langerhans cells isolated from normal human skin, tacrolimus reduced the stimulatory activity towards T cells. eosinophils. that resemble human atopic dermatitis. Tacrolimus ointment did not reduced skin thickness and did not cause skin atrophy in animals. In patients with atopic dermatitis, improvement of skin lesions during treatment with Tacrolimus ointment was associated with reduced Fc receptor expression on Langerhans cells and a reduction of their hyperstimulatory activity Pharmacokinetics Absorption Data from healthy human subject indicate that there is little or no systemic exposure to tacrolimus following single or repeated topical application of Tacrolimus ointment. Target through concentrations for systemic immunosuppression for oral Tacrolimus are 5-20 ng/mL ion transplant patients. Most atopic dermatitis patients (adult and children) treated with single or repeated application of Tacrolimus ointment (0.03-0.1%), and infants from age of 5 months treated with Tacrolimus ointment (0.03%) had blood concentrations <1.0 ng/mL. When observed, blood concentrations exceeding 1.0 ng/mL were transient. Systemic exposure increases with increasing treatment areas. However, both the extent and the rate of topical absorption of Tacrolimus decrease as the skin heals. In both adults and children with an average of 50% body surface area treated, systemic exposure (i.e. AUC) of Tacrolimus from Tacrolimus ointment is approximately 30-fold less than that seen with oral immunosuppressive doses in kidney and in liver transplant patients. The lowest Tacrolimus blood concentration at There was no evidence of systemic accumulation of Tacrolimus in patients (adults and children) treated for prolonged periods (up to one year) with Tacrolimus ointment. Distribution As systemic exposure is low with Tacrolimus ointment, the high binding of Tacrolimus (>98.8%) to plasma proteins is considered not to be clinically relevant. into the systemic circulation. Biotransformation Metabolism of Tacrolimus by human skin was not detectable. Systematically available Tacrolimus is extensively metabolized in the liver via CYP3A4. Elimination When administered intravenously, tacrolimus has been shown to have a low clearance rate. The average total body clearance is approximately 2.25 l/h. The hepatic clearance of systematically available Tacrolimus could be reduced in subjects with severe hepatic impairment, or in subjects who are co-treated with drugs that are potent inhibitors of CYP3A4. Following repeated topical application of the ointment the average half-life of Tacrolimus was estimated to be 75 hours for adults and 65 hours for children.",1,1,Product Description,Treatment for moderate to severe atopic dermatitis.,1,1,Indication,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:25:15.648576+00:00
