PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13146,Paracetamol,Medpara IV,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gaVSh5B8wUQwRW3a-HL9nC7VJwUy7IrU/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13146_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gaVSh5B8wUQwRW3a-HL9nC7VJwUy7IrU_view_usp_drivesdk_f49b227776.pdf,page_text/DRP-13146_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gaVSh5B8wUQwRW3a-HL9nC7VJwUy7IrU_view_usp_drivesdk_f49b227776.json,cc8715679ff608aa5ad2c41af0c8fdd4ad6ec5f2a2a82a8ca5ca020af7be759a,738150,4,digital_text,A clear colourless to pale yellow color solution,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for the short -term treatment of moderate pain, especially following surgery, and for the short-term treatment of fever, when administration by intraven ous route is clinically justified by an urgent need to treat pain or hyperthermia and/or when other routes of administration are not possible.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:25:37.611615+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13149,Ascorbic Acid + Zinc,ZinCee,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1QRWgdXYxS_LiEuF4TaRO7gKetJSZvrxy/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13149_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QRWgdXYxS_LiEuF4TaRO7gKetJSZvrxy_view_usp_drivesdk_e10773fe30.pdf,page_text/DRP-13149_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QRWgdXYxS_LiEuF4TaRO7gKetJSZvrxy_view_usp_drivesdk_e10773fe30.json,d74119387ff58e0093190a9587820b02fb522388d8226eadd958b284bbd46a5c,241930,1,digital_text,"ZinCee capsule contains Sodium Ascorbate , a sodium salt of Ascorbic Acid, and Zinc Sulfate Monohydrate . It is a white to slightly yellow crystalline powder encapsulated in a metallic gold cap and body, size 0 hard gelatin capsule. What is in the Medicine? This product contains Sodium ascorbate , a non -acidic form of Vitamin C. It is a cofactor of enzymes involved in the formation of collagen, the most abundant protein essential in the formation of teeth, bones, cartilage and skin. It also helps boost the immune system and increase body resistance to physical stress, common colds, viral and other type of",1,1,Description of the Product:,"Zinc on the other hand plays a major role in the creation of DNA , growth of cells, building proteins, healing damaged tissue, and supporting a healthy immune system. Strength of the Medicine: This product contains 500 mg of Ascorbic Acid (as Sodium Ascorbate equivalent to 562.43 mg) and 10 mg of Zinc (as Zinc Sulfate Monohydrate equivalent to 27.5 mg) What is this medicine used for? Ascorbic Acid + Zinc (ZinCee) capsule is used for the treatment and prevention of Vitamin C and Zinc deficiencies. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Take Ascorbic Acid + Zinc (ZinCee) capsule orally once a day with or without food. Or as prescribed by the physician. When should you NOT take this medicine? This medicine should not be taken if Sodium Ascorbate can potencially interact with other drugs or substances, other interacting conditions present like hyperoxaluria and G6PD deficiency, tolerance is developed due to prolonged intake of large doses and gastrointestinal disturbances like diarrhea are developed due to intake of large doses. Also, if allergy to any component of this product is possible. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine ● Ask a doctor before use if you are on a sodium restricted diet. ● Do not take more than the recommended dose. ● Do not use this product after its expiration date. What are the undesirable effects of this medicine? ● Ascorbic Acid Large doses are reported to cause diarrhea and other gastrointestinal disturbances, nausea, vomiting, heartburn, abdominal cramps, insomnia, fatigue and sleepiness. Tolerance may be induced with prolonged use of large doses, resulting in symptoms of deficiency when intake is reduced to normal. ● Zinc Frequently Zinc causes gastrointestinal side effects which include abdominal pain, dyspepsia, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, gastric irritation and gastritis.These are particularly common if zinc salts are taken with an empty stomach and maybe reduced by giving them with meals. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine?  Iron containing products  Fluphenazine  Warfarin  Copper containing products  Tetracyclines What should you do if you miss a dose of this medicine? Take the missed dose as soon as you remember it. However, if it is almost time for your next dose, skip the missed dose and continue with the regular dosing schedule. Do not take a double dose. What are the signs and symptoms of overdose?  Large doses intake are reported to cause diarrhea and other gastrointestinal disturbances. What should you do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? Consult a doctor or contact the nearest hospital immediately. Bring the container or label with you to help doctors with necessary information. How should you keep/ store this medicine? ● Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C . ● Protect from light. ● Keep out of reach and sight of children. When should you consult your doctor?  If any undesirable effect occurs.  If the patient is taking any vitamin or medicines. Pregnancy and breast feeding. Ask your doctor or pharmacist for advice before taking any medicine. Sodium Ascorbate (Cigla-Kas) should be taken with precaution for women who are pregnant and breastfeeding. Name and Address of the Manufacturer and Marketing Authorization Holder: St. Martin Pharm Lab Co. 55 Lakandula Street, Parang, Marikina City, Philippines “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph” “Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction.” Registration Number: DRP-13149 Date of First Authorization/ Renewal of the Authorization: 12/12/2022 / 12/12/2027 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: 12/12/2022 ASCORBIC ACID ZINC [Page 2]",1,1,infections.,low,needs_human_review,2026-06-29T16:25:40.756641+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13150,Doripenem (as monohydrate),Drofepen,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IINKBIoTgr911u0xQY2n-hh3u6WwAHY8/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13150_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IINKBIoTgr911u0xQY2n-hh3u6WwAHY8_view_usp_drivesdk_489530a947.pdf,page_text/DRP-13150_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IINKBIoTgr911u0xQY2n-hh3u6WwAHY8_view_usp_drivesdk_489530a947.json,89a5855db9a0064de9ada8710df455837e14207ae8d1574042d1610d173e0d9e,2169883,2,digital_text,"Drofepen contains doripenem monohydrate, which is a synthetic broad-spectrum carbapenem antibiotic structurally related to beta-lactarn antibiotics. The chemical name for doripenem monohydrate is (4R, 5S, 6S)-3-[((3S, 5S)-5- [[(aminosulfonyl) amino] methyl]-3-pyrrolidinyl)thio]-6-[(1 R)-1- hydroxyethyl]-4-methyl-7 -oxo-1-azabicyclo[3.2 .0)hept- 2-ene-2- carboxylic acid monohydrate. Its molecular formula is C H N O S •H O and its molecular weight is 438.52. 15 24 4 6 2 2 The chemical structure doripenem monohydrate is given below: White to yellow colour powder STRUCTURAL FORMULA (DORIPENEM MONOHYDRATE )",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Race: The effect of race on doripenem pharmacokinetics was examined using a population pharmacokinetic analysis of data from phase 1 and 2 studies. Compared to Caucasians, mean doripenem clearance was 14% greater in Hispanic / Latino subjects whereas no difference in clearance was observed for African Americans. Doripenem clearance in Japanese studies is similar to what has been observed in Western populations. No dosage adjustment is recommended based on race. The recommended dosage of Doripenem is 500 mg administered every 8 hours by intravenous infusion over one hour in patients ≥18 years of age. The recommended dosage and administration by infection is described in Table 1: A single 500 mg dose of doripenem was administered to subjects with end stage renal disease (ESRD) either one hour prior to or one hour after hemodialysis (HD). The mean doripenem AUC following the post-HD infusion was 7.8-times that of healthy subjects with normal renal function. The mean total recovery of doripenem and doripenem-M1 in the dialysate following a 4-hour HD session was 231 mg and 28 mg, respectively, or a total of 259 mg (52% of the- dose). There is insufficient information to make dose adjustment recommendations in patients on hemodialysis.",1,1,INDICATlONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:25:44.828675+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13155,Pregabalin,Pregamed 150,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DO4E0c4c2pyU2dzYO1pkVgqjrWWwZLNv/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13155_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1DO4E0c4c2pyU2dzYO1pkVgqjrWWwZLNv_view_usp_drivesdk_23453eb383.pdf,page_text/DRP-13155_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1DO4E0c4c2pyU2dzYO1pkVgqjrWWwZLNv_view_usp_drivesdk_23453eb383.json,12a18ed2719dc24a82277b9ead6b7b4e1fc9227ddfa5a0c41b081517396448bd,189542,4,digital_text,Hard gelatin capsules size “1” with dark green coloured cap and white colored body containing white to off white colored pellets.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Neuropathic pain Indicated for the treatment of peripheral and central neuropathic pain in adults. Epilepsy Indicated as adjunctive therapy in adults with partial seizures with or without secondary generalisation. Generalised anxiety disorder Indicated for the treatment of Generalised Anxiety Disorder (GAD) in adults.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:25:48.053281+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13156,Pioglitazone (as Hydrochloride),Pioglinova-15,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1v2lotuoSApsMMVC2qvmx8LIjNUAdYAMR/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13156_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1v2lotuoSApsMMVC2qvmx8LIjNUAdYAMR_view_usp_drivesdk_282b48c997.pdf,page_text/DRP-13156_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1v2lotuoSApsMMVC2qvmx8LIjNUAdYAMR_view_usp_drivesdk_282b48c997.json,75d45f06b1831bcea22f51b8103148ec3a9d6d7c03226171cee9c5d455aef973,789711,6,digital_text,"Pioglinova-45: White to off white, round, flat, beveled edged, uncoated tablets embossed “45” on one side and plain on the other side. Pioglinova-30: White to off white, round, flat, beveled edged, uncoated tablets embossed “30” on one side and plain on the other side. Pioglinova-15: White to off white, round, flat, beveled edged, uncoated tablets embossed “15” on one side and plain on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Pioglitazone is indicated as second or third line treatment of type 2 diabetes mellitus as described below: as monotherapy - in adult patients (particularly overweight patients) inadequately controlled by diet and exercise for whom metformin is inappropriate because of contraindications or intolerance as dual oral therapy in combination with - metformin, in adult patients (particularly overweight patients) with insufficient glycaemic control despite maximal tolerated dose of monotherapy with metformin - a sulphonylurea, only in adult patients who show intolerance to metformin or for whom metformin is contraindicated, with insufficient glycaemic control despite maximal tolerated dose of monotherapy with a sulphonylurea. As triple oral therapy in combination with - metformin and a sulphonylurea, in adult patients (particularly overweight patients) with insufficient glycaemic control despite dual oral therapy. Pioglitazone is also indicated for combination with insulin in type 2 diabetes mellitus adult patients with insufficient glycaemic control on insulin fo r whom metformin is inappropriate because of contraindications or intolerance. After initiation of therapy with pioglitazone, patients should be reviewed after 3 to 6 months to assess adequacy of response to treatment (e.g. reduction in HbA1c). In patients who fail to show an adequate response, pioglitazone should be discontinued. In light of potential risks with prolonged therapy, PIOGLITAZONE HYDROCHLORIDE PIOGLINOVA-45 PIOGLINOVA-30 PIOGLINOVA-15 45 mg Tablet 30 mg Tablet 15 mg Tablet ORAL HYPOGLYCEMIC AGENT [Page 2] prescribers should confirm at subsequent routine reviews that the benefit of pioglitazone is maintained.",1,2,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:25:51.333902+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13157,Levothyroxine sodium,Thyres 50,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/10_dGILDSjQhThi29kFCJnUNu-gfyEnr5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13157_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_10_dGILDSjQhThi29kFCJnUNu-gfyEnr5_view_usp_drivesdk_c2164fd854.pdf,page_text/DRP-13157_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_10_dGILDSjQhThi29kFCJnUNu-gfyEnr5_view_usp_drivesdk_c2164fd854.json,0e9486e306c9bc3cee9d927a3c62cf4908e8b60b126ff2f5515ae98fcd8b5f61,619942,2,digital_text,"THYRES 50: Pink colored, oval shaped bi-convex tablet having break line on one side and plain on other side. THYRES 100: Pale orange colored, oval shaped bi-convex tablet having break line on one side and plain on other side. Pharmacology: Pharmacologic Category: Belongs to the class of thyroid hormones. ATC code: H03AA01. Pharmacodynamics: Thyroxine (T4) is a naturally occurring hormone produced by the thyroid gland and converted to the more active hormone triiodothyronine (T3) in peripheral tissues. The precise signals controlling the conversion of T4 to T3 within the cell are not known. The thyroid hormones are required for normal growth and development, particularly of the nervous system. They increase the resting or basal metabolic rate of the whole organism and have stimulatory effects on the heart, skeletal muscle, liver and kidney. Thyroid hormones enhance lipolysis and the utilization of carbohydrate. 100 microgram thyroxine is equivalent in activity to 20 to 30 microgram liothyronin/triiodothyronine or 60 mg Thyroid BP and/or local pharmacopoiea specification. Pharmacokinetics: Absorption: Following oral administration, the absorption of thyroxine is incomplete and variable, especially when taken with food. The amount absorbed increases during fasting conditions. Distribution: Thyroxine is nearly totally bound to serum protein. Metabolism: The main pathway for the metabolism of thyroxine (T4) is its conversion, by de-iodination, to the active metabolite triiodothyronine (T3). Further de-iodination of T4 and T3 leads to production of inactive products. Elimination: Thyroxine is eliminated slowly from the body with a half-life of approximately seven days in a normal person. This may be reduced in hyperthyroid states or increased in hypothyroid patients. In man, approximately 20 to 40% of thyroxine is eliminated in the faeces and approximately 30 to 55% of a dose of thyroxine is excreted in the urine.",1,1,Product Description:,"• Control of hypothyroidism, • Congenital hypothyroidism in infants, • Acquired hypothyroidism in children and • Juvenile myxedema",1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:25:58.398178+00:00
