PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-134,Multivitamins,Unbranded,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1kTIUYhgK6MkXPjpUhLWayl92_Ra20ZEN/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-134_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kTIUYhgK6MkXPjpUhLWayl92_Ra20ZEN_view_usp_drivesdk_1ffab9e6f2.pdf,page_text/DRP-134_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kTIUYhgK6MkXPjpUhLWayl92_Ra20ZEN_view_usp_drivesdk_1ffab9e6f2.json,1c0593aae31fa75234181b9d36e76ec99e692d26290a1d22430186e602f5e2b5,3775528,1,ocr,"The medicine is a yellow to reddish orange syrup with orange flavor and taste, contains chlorella, an insoluble particle contained in a 60 mL,120ml and 250ml amber round bottle. What is in the medicine? The medicine contains multivitamins with Omega-3-Fatty Acid and Chlorella Growth Factor which are organic substances required for various metabolic processes. It is equally necessary for proper growth, maintenance of health, and proper development of the brain and heart. The body cannot synthesize several vitamins and minerals, thus they must be supplied through diet or dietary supplements. The vitamins function with chemicals called enzymes which are mainly responsible for the oxidation process within the body. Enzymes are also a major factor in biochemical processes such as growth, metabolism, cellular teproduction and digestion. Strength of the medicine: Each 5 milliliter (1 teaspoonful) syrup contains: Retinol Palmitate (Vitamin A), 2,500 IU 400 IU Cholecalciferol (Vitamin D3). Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C). 60 mg L-Lysine. 12.5 mg Lecithin. 10 mg 10 mg Calcium Carbonate 5 mg Omega-3-Fatty Acids. 5 mg d-Panthenol 3 mg Pyridoxine Hydrochlori itamin BE 2mg Thiamine ‘Vitamin Bt), 1.5 mg Riboflavin Sodium Phosphate (Vitamin B2). 41.5 mg Chlorella Growth Factor. 100 meg Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12 2 meg What is this medicine used for? Multivitamins syrup is used to provide nutritional balance necessary for physical growth and mental development. This is used for the treatment and of vitamit nutritional to stimulate appetite, growth and weight gain, enhances body resistance against stress, infections, and diseases. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Children: 26 years old: 2.5 mL- 5 mL (1/2 to 1 teaspoonful) 7-12 years old: 5 mL-10 mL (1-2 teaspoonfuls) To be taken once a day, or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? -lf you are allergic to any of the components in the product. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: -Do not take more than the recommended dose. -Do not use after the expiry date stated on the label, Undesirable effects of this medicine: Retinol Palmitate (Vitamin A)- Hypervitaminosis A due to intake of very high doses can cause fatigue, irritability, anorexia, loss of weight, vomiting, sedation, dizziness, confusion, diarrhea. Cholecalciferol (Vitamin D3)- Excessive intake may lead to hypercalcemia or hyperphosphatemia Riboflavin Sodium Phosphate (Vitamin B2)- Large doses may result to bright yellow discoloration in urine. Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12)- Allergic hypersensitivity reactions have occurred rarely that includes rash, itching, anaphylaxis. Niacinamide- side effects are minimal but at high doses liver problems may occur. Chilorella- itis possibly safe when taken by mouth, short-term (up to 2 months). The most common side effects include diarrhea, nausea, gas (flatulence), green discoloration of the stools, and stomach cramping, especially in the first week of use.Chlorella has caused serious allergic reactions, including asthma and other dangerous breathing problems.Chlorella can cause skin to become extra sensitive to the sun. Omega-3-Fatty Acid- the most common adverse effects includes gastrointestinal disturbances, particularly at high doses, including nausea, eructation, vomiting, abdominal distension, diarrhea, and constipation. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Retinol Palmitate (Vitamin A)- Neomycin, Cholestyramine or Liquid paraffin may reduce the absorption of Vitamin A. Increase risk of hypervitaminosis A if given with retinoids such as isotretinoin and tretinoin. Cholecalciferol (Vitamin D3)- Increased risk of hypercalcaemia if Vitamin D is given with Aes diuretics, Calcium, ee Pyridoxine HCI (Vitamin B6)- Pyridoxine reduces the effects of Levodopa and Alltret and Phenytoin. Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12)- Neomycin, Aminosalicylic Acid, Histamine H2 Antagonist, Omeprazole, Colchicine Eu the absorption of Vitamin B12. Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C)- Omeprazole Chlorella- Chlorla might increase the immune system. By increasing the immune system, chlorella might decrease the effectiveness of medications that are used to decrease the immune system (Azathioprine, Daclizumab, facrolimus, Sirolimus, Prednisone, Corticosteroids). Chlorella might decrease the effectiveness of warfarin (Coumadin) since CGF contains large amounts of vitamin K. one Kis used by the body to help blood clot. Omega-3-Fatty Acid- it has an antithrombotic activity and should not be given to patients receiving anticoagulants or other drugs affecting coagulation What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: The following symptoms might be seen in large dose: Retinol Palmitate (Vitamin A)- Intake in excess of 10,000 IU daily or weekly intakes in excess of 25,000 IU have resulted to hypervitaminosis A (fatigue, irritability, anorexia, loss of weight, vomiting, sedation dizziness, confusion, diarrhea’ Cholecalciferol (Vitamin D3)- Anorexia, lassitude, nausea, vomiting, constipation, diarrhea, polyuria, nocturia, sweating, headache, thirst, somnolence, vertigo. Eynidoaiie HCl (Vitamin B6)- Long term use of large doses is associated with the development of severe peripheral neuropathies. itamin B12)- fever, chills, hot flushing, dizziness, malaise, acneform, eruptions, tremor. Room Acid (Vitamin C)- Large doses may cause diarrhea, abdominal pain and disturbances. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. When should you consult your doctor? If any undesirable effect occurs. “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph” Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration number: ¥ Date of Renewal Authorization: August 16, 2022 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: September 17, 20: Manufactured by: Diamond Laboratories, Inc. #8 Feria Rd., Commonwealth Ave Diliman, Quezon City [Page 2]",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T16:32:49.204725+00:00
