e 2 diabetes mellitus adult patients with insufficient glycaemic control on insulin fo r whom metformin is inappropriate because of contraindications or intolerance. After initiation of therapy with pioglitazone, patients should be reviewed after 3 to 6 months to assess adequacy of response to treatment (e.g. reduction in HbA1c). In patients who fail to show an adequate response, pioglitazone should be discontinued. In light of potential risks with prolonged therapy, PIOGLITAZONE HYDROCHLORIDE PIOGLINOVA-45 PIOGLINOVA-30 PIOGLINOVA-15 45 mg Tablet 30 mg Tablet 15 mg Tablet ORAL HYPOGLYCEMIC AGENT [Page 2] prescribers should confirm at subsequent routine reviews that the benefit of pioglitazone is maintained.",1,2,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:35:56.970723+00:00
