PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13494,Oxymetazoline Hydrochloride,Nasathix,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-fS8nFpATLbuLyuAoG1zK4uluwx7-BsE/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13494_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-fS8nFpATLbuLyuAoG1zK4uluwx7-BsE_view_usp_drivesdk_59c1ec8c1f.pdf,page_text/DRP-13494_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-fS8nFpATLbuLyuAoG1zK4uluwx7-BsE_view_usp_drivesdk_59c1ec8c1f.json,04ca2343cd8b2c938c78f2fca1d6ccbf673f268ab3b011c1c19c94edc655b27d,842765,2,digital_text,"Clear, colourless, odourless, liquid ﬁlled in LDPE squeeze bottle with screw cap. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? The product contains Oxymetazoline hydrochloride USP 0.05%w/v in an aqueous isotonic solution using puriﬁed water and Benzalkonium chloride Solution 0.022% w/v as preservative. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Each mL contains: Oxymetazoline Hydrochloride USP… 500 mcg/mL (0.05%w/v) WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? For the fast relief of stuffy nose due to head colds and hay fever. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Hold the bottle upright and insert nozzle into nostril. Adults and children over 12 years 1-2 sprays up each nostril every 6-8 hours. Children under 12 years old Not to be administered to children under 12 years. Elderly There is no need for dosage reduction in the elderly. For : nasal administration. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Hypersensitivity to any of the ingredients oxymetazoline or . Use Oxymetazoline 0.05% with extreme caution in patients receiving monoamine oxidase inhibitors or within 14 days of stopping such Hydrochloride 500 mcg/mL (0.05% w/v) Nasal Spray Nasal Decongestant NASATHIX This product should not be more than 5 days. if symptoms persist consult a doctor. Prolonged use or excessive application to the nasal mucosa may produce rebound congestion and rhinorrhoea. The use of this container by more than one person may spread infection. Warnings and Special Precautions Not recommended for children under 6 years of age. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE Keep away from the eyes. Table 1 The following side-effects have been reported and the frequencies are unknown UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THE MEDICINE Occasionally may cause local irritation and dryness of the mouth and throat. Prolonged use may cause rebound congestion and rhinitis medicamentosa. Pregnancy and lactation The safety of Oxymetazoline Nasal Spray during pregnancy and lactation has not been established, but is not thought to constitute a hazard during these periods. treatment. Children may be especially sensitive to the effects of these medicines. Should be used with caution in patients with: Hypertension, hyperthyroidism, cardiovascular disease such as ischaemic heart disease, arrhythmias, tachycardia, occlusive vascular disease, arteriosclerosis, aneurysms, diabetes mellitus, closed-angle glaucoma, prostatic hypertrophy. Oxymetazoline Hydrochloride USP………………..….. 500 mcg ONMEII000 FOR EXTERNAL USE ONLY FOR INTRANASAL USE ONLY WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? [Page 2] HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Store at a temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Do not freeze or refrigerate. Keep out of reach of children Shake well before use. Keep away from children. Close cap tightly after every use. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? Hypersensitivity to the active substance or to any of the excipients. ADR Reporting Statement: For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph Seek medical attention immediately at the reaction. ﬁrst sign of any adverse drug Reg. No.: DRP-13494 Date of Authorization: 28 FEB 2023 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaﬂet: 28 MAR 2023 Imported and Distributed by: 6F RFM Corporate Center, Pioneer St. Mandaluyong City, Metro Manila Manufactured by: Biodeal Pharmaceuticals Pvt. Ltd. Vill. Saini Majra, Nalagarh-Ropar Road, Nalagarh, Distt. Solan, Himachal Pradesh, 174101, India For: Aztec Pharma Pvt. Ltd. Surendra Nagar, Gujarat 363001, India",1,2,DESCRIPTION:,,1,1,infection.,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-29T16:36:19.795484+00:00
