PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13523-02,Losartan potassium + Amlodipine (as besilate),Colixtan,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ci4dcam6ARF3V5eCDjV0PkoBkUJiq2_t/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13523-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ci4dcam6ARF3V5eCDjV0PkoBkUJiq2_t_view_usp_drivesdk_e46dfc59d6.pdf,page_text/DRP-13523-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ci4dcam6ARF3V5eCDjV0PkoBkUJiq2_t_view_usp_drivesdk_e46dfc59d6.json,49594ad53fe0f592b9231b411ca95efb0b812430201c38b4b48ec940f70e36d7,519831,1,digital_text,"Yellow, round, biconvex, film-coated tablets, plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Fixed-dose combination of Losartan and Amlodipine is indicated for the treatment of essential hypertension in adult patients whose blood pressure is not adequately controlled on either monotherapy.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:36:48.198431+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13524,Gabapentin,Gabaknock,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/11a6jRXhifTn0iX7zmcYDNSYj_qyqt5LS/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13524_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11a6jRXhifTn0iX7zmcYDNSYj_qyqt5LS_view_usp_drivesdk_5d849fdc41.pdf,page_text/DRP-13524_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11a6jRXhifTn0iX7zmcYDNSYj_qyqt5LS_view_usp_drivesdk_5d849fdc41.json,12b374b93fda252a9fd862ec94f77a207fe5acd0c6014f1bbb8ee08dbcb6a8be,2835626,1,digital_text,"White/white coloured, non brittle hard gelatin capsule size '2' containing white powder.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Epilepsy: Gabapentin is indicated as monotherapy in the treatment of partial seizures with and without secondary generalization in adults and children aged 12 years and older. Safety and effectiveness for monotherapy in children younger than 12 years have not been established (see Dosage & Administration: Epilepsy: Adults and pediatric patients over 12 years of age). Gabapentin is indicated as adjunctive therapy in the treatment of par tial seizures with and without secondary generalization in adults and children aged 3 years and older. Safety and effectiveness for adjunctive therapy in pediatric patients younger than 3 years have not been established (see Dosage & Administration: Epilepsy: Pediatric patients aged 3 to 12 years). Neuropathic pain: Gabapentin is indicated for the treatment of neuropathic pain in adults aged 18 years and older. Safety and effectiveness in patients younger than 18 years have not been established.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:36:55.321743+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13525,Clindamycin (As Hydrochloride),Clindanova,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/17ISjLSXcn3nx_NlKrgzJDAQQfVoG9EVx/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13525_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17ISjLSXcn3nx_NlKrgzJDAQQfVoG9EVx_view_usp_drivesdk_031524e6af.pdf,page_text/DRP-13525_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17ISjLSXcn3nx_NlKrgzJDAQQfVoG9EVx_view_usp_drivesdk_031524e6af.json,692278c3f6dd65c521ea9d8abe5b8384392c6c61027c19740fc6b34dffe6817e,723586,2,digital_text,Orange/Orange colored “Saga/Saga” printed size “0” capsule,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Clindamycin is indicated for the treatment of: Serious infections caused by anaerobic bacteria, including intra -abdominal infections, skin and soft tissue infections. As needed, clindamycin should be administered in conjunction with another antibacterial agent that is active against gram negative aerobic bacteria. - Tonsillitis - Dental infection Consideration should be given to the official guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:36:59.338832+00:00
