PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13647,Pregabalin,Rebalin 75,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-uYtWtH8rlJYcBeatzwHEV3iR1_xU5rL/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13647_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-uYtWtH8rlJYcBeatzwHEV3iR1_xU5rL_view_usp_drivesdk_b6b2357807.pdf,page_text/DRP-13647_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-uYtWtH8rlJYcBeatzwHEV3iR1_xU5rL_view_usp_drivesdk_b6b2357807.json,004f4256c9cea134f793197f9b9aa9db75faac71c74b778418a0593a1fc593dd,820277,2,digital_text,"Size ‘1’ hard gelatin capsule with yellow opaque cap and yellow opaque body, containing white colored granular powder.",1,1,Product Description,"Neuropathic Pain: Pregabalin is indicated for the treatment of neuropathic pain in adults, including neuropathic pain associated with spinal cord injury. Epilepsy: Pregabalin is indicated as adjunctive therapy in adults with partial seizures, with or without secondary generalization. Generalized Anxiety Disorder: Pregabalin is indicated for the treatment of Generalized Anxiety Disorder (GAD) in adults. Fibromyalgia: Pregabalin is indicated for the management of fibromyalgia.",1,1,Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:41:17.227674+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13662,Enalapril maleate,Enaprimed-5,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fp641JcPvl9KAiIIkdY0zP8tFvSDOJFm/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13662_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1fp641JcPvl9KAiIIkdY0zP8tFvSDOJFm_view_usp_drivesdk_1233ddcffc.pdf,page_text/DRP-13662_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1fp641JcPvl9KAiIIkdY0zP8tFvSDOJFm_view_usp_drivesdk_1233ddcffc.json,8e0b92e9f50967c4782dbe1cfce742fdc772e243fea7332ae68235fdf11ede0d,939024,4,digital_text,White coloured round and flat uncoated tablets with break-line on one side and plain on other side.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,• Treatment of Hypertension • Treatment of Symptomatic Heart Failure • Prevention of Symptomatic Heart Failure in patients with Asymptomatic Left Ventricular Dysfunction (ejection fraction ≤35%) Enalapril can be used alone or in combination with other antihypertensive agents,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:41:20.942961+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13668,Lidocaine + Prilocaine,Anesta,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yhTWoiqbDbx8fZWzBsXGaSc4zKSd4mTB/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13668_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1yhTWoiqbDbx8fZWzBsXGaSc4zKSd4mTB_view_usp_drivesdk_7f2c02da05.pdf,page_text/DRP-13668_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1yhTWoiqbDbx8fZWzBsXGaSc4zKSd4mTB_view_usp_drivesdk_7f2c02da05.json,756fafded37fe189eebf1bd13b2dd0d1b2593317ac450448f4aec45d00cc6b8d,724222,1,digital_text,"White to off white, smooth, homogenous cream. Pharmacokinetics: Systemic absorption of lidocaine and prilocaine from Lidocaine + Prilocaine (Anesta) is dependent upon the dose, application time, and the thickness of the skin, which varies between different areas of the body. Intact skin: In order to provide reliable dermal analgesia, Lidocaine + Prilocaine (Anesta) should be applied under an occlusive dressing for at least 1 hour. The duration of analgesia after an application time of 1-2 hours is at least 2 hours after removal of the dressing. After the application of Lidocaine + Prilocaine (Anesta) to intact male genital skin for 15 minutes (median 1g), plasma concentrations of lidocaine and prilocaine (mean 6.6 nanogram/mL and 4.1 nanogram/mL) were reached after approximately 1.5 hours. After application to the thigh in adults (60 g cream/400 cm2 for 3 hours) the extent of absorption was approximately 5% of lidocaine and prilocaine. Maximum plasma concentrations (mean 0.12 and 0.07 µg/mL) were reached approximately 2-6 hours after the application. 2 The extent of systemic absorption was approximately 10% following application to the face (10 g/100 cm for 2 hours). Maximum plasma levels (mean 0.16 and 0.06 µg/mL) were reached after approximately 1.5-3 hours. Genital mucosa: Absorption from the genital mucosa is more rapid than after application to the skin. After the application of 10 g Lidocaine + Prilocaine (Anesta) for 10 minutes to vaginal mucosa maximum plasma concentrations of lidocaine and prilocaine (mean 0.18 micrograms/mL and 0.15 micrograms/mL respectively) were reached after 20-45 minutes. Pharmacodynamics: Lidocaine + Prilocaine (Anesta), applied to intact skin under occlusive dressing, provides dermal analgesia by the release of lidocaine and prilocaine from the cream into the epidermal and dermal layers of the skin and by the accumulation of lidocaine and prilocaine in the vicinity of dermal pain receptors and nerve endings. Lidocaine and prilocaine are amide-type local anesthetic agents. Both lidocaine and prilocaine stabilize neuronal membranes by inhibiting the ionic fluxes required for the initiation and conduction of impulses, thereby effecting local anesthetic action.",1,1,Product Description:,Lidocaine + Prilocaine (Anesta) is indicated as a topical anaesthetic for use on: - normal intact skin for local analgesia. - genital mucous membranes for superficial minor surgery and as pretreatment for infiltration anaesthesia.,1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:41:24.062596+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13669,Oxytocin,Syntomax,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RlZleJErM23pIUZD1NOaDYnfWUn0M5Z4/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13669_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RlZleJErM23pIUZD1NOaDYnfWUn0M5Z4_view_usp_drivesdk_351cfcde77.pdf,page_text/DRP-13669_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RlZleJErM23pIUZD1NOaDYnfWUn0M5Z4_view_usp_drivesdk_351cfcde77.json,ba7fce471daa613cacfa79c1c2d255c4be6b73ed8fbdd61b3670f5c2fbd7527f,2101469,2,digital_text,"Oxytocin In jection is a clear, colorless solution filled in 1 mL clear glass ampou le with a black ring around the neck black pr inted text. PHARMACO DYNAMICS AND PHARMACOKINETICS",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Oxytocin is ind icated for the ind uction of labour for med ical reasons, e.g. in cases of post-term gestation, pr emature ru pture of the membranes, pregnancy-induced hypertension (pre-eclampsia). Stimulation of labour in hypoto nic uterine inertia. Early s tages of pregn ancy as adjun ctive therapy for the manag ement of incomp lete, inev itable, or missed abor tion. During caesarean s ection following d elivery of the child. Prevention and tr eatment of postpartum uterine atony and h aemorrhage. DO",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T16:41:27.958956+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13670,Paracetamol,Probiogal,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lCBzXC3shuFQ6TiltcLrFtiZLK5x8wwD/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13670_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1lCBzXC3shuFQ6TiltcLrFtiZLK5x8wwD_view_usp_drivesdk_fa0d1ce2a8.pdf,page_text/DRP-13670_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1lCBzXC3shuFQ6TiltcLrFtiZLK5x8wwD_view_usp_drivesdk_fa0d1ce2a8.json,865215e0cbc1b57b914107b6ab9b5ed9e258e6003a28ee289ba759a732054a67,465953,1,digital_text,It is a clear and colorless solution.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Paracetamol is indicated for the short-term treatment of moderate pain, especially following surgery, and for the short- term treatment of fever, when administration by intravenous route is clinically justiﬁed by an urgent need to treat pain or hyperthermia and/or when other routes of administration are not possible.",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T17:17:39.221875+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13685,Ceftriaxone (as sodium),Medtaxone,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/14Mq66ink87De_makrO9uBYxH16mzNmqd/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13685_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14Mq66ink87De_makrO9uBYxH16mzNmqd_view_usp_drivesdk_57e0c765b5.pdf,page_text/DRP-13685_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14Mq66ink87De_makrO9uBYxH16mzNmqd_view_usp_drivesdk_57e0c765b5.json,ec1925e75ff0f52e257b53e5e1c45592fdd29a46369936d026334b2453b56ed0,809572,7,digital_text,Powder: White to yellowish-orange crystalline powder Sterile Water: Clear and colorless liquid,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated in the treatment of the following infections in adults and children including term neonates (from birth): Bacterial Meningitis Community acquired pneumonia Hospital acquired pneumonia CEFTRIAXONE MEDTAXONE 1 g Powder for Injection (IM/IV) ANTIBACTERIAL (CEPHALOSPORIN) [Page 2] Acute otitis media Intra-abdominal infections Complicated urinary tract infections (including pyelonephritis) Infections of bones and joints Complicated skin and soft tissue infections Gonorrhoea Syphilis Bacterial endocarditis Ceftriaxone may be used: For treatment of acute exacerbations of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease in adults For treatment of disseminated Lyme borreliosis (early (stage II) and late (stage III)) in adults and children including neonates from 15 days of age. For Pre-operative prophylaxis of surgical site infections In the management of neutropenic patients with fever that is suspected to be due to a bacterial infection In the treatment of patients with bacteraemia that occurs in association with, or is suspected to be associated wi th, any of the infections listed above Ceftriaxone should be co -administered with other antibacterial agents whenever the possible range of causative bacteria would not fall within its spectrum. Consideration should be given to official guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents.",1,2,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T17:17:46.467130+00:00
