PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13702,Finasteride,Fenchride,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oxdT7T9OdqieaECIeM_Lfv15p5c5DTyr/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13702_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oxdT7T9OdqieaECIeM_Lfv15p5c5DTyr_view_usp_drivesdk_e4f7e69ad4.pdf,page_text/DRP-13702_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oxdT7T9OdqieaECIeM_Lfv15p5c5DTyr_view_usp_drivesdk_e4f7e69ad4.json,0610f9951640ebe63addc15db7cc05f5d1a6797ff43958bb34593dc67692a666,526251,1,digital_text,"Blue coloured, round, biconvex, both sides plain, lm-coated tablet.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Finasteride is indicated for the treatment and control of benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH) and for the prevention of urologic events to: Reduce the risk of acute urinary retention; Reduce the risk of surgery including transurethral resection of the prostate (TURP) and prostatectomy. Finasteride causes regression of the enlarged prostate, improves urinary ow and improves the symptoms associated with BPH. Patients with an enlarged prostate are the appropriate candidates for therapy with Finasteride.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-29T18:01:17.034862+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13703,Metformin hydrochloride + Glibenclamide,Glixfort,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yMKWnAeTYgX8ads-h9nkv9LgR5A_u86_/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13703_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1yMKWnAeTYgX8ads-h9nkv9LgR5A_u86__view_usp_drivesdk_e35ac2be3c.pdf,page_text/DRP-13703_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1yMKWnAeTYgX8ads-h9nkv9LgR5A_u86__view_usp_drivesdk_e35ac2be3c.json,0596a8b47abdfcf3eb09c41811040a99b9856bc74b765f3630ea83e0aeacfd80,476935,1,digital_text,"White to off white, smooth, capsule shaped, biconvex, uncoated tablet having break line on one side and plain on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Treatment of type 2 diabetes in adults; as second-line therapy, when diet, exercise and initial treatment with metformin or glibenclamide (or another sulfonylurea) do not result in adequate glycemic control; as replacement for previous treatment with metformin and glibenclamide in patients whose glycemia is stable and well-controlled.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:26:37.449156+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13708,,,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1YcG7ntO8cGb9NicPL7Vsqv_CSViW6FlL/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13708_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YcG7ntO8cGb9NicPL7Vsqv_CSViW6FlL_view_usp_drivesdk_a1189f4042.pdf,page_text/DRP-13708_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YcG7ntO8cGb9NicPL7Vsqv_CSViW6FlL_view_usp_drivesdk_a1189f4042.json,b1385db120a51d921b8296f6c0a12279f4b4aa0be11934c48926f9aeeff808fc,468171,1,digital_text,,1,1,prescription.,"The usual dose is 100 mg twice daily, at least 30 minutes before meal or 2 hours after meal; doses should be reduced in patients taking enzyme inhibitors . Response to treatment ma y occur in 2 to 4 weeks, but up to 12 weeks may be required. Or as prescribed by the physician.",1,1,USES AND ADMINISTRATION:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:26:42.933760+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13708-01,,,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bfOBvYfxGfeqP3pF9w0DxH-tv_fChed4/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13708-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bfOBvYfxGfeqP3pF9w0DxH-tv_fChed4_view_usp_drivesdk_95423e77e2.pdf,page_text/DRP-13708-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bfOBvYfxGfeqP3pF9w0DxH-tv_fChed4_view_usp_drivesdk_95423e77e2.json,dde1a2d8ab04f6d29f9fab8fa37ffdee6a5c07ffe63cf9a2d108266c2fe162fb,182954,1,digital_text,,,,,"It is used in the management of peripheral vascular disease; often used for atherosclerotic or occlusive arterial disease but in its widest sense covers both arterial and venous disorders and may be due to atherosclerosis, vasospasm, or thromboembolism.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:26:40.175221+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1371,Co-Amoxiclav,Bioclavid,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rqFVo2Jg2AtGnkP-GqNURkBE7b4dZGCT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1371_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rqFVo2Jg2AtGnkP-GqNURkBE7b4dZGCT_view_usp_drivesdk_d0fcdc1d23.pdf,page_text/DRP-1371_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rqFVo2Jg2AtGnkP-GqNURkBE7b4dZGCT_view_usp_drivesdk_d0fcdc1d23.json,a9afb37cb1bd3cfcd5bac63c4eece7b61d75f8061a05b22affa9e68cdfa9e51c,307759,16,digital_text,"Co-amoxiclav (Bioclavid®) 250 mg/125 mg film-coated tablet: Film-coated tablet. Off-white, oblong, biconvex and scored on both sides. Co-amoxiclav (Bioclavid®) 500 mg/125 mg film-coated tablet: Film-coated tablet. Off-white, oval, biconvex and scored on both sides. CLINICAL PARTICULARS Therapeutic indications For the treatment of common bacterial infections where oral therapy is indicated, including: - upper respiratory tract infections (including ENT): sinusitis, tonsillitis, otitis media - skin and soft tissue infections: boils/abscesses, cellulitis, wound infections, intra-abdominal sepsis - lower respiratory tract infections: acute and chronic bronchitis, pneumonia, lung abscess - genitourinary tract infections: cystitis, urethritis, pyelonephritis, septic abortion, pelvic infection, gonorrhea - other infections: osteomyelitis, septicemia, peritonitis, post-operative infections Dosage and method of administration Dosage Doses are expressed throughout in terms of amoxicillin/clavulanic acid content except when doses are stated in terms of an individual component. The dose of amoxicillin/clavulanic acid that is selected to treat an individual infection should take into account: Co-Amoxiclav [Page 2] Co-Amoxiclav 250 mg/ 125 mg, 500 mg/ 125 mg Film-coated Tablets Bioclavid® • The expected pathogens and their likely susceptibility to antibacterial agents (see Special warnings and precautions for use) • The severity and the site of the infection • The age, weight and renal function of the patient as shown below. The use of alternative presentations of amoxicillin/clavulanic acid (e.g. those that provide higher doses of amoxicillin and/or different ratios of amoxicillin to clavulanic acid) should be considered as necessary (see Special warnings and precautions for use and Pharmacodynamic properties). For adults and children ≥ 40 kg, this formulation of amoxicillin/clavulanic acid provides a total daily dose of 1750 mg amoxicillin/ 250 mg clavulanic acid with twice daily dosing and 2625 mg amoxicillin/375 mg clavulanic acid with three times daily dosing, when administered as recommended below. For adults and children ≥ 40 kg, this formulation of co-amoxiclav provides a total daily dose of 1500 mg amoxicillin/375 mg clavulanic acid, when administered as recommended below. For children < 40 kg, this formulation of co-amoxiclav provides a maximum daily dose of 2400 mg amoxicillin/600 mg clavulanic acid, when administered as recommended below. If it is considered that a higher daily dose of amoxicillin is required, it is recommended that another preparation of co-amoxiclav is selected in order to avoid administration of unnecessary high daily doses of clavulanic acid (see special warnings and precautions for use regarding prolonged therapy). Adults and children ≥ 40 kg One 500 mg/125 mg dose taken three times a day. Children < 40 kg 20 mg/5 mg/kg/day to 60 mg/15 mg/kg/day given in three divided doses. Children may be treated with co-amoxiclav tablets, suspensions or pediatric sachets. Children aged 6 years and below should preferably be treated with co-amoxiclav suspension or pediatric sachets. No clinical data are available on doses of co-amoxiclav 4:1 formulations higher than 40 mg/10 mg/kg per day in children under 2 years. Elderly No dose adjustment is considered necessary. Renal impairment No dose adjustment is required in patients with creatinine clearance (CrCl) greater than 30 mL/min. In patients with creatinine clearance less than 30 mL/min, the use of amoxicillin/clavulanic acid presentations with an amoxicillin to clavulanic acid ratio of 7:1 is not recommended, as no recommendations for dose adjustments are available. Hepatic impairment [Page 3] Co-Amoxiclav 250 mg/ 125 mg, 500 mg/ 125 mg Film-coated Tablets Bioclavid® Dose with caution and monitor hepatic function at regular intervals (see Contraindications and Special warnings and precautions for use). Method of administration Co-amoxiclav is for oral use. Administer at the start of a meal to minimise potential gastrointestinal intolerance and optimise absorption of amoxicillin/clavulanic acid.",1,3,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"For the treatment of common bacterial infections where oral therapy is indicated, including: - upper respiratory tract infections (including ENT): sinusitis, tonsillitis, otitis media - skin and soft tissue infections: boils/abscesses, cellulitis, wound infections, intra-abdominal sepsis - lower respiratory tract infections: acute and chronic bronchitis, pneumonia, lung abscess - genitourinary tract infections: cystitis, urethritis, pyelonephritis, septic abortion, pelvic infection, gonorrhea - other infections: osteomyelitis, septicemia, peritonitis, post-operative infections",1,1,Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:26:46.254344+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13712,"""Moxifloxacin (as hydrochloride) + Dexamethasone
phosphate (as sodium)""",Modexeye,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CEVJ3pf_78R9y0A-aIJJqxJexqvqtBku/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13712_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1CEVJ3pf_78R9y0A-aIJJqxJexqvqtBku_view_usp_drivesdk_1c2d7c8fa6.pdf,page_text/DRP-13712_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1CEVJ3pf_78R9y0A-aIJJqxJexqvqtBku_view_usp_drivesdk_1c2d7c8fa6.json,fbbf35fe1bfc9da3b44645f4aa65b13c8254b5e586c708ef8539f9f907b237f1,3403794,1,ocr,"can be absorb and can cause of foetal +D in pregnant animals. Although the relevance of these findings to human has not been ‘as (as sodium) Opthalmic solution is a colourless to pale yellow liquid. established, the use of this product during pregnancy should be avoided. Breastfeeding:| Itis unknown whether moxifloxacin/metabolites are excreted in human milk. Animal studies have shown excretion of low levels in breast milk after",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"Solution and are classified according to the subsequent convention: very common (21/10), common (21/100 to <1/10), uncommon (21/1,000 to <1/100 caused b’ strains, and For the topical treatment of purulent bacterial inditions of the anterior segment of the eye and rare (21/10,000 to <1/1,000) and very rare (<1/10,000). Within each frequency-grouping, adverse reactions are presented in order of decreasing seriousness. (See Table 1.) acute phase of severe allergic conjunctivitis not responding to standard therapy. Consideration should be given to official guidance on the appropriate use of bacterial agents. Table 1",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T12:27:00.864638+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13729,Cetirizine dihydrochloride,Allerkid,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MaWnp7fAJM8doGr_qqdW1UPSfSBANjJ7/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13729_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MaWnp7fAJM8doGr_qqdW1UPSfSBANjJ7_view_usp_drivesdk_33f68ec992.pdf,page_text/DRP-13729_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MaWnp7fAJM8doGr_qqdW1UPSfSBANjJ7_view_usp_drivesdk_33f68ec992.json,707e2a55e9eec9de5108e49d62037b789847891d439cf68565f28574459ed06b,1118134,1,digital_text,"Cetirizine dihydrochloride (Allerkid®) 2.5 mg/mL syrup (oral drops): colorless to slightly yellow-colored, clear syrup with fruity grape odor, and sweet grape taste using the TasteRite®Tech- nology. Cetirizine dihydrochloride (Allerkid®) 5 mg/5 mL syrup: colorless to slightly yellow-colored, clear syrup with fruity grape odor, and sweet grape taste using the TasteRite®Technology. TasteRite® technology is a unique tastemasking system developed specifically for liquid dosage forms. This technology significantly reduces the bitterness of medicine so that children taste the flavor and not the medicine. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This medicine contains cetirizine, an anti-allergy, which blocks the action of histamine, a substance that causes allergic symptoms. Cetirizine is less likely to cause drowsiness and dizziness than the older class of anti-allergy medicines. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTIONS,"Gastrointestinal disorders: Changed taste, constipation, diarrhea, dry mouth, dyspepsia (indigestion, feeling of fullness), enlarged abdomen, eructation (burping), flatulence (gassiness), gastritis (inflammation of the stomach), increased salivation, melena (black stools), stomatitis/ulcerative stomatitis (mouth sores), swelling of the tongue, taste loss, tongue discoloration, tooth caries Hepatobiliary disorders: Abnormal liver function (elevated liver enzymes and bilirubin), cholestasis (inflammation of the gall bladder), hepatitis Skin and subcutaneous tissue disorders: Acne, alopecia (baldness), bullous eruption (large blisters), dermatitis (skin inflammation), dry skin, eczema, fixed drug eruption, furunculosis (boils), hyperkeratosis (thickened skin), hypertrichosis (excessive hair growth), photosensitivity, pruritus (itchiness), purpura (small purple-red skin marks), rash, seborrhea (oily skin), skin disorder, skin nodule Musculoskeletal and connective tissue disorders: Back pain, hypertonia (muscle stiffness), rigors (shaking), twitching Renal and urinary disorders: Cystitis (inflammation of the urinary bladder), difficulty in urinating, dysuria (painful urination), hematuria (blood in the urine), polyuria (excessive urination), urinary incontinence, urinary retention, urinary tract infection, urination frequency Reproductive system and breast disorders: Breast pain in women, decreased libido, dysmenorrhea, intermenstrual bleeding, leukorrhea (whitish vaginal discharge), menorrhagia (heavy menstrual bleeding), vaginitis (inflammation of the vagina) General disorders and administration site conditions: Asthenia (weakness), ataxia (incoordination), fever, malaise (feeling of bodily discomfort), pain Investigations: Increased weight Injury, poisoning and procedural complications: Accidental injury, ototoxicity (ear poisoning) WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Do not use this product together with alcohol, medicines for anxiety or sleep disorder (e.g., Alprazolam, Diazepam, Chlordiazepoxide, Temazepam, Triazolam, etc.), medicines for depression (e.g., Amitriptyline, Doxepin, Nortriptyline, Fluoxetine, Sertraline, Paroxetine, etc.), other cold or allergy medicines, or any other medicines that cause drowsiness, sleepiness and relaxation because of the possibility for increased toxicity. The extent of absorption of cetirizine is not reduced with food, although the rate of absorption is decreased by 1 hour. Tell your doctor if you are taking other medicines, including vitamins, supplements, and herbal medicines. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, just take the next dose if still needed for the condition being treated and the subsequent doses at the recommended time or schedule. Do not double the dose. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? • Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C • Keep the product out of sight and reach of children SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE Adverse events reported after intake of at least 5 times the recommended daily dose are: confusion, diarrhea, dizziness, excessive tiredness, headache, feeling of bodily discomfort, mydriasis (pupil dilatation), itchiness, restlessness, sedation, somnolence (drowsiness/sleepiness), stupor (decreased mental alertness), tachycardia (rapid heart rate), tremor, and urinary retention. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE • May cause drowsiness. Exercise caution when engaging in activities requiring mental alertness. • Avoid excessive alcohol consumption when taking this medicine. • Do not take more than the recommended dose. • Do not use after the expiry date on the label. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? • Ask a doctor before use if: o You have kidney or liver disease o You are epileptic or at risk of convulsions o You have difficulty passing urine o You are pregnant or breastfeeding o Are due for an allergy testing • Stop use and ask a doctor if: o Symptoms worsen or do not improve o New symptoms occur o Any undesirable effect occurs ADVERSE DRUG REACTION REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adverse drug reaction, seek medical attention immediately and report to the FDA at www.fda.gov.ph AND Unilab at +632-8-UNILAB-1 (+632-8-864522-1) for Metro Manila or toll-free +1-800-10-UNILAB-1 for provinces, or e-mail productsafety@unilab.com.ph. By reporting undesirable effects, you can help provide more information on the safety of this medicine. AVAILABILITY Cetirizine dihydrochloride (Allerkid®) 2.5 mg/mL syrup (oral drops): Amber Glass Bottle x 10 mL with Dropper (Box of 1’s) Cetirizine dihydrochloride (Allerkid®) 5 mg/5 mL syrup: Amber Glass Bottle x 30 mL and 60 mL (Box of 1's) DATE OF FIRST AUTHORIZATION FOR ALLERKID® 2.5 MG/ML SYRUP (ORAL DROPS), DRP-13730: April 2010",1,1,infection,low,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T12:27:04.424004+00:00
