PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13751,Ibandronic Acid (as sodium monohydrate),Ibandoprim,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/12akA7JFuyKyDYSVye_rnsRrhhJE1l72a/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13751_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_12akA7JFuyKyDYSVye_rnsRrhhJE1l72a_view_usp_drivesdk_3b9f983cdb.pdf,page_text/DRP-13751_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_12akA7JFuyKyDYSVye_rnsRrhhJE1l72a_view_usp_drivesdk_3b9f983cdb.json,d5abadc1ff955d07a2b6c1966a594a16a101b385dfdb5ded9388787b52302ba6,460155,1,digital_text,"White coloured, capsule shaped, biconvex film-coated tablet having plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Ibandronic acid is indicated for the treatment of postmenopausal osteoporosis, to reduce the risk of fractures. Treatment of Osteoporosis: Osteoporosis may be confirmed by the finding of low bone mass (T score <-2.0 SD) and the presence or history of osteoporotic fracture, or a low bone mass (T-score <-2.5 SD) in the absence of documented pre-existing osteoporotic fracture.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:27:11.608370+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13752,Clarithromycin,Clartrixel,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/19iJwr0w-kyXmkDUbmoZXXNbgVNqU3ZF9/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13752_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19iJwr0w-kyXmkDUbmoZXXNbgVNqU3ZF9_view_usp_drivesdk_b263b0a687.pdf,page_text/DRP-13752_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19iJwr0w-kyXmkDUbmoZXXNbgVNqU3ZF9_view_usp_drivesdk_b263b0a687.json,021dc29531bc0fcb88dc2b069c7ea504e5d63d1a804cd0155525206344bcfb68,644761,2,digital_text,"Yellow coloured, oblong, biconvex film coated tablet, plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Clarithromycin is indicated for treatment of infections due to susceptible organisms in adults and children 12 years and older. Such infections include: Lower respiratory tract infections (e.g., bronchitis, pneumonia). Upper respiratory tract infections (e.g., pharyngitis, sinusitis). Skin and soft tissue infections (e.g., folliculitis, cellulitis, erysipelas) Disseminated or localized mycobacterial infections due to Mycobacterium avium or Mycobacterium intracellulare. Localized infections due t o M y c o b a c t e r i u m c h e l o n a e , M y c o b a c t e r i u m f o r t u i t u m , o r M y c o b a c t e r i u m k a n s a s i i . Clarithromycin is indicated for the prevention of disseminated Mycobacterium avium complex infection in HIV-infected patients with CD4 lymphocyte counts less than or equal to 100/mm3. Clarithromycin in the presence of acid suppression is also indicated for the eradication of H. pylori resulting in decreased recurrence of duodenal ulcer Treatment of odontogenic infections. Consideration should be given to national official guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents.",1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:27:15.234168+00:00
