PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13761,Sitagliptin (as phosphate monohydrate),Sitadin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GH9AM84L-t7D9QK89HIYY37atI8Go3fv/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13761_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GH9AM84L-t7D9QK89HIYY37atI8Go3fv_view_usp_drivesdk_a72156a3f1.pdf,page_text/DRP-13761_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GH9AM84L-t7D9QK89HIYY37atI8Go3fv_view_usp_drivesdk_a72156a3f1.json,b0b47a82bf79d660123a6ee8515146c0f711324de5ddac58db8bfd775bd3a7f3,6092964,1,ocr,"may be considered to reduce the risk of sulfonylurea — or insulin — induced hypoglycemia. Light peach to peach, 7 mm, round biconvex, film-coated tablet. Hypersensitivity reactions: These reactions include anaphylaxis, angioedema, and exfoliative skin conditions including Stevens-Johnson",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Sitagliptin is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus. It can also be “For suspected adverse drug reactions, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. used in combination with metformin, sulfonylurea, PPARy agonist, metformin and sulfonylurea, metformin and a PPARy agonist, and Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction.” insulin, to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T12:27:34.130228+00:00
