PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13800,Co-Amoxiclav,Moxinova CV,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lLmNtD2xN9J54j9sWMPMjE7Px5B1K8cR/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13800_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1lLmNtD2xN9J54j9sWMPMjE7Px5B1K8cR_view_usp_drivesdk_4779aa714b.pdf,page_text/DRP-13800_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1lLmNtD2xN9J54j9sWMPMjE7Px5B1K8cR_view_usp_drivesdk_4779aa714b.json,b74bc5adde76adbd0abffe80af140506482745127ea81458bd50f8e72176161c,1016886,3,digital_text,Creamy white crystalline powder,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for the treatment of the following infections in adults and children: • Acute bacterial sinusitis (adequately diagnosed) • Acute otitis media • Acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis (adequately diagnosed) • Community acquired pneumonia • Cystitis • Pyelonephritis • Skin and soft tissue infections in particular cellulitis, animal bites, severe dental abscess with spreading cellulitis. • Bone and joint infections, in particular osteomyelitis. Consideration should be given to official guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:28:43.701709+00:00
