ntact your doctor or the nearest hospital Accident and Emergency Always use this medicine exactly as your doctor or pharmacist has told you. Department immediately. Check with your doctor or pharmacist if you are not sure. How should you keep this medicine? For use on the skin only. Do not mix Mupirocin Ointment with other creams or ointments on the infected Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. area of your skin, as this may reduce the effectiveness of Mupirocin Ointment. Keep all medicines out of reach of children. If you are using Mupirocin Ointment on your face, you should be careful not to When should you consult your doctor? getitin your eyes orin your nose. If you stop using Mupirocin (Mupiriv) If you accidentally get Mupirocin Ointment in your eyes, wash them thoroughly with water and contact your doctor or nearest hospital Accident and If you stop using Mupirocin Ointment too early, not all of the bacteria, causing Emergency Department immediately. your skin infection, may have been killed, and your infection may come back. Ask your doctor, pharmacist or nurse when to stop using the ointment. Wash and dry your hands before and after using Mupirocin Ointment. For adults, the elderly, and children. If you have any further questions on the use of this medicine, ask your doctor, Mupirocin Ointment should be applied to the affected area two to three times a pharmacist, or nurse. day for up to ten days, depending on the response. ADR Reporting Statement: - You can cover the infected area with a plaster (s) or suitable dressing (s) For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. unless your doctor has told you to leave it uncovered. - Replace the cap on the tube and wash your hands. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug - Use Mupirocin Ointment for as long as your doctor has told you. The bacteria reaction. are normally cleared from your skin within 10 days of starting treatment. Do not Availability: use for more than 10 days. If your symptoms persist, talk to your doctor or pharmacist. Laminated Tube x 5 g (Box of 1's) - Throw away any ointment that is left over. DRP-13828 Date of First Authorization: April 27, 2023 When should you not take this medicine? Do not take Mupirocin (Mupiriv) Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: August 01, 2023 - If you are allergic to Mupirocin or any of the other ingredients of this medicine. - To treat infections in your nose. Manufactured by: EAST AFRICAN (INDIA) OVERSEAS - To treat infections in your eyes. - Around intravenous cannula (“drip”) sites. Symptoms of an allergic reaction Plot No. 1, Pharmacity, Selaqui, Dehradun- may include a red and lumpy skin rash, difficulty breathing, swelling of the face, 248011 (U.K.), India mouth lips, or eyelids, unexplained high temperature (fever), and feeling faint. Imported and Distributed by: If the swelling affects your throat and makes breathing and swallowing difficult, AMBICAINTERNATIONAL CORPORATION go to the hospital straight away. No. 9Amsterdam Extension, Merville Park Subdivision, Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: Parafaque City, Metro Manila Warnings and Precautions Talk to your doctor, pharmacist, or nurse before using Mupirocin Ointment - Ifyou have problems with your kidneys. - If you have open wounds or damaged skin. If you use Mupirocin Ointment for along period of time, you may develop thrush (a yeast infection). If this occurs, tell your doctor or pharmacist. Pregnancy and Breastfeeding - If you are pregnant or breast-feeding, think you may be pregnant, or are planning to have a baby, ask your doctor or pharmacist for advice before taking this medicine. - If your doctor has given you Mupirocin Ointment to treat a cracked nipple, the ointment must be thoroughly washed off prior to breastfeeding. Driving and Using Machines It is unlikely that Mupirocin Ointment will affect your ability to drive or operate machinery. Undesirable effects of this medicine: This medicine can cause side effects like all medicines, although not everybody gets them. Very rare (may affect up to 1 in 10,000 people) If you have any of the following very rare side effects while using your medicine, rinse the product off of your skin and tell your doctor immediately or go to ahospital straight away: [Page 2]",1,1,Product Description:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:29:20.972139+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13828-01,Mupirocin,Bactestop,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1U8nzAi1y46yHRitURkNroFDyVdS7_V4O/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13828-01_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1U8nzAi1y46yHRitURkNroFDyVdS7_V4O_view_usp_drivesdk_0f12515392.pdf,page_text/DRP-13828-01_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1U8nzAi1y46yHRitURkNroFDyVdS7_V4O_view_usp_drivesdk_0f12515392.json,0ee6bc4862c041a0b9939dcc6eeae696fe0ce8635a6e08155492fe2387bcafba,1089936,1,digital_text,"Clear colorless, soft mass. WHAT IS THE NAME OF PRODUCT? Mupirocin 2% w/w Ointment (Bactestop) Mupirocin is an antibiotic. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Each tube of Mupirocin Ointment contains 5g of ointment. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Mupirocin is an antibiotic. It is used to kill bacteria in skin infections such as impetigo (which may appear as a small scratch or itchy patch of eczema), folliculitis (swelling of the skin around the hair roots) and boils. Mupirocin ointment is for external use on your skin only. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Always use this medicine exactly as your doctor or pharmacist has told you. Check with your doctor or pharmacist if you are not sure. For use on the skin only • Do not mix Mupirocin Ointment with other creams or ointments on the infected area of your skin, as this may reduce the effectiveness of Mupirocin Ointment. Mupirocin 2% w/w Ointment is an antibiotic. • If you are using Mupirocin Ointment on your face, you should be careful not to get it in your eyes or in your nose. • If you accidentally get Mupirocin Ointment in your eyes, wash them thoroughly with water and contact your doctor or nearest hospital Accident and Emergency Department immediately. Wash and dry your hands before, and after, you use Mupirocin Ointment. Adults, the elderly and children • Mupirocin Ointment should be applied to the affected area Two to three times a day for up to ten days, depending on the response. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Do not take Mupirocin (Bactestop) Talk to your doctor, pharmacist or nurse before using Mupirocin Ointment. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine It is unlikely that Mupirocin Ointment will affect your ability to drive or operate machinery. • If you are allergic to Mupirocin or any of the other ingredients of this medicine. • Replace the cap on the tube and wash your hands. • Throw away any ointment that is left over. • If you have problems with your kidneys. DRIVING AND USING MACHINES • Use Mupirocin Ointment for as long as your doctor has told you. The bacteria are normally cleared from your skin within 10 days of starting treatment. Do not use for more than 10 days. If your symptoms persist, talk to your doctor or pharmacist. • You can cover the infected area with a plaster (s) or suitable dressing (s), unless your doctor has told you to leave it uncovered. • Around intravenous cannula (“drip”) sites. Symptoms of an allergic reaction may include a red and lumpy skin rash, difficulty breathing, swelling of face, mouth lips or eyelids, unexplained high temperature (fever) and feeling faint. If the swelling affects your throat and makes breathing and swallowing difficult, go to hospital straight away. • If your doctor has given you Mupirocin Ointment to treat a cracked nipple, the ointment must be thoroughly washed off prior to breastfeeding. • To treat infections in your nose. WARNINGS AND PRECAUTIONS • To treat infections in your eyes. • If you have open wounds or damaged skin. If you use Mupirocin Ointment for a long period of time, you may develop thrush (a yeast infection). If this occurs, tell your doctor or pharmacist. PREGNANCY AND BREASTFEEDING • If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, think you may be pregnant or are planning to have a baby, ask your doctor or pharmacist for advice before taking this medicine. For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:29:10.145765+00:00
