PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13897,Etoricoxib,Starcox,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lRqfF-r4wuSgOiGuVPyVNOpDP3zjpmDY/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13897_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1lRqfF-r4wuSgOiGuVPyVNOpDP3zjpmDY_view_usp_drivesdk_9512c38b39.pdf,page_text/DRP-13897_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1lRqfF-r4wuSgOiGuVPyVNOpDP3zjpmDY_view_usp_drivesdk_9512c38b39.json,f2878e1a1f5872d426ddf397782e5840a497012d10c02d41d420c462abdc951b,312796,2,digital_text,"Etoricoxib (Starcox ®) 60mg film-coated tablet is a white colored round shaped tablet embossed “GP” on one side and plain on other side. Etoricoxib 90mg (Starcox ®) film-coated tablet is a reddish brown colored, round shaped, biconvex film coated tablet, “GETZ” debossed on one side and plain on other side. Etoricoxib 120mg (Starcox ®) film-coated tablet is a reddish brown colored, round shaped, biconvex film coated tablet, “GP” debossed on one side and plain on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Etoricoxib (Starcox ®) is indicated for: - Symptomatic relief of osteoarthritis (OA) and rheumatoid arthritis (RA) - The management of ankylosing spondylitis (AS) - Relief of chronic low back pain (CLBP) - Treatment of acute gouty arthritis - Relief of acute pain - Relief of chronic musculoskeletal pain - Treatment of primary dysmenorrhea - Treatment of moderate to severe acute post-operative pain associated with dental surgery - Treatment of moderate to severe acute post-operative pain associated with abdominal gynecological surgery The decision to prescribe a selective COX-2 inhibitor should be based on an assessment of the individual patient's overall risks.,1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:31:10.860644+00:00
