PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13939,Cefpodoxime (as proxetil),Cifambic,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1iBSaB3QckFCTTGD3IIsVE8rPxEHnnOmF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13939_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1iBSaB3QckFCTTGD3IIsVE8rPxEHnnOmF_view_usp_drivesdk_37cdaab660.pdf,page_text/DRP-13939_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1iBSaB3QckFCTTGD3IIsVE8rPxEHnnOmF_view_usp_drivesdk_37cdaab660.json,0dbbfab187a27478961f974332895bdbf52cfa6dcf379046e3b0d6d4dfaefe18,1433427,1,digital_text,"Brown colored, capsule shaped, standard biconvex with break line on one side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Adults: Upper Respiratory Tract Infection Sinusitis: 200mg twice daily (morning and evening). Pharyngitis, tonsillitis: 100mg twice daily (morning and evening). Other upper respiratory tract infections: 100mg twice daily. Tablets should be taken during meals. Lower Respiratory Tract Infections For lower respiratory tract infections caused by organisms sensitive to cefpodoxime, including acute bronchitis, relapses or exacerbations of chronic bronchitis and bacterial pneumonia; 100-200 mg twice daily, dependent on the severity of the infection. Uncomplicated Lower Urinary Tract Infections: 100mg to be taken twice daily. Uncomplicated Upper Urinary Tract Infections: 200mg to be taken twice daily. Uncomplicated Gonococcal Urethritis: 200mg to be taken as a single dose. Skin and Soft Tissue Infections: 200mg to be taken twice daily. Tablets should be taken during meals with some liquid, for optimum absorption (morning and evening). Elderly: In the elderly, provided renal function is normal, it is not necessary to modify the dosage. Children: Cefpodoxime Proxetil in pediatric is available to treat infants (over 15 days old) and children. Please refer to its separate prescribing information for details. Renal Impairment: The dosage of Cefpodoxime proxetil does not require modication if creatinine clearance exceeds 40 ml/min. Below this value, pharmacokinetic studies indicate an increase in plasma elimination half-life and maximum plasma concentrations, and hence the dosage should be adjusted appropriately. Creatinine Clearance (Ml/Min) 39-10 Unit dose administered as a single dose every 24 hours (i.e., half of the usual adult dose) <10 Unit dose administered as a single dose every 48 hours (i.e., quarter of the usual adult dose) Haemodialysis Patients Unit dose administered after each dialysis session. Hepatic Impairment: The dosage does not require modication in cases of hepatic impairment.",1,1,INDICATION(S) AND ROUTE OF ADMINISTRATION,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:32:51.700260+00:00
