PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13996,Propranolol hydrochloride,Saphanolol,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wxq5IUXoIRGohgMZ5I3ooOhXoCjQCxP-/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13996_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wxq5IUXoIRGohgMZ5I3ooOhXoCjQCxP-_view_usp_drivesdk_8c5014cf7c.pdf,page_text/DRP-13996_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wxq5IUXoIRGohgMZ5I3ooOhXoCjQCxP-_view_usp_drivesdk_8c5014cf7c.json,79516d7f34801fe02ba5eb4f69842a8271952745e90ae642cd5b8c7b38dfc6b3,1772806,4,digital_text_and_ocr,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T12:37:11.883089+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13998,Gemcitabine (As Hydrochloride),Gem Pan 1000,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bPTGM3YH8JNwRWbmnUAyQcx5J6ePfgpS/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13998_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bPTGM3YH8JNwRWbmnUAyQcx5J6ePfgpS_view_usp_drivesdk_9a027e55bb.pdf,page_text/DRP-13998_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bPTGM3YH8JNwRWbmnUAyQcx5J6ePfgpS_view_usp_drivesdk_9a027e55bb.json,586314204f4ea55e136f354bab95299368d9b9b2d34bd87f9c201e9188bae921,869762,7,digital_text,White to off-white lyophilized cake or powder,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for the treatment of locally advanced or metastatic bladder cancer in combination with cisplatin. Gemcitabine is indicated for treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic adenocarcinoma of the pancreas. Gemcitabine, in combination with cisplatin is indicated as first line treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC). Gemcitabine monotherapy can be considered in elderly patients or those with performance status 2. Gemcitabine is indicated for the treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic epithelial ovarian carcinoma, in combination with carboplatin, in patients with relapsed disease following a recurrence-free interval of at least 6 months after platinum-based, first-line therapy. Gemcitabine, in combination with paclitaxel, is indicated for the treatment of patients with unresectable, locally recurrent or metastatic breast cancer who have relapsed following adjuvant/neoadjuvant chemotherapy. Prior chemotherapy should have included an anthracycline unless clinically",2,2,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:37:15.475676+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-13999,Gemcitabine (As Hydrochloride),Gem Pan 200,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1t7GkKMhcxCs5-B3QAlvslXO97VLAKbiR/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-13999_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1t7GkKMhcxCs5-B3QAlvslXO97VLAKbiR_view_usp_drivesdk_8451e53e86.pdf,page_text/DRP-13999_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1t7GkKMhcxCs5-B3QAlvslXO97VLAKbiR_view_usp_drivesdk_8451e53e86.json,113d57eca01c707ea08bb8eb8d01bca1ac9d7f86798100429518cbd0f6bb776b,870980,7,digital_text,White to off-white lyophilized cake or powder,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for the treatment of locally advanced or metastatic bladder cancer in combination with cisplatin. Gemcitabine is indicated for treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic adenocarcinoma of the pancreas. Gemcitabine, in combination with cisplatin is indicated as first line treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC). Gemcitabine monotherapy can be considered in elderly patients or those with performance status 2. Gemcitabine is indicated for the treatment of patients with locally advanced or metastatic epithelial ovarian carcinoma, in combination with carboplatin, in patients with relapsed disease following a recurrence-free interval of at least 6 months after platinum-based, first-line therapy. Gemcitabine, in combination with paclitaxel, is indicated for the treatment of patients with unresectable, locally recurrent or metastatic breast cancer who have relapsed following adjuvant/neoadjuvant chemotherapy. Prior chemotherapy should have included an anthracycline unless clinically",2,2,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:37:19.335641+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14001,Meropenem (as trihydrate),Eonem 1000,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XufIpw5p2onuqJKxLQvHkK9CMPfIStUX/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14001_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1XufIpw5p2onuqJKxLQvHkK9CMPfIStUX_view_usp_drivesdk_0e9d0ce138.pdf,page_text/DRP-14001_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1XufIpw5p2onuqJKxLQvHkK9CMPfIStUX_view_usp_drivesdk_0e9d0ce138.json,cfb98315d566c6fa77b7160e15f4a021412c2b9bc43b0769b37e8c758628eea5,832042,2,digital_text,"Meropenem for injection is a sterile, pyrogen-free, synthetic, ultra-broadspectrum, Carbapenem antibiotic for intravenous administration. It is Chemically (4R,5S,6S)-3-[[(3S,5S)-5-Dimethylcarbamoyl)-3-pyrrolidinyl]thio]-6-[(1R)- 1-hydroxyethyl]-4-methyl-7-oxo-1-azabicyclo[3.2.0]hept-2-ene-2-carboxylic acid, trihydrate. Meropenem penetrates well into most body ﬂuids and tissues including cerebrospinal ﬂuid, achieving concentrations matching or exceeding those required to inhibit most susceptible bacteria.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"It is used in the treatment of susceptible infections, including intra-abdominal infections, meningitis, respiratory tract infections (including cystic ﬁbrosis patients), septicaemia, skin infections, urinary tract infections, and infections in immunocompromised patients.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:37:22.932856+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14002,Ifosfamide,Fosfalex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Sbj-s9CXPMC_VEPPZGMQS4kobYPYWccJ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14002_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Sbj-s9CXPMC_VEPPZGMQS4kobYPYWccJ_view_usp_drivesdk_a4fbd83218.pdf,page_text/DRP-14002_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Sbj-s9CXPMC_VEPPZGMQS4kobYPYWccJ_view_usp_drivesdk_a4fbd83218.json,b8f2fb20e15b7cb18a12f5b6615b1e891b645b5a1c60281328e9c2910716fa45,605535,2,digital_text,"Every vial of Ifosfamide (Fosfalex) contains 1 g of white to yellowish lyophilized powder. Ifosfamide (Fosfalex) is a chemotherapeutic agent chemically related to the nitrogen mustards and a synthetic analog of cyclophosphamide. Ifosfamide is 3-(2-chloroethyl)-2-[(2-chlo- roethyl)amino] tetrahydro-2H1,3,2-oxazaphosphorine 2-oxide. CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY Ifosfamide has been shown to require metabolic activation by microsomal liver enzymes to produce biologically active metabolites. Activation occurs by hydroxylation at the ring carbon atom “4” to form the unstable intermediate 4-hydroxyi- fosfamide. These urinary metabolites have not been found to be cytotoxic. N, N-bis (2-chloroethyl)-phosphoric acid diamide (ifosphoramide) and acrolein are also found. Enzymatic oxidation of the chloroethyl side chains and subsequent dealkylation produces the major urinary metabolites, dechloroethyl ifosfamide and dechloroethyl cyclophosphamide. The alkylated metabolites of ifosfamide have been shown to interact with DNA. In vitro incubation of DNA with activated ifosfamide has produced phosphotriesters. The treatment of intact cell nuclei may also result in the formation of DNA-DNA cross-links. DNA repair most likely occurs in G-1 and G-2 stage cells. Pharmacokinetics Ifosfamide exhibits dose-dependent pharmacokinetics in humans. At single doses of 3.8 to 5.0 g/m 2, the plasma concentrations decay bi-phasically and the mean terminal elimination half-life is about 15 hours. At doses of 1.6 to 2.4 g/m2/day, the plasma decay is monoexponential and the terminal elimination half-life is about 7 hours. Ifosfamide is extensively metabolized in humans and the metabolic pathways appear to be saturated at high doses. After administration of doses of 5 g/m 2 of 14C-labeled ifosfamide, from 70% to 86% of the dosed radioactivity was recovered in the urine, with about 61% of the dose excreted as parent compound. At doses of 1.6 to 2.4 g/m2 only 12% to 18% of the dose was excreted in the urine as unchanged drug within 72 hours. Two diﬀerent dechloroethylated derivatives of ifosfamide, 4-carboxyifosfamide, thiodiacetic acid and cysteine conjugates of chloroacetic acid have been identi/f_ied as the major urinary metabolites of ifosfamide in humans and only small amounts of 4-hydroxyifosfamide and acrolein are present. Small quantities (nmole/mL) of ifosfamide mustard and 4hydroxyifosfamide are detectable in human plasma. Metabolism of ifosfamide is required for the generation of the biologically active species and while metabolism is extensive, it is also quite variable among patients.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Ifosfamide, used in combination with certain other approved antineoplastic agents, is indicated for third line chemotherapy of germ cell testicular cancer. It should be used in combination with a prophylactic agent for hemorrhagic cystitis, such as mesna.",1,1,INDICATIONS AND USES,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:37:27.157152+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14010,Cefixime (as trihydrate),Feximwin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1T8NrYrVUmIwksAn5qlRBLzAdOEa6y9cO/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14010_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1T8NrYrVUmIwksAn5qlRBLzAdOEa6y9cO_view_usp_drivesdk_8081c0e07c.pdf,page_text/DRP-14010_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1T8NrYrVUmIwksAn5qlRBLzAdOEa6y9cO_view_usp_drivesdk_8081c0e07c.json,b46271e52fa943bd9fadb0dc7bfe682f422b6741513835e81558db67e7338ff6,1459516,1,digital_text,"White to off white coloured, capsule shape, standard biconvex and lm coated tablet with break line on one side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Cexime Tablet is an orally active cephalosporin antibiotic which has marked in vitro bactericidal activity against a wide variety of Gram-positive and Gram- negative organisms. It is indicated for the treatment of the following acute infections when caused by susceptible micro-organisms: Upper Respiratory Tract Infections (URTI): e.g., otitis media; and other URTI where the causative organism is known or suspected to be resistant to other commonly used antibiotics, or where treatment failure may carry signicant risk. Lower Respiratory Tract Infection: e.g., bronchitis. Urinary Tract Infections: e.g., cystitis, cystourethritis, uncomplicated pyelonephritis. Clinical efcacy has been demonstrated in infections caused by commonly occuring pathogens including Streptococcus pneumoniae, Streptococcus pyogenes, Escherichia coli, Proteus mirabilis, Kliebsiella species, Haemophilus inuenzae (beta-lactamase positive and negative), Branhamella catarrhalis (beta- lactamase positive and negative) and Enterobacter species. Cexime is highly stable in the presence of beta- lactamase enzymes. Most strains of enterococci (Streptococcus faecalis, group D Streptococci) and Staphylococci (including coagulase positive and negative strains and meticillin- resistant strains) are resistant to Cexime. In addition, most strains of Pseudomonas, Bacteriodes fragalis, Listeria monocytogenes and Clostridia are resistant to Cexime.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:37:30.425894+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14019,Co-Amoxiclav,Comxicla,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uwDOW1Xzefe5DP5e6_ddgc4ggYEl4dlo/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14019_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uwDOW1Xzefe5DP5e6_ddgc4ggYEl4dlo_view_usp_drivesdk_56c9d0aca8.pdf,page_text/DRP-14019_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uwDOW1Xzefe5DP5e6_ddgc4ggYEl4dlo_view_usp_drivesdk_56c9d0aca8.json,2fec00007dc9607293d64558f4083b824983696c2cc18f1e071d8f074a49cf6c,450907,1,digital_text,"A white to off white free flowing powder filled in 60 mL marked amber coloured glass bottle. On reconstitution with water, white to off white homogenous suspension, having characteristic flavor.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for the treatment of the following infections in adults and children: • Acute bacterial sinusitis (adequately diagnosed) • Acute otitis media • Acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis (adequately diagnosed) • Community acquired pneumonia • Cystitis • Pyelonephritis • Skin and soft tissue infections in particular cellulitis, animal bites, severe dental abscess with spreading cellulitis. • Bone and joint infections, in particular osteomyelitis.",1,1,INDICATIONS :,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:37:33.718993+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14024,Enalapril Maleate,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZD-85tC-ebOfVfTRVxFkC7zbAj-VieLD/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14024_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZD-85tC-ebOfVfTRVxFkC7zbAj-VieLD_view_usp_drivesdk_72ed2f3c52.pdf,page_text/DRP-14024_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZD-85tC-ebOfVfTRVxFkC7zbAj-VieLD_view_usp_drivesdk_72ed2f3c52.json,ea8923585a810967151f6937c17af316900868738970e543569153cf7e0cd995,486365,1,digital_text,"White coloured, round shaped, ﬂat, uncoated tablet having breakline on one side and plain on other side.",1,1,Product Description:,"Treatment of: All Grades of Essential Hypertension, Renovascular Hypertension. All Degrees of Heart Failure: In patients with symptomatic heart failure, Enalapril Maleate is also indicated to: Improve Survival, Retard the Progression of Heart Failure, Reduce Hospitalization for Heart Failure. Prevention of Symptomatic Heart Failure: In asymptomatic patients with left ventricular dysfunction, Enalapril Maleate is indicated to: Retard the Development of Symptomatic Heart Failure, Reduce Hospitalization for Heart Failure. Prevention of Coronary Ischemic Events in Patients with Left Ventricular Dysfunction: Enalapril Maleate is indicated to: Reduce the Incidence of Myocardial Infarction, Reduce Hospitalization for Unstable Angina Pectoris.",1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:37:36.818879+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14027,Amlodipine ( as besilate),Dipinew,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MQRnBuVUT2M6i_22cRBNwcdihbLvkbAY/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14027_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MQRnBuVUT2M6i_22cRBNwcdihbLvkbAY_view_usp_drivesdk_ef97fa9e7e.pdf,page_text/DRP-14027_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MQRnBuVUT2M6i_22cRBNwcdihbLvkbAY_view_usp_drivesdk_ef97fa9e7e.json,a73c788d9748c2be281aada2488086e4e903964e908737b545c336d21c78d1bb,5065303,1,digital_text,"White coloured, round shaped, flat, uncoated tablet having break line on one side plain on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Hypertension: amlodipine is indicated for the first-line treatment of hypertension and can be used as the sole agent to control blood pressure in the majority of patients. Patients not adequately controlled on a single antihypertensive agent (other than amlodipine) may benefit from the addition of amlodipine, which has been used in combination with a thiazide diuretic, alpha blockers, beta adrenoceptor blocking agent or an angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitor. amlodipine is also indicated to reduce the risk of fatal coronary heart disease (CHD) and non-fatal myocardial infarction (MI), and to reduce the risk of stroke. Coronary Artery Disease: amlodipine is indicated to reduce the risk of coronary revascularization and the need for hospitalization due to angina in patients with coronary artery disease (CAD). Chronic Stable Angina: amlodipine is indicated for the first-line treatment of myocardial ischemia, whether due to fixed obstruction (stable angina) and/or vasospasm/vasoconstriction (Prinzmetal's or variant angina) of coronary vasculature. amlodipine may be used where the clinical presentation suggests a possible vasospastic/vasoconstrictive component but where vasospasm/vasoconstriction has not been confirmed. Amlodipine may be used alone, as monotherapy or in combination with other anti-anginal drugs in patients with angina that is refractory to nitrates and/or adequate doses of beta-blockers.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:37:41.161901+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14029,"""Pantoprazole (as sodium sesquihydrate) + Domperidone
(as maleate)""",Pantozisaph,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Eh1QCK3VmJ_-TZ6J4JGzrroPMWLF3yRj/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14029_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Eh1QCK3VmJ_-TZ6J4JGzrroPMWLF3yRj_view_usp_drivesdk_f932a4cbd4.pdf,page_text/DRP-14029_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Eh1QCK3VmJ_-TZ6J4JGzrroPMWLF3yRj_view_usp_drivesdk_f932a4cbd4.json,1e5639cee388da71ad3fee64d4c31e5b6393d724e1a59875af62f48b25f9b95e,3239940,1,digital_text,Hard gelatin capsule of size ''2'' having green coloured cap and clear transparent body filled with brilliant blue and sunset yellow coloured coated pellets.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Management of GERD; gastritis, NUD, gastric or duodenal ulcer, dyspepsia, bloating, fullness, belching, nonsteroidal anti- inflammatory drug (NSAID)-induced dyspepsia.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:37:45.094074+00:00
