PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14067,Levothyroxine sodium,Thyres 100,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/10A8hm6duJuhhtMQTbzf19F-jlP46CNCK/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14067_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_10A8hm6duJuhhtMQTbzf19F-jlP46CNCK_view_usp_drivesdk_abd988d2b2.pdf,page_text/DRP-14067_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_10A8hm6duJuhhtMQTbzf19F-jlP46CNCK_view_usp_drivesdk_abd988d2b2.json,0e9486e306c9bc3cee9d927a3c62cf4908e8b60b126ff2f5515ae98fcd8b5f61,619942,2,digital_text,"THYRES 50: Pink colored, oval shaped bi-convex tablet having break line on one side and plain on other side. THYRES 100: Pale orange colored, oval shaped bi-convex tablet having break line on one side and plain on other side. Pharmacology: Pharmacologic Category: Belongs to the class of thyroid hormones. ATC code: H03AA01. Pharmacodynamics: Thyroxine (T4) is a naturally occurring hormone produced by the thyroid gland and converted to the more active hormone triiodothyronine (T3) in peripheral tissues. The precise signals controlling the conversion of T4 to T3 within the cell are not known. The thyroid hormones are required for normal growth and development, particularly of the nervous system. They increase the resting or basal metabolic rate of the whole organism and have stimulatory effects on the heart, skeletal muscle, liver and kidney. Thyroid hormones enhance lipolysis and the utilization of carbohydrate. 100 microgram thyroxine is equivalent in activity to 20 to 30 microgram liothyronin/triiodothyronine or 60 mg Thyroid BP and/or local pharmacopoiea specification. Pharmacokinetics: Absorption: Following oral administration, the absorption of thyroxine is incomplete and variable, especially when taken with food. The amount absorbed increases during fasting conditions. Distribution: Thyroxine is nearly totally bound to serum protein. Metabolism: The main pathway for the metabolism of thyroxine (T4) is its conversion, by de-iodination, to the active metabolite triiodothyronine (T3). Further de-iodination of T4 and T3 leads to production of inactive products. Elimination: Thyroxine is eliminated slowly from the body with a half-life of approximately seven days in a normal person. This may be reduced in hyperthyroid states or increased in hypothyroid patients. In man, approximately 20 to 40% of thyroxine is eliminated in the faeces and approximately 30 to 55% of a dose of thyroxine is excreted in the urine.",1,1,Product Description:,"• Control of hypothyroidism, • Congenital hypothyroidism in infants, • Acquired hypothyroidism in children and • Juvenile myxedema",1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:42:19.395419+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14067-01,Levothyroxine Sodium,Thyroxil,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VzoTesSLY_5PcRKpPL4R_adfxJ97SZld/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14067-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VzoTesSLY_5PcRKpPL4R_adfxJ97SZld_view_usp_drivesdk_6864016c8e.pdf,page_text/DRP-14067-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VzoTesSLY_5PcRKpPL4R_adfxJ97SZld_view_usp_drivesdk_6864016c8e.json,640e7ba30a6f9a2563d613073f3f42af0aead8db1c95de65cbf4adcdd87770d4,1437629,2,digital_text,"Levothyroxine sodium (Thyroxil) 50 mcg Tablet: Pink colored, oval shaped bi-convex tablet having break line on one side and plain on other side. Levothyroxine sodium (Thyroxil) 100 mcg Tablet: Pale orange colored, oval shaped bi-convex tablet having break line on one side and plain on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Ÿ Control of hypothyroidism, Ÿ Congenital hypothyroidism in infants, Ÿ Acquired hypothyroidism in children and Ÿ Juvenile myxedema",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:42:16.166269+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14068,Lisinopril (as dihydrate),Lislin-20,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/19lv2a5QD7AeYH-Jrm9Za3ARZxkstbi8t/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14068_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19lv2a5QD7AeYH-Jrm9Za3ARZxkstbi8t_view_usp_drivesdk_f1fe191129.pdf,page_text/DRP-14068_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19lv2a5QD7AeYH-Jrm9Za3ARZxkstbi8t_view_usp_drivesdk_f1fe191129.json,8a767ab70d91bad7eb32d724601f3648bb470f412ee37b027f13d3d829aed5ae,508916,1,digital_text,"White, round shaped flat uncoated tablet with breakline on one side and plain on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Hypertension: Lisinopril is indicated in the treatment of hypertension and in renovascular hypertension. It may be used alone or concomitantly with other classes of antihypertensive agents. Congestive Heart failure: Lisinopril is indicated in the management of congestive heart failure as an adjunctive treatment with diuretics and, where appropriate, digitalis. High doses reduce the risk of the combined outcomes of mor tality and hospitalization. Acute myocardial infarction: Lisinopril is indicated for the treatment of hemodynamically stable patients within 24 hours of an acute myocardial infarction, to prevent the subsequent development of left ventricular dysfunction or heart failure and to improve survival. Patients should receive, as appropriate, the standard recommended treatments such as thrombolytics, aspirin and beta-blockers. Renal complications of diabetes mellitus: In normotensive insulin-dependent and hypertensive non-insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus patients who have incipient nephropathy characterized by microalbuminuria, Lisinopril reduces urinary albumin excretion rate.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:42:22.590959+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14070,Lisinopril (as dihydrate),Lislin-5,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1YqhPKMlfZywDG3RgEZ3zhbB33LMKE348/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14070_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YqhPKMlfZywDG3RgEZ3zhbB33LMKE348_view_usp_drivesdk_f2863258e4.pdf,page_text/DRP-14070_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YqhPKMlfZywDG3RgEZ3zhbB33LMKE348_view_usp_drivesdk_f2863258e4.json,17babb1c649bdca5394baa7f1ed2d41e440bd53da10277a1cc855498b6dbd28f,576780,1,digital_text,"White, round shaped flat uncoated tablet with breakline on one side and plain on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Hypertension: Lisinopril is indicated in the treatment of hypertension and in renovascular hypertension. It may be used alone or concomitantly with other classes of antihypertensive agents. Congestive Heart failure: Lisinopril is indicated in the management of congestive heart failure as an adjunctive treatment with diuretics and, where appropriate, digitalis. High doses reduce the risk of the combined outcomes of mor tality and hospitalization. Acute myocardial infarction: Lisinopril is indicated for the treatment of hemodynamically stable patients within 24 hours of an acute myocardial infarction, to prevent the subsequent development of left ventricular dysfunction or heart failure and to improve survival. Patients should receive, as appropriate, the standard recommended treatments such as thrombolytics, aspirin and beta-blockers. Renal complications of diabetes mellitus: In normotensive insulin-dependent and hypertensive non-insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus patients who have incipient nephropathy characterized by microalbuminuria, Lisinopril reduces urinary albumin excretion rate.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:42:25.647516+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1408,PARACETAMOL,UNIGESIC,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1SQh8EG7Mbk4J_TBA1-engeaGRMx1uhXt/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1408_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1SQh8EG7Mbk4J_TBA1-engeaGRMx1uhXt_view_usp_drivesdk_f54d0f562b.pdf,page_text/DRP-1408_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1SQh8EG7Mbk4J_TBA1-engeaGRMx1uhXt_view_usp_drivesdk_f54d0f562b.json,b41d201d75c055fe1d038ecfa9580c112b1be96a609ca852cf954f0a40f03d45,244484,1,digital_text,"Paracetamol is a white crystalline powder that is sparingly soluble in water but freely soluble in ether and in methylene chloride. Paracetamol belongs to a group of medicines called Analgesics and Antipyretics. It works by relieving pain and reducing high temperature and fever. What is in the Medicine? Unigesic contains Paracetamol which is indicated for the treatment of mild to moderate pain and as antipyretic. Strength of the Medicine: (Refer to the formulation) What is Paracetamol (Unigesic) used for? Paracetamol (Unigesic) is indicated for the treatment of mild to moderate pain and as antipyretic. It is also indicated for symptomatic relief of headache, migraine, neuralgia, toothache and teething pains, sore throat, rheumatic aches and pains, influenza and colds. Paracetamol tablets are also recommended for menstrual pains and for the relief of pain associated with osteoarthritis. How much and how often should you use Paracetamol (Unigesic)? Paracetamol oral formulations should not be taken for more than three consecutive days without seeking medical advice. Tablet: (500mg) Adults and Children over 12 years: 1 – 2 tablets 3 to 4 times a day to a maximum of 8 tablets or 4g Paracetamol. Or as prescribed by the physician. Oral Solution (250mg/5mL) Adults and children over 12 years: 10 – 20mL (2 – 4 tsp.) Children: 6 – 12 years: 5 – 10mL (1 – 2 tsp.) Children: 1 – 6 years: 2.5 – 5 mL (1/2 – 1 tsp.) The dose may be repeated 3 – 4 times a day but with an interval of 4 hours or more between each dose. Or as prescribed by the physician. Infant Solution (Oral Drops) 100mg/mL Children 1 – 2 years: 1.2 – 1.8mL Infants 6 – 12 months: 0.6 – 1.2mL Infants 0 – 6 months: 0.3 – 0.6mL The doses may be repeated 3 – 4 times a day Or as prescribed by the physician. When should you NOT take Paracetamol (Unigesic)?  If you are allergic to paracetamol or any of the other ingredients of Paracetamol tablets  If you are taking any other products that contain Paracetamol. Care that should be taken when taking Paracetamol (Unigesic) : • Check with your doctor if you have severe kidney or liver damage, including non-cirrhotic alcoholic liver disease. *Tell your doctor if you are taking any other medicines. What are the undesirable effects of Paracetamol (Unigesic)? Like all medicines, Paracetamol can cause side effects, although not everybody gets them. If you experience any of the following serious effects STOP taking this medicine immediately and contact your doctor or pharmacist:  Severe allergic reactions include: difficulty in breathing , skin rash and itching, swelling of the face and throat, runny nose  Occasionally the blood does not clot well, which may result in easy bruising or bleeding. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking Paracetamol (Unigesic)?  Patient who have taken barbiturates, tricyclic antidepressants and alcohol may show diminished ability to metabolize large doses of paracetamol.  Chronic ingestion of anticonvulsants or oral steroids contraceptives induce liver enzymes and may prevent attainment of therapeutic paracetamol levels by increasing first pass metabolism or clearance. What should you do if you miss a dose of Paracetamol (Unigesic)? If you miss a dose, leave it out and take the next dose whenever it is due. After that, just carry on as before. Do not take double the dose. If you have any further questions, ask your doctor or pharmacist. What are the signs and symptoms of overdose? Paracetamol o verdosage signs and symptoms: pallor, anorexia, nausea and vomiting are frequent early symptoms of paracetamol overdosage. Hepatic necrosis is a dose related complication of paracetamol overdosage . Hepatic enzymes may become elevated and proth rombin time prolonged within 12 to 48 hours but clinical symptoms may not be apparent for 1 to 6 days after ingestion. What should you do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? Contact your doctor, or hospital immediately for consult. Bring the container or label with you to help doctors with necessary information. How should you keep/ store Paracetamol (Unigesic)? Tablet : Store at temperatures not exceeding 30 oC. Keep dry. Oral Solution/ Solution (Oral) Drops : Store at temperatures not exceeding 30oC. Protect from light. Medicines should not be disposed of via wastewater or household waste. Ask your pharmacist how to dispose of medicines no longer required. These measures will help to protect the environment. When should you consult your doctor?  If any undesirable effect occur.  If the patient is taking any vitamin or medicines. Pregnancy and breast feeding. Ask your doctor or pharmacist for advice before taking any medicine. Paracetamol (Unigesic) should be taken with precaution for wo men who are pregnant and breastfeeding. Name and Address of the Manufacturer and Marketing Authorization Holder: St. Martin Pharm Lab Co. 55 Lakandula Street, Parang, Marikina City, Philippines Registration Number: Tablet : DRP - 1408 Oral Solution : DRP - 3644 Oral Solution Drops : DRP - 3529 Date of Renewal of the Authorization: Tablet : Dec. 28, 2023 Oral Solution : Aug. 11, 2024 Oral Solution Drops : Aug. 1, 2024 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: Dec. 14, 2022 “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph” Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. PARACETAMOL [Page 2]",1,1,Description of the Product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:42:28.990415+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14096,Clindamycin (as phosphate),Afrenda,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IJKHUbprh84y_zhfg8myevwV5fSJS4lj/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14096_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IJKHUbprh84y_zhfg8myevwV5fSJS4lj_view_usp_drivesdk_77dc740f33.pdf,page_text/DRP-14096_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IJKHUbprh84y_zhfg8myevwV5fSJS4lj_view_usp_drivesdk_77dc740f33.json,c38931edd4f725758a8edac54d0d61ae4673b226507a62a87f6037bdee23c9c0,448270,1,digital_text,"Clear, colorless, solution.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Clindamycin is antibacterial indicated for the treatment of severe infections caused by susceptible Gram-Positive organisms, staphylococci (both penicillinase- and non-penicillinase-producing), streptococci (except Streptococcus faecailis) and pneumococci. It is also indicated in serious infections caused by susceptible anaerobic pathogens such as Bacteroides spp, Fusobacterium spp, Propionibacterium spp, Peptostreptococcus spp, and microaerophilic streptococci. Consideration should be given to official guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents. Clindamycin does not penetrate the blood/brain barrier in therapeutically effective quantities.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:42:31.958653+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-141,Captopril,Angiovert,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1egw68h9JtOr_02WXkbnhvCXaA0FUeZAZ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-141_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1egw68h9JtOr_02WXkbnhvCXaA0FUeZAZ_view_usp_drivesdk_86fe363cf6.pdf,page_text/DRP-141_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1egw68h9JtOr_02WXkbnhvCXaA0FUeZAZ_view_usp_drivesdk_86fe363cf6.json,9e493a41219407f13d308486654bab367f5b9e3a9bf9e067d2922776e02eb2a2,1349511,1,ocr,,,,,Captopril is used in the treatment of hypertension and heart failure and are given to improve survival following myocardial infarction and for the prophylaxis or cardiovascular events in patients with certain risk factors. They are also used in the treatment of diabetic nephropathy.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:42:39.919734+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14125,Glibenclamide,Dialin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FUIcO3j7SF1o0BiqfPG7DKrAzWD3Jd94/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14125_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FUIcO3j7SF1o0BiqfPG7DKrAzWD3Jd94_view_usp_drivesdk_c759e7c28d.pdf,page_text/DRP-14125_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FUIcO3j7SF1o0BiqfPG7DKrAzWD3Jd94_view_usp_drivesdk_c759e7c28d.json,fc8b0a909a76f6623c99fdb05820090023a92451858034f9ea0a91d02c6c6d9d,671441,1,digital_text,"White or off-white coloured, round shaped,flat, breakline on one side and other side plain uncoated tablet.",1,1,Product Description:,Glibenclamide is a hypoglycaemic agent indicated in the treatment of non-insulin dependent diabetes in patients who respond inadequately to dietary measures alone.,1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:42:43.011632+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14126,Glimepiride,Limglim,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1y2iqLEF848TGtoBIu4hUhiD8vnHECHee/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14126_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1y2iqLEF848TGtoBIu4hUhiD8vnHECHee_view_usp_drivesdk_27a4fd2f04.pdf,page_text/DRP-14126_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1y2iqLEF848TGtoBIu4hUhiD8vnHECHee_view_usp_drivesdk_27a4fd2f04.json,c5a2cc91ae504279813fa06197b22b9378c5ed009906896e66d0f93da26caf73,559810,1,digital_text,"Green coloured, round shaped, biconvex plain on both side lm coated tablet.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Glimepiride is indicated for the treatment of type 2 diabetes mellitus, when diet, physical exercise and weight reduction alone are not adequate.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:42:45.994901+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14127,Olanzapine,Joyola,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/14MPB6qzzJkTRFNOWR21J_71-ewUJbnMD/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14127_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14MPB6qzzJkTRFNOWR21J_71-ewUJbnMD_view_usp_drivesdk_f35669a2ce.pdf,page_text/DRP-14127_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14MPB6qzzJkTRFNOWR21J_71-ewUJbnMD_view_usp_drivesdk_f35669a2ce.json,e7777df4dffc28d98cc76b3b909de0117fd6d22c803dcf43af003e75b46edeb0,1299770,1,digital_text,"Orange coloured, round shaped, biconvex, film coated tablet plain on both side",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Adults Olanzapine is indicated for the treatment of schizophrenia. Olanzapine is effective in maintaining the clinical improvement during continuation therapy in patients who have shown an initial treatment response. Olanzapine is indicated for the treatment of moderate to severe manic episode. In patients whose manic episode has responded to olanzapine treatment, olanzapine is indicated for the prevention of recurrence in patients with bipolar disorder. Or as prescribed by the physician",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:42:49.644580+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14129,,,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/17bMiRNEGKaRkqW1RG6wVn-pMLOrQvhuF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14129_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17bMiRNEGKaRkqW1RG6wVn-pMLOrQvhuF_view_usp_drivesdk_20a3af56b6.pdf,page_text/DRP-14129_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17bMiRNEGKaRkqW1RG6wVn-pMLOrQvhuF_view_usp_drivesdk_20a3af56b6.json,9273982eb2d48fcfbcdfdd7d0bb3e739ef667f41926203fbbbbf149f81affb20,439849,1,digital_text,,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"The usual adult daily dose (in terms of Ceftriaxone) is 1-2 grams given once a day (or in equally divided doses twice a day) depending on the type and severity of the infection. The total daily dose should not exceed 4 grams. Dosage regimen for Ceftriaxone + Sulbactam (Stacef Plus) should be adjusted in patients with marked decrease in renal function (creatinine clearance of < 30 mL/min) and to compensate for reduced clearance less than 15 mL/min, patient should receive a maximum of 500 mg of sulbactam every 12 hours (maximum dose 1 gram of sulbactam). Pediatric Patients For treatment of skin and soft tissue infections, the recommended total daily dose (in terms of Ceftriaxone) is 50-75 mg/kg given once a day or (in equally divided doses twice a day). The total daily dose should not exceed 1 gram. For treatment of meningitis: The initial therapeutic dose in terms of Ceftriaxone should be 100 mg/kg (not to exceed 4 grams). Daily dose may be administered once a day or in equally divided doses every12 hours. The usual duration of therapy is 7-14 days. For treatment of serious infections other than meningitis: Recommended total daily dose in terms of Ceftriaxone is 50-75 mg/kg given in divided doses every 12 hours. The total daily dose (in terms of Ceftriaxone) should not exceed more than 2 grams. Ceftriaxone is not metabolized in the body and is eliminated unchanged via two pathways, urine and bile. 40-50% of parenterally administered dose is excreted into the urine within 48 hours as active drug. Thus, high concentrations are attained in urine, whatever is not excreted via kidney is excreted through bile. Metabolism of sulbactam is less than 25%. 70-80% of Sulbactam is excreted by the kidney. Biliary excretion is minimal and renal excretion is blocked by probenecid. Sulbactam and Ceftriaxone can be removed by hemodialysis. Impaired Renal Function and Hepatic insufficiency: Ceftriaxone is excreted via both renal and biliary pathways; therefore, patients with renal failure normally require no adjustments of dose. However concentration of the drug should be monitored in such patients and if there is evidence of drug accumulation then dosage adjustments should be made accordingly. Dosage adjustments are not necessary in patients with hepatic dysfunction; however; in patients with both hepatic dysfunction and significant renal failure, dosage should not exceed more than 2 grams daily with close monitoring of serum concentrations. Adults For treatment of acute bacterial otitis media: A single intramuscular dose of 50 mg/kg (not to exceed 1gram) is recommended. Route of Administration: Intramuscular/Intravenous",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:42:52.500888+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14137,Risperidone,Rispemind,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1OIOYF5Iv02YQRidnqDl8KEzWsNwdNTm0/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14137_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OIOYF5Iv02YQRidnqDl8KEzWsNwdNTm0_view_usp_drivesdk_7a38352095.pdf,page_text/DRP-14137_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OIOYF5Iv02YQRidnqDl8KEzWsNwdNTm0_view_usp_drivesdk_7a38352095.json,b1deac1f137bca77e886f3c7e20629826682a8ca315f3236775e87a8e8b2f10c,828264,1,digital_text,"Clear, colorless solution.",1,1,Product Description:,"Risperidone is indicated for the treatment of schizophrenic patients and other psychotic disorders including first episode psychoses, acute schizophrenic exacerbations, chronic schizophrenia and other psychotic conditions, in which positive symptoms (such as hallucinations, delusions, thought disturbances, hostility, suspiciousness), and/or negative symptoms (such as blunted affect, emotional and social withdrawal, poverty of speech) are prominent. Risperidone also alleviates affective symptoms (such as depression, guilt-feelings, anxiety) associated with schizophrenia. Risperidone also appears effective in maintaining the clinical improvement during continuation therapy in adult patients who have shown an initial response to treatment with this agent. Risperidone is indicated for the treatment of manic episodes associated with bipolar disorders. These episodes are characterised by symptoms such as elevated, expansive or irritable mood, inflated self esteem, decreased need for sleep, difficulty in speaking, racing thoughts, distractability, or poor judgement, including disruptive or aggressive behaviours. Risperidone is also indicated for the treatment of conduct and other disruptive behaviour disorders where aggressive or destructive behaviours are prominent. Risperidone is also effective in maintaining the clinical improvement during continuation therapy in children and adolescents who have shown an initial treatment response. Risperidone is indicated for the treatment of anxiety (aggression, self-injury, anger attacks, sudden mood changes) due to autistic disorder in children and adolescents.",1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:42:55.688611+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14140,Cefazolin (as Sodium),Novazolin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1D3RF8aXjhKZnYo8MWtRTfCu_P1yCzZp0/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14140_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1D3RF8aXjhKZnYo8MWtRTfCu_P1yCzZp0_view_usp_drivesdk_c5f5289038.pdf,page_text/DRP-14140_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1D3RF8aXjhKZnYo8MWtRTfCu_P1yCzZp0_view_usp_drivesdk_c5f5289038.json,7bdc73a21fc4779341421f334333061a068044091916ad33c25a93a2d1b76472,424020,4,digital_text,White powder very hygroscopic,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated in the treatment of the following serious infections due to susceptible organisms: Respiratory Tract Infections: Due to S. pneumoniae, Klebsiella species, H. influenzae, S. aureus (penicillin -sensitive and penicillin-resistant), and group A beta-hemolytic streptococci. Injectable benzathine penicillin is considered to be the drug of choice in treatment and prevention of streptococcal infections, including the prophylaxis of rheumatic fever. Cefazolin is effective in the eradication of streptoco cci from the nasopharynx; however, data establishing the efficacy of Cefazolin in the subsequent prevention of rheumatic fever are not available at present. Urinary Tract Infections: Due to E. coli, P. mirabilis, Klebsiella species, and some strains of enterobacter and enterococci. Skin and Skin Structure Infections: Due to S. aureus (penicillin - sensitive and penicillin -resistant), group A beta -hemolytic streptococci, and other strains of streptococci. Biliary Tract Infections: Due to E. coli, various st rains of streptococci, P. mirabilis, Klebsiella species, and S. aureus.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:42:58.708531+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14149,Fenofibrate,Finofen,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xYw5V58uYqNsOT1E1BZBV-NzEjE_hn_u/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14149_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xYw5V58uYqNsOT1E1BZBV-NzEjE_hn_u_view_usp_drivesdk_8573ebf6ab.pdf,page_text/DRP-14149_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xYw5V58uYqNsOT1E1BZBV-NzEjE_hn_u_view_usp_drivesdk_8573ebf6ab.json,f4f3efa88ec332afd7d2ae8e1bbbca004806e1933daf02b53bc7c6f31b9c6e15,1402553,5,digital_text,White coloured capsule,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Fenofibrate 200 mg capsules are indicated as an adjunct to diet and other non pharmacological treatment (e.g. exercise, weight reduction) for the following: - Treatment of severe hypertriglyceridaemia with or without low HDL cholesterol. - Mixed hyperlipidaemia when a statin is contraindicated or not tolerated. - Mixed hyperlipidaemia in patients at high cardiovascular risk in addition to a statin when triglycer ides and HDL cholesterol are not adequately controlled.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:43:02.180058+00:00
