PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14217,Irbesartan,Irbenov-150,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1a-9tLfeLJUjZH86pZZG6dJk-ux1V5FVR/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14217_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1a-9tLfeLJUjZH86pZZG6dJk-ux1V5FVR_view_usp_drivesdk_dd1a2f7f96.pdf,page_text/DRP-14217_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1a-9tLfeLJUjZH86pZZG6dJk-ux1V5FVR_view_usp_drivesdk_dd1a2f7f96.json,0206e25828418bdb5d223c512557d9ad2cf2f557649bc4d7f6d3d3ca059e768d,470807,5,digital_text,White to off white oval film-coated tablets debossed with “ML 95” on one side and plain on other side.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Indicated in adults for the treatment of essential hypertension. It is also indicated for the treatment of renal disease in adult patients with hypertension and type 2 diabetes mellitus as part of an antihypertensive medicinal product regimen.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:46:18.901659+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14218,Ceftazidime (As Sodium),Medtazime,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1y_2i0YB7Wkcc4Q0X1Pu_nctkO1ju6U0O/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14218_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1y_2i0YB7Wkcc4Q0X1Pu_nctkO1ju6U0O_view_usp_drivesdk_1c00e703bc.pdf,page_text/DRP-14218_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1y_2i0YB7Wkcc4Q0X1Pu_nctkO1ju6U0O_view_usp_drivesdk_1c00e703bc.json,9c9d07e09ff8cbe2232fcab8aadf1088d610323ec95d214c540123f5d091056c,205414,3,digital_text,Almost white crystalline powder.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Ceftazidime is indicated for the treatment of the infections listed below in adults and children including neonates (from birth). • Nosocomial pneumonia • Broncho-pulmonary infections in cystic fibrosis • Bacterial meningitis • Chronic suppurative otitis media • Malignant otitis externa • Complicated urinary tract infections • Complicated skin and soft tissue infections • Complicated intra-abdominal infections • Bone and joint infections • Peritonitis associated with dialysis in patients on CAPD. Treatment of patients with bacteraemia that occurs in association with, or is suspected to be associated with, any of the infections listed above. Ceftazidime may be used in the management of neutropenic patients with fever that is suspected to be due to a bacterial infection. Ceftazidime may be used in the peri -operative prophylaxis of urinary tract infections for patients undergoing trans-urethral resection of the prostate (TURP). The selection of ceftazidime should take into account its antibacterial spectrum, which is mainly restricted to aerobic Gram negative bacteria. Ceftazidime should be co-administered with other antibacterial agents whenever the possible range of causative bacteria would not fall within its spectrum of activity.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:46:22.123664+00:00
