PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14343,Fusidic Acid,Fusinox,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1F1qqrV_DhYbzOOR-4r4Ub0CoHsUaa_Iq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14343_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1F1qqrV_DhYbzOOR-4r4Ub0CoHsUaa_Iq_view_usp_drivesdk_3c02b3c621.pdf,page_text/DRP-14343_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1F1qqrV_DhYbzOOR-4r4Ub0CoHsUaa_Iq_view_usp_drivesdk_3c02b3c621.json,477cca697c45a800f602716aa91e4a99629bbe66d4fdf01f65e27a625fa5ae2a,2716954,2,ocr,"Awhite color smooth cream filled in 15 gram aluminum collapsible tube. Such 1 tube is packed in a printed carton with patient information leaflet. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Each gram contains Fusidic Acid, BP 20 mg (2% w/w) STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE? 2% w/w WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Topical treatment for infections caused by bacteria sensitive to fusidic acid in particular S. aureus. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Always use this medicine exactly as your doctor or pharmacist has told you. Check with your doctor or pharmacist if you are not sure. Recommended dose Apply 3-4 times daily or as prescribed by a physician. Use in adults and children Usually, a small amount of cream is applied to the infected skin three or four times each day. If your doctor advises you to use a sterile bandage or dressing, you usually can reduce the number of applications. A nappy on a baby may act as a dressing. Follow the advice of your doctor. If you think that the effect of Fusidic acid cream is too strong or too weak, ask your doctor or pharmacist for advice. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Do not use Fusidic acid cream if you are allergic to fusidic acid or any of the other ingredients of this medicine. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Talk to your doctor, pharmacist or physician before using Fusidic acid cream + if you use Fusidic acid cream on the face. The cream should not be applied in or near the eye because it can lead to a prickling feeling in the eye + if you use the cream for a long time or in large amounts as it may make the chance of getting any side effects higher. Also your skin may get more sensitive to the cream. Please tell your doctor if one of the above warnings applies to you or has applied to you in the past. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Like all medicines, this medicine can cause side effects, although not everybody gets them. The most frequently reported side effects are various skin reactions and in particular application site reactions. The frequency of occurrence of side effects is as follows: Uncommon: may affect up to 1 in 100 people Rare: may affect up to 1 in 1,000 people If you have any of the following rare side effects while using your medicine, tell your doctor immediately or go to hospital straight away: [Page 2] + Severe allergic reaction which may include a red and lumpy skin rash, difficulty breathing, swelling of face, mouth, lips or eyelids, unexplained high temperature (fever and feeling faint). If the swelling affects your throat and makes breathing and swallowing difficult, go to hospital straight away. Uncommon * Itching * Rash + Eczema + Skin sensitivity reactions (contact dermatitis) + Irritation at site of application (including pain, stinging, burning and redness of the skin). Rare * Blister + Swelling of the skin + Hives + Conjunctivitis. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Please tell your doctor or pharmacist if you are taking, or have recently taken any other medicines. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Apply the cream as soon as possible, then continue the rest of your treatment as usual. This includes medicines you have bought without a prescription or herbal medicines. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you apply too much or accidentally swallow Fusidic acid cream, it is unlikely to cause any harm. However, if you notice any effect or are worried, contact your doctor or pharmacist. You should contact the doctor if Fusidic acid cream is accidentally swallowed by an infant. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If you get any side effects, talk to your doctor, pharmacist or nurse. This includes any possible side effects not listed in this leaflet. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Keep out of reach of children. Shelf-life: 24 months",1,2,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:49:25.248629+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14344,Clotrimazole,Destrimole,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1z-N7Xep1NXJ4z6h_UyP8ujZ1MREjkYoG/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14344_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1z-N7Xep1NXJ4z6h_UyP8ujZ1MREjkYoG_view_usp_drivesdk_57eb97fd92.pdf,page_text/DRP-14344_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1z-N7Xep1NXJ4z6h_UyP8ujZ1MREjkYoG_view_usp_drivesdk_57eb97fd92.json,a36fae11dd621f3825203f9fec84b28c42e64723157e8868b5293f567ab519f1,2370711,2,ocr,"A white color smooth cream filled in 15 g aluminum collapsible tube. Such 1 tube is packed in a printed carton with patient information leaflet. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Each gram contains: Clotrimazole, BP 10 mg (1% w/w) STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE? 10 mg/g (1% w/w) WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? The active substance is clotrimazole. Clotrimazole belongs to a group of medicines called imidazoles and is an antifungal agent which fights the cause of fungal skin infections. Clotrimazole is used to treat fungal skin infections such as ringworm, athlete’s foot, fungal nappy rash and fungal sweat rash. It is also used to relieve irritation of the vulva (external thrush) or the end of the penis, which may be associated with thrush. When Clotrimazole is applied to the infected area of skin it works by destroying the fungus or yeast which has caused the infection. Treatment of dermatomycoses, caused by dermatophytes, yeasts, molds and other fungi: Relieves itching, redness, burning sensation caused by ringworm, pityriasis versicolor, athlete's foot, jock itch, diaper dermatitis, dandruff and other skin & nail fungal infections (cutaneous candidiasis, erythrasma). HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Apply thinly two to three times daily. A strip of cream (/2 cm long) is enough to treat an area of about the size of the hand. To ensure complete healing depending on the indication, the treatment should be continued according to the indications specified even if symptoms disappear: Dermatomycoses: 3-4 weeks. Erythrasma: 2-4 weeks. Pityriasis versicolor: 1-3 weeks. Candida vulvitis and Candida balanitis: 1-2 weeks. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? People who are hypersensitive to any ingredient in the preparation. First trimester of pregnancy. Children <2 years. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Avoid contact with eyes. Do not swallow. Clotrimazole cream may reduce the effectiveness and safety of latex products such as, condoms and diaphragms when applied on the genital area (women: labia and adjacent area of the vulva; men: prepuce and glans of the penis). The effect is temporary and occurs only during treatment. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Signs of an allergic reaction may include: ¢ Ras ¢ Swallowing or breathing problems ¢ Swelling of the lips, face, throat or tongue ¢ Weakness, feeling dizzy or faint [Page 2] « Nausea After you apply the cream, you might experience: ¢ Itching, rash, blisters, burning, discomfort, swelling, irritation, pins and needles, redness or peeling of skin. This may mean that you are allergic to the cream. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Clotrimazole is not known to interact with any other medicines. As with other creams, Clotrimazole may reduce the effectiveness of rubber contraceptives, such as condoms or diaphragms. Consequently, if you are using this cream on the vulva or penis, you should use alternative precautions for at least five days after using this product. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Apply the cream as soon as possible, then continue the rest of your treatment as usual. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you take more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? Patients should consult their physician if there is no improvement after 4 weeks of treatment. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Keep out of reach of children.",1,2,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:49:33.470736+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14354,Salbutamol (as sulfate),Salv100,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JEgYNqW9-BGnDfufloK4DXRwgO1GkuBU/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14354_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1JEgYNqW9-BGnDfufloK4DXRwgO1GkuBU_view_usp_drivesdk_b74d3ecb65.pdf,page_text/DRP-14354_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1JEgYNqW9-BGnDfufloK4DXRwgO1GkuBU_view_usp_drivesdk_b74d3ecb65.json,5fcfb4d253a8c4e906ac058f07484cf37eebc64301acdbfa96d7abb109d99d0a,1075486,3,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T12:49:41.490306+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14354-01,Salbutamol (as sulfate),Salbpress,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J6qoCCHtTnj-cnnNDcuP_GSm6pkH7aIO/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14354-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1J6qoCCHtTnj-cnnNDcuP_GSm6pkH7aIO_view_usp_drivesdk_39ee413246.pdf,page_text/DRP-14354-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1J6qoCCHtTnj-cnnNDcuP_GSm6pkH7aIO_view_usp_drivesdk_39ee413246.json,c9b19ce8ea954d61e10480851aef7a2eecabeb1d21165d91200f2d98fa65eed4,2516772,1,digital_text,It is a suspension of Salbutamol sulfate in a suitable liquid in a pressurized container ﬁtted with a metering dose valve.,1,1,Product Description:,"It is indicated for the relief of bronchospasm in patients with asthma or chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (reversible obstructive airway disease), and for acute prophylaxis against exercise-induced asthma or other stimuli known to induce bronchospasm. Strength One canister provides 200 actuations. Each actuation delivers 100 micrograms of salbutamol.",1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:49:38.002216+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-14363,Cholecalciferol (Vitamin D3),Calciubone Vita 3,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qDEvmc_ObbJkAEhTpB84K9Mugxsp3VoI/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-14363_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qDEvmc_ObbJkAEhTpB84K9Mugxsp3VoI_view_usp_drivesdk_c344bcd997.pdf,page_text/DRP-14363_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qDEvmc_ObbJkAEhTpB84K9Mugxsp3VoI_view_usp_drivesdk_c344bcd997.json,2474383d6904119918036e2d457573737b2298b3424c4b343adaf6f8d81b15e5,3687496,1,ocr,"Calciubone in an off-white oblong-shaped film-coated tablet with score on one side that contains HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? calcium and Cholecalciferol (Vitamin D3) at its safe level. Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°c. Keep out of reach of children. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Protect from light. One tablet twice a day with food and a full glass of water or as prescribed by the physician. Availability: Aluminum foil strip x 10 (box of 100’s) WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Physician samples: Flap x 1 and Starter dose x 4 Take the medicine as soon as you can, but skip the missed dose if it is almost time for your next dose. Do not take two doses at one time. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSAGE For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph Symptoms of overdose may include: nausea/vomiting, loss of appetite, mental/mood changes, headache, drowsiness, weakness, tiredness. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? Manufactured for: If someone has overdosed and has serious symptoms such as passing out or trouble breathing,",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T12:49:56.339803+00:00
