PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1499-14,Omeprazole,Omzyn IV,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Y5EmuybRPISwjcT1FU-Ge1vnEuw7z7Xp/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1499-14_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Y5EmuybRPISwjcT1FU-Ge1vnEuw7z7Xp_view_usp_drivesdk_0efb38a009.pdf,page_text/DRP-1499-14_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Y5EmuybRPISwjcT1FU-Ge1vnEuw7z7Xp_view_usp_drivesdk_0efb38a009.json,8862d53a07ef2dd8a2774beeaeca37bbdd33f9ea1d821961bac15fbeb880c803,497061,2,digital_text,"Storage Store at temperatures not exceeding 25°C. Protect from light Incompatibilities Infusions with low pH should not be used for diluting Omzyn IV Injection as fading & discoloration of solution can occur. Caution: Foods, Drugs, Devices and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription. Availability Each pack contains one USP Type I amber drug vial and 10 mL ampoule of Sterile Water for Injection USP Shelf-life: 24 months For suspected adverse drug reaction report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. DRP-1499-14 Date of Authorization: 23 NOV 2022 Date of leaflet revision: 23 NOV 2022 Manufactured by:",2,2,PHARMACEUTICAL INFORMATION,"Omeprazole (Omzyn IV) is indicated primarily for the treatment of Zollinger-Ellison syndrome, and may also be used for the treatment of gastric ulcer, duodenal ulcer and reflux oesophagitis.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T12:55:05.160709+00:00
