PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-15011,Metfromin Hydrochloride,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Bs9RT43eCE-pet-zBFzE0nnjHBrAybZ4/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-15011_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Bs9RT43eCE-pet-zBFzE0nnjHBrAybZ4_view_usp_drivesdk_3c1c28f7e5.pdf,page_text/DRP-15011_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Bs9RT43eCE-pet-zBFzE0nnjHBrAybZ4_view_usp_drivesdk_3c1c28f7e5.json,8f5a7b7cfc16008cfb32ed4d0bfe7ebedbb5bb044f1aa245d5a72d06461a6afc,1392977,2,ocr,"Metformin Hydrochloride is an oral antihyperglycemic drug used in the management of type 2 diabetes. Metformin hydrochloride (N,N-dimethylimidodicarbonimidic diamide hydrochloride) is not chemically or pharmacologically related to any other classes of oral antihyperglycemic agents. The structural formula is as shown: Hg N—C—NH—C—NHp * HCI set ll H3C NH NH Molecular formula of Metformin hydrochloride is CH ,,NsHCI, Chemical IUPAC Name is (N, N-dimethylimidodicarbonimidic diamide hydrochloride), Molecular weight is 165.63",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"Treatment of type 2 diabetes mellitus in adults, particularly in overweight patients, wnen dietary management and exercise alone does not result in adequate glycaemic control. DIAVIN XR may be used as monotherapy or in combination with other oral antidiabetic agents, or with insulin.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T12:55:46.974378+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-15017,,,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/15BR_nvUBIiVf7yiZNR5UMqOaq8k9-3Px/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-15017_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15BR_nvUBIiVf7yiZNR5UMqOaq8k9-3Px_view_usp_drivesdk_36e9df3c13.pdf,page_text/DRP-15017_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15BR_nvUBIiVf7yiZNR5UMqOaq8k9-3Px_view_usp_drivesdk_36e9df3c13.json,ebde076e14c288e61e2ada03ebb3243ad24da9e1d771555adfb6022a175d3acd,804886,1,digital_text,"A white or almost white powder. Slightly soluble in water and in isopropyl alcohol; sparingly soluble in dehydrated alcohol; freely soluble in methyl alcohol. Store in airtight containers. Protect from light. Amlodipine (as Besilate), USP ..........................10 mg Amlodipine is a dihydropyridine blocker. It is a peripheral and coronary vasodilator but unlike the blockers Verapamil or Diltiazem, has little or no effect on cardiac conduction and negative inotropic activity is rarely seen at therapeutic doses. Administration results primarily in vasodilation, with reduced peripheral resistance, blood pressure, and afterload, increased coronary blood , and a increase in heart rate. This in turn results in an increase in myocardial oxygen supply and cardiac output. It has no antiarrhythmic activity. Amlodipine maybe even more selective than Nifedipine for vascular smooth muscle. Most of the dihydropyridine blockers are chiral compounds used as racemic mixtures. Each ablet contains:",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Increased Angina or Myocardial Infarction Amlodipine (Amlocare) is contraindicated in patients with known sensitivity to Amlodipine. Hypotension,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:55:50.174801+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-15034,Teicoplanin,Teiconova-400,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Xzjn-IsCMq0gUU_NDHXaZ4bFQ9L5OQJG/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-15034_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Xzjn-IsCMq0gUU_NDHXaZ4bFQ9L5OQJG_view_usp_drivesdk_c285dfcb7b.pdf,page_text/DRP-15034_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Xzjn-IsCMq0gUU_NDHXaZ4bFQ9L5OQJG_view_usp_drivesdk_c285dfcb7b.json,216d8524388add2d46de163eaeeed3be515bddf4d3139a4ec0c878e607c37b36,511087,3,digital_text,Spongy ivory coloured homogenous powder.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated in adults and in children from birth for the parenteral treatment of the following infections • Complicated skin and soft tissue infections, • Bone and joint infections, • Hospital acquired pneumonia, • Community acquired pneumonia, • Complicated urinary tract infections, • Infective endocarditis, • Peritonitis associated with continuous ambulatory peritoneal dialysis (CAPD), • Bacteraemia that occurs in association with any of the indications listed above. Teicoplanin is also indicated as an alternative oral treatment for Clostridium difficile infection-associated diarrhoea and colitis. Where appropriate, teicoplanin should be admin istered in combination with other antibacterial agents. Consideration should be given to official guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T12:55:53.399484+00:00
