PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-15483,Dapagliflozin (as propanediol monohydrate),Dapastal-10,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/176eLIsKXpE8gQ30k8xKxeytaAwi14_wc/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-15483_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_176eLIsKXpE8gQ30k8xKxeytaAwi14_wc_view_usp_drivesdk_8d02fd1724.pdf,page_text/DRP-15483_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_176eLIsKXpE8gQ30k8xKxeytaAwi14_wc_view_usp_drivesdk_8d02fd1724.json,8a6da64c8e2237babfd457cdd8b393e3dcf4427b0964cf236b5b0f2019185461,1003716,1,digital_text,"Yellow colour, round shaped, biconvex, ﬁlm coated tablet having both sides plain.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Type 2 diabetes mellitus Dapagliﬂozin Tablet is indicated in adults aged 18 years and older with type 2 diabetes mellitus as: Monotherapy: When diet and exercise alone do not provide adequate glycaemic control in patients for whom use of metformin is considered inappropriate due to intolerance. Add-on combination therapy: In combination with other glucose-lowering medicinal products including insulin, when these, together with diet and exercise, do not provide adequate glycaemic control. Initial Combination: Dapagliﬂozin Tablet is indicated for use as initial combination therapy with metformin, as an adjunct to diet and exercise, to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus when diet and exercise have failed to provide adequate glycemic control and there are poor prospects for response to metformin monotherapy (for example, high initial HbA1c levels).",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:01:41.517544+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-15483-02,Dapagliflozin (as propanediol monohydrate),Flosazin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1D0__dg3XQM3vHOyICNUPY45nb6mgap6h/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-15483-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1D0__dg3XQM3vHOyICNUPY45nb6mgap6h_view_usp_drivesdk_846461459b.pdf,page_text/DRP-15483-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1D0__dg3XQM3vHOyICNUPY45nb6mgap6h_view_usp_drivesdk_846461459b.json,79119ffdaf48d364ef09f39aec1ace755e22d3512d7883cfb6919c13ca570f24,440431,1,digital_text,"Yellow colour, round shaped, biconvex, film coated tablet having both sides plain.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Type 2 diabetes mellitus Dapagliflozin Tablet is indicated in adults aged 18 years and older with type 2 diabetes mellitus as: Monotherapy: When diet and exercise alone do not provide adequate glycaemic control in patients for whom use of metformin is considered inappropriate due to intolerance. Add-on combination therapy: In combination with other glucose-lowering medicinal products including insulin, when these, together with diet and exercise, do not provide adequate glycaemic control. Initial Combination: Dapagliflozin Tablet is indicated for use as initial combination therapy with metformin, as an adjunct to diet and exercise, to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus when diet and exercise have failed to provide adequate glycemic control and there are poor prospects for response to metformin monotherapy (for example, high initial HbA1c levels).",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:01:23.484793+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-15483-03,Dapagliflozin (as propanediol monohydrate),Cardiogly,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-e0E_NPWhZdCsl5xwyXNEiV4l5cuw9iP/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-15483-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-e0E_NPWhZdCsl5xwyXNEiV4l5cuw9iP_view_usp_drivesdk_0e151c3c3f.pdf,page_text/DRP-15483-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-e0E_NPWhZdCsl5xwyXNEiV4l5cuw9iP_view_usp_drivesdk_0e151c3c3f.json,dc461cbbeffea037c8c4ae559eb7b5e7d1111375167c843fda34a013c07a5d9e,4401456,1,digital_text,"Yellow colour, round shaped, biconvex, ﬁlm coated tablet having both sides plain.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Type 2 diabetes mellitus Dapagliﬂozin Tablets is indicated in adults aged 18 years and older with type 2 diabetes mellitus as: Monotherapy When diet and exercise alone do not provide adequate glycaemic control in pa␀ents for whom use of me␀ormin is considered inappropriate due to intolerance. Add-on combina␀on therapy In combina␀on with other glucose-lowering medicinal products including insulin, when these, together with diet and exercise, do not provide adequate glycaemic control. Ini␀al Combina␀on Dapagliﬂozin Tablets is indicated for use as ini␀al combina␀on therapy with me␀ormin, as an adjunct to diet and exercise, to improve glycemic control in pa␀ents with type 2 diabetes mellitus when diet and exercise have failed to provide adequate glycemic control and there are poor prospects for response to me␀ormin monotherapy (for example, high ini␀al HbA1c levels).",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:01:30.923559+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-15483-11,Dapagliflozin (as propanediol monohydrate),Dafadin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1omafcLZO4qQNOXwNlS-_kliUaMwaOuLF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-15483-11_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1omafcLZO4qQNOXwNlS-_kliUaMwaOuLF_view_usp_drivesdk_c5983eb0a8.pdf,page_text/DRP-15483-11_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1omafcLZO4qQNOXwNlS-_kliUaMwaOuLF_view_usp_drivesdk_c5983eb0a8.json,c866a539697a176547e02d414a08a63afc79e321ae21a8cd12ffec2908b0a537,4730032,1,digital_text,"Yellow color, round shaped, biconvex, ﬁlm coated tablet having both sides plain.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Type 2 diabetes mellitus Dapagliﬂozin tablet is indicated in adults aged 18 years and older with type 2 diabetes mellitus as: Monotherapy When diet and exercise alone do not provide adequate glycemic control in patients for whom use of metformin is considered inappropriate due to intolerance. Add-on combination therapy In combination with other glucose-lowering medicinal products including insulin, when these, together with diet and exercise, do not provide adequate glycemic control. Initial Combination Dapagliﬂozin tablet is indicated for use as initial combination therapy with metformin, as an adjunct to diet and exercise, to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus when diet and exercise have failed to provide adequate glycemic control and there are poor prospects for response to metformin monotherapy (for example, high initial HbA1c levels).",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:01:36.107952+00:00
