PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1605,,Syclovir,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xy_XgjzoIcE6ClVDRIwM8nMTUzOmDN-Q/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1605_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xy_XgjzoIcE6ClVDRIwM8nMTUzOmDN-Q_view_usp_drivesdk_e8276dd364.pdf,page_text/DRP-1605_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xy_XgjzoIcE6ClVDRIwM8nMTUzOmDN-Q_view_usp_drivesdk_e8276dd364.json,8f591eadf01f38209443678ad2cc279d541da9832f387dc6e1961511e5765d6a,3616576,7,digital_text_and_ocr,"Aciclovir (Syclovir) 400 mg Tablet is a white, round, flat, beveled-edge tablet, plain on one side and scored on the other side. Aciclovir (Syclovir) 800 mg Tablet is a white, capsule-shaped, biconvex tablet, scored on one side and plain on the other side.",7,7,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for the initial treatment and prophylaxis of recurrent mucosal and cutaneous herpes (HSV1, HSV2) infections; For herpes simplex encephalitis; For varicella-zoster infections in healthy non-pregnant patients ≥13 years of age, children >12 months of age w ith a chronic lung disorder or are r eceiving long-term aspirin therapy, and immunocompromised patients; For herpes zoster infections; For the treatment of disseminated herpes infections in neonates.",7,7,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T13:07:36.671273+00:00
