PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1612,Co-Amoxiclav,Bioclavid,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gDMWUDlEBmtF-cOvSeIn5QjYYcKz_qBN/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1612_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gDMWUDlEBmtF-cOvSeIn5QjYYcKz_qBN_view_usp_drivesdk_4852c3c25d.pdf,page_text/DRP-1612_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gDMWUDlEBmtF-cOvSeIn5QjYYcKz_qBN_view_usp_drivesdk_4852c3c25d.json,59386452869ae1ea219d3b5963f4fe78d62ca46830747f58d294d3bf0b23272d,323666,16,digital_text,"Film-coated tablet. W hite to light yellow, oblong, biconvex film-coated tablet, scored on both sides. C LINICAL PARTICULARS Therapeutic indications Amoxicillin/clavulanic acid is indicated for the treatment of the following infections in adults and children (see Dosage and method of administration, Special warnings and precautions for use and",1,1,HARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Amoxicillin/clavulanic acid is indicated for the treatment of the following infections in adults and children (see Dosage and method of administration, Special warnings and precautions for use and Pharmacodynamic properties): • A cute bacterial sinusitis (adequately diagnosed) • Acute otitis media • Acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis (adequately diagnosed) • Community-acquired pneumonia • Cystitis • Pyelonephritis • Skin and soft tissue infections in particular cellulitis, animal bites, severe dental abscess with spreading cellulitis. • Bone and joint infections, in particular osteomyelitis. C onsideration should be given to official guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents. D",1,1,Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:08:09.376278+00:00
