PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1617,Ampicillin (as sodium),Sumpilin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rHq6QbzHqpSj2GLFuGzPIjv4QI0DB4qv/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1617_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rHq6QbzHqpSj2GLFuGzPIjv4QI0DB4qv_view_usp_drivesdk_f210cf05fe.pdf,page_text/DRP-1617_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rHq6QbzHqpSj2GLFuGzPIjv4QI0DB4qv_view_usp_drivesdk_f210cf05fe.json,107a4442230f3acf8fbb747b6e2f78c1b884753d787ff11480c7501818582f0f,657176,1,digital_text,White or almost white powder.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Ampicillin is a broad-spectrum penicillin, indicated for the treatment of a wide range of bacterial infections caused by ampicillin-sensitive organisms. Typical indications include: ear, nose and throat infections, bronchitis, pneumonia, urinary tract infections, gonorrhoea, gynaecological infections, septicaemia, peritonitis, endocarditis, meningitis, enteric fever, gastro-intestinal infections. Extraperitoneal application of Ampicillin to wounds can be used to prevent infection following abdominal surgery.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:08:26.330669+00:00
