PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-16473,Clopidogrel (as bisulfate),Platikon,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/10v-lrt0CQ2kkl8G7Y3AXjcCyCmsJDob1/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-16473_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_10v-lrt0CQ2kkl8G7Y3AXjcCyCmsJDob1_view_usp_drivesdk_47f6d3416d.pdf,page_text/DRP-16473_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_10v-lrt0CQ2kkl8G7Y3AXjcCyCmsJDob1_view_usp_drivesdk_47f6d3416d.json,5c74e3dbed425510c4b0be4eddb6cc8ee8f767fa66e181eca052be7cb1950a9f,1115607,5,digital_text,"Clopidogrel is a white to oﬀ-white crystalline powder, Freely soluble in water and in methanol, practically insoluble in ether & cardioprotectant. Clopidogrel is chemically designated as Clopidogrel Bisulphate, (aS)- a -(2-Chlorophenyl) -6,7 - dihydrothieno,[3,2-C] pyridine - 5(4H) - acetic acid methyl ester. Its empirical formula is C₁₆H₁₆C1NO₂S.H₂SO₄, its molecular weight is 419.90 and its structural formula is: Clopidogrel (PLATIKON) It contains the following inactive ingredients: Lactose, Maize Starch, Povidone K-30, Magnesium Stearate, Sodium Benzoate, Puri␀ied Talc, Colloidal Anhydrous Silica, Croscarmellose Sodium, Sodium Starch Glycollate, Hydroxypropyl methyl cellulose, Titanium Dioxide, Polyethylene Glycol 400, Polyethylene Glycol 6000, Iso Propyl Alcohol, Dichloromethane, Col. Ferric Oxide Red & Puri␀ied water .",3,3,DESCRIPTION,"Prevention of atherothrombotic events Clopidogrel is indicated in: • Adult patients suﬀering from myocardial infarction (from a few days until less than 35 days), ischaemic stroke (from 7 days until less than 6 months) or established peripheral arterial disease. • Adult patients suﬀering from acute coronary syndrome: See package insert for complete information. “For suspected adverse drug reaction reportto the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. Seek medical attention immediately at the ﬁrst sign of any adverse drug reaction.” FDA Reg. No. : Mfg. Lic. No. : Batch No.: Mfg. Date: Exp. Date : 0 000000 000000 ANTITHROMBOTIC",1,1,INDICATION :,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:11:16.464884+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1651-06,Folic Acid,Folee,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1isuKTkORzyL9LQfpdBhMleKGBazFGHmj/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1651-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1isuKTkORzyL9LQfpdBhMleKGBazFGHmj_view_usp_drivesdk_4691946388.pdf,page_text/DRP-1651-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1isuKTkORzyL9LQfpdBhMleKGBazFGHmj_view_usp_drivesdk_4691946388.json,6387d14cf47d41a01b4ba5e0d40bb38dff01e7009f1dff2626ea77d8a5bde966,240551,1,ocr,"Large and continuous dosage folic acid may lower the blood A light yellow to yellow, 8 mm round, biconvex tablet, plain on both concentration of vitamin B12. Folic acid does not correct folate sides. deficiency due to dihydrofolate reductase inhibitors.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,It is used in the treatment and prevention of folate deficiency state. STORAGE CONDITION Also used in women of child-bearing potential and pregnant women Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. to protect against neural tube defects in their offspring. It is also Keep the product out of reach and sight of children. indicated for the treatment of megaloblastic anemia. CAUTION STATEMENT,1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T13:11:23.742923+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1652,Hyoscine-N-Butylbromide,Hyos,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gu-WbWrwn0-uloDI3V1iQqPQqSBqlKIj/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1652_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gu-WbWrwn0-uloDI3V1iQqPQqSBqlKIj_view_usp_drivesdk_035db1bb6a.pdf,page_text/DRP-1652_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gu-WbWrwn0-uloDI3V1iQqPQqSBqlKIj_view_usp_drivesdk_035db1bb6a.json,dad0a184e696acfca1348d3e3b1f4b86f52153a90e5a2b64341bf78e5e31bea3,787824,1,digital_text,"Hyoscine-N-butylbromide (Hyos®) 20 mg/mL Solution for Injection is a clear, colorless, sterile, aqueous solution free from extraneous matter in a 2 mL clear ampule. PHARMACODYNAMICS Hyoscine-N-butylbromide is a quaternary ammonium derivative of hyoscine. It relaxes the smooth muscles of the gastrointestinal, biliary and urinary tracts by blocking the action of acetylcholine. Hyoscine-N-butylbromide reduces the tone and peristalsis of smooth muscles in hollow organs with parasympathetic innervation. It has peripheral anticholinergic effects that are less pronounced and of shorter duration than those of atropine. It does not penetrate the blood-brain barrier contributing to its minimal central effects. PHARMACOKINETICS Hyoscine-N-butylbromide is rapidly distributed into the tissues after intravenous administration. It is partially metabolized in the liver to inactive compounds. The terminal elimination half-life is approximately 5 hours. Its main route of excretion is through the kidneys; total body clearance is 1.2 L/minute. The main metabolites found in the urine are poorly bound to muscarinic receptors. It is not known whether hyoscine-N-butylbromide is removed by peritoneal dialysis or hemodialysis.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION," For the symptomatic relief of :  Gastrointestinal and genitourinary disorders characterized by smooth muscle spasm  Spasm and dyskinesia of the biliary system  Irritable bowel syndrome (IBS)  As an aid to produce smooth muscle relaxation prior to radiological or other diagnostic procedures where spasm may be a problem (e.g., gastroduodenal endoscopy)",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:11:27.060586+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-16534,Ceftriaxone (as sodium),Swixo,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lNtSK4zyscK54agHGcAx5lufe0zvngfV/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-16534_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1lNtSK4zyscK54agHGcAx5lufe0zvngfV_view_usp_drivesdk_4307191fa3.pdf,page_text/DRP-16534_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1lNtSK4zyscK54agHGcAx5lufe0zvngfV_view_usp_drivesdk_4307191fa3.json,184e91d04e58b27c39cc9cff5e5457d609260c630ec77e3f369df2a7daf3f8d2,530922,3,digital_text,"Mechanism of action Ceftriaxone inhibits bacterial cell wall synthesis following attachment to penicillin binding proteins (PBPs). This results in the interruption of cell wall (peptidoglycan) biosynthesis, which leads to bacterial cell lysis and death. Resistance Bacterial resistance to ceftriaxone may be due to one or more of the following mechanisms: Amp C enzymes that may be induced or stably derepressed in certain aerobic Gram-negative bacterial species. Ceftriaxone (as sodium) 1 g Powder for Injection (I.M./I.V.) is a white to yellowish orange crystalline powder in glass vials.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Ceftriaxone is indicated in the treatment of the following infections in adults and children including term neonates (from birth): -Acute otitis media -Complicated skin and soft tissue infections -Bacterial endocarditis Ceftriaxone may also be used: For treatment of acute exacerbations of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease in adults In the management of neutropenic patients with fever that is suspected to be due to a bacterial infection For treatment of disseminated Lyme borreliosis (early (stage II) and late (stage III)) in adults and children including neonates from 15 days of age. In the treatment of patients with bacteraemia that occurs in association with, or is suspected to be associated with, any of the infections listed above Ceftriaxone should be co-administered with other antibacterial agents whenever the possible range of causative bacteria would not fall within its spectrum Consideration should be given to oﬃcial guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents. For Pre-operative prophylaxis of surgical site infections * In documented bacteraemia, the higher end of the recommended dose range should be considered. ** Twice daily (12 hourly) administration may be considered where doses greater than 2 g daily are administered. Acute otitis media Syphilis The generally recommended doses are 500 mg-1 g once daily increased to 2 g once daily for neurosyphilis for 10-14 days. The dose recommendations in syphilis, including neurosyphilis, are based on limited data. National or local guidance should be taken into consideration. Indications for adults and children over 12 years of age (≥ 50 kg) that require specific dosage schedules: 2 g once daily for 14-21 days. The recommended treatment durations vary and national or local guidelines should be taken into consideration. Paediatric population Neonates, infants and children 15 days to 12 years of age (< 50 kg) For children with bodyweight of 50 kg or more, the usual adult dosage should be given. Gonorrhoea Pre-operative prophylaxis of surgical site infections A single intramuscular dose of Ceftriaxone 1-2 g can be given. Limited data suggest that in cases where the patient is severely ill or previous therapy has failed, Ceftriaxone may be effective when given as an intramuscular dose of 1-2 g daily for 3 days. 500 mg as a single intramuscular dose. Disseminated Lyme borreliosis (early [Stage II] and late [Stage III]) 2 g as a single pre-operative dose. Indications for neonates, infants and children 15 days to 12 years (< 50 kg) that require specific dosage schedules: Syphilis The generally recommended doses are 75-100 mg/kg (max 4 g) once daily for 10-14 days. The dose recommendations in syphilis, including neurosyphilis, are based on very limited data. National or local guidance should be taken into consideration. Disseminated Lyme borreliosis (early [Stage II] and late [Stage III]) Acute otitis media * In documented bacteraemia, the higher end of the recommended dose range should be considered. ** Twice daily (12 hourly) administration may be considered where doses greater than 2 g daily are administered. 50–80 mg/kg once daily for 14-21 days. The recommended treatment durations vary and national or local guidelines should be taken into consideration. For initial treatment of acute otitis media, a single intramuscular dose of Ceftriaxone 50 mg/kg can be given. Limited data suggest that in cases where the child is severely ill or initial therapy has failed, Ceftriaxone may be effective when given as an intramuscular dose of 50 mg/kg daily for 3 days. Ceftriaxone is contraindicated in premature neonates up to a postmenstrual age of 41 weeks (gestational age + chronological age). Pre-operative prophylaxis of surgical site infections 50-80 mg/kg as a single pre-operative dose. Neonates 0-14 days Pre-operative prophylaxis of surgical site infections For initial treatment of acute otitis media, a single intramuscular dose of Ceftriaxone 50 mg/kg can be given. Indications for neonates 0-14 days that require specific dosage schedules: Acute otitis media Syphilis * In documented bacteraemia, the higher end of the recommended dose range should be considered. 20-50 mg/kg as a single pre-operative dose. The generally recommended dose is 50 mg/kg once daily for 10-14 days. The dose recommendations in syphilis, including neurosyphilis, are based on very limited data. National or local guidance should be taken into consideration. Duration of therapy A maximum daily dose of 50 mg/kg should not be exceeded. The duration of therapy varies according to the course of the disease. As with antibiotic therapy in general, administration of ceftriaxone should be continued for 48 - 72 hours after the patient has become afebrile or evidence of bacterial eradication has been achieved.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:11:30.408108+00:00
