PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-16753,Dapagliflozin (as propanediol monohydrate),Seren 5,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IEZC-pBjv-bHh48wELeLev131mjmz62V/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-16753_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IEZC-pBjv-bHh48wELeLev131mjmz62V_view_usp_drivesdk_1b4c4b8c1c.pdf,page_text/DRP-16753_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IEZC-pBjv-bHh48wELeLev131mjmz62V_view_usp_drivesdk_1b4c4b8c1c.json,f1870b74dfc7ad977f4adae747f646a5cd6993b23e99210421be24f2b00d1aa9,232302,2,digital_text,"SEREN 5: White to off white colored, round shaped, film coated tablets, plain on both side. SEREN 10: White to off white colored, oval shaped, film coated tablets, plain on both side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Dapagliflozin tablet is indicated for: • Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus: a. as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus b. to reduce the risk of hospitalization for heart failure in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus and established cardiovascular disease (CVD) or multiple cardiovascular (CV) risk factors. • Heart Failure It is indicated to reduce the risk of cardiovascular death and hospitalization for heart failure in adults with heart failure (NYHA class II-IV) with reduced ejection fraction. • Limitations of Use Dapagliflozin tablet is not recommended for patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus or for the treatment of diabetic ketoacidosis.,2,2,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:12:35.742334+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-16755,Salbutamol (as sulfate),none,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KVN3Vhr7pREJ-yE6vttZ5mIt7AL_JQ_Q/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-16755_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1KVN3Vhr7pREJ-yE6vttZ5mIt7AL_JQ_Q_view_usp_drivesdk_ea781b65c1.pdf,page_text/DRP-16755_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1KVN3Vhr7pREJ-yE6vttZ5mIt7AL_JQ_Q_view_usp_drivesdk_ea781b65c1.json,1603d4548edf2dc36487a9e35302bac148708f278d2f62535b234196826adf2c,186986,3,digital_text,"Salbutamol Nebulizer Solution is a solution of salbutamol sulfate in sodium chloride, sulfuric acid and water for injection.",1,1,2. Product Description,"Salbutamol Nebuliser Solution is indicated for use in the routine management of chronic bronchospasm unresponsive to conventional therapy, and in the treatment of acute severe asthma. 5. Recommended Dose Adults: 2.5mg-5mg of salbutamol is placed in the nebuliser and the patient allowed to inhale the nebulised solution until bronchodilation is achieved. This usually takes 3 -5 minutes. Some adult patients may require higher doses of salbutamol up to 10mg. Children: The minimum starting dosage for children under the age of 12 years is 2.5mg of salbutamol. The same mode of administration for intermittent administration is also applicable to children. Some children may, however, require higher doses of salbutamol up to 5mg. Intermittent treatment may be repeated up to four times daily.",1,1,4. Indication,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:12:39.011376+00:00
