PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1752,Ascorbic Acid,Cigla-Kas,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1igDpK777CUy_I_OQUznUlLbgiraHSpkG/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1752_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1igDpK777CUy_I_OQUznUlLbgiraHSpkG_view_usp_drivesdk_c6361baa88.pdf,page_text/DRP-1752_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1igDpK777CUy_I_OQUznUlLbgiraHSpkG_view_usp_drivesdk_c6361baa88.json,c4651b38874d060f01938276814f147d782fb73e9bafdc9dbaff26478617de27,268081,1,digital_text,"Cigla-Kas capsule contains Sodium Ascorbate , a sodium salt of Ascorbic Acid, which is a white to slightly yellow crystalline powder encapsulated in a size 0 hard gelatin, orange cap and orange body capsule. What is in the Medicine? This product contains Sodium ascorbate , a non -acidic form of Vitamin C . It is a cofactor of enzymes involved in the formation of collagen, the most abundant protein essential in the formation of teeth, bones, cartilage and skin. It also helps boost the immune system and increase body resistance to physical stress, common colds, viral and other type of infections. Strength of the Medicine: This product contains 533.4 mg of Ascorbic Acid as Sodium Ascorbate equivalent to 600 mg. What is this medicine used for? Sodium Ascorbate (Cigla-Kas) is used for the treatment and prevention of Vitamin C deficiency. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Sodium Ascorbate (Cigla-Kas) capsule should be taken with or without food. For daily maintenance – 1 to 2 capsules daily For cold symptoms – 2 to 3 capsules daily Or as prescribed by the physician. When should you NOT take this medicine? ● If you are allergic to any component of the product. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine ● Ask a doctor before use if you are on a sodium restricted diet. ● Do not take more than the recommended dose. ● Do not use after the expiry date on the label. What are the undesirable effects of this medicine? Sodium Ascorbate (Cigla-Kas) is usually well tolerated. Large doses are reported to cause diarrhea and other gastrointestinal disturbances. It has also been stated that large doses may result in hyperoxaluria. Tolerance may be induced with prolonged use of large doses, resulting in s ymptoms of deficiency when intake is reduced to normal. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine?  Desferrioxamine  Fluphenazine  Warfarin  Contraceptives What should you do if you miss a dose of this medicine? If you miss a dose, leave it out and take the next dose whenever it is due. After that, just carry on as before. Do not take a double dose. What are the signs and symptoms of overdose?  Large doses intake are reported to cause diarrhea and other gastrointestinal disturbances. What should you do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? Consult a doctor or contact a hospital immediately. Bring the container or label with you to help doctors with necessary information. How should you keep/ store this medicine? Keep out of reach and sight of children. Do not use Sodium Ascorbate capsule after the expiry date wh ich is stated on the label. It should be stored at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Keep in original container to protect from l ight. This should not be disposed of via wastewater or household waste. Ask your pharmacist how to dispose this expired medicine . These measures will help to protect the environment. When should you consult your doctor?  If any undesirable effect occurs.  If the patient is taking any vitamin or medicines. Name and Address of the Manufacturer and Marketing Authorization Holder: St. Martin Pharm Lab Co. 55 Lakandula Street, Parang, Marikina City, Philippines “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph” Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration Number: DRP-1752 Date of First Authorization/ Renewal of the Authorization: July 27, 2009 / July 27, 2027 Date of R evision of Patient Information Leaflet : September 16, 2022 ASCORBIC ACID [Page 2]",1,1,Description of the Product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T13:15:51.821398+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1762,Rosuvastatin (as calcium),Rovast,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/13S4HTs5yqigseZQzSkuFjiDz6pEKXT2S/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1762_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13S4HTs5yqigseZQzSkuFjiDz6pEKXT2S_view_usp_drivesdk_451d23877b.pdf,page_text/DRP-1762_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13S4HTs5yqigseZQzSkuFjiDz6pEKXT2S_view_usp_drivesdk_451d23877b.json,f42fddbbc1f5372e350fb53c2b2d23a74e6fd517d129be8fee721eb82e04ce37,133259,1,ocr,"ir/Pari PA levels Ritonavir Rosuvastatin (as calcium) (Rovast) 20 mg Film-coated Tablet is an old rose, round, biconvex, film-coated Elbasvir/Grazoprevir Do not exceed 10 mg once daily. Increased risk of myopathy and tablet, plain on both sides. rhabdomyolysis Sofosbuvir/Velpatasvir Glecaprevir/Pibrentasvir",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"INR monitoring prior to taking rosuvastatin, cessation and dosage adjustment of rosuvastatin therapy. Mar it of hyperlipid including primary hypercholesterolaemia (type tla), mixed dyslipidaemia (type IIb), and hypertriglyceridaemia {type IV). It may also be used in patients with",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T13:16:00.809188+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1791-03,Clopidogrel,Clopilar,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xTTyNgEe1g9UckKTC2dsuTUdehl1iJGn/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1791-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xTTyNgEe1g9UckKTC2dsuTUdehl1iJGn_view_usp_drivesdk_2eac6d725e.pdf,page_text/DRP-1791-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xTTyNgEe1g9UckKTC2dsuTUdehl1iJGn_view_usp_drivesdk_2eac6d725e.json,8e050477d4968e7e73d05553f22d06cf25f6ad302b183561d0addf3d7432346e,440818,1,digital_text,"Reddish brown coloured, round shaped, biconvex, film-coated tablet plain on both side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION :,"Clopidogrel is a thienopyridine antiplatelet drug used in thromboembolic disorders. It is an analogue of ticlopidine and acts by inhibiting adenosine diphosphate-mediated platelet aggregation. It is given prophylactically as an alternative to aspirin in patients at risk of thromboembolic disorders such as myocardial infarction , peripheral arterial disease, and stroke. Clopidogrel is also used with aspirin in the management of patients with unstable angina, as an adjunct to medical or interventional management.",1,1,INDICATIONS :,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:16:04.104195+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1796,Doxofylline,Maxivent,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/15Z8b6GzezDAEM-X5jiV0-_vbHQS_Vqo2/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1796_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15Z8b6GzezDAEM-X5jiV0-_vbHQS_Vqo2_view_usp_drivesdk_b1de5dbc44.pdf,page_text/DRP-1796_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15Z8b6GzezDAEM-X5jiV0-_vbHQS_Vqo2_view_usp_drivesdk_b1de5dbc44.json,3b4895609c9cb0b64daf9aa8367c5bbb6e667c96c567da21e21bfb761191da46,1647305,2,digital_text,"200mg - White to off white colored plain circular biconvex uncoated tablet. 400mg - White to off white colored, circular biconvex, uncoated tablet with breakline on one side and plain on other side. PHARMACODYNAMICS Doxofylline is a novel bronchodilator xanthine that differs from theophylline for the presence of a dioxalane group in position 7. Like theophylline, Doxofylline's mechanism of action is related to the inhibition of phosphodiesterase activities. However, differently from theophylline, Doxofylline appears to have decrease affinities towards adenosine A1 and A2 receptors, which may account for the better safety profile of the drug. PHARMACOKINETICS The half-life of Doxofylline is greater than six hours; so as to allow effective constant plasma levels with a t.i.d. dose regimen. Single dose pharmacokinetic studies in man after oral and intravenous administration defined distribution and absorption of the drug. After i.v. administration of 100 mg to 5 healthy volunteers, distribution of Doxofylline in plasma followed a bi- compartmental model. During the distribution phase the plasma AUC was only a modest portion of the total AUC; plasma clearance was somewhat high, ranging from 444 mL/min to 806 mL/min; apparent volume of distribution was about 1 L/kg. The mean half-life after i.v. administration was about 65 min. (from 40 min to 96 min). After oral administration (tablets), peak plasma levels were reached after one hour. Absolute bioavailability is about 62.6%; at pH 7.4 plasma proteins binding the compound is about 48%. Less than 4% of an orally administered dose is excreted unchanged in the urine. Doxofylline is almost completely metabolized in the liver (90% of the total drug clearance). Hydroxyethyltheophylline is the only detectable circulating metabolite of Doxofylline. After repeated administrations Doxofylline reaches the steady state in about 4 days; the elimination half-life during long-term treatment is 8-10 hours: this allows a twice-daily dose regimen. No accumulation of the drug was noted after one week of treatment.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Doxofylline is indicated for the treatment of bronchial asthma, pulmonary disease with spastic bronchial component and Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:16:07.932908+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-1822,Montelukast (as sodium) + Levocetirizine hydrochloride,Co-Altria,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1QKmIKh0sVajT2_UFCFwaOF-MlmdNy_Cl/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-1822_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QKmIKh0sVajT2_UFCFwaOF-MlmdNy_Cl_view_usp_drivesdk_3e68b5c462.pdf,page_text/DRP-1822_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QKmIKh0sVajT2_UFCFwaOF-MlmdNy_Cl_view_usp_drivesdk_3e68b5c462.json,ebc1e2320e91f012946776680e40de0a31ee3b245d54ab60a6cc40381a27a746,10592850,2,ocr,"Elimination Circular, flat, beveled edge, plain, uncoated bilayered tablets, of which one layer is light yellow to creamish yellow and the other The plasma half-life in adults is 7.9 + 1.9 hours. The half-life is shorter in small children. layer is light pink to pink coloured, with slight mottled appearance on both the layers. The mean apparent total body clearance in adults is 0.63 mL/min/kg. The major route of excretion of levocetirizine and metabolites is via urine, accounting for a",1,1,DESCRIPTION,mean of 85.4% of the dose. Excretion via feces accounts for only 12.9% of the dose. Levocetirizine is excreted both by glomerular filtration and active tubular secretion. Indicated for the relief of symptoms associated with seasonal and perennial allergic rhinitis.,1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T13:16:40.389152+00:00
