PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2002,Quinapril Hydrochloride,Accupril,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1U_J2EZ5VPwIWnwEfofVtcjsEe282Jyxb/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2002_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1U_J2EZ5VPwIWnwEfofVtcjsEe282Jyxb_view_usp_drivesdk_8e8ac2fa95.pdf,page_text/DRP-2002_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1U_J2EZ5VPwIWnwEfofVtcjsEe282Jyxb_view_usp_drivesdk_8e8ac2fa95.json,3a8bf5ef3571f947e1e5a276f09996d8e88722894fdc221dbc88636e0605c34e,269347,15,digital_text,"Quinapril hydrochloride is the salt of quinapril, the ethyl ester of a non-sulfhydryl, angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitor, quinaprilat. Quinapril hydrochloride is chemically described as [3S-[2[R*(R*)], 3R*]]-2-[2-[[1-(ethoxycarbonyl)- 3-phenylpropyl] amino]-1-oxopropyl]-1, 2, 3, 4-tetrahydro-3-isoquinolinecarboxylic acid, monohydrochloride. Its empirical formula is C25H30N2O5  HCl and its structural formula is Quinapril hydrochloride is a white to off-white amorphous powder, freely soluble in aqueous solvents with a melting point of 108 to 115°C. Quinapril hydrochloride (Accupril) 5 mg tablets are brown elliptical film-coated tablets with the dosage strength “5” embossed on one side, bisecting score and “PD 527” embossed on the other. Quinapril hydrochloride (Accupril) 10 mg tablets are reddish brown triangular biconvex film-coated tablets with bisecting score on both sides and debossing “10” on one side. Quinapril hydrochloride (Accupril) 20 mg tablets are reddish brown round film-coated tablets with the dosage strength “20” debossed on one side and bisecting score and “PD 532” debossed on the other.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Hypertension Quinapril Viewed on: Sunday, July 7, 2024 - 10:33:15 PM Eastern Time [Page 2] 2 Quinapril is indicated for the treatment of hypertension. Quinapril is effective as monotherapy or concomitantly with thiazide diuretics and beta-blockers in patients with hypertension. Congestive Heart Failure Quinapril is effective in the treatment of congestive heart failure when given concomitantly with a diuretic and/or cardiac glycoside.",1,2,4.1. Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:21:55.075390+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2009,Diltiazem Hydrochloride,Dilzem OD,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mgSBPJuR3icHNjnCWGs1mcCziNpPCkwA/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2009_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mgSBPJuR3icHNjnCWGs1mcCziNpPCkwA_view_usp_drivesdk_ac6e322efc.pdf,page_text/DRP-2009_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mgSBPJuR3icHNjnCWGs1mcCziNpPCkwA_view_usp_drivesdk_ac6e322efc.json,6711cd2eb2a49c8d229335a34e203e0bad986f2b1cd726b54c79f654d18617d1,232877,12,digital_text,"Diltiazem hydrochloride is a calcium ion influx inhibitor (slow channel blocker or calcium antagonist). Chemically, diltiazem hydrochloride is 1, 5-benzothiazepin-4(5H) one, 3- (acetyloxy)-5-[2-(dimethylamino)-ethyl]-2-3-dihydro-2-(4-methoxyphenyl), - monohydrochloride, (+)-cis-. Its empirical formula is C22H26N2O4S.HCl. The chemical structure is: MW = 450.98 Diltiazem hydrochloride is a white to off-white crystalline powder with a bitter taste. It is soluble in water, methanol, and chloroform.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"A. ORAL Unstable Angina Pectoris including Angina Due to Coronary Artery Spasm or Following Myocardial Infarction Diltiazem is indicated for the treatment of angina pectoris due to coronary artery spasm. Diltiazem has been shown to be effective in the treatment of spontaneous coronary artery DILTIAZEM HCL Viewed on: Thursday, May 16, 2024 - 10:43:42 PM Eastern Time [Page 2] 2 spasm presenting as Prinzmetal’s variant angina (resting angina with ST-segment elevation occurring during attacks). Chronic Stable Angina (Classic Effort-associated Angina) Diltiazem is indicated for the management of chronic stable angina in patients who cannot tolerate therapy with beta-blockers and/or nitrates or who remain symptomatic despite adequate doses of these agents. Hypertension Diltiazem is indicated for the treatment of hypertension. It may be used alone or in combination with other antihypertensive medications, such as diuretics. Kidney Transplantation Diltiazem is indicated for the prevention of graft failure following kidney transplantation. Diltiazem is indicated for the reduction of ciclosporin A nephrotoxicity during immunosuppressive therapy after kidney transplantation.",1,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:21:58.245246+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-201,Cefalexin (as Monohydrate),Diacef,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VWes4nfxoBF1sf3Zmw7g8bgvrVcEyDVl/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-201_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VWes4nfxoBF1sf3Zmw7g8bgvrVcEyDVl_view_usp_drivesdk_a0106ab656.pdf,page_text/DRP-201_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VWes4nfxoBF1sf3Zmw7g8bgvrVcEyDVl_view_usp_drivesdk_a0106ab656.json,2c2cb7ea5025f722f6f1d8edc16c5dab89a3a1fb914f4a8dd416896ce2c5568e,1343380,1,ocr,(CEPHALOSPORIN) Cefalexin (DIACEF) is a fine white powder which becomes a light pink suspension with a strawberry flavor when reconstituted with water.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of the respiratory, gastrointestinal and urinary tract infections, as well as otic, bone, skin and soft tissues, including penicillinase producing Staphylococcus aureus infection.",1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T13:22:06.216076+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2010,Diltiazem Hydrochloride,Dilzem,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wHhMt54HyCLCIJxQk32yk-kJ0VsvEdBQ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2010_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wHhMt54HyCLCIJxQk32yk-kJ0VsvEdBQ_view_usp_drivesdk_0ae554d24c.pdf,page_text/DRP-2010_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wHhMt54HyCLCIJxQk32yk-kJ0VsvEdBQ_view_usp_drivesdk_0ae554d24c.json,6711cd2eb2a49c8d229335a34e203e0bad986f2b1cd726b54c79f654d18617d1,232877,12,digital_text,"Diltiazem hydrochloride is a calcium ion influx inhibitor (slow channel blocker or calcium antagonist). Chemically, diltiazem hydrochloride is 1, 5-benzothiazepin-4(5H) one, 3- (acetyloxy)-5-[2-(dimethylamino)-ethyl]-2-3-dihydro-2-(4-methoxyphenyl), - monohydrochloride, (+)-cis-. Its empirical formula is C22H26N2O4S.HCl. The chemical structure is: MW = 450.98 Diltiazem hydrochloride is a white to off-white crystalline powder with a bitter taste. It is soluble in water, methanol, and chloroform.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"A. ORAL Unstable Angina Pectoris including Angina Due to Coronary Artery Spasm or Following Myocardial Infarction Diltiazem is indicated for the treatment of angina pectoris due to coronary artery spasm. Diltiazem has been shown to be effective in the treatment of spontaneous coronary artery DILTIAZEM HCL Viewed on: Thursday, May 16, 2024 - 10:43:42 PM Eastern Time [Page 2] 2 spasm presenting as Prinzmetal’s variant angina (resting angina with ST-segment elevation occurring during attacks). Chronic Stable Angina (Classic Effort-associated Angina) Diltiazem is indicated for the management of chronic stable angina in patients who cannot tolerate therapy with beta-blockers and/or nitrates or who remain symptomatic despite adequate doses of these agents. Hypertension Diltiazem is indicated for the treatment of hypertension. It may be used alone or in combination with other antihypertensive medications, such as diuretics. Kidney Transplantation Diltiazem is indicated for the prevention of graft failure following kidney transplantation. Diltiazem is indicated for the reduction of ciclosporin A nephrotoxicity during immunosuppressive therapy after kidney transplantation.",1,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:22:09.507074+00:00
