PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2052-01,Celecoxib,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ocMl6kGuM6IzO9fP3oFQP9tpypMaJveO/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2052-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ocMl6kGuM6IzO9fP3oFQP9tpypMaJveO_view_usp_drivesdk_55bf3a1c2b.pdf,page_text/DRP-2052-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ocMl6kGuM6IzO9fP3oFQP9tpypMaJveO_view_usp_drivesdk_55bf3a1c2b.json,024bac3e2db1397b98bd786c26ccb806f8bf9f20403e1415a84285b4230f44d1,268228,26,digital_text,"Celecoxib is chemically designated as 4-[5-(4-methylphenyl)-3-(trifluoromethyl)-1H- pyrazol-1-yl] benzenesulfonamide and is a diaryl-substituted pyrazole. It has the following chemical structure: CH3 NN CF3 S NH2 O O The empirical formula for celecoxib is C17H14F3N3O2S, and the molecular weight is 381.38.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,1) Symptomatic treatment of osteoarthritis (OA) and rheumatoid arthritis (RA) 2) Relief of signs and symptoms of ankylosing spondylitis (AS) 3) Management of acute pain 4) For the treatment of primary dysmenorrhea 5) For acute and chronic low back pain,2,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:24:38.126769+00:00
