PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2065,Rosuvastatin (as calcium),Rosucol,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/16KnaR4aTor-OBko-ZuOROi6KuVL4hiiw/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2065_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_16KnaR4aTor-OBko-ZuOROi6KuVL4hiiw_view_usp_drivesdk_cee7ca04c6.pdf,page_text/DRP-2065_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_16KnaR4aTor-OBko-ZuOROi6KuVL4hiiw_view_usp_drivesdk_cee7ca04c6.json,9aa34667170b8948c1583d12003e8b42722e0f22b681ec7b080cc9915af93ff7,1957670,2,digital_text,"5mg - White to off-white coloured, circular, biconvex, film-coated tablets, plain on both sides. 10mg - Light pink to pink coloured, circular, biconvex, film-coated tablets, plain on both sides. 20mg - White to off-white coloured, circular, biconvex, film-coated tablets, plain on both sides. s. Pregnant and nursing women. PHARMACODYNAMICS PHARMACOKINETICS Each film-coated tablet contains: As As radio-labeled dose is in vitro CrCl2 CrCl > 80 mL/min/1.73m semi-annually ≥ 65 Front Size: 150 x 160 mm 5mg Film-Coated Tablet 10mg Film-Coated Tablet 20mg Film-Coated Tablet HMG CoA Reductase Inhibitor",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Rosuvastatin is indicated: a.) As an adjunct to diet to reduce elevated total-C, LDL-C, ApoB, non-HDL-C, and TG levels and to increase HDL-C in patients with primary hypercholesterolemia (excluding heterozygous familial and nonfamilial hypercholesterolemia) and mixed dyslipidemia (Fredrickson Type IIa and IIb). b.) As an adjunct to diet for the treatment of patients with elevated serum TG levels (Fredrickson Type IV). c.) To reduce LDL-C, total-C, and ApoB in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia as an adjunct to other lipid-lowering treatments (e.g., LDL apheresis) or if such treatments are unavailable.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:24:47.059631+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-207,Amoxicillin (as trihydrate),Axmel,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IYxkwHE7_VOS_C7Y5y-tVmgnoq8r5_ZK/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-207_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IYxkwHE7_VOS_C7Y5y-tVmgnoq8r5_ZK_view_usp_drivesdk_990d2d18b7.pdf,page_text/DRP-207_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IYxkwHE7_VOS_C7Y5y-tVmgnoq8r5_ZK_view_usp_drivesdk_990d2d18b7.json,8d882cda85d7c4fc2f314325fd328f540c1f0d6505faeb535a3e74e69d63c051,483882,1,digital_text,Amoxicillin (Axmel) 500 mg Capsule is a white to yellowish white powder contained in a red/white hard gelatin capsule. Amoxicillin (Axmel) 250 mg Capsule is a white to yellowish white powder contained in a red/white hard gelatin capsule. Amoxicillin (Axmel) 250 mg/5 mL Powder for Suspension is a white to yellowish white powder and light yellow suspension upon reconstitution with characteristic of pineapple ﬂavor. Amoxicillin (Axmel) 125 mg/5 mL Powder for Suspension is a white to yellowish white powder and light yellow to yellow suspension upon reconstitution with characteristic of pineapple ﬂavor. Amoxicillin (Axmel) 100 mg/mL Powder for Suspension (Oral Drops) is a white to yellowish white powder and a very light yellow to light yellow suspension upon reconstitution with characteristic of pineapple ﬂavor.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,For the treatment of infections caused by susceptible strains of Gram-positive and Gram-negative microorganisms. • Acute bacterial sinusitis • Acute otitis media • Acute streptococcal tonsillitis and pharyngitis • Acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis • Community acquired pneumonia • Acute cystitis • Asymptomatic bacteriuria in pregnancy • Acute pyelonephritis • Typhoid and paratyphoid fever • Dental abscess with spreading cellulitis • Prosthetic joint infections • Helicobacter pylori eradication,1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:24:50.584237+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2072,Sildenafil (as citrate),Viagra,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_NktzESieR-rH6FBf5ZT7bOkT9SWsCVw/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2072_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_NktzESieR-rH6FBf5ZT7bOkT9SWsCVw_view_usp_drivesdk_54caed0f7e.pdf,page_text/DRP-2072_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_NktzESieR-rH6FBf5ZT7bOkT9SWsCVw_view_usp_drivesdk_54caed0f7e.json,a6448e5eb818348678365ee6215a9d9a008a9cb95cea2042aaa065fd5a9075b5,4908595,15,digital_text_and_ocr,"Manufactured by: Fareva Amboise Zone Industrielle 29 route des Industries, 37530 Poce Sur Cisse, France Marketing Authorization Holder:",14,14,prescription.,"Use of sildenafil is contraindicated in patients with a known hypersensitivity to any component of the tablet including microcrystalline cellulose, calcium hydrogen phosphate, croscarmellose sodium, magnesium stearate, hydroxypropyl methylcellulose, titanium dioxide, lactose, triacetin, and FD & C Blue #2 aluminum lake. Sildenafil was shown to potentiate the hypotensive effects of acute and chronic nitrates, and its administration to patients who are concurrently using nitric oxide donors, organic nitrates or organic nitrites in any form either regularly or intermittently is therefore contraindicated (see Section 4.5 Interaction with Other Medicinal Products and Other Forms of Interaction). The co-administration of PDES inhibitors, including sildenafil, with guanylate cyclase stimulators, such as riociguat, is contraindicated as it may potentially lead to symptomatic hypotension. 4.4",3,3,Contraindications,low,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T13:25:30.422482+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2072,Sildenafil (as citrate),Viagra,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vC4ks4Z22CSrrTVlNgEjwV0e0Km9PBSq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2072_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vC4ks4Z22CSrrTVlNgEjwV0e0Km9PBSq_view_usp_drivesdk_f64c281edc.pdf,page_text/DRP-2072_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vC4ks4Z22CSrrTVlNgEjwV0e0Km9PBSq_view_usp_drivesdk_f64c281edc.json,63d0e05eac69317d5956cb1af48afe76691ff621955b9d3b19947849364c7f4f,1172821,2,digital_text,"Sildenafil, as citrate (Viagra®), an oral therapy for erectile dysfunction, is the citrate salt of sildenafil, a selective inhibitor of cyclic guanosine monophosphate (cGMP)‑specific phosphodiesterase type 5 (PDE5). Sildenafil citrate is designated chemically as 1‑[[3‑(6,7‑dihydro‑1‑methyl‑7‑oxo‑3‑propyl‑1H‑ pyrazolo[4,3‑d]pyrimidin‑5‑yl)‑4‑ethoxyphenyl]sulfonyl]‑ 4‑methylpiperazine citrate and has the following structural formula: Sildenafil citrate is a white to off‑white crystalline powder with a solubility of 3.5 mg/mL in water and a molecular weight of 666.7.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Sildenafil is indicated for the treatment of erectile dysfunction, which is the inability to achieve or maintain a penile erection sufficient for satisfactory sexual performance. In order for sildenafil to be effective, sexual stimulation is required.",1,1,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:25:34.252924+00:00
