PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2073-01,Sildenafil (as Citrate),None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JMJgdR5smDOU0HXAs3EJ8NDkmKCkegYb/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2073-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1JMJgdR5smDOU0HXAs3EJ8NDkmKCkegYb_view_usp_drivesdk_8e17a38570.pdf,page_text/DRP-2073-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1JMJgdR5smDOU0HXAs3EJ8NDkmKCkegYb_view_usp_drivesdk_8e17a38570.json,f7afef6ba35c59412259c2619b50c23da7f5a685c0ab130bbf6d03f212f2ed0c,178188,15,digital_text,Pregabalin is a gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA) analogue (S)-3-(aminomethyl)-5- methylhexanoic acid) with an empirical formula of C8H17NO2 and molecular weight of 159.23. The molecular structure of pregabalin is:,1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Neuropathic Pain Pregabalin is indicated for the treatment of neuropathic pain in adults, including neuropathic pain associated with spinal cord injury. Epilepsy Pregabalin is indicated as adjunctive therapy in adults with partial seizures, with or without secondary generalization. Generalized Anxiety Disorder Pregabalin is indicated for the treatment of Generalized Anxiety Disorder (GAD) in adults. Fibromyalgia Pregabalin is indicated for the management of fibromyalgia. PREGABALIN [Page 2] 2",1,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:25:37.908736+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2074,Mefenamic Acid,PonstanÂ® SF 250,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FIPd-M9Kz5CjfzdViHaAAvXTzwTd7oZH/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2074_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FIPd-M9Kz5CjfzdViHaAAvXTzwTd7oZH_view_usp_drivesdk_ffb34ecb9f.pdf,page_text/DRP-2074_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FIPd-M9Kz5CjfzdViHaAAvXTzwTd7oZH_view_usp_drivesdk_ffb34ecb9f.json,cd053e20584c1aabda9bf0ef30a179de12da917fa31f81fac3bc36eb02689561,94306,4,digital_text,"Mefenamic acid (Ponstan® SF 250) is available in hard gelatin capsule with scarlet opaque body imprinted with “Ponstan SF 250” in white and scarlet opaque cap imprinted with “SF” in white, containing white to slightly off-white powder. It is in blister of 10’s in boxes of 200’s. 3.0 WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Mefenamic acid (Ponstan® SF 250) is a non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) used to relieve pain (analgesic) and swelling (anti-inflammatory). Each capsule contains 250 mg of Mefenamic acid. 4.0 STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE 250 mg 5.0 WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Mefenamic acid (Ponstan® SF 250) is used to relieve various types of pain such as: • headache • body aches (rheumatoid arthritis [including Still's Disease]), osteoarthritis • muscle and joint pains • toothache • sprains • painful menstruation (dysmenorrhea) • trauma-related pains 6.0 HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Undesirable effects may be minimized by using the minimum effective dose for the shortest duration necessary to control symptoms. For adults and children over 14 years old, take one to two capsules initially, then one capsule three times a day, as needed, preferably taken with food. 7.0 WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Ask your doctor before using this product if you: • are allergic to Mefenamic Acid or any components of this product such as lactose, gelatin, sodium lauryl sulfate, purified water, corn starch, corn starch pregelatinized, methyl cellulose, microcrystalline cellulose, silicon dioxide, magnesium stearate, polyethylene glycol, polysorbate 80, saccharin sodium, vanillin, opaspray yellow, wax candelilla FCC powder, veegum, povidone, sodium hydroxide, glucono delta lactone, hydrochloric acid, sorbitol solution, sodium benzoate, sodium carboxymethylcellulose granulated sugar, artificial banana flavor, anise mint flavor, alcohol and chocolate flavor • are allergic to other NSAIDs or aspirin [Page 2] 2 • have previous or active peptic ulcer or chronic gastrointestinal tract inflammation • have liver disease or kidney disease • have heart disease • have hyperacidity • have history of asthma or develop asthma attacks due to other medicines 8.0 CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Mefenamic Acid (Ponstan® SF 250) should not be taken continuously b eyond seven days except on the advice of the doctor. Taking NSAIDs for very long periods of time or in very high doses increases the risk of stomach irritation, bleeding, as well as other side effects and should be done only under medical supervision. Consult your doctor if you: • develop any signs and/or symptoms of serious cardiovascular toxicity • have high blood pressure • have diarrhea or serious gastrointestinal side effects (inflammation, bleeding, ulceration, perforation) • develop skin rash, mucosal lesions, or any other sign of hypersensitivity • are taking other medications • are having difficulties conceiving or undergoing investigation of infertility • are pregnant or nursing a baby 9.0 UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Stop taking Mefenamic acid immediately if the following potential side effects occur: • loose bowel movement, nausea with or without vomiting, upset stomach, peptic ulcer, gastrointestinal tract inflammatory o r bleeding, mild liver toxicity or any o ther stomach/liver problems • blurred vision, nervousness, dizziness, drowsiness, insomnia, headache, aseptic meningitis • eye irritation, loss of color vision • skin reactions: rash or skin itching, excessive perspiration, edema, drug reaction with eosinophilia and systemic symptoms (DRESS syndrome), exfoliative dermatitis, Stevens-Johnson syndrome, toxic epidermal necrolysis (Lyell's syndrome), and generalized bullous fixed drug eruption (GBFDE) • ear pain • asthma, difficulty in breathing • cardiovascular events (irregular heartbeat, high/low blood pressure) • blood problems • kidney and urinary problems including related test results such as urobilinogen urine (false-positive), liver function test abnormal • abnormally low body temperature in children Consult your doctor if any of these side effects occur. Elderly i ndividuals are more prone to side effects, therefore, report all side effects to your doctor immediately. 10.0 WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Mefenamic Acid (Ponstan® SF 250) may interact with the following medications: • Antiplatelet or Acetylsalicylic acid (e.g. Aspirin) [Page 3] 3 • Other nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs • Corticosteroids • Anti-coagulants • Diuretics or other anti-hypertensives • Hypoglycemic agents • Methotrexate • Lithium • Tacrolimus • Cyclosporine If you are taking or about to take any of the above medications, consult your doctor first before using mefenamic acid. 11.0 WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Not applicable. 12.0 SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE You may e xperience seizures, acute renal failure, coma, confusional state, dizziness, and hallucination. 13.0 WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? In case of accidental overdosage, call for emergency help immediately. Patients should be managed by symptomatic and supportive care following an overdose. There are no specific antidotes. 14.0 HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. 15.0 WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? Consult your doctor if: • before using this product, if you have any conditions mentioned in section 7.0 When should you not take this medicine? and section 8.0 Care that should be taken when taking this medicine. • you experience any of the side effects mentioned in section 9.0 Undesirable effects of this medicine. • you are taking or about to take any of the medications mentioned in section 10.0 What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? • you experience an overdosage. • you have any questions about using this product. 16.0 FDA REGISTRATION NUMBER Mefenamic acid (Ponstan® SF) 250 mg capsule: DRP-2074 17.0 DATE OF FIRST AUTHORIZATION/RENEWAL OF THE AUTHORIZATION Mefenamic acid (Ponstan® SF) 250 mg Capsule: 20 August 1964 Keep out of reach of children. For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph [Page 4] 4 Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Manufactured by: Interphil Laboratories, Inc. Canlubang Industrial Estate Bo. Pittland, Cabuyao, Laguna Marketing Authorization Holder: Pfizer, Inc. 19F-20F, 8 Rockwell Building, Hidalgo Drive, Rockwell Center, Poblacion, Makati City 1210 Metro Manila, Philippines Under authority of PFIZER, INC., New York, N.Y., USA Revision No.: 6.0 Revision date: 06 July 2023 Reference: CDS version 17.0/LPD version 14.0 Reference Date: 31 May 2023/06 July 2023 [Page 5]",1,4,2.0 DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T13:26:22.781084+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-208,Paracetamol,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/19qHTJSKdVFtIxByFaHqJMElhl2hATWK_/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-208_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19qHTJSKdVFtIxByFaHqJMElhl2hATWK__view_usp_drivesdk_c051dacc3d.pdf,page_text/DRP-208_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19qHTJSKdVFtIxByFaHqJMElhl2hATWK__view_usp_drivesdk_c051dacc3d.json,2bab2effab830f3acf970b27601af6b9d940e933a32d46112b8dd3e80f21a445,1629129,1,ocr,"Paracetamol is a clear red syrupy, strawberry flavored syrup.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Painful conditions including headache, migraine, bodyache, earache, toothache, dysmenorrhea, neuralgia, arthralgia and post- operative pain. Also indicated for fever due to common colds, influenza, measles, teething discomforts and post vaccination reactions, respiratory as well as urinary tract infections.",1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T13:26:32.449138+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2082-02,Levofloxacin (as hemihydrate),Loxeva,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1E9cvP26wMSsiv1azLCM-PXyTIzwYYKv0/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2082-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1E9cvP26wMSsiv1azLCM-PXyTIzwYYKv0_view_usp_drivesdk_8ea387d7a2.pdf,page_text/DRP-2082-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1E9cvP26wMSsiv1azLCM-PXyTIzwYYKv0_view_usp_drivesdk_8ea387d7a2.json,846c3482dfddae8fb7e9d6c2b009b918be74215b934d6a40a78bac684c1d1145,1841870,2,digital_text,"Levofloxacin is a fluoroquinolone antimicrobial available for intravenous administration. It is the optically active L-isomer of ofloxacin. Clinically levofloxacin, a chiral fluorinated carboxyquinolone, is the pure enantiomer of the racemic drug substance ofloxacin. Antibacterial Spectrum Levofloxacin has in vitro activity against a wide range of gram-negative and gram-positive microorganism as well as against typical pathogens and certain non-spore forming anaerobes. Levofloxacin has been shown to be active against most strains of the following microorganism both in vitro and in clinical",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"Levofloxacin solution for infusion is indicated in adults for the treatment of the following infections: • Community-acquired pneumonia • Complicated skin and soft tissue infections In complicated skin and soft tissue infections, levofloxacin should be used only when it is considered inappropriate to use other antibacterial agents that are commonly recommended for the treatment of these infections. • Acute pyelonephritis and complicated urinary tract infections • Chronic bacterial prostatitis • Inhalation anthrax: post-exposure prophylaxis and curative treatment Consideration should be given to official guidance on the appropriate use of antibacterial agents.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:26:36.857746+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2092,Mefenamic Acid,Ponstan,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1G13Pe-z9V1cfs-kKg5h25iyO0ZRtlwMp/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2092_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1G13Pe-z9V1cfs-kKg5h25iyO0ZRtlwMp_view_usp_drivesdk_1138183e4a.pdf,page_text/DRP-2092_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1G13Pe-z9V1cfs-kKg5h25iyO0ZRtlwMp_view_usp_drivesdk_1138183e4a.json,64f9c6c9c54339a7ba2c76466ac886aabbbd28d16fe9c388cc166e0f0e31a650,114396,10,digital_text,"Mefenamic acid is N-(2,3,-xylyl)-anthranilic acid. It is an orally active analgesic agent. The structure for mefenamic acid is: NH COOH CH3 CH3 It is a white powder with a melting point of 230°C -231°C, molecular weight of 241.28, and water solubility of 0.004% at pH 7.1. Mefenamic acid (Ponstan SF) 500 mg Capsule: Red opaque body, yellow opaque cap imprinted with “Parke Davis” and “Ponstan SF 500 mg” in black. Mefenamic acid (Ponstan) 500 mg Tablet: Elliptical, smooth yellow film-coated tablet.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,Mefenamic acid (Ponstan) is indicated for: MEFENAMIC ACID,1,1,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:26:43.759423+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2092-01,Mefenamic Acid,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RzFZJ2rxVFBY5k4Ex2wu7TfXWjzs6p2F/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2092-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RzFZJ2rxVFBY5k4Ex2wu7TfXWjzs6p2F_view_usp_drivesdk_baf14e53fc.pdf,page_text/DRP-2092-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RzFZJ2rxVFBY5k4Ex2wu7TfXWjzs6p2F_view_usp_drivesdk_baf14e53fc.json,a3bc584f206838bd260cc060315f41516af6012c422602a27b9388cd6abc4229,176881,12,digital_text,"Mefenamic acid is N-(2,3,-xylyl)-anthranilic acid. It is an orally active analgesic agent. The structure for mefenamic acid is: NH COOH CH3 CH3 It is a white powder with a melting point of 230°C-231°C, molecular weight of 241.28, and water solubility of 0.004% at pH 7.1. Rhea Mefenamic acid 500 mg tablet is elliptical, smooth yellow film coated tablet.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,Mefenamic acid is indicated for:,1,1,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:26:40.035891+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2095,Sunitinib malate,Sutent,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/18Xo06LEISX6ymrnpxXha-qjp6uVGDdNh/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2095_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18Xo06LEISX6ymrnpxXha-qjp6uVGDdNh_view_usp_drivesdk_2899518a28.pdf,page_text/DRP-2095_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18Xo06LEISX6ymrnpxXha-qjp6uVGDdNh_view_usp_drivesdk_2899518a28.json,f29b849328b38d4bb58cce6dc224166756b6a3807de6794390fc0a8140f21c2b,568911,31,digital_text,"Sunitinib malate (SUTENT), an oral multi-kinase inhibitor targeting several receptor tyrosine kinases (RTK), is the malate salt of sunitinib. Sunitinib malate is described chemically as Butanedioic acid, hydroxy-, (2S)-, compound with N-[2-(diethylamino) ethyl]-5-[(Z)-(5- fluoro-1, 2-dihydro-2-oxo-3H-indol-3-ylidine) methyl]-2, 4-dimethyl-1H-pyrrole-3- carboxamide (1:1). The molecular formula is C22H27FN4O2C4H6O5 and the molecular weight is 532.6 Daltons. The chemical structure of sunitinib malate is: N H N H CH3 CH3 F O N H O N CH3 CH3 OH H HO2C",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,Sunitinib is indicated for the treatment of gastrointestinal stromal tumor (GIST) after failure of imatinib mesylate treatment due to resistance or intolerance (see Section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic Properties). Sunitinib is indicated for the treatment of treatment-naïve advanced and/or metastatic renal cell carcinoma (MRCC) (see Section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic Properties). Sunitinib is indicated for the treatment of advanced and/or MRCC after failure of cytokine-based therapy (see Section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic Properties). Sunitinib is indicated for the treatment of unresectable or metastatic; well-differentiated pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors (pNET) with disease progression (see Section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic Properties).,2,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:26:49.145771+00:00
