PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2098,Sunitinib malate,Sutent,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/188ZfC8c1G6sTc3GMsxbGkydT64_YFiVt/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2098_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_188ZfC8c1G6sTc3GMsxbGkydT64_YFiVt_view_usp_drivesdk_0bb080ed0e.pdf,page_text/DRP-2098_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_188ZfC8c1G6sTc3GMsxbGkydT64_YFiVt_view_usp_drivesdk_0bb080ed0e.json,f29b849328b38d4bb58cce6dc224166756b6a3807de6794390fc0a8140f21c2b,568911,31,digital_text,"Sunitinib malate (SUTENT), an oral multi-kinase inhibitor targeting several receptor tyrosine kinases (RTK), is the malate salt of sunitinib. Sunitinib malate is described chemically as Butanedioic acid, hydroxy-, (2S)-, compound with N-[2-(diethylamino) ethyl]-5-[(Z)-(5- fluoro-1, 2-dihydro-2-oxo-3H-indol-3-ylidine) methyl]-2, 4-dimethyl-1H-pyrrole-3- carboxamide (1:1). The molecular formula is C22H27FN4O2C4H6O5 and the molecular weight is 532.6 Daltons. The chemical structure of sunitinib malate is: N H N H CH3 CH3 F O N H O N CH3 CH3 OH H HO2C",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,Sunitinib is indicated for the treatment of gastrointestinal stromal tumor (GIST) after failure of imatinib mesylate treatment due to resistance or intolerance (see Section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic Properties). Sunitinib is indicated for the treatment of treatment-naïve advanced and/or metastatic renal cell carcinoma (MRCC) (see Section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic Properties). Sunitinib is indicated for the treatment of advanced and/or MRCC after failure of cytokine-based therapy (see Section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic Properties). Sunitinib is indicated for the treatment of unresectable or metastatic; well-differentiated pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors (pNET) with disease progression (see Section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic Properties).,2,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:26:58.076884+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2099,Mefenamic Acid,Ponstan Sf,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-CUKvxpNVouHipKokYaB2t2R1CAATIAy/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2099_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-CUKvxpNVouHipKokYaB2t2R1CAATIAy_view_usp_drivesdk_485ad22a6d.pdf,page_text/DRP-2099_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-CUKvxpNVouHipKokYaB2t2R1CAATIAy_view_usp_drivesdk_485ad22a6d.json,64f9c6c9c54339a7ba2c76466ac886aabbbd28d16fe9c388cc166e0f0e31a650,114396,10,digital_text,"Mefenamic acid is N-(2,3,-xylyl)-anthranilic acid. It is an orally active analgesic agent. The structure for mefenamic acid is: NH COOH CH3 CH3 It is a white powder with a melting point of 230°C -231°C, molecular weight of 241.28, and water solubility of 0.004% at pH 7.1. Mefenamic acid (Ponstan SF) 500 mg Capsule: Red opaque body, yellow opaque cap imprinted with “Parke Davis” and “Ponstan SF 500 mg” in black. Mefenamic acid (Ponstan) 500 mg Tablet: Elliptical, smooth yellow film-coated tablet.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,Mefenamic acid (Ponstan) is indicated for: MEFENAMIC ACID,1,1,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:27:01.740637+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2100,Diltiazem Hydrochloride,Dilzem,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1pyThEp_jAblsegkJUH65JUuuwVH1h2YD/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2100_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1pyThEp_jAblsegkJUH65JUuuwVH1h2YD_view_usp_drivesdk_ed5116e5a0.pdf,page_text/DRP-2100_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1pyThEp_jAblsegkJUH65JUuuwVH1h2YD_view_usp_drivesdk_ed5116e5a0.json,6711cd2eb2a49c8d229335a34e203e0bad986f2b1cd726b54c79f654d18617d1,232877,12,digital_text,"Diltiazem hydrochloride is a calcium ion influx inhibitor (slow channel blocker or calcium antagonist). Chemically, diltiazem hydrochloride is 1, 5-benzothiazepin-4(5H) one, 3- (acetyloxy)-5-[2-(dimethylamino)-ethyl]-2-3-dihydro-2-(4-methoxyphenyl), - monohydrochloride, (+)-cis-. Its empirical formula is C22H26N2O4S.HCl. The chemical structure is: MW = 450.98 Diltiazem hydrochloride is a white to off-white crystalline powder with a bitter taste. It is soluble in water, methanol, and chloroform.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"A. ORAL Unstable Angina Pectoris including Angina Due to Coronary Artery Spasm or Following Myocardial Infarction Diltiazem is indicated for the treatment of angina pectoris due to coronary artery spasm. Diltiazem has been shown to be effective in the treatment of spontaneous coronary artery DILTIAZEM HCL Viewed on: Thursday, May 16, 2024 - 10:43:42 PM Eastern Time [Page 2] 2 spasm presenting as Prinzmetal’s variant angina (resting angina with ST-segment elevation occurring during attacks). Chronic Stable Angina (Classic Effort-associated Angina) Diltiazem is indicated for the management of chronic stable angina in patients who cannot tolerate therapy with beta-blockers and/or nitrates or who remain symptomatic despite adequate doses of these agents. Hypertension Diltiazem is indicated for the treatment of hypertension. It may be used alone or in combination with other antihypertensive medications, such as diuretics. Kidney Transplantation Diltiazem is indicated for the prevention of graft failure following kidney transplantation. Diltiazem is indicated for the reduction of ciclosporin A nephrotoxicity during immunosuppressive therapy after kidney transplantation.",1,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:27:04.711801+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2105,Gemfibrozil,Lopid OD,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lRy-MPQJ8N5ccCMlUlnQEbCRnp3sbtVy/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2105_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1lRy-MPQJ8N5ccCMlUlnQEbCRnp3sbtVy_view_usp_drivesdk_5f26805403.pdf,page_text/DRP-2105_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1lRy-MPQJ8N5ccCMlUlnQEbCRnp3sbtVy_view_usp_drivesdk_5f26805403.json,a6b06a3bbe17fb3bcd822bfe2424b7cb6fa6f47b8f0ceb7fcac72b8705dba3a0,2499946,10,ocr,"Gemfibrozil (Lopid OD) 900 mg tablet is a white, oval, biconvex film-coated tablet. Gemfibrozil is a non-halogenated phenoxypentanoic acid with the following structural",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Gemfibrozil is a lipid-regulating agent that is indicated for the following: 1. Primary prevention of coronary heart disease (CHD) and myocardial infarction (MI) in patients with hypercholesterolemia, mixed dyslipidemia and hypertriglyceridemia, Fredrickson's classification types Ila, IIb, and IV. Viewed on: Monday, February 26, 2024 - 10:03:57 AM Eastern Time [Page 2] 2. Treatment of other dyslipidemias: a. Fredrickson types III and V b. Associated with diabetes c. Associated with xanthomata 3. Treatment of adult patients with elevated levels of serum triglycerides (types IV and V hyperlipidemia) who present a risk of pancreatitis and do not respond adequately to a determined dietary effort to control them.",1,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T13:27:32.440026+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2108,Fexofenadine Hydrochloride,Telfast,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1EmNvSp96BYGTRc26Y1Y3TygaXzRAewCd/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2108_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1EmNvSp96BYGTRc26Y1Y3TygaXzRAewCd_view_usp_drivesdk_df6debe817.pdf,page_text/DRP-2108_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1EmNvSp96BYGTRc26Y1Y3TygaXzRAewCd_view_usp_drivesdk_df6debe817.json,bb2c3c41a8fdcfdaffb366eba21816c88a908cf84a4cceccb4b21ea321e75e5f,553735,1,digital_text,"Peach, capsule-shaped, debossed film-coated tablet For suspected adverse drug reactions, report to www.fda.gov.ph and CHCPV@sanofi.com. Patients should seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. By reporting side effects, you can help provide more information on the safety of this product. [Page 2]",1,1,Product Description,For the relief of symptoms associated with chronic idiopathic urticaria in adults and children 12 years of age and older. For the treatment of seasonal and perennial allergic rhinitis.,1,1,Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:27:35.859548+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2109,Fexofenadine Hydrochloride,Telfast,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HiSVxZ_BDCMMYaao3zqIMVOzj0IGAIsp/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2109_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HiSVxZ_BDCMMYaao3zqIMVOzj0IGAIsp_view_usp_drivesdk_660024d6d0.pdf,page_text/DRP-2109_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HiSVxZ_BDCMMYaao3zqIMVOzj0IGAIsp_view_usp_drivesdk_660024d6d0.json,bb2c3c41a8fdcfdaffb366eba21816c88a908cf84a4cceccb4b21ea321e75e5f,553735,1,digital_text,"Peach, capsule-shaped, debossed film-coated tablet For suspected adverse drug reactions, report to www.fda.gov.ph and CHCPV@sanofi.com. Patients should seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. By reporting side effects, you can help provide more information on the safety of this product. [Page 2]",1,1,Product Description,For the relief of symptoms associated with chronic idiopathic urticaria in adults and children 12 years of age and older. For the treatment of seasonal and perennial allergic rhinitis.,1,1,Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:27:38.633364+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2111-01,Amlodipine (As Besilate),Eurovasc-5,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Rbt0Y60j-sWs9sCizXrI2dAr0eYNyshU/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2111-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Rbt0Y60j-sWs9sCizXrI2dAr0eYNyshU_view_usp_drivesdk_b8afc1a32d.pdf,page_text/DRP-2111-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Rbt0Y60j-sWs9sCizXrI2dAr0eYNyshU_view_usp_drivesdk_b8afc1a32d.json,f12901d2853cb381e65172894e4c8fc3a9f0baa8c0814703bf5bef226a62b85a,583352,1,digital_text,"PHARMACODYNAMICS Exertional Angina: In patients with exertional angina, Amlodipine reduces the total peripheral resistance (afterload) against which the heart works and reduces the rate pressure product, and thus myocardial oxygen demand, at any given level of exercise. White to off white, round flat tablets with break line on one side. The precise mechanisms by which Amlodipine relieves angina have not been fully delineated, but are thought to include the following:",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Amlodipine may be used alone or in combination with other antianginal agents. Elimination After oral administration of therapeutic doses, Amlodipine is well absorbed with peak blood levels between 6-12 hours post dose. Absorption of Amlodipine is not influenced by concomitant food intake. Absolute bioavailability of the unchanged active substance is estimated to be 64-80%. Peak plasma levels are reached 6-12 hours after administration. The volume of distribution is approximately 21 L/kg. The pKa of Amlodipine is 8.6. Hypertension Vasospastic Angina (Prinzmetal’s or Variant Angina) Grapefruit Juice Co-administration of 240 mL of grapefruit juice with a single oral dose of Amlodipine 10 mg in 20 healthy volunteers had no significant effect on the pharmacokinetics of Amlodipine. Cimetidine Co-administration of Amlodipine with cimetidine did not alter the pharmacokinetics of Amlodipine. Co-administration of a magnesium and aluminum hydroxide antacid with a single dose of Amlodipine had no significant effect on the pharmacokinetics of Amlodipine. Sildenafil A single 100 mg dose of sildenafil in subjects with essential hypertension had no effect on the pharmacokinetic parameters of Amlodipine. When Amlodipine and sildenafil were used in combination, each agent independently exerted its own blood pressure lowering effect. Magnesium and Aluminum Hydroxide Antacid Fertility",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:27:42.213960+00:00
