PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2219-02,None,Amlodipine (As Besilate),PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1SrmfDlciNzsHbpWDErgN0DEQa7TlB9Jq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2219-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1SrmfDlciNzsHbpWDErgN0DEQa7TlB9Jq_view_usp_drivesdk_5168ef9c0f.pdf,page_text/DRP-2219-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1SrmfDlciNzsHbpWDErgN0DEQa7TlB9Jq_view_usp_drivesdk_5168ef9c0f.json,76380e3995bdfb66ebc6880987793f489486dd32a04a1b8395d8745db00b14ed,577766,1,digital_text,"White to off-white colored, round shaped, biconvex, uncoated tablets with both sides plain. PROPERTIES Amlodipine besilate is the besilate salt of Amlodipine, a long-acting calcium channel blocker. Amlodipine besilate is chemically described as 3-Ethyl-5-methyl (±)-2-[(2-aminoethoxy) methyl]-4-(2- chlorophenyl)-1,4-dihydro-6-methyl-3,5-pyridinedicarboxylate, m o n o b e n z e n e s u l p h o n a te . I t s e m p i r i c a l f o r m u l a i s C H ClN O .C H O S, and the molecular weight is 567.1.20 25 2 5 6 6 3 The structural formula is as shown: CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,For the treatment of hypertension and prophylaxis of Angina.,1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:35:39.021234+00:00
