iety of Hospital Pharmacists. ASHP technical assistance bulletin on handling cytotoxic and hazardous drugs. Am J Hosp Pharm. 1990;47:1033- 1049. 8. Controlling occupational exposure to hazardous drugs. (OSHA Work-Practice Guidelines.) Am J Health-Syst Pharm. 1996;53:1669-1685. 5. Clinical Oncological Society of Australia. Guidelines and recommendations for safe handling of antineoplastics agents. Med J Aust. 1983; 1; 426-428. Manufactured by:",2,2,prescription.,,1,1,INDICATIONS & USAGE,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T13:35:49.263121+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2251-04,Loratadine,Godine,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IDPEA-uVrnXWvNEtnmSinSyQUDy1XrLY/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2251-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IDPEA-uVrnXWvNEtnmSinSyQUDy1XrLY_view_usp_drivesdk_e6b41f4c56.pdf,page_text/DRP-2251-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IDPEA-uVrnXWvNEtnmSinSyQUDy1XrLY_view_usp_drivesdk_e6b41f4c56.json,7a74986bb9e0eabe22d5c6d6a6ef93357fef7d5118c5d176bac4cf4a63a860c1,164188,1,digital_text,"White, round, plain, uncoated tablet, scored on one side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Effects on ability to drive and use machines In clinical studies that assessed driving ability, no impairment was observed in patients receiving loratadine. Loratadine Tablets has no or negligible influence on the ability to drive and use machines. However, patients should be informed that very rarely some people experience drowsiness, which may affect their ability to drive or use machines.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:37:05.271773+00:00
