Ia or Iib hyperlipoproteinemias), hypertriglyceridaemia (Type IV), and dysbetalipoproteinemia (Type III) and also can be effective as adjunct therapy in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia who have some LDL-receptor function.",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:37:31.591224+00:00
