PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2258,Metoclopramide Hydrochloride,Myclosil,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1i-A1ImobrQZ9BVVPdVX7gfZmlTiP_UUT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2258_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1i-A1ImobrQZ9BVVPdVX7gfZmlTiP_UUT_view_usp_drivesdk_4d43ce9f64.pdf,page_text/DRP-2258_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1i-A1ImobrQZ9BVVPdVX7gfZmlTiP_UUT_view_usp_drivesdk_4d43ce9f64.json,19c8b679c31961d9ecc2da4f1235696b54c5e48e05ae2c302b7ddb836db8411f,90616,1,digital_text,"Metoclopramide (Myclosil) 10 mg Tablet is a 6 mm, light blue mottled, round, ﬂat, beveled, plain on both sides tablet. Metoclopramide (Myclosil) 5 mg/5 mL Syrup is a clear, colorless to pale yellow liquid with characteristic of menthol and orange.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"It is used in disorders of decreased gastrointestinal motility such as gastroparesis or ileus in gastro- esophageal reﬂux disease and dyspepsia and in nausea and vomiting associated with various gastro- intestinal disorders, with migraine, following surgery, and with cancer therapy. It may also be used to stimulate gastric emptying during radiographic examinations, to facilitate intubation of the small bowel, and in the management of aspiration syndromes.",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:38:16.784661+00:00
