ta are described in Undesirable effects, pharmacodynamic properties, and pharmacokinetic properties but no recommendation on a posology can be made. Other pharmaceutical forms/strengths may be more appropriate for this population. Method of administration Atorvastatin is for oral administration. Each daily dose of atorvastatin is given all at once and may be given at any time of day with or without food.",1,3,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Hypercholesterolaemia Atorvastatin is indicated as an adjunct to diet for reduction of elevated total cholesterol (total-C), LDL- cholesterol (LDL-C), apolipoprotein B, and triglycerides in adults, adolescents and children aged 10 years or older with primary hypercholesterolaemia including familial hypercholesterolaemia (heterozygous variant) or combined (mixed) hyperlipidaemia (corresponding to Types IIa and IIb of the Fredrickson classification) when response to diet and other nonpharmacological measures is inadequate. Atorvastatin is also indicated to reduce total-C and LDL-C in adults with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia as an adjunct to other lipid-lowering treatments (e.g. LDL apheresis) or if such treatments are unavailable. Prevention of cardiovascular disease Prevention of cardiovascular events in adult patients estimated to have a high risk for a first cardiovascular event (see Pharmacodynamic properties), as an adjunct to correction of other risk factors.",1,1,Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:38:47.351798+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2288-03,Simvastatin,Cardiosim,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fDRn7j-J-ujpOvNXRRgNygfxt9W5nPM_/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2288-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1fDRn7j-J-ujpOvNXRRgNygfxt9W5nPM__view_usp_drivesdk_0ed51dcfb0.pdf,page_text/DRP-2288-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1fDRn7j-J-ujpOvNXRRgNygfxt9W5nPM__view_usp_drivesdk_0ed51dcfb0.json,ff15e983c19443930b29855924a5c71519e61b62f450c78ee5eb9edf772f5d9d,475351,1,digital_text,"A brown coloured, round, biconvex, film-coated tablet plain on both sides. PHARMACODYNAMICS Interactions with lipid-lowering medicinal products that can cause myopathy when given alone. Effects of other medicinal products on Simvastatin Simvastatin is a substrate of cytochrome P450 3A4. Potent inhibitors of cytochrome P450 3A4 increase the risk of myopathy and rhabdomyolysis by increasing the concentration of HMG-CoA reductase inhibitory activity in plasma during Simvastatin therapy. Such inhibitors include itraconazole, ketoconazole, posaconazole, voriconazole, erythromycin, clarithromycin, telithromycin, HIV protease inhibitors (e.g., nelfinavir), boceprevir, telaprevir, nefazodone and medicinal products containing cobicistat. Concomitant administration of itraconazole resulted in a more than 10-fold increase in exposure to Simvastatin acid (the active beta-hydroxyacid metabolite). Telithromycin caused an 11-fold increase in exposure to Simvastatin acid.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Posology Hypercholesterolemia PHARMACOKINETICS The risk of myopathy, including rhabdomyolysis, is increased during concomitant administration with fibrates. Additionally, there is a pharmacokinetic interaction with gemfibrozil resulting in increased Simvastatin plasma levels. When Simvastatin and fenofibrate are given concomitantly, there is no evidence that the risk of myopathy exceeds the sum of the individual risks of each agent. Adequate pharmacovigilance and pharmacokinetic data are not available for other fibrates. Rare cases of myopathy / rhabdomyolysis have been associated with Simvastatin co-administered with lipid- modifying doses (≥ 1 g/day) of niacin. Prescribing recommendations for interacting agents are summarized in the table below. Interactions involving inhibitors of CYP3A4 Combination with itraconazole, ketoconazole, posaconazole, voriconazole, HIV protease inhibitors (e.g., nelfinavir), boceprevir, telaprevir, erythromycin, clarithromycin, telithromycin, nefazodone and medicinal products containing cobicistat is contraindicated, as well as gemfibrozil, ciclosporin, and danazol. If treatment with potent CYP3A4 inhibitors (agents that increase AUC approximately 5 fold or greater) is unavoidable, therapy with Simvastatin must be suspended (and use of an alternative statin considered) during the course of treatment. Caution should be exercised when combining Simvastatin with certain other less potent CYP3A4 inhibitors: fluconazole, verapamil, or diltiazem. Treatment of primary or secondary lipid disorders, secondary prevention of coronary artery disease; primary prevention in patients at high risk for coronary artery disease.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:38:50.298935+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2304-01,Amlodipine (As Besilate) + Atorvastatin (As Calcium),Amlitor Forte,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Zw0M5DrefK8wdNFCMGP-WwvMh1zdcZIw/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2304-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Zw0M5DrefK8wdNFCMGP-WwvMh1zdcZIw_view_usp_drivesdk_8f87b19982.pdf,page_text/DRP-2304-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Zw0M5DrefK8wdNFCMGP-WwvMh1zdcZIw_view_usp_drivesdk_8f87b19982.json,b0f18d94de3a616a982eddd1cd15db59cb0eb4b153a1770f7d1dc08734f53e87,520943,1,digital_text,A white coloured round shaped biconvex film-coated tablet plain on both sides.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,For the treatment of patients with cardiovascular risk due to concomitant hypertension and dyslipidemia.,1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:38:53.429823+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-231,Cefalexin (as monohydrate),Exel,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/18zt-tJJWyaMFNdq70KRxzxZBUhGI2A1m/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-231_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18zt-tJJWyaMFNdq70KRxzxZBUhGI2A1m_view_usp_drivesdk_2bedc6c5c4.pdf,page_text/DRP-231_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18zt-tJJWyaMFNdq70KRxzxZBUhGI2A1m_view_usp_drivesdk_2bedc6c5c4.json,85acfc9bbbdd00a7f1a47637f4e18af3b678d3b8f6cb8135db334a0764a16aa3,79358,1,digital_text,"Cefalexin (Exel) 500 mg Capsule is a white to oﬀ-white crystalline powder contained in gray/yellow rich hard gelatin capsule. Cefalexin (Exel) 250 mg Capsule is a white to oﬀ-white powder contained in scarlet/gray hard gelatin capsule. Cefalexin (Exel) 250 mg/5 mL Powder for Suspension is a white to oﬀ-white powder, and very light to light orange suspension upon reconstitution, orange ﬂavored, and with characteristic odor. Cefalexin (Exel) 125 mg/5 mL Powder for Suspension is a white to white-cream powder, and light orange to orange suspension upon reconstitution, orange ﬂavored and with characteristic odor. Cefalexin (Exel) 100 mg/mL Powder for Suspension (Oral Drops) is a white to oﬀ- white powder, peach to light orange suspension upon reconstitution, orange ﬂavored and with characteristic odor.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"the following conditions, when caused by susceptible bacteria. Respiratory tract infections, Acute and chronic bronchitis and infected bronchiectasis. Ear, nose and throat infections: Otitis media, mastoiditis, sinusitis, follicular tonsillitis and pharyngitis. Urinary tract infections: Acute and chronic pyelonephritis, cystitis and prostatitis. Prophylaxis of recurrent urinary tract infection. Gynaecological and obstetric infections Skin, soft -tissue and bone infections. DOSAGE AND MODE OF",1,1,INDICATION: It is indicated for treatment of,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:38:56.518228+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2313,Multivitamins + Minerals + Ginseng,Ginsovit,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1B5FwkyH6xVUjjZ5idIV4h3UkOqlIu8lR/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2313_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1B5FwkyH6xVUjjZ5idIV4h3UkOqlIu8lR_view_usp_drivesdk_2e427aa70b.pdf,page_text/DRP-2313_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1B5FwkyH6xVUjjZ5idIV4h3UkOqlIu8lR_view_usp_drivesdk_2e427aa70b.json,98df91c649276b781a1e1971e38386235fee0e821d887e11ace4538bcab348eb,424067,1,digital_text,"Black, oblong soft gelatin capsules containing yellowish brown paste.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Multivitamins + Minerals + Ginseng is recommended in the following conditions: 1. Reduced physical and mental efficiency, fatigue, exhaustion, inability to concentrate or sleep, irritability. 2. Stressful conditions like convalescence from prolonged illness, debility, physical and mental stress and chronic alcohol intake. 3. As an adjunct to specific therapy in diabetes mellitus, tuberculosis and other chronic diseases. 4. Mineral deficiency states.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:39:00.474147+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2320,Iron (III) Hydroxide Polymaltose Complex,Ferium,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/110yD3is3w-BWdQNb66831QRdtVbL_LqV/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2320_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_110yD3is3w-BWdQNb66831QRdtVbL_LqV_view_usp_drivesdk_8fddc6c717.pdf,page_text/DRP-2320_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_110yD3is3w-BWdQNb66831QRdtVbL_LqV_view_usp_drivesdk_8fddc6c717.json,5bf83dfb625ee918cfe1af8bd25999b18e57bdc49d424fffe3d711cbd23f7437,6305620,5,digital_text,,,,,"All cases of Iron deficiency anemia as in pregnancy, lactation, childhood and post surgical condition. Sapcode Store at temperature notO exceeding 25 C. Shake well before use. Iron (III) - Hydroxide Polymaltose Complex Ferium® RX 50 mg/5 mL Syrup ANTI-ANEMIC Imported and Distributed by: Emcure Pharma Philippines Inc. Frabelle Business Center, 111 Rada Street, Legaspi Village, Makati City, Metro Manila, Philippines Manufactured by: Emcure Pharmaceuticals Ltd. Lane No. 3, Phase-II, SIDCO, Bari-Brahmana, Jammu - 181 133, India. ® Registered Trade Mark Owners. DOSAGE: Adults (15 yrs. & above) 5 mL (1 teaspoonful) 2-3 x daily Children (5-12 yrs.) 5 mL (1 teaspoonful) 1-2 x daily Or as prescribed by the physician.",2,2,INDICATION:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T13:39:05.455686+00:00
