PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2420-02,Metronidazole,DYMETRAZOLE,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IgXievIt4AZyP-j_TnDlQ7lOjmiTKfzM/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2420-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IgXievIt4AZyP-j_TnDlQ7lOjmiTKfzM_view_usp_drivesdk_c1d483054d.pdf,page_text/DRP-2420-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IgXievIt4AZyP-j_TnDlQ7lOjmiTKfzM_view_usp_drivesdk_c1d483054d.json,ef6078dca574092fe335d6a049bb8d96f472dfbbf78646afd9aa97fe1acd924d,1610160,1,ocr,"When given with alcohol, metronidazole may provok a disulfiram-like reaction in some patients. Acute psychosis or confusion have been associated with the use of metronidazole and disulfiram together. Metronidazole (Dymetrazole) is a white to off-white, round and viconvex tablet with around 12.00 mm diameter. Dymetrazole is Metronidazole 2-methyl-5-nitroimidazole-1-ethanol; 1-(2-h H 1)-2-methyl-5- nit 3 Metronidazole is reported to impair the metabolism or excretion of several drugs including wartafin and phenytoin, or C6H9N3O3 with molecular weight of 171.16. lithium, ciclosporin, and fluorouracil, with the consequent potential for an increased incidence of adverse effects.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"For the of ic and trichomoniasis, infections due to susceptible anaerobic bacteria, Single oral doses of metronidazole, up to 12 g, have been reported in suicide attempts and accidental overdoses. Symptoms reported include nausea, vomiting, and ataxia. Oral metronidazole has been studied as a radiation sensitizer intestinal and hepatic amoebiasis and giardiasis. on the treatment of malignant tumors. Neurotoxic effects including seizures and peripheral neurpathy have been",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T13:40:45.780824+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2423,Digoxin,Digox,PI_02,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UcPA08rIIyK3tph7_Aj82q8mRlmnA4t-/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2423_PI_02_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UcPA08rIIyK3tph7_Aj82q8mRlmnA4t-_view_usp_drivesdk_34bfae8c3d.pdf,page_text/DRP-2423_PI_02_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UcPA08rIIyK3tph7_Aj82q8mRlmnA4t-_view_usp_drivesdk_34bfae8c3d.json,6a41dc88053a1b822a679d5323115f3c46b0e91127e6a442c28d6a477b41073c,2026978,2,ocr,"White to off-white, round, biconvex, uncoated tablet, plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Digoxin is a cardiac glycoside used in the management of supraventricular arrhythmias, particularly atrial fibrillation, and in heart failure. The principal actions of Digoxin are an increase in the force of myocardial contraction (positive inotropic activity) and a reduction in the conductivity of the heart, particularly in conduction through the atrioventricular (AV) node. Digoxin also has a direct action on vascular smooth muscle and indirect effects mediated primarily by the autonomic nervous system, and particularly by an increase in vagal activity. These are also reflex alterations in autonomic activity due to the effects on the circulation. Overall, these actions result in positive inotropic effects, and decreased AV nodal activity.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T13:40:58.772324+00:00
