cid, Dose of allopurinol should be at the lower end of the recommended dose schedule. Ifurate nephropathy or other pathology has compromised renal function, the advice given in Renal impairment should be followed. These steps may reduce the risk of xanthine andlor oxipurinol deposition complicating the clinical situation (See Interactions with other medicinal products and Undesirable effects). Monitoring advice The dose should be adjusted by monitoring serum urate concentrations and urinary urate/uric acid levels at appropriate intervals. Method and duration of treatment Allopurinol may be taken orally once a day after a meal If the daily dose exceeds 300 mg and gastrointestinal intolerance is evident, a divided doses regimen may be appropriate.",1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"-All forms of hyperuricaemia not controllable by diet, including secondary hyperuricaemia of differing origin and clinical complications of hyperuricaemic states, particularly manifest gout, urate nephropathy and for the dissolution and prevention of uric acid stone The management of recurrent mixed calcium oxalate stones in concurrent hyperuricaemia, when fluid, dietary and similar measures have failed. Children and adolescents Secondary hyperuricaemia of differing origin Uric acid nephropathy during treatment of leukaemia Hereditary enzyme deficiency disorders, Lesch-Nyhan syndrome (partial or total hyp thi gt defi and adenine transferase deficiency",1,1,heapeutic indications,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T13:42:32.299217+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2457,Sodium Fusidate,Fuson,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gffDlbws6h_qgpD3lrdNW8ZvdRN4xn0j/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2457_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gffDlbws6h_qgpD3lrdNW8ZvdRN4xn0j_view_usp_drivesdk_4be474467d.pdf,page_text/DRP-2457_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gffDlbws6h_qgpD3lrdNW8ZvdRN4xn0j_view_usp_drivesdk_4be474467d.json,18586f3d5b97adad347f98776d7298e53284ea18e8e0e655c0654e6663d64f72,3851781,1,ocr,,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"instance a child of this particular age group is unlikely to ingest a whole tube of Sodium Fusidate ointment. The concentration of the excipients is too low to constitute a safety risk. Sodium Fusidate is indicated, either alone or in combination with systemic therapy, in the treatment of skin infections caused by Staphylococci,",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T13:42:42.729291+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2458,Fusidic Acid,Fuson,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1a81MrfKGaG_VefPRDX6Iqn4lF-seOMcg/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2458_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1a81MrfKGaG_VefPRDX6Iqn4lF-seOMcg_view_usp_drivesdk_ee06a4d1a5.pdf,page_text/DRP-2458_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1a81MrfKGaG_VefPRDX6Iqn4lF-seOMcg_view_usp_drivesdk_ee06a4d1a5.json,eed73dc318a3b81ac30a00c2eac62da916d376f5d95afeabf14224c85142c7e3,832403,1,digital_text,,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Fusidic Acid is indicated, either alone or in combination with systemic therapy, in the treatment of skin infections caused by .Staphylococci Fusidic acid 20 mg/g cream contains butylhydroxyanisole, cetyl alcohol and potassium sorbate which may cause local skin reactions (e.g. contact dermatitis). Butylhydroxyanisole may also cause irritation to the eyes and mucous membranes.",1,1,INDICATION:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T13:42:54.731627+00:00
