PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2460,Piperacillin (As Sodium) + Tazobactam (As Sodium),Pizobac,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1eXAlAsRzv18aqNpFW_s00oXVH1XqlM4m/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2460_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eXAlAsRzv18aqNpFW_s00oXVH1XqlM4m_view_usp_drivesdk_394e028ec1.pdf,page_text/DRP-2460_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eXAlAsRzv18aqNpFW_s00oXVH1XqlM4m_view_usp_drivesdk_394e028ec1.json,9806560f3e92f699943e8f54bb63bf3e5e6a40529cccba4fe97af7ae289f851a,10501238,2,ocr,"2.25 g, 4.5 g : White or almost white cryodesiccated powder in a colorless vial.",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Piperacillin+Tazobactam is indicated for treatment of the following systemic and/or local bacterial infections in which susceptible organisms have been detected or are suspected Adults and the Elderly: Lower respiratory tract infections Urinary tract infections (complicated and uncomplicated) Intra-abdominal infections Skin and skin structure infections Bacterial septicaemia Bacterial infections in neutropenic adults in combination with an aminoglycoside Children: Bacterial infections in neutropenic children in combination with an aminoglycoside. Appendicitis complicated by rupture with peritonitis and/or abscess formation in children aged 2-12 years. Susceptible strains of microorganisms would include: 1) Non-penicillinase-producing strains - Gram-positive cocci: Penicillin-susceptible streptococcus, Streptococcus pneumoniae, Enterococcus faecium, Non- penicillinase-producing Staphylococcus - Gram-negative cocci: Neisseria meningitidis, Non- -lactamase-producing Neisseria gonorrhoeae - Gram-positive bacilli: Listeria monocytogenes, Erysipelothrix rhusiopathiae, Corynebacterium species Gram-negative bacilli: Non-penicillinase-producing Escherichia coli, Salmonella, Shigella dysenteriae, Proteus mirabilis, Enterobacter, Citrobacter, Serratia 2) Non-penicillinase-producing Haemophilus influenzae 3) Non- -lactamase-producing strains Anaerobe gram-positive microorganisms: Peptostreptococcus, Clostridium, Actinomyces, Propionibacterium, Eubacterium Anaerobe gram-negative microorganisms: Veillonella 4) Pericillinase producing strains Methicillin-susceptible staphyolococcus, Haemophilus influenzae, Moraxella catarrhalis, Neisseria gonorrhoeae, Bacteroides fragilis, Enterobacter",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T13:43:13.948269+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2461,Piperacillin (as Sodium) + Tazobactam (as Sodium),Pizobac,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mgfs-0DbgyXW4B7A-wn-lmubS12Y0Yzf/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2461_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mgfs-0DbgyXW4B7A-wn-lmubS12Y0Yzf_view_usp_drivesdk_4038c8235a.pdf,page_text/DRP-2461_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mgfs-0DbgyXW4B7A-wn-lmubS12Y0Yzf_view_usp_drivesdk_4038c8235a.json,9806560f3e92f699943e8f54bb63bf3e5e6a40529cccba4fe97af7ae289f851a,10501238,2,ocr,"2.25 g, 4.5 g : White or almost white cryodesiccated powder in a colorless vial.",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Piperacillin+Tazobactam is indicated for treatment of the following systemic and/or local bacterial infections in which susceptible organisms have been detected or are suspected Adults and the Elderly: Lower respiratory tract infections Urinary tract infections (complicated and uncomplicated) Intra-abdominal infections Skin and skin structure infections Bacterial septicaemia Bacterial infections in neutropenic adults in combination with an aminoglycoside Children: Bacterial infections in neutropenic children in combination with an aminoglycoside. Appendicitis complicated by rupture with peritonitis and/or abscess formation in children aged 2-12 years. Susceptible strains of microorganisms would include: 1) Non-penicillinase-producing strains - Gram-positive cocci: Penicillin-susceptible streptococcus, Streptococcus pneumoniae, Enterococcus faecium, Non- penicillinase-producing Staphylococcus - Gram-negative cocci: Neisseria meningitidis, Non- -lactamase-producing Neisseria gonorrhoeae - Gram-positive bacilli: Listeria monocytogenes, Erysipelothrix rhusiopathiae, Corynebacterium species Gram-negative bacilli: Non-penicillinase-producing Escherichia coli, Salmonella, Shigella dysenteriae, Proteus mirabilis, Enterobacter, Citrobacter, Serratia 2) Non-penicillinase-producing Haemophilus influenzae 3) Non- -lactamase-producing strains Anaerobe gram-positive microorganisms: Peptostreptococcus, Clostridium, Actinomyces, Propionibacterium, Eubacterium Anaerobe gram-negative microorganisms: Veillonella 4) Pericillinase producing strains Methicillin-susceptible staphyolococcus, Haemophilus influenzae, Moraxella catarrhalis, Neisseria gonorrhoeae, Bacteroides fragilis, Enterobacter",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T13:43:31.561667+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2465,Co-Amoxiclav,Pencla,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1miBqEpMdRq15L3bfoq0kWhqTHc0S17kG/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2465_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1miBqEpMdRq15L3bfoq0kWhqTHc0S17kG_view_usp_drivesdk_cbecccd4a7.pdf,page_text/DRP-2465_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1miBqEpMdRq15L3bfoq0kWhqTHc0S17kG_view_usp_drivesdk_cbecccd4a7.json,4bc7d68ef1acd2eab511cd7f76c0a216f51d5e03647d2dc84b26d403a2458469,9850296,2,ocr,"White or almost-white, oval film-coated tablet, scored on one side engraved with “KI” and “I” “AMC” on the other side PHARMACOKINETICS Amoxicillin is resistant to inactivation by gastric acid. It is more rapidly and more completely absorbed than ampicillin when given by mouth. Peak plasma-amoxicillin concentrations of about 5 micrograms/mL have been observed 1 to 2 hours after a dose of 250 mg, with detectable amounts present for up to 8 hours. Doubling the dose can double the concentration. The presence of food in the stomach does not appear to diminish the total amount absorbed. About 20% is bound to plasma proteins and plasma half-lives of 1 to 1.5 hours have been reported. The half-life may be prolonged in neonates, the elderly, and patients with renal impairment the half-life may be 7 to 20 hours. Amoxicillin is widely distributed at varying concentrations in body tissues and fluids. It crosses the placenta; small amounts are distributed into breast milk. Little amoxicillin passes into the CSF unless the meninges are inflamed Amoxicillin is metabolized to a limited extent to penicilloic acid which is excreted in the urine About 60% of an oral dose of amoxicillin is excreted unchanged in the urine in 6 hours by glomerular filtration and tubular secretion. Urinary concentrations above 300 mcg/mL have been reported after a dose of 250 mg,",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Co-amoxiclav is indicated for use in the treatment of infections caused by susceptible strains of microorganisms involved in the following: Acute and chronic bronchitis, pneumonia, lung abscess, tonsillitis, sinusitis, otitis media, cystitis urethritis, pyelonephritis, septic abortion, puerperal sepsis, chancroid, furunculosis, cellulitis, wound infection, intra-abdominal sepsis, osteomyelitis, and post-operative infections. Urinary tract infections. Susceptible strains of microorganisms would include: *Staphylococcus aureus, *Staphylococcus epidermidis, Streptococcus pneumoniae, Streptococcus. pyogenes, Viridans group Streptococcus, *Enterococcus faecalis, *Enterococcus faecium, Corynebacterium spp., *Bacillus anthracis, Listeria monocytogenes, Clostridium spp., Peptococcus spp., Peptostre ptococcus spp. “Escherichia coli, “Proteus mirabilis, “Proteus vulgaris, *Klebsiella spp., “Salmonella spp., *Shigella spp Bordetella pertussis, *Yersinia enterocolitica, G ardnerella vaginalis, Brucella spp., *Neisseria gonorrhea, *Moraxella catarrhalis, *Haemophilus influenzae, *Haemophilus ducreyi, Pasteurella multocida, Campylobacter jejuni, Vibrio Cholera, Helicobacter pylori, Legionella spp., *Bacteroides spp., “Fusobacterium spp. - including 8-lactamase producing strains which are resistant to ampicillin or amoxicillin",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T13:43:47.027625+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-247,Amoxicillin (as trihydrate),none,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RaKy2k-oXosURw6qxMs_mutm9501-yO1/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-247_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RaKy2k-oXosURw6qxMs_mutm9501-yO1_view_usp_drivesdk_eb472d3928.pdf,page_text/DRP-247_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RaKy2k-oXosURw6qxMs_mutm9501-yO1_view_usp_drivesdk_eb472d3928.json,c8d857eaab615c1145840293bca36b60458328a84fcd73a8484b2eaf8ca1c9d3,2297077,1,ocr,Penicillins including amoxicillin may decrease renal clearance of methotrexate by inhibiting renal tubular secretion of the drug. Oral probenecids prolongs the half-life of penicillins by Amoxicillin is a white to off white crystalline powder contained in a scarlet/white gelatin capsule:500 mg (EGC #0) competing with it for renal tubular secretion. Concomitant use of penicillins with oral contraceptives may cause breakthrough bleeding.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated in a wide range of infections such as repiratory, genito-urinary, skin and soft tissue Manufactured by the Marketing Authorization Holder: infections, otitis media, tonsillitis, pharyngitis, laryngitis, septicemia, osteomyelitis,",1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T13:43:54.942037+00:00
