PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2494,Paracetamol,Alagesic,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1q4jfQ2wu-O1w9zpLEKIGDXg8mYhlUTRC/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2494_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1q4jfQ2wu-O1w9zpLEKIGDXg8mYhlUTRC_view_usp_drivesdk_e690ade52f.pdf,page_text/DRP-2494_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1q4jfQ2wu-O1w9zpLEKIGDXg8mYhlUTRC_view_usp_drivesdk_e690ade52f.json,3a78c10be368b05764aeb33e4f4d7ffcbf836993ba1a42bec5b09ab4e7f01b98,1293882,1,ocr,"Paracetamol (ALAGESIC) is a clear yellow, lemon flavored syrup contained in a 60 ml amber bottle What is in the medicine? Paracetamol has analgesic and anti-pyretic properties and weak anti-inflammatory activity. Paracetamol is often the analgesic or anti-pyretic of choice, especially in the elderly and in patients in whom salicylates or other NSAIDs are contraindicated. Such patients include asthmatics, those with a history of peptic ulcer, and children. Strength of the medicine: Each 5 mL of syrup contains 125 mg Paracetamol. What is this medicine used for? Paracetamol (ALAGESIC) is used for relief of painful conditions including headache, migraine, bodyache, earache, toothache, _— dysmenorrhea, neuralgia, arthralgia and post operative pain. Also indicated for reduction of fever. so — How much and how often should you use this medicine? om Children: me 3-5 years old . 5 mL (1 teaspoonful) 6-12 years old .... . 10 mL (2 teaspoonfuls) To be taken 3 - 4 times a day. Or as prescri ib ed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? Do not use this medicine if you are allergic to acetaminophen or paracetamol. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: Paracetamol should be given with care to patients with impaired kidney or liver function and to patients with alcohol dependence. Chronic use should be avoided. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Adverse effects of Paracetamol are rare and usually mild, although haematological reaction including thrombocytopenia, leucopenia, pancytopenia, neutropenia, and agranulocytosis have been reported. Skin rashes and other hypersensitivity ee reaction occur occasionally. —_ a ~ What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? a The risk of Paracetamol toxicity may be increased in patients receiving other potentially hepatotoxic drugs or drugs that induce liver microsomal enzymes. The absorption of paracetamol may be accelerated by drugs such as metoclopramide. es = = = Excretion may be affected and plasma concentrations altered when given with probenecid. Colestyramine reduces the absorption of paracetamol if given within 1 hour of paracetamol. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: Adults taking as little as 10g to 15g of paracetamol within 24 hours may develop severe liver damage and less often, renal tubular necrosis. Early signs of overdosage with paracetamol are nausea, vomiting, and may also include lethargy and sweating usually settles within 24hours. Abdominal pain may be the first indication of liver damage which is not usually apparent for 24 to 48hours and sometime may be delayed for up to 4 to 6 days after ingestion. Activated charcoal may be used to reduce gastrointestinal absorption, if it can be given within 1 hour of the overdose, and if more than 150 mg/kg or 12g of paracetamol has been ingested. There is little evidence that gastric lavage is of benefit in those who have been overdosed solely in paracetamol. If there is any doubt about the timing or the need to treat, then a patient should be treated with an antidote of choice (Acetylcysteine). What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. — Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? If symptoms persist and any undesirable effect occurs, consult your doctor. — “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph”. af — Seek rv | attention i diately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. DRP-2494 Date of Renewal Authorization: July 14, 2021 Patient Information Leaflet Date of Revision: August 15, 2021 Manufactured by the Marketing Authorization Holder: Distributed by: % ABORA",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T13:45:52.714304+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2501-01,Metformin Hydrochloride,Fornidd XR,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/19sjAc6Ta4Rt8NNc-c_ESrr2GW51Fvfy5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2501-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19sjAc6Ta4Rt8NNc-c_ESrr2GW51Fvfy5_view_usp_drivesdk_b0ba92dfa1.pdf,page_text/DRP-2501-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19sjAc6Ta4Rt8NNc-c_ESrr2GW51Fvfy5_view_usp_drivesdk_b0ba92dfa1.json,986a492be2c69797e4d580112175c4523a4f15765444b1e490235a2735405cce,1690232,2,digital_text_and_ocr,,,,,"Metformin Hydrochloride (Fornidd XR) is used for treatment of non-insulin dependent diabetes mellitus (NIDDM) or type Clinical Pharmacology 2 DM, particularly in obese and juvenile diabetics in whom diet alone has failed as monotherapy. Metformin could also Metformin Hydrochloride is an antihyperglycemic agent which improves glucose tolerance in NIDDM (type 2 diabetes be used as adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in patients with type I| diabetes. mellitus) subjects, lowering both basal and postprandial plasma glucose. Its pharmacological mechanisms of action are different from those of sulfonylureas.",1,1,Indications,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T13:46:02.257534+00:00
