PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2591-01,Losartan Potassium,Zarpose,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1z0o9rpPCgnI7lDurLx-0UBXaOMC4cOgq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2591-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1z0o9rpPCgnI7lDurLx-0UBXaOMC4cOgq_view_usp_drivesdk_b1146de778.pdf,page_text/DRP-2591-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1z0o9rpPCgnI7lDurLx-0UBXaOMC4cOgq_view_usp_drivesdk_b1146de778.json,fe6de3ab91bee98304c6ceaaf56fcf4091cb21f8a2f94da0afbdb9f26723eb43,3232650,2,ocr,"cases of rhabdomyolysis have been reported in patients receiving angiotensin II receptor blockers. Pink-coloured heart-shaped, biconvex film-coated tablets. Nervous system disorders: Dysgeusia",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T13:48:19.007179+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2591-03,Losartan Potassium,Mysartan,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VRGLXX3zDr8Txpq5D4OCFzBx1RC2pPW5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2591-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VRGLXX3zDr8Txpq5D4OCFzBx1RC2pPW5_view_usp_drivesdk_be50a1df67.pdf,page_text/DRP-2591-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VRGLXX3zDr8Txpq5D4OCFzBx1RC2pPW5_view_usp_drivesdk_be50a1df67.json,5909cf6167e68cb4c2963cc6bf73e321d37bcd86dd77778f11484c25ea577788,2059918,1,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T13:48:24.263703+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2591-04,Losartan Potassium,Congezar,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1za1Jeo6CLco2ug-Ps2bTJg0BW_Dp0kUe/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2591-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1za1Jeo6CLco2ug-Ps2bTJg0BW_Dp0kUe_view_usp_drivesdk_d53c8fdcf6.pdf,page_text/DRP-2591-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1za1Jeo6CLco2ug-Ps2bTJg0BW_Dp0kUe_view_usp_drivesdk_d53c8fdcf6.json,d3d0c1ef1a644043084db1a7c0401f4eafcf3bbb7238a230cd20c4d66426a9c1,833771,1,digital_text,"Losartan is readily absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract after oral doses, but undergoes substantial first pass metabolism resulting in a systematic bioavailability of about 33%. It is metabolized to an active carboxylic acid metabolite E-3174 (EXP-3174), which has greater pharmacological activity than Losartan; some inactive metabolites are also formed. Metabolism is primarily by cytochrome P450 isoenzymes CYP2C9 and CYP34A. Peak plasma concentrations of Losartan and E3174 occur about 1 hour and 3 to 4 hours, respectively, after morning oral dose. Both Losartan and E-3174 are more than 98% bound to plasma proteins. Losartan is excreted in the urine, and in the faeces via bile, as unchanged drug metabolites. About 4% of an oral dose is excreted unchanged in the urine and about 6% is excreted in urine as the active metabolite. The terminal elimination half-lives of Losartan and E-3174 are about 1.5 to 2.5 hours and 3 to 9 hours, respectively.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Adult Hypertension: The usual dose is 50 mg once daily. The dose may be increased if necessary to 100 mg daily as a single dose or in two divided doses. An initial dose of 25 mg once daily should be given to patients with intravascular fluid depletion. Management of hypertension and treatment of diabetic nephropathy. Heart Failure: The initial dose for patients with heart failure is 2.5 mg once a day. The dose may be increased by 1.25 mg at week’s interval to the usual maintenance dose of 50 mg once a day or as the patient can tolerate. Or as prescribed by the physician.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T13:48:27.732247+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2591-05,Losartan Potassium,Q-Pid,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UqoFxcLcRwuy5Gu5y54XN6r4up5V8yjK/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2591-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UqoFxcLcRwuy5Gu5y54XN6r4up5V8yjK_view_usp_drivesdk_54162fdfeb.pdf,page_text/DRP-2591-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UqoFxcLcRwuy5Gu5y54XN6r4up5V8yjK_view_usp_drivesdk_54162fdfeb.json,9f95c38f16170c124d4ffe78aef04a1697eb3a22ed96564fd8816c79387ee8e7,5592989,1,ocr,"including Henoch-Schénlein purpura, has been reported. Anaphylactic reactions have been reported. Metabolic and Nutrition: Hyperkalemia, hyponatremia have been reported with losartan. Pink-coloured heart-shaped, biconvex film-coated tablets. Musculoskeletal: Rare cases of rhabdomyolysis have been reported in patients receiving angiotensin ||",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T13:48:38.080631+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2591-06,Losartan Potassium,Zilzart,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mxVB2ZY69DI2HHXG27O52Trp2Lm3aodF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2591-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mxVB2ZY69DI2HHXG27O52Trp2Lm3aodF_view_usp_drivesdk_940afa563f.pdf,page_text/DRP-2591-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mxVB2ZY69DI2HHXG27O52Trp2Lm3aodF_view_usp_drivesdk_940afa563f.json,16780f29fdbf503b83fa5ce0298264684a11a9ec58e8610efa5013579f76e3b6,2157624,1,ocr,"Musculoskeletal: Rare cases of rhabdomyolysis have been reported in patients receiving angiotensin II receptor Pink-coloured heart-shaped, biconvex film-coated tablets. blockers.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Foods, Drugs, Devices, and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription. Management of hypertension and treatment of diabetic nephropathy.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T13:48:48.446026+00:00
