PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2812-01,Clindamycin (as phosphate),Klindex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1SjejbZWLafd-iOA6kYK_jmD3diZX34C8/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2812-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1SjejbZWLafd-iOA6kYK_jmD3diZX34C8_view_usp_drivesdk_87f5d98527.pdf,page_text/DRP-2812-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1SjejbZWLafd-iOA6kYK_jmD3diZX34C8_view_usp_drivesdk_87f5d98527.json,65b36f46259272d2da896926573544ca3db19d1b155f8b6e7d3f9afcccaa9d34,1379326,2,ocr,"Solution for Injection CLINICAL PARTICULARS Therapeutic Indications Acute and chronic bacterial infections caused by clindamycin-sensitive pathogens, such as - Infections of bones and joints - Infections of the ear, nose and throat area - Infections of the dental and maxillary area - Infections of the deep respiratory tract - Infections of the pelvic and abdominal area - Infections of female genitalia - Infections of skin and soft tissues - Scarlet fever - Septicaemia - Endocarditis Dosage and administration Adults and adolescents above 14 years of age Receive in - moderately severe infections: 8-12 mL of clindamycin daily (equivalent to 1.2-1.8 g clindamycin) in 2-4 single doses - severe infections: 16-18 mL of clindamycin daily (equivalent to 2.4-2.7 g clindamycin) in 2-4 single doses. The maximum daily dose for adults and adolescents above 14 years of age is 32 mL of clindamycin (equivalent to 4.8 g clindamycin) in 2-4 single doses. Infants (over 4 weeks of age), children (up to 14 years of age) Depending on the localisation and severity of the infection: 20-40 mg clindamycin per kg body weight in 3-4 single doses. Dosage in hepatopathies In patients with moderate to severe hepatopathies, the elimination half-life of clindamycin is prolonged. Dose reduction is usually not necessary when clindamycin is administered every 8 hours. In patients with severe hepatic insufficiency, however, the plasma levels of clindamycin should be monitored. According to the results of this measure, dose reduction or prolonged dosage interval may become necessary. Dosage in nephropathies In case of nephropathy, the elimination half-life is prolonged. However, no dose reduction is necessary in mild to moderate impairment in renal function. In patients with severe renal insufficiency or anuria, however, the plasma levels should be monitored. According to the results of this measure, dose reduction or alternatively prolonged dosage interval of 8 or even 12 hours may be necessary. Dosage in haemodialysis Clindamycin is not haemodialysable. No additional dose is therefore necessary prior to or after dialysis. Mode of administration of ge iasl Clindamycin is injected intramuscularly or infused intravenously. a5 Uva 3s a: ag so Clindamycin must never be injected undiluted intravenously! In case of intramuscular administration, a single dose of 600 mg clindamycin should not be exceeded. Prior to intravenous infusion, the solution is to be diluted in such a way that the concentration is not more than 12 mg clindamycin per mL solution. The infusion rate should not exceed 30 mg clindamycin per minute. Not more than 1,200 mg clindamycin per hour should be given as single infusion.",1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Acute and chronic bacterial infections caused by clindamycin-sensitive pathogens, such as - Infections of bones and joints - Infections of the ear, nose and throat area - Infections of the dental and maxillary area - Infections of the deep respiratory tract - Infections of the pelvic and abdominal area - Infections of female genitalia - Infections of skin and soft tissues - Scarlet fever - Septicaemia - Endocarditis",1,1,Therapeutic Indications,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T14:22:30.844369+00:00
