nce at cardiovascular risk",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:23:10.935175+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2864,Famotidine,Femostal-20,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1C8mB5_G5ECO1-CIc_T0rNNBygKBLunwX/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2864_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1C8mB5_G5ECO1-CIc_T0rNNBygKBLunwX_view_usp_drivesdk_1cfd90b83f.pdf,page_text/DRP-2864_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1C8mB5_G5ECO1-CIc_T0rNNBygKBLunwX_view_usp_drivesdk_1cfd90b83f.json,17213cc6809a5a30e9c1ac501bd59b616aad89ad813491870064f150b404f9b1,420791,1,digital_text,Duodenal ulcer,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Prevention of relapses of duodenal ulceration Prevention of relapses of benign gastric ulcer Hypersecretory conditions such as Zollinger-Ellison syndrome Healing of eosophageal erosion or ulceration associated with gastroesophageal reflux disease Duodenal Ulcer: The recommended dose is 40 mg once daily at bedtime for 4 to 8 weeks. Alternatively, 20 mg twice daily may be administered if the ulcers have not healed completely after 4 weeks then treatment should be continued for a further 4 week period. Benign gastric ulcer: The recommended dose is 40 mg once daily taken at night. Alternatively, 20 mg twice daily may be administered. Gastroesophageal Reflux disease: For mild to moderate disease, the recommended dosage is 20 mg twice daily. For erosive oesophagitis associated with gastroesophageal reflux disease, the recommended dosage is 40 mg twice daily. Elderly patients: Dosage adjustments are not necessary for geriatric patients unless there is a decrease in renal function, where the clearance of the drug may be reduced. Children: Safety and effectiveness of famotidine have not been established. Or as prescribed by the physician.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:23:14.097529+00:00
