PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2939,Calcium Folinate,Cafonate,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dBlRlwwYgPcBRFDYRJuzgjZEBTBKCvFu/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2939_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dBlRlwwYgPcBRFDYRJuzgjZEBTBKCvFu_view_usp_drivesdk_acd7d7acba.pdf,page_text/DRP-2939_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dBlRlwwYgPcBRFDYRJuzgjZEBTBKCvFu_view_usp_drivesdk_acd7d7acba.json,55f7a90a7e122780a2c04ab88cbe195b1f69b4ce4b51e5a715bd0393a12a6993,1952211,2,digital_text,A clear pale yellow colored solution.,1,1,Description:,"Calcium Folinate is used principally as an antidote to folic acid antagonists, such as methotrexate, which blocks the conversion of folic acid to tetrahydrofolate by binding to enzyme dihydrofolate reductase. It does not block the antimicrobial action of folate antagonists such as trimethoprim or pyrimethamine, but may reduce their haematological toxicities. It is also used as an adjunct to Fluorouracil in the treatment of colorectal cancer.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:27:01.183798+00:00
