PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2983,Felodipine,Felostal-5 ER,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fHNyxTDGXKFSEJ-CjF48MDOoAflke2Dw/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2983_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1fHNyxTDGXKFSEJ-CjF48MDOoAflke2Dw_view_usp_drivesdk_d0eac485a0.pdf,page_text/DRP-2983_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1fHNyxTDGXKFSEJ-CjF48MDOoAflke2Dw_view_usp_drivesdk_d0eac485a0.json,0da3be16e72e5a381a7e69e367799a8fe3726d68519b7bc00cb332682816e967,473896,1,digital_text,"Felodipine is a dihydropyridine class calcium antagonist which lowers the arterial blood pressure by decreasing vascular resistance. In-vitro selectivity for smooth muscle in the arterioles is exhibited by Felodipine. In therapeutic doses, Felodipine has no direct effect on cardiac contractility. Felodipine does not affect venous smooth muscle or adrenergic vasomotor control. It has been shown by electrophysiological studies that Felodipine has no direct effect on conduction in the specialized conducting system of the heart and has no effect on the AV nodal refractoriness. Felodipine produces an increase in heart rate which is counteracted when concurrent beta receptor blockers are administered. A white to off white coloured round shaped biconvex plain on both sides extended release uncoated tablet. Pharmacodynamics Site and mechanism of action: The predominant pharmacodynamic feature of Felodipine is its pronounced vascular vs myocardial selectivity. Myogenically active smooth muscles in arterial resistance vessels are particularly sensitive to Felodipine. Felodipine inhibits electrical and contractile activity of vascular smooth muscle cells via an effect on the calcium channels in cell membranes.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"In cyclosporin-treated renal transplant recipients, Felodipine reduces blood pressure and improves both the renal blood flow and the glomerular filtration rate. Felodipine may also improve early renal graft function. Effects on Ability to Drive and Use Machines: Cardiac effects: Felodipine in therapeutic doses has no effect on cardiac contractility or atrioventricular conduction or refractoriness. In patients with heart failure, Felodipine favorably affects left ventricular function, as assessed by ejection fraction or stroke volume, and does not cause neurohormonal activation. However, Felodipine does not seem to affect survival. In patients with hypertension or angina pectoris, Felodipine (Felostal-5 ER) can be used also in case of impaired left ventricular function. Antihypertensive treatment with Felodipine is associated with significant regression of pre-existing left ventricular hypertrophy. Felodipine is given by mouth, generally in a modified release formulation for administration once daily in the morning. In hypertension, the usual initial dose is 5 mg daily by mouth, adjusted as required; the usual maintenance dose is 2.5 to 10 mg daily and doses above 20 mg daily are not usually needed. In angina, the usual initial dose is 5 mg daily increased if necessary to 10 mg daily. Lower doses may be required in the elderly and in patients with impaired liver function. Or as prescribed by the physician.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:29:55.561880+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2983-01,Felodipine,Gofepine,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rH_grmb3zdRQVTgBgx2eXFZC9KMiI6qw/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2983-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rH_grmb3zdRQVTgBgx2eXFZC9KMiI6qw_view_usp_drivesdk_c1caccacb3.pdf,page_text/DRP-2983-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rH_grmb3zdRQVTgBgx2eXFZC9KMiI6qw_view_usp_drivesdk_c1caccacb3.json,6fb3bd288e0525931ae9eaa30da1b2147612442b93f8cf9e01cbb23a21ea2025,448081,1,digital_text,A white to off white coloured round shaped biconvex plain on both sides extended release uncoated tablet.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,It is used in the management of hypertension and angina pectoris.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:29:43.443178+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2983-02,Felodipine,Felo-5,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BuiRLrKTPzY2EzETOe-6qsjOzbiQrtlz/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2983-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1BuiRLrKTPzY2EzETOe-6qsjOzbiQrtlz_view_usp_drivesdk_a5c43532eb.pdf,page_text/DRP-2983-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1BuiRLrKTPzY2EzETOe-6qsjOzbiQrtlz_view_usp_drivesdk_a5c43532eb.json,a7823f85a478843d0674d8328768fc3548ea04d7af105fc6cf3273284da70ecf,494679,1,digital_text,,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Felodipine is given by mouth, generally in a modified release formulation for administration once daily in the morning. In hypertension, the usual initial dose is 5 mg daily by mouth, adjusted as required; the usual maintenance dose is 2.5 to 10 mg daily and doses above 20 mg daily are not usually needed. In angina, the usual initial dose is 5 mg daily increased if necessary to 10 mg daily. Lower doses may be required in the elderly and in patients with impaired liver function. Or as prescribed by the physician. In cyclosporin-treated renal transplant recipients, Felodipine reduces blood pressure and improves both the renal blood flow and the glomerular filtration rate. Felodipine may also improve early renal graft function. It is used in the management of hypertension and angina pectoris.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T14:29:46.737369+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2983-07,Felodipine,Felojen,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/18fabzEU1oX-4Xq82b2O9oJBTwGuasl1e/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2983-07_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18fabzEU1oX-4Xq82b2O9oJBTwGuasl1e_view_usp_drivesdk_d66f75afc8.pdf,page_text/DRP-2983-07_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18fabzEU1oX-4Xq82b2O9oJBTwGuasl1e_view_usp_drivesdk_d66f75afc8.json,8b229ec5e16e7680f9330b05d939e046dbaaa161f5ad5ea4e585b204fe3915e3,1547230,1,digital_text,A white to off-white coloured round shaped biconvex plain on both sides extended release uncoated tablet.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,It is used in the management of hypertension and angina pectoris.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:29:49.972975+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2983-09,Felodipine,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uGg_1-7gBPk_v8Tx9Pr5YYcEd5291BMO/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2983-09_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uGg_1-7gBPk_v8Tx9Pr5YYcEd5291BMO_view_usp_drivesdk_7a82e19fb1.pdf,page_text/DRP-2983-09_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uGg_1-7gBPk_v8Tx9Pr5YYcEd5291BMO_view_usp_drivesdk_7a82e19fb1.json,b5e94c12b2b6be5f38282d3c80f4cd6c067f3414b5ad709c921088e840c14746,525016,1,digital_text,"Cardiac effects: Felodipine in therapeutic doses has no effect on cardiac contractility or atrioventricular conduction or refractoriness. In patients with heart failure, Felodipine favorably affects left ventricular function, as assessed by ejection fraction or stroke volume, and does not cause neurohormonal activation. However, Felodipine does not seem to affect survival. In patients with hypertension or angina pectoris, Felodipine can be used also in case of impaired left ventricular function. Antihypertensive treatment with Felodipine is associated with significant regression of pre- existing left ventricular hypertrophy. Renal effects: Felodipine has a natriuretic and diuretic effect due to reduced tubular reabsorption of filtered sodium. This counteracts the salt and water retention observed with other vasodilators. Felodipine does not affect daily potassium excretion. The renal vascular resistance is decreased by Felodipine. Normal glomerular filtration rate is unchanged. In patients with impaired renal function, the glomerular filtration rate may increase. Felodipine does not influence urinary albumin excretion. A white to off white coloured round shaped biconvex plain on both sides extended release uncoated tablet. In cyclosporin-treated renal transplant recipients, Felodipine reduces blood pressure and improves both the renal blood flow and the glomerular filtration rate. Felodipine may also improve early renal graft function.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Felodipine is given by mouth, generally in a modified release formulation for administration once daily in the morning. In hypertension, the usual initial dose is 5 mg daily by mouth, adjusted as required; the usual maintenance dose is 2.5 to 10 mg daily and doses above 20 mg daily are not usually needed. In angina, the usual initial dose is 5 mg daily increased if necessary to 10 mg daily. Lower doses may be required in the elderly and in patients with impaired liver function. Or as prescribed by the physician. Felodipine is not likely to affect the ability to drive or use machines. Felodipine extended release tablet should not be used in women of child-bearing potential, in people who have hypersensitive to Felodipine, or in patients with cardiogenic shock. It is not known whether Felodipine is excreted in breast milk or whether it has harmful effects on the newborn. Effects on Ability to Drive and Use Machines:",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:29:52.770973+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2985,Azithromycin (as Dihydrate),Anzal-500,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/10LztJHqVZnxrUS70be1EzURuA9_z8SkE/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2985_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_10LztJHqVZnxrUS70be1EzURuA9_z8SkE_view_usp_drivesdk_c4274e4c78.pdf,page_text/DRP-2985_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_10LztJHqVZnxrUS70be1EzURuA9_z8SkE_view_usp_drivesdk_c4274e4c78.json,1baa108a081bd8bfd6278ae2b3507010114da09b4c1fe95e00af11a61014f87f,1161311,1,digital_text,White coloured round shaped biconvex film coated tablet plain both sides.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Azithromycin is indicated for the treatment for Infection from respiratory tract pathogens (e.g., S.pyogenes, sp., pneumoniae, M. catarrhalis, C. trachomatis, Legionella), C. pnuemoniae and M. avium infection; uncomplicated chlamydial urethritis, cervicitis or pharyngitis; alternative drug for multi-drug resistant Salmonella typhi infection outside the Central Nervous System (CNS).",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:30:04.812323+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2985-03,Azithromycin (as Dihydrate),Berazith,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/162aMka40-A-jQNSOq5S7bZdmfKwEe4SI/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2985-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_162aMka40-A-jQNSOq5S7bZdmfKwEe4SI_view_usp_drivesdk_cbe41cb092.pdf,page_text/DRP-2985-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_162aMka40-A-jQNSOq5S7bZdmfKwEe4SI_view_usp_drivesdk_cbe41cb092.json,b3138209160411d43da9d75cbbb0b4c40f39d6b522719bb218fb3458a5382f8b,467210,1,digital_text,Each tablet contains: Adults and adolescents - 1 gram taken once as a single dose. Children up to 16 years of age - Use and dose must be determined by your doctor. For sinusitis: Adults and adolescents - 500 mg a day for 3 days. Children up to 16 years of age - Use and dose must determined by your doctor. For pelvic inflammatory disease: Adults and adolescents 16 years of age and older - 500 milligrams (mg) once a day for one or two days injected into a vein.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Children up to 2 years of age - Use and dose must be determined by doctor. For bronchitis, strep throat, pneumonia, and skin infections: Adults and adolescents 16 years of age and older - 500 milligrams (mg) on the first day, then 250 mg once a day on days two to five.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:29:58.425148+00:00
