PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-2992-02,Colchicine,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1eQyc7Xg5foDD27PXpcuSJYCjHlabKDpD/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-2992-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eQyc7Xg5foDD27PXpcuSJYCjHlabKDpD_view_usp_drivesdk_d713f73109.pdf,page_text/DRP-2992-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eQyc7Xg5foDD27PXpcuSJYCjHlabKDpD_view_usp_drivesdk_d713f73109.json,357311741f97dd89d80ba5563f1c5d109ad01e5181cda99efe08cbfbfd81253c,2211978,1,ocr,"The most frequent adverse effects of oral Colchicine are those involving the gastrointestinal tract and may be associated with its antimitotic action. Diarrhea, nausea, vomiting and abdominal pain White, circular, uncoated tablets with “Inga” monogram on one side and line of division on the other side are often the first signs of toxicity and are usually an indication that Colchicine therapy should be stopped",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"No antidote is available. Colchicine is used for the relief of acute gout and for the prophylaxis of acute attacks, particularly during Elimination of toxins by gastric lavage within one hour of acute poisoning the first few months of treatment with allopurinol or uricosurics. Colchicine has also been used in several Consider oral activated charcoal in adults who have ingested more than 0.1 mg/kg body weight within other conditions including amyloidosis, Behcet’s syndrome, Familial Mediterranean fever, idiopathic 1 hour of presentation and in children who have ingested any amount within 1 hour of presentation thrombocytopenic purpura, pericarditis, primary biliary cirrhosis and pyoderma gangrenosum. Hemodialysis has no efficacy (high apparent distribution volume)",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T14:30:20.202509+00:00
