PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3040-04,Ferrous Sulfate Heptahydrate + Folic Acid,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qJSOgGrjLh0SDpJW1Na37ZS01CL65yP0/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3040-04_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qJSOgGrjLh0SDpJW1Na37ZS01CL65yP0_view_usp_drivesdk_7adbaf64e6.pdf,page_text/DRP-3040-04_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qJSOgGrjLh0SDpJW1Na37ZS01CL65yP0_view_usp_drivesdk_7adbaf64e6.json,a796b6acbf86fcd25d8c76ecb2fefaca79111ac8b7719b964bf75ab26221a471,169077,1,digital_text,"RiteMED® Iron + Folic Acid 60 mg/ 250 mcg Tablet is an old rose colored bi-convex, plain on both sides of the tablet. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Each tablet contains Ferrous Sulfate Heptahydrate 300 mg equivalent to 60 mg elemental iron and 250 mcg Folic Acid. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? This medicine is used for the prevention of iron deficiency anemia and as a prenatal hematinic. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? One tablet daily. Or as prescribed by the physician. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? When you are allergic to any ingredient of the product. Iron salts should not be given to patients receiving repeated blood transfusions or to patients with anemias not produced by iron deficiency. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS The following undesirable effects may occur: • Dark discoloration of faeces • Gastrointestinal irritation and abdominal pain • Nausea and vomiting • Diarrhea or constipation WHAT OTHER MEDICINES OR FOODS SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? The following medicines can affect or be affected by Iron + Folic Acid 60 mg/ 250 mcg Tablet: • Injectible iron medicines. Oral iron should not be administered concomitantly with parenteral iron. • Compaound containing calcium and magnesium including antacids and mineral supplements and bicarbonates, carbonates, oxalates or phosphares may impair the absorption of iron. • Zinc salts may decrease the absorption of iron • Tetracyclines and iron salts diminish absorption when taken together orally. • The response to iron may be delayed in patients receiving systemic chloramphenicol. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, take another dose as soon as you remember it and then your next dose at the usual recommended schedule. Never take two doses at the same time. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Keep this product out or reach and sight of children. Store at temperatures not exceeding 30 o",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T14:32:03.118033+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3040-06,Ferrous Sulfate + Folic Acid,United Home Fersulfate Plus,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ULHdaR8Agdq4PthBGq85ERcKWX37aG-D/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3040-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ULHdaR8Agdq4PthBGq85ERcKWX37aG-D_view_usp_drivesdk_bf0003f4c8.pdf,page_text/DRP-3040-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ULHdaR8Agdq4PthBGq85ERcKWX37aG-D_view_usp_drivesdk_bf0003f4c8.json,993358bd15d24e0ced1835c54632bb37b0c9538c40812ce24852d973325e6b1c,1275261,2,digital_text,"®Iron + Folic Acid (United Home Fersulfate Plus) 60 mg / 250 mcg Tablet is an old-rose colored bi-convex, plain on both sides of the tablet. STREN GTH OF THE MEDICINE See Formulation. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE U SED FOR? This medicine is used for the prevention of iron deﬁciency anemia and as a prenatal hematinic. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? One tablet, daily. Or as prescribed by the physician. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? When you are allergic to any ingredient of the product. Iron salts should not be given to patients receiving repeated blood transfusions or to patients with anemia not produced by iron deﬁciency. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS The following undesirable eﬀects may occur: • Dark discoloration of feces • Gastrointestinal irritation and abdominal pain • Nausea and vomiting • Diarrhea or constipation WHAT OTHE R MEDICINES O R FOODS SHOUL D BE AVOIDED WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? The following medicines can aﬀect or be aﬀected by Iron + Folic acid 60mg/250mcg Tablet: • Injectable iron medicines. Oral iron should not be administered concomitantly with parenteral iron. • Compounds containing calcium and magnesium including antacids, mineral supplements and bicarbonates, carbonates, oxalates or phosphates may impair the absorption of iron. • Zinc salts may decrease the absorption of iron. • Tetracyclines and iron salts diminish absorption when taken together orally. • The response to iron may be delayed in patients receiving systemic chloramphenicol. WHAT SHOULD YO U DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, take another dose as soon as you remember it and then your next dose at the usual recommended schedule. Never take two doses at the same time. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Keep this product out of reach and sight of children. Store at temperatures not exceeding 30ºC. Protect from direct sunlight. SIGNS AND SYMPTO MS OF OVERDOSAGE Since Folic acid is a water-soluble vitamin, overdose is rather unlikely to    ",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T14:32:07.166749+00:00
