ion with Clotrimazole vaginal tablets in the management of Candida vulvovaginitis or infection of the peri-anal area, while application of the cream to the glans penis of the partner may help prevent reinfection of the female. It is suggested that treatment be timed so as to avoid the menstrual period and to be completed before the onset of menstruation. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT USE THIS MEDICINE? If you are hypersensitive to Clotrimazole or any of the ingredients in this medicine. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Keep all medicines out of reach of children. Avoid contact with eyes. Do not swallow. Cream may reduce the effectiveness and safety of latex products such as condoms and diaphragms when applied on the genital area (women: labia and adjacent area of the vulva; men: prepuce and glans of the penis), The effect is temporary and occurs only during treatment. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE? Clotrimazole cream is generally well tolerated after local application. The following have been reported infrequently: erythema, stinging, blistering, peeling, edema, pruritus, urticaria and general irritation. WHAT OTHER MEDICINES OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? None known. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? No available information. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSAGE No risk of acute intoxication is seen as it is unlikely to occur following a single dermal application of an overdose (application over a large area under conditions favourable to absorption) or inadvertent oral ingestion. There is no specific antidote. However, in the event of accidental oral ingestion, gastric lavage is rarely required and should be considered only if a life-threatening amount of Clotrimazole has been ingested within the preceding hour or if clinical symptoms of overdose become apparent (e.g. dizziness, nausea or vomiting). Gastric lavage should be carried out only if the airway can be protected adequately. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? There is no specific antidote however patients should still consult their physician. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? Patients should consult their physician if there is no improvement after 4 weeks of treatment.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T14:35:08.189975+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3180,Alprazolam,Altrox 500,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FInbFP-1yUXA5Em65lWc_bMWO6JMMmEA/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3180_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FInbFP-1yUXA5Em65lWc_bMWO6JMMmEA_view_usp_drivesdk_3063997987.pdf,page_text/DRP-3180_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FInbFP-1yUXA5Em65lWc_bMWO6JMMmEA_view_usp_drivesdk_3063997987.json,e330b13d90f77bfb6002ac28dc2d2daa8cd5acb5ba5b33c6b7ada28cf4dda579,323371,1,digital_text,"Alprazolam is a triazolo analog of the 1,4-benzodiazepine class of central nervous system active compound. Its chemical name is 8-chloro-1-methyl-6-phenyl-4H-s-triazolo [4,3-α] [1,4] benzodiazepine. Alprazolam is a white crystalline powder, soluble in methanol or ethanol but with no appreciable solubility in water at physiological pH. Alprazolam (Altrox 250) 250 mcg is a light yellow coloured, round ﬂat beveled edge uncoated tablet with bisecting line on one side. Alprazolam (Altrox 500) 500 mcg is a light orange coloured, round ﬂat beveled edge uncoated tablet with bisecting line on one side. CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY Pharmacodynamics CNS agents of the 1,4-benzodiazepine class presumably exert their effects by binding at stereo specific receptors at several sites within the central nervous system. Their exact mechanism of action is unknown. Clinically all benzodiazepines cause a dose-related depressant effect on the central nervous system varying from mild to impairment of task performance to hypnosis. Pharmacokinetics Following oral administration, alprazolam is readily absorbed. Peak concentrations in the plasma occur in one to two hours following administration. Plasma levels are proportions to the dose given over the dose range of 0.5 to 3.0 mg. Peak levels of 8.0 to 37 mg/mL were observed. The mean elimination half-life of alprazolam is 12-15 hours. The predominant metabolites are α-hydroxy-alprazolam and a benzophenone derived from alprazolam. The biological activity of α-hydroxy-alprazolam is approximately one-half that of alprazolam. The benzophenone metabolites are essentially inactive. Plasma levels of these metabolites are extremely low, thus, precluding precise pharmacokinetic description. However, their half-lives appear to be of the same order of magnitude as alprazolam. Alprazolam and its metabolites are excreted primarily in the urine. The ability of alprazolam to induce human hepatic enzyme systems has not yet been determined. However, this is not a property of benzodiazepines in general. Further, alprazolam did not affect the prothrombin or plasma warfarin levels in male volunteers administered sodium warfarin orally. In vitro, alprazolam is bound (80%) to human serum protein. Changes in the absorption, distribution, metabolism and excretion of benzodiazepines have been reported in a variety of disease states including alcoholism, impaired hepatic function and impaired renal function changes have also been demonstrated in geriatric patients. It has not yet been determined if similar changes occur in the pharmacokinetics of alprazolam.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"It is indicated for the management of anxiety disorders and short-term relief of the symptoms of anxiety, anxiety associated depression and for the treatment of panic disorders.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:35:17.427407+00:00
