PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3322,Azithromycin (as dihydrate),Anzal-DS,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KWmwg7HGZsh_4a7VgTv6KO1n2mjh_syS/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3322_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1KWmwg7HGZsh_4a7VgTv6KO1n2mjh_syS_view_usp_drivesdk_077db0f3cb.pdf,page_text/DRP-3322_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1KWmwg7HGZsh_4a7VgTv6KO1n2mjh_syS_view_usp_drivesdk_077db0f3cb.json,ebbcfd15e8b90cce0946f312764ec767d394e52705b15c3abdd09c54b9d8edac,508388,1,digital_text,"Pharmacotherapeutic group: Antibacterials for systemic use. Mode of Action: Resistance to Azithromycin may be inherent or acquired. There are three main mechanisms of resistance in bacteria: target site alteration, alteration in antibiotic transport and modification of the antibiotic. Azithromycin, a semisynthetic antibiotic belonging to the macrolide subgroup of Azithromycin ides, is used to treat STDs due to chlamydia and gonorrhea, community-acquired pneumonia, pelvic inflammatory disease, pediatric otitis media and pharyngitis, and Mycobacterium avium complex (MAC) in patients with advanced HIV disease. Similar in structure to erythromycin, Azithromycin reaches higher intracellular concentrations than erythromycin, increasing its efficacy and duration of action. General properties A yellow coloured powder, after reconstitution, forms yellow colored suspension. Azithromycin (as dihydrate) ....................... 200 mg Mechanism of Resistance:",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Azithromycin demonstrates cross resistance with erythromycin resistant gram-positive isolates. A decrease in macrolide susceptibility over time has been noted particularly in Streptococcus pneumoniae and Staphylococcus aureus. Similarly, decreased susceptibility has been observed among Streptococcus viridans and Streptococcus agalactiae (Group B streptococcus) against other macrolides and lincosamides. terminal elimination half-life is about 68 hours. Azithromycin is contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to Azithromycin, erythromycin or any macrolides or ketolide antibiotic.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:41:49.346369+00:00
