PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3423,Cefaclor (as monohydrate),Verzat,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZFEc7w4fNLG4NrHJCGVTIOgbyiLtbfDp/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3423_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZFEc7w4fNLG4NrHJCGVTIOgbyiLtbfDp_view_usp_drivesdk_8f6c5e0c69.pdf,page_text/DRP-3423_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZFEc7w4fNLG4NrHJCGVTIOgbyiLtbfDp_view_usp_drivesdk_8f6c5e0c69.json,6158e77f000e3ba46f3ce5b8b71550a8abc82cd6669fbf07be684bb4652205e0,484520,1,digital_text,"Cefaclor is a semisynthetic second generation cephalosporin antibiotic. It is chemically designated as 3-chloro-7-D-(2- phenylglycinamido)-3-cephem-4-carboxylic acid monohydrate. Its empirical formula is C H CIN O S.H O and its molecular weight is 15 14 3 4 2 385.8. Characterized by off-white to pinkish-white free flowing granules, turns to pink suspension when reconstituted with a strawberry flavor.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of susceptible infections including upper and lower respiratory tract infections, skin infections and urinary tract infections.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:44:11.303603+00:00
