PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3447,Gabapentin,Neurontin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WHYoLLuFK-wapJnVjfthLgqdIl7OZpeo/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3447_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WHYoLLuFK-wapJnVjfthLgqdIl7OZpeo_view_usp_drivesdk_3c95c779cb.pdf,page_text/DRP-3447_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WHYoLLuFK-wapJnVjfthLgqdIl7OZpeo_view_usp_drivesdk_3c95c779cb.json,5c353ac0a6d501ce79827cefef608bcb35898c608cf68a8c62b0f8bcb74f0977,179544,14,digital_text,Gabapentin is described as 1-(aminomethyl) cyclohexaneacetic acid with an empirical formula of C9H17NO2 and a molecular weight of 171.24. The molecular structure of gabapentin is: Gabapentin is a white to off-white crystalline solid. It is freely soluble in water and both basic and acidic aqueous solutions.,1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,Epilepsy Gabapentin is indicated as monotherapy in the treatment of partial seizures with and without secondary generalization in adults and children aged 12 years and older. Safety and effectiveness for monotherapy in children younger than 12 years have not been established (see section 4.2 – Dosage and method of administration: Epilepsy: Adults and pediatric patients over 12 years of age). Gabapentin is indicated as adjunctive therapy in the treatment of partial seizures with and without secondary generalization in adults and children aged 3 years and older. Safety and effectiveness for adjunctive therapy in pediatric patients younger than 3 years have not been established (see section 4.2 – Dosage and method of administration: Epilepsy: Pediatric patients aged 3 to 12 years). Neuropathic pain Gabapentin is indicated for the treatment of neuropathic pain in adults aged 18 years and older. Safety and effectiveness in patients younger than 18 years have not been established. GABAPENTIN Module PART 1 Volume Pg. 0 [Page 2] Page 2 of 14,1,2,4.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:45:31.096007+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-346,Enalapril Maleate,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1TOIM2C2d4zBeTj6NMF5FD1PgrDBwp_8Z/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-346_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1TOIM2C2d4zBeTj6NMF5FD1PgrDBwp_8Z_view_usp_drivesdk_a8831a4f5e.pdf,page_text/DRP-346_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1TOIM2C2d4zBeTj6NMF5FD1PgrDBwp_8Z_view_usp_drivesdk_a8831a4f5e.json,4e47544c8549abff7839578284c10a6379c05fea283418e90adc5dbaf816c6d9,1135226,2,ocr,"Enalapril Maleate 10 mg Tablet is white to off-white, round, biconvex tablet plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Enalapril is an ACE inhibitor used in the treatment of hypertension and heart failure. It may also be given prophylactically to patients with asymptomatic left ventricular dysfunction to delay the onset of symptomatic heart failure and to those with left ventricular dysfunction to reduce the incidence of coronary ischemic events, including myocardial infarction.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T14:45:40.550916+00:00
