PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3564,Montelukast (as Sodium),Montelast,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-v_n3-Z4FQmUW8YT4iyW7Jyb3oRqDe4P/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3564_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-v_n3-Z4FQmUW8YT4iyW7Jyb3oRqDe4P_view_usp_drivesdk_9115c69dff.pdf,page_text/DRP-3564_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-v_n3-Z4FQmUW8YT4iyW7Jyb3oRqDe4P_view_usp_drivesdk_9115c69dff.json,457977497044bd4cf19ff9a669d8df79ab9e2b9a732a82ce8db33e09165eef70,903001,1,digital_text,"Montelukast is a selective leukotriene receptor antagonist. It works by blocking the reaction of substance that causes the inflammation, fluid retention, mucous secretion and constriction in the lungs. Montelukast (Montelast) 10 mg is a white to off white, round, biconvex film-coated tablet, plain on one side and bisected on the other side. Montelukast (Montelast) 5 mg is a pink to reddish pink with mottling tablet, round, biconvex and plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Prophylaxis and chronic treatment of asthma as adjunctive therapy in combination with a corticosteroid. There is a place for Montelukast in children aged 2-5years with intermittent viral induced asthma, where leukotrienes play a major role.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:47:49.672260+00:00
