PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3701-03,Silver Sulfadiazine,Flovidiazine,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1a2fXThm9tuGuYry_75NaRQ9ax8Ai3ctq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3701-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1a2fXThm9tuGuYry_75NaRQ9ax8Ai3ctq_view_usp_drivesdk_2a9d85489e.pdf,page_text/DRP-3701-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1a2fXThm9tuGuYry_75NaRQ9ax8Ai3ctq_view_usp_drivesdk_2a9d85489e.json,50dbc79f2e3a167636962d5588ca577493526eaf2a21cbee61061669e4b49edf,1475078,1,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T14:51:32.886072+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3707,Cetirizine Hydrochloride,Aletor,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1iKPerUfIbpKVMNAOqsa6_ZlAZ_6yDFsA/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3707_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1iKPerUfIbpKVMNAOqsa6_ZlAZ_6yDFsA_view_usp_drivesdk_9182e2be0a.pdf,page_text/DRP-3707_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1iKPerUfIbpKVMNAOqsa6_ZlAZ_6yDFsA_view_usp_drivesdk_9182e2be0a.json,83251df6a315e63d2ba97d3961369988acf92164ce975fade850439393afa241,822995,1,digital_text,"Orange coloured syrup with sweet orange flavour. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? The active ingredient in your medicine is cetirizine hydrochloride, which belongs to a group of medicines called antihistamines. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Please see formulation. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? These are used to relieve the symptoms of seasonal allergic rhinitis (e.g., hay fever), perennial allergic rhinitis (e.g., year-round allergies often due to house dust mites or animal allergies) and urticaria (itchy, red, swollen skin). These symptoms include itchy skin rashes; sneezing; itchy, runny or blocked nose; red, itchy and watering eyes. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? In adult and children aged 6 years and over: 5 mL twice daily. Children aged 2 or 5 years: 5 mL once daily or 2.5 mL twice daily. Or as prescribed by the physician. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Do not take Cetirizine Syrup if you: · are allergic (hypersensitive) to cetirizine hydrochloride, hydroxyzine, piperazine derivatives or any of the other ingredients in Cetirizine Syrup. · have a severe kidney disease (severe renal failure with creatine clearance below 10 mL/min) have hereditary problems of galactose intolerance, Lapp lactase deficiency or glucose galactose malabsorption. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Warnings and Precautions Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before taking Cetirizine Syrup: · If you have spinal cord lesion or enlargement of the prostate or any predisposing factors for urinary retention. · If you are an epileptic patient or a patient at risk of convulsions (fits). · If you have renal insufficiency or have kidney problems. Cetirizine Syrup can affect the results of allergy skin tests. If you require an allergy test you should stop taking Cetirizine Syrup three days before you have the test. Long term treatment with cetirizine can increase the risk of tooth decay due to mouth dryness. Appropriate oral hygiene is important in long term use. Pregnancy, Breastfeeding and Fertility If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, think you might be pregnant or are planning to become pregnant, ask your doctor or pharmacist for advice before taking this medicine. As with other drugs, the use of Cetirizine Syrup should be avoided in pregnant women. Accidental use of the drug by a pregnant woman should not produce any harmful effects on the fetus. Nevertheless, the administration of the medicine should be discontinued. You should not take Cetirizine Syrup during breastfeeding because cetirizine passes into your breast milk. Ask your doctor or pharmacist for advice before taking this medicine. Driving and Using Machines Clinical studies have produced no evidence of impaired attention, alertness and driving capabilities after taking Cetirizine Syrup at the recommended dose. If you are intending to drive, engage in potentially hazardous activities or operate machinery, you should not exceed the recommended dose. You should closely observe your response to the drug. If you are a sensitive patient, you may find that the simultaneous use of alcohol or other nervous depressant agents may additionally affect your attention and ability to react. Do not drive or operate machinery if the solution makes you feel drowsy. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Like all medicines, Cetirizine Syrup can cause side effects, although not everybody gets them. If you get any of the following symptoms after taking this medicine you should contact your doctor or pharmacist immediately: · any sudden wheeziness, difficulty in breathing · dizziness · sudden signs of an allergic reaction such as developing a rash, swelling of the eyelids, face, lips or throat · loss of consciousness · convulsions or fits · bruising or bleeding more easily than normal · weight loss · worsening cough · fatigue Common side effects (seen in less than 1 in 10 patients but in more than 1 in 100 patients): · drowsiness, fatigue · dry mouth, nausea (feeling sick), diarrhea · dizziness, headache · sore or inflamed throat · swelling and irritation of the lining of the nose (runny nose) · restlessness · abdominal pain Uncommon side effects (seen in less than 1 in 100 patients but in more than 1 per 1000 patients): · agitation · burning, prickling sensation (feeling of pins and needles) · stomach ache · rash, itching · feelings of weakness and/or extreme tiredness, feeling unwell Rare side effects (seen in less than 1 in 1000 patients) · allergic reactions, some severe (very rare) · feelings of aggression, confusion and depression · hallucinations, difficulty in sleeping · convulsions (fits), movement disorders · involuntary eye movements · muscle spasm and tics · rapid heart beat · edema (swelling of the feet or ankles) · hives (urticaria) · unusual weight gain · changes in liver function tests, indicating the possibility of damage to the liver Very rare side effects (seen in less than 1 in 10,000 patients) · serious allergic reaction which causes difficulty in breathing or dizziness · tics, shaking · distorted sense of taste · fainting · involuntary movements or muscle contractions · blurred vision, difficulty in focusing, eyes having uncontrolled circular movements (oculogyration) · swelling of the face, lips or throat · severe blistering skin rash · difficult and/or painful urination · loss of urinary control · an increased tendency to bruise or bleed easily Side effects of unknown frequency · forgetfulness, memory impairment · increased appetite, · difficulty passing water or · a feeling of dizziness (vertigo) In very rare cases, people have had suicidal thoughts when taking this medicine. If you experience this, stop taking the medicine and see your doctor. Long term treatment with Cetirizine Syrup can lead to a dry mouth, it is therefore important that adequate oral hygiene is maintained. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Other Medicines and Cetirizine Please tell your doctor or pharmacist if you are taking, have recently taken or might take any other medicines. Medication for anxiety or stress (CNS depressants) should be used in caution with cetirizine. Cetirizine with Food, Drink and Alcohol Cetirizine Syrup can be taken with or without food. Be careful when drinking alcohol while using cetirizine. It can increase the effects of drinking. No interactions susceptible to have a noticeable impact have been observed between alcohol (at the blood level of 0.5 per mL corresponding to one glass of wine) and cetirizine used at the normal doses. However, as is the case with all antihistamines, it is recommended to avoid concurrent consumption of alcohol. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you have forgotten to take your medicine, take it as soon as you remember and then wait 24 hours before taking your next dose. Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten dose. If you have any further questions on the use of this product, ask your doctor or pharmacist. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE The most common signs and symptoms of overdose may include feeling unwell, headache, confused, restless, shaky, dizzy, tired or very sleepy. You may also notice a rapid heartbeat, having dilated pupils or blurred vision, and experience headache, itching, diarrhea, or difficulty urinating. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have accidentally taken more than the recommended/prescribed dose, contact your nearest hospital casualty department or tell your doctor or pharmacist immediately. Remember to take the pack and any remaining medicine with you. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If any undesirable effect occurs. If you have taken more than the recommended dose. If you are pregnant or think you may be, or are planning to become pregnant, or are breastfeeding. AVAILABILITY Amber Glass Bottle with Measuring Cap x 60 mL (Box of 1's) ADR REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. DRP-3707 Date of First Authorization: December 21, 2009 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: July 26, 2023 Imported and Exclusively Distributed by: AMBICA INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION #9 Amsterdam Extension, Merville Park Subd., Parañaque City www.ambicaglobal.com Size : 133x216 mm Manufactured by:",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T14:52:01.656588+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3707-01,Cetirizine Hydrochloride,Unbranded,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1u1ryqLNr190EbJvgDHD3PpIK72HmBuV1/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3707-01_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1u1ryqLNr190EbJvgDHD3PpIK72HmBuV1_view_usp_drivesdk_6d5a12ea86.pdf,page_text/DRP-3707-01_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1u1ryqLNr190EbJvgDHD3PpIK72HmBuV1_view_usp_drivesdk_6d5a12ea86.json,7dc0c322eff6d2f8ff978612033d9aa4d7c3f2553c85c5802948b57dd32ab8d2,818020,1,digital_text,"These are used to relieve the symptoms of seasonal allergic rhinitis (e.g., hay fever), perennial allergic rhinitis (e.g., year-round allergies often due to house dust mites or animal allergies) and urticaria (itchy, red, swollen skin). These symptoms include itchy skin rashes; sneezing; itchy, runny or blocked nose; red, itchy and watering eyes. The active ingredient in your medicine is cetirizine hydrochloride, which belongs to a group of medicines called antihistamines. Each 5 mL syrup contains: Cetirizine Hydrochloride BP .... 5 mg Please see formulation. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR?",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T14:51:41.960157+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3707-02,Cetirizine Hydrochloride,Unbranded,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ayvKu0e7HqGzbcdEBMgvhjzCE6jnglio/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3707-02_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ayvKu0e7HqGzbcdEBMgvhjzCE6jnglio_view_usp_drivesdk_77bf333a38.pdf,page_text/DRP-3707-02_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ayvKu0e7HqGzbcdEBMgvhjzCE6jnglio_view_usp_drivesdk_77bf333a38.json,2f004c4b9d5dc71ff9b89018f119bc552f872fc557182a16a2233ed4a33bd2bf,834114,1,digital_text,"Orange coloured syrup with sweet orange flavour. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? The active ingredient in your medicine is cetirizine hydrochloride, which belongs to a group of medicines called antihistamines. ∙ dizziness ∙ sudden signs of an allergic reaction such as developing a rash, swelling of the eyelids, face, lips or throat ∙ convulsions or fits ∙ dizziness, headache ∙ abdominal pain ∙ drowsiness, fatigue ∙ dry mouth, nausea (feeling sick), diarrhea ∙ restlessness ∙ loss of consciousness Common side effects (seen in less than 1 in 10 patients but in more than 1 in 100 patients): ∙ worsening cough ∙ fatigue ∙ sore or inflamed throat ∙ bruising or bleeding more easily than normal ∙ weight loss ∙ swelling and irritation of the lining of the nose (runny nose) UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Like all medicines, Cetirizine Syrup can cause side effects, although not everybody gets them. If you get any of the following symptoms after taking this medicine you should contact your doctor or pharmacist immediately: ∙ rash, itching ∙ tics, shaking ∙ fainting ∙ unusual weight gain ∙ agitation ∙ changes in liver function tests, indicating the possibility of damage to the liver ∙ muscle spasm and tics ∙ allergic reactions, some severe (very rare) ∙ hallucinations, difficulty in sleeping ∙ rapid heart beat ∙ stomach ache ∙ hives (urticaria) ∙ serious allergic reaction which causes difficulty in breathing or dizziness ∙ edema (swelling of the feet or ankles) Uncommon side effects (seen in less than 1 in 100 patients but in more than 1 per 1000 patients): Rare side effects (seen in less than 1 in 1000 patients) WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? ∙ feelings of weakness and/or extreme tiredness, feeling unwell ∙ a feeling of dizziness (vertigo) ∙ convulsions (fits), movement disorders ∙ burning, prickling sensation (feeling of pins and needles) ∙ involuntary eye movements Very rare side effects (seen in less than 1 in 10,000 patients) ∙ feelings of aggression, confusion and depression ∙ distorted sense of taste Side effects of unknown frequency ∙ an increased tendency to bruise or bleed easily ∙ forgetfulness, memory impairment ∙ difficulty passing water or In very rare cases, people have had suicidal thoughts when taking this medicine. If you experience this, stop taking the medicine and see your doctor. Long term treatment with Cetirizine Syrup can lead to a dry mouth, it is therefore important that adequate oral hygiene is maintained. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Other Medicines and Cetirizine Please tell your doctor or pharmacist if you are taking, have recently taken or might take any other medicines. Medication for anxiety or stress (CNS depressants) should be used in caution with cetirizine. ∙ involuntary movements or muscle contractions ∙ severe blistering skin rash ∙ difficult and/or painful urination Cetirizine Syrup can be taken with or without food. Be careful when drinking alcohol while using cetirizine. It can increase the effects of drinking. No interactions susceptible to have a noticeable impact have been observed between alcohol (at the blood level of 0.5 per mL corresponding to one glass of wine) and cetirizine used at the normal doses. However, as is the case with all antihistamines, it is recommended to avoid concurrent consumption of alcohol. ∙ swelling of the face, lips or throat If you have forgotten to take your medicine, take it as soon as you remember and then wait 24 hours before taking your next dose. Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten dose. ∙ loss of urinary control If you have any further questions on the use of this product, ask your doctor or pharmacist. Cetirizine with Food, Drink and Alcohol ∙ blurred vision, difficulty in focusing, eyes having uncontrolled circular movements (oculogyration) ∙ increased appetite, If any undesirable effect occurs. Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: September 15, 2023 Date of First Authorization: September 11, 2012 WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If you have accidentally taken more than the recommended/prescribed dose, contact your nearest hospital casualty department or tell your doctor or pharmacist immediately. Remember to take the pack and any remaining medicine with you. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have taken more than the recommended dose. AVAILABILITY Amber Glass Bottle with Measuring Cap x 60 mL (Box of 1's) ADR REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. If you are pregnant or think you may be, or are planning to become pregnant, or are breastfeeding. DRP-3707-02 The most common signs and symptoms of overdose may include feeling unwell, headache, confused, restless, shaky, dizzy, tired or very sleepy. You may also notice a rapid heartbeat, having dilated pupils or blurred vision, and experience headache, itching, diarrhea, or difficulty urinating. Size : 133x216 mm act med Imported by : AMBICA INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION No. 9 Amsterdam Extension, Merville Park Subd., Parañaque City, Philippines www.ambicaglobal.com Manufactured by :",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T14:51:45.328319+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3707-03,Cetirizine Hydrochloride,Unbranded,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WpIC911Kvif3JEg79hbFO5qG-H7auV_X/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3707-03_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WpIC911Kvif3JEg79hbFO5qG-H7auV_X_view_usp_drivesdk_5f6db4a0e7.pdf,page_text/DRP-3707-03_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WpIC911Kvif3JEg79hbFO5qG-H7auV_X_view_usp_drivesdk_5f6db4a0e7.json,f54a5fa783449ced47960b4767a012c1de4222e16552232f76c40e955f119c89,827988,1,digital_text,"Orange coloured syrup with sweet orange flavour. Cetirizine Hydrochloride BP .... 5 mg HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Children aged 2 or 5 years: 5 mL once daily or 2.5 mL twice daily. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Please see formulation. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? These are used to relieve the symptoms of seasonal allergic rhinitis (e.g., hay fever), perennial allergic rhinitis (e.g., year-round allergies often due to house dust mites or animal allergies) and urticaria (itchy, red, swollen skin). These symptoms include itchy skin rashes; sneezing; itchy, runny or blocked nose; red, itchy and watering eyes. Or as prescribed by the physician. In adults and children aged 6 years and over: 5 mL twice daily. The active ingredient in your medicine is cetirizine hydrochloride, which belongs to a group of medicines called antihistamines. Each 5 mL syrupcontains: For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. DRP-3707-03 ADR REPORTING STATEMENT Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Date of First Authorization: October 08, 2012 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: July 26, 2023 AVAILABILITY 60 mL Amber Glass Bottle (Box of 1's) If you are pregnant or think you may be, or are planning to become pregnant, or are breastfeeding. ∙ tics, shaking ∙ distorted sense of taste ∙ fainting ∙ involuntary movements or muscle contractions ∙ blurred vision, difficulty in focusing, eyes having uncontrolled circular movements (oculogyration) ∙ swelling of the face, lips or throat ∙ severe blistering skin rash ∙ difficult and/or painful urination SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE ∙ forgetfulness, memory impairment Remember to take the pack and any remaining medicine with you. ∙ an increased tendency to bruise or bleed easily Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Medication for anxiety or stress (CNS depressants) should be used in caution with cetirizine. Other Medicines and Cetirizine If any undesirable effect occurs. If you have taken more than the recommended dose. Side effects of unknown frequency ∙ increased appetite, Please tell your doctor or pharmacist if you are taking, have recently taken or might take any other medicines. Cetirizine with Food, Drink and Alcohol WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you have forgotten to take your medicine, take it as soon as you remember and then wait 24 hours before taking your next dose. Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten dose. ∙ loss of urinary control ∙ difficulty passing water or In very rare cases, people have had suicidal thoughts when taking this medicine. If you experience this, stop taking the medicine and see your doctor. ∙ a feeling of dizziness (vertigo) Long term treatment with Cetirizine Syrup can lead to a dry mouth, it is therefore important that adequate oral hygiene is maintained. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Cetirizine Syrup can be taken with or without food. Be careful when drinking alcohol while using cetirizine. It can increase the effects of drinking. No interactions susceptible to have a noticeable impact have been observed between alcohol (at the blood level of 0.5 per mL corresponding to one glass of wine) and cetirizine used at the normal doses. However, as is the case with all antihistamines, it is recommended to avoid concurrent consumption of alcohol. If you have any further questions on the use of this product, ask your doctor or pharmacist. The most common signs and symptoms of overdose may include feeling unwell, headache, confused, restless, shaky, dizzy, tired or very sleepy. You may also notice a rapid heartbeat, having dilated pupils or blurred vision, and experience headache, itching, diarrhea, or difficulty urinating. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have accidentally taken more than the recommended/prescribed dose, contact your nearest hospital casualty department or tell your doctor or pharmacist immediately. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? ∙ serious allergic reaction which causes difficulty in breathing or dizziness ∙ agitation ∙ hallucinations, difficulty in sleeping ∙ burning, prickling sensation (feeling of pins and needles) ∙ involuntary eye movements ∙ convulsions (fits), movement disorders ∙ feelings of weakness and/or extreme tiredness, feeling unwell ∙ hives (urticaria) ∙ rash, itching ∙ stomach ache Rare side effects (seen in less than 1 in 1000 patients) ∙ feelings of aggression, confusion and depression ∙ rapid heart beat ∙ edema (swelling of the feet or ankles) Uncommon side effects (seen in less than 1 in 100 patients but in more than 1 per 1000 patients): ∙ muscle spasm and tics ∙ allergic reactions, some severe (very rare) ∙ unusual weight gain ∙ changes in liver function tests, indicating the possibility of damage to the liver Very rare side effects (seen in less than 1 in 10,000 patients) Size : 133x216 mm [Page 2]",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T14:51:48.350988+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3707-04,Cetirizine Hydrochloride,Qualcet,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1eJtrPMZK1tF4Cny9cQxV5S7h0T2VJZy1/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3707-04_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eJtrPMZK1tF4Cny9cQxV5S7h0T2VJZy1_view_usp_drivesdk_0ad696bb70.pdf,page_text/DRP-3707-04_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eJtrPMZK1tF4Cny9cQxV5S7h0T2VJZy1_view_usp_drivesdk_0ad696bb70.json,a5532dd3c12f929151642024dd6e75db3b4a8f58de06f4aba7386b6364d6f544,454920,1,digital_text,"These are used to relieve the symptoms of seasonal allergic rhinitis (e.g., hay fever), perennial allergic rhinitis (e.g., year-round allergies often due to house dust mites or animal allergies) and urticaria (itchy, red, swollen skin). These symptoms include itchy skin rashes; sneezing; itchy, runny or blocked nose; red, itchy and watering eyes. ∙ are allergic (hypersensitive) to cetirizine hydrochloride, hydroxyzine, piperazine derivatives or any of the other ingredients in Cetirizine Syrup. ∙ If you have renal insufficiency or have kidney problems. If you are intending to drive, engage in potentially hazardous activities or operate machinery, you should not exceed the recommended dose. You should closely observe your response to the drug. If you are a sensitive patient, you may find that the simultaneous use of alcohol or other nervous depressant agents may additionally affect your attention and ability to react. Do not drive or operate machinery if the solution makes you feel drowsy. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Like all medicines, Cetirizine Syrup can cause side effects, although not everybody gets them. If you get any of the following symptoms after taking this medicine you should contact your doctor or pharmacist immediately: ∙ any sudden wheeziness, difficulty in breathing If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, think you might be pregnant or are planning to become pregnant, ask your doctor or pharmacist for advice before taking this medicine. As with other drugs, the use of Cetirizine Syrup should be avoided in pregnant women. Accidental use of the drug by a pregnant woman should not produce any harmful effects on the fetus. Nevertheless, the administration of the medicine should be discontinued. You should not take Cetirizine Syrup during breastfeeding because cetirizine passes into your breast milk. ∙ sudden signs of an allergic reaction such as developing a rash, swelling of the eyelids, face, lips or throat ∙ loss of consciousness Pregnancy, Breastfeeding and Fertility Clinical studies have produced no evidence of impaired attention, alertness and driving capabilities after taking Cetirizine Syrup at the recommended dose. ∙ convulsions or fits ∙ dizziness ∙ worsening cough ∙ fatigue Common side effects (seen in less than 1 in 10 patients but in more than 1 in 100 patients): ∙ dry mouth, nausea (feeling sick), diarrhea ∙ dizziness, headache ∙ sore or inflamed throat ∙ abdominal pain ∙ restlessness WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? AVAILABILITY Medication for anxiety or stress (CNS depressants) should be used in caution with cetirizine. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? The most common signs and symptoms of overdose may include feeling unwell, headache, confused, restless, shaky, dizzy, tired or very sleepy. You may also notice a rapid heartbeat, having dilated pupils or blurred vision, and experience headache, itching, diarrhea, or difficulty urinating. Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: September 15, 2023 SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE Cetirizine Syrup can be taken with or without food. Be careful when drinking alcohol while using cetirizine. It can increase the effects of drinking. No interactions susceptible to have a noticeable impact have been observed between alcohol (at the blood level of 0.5 per mL corresponding to one glass of wine) and cetirizine used at the normal doses. However, as is the case with all antihistamines, it is recommended to avoid concurrent consumption of alcohol. Long term treatment with Cetirizine Syrup can lead to a dry mouth, it is therefore important that adequate oral hygiene is maintained. Cetirizine with Food, Drink and Alcohol If you have any further questions on the use of this product, ask your doctor or pharmacist. If you have forgotten to take your medicine, take it as soon as you remember and then wait 24 hours before taking your next dose. Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten dose. Remember to take the pack and any remaining medicine with you. In very rare cases, people have had suicidal thoughts when taking this medicine. If you experience this, stop taking the medicine and see your doctor. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? If you have accidentally taken more than the recommended/prescribed dose, contact your nearest hospital casualty department or tell your doctor or pharmacist immediately. Please tell your doctor or pharmacist if you are taking, have recently taken or might take any other medicines. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? If any undesirable effect occurs. Other Medicines and Cetirizine If you are pregnant or think you may be, or are planning to become pregnant, or are breastfeeding. If you have taken more than the recommended dose. 60 mL Amber Glass Bottle (Box of 1's) Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. ADR REPORTING STATEMENT Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. DRP-3707-04 Date of First Authorization: August 22, 2013 ∙ difficulty passing water or ∙ severe blistering skin rash ∙ forgetfulness, memory impairment ∙ blurred vision, difficulty in focusing, eyes having uncontrolled circular movements (oculogyration) ∙ increased appetite, ∙ difficult and/or painful urination Side effects of unknown frequency ∙ loss of urinary control ∙ a feeling of dizziness (vertigo) ∙ swelling of the face, lips or throat ∙ an increased tendency to bruise or bleed easily Uncommon side effects (seen in less than 1 in 100 patients but in more than 1 per 1000 patients): ∙ agitation ∙ involuntary eye movements ∙ hallucinations, difficulty in sleeping ∙ distorted sense of taste ∙ edema (swelling of the feet or ankles) ∙ tics, shaking ∙ fainting Very rare side effects (seen in less than 1 in 10,000 patients) ∙ involuntary movements or muscle contractions ∙ muscle spasm and tics ∙ burning, prickling sensation (feeling of pins and needles) ∙ allergic reactions, some severe (very rare) ∙ rapid heart beat ∙ stomach ache ∙ feelings of weakness and/or extreme tiredness, feeling unwell Rare side effects (seen in less than 1 in 1000 patients) ∙ convulsions (fits), movement disorders ∙ unusual weight gain ∙ hives (urticaria) ∙ feelings of aggression, confusion and depression ∙ changes in liver function tests, indicating the possibility of damage to the liver ∙ serious allergic reaction which causes difficulty in breathing or dizziness ∙ rash, itching Size : 133x216 mm 5 mg / 5 mL Syrup ANTIHISTAMINE QUALCET CETIRIZINE [Page 2]",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T14:51:51.775586+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3707-05,Cetirizine Hydrochloride,Unbranded,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-WnGhP0XGm9fpo6yyJYoAwFKLWF5nMn6/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3707-05_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-WnGhP0XGm9fpo6yyJYoAwFKLWF5nMn6_view_usp_drivesdk_bf131934df.pdf,page_text/DRP-3707-05_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-WnGhP0XGm9fpo6yyJYoAwFKLWF5nMn6_view_usp_drivesdk_bf131934df.json,7eeea037fbcfad8af319b5e24ba93bf620c551fd315f64e132774f1c54aef0fb,830477,1,digital_text,,1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T14:51:55.546983+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3707-06,Cetirizine Hydrochloride,Ziridim,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/19Xa69oHAl47iOQvWq35r6d413gTm8nZa/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3707-06_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19Xa69oHAl47iOQvWq35r6d413gTm8nZa_view_usp_drivesdk_8518b78e34.pdf,page_text/DRP-3707-06_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19Xa69oHAl47iOQvWq35r6d413gTm8nZa_view_usp_drivesdk_8518b78e34.json,331d025a095a3ab35a226dd56e51c2ef14f658943872ec2188274b2a869bc767,451746,1,digital_text,"Or as prescribed by the physician. Orange coloured syrup with sweet orange flavour. The active ingredient in your medicine is cetirizine hydrochloride, which belongs to a group of medicines called antihistamines. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Please see formulation. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? In adults and children aged 6 years and over: 5 mL twice daily. Children aged 2 or 5 years: 5 mL once daily or 2.5 mL twice daily.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T14:51:58.442217+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-371,Valsartan + Hydrochlorothiazide,Co-Diovan,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/13UMX3ruWzO52E29pXfGzlKVSxKDAHB0P/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-371_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13UMX3ruWzO52E29pXfGzlKVSxKDAHB0P_view_usp_drivesdk_b5a5d17425.pdf,page_text/DRP-371_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13UMX3ruWzO52E29pXfGzlKVSxKDAHB0P_view_usp_drivesdk_b5a5d17425.json,ea14f05455698a48f32a06d6b66a53e2a764555130354d40623f4b8fe5b9490f,266701,22,digital_text,"Film-coated tablets (FCT) 80/12.5 mg, 160/12.5 mg, 160/25 mg, 320/12.5 mg, 320/25 mg. Co-Diovan 80/12.5 mg: Ovaloid slightly convex, non -divisible, film -coated tablets measuring approximately 10.2 mm in length and approximately 5.4 mm in width, and weighing approximately 156 mg. The tablets are colored light orange and debossed “HGH” on one side and “CG” on the other side. Co-Diovan 160/12.5 mg: Ovaloid slightly convex, non -divisible, film -coated tablets measuring approximately 15.2 mm in length and approximately 6.2 mm in width, and weighing approximately 312 mg. The tablets are colored dark red and debossed “HHH” on one side and “CG” on the other side. Co-Diovan 160/25 mg: Ovaloid slightly convex, non -divisible, film -coated tablets measuring approximately 14.2 mm in length and approximately 5.7 mm in width, and weighing approximately 310 mg. The tablets are colored brown -orange and debossed “HXH” on one side and “NVR” on the other side. Co-Diovan 320/12.5 mg: Ovaloid slightly convex, non -divisible, film -coated tablets measuring approximately 17.6 mm in length and approximately 8.2 mm in width, and weighing approximately 608 mg. The tablets are colored pink and debossed “HIL” on one side and “NVR” on the other side. Co-Diovan 320/25 mg: Ovaloid slightly convex, non -divisible, film -coated tablets measuring approximately 17.7 mm in length and approximately 8.2 mm in width, and weighing approximately 620 mg. The tablets are colored yellow and debossed “CTI” on one side and “NVR” on the other side. Co-Diovan® FCT cannot be divided into equal doses. Valsartan Hydrochlorothiazide [Page 2] Active substances One tablet contains 80 mg valsartan and 12.5 mg hy drochlorothiazide, or 160 mg valsartan and 12.5 mg hydrochlorothiazide, or 160 mg valsartan and 25 mg hydrochlorothiazide, or 320 mg valsartan and 12.5 mg hydrochlorothiazide, or 320 mg valsartan and 25 mg hydrochlorothiazide. Appearance of tablets may var y between countries. Certain dosage strengths may not be available in all countries. EXCIPIENTS 80/12.5 mg: Colloidal silicon dioxide; crospovidone; hydroxypropyl methylcellulose; magnesium stearate; microcrystalline cellulose; polyethylene glycol; talc; titanium dioxide (E171); red iron oxide (E172); yellow iron oxide (E172). 160/12.5 mg: Colloidal silicon dioxide; crospovidone; hydroxypropyl -methylcellulose; magnesium stearate; microcrystalline cellulose; polyethylene glycol; talc; titanium dioxide (E171); red iron oxide (E172). 160/25 mg: Colloidal silicon dioxide; crospovidone; hydroxypropyl methylcellulose; magnesium stearate; microcrystalline cellulose; polyethylene glycol; talc; titanium dioxide (E171), red iron oxide (E172), yellow iron oxide (E172) , black iron oxide",1,2,Pharmaceutical form,"Treatment of hypertension in adults, 18 years of age and older . Treatment of hypertension in patients whose blood pressure is not adequately controlled by monotherapy. As initial therapy in patients who are likely to need multiple drugs to achieve blood pressure goals. The choice as initial therapy for hypertension should be based on an assessment of potential benefits and risks. [Page 3]",2,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:52:05.369843+00:00
