PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3746-01,Co-Amoxiclav,Amoclav,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NWdTYIN0ugxOSo87PuuPDvKtPwzNC4TC/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3746-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1NWdTYIN0ugxOSo87PuuPDvKtPwzNC4TC_view_usp_drivesdk_d6e98489bd.pdf,page_text/DRP-3746-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1NWdTYIN0ugxOSo87PuuPDvKtPwzNC4TC_view_usp_drivesdk_d6e98489bd.json,4e0e6c30e2129fb0efeefb4f892575dec996e578cc2f9c470946d16c66937af6,830903,1,digital_text,"Skin and soft tissue infections typically caused by Staphylococcus aureus, Streptococcus pyogenes and Bacteroides species.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"produce these enzymes. Clavulanic acid is a beta-lactam structurally related to penicillins. It inactivates some beta-lactamase enzymes thereby preventing inactivation of amoxicillin. Eq. to Amoxicillin.......................................500 mg Amoxicillin Sodium BP PRODUCT DESCRIPTION Skin and soft tissue infections typically caused by Staphylococcus aureus, Streptococcus pyogenes and Bacteroides species. FORMULATION Clavulanic acid alone does not exert a clinically useful antibacterial effect. catarrhalis and Streptococcus pyogenes. Lower respiratory tract infections e.g. acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis, lobar and bronchopneumonia, typically caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae, Haemophilus influenzae Amoxicillin is a semisynthetic penicillin (beta-lactam antibiotic) that inhibits one or more enzymes (often referred to as penicillin-binding proteins, PBPs) in the biosynthetic pathway of PHARMACODYNAMICS Each vial contains: Potassium Clavulanate BP Amoxicillin is susceptible to degradation by beta-lactamases produced by resistant bacteria and therefore the spectrum of activity of amoxicillin alone does not include organisms which Eq. to Clavulanic Acid...............................100 mg bacterial peptidoglycan, which is an integral structural component of the bacterial cell wall. Inhibition of peptidoglycan synthesis leads to weakening of the cell wall, which is usually followed The pharmacokinetics of the two components of Co-amoxiclav are closely matched. In Infant Drops, peak serum levels of both occur about 1 hour after oral administration. Absorption of Co-amoxiclav is optimised at the start of a meal. Doubling the dosage of Co-amoxiclav approximately doubles the serum levels achieved. A white to off white coloured free flowing powder filled in an intactly sealed clear glass vials after reconstitution with sterile water for injection 10 mL it forms a white to off white coloured clear solution. by cell lysis and death. Mechanism of Action: Both clavulanate and amoxicillin have low levels of serum-binding; about 70% remains free in the serum. PHARMACOKINETICS Co-amoxiclav should be used in accordance with local official antibiotic-prescribing guidelines and local susceptibility data. Adult Formulations: Co-amoxiclav is indicated for short term treatment of bacterial infections at the following sites when caused by amoxicillin-clavulanate-susceptible organisms: Upper respiratory tract infections (including ENT) e.g. recurrent tonsillitis, sinusitis, otitis media, typically caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae , Haemophilus influenzae, Moraxella and Moraxella catarrhalis. Genitourinary tract infections e.g. cystitis, urethritis, pyelonephritis and female genital infections typically caused by Enterobacteriaceae (mainly Escherichia coli ), Staphylococcus saprophyticus and Enterococcus species and gonorrhea caused by Neisseria gonorrhoeae. Bone and joint infections e.g. osteomyelitis typically caused by Staphylococcus aureus, where more prolonged therapy may be appropriate. Other infections e.g. septic abortion, puerperal sepsis, intra-abdominal sepsis. Upper respiratory tract infections (including ENT) e.g. recurrent tonsillitis, sinusitis, otitis media typically caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae , Haemophilus influenzae, Moraxella Pediatric Formulations: Co-amoxiclav is indicated for short term treatment of bacterial infections at the following sites when caused by amoxicillin-clavulanate sensitive organisms: Skin and soft tissue infections typically caused by Staphylococcus aureus, Streptococcus pyogenes and Bacteroides species. Co-amoxiclav Pediatric Three Times Daily: The pediatric three times daily dosing regimen is also indicated for the following infections: Bone and joint infections e.g. osteomyelitis typically caused by Staphylococcus aureus, where more prolonged therapy may be appropriate. Other infections e.g. septic abortion, puerperal sepsis, intra-abdominal sepsis. Lower respiratory tract infections e.g. acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis, lobar and bronchopneumonia typically caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae, Haemophilus influenzae and Moraxella catarrhalis . Genitourinary tract infections e.g. cystitis, urethritis, pyelonephritis, female genital infections typically caused by Enterobacteriaceae (mainly Escherichia coli ), Staphylococcus saprophyticus and Enterococcus species and gonorrhea caused by Neisseria gonorrhoeae. Susceptibility to Co-amoxiclav will vary with geography and time. Local susceptibility data should be consulted where available, and microbiological sampling and susceptibility testing performed where necessary. Infection caused by amoxicillin-susceptible organisms are amenable to Co-amoxiclav treatment due to its amoxicillin content. Mixed infections caused by amoxicillin-susceptible organisms catarrhalis and Streptococcus pyogenes. All Formulations: Some members of these species of bacteria produce beta-lactamase, rendering them insensitive to amoxicillin alone. in conjunction with amoxicillin-clavulanate-susceptible beta-lactamase-producing organisms may therefore be treated with Co-amoxiclav. Injection: Co-amoxiclav intravenous is also indicated for prophylaxis against infection which may be associated with major surgical procedures such as gastrointestinal, pelvic, head and neck, cardiac, renal, joint replacement and biliary tract.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:52:49.677151+00:00
