PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3810,Pyrazinamide + Ethambutol hydrochloride + Rifampicin + Isoniazid,Myrin P Forte,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mm9FYHX0Yjbg_0quVFSNEioDdyFsCaZZ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3810_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mm9FYHX0Yjbg_0quVFSNEioDdyFsCaZZ_view_usp_drivesdk_157cf7e7ad.pdf,page_text/DRP-3810_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mm9FYHX0Yjbg_0quVFSNEioDdyFsCaZZ_view_usp_drivesdk_157cf7e7ad.json,2288b8f2e70a55cccbe2991c2aac40e4e1cde5b865aee994d850677fa2e1f5b4,331496,19,digital_text,"Ethambutol has a chemical name (S,S)-N,N′-Ethylenebis (2-aminobutan-1-ol) dihydrochloride. It is a white or almost white, hygroscopic, crystalline powder. Freely soluble in water; soluble in alcohol. A 2% solution in water has a pH of 3.7 to 4.0. Rifampicin has a chemical name 3-(4-Methylpiperazine-1-yliminomethyl) rifamycin SV; (12Z,14E,24E)-(2S,16S,17S,18R,19R,20R,21S,22R,23S)-1,2-Dihydro-5,6,9,17,19- pentahydroxy-23-methoxy-2,4,12,16,18,20,22-heptamethyl-8-(4-methylpiperazin-1- yliminomethyl)-1,11-dioxo-2,7-(epoxypentadeca[1,11,13] trienimino) naphtho[2,1-b] furan- 21-yl acetate. It is a reddish-brown or brownish-red, crystalline powder. Slightly soluble in water, in alcohol, and in acetone; soluble in methyl alcohol. A 1% suspension has a pH of 4.5 to 6.5. Isoniazid has a chemical name Isonicotinohydrazide. It is a white or almost white, crystalline powder or colorless crystals. Freely soluble in water; sparingly soluble in alcohol. A 5% solution in water has a pH of 6.0 to 8.0. Pyrazinamide has a chemical name Pyrazine-2-carboxamide. It is a white or almost white, crystalline powder. It shows polymorphism. Sparingly soluble in water; slightly soluble in alcohol and in dichloromethane.",1,1,2.0. DESCRIPTION,"Pyrazinamide + Ethambutol HCl + Rifampicin + Isoniazid (Myrin-P Forte) is indicated for the initial or intensive phase treatment of new and re-treatment cases of pulmonary and extrapulmonary tuberculosis (TB) caused by susceptible strains of mycobacteria. New patients: Never had treatment for TB, or have taken anti-TB drugs for less than 1 month. These patients may have positive or negative bacteriology and may have disease at any anatomical site. Previously treated patients: Patients who have received 1 month or more of anti-TB drugs in the past, may h ave positive or negative bacteriology a nd may h ave disease at any anatomical site.",2,2,4.1. Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:53:57.521654+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3818-02,Tamsulosin Hydrochloride,Tamzu,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ErGG8whq21JBL1OVK0SDoc24Kpcu0Is6/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3818-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ErGG8whq21JBL1OVK0SDoc24Kpcu0Is6_view_usp_drivesdk_4b0f58e20d.pdf,page_text/DRP-3818-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ErGG8whq21JBL1OVK0SDoc24Kpcu0Is6_view_usp_drivesdk_4b0f58e20d.json,bd7def9df962257f48a1cc90618ddc90d0096bb3cbc3e7eddb5b108b0909185b,424553,1,digital_text,Orange colored diamond biconvex shaped ﬁlm coated tablet with break line on one side other side plain.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Tamsulosin is an alpha1-adrenoceptor blocker with ac␀ons similar to those of prazosin; it is reported to be more selec␀ve for the alpha1-adrenoceptor subtype, which accounts for about 70% of the alpha1-adrenoceptors in the prostate. It is used in benign prosta␀c hyperplasia to relieve symptoms of urinary obstruc␀on.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:54:00.446223+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3821,Ketoconazole,Funginil-K,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ldmeSNGRX6-J4-J6iawoy7eas5IxD9HN/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3821_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ldmeSNGRX6-J4-J6iawoy7eas5IxD9HN_view_usp_drivesdk_8d17d96a17.pdf,page_text/DRP-3821_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ldmeSNGRX6-J4-J6iawoy7eas5IxD9HN_view_usp_drivesdk_8d17d96a17.json,4617257125d3cfaee8dac51e3d73d240fafae86fa24a45803d3c41abda965c18,1421517,1,digital_text,A white colour smooth cream filled in aluminum collapsible tube.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Ketoconazole is indicated for topical application in the treatment of dermatophyte infections of the skinTinea corporis, Tinea cruris, Tinea manus, and Tinea pedis due to Trichophyton rubrum, as well as in the treatment of cutaneous candidiasis and Tinea (pityriasis) versicolor.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:54:03.712111+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3826-01,Spironolactone,Beralactone,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KA-WUeYZuJyI_t3M5Wt--frt6A7zvdGF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3826-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1KA-WUeYZuJyI_t3M5Wt--frt6A7zvdGF_view_usp_drivesdk_bb5647e5f1.pdf,page_text/DRP-3826-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1KA-WUeYZuJyI_t3M5Wt--frt6A7zvdGF_view_usp_drivesdk_bb5647e5f1.json,59946b3ec504818fe5a55a4a2d27f76b9477beb71707d213da15237b91cf1153,905284,1,digital_text,"Buff-colored, biconvex, round-shaped tablets, engraved ""SEARLE"" on one side and plain on other side with odour of peppermint.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Spironolactone is used in the management heart failure, both to treat refractory edema and in lower doses as an adjunct to standard therapy. It is also used for refractory edema associated with cirrhosis of the liver (with or without ascites), or nephrotic syndrome, and in ascites associated with malignancy. It is frequently given thiazides, furosemide, or similar diuretics, where it adds to their natriuretic but diminishes their kaliuretic effect, hence conserving potassium in those at risk from hypokalemia. It has been used in the treatment of primary essential hypotension. Spironolactone is also used in the diagnosis and treatment of primary hyperaldosteronism. Other conditions in which spironolactone has been tried on the basis of its anti-androgenic properties include hirsutism, particularly in the polycystic ovary syndrome.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:54:07.015196+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3834,Loratadine,Lorfast,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zDpGiiUrmpLk3EkulAmt4m3r-EVgFVZO/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3834_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zDpGiiUrmpLk3EkulAmt4m3r-EVgFVZO_view_usp_drivesdk_e59a79a99f.pdf,page_text/DRP-3834_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zDpGiiUrmpLk3EkulAmt4m3r-EVgFVZO_view_usp_drivesdk_e59a79a99f.json,edd6f8afbf2e88a2a93bc8e5e41bf46a76a0d8c11f98e5cd6a29ab5f017bc1c5,659071,1,digital_text,"White round, smooth, flat, bevel edged uncoated tablets.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Loratadine is indicated in conditions which respond to antihistaminic therapy such as: - Seasonal allergic-rhinitis - Perennial allergic-rhinitis - Acute Coryza (common colds) - Chronic idiopathic urticaria and similar allergic and dermatological disorders,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:54:15.493816+00:00
