ased on cumula�ve meta-analysis with pooling of trials represen�ng exposure in 38,102 pa�ents. In ﬁnal data (adjudicated) from the APC and PreSAP trials in pa�ents treated with celecoxib 400 mg daily for up to 3 years (pooled data from both trials; see Pharmacodynamic proper�es for results from individual trials), the excess rate over placebo for myocardial infarc�on was 7.6 events per 1,000 pa�ents (uncommon) and there was no excess rate for stroke (types not diﬀeren�ated) over placebo. Overdose There is no clinical experience of overdose. Single doses up to 1,200 mg and mul�ple doses up to 1,200 mg twice daily have been administered to healthy subjects for nine days without clinically signiﬁcant adverse eﬀects. In the event of suspected overdose, appropriate suppor�ve medical care should be [Page 12] Celecoxib (Coﬁdec) 100, 200 mg Capule SDZ provided e.g. by elimina�ng the gastric contents, clinical supervision and, if necessary, the ins�tu�on of symptoma�c treatment. Dialysis is unlikely to be an eﬃcient method of medicinal product removal due to high protein binding.",1,12,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,In adults for the symptoma�c relief in the treatment of - osteoarthri�s - rheumatoid arthri�s - ankylosing spondyli�s. The decision to prescribe a selec�ve cyclooxygenase-2 (COX-2) inhibitor should be based on an assessment of the individual pa�ent's overall risks (see Contraindica�ons and Special warnings and precau�ons for use).,1,1,Therapeu�c indica�ons,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T14:55:35.102467+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3857,Celecoxib,Cofidec,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DjykQySZM5vylyOQrfEpePH4-OJ3ngxT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3857_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1DjykQySZM5vylyOQrfEpePH4-OJ3ngxT_view_usp_drivesdk_f2ad4a3fe1.pdf,page_text/DRP-3857_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1DjykQySZM5vylyOQrfEpePH4-OJ3ngxT_view_usp_drivesdk_f2ad4a3fe1.json,9d7d4f0009ad64592b5a00885297fda29ebb7c4619d8bd59fa2a106f3e09a6e9,355916,16,digital_text,"Capsule CLINICAL PARTICULARS Therapeu�c indica�ons In adults for the symptoma�c relief in the treatment of - osteoarthri�s - rheumatoid arthri�s - ankylosing spondyli�s. The decision to prescribe a selec�ve cyclooxygenase-2 (COX-2) inhibitor should be based on an assessment of the individual pa�ent's overall risks (see Contraindica�ons and Special warnings and precau�ons for use). Dosage and method of administra�on Dosage As the cardiovascular risks of celecoxib may increase with dose and dura�on of exposure, the shortest dura�on possible and the lowest eﬀec�ve daily dose should be used. The pa�ent's need for symptoma�c relief and response to therapy should be re-evaluated periodically, especially in pa�ents with osteoarthri�s (see Contraindica�ons, Special warnings and precau�ons for use, Undesirable eﬀects and Pharmacodynamic proper�es). Osteoarthritis The usual recommended daily dose is 200 mg taken once daily or in two divided doses. In some pa�ents, with insuﬃcient relief from symptoms, an increased dose of 200 mg twice daily may increase eﬃcacy. In the absence of an increase in therapeu�c beneﬁt a�er two weeks, other therapeu�c op�ons should be considered. Rheumatoid arthritis The ini�al recommended daily dose is 200 mg taken in two divided doses. The dose may, if needed, later be increased to 200 mg twice daily. In the absence of an increase in therapeu�c beneﬁt a�er two weeks, other therapeu�c op�ons should be considered. Ankylosing spondylitis The recommended daily dose is 200 mg taken once daily or in two divided doses. In a few pa�ents, with insuﬃcient relief from symptoms, an increased dose of 400 mg once daily or in two divided doses may increase eﬃcacy. In the absence of an increase in therapeu�c beneﬁt a�er two weeks, other Celecoxib [Page 2] Celecoxib (Coﬁdec) 100, 200 mg Capule SDZ therapeu�c op�ons should be considered. The maximum recommended daily dose is 400 mg for all indica�ons. Special populations Elderly (>65 years) As in younger adults, 200 mg per day should be used ini�ally. The dose may, if needed, later be increased to 200 mg twice daily. Par�cular cau�on should be exercised in elderly with a body weight less than 50 kg (see Special warnings and precau�ons for use and Pharmacokine�c proper�es). Hepatic impairment Treatment should be ini�ated at half the recommended dose in pa�ents with established moderate liver impairment with a serum albumin of 25-35 g/L. Experience in such pa�ents is limited to cirrho�c pa�ents (see Contraindica�ons, Special warnings and precau�ons for use and Pharmacokine�c proper�es). Renal impairment Experience with celecoxib in pa�ents with mild or moderate renal impairment is limited, therefore such pa�ents should be treated with cau�on (see Contraindica�ons, Special warnings and precau�ons for use and Pharmacokine�c proper�es). Paediatric population Celecoxib is not indicated for use in children. CYP2C9 poor metabolisers Pa�ents who are known, or suspected to be CYP2C9 poor metabolisers based on genotyping or previous history/experience with other CYP2C9 substrates should be administered celecoxib with cau�on as the risk of dose-dependent adverse eﬀects is increased. Consider reducing the dose to half the lowest recommended dose (see Pharmacokine�c proper�es). Method of administra�on Oral use. Celecoxib may be taken with or without food. For pa�ents who have diﬃculty swallowing capsules, the contents of a celecoxib capsule can be added to applesauce, rice gruel, yogurt or mashed banana. To do so, the en�re capsule contents must be carefully emp�ed onto a level teaspoon of cool or room temperature applesauce, rice gruel, yogurt or mashed banana and should be ingested immediately with 240 mL of water. The sprinkled capsule contents on applesauce, rice gruel or yogurt are stable for up to 6 hours under refrigerated condi�ons (2-8°C). The sprinkled capsule contents on mashed banana should not be stored under refrigerated condi�ons and should be ingested immediately. Contraindica�ons - Hypersensi�vity to the ac�ve substance or to any of the excipients. - Known hypersensi�vity to sulphonamides. - Ac�ve pep�c ulcera�on or gastrointes�nal (GI) bleeding. [Page 3] Celecoxib (Coﬁdec) 100, 200 mg Capule SDZ - Pa�ents who have experienced asthma, acute rhini�s, nasal polyps, angioneuro�c oedema, ur�caria or other allergic-type reac�ons a�er taking acetylsalicylic acid (aspirin) or other nonsteroidal an�-inﬂammatory drugs (NSAIDs) including COX-2 inhibitors. - In pregnancy and in women of childbearing poten�al unless using an eﬀec�ve method of contracep�on (see Pregnancy and lacta�on). Celecoxib has been shown to cause malforma�ons in the two animal species studied (see Pregnancy and lacta�on and Preclinical safety data). The poten�al for human risk in pregnancy is unknown, but cannot be excluded - Breas�eeding (see Pregnancy and lacta�on and Preclinical safety data). - Severe hepa�c dysfunc�on (serum albumin <25 g/L or Child-Pugh score ≥10). - Pa�ents with es�mated crea�nine clearance <30 mL/min. - Inﬂammatory bowel disease. - Conges�ve heart failure (NYHA II-IV). - Established ischaemic heart disease, peripheral arterial disease and/or cerebrovascular disease. Special warnings and precau�ons for use Gastrointes�nal (GI) eﬀects Upper and lower gastrointes�nal complica�ons [perfora�ons, ulcers or bleedings (PUBs)], some of them resul�ng in fatal outcome, have occurred in pa�ents treated with celecoxib. Cau�on