 proper�es). Pa�ents with signiﬁcant risk factors for cardiovascular events (e.g. hypertension, hyperlipidaemia, diabetes mellitus, smoking) should only be treated with celecoxib a�er careful considera�on (see Pharmacodynamic proper�es). COX-2 selec�ve inhibitors are not a subs�tute for acetylsalicylic acid for prophylaxis of cardiovascular thromboembolic diseases because of their lack of an�platelet eﬀects. Therefore, an�platelet therapies should not be discon�nued (see Pharmacodynamic proper�es). Fluid reten�on and oedema As with other medicinal products known to inhibit prostaglandin synthesis ﬂuid reten�on and oedema have been observed in pa�ents taking celecoxib. Therefore, celecoxib should be used with cau�on in pa�ents with history of cardiac failure, le� ventricular dysfunc�on or hypertension, and in pa�ents with pre-exis�ng oedema from any other reason, since prostaglandin inhibi�on may result in deteriora�on of renal func�on and ﬂuid reten�on. Cau�on is also required in pa�ents taking diure�c treatment or otherwise at risk of hypovolaemia. Hypertension As with all NSAIDS, celecoxib can lead to the onset of new hypertension or worsening of pre-exis�ng hypertension, either of which may contribute to the increased incidence of cardiovascular events. Therefore, blood pressure should be monitored closely during the ini�a�on of therapy with celecoxib and throughout the course of therapy. Hepa�c and renal eﬀects Compromised renal or hepa�c func�on and especially cardiac dysfunc�on are more likely in the elderly and therefore medically appropriate supervision should be maintained. NSAIDs, including celecoxib, may cause renal toxicity. Clinical trials with celecoxib have shown renal eﬀects similar to those observed with comparator NSAIDs. Pa�ents at greatest risk for renal toxicity are those with impaired renal func�on, heart failure, liver dysfunc�on, those taking diure�cs, angiotensin conver�ng enzyme (ACE-)-inhibitors, angiotensin II receptor antagonists, and the elderly (see Interac�on with other medicinal products and other forms of interac�ons). Such pa�ents should be carefully monitored while receiving treatment with celecoxib. Some cases of severe hepa�c reac�ons, including fulminant hepa��s (some with fatal outcome), liver necrosis and, hepa�c failure (some with fatal outcome or requiring liver transplant), have been reported with celecoxib. Among the cases that reported �me to onset, most of the severe adverse hepa�c events developed within one month a�er ini�a�on of celecoxib treatment (see Undesirable eﬀects). If during treatment, pa�ents deteriorate in any of the organ system func�ons described above, appropriate measures should be taken and discon�nua�on of celecoxib therapy should be considered. CYP2D6 inhibi�on Celecoxib inhibits CYP2D6. Although it is not a strong inhibitor of this enzyme, a dose reduc�on may be [Page 5] Celecoxib (Coﬁdec) 100, 200 mg Capule SDZ necessary for individually dose-�trated medicinal products that are metabolised by CYP2D6 (see Interac�on with other medicinal products and other forms of interac�ons). CYP2C9 poor metabolisers Pa�ents known to be CYP2C9 poor metabolisers should be treated with cau�on (see Pharmacokine�c proper�es). Skin and systemic hypersensi�vity reac�ons Serious skin reac�ons, some of them fatal, including exfolia�ve derma��s, Stevens-Johnson syndrome, and toxic epidermal necrolysis, have been reported very rarely in associa�on with the use of celecoxib (see Undesirable eﬀects). Pa�ents appear to be at highest risk for these reac�ons early in the course of therapy: the onset of the reac�on occurring in the majority of cases within the ﬁrst month of treatment. Serious hypersensi�vity reac�ons (including anaphylaxis, angioedema and drug rash with eosinophilia and systemic symptoms (DRESS), or hypersensi�vity syndrome), have been reported in pa�ents receiving celecoxib (see Undesirable eﬀects). Pa�ents with a history of sulphonamide allergy or any drug allergy may be at greater risk of serious skin reac�ons or hypersensi�vity reac�ons (see Contraindica�ons). Celecoxib should be discon�nued at the ﬁrst appearance of skin rash, mucosal lesions, or any other sign of hypersensi�vity. General Celecoxib may mask fever and other signs of inﬂamma�on. Use with oral an�coagulants In pa�ents on concurrent therapy with warfarin, serious bleeding events, some of them fatal, have been reported. Increased prothrombin �me (INR) with concurrent therapy has been reported. Therefore, this should be closely monitored in pa�ents receiving warfarin/coumarin-type oral an�coagulants, par�cularly when therapy with celecoxib is ini�ated or celecoxib dose is changed (see Interac�on with other medicinal products and other forms of interac�ons). Concomitant use of an�coagulants with NSAIDS may increase the risk of bleeding. Cau�on should be exercised when combining celecoxib with warfarin or other oral an�coagulants, including novel an�coagulants (e.g. apixaban, dabigatran, and rivaroxaban). Interac�on with other medicinal products and other forms of interac�on Pharmacodynamic interac�ons Anticoagulants An�coagulant ac�vity should be monitored par�cularly in the ﬁrst few days a�er ini�a�ng or changing the dose of celecoxib in pa�ents receiving warfarin or other an�coagulants since these pa�ents have an increased risk of bleeding complica�ons. Therefore, pa�ents receiving oral an�coagulants should be closely monitored for their prothrombin �me INR, par�cularly in the ﬁrst few days when therapy with celecoxib is ini�ated or the dose of celecoxib is changed (see Special warnings and precau�ons for use). Bleeding events in associa�on with increases in prothrombin �me have been reported, predominantly in the elderly, in pa�ents receiving celecoxib concurrently with warfarin, some of them fatal. [Page 6] Celecoxib (Coﬁdec) 100, 200 mg Capule SDZ Anti-hypertensives NSAIDs may reduce the eﬀect of an�-hypertensive medicinal products including ACE-inhibitors, angiotensin II receptor antagonists, diure�cs and beta-blockers. As for NSAIDs, the risk of acute renal insuﬃciency, which is usually reversible, may be increased in some pa�ents with compromised renal func�on (e.g. dehydrated pa�ents, pa�ents on diure�cs, or elderly pa�ents) when ACE inhibitors, angiotensin II receptor antagonists, and/or diure�cs are combined with NSAIDs, including celecoxib (see Special warnings and precau�ons for use). Therefore, the combina�on should be administered with cau�on, especially in the elderly. Pa�ents should be adequately hydrated and considera�on should be given to monitoring of renal func�on a�er ini�a�on of concomitant therapy, and periodically therea�er. In a 28-day clinical study in pa�ents with lisinopril-controlled Stage I and II hypertension, administra�on of celecoxib 200 mg BID resulted in no clinically signiﬁcant increases, when compared to placebo treatment, in mean daily systolic or diastolic blood pressure as determined using 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure monitoring. Among pa�ents treated with celecoxib 200 mg BID, 48% were considered unresponsive to lisinopril at the ﬁnal clinic visit (deﬁned as either cuﬀ diastolic blood pressure >90 mmHg or cuﬀ diastolic blood pressure increased >10% compared to baseline), compared to 27% of pa�ents treated with placebo; this diﬀerence was sta�s�cally signiﬁcant. Ciclosporin and tacrolimus Co-administra�on of NSAIDs and ciclosporin or tacrolimus may increase the nephrotoxic eﬀect of ciclosporin or tacrolimus, respec�vely. Renal func�on should be monitored when celecoxib and any of these medicinal products are combined. Acetylsalicylic acid Celecoxib can be used with low-dose acetylsalicylic acid but is not a subs�tute for acetylsalicylic acid for cardiovascular prophylaxis. In the submited studies, as with other NSAIDs, an increased risk of gastrointes�nal ulcera�on or other gastrointes�nal complica�ons compared to use of celecoxib alone was shown for concomitant administra�on of low-dose acetylsalicylic acid (see Pharmacodynamic proper�es). Pharmacokine�c interac�ons Eﬀects of celecoxib on other medicinal products CYP2D6 Inhibition Celecoxib is an inhibitor of CYP2D6. The plasma concentra�ons of medicinal products that are substrates of this enzyme may be increased when celecoxib is used concomitantly. Examples of medicinal products which are metabolised by CYP2D6 are an�depressants (tricyclics and SSRIs), neurolep�cs, an�-arrhythmic medicinal products, etc. The dose of individually dose-�trated CYP2D6 substrates may need to be reduced when treatment with celecoxib is ini�ated or increased if treatment with celecoxib is terminated. Concomitant administra�on of celecoxib 200 mg twice daily resulted in 2.6-fold and 1.5-fold increases in plasma concentra�ons of dextromethorphan and metoprolol (CYP2D6 substrates), respec�vely. These increases are due to celecoxib inhibi�on of the CYP2D6 substrate metabolism. [Page 7] Celecoxib (Coﬁdec) 100, 200 mg Capule SDZ CYP2C19 inhibition In vitro studies have shown some poten�al for celecoxib to inhibit CYP2C19 catalysed metabolism. The clinical signiﬁcance of this in vitro ﬁnding is unknown. Examples of medicinal products which are metabolised by CYP2C19 are diazepam, citalopram and imipramine. Methotrexate In pa�ents with rheumatoid arthri�s celecoxib had no sta�s�cally signiﬁcant eﬀect on the pharmacokine�cs (plasma or renal clearance) of methotrexate (in rheumatologic doses). However, adequate monitoring for methotrexate-related toxicity should be considered when combining these two medicinal products. Lithium In healthy subjects, co-administra�on of celecoxib 200 mg twice daily with 450 mg twice daily of lithium resulted in a mean increase in Cmax of 16% and in area under the curve (AUC) of 18% of lithium. Therefore, pa�ents on lithium treatment should be closely monitored when celecoxib is introduced or withdrawn. Oral contraceptives In an interac�on study, celecoxib had no clinically relevant eﬀects on the pharmacokine�cs of oral contracep�ves (1 mg norethisterone /35 μg ethinylestradiol). Glibenclamide/tolbutamide Celecoxib does not aﬀect the pharmacokine�cs of tolbutamide (CYP2C9 substrate), or glibenclamide to a clinically relevant extent. Eﬀects of other medicinal products on celecoxib CYP2C9 poor metabolisers In individuals who are CYP2C9 poor metabolisers and demonstrate increased systemic exposure to celecoxib, concomitant treatment with CYP2C9 inhibitors such as ﬂuconazole could result in further increases in celecoxib exposure. Such combina�ons should be avoided in known CYP2C9 poor metabolisers (see Dosage and method of administra�on and Pharmacokine�c proper�es). CYP2C9 inhibitors and inducers Since celecoxib is predominantly metabolised by CYP2C9 it should be used at half the recommended dose in pa�ents receiving ﬂuconazole. Concomitant use of 200 mg single dose of celecoxib and 200 mg once daily of ﬂuconazole, a potent CYP2C9 inhibitor, resulted in a mean increase in celecoxib Cmax of 60% and in AUC of 130%. Concomitant use of inducers of CYP2C9 such as rifampicin, carbamazepine and barbiturates may reduce plasma concentra�ons of celecoxib. Ketoconazole and antacids Ketoconazole or antacids have not been observed to aﬀect the pharmacokine�cs of celecoxib. Paediatric popula�on Interac�on studies have only been performed in adults. Pregnancy and lacta�on Pregnancy [Page 8] Celecoxib (Coﬁdec) 100, 200 mg Capule SDZ Studies in animals (rats and rabbits) have shown reproduc�ve toxicity, including malforma�ons (see Contraindica�ons and Preclinical safety data). Inhibi�on of prostaglandin synthesis might adversely aﬀect pregnancy. Data from epidemiological studies suggest an increased risk of spontaneous abor�on a�er use of prostaglandin synthesis inhibitors in early pregnancy. The poten�al for human risk in pregnancy is unknown, but cannot be excluded. Celecoxib, as with other medicinal products inhibi�ng prostaglandin synthesis, may cause uterine iner�a and premature closure of the ductus arteriosus during the last trimester. During the second or third trimester of pregnancy, NSAIDs including celecoxib may cause foetal renal dysfunc�on which may result in reduc�on of amnio�c ﬂuid volume or oligohydramnios in severe cases. Such eﬀects may occur shortly a�er treatment ini�a�on and are usually reversible. Celecoxib is contraindicated in pregnancy and in women who can become pregnant (see Contraindica�ons and Special warnings and precau�ons for use). If a woman becomes pregnant during treatment, celecoxib should be discon�nued. Breas�eeding Celecoxib is excreted in the milk of lacta�ng rats at concentra�ons similar to those in plasma. Administra�on of celecoxib to a limited number of lacta�ng women has shown a very low transfer of celecoxib into breast milk. Women who take celecoxib should not breas�eed. Fer�lity Based on the mechanism of ac�on, the use of NSAIDs, including celecoxib, may delay or prevent rupture of ovarian follicles, which has been associated with reversible infer�lity in some women. Eﬀects on ability to drive and use machines Pa�ents who experience dizziness, ver�go or somnolence while taking celecoxib should refrain from driving or opera�ng machinery. Undesirable eﬀects Adverse reac�ons are listed by system organ class and ranked by frequency in the list below, reﬂec�ng data from the following sources: - Adverse reac�ons reported in osteoarthri�s pa�ents and rheumatoid arthri�s pa�ents at incidence rates greater than 0.01% and greater than those reported for placebo during 12 placebo- and/or ac�ve-controlled clinical trials of dura�on up to 12 weeks at celecoxib daily doses from 100 mg up to 800 mg. In addi�onal studies using non-selec�ve NSAID comparators, approximately 7,400 arthri�s pa�ents have been treated with celecoxib at daily doses up to 800 mg, including approximately 2,300 pa�ents treated for 1 year or longer. The adverse reac�ons observed with celecoxib in these addi�onal studies were consistent with those for osteoarthri�s and rheumatoid arthri�s pa�ents listed below. [Page 9] Celecoxib (Coﬁdec) 100, 200 mg Capule SDZ - Adverse reac�ons reported at incidence rates greater than placebo for subjects treated with celecoxib 400 mg daily in long-term polyp preven�on trials of dura�on up to 3 years (the Adenoma Preven�on with Celecoxib (APC) and Preven�on of Colorectal Sporadic Adenomatous Polyps (PreSAP) trials; see Pharmacodynamic proper�es: Cardiovascular safety – long-term studies involving pa�ents with sporadic adenomatous polyps). - Adverse reac�ons from post-marke�ng surveillance as spontaneously reported during a period in which an es�mated >70 million pa�ents were treated with celecoxib (various doses, dura�ons, and indica�ons). Even though these were iden�ﬁed as reac�ons from post marke�ng reports, trial data were consulted to es�mate frequency. Frequencies are based on a cumula�ve meta-analysis with pooling of trials represen�ng exposure in 38,102 pa�ents. Adverse reac�ons in celecoxib clinical trials and surveillance experience (MedDRA preferred terms)1,2 Very common (≥1/10) Common (≥1/100 to <1/10) Uncommon (≥1/1,000 to <1/100) Rare (≥1/10,000 to <1/1,000) Very rare (<1/10,000) Not known (cannot be es�mated from the available data) Infec�ons and infesta�ons Common: Sinusi�s, upper respiratory tract infec�on, pharyngi�s, urinary tract infec�on Blood and lympha�c system disorders Uncommon: Anaemia Rare: Leucopenia, thrombocytopenia Very rare: Pancytopenia4 Immune system disorders Common: Hypersensi�vity Very rare: Anaphylac�c shock4, anaphylac�c reac�on4 Metabolism and nutri�on disorders Uncommon: Hyperkalaemia Psychiatric disorders Common: Insomnia Uncommon: Anxiety, depression, fa�gue Rare: Confusional state, hallucina�ons4 Nervous system disorders Common: Dizziness, hypertonia, headache4 Uncommon: Cerebral infarc�on1, paraesthesia, somnolence Rare: Ataxia, dysgeusia Very rare: Haemorrhage intracranial (including fatal intracranial haemorrhage)4, meningi�s asep�c4, epilepsy (including aggravated epilepsy)4, ageusia4, anosmia4 Eye disorders Uncommon: Vision blurred, conjunc�vi�s4 [Page 10] Celecoxib (Coﬁdec) 100, 200 mg Capule SDZ Rare: Eye haemorrhage4 Very rare: Re�nal artery occlusion4, re�nal vein occlusion4 Ear and labyrinth disorders Uncommon: Tinnitus, hypoacusis1 Cardiac disorders Common: Myocardial infarc�on1 Uncommon: Cardiac failure, palpita�ons, tachycardia Rare: Arrhythmia4 Vascular disorders Very common: Hypertension1 (including aggravated hypertension) Rare: Pulmonary embolism4, ﬂushing4 Very rare: Vasculi�s4 Respiratory, thoracic, and medias�nal disorders Common: Rhini�s, cough, dyspnoea1 Uncommon: Bronchospasm4 Rare: Pneumoni�s4 Gastrointes�nal disorders Common: Nausea4, abdominal pain, diarrhoea, dyspepsia, ﬂatulence, vomi�ng1, dysphagia1 Uncommon: Cons�pa�on, gastri�s, stoma��s, gastrointes�nal inﬂamma�on (including aggrava�on of gastrointes�nal inﬂamma�on), eructa�on Rare: Gastrointes�nal haemorrhage4, duodenal ulcer, gastric ulcer, oesophageal ulcer, intes�nal ulcer, large intes�nal ulcer, intes�nal perfora�on, oesophagi�s, melaena, pancrea��s, coli�s4 Hepatobiliary disorders Uncommon: Hepa�c func�on abnormal, hepa�c enzyme increased (including increased SGOT and SGPT) Rare: Hepa��s4 Very rare: Hepa�c failure4 (some�mes fatal or requiring liver transplant), hepa��s fulminant4 (some with fatal outcome), hepa�c necrosis4, cholestasis4, hepa��s cholesta�c4, jaundice4 Skin and subcutaneous �ssue disorders Common: Rash, pruritus (includes pruritus generalised) Uncommon: Ur�caria, ecchymosis4 Rare: Angioedema4, alopecia, photosensi�vity Very rare: Derma��s exfolia�ve4, erythema mul�forme4, Stevens-Johnson syndrome4, toxic epidermal necrolysis4, drug reac�on with eosinophilia and systemic symptoms (DRESS)4, acute generalised exanthematous pustulosis (AGEP)4, derma��s bullous4 Musculoskeletal and connec�ve �ssue disorders Common: Arthralgia4 Uncommon: Muscle spasms (leg cramps) [Page 11] Celecoxib (Coﬁdec) 100, 200 mg Capule SDZ Very rare: Myosi�s4 Renal and urinary disorders Uncommon: Blood crea�nine increased, blood urea increased (BUN) Rare: Renal failure acute4, hyponatraemia4 Very rare: Tubulointers��al nephri�s4, nephro�c syndrome4, glomerulonephri�s minimal lesion4 Reproduc�ve system and breast disorders Rare: Menstrual disorder4 Not known: Infer�lity female (female fer�lity decreased)3 General disorders and administra�ve site condi�ons Common: Inﬂuenza-like illness, oedema peripheral/ﬂuid reten�on Uncommon: Face oedema, chest pain4 Injury, poisoning and procedural complica�ons Common: Injury (accidental injury) 1 Adverse reac�ons that occurred in polyp preven�on trials, represen�ng subjects treated with celecoxib 400 mg daily in 2 clinical trials of dura�on up to 3 years (the APC and PreSAP trials). The adverse reac�ons listed above for the polyp preven�on trials are only those that have been previously recognised in the post-marke�ng surveillance experience, or have occurred more frequently than in the arthri�s trials. 2 Furthermore, the following previously unknown adverse reac�ons occurred in polyp preven�on trials, represen�ng subjects treated with celecoxib 400 mg daily in 2 clinical trials of dura�on up to 3 years (the APC and PreSAP trials): Common: angina pectoris, irritable bowel syndrome, nephrolithiasis, blood crea�nine increased, benign prosta�c hyperplasia, weight increased. Uncommon: helicobacter infec�on, herpes zoster, erysipelas, bronchopneumonia, labyrinthi�s, gingival infec�on, lipoma, vitreous ﬂoaters, conjunc�val haemorrhage, deep vein thrombosis, dysphonia, haemorrhoidal haemorrhage, frequent bowel movements, mouth ulcera�on, allergic derma��s, ganglion, nocturia, vaginal haemorrhage, breast tenderness, lower limb fracture, blood sodium increased. 3 Women intending to become pregnant are excluded from all trials, thus consulta�on of the trial database for the frequency of this event was not reasonable. 4 Frequencies are based on cumula�ve meta-analysis with pooling of trials represen�ng exposure in 38,102 pa�ents. In ﬁnal data (adjudicated) from the APC and PreSAP trials in pa�ents treated with celecoxib 400 mg daily for up to 3 years (pooled data from both trials; see Pharmacodynamic proper�es for results from individual trials), the excess rate over placebo for myocardial infarc�on was 7.6 events per 1,000 pa�ents (uncommon) and there was no excess rate for stroke (types not diﬀeren�ated) over placebo. Overdose There is no clinical experience of overdose. Single doses up to 1,200 mg and mul�ple doses up to 1,200 mg twice daily have been administered to healthy subjects for nine days without clinically signiﬁcant adverse eﬀects. In the event of suspected overdose, appropriate suppor�ve medical care should be [Page 12] Celecoxib (Coﬁdec) 100, 200 mg Capule SDZ provided e.g. by elimina�ng the gastric contents, clinical supervision and, if necessary, the ins�tu�on of symptoma�c treatment. Dialysis is unlikely to be an eﬃcient method of medicinal product removal due to high protein binding.",1,12,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,In adults for the symptoma�c relief in the treatment of - osteoarthri�s - rheumatoid arthri�s - ankylosing spondyli�s. The decision to prescribe a selec�ve cyclooxygenase-2 (COX-2) inhibitor should be based on an assessment of the individual pa�ent's overall risks (see Contraindica�ons and Special warnings and precau�ons for use).,1,1,Therapeu�c indica�ons,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T14:55:38.171211+00:00
