PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3880,Salbutamol (As Sulfate),Asmacaire,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1t8qEuDTfg8RPvrG94OpSU89H5rz7h-aW/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3880_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1t8qEuDTfg8RPvrG94OpSU89H5rz7h-aW_view_usp_drivesdk_88c6659870.pdf,page_text/DRP-3880_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1t8qEuDTfg8RPvrG94OpSU89H5rz7h-aW_view_usp_drivesdk_88c6659870.json,7e9f4df9ee21ecca3bd6bdbd2879af517ec438d5a20740cd153538aaf1080ba7,528672,2,digital_text,"Salbutamol (Asmacaire) 2 mg / 5 mL Syrup: Clear, colorless, odorless solution. PHARMACODYNAMICS Salbutamol is a selective beta-2 adrenoceptor agonist. At therapeutic doses it acts on the beta-2 adrenoceptors of bronchial muscle providing short acting (4-6 hours) bronchodilation in reversible airways obstruction. PHARMACOKINETICS Salbutamol administered intravenously has a half life of 4 to 6 hours and is cleared partly renally and partly by metabolism to the inactive 4' -O-sulfate (phenolic sulfate) which is also excreted primarily in the urine. The faeces are a minor route of excretion. The majority of a dose of salbutamol given intravenously, orally or by inhalation is excreted within 72 hours. Salbutamol is bound to plasma proteins to the extent of 10%. After oral administration, salbutamol is absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract and undergoes considerable first-pass metabolism to the phenolic sulfate. Both unchanged drug and conjugate are excreted primarily in the urine. The bioavailability of orally administered salbutamol is about 50%. Preclinical Safety Data In common with other potent selective β2-agonists, salbutamol has been shown to be teratogenic in mice when given subcutaneously. In a reproductive study, 9.3% of fetuses were found to have cleft palate at 2.5 mg/kg dose, 4 times the maximum human oral dose. In rats, treatment at the levels of 0.5, 2.32, 10.75 and 50 mg/kg/day orally throughout pregnancy resulted in no significant fetal abnormalities. The only toxic effect was an increase in neonatal mortality at the highest dose level as the result of lack of maternal care. Reproductive studies in the rabbit at doses of 50 mg/kg/day orally (i.e. much higher than the normal human dose) have shown fetuses with treatment related changes; these included open eyelids (ablepharia), secondary palate clefts (palatoschisis), changes in ossification of the frontal bones of the cranium (cranioschisis) and limb flexure. In an oral fertility and general reproductive performance study in rats at doses of 2 and 50 mg/kg/day, with the exception of a reduction in number of weanlings surviving to day 21 post partum at 50 mg/kg/day, there were no adverse effects on fertility, embryofetal development, litter size, birth weight or growth rate.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Salbutamol is a bronchodilator indicated for the prevention and symptomatic relief of bronchospasm in patients with reversible obstructive respiratory diseases such as bronchial asthma. It may also be used to arrest premature labor in conjunction with parenteral salbutamol.,1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:55:54.865733+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3881-06,Montelukast (As Sodium),None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/13mqPy_w_IyFDnHj9VuTAHBUaTUlWszUr/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3881-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13mqPy_w_IyFDnHj9VuTAHBUaTUlWszUr_view_usp_drivesdk_17098003cc.pdf,page_text/DRP-3881-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13mqPy_w_IyFDnHj9VuTAHBUaTUlWszUr_view_usp_drivesdk_17098003cc.json,d52935e94083ba07e3cc18457e9aaa381a321ca1252b7c8c319a26f0295e2e19,1445443,1,digital_text,"Montelukast is a type of medicine known as a leukotriene receptor antagonist. It works by blocking the action of leukotrienes, which are chemicals released by the body as part of allergic and inflammatory reactions. This prevents the mucous production, inflammation and narrowing of the airways and so asthma attacks. It is also useful for preventing asthma triggered by exercise. Montelukast is used for people whose asthma is not fully controlled by using regular inhaled corticosteroids and short acting beta agonist relievers such as Salbutamol. It is used in addition to these medicines. Montelukast should be taken regularly to prevent asthma attacks. Y ou should continue to take it even when your symptoms is under control. Mechanism of action Light yellow, circular, flat, beveled edge, uncoated flavored chewable tablet, having breakline on one side and plain on other side. Montelukast is extensively metabolised. In studies with therapeutic doses, plasma concentrations of metabolites of Montelukast are undetectable at steady state in adults and children. Each chewable tablet contains:",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Used in the management of chronic asthma and allergic rhinitis, and as prophylaxis for exercise- induced asthma. In vitro studies using human liver microsomes indicate that cytochromes P450 3A4, 2A6 and 2C9 are involved in the metabolism of Montelukast. Based on further in vitro results in human liver microsomes, therapeutic plasma concentrations of Montelukast do not inhibit cytochromes P450 3A4, 2C9, 1A2, 2A6, 2C19, or 2D6. The contribution of metabolites to the therapeutic effect of Montelukast is minimal. Elimination",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:55:58.541687+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3888,Hydrocortisone (As Acetate) + Miconazole (As Nitrate),Gemison,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rt0ric42wluQJTlWIH9VSHYoBdsOLQYf/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3888_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rt0ric42wluQJTlWIH9VSHYoBdsOLQYf_view_usp_drivesdk_d900bbf94c.pdf,page_text/DRP-3888_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rt0ric42wluQJTlWIH9VSHYoBdsOLQYf_view_usp_drivesdk_d900bbf94c.json,05cdf192265fdd12e19ef60f83f0d327a01608ae59864d20fda739f0e3fae64d,903714,3,digital_text,XXXXXX,3,3,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,It is used in the treatment of inflammatory skin infections by dermatophytose or candida sp.: Adjunct to concomitant antibacterial therapy for treatment of mycotic affections with bacterial superinfections.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:56:02.663932+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-389,Co-Amoxiclav,Bactiv,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MeVJgJoDbPwfFi_SJy_BsDKzayjGcXMO/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-389_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MeVJgJoDbPwfFi_SJy_BsDKzayjGcXMO_view_usp_drivesdk_59add77f12.pdf,page_text/DRP-389_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MeVJgJoDbPwfFi_SJy_BsDKzayjGcXMO_view_usp_drivesdk_59add77f12.json,d3fdd78360c61b972cba11be65f48545c7302eeddfe08380d595bd1c2c501922,1886399,2,digital_text,"Co-Amoxiclav (Bactiv) 500 mg / 100 mg Sterile Powder for Injection is an odorless, white to cream powder. It is supplied in a sterilized 10mL Type III clear glass vial with sterilized rubber stopper and aluminum seal. Co-Amoxiclav (Bactiv) 1 g / 200 mg Sterile Powder for Injection is an odorless, white to cream powder. It is supplied in a sterilized 20mL Type III clear glass vial with sterilized rubber stopper and aluminum seal. PHARMACODYNAMICS The spectrum of activity of Amoxicillin may be extended by the concomitant use of Beta-lactamase inhibitor such as Clavulanic acid. As well as reversing resistance to Amoxicillin in Beta-lactamase producing strains of species otherwise sensitive, Clavulanic acid has also been reported to enhance the activity of Amoxicillin against several species not generally considered sensitive. Co-Amoxiclav (Bactiv) is bactericidal to a wide range of organism including: PHARMACOKINETICS Amoxicillin and Clavulanate appear to be well-absorbed into systemic circulation after administration of the oral tablet or suspension formulations. The pharmacokinetic disposition characteristics of Amoxicillin and Clavulanate are unaffected when the two drugs are administered at the same patient. In contrast, a minor yet statistically significant decrease in the time to reach the peak serum Amoxicillin concentration (T ) and a slight increase in the peak serum Amoxicillin concentration (C ) was max max reported when the drug combination was co-administered with magnesium hydroxide and/or aluminum hydroxide antacids. No such effect on these or any other pharmacokinetic parameters have been described for Clavulanate. This difference, observed in the T and C for Amoxicillin when co-administered with these max max antacids, would appear to be of little to no clinical significance. Amoxicillin is primarily eliminated from the body by the kidney as unchanged drug and undergoes active renal tubular secretion and thus concurrent probenecid will competitively inhibit the clearance of the drug. Clavulanic acid undergoes considerable metabolism although, the route is unknown. It is postulated that Clavulanic acid is hydrolyzed with subsequent decarboxylation. The Clavulanic acid that is excreted in the urine appears to undergo simple glomerular filtration with no active secretion. Clearance of Clavulanic acid decreases with decreasing renal function, but not to the same extent as for Amoxicillin. Clavulanic acid is removed by haemodialysis.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Bacterial infections caused by amoxicillin-resistant beta-lactamase producing strains. These includes: ! Sinusitis, otitis media, recurrent tonsillitis ! Acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis ! Bronchopneumonia ! Urinary tract infections, especially when recurrent or complicated, but not prostatitis ! Septic abortion, pelvic or puerperal sepsis, and intra-abdominal sepsis ! Cellulitis animal bites, and severe dental abscess with spreading cellulitis.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:56:06.590794+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3895,Ursodeoxycholic Acid,Udcacid 300,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Tps7jBHmXKNLPYCK3W_11Cg67n2dEEL3/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3895_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Tps7jBHmXKNLPYCK3W_11Cg67n2dEEL3_view_usp_drivesdk_a4418db56c.pdf,page_text/DRP-3895_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Tps7jBHmXKNLPYCK3W_11Cg67n2dEEL3_view_usp_drivesdk_a4418db56c.json,1b6560842bb8312e4ccfbb85c1fa8d2afa36a01c0f37a25007e4b638f5548e4e,3737889,1,ocr,"White, round tablet, scored on one side marked with ""D/W"" on the top and “300” on the bottom. Pregnancy There are no or limited amount of data from the use of ursodeoxycholic acid in pregnant women. Studies in animals 140 X 200 mm",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"have shown reproductive toxicity during the early gestation phase. Ursodeoxycholic acid must not be used during pregnancy, unless clearly necessary. SOAS It is Used for the dissolution of cholesterol-rich gallstones in patients with functioning gallbladers. It is also used in primary biliary cirrhosis. Women of childbearing potential Women of childbearing potential should be treated with ursodeoxycholic acid, only if they practice reliable contracep- 4-80",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T14:56:20.190537+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3897,Tamsulosin Hydrochloride,Urilax,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1siBgDkKxxhJQUPwOWC-Kf-sw2UFwYJcQ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3897_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1siBgDkKxxhJQUPwOWC-Kf-sw2UFwYJcQ_view_usp_drivesdk_caba5112d0.pdf,page_text/DRP-3897_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1siBgDkKxxhJQUPwOWC-Kf-sw2UFwYJcQ_view_usp_drivesdk_caba5112d0.json,83ee5bc5d80441c421f4c1094f0f2a91d09e5b22a6566039c625af444e30b183,6133178,3,digital_text,"White round tablet marked with Korean characters on one side and “U” on the other side. (equivalent to Tamsulosin 200 mcg) Each extended release tablet contains: Tamsulosin (as Hydrochloride), JP..................... 183.5mcg 200 mcg Extended Release Tablet Alpha-Adrenoceptor Antagonist [Page 2] drugs which may reduce blood pressure especially other alpha adrenergic blockers but which will also include anesthetic agents, calcium channel blockers and beta blockers. Tamsulosin (Urilax) is not intended to be used in women or children. In case of an overdose with tamsulosin, blood pressure and heart rate should be closely monitored and in situations where hypotension is encountered, patients should be placed in the supine position and administration of intravenous fluids with or without vasopressors instituted when necessary. Since tamsulosin (urilax) is highly protein-bound, dialysis would not likely be of any benefit.",1,2,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Tamsulosin (Urilax) is indicated for use in the symptomatic treatment of benign prostatic hyperplasia.,1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:56:28.716826+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-390,Co-Amoxiclav,Bactiv,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mQgWqyu0TUl1Q44vP9mqxrEeT7i--tTs/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-390_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mQgWqyu0TUl1Q44vP9mqxrEeT7i--tTs_view_usp_drivesdk_2d37757761.pdf,page_text/DRP-390_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mQgWqyu0TUl1Q44vP9mqxrEeT7i--tTs_view_usp_drivesdk_2d37757761.json,c447f7a67ea2ea62d72375ac97c4729c6c2d4bcc40ed562919ce664dc665bbb7,1886401,2,digital_text,"Co-Amoxiclav (Bactiv) 500 mg / 100 mg Sterile Powder for Injection is an odorless, white to cream powder. It is supplied in a sterilized 10mL Type III clear glass vial with sterilized rubber stopper and aluminum seal. Co-Amoxiclav (Bactiv) 1 g / 200 mg Sterile Powder for Injection is an odorless, white to cream powder. It is supplied in a sterilized 20mL Type III clear glass vial with sterilized rubber stopper and aluminum seal. PHARMACODYNAMICS The spectrum of activity of Amoxicillin may be extended by the concomitant use of Beta-lactamase inhibitor such as Clavulanic acid. As well as reversing resistance to Amoxicillin in Beta-lactamase producing strains of species otherwise sensitive, Clavulanic acid has also been reported to enhance the activity of Amoxicillin against several species not generally considered sensitive. Co-Amoxiclav (Bactiv) is bactericidal to a wide range of organism including: PHARMACOKINETICS Amoxicillin and Clavulanate appear to be well-absorbed into systemic circulation after administration of the oral tablet or suspension formulations. The pharmacokinetic disposition characteristics of Amoxicillin and Clavulanate are unaffected when the two drugs are administered at the same patient. In contrast, a minor yet statistically significant decrease in the time to reach the peak serum Amoxicillin concentration (T ) and a slight increase in the peak serum Amoxicillin concentration (C ) was max max reported when the drug combination was co-administered with magnesium hydroxide and/or aluminum hydroxide antacids. No such effect on these or any other pharmacokinetic parameters have been described for Clavulanate. This difference, observed in the T and C for Amoxicillin when co-administered with these max max antacids, would appear to be of little to no clinical significance. Amoxicillin is primarily eliminated from the body by the kidney as unchanged drug and undergoes active renal tubular secretion and thus concurrent probenecid will competitively inhibit the clearance of the drug. Clavulanic acid undergoes considerable metabolism although, the route is unknown. It is postulated that Clavulanic acid is hydrolyzed with subsequent decarboxylation. The Clavulanic acid that is excreted in the urine appears to undergo simple glomerular filtration with no active secretion. Clearance of Clavulanic acid decreases with decreasing renal function, but not to the same extent as for Amoxicillin. Clavulanic acid is removed by haemodialysis.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Bacterial infections caused by amoxicillin-resistant beta-lactamase producing strains. These includes: ! Sinusitis, otitis media, recurrent tonsillitis ! Acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis ! Bronchopneumonia ! Urinary tract infections, especially when recurrent or complicated, but not prostatitis ! Septic abortion, pelvic or puerperal sepsis, and intra-abdominal sepsis ! Cellulitis animal bites, and severe dental abscess with spreading cellulitis.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:56:32.517750+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3915-01,Candesartan Cilexetil,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LTU_fQA04vBsQULMnr02xKSxWmQIa4oH/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3915-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LTU_fQA04vBsQULMnr02xKSxWmQIa4oH_view_usp_drivesdk_090b5d2e41.pdf,page_text/DRP-3915-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LTU_fQA04vBsQULMnr02xKSxWmQIa4oH_view_usp_drivesdk_090b5d2e41.json,9d8d7bfc80d66a7542e3f29959ee3a68263462c4d3b0c72da213d6534e53a768,9647387,1,ocr,"The antihypertensive effect of candesartan may be enhanced by other medicinal products with blood pressure lowering properties, whether prescribed as an antihypertensive or prescribed for other Pink coloured round shaped biconvex uncoated tablets plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,oo,1,1,indications.,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T14:56:56.680156+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3915-02,Candesartan Cilexetil,Candego-8,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1EcCE5hL54jYPi3bVmDge08P-bq7S_NTX/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3915-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1EcCE5hL54jYPi3bVmDge08P-bq7S_NTX_view_usp_drivesdk_fdc1827b22.pdf,page_text/DRP-3915-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1EcCE5hL54jYPi3bVmDge08P-bq7S_NTX_view_usp_drivesdk_fdc1827b22.json,70067631687bdda0ef22252a5751e20a2b7d1e6e91133e7d11cf626143abe44f,1491809,1,digital_text,"Absorption and Distribution Following oral administration, candesartan cilexetil is converted to the active substance candesartan. The absolute bioavailability of candesartan is approximately 40% after an oral solution of candesartan cilexetil. The relative bioavailability of the tablet formulation compared with the same oral solution is approximately 34% with very little variability. The estimated absolute bioavailability of the tablet is therefore 14%. The mean peak serum concentration (C ) is reached 3-4 hours following tablet intake. The candesartan serum concentrations increase linearly with increasing doses in the therapeutic dose range. No gender related differences in the max pharmacokinetics of candesartan have been observed. The area under the serum concentration versus time curve (AUC) of candesartan is not significantly affected by food. Candesartan is highly bound to plasma protein (more than 99%). The apparent volume of distribution of candesartan is 0.1 L/kg. The bioavailability of candesartan is not affected by food.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Hypertension: Dosage must be individualized. Blood pressure response is dose related over the range of 2 to 32 mg. The usual recommended starting dose of Candesartan (CANDEGO-8) is 16 mg once daily when used as monotherapy in patients who are not volume depleted. Candesartan (CANDEGO-8) can be administered once or twice daily with total daily doses ranging from 8 to 32 mg. Larger doses do not appear to have a greater effect, and there is relatively little experience with such doses. Most of the antihypertensive effect is present within 2 weeks, and maximal blood pressure reduction is generally obtained within 4 to 6 weeks of treatments with Candesartan (CANDEGO-8). If blood pressure is not controlled by Candesartan (CANDEGO-8) alone, a diuretic may be added. Candesartan (CANDEGO-8) may be administered with other antihypertensive agents. Evaluation of patients with heart failure should include periodic assessments of renal function, especially in elderly patients 75 years or older, and patients with impaired renal function. During dose titration of Candesartan Cilexetil, monitoring of serum creatinine and potassium is recommended. Clinical trials in heart failure did not include patients with serum creatinine >265 μmol/L (>3 mg/dL).",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:57:00.165576+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3915-04,Candesartan Cilexetil,Retadesartz,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/10oa-PqkxJwjx_4YTP4XjIS6I8NqesNN0/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3915-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_10oa-PqkxJwjx_4YTP4XjIS6I8NqesNN0_view_usp_drivesdk_1fc748f2cf.pdf,page_text/DRP-3915-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_10oa-PqkxJwjx_4YTP4XjIS6I8NqesNN0_view_usp_drivesdk_1fc748f2cf.json,47b374ba26bcf9cc49940b1e1687ddce52af611f007c4b7b69971cc789c55fbb,507952,1,digital_text,Pink coloured round shaped biconvex uncoated tablet plain on both sides.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Candesartan is indicated for the treatment of hypertension. It may be used alone or in combination with other antihypertensive agents. Candesartan is indicated for the treatment of heart failure (NYHA class II-IV) in patients with left ventricular systolic dysfunction (ejection fraction = 40%) to reduce cardiovascular death and to reduce heart failure hospitalizations. Candesartan has also an added effect on these outcomes when used with an ACE inhibitor.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:57:03.669719+00:00
