PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3995,Cefuroxime (As Sodium),2-Gen 750,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MZDBDulO0SsSL3LJyQ-79p57jQEsHNBr/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3995_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MZDBDulO0SsSL3LJyQ-79p57jQEsHNBr_view_usp_drivesdk_9f3995b507.pdf,page_text/DRP-3995_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MZDBDulO0SsSL3LJyQ-79p57jQEsHNBr_view_usp_drivesdk_9f3995b507.json,9d3e148b751b69df4cabda63a0d894e0412bb68d506746ecbed7e87b437e0b7e,141167,1,digital_text,Faintly yellow powder.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Used in the treatment of susceptible infections such as bone and joint infections, bronchitis (and other lower respiratory tract infections), gonorrhea, meningitis (although treatment failures have been reported in meningitis), otitis media, peritonitis, pharyngitis, sinusitis, skin infections (including soft tissue H. influenzae - infections), and urinary tract infections. It is also used for surgical infection prophylaxis.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:00:15.300217+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3995-01,Cefuroxime (As Sodium),Goxime Iv,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oCB9pyJiU8k32kgonMbMMc684h9EtMj5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3995-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oCB9pyJiU8k32kgonMbMMc684h9EtMj5_view_usp_drivesdk_d79049558c.pdf,page_text/DRP-3995-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oCB9pyJiU8k32kgonMbMMc684h9EtMj5_view_usp_drivesdk_d79049558c.json,f98af5f3c029c3dc37fab5d21f31497dfbb8e4a4a2ffdf04fd8a44918533e4bd,462415,1,digital_text,"Pharmacotherapeutic group: Antibacterials for systemic use, second-generation cephalosporins. Cefuroxime is excreted unchanged, by glomerular filtration and renal tubular secretion, and high concentrations are achieved in the urine. On injection, most of dose of Cefuroxime is excreted within 24 hours, the majority within 6 hours. Probenecid competes for renal tubular secretion with Cefuroxime resulting the in higher and more prolonged plasma concentrations of Cefuroxime. Small amounts of Cefuroxime are excreted in bile.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Adults: I.V. three times daily I.V. The usual dose of Cefuroxime is 750 mg three times daily by I.M. or Injection, which may be increased to 1.5 g in severe infections. The frequency of administration can be increased to six-hourly if necessary, giving total doses of 3 g to 6 g daily. Cefuroxime may be administered intravenously or intramuscularly.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:58:54.134703+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3995-02,Cefuroxime (As Sodium),Centroxime,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hr0nMY6KjQd5TxOhP8SG4DIuG15MbkHO/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3995-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hr0nMY6KjQd5TxOhP8SG4DIuG15MbkHO_view_usp_drivesdk_e291ad5e37.pdf,page_text/DRP-3995-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hr0nMY6KjQd5TxOhP8SG4DIuG15MbkHO_view_usp_drivesdk_e291ad5e37.json,107f8c631a41abd66d7a401cf63ec955b8103b27e9e55c849dbc4df665a82fbc,1202908,1,digital_text,"Faintly yellow powder. Cefuroxime (as odium) USP .........750 mgs ,",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Plasma concentrations are reduced by dialysis. Cefuroxime is excreted unchanged, by glomerular filtration and renal tubular secretion, and high concentrations are achieved in the urine. On injection, most of dose of Cefuroxime is excreted within 24 hours, the majority within 6 hours. Probenecid competes for renal tubular the secretion with Cefuroxime resulting in higher and more prolonged plasma concentrations of Cefuroxime. Small amounts of Cefuroxime are excreted in bile. Cefuroxime is widely distributed in the body including pleural fluid, sputum, bone, synovial fluid, and aqueous humour, but only achieves therapeutic concentrations in the CSF when the meninges are inflamed. It crosses the placenta and has been detected in breast milk.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:58:57.716415+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3995-03,Cefuroxime (As Sodium),Cefell-Med,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1W71wxsZOiT7qbx3JjYzBFZFdph7Ru0Hh/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3995-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1W71wxsZOiT7qbx3JjYzBFZFdph7Ru0Hh_view_usp_drivesdk_7613ea0407.pdf,page_text/DRP-3995-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1W71wxsZOiT7qbx3JjYzBFZFdph7Ru0Hh_view_usp_drivesdk_7613ea0407.json,e41d80e845b617c7d6060230779d7df990a991a10a039ec2229aaad155aa197a,453399,1,digital_text,,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Faintly yellow powder. Infants and children: increased to 100 mg/kg daily if necessary 30 to 60 mg/kg/day given as three or four divided doses. A dose of 60 mg/kg/day will be appropriate for most infections. Elderly: As prescribed by the physician. Pharmacotherapeutic group: Antibacterials for systemic use, second-generation cephalosporins. Mechanism of action: Cefuro ime inh bits bacterial cell wall synthesis following attachment to penicillin-binding proteins (PBPs). This results in thex i interruption of cell wall (peptidoglycan) biosynthesis, which leads to bacterial cell lysis and death. Each ampoule contains:",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T14:59:00.962492+00:00
