PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3995-08,Cefuroxime (As Sodium),Cefuget,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hA04IjkLvo06vIy3Q6Y_32hKoAPmpqk5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3995-08_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hA04IjkLvo06vIy3Q6Y_32hKoAPmpqk5_view_usp_drivesdk_4fc9ef0c63.pdf,page_text/DRP-3995-08_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hA04IjkLvo06vIy3Q6Y_32hKoAPmpqk5_view_usp_drivesdk_4fc9ef0c63.json,46a8b4a343f43e088d801e760fffe389bdabc7c66da145eaad9b927866344dac,1203078,1,digital_text,"Each ampoule contains: Mechanism of action: Cefuro ime inh bits bacterial cell wall synthesis following attachment to penicillin-binding proteins (PBPs). This results in thex i interruption of cell wall (peptidoglycan) biosynthesis, which leads to bacterial cell lysis and death. The sodium salt is given by intramuscular or intravenous injection. Peak plasma concentrations of about 27 micrograms/mL have been achieved 45 minutes after an intramuscular dose of 750 mg with measurable amounts present 8 hours after a dose. Up to 50% of Cefuroxime in the circulation is bound to plasma proteins. The plasma half-life is about 70 minutes and is prolonged in patients with renal impairment and in neonates. Cefuroxime is widely distributed in the body including pleural fluid, sputum, bone, synovial fluid, and aqueous humour, but only achieves therapeutic concentrations in the CSF when the meninges are inflamed. It crosses the placenta and has been detected in breast milk. Plasma concentrations are reduced by dialysis. Cefuroxime may be administered intravenously or intramuscularly. DRP-3995-08 Date of Revision of Package Insert: March 17, 2023 Box of 20 mL USP Type III Clear Glass Vial + Gl ss Ampoule x 10 mL (diluent).a Date of First Authorization: December 17, 2015",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Cefuroxime (as odium) USP .........750 mgs , Faintly yellow powder. Used in the treatment of susceptible infections such as bone and joint infections, bronchitis (and other lower respiratory tract infections), gonorrhea, meningitis (although treatment failures have been reported in meningitis), otitis media, peritonitis, pharyngitis, sinusitis, skin infections H. influenzae (including soft tissue infections), and urinary tract infections. It is also used for surgical infection prophylaxis.- Sterile Water for Injection, BP .......... 10 mL Each vial contains:",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:59:07.547614+00:00
