PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-3995-17,Cefuroxime (as Sodium),Rezafil IV,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/17waWoOXMBr5VhraJyZJMCOMjELEKROI1/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-3995-17_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17waWoOXMBr5VhraJyZJMCOMjELEKROI1_view_usp_drivesdk_7ed0ab64d9.pdf,page_text/DRP-3995-17_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17waWoOXMBr5VhraJyZJMCOMjELEKROI1_view_usp_drivesdk_7ed0ab64d9.json,e53df2dd3d9d8bcc97af3d98c6e59e6a7f4dca24002905f432765010dd509288,466484,1,digital_text,"Cefuroxime (as odium) USP .........750 mgs , Mechanism of action: Cefuro ime inh bits bacterial cell wall synthesis following attachment to penicillin-binding proteins (PBPs). This results in thex i interruption of cell wall (peptidoglycan) biosynthesis, which leads to bacterial cell lysis and death. Although Cefuroxime rarely produces alterations in kidney function, evaluation of renal status during treatment is recommended, especially in patients receiving the maximum doses. In case superinfection occurs, appropriate measures should be taken. Cefuroxime is generally well tolerated. Adverse reactions have been generally mild and transient in nature. and other emergency measures, including oxygen, intravenous fluids, intravenous antihistamines, corticosteroids, pressor amines and airway management, as clinically indicated. Pseudomembranous colitis has been reported with nearly all antibacterial agents, including Cefuroxime, and may range from mild to life-threatening. Therefore, it is important to consider this diagnosis in patients with diarrhea subsequent to the administration of antibacterial agents. Treatment with antibacterial agents alters the normal flora of the colon and may permit overgrowth of clostridia, such as, which is a primary cause of ‘‘antibiotic-associated colitis’’ In case of the occurrence of pseudomembranous Clostridium difficile . colitis, therapeutic measures should be initiated. Mild cases of pseudomembranous colitis usually respond to discontinuation of the drug alone. In moderate to severe cases consideration should be given to management with fluids and electrolytes, protein supplementation and treatment with an antibacterial drug effective against . Clostridium difficile",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,The sodium salt is given by intramuscular or intravenous injection. Peak plasma concentrations of about 27 micrograms/mL have been achieved 45 minutes after an intramuscular dose of 750 mg with measurable amounts present 8 hours after a dose. Up to 50% of Cefuroxime in the circulation is bound to plasma proteins. The plasma half-life is about 70 minutes and is prolonged in patients with renal impairment and in neonates.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T14:59:16.862507+00:00
