PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4013-04,Carbamazepine,Zemacarm,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/14NVT0fL2ClV0YwlOX4iEfNso1agMvwhx/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4013-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14NVT0fL2ClV0YwlOX4iEfNso1agMvwhx_view_usp_drivesdk_72c0d66562.pdf,page_text/DRP-4013-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14NVT0fL2ClV0YwlOX4iEfNso1agMvwhx_view_usp_drivesdk_72c0d66562.json,229f44e7752dcb5f6b714d5aa567cf08f7136624c1ee964f652b3dfa78b1d377,446216,1,digital_text,,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of epilepsy, trigeminal neuralgia, mania, and bipolar disorders.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T15:00:31.805348+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4013-05,Carbamazepine,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bX8F8ztu2VNxiNXD8R7xtBww9HnEZlLY/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4013-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bX8F8ztu2VNxiNXD8R7xtBww9HnEZlLY_view_usp_drivesdk_b30406377a.pdf,page_text/DRP-4013-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bX8F8ztu2VNxiNXD8R7xtBww9HnEZlLY_view_usp_drivesdk_b30406377a.json,df4471b9413b31b45149ca9dc82056d352bfcc4c13f39fb06fd2f8f3cf60475d,695964,1,digital_text,"As a psychotropic agent, Carbamazepine proved to have clinical eﬃcacy in aﬀec␀ve disorders, i.e. as treatment for acute mania as well as for maintenance treatment of (manic-depressive) bipolar aﬀec␀ve disorders, when given either as monotherapy or in combina␀on with neurolep␀cs, an␀depressants, or lithium, in excited schizo-aﬀec␀ve disorder and excited mania in combina␀on with other neurolep␀cs, and in rapid cycling episodes. Mechanism of Action The mechanism of ac␀on of Carbamazepine, the ac␀ve substance, has only been par␀ally elucidated. Carbamaze- pine stabilizes hyperexcited nerve membranes, inhibits r epe␀␀ve neuronal discharges, and reduces synap␀c propaga␀on of excitatory impulses. It is conceivable that prev en␀on of repe␀␀ve ﬁring of sodium-dependent ac␀on poten␀als in depolarized neurons via use- and voltage-dependent blockade of sodium channels may be its main mechanism of ac␀on. Bipolar Disorder: Carbamazepine is given as an ini␀al oral dose of 400 mg daily in divided doses, increased gradually as necessary up to a maximum of 1.6 g daily; the usual maintenance dose range is 400 to 600 mg daily. Alterna␀vely, the dose may be expressed in terms of the age of the child and suggested daily doses are: up to 1 Or as prescribed by the physician. Trigeminal neuralgia: The ini␀al dose of Carbamazepine is 100 mg once or twice daily by mouth increased gradually as necessary. Epilepsy: The suggested ini␀al oral dose is 100-200 mg once or twice daily gradually increased by increments of 100 to 200 mg every 2 weeks to a usual maintenance dose of 0.8 to 1.2 g daily in divided doses; up to 2 g daily may occasionally be necessary. The usual oral dosage in children is 10 to 20 mg/kg daily in divided doses.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"year of age, 100 to 200 mg 5 to 10 years, 400 to 600 mg Risk summary: Oﬀspring of epilep␀c mothers are known to be more prone to developmental disorders, including malforma␀ons. Although conclusive evidence from controlled studies with Carbamazepine monotherapy is lacking, developmental disorders and malforma␀ons, including spina biﬁda and also other congenital anomalies, e.g., craniofacial defects, cardiovascular malf orma␀ons, hypospadias and anomalies involving various body systems, have been reported in associa␀on with the use of Carbamazepine. Based on the data in a North American pregnancy registry, the rate of major congenital malforma␀ons, deﬁned as a structural abnormality with surgical, medical, or cosme␀c importance, diagnosed within 12 weeks of birth was 3.0% (95% CI 2.1 to 4.2%) among mothers exposed to Carbamazepine monotherapy in the ﬁrst trimester and 1.1% (95% CI 0.35 to 2.5%) among pregnant women not taking any an␀epilep␀c drug (rela␀ve risk 2.7, 95% CI 1.1 to 7.0). Clinical considera␀ons: T aking these data into considera␀on: Pregnant women with epilepsy should be treated with special care. If women receiving Carbamazepine become pregnant or plan to become pregnant, or if the need of ini␀a␀ng treatment arises during pregnancy, the drug's expected beneﬁts must be carefully weighed against its possible hazards, par␀cularly in the ﬁrst 3 months of pregnancy. In women of childbearing poten␀al, Carbamazepine should, wherever possible, be prescribed as monotherapy, because the incidence of congenital abnormali␀es in the oﬀspring of women treated with a combina␀on of an␀epilep␀c drugs is greater than in those of mothers receiving the individual drugs as monotherapy. The risk of malforma␀ons following exposure to Carbamazepine as polytherapy may vary depending on the speciﬁc drugs used and may be higher in polytherapy combina␀ons that include valproate. Avoid alcoholic beverages. Call physician immediately if seizures worsen. May cause drowsiness and dizziness.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:00:35.170176+00:00
