PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4229-6,,,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zTgZSfv5_CAxuSyolMWaFbagCJeF_B3L/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4229-6_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zTgZSfv5_CAxuSyolMWaFbagCJeF_B3L_view_usp_drivesdk_195e0fbfd5.pdf,page_text/DRP-4229-6_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zTgZSfv5_CAxuSyolMWaFbagCJeF_B3L_view_usp_drivesdk_195e0fbfd5.json,83de7bffc0b12700c9a20868d4e426f1e814f5dfc6665f8ce9022ceeba6b80fe,546988,1,digital_text,"Each capsule contains a high potency formulation of the three neurotropic Vitamin B , B , B1 6 12 which is sc ientifically-based. This pharmacodynamic and neurotropic concentrat ion of Thiamine, Pyridoxine and Cyanocobalamin precisely works in providing etiologic and symptomatic therapy of painful neurological conditions. Characterized by white to off-white powder free from dirt and lumps encapsulated in empty gelatin capsule size #0 with brown cap and brown body.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Neuropathies are described under long-term intake (6-12 months) of >50 mg mean daily dose of Vitamin B . Therefore, under long-term treatment, regular monitoring is recommended. 6 Use in Children: Vitamin B , B and B capsules are not suitable for the treatment of children 1 6 12 due to high content of vitamin B-complex. For prevention and treatment of Vitamin B , B and B deficiency.1 6 12",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:06:27.953900+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4230,Co-Amoxiclav,Clavmoxwel,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sI3ACBo_XQYg9pfOkFdoGK4qH93Oshlp/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4230_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1sI3ACBo_XQYg9pfOkFdoGK4qH93Oshlp_view_usp_drivesdk_80ed38d3b9.pdf,page_text/DRP-4230_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1sI3ACBo_XQYg9pfOkFdoGK4qH93Oshlp_view_usp_drivesdk_80ed38d3b9.json,63324261b6b99d20a1abfe2c96a9c18f88dc3250224b54430fb1cbc156de0a07,79677,1,digital_text,"White to off white, elongated, biconvex & film-coated tablets.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of infections due to beta-lactamase producing strains (where Amoxicillin alone is not appropriate) including respiratory tract infections, genito-urinary and abdominal infections, cellulitis, animal bites, severe dental infection with spreading cellulitis or dental infection not responding to first-line Antibacterial.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:06:49.419307+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4230-05,Co-Amoxiclav,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_VHUf72joke2MmBcvO-qvE6yl-xT-f06/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4230-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_VHUf72joke2MmBcvO-qvE6yl-xT-f06_view_usp_drivesdk_1e101d14e2.pdf,page_text/DRP-4230-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_VHUf72joke2MmBcvO-qvE6yl-xT-f06_view_usp_drivesdk_1e101d14e2.json,16c82a540c70f856e034a97359b0b62a60c4e6fb1888f493bfc0f6ab65b61b01,5524797,1,ocr,"In patients with reduced urine output, crystalluria has been observed very rarely, predominantly with parenteral therapy. During the administration of high doses of amoxicillin, it is advisable to maintain adequate fluid intake and urinary output in order to reduce the White to off white, elongated, biconvex & film-coated tablets. possibility of amoxicillin crystalluria. In patients with bladder catheters, a regular check of patency should be maintained.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of infections due to beta-lactamase producing strains (where Amoxicillin alone is not appropriate) including respiratory tract infections, genito-urinary and abdominal infections, cellulitis, animal bites, severe dental infection with spreading",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T15:06:46.580316+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4231,Co-Amoxiclav,Clavmoxwel-156.25,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1QCscEdzKJPuZqWnIDlun8gWQY1d3pyLM/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4231_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QCscEdzKJPuZqWnIDlun8gWQY1d3pyLM_view_usp_drivesdk_203e9e1b6b.pdf,page_text/DRP-4231_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QCscEdzKJPuZqWnIDlun8gWQY1d3pyLM_view_usp_drivesdk_203e9e1b6b.json,7dd5949d2db0c911ceecb3cc2be9feb5dec6d1523bc03dd5a71cbb3a9c6f22b7,848470,1,digital_text,"Amoxicillin with Clavulanic acid are well absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract after oral administration of Amoxicillin with Clavulanic acid. The safety and efficacy of Amoxicillin with Clavulanic acid have been established in clinical trials where Amoxicillin with Clavulanic acid was taken without regard to meals. Amoxicillin diffuses readily into most body tissues and fluids with the exception of the bread and spinal fluid. The results of experiments involving the administration of Clavulanic acid to animals suggests that this compound, like Amoxicillin, is well distributed in body tissues. Approximately 50% to 70% of the Amoxicillin and approximately 25% to 40% of the Clavulanic acid are excreted unchanged in urine the first 6 hour after oral administration of 500 + 125 mg of Amoxicillin with Clavulanic acid Tablet. Concurrent administration of Probenecid delays renal excretion of Amoxicillin but does not delay renal excretion of Clavulanic acid.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"CrCl < 10 mL /min 15 mg/3.75 mg/kg as a single daily dose (maximum 500 mg/125 mg). Adults and children ≥ 40 kg Haemodialysis For adults and children ≥ 40 kg, this formulation of Amoxicillin/Clavulanic acid provides a total daily dose of 1500 mg amoxicillin/375 mg clavulanic acid, when administered as recommended below. For children < 40 kg, this formulation of Amoxicillin/Clavulanic acid provides a maximum daily dose of 2400 mg amoxicillin/600 mg clavulanic acid, when administered as recommended below. If it is considered that a higher daily dose of amoxicillin is required, it is recommended that another preparation of Amoxicillin/Clavulanic acid is selected in order to avoid administration of unnecessarily high daily doses of Clavulanic acid. CrCl: 10-30 mL/min 15 mg/3.75 mg/kg twice daily (maximum 500 mg/125 mg twice daily). The duration of therapy should be determined by the response of the patient. Some infections (e.g. osteomyelitis) require longer periods of treatment. Treatment should not be extended beyond 14 days without review. No clinical data are available on doses of Amoxicillin/Clavulanic acid 4:1 formulations higher than 40 mg/10 mg/kg per day in children under 2 years. Elderly Dose with caution and monitor hepatic function at regular intervals The severity and the site of the infection. Dose adjustments are based on the maximum recommended level of amoxicillin. 20 mg/5 mg/kg/day to 60 mg/15 mg/kg/day given in three divided doses.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:06:52.783244+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4243,Cefaclor (as monohydrate),Verzat,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gz9ALo8LNuoRh0Kp-rTWLzv-KYd_81xi/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4243_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gz9ALo8LNuoRh0Kp-rTWLzv-KYd_81xi_view_usp_drivesdk_f14caca18a.pdf,page_text/DRP-4243_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gz9ALo8LNuoRh0Kp-rTWLzv-KYd_81xi_view_usp_drivesdk_f14caca18a.json,dd929762228034c69beb4aa88f644d70f07847d00781a7c3635edcaa308fa8a2,3146894,1,digital_text,Cefaclor is a semisynthetic second generation cephalosporin antibiotic. It is chemically designated as 3-chloro-7-D-(2-phenylglycinamido)-3- cephem-4-carboxylic acid monohydrate. Its empirical formula is C H CIN O S.H O and its molecular weight is 385.8. 15 14 3 4 2 Cefaclor (Verzat) 250 mg / 5 mL Granules for Suspension: Dry Product: White to off white free flowing fruit flavored granules. Reconstituted product: Red suspension. Flavor: Strawberry Cefaclor (Verzat) 125 mg / 5 mL Granules for Suspension: Dry Product: White to off white free flowing fruit flavored granules. Reconstituted product: Red suspension. Flavor: Strawberry,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of susceptible infections including upper and lower respiratory tract infections, urinary tract infection and skin and soft tissue infections.",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:06:57.976779+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4244,Levothyroxine Sodium,Eurolev,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oATJlJw7uuE5ZSTzJhVuOuPF-Zaoyvvt/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4244_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oATJlJw7uuE5ZSTzJhVuOuPF-Zaoyvvt_view_usp_drivesdk_19e1d0f9c1.pdf,page_text/DRP-4244_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oATJlJw7uuE5ZSTzJhVuOuPF-Zaoyvvt_view_usp_drivesdk_19e1d0f9c1.json,e4823218b4ca8f98787fefd9c4b7a679d9c7b9c212add240f90aff974de957b0,99866,2,digital_text,"White, round biconvex tablet, plain on one side and bisected on the other side.",1,1,Product Description,"It is used as replacement therapy in the treatment of hypothy- roidism, to suppress TSH production in the treatment of thyroid carcinoma and as a diagnostic agent for the differen- tial diagnosis of hypothyroidism. Product Description White, round biconvex tablet, plain on one side and bisected on the other side. Pharmacological Properties Pharmacodynamics Levothyroxine sodium is the monosodium salt of the levorota- ry isomer of thyroxine. Thyroxine (T4) is a naturally occurring hormone produced by the thyroid gland and converted to the more active hormone triiodothyronine (T3) in peripheral tissues. The precise signals controlling the conversion of T4 to T3 within the cell are not known. The thyroid hormones are required for normal growth and development, particularly of the nervous system. They increase the resting or basal metabolic rate of the whole organism and have stimulatory effects on the heart, skeletal muscle, liver and kidney. Thyroid hormones enhance lipolysis and the utilization of carbohydrate. Pharmacokinetics Levothyroxine sodium is variably but adequately absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract following oral administration. Fasting increases absorption. Once in the circulation, levothyroxine sodium is extensively protein bound, principally to thyroxine-binding globulin (TBG) but also to a lesser extent to thyroxine-binding pre-albumin (TBPA) or to albumin. Levothyroxine sodium has a plasma half-life in euthyroidism of about 6 to 7 days; the half-life is prolonged in hypothyroid- ism and reduced in hyperthyroidism. Levothyroxine sodium is primarily metabolized in the liver and kidney to tri-iodothyronine (liothyronine) and, about 40%, to inactive reverse triiodothyronine (reverse T3) both of which undergo further deiodination to inactive metabolites. Further metabolites result from the deamination and decarboxylation of levothyroxine sodium to tetrac. Levothyroxine sodium is reported to undergo enterohepatic recycling and excretion in the faeces. The distribution of thyroid hormones across the placenta and into breast milk is discussed under Pregnancy and Breast feeding.",1,1,Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:07:03.793504+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4244-01,Levothyroxine Sodium,Eurolev,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1YUGYXx5GDbHmTAXUauW5WGcgzDh9JNhT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4244-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YUGYXx5GDbHmTAXUauW5WGcgzDh9JNhT_view_usp_drivesdk_2a76251b44.pdf,page_text/DRP-4244-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YUGYXx5GDbHmTAXUauW5WGcgzDh9JNhT_view_usp_drivesdk_2a76251b44.json,3af91de6f332f9483862d8f425aed551303cc80844976397638b42a2b6ce2d15,117138,2,digital_text,"White, round biconvex tablet, plain on one side and bisected on the other side.",1,1,Product Description:,"It is used as replacement therapy in the treatment of hypothyroidism, to suppress TSH production in the treatment of thyroid carcinoma and as a diagnostic agent for the differential diagnosis of hypothyroidism. Product Description: White, round biconvex tablet, plain on one side and bisected on the other side. Pharmacological Properties Pharmacodynamics Levothyroxine sodium is the monosodium salt of the levorotary isomer of thyroxine. Thyroxine (T4) is a naturally occurring hormone produced by the thyroid gland and converted to the more active hormone triiodothyronine (T3) in peripheral tissues. The precise signals controlling the conversion of T4 to T3 within the cell are not known. The thyroid hormones are required for normal growth and development, particularly of the nervous system. They increase the resting or basal metabolic rate of the whole organism and have stimulatory effects on the heart, skeletal muscle, liver and kidney. Thyroid hormones enhance lipolysis and the utilization of carbohydrate. Pharmacokinetics Levothyroxine sodium is variably but adequately absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract following oral administration. Fasting increases absorption. Once in the circulation, levothyroxine sodium is extensively protein bound, principally to thyroxine-binding globulin (TBG) but also to a lesser extent to thyroxine-binding pre-albumin (TBPA) or to albumin. Levothyroxine sodium has a plasma half-life in euthyroidism of about 6 to 7 days; the half-life is prolonged in hypothyroidism and reduced in hyperthyroidism. Levothyroxine sodium is primarily metabolized in the liver and kidney to tri-iodothyronine (liothyronine) and, about 40%, to inactive reverse triiodothyronine (reverse T3) both of which undergo further deiodination to inactive metabolites. Further metabolites result from the deamination and decarboxylation of levothyroxine sodium to tetrac. Levothyroxine sodium is reported to undergo enterohepatic recycling and excretion in the faeces. The distribution of thyroid hormones across the placenta and into breast milk is discussed under Pregnancy and Breast feeding.",1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:07:00.805686+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4245,Rabeprazole sodium,Rabesta-20,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Th9JXpW_s2Ra-NPwtj46fElLOrnbg0Qg/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4245_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Th9JXpW_s2Ra-NPwtj46fElLOrnbg0Qg_view_usp_drivesdk_fe35f74280.pdf,page_text/DRP-4245_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Th9JXpW_s2Ra-NPwtj46fElLOrnbg0Qg_view_usp_drivesdk_fe35f74280.json,4503a41b2637c600c5386ae0edd1d8a3b6eba6a67682b10c17e026a11bba5c2c,738495,1,digital_text,"Peak plasma-rabeprazole concentrations are reached about 3.5 hours after a dose by mouth. The oral bioavailability is about 52% with the enteric-coated tablet formulation because of first-pass metabolism, and does not appear to vary after single or repeated doses. Rabeprazole is 97% bound to plasma proteins. It is extensively metabolized in the liver by cytochrome P450 isoenzymes CYP2C19 and CYP3A4 to the thioether, thioether carboxylic acid, sulfone, and desmethyl thioether. Metabolites are excreted principally in the urine about 90% with the remainder in the feces. The plasma half-life is about 1 hour, increased two or three-fold in hepatic impairment, 1.6 times in CYP2C19 slow metabolizers and by 30% in the elderly.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Each enteric-coated tablet contains: Orange coloured round shaped biconvex enteric coated tablets plain on both sides. Rabeprazole sodium is a substituted benzimidazole that inhibits gastric acid secretion. Rabeprazole sodium is known chemically as 2-[4- (3-methoxypropoxy)-3-methyl-2-pyridinyl]-methyl]sulfinyl]–1H benzimidazole sodium salt. It has an empirical formula C H N NaO S and a molecular weight of 381.43. Rabeprazole sodium is a white to slightly 18 20 3 3 yellowish-white solid. It is very soluble in water and methanol, freely soluble in ethanol, chloroform and ethyl acetate and insoluble in ether and n-hexane. The stability of Rabeprazole sodium is a function of pH; it is rapidly degraded in acid media, and is more stable under alkaline conditions. PHARMACOLOGIC ACTION Rabeprazole sodium is a proton pump inhibitor. It is a prodrug. After administration, it diffuses into the parietal cell of the stomach and accumulates in the secretory canaliculi. In the acidic medium, Rabeprazole is converted to sulfonamide. This sulfonamide covalently interacts with sulfhydryl (SH) group in the proton pump (H + K + ATPase) and inhibits the exchange of extra cellular K + for intracellular H + ion. Rabeprazole sodium irreversibly inhibits proton pump activity and decreases gastric acid secretion. Rabeprazole produces fastest acid suppression and helps in mucin synthesis. Rabeprazole Sodium .................................................................20 mg DESCRIPTION Treatment with PPIs, including Rabeprazole, may possibly increase the risk of gastrointestinal infections such as Salmonella, Campylobacter and Clostridium difficile. Co-administration of Atazanavir with Rabeprazole is not recommended. Special precautions are to be exercised specifically in the event of hepatic impairment. Monitor gastric malignancy. Symptomatic response to therapy with Rabeprazole sodium does not preclude the presence of gastric or esophageal malignancy, therefore the possibility of malignancy should be excluded prior to commencing treatment with Rabeprazole.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:07:10.785817+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4245,Rabeprazole sodium,Rabesta-20,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UplsLk8nmSx7N_xt5ht3EetP58CPQRsW/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4245_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UplsLk8nmSx7N_xt5ht3EetP58CPQRsW_view_usp_drivesdk_08c2e6c400.pdf,page_text/DRP-4245_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UplsLk8nmSx7N_xt5ht3EetP58CPQRsW_view_usp_drivesdk_08c2e6c400.json,2ffc2063eebd4921cae2043322e331150da7e48ba4238fb7e31c02192d4ce53c,517748,1,digital_text,"Orange coloured round shaped biconvex enteric coated tablets plain on both sides. DESCRIPTION Rabeprazole sodium is a substituted benzimidazole that inhibits gastric acid secretion. Rabeprazole sodium is known chemically as 2-[4- (3-methoxypropoxy)-3-methyl-2-pyridinyl]-methyl]sulfinyl]–1H benzimidazole sodium salt. It has an empirical formula C H N NaO S and a molecular weight of 381.43. Rabeprazole sodium is a white to slightly 18 20 3 3 yellowish-white solid. It is very soluble in water and methanol, freely soluble in ethanol, chloroform and ethyl acetate and insoluble in ether and n-hexane. The stability of Rabeprazole sodium is a function of pH; it is rapidly degraded in acid media, and is more stable under alkaline conditions. Rabeprazole tablets are available for oral administration as delayed-release, enteric-coated tablets containing 20 mg of Rabeprazole sodium. Inactive ingredients are carnauba wax, crospovidone, deacetylated monoglyceride, ethyl cellulose, hydroxypropyl cellulose, hypromellose phthalate, magnesium stearate, mannitol, sodium hydroxide, sodium stearyl fumarate, talc, titanium dioxide, and sunset yellow FCF as a coloring agent. PHARMACOLOGIC ACTION Rabeprazole sodium is a proton pump inhibitor. It is a prodrug. After administration, it diffuses into the parietal cell of the stomach and accumulates in the secretory canaliculi. In the acidic medium, Rabeprazole is converted to sulfonamide. This sulfonamide covalently interacts with sulfhydryl (SH) group in the proton pump (H + K + ATPase) and inhibits the exchange of extra cellular K + for intracellular H + ion. Rabeprazole sodium irreversibly inhibits proton pump activity and decreases gastric acid secretion. Rabeprazole produces fastest acid suppression and helps in mucin synthesis. PHARMACOKINETICS Peak plasma-rabeprazole concentrations are reached about 3.5 hours after a dose by mouth. The oral bioavailability is about 52% with the enteric-coated tablet formulation because of first-pass metabolism, and does not appear to vary after single or repeated doses. Rabeprazole is 97% bound to plasma proteins. It is extensively metabolized in the liver by cytochrome P450 isoenzymes CYP2C19 and CYP3A4 to the thioether, thioether carboxylic acid, sulfone, and desmethyl thioether. Metabolites are excreted principally in the urine about 90% with the remainder in the feces. The plasma half-life is about 1 hour, increased two or three-fold in hepatic impairment, 1.6 times in CYP2C19 slow metabolizers and by 30% in the elderly.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Rabeprazole is indicated in active duodenal ulcer, benign gastric ulcer, Zollinger-Ellison syndrome, and ulcerative or erosive gastroesophageal reflux disease",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:07:13.927683+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4245-02,Rabeprazole sodium,Gerdsol,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1eSZ7N4hsFAC9qOi0bsT0WQvSls3_NZTs/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4245-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eSZ7N4hsFAC9qOi0bsT0WQvSls3_NZTs_view_usp_drivesdk_055a0160e8.pdf,page_text/DRP-4245-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eSZ7N4hsFAC9qOi0bsT0WQvSls3_NZTs_view_usp_drivesdk_055a0160e8.json,8df80ed91d0ba6c5da43f2b678d6e36663aab61a83cb9138f8262b8fd5cbe2ec,916128,1,digital_text,"Orange coloured round shaped biconvex enteric coated tablet plain on both sides. Rabeprazole sodium is a substituted benzimidazole that inhibits gastric acid secretion. Rabeprazole sodium is known chemically as 2-[4- (3-methoxypropoxy)-3-methyl-2-pyridinyl]-methyl]sulfinyl]–1H benzimidazole sodium salt. It has an empirical formula C H N NaO S and a molecular weight of 381.43. Rabeprazole sodium is a white to slightly 18 20 3 3 yellowish-white solid. It is very soluble in water and methanol, freely soluble in ethanol, chloroform and ethyl acetate and insoluble in ether and n-hexane. The stability of Rabeprazole sodium is a function of pH; it is rapidly degraded in acid media, and is more stable under alkaline conditions. Rabeprazole tablets are available for oral administration as delayed-release, enteric-coated tablets containing 20 mg of Rabeprazole sodium. Inactive ingredients are carnauba wax, crospovidone, deacetylated monoglyceride, ethyl cellulose, hydroxypropyl cellulose, hypromellose phthalate, magnesium stearate, mannitol, sodium hydroxide, sodium stearyl fumarate, talc, titanium dioxide, and sunset yellow FCF as a coloring agent. PHARMACOLOGIC ACTION Rabeprazole sodium is a proton pump inhibitor. It is a prodrug. After administration, it diffuses into the parietal cell of the stomach and accumulates in the secretory canaliculi. In the acidic medium, Rabeprazole is converted to sulfonamide. This sulfonamide covalently interacts with sulfhydryl (SH) group in the proton pump (H + K + ATPase) and inhibits the exchange of extra cellular K + for intracellular H + ion. Rabeprazole sodium irreversibly inhibits proton pump activity and decreases gastric acid secretion. Rabeprazole produces fastest acid suppression and helps in mucin synthesis. PHARMACOKINETICS Peak plasma-rabeprazole concentrations are reached about 3.5 hours after a dose by mouth. The oral bioavailability is about 52% with the enteric-coated tablet formulation, because of first-pass metabolism, and does not appear to vary after single or repeated doses. Rabeprazole is 97% bound to plasma proteins. It is extensively metabolized in the liver by cytochrome P450 isoenzymes CYP2C19 and CYP3A4 to the thioether, thioether carboxylic acid, sulfone, and desmethyl thioether. Metabolites are excreted principally in the urine about 90% with the remainder in the feces. The plasma half-life is about 1 hour, increased two or three-fold in hepatic impairment, 1.6 times in CYP2C19 slow metabolizers and by 30% in the elderly.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Rabeprazole is indicated in active duodenal ulcer, benign gastric ulcer, Zollinger-Ellison syndrome, and ulcerative or erosive gastroesophageal reflux disease.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:07:06.918279+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4249,RIFAMPICIN,RIFASOL,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1kHk4notM8jOHJw9Gxpa_W0H76O8q8ZeR/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4249_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kHk4notM8jOHJw9Gxpa_W0H76O8q8ZeR_view_usp_drivesdk_dca19c76c3.pdf,page_text/DRP-4249_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kHk4notM8jOHJw9Gxpa_W0H76O8q8ZeR_view_usp_drivesdk_dca19c76c3.json,b7e54c0830a0a0845799b07790544a0ef912e212aa61236773f9134d1616af8f,423720,1,digital_text,Rifampicin (Rifasol®) Suspension: is a red to brick red suspension with strawberry flavor and sweet fruit taste.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Used primarily in the treatment of infections due to Mycobacterium tuberculosis. May also be used in association with other anti-tuberculosis drugs and anti-epileptics in the treatment of leprosy.,1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:07:17.253912+00:00
