PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4302-03,Betahistine Dihydrochloride,Vexamine,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1i17Xy-hgziWoerOet_6HBFcIZ-6OsA4n/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4302-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1i17Xy-hgziWoerOet_6HBFcIZ-6OsA4n_view_usp_drivesdk_e327d1ea46.pdf,page_text/DRP-4302-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1i17Xy-hgziWoerOet_6HBFcIZ-6OsA4n_view_usp_drivesdk_e327d1ea46.json,235c8861bf5e2df09e1095f50078a65f8497dae64835fe0a806c9a8980a731d1,1343238,1,digital_text,"Gastrointestinal disorders: Common: nausea and dyspepsia. Immune System disorders: Gastrointestinal disorders: Skin and subcutaneous tissue disorders: Hypersensitivity reactions, e.g., anaphylaxis. Nervous system disorders: Mild gastric complaints (e.g., vomiting, gastrointestinal pain, abdominal distension and bloating). These can normally be dealt with by taking the dose during meals or by lowering the dose. Cutaneous and subcutaneous hypersensitivity reactions, in particular angioneurotic edema, urticaria, rash, and pruritus.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"It is used to reduce the symptoms of vertigo, tinnitus and hearing loss associated with Ménière's disease. Adults: 8 to 16 mg three times daily taken preferably with meals. Or as prescribed by the physician.",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:10:53.149948+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4337,,Amefocin,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VGMTU2S6cJgHr0A7pbO9ImMxnD6qwclC/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4337_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VGMTU2S6cJgHr0A7pbO9ImMxnD6qwclC_view_usp_drivesdk_249f7b62f3.pdf,page_text/DRP-4337_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VGMTU2S6cJgHr0A7pbO9ImMxnD6qwclC_view_usp_drivesdk_249f7b62f3.json,3e5b2646e7e506f306a4e21213d713c54c76fda776f0335f4ef36b05ec27f61a,450244,1,digital_text,"Folic acid 5 mg Tablet (Amefocin) is a round, flat, beveled edge plain on both sides, yellow tablet. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This product contains Folic acid which is a member of the vitamin B group. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Please see formulation. WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? Folic acid is used in the treatment and prevention of the folate deficiency state, which can result in megaloblastic anemia, due to inadequate dietary intake (as in malnutrition), when there is malabsorption (as in sprue), increased in utilization (as in pregnancy conditions such as haemolytic anemia), increased loss (as in haemodialysis), or as a result of the use of folate antagonists and other drugs that interfere with normal folate metabolism. Folic acid is also used in women of child-bearing potential and pregnant women to protect against neural tube defacts in their offspring. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? For the treatment of folate-defciency megaloblastic anemia: Adults - Given orally in doses of 5 mg daily for 4 months. For children up to 1 year old - 500 micrograms/Kg once daily. For prophylaxis of megaloblastic anemia in children on dialysis: 1 month to 12 months of age -250 micrograms/Kg once daily. Children 1 years old and above - 5 mg to 10 mg daily. Prophylaxis of megaloblastic anemia of pregnancy: 200 micrograms to 500 micrograms daily. Women of child-bearing potential: 400 microgarms daily Or as prescribed by the physician. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Folic acid should never be given alone or with inadequate amounts of Vitamin B12 for the treatment of undiagnosed megaloblastic anemia. If you are allergic to any component of the product. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS Folic acid is generally well tolerated. Gastrointesitinal disturbances and hypersensitivity reactions have been reported rarely. WHAT OTHER MEDICINES OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Please tell your doctor or pharmacist if you are taking or have recently taken any other medicines, including medicines obtained without a prescription. Especially: • Antiepileptics • Oral contraceptives • Antituberculosis drugs • Antibacterials such as cotrimoxazole • Methotrexate • Pyrimethamine • Triamterene WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF I MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, just take the next dose and the subsequent doses at the usual recommended schedule, i.e., once or twice a day. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? • Keep the product out of sight and reach of children. • Store at temperatures not exceeding 30ºC. • Protect from light. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSAGE Since folic acid is a water-soluble vitamin, overdose is rather unlikely to happen. However, the possibility of an overdose cannot be discounted especially in patients taking high doses of folic acid in long-term situations such as during pregnancy. In rare cases, patients have shown overdose symptoms that include: • Gastrointestinal side effects (such as nausea, vomiting, stomach pain, diarrhea or gas) • Rash WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor or contact a Poison Control Center right away. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE • Do not take more than the recommended dosage. • Do not use after the expiry date on the label. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If an y undesir able effects occurs. AVAILABILITY Folic Acid (Amefoci n) 5 mg Tablet - Alu-PVC B lister pack x 10’s (Box of 100’s) ADVERSE DRUG REACTION REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adv erse drug reaction, report to FDA: www.fda.gov.ph REGISTRATION NUMBER DRP-4337 DATE OF FIRST AUTHORIZATION 11 January 2011 DATE REVISION OF PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET :March 2021",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T15:11:06.006385+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4337-01,Folic Acid,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mMVzv0JKuETSz7hTwx_rlDD17C6V_qQq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4337-01_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mMVzv0JKuETSz7hTwx_rlDD17C6V_qQq_view_usp_drivesdk_7b1708002b.pdf,page_text/DRP-4337-01_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mMVzv0JKuETSz7hTwx_rlDD17C6V_qQq_view_usp_drivesdk_7b1708002b.json,528dcc3fa20d2fba1b4690f1d9cd5fd1ad47410cec1e331f665984366e3f6578,196675,1,digital_text,"RiteMED ® Folic Acid 5 mg Tablet is a round, flat, beveled edge, plain on both sides, yellow tablet. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This product contains Folic acid which is a member of the vitamin B group. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Please see formulation. WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? Folic acid is used in the treatment and prevention of the folate deficiency state, which can result in meg - aloblastic anemia, due to inadequate dietary intake (as in malnutrition), when there is malabsorption (as in sprue), increased in utilization (as in pregnancy conditions such as haemolytic anemia), increased loss (as in haemodialysis), or as a result of the use of folate antagonists and other drugs that interfere with normal folate metabolism. Folic acid is also used in women of childbearing potential and pregnant women to protect against neural tube defects in their offspring. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? For the treatment of folate-deficiency megaloblastic anemia: Adults- Given orally in doses of 5 mg daily for 4 months. For children up to 1 year old - 500 micrograms/ Kg once daily. For prophylaxis of megaloblastic anemia in children on dialysis: 1 month to 12 months of age - 250 micrograms/ Kg once a day. Children 1 year old and above - 5 mg to 10 mg daily. Prophylaxis of megaloblastic anemia of pregnancy: 200 micrograms to 500 micrograms daily. Women of child-bearing potential: 400 micrograms daily. Or, as prescribed by the physician. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Folic acid should never be given alone or with inadequate amounts of Vitamin B 12 for the treatment of undiagnosed megaloblastic anemia. If you are allergic to any component of the product. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS Folic acid is generally well tolerated. Gastrointestinal disturbances and hypersensitivity reactions have been reported rarely. WHAT OTHER MEDICINES OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Please tell your doctor or pharmacist if you are taking or have recently taken any other medicines, including medicines obtained without a prescription. Especially: • Antiepileptics • Oral contraceptives • Antituberculosis drugs • Antibacterials such as cotrimoxazole • Methotrexate • Pyrimethamine • Triamterene WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, just take the next dose and the subsequent doses at the usual recommended schedule, i.e., once or twice a day. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? • Keep the product out of sight and reach of children. • Store at temperatures not exceeding 30oC. • Protect from light. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSAGE Since folic acid is a water-soluble vitamin, overdose is rather unlikely to happen. However, the possibility of an overdose cannot be discounted especially in patients taking high doses of folic acid in long-term situations such as during pregnancy. In rare cases, patients have shown overdose symptoms that include: • Gastrointestinal side effects (such as nausea, vomiting, stomach pain, diarrhea or gas) • Rash WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor or contact a Poison Control Center right away. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE • Do not take more than the recommended dosage. • Do not use after the expiry date on the label. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If any undesirable effects occurs. AVAILABILITY RiteMED® Folic Acid 5 mg Tablet, in Alu/PVC Blister Pack x 10’s (Box of 100’s) ADVERSE DRUG REACTION REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adverse drug reaction, seek medical attention immediately and report to the FDA at www.fda. gov.ph AND RiteMED at (+632) 8-726-0835 or e-mail productsafety@ritemed.com.ph. By reporting undesirable effects, you can help provide more information on the safety of this medicine. Manufactured by Am-Europharma Corporation Brgy. Saimsim, Calamba City, Laguna Distributed by RiteMED Phils., Inc. 56 Epifanio Delos Santos Ave., Mandaluyong Metro Manila Date of First Authorization: July 11, 2018 Date of Revision: June 2022 DRP-4337-01 RTM700166IN02 Reg. IPOPHIL v v v v 216 mm 93 mm • F. A. Revision Date: 2 June 2022 • RM-Folic Acid 5 mg Tablet Product Information Leaflet -- PIL (Version 4) COLOR GUIDE Pantone 2756 C • FRONT • BACK R [Page 2]",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T15:10:59.573523+00:00
