PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4371,Atorvastatin (as calcium),Choltrol,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FGLdUTNnB1DEB9VAQvMROGwf3AL5h0YF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4371_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FGLdUTNnB1DEB9VAQvMROGwf3AL5h0YF_view_usp_drivesdk_d5d77e2593.pdf,page_text/DRP-4371_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FGLdUTNnB1DEB9VAQvMROGwf3AL5h0YF_view_usp_drivesdk_d5d77e2593.json,0b344d8dba7dca9fad83ebf078a1312c3d1ee17719ce94bd9cd1d3ee58d2970c,589541,1,digital_text,"Atorvastatin is a selective, competitive inhibitor of HMG-CoA reductase, the rate-limiting enzyme that converts 3- hydroxy-3-methylglutaryl-coenzyme A to mevalonate, a precursor of sterols, including cholesterol. Cholesterol and triglycerides circulate in the bloodstream as part of lipoprotein complexes. With ultracentrifugation, these complexes separate into HDL (high-density lipoprotein), IDL (intermediate-density lipoprotein), LDL (low-density lipoprotein and VLDL (very-low-density lipoprotein) fractions. Triglycerides (TG) and cholesterol in the liver are incorporated into VLDL and released into the plasma for delivery to peripheral tissues. LDL is formed from VLDL and is catabolized primarily through the high-affinity LDL receptor. Clinical and pathologic studies show that elevated plasma levels of total cholesterol (total-C), LDL-cholesterol (LDL-C) and apolipoprotein B (apo B) promote human atherosclerosis and are risk factors for developing cardiovascular disease, while increased levels of HDL-C are associated with a decreased cardiovascular risk.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,ATORVASTATIN CALCIUM CHOLTROL40 mg Film-Coated Tablet HMG CoA Reductase Inhibitor 90mm 130mm PPIPHC047 PACK INSERT PACKAGING DEVELOPMENT NOTE: Do not use any Symbol Product Name : Choltrol 40mg Tablet Size : L-90mm x H-130mm Colour : Black ( Single Colour ) ERP Code : PPIPHC047 Date : 30/11/2019 Pack : 10 Tablets Pack Insert Country : Philippines - Order Size after folding : L-90 mm x H-33 mm Grammage : 57gsm ±5% Map - Litho paper Proof No. : Regulatory Packaging Develop. QA Prepared by Artist Sign: Date: Brand Name Generic Name Label Claim Storage Condition Mfd. Lic. No. Address. Overprinting Area ERP Code Dimensions Specifications Barcode Warnings Reg. No. Colour Check Points Reg. Pkg. Dev. QA A/W Dosage,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:12:19.182217+00:00
