PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4428,Medroxyprogesterone Acetate,Db-5,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HPw9GKwV3PI3BYOwrn-Bt4bAaCB3XOIT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4428_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HPw9GKwV3PI3BYOwrn-Bt4bAaCB3XOIT_view_usp_drivesdk_f58e8bb8af.pdf,page_text/DRP-4428_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HPw9GKwV3PI3BYOwrn-Bt4bAaCB3XOIT_view_usp_drivesdk_f58e8bb8af.json,40231a2598cd9f186073be391e045e903b28f7d03590e857799e328bc90fa7da,460701,1,digital_text,"White round shaped, biconvex, uncoated tablets with break line one side and other side plain. DRP-4428 Date of First Authorization: May 23, 2013 Date of Revision of Package Insert: October 15, 2025 [Page 2]",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Medroxyprogestrone tablets are used for treating secondary amenorrhea (cessation of menstruation); abnormal bleeding from the uterus due to hormonal imbalance and not due to fibroids, or cancer; and to prevent endometrial hyperplasia (overgrowth in the endometrial lining) in postmenopausal women who have not undergone a hysterectomy and conjugated estrogens.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:31:20.826930+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4430,BROMHEXINE HYDROCHLORIDE,Unbranded,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/19Q3plZsYEUrqjTh2c6Jg1zXmSJuMHNDY/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4430_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19Q3plZsYEUrqjTh2c6Jg1zXmSJuMHNDY_view_usp_drivesdk_f672c9972c.pdf,page_text/DRP-4430_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19Q3plZsYEUrqjTh2c6Jg1zXmSJuMHNDY_view_usp_drivesdk_f672c9972c.json,126a3204754bb1d828bd8467930ccd9b0060ae68935edc0cda6f10731919f0a0,908413,1,digital_text,"Bromhexine Hydrochloride is White, round, flat, beveled edge and plain on both sides tablet. Strength of the medicine Each tablet contains 8mg of the active ingredients Bromhexine Hydrochloride What is the medicine used for? The medicine is used for the treatment of respiratory disorders associated with viscid mucus. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Always take the medicine as directed by your physician or as mentioned in the packet. Usually the recommended doses are stated below: Usual Adult Dose: 8mg to 16mg (1 to 2 tablets) three times a day Children: 7 - 12 years old: 4 mg (1/2 tablet) three times a day 2 - 6 years old: 4 mg (1/2 tablet) two times a day Or prescribed by the physician When should you not take this medicine? Not recommended for children below 2 years of age without medical advice. Tell your doctor if you have liver problems, kidney problems, not stomach ulcers before takin the Medicine. If you buy Bromhexine Hydrochloride over-the-counter then for adults and older children who are normaly in healthy condition, the medicine should not be consumed for more than one week. Not recommended for women who are pregnant or breast feeding. Undesirable effects Occassional, mild side effects includes Diarrhea Nausea Indigestion a bloated feeling Headache At times though very rarely, allergic reactions might occur such as skin rashes difficulty in breathing swelling of the lips, mouth, face, tounge or throat What other medicines or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Be sure to inform your doctor and/or pharmacist if you are taking, recently taken or plan to take oth medications, nutritional supplements or herbal products. Alert your doctor or pharmacist if you are taking any antibiotics as bromhexine may increase the absorption of antibiotics Storage Condition: Store at room temperatures not exceeding 30ºC 8 [Page 2]",1,1,Product Description:,"a bloated feeling Headache At times though very rarely, allergic reactions might occur such as skin rashes difficulty in breathing swelling of the lips, mouth, face, tounge or throat What other medicines or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Be sure to inform your doctor and/or pharmacist if you are taking, recently taken or plan to take oth medications, nutritional supplements or herbal products. Alert your doctor or pharmacist if you are taking any antibiotics as bromhexine may increase the absorption of antibiotics Storage Condition: Store at room temperatures not exceeding 30ºC 8 [Page 2]",1,1,Indigestion,low,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T15:31:24.390997+00:00
