PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4459,Multivitamins + Minerals,Telvit-M,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ybgeGqJpbSJvq1KlqjU0MM1kJSrpAwpJ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4459_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ybgeGqJpbSJvq1KlqjU0MM1kJSrpAwpJ_view_usp_drivesdk_2503e0bc25.pdf,page_text/DRP-4459_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ybgeGqJpbSJvq1KlqjU0MM1kJSrpAwpJ_view_usp_drivesdk_2503e0bc25.json,2e6949b21e628e2a838addc6dd36a8e006e37f9f9fabc6db7f5112e9f7d39a92,3155728,1,ocr,"While taking Multivitamins + Minerals, both protein and energy are also required to provide complete nutrition in the daily diet. No other vitamins, minerals or Red, circular, biconvex, sugar-coated tablet, plain on both sides. supplements with or without vitamin A should be taken with this preparation except under medical supervision.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Thiamine Mononitrate (Vitamin B:) B Omg Riboflavin (Vitamin Bz) BP................. 1.0mg For the treatment and prevention of vitamins and minerals deficiencies. Pyridoxine Hydrochloride (Vitamin Be) BP. 1.34mg,1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T15:32:33.941005+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4460,Multivitamins + Minerals,We Care,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JyErD_8AESx4Po5xd8Ydu7HMMM7UCnPC/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4460_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1JyErD_8AESx4Po5xd8Ydu7HMMM7UCnPC_view_usp_drivesdk_8139138c89.pdf,page_text/DRP-4460_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1JyErD_8AESx4Po5xd8Ydu7HMMM7UCnPC_view_usp_drivesdk_8139138c89.json,c21bce326b6e6cb3c5a2f782fd86d981fee31caff79d9292aa8607289073340f,1411077,1,digital_text,"Red, circular, biconvex, sugar-coated tablet, plain on both sides. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Multivitamins + Minerals Sugar-Coated Tablet (WE CARE) is a multivitamin and mineral supplement. It contains a combination of 12 essential vitamins and minerals. The human body requires a wide variety of vitamins and minerals to perform crucial daily tasks such as releasing energy from food and repairing cell damage. During certain illnesses, your body either cannot get or cannot efficiently use all of the vitamins and minerals it needs. Each tablet contains the following 12 essential vitamins and minerals each of which plays a vital role in the efficient daily maintenance of many body processes. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Please see formulation. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Multivitamins + Minerals (WE CARE) is used for the treatment and prevention of vitamin and mineral deficiencies. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Multivitamins + Minerals (WE CARE) should be taken orally. The recommended dose is: Adults and elderly: One tablet daily, preferably taken one hour after meals. Do not exceed the stated dose. The tablet should be swallowed whole with water. Children under 12 years of age: Multivitamins + Minerals (WE CARE) tablets are not Recommended for this age group. Or as prescribed by the physician. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Do not take Multivitamins + Minerals (WE CARE) Tablets: 1.) If you have previous history of hypersensitivity to any of its ingredients 2.) Consult doctor before administration in children CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? While taking Multivitamins + Minerals (WE CARE) Tablets, both protein and energy are also required to provide complete nutrition in the daily diet. No other vitamins, minerals or supplements with or without Vitamin A should be taken with this preparation except under medical supervision. Do not take Multivitamins + Minerals (WE CARE) Tablets on an empty stomach. Do not exceed the stated dose. Patients with thyroid disorders should see medical advice before taking Multivitamins + Minerals (WE CARE) Tablets. An allowance should be made for vitamins and minerals obtained from other sources. Evidence from Randomized Control Trials suggests that high doses (20-30 mg/day) b-carotene intake may increase the risk of lung cancer in current smokers and those previously exposed to asbestos. The high-risk population should consider the potential risks and benefits of Multivitamins + Minerals (WE CARE) Tablets, which contain 4.5 mg per recommended daily dose before use. Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before taking Multivitamins + Minerals (WE CARE) Tablets if: 1. You are pregnant, might become pregnant or think you may be pregnant. 2. Allergy 3. Adverse effects It is important to ask your doctor or pharmacist if Multivitamins + Minerals (WE CARE) Tablet is safe for you when you are taking any other medicines, including medicines obtained without prescription.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T15:32:37.822388+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4463,Carvedilol,Carvetop,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1T7IFGFYD8j17nNFJ84xRhrSdYywEayzE/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4463_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1T7IFGFYD8j17nNFJ84xRhrSdYywEayzE_view_usp_drivesdk_e3618de145.pdf,page_text/DRP-4463_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1T7IFGFYD8j17nNFJ84xRhrSdYywEayzE_view_usp_drivesdk_e3618de145.json,2deed726f6971f15eaa2e97982ba75b645a5dfa6fdee087ea1e0c7ee7a3d99db,1586276,1,digital_text,"White, circular, biconvex, uncoated tablet, plain on both sides. Carvedilol is a non-cardioselective beta blocker . It also has a vasodilating properties that are attributed mainly to its blocking activity at alpha1 receptors: at higher doses calcium-channel blocking activity may contribute.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Used in the management of hypertension and angina pectoris, and as an adjunct to standard therapy in symptomatic heart failure.",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:33:03.378399+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4463-04,Carvedilol,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/18iyd1w80WfGaPWvOelZDJX98q3HTYAJN/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4463-04_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18iyd1w80WfGaPWvOelZDJX98q3HTYAJN_view_usp_drivesdk_a984c13801.pdf,page_text/DRP-4463-04_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18iyd1w80WfGaPWvOelZDJX98q3HTYAJN_view_usp_drivesdk_a984c13801.json,7cf266ae65529fbcd7c2c90aad0c0334da3694795ec2d37d3fe680c3809ecade,639916,1,digital_text,Carvedilol is a non-cardioselective beta blocker. It also has a vasodilating properties that are attributed mainly to its blocking activity at alpha1 receptors: at higher doses calcium-channel blocking activity may contribute.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"The most frequent and serious adverse effects of these drugs are related to their beta adrenergic blocking activity. Among the most serious are heart failure, heart block, and bronchospasm. Troublesome subjective include fatigue and coldness of extremities. Other BP lowering drugs, reserpine, guanethidine, methyldopa, clonidine or guanfacine and rifampicin. Beta-blockers reduce placental perfusion, which may result in intrauterine foetal death, and immature and premature deliveries. In addition, adverse effects (especially hypoglycaemia and bradycardia) may occur in the foetus and neonate. There may be an increased risk of cardiac and pulmonary complications in the neonate in the postnatal period. There is no evidence from animal studies that carvedilol has any teratogenic effects.",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:32:41.153961+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4463-05,Carvedilol,Zerevedil,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FGW3LNug52AyOAOIdaxPMbsU98chjQDH/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4463-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FGW3LNug52AyOAOIdaxPMbsU98chjQDH_view_usp_drivesdk_1350ba7b53.pdf,page_text/DRP-4463-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FGW3LNug52AyOAOIdaxPMbsU98chjQDH_view_usp_drivesdk_1350ba7b53.json,c53107b21f2c300a22c6768978cd69c8d5452c8ef940a2b904005226b8097334,5434750,1,ocr,"reduced death or major cardiovascular hospitalisation by 17% (p= 0.019). White, circular, biconvex, uncoated tablet, plain on both sides. Special Precautions Carvedilol is a non-cardioselective beta blocker. It also has vasodilating properties that are attributed mainly to its blocking General: Chronic Congestive Heart Failure: activity at alpha-1 receptors: at higher doses calcium-channel blocking activity may contribute. In congestive heart failure patients, worsening cardiac failure or fluid retention may occur during up-titration of carvedilol. If such symptoms occur, diuretics should be increased and the carvedilol dose should not be further increased until clinical",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Used in the management of hypertension and angina pectoris, and as an adjunct to standard therapy in symptomatic heart Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. failure.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T15:32:59.696639+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4464,Paracetamol,Stalpara,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Ivenzp0JGGjm8hk1Z328qSBzN2N-lIwa/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4464_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Ivenzp0JGGjm8hk1Z328qSBzN2N-lIwa_view_usp_drivesdk_50f1b0ab23.pdf,page_text/DRP-4464_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Ivenzp0JGGjm8hk1Z328qSBzN2N-lIwa_view_usp_drivesdk_50f1b0ab23.json,2d9e0a01e8c51ebe333f63f660dc48f68f082a4b30e42f6179e0973e7ae4409c,536654,1,digital_text,Paracetamol provides onset of pain relief within 5 to 10 minutes after the start of administration. The peak analgesic effect is obtained in 1 hour and the duration of this effect is usually 4 to 6 hours. Paracetamol reduces fever within 30 minutes after the start of administration with a duration of the antipyretic effect of at least 6 hours.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Used for the treatment of mild to moderate pain and/or fever. Special populations:,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:33:06.786940+00:00
