PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4550,Clarithromycin,Cleocin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mUABGWv52e0rAMjV551fOHPEw5w9vYIJ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4550_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mUABGWv52e0rAMjV551fOHPEw5w9vYIJ_view_usp_drivesdk_3c1580295b.pdf,page_text/DRP-4550_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mUABGWv52e0rAMjV551fOHPEw5w9vYIJ_view_usp_drivesdk_3c1580295b.json,a81147a823006610fe1e1510bd41ff462e281c47a76cb94d214d091cd2c3bd97,1446355,1,digital_text,,,,,"Clarithromycin is used in the treatment of infec␀ons from respiratory pathogens (e.g. S. Pyogenes, S. Pneumoniae, other streptococci, M. Catarrhalis, C. trachomalis, C. Pneumoniae, Legionella sp., Mycoplasma pneumonia, S. Aureus and H. Inﬂuenzae) and in the treatment and preven␀on of M. Avium complex in pa␀ents with AIDS. It is also used in the treatment of gastric ulcer and duodenal ulcer relapses as an an␀ Helicobacter pylori in conjunc␀on with bismuth subcitrate or proton pump inhibitor. Pharmacokine␀cs: Clarithromycin is rapidly absorbed from the gastrointes␀nal tract and undergoes ﬁrst-pass metabolism, the bioavailability of the parent drug is about 55%. The extent of absorp␀on is rela␀vely unaﬀected by the presence of food. Peak plasma concentra␀ons occur 2 to 3 hours a␀er an oral dose. At steady state, peak plasma concentra␀ons of clarithromycin and its principal ac␀ve metabolite, 14-hydroxyclarithromycin, are about 1 and 0.6 micrograms/mL, respec␀vely, a␀er 250 mg orally every 12 hours as tablets. The same dose given as a suspension to fas␀ng subjects produces steadystate plasma concentra␀ons of about 2 m i c ro g ra m s / m L o f c l a r i t h ro myc i n a n d a b o u t 0 . 7 m i c ro g ra m s / m L o f 1 4 - hydroxyclarithromycin. Steady state concentra␀ons are reached within 3 to 4 days. The pharmacokine␀cs of clarithromycin are non-linear and dose dependent; high doses may produce dispropor␀onate increases in peak concentra␀ons of the parent, due to satura␀on of the metabolic pathways. However, the non-linearity is slight at the recommended doses of 250 to 500 mg every 8 to 12 hours. Clarithromycin and 14-hydroxyclarithromycin are widely distributed, and ␀ssue concentra␀ons exceed those in serum, in part because of intracellular uptake. Plasma protein binding has been reported to be about 80%, clarithromycin has been detected in breast milk. It is extensively metabolised in the liver. And excreted in faeces via the bile; 5 to 10% of the parent drug is recovered from the faeces. At steady state, about 20% and 30% of a 250-mg or 500-mg dose as tablets, respec␀vely, and about 40% of a 250-mg dose as suspension, is excreted in the urine as unchanged drug, 14-Hydroxyclarithromycin as well as other metabolites are also excreted in the urine, according for 10 to 15% of the dose. The elimina␀on half-lives of clarithromycin and 14-hydroxyclarithromycin are about 3 to 4 and 5 to 6 hours, respec␀vely in pa␀ents receiving 250 mg every 12 hours, and about 5 to 7 and 7 to 9 hours respec␀vely, in those receiving 500 mg every 8 to 12 hours. The half-life is prolonged in renal impairment.",1,1,Indica␀on:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T15:36:38.712585+00:00
