PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4565,Ampicillin (as Sodium),Excillin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rOyhinrjvM8gCTSEtjdrfnN-GrOArgx3/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4565_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rOyhinrjvM8gCTSEtjdrfnN-GrOArgx3_view_usp_drivesdk_39006b979a.pdf,page_text/DRP-4565_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rOyhinrjvM8gCTSEtjdrfnN-GrOArgx3_view_usp_drivesdk_39006b979a.json,fc841976cf08fe41e8cbee168c8f974d28daffb607c88d7e985d09dc182f9f0d,363077,16,digital_text_and_ocr,Powder for injection (IM/IV) CLINICAL PARTICULARS,1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"For the initiation of treatment of infections caused by susceptible strains of both Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria, and the treatment of severe infections, particularly in patients for whom oral administration is impossible. Infections of the respiratory tract (particularly those caused by Haemophilus influenzae) - Infections and mixed infections of the upper respiratory tract and ENT region, e.g. sinusitis, otitis media - I nfections of the lower respiratory tract, e.g. acute and chronic bronchitis, pneumonia Skin and soft tissue infections Infections of the urogenital tract - Acute and chronic pyelonephritis, pyelitis, cystitis, urethritis, prostatitis, etc. - Gonorrhoea - I nfections in the region of the female reproductive organs and true pelvis, e.g. infected abortion, inflammation of the uterine adnexa, salpingitis, endometritis, and parametritis, pelvic peritonitis, puerperal fever, etc. Infections of the gastrointestinal tract - Bacterial diarrhoea, salmonellosis, shigellosis, typhoid fever, paratyphoid fever; treatment of Salmonella carriers - Infections of the bile ducts (cholangiolitis, cholangitis, cholecystitis) Acute a nd latent listeriosis, leptospirosis, possibly in combination with gentamicin or kanamycin, meningitis, possibly in combination with chloramphenicol, endocarditis (e.g. caused by enterococci, in combination with an aminoglycoside), bacterial meningitis Septicaemia caused by pathogens. that are susceptible to ampicillin bile ducts (cholangiolitis, cholangitis, cholecystitis) Ampicillin sodium [Page 2] Ampicillin 250 mg, 500 mg, 1g Powder for Injection Ampicillin has been used successfully in the treatment of granuloma inguinale and leptospirosis. Prophylaxis Perioperative infection prophylaxis (up to 24 (-48) hours after surgery)",1,2,Indications,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T15:37:16.217316+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4575,Ampicillin (As Sodium),Excillin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DuBx8FzxPixdHYwNfy4nIJcJYlttY0kQ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4575_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1DuBx8FzxPixdHYwNfy4nIJcJYlttY0kQ_view_usp_drivesdk_c72fad57ea.pdf,page_text/DRP-4575_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1DuBx8FzxPixdHYwNfy4nIJcJYlttY0kQ_view_usp_drivesdk_c72fad57ea.json,fc841976cf08fe41e8cbee168c8f974d28daffb607c88d7e985d09dc182f9f0d,363077,16,digital_text_and_ocr,Powder for injection (IM/IV) CLINICAL PARTICULARS,1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"For the initiation of treatment of infections caused by susceptible strains of both Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria, and the treatment of severe infections, particularly in patients for whom oral administration is impossible. Infections of the respiratory tract (particularly those caused by Haemophilus influenzae) - Infections and mixed infections of the upper respiratory tract and ENT region, e.g. sinusitis, otitis media - I nfections of the lower respiratory tract, e.g. acute and chronic bronchitis, pneumonia Skin and soft tissue infections Infections of the urogenital tract - Acute and chronic pyelonephritis, pyelitis, cystitis, urethritis, prostatitis, etc. - Gonorrhoea - I nfections in the region of the female reproductive organs and true pelvis, e.g. infected abortion, inflammation of the uterine adnexa, salpingitis, endometritis, and parametritis, pelvic peritonitis, puerperal fever, etc. Infections of the gastrointestinal tract - Bacterial diarrhoea, salmonellosis, shigellosis, typhoid fever, paratyphoid fever; treatment of Salmonella carriers - Infections of the bile ducts (cholangiolitis, cholangitis, cholecystitis) Acute a nd latent listeriosis, leptospirosis, possibly in combination with gentamicin or kanamycin, meningitis, possibly in combination with chloramphenicol, endocarditis (e.g. caused by enterococci, in combination with an aminoglycoside), bacterial meningitis Septicaemia caused by pathogens. that are susceptible to ampicillin bile ducts (cholangiolitis, cholangitis, cholecystitis) Ampicillin sodium [Page 2] Ampicillin 250 mg, 500 mg, 1g Powder for Injection Ampicillin has been used successfully in the treatment of granuloma inguinale and leptospirosis. Prophylaxis Perioperative infection prophylaxis (up to 24 (-48) hours after surgery)",1,2,Indications,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T15:37:20.481282+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4584,Levetiracetam,Akucetam-1000,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/15Vpg3kftI3BglR4M4PVI3bCQMvLtQBay/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4584_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15Vpg3kftI3BglR4M4PVI3bCQMvLtQBay_view_usp_drivesdk_3719909302.pdf,page_text/DRP-4584_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15Vpg3kftI3BglR4M4PVI3bCQMvLtQBay_view_usp_drivesdk_3719909302.json,239d13afbefa9a2a2f928b8c0601ea60e8654001843d2945477b510a3b62e1c1,427327,1,digital_text,"White, elongated, biconvex, plain on both side and film-coated tablets.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Levetiracetam is used as an adjunct in the treatment of partial seizures with or without secondary generalizations, myoclonic seizures, and primary generalized tonic-clonic seizures.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:37:34.034949+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4584-01,Levetiracetam,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uMn2VkpX2LXAqGYCgUGGH1r5qF9chpVr/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4584-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uMn2VkpX2LXAqGYCgUGGH1r5qF9chpVr_view_usp_drivesdk_5769292359.pdf,page_text/DRP-4584-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uMn2VkpX2LXAqGYCgUGGH1r5qF9chpVr_view_usp_drivesdk_5769292359.json,99e87ffb046af534c287ad3928fcda94beee44573fc5dcd56d6697c924b84f4c,480702,1,digital_text,"White, elongated, biconvex, plain on both side and film-coated tablets. Pharmacotherapeutic group: antiepileptics, other antiepileptics The active substance, levetiracetam, is a pyrrolidone derivative (S-enantiomer of α-ethyl-2-oxo-1-pyrrolidine acetamide), chemically unrelated to existing antiepileptic active substances. Mechanism of action The mechanism of action of levetiracetam still remains to be fully elucidated. In vitro and in vivo experiments suggest that levetiracetam does not alter basic cell characteristics and normal neurotransmission. In vitro studies show that levetiracetam affects intraneuronal Ca2+ levels by partial inhibition of N-type Ca2+ currents and by reducing the release of Ca2+ from intraneuronal stores. In addition it partially reverses the reductions in GABA- and glycine-gated currents induced by zinc and β-carbolines. Furthermore, levetiracetam has been shown in in vitro studies to bind to a specific site in rodent brain tissue. This binding site is the synaptic vesicle protein 2A, believed to be involved in vesicle fusion and neurotransmitter exocytosis. Levetiracetam and related analogs show a rank order of affinity for binding to the synaptic vesicle protein 2A which correlates with the potency of their anti-seizure protection in the mouse audiogenic model of epilepsy. This finding suggests that the interaction between levetiracetam and the synaptic vesicle protein 2A seems to contribute to the antiepileptic mechanism of action of the medicinal product. Pharmacodynamic effects Levetiracetam induces seizure protection in a broad range of animal models of partial and primary generalised seizures without having a pro-convulsant effect. The primary metabolite is inactive. In man, an activity in both partial and generalised epilepsy conditions (epileptiform discharge/photoparoxysmal response) has confirmed the broad spectrum pharmacological profile of levetiracetam. 1 months to < 6 months - initial daily dose of 14 mg/kg in two divided doses (7 mg/kg twice daily). Treatment should be initiated with a dose of 1000 mg/day, given as twice-daily dosing (500 mg twice daily). Dosage should be increased by 1000 mg/day every 2 weeks to the recommended daily dose of 3000 mg. Adult 16 years and older - Treatment should be initiated with a dose of 1000 mg/day, given as twice-daily dosing (500 mg twice daily). Pediatric patients ages 6 to < 16 years - Treatment should be initiated with a daily dose of 20 mg/kg in 2 divided doses (10 mg/kg twice daily). Or as prescribed by the physician.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Partial Onset Seizures: 4 years to < 16 years - initial daily dose of 20 mg/kg in 2 divided doses (10 mg/kg twice daily). The daily dose should be increased every 2 weeks by increments of 20 mg/kg to the recommended daily dose of 60 mg/kg (30 mg/kg twice daily). 6 months to < 4 years - initial daily dose of 20 mg/kg in 2 divided doses (10 mg/kg twice daily).The daily dose should be increased in 2 weeks by an increment of 20 mg/kg to the recommended daily dose of 50 mg/kg (25 mg/kg twice daily) Adults 16 years and older - initial daily dose of 1000 mg/day given as twice- daily dosing (500 mg twice daily). Levetiracetam is used as an adjunct in the treatment of partial seizures with or without secondary generalizations, myoclonic seizures, and primary generalized tonic-clonic seizures. Primary generalized tonic- clonic seizures:",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:37:23.618483+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4584-02,Levetiracetam,Devetam 1000,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FQPpzndWLT-cuRCibjhGXsy2RJHBz9h5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4584-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FQPpzndWLT-cuRCibjhGXsy2RJHBz9h5_view_usp_drivesdk_348bf3581c.pdf,page_text/DRP-4584-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FQPpzndWLT-cuRCibjhGXsy2RJHBz9h5_view_usp_drivesdk_348bf3581c.json,e5a7d3277abc8e356ee87dda7b237fb4ff078ddbaa587cfcf9589ec2b2d6d550,501569,1,digital_text,"Pharmacotherapeutic group: antiepileptics, other antiepileptics Levetiracetam ........................... 1000 mg Mechanism of action In vitro studies show that levetiracetam affects intraneuronal Ca2+ levels by partial inhibition of N-type Ca2+ currents and by reducing the release of Ca2+ from intraneuronal stores. In addition it partially reverses the reductions in GABA- and glycine-gated currents induced by zinc and β-carbolines. Furthermore, levetiracetam has been shown in in vitro studies to bind to a specific site in rodent brain tissue. This binding site is the synaptic vesicle protein 2A, believed to be involved in vesicle fusion and neurotransmitter exocytosis. Levetiracetam and related analogs show a rank order of affinity for binding to the synaptic vesicle protein 2A which correlates with the potency of their anti-seizure protection in the mouse audiogenic model of epilepsy. This finding suggests that the interaction between levetiracetam and the synaptic vesicle protein 2A seems to contribute to the antiepileptic mechanism of action of the medicinal product. The active substance, levetiracetam, is a pyrrolidone derivative (S-enantiomer of α-ethyl-2-oxo-1-pyrrolidine acetamide), chemically unrelated to existing antiepileptic active substances. The mechanism of action of levetiracetam still remains to be fully elucidated. In vitro and in vivo experiments suggest that levetiracetam does not alter basic cell characteristics and normal neurotransmission. Pharmacodynamic effects Levetiracetam induces seizure protection in a broad range of animal models of partial and primary generalised seizures without having a pro-convulsant effect. The primary metabolite is inactive. In man, an activity in both partial and generalised epilepsy conditions (epileptiform discharge/photoparoxysmal response) has confirmed the broad spectrum pharmacological profile of levetiracetam. White, elongated, biconvex, plain on both side and film-coated tablets.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Levetiracetam is used as an adjunct in the treatment of partial seizures with or without secondary generalizations, myoclonic seizures, and primary generalized tonic-clonic seizures.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:37:27.274247+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4584-03,Levetiracetam,Levtrawell,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1jU7b-unWaO5xBrxLmDB2LOXDy1vbxNGN/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4584-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jU7b-unWaO5xBrxLmDB2LOXDy1vbxNGN_view_usp_drivesdk_81b5ab7a95.pdf,page_text/DRP-4584-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jU7b-unWaO5xBrxLmDB2LOXDy1vbxNGN_view_usp_drivesdk_81b5ab7a95.json,91cc4e439ef91aadb8b0e89a83ce541ab7bc8c001a8bf7e821868efe2e9a538d,505612,1,digital_text,"Levetiracetam ........................... 1000 mg Each film-coated tablet contains : Colour : Titanium Dioxide BP White, elongated, biconvex, plain on both side and film-coated tablets. Pharmacotherapeutic group: antiepileptics, other antiepileptics Mechanism of action The mechanism of action of levetiracetam still remains to be fully elucidated. In vitro and in vivo experiments suggest that levetiracetam does not alter basic cell characteristics and normal neurotransmission. Levetiracetam induces seizure protection in a broad range of animal models of partial and primary generalised seizures without having a pro-convulsant effect. The primary metabolite is inactive. In man, an activity in both partial and generalised epilepsy conditions (epileptiform discharge/photoparoxysmal response) has confirmed the broad spectrum pharmacological profile of levetiracetam.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Levetiracetam is used as an adjunct in the treatment of partial seizures with or without secondary generalizations, myoclonic seizures, and primary generalized tonic-clonic seizures. Partial Onset Seizures: Adults 16 years and older - initial daily dose of 1000 mg/day given as twice- daily dosing (500 mg twice daily). 1 months to < 6 months - initial daily dose of 14 mg/kg in two divided doses (7 mg/kg twice daily). 6 months to < 4 years - initial daily dose of 20 mg/kg in 2 divided doses (10 mg/kg twice daily).The daily dose should be increased in 2 weeks by an increment of 20 mg/kg to the recommended daily dose of 50 mg/kg (25 mg/kg twice daily) 4 years to < 16 years - initial daily dose of 20 mg/kg in 2 divided doses (10 mg/kg twice daily). The daily dose should be increased every 2 weeks by increments of 20 mg/kg to the recommended daily dose of 60 mg/kg (30 mg/kg twice daily). Myoclonic Seizures in patients 12 years of age and older: Primary generalized tonic- clonic seizures: Adult 16 years and older - Treatment should be initiated with a dose of 1000 mg/day, given as twice-daily dosing (500 mg twice daily). Treatment should be initiated with a dose of 1000 mg/day, given as twice-daily dosing (500 mg twice daily). Dosage should be increased by 1000 mg/day every 2 weeks to the recommended daily dose of 3000 mg. Pediatric patients ages 6 to < 16 years - Treatment should be initiated with a daily dose of 20 mg/kg in 2 divided doses (10 mg/kg twice daily). Or as prescribed by the physician. Alu/Alu Blister Pack x 10’s (Box of 10 Tablets) Date of First Authorization: September 06, 2021 Hypersensitivity to the active substance or other pyrrolidone derivatives or to any of the excipients. For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Date of Revision of Package Insert: December 07, 2022 Levetiracetam should be used with caution and in reduced doses in patients with renal impairment, those undergoing haemodialysis and in patients with severe hepatic impairment. Symptoms Foods, Drugs, Devices, and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription. Potential pharmacokinetics interactions of or with levetiracetam were assessed in clinical pharmacokinetic studies (phenytoin, valproate, warfarin, digoxin, oral contraceptive, probenecid) and through pharmacokinetics screening in the placebo-controlled clinical studies in epilepsy patients. Symptoms of carbamazepine toxicity have been reported when levetiracetam was added to carbamazepine therapy; this interaction appeared to be due to pharmacodynamic mechanism as blood levels of carbamazepine and its epoxide metabolite were not altered.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:37:30.616975+00:00
