PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4649-03,Glimepiride,Glyperide,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/172T6tR7bNK7yUuDwWViJJTmFVV5ZVbiV/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4649-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_172T6tR7bNK7yUuDwWViJJTmFVV5ZVbiV_view_usp_drivesdk_eb59d7a50e.pdf,page_text/DRP-4649-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_172T6tR7bNK7yUuDwWViJJTmFVV5ZVbiV_view_usp_drivesdk_eb59d7a50e.json,b161d15a2ef4de636ee71bedb4eb99c7e736a714a90e9d31e655cc652533dcc3,376055,1,digital_text,"A light pink to pink, 6 mm round, flat tablet, bisected on one side and plain on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Glimepiride is indicated for the management of non-insulin dependent (Type II) diabetes mellitus that can sometimes be controlled by good diet, exercise and weight control, where this is not enough, glimepiride is used. In adults, as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control as monotherapy. It may also be indicated for use in combination with metformin or insulin to lower blood glucose in patients with type II diabetes whose high blood sugar levels cannot be controlled by diet and exercise in conjunction with an oral hypoglycemic (a drug used to lower blood sugar levels) agent alone.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:39:22.586759+00:00
