PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4659,Levofloxacin (As Hemihydrate),None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gabOOLjRYZ1BCPQWd0foohSC14qh6mZe/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4659_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gabOOLjRYZ1BCPQWd0foohSC14qh6mZe_view_usp_drivesdk_26e676dc72.pdf,page_text/DRP-4659_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gabOOLjRYZ1BCPQWd0foohSC14qh6mZe_view_usp_drivesdk_26e676dc72.json,325e0002eaa4f275a2580e135e242655cc4b7b9465e0cc14abe3d20c0981009d,495620,1,digital_text,Eq. to Levofloxacin ........... 500 mg,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Mechanism of action As a fluoroquinolone antibacterial agent, levofloxacin acts on the DNA-DNA-gyrase complex and topoisomerase IV. INDICATION : Used i n the treatment of acute sinusitis, exacerbation of chronic bronchitis, community acquired pneumonia, urinary tract infections, chronic prostatis, skin and soft-tissue infections. Usually doses range from 250 mg once daily for 3 days for uncomplicated urinary-tract infections to 250 or 500 mg once or twice daily for 10 to 14 days for most susceptible infections. A 28 day course of treatment with a dose of 500 mg once daily should be given for chronic bacterial prostatitis. An alternative regimen of 750 mg once daily for 7 to147 days may be used for complicated skin infections and for hospital-acquired pneumonia; a shorter course of 750 mg once daily for 5 days may be given for community-acquired pneumonia or for acute bacterial sinusitis. Dosage should be reduced in patients with renal impairment. Or as directed by the physician. Levofloxacin is generally considered to be about twice as active as ofloxacin (p.310), the racemic substance. Levofloxacin has a broad spectrum of activity which includes Gram-positive bacteria. Levofloxacin is contraindicated in persons with a history of hypersensitivity of levofloxacin, quinolone antimicrobial agents, or any other components of this product.",1,1,CONTRAINDICATIONS :,low,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T15:39:51.803026+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4662,Spironolactone,Lactone,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sHsOoBhEG4oCEY48i93F75VmYe6AmOn4/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4662_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1sHsOoBhEG4oCEY48i93F75VmYe6AmOn4_view_usp_drivesdk_68e36a2e71.pdf,page_text/DRP-4662_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1sHsOoBhEG4oCEY48i93F75VmYe6AmOn4_view_usp_drivesdk_68e36a2e71.json,c0410e4643677ec8c640d619d99ec6eaa0e1cae7ab5e21d1a10813ae94de9775,4138906,1,ocr,"and polyps) Blood and Agranulocytosis, side. White round shape, biconvex uncoated tablet with breakline on one side and plain on other lymphatic system Leukopenia, disorders Metabolism and Hyperkalaemia Electrolyte",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Watch your diet while you are taking Spironolactone (LACTONE). Ask your prescriber or Used in the management of heart failure, both to treat refractory edema and in lower doses as health care professional about both potassium and sodium intake. Spironolactone (LACTONE) can make your body retain potassium and you may have too much. Elderly an adjunct to standard therapy. Itis also used for refractory edema associated with cirrhosis of patients, the severely ill, diabetics, or patients with kidney problems are more likely to suffer the liver, or the nephrotic syndrome, and in ascites associated with malignancy. from the effects of too much potassium. Avoid salt-substitutes and nutritional supplements. which contain potassium, unless your prescriber or health care professional tells you",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T15:40:33.519956+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4662-01,Spironolactone,Corlactone,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1y3P1YzMSo74gMKE9MVznMVS_0-kIcpkw/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4662-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1y3P1YzMSo74gMKE9MVznMVS_0-kIcpkw_view_usp_drivesdk_bef0fba0e6.pdf,page_text/DRP-4662-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1y3P1YzMSo74gMKE9MVznMVS_0-kIcpkw_view_usp_drivesdk_bef0fba0e6.json,3e73446144c79480611756950a1b7de96af9f4d56644cd64627a6a1feeb4f9be,1427793,1,digital_text,"Pediatric population Pediatric population Spironolactone, as a competitive aldosterone antagonist, increases sodium excretion whilst reducing potassium loss at the distal renal tubule. It has a gradual and prolonged action. Side effects that you should report to your prescriber or health care professional as soon as possible: • You are pregnant or think you might be pregnant. Spironolactone or its metabolites may cross the placental barrier. With Spironolactone, feminisation has been observed in male rat fetuses. • You are breastfeeding. Take Spironolactone (Corlactone) tablets by mouth. Follow the directions on the prescription label. Swallow the tablets with a drink of water. If Spironolactone (Corlactone) upsets your stomach, take it with food or milk. Take your doses at regular intervals. Do not take your medicine more often than directed. Remember that you will need to pass urine frequently after taking Spironolactone (Corlactone). Do not take your doses at a time of day that will cause you problems. Do not take at bedtime. The drug may appear in the breast milk and be passed to the infant. • You are allergic to Spironolactone or to any of the ingredients. Fertility There are no studies in pregnant women.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"There are no pharmacokinetic data available in respect of use in pediatric population. The dosage recommendations for pediatrics are based upon clinical experience and case studies documented in the scientific literature. If you have an allergic reaction you may get a skin rash, have difficulty in breathing, or faint. Imported by: Ambica International Corporation 9 Amsterdam Extension, Merville Park Subd., Parañaque, Metro Manila Manufactured by: Unicure Remedies Pvt. Ltd. F/25, BIDC Estate, Gorwa, Baroda-390 016, India Distributed by: Ambicare Pharmaceuticals, Inc. 2/F Ambica Building, Amsterdam Extn., Merville Park Subd., Parañaque, Metro Manila 07312-02 25 mg Tablet Antialdosterone/ Renin Angiotensin Aldosterone (RAA) Modulator Corlactone Spironolactone [Page 2]",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:39:55.172957+00:00
