PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4667-01,Meloxicam,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1k7VafhkVTmqSfS8aoS3vddP7XDt6Pg_4/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4667-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1k7VafhkVTmqSfS8aoS3vddP7XDt6Pg_4_view_usp_drivesdk_5e6d0d1694.pdf,page_text/DRP-4667-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1k7VafhkVTmqSfS8aoS3vddP7XDt6Pg_4_view_usp_drivesdk_5e6d0d1694.json,bdc51a90157943946e2584176f90b950a514ab0005a97e14ef30fce5a12152b5,460564,1,digital_text,"Light yellow, circular, slightly biconvex uncoated tablet, plain on both sides. Pharmacotherapeutic group: Non steroidal anti-inflammatory agents, oxicams. Meloxicam is a non-steroidal anti-Inflammatory Drug (NSAID) of the oxicam family, with anti-inflammatory, analgesic and antipyretic properties. The anti-inflammatory activity of Meloxicam has been proven in classical models of inflammation. As with other NSAIDs, its precise mechanism of action remains unknown. However, there is at least one common mode of action shared by all NSAID (including Meloxicam): inhibition of the biosynthesis of prostaglandins, known inflammation mediators. Meloxicam is a Non-Steroidal Anti-Inflammatory Drug (NSAID) that exhibits anti-inflammatory, analgesic and antipyretic activities in animal models. The mechanism of action of Meloxicam, like that of other NSAIDs, may be related to prostaglandin synthetase (cyclo-oxygenase) inhibition. Ankylosing Spondylitis: Usual dose of 15 mg daily as single dose. Or as prescribed by the physician. Rheumatoid arthritis: 7.5 to 15 mg / day. The total dose of 15 mg / day should not be exceeded.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,a. Contraindication in patients with history of hypersensitivity to ASA or other NSAIDs.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:40:36.837203+00:00
