PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4719,Etoricoxib,Xibra-90,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1r3u-4iNZrSv-BodQv4zsVBzeQ2NePVjS/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4719_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1r3u-4iNZrSv-BodQv4zsVBzeQ2NePVjS_view_usp_drivesdk_1a2c94227d.pdf,page_text/DRP-4719_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1r3u-4iNZrSv-BodQv4zsVBzeQ2NePVjS_view_usp_drivesdk_1a2c94227d.json,b411b88f7b9511296a74e4127adfedf304a70ea0f8af8aa584538e635cac42f2,408071,2,ocr,"A light blue- colored, oval and biconvex film coated tablet having no identification mark.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Etoricoxib is Non-Steroidal Anti-Inflammatory Drug (NSAID) reported to be a Selective Inhibitor of Cyclo-Oxygenase-2 (COX-2). It is used in the of symptomatic relief Rheumatoid — Arthritis, Osteoarthritis, and Acute Gouty Arthritis.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T15:45:46.592721+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-472,Betahistine Hydrochloride,Serc,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/15MsQOQCTnP3aoRLRFxasuDrpH76O1ntm/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-472_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15MsQOQCTnP3aoRLRFxasuDrpH76O1ntm_view_usp_drivesdk_58d0f55c45.pdf,page_text/DRP-472_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15MsQOQCTnP3aoRLRFxasuDrpH76O1ntm_view_usp_drivesdk_58d0f55c45.json,5e4516ec12843f28c076b5ccf1c4abef0959693122bdbdea4fc88eb90f6ba140,463106,2,digital_text,"Serc® tablet, 8 mg: A round, flat, white to almost white tablet with beveled edges. The diameter is 7 mm; the tablet weight is about 125 mg. The inscription is 256 on one tablet-side. Serc® tablet, 16 mg: A round , biconvex, scored, white to almost white tablet with beveled edges . The diameter is 8.5 mm; the tablet weight is about 250 mg. The inscription is 267 on either side of the score on one tablet-side. The tablet can be divided into equal halves. CLINICAL PARTICULARS Therapeutic indications Ménière’s Syndrome as defined by the following triad of core symptoms:  vertigo (with nausea/vomiting)  hearing loss (hardness of hearing)  tinnitus Symptomatic treatment of vestibular vertigo. Posology and method of administration The dosage for adults is 24-48 mg divided over the day . 8 mg tablets 16 mg tablets 1 - 2 tablets 3 times/day ½ - 1 tablet 3 times/day Method of administration: Should be swallowed with water. The dosage should be individually adapted according to the response. Improvement can sometimes only be observed after a couple of weeks of treatment. The best results are sometimes obtained after a few months. There are indications that treatment from the onset of the disease prevents the progression of the disease and/or the loss of hearing in later phases of the disease. Pediatric population: Serc® is not recommended for use in children below 18 years due to insufficient data on safety and efficacy. Geriatric population: Although there are limited data from clinical studies in this patient group, extensive post marketing experience suggests that no dose adjustment is necessary in this patient population. Renal impairment: There are no specific clinical trials available in this patient group, but according to post-marketing experience no dose adjustment appears to be necessary. Hepatic impairment: There are no specific clinical trials available in this patient group, but according to post-marketing experience no dose adjustment appears to be necessary .",1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,Ménière’s Syndrome as defined by the following triad of core symptoms:  vertigo (with nausea/vomiting)  hearing loss (hardness of hearing)  tinnitus Symptomatic treatment of vestibular vertigo.,1,1,Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:45:49.837344+00:00
