PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4826-02,Escitalopram (As Oxalate),Escitadin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ma58_IDMvlYOuhgxfdHOiWkKV8r-j2SY/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4826-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ma58_IDMvlYOuhgxfdHOiWkKV8r-j2SY_view_usp_drivesdk_18a9072352.pdf,page_text/DRP-4826-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ma58_IDMvlYOuhgxfdHOiWkKV8r-j2SY_view_usp_drivesdk_18a9072352.json,287f37823b7d7ab537354dcf6b2498d96642979afd60d63357036bd37a7568ee,438826,1,digital_text,,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"MECHANISM OF ACTION Escitalopram Oxalate eq. to Escitalopram…………………………………. 10 mg Used in the treatment of depression, panic disorder with or without agoraphobia, generalized anxiety disorder, social anxiety disorder, and obsessive-compulsive disorder. White to off white, round, biconvex, plain on both side and film-coated tablet. PHARMACOKINETICS",1,1,INDICATIONS,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T15:50:27.228917+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4826-03,Escitalopram (As Oxalate),Scitapram,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1f-L4TLOZqFlOILtf-dsQgBH63c1rqIH6/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4826-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1f-L4TLOZqFlOILtf-dsQgBH63c1rqIH6_view_usp_drivesdk_6a8cc908c5.pdf,page_text/DRP-4826-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1f-L4TLOZqFlOILtf-dsQgBH63c1rqIH6_view_usp_drivesdk_6a8cc908c5.json,460e53738c77d4f6c1842890390c604045b6ac0b9ee60805f5d46c9c76123a0b,425617,1,digital_text,"Hypersensitivity to escitalopram or to any of the excipients. Children: as safety and efficacy have not been established in this population. Monoamine Oxidase Inhibitors-Cases of serious reactions have been reported in patients receiving an SSRI such as Escitalopram in combination with a monoamine oxidase inhibitor (MAOI), and in patients who have recently discontinued an SSRI and have been started on a MAOI. Used in the treatment of depression, panic disorder with or without agoraphobia, generalized anxiety disorder, social anxiety disorder, and obsessive-compulsive disorder. It is given orally as the oxalate although doses are expressed in terms of the base; Escitalopram oxalate 12.8 mg is equivalent to about 10 mg of Escitalopram.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"MECHANISM OF ACTION Initial treatment with half the usual recommended dose and a lower maximum dose should be considered in elderly patients. Patients with hepatic impairment or those who are poor metaboliser with respect to the cytochrome P450 isoenzyme CYP2C19 may also require lower doses. Escitalopram is a selective inhibitor of serotonin (5-HT) re-uptake. The inhibition of 5-HT re-uptake is the only likely mechanism of action explaining the pharmacological and clinical effects of escitalopram. Escitalopram has no or low affinity for a number of receptors including 5-HT1A, 5-HT2, DA D1 and D2 receptors, α1-, α2-, β- adrenoceptors, histamine H1, muscarine cholinergic, benzodiazepine and opioid receptors. Paradoxial anxiety – Some patients with panic disorder may experience increased anxiety symptoms at the start of treatment with antidepressants. Pharmacology: PRODUCT DESCRIPTION Hypersensitivity to escitalopram or to any of the excipients. Children: as safety and efficacy have not been established in this population. Monoamine Oxidase Inhibitors-Cases of serious reactions have been reported in patients receiving an SSRI such as Escitalopram in combination with a monoamine oxidase inhibitor (MAOI), and in patients who have recently discontinued an SSRI and have been started on a MAOI. Used in the treatment of depression, panic disorder with or without agoraphobia, generalized anxiety disorder, social anxiety disorder, and obsessive-compulsive disorder. It is given orally as the oxalate although doses are expressed in terms of the base; Escitalopram oxalate 12.8 mg is equivalent to about 10 mg of Escitalopram. PHARMACODYNAMIC PROPERTIES PHARMACOKINETICS",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:50:34.128211+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4826-04,Escitalopram (As Oxalate),None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Hl3jtgthBN9hfFp56klISfueI1DfSx5a/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4826-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Hl3jtgthBN9hfFp56klISfueI1DfSx5a_view_usp_drivesdk_f926d9c168.pdf,page_text/DRP-4826-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Hl3jtgthBN9hfFp56klISfueI1DfSx5a_view_usp_drivesdk_f926d9c168.json,3fa019b5dfdc37d12e08cda7d6b09558c66883947212de64974ec00e414084c5,792858,1,digital_text,"Escitalopram is a selective inhibitor of serotonin (5-HT) re-uptake. The inhibition of 5-HT re-uptake is the only likely mechanism of action explaining the pharmacological and clinical effects of Escitalopram. Escitalopram has no or low affinity for a number of receptors including 5-HT1A, 5-HT2, DA D1 and D2 receptors, α1-, α2-, β-adrenoceptors, histamine H1, muscarine cholinergic, benzodiazepine and opioid receptors. Absorption is independent of food intake (mean Tmax is 4 hours after multiple dosing). The apparent volume of distribution (Vd, beta/F) after oral administration is about 12 to 26 L/kg. The plasma protein binding of Escitalopram is approximately 55%. Escitalopram is metabolised in the liver to the didemethylated metabolites and partly excreted as glucuronides. Unchanged Escitalopram is the predominant compound in plasma. After multiple dosing the mean concentrations of the dimethyl and didemethyl metabolites are usually 28-31% and 5% of the Escitalopram concentration, respectively. The elimination half-life after multiple dosing is about 30 hours and the oral plasma clearance is about 0.60 L/min. Escitalopram and major metabolites are – like racemic citalopram – assumed to be eliminated by the hepatic (metabolic) and renal routes with the major part of the dose. Escitalopram should be withdrawn gradually to reduce the risk of withdrawal symptoms. Or as prescribed by the physician.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of panic disorder with or without agoraphobia, initial doses are 5 mg once daily, increased after a week to 10 mg once daily; further increases up to a maximum of 20 mg daily may be necessary in some patients.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:50:37.367331+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4827,Finasteride,FINFLOW-5,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lvHfjySfLxUhkP_4ufrpnK2qbI-4Jl-r/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4827_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1lvHfjySfLxUhkP_4ufrpnK2qbI-4Jl-r_view_usp_drivesdk_f717f8f080.pdf,page_text/DRP-4827_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1lvHfjySfLxUhkP_4ufrpnK2qbI-4Jl-r_view_usp_drivesdk_f717f8f080.json,ac45e3b46946a121425ace20e653579a6bfbf891d7e3f0f071223afbba038696,480751,1,digital_text,"In clinical studies of patients with moderate to severe symptoms of BPH, an enlarged prostate on digital rectal examination and low residual urinary volumes, finasteride reduced the incidence of acute retention of urine from 7/100 to 3/100 over four years and the need for surgery (TURP or prostatectomy) from 10/100 to 5/100. These reductions were associated with a 2-point improvement in QUASI-AUA symptom score (range 0-34), a sustained regression in prostate volume of approximately 20% and a sustained increase in urinary flow rate. After an oral dose of 14C-finasteride in man, 39% of the dose was excreted in the urine in the form of metabolites (virtually no unchanged drug was excreted in the urine), and 57% of total dose was excreted in the faeces. Two metabolites have been identified which possess only a small fraction of the Type II 5 α-reductase activity of finasteride. In the elderly, the elimination rate of finasteride is somewhat decreased. Half-life is prolonged from a mean half-life of approximately six hours in men aged 18-60 years to eight hours in men aged more than 70 years. This is of no clinical significance and does not warrant a reduction in dosage. White colour round biconvex film-coated tablet.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Benign prostatic hyperplasia: Given orally in a dose of 5 mg daily (response may be delayed and treatment may be required for 6 months or more to assess whether benefit has been achieved). ● Sexual difficulties (less sexual desire or ability to get an erection);,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:50:40.401258+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4840,Potassium Citrate,Kaitrate,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Db1WfSMJhOVr4knhR1UTweah48Y4wl2N/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4840_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Db1WfSMJhOVr4knhR1UTweah48Y4wl2N_view_usp_drivesdk_7ee1c3d4c2.pdf,page_text/DRP-4840_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Db1WfSMJhOVr4knhR1UTweah48Y4wl2N_view_usp_drivesdk_7ee1c3d4c2.json,0291433aa1202e3f8b1b719fb9634fcca1fbb9ec12bedc904aa3ca21bee5625d,1445033,1,digital_text,White to off white colour elongated biconvex extended-release tablets having scored on one side.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Potassium Citrate is indicated for the management of renal tubular acidosis (RTA) with calcium stones, hypocitraturic calcium oxalate nephrolithiasis of any etiology, and uric acid lithiasis with or without calcium stones.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:51:33.275766+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4840-02,Potassium Citrate,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ork6Cbrxy307kFDvzS44QqnrReSyLLuw/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4840-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ork6Cbrxy307kFDvzS44QqnrReSyLLuw_view_usp_drivesdk_ebcba81ed0.pdf,page_text/DRP-4840-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ork6Cbrxy307kFDvzS44QqnrReSyLLuw_view_usp_drivesdk_ebcba81ed0.json,41431d8ab1e4c20e6c251fb26d07f7ad813b827e350e1792a8c04a6e0e46422f,802997,1,digital_text,,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"When Potassium Citrate is used to alkalinize the urine, urinary citrate and urinary pH values are important. In the setting of normal renal function, the rise in urinary citrate following a single dose of extended-release Potassium Citrate begins by the first hour and lasts for 12 hours.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T15:50:43.518682+00:00
