PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4853-06,Acetylcysteine,Mucocetyl,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/17e5PFyk6SJ4Kkv51eByZugYs3dbDnv7Z/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4853-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17e5PFyk6SJ4Kkv51eByZugYs3dbDnv7Z_view_usp_drivesdk_e8873ef2c4.pdf,page_text/DRP-4853-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17e5PFyk6SJ4Kkv51eByZugYs3dbDnv7Z_view_usp_drivesdk_e8873ef2c4.json,d58d66e0894fb097b6aae251118cbf8d391c63b0544363c5f677762b0837797a,1478535,1,digital_text,"Furthermore, Acetylcysteine exerts a direct antioxidant action, having a free thiol (-SH) nucleophilic group that is able to interact directly with electrophilic groups of oxidant radicals. Of particular interest is the recent finding that acetylcysteine protects α1-antitrypsin enzyme inhibiting elastase from inactivation by hypochlorous acid (HOCl), a powerful oxidant agent produced by the myeloperoxidase enzyme of activated phagocytes. Due to its molecular structure, Acetylcysteine can readily cross cell membranes. Inside the cell, NAC is deacetylated to L-cysteine, an amino acid essential for glutathione synthesis (GSH). Generalized urticaria has been observed rarely in patients receiving Acetylcysteine for acetaminophen overdose. If this occurs or other allergic symptoms appear, treatment with a Acetylcysteine should be discontinued unless it is deemed essential and the allergic symptoms can be otherwise controlled. Foods, Drugs, Devices, and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription. Hypersensitivity to Acetylcysteine or any component of the formulation.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"There is insufficient information on the excretion of Acetylcysteine in human milk. A risk to the newborns/infants cannot be excluded. These features make Acetylcysteine 200 mg Powder for Oral Solution particularly suitable for the treatment of acute and chronic infections of the respiratory system, characterised by thick, viscous mucous and mucopurulent secretions. There is no evidence on the efficacy and safety of mucolytics including Acetylcysteine in acute bronchitis.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:51:45.655274+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4853-07,Acetylcysteine,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1TIG9Lee7q2KNsJ_oNZqTxW9fMbMMos_e/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4853-07_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1TIG9Lee7q2KNsJ_oNZqTxW9fMbMMos_e_view_usp_drivesdk_e3e13e17ad.pdf,page_text/DRP-4853-07_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1TIG9Lee7q2KNsJ_oNZqTxW9fMbMMos_e_view_usp_drivesdk_e3e13e17ad.json,99a3bf26d5d2d4c9d936ac283a88633a76f8de0c60a7c1061af18cd8c654b21d,1422072,1,digital_text,Mixture of Light and Dark Orange Granular Powder with Pungent odour.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Used for its mucolytic activity in respiratory disorders associated with productive cough and in the management of Paracetamol overdosage.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:51:48.916993+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4853-08,Acetylcysteine,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NMWqjt3fS59WsDkdvTcETGZYXldVs5b5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4853-08_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1NMWqjt3fS59WsDkdvTcETGZYXldVs5b5_view_usp_drivesdk_71761b2168.pdf,page_text/DRP-4853-08_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1NMWqjt3fS59WsDkdvTcETGZYXldVs5b5_view_usp_drivesdk_71761b2168.json,7aea7e7810dd1579527192eaedc1ec6d2d29a1674c340a75dd1349c1a763edf2,430200,1,digital_text,"N-acetyl-L-cysteine (NAC), the active ingredient in Acetylcysteine 200 mg Powder for Oral Solution exerts an intense mucolytic-fluidizing action on mucous and mucopurulent secretions by depolymerizing the mucoproteic complexes and the nucleic acids which confer viscosity to the vitreous and purulent component of the sputum and other secretions. GSH is a highly reactive tripeptide found ubiquitously in the various tissues of animals and is essential for the maintenance of functional capacity as well as cellular morphological integrity. It is the most important protective intracellular mechanism against oxidant radicals, both exogenous and endogenous, as well as toward numerous cytotoxic substances. These features make Acetylcysteine 200 mg Powder for Oral Solution particularly suitable for the treatment of acute and chronic infections of the respiratory system, characterised by thick, viscous mucous and mucopurulent secretions. Mixture of light & dark orange granular powder with pungent odour.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T15:51:51.818253+00:00
