PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4879-07,Atorvastatin (as calcium),Atorschwartz 20,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/16XEgjhty0WwO1_hyiy79l24sM85pN5fM/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4879-07_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_16XEgjhty0WwO1_hyiy79l24sM85pN5fM_view_usp_drivesdk_3ab16cdc69.pdf,page_text/DRP-4879-07_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_16XEgjhty0WwO1_hyiy79l24sM85pN5fM_view_usp_drivesdk_3ab16cdc69.json,f30bf12f2c5d7747fe377b35e94b03d82c024463ea57e9690557bfa1dbeaf119,818088,1,digital_text,Reddish brown colored round shaped biconvex film-coated tablet plain on both side.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"It is used to reduce LDL-cholesterol, apolipoprotein B, and triglycerides, and to increase HDL-cholesterol in the treatment of hyperlipidemias, including hypercholesterolemias and combined (mixed) hyperlipidemia (type IIa or Iib hyperlipoproteinemias), hypertriglyceridemia (type IV) and dysbetalipoproteinemia (type III). It can also be effective as adjunctive therapy in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia who have some LDL-receptor function.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:57:23.618180+00:00
