PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4893,Vildagliptin + Metformin Hydrochloride,Galvusmet,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hlTL4GvwuVhf1G9fS3f3OdUkoMiR0Ul3/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4893_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hlTL4GvwuVhf1G9fS3f3OdUkoMiR0Ul3_view_usp_drivesdk_89a63335f8.pdf,page_text/DRP-4893_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hlTL4GvwuVhf1G9fS3f3OdUkoMiR0Ul3_view_usp_drivesdk_89a63335f8.json,3d320210cfec9dd44fda29034c15185b22e27092686bbdd21ff883ca15379382,309675,23,digital_text,"Pharmaceutical Forms • 50 mg/500 mg: light yellow, ovaloid beveled edge, film-coated tablet imprinted with ""NVR"" on one side and ""LLO"" on the other side. • 50 mg/850 mg: yellow, ovaloid beveled edge, film-coated tablet imprinted with ""NVR"" on one side and ""SEH"" on the other side. • 50 mg/1,000 mg: dark yellow, ovaloid beveled edge, film-coated tablet imprinted with ""NVR"" on one side and ""FLO"" on the other side. Certain dosage strengths and dosage forms may not be available in all countries Active substances Vildagliptin Metformin hydrochloride Three strengths are available. • 50 mg vildagliptin and 500 mg metformin hydrochloride. • 50 mg vildagliptin and 850 mg metformin hydrochloride. • 50 mg vildagliptin and 1 g metformin hydrochloride Active moieties Vildagliptin and metformin Excipients Hydroxypropyl cellulose, hypromellose, iron oxide yellow, iron oxide red, macrogol, magnesium stearate, talc and titanium dioxide. Pharmaceutical formulations may vary between countries. Vildagliptin + Metformin [Page 2]",1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,"Galvus Met® is indicated in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control: • as initial therapy when diabetes is not adequately controlled by diet and exercise alone • as therapy in patients inadequately controlled with metformin hydrochloride or vildagliptin alone or who are already treated with the combination of vildagliptin and metformin hydrochloride, as separate tablets • as combination therapy- in combination with other medicinal products for the treatment of diabetes, including insulin, when these do not provide adequate glycemic control (see sections",2,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:57:43.349587+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4893-01,Vildagliptin + Metformin Hydrochloride,Proglin Met,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yhUUQFJp5a0o-c8uv-kXarggIj8jnaCy/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4893-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1yhUUQFJp5a0o-c8uv-kXarggIj8jnaCy_view_usp_drivesdk_1c1d007e52.pdf,page_text/DRP-4893-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1yhUUQFJp5a0o-c8uv-kXarggIj8jnaCy_view_usp_drivesdk_1c1d007e52.json,114ce19b0b8b8d7248eb979eba56883305f388e0dbb25fd0c509f38fdac7b2ed,1941721,2,digital_text,"Pharmaceutical Forms • 50 mg/500 mg: light yellow, ovaloid beveled-edged, film-coated tablet imprinted with “NVR” on one side and “LLO” on the other side • 50 mg/850 mg: yellow, ovaloid beveled-edged, film-coated tablet imprinted with “NVR” on one side and “SEH” on the other side • 50 mg/1,000 mg: dark yellow, ovaloid beveled-edged, film-coated tablet imprinted with “NVR” on one side and “FLO” on the other side Certain dosage strengths and dosage forms may not be available in all countries. Active substances Vildagliptin Metformin hydrochloride Three strengths are available. One tablet of vildagliptin + metformin (ProglinMet®) contains: • 50 mg vildagliptin and 500 mg metformin hydrochloride. • 50 mg vildagliptin and 850 mg metformin hydrochloride. • 50 mg vildagliptin and 1 g metformin hydrochloride. Active moieties Vildagliptin and metformin Excipients Hydroxypropyl cellulose, hypromellose, iron oxide yellow, iron oxide red, macrogol, magnesium stearate, talc and titanium dioxide",1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,"ProglinMet® is indicated in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control: • as initial therapy when diabetes is not adequately controlled by diet and exercise alone • as therapy in patients inadequately controlled with metformin hydrochloride or vildagliptin alone or who are already treated with the combination of vildagliptin and metformin hydrochloride, as separate tablets • as combination therapy - in combination with other medicinal products for the treatment of diabetes, including insulin, when these do not provide adequate glycemic control (see sections",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:57:39.158231+00:00
