PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4916,Ceftazidime (As Pentahydrate),Cefwide,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/12oVkzQCcXHqdcP3kdAunQeh_DulZpcVB/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4916_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_12oVkzQCcXHqdcP3kdAunQeh_DulZpcVB_view_usp_drivesdk_4d0afa6393.pdf,page_text/DRP-4916_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_12oVkzQCcXHqdcP3kdAunQeh_DulZpcVB_view_usp_drivesdk_4d0afa6393.json,385c1a4b6b6e973777dc0c276d21472ceeddad9c8990e81322407ba8c05ff6cd,458725,1,digital_text,White crystalline powder.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of suspected or documented susceptible P. aeruginosa infections, and infections due to other susceptible aerobic Gram-negative organisms. It is used as an empiric therapy of febrile granulocytopenic patients usually in combination with antipseudomonal/aminoglycosides.",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:58:53.442590+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4916,Ceftazidime (As Pentahydrate),Cefwide,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yYQP0jkkDFYHrkcvF9PuPjvbTfTaw6vi/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4916_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1yYQP0jkkDFYHrkcvF9PuPjvbTfTaw6vi_view_usp_drivesdk_cf24e5e03c.pdf,page_text/DRP-4916_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1yYQP0jkkDFYHrkcvF9PuPjvbTfTaw6vi_view_usp_drivesdk_cf24e5e03c.json,385c1a4b6b6e973777dc0c276d21472ceeddad9c8990e81322407ba8c05ff6cd,458725,1,digital_text,White crystalline powder.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of suspected or documented susceptible P. aeruginosa infections, and infections due to other susceptible aerobic Gram-negative organisms. It is used as an empiric therapy of febrile granulocytopenic patients usually in combination with antipseudomonal/aminoglycosides.",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:58:57.002903+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4921-02,Sertraline (As Hydrochloride),Sertragen,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xNkXG9eUYP8XYXGr9yNireWVf6MIFtcM/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4921-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xNkXG9eUYP8XYXGr9yNireWVf6MIFtcM_view_usp_drivesdk_cb882c9a62.pdf,page_text/DRP-4921-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xNkXG9eUYP8XYXGr9yNireWVf6MIFtcM_view_usp_drivesdk_cb882c9a62.json,22f8c2e0830c9ec10e6db5dd1f038637ce62ea10ffee07fb7efd551463c583cf,574539,1,digital_text,"Liver disease– The administration of sertraline is delayed in patients with impaired liver function. Dosages should be reduced. Or as prescribed by the physician. The minimum effective dose in OCD is also 50 mg daily and increases above 100 mg daily did not have any additional benefit. Full activity is usually seen after 2-4 weeks and even longer in OCD. Effect may however be seen within 7 days. Panic Disorder The mechanism of action of sertraline is presumed to be linked to the inhibition of central nervous system neuronal uptake of serotonin (5HT). Sertraline blocks the reuptake of serotonin into human platelets. Sertraline is a specific inhibitor of neuronal serotonin reuptake and has only very weak effects on the norepinephrine and dopamine neuronal reuptake. Panic disorder: Sertraline exhibits dose proportional pharmacokinetics over the range 50 mg to 200 mg. After oral administration over the range of 50 mg to 200 mg once daily for 14 days, mean peak blood levels are reached at 4.5 - 8.4 hours post dose. The average terminal plasma half-life is about 26 hours. Steady- state plasma levels are reached after approximately one week of once daily dosing. Approximately 98% of the circulating drug is bound to plasma proteins. Consistent with the terminal elimination half-life, there is approximately two- fold accumulation with repeated dosing as compared to a single dose. Sertraline undergoes extensive first pass hepatic metabolism. Both in vitro biochemical and in vivo pharmacological testing have shown the principal metabolite, N-desmethylsertraline, to have significantly less clinical activity. Both Sertraline and N- desmethylsertraline are extensively metabolized with only a small amount <0.2% of unchanged sertraline excreted in the urine. About 40-45% of the dose administered radioactively was recovered in the urine and a similar amount in the feces, including 12-14% unchanged sertraline. The terminal elimination half-life of N-desmethylsertraline is approximately 62 to 104 hours. Desmethylsertraline exhibits time related dose dependent increases in AUC, C , and C with a 5 to 9 max min fold increase in their parameters between day 1 and day 14. Sertraline should be given as a single daily dose with or without food.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Panic disorder is characterized by the occurrence of unexpected panic attacks and associated concern about having additional attacks, worry about the implications or consequences of the attacks, and/or a significant change in behavior related to the attacks. The starting dose is 50 mg daily and the usual therapeutic dose in depression is 50 mg daily. In difficult to treat patients, the dose may be titrated up in 50 mg increments at 2 weekly intervals, to 150 mg - 200 mg. It is devoid of stimulant, sedative or anticholinergic activity or cardiotoxicity in animals.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:59:00.123103+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4929,Itraconazole,Itrason,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1l8g_ZNW4w7E3SGR7JJ7O-mztU-eluN_e/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4929_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1l8g_ZNW4w7E3SGR7JJ7O-mztU-eluN_e_view_usp_drivesdk_ef1694ac10.pdf,page_text/DRP-4929_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1l8g_ZNW4w7E3SGR7JJ7O-mztU-eluN_e_view_usp_drivesdk_ef1694ac10.json,efbb8e0fef23d53b819272bac6d84dc19b8638421bb4f81d853358d83090a054,4668583,1,ocr,"used when prescribing Itraconazole (Itrason) to patients with hypersensitivity to other azoles. 0"" size capsule with dark blue cap and white body, containing white to off-white spherical tablets.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Foods, Drugs, Devices, and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription For the treatment of oropharyngeal and vulvovaginal candidiasis, for pityriasis versicolor, for dermatophytoses unresponsive to topical treatment, for onychomycosis; for fstemic infections including asperg llosis, blastomycosis, candidiasis, For suspected adverse drug reaction, repart to the FDA: www fda.gov ph. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of chromoblastamycasis, coccidioidomycosis, cryptococcosis, h P osis, par ycasis, and sporotrichosis any adverse drug reaction",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T15:59:24.529683+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4929-01,Itraconazole,Itranaz,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1EjTnYJbheYWyfnRZCj5s_TSYWKpCxzhw/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4929-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1EjTnYJbheYWyfnRZCj5s_TSYWKpCxzhw_view_usp_drivesdk_f09f0c1cd2.pdf,page_text/DRP-4929-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1EjTnYJbheYWyfnRZCj5s_TSYWKpCxzhw_view_usp_drivesdk_f09f0c1cd2.json,b7b1726beaa6770bf12b18c1b99d90c9928deeb141399896fb98164f8cc78a33,459878,1,digital_text,"“0” size capsule with dark blue cap and white body, containing white to off-white spherical tablets. CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of oropharyngeal and vulvovaginal candidiasis, for pityriasis versicolor, for dermatophytoses unresponsive to topical treatment, for onychomycosis; for systemic infections including aspergillosis, blastomycosis, candidiasis, chromoblastomycosis, coccidioidomycosis, cryptococcosis, histoplasmosis, paracoccidioidomycosis, and sporotrichosis.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:59:03.154501+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-493-02,Aluminum Hydroxide + Magnesium Hydroxide,Neutracid,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Pz0EvM0d-adS7rXE7BdaTH3gIQQVhCPl/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-493-02_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Pz0EvM0d-adS7rXE7BdaTH3gIQQVhCPl_view_usp_drivesdk_7339688b60.pdf,page_text/DRP-493-02_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Pz0EvM0d-adS7rXE7BdaTH3gIQQVhCPl_view_usp_drivesdk_7339688b60.json,2cd880eb1d47051f9c9f97d2c2d62dbe7d3d61e9c1c2a9bb2426c22e3f0ff2f2,187938,1,digital_text,,,,,"Symptomatic relief of hyperacidity associated with the diagnosis of peptic ulcer, gastritis, peptic esophagitis and gastric hyperacidity and heartburn. PRECAUTION Do not use in patients taking a prescription antibiotic drug containing any form of tetracycline. Avoid taking prepa- ration containing antacids in the first trimester of pregnancy. Excessive doses or even normal doses in patients with low phosphate diets may lead to phosphate depletion, accompanied by increased absorption and urinary excretion of calcium with risk of osteomalacia.",1,1,INDICATION,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T15:59:27.830586+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4930,Tamsulosin Hydrochloride,Prostalife,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uS5gVAJC2NyBgIzold4IllwptBvyBBNF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4930_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uS5gVAJC2NyBgIzold4IllwptBvyBBNF_view_usp_drivesdk_bf0f848b7a.pdf,page_text/DRP-4930_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uS5gVAJC2NyBgIzold4IllwptBvyBBNF_view_usp_drivesdk_bf0f848b7a.json,8e607b436b764c6d4460183ff060c968a1f8b4ecdc0e10adc894ae8564160e43,485434,1,digital_text,"Red/white gelatin capsule size “2” containing white to off white pellets. Tamsulosin, an alpha-1 adrenoceptor blocking agent, exhibits selectivity for alpha-1 receptors in the human prostate. At least three discrete alpha-1 adrenoceptor subtypes have been identified: Alpha, alpha1B and alpha1D; their distribution differs between human organs and tissue. Approximately 70% of the alpha-1 receptors in human prostate are of the Alpha subtype. (In modified-release form) Tamsulosin Hydrochloride capsules are not intended for use as an antihypersensitive drug. The pharmacokinetics of Tamsulosin Hydrochloride have been evaluated in healthy adults volunteers and in patients with BPH after single and/or multiple administration with doses ranging from 0.1 mg to 1 mg. Absorption:",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Tamsulosin Hydrochloride capsules are contraindicated in patients known to be hypersensitive to Tamsulosin Hydrochloride or any 1011/09/R/PHIL/002-30/05/2022 component of capsules. Or as prescribed by the physician.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T15:59:31.207716+00:00
