PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4947-06,Piperacillin (as sodium) + Tazobactam (as sodium),Piptazonav 2.25,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ezF2sKYI5G7MevRb5xgLFz71Tg_h4byF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4947-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ezF2sKYI5G7MevRb5xgLFz71Tg_h4byF_view_usp_drivesdk_dc19506884.pdf,page_text/DRP-4947-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ezF2sKYI5G7MevRb5xgLFz71Tg_h4byF_view_usp_drivesdk_dc19506884.json,8d510ca86efe732a3fd8e21664990d0045ca8b25561d04054ef50cd83f3f08ad,505895,1,digital_text,"Mechanism of action A white to off white coloured powder. Piperacillin, a broad-spectrum, semisynthetic penicillin exerts bactericidal activity by inhibition of both septum and cell-wall synthesis. Pharmacokinetic / Pharmacodynamic relationship Dissolve the contents of a vial in 10 mL Sterile Water for Injection USP. The reconstituted solution should be used immediately after preparation and discard the unused remaining portion. It should not be allowed to freeze. Renal Insufficiency: In patients with renal insufficiency (creatinine clearance <40 mL/min), the intravenous dose of Piperacillin/Tazobactam should be adjusted to the degree of actual renal function impairment. In patients with nosocomial pneumonia receiving concomitant aminoglycoside therapy, the aminoglycoside dosage should be adjusted according to the recommendation of the manufacturer.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Adults: Piperacillin/Tazobactam should be administered by intravenous infusion over 30 minutes. Or as prescribed by the physician.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T16:01:38.359918+00:00
