PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4948-01,Piperacillin (as sodium) + Tazobactam (as sodium),Tazur,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1pLgXANJcS-hGU8GJS9pXvslR_JYwQzrt/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4948-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1pLgXANJcS-hGU8GJS9pXvslR_JYwQzrt_view_usp_drivesdk_476b722b83.pdf,page_text/DRP-4948-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1pLgXANJcS-hGU8GJS9pXvslR_JYwQzrt_view_usp_drivesdk_476b722b83.json,806dbbe58d681d934a19aa33934bd44cb04b00eb2cb342b49debd853ff500286,534075,1,digital_text,"A white to off white coloured powder. • Alteration of penicillin-binding proteins (PBPs), which results in the reduction of the affinity of Piperacillin for the molecular target in bacteria.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Piperacillin, a broad-spectrum, semisynthetic penicillin exerts bactericidal activity by inhibition of both septum and cell-wall synthesis. Pediatrics: The two main mechanisms of resistance to Piperacillin/Tazobactam are:",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T16:01:49.374735+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-4948-02,Piperacillin (As Sodium) + Tazobactam (As Sodium),Pipercil-4.5,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DGEe_uPd6EjXH5ctW6usCphg-dQrzAns/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-4948-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1DGEe_uPd6EjXH5ctW6usCphg-dQrzAns_view_usp_drivesdk_c793793061.pdf,page_text/DRP-4948-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1DGEe_uPd6EjXH5ctW6usCphg-dQrzAns_view_usp_drivesdk_c793793061.json,7e5daff39586dce7530e92865de30f93c8f92e19990195421ad14ff4e7e95302,1951373,1,digital_text,"White to off white powder, highly hygroscopic. PIPERCIL-4.5 4 g/500 mg Powder for Injection (I.M/I.V) PIPERACILLIN SODIUM + TAZOBACTAM SODIUM",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of serious bacterial infections caused by susceptible strains of beta-lactamase producing organisms in the following conditions: Lower respiratory tract infections; complicated and uncomplicated urinary tract infections; intra-abdominal infections; skin and skin structure infections; bacterial septicemia; gynaecological infections. Infection/IndicationAge of pediatric patients Recommended Dosage 2 months and 9 months of age 9 months or older weighing up to 40 kg Weighing over 40 kg 80 mg Piperacillin/10 mg Tazobactam per kg q 8 hr 100 mg Piperacillin/12.5 mg Tazobactam per kg q 8 hr 3.375 gm Piperacillin / Tazobactam (PIPERCIL-4.5) q 6 hr (16.0 gm Piperacillin/2.0 gm Tazobactam per day) + aminoglycoside 4.5 gm Piperacillin / Tazobactam (PIPERCIL-4.5) q 6 hr (16.0 gm Piperacillin/2.0 gm Tazobactam) ________________ ________________ ________________ ________________ ________________________________ Community-acquired pneumonia, Intra-abdominal infections (appendicitis and/ or peritonitis), Uncomplicated and complicated skin and skin structure infections, pelvic inflammatory disease For patients on haemodialysis, the maximum dose is 2.25 g every twelve hours for all indications other than nosocomial pneumonia and 2.25 g every eight hours for nosocomial pneumonia. Since haemodialysis removes 30% to 40% of the administered dose, an additional dose of 0.75 g Piperacillin/Tazobactam (PIPERCIL-4.5) should be administered following each dialysis period on haemodialysis days. No additional dosage of Piperacillin/Tazobactam (PIPERCIL-4.5) is necessary for CAPD patients. Pediatrics: There are no dosage recommendation for Piperacillin/Tazobactam in pediatric patients with impaired renal function.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T16:01:53.331849+00:00
