PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5025-31,Omeprazole (as Sodium),Omexac-40,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N99ElrvZKhwbi2KHV5RFZoyVFdLkOyfj/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5025-31_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1N99ElrvZKhwbi2KHV5RFZoyVFdLkOyfj_view_usp_drivesdk_5adee08a58.pdf,page_text/DRP-5025-31_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1N99ElrvZKhwbi2KHV5RFZoyVFdLkOyfj_view_usp_drivesdk_5adee08a58.json,4c5dfce4d141608a77f28d8f7583cc7f3aac9714dc376bdd5bc7d135c5626f1f,487606,1,digital_text,"White powder. This effect is dose-related and leads to inhibition of both basal and stimulated acid secretion. Distribution The apparent volume of distribution in healthy subjects is approximately 0.3 L/kg body weight. Omeprazole is 97% plasma protein bound. Omeprazole is a proton pump inhibitor that belongs to a class of antisecretory compounds, the substituted benzimidazoles. It suppresses gastric acid secretion by specific inhibition of the H + K+ ATPase enzyme system at the secretory surface of the gastric parietal cell. Because this enzyme system is regarded as the acid (proton) pump within the gastric mucosa, Omeprazole has been characterized as a gastric acid-pump inhibitor, in that it blocks the final step of acid production. Elimination Hepatic impairment The metabolism of Omeprazole in patients with liver dysfunction is impaired, resulting in an increased AUC. Omeprazole has not shown any tendency to accumulate with once-daily dosing. Renal impairment Special populations The pharmacokinetics of Omeprazole, including systemic bioavailability and elimination rate, are unchanged in patients with reduced renal function. Older people The metabolism rate of Omeprazole is somewhat reduced in elderly subjects (75 to 79 years of age).",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T16:05:49.977001+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5025-32,Omeprazole (as Sodium),Omeproviv,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1R9ZKiBatdK4vI-h-HHNQm_nglRPz4T8x/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5025-32_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1R9ZKiBatdK4vI-h-HHNQm_nglRPz4T8x_view_usp_drivesdk_26b74f2151.pdf,page_text/DRP-5025-32_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1R9ZKiBatdK4vI-h-HHNQm_nglRPz4T8x_view_usp_drivesdk_26b74f2151.json,f832bae9430260f9b068208a28506673cc04182b488d64a4c56090fa641afbfa,450766,1,digital_text,Each vial contains: equivalent to Omeprazole ...... 40 mg Each ampoule contains: Sterile Water for Injection BP .. 10 mL (diluent) White powder.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Omeprazole Sodium is excreted in human milk. In rats, Omeprazole Sodium has been shown to be excreted in milk at low concentrations. Decision should be made whether to discontinue Omeprazole Sodium or breastfeeding since Omeprazole Sodium may cause potential serious adverse effects to the baby. Gastritis has been reported occasionally in gastric corpus biopsies from patients on long-term Omeprazole therapy. Before giving Omeprazole Sodium or other proton pump inhibitors to patients with gastric ulcers, the possibility of malignancy should be considered since these drugs may mask symptoms and delay diagnosis. Omeprazole Sodium and other proton pump inhibitors should be used with caution in hepatic impairment. Gastric malignancy should be excluded at initiation of treatment and at follow-up of gastric ulcer therapy. Severe peptic ulcer bleeding initial intravenous infusion of 80 mg then by continuous intravenous infusion, 8 mg/hr for 72 hours (then change to oral therapy). Administration: Omeprazole Sodium 40 mg I.V. injection should only be administered intravenously. It should not be given by any other route. Benign gastric ulcer, duodenal ulcer and gastroesophageal reflux, 40 mg once daily until oral administration is possible. Injection: For I.V. injection, each single dose vial containing lyophilized powder for Omeprazole Sodium 40 mg should be reconstituted with 10 mL of Sterile Water for Injection. The resulting concentration is 4 mg/mL of Omeprazole Sodium which should be given slowly (over a period of 5 minutes) as an intravenous injection.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T16:05:52.980862+00:00
