PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5095-03,Losartan Potassium,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Dxr9f5Ve69jy6prOFaRQVZ0FLw-jO70R/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5095-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Dxr9f5Ve69jy6prOFaRQVZ0FLw-jO70R_view_usp_drivesdk_0df7ea9a56.pdf,page_text/DRP-5095-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Dxr9f5Ve69jy6prOFaRQVZ0FLw-jO70R_view_usp_drivesdk_0df7ea9a56.json,5e37e5851f538ac773e6c964f23d37a5551cd147c90383651cc02c473212e2bf,151310,1,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T16:09:35.796501+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5095-04,Losartan Potassium,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WQ_zMFJenwSDAeKr3HK-JSD4wekcnpiD/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5095-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WQ_zMFJenwSDAeKr3HK-JSD4wekcnpiD_view_usp_drivesdk_672bc1f7e9.pdf,page_text/DRP-5095-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WQ_zMFJenwSDAeKr3HK-JSD4wekcnpiD_view_usp_drivesdk_672bc1f7e9.json,8cfe7eede4e7b217b19b55914c0a9c15cb5b4e658174ef9977039bcb04ef6d37,99606,1,digital_text,"Losartan Potassium 50mg and 100mg are white to off-white, egg-shaped biconvex film-coated tablets, plain on both sides. Losartan Potassium is an angiotensin ll receptor blocker acting on the AT1 receptor subtype. It is a non-peptide molecule chemically described as 2-butyl-4chloro-1-[p-(o-1Htetra- zol-5-ylphenyl)benzyl] -imidazole-5-methanol monopotas- sium salt. It contains NLT 98.5% and NMT 101.0% of losartan potassium (C22H22CIKN60), calculated on the anhydrous, solvent-free basis. Losartan Potassium is a white to off-white-free-flowing crystalline powder with a molecular weight of 461.01. It is freely soluble in water, soluble in alcohols and slightly soluble in common organic solvents such as acetonitrile and methyl ethyl ketone. Oxidation of the 5-hydroxymethyl group on the imidazole ring results in the active metabolite of losartan.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"It is used in the treatment of hypertension, particularly in patients who develop cough with Angiotensin Converting Enzyme (ACE) inhibitors, to reduce the risk of stroke in patients with left ventricular hypertrophy and in the treatment of diabetic nephropathy. It has also been used in heart failure and in myocardial infarction.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T16:09:38.753883+00:00
