PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5122,Valsartan,Diovan,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N9U30aBIT_s4r24sLFAfScw8Enhcbg6D/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5122_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1N9U30aBIT_s4r24sLFAfScw8Enhcbg6D_view_usp_drivesdk_fbd3573e33.pdf,page_text/DRP-5122_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1N9U30aBIT_s4r24sLFAfScw8Enhcbg6D_view_usp_drivesdk_fbd3573e33.json,1abb9db07d7520f941c1b00ef5147999a94e24a41d61020936587fcdbd340a9b,161842,21,digital_text,"Film-coated tablet (FCT) Diovan 80 mg: Pale red, round with bevelled edges, scored on one side; with debossing “D/V” on the scored side and “NVR” on the other side Diovan 160 mg: Grey-orange, ovaloid, scored on one side; with debossing “DX/DX” on the scored side and “NVR” on the other side Diovan 320 mg: Dark grey-violet, ovaloid with bevelled edges with debossing “DXL” on one side and “NVR” on the other side. The score line on one side of Valsartan 80 mg, 160 mg or 320 mg FCT is only to facilitate breaking for ease of swallowing and not to divide into equal doses. Appearance of tablets may differ between countries. Certain dosage strengths and dosage forms may not be available in all countries. Active substance One tablet contains 80 mg, 160 mg or 320 mg valsartan. Excipients Tablets: Microcrystalline cellulose, crospovidone, colloidal anhydrous silica, magnesium stearate, hypromellose, titanium dioxide (E171), Macrogol 8000, red iron oxide (E172), yellow iron oxide (E172), black iron oxide (E172; 40 mg, 160 mg and 320 mg tablets only), brown iron oxide (mixture of r ed iron oxide and black iron oxide (320 mg tablets only). Pharmaceutical formulations may vary between countries. Valsartan [Page 2]",1,1,Pharmaceutical form,"Hypertension Treatment of hypertension in adults and in children and adolescents 6-18 years of age. Heart failure Treatment of heart failure (NYHA class II -IV) in patients receiving standard therapy such as diuretics, digitalis and either angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitors or beta-blockers but not both; presence of all these standard therapies is not mandatory. Valsartan (Diovan®) improves morbidity in these patients, primarily via reduction in hospitalization for heart failure. It also slows the progression of heart failure, improves NYHA functional class, ejection fraction and signs and symptoms of heart failure and improves quality of life versus placebo (see section CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY). Post-myocardial infarction Valsartan (Diovan®) is indicated to improve survival following myocardial infarction in clinically stable patients with signs, symptoms or r adiological evidence of left ventricular failure and/or with left ventricular systolic dysfunction (see section",2,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T16:11:21.510309+00:00
