PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5180,Valsartan + Hydrochlorothiazide,Co-Tareg,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J1g0yjDY9BkAW-cMFq5hhE7FfpAoD8ee/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5180_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1J1g0yjDY9BkAW-cMFq5hhE7FfpAoD8ee_view_usp_drivesdk_c1538e628e.pdf,page_text/DRP-5180_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1J1g0yjDY9BkAW-cMFq5hhE7FfpAoD8ee_view_usp_drivesdk_c1538e628e.json,8bcd4e26bc27393accc11222b9ee608ec479eb256bf2d61f2328cd7f465990a1,5131412,2,digital_text,"Film-coated Tablet. Valsartan/hydrochlorothiazide 80 mg/ 12.5 mg film-coated tablets: Film-coated tablet, light orange, ovaloid, slightly convex faces, imprinted (debossed) with “HGH” on one side and “CG” on the reverse side Valsartan/hydrochlorothiazide 160 mg/ 12.5 mg film-coated tablets: Film-coated tablet, dark red, ovaloid, slightly convex faces, imprinted (debossed) with “HHH” on one side and “CG” on the reverse side CLINICAL PARTICULARS Therapeutic indications Treatment of hypertension in adults, 18 years of age and older Valsartan/hydrochlorothiazide may be used for the treatment of hypertension in patients whose blood pressure is not adequately controlled by monotherapy. Valsartan/hydrochlorothiazide may be used as initial therapy in patients who are likely to need multiple drugs to achieve blood pressure goals. The choice of valsartan/hydrochlorothiazide as initial therapy for hypertension should be based on an assessment of potential benefits and risks. Dosage and method of administration Dosage The recommended dose of valsartan/hydrochlorothiazide is one film-coated tablet per day. When clinically appropriate either 80 mg valsartan and 12.5 mg hydrochlorothiazide or 160 mg valsartan and 12.5 mg hydrochlorothiazide or 320 mg valsartan and 12.5 mg hydrochlorothiazide may be used. When necessary 160 mg valsartan and 25 mg hydrochlorothiazide or 320 mg valsartan and 25 mg hydrochlorothiazide may be used. For initial therapy, the usual starting dose is valsartan/hydrochlorothi- azide 160/12.5 mg once daily. The dosage can be increased after 1 to 2 weeks of therapy to a maximum of one 320/25 mg tablet once daily as needed to control blood pressure. Valsartan/hydrochlorothiazide is not recommended as initial therapy in patients with intravascular volume depletion (see Special warnings and precautions for use). The maximum daily dose is 320 mg/25 mg. The maximum antihypertensive effect is seen within 2 to 4 weeks. Renal impairment No dosage adjustment is required for patients with mild to moderate renal impairment (Glomerular Filtration Rate (GFR) ≥ 30 mL/min). Due to the hydrochlorothiazide component, valsartan/hydrochlorothiazide is contraindicated in patients with anuria (see Contraindications) and should be used with caution in patients with severe renal impairment (GFR < 30 mL/min) (see Special warnings and precautions for use and Pharmacokinetic properties). Thiazide diuretics are ineffective as monotherapy in severe renal impairment (GFR < 30 mL/min) but may be useful in these patients, when used with due caution in combination with a loop diuretic even in patients with GFR < 30 mL/min. Hepatic impairment No dosage adjustment is required in patients with mild to moderate hepatic impairment. Due to the hydrochlorothiazide component, valsartan/hydrochlorothiazide should be used with particular caution in patients with severe hepatic impairment. Due to the valsartan component, valsartan/hydrochlorothiazide should be used with particular caution in patients with biliary obstructive disorders (see Special warnings and precautions for use). Pediatric patients (below 18 years) The safety and efficacy of valsartan/hydrochlorothiazide has not been established in children below the age of 18 years.",1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Treatment of hypertension in adults, 18 years of age and older Valsartan/hydrochlorothiazide may be used for the treatment of hypertension in patients whose blood pressure is not adequately controlled by monotherapy. Valsartan/hydrochlorothiazide may be used as initial therapy in patients who are likely to need multiple drugs to achieve blood pressure goals. The choice of valsartan/hydrochlorothiazide as initial therapy for hypertension should be based on an assessment of potential benefits and risks.",1,1,Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T16:13:47.690933+00:00
