PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5237-01,Tranexamic Acid,Actranex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ypj-aU4eXg-DEJtablMQmhQiVifUm-GD/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5237-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ypj-aU4eXg-DEJtablMQmhQiVifUm-GD_view_usp_drivesdk_001a691e15.pdf,page_text/DRP-5237-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ypj-aU4eXg-DEJtablMQmhQiVifUm-GD_view_usp_drivesdk_001a691e15.json,f0d146fa8b9eee9c29c3c045f4daf09922afb9c844e0d526d7fd2d97bbf0de3e,477143,1,digital_text,"Tranexamic acid exerts an antihaemorrhagic activity by inhibiting the fibrinolytic properties of plasmin. Each mL contains: The activity of the tranexamic acid-plasmin complex on the activity on fibrin is lower than the activity of free plasmin alone. Clear colorless solution. Pharmacotherapeutic group: Antihemorrhagics, Antifibrinolytics, Aminoacids. PHARMACODYNAMIC Acomplex involving tranexamic acid, plasminogen is constituted; the tranexamic acid being linked to plasminogen when transformed into plasmin. In vitro studies showed that high tranexamic dosages decreased the activity of complement. - continuous infusion of 10 mg/kg/h or injection into the CPB pump prime at a dose adapted on the CPB procedure, either according to patient weight with a 10 mg/kg dose, either according to CPB pump prime volume, It is used in the treatment and prophylaxis of haemorrhage associated with excessive fibrinolysis.It is also used in the prophylaxis of hereditary angioedema. - last injection of 10 mg/kg at the end of CPB.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Peak plasma concentrations of tranexamic acid are obtained rapidly after a short intravenous infusion after which plasma concentrations decline in a multi-exponential manner. - first bolus of 10 mg/kg after induction of anaesthesia and prior to skin incision, PHARMACOKINETIC",1,1,INDICATION,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T16:15:33.624127+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5244,Amoxicillin Trihydrate,Amorex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1h7N9mkAmUYUb3f39OeiadaOq0wiEoMI2/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5244_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1h7N9mkAmUYUb3f39OeiadaOq0wiEoMI2_view_usp_drivesdk_a8dce8c94b.pdf,page_text/DRP-5244_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1h7N9mkAmUYUb3f39OeiadaOq0wiEoMI2_view_usp_drivesdk_a8dce8c94b.json,6ee706fcfb9b9de7569dc37d12cf2c4e95744dd30405da1657ca0d1a8923ae56,502481,1,digital_text,"500 mg Capsule - Creamy to yellowish white powder in scarlet cap / white body EGC in size 0 250 mg Capsule - Yellowish white powder in scarlet cap / white body in EGC #1 250 mg / 5 mL Powder for Suspension - Yellowish white powder, yellow suspension with tutti frutti flavor 125 mg / 5 mL Powder for Suspension - White to yellowish white powder, yellow suspension with tutti frutti flavor 100 mg / mL Powder for Suspension (Oral Drops) - White to creamy white powder, white suspension with tutti frutti flavor",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for the treatment of genitourinary, respiratory and gastrointestinal tract infections due to susceptible strains of Gram-negative bacteria including Salmonella typhosa and other Salmonella, E. coli, H. influenzae, N. gonorrhea, N. meningitis, Proteus mirabilis, Klebsiella (Aerobacter). Also indicated in infections due to susceptible Gram-positive bacteria such as Streptococcus and Diplococcus and the non-penicillinase producing Staphylococci. Reports of miscellaneous infections treated successfully have included bacterial endocarditis (due to Streptococcus viridans, S. fecales, H. influenzae or D. pneumoniae) and Gram-negative Septicemia (due to E. Coli, Proteus and Aerobacter). Since AMOXICILLIN is a bactericidal antibiotic with a wide spectrum of activity, it may be used as an empiric antimicrobial until the results of in vitro sensitivity tests have been obtained.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T16:15:36.570327+00:00
