PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5247,Clonidine Hydrochloride,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qZED9UNNuuwvKUklHHmf8mFwE3CwIZ7t/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5247_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qZED9UNNuuwvKUklHHmf8mFwE3CwIZ7t_view_usp_drivesdk_e68a041a04.pdf,page_text/DRP-5247_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qZED9UNNuuwvKUklHHmf8mFwE3CwIZ7t_view_usp_drivesdk_e68a041a04.json,5806dbbe0deb0dec3efa50faa98fd2c7e0d959c4cae0112b16a1dcb29b7bf686,422883,1,digital_text,"White, round, flat-tablet bisected on one side, size 6mm.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Clonidine is an imidazoline antihypertensive that appears to act centrally to reduce sympathetic tone, resulting in a fall in diastolic and systolic blood pressure and a reduction in heart rate. It also acts peripherally, and this peripheral activity may be responsible for the transient increase in blood pressure seen during rapid intravenous administration as well as contributing to the hypotensive effect during chronic administration. Peripheral resistance is reduced during continuous treatment. Clonidine is used in the management of hypertension, including hypertensive crises. It may be given in conjunction with a thiazide diuretic, but combination with a beta blocker should be avoided where possible. Clonidine has also been used in the prophylactic treatment of migraine or recurrent vascular headaches and in the treatment of menopausal flushing. It is also used in conjunction with opioids in the management of cancer pain and has been tried for various other forms of pain.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T16:15:45.418944+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5247-02,,,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/126mqyeIjAwVp7HxzOzPpxWXSdGV9gdua/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5247-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_126mqyeIjAwVp7HxzOzPpxWXSdGV9gdua_view_usp_drivesdk_bacbdce66e.pdf,page_text/DRP-5247-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_126mqyeIjAwVp7HxzOzPpxWXSdGV9gdua_view_usp_drivesdk_bacbdce66e.json,2c8f1e64b506b077b74957c1eeb8e0c15c2afa36cd5eea907fcd50f7b67f3836,185808,1,digital_text,"White, round, /f_lat-tablet bisected on one side, size 6mm.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Clonidine is an imidazoline antihypertensive that appears to act centrally to reduce sympathetic tone, resulting in a fall in diastolic and systolic blood pressure and a reduction in heart rate. It also acts peripherally, and this peripheral activity may be responsible for the transient increase in blood pressure seen during rapid intravenous administration as well as contributing to the hypotensive eﬀect during chronic administration. Peripheral resistance is reduced during continuous treatment. Clonidine is used in the management of hypertension, including hypertensive crises. It may be given in conjunction with a thiazide diuretic, but combination with a beta blocker should be avoided where possible. Clonidine has also been used in the prophylactic treatment of migraine or recurrent vascular headaches and in the treatment of menopausal /f_lushing. It is also used in conjunction with opioids in the management of cancer pain and has been tried for various other forms of pain.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T16:15:42.286615+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5248-04,Salbutamol (as sulfate),Aero-vent,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1YHgM7ka5o9LyVKrf--P58IRSLbugxyvy/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5248-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YHgM7ka5o9LyVKrf--P58IRSLbugxyvy_view_usp_drivesdk_b3b4d15aea.pdf,page_text/DRP-5248-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YHgM7ka5o9LyVKrf--P58IRSLbugxyvy_view_usp_drivesdk_b3b4d15aea.json,1698c3c308312f13357d9b799a2b3787b69ee25d43367eff40f96cab5dd9ed48,432698,1,digital_text,"Salbutamol (Aero-vent) 4 mg Tablet is a white, round flat tablet, scored on one side, size 8 mm. Salbutamol (Aero-vent) 2 mg Tablet is a white, round flat tablet, scored on one side, size 6 mm. Salbutamol (Aero-vent) 2 mg / 5 mL Syrup is a clear, orange syrup with orange flavor.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the relief of bronchospasm in bronchial asthma, chronic bronchitis and emphysema. Also indicated for the treatment or reversible bronchospasm associated with bronchitis, pulmonary emphysema, bronchiectasis and other obstructive pulmonary disease.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T16:15:48.678598+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-525,Ambroxol Hydrochloride,Amectuss,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GbOQZ69-bY6GXV8NnEC-d6CmFrqhjfTQ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-525_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GbOQZ69-bY6GXV8NnEC-d6CmFrqhjfTQ_view_usp_drivesdk_d8ec751d9b.pdf,page_text/DRP-525_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GbOQZ69-bY6GXV8NnEC-d6CmFrqhjfTQ_view_usp_drivesdk_d8ec751d9b.json,29002b50c33c5ff9749dc34abc746b2342d751db1b2f3428264a9f1a9fb65711,993464,1,digital_text,"• Ambroxol hydrochloride 15 mg / 5 mL Syrup (Amectuss) is a clear, light yellow, viscous lemon flavored syrup. • Ambroxol hydrochloride 30 mg / 5 mL Syrup (Amectuss) is a clear, light, yellow, , viscous cola flavored syrup. What is in the medicine? The medicine contains ambroxol hydrochloride which is a mucolytic agent and alters the structure of mucus to decrease its viscosity there by facilitating its removal by ciliary action or expectoration. Strength of the medicine Please see formulation. What is this medicine for? This medicine is used for the treatment of respiratory disorders associated with viscid mucus. How much and how often should you use this medicine? • Ambroxol hydrochloride 15 mg / 5 mL Syrup (Amectuss) Children 6 to 12 years old - 5 mL (1 teaspoonful) 2 to 3 times daily. Children 2 to 6 years old - 2.5 mL (1/2 teaspoon) 2 to 3 times daily. Children 1 to 2 years old - 2.5 mL (1/2 teaspoon) 2 times daily. •Ambroxol hydrochloride 30 mg / 5 mL Syrup (Amectuss) Children 6 to 12 years old - 5 mL (1 teaspoonful) 2 to 3 times daily. Children 2 to 6 years old - 2.5 mL (1/2 teaspoon) 2 to 3 times daily. Children 1 to 2 years old - 2.5 mL (1/2 teaspoon) 2 times daily. Or, as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? If you are allergic to ambroxol or any ingredient in the product. If you are pregnant or breastfeeding. Undesirable effects Rarely adverse gastrointestinal effects (nausea, abdominal pain) and allergic reactions (skin rash, facial swelling, severe respiration-impairment, temperature increase with fever) might be observed during treatment. What other medicines or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Please tell your doctor or pharmacist if you are taking/using or have recently taken/ used any other medicines, including medicines obtained without prescription. There are no clinically significant adverse interactions with other drugs. What should you do if you miss a dose? If you miss a dose just take the next prescribed dose at the usual time. Do not double the dose. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30ºC. Keep away from light. Keep bottle tightly closed. AMBROXOL Hydrochloride 15 mg / 5 mL Syrup 30 mg / 5 mL Syrup Mucolytic AMECTUSS Dimensions: 216mm x 93mm Signs and symptoms of over dosage No severe poisoning symptoms have been observed. Transient agitation and diarrhea may occur. In case of significant overdose, increased salivation may occur, as well as nausea, vomiting and hypotension. A doctor should be consulted. Usually immediate intervention such as induction of vomiting and gastric lavage is unnecessary; such management can be considered in case of acute overdose. Treatment dependent on the observed symptoms of overdosage is recommended. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dose? If you have taken more than the recommended dose, although no poisoining symptoms have been observed, consult a doctor right away. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine Do not take more than the recommended dose. Do not use after the expiry date of the label. Keep out of reach and sight of children. When should you consult a doctor? When undesirable effects occur, stop treatment and consult a doctor. Adverse Drug Reaction Reporting Statement: For suspected adverse drug reaction report to FDA: www.fda.gov.ph Availability - Ambroxol hydrochloride 15 mg / 5 mL Syrup (Amectuss) in bottles of 60 mL and 120 mL - Ambroxol hydrochloride 30 mg / 5 mL Syrup (Amectuss) in bottles of 60 mL and 120 mL Date revision of Patient Information Leaflet: 01 August 2017 Date of renewal of authorization : Ambroxol hydrochloride 15 mg / 5 mL Syrup (Amectuss) - 30 March 2016 Ambroxol hydrochloride 30 mg / 5 mL Syrup (Amectuss) - 03 February 2015 Manufactured by Am-Europharma Corporation Brgy. Saimsim, Calamba City, Laguna Distributed by",1,1,Product description,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T16:15:56.734677+00:00
