PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5343-01,Co-Amoxiclav,Wilgiclav,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/13uTMUuUkvfImdrTxvwxoxdDNcfjN3S3s/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5343-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13uTMUuUkvfImdrTxvwxoxdDNcfjN3S3s_view_usp_drivesdk_ee4f86c685.pdf,page_text/DRP-5343-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13uTMUuUkvfImdrTxvwxoxdDNcfjN3S3s_view_usp_drivesdk_ee4f86c685.json,f62d7ace7df79723e17f8f46db28475bb944ed477b892d80b9db0bf43860aeed,3116106,1,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T16:21:11.148233+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5345-01,MONTELUKAST (AS SODIUM),AEROKIDS,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1agLox51CX-DIWSEnHe4CboakvLf1oO0D/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5345-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1agLox51CX-DIWSEnHe4CboakvLf1oO0D_view_usp_drivesdk_1b8f5f96ac.pdf,page_text/DRP-5345-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1agLox51CX-DIWSEnHe4CboakvLf1oO0D_view_usp_drivesdk_1b8f5f96ac.json,91407126ede4a63e46ea7e889c0cf2c1b7fff938c3fea59de49d59d67a33fbab,4781922,2,ocr,"Chewable tablet | CLINICAL PARTICULARS Therapeutic Indications Montelukast is indicated in the treatment of asthma as add-on therapy in those 6 to 14 years old patients with mild to moderate persistent asthma who are inadequately controlled on inhaled corticosteroids and in whom “as-needed” short-acting B-agonists provide inadequate clinical control of asthma. Montelukast may also be an alternative treatment option to low-dose inhaled corticosteroids for 6 to 14 years old patients with mild persistent asthma who do not have a recent history of serious asthma attacks that required oral corticosteroid use, and who have demonstrated that they are not capable of using inhaled corticosteroids (see Dosage and administration). Montelukast is also indicated in the prophylaxis of asthma from 6 years of age and older in which the predominant component is exercise- induced bronchoconstriction Dosage and administration This medicinal product is to be given to a child under adult supervision. The dose for paediatric patients 6-14 years of age is one 5 mg chewable tablet daily to be taken in the evening. If taken in connection with food, montelukast should be taken 1 hour before or 2 hours after food. No dose adjustment within this age group is necessary. The montelukast 5 mg chewable tablet formulation is not recommended below 6 years of age. Method of administration For oral use. General recommendations The therapeutic effect of montelukast on parameters of asthma control occurs within one day. Patients should be advised to continue taking montelukast even if their asthma is under control, as well as during periods of worsening asthma. No dose adjustment is necessary for patients with renal insufficiency, or mild to moderate hepatic impairment. There are no data on patients with severe hepatic impairment. The dose is the same for both male and female patients. Montelukast as an alternative treatment option to low-dose inhaled corticosteroids for mild persistent asthma Montelukast is not recommended as monotherapy in patients with moderate persistent asthma. The use of montelukast as an alternative treatment option to low-dose inhaled corticosteroids for children with mild persistent asthma should only be considered for patients who do not have a recent history of serious asthma attacks that required oral corticosteroid use and who have demonstrated that they are not capable of using inhaled corticosteroids (see Therapeutic Indications). Mild persistent asthma is defined as asthma symptoms more than once a week but less than once a day, nocturnal symptoms more than twice a month but less than once a week, normal lung function between episodes. If satisfactory control of asthma is not achieved at follow-up (usually within one month), the need for an additional or different anti-inflammatory therapy based on the step system for asthma therapy should be evaluated. Patients should be periodically evaluated for their asthma control. Therapy with montelukast in relation to other treatments for asthma When treatment with montelukast is used as add-on therapy to inhaled corticosteroids, montelukast should not be abruptly substituted for inhaled corticosteroids (see Special warnings and precautions for use). 5 mg chewable tablets are available for paediatric patients 6 to 14 years of age.",1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Montelukast is indicated in the treatment of asthma as add-on therapy in those 6 to 14 years old patients with mild to moderate persistent asthma who are inadequately controlled on inhaled corticosteroids and in whom “as-needed” short-acting B-agonists provide inadequate clinical control of asthma. Montelukast may also be an alternative treatment option to low-dose inhaled corticosteroids for 6 to 14 years old patients with mild persistent asthma who do not have a recent history of serious asthma attacks that required oral corticosteroid use, and who have demonstrated that they are not capable of using inhaled corticosteroids (see Dosage and administration). Montelukast is also indicated in the prophylaxis of asthma from 6 years of age and older in which the predominant component is exercise- induced bronchoconstriction",1,1,Therapeutic Indications,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T16:21:37.820361+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5349,Finasteride,Finaplasia-1,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WAu2wmRJMvUw6inw5X2z-RG3IGczF_DG/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5349_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WAu2wmRJMvUw6inw5X2z-RG3IGczF_DG_view_usp_drivesdk_290266c14e.pdf,page_text/DRP-5349_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WAu2wmRJMvUw6inw5X2z-RG3IGczF_DG_view_usp_drivesdk_290266c14e.json,59f7d9b71a1eb5821050be7d8908f448b29b09b80132fe991daa54dc20c6920c,554172,1,digital_text,"A white, round, film-coated tablets, plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Finasteride 1 mg is indicated for treatment of the first stage of the hair loss (androgenetic alopecia) in males. Finasteride 1 mg stabilizes the process of the androgenetic alopecia in the 18-41 year old males. Its effectiveness in bitemporary recession nor in the loss of hair has not been determined. Finasteride is not indicated for use in women or children and adolescents.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T16:21:40.879044+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5357-01,Co-Amoxiclav,Geoxiclav,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/180hpNcptw3qwKPlDJvDGgKb5_hM9-zkJ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5357-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_180hpNcptw3qwKPlDJvDGgKb5_hM9-zkJ_view_usp_drivesdk_a1dd1d9968.pdf,page_text/DRP-5357-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_180hpNcptw3qwKPlDJvDGgKb5_hM9-zkJ_view_usp_drivesdk_a1dd1d9968.json,f2a19b0e32b9d9cbf05268ffddcc215fd8dac8d476913ba9a106698cd06ffa1f,446302,1,digital_text,White to off white oval shaped film-coated tablets having scoring on one side.,1,1,Product Description:,"Used for the treatment of urinary tract infections due to susceptible organisms; for otitis media or sinusitis due to resistant microorganism (e.g., H. influenzae, S. pneumoniae, M. catarrhalis); for lower respiratory tract and skin infections due to susceptible organism; and for polymicrobial infections with mixed aerobic and anaerobic such as diabetic foot, gynecologic infections and intra-abdominal infections.",1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T16:21:43.798353+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5357-01,Co-Amoxiclav,Geoxiclav,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N0vCuUdv2BUdWpYFd4blgAKGN3rZb595/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5357-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1N0vCuUdv2BUdWpYFd4blgAKGN3rZb595_view_usp_drivesdk_9ce1f1a65e.pdf,page_text/DRP-5357-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1N0vCuUdv2BUdWpYFd4blgAKGN3rZb595_view_usp_drivesdk_9ce1f1a65e.json,b4f74f9d7a05d20d895477e3b57b9cad97cb1a5d1d09ffc7603d234b0b922277,850622,1,ocr,White to off white oval shaped film-coated tablets having scoring on one side. by the physician. Use in Lactation:,1,1,Product Description:,"Alu/Alu Blister Pack x7's (Box of 14's) Used for the treatment of urinary tract infections due to susceptible organisms; for otitis media or sinusitis due to resistant microorganism (e.g., H. influenzae, S$. pneumoniae, M. catarrhalis); for lower respiratory tract and skin DRP-5357-01 infections due to susceptible organism; and for polymicrobial infections with mixed aerobic and anaerobic Date of First Authorization: June 2, 2015 such as diabetic foot, gynecologic infections and intra-abdominal infections. Date of Revision of Package Insert: March 20, 2024",1,1,Indications:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T16:21:55.032426+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5357-06,Co-Amoxiclav,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ojV7ZLkYNsiNN8zHK4PgrYa4MF4J9Z8G/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5357-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ojV7ZLkYNsiNN8zHK4PgrYa4MF4J9Z8G_view_usp_drivesdk_13b5db8ba8.pdf,page_text/DRP-5357-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ojV7ZLkYNsiNN8zHK4PgrYa4MF4J9Z8G_view_usp_drivesdk_13b5db8ba8.json,11cd6456789e3ad5ba2c354e14649ac374f82afbb15ce520dbc8b909eaefd8cd,2454765,1,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T16:22:00.873737+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5360,Sitagliptin + Metformin Hydrochloride,Janumet XR,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-ghh_yAOLhDKc016lIiC2TfzyGBBbbxL/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5360_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-ghh_yAOLhDKc016lIiC2TfzyGBBbbxL_view_usp_drivesdk_ce3dfc1bb3.pdf,page_text/DRP-5360_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-ghh_yAOLhDKc016lIiC2TfzyGBBbbxL_view_usp_drivesdk_ce3dfc1bb3.json,c7998497c06e0014bc3a2b7659e6973c99bcea0a72caa07fee0168e327bde7fd,331874,47,digital_text,"SITAGLIPTIN + METFORMIN HCl (JANUMET XR) contains sitagliptin phosphate and metformin hydrochloride. SITAGLIPTIN + METFORMIN HCl (JANUMET XR) tablets consist of sitagliptin and an extended-release formulation of metformin. Sitagliptin phosphate [Page 13] The chemical name of sitagliptin phosphate is 7 -[(3 R )-3-amino-1-oxo-4-(2,4,5- trifluorophenyl)butyl]-5,6,7,8-tetrahydro-3-(trifluoromethyl)-1,2,4-triazolo[4,3- a ]pyrazine phosphate (1:1) monohydrate. The empirical formula is C16H15F6N5O•H3PO4•H2O and the molecular weight is 523.32. The structural formula is: Sitagliptin phosphate monohydrate is a white to off -white, crystalline, non-hygroscopic powder. It is soluble in water and N,N-dimethyl formamide; slightly soluble in methanol; very slightly soluble in ethanol, acetone, and acetonitrile; and insoluble in isopropanol and isopropyl acetate. Metformin hydrochloride Metformin hydrochloride ( N , N -dimethylimidodicarbonimidic diamide hydrochloride) is not chemically or pharmacologically related to any other classes of oral antihyperglycemic agents. The structural formula is as shown: Metformin hydrochloride is a white to off-white crystalline compound with a molecular formula of C4H11N5•HCl and a molecular weight of 165.63. Metformin hydrochloride is freely soluble in water and is practically insoluble in acetone, ether and chloroform. The pKa of metformin is 12.4. The pH of a 1% aqueous solution of metformin hydrochloride is 6.68.",12,13,I I . PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"SITAGLIPTIN + METFORMIN HCl (JANUMET XR) is indicated as initial therapy in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus to improve glycemic control when diet and exercise do not provide adequate glycemic control. SITAGLIPTIN + METFORMIN HCl (JANUMET XR) is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus inadequately controlled on metformin or sitagliptin alone or in patients already being treated with the combination of sitagliptin and metformin. SITAGLIPTIN + METFORMIN HCl (JANUMET XR) is indicated as part of triple combination therapy with a sulfonylurea as an adjunct to diet and exercise in patients with type 2 diabetes [Page 25] mellitus inadequately controlled with any two of the three agents: metformin, sitagliptin, or a sulfonylurea. SITAGLIPTIN + METFORMIN HCl (JANUMET XR) is indicated as part of triple combination therapy with a PPARγ agonist (i.e., thiazolidinediones) as an adjunct to diet and exercise in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus inadequately controlled with any two of the three agents: metformin, sitagliptin, or a PPARγ agonist. SITAGLIPTIN + METFORMIN HCl (JANUMET XR) is indicated in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in combination with insulin.",24,25,V . INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T16:22:29.979107+00:00
