PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5362-18,Acetylcysteine,Aecys 600,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qkRiM3BpnnXr5UqBGkxJgMi6WOHhkcwc/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5362-18_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qkRiM3BpnnXr5UqBGkxJgMi6WOHhkcwc_view_usp_drivesdk_8e3fd93716.pdf,page_text/DRP-5362-18_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qkRiM3BpnnXr5UqBGkxJgMi6WOHhkcwc_view_usp_drivesdk_8e3fd93716.json,30e3f3661cb38e881287223681d24f1c8d5ae6e02078c5e55a270daec7b881c7,1465832,1,digital_text,"These features make Acetylcysteine 200 mg Powder for Oral Solution particularly suitable for the treatment of acute and chronic infections of the respiratory system, characterised by thick, viscous mucous and mucopurulent secretions. Hypersensitivity to Acetylcysteine or any component of the formulation. Children with inhalation injury who were treated with aerolised heparin 5000 units alternating with 3 mL of 20% Acetylcysteine solution, inhaled every 2 hours for the 1st 7 days after injury, appeared to have significantly reduced mortality and reintubation rates compared with historical control. Or as prescribed by the physician.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Used for its mucolytic activity in respiratory disorders associated with productive cough and in the management of Paracetamol overdosage.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T16:23:07.047275+00:00
