PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5457,Tramadol (as hydrochloride),Ridil-50,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1eskIj0Yfo41hgIv87iGpwaE5bTzzyBnb/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5457_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eskIj0Yfo41hgIv87iGpwaE5bTzzyBnb_view_usp_drivesdk_59b874b1b2.pdf,page_text/DRP-5457_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eskIj0Yfo41hgIv87iGpwaE5bTzzyBnb_view_usp_drivesdk_59b874b1b2.json,4f30a8ddcd819c2a4a531fccad842e7d19ef4513b2ba7c2fa29d2923c33d17bf,482153,1,digital_text,"Tramadol Hydrochloride is readily absorbed following oral administration. Oral bioavailability is approximately 68% after a single dose and increases to 90% at steady state. Onset of action is dose dependent but generally occurs within an hour of dosing, peaking within 2 to 3 hours. Duration of analgesia is about 6 hours. The rate or extent of absorption is not significantly affected by co-administration with food. The bioavailability of Tramadol Hydrochloride after intramuscular injection or intravenous administration is the same; the mean peak serum concentration is achieved after 45 minutes. Tramadol Hydrochloride is primarily metabolised in the liver (90%) with one of its metabolites, mono-O-desmethyltramadol (M1), being 2 to 4 times as potent as the parent compound. Tramadol Hydrochloride has a linear pharmacokinetic profile within the therapeutic dosage range. Tramadol Hydrochloride crosses the blood-brain and placental barrier. Small amounts are excreted in breast milk unchanged or as the metabolite M1. Tramadol Hydrochloride and its metabolites are excreted mainly in the urine. The elimination half-life is 5 to 7 hours, but is prolonged in impaired hepatic and renal function. Tramadol is a centrally acting analgesic which possesses opioid agonist properties.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Tramadol Hydrochloride is indicated for the management of moderate to moderately severe pain. Use with caution in patients with a history of epilepsy or those susceptible to seizures (e.g., patients taking neuroleptics and other drugs that reduce the seizure threshold). Clear colourless solution, free from particulate matter and fibers, filled in 2 mL clear, USP type I glass ampoule. Each mL contains:",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:06:01.597687+00:00
