PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5518-03,Cefixime (as trihydrate),Refixime-DS,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1v96sKAejUcwoyGNpmBaeeix4Q_YPgIrC/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5518-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1v96sKAejUcwoyGNpmBaeeix4Q_YPgIrC_view_usp_drivesdk_7ca66512f0.pdf,page_text/DRP-5518-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1v96sKAejUcwoyGNpmBaeeix4Q_YPgIrC_view_usp_drivesdk_7ca66512f0.json,aa65bc8e8f79bfe2269ebe4415e671dac9a76f216d268e01d81b7e4001616b8f,2396591,1,ocr,"frequent stools 6%, abdominal pain 3%, nausea 7%, dyspepsia 3%, and flatulence 4%. The incidence of gastrointestinal adverse ion was lo the seen White to light yellow/orange coloured, orange flavored, free flowing powder when reconstituted it gives yellow to orange coloured reactions, including diarrhea and loose stools, in pediatric patients receiving the pi suspension. in adult patients receiving tablets. Several patients developed severe diarrhea and/or documented pseudomembranous colitis, and a few required hospitalization.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,STORAGE CONDITION For the treatment of infections due to sensitive Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria. Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T17:08:58.033048+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5518-04,Cefixime (as trihydrate),Trimax,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1t6mG_rCr-8xuCjFVroZrD2ZmZG3Jt2FR/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5518-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1t6mG_rCr-8xuCjFVroZrD2ZmZG3Jt2FR_view_usp_drivesdk_d1408ba972.pdf,page_text/DRP-5518-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1t6mG_rCr-8xuCjFVroZrD2ZmZG3Jt2FR_view_usp_drivesdk_d1408ba972.json,38691ed5162a5dbb27d71efcbdb60e9153877d86777a45bc20558f42d7842384,476169,1,digital_text,"Cefixime is a third generation cephalosporin with antibacterial activity similar to penicillins, carbacephems and cephamycins. Cefixime exerts its bactericidal activity by interfering with the synthesis of the bacterial cell wall. It binds to specific penicillin-binding proteins responsible for the synthesis of peptidoglycan, a heteropolymeric structure that gives the cell wall its mechanical stability. The final stage of peptidoglycan synthesis involves completion of the cross-linking of the terminal glycine residue of the pentaglycine bridge to the fourth residue of the pentapeptide. The transpeptidase that catalyzes this step is inhibited by cephalosporins. Thus, inhibition of the transpeptidase interrupts peptidoglycan synthesis, causing formation of defective cell walls and osmotically unstable spheroplasts and lysis of the bacteria.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T17:09:01.296327+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5518-05,Cefixime (as trihydrate),Argifix,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1OUiLwXsAStGC9hwXc4Uz8VQbLihxNYJg/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5518-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OUiLwXsAStGC9hwXc4Uz8VQbLihxNYJg_view_usp_drivesdk_f98283860e.pdf,page_text/DRP-5518-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OUiLwXsAStGC9hwXc4Uz8VQbLihxNYJg_view_usp_drivesdk_f98283860e.json,cb930a9c4dcb7a0820a335d98183657a68b2c58136cd69da8d1495e53e11b150,108947,1,digital_text,"White to light yellow/orange coloured, orange avored, free owing powder when reconstituted it gives yellow to orange coloured suspension. For the treatment of infections due to sensitive Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria. Treatment with broad spectrum antibiotics, including Cexime, alters the normal ora of the colon and may permit overgrowth of clostridia. Studies indicate that a toxin produced by Clostridium difcile is a primary cause of severe antibiotic-associated diarrhea including pseudomembranous colitis. Pseudomembranous colitis has been reported with the use of Cexime and other broadspectrum antibiotics (including macrolides, semisynthetic penicillins, and cephalosporins); therefore, it is important to consider this diagnosis in patients who develop diarrhea in association with the use of antibiotics.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Children 1 to 4 years: 10 mL daily. Shake well before use. Children over 6 months: 8 mg/kg daily in 1 to 2 divided doses; or Or as prescribed by the physician. Cexime for oral suspension is contraindicated in patients with known allergy to Cexime or other cephalosporins. Anaphylactic/anaphylactoid reactions (including shock and fatalities) have been reported with the use of cexime. Antibiotics, including cexime, should be administered cautiously to any patient who has demonstrated some form of allergy, particularly to drugs. The usual course of treatment is 7 days. This may be continued for up to 14 days if required.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:09:04.582499+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5518-06,Cefixime (as trihydrate),Elvofix,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/18XXRwVRl4jDV7bTb1S5suA_yRNOajobq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5518-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18XXRwVRl4jDV7bTb1S5suA_yRNOajobq_view_usp_drivesdk_cbfe99392a.pdf,page_text/DRP-5518-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18XXRwVRl4jDV7bTb1S5suA_yRNOajobq_view_usp_drivesdk_cbfe99392a.json,145a2e30a22ec42f4b01b1cbc90efbb425e90992691973b97794746e2d2409c6,2360342,1,ocr,"White to light yellow/orange coloured, orange flavored, free flowing powder when reconstituted it gives yellow to orange coloured suspension. Elevated levels have been reported when administered concomitantly with Cefixime. Drug monitoring when these ‘iuge are given together is advised Wartarin and Anticoagulants: Increased prothrombin time, with or without clinical bleeding, has been reported when cefixime is administered",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"anemia, hemolytic anemia, hemorrhage, and colitis. Several cephalosporins have been implicated in triggering seizures, particularly in patients with renalimpairment when the dosage was not reduced. For the treatment of infections due to sensitive Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T17:09:16.287483+00:00
