PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5518-13,Cefixime (as trihydrate),Comfixime,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/12SkC6wLCCUCh1nCzd1FMdNNyL8dSe-ez/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5518-13_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_12SkC6wLCCUCh1nCzd1FMdNNyL8dSe-ez_view_usp_drivesdk_4efd59fcb8.pdf,page_text/DRP-5518-13_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_12SkC6wLCCUCh1nCzd1FMdNNyL8dSe-ez_view_usp_drivesdk_4efd59fcb8.json,43d0b9be2d95c5e7dad53f7dae441ae6dad95f89f92c810656e1838d368d25ab,1859797,1,digital_text,For the treatment of infections due to sensitive Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria. Children over 6 months: 8 mg/kg daily in 1 to 2 divided doses; or 6 months up to 1 year: 7.5 mL daily. Children 5 to10 years: 20 mL daily. The usual course of treatment is 7 days. This may be continued for up to 14 days if required. Or as prescribed by the physician. Shake bottle to loosen the powder. Slowly add boiled and then cooled water up to the mark on the bottle. Shake vigorously. The reconstituted suspension should be stored at temperatures between 2°C to 8°C and should be used within 7 days.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T17:10:00.453161+00:00
