PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5654,Piozulin 15,Pioglitazone (As Hydrochloride),PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PCtKD_FKsLLYZ3xZjSWrr8hTQlGQRQPz/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5654_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PCtKD_FKsLLYZ3xZjSWrr8hTQlGQRQPz_view_usp_drivesdk_686cab34c9.pdf,page_text/DRP-5654_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PCtKD_FKsLLYZ3xZjSWrr8hTQlGQRQPz_view_usp_drivesdk_686cab34c9.json,46cd71adb5a17b0deccff30b54e5f08435e7b7edfb0761dd1905e0142ec25946,614110,1,digital_text,"White coloured, round shaped, uncoated tablets with breakline on one side and plain on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Pioglitazone (PIOZULIN) is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetis (non-insulin dependent diabetis mellitus, NIDDM). Pioglitazone(PIOZULIN) is indicated for monotherapy. Pioglitazone (PIOZULIN) is also indicated for use in combination with a sulfonylurea, metformin, or insulin when diet and exercise with plus the single agent does not result in adequate glycemic control. Management of type 2 diabetis should also include nutritional counseling, weight reduction as needed, and exercise. These efforts are important not only in the primary treatment of type 2 diabetes, but also to maintain the efficacy of drug therapy.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:16:33.544365+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5654,Piozulin 15,Pioglitazone (As Hydrochloride),PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bHkLso_xzLd6twu60Br4Ev9Jjl6Pgfne/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5654_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bHkLso_xzLd6twu60Br4Ev9Jjl6Pgfne_view_usp_drivesdk_d45fb99e70.pdf,page_text/DRP-5654_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bHkLso_xzLd6twu60Br4Ev9Jjl6Pgfne_view_usp_drivesdk_d45fb99e70.json,46cd71adb5a17b0deccff30b54e5f08435e7b7edfb0761dd1905e0142ec25946,614110,1,digital_text,"White coloured, round shaped, uncoated tablets with breakline on one side and plain on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Pioglitazone (PIOZULIN) is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetis (non-insulin dependent diabetis mellitus, NIDDM). Pioglitazone(PIOZULIN) is indicated for monotherapy. Pioglitazone (PIOZULIN) is also indicated for use in combination with a sulfonylurea, metformin, or insulin when diet and exercise with plus the single agent does not result in adequate glycemic control. Management of type 2 diabetis should also include nutritional counseling, weight reduction as needed, and exercise. These efforts are important not only in the primary treatment of type 2 diabetes, but also to maintain the efficacy of drug therapy.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:16:30.826591+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5665,Diphenhydramine Hydrochloride,Histamox,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vU1UFFc3RoqDebvehKK9OV3rqWLC8Vzb/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5665_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vU1UFFc3RoqDebvehKK9OV3rqWLC8Vzb_view_usp_drivesdk_f986939dbd.pdf,page_text/DRP-5665_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vU1UFFc3RoqDebvehKK9OV3rqWLC8Vzb_view_usp_drivesdk_f986939dbd.json,c5cd6bf7943408a5f4db12ed0367718188977ef85ecccdeb9c2e0f176fd1946d,419846,1,digital_text,"Diphenhydramine Hydrochloride is a white powder, in gray cap/ yellow body EGC size 3mm",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Diphenhydramine, a monoethanolamine derivative, is a sedating antihistamine with antimuscarinic and pronounced sedative properties. It is used for the symptomatic relief of allergic conditions including urticaria, angioedema, rhinitis and conjunctivitis, and pruritic skin disorders. It is also used for its antiemetic properties in the treatment of nausea and vomiting, particularly in the prevention and treatment of motion sickness, and in the treatment of vertigo of various causes. Diphenhydramine is used for it’s antimuscarinic properties in the control of parkinsonism, and drug induced extrapyramidal disorders. Diphenhydramine has pronounced central sedative properties and may be used as a hypnotic in the short-term management of insomnia. It is common ingredient of compound preparations for symptomatic relief of coughs and common colds. Usage in respiratory diseases: In general antihistamines are not recommended to treat lower respiratory tract symptoms including asthma, as their anticholinergic (drying) effects may cause thickening of secretions and impaired expectoration. However several reports indicate antihistamines can be safely used in asthmatic patients with severe perennial allergic rhinitis without exacerbating the asthma. Sedatives /CNS Depressants: Avoid sedatives and CNS depressants in patients with a history of sleep apnea. Usage in elderly (over 60 years): Antihistamines are more likely to cause dizziness, excessive sedation, syncope, toxic confusional states and hypotension in elderly patients. Dosage reduction may be required. Usage in Children: Antihistamines overdosage may cause hallucinations and death. Antihistamines may diminish mental alertness. In the young child they may cause paradoxical excitation.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:16:40.112270+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5665-01,Diphenhydramine Hydrochloride,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1YSD813Uv_NHHThv5zXJfrsl5zEKa0Ofb/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5665-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YSD813Uv_NHHThv5zXJfrsl5zEKa0Ofb_view_usp_drivesdk_7c68953fdc.pdf,page_text/DRP-5665-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YSD813Uv_NHHThv5zXJfrsl5zEKa0Ofb_view_usp_drivesdk_7c68953fdc.json,eac36f2a4111a131e62c24b8a2ede564641b9aeff441a0e76532221a4532459f,429875,1,digital_text,"Diphenhydramine Hydrochloride is a white powder, in gray cap/yellow body EGC size 3mm",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Diphenhydramine, a monoethanolamine derivative, is a sedating antihistamine with antimuscarinic and pronounced sedative properties. It is used for the symptomatic relief of allergic conditions including urticaria, angioedema, rhinitis and conjunctivitis, and pruritic skin disorders. It is also used for its antiemetic properties in the treatment of nausea and vomiting, particularly in the prevention and treatment of motion sickness, and in the treatment of vertigo of various causes. Diphenhydramine is used for it’s antimuscarinic properties in the control of parkinsonism, and drug induced extrapyramidal disorders. Diphenhydramine has pronounced central sedative properties and may be used as a hypnotic in the short-term management of insomnia. It is common ingredient of compound preparations for symptomatic relief of coughs and common colds. Usage in respiratory diseases: In general antihistamines are not recommended to treat lower respiratory tract symptoms including asthma, as their anticholinergic (drying) effects may cause thickening of secretions and impaired expectoration. However several reports indicate antihistamines can be safely used in asthmatic patients with severe perennial allergic rhinitis without exacerbating the asthma. Sedatives / Central Nervous System Depressants: Avoid sedatives and Central Nervous System depressants in patients with a history of sleep apnea. Usage in elderly (over 60 years): Antihistamines are more likely to cause dizziness, excessive sedation, syncope, toxic confusional states and hypotension in elderly patients. Dosage reduction may be required. Usage in Children: Antihistamines overdosage may cause hallucinations and death. Antihistamines may diminish mental alertness. In the young child they may cause paradoxical excitation.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:16:36.985069+00:00
