PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-570,Omeprazole,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KJUpMiJyluNMy394ySKFgSPrIozhEPo-/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-570_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1KJUpMiJyluNMy394ySKFgSPrIozhEPo-_view_usp_drivesdk_c8928b999d.pdf,page_text/DRP-570_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1KJUpMiJyluNMy394ySKFgSPrIozhEPo-_view_usp_drivesdk_c8928b999d.json,94f95205149dc4163e93c53809a3cbac67db149f49ba0d562adfb7782afbddb2,423439,1,digital_text,Omeprazole 20 mg Capsule is a white granules with yellow/gray capsule size 1 mm.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Used in conditions where inhibition of gastric acid secretion may be beneficial, including aspiration syndromes, dyspepsia, gastroesophageal reflux disease, peptic ulcer disease and the Zollinger- Ellison syndrome.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:18:48.436759+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5702,Danazol,Dazol-200,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mDu8zNuM98U95QvYIqmab-kcIu8fruIj/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5702_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mDu8zNuM98U95QvYIqmab-kcIu8fruIj_view_usp_drivesdk_24b2fa210b.pdf,page_text/DRP-5702_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mDu8zNuM98U95QvYIqmab-kcIu8fruIj_view_usp_drivesdk_24b2fa210b.json,2bf68a41fded93f90ba7b995c5b92e28068897adbc28736780151bc79d4b2db2,988514,1,digital_text,"1. Relatively marked affinity for androgen receptors, less marked affinity for progesterone receptors and least affinity for oestrogen receptors. Danazol is a weak androgen but in addition antiandrogenic, progestogenic, antiprogestogenic, oestrogenic and antioestrogenic actions have been observed. Red/White colour ""0"" size hard gelatin capsule containing white colour powder. 4. A wide range of actions on plasma proteins, including increasing prothrombin, plasminogen, antithrombin III, alpha-2 macroglobulin, C1 esterase inhibitor, and erythropoietin and reducing fibrinogen, thyroid binding and sex hormone binding globulins. Danazol increases the proportion and concentration of testosterone carried unbound in plasma. 5. The suppressive effects of danazol on the hypothalmic-pituitary-gonadal axis are reversible, cyclical activity reappearing normally within 60-90 days after therapy. Pharmacotherapeutic group: sex hormones and modulators of the genital system, antigondotropics and similar agents. 3. Inhibition of the mid-cycle surge of FSH and LH as well as alterations in the pulsatility of LH. Danazol can also reduce the mean plasma levels of these gonadotrophins after the menopause. 2. Interference with the synthesis of gonadal steroids, possibly by inhibition of the enzymes of steroidogenesis, including 3β hydroxysteroid dehydrogenase,17β hydroxysteroid dehydrogenase, 17 hydroxylase, 17, 20 lyase, 11β hydroxylase, 21 hydroxylase and cholesterol side chain cleavage enzymes, or alternatively by inhibition of the cyclic AMP accumulation usually induced by gonadotrophic hormones in granulosa and luteal cells. Mechanism of Action: Danazol (Dazol-200) suppresses the pituitary-ovarian axis. This suppression is probably a combination of depressed hypothalamic-pituitary response to lowered estrogen production, the alteration of sex steroid metabolism, and interaction of Danazol (Dazol-200) with sex hormone receptors. The only other demonstrable hormonal effect is weak androgenic activity. Danazol (Dazol-200) depresses the output of both follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) and luteinizing hormone (LH). Recent evidence suggests a direct inhibitory effect at gonadal sites and a binding of Danazol (Dazol-200) to receptors of gonadal steroids at target organs. In addition, Danazol (Dazol-200) has been shown to significantly decrease IgG, IgM and IgA levels, as well as phospholipid and IgG isotope autoantibodies in patients with endometriosis and associated elevations of autoantibodies, suggesting this could be another mechanism by which it facilitates regression of the disease. Generally, the pituitary-suppressive action of Danazol (Dazol-200) is reversible. Ovulation and cyclic bleeding usually return within 60 to 90 days when therapy with Danazol (Dazol-200) is discontinued.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Administration of Danazol (Dazol-200) has been reported to cause exacerbation of the manifestations of acute intermittent porphyria. Since hepatic dysfunction manifested by modest increases in serum transaminase levels has been reported in patients treated with Danazol (Dazol-200), periodic liver function tests should be performed. Following oral administration and absorption, Danazol (Dazol-200) is extensively metabolised. However, plasma levels of unchanged Danazol rise quickly, indicating a rapid onset of absorption. Peak plasma levels have been recorded occurring within 2-8 hours of medicine administration in a number of studies. A considerable difference in peak plasma levels has been observed in individuals receiving the same dosage, and in bioavailability studies, levels do not increase in proportion to the administered dose. When the dose of Danazol (Dazol-200) is doubled the increase in plasma levels is about 35% to 40%. Danazol (Dazol-200) has no significant effect on prolactin levels, or on thyroid or adrenal function. Reduced serum thyroxine levels may occur and are attributed to competition between thyroxine and Danazol (Dazol-200) for binding sites on thyroxine-binding plasma proteins.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:18:51.587318+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5705,Tramadol Hydrochloride,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cS945qyyhY9Eih7fLvkp0EUfMqim0jEw/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5705_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cS945qyyhY9Eih7fLvkp0EUfMqim0jEw_view_usp_drivesdk_dfd2033e34.pdf,page_text/DRP-5705_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cS945qyyhY9Eih7fLvkp0EUfMqim0jEw_view_usp_drivesdk_dfd2033e34.json,d1d5b6d69982bca30c66b2a12d8bcd6ca05487f4fc054f342ea503fc32b8d870,1719048,2,ocr,"Tramadol Hydrochloride 50 mg / mL (100 mg / 2 mL) Solution for Injection is a clear, colorless, odorless solution, free from visible foreign matter.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Tramadol HCI is an opioid analgesic. It also has noradrenergic and serotonergic properties that may contribute for its analgesic activity. Tramadol is used for moderate to severe pain.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T17:19:00.097694+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5708,Celecoxib,Selex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lkDw838fhE2kS_5sRqJhWPWWvwOkbRaF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5708_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1lkDw838fhE2kS_5sRqJhWPWWvwOkbRaF_view_usp_drivesdk_243bcb25dd.pdf,page_text/DRP-5708_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1lkDw838fhE2kS_5sRqJhWPWWvwOkbRaF_view_usp_drivesdk_243bcb25dd.json,84482de7977f917b4e2da127c14b811834800ca157424b9d8429c6731dbec485,427714,1,digital_text,Celecoxib 400 mg Capsule is a white fine powder in powder blue / light blue size “0” Celecoxib 200 mg Capsule is a white fine powder in scarlet cap/white body size “1” plain capsule,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the relief of the sign and symptoms of osteoarthritis and rheumatoid arthritis in adults and adjunct for the reduction of number of adenomatous colorectal polyps in familial polyposis. It is also indicated for the management of the signs and symptoms of juvenile rheumatoid arthritis in patients 2 years and older, and ankylosing spondylitis; for the management of acute pain in adults, and for the management of primary dysmenorrhea.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:19:06.044388+00:00
