PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5715,Irbesartan,Aprovel,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/14T9k4m7bQ49U4G1pvc7kgy_A-U5Iwmcq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5715_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14T9k4m7bQ49U4G1pvc7kgy_A-U5Iwmcq_view_usp_drivesdk_03c936111f.pdf,page_text/DRP-5715_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14T9k4m7bQ49U4G1pvc7kgy_A-U5Iwmcq_view_usp_drivesdk_03c936111f.json,d89424fdcd1979756b83181a411a52ed722c307be71e8302097633364859fd6f,206942,10,digital_text,"Irbesartan (Aprovel) 150 mg film-coated tablet: White to off -white, biconvex, and oval -shaped with a heart debossed on one side and the number 2872 engraved on the other side. Irbesartan (Aprovel) 300 mg film-coated tablet: White to off -white, biconvex, and oval-shaped with a heart debossed on one side and the number 2873 engraved on the other side. Clinical Particulars",1,1,Pharmaceutical Form,"Irbesartan (Aprovel) is indicated for the treatment of hypertension. It may be used either alone or in combination with other antihypertensive agents (eg, thiazide diuretics, beta - adrenergic blocking agents, long-acting calcium-channel blocking agents). Irbesartan ( Aprovel) is indicated for the treatment of renal disease in patients with hypertension and type 2 diabetes.",1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:19:12.571908+00:00
