PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5785,Cetirizine Dihydrochloride,Cope,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oR6ORxUrQVNmUBxXj2bwlGeEUFO0pYg7/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5785_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oR6ORxUrQVNmUBxXj2bwlGeEUFO0pYg7_view_usp_drivesdk_5f99206ca6.pdf,page_text/DRP-5785_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oR6ORxUrQVNmUBxXj2bwlGeEUFO0pYg7_view_usp_drivesdk_5f99206ca6.json,edc94bb20cb49e96331dba46c48c407bcd874b5dafaa582dedc6b89292018c45,460705,3,digital_text,"White to off white, round, biconvex & film-coated tablet. PHARMACODYNAMICS Cetirizine, a human metabolite of hydroxyzine, is an antihistamine; its principal effects are mediated via selective inhibition of peripheral H1 receptors. PHARMACOKINETICS Cetirizine is rapidly absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract after oral administration, peak plasma concentration being attained in about one hour. Food delays the time to peak plasma concentrations but does not decrease the amount of drug absorbed. Cetirizine is highly bound to plasma proteins and has an elimination half life of about 10 hours. It has been detected in breast milk. Cetirizine is excreted primarily in the urine mainly as unchanged drug. It does not appear to cross the blood-brain barrier to a significant extent.",3,3,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Used for symptomatic relief of allergy such as hay fever, urticaria.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:21:51.106047+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5789,Albendazole,Medzole,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xW-so-RlZzaXbKxaB0LxfA2-C3VAKlv1/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5789_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xW-so-RlZzaXbKxaB0LxfA2-C3VAKlv1_view_usp_drivesdk_4e0ad2f443.pdf,page_text/DRP-5789_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xW-so-RlZzaXbKxaB0LxfA2-C3VAKlv1_view_usp_drivesdk_4e0ad2f443.json,44ad3805e811b8de7d2577bfb1ef2a3c2410805c782daadecc5d90fcb94fdce9,803806,1,digital_text,,,,,"For parenchymal neurocysticerosis and cystic hyatid disease of the liver, roundworm infestation and microsporidoses and giardiasis in AIDS. Pharmacokinetics Absorption of albendazole from the gastrointestinal tract is poor but may be enhanced by a fatty meal. Albendazole rapidly undergoes extensive ﬁrst-pass metabolism. Its principal metabolite albendazole sulfoxide has anthelmintic activity and a plasma half- life of about 8.5 hours. Albendazole sulfoxide is widely distributed throughout the body including into the bile and the CSF. It is about 70% bound to plasma protein. Albendazole sulfoxide is eliminated in the bile; only a small amount appears to be excreted in the urine.",1,1,Indication:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T17:21:54.158661+00:00
