PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5902,Carboplatin,Cisamin-450,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qvQb_aqTjK25YRK8cjPfZH03OSRiAGIZ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5902_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qvQb_aqTjK25YRK8cjPfZH03OSRiAGIZ_view_usp_drivesdk_0922344eb7.pdf,page_text/DRP-5902_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qvQb_aqTjK25YRK8cjPfZH03OSRiAGIZ_view_usp_drivesdk_0922344eb7.json,06cdc3f5d5ab9d0ab0dd3e3a117a1afa0c69e21c0eccb53e7d93622937697fe0,1428297,1,digital_text,"A clear colorless solution. Carboplatin is excreted primarily by glomerular filtration in urine, with recovery of 65% of a dose within 24 hours. Most of the drug is excreted within the first six hours. Approximately 32% of a given dose of Carboplatin is excreted unchanged.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Pediatric population Antineoplastic agent indicated in the treatment of ovarian carcinoma of epithelial origin and small cell lung carcinoma. Carboplatin is an antineoplastic agent, analogue of cisplatin, and interferes with DNA intrastrand and interstrand crosslinks in cells exposed to the drug. DNA reactivity has been correlated with cytotoxicity. Pediatric population Protein binding of Carboplatin reaches 85-89% within 24 hours of administration, although during the first 4 hours, only up to 29% of the dose is protein bound. Patients with poor renal function may require dosage adjustments due to altered pharmacokinetics of Carboplatin. The safety and efficacy in children has not yet been determined. Carboplatin clearance in children has been reported as 3 to 4 times the clearance in adults.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:24:35.436783+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5915-02,Ofloxacin + Dexamethasone,Foxadex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hv_aec-KMHi-MOxAlOFim7p_sfhz_dwy/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5915-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hv_aec-KMHi-MOxAlOFim7p_sfhz_dwy_view_usp_drivesdk_f9253d972c.pdf,page_text/DRP-5915-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hv_aec-KMHi-MOxAlOFim7p_sfhz_dwy_view_usp_drivesdk_f9253d972c.json,e92bd6f2b02676643af491b4a7de77e9d3425b90e380c31749b68765835d375a,476187,1,digital_text,Clear colourless solution should be free from any type of visible particles.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Ofloxacin + Dexamethasone is indicated for steroid-responsive inflammatory ocular conditions for which a corticosteroid is indicated and where bacterial ocular infection or a risk infection exists. Ofloxacin + Dexamethasone is indicated in inflammatory conditions of the palpebral and bulbar conjunctiva, cornea and anterior segment of the globe where the inherent risk of steroid use in certain infective conjunctivitis is accepted to obtain a diminution in edema and inflammation. Ofloxacin + Dexamethasone is indicated in chronic anterior uveitis and corneal injury from chemical radiation, thermal burns, or penetration of foreign bodies, where the risk of infection is high or where there is an expectation that potentially dangerous numbers of bacteria will be present in the eye.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:24:38.387671+00:00
