PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5938-01,Orlistat,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zWTObalroEJTJhm9T09xWLpxruaTgomY/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5938-01_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zWTObalroEJTJhm9T09xWLpxruaTgomY_view_usp_drivesdk_5b9d748b5a.pdf,page_text/DRP-5938-01_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zWTObalroEJTJhm9T09xWLpxruaTgomY_view_usp_drivesdk_5b9d748b5a.json,080b30f203eae7283457f453293143a5251f82f76224fc904146e6446c26941a,1151731,1,ocr,"prevents you from absorbing nutrients from food, WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? or cholestasis, where flow of bile from your liver is If you missed a dose, you may take it as soon as you ADVERSE DRUG REACTION REPORTING Orlistat 120 mg Capsule contains white to off-white slowed or blocked. STATEMENT cylindrical pellets, encapsulated in Empty Gelatin remember. However, if you remember it at a time You should not take this medicine if you have that is already close to the next dose, just skip the For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the Capsule (EGC) # 2, with light blue body and cap. missed dose and take the next dose as scheduled.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T17:27:54.965458+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5946,Finasteride,Figna-5,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dgrIh9jmsM481cMpJXQtnISCWsCNGPnx/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5946_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dgrIh9jmsM481cMpJXQtnISCWsCNGPnx_view_usp_drivesdk_6a18db9962.pdf,page_text/DRP-5946_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dgrIh9jmsM481cMpJXQtnISCWsCNGPnx_view_usp_drivesdk_6a18db9962.json,4340be7cc4405de26f4b90e139e6e540a22745d9dbb5020626ed12ade2c5e46f,1581973,1,digital_text,"The Medical Therapy of Prostatic Symptoms (MTOPS) Trial was a 4- to 6-year study in 3047 men with symptomatic BPH who were randomised to receive Finasteride 5 mg/day, Doxazosin 4 or 8 mg/day*, the combination of Finasteride 5 mg/day and Doxazosin 4 or 8 mg/day*, or placebo. The primary endpoint was time to clinical progression of BPH, defined as a =4 point confirmed increase from baseline in symptom score, acute urinary retention, BPH- related renal insufficiency, recurrent urinary tract infections or urosepsis, or incontinence. Compared to placebo, treatment with Finasteride, Doxazosin, or combination therapy resulted in a significant reduction in the risk of clinical progression of BPH by 34% (p=0.002), 39% (p<0.001), and 67% (p<0.001), respectively. The majority of the events (274 out of 351) that constituted BPH progression were confirmed =4 point increases in symptom score; the risk of symptom score progression was reduced by 30% (95% CI 6 to 48%), 46% (95% CI 25 to 60%), and 64% (95% CI 48 to 75%) in the Finasteride, Doxazosin, and combination groups, respectively, compared to placebo. Acute urinary retention accounted for 41 of the 351 events of BPH progression; the risk of developing acute urinary retention was reduced by 67% (p=0.011), 31% (p=0.296), and 79% (p=0.001) in the Finasteride, Doxazosin, and combination groups, respectively, compared to placebo. Only the Finasteride and combination therapy groups were significantly different from placebo. * Titrated from 1 mg to 4 or 8 mg as tolerated over a 3-week period.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T17:28:05.186553+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5950,Esomeprazole (As Magnesium Trihydrate),Esomap-40,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_uD0wRVWNBAVtY6lcqF9CCh7BD-QL9aZ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5950_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_uD0wRVWNBAVtY6lcqF9CCh7BD-QL9aZ_view_usp_drivesdk_94b637ee77.pdf,page_text/DRP-5950_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_uD0wRVWNBAVtY6lcqF9CCh7BD-QL9aZ_view_usp_drivesdk_94b637ee77.json,d2d509447d85ee8054ba83a3dd830a7e4d7d65b8ec46830ab0703e86db09bdb7,3536761,4,digital_text,"During treatment with antisecretory medicinal products, serum gastrin increases in response to the decreased acid secretion. Also Chromogranin A (CgA) increases due to decreased gastric acidity. The increased CgA level may interfere with investigations for neuroendocrine tumours. Literature reports indicate that proton pump inhibitor treatment should be stopped at least 5 days before CgA measurement. If CgA and gastrin levels have not normalised after 5 days, measurements should be repeated 14 days after cessation of Esomeprazole treatment. Decreased gastric acidity due to any means including proton pump inhibitors, increases gastric counts of bacteria normally present in the gastrointestinal tract. Treatment with proton pump inhibitors may lead to slightly increased risk of gastrointestinal infections such as Salmonella and Campylobacter and, in hospitalised patients, possibly also Clostridium difficile. Pediatric population Clinical efficacy In a study in pediatric GERD patients (<1 to 17 years of age) receiving long-term PPI treatment, 61% of the children developed minor degrees of ECL cell hyperplasia with no known clinical significance and with no development of atrophic gastritis or carcinoid tumours. Excretion :The plasma elimination half-life of Esomeprazole is approximately 1 to 1.5 hours. Less than 1% of parent drug is excreted in the urine. Approximately 80% of an oral dose of Esomeprazole is excreted as inactive metabolites in the urine, and the remainder is found as inactive metabolites in the feces.",4,4,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Please see package insert. Batch No.: Mfg. Date: Exp. Date: DRP-5950 Mfg. Lic. No.: 000620 Colour: RGB Dimension:140 mm x 85 mm x 17 mm 140 mm 85 mm 17 mm 4 806524 783827 [Page 2] ESOMEPRAZOLE ESOMEPRAZOLE ESOMAP-40 ESOMAP-40 28 Capsules 28 Capsules,1,2,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:28:12.307196+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5950-02,Esomeprazole (As Magnesium Trihydrate),Esmegerd,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1if5HTrt04kZKxpNKcIC05o3jX70pmTnx/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5950-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1if5HTrt04kZKxpNKcIC05o3jX70pmTnx_view_usp_drivesdk_a71922a858.pdf,page_text/DRP-5950-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1if5HTrt04kZKxpNKcIC05o3jX70pmTnx_view_usp_drivesdk_a71922a858.json,610de0289c4a593b2b4cd6f27392ba8f969ce2d178f994d93df3e9f1b52f2ecf,447721,1,digital_text,A violet body and cap capsule filled with off white to gray colored pellets.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of peptic ulcer disease, and other conditions where inhibition of gastric acid secretion may be beneficial, including aspiration syndrome, healing of erosive esophagitis, dyspepsia, gastroesophageal reflux disease, Zollinger Ellison Syndrome.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:28:08.392752+00:00
