PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5955-01,Meloxicam,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J062pePadeBxxz7vWUGhsikGGXSrd_jg/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5955-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1J062pePadeBxxz7vWUGhsikGGXSrd_jg_view_usp_drivesdk_59f402d583.pdf,page_text/DRP-5955-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1J062pePadeBxxz7vWUGhsikGGXSrd_jg_view_usp_drivesdk_59f402d583.json,237d0c40c1256a3651160295461071b6b8d037d69147a3cbc47d22399feecfb2,920616,1,ocr,"+ Uncontrolled hypertension + Congestive Heart Failure (CHF) NYHA-II-IV hypertension, acute renal failure, hepatic dysfunction, Meloxicam |5mg Tablet: Pale yellow, round, flat, beveled respiratory depression, coma, convulsions, cardiovascular edge tablet bisected on one side with engraved ""P"" on the",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T17:28:22.426271+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5960-04,Losartan Potassium,Losartfix,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dja69T8WiGPBdywpY0FDlAoyrdB1M_0L/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5960-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dja69T8WiGPBdywpY0FDlAoyrdB1M_0L_view_usp_drivesdk_b041d14291.pdf,page_text/DRP-5960-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dja69T8WiGPBdywpY0FDlAoyrdB1M_0L_view_usp_drivesdk_b041d14291.json,7b658c7a5c5e9dcebf21edcce349176a6795e1e287df1ed0dbe9a44a93de1091,437791,1,digital_text,"White to off white, round, biconvex film-caoted tablet PHARMACODYNAMICS Losartan is an orally active, non-peptide angiotensin II receptor antagonist. Losartan and its active metabolite block the vasoconstrictor and aldosterone-secreting effects of angiotensin II selectively blocking the binding of angiotensin II to the AT receptor found in many tissues (e.g., vascular smooth muscle, adrenal gland).1 PHARMACOKINETICS Losartan is readily absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract following oral administration with an oral bioavailability of about 33%. It undergoes first pass metabolism to form an active carboxylic acid metabolite E-3174, which has greater pharmacological activity than Losartan and some inactive metabolites. Peak plasma concentrations of Losartan and E-3174 occur about 1 hour and 3 to 4 hours, respectively, after an oral dose. Both Losartan and E-3174 are more than 98% bound to plasma proteins. Losartan is excreted in the urine and in faeces via bile, as unchanged drug and metabolites. Following oral dosing about 35% of the dose is excreted in the urine and about 60% in the faeces. The terminal elimination half-lives of Losartan and E-3174 are about 1.5 to 2.5 hours and 3 to 9 hours respectively.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Used in the management of hypertension.,1,1,INDICATION,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:28:34.136608+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5965-03,,,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LZRJXspAVdu3Gli973ERF9PlmvGFQvHa/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5965-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LZRJXspAVdu3Gli973ERF9PlmvGFQvHa_view_usp_drivesdk_9631babfce.pdf,page_text/DRP-5965-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LZRJXspAVdu3Gli973ERF9PlmvGFQvHa_view_usp_drivesdk_9631babfce.json,004e82976486e23eae4bcad2f9843125845a606cc0df93bdc739c79ec0be6957,2468064,1,digital_text,"Ceftriaxone for injection, USP is a sterile, semi-synthetic, broad- spectrum cephalosporin antibiotic for intravenous or intramuscular administration. PHARMACOLOGY MECHANISM OF ACTION Ceftriaxone exerts antibacterial action by inhibiting cell wall synthesis of the invading bacteria. It inhibits the final step in cell wall synthesis. SPECTRUM OF ANTIBACTERIAL ACTIVITY Ceftriaxone has a broad spectrum activity in-vitro which includes Gram- positive and Gram negative, Aerobic and some Anaerobic. Ceftriaxone shows good in-vitro activity against the following organisms. Gram negative Aerobes: Enterobacter aerogenes, Enterobacter cloacae, E.Coli, H. influenzae (including Ampicillin resistant strains), H. parainfluenzae, Klebsiella spp (including K. pneumoniae), N.gonorrhoeae (inlcuding penicillinase and non-penicillinase producing strains) P. mirabilis, P. vulgari , Morganeita morganii, Serratia marcescens, Ps.aeruginosa, Citrobacter freundii, Citrobacter diversus, Providencia-spp, Salmonella spp, Shigella spp, Acinetobacter calcoaceticus Gram-Positive Aerobes: Staph. aureus including penicillinase producing strains, Staph. Epidermidis, Strep. pyogenes (Group A Beta-nernolytlc), Strep. agalactiae (Group B streptococci), Strep. Pneumonia Anaerobes Bacteroides spp, Clostridia (but most CI. difficile strains are resistant) PHARMACOKINETICS Ceftriaxone is administered as intravenous and intramuscular injection. The mean elimination half life in healthy adults is about 6-9 hours and is much longer than any other cephalosporins or cephamycins. The half life does not alter with change in the route of administration. Ceftriaxone was completely absorbed following IM administration with mean maximum plasma concentrations occurring between 2 and 3 hours post dosing. Multiple IV or IM doses ranging from 0.5 to 2 g at 12– to 24–hour intervals resulted in 15% to 36% accumulation of ceftriaxone above single dose values. 33% to 67% of a ceftriaxone dose was excreted in the urine as unchanged drug and the remainder was secreted in the bile and ultimately found in the feces as microbiologically inactive compounds. Ceftriaxone crosses the blood placenta barrier. In Infants and Children Elimination half-life in neonates is prolonged (almost equal to adults) but decreases with increasing postnatal age. In patients with renal failure, non-renal elimination may compensate.",1,1,DESCRIPTION,- Lower Respiratory Tract Infection. - Skin and Skin Structure Infections - Urinary Tract Infections (Complicated and Uncomplicated) - Uncomplicated Gonorrhoea - Cervical/Urethral/Rectal. - Pelvic Inflammatory disease - Bacterial Septicemia - Bone and Joint Infections - Intra-Abdominal Infections - Meningitis - Surgical Prophylaxis,1,1,INDICATIONS AND USAGE:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:28:38.220164+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5966-07,Co-Amoxiclav,Maxlavco 457,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HNmpKE-J6Vxk7UFS0y3iEnaCx1B2Y2OF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5966-07_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HNmpKE-J6Vxk7UFS0y3iEnaCx1B2Y2OF_view_usp_drivesdk_c7ec3c369e.pdf,page_text/DRP-5966-07_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HNmpKE-J6Vxk7UFS0y3iEnaCx1B2Y2OF_view_usp_drivesdk_c7ec3c369e.json,a234295c5b32e7d4bb17873d8c300136f20233bd32896c367ce09174e8d0fc7a,886535,1,ocr,"White coloured homogenous free flowing with raspberry flavour powder. Following administration of ampicillin to pregnant women, a transient decrease in plasma concentration of total conjugated estriol and estradiol has been noted. This effect may also occur with amoxicillin and therefore, with co- amoxiclav. Probenecid decreases the renal tubular secretion of amoxicillin but does not affect clavulanic acid",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T17:28:48.201066+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-5966-19,Co-Amoxiclav,Cozeal 457,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ASSrknkcOnYpzvpXTWGBturc_1voU8s-/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-5966-19_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ASSrknkcOnYpzvpXTWGBturc_1voU8s-_view_usp_drivesdk_c0ed1d6093.pdf,page_text/DRP-5966-19_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ASSrknkcOnYpzvpXTWGBturc_1voU8s-_view_usp_drivesdk_c0ed1d6093.json,8c13ef40ae939dfc8a8f95963b4761208602b7ffdf7a890df7f1b756156ece41,446061,1,digital_text,White coloured homogenous free ﬂowing powder with raspberry ﬂavour.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Co-amoxiclav is indicated for the short term treatment of common bacterial infections such as Upper Respiratory Tract Infections, including ENT (e.g., tonsillitis, sinusitis, otitis media), Lower Respiratory Tract Infections (e.g., acute and chronic bronchitis, lobar and bronchopneumonia), Genitourinary Tract Infections (e.g., cystitis, urethritis, pyelonephritis, female genital infections), Skin and Soft Tissue Infections, Bone and Joint Infections (e.g., osteomyelitis), and other infections (e.g., septic abortion, puerperal sepsis, intra-abdominal sepsis, septicemia, peritonitis and post-surgical infections). Co-amoxiclav is indicated for prophylaxis against infections which may be associated with major surgical procedures such as gastrointestinal, pelvic, head and neck, cardiac, renal, joint replacement and biliary tract.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:28:51.211748+00:00
