PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6036,Candesartan (As Cilexetil),Giran-16,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BwCIPksNcrzqgZ9dhpxxhyXHBI6YgOfM/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6036_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1BwCIPksNcrzqgZ9dhpxxhyXHBI6YgOfM_view_usp_drivesdk_cb4395fe16.pdf,page_text/DRP-6036_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1BwCIPksNcrzqgZ9dhpxxhyXHBI6YgOfM_view_usp_drivesdk_cb4395fe16.json,98e114718cf48aa84a9ac6d87238b9257c68ce7cd76680960abb31741973a9b0,504487,2,ocr,"Giran-8: A light blue colored, square and biconvex tablet, having cross breakline on both sides. Giran-16: A light pink colored, square and biconvex tablet, having cross breakline on both sides",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"It is used in the management of hypertension and may also be used in heart failure in patients with impaired left ventricular systolic function, either when ACE inhibitors are not tolerated, or in addition to ACE inhibitors.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T17:30:53.325449+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-605,Folic Acid,Folacid,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1D2-TvVGsZ4LqaW3jPXf5XE2dOD0DECcN/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-605_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1D2-TvVGsZ4LqaW3jPXf5XE2dOD0DECcN_view_usp_drivesdk_a370844da6.pdf,page_text/DRP-605_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1D2-TvVGsZ4LqaW3jPXf5XE2dOD0DECcN_view_usp_drivesdk_a370844da6.json,06da008fb9309c35e23676baef42e40554a4c65727476a7eb1916dcf318f4d3e,426208,1,digital_text,"Folic acid is a member of the vitamin B group. Folic acid is reduced in the body to tetrahydrofolate, which is a coenzyme for various metabolic processes including the synthesis of purine and pyrimidine nucleotides, and hence in the synthesis of DNA; it is also involved in some amino-acid conversions, and in the formation and utilization of formate. Deficiency, which can result in megaloblastic anemia develops when the dietary intake is inadequate (as in malnutrition), when there is malabsorption (as in sprue), increased utilization (as in pregnancy or conditions such as hemolytic anemia), increased loss (as in hemodialysis), or as a result of the administration of folate antagonists and other drugs that interfere with normal folate metabolism.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Folic acid is used in the treatment and prevention of the folate deficiency state. It is also used in women of child-bearing potential and pregnant women to protect against neural tube defects in their offspring.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:30:56.227975+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6050,Rabeprazole Sodium,Raben,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Omwm3JHdRuLixkuf1PE29rJ2nmCD3A6B/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6050_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Omwm3JHdRuLixkuf1PE29rJ2nmCD3A6B_view_usp_drivesdk_ff772dc7dc.pdf,page_text/DRP-6050_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Omwm3JHdRuLixkuf1PE29rJ2nmCD3A6B_view_usp_drivesdk_ff772dc7dc.json,ec970cfe82d95bd6b1675bd4bc3834f180405f2ab350d0f7405a8ee59337f508,1412787,1,digital_text,"Rabeprazole sodium is a proton pump inhibitor. It is a prodrug. After administration, it diffuses in to the parietal cell of the stomach and accumulates in the secretory canaliculi. In the acidic medium, Rabeprazole is converted to sulfenamide. This sulfenamide covalently interacts with sulfhydryl (SH) group in the proton pump (H+ K+ATPase) and inhibits the exchange of extracellular K+ for intracellular H+ion. Rabeprazole produces fastest acid suppression and helps in mucin synthesis. Rabeprazole Sodium ......................... 20 mg Absorption and distribution: Absolute bioavailability rabeprazole I.V. is 100%. Rabeprazole is 96.3% bound to human plasma proteins.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T17:31:06.688913+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6050-03,Rabeprazole Sodium,Prasberex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Wt7-I3Y21iU2I3dCLsGY9PmKOptpyELi/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6050-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Wt7-I3Y21iU2I3dCLsGY9PmKOptpyELi_view_usp_drivesdk_11127998ef.pdf,page_text/DRP-6050-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Wt7-I3Y21iU2I3dCLsGY9PmKOptpyELi_view_usp_drivesdk_11127998ef.json,06cee80fc57ecfd0522e21d1a55798db0fab81cc8b670ecf89a2e0ee99ba7b2e,1433987,1,digital_text,"Rabeprazole sodium is a proton pump inhibitor. It is a prodrug. After administration, it diffuses in to the parietal cell of the stomach and accumulates in the secretory canaliculi. In the acidic medium, Rabeprazole is converted to sulfenamide. This sulfenamide covalently interacts with sulfhydryl (SH) group in the proton pump (H+ K+ATPase) and inhibits the exchange of extracellular K+ for intracellular H+ion. Rabeprazole produces fastest acid suppression and helps in mucin synthesis. Pharmacodynamics: Off-White coloured powder.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of severe (erosive or ulcerative) gastroesophageal reflux diseases, active peptic ulcer disease and Zollinger-Ellison syndrome. Pharmacokinetics:",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:30:59.880527+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6050-04,Rabeprazole Sodium,Centrabez,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1eKSvSqM2-rBqF_kjglJEqwOKnh2gXK9J/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6050-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eKSvSqM2-rBqF_kjglJEqwOKnh2gXK9J_view_usp_drivesdk_01da51552a.pdf,page_text/DRP-6050-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1eKSvSqM2-rBqF_kjglJEqwOKnh2gXK9J_view_usp_drivesdk_01da51552a.json,f3ca6312ac94d209cf22a170f9cf7490335e61ff1fe4837a3c331acd06b404b8,458458,1,digital_text,,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Adult: 10-20 mg/day I.V. Duodenal ulcer: 20 mg/day I.V. for 1 month. Rabeprazole belongs to a class of antisecretory compounds (substituted benzimidazole proton-pump inhibitors) that do not exhibit anticholinergic or histamine H2-receptor antagonist properties, but suppress gastric acid secretion by inhibiting the gastric H+/K+ ATPase at the secretory surface of the gastric parietal cell. Because this enzyme is regarded as the acid (proton) pump within the parietal cell, Rabeprazole has been characterized as a gastric proton-pump inhibitor. Rabeprazole blocks the final step of gastric acid secretion. In gastric parietal cells, Rabeprazole is protonated, accumulates, and is transformed to an active sulfenamide. When studied in vitro, Rabeprazole is chemically activated at pH 1.2 with a half-life of 78 seconds. It inhibits acid transport in porcine gastric vesicles with a half-life of 90 seconds. Zollinger-Ellison syndrome: Initial dose: 60 mg/day I.V. Pregnancy: This drug should be used during pregnancy only if clearly needed. Patients receiving proton pump inhibitors, including abeprazole and warfarin concomitantly may lead to abnormal bleeding and even death because of increases in INR and R prothrombin time. Co-administration of Rabeprazole sodium results in a 33% decrease in ketoconazole levels. Rabeprazole-Digoxin co-administration results in increased trough digoxin levels in normal subjects. Not to be used if reconstituted solution contains visible solid particles.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T17:31:02.881301+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6051-01,Ketoanalogues + Essential Amino Acids,Esselogue,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GtJDCxIcdVHphoC_-Zx2wmpviO3Hmzat/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6051-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GtJDCxIcdVHphoC_-Zx2wmpviO3Hmzat_view_usp_drivesdk_25e93621c4.pdf,page_text/DRP-6051-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1GtJDCxIcdVHphoC_-Zx2wmpviO3Hmzat_view_usp_drivesdk_25e93621c4.json,af28850dd6fd03b1e3a8034ef6096a510b7e77c1cd38c467a9bc06b6c09cd02d,430114,1,digital_text,"Yellow coloured, capsule shaped both sides plain film-coated tablet.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,-Disturbed amino acid metabolism. For oral use.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:31:09.858449+00:00
