PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6108,Piperacillin (As Sodium) + Tazobactam (As Sodium),Endtaz-2.25,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1b4eQZbsXeV4mVEX62-gepeeL4DQ_IirB/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6108_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1b4eQZbsXeV4mVEX62-gepeeL4DQ_IirB_view_usp_drivesdk_a5bd05e9cb.pdf,page_text/DRP-6108_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1b4eQZbsXeV4mVEX62-gepeeL4DQ_IirB_view_usp_drivesdk_a5bd05e9cb.json,b26dcdeba472112bd881bd3519ff0cedf2b865e0af8ecf28eaa42fea5089fdc0,575263,1,digital_text,,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Appendicitis (complicated by rupture or abscess) and peritonitis caused by β-lactamase producing isolates of Escherichia coli or the following members of the Bacteroides fragilis group: B. fragilis, B. ovatus, B. thetaiotaomicron, or B. vulgatus. The individual members of this group were studied in fewer than 10 cases.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T17:32:37.912906+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6110,Methylprednisolone (as sodium succinate),Methylpred,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rX5rmSytgMUZ7nsBZbBRBgwmL5s6BwjA/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6110_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rX5rmSytgMUZ7nsBZbBRBgwmL5s6BwjA_view_usp_drivesdk_c3d3897c69.pdf,page_text/DRP-6110_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rX5rmSytgMUZ7nsBZbBRBgwmL5s6BwjA_view_usp_drivesdk_c3d3897c69.json,ea995464ee4d11f7bb91c7860b84f52a3bded4e26f0b1c09614b2ca6bf7a3215,678022,1,digital_text,"Methylprednisolone Sodium Succinate for Injection, USP sterile powder contains Methylprednisolone sodium succinate as the active ingredient. MethyIprednisolone sodium succinate occurs as a white, or nearly white, odorless hygroscopic, amorphous solid. It is very soluble in water and in alcohol; it is insoluble in chloroform and is very slightly soluble in acetone. The chemical name for methylprednisolone sodium succinate is 11β,17,21-Trihydroxy-6α-methylpregna-1,4-diene-3,20- dione 21-(sodium succinate), and the molecular weight is 496.53. Methylprednisolone sodium succinate is so extremely soluble in water that it may be administered in a small volume of diluent and is especially well suited for intravenous use in situations in which high blood levels of Methylprednisolone are required rapidly.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"When oral therapy is not feasible, and the strength, dosage form, and route of administration of the drug reasonably lend the preparation to the treatment of the condition, the intravenous or intramuscular use of Methylprednisolone Sterile powder is indicated as follows: Allergic states: Control of severe or incapacitating allergic conditions intractable to adequate trials of conventional treatment METHYLPRED METHYLPREDNISOLONE SODIUM SUCCINATE 40 mg Powder for Solution for Injection (IM/IV) CORTICOSTEROID It should be emphasized that dosages requirements are variable and must be individualized on the basis of the diseases under treatment and the response of the patients. After a favorable response is noted, the proper maintenance dosage should be determined the initial drug dosage in small decrements at appropriate time intervals until the lowest dosage which will maintain an adequate clinical response is reached. Situations which may make dosage adjustments necessary are changes in clinical status secondary to remissions or exacerbations in the disease processes, the patient’s individual drug responsive, and effect of patient exposure to stressful situations not directly related to the disease entity under treatment. In this latter situation, it may be necessary to increase the dosage of the corticosteroid for a period of time consistent with patient’s condition. If after long-term therapy the drug is to be stopped, it is recommended that it be withdrawn gradually rather than abruptly. To prepare solutions for intravenous infusion, first prepare the solution for injection as directed. The solution may than be added to indicated amounts of 5% dextrose in water, isotonic saline solution, or 5% dextrose in isotonic saline solution. In pediatric patients, the initial dose of Methylpredisolone may vary depending on the specific disease entity being treated. The range of initial doses is 0.11 to 1.6 mg/kg/day in three or four divided doses (3.2 to 48 mg/m² bsa/day). Dosage must be decreased or discontinued gradually when the drugs has been administered for more than a few days. If a period of spontaneous remission occurs in chronic condition, treatment should be discontinued. Routine laboratory studies, such as urinalysis, two-hour postprandial blood sugar, determination of blood pressure and body weight, and a chest-X-ray should be made at regular intervals during prolonged therapy. Upper GI X-rays are desirable in patients with an ulcer history or significant dyspepsia. In treatment of acute exacerbations of multiple sclerosis, daily doses of 160 mg of Methylprednisolone for a week followed by 64 mg every other day for 1 month have been shown to be effective.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:32:48.155822+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6110-03,Methylprednisolone (as sodium succinate),Methyl-One,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FIs3L1KdKFGoTTu3egwxkMAndLo4gFq3/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6110-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FIs3L1KdKFGoTTu3egwxkMAndLo4gFq3_view_usp_drivesdk_32f62c8a8e.pdf,page_text/DRP-6110-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FIs3L1KdKFGoTTu3egwxkMAndLo4gFq3_view_usp_drivesdk_32f62c8a8e.json,32ab9b23104e76991d74dbe363d802fdc811b43f759085a0f33abc1291ce074e,792895,3,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T17:32:41.337976+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6110-04,Methylprednisolone (as sodium succinate),Mepresone 40,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/14aQbBscW-G9YokCckh0xQTc-Baeca8DR/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6110-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14aQbBscW-G9YokCckh0xQTc-Baeca8DR_view_usp_drivesdk_998e4aa46a.pdf,page_text/DRP-6110-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14aQbBscW-G9YokCckh0xQTc-Baeca8DR_view_usp_drivesdk_998e4aa46a.json,fb9f823618c80b656d119af8066e41c67c9ee08b46b91a2bcc7bc7ce32619de2,1016514,1,digital_text,"Methylprednisolone Sodium Succinate for Injection, USP sterile powder contains Methylprednisolone sodium succinate as the active ingredient. MethyIprednisolone sodium succinate occurs as a white, or nearly white, odorless hygroscopic, amorphous solid. It is very soluble in water and in alcohol; it is insoluble in chloroform and is very slightly soluble in acetone. The chemical name for methylprednisolone sodium succinate is 11β,17,21-Trihydroxy-6α-methylpregna-1,4-diene-3,20- dione 21-(sodium succinate), and the molecular weight is 496.53. Methylprednisolone sodium succinate is so extremely soluble in water that it may be administered in a small volume of diluent and is especially well suited for intravenous use in situations in which high blood levels of Methylprednisolone are required rapidly.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"When oral therapy is not feasible, and the strength, dosage form, and route of administration of the drug reasonably lend the preparation to the treatment of the condition, the intravenous or intramuscular use of Methylprednisolone Sterile powder is indicated as follows: Allergic states: Control of severe or incapacitating allergic conditions intractable to adequate trials of conventional treatment in asthma, atopic dermatitis, contact dermatitis, drug hypersensitivity reactions, perennial or seasonal allergic rhinitis, serum sickness, transfusion reactions. determined the initial drug dosage in small decrements at appropriate time intervals until the lowest dosage which will maintain an adequate clinical response is reached. Situations which may make dosage adjustments necessary are changes in clinical status secondary to remissions or exacerbations in the disease processes, the patient’s individual drug responsiveness, and effect of patient exposure to stressful situations not directly related to the disease entity under treatment. In this latter situation, it may be necessary to increase the dosage of the corticosteroid for a period of time consistent with patient’s condition. If after long-term therapy the drug is to be stopped, it is recommended that it be withdrawn gradually rather than abruptly. To prepare solutions for intravenous infusion, first prepare the solution for injection as directed. The solution may then be added to indicated amounts of 5% dextrose in water, isotonic saline solution, or 5% dextrose in isotonic saline solution. In pediatric patients, the initial dose of Methylprednisolone may vary depending on the specific disease entity being treated. The range of initial doses is 0.11 to 1.6 mg/kg/day in three or four divided doses (3.2 to 48 mg/m² bsa/day). Dosage must be decreased or discontinued gradually when the drugs has been administered for more than a few days. If a period of spontaneous remission occurs in chronic condition, treatment should be discontinued. Routine laboratory studies, such as urinalysis, two-hour postprandial blood sugar, determination of blood pressure and body weight, and a chest-X-ray should be made at regular intervals during prolonged therapy. Upper GI X-rays are desirable in patients with an ulcer history or significant dyspepsia. In treatment of acute exacerbations of multiple sclerosis, daily doses of 160 mg of Methylprednisolone for a week followed by 64 mg every other day for 1 month have been shown to be effective.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T17:32:44.898380+00:00
