PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6125,Atorvastatin (as calcium),Sydenvast,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PWJ4eVFMo0LBsZgf0L4TuITUFE_l05sF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6125_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PWJ4eVFMo0LBsZgf0L4TuITUFE_l05sF_view_usp_drivesdk_01bb11b822.pdf,page_text/DRP-6125_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PWJ4eVFMo0LBsZgf0L4TuITUFE_l05sF_view_usp_drivesdk_01bb11b822.json,417d14e5b872c08008faec4336bafeb7bc045d453fe5c770d20b9d20c335faf4,2773846,6,digital_text_and_ocr,"Atorvastatin (as Calcium) 20 mg is a white, 11 mm x 6 mm, oval-shaped, biconvex, film-coated tablet, scored on one side and plain on the other side. Atorvastatin (as Calcium) 40 mg is a white, 15 mm x 6 mm, capsule-shaped, biconvex, film-coated tablet, scored on one side and plain on the other side.",6,6,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"It is used to reduce LDL - cholesterol, apolipoprotein B, and triglycerides, and to increase HDL - cholesterol in the treatment of hyperlipidaemias, including hypercholesterolaemias and combined (mixed) hyperlipidaemia (type IIa or IIb hyperlipoproteinaemias), hypertriglyceridaemia (type IV) and dysbetalipoproteinaemia (type III); can also be effective as adjunctive therapy in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia who have some LDL - receptor function.",6,6,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-07-01T16:20:26.608560+00:00
