PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6157-10,Doxofylline,Dilatair,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1EftCRKOHax8FgVnp9kmZ9xsYtCDO8avh/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6157-10_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1EftCRKOHax8FgVnp9kmZ9xsYtCDO8avh_view_usp_drivesdk_5cbcc7ce8c.pdf,page_text/DRP-6157-10_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1EftCRKOHax8FgVnp9kmZ9xsYtCDO8avh_view_usp_drivesdk_5cbcc7ce8c.json,b031af9d8eaff8c61808f3dcea9c0e1016ad9f8da74fc18b6c3cff98a63c6146,1995814,1,digital_text,"Doxofylline tablets is a xanthine derivative drug used for Obstructive Airway Diseases. Doxofylline is chemically described as 7-(1,3-dioxolan-2-ylmethyl)-1,3 dimethylpurine-2,6-dione. Its empirical formula is C␀␀H␀␀N␀O␀, its molecular weight is 266.25 g/mol, and its structural formula is: Doxofylline is a white to off white crystalline powder. It is Sparingly Soluble in water, in acetone, in ethyl acetate and in benzene; practically insoluble in ethyl ether. Doxofylline 400 mg tablets (Dilatair) are available in white, round, biconvex, uncoated tablets, plain on both sides for oral administration. It contains the following inactive ingredients: Maize Starch, Microcrystalline Cellulose, Povidone, Purified Water, Purified Talc, Magnesium Stearate, Colloidal Anhydrous Silica, Sodium Starch Glycolate.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,For maintenance therapy in patients suffering with Asthma and Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD).,1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:23:17.450513+00:00
