PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6229,Cetirizine Dihydrochloride,Alletrin,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sPje80KDLaAh8s9Vnsaa_eUuO2eORcTA/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6229_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1sPje80KDLaAh8s9Vnsaa_eUuO2eORcTA_view_usp_drivesdk_ef82bee452.pdf,page_text/DRP-6229_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1sPje80KDLaAh8s9Vnsaa_eUuO2eORcTA_view_usp_drivesdk_ef82bee452.json,864171a57af8d00685017e8aae0093541e9c45c05907bc004ba7f6cec794f20e,1444651,2,ocr,"Cetirizine diHydrochloride 5 mg / 5 mL Syrup is a clear, colorless to yellowish, strawberry-menthol flavoured syrup. Cetirizine diHydrochloride 10 mg Film-coated Tablet is a white to off-white, round, biconvex, film-coated tablet, bisected on one side, plain on the other. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This medicine contains Cetirizine, an anti-allergy. Cetirizine blocks the action of histamine, a substance that causes allergic symptoms. Cetirizine is less likely to cause drowsiness and dizziness than the older class of anti-allergy medicines.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T16:27:12.755492+00:00
