PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-630-05,Salbutamol Sulfate,Asmacaire,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1nBNrzH-W32l_-OCweA3IXCG40Op8PwUr/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-630-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1nBNrzH-W32l_-OCweA3IXCG40Op8PwUr_view_usp_drivesdk_d24c7116c9.pdf,page_text/DRP-630-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1nBNrzH-W32l_-OCweA3IXCG40Op8PwUr_view_usp_drivesdk_d24c7116c9.json,234d0fb945bede6489f687537fb1840d3c042b34989e6daa46f3e0047beaf879,1153216,4,digital_text,"A solution is clear, colourless and free from extraneous particles. Salbutamol is a direct-acting sympathomimetic with predominantly beta-adrenergic activity and a selective action on beta receptors. This results in its bronchodilating action being more prominent that its eﬀect on the heart.",3,3,DESCRIPTION:,"Salbutamol sulfate is indicated in the treatment of acute severe asthma and routine management of chronic bronchospasm unresponsive to conventional therapy. Its main clinical use is in asthma. It may be used for the symptomatic relief of an acute attack, as a part of the emergency treatment of acute severe asthma, and as a part of the long-term chronic therapy of asthma. PRESERVATIVE FREE Distributed by",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:30:47.463618+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-630-09,Salbutamol (as sulfate),Provexel NS,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BnbNsmAC5QSukcQezXtYi2tQNRh5OFzZ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-630-09_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1BnbNsmAC5QSukcQezXtYi2tQNRh5OFzZ_view_usp_drivesdk_613394cfef.pdf,page_text/DRP-630-09_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1BnbNsmAC5QSukcQezXtYi2tQNRh5OFzZ_view_usp_drivesdk_613394cfef.json,405bb316e35704f94fbe7760d5318a4b922cb7bc92f217d5efdc2b8763e3c823,692632,1,digital_text,"A solution is clear, colourless and free from extraneous particles. Salbutamol is a direct-acting sympathomimetic with predominantly beta- adrenergic activity and a selective action on beta receptors. This results in its bronchodilating action being more prominent that its eﬀect on the heart.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"Salbutamol sulfate is indicated in the treatment of acute severe asthma and routine management of chronic bronchospasm unresponsive to conventional therapy. Its main clinical use is in asthma. It may be used for the symptomatic relief of an acute attack, as a part of the emergency treatment of acute severe asthma, and as a part of the long-term chronic therapy of asthma.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:30:51.032515+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6300-01,Clonidine,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1U-wYlMh1h0_1un11cgf3qbJ3fQBS1tqo/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6300-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1U-wYlMh1h0_1un11cgf3qbJ3fQBS1tqo_view_usp_drivesdk_eba2936f9b.pdf,page_text/DRP-6300-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1U-wYlMh1h0_1un11cgf3qbJ3fQBS1tqo_view_usp_drivesdk_eba2936f9b.json,c47ef219c2eaa8c4506e842b8d83ba097dbe6cce1af9f5fad9d7d57a9135b11a,268713,1,digital_text,Clonidine hydrochloride is a white or almost white crystalline powder. It is soluble in water and in dehydrated alcohol. 5% of its solution in water has a pH of 4.0 to 5.0.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,For the management of hypertension.,1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:30:54.177462+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6300-02,Clonidine,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1pMAWCzZSOdPSaup2QCFYPXPvEnOndr0C/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6300-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1pMAWCzZSOdPSaup2QCFYPXPvEnOndr0C_view_usp_drivesdk_0b7c5ef051.pdf,page_text/DRP-6300-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1pMAWCzZSOdPSaup2QCFYPXPvEnOndr0C_view_usp_drivesdk_0b7c5ef051.json,5e0aefef0834f67edbf383674439982c9b3e437c84ba997468859206d6608bbe,565685,1,digital_text,Clonidine is a white or almost white crystalline powder. It is soluble in water and in dehydrated alcohol. 5% of its solution in water has a a pH of 4.0 to 5.0.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,For the management of hypertension.,1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:30:57.461801+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-632-01,Silymarin + Multivitamins,Liverone,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PA7GGDhQDGxWKiNGD13z_ACuWuRheysf/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-632-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PA7GGDhQDGxWKiNGD13z_ACuWuRheysf_view_usp_drivesdk_38a2e48583.pdf,page_text/DRP-632-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PA7GGDhQDGxWKiNGD13z_ACuWuRheysf_view_usp_drivesdk_38a2e48583.json,0380f197720a1f2e9576cbf69a05a718b2d6b2e7f43ebb9061ff4288a8ce191f,55908,1,digital_text,"Each dark red, oval softgel capsule is filled with yellowish brown liquid. PHARMACODYNAMICS Silymarin Plus Multivitamins refers to a group of water-soluble vitamins. It has high biological activity. Silymarin Plus Multivitamins is necessary for normal hematopoiesis (promotes maturation of erythrocytes). It is involved in the processes of transmethylation, hydrogen transport, synthesis of methionine, nucleic acids, choline, creatine. It contributes to the accumulation in erythrocytes of compounds containing sulfhydryl groups. It also has a beneficial effect on liver function and the nervous system. It activates the coagulation of blood in high doses which causes an increase in the activity of thromboplastin and prothrombin. PHARMACOKINETICS After oral administration, Silymarin Plus Multivitamins is absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract. It is then metabolized in the tissues, becoming a co-enzyme form - adenosylcobalamin which is the active form of cyanocobalamin. It is excreted in bile and urine.",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"LIVERONE (Silymarin Plus Multivitamins) is used as an aid in the treatment of the following: Chronic liver disease, fatty liver, cirrhosis of liver and toxic liver disease.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:31:00.472425+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6328,Bisacodyl,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1O6ywyqKepdAt89fYR6gYA8_TEwCEto5n/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6328_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1O6ywyqKepdAt89fYR6gYA8_TEwCEto5n_view_usp_drivesdk_c22fe93565.pdf,page_text/DRP-6328_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1O6ywyqKepdAt89fYR6gYA8_TEwCEto5n_view_usp_drivesdk_c22fe93565.json,ff1e3ce045ba944883d1dc2819f233f48e0349c96fd953c53f031939de92adee,3460435,1,ocr,"* Bisacodyl should not be taken together with products which reduce the acidity of the stomach, such as milk, antacids e.g., aluminum hydroxide and magnesium carbonate) or proton pump inhibitors (e.g., omeprazole, esomeprazole), RiteMED® Bisacodyl 5 mg delayed-release tablet is a round, biconvex, enteric-coated tablet, plain on both sides. since these medicines may reduce the tablet's coating resistance and may result to dyspepsia and gastric irritation. COLOR GUIDE WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? + Taking corticosteroids (prednisone. prednisolone, etc.) and diuretics (e.g., furosemide, mannitol) may increase the risk This product contains bisacodyl, a stimulant laxative which works by acting on the lining of the bowel (large intestine) to of electrolyte loss. stimulate movement. This movement produces soft formed stools. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Bisacodyl produces its effect 6 to 12 hours after administration. If you miss a dose, just take the next dose and the subsequent doses at the usual recommended schedule, i.e., once a day, usually at bedtime. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Do not double the dose unless recommended by a doctor.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T16:31:10.621187+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6330,Gemcitabine (as hydrochloride),Gemsafe,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mSlX1XfWPth_nKBXev_OQD0Nzp5Ww2nU/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6330_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mSlX1XfWPth_nKBXev_OQD0Nzp5Ww2nU_view_usp_drivesdk_7c55cfea0a.pdf,page_text/DRP-6330_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mSlX1XfWPth_nKBXev_OQD0Nzp5Ww2nU_view_usp_drivesdk_7c55cfea0a.json,838e0c03c1d7bf3ab17d077a958c00560c3612d2dc56c412d552437bc4ffc64b,1909991,2,digital_text,"Gemcitabine HCl is a nucleoside analogue that exhibits antitumor activity. Gemcitabine HCl is 2´- deoxy-2´, 2´- difluorocytidine monohydrochloride (β isomer). The structural formula is as follows: The empirical formula for Gemcitabine HCl is C H F N O .HCl. It has a molecular 9 11 2 3 4 weight of 299.66. Gemcitabine HCl is a white to off white solid. It is soluble in water, slightly soluble in methanol, and practically insoluble in ethanol and polar organic solvents.",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Ovarian Cancer - Gemcitabine in combination with carboplatin is indicated for the treatment of patients with advanced ovarian cancer that has relapsed at least 6 months after completion of platinum based therapy. Breast Cancer - Gemcitabine in combination with paclitaxel is indicated for the first line treatment of patients with metastatic breast cancer after failure of prior anthracycline containing adjuvant chemotherapy, unless anthracyclines were clinically contraindicated. Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer - Gemcitabine is indicated in combination with cisplatin for the first line treatment of patients with inoperable, locally advanced (Stage IIIA or IIIB), or metastatic (Stage IV) non small cell lung cancer. Pancreatic Cancer - Gemcitabine is indicated as the first line treatment for patients with locally advanced (nonresectable Stage II or Stage III) or metastatic (Stage IV) adenocarcinoma of the pancreas. Gemcitabine is also indicated for patients previously treated with 5-FU.",2,2,INDICATION(S),high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:31:23.165652+00:00
