PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6450-01,Losartan Potassium + Amlodipine (as besilate),Quezar Plus,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ceOie2r8z28rJO6aqc1FNOHgt8-e1OtX/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6450-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ceOie2r8z28rJO6aqc1FNOHgt8-e1OtX_view_usp_drivesdk_ba479b769c.pdf,page_text/DRP-6450-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ceOie2r8z28rJO6aqc1FNOHgt8-e1OtX_view_usp_drivesdk_ba479b769c.json,78deeae7e152fb74941a47d77f3162145d194f2176f1121a0085b2804a3d9a40,479584,1,digital_text,A pink colour round shaped biconvex film-coated tablet plain on both sides.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Losartan potassium /Amlodipine besilate is indicated for the treatment of hypertension, angina pectoris and mild to moderate hypertension, alone or in combination with other antihypertensives.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:18:30.072133+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6450-03,Losartan Potassium + Amlodipine (As Besilate),Co-Dilavasc,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WjUQYZIkZZ1uPoVmGq7WXnyM4cKnmqr9/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6450-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WjUQYZIkZZ1uPoVmGq7WXnyM4cKnmqr9_view_usp_drivesdk_40d3a6396d.pdf,page_text/DRP-6450-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1WjUQYZIkZZ1uPoVmGq7WXnyM4cKnmqr9_view_usp_drivesdk_40d3a6396d.json,a15ad27bc49fda7840f9e4fca5e102732c164d2197ce61007a218fb362f51d25,441194,1,digital_text,"Losartan potassium/Amlodipine besilate (Co-Dilavasc) is contraindicated in pregnancy and should be used with care, at all, during breastfeeding. Losartan potassium /Amlodipine besilate (Co-Dilavasc) should be used with caution in patients with bilateral renal artery stenosis or stenosis of an artery to single kidney, aortic valve stenosis, and hypertrophic obstructive cardiomyopathy. Symptomatic hypotension may occur after initiation of Losartan potassium/ Amlodipine besilate (Co-Dilavasc). Reduced doses must be considered in patients with hepatic impairment. Safety and efficacy has not been established. Use in Heart Failure: The usual starting and maintenance dose is one tablet once daily for most patients. The dose may be increased to 2 tablets once daily. A lower dose should be considered for patients with a history of hepatic impairment. Or as prescribed by the physician.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T18:18:33.678342+00:00
