PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6498,Pantoprazole (as Sodium),Axepron,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qUTwEm8Mzpsval1Y6YISaGFig-VGTeew/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6498_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qUTwEm8Mzpsval1Y6YISaGFig-VGTeew_view_usp_drivesdk_02c853d35b.pdf,page_text/DRP-6498_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qUTwEm8Mzpsval1Y6YISaGFig-VGTeew_view_usp_drivesdk_02c853d35b.json,0fc7fdf98ff399651478a9e1382688f2a48f53ccdd60ab4d60d7409ab8f44f02,3104929,1,digital_text,"Pantoprazole (Axepron) 40 mg for injection is white or almost white powder. PHARMACOKINETICS Pantoprazole is rapidly absorbed and peak plasma Pantoprazole concentrations occur about 2 to 2.5 hours after an oral dose. The oral bioavailability is about 77% with the enteric-coated tablet formulation, and does not vary after single or multiple doses. Pantoprazole is about 98% bound to plasma proteins. It is extensively metabolized in the liver, primarily by the cytochrome P450 isoenzyme CYP2C19, to desmethylpantoprazole; small amounts are also metabolized by CYP3A4, CYP2D6, and CYP2C9. Metabolites are excreted mainly (about 80%) in the urine, with the remainder being excreted in feces via the bile. The terminal elimination half-life is about 1 hour, and is prolonged in hepatic impairment; the half-life inpatients with cirrhosis was 3 to 6 hours. Although the elimination half-life has been reported to be 3.5 to 10 hours in slow metabolizers, minimal accumulation occurs with once-daily dosing. PHARMACODYNAMICS The fasting gastrin values increase under Pantoprazole. On short-term use, in most cases they do not exceed the upper limit of normal. During long-term treatment, gastrin levels double in most cases. An excessive increase, however, occurs only in isolated cases. As a result, a mild to moderate increase in hyperplasia). However, according to the studies conducted so far the formation of carcinoid precurcors (atypical hyperplasia) or gastric carcinoids as cannot be completely ruled out on endocrine parameters of the thyroid according to results in animal studies. During treatment with antisecretory medicinals products, serum gastrin increases in response to the decreased acid secretion. Also CgA increases due to decreased gastric acidity. The increased CgA level may interfere with investigations for neuroendocrine tumors. Available published evidence suggests that proton pump inhibitors should be discontinued between 5 days and 2 weeks prior to CgA measurements. This is to allow CgA levels that might be spuriously elevated following PPI treatment to return to reference range.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,(GERD) and a history of erosive esophagitis. demonstrated. Pathological hypersecretion including Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome Pantoprazole (Axepron) 40 mg for injection is indicated for the treatment of pathological hypersecretory condition including Zollinger-Ellison syndrome in adults.,1,1,INDICATION,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:26:04.493669+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6498-03,Pantoprazole (As Sodium),Reductazid,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Yf5pBWZI2E6dMXw8HdvdyactJebP8pW7/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6498-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Yf5pBWZI2E6dMXw8HdvdyactJebP8pW7_view_usp_drivesdk_39bc4c8e0f.pdf,page_text/DRP-6498-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Yf5pBWZI2E6dMXw8HdvdyactJebP8pW7_view_usp_drivesdk_39bc4c8e0f.json,87c0a868486e6f0e9bfe2e13687a5d428adad53701917404dad6eeeddc113738,519289,1,digital_text,,,,,Gastroesophageal re/f_lux disease associated with a history of erosive esophagitis. Pantoprazole for injection is indicated for short-term treatment (7 to 10 days) of adult patients with gastroesophageal re/f_lux disease (GERD) and a history of erosive esophagitis. Safety and eﬃcacy of Pantoprazole for injection as treatment of patients with GERD and a history or erosive esophagitis for more than 10 days have been demonstrated. Pathological hypersecretion including Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome Pantoprazole for injection is indicated for the treatment of pathological hypersecretory conditions including Zollinger-Ellison syndrome in adults.,1,1,INDICATIONS,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T18:25:51.057314+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6498-06,Pantoprazole (As Sodium),Pantohab,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dTfsVL0AADwh2moY9v_XAeVlV7DEyMCK/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6498-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dTfsVL0AADwh2moY9v_XAeVlV7DEyMCK_view_usp_drivesdk_05947c8c96.pdf,page_text/DRP-6498-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dTfsVL0AADwh2moY9v_XAeVlV7DEyMCK_view_usp_drivesdk_05947c8c96.json,d41d0afd8e3b6c0525db4aa1b4d2054427c53e3300b8cf06d9e6094652ea59f2,676829,1,digital_text,Pantohab is white or nearly white powder. [Page 2],1,1,Product Description:,Gastroesophageal Reflux Disease Associated with a History of Erosive Esophagitis Pantoprazole for Injection is indicated for short-term treatment (7 to 10 days) of adult patients with gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD) and a history of erosive esophagitis. Safety and efficacy of Pantoprazole for injection as treatment of patients with GERD and a history or erosive esophagitis for more 10 days have been demonstrated. Pathological Hypersecretion Including Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome Pantoprazole for injection is indicated for the treatment of pathological hypersecretory conditions including Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome in adults.,1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:25:54.259080+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6498-07,Pantoprazole (as sodium),Pantocent,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1v2AgnAFwmBsu5N3jx5zPOap78yMYfhM6/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6498-07_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1v2AgnAFwmBsu5N3jx5zPOap78yMYfhM6_view_usp_drivesdk_b6b879cd4d.pdf,page_text/DRP-6498-07_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1v2AgnAFwmBsu5N3jx5zPOap78yMYfhM6_view_usp_drivesdk_b6b879cd4d.json,0bd50bdf9f7edaf87ee221418db200e9dad646a6786b761cafabd003314b0548,2487557,1,digital_text,"Pantoprazole 40 mg for injection is white or almost white powder. PHARMACOKINETICS Pantoprazole is rapidly absorbed and peak plasma pantoprazole concentrations occur about 2 to 2.5 hours after an oral dose. The oral bioavailability is about 77% with the enteric-coated tablet formulation, and does not vary after single or multiple doses. Pantoprazole is about 98% bound to plasma proteins. It is extensively metabolized in the liver, primarily by the cytochrome P450 isoenzyme CYP2C19, to desmethylpantoprazole; small amounts are also metabolized by CYP3A4, CYP2D6, and CYP2C9. Metabolites are excreted mainly (about 80%) in the urine, with the remainder being excreted in faeces via the bile. The terminal elimination half-life is about 1 hour, and is prolonged in hepatic impairment; the half-life inpatients with cirrhosis was 3 to 6 hours. Although the elimination half-life has been reported to be 3.5 to 10 hours in slow metabolisers, minimal accumulation occurs with once-daily dosing. PHARMACODYNAMICS The fasting gastrin values increase under pantoprazole. On short-term use, in most cases they do not exceed the upper limit of normal. During long-term treatment, gastrin levels double in most cases. An excessive increase, however, occurs only in isolated minority of cases during long-term treatment (simple to adenomatoid hyperplasia). However, according to the studies conducted so far the formation of carcinoid precurcors (atypical hyperplasia) or gastric carcinoids as were found in animal experiment have completely ruled out on endocrine parameters of the thyroid according to results in animal studies. During treatment with antisecretory medicinals products, serum gastrin increases in response to the decreased acid secretion. Also CgA increases due to decreased gastric acidity. The increased CgA level may interfere with investigations for neuroendo- crine tumors. Available published evidence suggests that proton pump inhibitors should be discontinued between 5 days and 2 weeks prior to CgA measurements. This is to allow CgA levels that might be spuriously elevated following PPI treatment to return to reference range.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,disease (GERD) and a history of erosive esophagitis. than 10 days have been demonstrated. Pathological hypersecretion including Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome Pantoprazole 40 mg for injection is indicated for the treatment of pathological hypersecretory conditions including Zollinger-Ellison syndrome in adults.,1,1,INDICATION,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:25:58.782672+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-650,Cefaclor (As Monohydrate),Verzat-ER,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1csGp2VP1RnfW-VwR_ZkHny9Hjw0HZZku/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-650_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1csGp2VP1RnfW-VwR_ZkHny9Hjw0HZZku_view_usp_drivesdk_0a9363cd00.pdf,page_text/DRP-650_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1csGp2VP1RnfW-VwR_ZkHny9Hjw0HZZku_view_usp_drivesdk_0a9363cd00.json,8455d6ec9713fe852ba9a39c061da728f72317dc7f5a94adff975efae7d16019,662507,1,digital_text,"Characterized by orange film coated tablet, capsule shaped, biconvex and plain on both sides. Cefaclor is a semisynthetic second generation cephalosporin antibiotic. It is chemically designated as 3-chloro-7-D-(2-phenylglycinamido)-3-cephem-4-carboxylic acid monohydrate. Its empirical formula is C15H14CIN3O4S.H2O and its molecular weight is 385.8.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Cefaclor is indicated in the treatment of respiratory tract infections, acute bronchitis and acute exacerbation of chronic bronchitis, pneumonia, otitis media, pharyngitis, tonsilitis, sinusitis, urinary tract infections and skin and soft tissue infections..",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:26:07.988865+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6500,Pyridostigmine bromide,Mustone,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Fpq47vlCXlRpDPfuQgY7MSZQUcEQYXSr/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6500_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Fpq47vlCXlRpDPfuQgY7MSZQUcEQYXSr_view_usp_drivesdk_f2daf283e2.pdf,page_text/DRP-6500_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Fpq47vlCXlRpDPfuQgY7MSZQUcEQYXSr_view_usp_drivesdk_f2daf283e2.json,f004a5a06cd27443c8737be50f75569717f9fc5e949a027a23a36c3136b4ae50,1435557,1,digital_text,"A maroon colored, round, biconvex film-coated tablet. Pyridostigmine bromide (MUSTONE) is an orally active cholinesterase inhibitor. Chemically, pyridostigmine bromide is 3-hydroxy-1-methylpyridinium bromide dimethylcarbamate. Its structural formula is: Pyridostigmine bromide (MUSTONE) is available in the following forms: Syrup containing 60 mg pyridostigmine bromide per teaspoonful in a vehicle containing 5% alcohol, glycerin, lactic acid, sodium benzoate, sorbitol, sucrose, FD&C Red No. 40, FD&C Blue No. 1, flavors and water. Tablets containing 60 mg pyridostigmine bromide; each tablet also contains lactose, silicon dioxide and stearic acid. Timespan Tablets containing 180 mg pyridostigmine bromide; each tablet also contains carnauba wax, corn-derived proteins , magnesium stearate, silica gel and tribasic calcium phosphate. ACTIONS: Pyridostigmine bromide (MUSTONE) inhibits the destruction of acetylcholine by cholinesterase and thereby permits freer transmission of nerve impulses across the neuromuscular junction. Pyridostigmine bromide is an analog of neostigmine (Prostigmin), but differs from it in certain clinically significant respects; for example, pyridostigmine bromide is characterized by a longer duration of action and fewer gastrointestinal side effects.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"Myasthenia gravis, paralytic ileus, postoperative urinary retention.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:26:11.568993+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6501,Cefoxitin (As Sodium),Cefoxid,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yf0qDIgz_Lv2sN6TesSvAVIVrJoqsBxK/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6501_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1yf0qDIgz_Lv2sN6TesSvAVIVrJoqsBxK_view_usp_drivesdk_7b1f97bac6.pdf,page_text/DRP-6501_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1yf0qDIgz_Lv2sN6TesSvAVIVrJoqsBxK_view_usp_drivesdk_7b1f97bac6.json,b56584aeceb3d7b983a2864176916c4ad90397a4ef440aad8040607476d062d4,274733,2,ocr,Cefoxitin ( CEFOXID ) is a white or almost white,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION;,"Itis used principally In the treatment and prophylaxis of 14g Powder for Injection (IM/IV) anaerobic and mixed bacterial infections, especially Antibacterial (Cephalosporin) intra-abdominal and pelvic infections. Indications include endometritis. (prophylaxis at caesarean section), FORMULATION; pelvic inflammatory disease, and surgical infection Each vial contains: Cefoxitin (as sodium) perrrereeerii tt tetris) 1g (prophylaxis). It may also be used in the treatment of gonorrhoea and urinary tract infections, PRODUCT DESCRIPTION; Cefoxitin ( CEFOXID ) is a white or almost white",1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T18:26:25.700808+00:00
