PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-664,AMBROXOL HYDROCHLORIDE,AMECTUSS,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uzPtP9m13qQEXjFA5th7Uvn-XnrzW9zP/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-664_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uzPtP9m13qQEXjFA5th7Uvn-XnrzW9zP_view_usp_drivesdk_be82dba089.pdf,page_text/DRP-664_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uzPtP9m13qQEXjFA5th7Uvn-XnrzW9zP_view_usp_drivesdk_be82dba089.json,29002b50c33c5ff9749dc34abc746b2342d751db1b2f3428264a9f1a9fb65711,993464,1,digital_text,"• Ambroxol hydrochloride 15 mg / 5 mL Syrup (Amectuss) is a clear, light yellow, viscous lemon flavored syrup. • Ambroxol hydrochloride 30 mg / 5 mL Syrup (Amectuss) is a clear, light, yellow, , viscous cola flavored syrup. What is in the medicine? The medicine contains ambroxol hydrochloride which is a mucolytic agent and alters the structure of mucus to decrease its viscosity there by facilitating its removal by ciliary action or expectoration. Strength of the medicine Please see formulation. What is this medicine for? This medicine is used for the treatment of respiratory disorders associated with viscid mucus. How much and how often should you use this medicine? • Ambroxol hydrochloride 15 mg / 5 mL Syrup (Amectuss) Children 6 to 12 years old - 5 mL (1 teaspoonful) 2 to 3 times daily. Children 2 to 6 years old - 2.5 mL (1/2 teaspoon) 2 to 3 times daily. Children 1 to 2 years old - 2.5 mL (1/2 teaspoon) 2 times daily. •Ambroxol hydrochloride 30 mg / 5 mL Syrup (Amectuss) Children 6 to 12 years old - 5 mL (1 teaspoonful) 2 to 3 times daily. Children 2 to 6 years old - 2.5 mL (1/2 teaspoon) 2 to 3 times daily. Children 1 to 2 years old - 2.5 mL (1/2 teaspoon) 2 times daily. Or, as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? If you are allergic to ambroxol or any ingredient in the product. If you are pregnant or breastfeeding. Undesirable effects Rarely adverse gastrointestinal effects (nausea, abdominal pain) and allergic reactions (skin rash, facial swelling, severe respiration-impairment, temperature increase with fever) might be observed during treatment. What other medicines or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Please tell your doctor or pharmacist if you are taking/using or have recently taken/ used any other medicines, including medicines obtained without prescription. There are no clinically significant adverse interactions with other drugs. What should you do if you miss a dose? If you miss a dose just take the next prescribed dose at the usual time. Do not double the dose. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30ºC. Keep away from light. Keep bottle tightly closed. AMBROXOL Hydrochloride 15 mg / 5 mL Syrup 30 mg / 5 mL Syrup Mucolytic AMECTUSS Dimensions: 216mm x 93mm Signs and symptoms of over dosage No severe poisoning symptoms have been observed. Transient agitation and diarrhea may occur. In case of significant overdose, increased salivation may occur, as well as nausea, vomiting and hypotension. A doctor should be consulted. Usually immediate intervention such as induction of vomiting and gastric lavage is unnecessary; such management can be considered in case of acute overdose. Treatment dependent on the observed symptoms of overdosage is recommended. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dose? If you have taken more than the recommended dose, although no poisoining symptoms have been observed, consult a doctor right away. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine Do not take more than the recommended dose. Do not use after the expiry date of the label. Keep out of reach and sight of children. When should you consult a doctor? When undesirable effects occur, stop treatment and consult a doctor. Adverse Drug Reaction Reporting Statement: For suspected adverse drug reaction report to FDA: www.fda.gov.ph Availability - Ambroxol hydrochloride 15 mg / 5 mL Syrup (Amectuss) in bottles of 60 mL and 120 mL - Ambroxol hydrochloride 30 mg / 5 mL Syrup (Amectuss) in bottles of 60 mL and 120 mL Date revision of Patient Information Leaflet: 01 August 2017 Date of renewal of authorization : Ambroxol hydrochloride 15 mg / 5 mL Syrup (Amectuss) - 30 March 2016 Ambroxol hydrochloride 30 mg / 5 mL Syrup (Amectuss) - 03 February 2015 Manufactured by Am-Europharma Corporation Brgy. Saimsim, Calamba City, Laguna Distributed by",1,1,Product description,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T18:31:23.042286+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6641,Allopurinol,Opunol-100,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MLE7VXaKbvYZfilujPq8cBQzjp6gpX35/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6641_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MLE7VXaKbvYZfilujPq8cBQzjp6gpX35_view_usp_drivesdk_98a0d227d5.pdf,page_text/DRP-6641_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1MLE7VXaKbvYZfilujPq8cBQzjp6gpX35_view_usp_drivesdk_98a0d227d5.json,2b1991d0948d4f80bfb318c6a6503d4df37d72959ebae49321e70bf37695b7ec,556360,3,digital_text,"White coloured, round shaped, uncoated tablet, plain on both sides.",3,3,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Allopurinol tablets are used in: • the management of gout and other conditions associated with too much uric acid in the body, such as kidney disease, metabolic disorders, • certain skin diseases, cancer and treatment with diuretic (“water tablets”). • Allopurinol is indicated for management of 2,8- dihydroxyadenine (2,8-DHA) renal stones related to deficient activity of adenine phosphoribosyl transferase. •Allopurinol is indicated for the management of recurrent mixed calcium oxalate renal stones in the presence of hyper uricosuria, when fluid, dietary & similar measures have failed.",3,3,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:31:27.052556+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6648,Metronidazole + Miconazole nitrate,Neo-Penotran,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/19RhJQC2EUhJZtGLNBPV7p2Pp2WwpKzfy/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6648_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19RhJQC2EUhJZtGLNBPV7p2Pp2WwpKzfy_view_usp_drivesdk_9a9a07ae8e.pdf,page_text/DRP-6648_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19RhJQC2EUhJZtGLNBPV7p2Pp2WwpKzfy_view_usp_drivesdk_9a9a07ae8e.json,1b792fafb9e7047494cc5d099424b14b2e27c46900d3801199971e4a9ac90565,1157230,2,digital_text,White to slightly yellow colored ellipsoid shaped vaginal suppository,1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Metronidazole + Miconazole nitrate (Neo-Penotran®) vaginal suppository is used for local treatment of vaginalis infection with the involvement of certain fungi (eg Candida albicans), some bacteria and other pathogenic organisms (Trichomonas vaginalis). Your doctor needs to decide whether Metronidazole + Miconazole nitrate (Neo-Penotran®) is suitable for the treatment of your condition. Phenytoin and Phosphenytoin: Increase in phenytoin toxicity risk (ataxia, hyperreflexia, nystagmus, tremor) Pimozide: Increase in cardiotoxicity risk (QT prolongation, torsades de pointes, cardiac arrest), Tolterodine: Increase in tolterodine bioavailability in individuals with deficient cytochrome P450 2D6 activity, Trimetrexate: Increase in trimetrexate toxicity (bone marrow suppression, renal and hepatic dysfunction and gastrointestinal ulceration). Additional Information on Special Populations: No interaction study has been conducted on special populations Pediatric population No interaction study has been conducted on children. PREGNANCY AND LACTATION General Advice is Pregnancy category C. Women of Childbearing Potential/Birth Control (Contraception) Since the effects of active ingredients in Metronidazole + Miconazole nitrate (Neo-Penotran®) for fetus and newborn growth are not clearly known, women who will use this product should avoid pregnancy with a proper birth control method. Pregnancy Preclinical studies on animals regarding the pregnancy, embryonal/fetal growth, perinatal and/or postnatal growth are insufficient. Potential risk for human is not known. Metronidazole + Miconazole nitrate (Neo-Penotran®) should not be used in the first trimester of pregnancy. In the second and third trimesters, benefit/risk ratio should be evaluated by a physician, should not be used unless it is necessary. Lactation Breastfeeding should be discontinued, since metronidazole appears in milk. Breastfeeding can be started again 24-48 hours after the end of treatment. Reproduction/Fertility There is no evidence regarding hazardous effect on human and animal fertility when metronidazole or miconazole nitrate is administered alone. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS The frequency of adverse events listed below is defined using the following convention: Very common (≥1/10); common (≥1/100 to <1/10); uncommon (≥1/1.000 to <1/100), rare (≥1/10.000 to <1/1.000); very rare (<1/10.000), not known (cannot be estimated from the available data). The frequency of systemic side/adverse effects is very rare since after intravaginal administration of metronidazole, very low plasma levels are observed (2% -12% compared to oral route). Miconazole nitrate can cause vaginal irritation (burning, itching) as all other imidazole derivative antifungal drugs applied intravaginally (2%-6%). In vaginitis, vaginal mucosa could be inflamed, therefore vaginal burning and itching may be seen after the first suppository is applied or toward to the third day of the treatment. These symptoms are fastly reduced while the treatment continues. If there is severe irritation symptoms, serious skin rashes, swelling in the face, lips, tongue and throat, shortness of breath occur, stop the treatment and consult your physician or nearest hospital immediately. Undesirable effects regarding systemic use of active ingredients of Metronidazole + Miconazole nitrate (Neo-Penotran®) are listed below: Blood and lymphatic system disorders: Not known: Leukopenia Immune system disorders: Not known: Hypersensitivity reactions, allergic reactions (anaphylaxis may occur in severe cases) Psychiatric disorders: Uncommon: Depression Very rare: Mental alterations Nervous system disorders: Common: Dizziness, headache. Not known: Tiredness or weakness, ataxia, convulsion, peripheral neuropathy due to intensive and/or prolonged metronidazole therapy. Gastrointestinal disorders: Not known: Taste changes, metallic taste, nausea, vomiting, constipation, dry mouth, diarrhea, lack of appetite, abdominal pain or cramp, General disorders and administration site conditions: Very common: Vaginal discharge, Common: Vaginitis, vulvovaginal irritation, pelvic discomfort,",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:31:32.205569+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6650,Rosuvastatin (As Calcium),Rosuple 10,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/16Qcq7VOQ2Ci8RTi-R_Z05qr2623_lmbd/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6650_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_16Qcq7VOQ2Ci8RTi-R_Z05qr2623_lmbd_view_usp_drivesdk_b596d49e99.pdf,page_text/DRP-6650_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_16Qcq7VOQ2Ci8RTi-R_Z05qr2623_lmbd_view_usp_drivesdk_b596d49e99.json,99655900da61951ee846922aaf70bdda53133aa045cf251f799d160a55c73cfc,489670,1,digital_text,Pink round film-coated tablet mark maple leaf on one side and plain on the other side.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Hyperlipidemia and Mixed Dyslipidemia Used to reduced LDL cholesterol, apolipoprotein B, and triglycerides, and to increase HDL-cholesterol in the management of hyperlipidemias, including primary hypercholesterolaemia (type lla), mixed dyslipidaemia (type llb), and Hypertriglyceridemia (type IV), as well as in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia. It is also used to reduced the progression of atherosclerosis. Homozygous Familial Antihyperlipidemic Rosuvastatin is indicated as adjunctive therapy to the lipid-lowering treatments (e.g., LDL apheresis) or alone if such treatments are unavailable to reduce LDL-C Total-C. and ApoB in adult patients with homozygous Antihyperlipidemic. Slowing of the progression of the atherosclerosis Rosuvastatin is indicated as adjunctive therapy to diet to slow the progression of atherosclerosis in adult patients is a part of a treatment strategy to lower Total-C and V dyslipidemias. Limitations of Use The effect of Rosuvastatin on cardiovascular morbidity and mortality has not been determined. Rosuvastatin has not been studied in Fredrickson Type I. III. and V dyslipidermined.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:31:35.514766+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6660,Olanzapine,Epilanz-10,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/16ZKAoi3cMuhSCpcMROnLjDBSzthbvdxT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6660_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_16ZKAoi3cMuhSCpcMROnLjDBSzthbvdxT_view_usp_drivesdk_c82548ab80.pdf,page_text/DRP-6660_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_16ZKAoi3cMuhSCpcMROnLjDBSzthbvdxT_view_usp_drivesdk_c82548ab80.json,88c109c01fac7b177572ffacc976265876bc19d83298dfcfac5bd61f2491ba5e,1016492,1,digital_text,"Light yellow elongated, biconvex, scored film-coated tablets.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Olanzapine is used for the management of schizophrenia and for the treatment of moderate to severe mania associated with bipolar disorder.,1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:31:38.988950+00:00
