PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6701,Multivitamins + Zinc,Cecon Plus,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/15XygMw8CuKkxrhK2CWbaEaFiJv5cEE-L/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6701_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15XygMw8CuKkxrhK2CWbaEaFiJv5cEE-L_view_usp_drivesdk_ec287277a7.pdf,page_text/DRP-6701_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15XygMw8CuKkxrhK2CWbaEaFiJv5cEE-L_view_usp_drivesdk_ec287277a7.json,75fe42a1fb923e40f55b2ac1fc8d943a3ee3c21abdbe32437b0c0aeb50d12c3b,156056,1,digital_text,"It is a vitamin B-complex with zinc supplement. It is intended for use in the correction of vitamin B-complex, vitamin C, vitamin E, and zinc deficiencies. Strength of the Medicine and What is in the Medicine? Each tablet contains: Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C) .......................................................................... 750 mg Zinc ........................................................................................................... 22.5 mg di-Alpha Tocopheryl Acetate (Vitamin E) ....................................... 60 mg/ (30 IU) Thiamine HCI (Vitamin Bl) .......................................................................... 15 mg Riboflavin (Vitamin B2) ................................................................................ 15 mg Niacin (Vitamin B3) .................................................................................... 100 mg Pantothenic Acid (Vitamin BS) .................................................................... 20 mg Pyridoxine (Vitamin 86) ................................................................................ 20 mg Folic Acid (Vitamin B9) ............................................................................. 400 mcg Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12) .................................................................. 12 mcg What is this medicine used for? • Strengthens immune system that helps increase body resistance to stress, common colds, viral and other types of infections. • Antioxidant which helps protect the body from harmful effects of Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C) free radicals, toxic chemicals and pollutants • Helps in collagen synthesis • Helps in wound healing and regeneration process • Co-factor in iron metabolism which enhances absorption of iron • Required for the normal development and maintenance of the immune system; helps regulate the activity of cells involved in Zinc immune function. • A cofactor of the enzyme superoxidedismutase which is involved in the removal of harmful free radicals. Vitamin B-complex • Facilitates energy generation inside the cells and maintaining Bl, B2, B3, BS, B6, B12 brain health. • It modulates the synthesis of prostaglandins important for the body's immune response. • The major fat-soluble antioxidant which stabilizes and protects VitaminE against free radicals in the lipid (fat) phase of cells. • Helps maintain healthy skin by inhibiting the formation of lipofuscin, a brown pigmentthat accumulates in tissues during aging. How much and how often should you use this Medicine? The usual adult dosage is 1 tablet daily after food or as directed by physician. When should you not take this Medicine? It is contraindicated in patients known to be hypersensitive to any of its components. This is not recommended for use in pediatric patients. High doses of pyridoxine should be avoided during pregnancy. Care that should be taken when taking this Medicine? Keep this product out of the reach of children. Caution should be exercised when dosing ascorbic acid in patients with chronic renal failure and in patients receiving acetylsalicylic acid. FRONT ARTWORK AGG �c-p�'RP� c-'�f't'�JOB DETAILS ... v -l vr r INTEGRATED PRINTING & PACKAGING ■ Black Client PT. ABBOTT INDONESIA Project Title INSERT CECON PLUS - PH Dimension 125 x 200 mm Material HVS 60 gram Finishing Lipat 2H lV C-1622-05 Code 05-P8152C30/04 Date 10 Mei 2022 Design Marketing Undesirable Effects of this Medicine Allergic reactions, including rash, pruritus, and anaphylaxis have been reported with vitamin use. Components of this product have been associated with gastrointestinal effects such as heartburn, eructation, abdominal pain and cramps, diarrhea, vomiting, nausea and anorexia. Hepatic dysfunction with abnormal liver function tests, including hyperbilirubinemia, has been noted. Deterioration of acneiform vulgaris, or eruption of acneiform exanthema, has been noted with several components. Bright yellow urine discoloration has been reported with riboflavin usage. Niacinamide has strong vasodilator effects, most often characterized by flushing, dizziness or faintness. Peripheral sensory neuropathies have been noted with the use of pyridoxine. With ascorbic acid usage, stone formation, crystalluria and oxalosis have been reported in the literature. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? With concomitant use of niacinamide and alcohol, toxic delirium and lactic acidosis have been noted. Concomitant use of niacinamide and nicotine has been reported to cause increased flushing and dizziness. Since pyridoxine is noted to have effects on dopamine, drug interactions are possible. A drug interaction with Levodopa is noted, but can be avoided if Levodopa is given in combination with a decarboxylase inhibitor. Serum phenytoin and phenobarbital levels have been reported to decrease in patients receiving 80 to 200 mg/day of pyridoxine. Use of anticonvulsants and sulfasalazine has been associated with folate deficiency, even when folic acid is supplied orally. Prothrombin times are decreased when ascorbic acid is used concomitantly with anticoagulants. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the next dose if you missed a dose. Signs and Symptoms of Overdose High doses of individual components of this product have been associated with eczematous and exanthematous skin lesions, fatigue and insomnia. In high doses of pyridoxine, sensory neuropathy and vesicular skin lesions have been reported. In higher doses of niacinamide, liver damage, gout and ulcer formation have been noted. Vasodilatory effects such as giddiness, faintness, vasovagal attacks and anaphylactic shock have also been reported. Hemolysis has been reported at high ascorbic acid doses, especially in patients with glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase deficiency. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor. How should you keep this Medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Keep away from heat and direct sunlight. Exposure to these conditions may lead to slight discoloration. When should you consult your doctor? Consult your doctor for any signs of adverse drug reaction. ""For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph"". Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration Number: DRP-6701 Date of First Authorization: 29 June 2010 Availability: Foil strip x G's (Box of G's and 30's); Physician's sample, foil strip x 2's Manufactured by: PT. ABBOTT INDONESIA JI. Raya Jakarta-Begor Km. 37 Kel. Sukamaju, Kee. Cilodong, Depok Jawa Barat, Indonesia Imported and Distributed by: ABBOTT LABORATORIES Venice Corporate Center, 8 Turin St. McKinley Town Center, Taguig Metro Manila, Philippines Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: June 2021 REVERSE Approval Notes PPIC Customer <:t � m u N Lf) ,-1 00 c.. Ji 0 Revision No. 1 [Page 2]",1,1,Description of the product -,"Components of this product have been associated with gastrointestinal effects such as heartburn, eructation, abdominal pain and cramps, diarrhea, vomiting, nausea and anorexia. Hepatic dysfunction with abnormal liver function tests, including hyperbilirubinemia, has been noted. Deterioration of acneiform vulgaris, or eruption of acneiform exanthema, has been noted with several components. Bright yellow urine discoloration has 