PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6837,Azithromycin (as Dihydrate),Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cXA-1jxn9WwR-ZZJaAqpkvd5yCOCalqS/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6837_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cXA-1jxn9WwR-ZZJaAqpkvd5yCOCalqS_view_usp_drivesdk_fbb75a99cd.pdf,page_text/DRP-6837_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cXA-1jxn9WwR-ZZJaAqpkvd5yCOCalqS_view_usp_drivesdk_fbb75a99cd.json,21f174503d42f01c4dbcdde8892e8b3505b4013a34fab5f5c0869e6376664fb7,4600658,2,ocr,Azithromycin 500 mg Tablet is a white to off-white cherry flavored powder. White to off-white cherry- flavored suspension when reconstituted.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"‘ di ycin isa ig containing or azalide with wide spectrum of activity that has been used in the treatment of a wide variety of infections caused by susceptible organisms. It is given in the treatment of respiratory tract infections (including otitis media), in skin and soft-tissue infections, and in uncomplicated genital infections. Azithromycin may also be used for the prophylaxis, and as a component of regimens in the treatment of Mycobacterium avium complex (MAC). It is used in some countries for the prophylaxis of endocarditis in at-risks patients unable to take penicillin. It is also used in the management of trachoma and typhoid.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T18:40:54.380010+00:00
