PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6855,Ethambutol Hydrochloride,NULL,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xy4ZGexR5ptCCc42TozZ0Ekk7EDanX1B/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6855_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xy4ZGexR5ptCCc42TozZ0Ekk7EDanX1B_view_usp_drivesdk_266eb733c2.pdf,page_text/DRP-6855_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xy4ZGexR5ptCCc42TozZ0Ekk7EDanX1B_view_usp_drivesdk_266eb733c2.json,4c65c3778c01bc2721d3ca9c9ace4427aa9d854b0bc15974cec7f91a7d62a53c,3218881,1,digital_text,"Ethambutol hydrochloride is indicated in the treatment of tuberculosis. Chemically, Ethambutol hydrochloride is 2,2' – (ethylenediimino) bis [(2S) – butan – 1 – ol] dihydrochloride. Its molecular formula is C H Cl NO, and molecular weight is 277.2.10 26 12 2 2",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"Ethambutol Tablets 400 mg is indicated in combination with other anti-tuberculosis agents for the treatment of all forms of tuberculosis caused by Mycobacterium tuberculosis. Ethambutol Tablets 400 mg is also used in the treatment of infections caused by atypical mycobacteria, such as Mycobacterium avium complex.",1,1,INDICATIONS AND USAGES:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:42:10.242931+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6900,VALSARTAN + AMLODIPINE Â (as besilate),VALSAR PLUS,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/181xDd1HwrSz1YOEAXNJ9YE18zlD9Ws0w/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6900_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_181xDd1HwrSz1YOEAXNJ9YE18zlD9Ws0w_view_usp_drivesdk_df6107272e.pdf,page_text/DRP-6900_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_181xDd1HwrSz1YOEAXNJ9YE18zlD9Ws0w_view_usp_drivesdk_df6107272e.json,3eba44fa734beeb506f06a3d85376c501b5efd79255e365fe94977cd29ea1e72,469141,2,digital_text,"Valsar Plus is a fixed combination of Amlodipine and Valsartan. Valsar Plus contains the besilate salt of Amlodipine, a dihydropyridine calcium-channel blocker (CCB). Amlodipine besilate is a white to pale yellow crystalline powder, slightly soluble in water and sparingly soluble in Ethanol. Amlodipine besilate’s chemical name is 3-Ethyl-5-Methyl(4RS)-2-[(2-Aminoethoxy)Methyl]-4- (2-Chlorophenyl)-6-Methyl-1,4-dihydropyridine-3,5-dicarboxylate Benzenesulphonate; its empirical formula is C H CN O C H O S and its molecular weight is 567.1.20 25 l 2 5 6 6 3 Valsartan is a non-peptide, orally active, and specific angiotensin II antagonist acting on the AT 1 receptor subtype. Valsartan is a white to practically white fine powder, soluble in Ethanol and Methanol and slightly soluble in water. Valsartan's chemical name is N-(1-Oxopentyl)-N-[[2'-(1H- Tetrazol-5-yl)[1,1'-Biphenyl]-4-yl]Methyl]-L-Valine; its empirical formula is C H N O and its 24 29 5 3 molecular weight is 435.5.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of hypertension, to lower blood pressure in patients not adequately controlled on monotherapy.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:42:13.470535+00:00
