PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6910,Orlistat,Morlesfat,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1a-AYh8DY1nekQtIwzgsTL6hbIwAit3Ih/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6910_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1a-AYh8DY1nekQtIwzgsTL6hbIwAit3Ih_view_usp_drivesdk_565f23967a.pdf,page_text/DRP-6910_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1a-AYh8DY1nekQtIwzgsTL6hbIwAit3Ih_view_usp_drivesdk_565f23967a.json,55971e2aace79f4c27f6e0908c28cd9685613b6e1c90a40801aabfe9b01e4ea2,2952247,2,ocr,"Orlistat 120 mg Capsule is a white to off-white granules contained in a white body / powder biuecap#1 WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Orlistat is a medicine used to treat obesity. It works in your digestive system to block about one-third of the fat in the food you eat from being di . Orlistat attaches to the enzymes in your digestive system (lipases) and blocks them from fat breaking —s some of the fat you have eaten ang your meal. The undigested by bedandis dby your STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE? Each capsule contains 120 mg of Orlistat. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Orlistat, in conjuction with a mildly hypocaloric diet, is indicated for treatment of obese patients or overweight patients with associated comorbidities. HOW MUCHAND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOUUSE THIS MEDICINE? The recommended dose of Orlistat is one 120 mg capsule with each main meal (during or up to one hour after the meal). If a meal is missed or contains no fat, the dose of Orlistat may be omitted. The patient should be on a nutritionally balanced, ny 1 diet that ‘. ine 30% of calories from fat. The on intake of fat, itn liesehi y and pi teats fictias bear’ over three main Dose above 120 mg three times daily have not been shown to provide additional benefit. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Orlistat should not be given to patients with ch iat rption syr or cholestasis and in patients with known itivity to any IP its of the drug",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T18:42:45.562275+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6922,Mayor-40,Atorvastatin (As Calcium),PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/18ynDSptIcO4Snkn6l_jAVf2wfuaN96Su/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6922_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18ynDSptIcO4Snkn6l_jAVf2wfuaN96Su_view_usp_drivesdk_ca195a91da.pdf,page_text/DRP-6922_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18ynDSptIcO4Snkn6l_jAVf2wfuaN96Su_view_usp_drivesdk_ca195a91da.json,012654994c92593529cb7041ade06f31ca87927968659741d6b72565576443c8,480695,1,digital_text,"White colored, biconvex round shaped, film-coated tablet.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Hypercholesterolaemia Atorvastatin is indicated as an adjunct to diet for reduction of elevated total cholesterol (total-C), LDL-cholesterol (LDL- C), apolipoprotein B, and triglycerides in adults, adolescents and children aged 10 years or older with primary hypercholesterolemia including familial hypercholesterolemia (heterozygous variant) or combined (mixed) hyperlipidemia (Corresponding to Types IIa and IIb of the Fredrickson classification) when response to diet and other nonpharmacological measures is inadequate. Atorvastatin is also indicated to reduce total-C and LDL-C in adults with homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia as an adjunct to other lipid-lowering treatments (e.g. LDL apheresis) or if such treatments are unavailable. Prevention of cardiovascular disease Prevention of cardiovascular events in adult patients estimated to have a high risk for a first cardiovascular event, as an adjunct to correction of other risk factors.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:42:56.708970+00:00
