PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6950-05,Cefoperazone (as Sodium) + Sulbactam (as Sodium),Cefsukeer,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hdOWZcH43z8y5UjsWS25VyRxrexdyZVX/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6950-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hdOWZcH43z8y5UjsWS25VyRxrexdyZVX_view_usp_drivesdk_406a5258fd.pdf,page_text/DRP-6950-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hdOWZcH43z8y5UjsWS25VyRxrexdyZVX_view_usp_drivesdk_406a5258fd.json,6930d6e14aab6ebdabc8735266daa219d01a0e03dac7e8519c0c7b1b4a7e6392,977436,1,digital_text,"Cefoperazone + Sulbactam for Injection is white crystalline powder filled in plain glass vial and it contains Cefoperazone Sodium USP and Sulbactam Sodium USP as its active ingredient. Chemical name of Cefoperazone Sodium USP is Sodium (6R, 7R )-7-[(R)-2-(4-ethyl-2,3-dioxo-1-piperazinecarboxamido)-2-(p- hydroxyphenyl)acetamido-3-[[(1-methyl-H-tetrazol-5-yl)thio]methyl]-8-oxo-5-thia-1-azabicyclo[4.2.0]oct-2- ene-2-carboxylate and Sulbactam Sodium USP is Sodium (2S, 5R )-3,3-dimethyl-7-oxo-4-thia-1- azabicyclo[3.2.0]heptane-2-carboxylate 4,4-dioxide. Its molecular structure is as mentioned below: All ADRs listed in the label are presented by MedDRA SOC and are presented in the order of clinical importance.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION :,"• Peritonitis, cholecystitis, cholangitis, and other intra-abdominal infections • Meningitis • Pelvic inflammatory disease, endometritis, gonorrhea, and other infections of the genital tract Each vial contains: Cefoperazone Sodium USP Equivalent to Cefoperazone .............1 g Sulbactam Sodium USP Equivalent to Sulbactam .......... 500 mg",1,1,INDICATIONS :,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:44:53.131211+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6951,Voriconazole,Vorzole,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1g6MbljI0RckZkxVYtmjydy8mbrAi2s-T/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6951_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1g6MbljI0RckZkxVYtmjydy8mbrAi2s-T_view_usp_drivesdk_26002cb355.pdf,page_text/DRP-6951_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1g6MbljI0RckZkxVYtmjydy8mbrAi2s-T_view_usp_drivesdk_26002cb355.json,9b94dcdf577294db929691de324cba14b89d33d9d4dcfd38ba433ee44b9e6542,2612428,2,digital_text_and_ocr,"White to pale yellow lyophilized powder/cake. When the recommended intravenous or oral loading dose regimens are administered to healthy subjects, peak plasma concentrations close to steady state are achieved within the first 24 hours of dosing. The volume of distribution at steady state for voriconazole is estimated to be 4.6 L/kg, suggesting extensive distribution into tissues. Plasma protein binding is estimated to be 58%. Antifungal spectrum: In vitro studies showed that voriconazole is metabolized by the hepatic cytochrome P450 enzymes. CYP2C19, CYP2C9, and CYP3A4. The inter- individual variability of voriconazole pharmacokinetics is high. In vivo studies indicated that CYP2C19 is significantly involved in the metabolism of voriconazole. The primary mode of action of voriconazole is inhibition of fungal cytochrome P450-mediated 14 alpha lanosterol demethylation, an essential step in ergosterol biosynthesis. The accumulation of 14 alpha-methyl sterols correlates with the subsequent loss of ergosterol in the fungal cell wall and may be responsible for the antifungal activity of voriconazole. It is shown to be more selective for fungal cytochrome P450 enzymes than for various mammalian cytochrome P450 enzyme systems. Other treated fungal infections (with partial or complete response) included isolated cases of Alternaria spp., Blastomyces dermatitidis, Blastoschizomyces capitatus, Cladosporium spp.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Lactation: The excretion of voriconazole into breast milk has not been over 1 to 2 hours. Voriconazole requires reconstitution and dilution prior to Voriconazole is indicated for use in patients 12 years of age and older in the investigated. Breastfeeding must be stopped on initiation of treatment with administration as an intravenous infusion. Voriconazole injection is not meant for treatment of the following fungal infections: voriconazole. bolus injection. 1. Treatment of invasive aspergillosis. Dermatological reactions: Patients have developed exfoliative cutaneous The vial constituents are reconstituted with 19 mL of water for injection to obtain a 2. Treatment of fluconazole resistant serious invasive Candida infections reactions, such as Stevens-Johnson syndrome, during treatment with clear solution containing 10 mg/mL of voriconazole and an extractable volume of (including C. krusei). voriconazole. If patients develop a rash, they should be monitored closely and 20 mL. For administration, the required volume of the reconstituted solution is 3. Treatment of candidaemia in non-neutropenic patients voriconazole discontinued if lesions progress. In addition, voriconazole has been added to a recommended compatible infusion solution to obtain a final 4. Serious fungal infections caused by Scedosporium apiospermum and associated with photosensitivity skin reactions, especially during long term Voriconazole solution containing 2-3 mg/mL. The final Voriconazole solution must Fusarium solani, in patients intolerant of, or refractory to, other therapy. therapy. be infused over 1-2 hours at a maximum rate of 3 mg/kg per hour. Specimens for fungal culture and other relevant laboratory studies (including histopathology) should be obtained prior to therapy to isolate and identify",2,2,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T18:45:09.199170+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6958,Zinc Sulfate Monohydrate,Ammuno-Z,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/126duteyMMTyayopO-Ovo6elha7NjkvHz/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6958_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_126duteyMMTyayopO-Ovo6elha7NjkvHz_view_usp_drivesdk_6f8fa01071.pdf,page_text/DRP-6958_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_126duteyMMTyayopO-Ovo6elha7NjkvHz_view_usp_drivesdk_6f8fa01071.json,dfa39f9acd76405023831e19de0bd5053be1e00b16da4b333baf82d6ac8db96b,132801,1,digital_text,,,,,"Water soluble zinc supplement are used to correct zinc deficiency; for example, in malabsorption syndromes, during parental feeding, in conditions with increased body losses (trauma, burns and protein-losing states) and in acrodermatitis enteropathica (a rare disorder characterized by severe zinc deficiency).",1,1,INDICATION:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T18:45:22.457315+00:00
