PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6980,Ibuprofen,Pain Gard,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dXRSb6rT4vZABKcPBg4t4e9giZePxjvw/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6980_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dXRSb6rT4vZABKcPBg4t4e9giZePxjvw_view_usp_drivesdk_93b115898f.pdf,page_text/DRP-6980_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dXRSb6rT4vZABKcPBg4t4e9giZePxjvw_view_usp_drivesdk_93b115898f.json,5c306b100b09e1278c90a86b8192f8b1b43cc39d07320cec81c2864eb9932aab,1652506,1,ocr,"toxicity is uncommon, but giving activated charcoal followed by supportive measures is Ibuprofen (PAIN GARD) is a white to off-white, round biconvex tablet, with score on one side and recommended if the quantity ingested within the previous hours exceeds 400 mg/kg. company logo on the other side, blister pack by 20's, box of 100's. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? What is in the medicine? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor The medicine contains Ibuprofen. Ibuprofen belongs to a group of Non-Steroidal immediately. Anti-inflammatory Drugs (NSAID’s) which has an analgesic (relieves pain), anti-inflammatory (redness or swelling), and antipyretic (reduce fever) properties. It works by blocking your body's How should you keep this medicine? production of certain natural substances that cause inflammation. This effect helps to decrease Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C swelling, pain, or fever. Protect from direct sunlight. Keep out from reach of children. Strength of the medicine: When should you consult your doctor? Each tablet contains 200 mg Ibuprofen, USP If symptoms persist and any undesirable effect occurs, consult your doctor. What is this medicine used for? “For suspected adverse drug reaction report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph”. Used in the management of mild to moderate pain and inflammation in conditions such as Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. dysmenorrhea, headache including migraine, post operative pain, dental pain, musculoskeletal and joint disorders such as ankylosing spondylitis, osteoarthritis; and rheumatoid arthritis DRP-6980 including juvenile idiopathic arthritis; periarticular disorders such as bursitis and tenosynovitis; and soft-tissue disorders such as sprains and strains. It is also used to reduce fever. Date of Renewal Authorization: March 20, 2020 How much and how often should you use this medicine? Patient Information Leaflet date of revision: April 21, 2020 1 tablet every 4-6 hours. Maximum of 6 tablets every 24 hours. When should you not take this medicine? -If you are allergic to aspirin and other NSAID’s, specifically Ibuprofen. -Do not use this medicine just before or after heart bypass surgery (coronary artery bypass graft, or CABG). Manufactured by the Distributed by: Marketing Authorization Holder: Fp FULL HEALT H INTERNATIONAL PHARMA Care that should be taken when taking this medicine:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T18:46:32.549050+00:00
