PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6985,LETROZOLE,FEMARA,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1aa6u-BFkP2ZWKjeX4idfDAophSg348Jo/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6985_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1aa6u-BFkP2ZWKjeX4idfDAophSg348Jo_view_usp_drivesdk_27198ec4f6.pdf,page_text/DRP-6985_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1aa6u-BFkP2ZWKjeX4idfDAophSg348Jo_view_usp_drivesdk_27198ec4f6.json,74add6126056c3bbe2dbbff926854b000f007b9e520366f1a0554913c180e4fe,217827,20,digital_text,"Pharmaceutical form Film-coated tablets. Coated tablet, dark yellow, round, slightly bico nvex with bevelled edges. One side bears the imprint “FV”, the other “CG”. Active substance 4,4'-[(1H-1,2,4-triazol-1-yl)-methylene]bis-benzonitrile (INN/USAN= letrozole). Each film-coated tablet contains 2.5 mg letrozole. Excipients Colloidal anhydrous si lica, microcristalline cellulose, lactose monohydrate, magnesium stearate, maize starch, sodium starch glycollate, hydroxypropyl methylcellulose, polyethylene glycol 8000, talc, titanium dioxide (E 171), iron oxide yellow (E 172). Pharmaceutical formulations may vary between countries.",1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,"Letrozole is not indicated in hormone receptor negative disease. Letrozole is indicated in: • Adjuvant treatment of postmenopausal women with hormone receptor positive invasive early breast cancer. • Extended adjuvan t treatment of invasive early breast cancer in post-menopausal women who have received prior standard adjuvant tamoxifen therapy for five years. • First-line treatment in postmenopausal women with hormone-dependent advanced breast cancer. • Advanced breast cancer after relapse or disease progression, in women with natural or artificially induced postmenopausal endocrine status, who have previously been treated with anti -estrogens. • Neo-adjuvant treatment of postmenopausal women with hormone receptor positive, H ER-2 negative breast cancer where chemotherapy is not suitable and immediate surgery not indicated . Letrozole [Page 2]",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:46:48.634120+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6986,Ibuprofen,Pain Gard,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uSqlyOzGbeCy_mafrjhTDCc7WXUceO9B/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6986_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uSqlyOzGbeCy_mafrjhTDCc7WXUceO9B_view_usp_drivesdk_270b749b8d.pdf,page_text/DRP-6986_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uSqlyOzGbeCy_mafrjhTDCc7WXUceO9B_view_usp_drivesdk_270b749b8d.json,0ba183cc136e4ba73777178e22a99e438c8faa12f542dcb5c152bc7ce553bb36,2927059,1,ocr,"NSAID’s may increase the effects of phenytoin and sulfonylurea antidiabetics. Ibuprofen (PAIN GARD) is a white capsule-shaped tablet with score on one side and company logo Use of more than one NSAID together (including aspirin) should be avoided because of the increased risk of engraved on the other side. adverse effects. The risk of gastrointestinal bleeding and ulceration associated with NSAIDs is increased when used with corticosteroids, the SSRIs, the SNRI venflaxacin, the antiplatelets clopidogrel and ticlopidine,",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C and protect from direct sunlight. It used in the management of mild to moderate pain and inflammation in conditions such as dysmenorrhea, headache including migraine, post operative pain, dental pain, musculoskeletal and joint disorders such as “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph.” ankylosing spondylitis, osteoarthritis, and rheumatoid arthritis including juvenile idiopathic arthritis, peri- articular disorders such as bursitis and tenosynovitis, and soft tissue disorders such as sprains and strains. It Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction is also used to reduce fever. REGISTRATION NUMBER: DRP-6986",1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T18:47:01.332321+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-6987,Montelukast (as sodium),Dironest,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RjJ7SW3vHVf519k7i4Ux6VUeihEwfAlF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-6987_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RjJ7SW3vHVf519k7i4Ux6VUeihEwfAlF_view_usp_drivesdk_0d082ea730.pdf,page_text/DRP-6987_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RjJ7SW3vHVf519k7i4Ux6VUeihEwfAlF_view_usp_drivesdk_0d082ea730.json,4982b663c96b136d0ab351e58ca6563d23e6ab47341e7d49f2e4b5ef2594362f,1114812,1,ocr,"Hovite syrup is multivitamin supplement for the management of vitamin deficiency states in children above one year of age and adults. PHARMACOLOGY Pharmacodynamics Multivitamin syrup contains Vitamin A concentrate (oily form), a fat soluble vitamin is required for vision and growth. Colecalciferol (Vitamin D,) is required for ensuring proper calcium absorption and utilization. Thiamine (Vitamin B,) is a member of Vitamin B complex playing a vital role in carbohydrate metabolism. Riboflavin and Nicotinamide is an important member of Vitamin B complex functioning as coenzymes in cellular oxidative processes. D-panthenol, member of Vitamin B complex is vital for amino acid and fatty acid metabolism. Pyridoxine plays a vital role in amino acid metabolism. Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C) is essential for synthesis of intercellular matrix collagen and it also plays an important rote as an antioxidant. Tocopheryl Acetate (Vitamin E) is an important antioxidant agent, which helps the body to take care of the oxidative stresses. Cyanocobalamin is essentially for the formation of blood and has a key role in the normal functioning of the brain and nervous sytem. Pharmacokinetics Colecalciferol (Vitamin D,) is required for ensuring proper calcium absorption and utilization. Thiamine (Vitamin B,) is a member of Vitamin B complex playing a vital role in carbohydrate 260 metabolism. D-panthenol, member of Vitamin B complex is vital for amino acid and fatty acid mm metabolism. Pyridoxine plays a vital role in amino acid metabolism.",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Multivitamin Syrup used for the treatment and prevention of vitamin A, B, C, D, E deficiencies.",1,1,INDICATIONS AND USAGE,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T18:47:11.533264+00:00
