ine? January 30, 2021 If you are allergic to any of the components in the product. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: = Do not take more than the recommended dose. = Do not use after the expiry date stated on the label. Manufactured by the Undesirable effects of this medicine: Marketing Authorization Holder: Riboflavin (Vitamin B2) - Large doses may result to bright yellow discoloration in urine. Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12) - Allergic hypersensitivity reactions have occured rarely that includes rash,",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T18:48:35.425745+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7002,Valsartan + Amlodipine (As Besilate),Amloval 160/10,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1K_64qpXyoRGpaR2nZTIdSKorhlkkYBbS/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7002_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1K_64qpXyoRGpaR2nZTIdSKorhlkkYBbS_view_usp_drivesdk_78499867dc.pdf,page_text/DRP-7002_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1K_64qpXyoRGpaR2nZTIdSKorhlkkYBbS_view_usp_drivesdk_78499867dc.json,4e4dfbbcd44c996ed60306549e915b219ec50574c350f20e3a5fab425e1d73f4,362543,1,digital_text,"Valsartan + Amlodipine (as Besilate) (Amloval 80/5) 80 mg / 5 mg Film-Coated Tablet is a yellow to dark yellow colored, oval shaped, beveled edge, biconvex film-coated tablet debossed with ""1071"" on one side and plain on other side. Valsartan + Amlodipine (as Besilate) (Amloval 160/5) 160 mg / 5 mg Film-Coated Tablet is a yellow to dark yellow colored, oval shaped, beveled edge, biconvex film-coated tablet debossed with ""1072"" on one side and plain on other side. Valsartan + Amlodipine (as Besilate) (Amloval 160/10) 160 mg / 10 mg Film-Coated Tablet is a light peach colored, oval shaped, beveled edge, biconvex film-coated tablet with breakline on both side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Treatment of essential hypertension. It is indicated in patients whose blood pressure is not adequately controlled on valsartan or amlodipine monotherapy.,1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:48:38.704693+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7004,Cefalexin (As Monohydrate),None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mxetlQqawne6_Q_DTYEGZwmpv9tO71eF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7004_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mxetlQqawne6_Q_DTYEGZwmpv9tO71eF_view_usp_drivesdk_192f88d5cd.pdf,page_text/DRP-7004_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1mxetlQqawne6_Q_DTYEGZwmpv9tO71eF_view_usp_drivesdk_192f88d5cd.json,e753d34b1f52b399755d5c5fb3e85c85e94bf8b4e787fa467b20b98c4c3d5158,1965101,1,ocr,Cefalexin is a fine white powder which becomes a light pink suspension with a strawberry flavor when reconstituted with water.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For the treatment of the respiratory, gastrointestinal and urinary tract infections, as well as otic, bone, skin and soft tissues, including penicillinase producing Staphylococcus aureus infection.",1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T18:48:55.524522+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7009-01,Doxofylline,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/17jGWmBbXbYH3cGTGKd-7PFHHxgoP3kiS/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7009-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17jGWmBbXbYH3cGTGKd-7PFHHxgoP3kiS_view_usp_drivesdk_f4c0265b07.pdf,page_text/DRP-7009-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17jGWmBbXbYH3cGTGKd-7PFHHxgoP3kiS_view_usp_drivesdk_f4c0265b07.json,eb2a5378e002e0fcf4e1c9c6076acd8b77deadcb455076277033cf4543358079,80130,1,digital_text,,,,,"Doxofylline is indicated for the treatment of COPD, bronchial asthma and pulmonary disease with spastic bronchial component. Dosage: Tablet: Elderly Patients: 1/2 tablet two or three times daily. Adults: 1 tablet two or three times daily. Or as prescribed by a physician. Clinical Trials: Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease In an open -label, non-comparative, multi-center clinical study in 169 Filipino patients, Doxofylline (ANSIMAR ®) administered as 400 mg tablet twice daily for eight (8) weeks, was better tolerated by elderly COPD patients while providing the same effective bronchodilatory effect as other methylxanthine preparations. The results of this study indicate that Doxofylline (ANSIMAR®) is an effective and well-tolerated agent for Filipino patients with stable chronic obstructive pulmonary disease.",1,1,Indications:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T18:48:59.206175+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7015,Ambroxol Hydrochloride,Ambrolem,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1aqVW8G14gGMxHgqQ0OomSKbrl71ZqSpF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7015_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1aqVW8G14gGMxHgqQ0OomSKbrl71ZqSpF_view_usp_drivesdk_1c11462ae7.pdf,page_text/DRP-7015_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1aqVW8G14gGMxHgqQ0OomSKbrl71ZqSpF_view_usp_drivesdk_1c11462ae7.json,195b89535763da3b979f2e8db7c3830a7079f9fa88246aa6eec95ba5b7dcce10,1150883,1,ocr,"Ambroxol Hydrochloride (AMBROLEM™) is a white, round biconvex tablet, scored on one side with company logo on the other side, contained in a by 20's blister, box of 100's. What is in the medicine? Ambrolem contains Ambroxol Hydrochloride which is a mucolytic agent used in the treatment of respiratory disorders associated with productive cough. Ambroxol stimulates the fluid secretion in the respiratory tract to make mucus (sputum) less thick and sticky and easier to cough up. It is helpful if you have a long-term (chronic) cough because they help you cough up mucus from your lungs. Strength of the medicine: Each tablet contains 30 mg Ambroxol Hydrochloride, PP. What is this medicine used for? Ambroxol Hydrochloride is a mucolytic agent used in the treatment of respiratory disorders associated with viscid or excessive mucus. This medicine is used for the relief of cough secondary to acute and chronic diseases of the respiratory tract accompanied by excessive lung secretions such as chronic bronchitis, asthmatic bronchitis and bronchial asthma. How much and how often should you use this medicine? 1 tablet (30 mg) to be given three times daily, or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? If you are allergic to Ambroxol Hydrochloride or any component of this medicine. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: -It should be given care to patients who are pregnant or breastfeeding unless advised by a physician. -Severe skin lesions such as SJS (Stevens-Johnson Syndrome) and Lyell's syndrome have been reported rarely with the administration of mucolytics such as Ambroxol. These may be due to the severity of the underlying disease or concomitant medication. If new skin or mucosal lesions appear, discontinue Ambroxol and consult a physician immediately. -Do not use after the expiry date stated on the label. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Ambroxol is generally well tolerated. Hypersensitivity reaction such as mild stomach disturbance such as_ heartburn, dyspepsia, diarrhea, nausea and vomiting may occur. Rash/urticaria, angioedema (rapid swelling of the skin), anaphylactic reactions and other allergic reactions have been reported. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? There were no reports of adverse drug interactions with other medications. Administration of Ambroxol with antibiotics (Amoxicillin, Cefuroxime, Erithromycin) leads to higher antibiotic concentration in bronchopulmonary secretions and in sputum. Tell your doctor about other medicines you are taking, especially other medicines for cough and cold or allergy. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: Overdose symptoms of Ambroxol leads to extension of undesirable effects such as heartburn, dyspepsia, diarrhea, nausea and vomiting, and other anaphylactic reactions. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? If symptoms persist, consult your doctor “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph.” Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration number: DRP-7015 Date of Renewal Authorization: May 9, 2023 Patient Information Leaflet Date of Revision: May 20, 2024 Manufactured by the Marketing Authorization Holder: = Distributed by: ¥",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T18:49:08.772701+00:00
