PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7035,Clomifene Citrate,Ovulant,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1o7rr4uck_9nNfAxni8VuwuLzEB8ClPp1/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7035_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1o7rr4uck_9nNfAxni8VuwuLzEB8ClPp1_view_usp_drivesdk_ac4f2c3e65.pdf,page_text/DRP-7035_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1o7rr4uck_9nNfAxni8VuwuLzEB8ClPp1_view_usp_drivesdk_ac4f2c3e65.json,f03655f3f19b002d8c1f761db58f47ba454e3fecc5c61e8429928c6535412fe5,603305,1,digital_text,"Clomifene is a selective estrogen receptor modulator (SERM) that increases production of gonadotropins by inhibiting negative feedback on the hypothalamus. It is used mainly in female infertility, mainly as ovarian stimulator, such as part of an in vitro fertilization procedure. Characterized by white to off-white uncoated tablet, round, flat, plain on one side and bisected on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,For the treatment of anovulatory infertility.,1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:49:52.306686+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7038-04,Pregabalin,Prebawell-75,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CsqbmaIa4RJLd3p-fkixURknD8n829n8/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7038-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1CsqbmaIa4RJLd3p-fkixURknD8n829n8_view_usp_drivesdk_c8f3b00847.pdf,page_text/DRP-7038-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1CsqbmaIa4RJLd3p-fkixURknD8n829n8_view_usp_drivesdk_c8f3b00847.json,7c9d245ed1c089f1ae1a9e7cd57c27f70620f0da1d49aac6d9018c95d6f3e4d8,447635,1,digital_text,"Blue/White colored hard gelatin capsule of size ""2” containing white crystalline powder.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Pregabalin is indicated for the management of neuropathic pain with diabetic peripheral neuropathy, management of postherpetic neuralgia, adjunctive therapy for adult patients with partial onset seizures, management of fibromyalgia, and management of neuropathic pain associated with spinal cord injury.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:49:57.600414+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-704-03,Rifampicin + Isoniazid,Duomax,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bKGuzwy_JqFhCGDOSoWoH6YnYpuCatGe/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-704-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bKGuzwy_JqFhCGDOSoWoH6YnYpuCatGe_view_usp_drivesdk_5927d59b63.pdf,page_text/DRP-704-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bKGuzwy_JqFhCGDOSoWoH6YnYpuCatGe_view_usp_drivesdk_5927d59b63.json,1330295ddb1d05a35e63089ffa959d0cf6a96c6d40d4eeef5618f525b1b52317,1641212,2,digital_text_and_ocr,"Rifampicin DUOMAX is a fixed-dose combination of Rifampicin, and Isoniazid for use in the treatment of tuberculosis. This has Gastrointestinal: Heartburn, epigastric distress, anorexia, nausea, vomiting, jaundice, flatulence, cramps and diarrhoea have been developed for improving patient compliance. been reported.",2,2,DESCRIPTION,"Duomax is indicated for the continuation phase of short course treatment of patients with pulmonary or Rifampicin extra-pulmonary tuberculosis. During this phase, Duomax should be administered on a daily continuous basis. Intermittent administration (once or twice weekly) of Rifampicin may cause “flu like syndrome’ with fever, chills and malaise This fixed-dosage combination drug is not recommended for initial therapy of tuberculosis or for prevention therapy. hematologic reactions (leukopenia, thrombocytopenia or acute hemolytic anemia), cutaneous and hepatic reactions more frequently. Duomax due to its Rifampicin content, may produce a reddish colouration of the urine, sweat, sputum and tears",2,2,INDICATIONS & USAGE:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T18:50:21.789443+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7042,Cloxacillin (as Sodium),Fulclox,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/17U1lh-RAoOy5cae0llEWzxV2J2yg4_HT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7042_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17U1lh-RAoOy5cae0llEWzxV2J2yg4_HT_view_usp_drivesdk_bc25e7f163.pdf,page_text/DRP-7042_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17U1lh-RAoOy5cae0llEWzxV2J2yg4_HT_view_usp_drivesdk_bc25e7f163.json,98d7a791eec4772d1a7efbf0ab03666b5c5d99d645cb8093872768195049f70d,1387258,1,ocr,,,,,"Cloxacillin is an isoxazolyl penicillin used similarly to flucloxacillin in the treatment of infections due to staphylococci resistant to benzylpenicillin. These include bone and joint infections, endocarditis, peritonitis (associated with continuous ambulatory peritoneal dialysis) pneumonia, skin disorders (including soft-tissue infections), surgical infections prophylaxis and toxic shock syndrome.",1,1,INDICATION:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T18:50:51.681130+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7044,Bisacodyl,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zXa2eM3HF00dSz0daYmQl4iRGjDzy1Bf/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7044_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zXa2eM3HF00dSz0daYmQl4iRGjDzy1Bf_view_usp_drivesdk_5525b2ca5d.pdf,page_text/DRP-7044_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zXa2eM3HF00dSz0daYmQl4iRGjDzy1Bf_view_usp_drivesdk_5525b2ca5d.json,ae1b538c45a2f09e2962361bbb43db1b29bc82c993bc76c0a11f3bca1bd037d8,1332643,2,ocr,"Bisacodyl 5 mg Enteric-Coated tablet is light-yellow to yellow, round, biconvex, enteric-coated tablet, plain on both sides. Whatis in the medicine Each enteric-coated tablet contains of 5 mg of bisacodyl as the active ingredients Other ingredients are: Povidone, Ethyl Alcohol, Lactose Monohydrate, Corn Starch, Pregelatinized Starch, Magnesium Stearate, Acryl-Eze White, Purified Water, D & C Yellow, Purified Water. Strength of the Medicine 5 mg Enteric-Coated Tablet. Whatis this medicine used for? It is used for the treatment of constipation and for bowel evaluation before investigation procedures or surgery. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Adults and children over 10 years - Take one or two tablets (5 or 10 mg) daily before bedtime - If you have not taken Bisacodyl Tablets before, start with one tablet and increase to two if necessary. - When you bowel regularity has returned to normal, the dose can usually be stopped. Children aged between 4 and 10 years - Should only be given if recommended by a doctor. The usual dose for children is: One Tablet (5 mg) daily before bedtime. When you should not take this medicine? 3) - Bisacodyl should not be taken on a continuous daily basis for more than five days without investigating the cause of constipation. | BISOCODYL -Bisacodyl should not be used in patients with ileus, intestinal obstruction, acute abdominal conditions icluding appendicitis, acute inflammatory bowel 5 mg Enteric-Coated Tablet diseases, and severe abdominal pain associated with nausea and vomiting which may be indicative of the aforementioned severe conditions. Laxative - Bisacodyl is also contraindicated in severe dehydration and in patients with known hypersensitivity to bisacodyl or any other component of the product. 7 | ZN Care that should be taken when taking this medicine -Bisacodyl Tablet should be swallowed whole not chewed, crushed or broken,as this would damage their special enteric coating. - Care should be taken in patients with infalammatory bowel disease. woh, Ss Ss hy In patients suffering from fluid loss where dehydration may be harmful (eg. (bisacodyl) renal insufficiency, elderly patients), Bisacodyl should be discontinued and - only be restarted under medical supervision. Laxatives do not help with weight loss.",1,1,Description of the product,"Adeverse events have been ranked under headings of frequency using the It is used for the treatment of constipation and for bowel evacuation before investigation procedures or surgery. following convention: Very common (2 1/10); common (2 1/100, < 1/10); uncommon (2 1/1000, <1/100); rare (2 1/10000, <1/1000); very rare (<1/10000).",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T18:51:33.249191+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7049,Etoricoxib,Coxigen-90,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rec1jRP41yquzItI3FRjZtGv9edaRbyH/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7049_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rec1jRP41yquzItI3FRjZtGv9edaRbyH_view_usp_drivesdk_5809dbbb4c.pdf,page_text/DRP-7049_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rec1jRP41yquzItI3FRjZtGv9edaRbyH_view_usp_drivesdk_5809dbbb4c.json,4ee5eb3256f353a5e7a7a9bff821e1c333bf736257e840b93ba0d8fe062fb591,252379,1,digital_text,"Coxigen-120 is a white to off-white, circular, biconvex, film coated tablet, with “120” embossed on one side and break line on the other side. Coxigen-90 is a white to off-white, circular, biconvex, film coate tablet, with “90” embossed on one side and break line on the other side. Coxigen-60 is is a white to off-white, circular, biconvex, film coate tablet, with “60” embossed on one side and break line on the other side. Cyclooxygenase (COX) is an enzyme that is responsible for the formation of prostanoids. The three main groups of prostanoids – prostaglandins, prostacyclins, and thromboxanes – each involved in the inflammatory response. There are two, if not three, known types of cyclooxygenase (COX-1, COX-2, and COX-3).",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Etoricoxib is used for the treatment of acute gout, inflammatory disease of the joints and osteoarthritis.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:51:37.167844+00:00
