PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7056,Atorvastatin (as calcium),Avas,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-vIae78miW3gR5KvKMUVjC6MZyg_7t3-/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7056_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-vIae78miW3gR5KvKMUVjC6MZyg_7t3-_view_usp_drivesdk_462ff35700.pdf,page_text/DRP-7056_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-vIae78miW3gR5KvKMUVjC6MZyg_7t3-_view_usp_drivesdk_462ff35700.json,44071d0f4a4267d30270355e8b8f0d3e817349d85ebe477ffe5826f529e48871,1463841,3,digital_text,"Atorvastatin Tablets 10 mg – Brownish orange coloured, circular, biconvex, film coated tablets with plain on both surfaces. Atorvastatin Tablets 20 mg - Brownish orange coloured, circular, biconvex, film coated tablets with a breakline on one surface. Atorvastatin Tablets 40 mg – White, circular, biconvex, film coated tablets with a breakline on one surface and plain on other.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Atorvastatin is used to reduce LDL-cholesterol, apolipoprotein B, and triglycerides, and to increase HDL- cholesterol in the treatment of hyperlipidaemias, including hypercholesterolaemias and combined (mixed) hyperlipidaemia (type IIa or IIb hyperlipoproteinaemias), hypertriglyceridaemias (type IV), and dysbetalipoproteinaemias (type III); can also be effective as adjunctive therapy in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia who have some LDL-receptor function.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T18:51:44.468804+00:00
