PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7121,GUAIFENESIN/AMMONIUM CHLORIDE/SODIUM CITRATE/CHLORPHENAMINE MALEATE,EUROCOF,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1R-1vPnJH9l_PSs_Ho8jyrWgt4l0rKZ5F/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7121_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1R-1vPnJH9l_PSs_Ho8jyrWgt4l0rKZ5F_view_usp_drivesdk_a35476efb0.pdf,page_text/DRP-7121_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1R-1vPnJH9l_PSs_Ho8jyrWgt4l0rKZ5F_view_usp_drivesdk_a35476efb0.json,548d70bf03d28d73d7ed5ce85569c2b5cd596fe5e4ef360ee2695eba348cc035,1413733,1,digital_text,"Guaifenesin, Ammonium Chloride, Sodium Citrate, Chlorpheniramine Maleate (Eurocof) is a clear pink, strawberry /f_lavoured syrup with sweet to salty with menthol taste in a 60 mL amber bottle. STRENGHT OF THE MEDICINE 50 mg Guaifenesin, 50 mg Ammonium Chloride, 100mg Sodium Citrate, 1mg Chlorpheniramine Maleate per 5 mL Syrup. WHAT IS THE MEDICATION USED FOR? Useful for the relief of respiratory infections due to common colds and allergies, acute and chronic bronchial asthma and for removal of thick mucus masses from the chest. HOW MUCH AND OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THE MEDICINE? To be taken three to four times daily. Infants: 2.5 mL (1/2 teaspoonful)3 to 4 times a day. Children: 2-6 years: 5 mL (1 teaspoonful)3 to 4 times a day. 7-12 years: 510 mL (1-2 teaspoonfuls)3 to 4 times a day. Adults:15 mL (1 tablespoonful) 3 to 4 times a day or as prescribed by physician. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THE MEDICINE? Dosing of Guaifenesin, Ammonium Chloride, Sodium Citrate, Chlorpheniramine Maleate (Eurocof) is not recommended if you have impared hepatic and renal function; also during the acute attack of asthma. . GUAIFENESIN SODIUM Citrate AMMONIUM Chloride CHLORPHENIRAMINE Maleate UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS Gastric disturbance, nausea and vomiting can be experienced. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Do not use other medicines that contain a cough suppressant, a decongestant, or an antihistamine. You may be getting more than a safe amount of these medicines. Do not drink alcohol while you are using this medicine. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Take a dose as soon as you remember. If it is almost time for your next dose, wait until then and take a regular dose. Do not take extra medicine to make up for a missed dose. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Protect from direct sunlight. Store at temperature not exceeding 30˚c Keep bottle tightly closed. Keep out of reach of children. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVER DOSAGE Irritant to gastric mucosa and may produce nausea and vomiting particularly in large doses. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSE? Consult your doctor if any undesirable eﬀects happen. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE Antihistamine may cause moderate drowsiness. Patients should be warned against driving automobiles or operating moving machinery while under treatment. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT A DOCTOR? If any undesirable eﬀects occur, or adverse allergic reactions like itching or hives, swelling in your face or hands, swelling or tingling in your mouth or throat, chest tightness, trouble breathing. AVAILABILITY Syrup: in bottle of 60 mL ADVERSE DRUG REACTION REPORTING For suspected adverse drug reaction, seek medical attention immediately and report to the FDA at www.fda.gov.ph Date of revision of patient information leaflet: March 28,2019 Date of renewal of authorization: Manufactured By: AM-EUROPHARMA CORPORATION Brgy. Saimsim, Calamba City, Laguna, Philippines Distributed By:",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T18:57:51.766381+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7131,Sodium Citrate/Dextromethorphan Hydrobromide/Phenylpropanolamine Hydrochloride/Chlorphenamine Maleate,Menthodex-DM,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gceOgqU7Ohya2QJUQwYi45JOWebfXuDU/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7131_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gceOgqU7Ohya2QJUQwYi45JOWebfXuDU_view_usp_drivesdk_b35f4f4b17.pdf,page_text/DRP-7131_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gceOgqU7Ohya2QJUQwYi45JOWebfXuDU_view_usp_drivesdk_b35f4f4b17.json,c53394c85b9bf35a470c899433e4ca8877a75f81ec78239b7d07da2b4b9a08b0,1759436,1,ocr,"The medicine is a yellow syrupy liquid with a sweet cola flavor, aroma and taste contained in a 60 mL and 120 mL amber round bottle. What is in the medicine? Menthodex-DM contains: - Dextromethorphan Hydrobromide used as control of cough associated with common colds, influenza, allergy and other respiratory infections, inhalation of irritating substance and psychogenic cough. - Phenylpropanolamine HCI which is a decongestant. It works by constricting (shrinking) blood vessels (veins and arteries) in your body. Constriction of blood vessels in your sinuses, nose and chest allows drainage of those area, which decreases congestion. - Chlorphenamine Maleate that is an antihistamine used for the symptomatic relief of allergic conditions. Strength of the medicine: Each mL contains: Sodium Citrate, USP 180 mg Dextromethorphan Hydrobromide 15 mg Phenylpropanolamine Hydrochloride 15 mg Chlorphenamine Maleate amine Maleate 2mg FD&C Yellow #5 (Tartrazine) 50 me 0.81% Ethyl Alcohol What is this medicine used for? Suppresses dry cough and promotes expectoration in productive cough associated with asthma, pneumonia, bronchitis, pertussis and other respiratory diseases allergic or non-allergic in nature. Also used as antitussive, decongestant and antihistamine. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Children: 1-9 years old 2.5 -5 mL (1/2-1 teaspoonful) dults 5 - 10 mL (1-2 teaspoonfuls) Every 4 hours or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? Use with caution in patients with a history of liver disorder, bronchial asthma and cardiac disorders. Increasing dosage can lead to psychotic reactions, cardiovascular changes and precipitation of anginal attacks. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: Antihistamines may cause drowsiness and dulling of mental alertness. Patients undergoing treatment with these drugs should not take charge of vehicles, other means of transportation or machinery where loss of attention may lead to accidents. Undesirable effects of this medicine: It appears to be rare and may include dizziness and gastrointestinal disturbances, CNS depression, drowsiness, headache, psychomotor impairment and antimuscarinic effects such as dry mouth, thickened respiratory tract secretions, blurred vision, urinary difficulty or retention, constipation and increased gastric reflux. It also may cause nervousness, restlessness, insomnia/sleep disturbances, feeling of uneasiness (anxiety), confusion, high blood pressure, rapid heartbeat (palpitation), chest tightness, muscle shi aking (tremor), agitation, irritabilt y, aggressiveness (particularly in young children) and nausea. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Dextromethorphan HBr - Amiodarone, Haloperidol, Propafenone, Quinidine, SSRI’s and Thioridazine. Phenylpropanolamine HCI: - Do not take Phenylpropanolamine if you have taken a monoamine oxidase inhibitor (MAOI) such as isocarboxazid, phenelzine or tranylcypromine in the last 14 days. A very dangerous drug interaction could occur, leading to serious hypertensive crisis (sudden, severe increase in blood pressure that can lead to stroke). - It may also enhance the sedative effects of Alcohol, Barbiturates, Hypnotics, Opioid Analgesics, Anxiolytic Sedatives and Antipsychotics. - Amantadine with Phenylpropanolamine is reportedly causes severe psychosis. - Other medicine that may also interact with Phenylpropanolamine includes furazolidone; guanethidine; indomethacin; methyldopa; bromocriptine; caffeine in cola, tea, coffee, chocolate and other products; theophylline; tricyclic antidepressants such as amitriptyline, doxepin and nortriptyline; other commonly used tricyclic antidepressants, including amoxapine, clomipramine, desipramine, imipramine, protriptyline and trimipramine: phenothiazines such as chlorpromazine, thioridazine and prochlorperazine; and other commonly used phenothiazines, including fluphenazine. : perphenazine, mesoridazine and trifluoperazine. Chlorphenamine Maleate - may enhance the sedative effects of Alcohol, Barbiturates, Hypnotics, Opioid Analgesics, Anxiolytic Sedatives and Antipsychotics. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose, skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Do not double the dose. Signs and symptoms of overdose: Dextromethorphan HBr - excitation, confusion and respiratory depression may occur after overdosage. Phenylpropanolamine HCl - extreme tiredness, sweating, dizziness, a slow heart beat and a coma. Chlorphenamine Maleate - Ataxia, excitement, tremors, psychoses, hallucinations and convulsions; hyperpyrexia may also occur. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? I —Sjore al temperatures not exceeding 3 lore at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? If symptoms persist, consult your doctor. “For suspected adverse drug rr eaction report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph”. ly at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. DRP-7131 Date of Renewal Authorization: July 02, 2019 Patient Information Leaflet Date of Revision: April 28, 2023 Manufactured by the ¢ Distributed by: Marketing Authorization Holder:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T18:58:02.741114+00:00
