PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7172,Ceterizine Hydrochloride,Dialix,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UPvsayfNDygygM54XfD2uEMVEOYrer7o/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7172_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UPvsayfNDygygM54XfD2uEMVEOYrer7o_view_usp_drivesdk_8967c49e89.pdf,page_text/DRP-7172_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UPvsayfNDygygM54XfD2uEMVEOYrer7o_view_usp_drivesdk_8967c49e89.json,51f0bc85d6a514c4a31d34c237e3aba39f84e3ceec38ed1fa07c05f9f7902c78,847905,1,ocr,"Acclear colorless syrup with banana flavor and aroma contained in a 60 mL amber round bottle. What is in the medicine? Dialix contains Cetirizine Hydrochloride. It is an anti-histamine (anti-allergy) medicine that blocks the substance that causes allergic symptoms. It is less likely to cause drowsiness and dizziness than any other anti-allergy medicines. Strength of the medicine: Each milliliter of Dialix Oral Solution contains 1 mg Cetirizine Hydrochloride. What is this medicine used for? ~ Dialix is indicated for the symptomatic relief of allergic conditions including rhinitis (sneezing, runny/itchy ~ - _ nose, and _itchy/watery eyes), allergic conjunctivitis, skin symptoms of allergy such as itch and rash; and chronic urticaria: a How much and how often should you use this medicine? ~ ~ Adults: — 10 mg (2 teaspoonfuls) once a day or —~ 5 mg (1 teaspoonful) twice a day. ss Children: Above 6 yrs. old: 10 mg (2 teaspoonfuls) once a day or 5 mg (1 teaspoonful) twice a day. 2 yrs. old to 6 yrs. old: 5 mg (1 teaspoonful) once a day or 2.5 mg (% teaspoon) twice a day. Patients with hepatic or renal impairment: Take half the usual daily dose or dosage of cetirizine should be reduced in patients with hepatic and renal impairment. May be taken with or without food. Or as prescribed by the physician. ae — When should you not take this medicine? mes -If you are allergic to Cetirizine Hydrochloride. eb -It is under Category B of pregnancy. Use only when clearly needed and when the potential benefits outweigh the potential hazards to the fetus. _ Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: -Do not take more than the recommended dose. -Extra caution should be given to patient suffering from severe kidney disease or renal problem. -May cause drowsiness. Care must take place to patient that requires mental alertness (e.g. driving or operating machines). Undesirable effects of this medicine: Undesirable effects with Cetirizine includes drowsiness, sleepiness, headache, nausea, vomiting and diarrhea. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? It should not be taken with alcohol, barbiturates, hypnotics, opioid analgesics, anxiolytic sedative and anti-psychotic. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose, skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Do not double the dose. Ss Signs and d mptoms of overdose: Symptoms o Cetirizine overdose includes sleepiness, drowsiness, restlessness and irritability. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. —_ t. Keep out of reach of children When should you consult your doctor? ” = If symptoms persist, consult your doctor. _— a a “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph.” Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. DRP-7172 Date of Renewal Authorization: October 19, 2022 Patient Information Leaflet Date of Revision: March 20, 2023 Manufactured by the Marketing Authorization Holder: Distributed by:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T19:06:52.880040+00:00
