pital or your doctor immediately. pain, fever, swelling and inflammation. This combination provided better analgesia than either drug alone (at the same dose), with a smaller chance of needing additional analgesia over about eight hours, and with a smaller chance of experiencing an adverse event. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C Strength of the medicine Protect from direct sunlight. Keep out from reach of children. Each capsule contains 325mg Paracetamol and 200mg Ibuprofen. When should you consult your doctor? What is this medicine used for? If symptoms persist and any undesirable effect occurs, consult your doctor. Ibuprofen + Paracetamol (DIATAFEN) is used for relief of mild to moderate pain, minor febrile conditions, and for acute “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph.” Seek medical attention and chronic inflammatory disorders such as osteoarthritis, rheumatoid arthritis, juvenile idiopathic arthritis, and ankylosing spondylitis. This is also used to relieve headache, dysmenorrheal, toothache, surgical operations and immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. reduction of fever. How much and how often should you use this medicine? DRP-7173 Adult: 1 capsule every 6 hours or as prescribed by the physician given by mouth. Date of Authorization: When should you not take this medicine? May 17, 2017 If you are allergic to Paracetamol or Ibuprofen. Patient Information Leaflet date of revision: Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: August 25, 2017 Paracetamol should be given with care to patients with impaired kidney or liver function and to patients with alcohol dependence. All NSAID’s including Ibuprofen must be given with care to patients with active peptic ulceration, and patients with severe heart failure, severe liver disease, and who are taking low-dose aspirin for the prevention of cardiovascular disease. If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, ask a doctor before use of Diatafen capsule. Manufactured by the Distributed by: Marketing Authorization Holder: Rilem Pharma Corp. Undesirable effects of this medicine: % Diamond Laboratories Inc. Ibuprofen may be better tolerated than other NSAID’s, possible adverse effects may include gastrointestinal 2711 Zamora Street, Pasay City #8 Feria Rd. Commonwealth Ave., Diliman Quezon City discomfort, nausea, diarrhea, headache, vertigo, dizziness, nervousness, tinnitus, depression, drowsiness and insomnia. Adverse effect of Paracetamol are rare and usually mild, although haematological reactions including thrombocytopenia, leucopenia, pancytopenia, neutropenia, and agranulocytosis have been reported. Skin rashes and other hypersensitivity reaction occurs occasionally. What other medicine or food should be avoided? The risk of Paracetamol toxicity may be increased in patients receiving other potentially hepatotoxic drugs or drugs that induce liver microsomal enzymes. The absorption of paracetamol may be accelerated by drugs such as metoclopramide. Excretion may be affected and plasma concentrations altered when given with probenecid. Colestyramine reduces the absorption of paracetamol if given within 1 hour of paracetamol. All NSAID’s including Ibuprofen must be given care to patients with active peptic ulceration. [Page 2]",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T19:07:03.751587+00:00
