PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7226,Ampicillin (as Sodium),Excillin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LYixwztKw48oTNgqIXupxpZECnLf__pl/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7226_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LYixwztKw48oTNgqIXupxpZECnLf__pl_view_usp_drivesdk_3d6d87c4c6.pdf,page_text/DRP-7226_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LYixwztKw48oTNgqIXupxpZECnLf__pl_view_usp_drivesdk_3d6d87c4c6.json,fc841976cf08fe41e8cbee168c8f974d28daffb607c88d7e985d09dc182f9f0d,363077,16,digital_text_and_ocr,Powder for injection (IM/IV) CLINICAL PARTICULARS,1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"For the initiation of treatment of infections caused by susceptible strains of both Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria, and the treatment of severe infections, particularly in patients for whom oral administration is impossible. Infections of the respiratory tract (particularly those caused by Haemophilus influenzae) - Infections and mixed infections of the upper respiratory tract and ENT region, e.g. sinusitis, otitis media - I nfections of the lower respiratory tract, e.g. acute and chronic bronchitis, pneumonia Skin and soft tissue infections Infections of the urogenital tract - Acute and chronic pyelonephritis, pyelitis, cystitis, urethritis, prostatitis, etc. - Gonorrhoea - I nfections in the region of the female reproductive organs and true pelvis, e.g. infected abortion, inflammation of the uterine adnexa, salpingitis, endometritis, and parametritis, pelvic peritonitis, puerperal fever, etc. Infections of the gastrointestinal tract - Bacterial diarrhoea, salmonellosis, shigellosis, typhoid fever, paratyphoid fever; treatment of Salmonella carriers - Infections of the bile ducts (cholangiolitis, cholangitis, cholecystitis) Acute a nd latent listeriosis, leptospirosis, possibly in combination with gentamicin or kanamycin, meningitis, possibly in combination with chloramphenicol, endocarditis (e.g. caused by enterococci, in combination with an aminoglycoside), bacterial meningitis Septicaemia caused by pathogens. that are susceptible to ampicillin bile ducts (cholangiolitis, cholangitis, cholecystitis) Ampicillin sodium [Page 2] Ampicillin 250 mg, 500 mg, 1g Powder for Injection Ampicillin has been used successfully in the treatment of granuloma inguinale and leptospirosis. Prophylaxis Perioperative infection prophylaxis (up to 24 (-48) hours after surgery)",1,2,Indications,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T19:09:25.204973+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7236,Sodium Chloride,Partners,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1E2voNjDDLnJ_PDWYmFPW50U69R7ZOmZE/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7236_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1E2voNjDDLnJ_PDWYmFPW50U69R7ZOmZE_view_usp_drivesdk_6876052b32.pdf,page_text/DRP-7236_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1E2voNjDDLnJ_PDWYmFPW50U69R7ZOmZE_view_usp_drivesdk_6876052b32.json,c5e6f164c91314949bcd9466f2f7d52600f24c0de3181e179c277efc3fce499a,800250,7,digital_text_and_ocr,"Yangzi Road , Economic & Technological Development Zone, Shijiazhuang City, Hebei, Province Imported & Distributed by: Champion Biotech and Pharma Corporation Rm 202 J:1141 F. Blumentritt St. San Juan City [Page 4] SODIUM CHLORIDE R PARTNERS 900mg I 1 00mL (0.9%w/v) Solution for Intravenous Infusion Electrolyte Solution",3,4,"PHAR MACEUTICAL CO., LTD .",It is used in the management of deficiencies of sodium and chloride ions in salt-losing conditions. As source of sodium chloride and water for hydration. It is also used as solution for irrigation.,3,3,INDICATIONS,low,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T19:09:47.438153+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7239,Diphenhydramine Hydrochloride,Diahist,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dwqrezRfaHkTViOB3H2DURSwvxymK_gu/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7239_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dwqrezRfaHkTViOB3H2DURSwvxymK_gu_view_usp_drivesdk_6022e3a61a.pdf,page_text/DRP-7239_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dwqrezRfaHkTViOB3H2DURSwvxymK_gu_view_usp_drivesdk_6022e3a61a.json,327b8f5f9c0aa467fb155fdcf6b7311074c308d5c7a0f1d0e56b2c3a583c9c1c,1185444,1,ocr,"The medicine is a clear red syrup with cherry flavor contained in a 60mL amber round bottle. What is in the medicine? Diahist Syrup contains Diphenhydramine as hydrochloride which belongs to the sedating class of antihistamines It reduces the effects of natural chemical histamine in the body. Histamine can produce symptoms of sneezing itching, watery eyes, and runny nose. It acts as a cough suppressant through its effect on the cough center in the brain, likewise as an antiemetic, it acts by suppressing the vomiting center in the brain Strength of the medicine: Each pms (1 serge of the syrup contains: enhydra eataneevssweet et Alcohol ee = ARG ma nme sme cee see sme sae cme see sae cme ses sne sas esesecss Fy What is this medicine used for? Diphenhydramine Hydrochloride is used for control of vasomotor rhinitis, hay fever, urticaria, angioneurotic edema, drug sensitization, serum and penicillin reaction, contact dermatitis, atopic eczema and other allergic states responsive to antihistamines. Also indicated for the active treatment of motion sickness (it should be given at least 30 minutes before travelling), and in the treatment of vertigo How much and how often should you use this medicine? Children (over 9 kgs of body weight) Adults 5-10 mL (1-2 teaspoonfuls), 3-4 times daily, maximum dose not to exceed 300 mg 20 mL (4 teaspoonfuls), 3-4 times daily Or as prescribed by the physician When should you not take this medicine? -Diahist Syrup should not be given to patients with allergy to any ingredient in the product. -It should not be given to infants and nursing mothers (pregnant or breastfeeding). -Patient taking medicines for depression Care that should be taken when taking this medicine -Care must take place to patient that requires mental alertness (e.g. driving or operating machines) -Do not take more than the recommended dose -Should be used with care in conditions such as angle-closure glaucoma, urinary retention, prostatic hyperplasia or pyloroduodenal obstruction. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Noeeceee —— Undesirable effect With sedating antihistamine including Diphenhydramine HCl is CNS depression, with effects varying from slight drowsiness to deep sleep, and including lassitude, dizziness. and incoordination. Other undesirable effects include muscle weakness, gastrointestinal discomfort, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea or constipation, dryness of the mouth, nose, throat, ringing in the ears, visual disturbances, blurred vision, insomnia tremor, nervousness, dizziness, headache, irritability, chest tightness, increased or decreased blood pressure palpitation, tachycardia (rapid heart rate), arrhythmia (irregular heart beat), and photosensitivity. What other medicine or food should be avoided? Diphenhydramine HCI may enhance the sedative effects of CNS depressants including alcohol, barbiturates. hypnotics, opioid analgesics, anxiolytic sedatives, and antipsychotics. It also has an additive antimuscarinic action with other antimuscarinic drugs, such as atropine and some antidepressants (both tricyclics and MAOIs). What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing Signs and symptoms of overdose Overdosage is associated with antimuscarinic, extrapyramidal and CNS effects. When CNS stimulation predominates over CNS depression, which is more likely in children or the elderly, it causes ataxia, excitement. tremors, psychosis, hallucinations and convulsions; hyperpyrexia may also occur. Deepening coma and cardiorespiratory collapse may follow. In adults, CNS depression is more common with drowsiness, coma, and convulsion, progressing to respiratory failure and cardiovascular collapse. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. cerry How should you keep this medi [OU KES ? BRE HCH REECE DE COE ECL ET EERE EECE ET ‘Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? If symptoms persist or any undesirable effects occur, consult your doctor. For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph."" Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction Registration No.: DRP-7239 Date of Renewal Authorization: November 26, 2021 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: June 14, 2022 Manufactured by the Marketing Authorization Holder: Distributed by",1,1,Description of the product,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T19:10:00.586237+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7246,Co-Amoxiclav,Altovox,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1YesFTKU2d58SAXWlgI1GbgP66R-4p6QJ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7246_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YesFTKU2d58SAXWlgI1GbgP66R-4p6QJ_view_usp_drivesdk_d92e4dc30d.pdf,page_text/DRP-7246_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YesFTKU2d58SAXWlgI1GbgP66R-4p6QJ_view_usp_drivesdk_d92e4dc30d.json,3f3e383e5f151a37e1982ab2add1a93bd82175d220a3245e8f708cade64fd03f,1248486,2,ocr,,,,,"For the treatment of infections due to susceptible organisms which include otitis media and sinusitis. It is also used for infections of the urinary tract, lower respiratory tract, skin and soft tissues.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T19:11:04.644043+00:00
