PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7277,Zoledronic acid,Zolerix,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wUNOg7JuHs09ArBAqv_DzQQ703OmQg-a/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7277_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wUNOg7JuHs09ArBAqv_DzQQ703OmQg-a_view_usp_drivesdk_74792cc6a0.pdf,page_text/DRP-7277_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wUNOg7JuHs09ArBAqv_DzQQ703OmQg-a_view_usp_drivesdk_74792cc6a0.json,1a48aa097bb85060ffb8bcd7d57511aeca28f7b1bb6e8d8b7517710c3eb46436,4293048,2,digital_text_and_ocr,"With caution: deciding whether to start therapy with zoledronic acid in Clear colorless liquid. patients with tumor-induced hypercalcemia, in renal impairment, assess a patient's condition and make conclusion whether potential benefit of product",1,1,Product description,"« Hypercalcemia of Malignancy. Adverse effects Zolerix® is indicated for the treatment of hypercalcemia of malignancy Adverse reactions related with zoledronic acid are usually mild. The criteria defined as an albumin-corrected calcium (cCa) of greater than or equal for frequency of adverse reactions: very common (21/10), common to 12 mg/dL [3.0 mmol/L] using the formula: cCa in mg/dL = Ca in (21/100, <1/10), uncommon (21/1000, <1/100), rare (21/10 000, mg/dL + 0.8 (4.0 g/dL — patient albumin [g/dL]). <1/1000), very rare (<1/10 000, including isolated cases). « Multiple Myeloma and Bone Metastases of solid Tumors. Blood and lymphatic system disorders: common — anemia, uncommon Zolerix® is indicated for the treatment of patients with multiple myeloma — thrombocytopenia, leukocytopenia; uncommon - pancytopenia. and patients with documented bone metastases from solid tumors, in Nervous system disorders: common — headache; uncommon — [Page 2] Imported and Distributed by: Ambica International Corporation #9 Amsterdam Extension, Merville Park Subd., Pañaque City, Metro Manila Manufactured by: CJSC Biocad Petrovo-Dalneye, Krasnogorsky District, Moscow Region, 143422, Russia DRP-7277 Date of First Authorization: July 28, 2017 Date of Revision of Package Insert: June 14, 2024 [Page 3]",1,2,Therapeutic indications,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T19:12:35.811361+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7279,Bortezomib,Dotrex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/16y7sAI7sZPYSdZIhgpU9OXBgBBFIx9ky/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7279_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_16y7sAI7sZPYSdZIhgpU9OXBgBBFIx9ky_view_usp_drivesdk_421c1d69c5.pdf,page_text/DRP-7279_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_16y7sAI7sZPYSdZIhgpU9OXBgBBFIx9ky_view_usp_drivesdk_421c1d69c5.json,fc3b0be6f4fe2f5fb6b0dd8af3ec1ae5f931b790303fa8ce8afb194740f8aa60,1217574,3,digital_text,"White Lyophilized Mass. Bortezomib for injection is an antineoplastic agent available for intravenous (Rapid bolus) use only. Bortezomib is a modified dipeptidyl boronic acid which is in the form of mannitol boronic ester, reconstituted form, consists of the mannitol ester in equilibrium with its hydrolysis product, the monomeric boronic acid. The chemical name for bortezomib, the monomeric boronic acid, is [(1R)-3-methyl-1-[[(2S)-1-oxo-3-phenyl-2-[(pyrazinylcarbonyl) amino]propyl]amino]butyl] boronic acid. Bortezomib has the following chemical structure: The molecular weight is 384.24. The molecular formula is C H BN O . The solubility of Bortezomib, as the monomeric boronic acid, in water is 3.3-3.8 mg /mL in a pH 19 25 4 4 range of 2.0-6.5.",3,3,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Bortezomib as monotherapy or in combination with pegylated liposomal doxorubicin or dexamethasone is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with progressive multiple myeloma who have received at least 1 prior therapy and who have already undergone or are unsuitable for haematopoietic stem cell transplantation. Bortezomib in combination with melphalan and prednisone is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with previously untreated multiple myeloma who are not eligible for high-dose chemotherapy with haematopoietic stem cell transplantation. Bortezomib in combination with dexamethasone, or with dexamethasone and thalidomide, is indicated for the induction treatment of adult patients with previously untreated multiple myeloma who are eligible for high-dose chemotherapy with haematopoietic stem cell transplantation.",3,3,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:12:43.574792+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7279-03,Bortezomib,Boramir,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/177luzSusMCoTmGM1PMezScr8X5AyHheV/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7279-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_177luzSusMCoTmGM1PMezScr8X5AyHheV_view_usp_drivesdk_f9de9f7054.pdf,page_text/DRP-7279-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_177luzSusMCoTmGM1PMezScr8X5AyHheV_view_usp_drivesdk_f9de9f7054.json,9bcf21ff23c0b06431e816885d763798dae2e9ca00200915d4442874dbb6d25c,509052,1,digital_text,"White Lyophilized Mass. Bortezomib for injection is an antineoplastic agent available for intravenous (Rapid bolus) use only. Bortezomib is a modified dipeptidyl boronic acid which is in the form of mannitol boronic ester, reconstituted form, consists of the mannitol ester in equilibrium with its hydrolysis product, the monomeric boronic acid. The chemical name for bortezomib, the monomeric boronic acid, is [(1R)-3-methyl-1-[[(2S)-1-oxo-3-phenyl-2-[(pyrazinylcarbonyl) amino]propyl]amino]butyl] boronic acid. Bortezomib has the following chemical structure: The molecular weight is 384.24. The molecular formula is C H BN O . The solubility of Bortezomib, as the monomeric boronic acid, in water is 3.3-3.8 mg /mL in a pH 19 25 4 4 range of 2.0-6.5.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Bortezomib as monotherapy or in combination with pegylated liposomal doxorubicin or dexamethasone is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with progressive multiple myeloma who have received at least 1 prior therapy and who have already undergone or are unsuitable for haematopoietic stem cell transplantation. Bortezomib in combination with melphalan and prednisone is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with previously untreated multiple myeloma who are not eligible for high-dose chemotherapy with haematopoietic stem cell transplantation. Bortezomib in combination with dexamethasone, or with dexamethasone and thalidomide, is indicated for the induction treatment of adult patients with previously untreated multiple myeloma who are eligible for high-dose chemotherapy with haematopoietic stem cell transplantation.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:12:39.214229+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7286,Ondansetron (as hydrochloride dihydrate),Vomiz 8,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/156pomgYr4dZHPXUr_JlLrIf5OHlsb6E3/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7286_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_156pomgYr4dZHPXUr_JlLrIf5OHlsb6E3_view_usp_drivesdk_f2c7511a0c.pdf,page_text/DRP-7286_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_156pomgYr4dZHPXUr_JlLrIf5OHlsb6E3_view_usp_drivesdk_f2c7511a0c.json,fb90751fc6b93ebe92f9c2b6658b547d06e7934d9a882940705c095ed264585c,86944,2,digital_text,"The active ingredient in Ondansetron Tablets, is ondansetron hydrochloride (HCl) as the dihydrate, the racemic form of ondansetron and a selective blocking agent of the serotonin 5-HT receptor type. Chemically it is (±) 1, 2, 3, 9-tetrahydro-9-methyl-3-[(2-methyl-1H-imidazol-1-yl) methyl]-4H-carbazol-4-one, representing a molecular weight of 365.9. Ondansetron HCl dihydrate is a white to off-white powder that is soluble in water and normal saline.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"• Prevention of nausea and vomiting associated with highly emetogenic cancer chemotherapy, including Cisplatin ≥ 50 mg/m2. • Prevention of nausea and vomiting associated with initial and repeat courses of moderately ematogenic cancer chemotherapy. • Prevention of nausea and vomiting associated with radiotherapy in patients receiving either total body irradiation, single high-dose fraction to the abdomen, or daily fractions to the abdomen. • Prevention of postoperative nausea and/or vomiting",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:12:46.787705+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7294,Multivitamins+Iron,Multilem Plus,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/19eaoJi7DZYymqIHL5KTtFD1My4PfH7gF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7294_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19eaoJi7DZYymqIHL5KTtFD1My4PfH7gF_view_usp_drivesdk_bee9696e81.pdf,page_text/DRP-7294_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19eaoJi7DZYymqIHL5KTtFD1My4PfH7gF_view_usp_drivesdk_bee9696e81.json,7a8f1eeb5c1b2c7774fb24fb032b553bfb96cf22738764045d413c88d1fa4bd5,1366302,1,ocr,"Mixture of brown and orange, odorless powder contained in dark brown/dark brown capsule size #1. Blister pack by 10’s, box of 30’s and 100’s. What is in the medicine? Multilem Plus capsule contains vitamins which are organic substances required for various metabollic processes. Strength of the medicine: Each capsule contains: Ferrous Fumarate, USP cece cece ec ee nec ecececeeececereeecececeecececececeeecececeeeecececeteececececeececececeececececeecececececeececeeccecececeeeseecececeeecececeececececeecececeteceecececeseeeeeese 325 mg (eq. to 105 mg Elemental Iron) Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C) . noose wavees eawerrets woomtra srotenses atten) 100 mg Niacin (Vitamin B3) Ceca ron 25 mg Thiamine Mononitrate (Vitamin B,) .. 10 mg eesisze Riboflavin (Vitamin Bz) .. 10 mg Calcium Pantothenate ... eeeeee 10 mg Pyridoxine Hydrochloride (Vitamin 6) 5 mg Folic Acid Seema ee ee eeeaeasceensenescenecesn 950 mcg suesaes Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B,2) .. 25 mcg What is this medicine used for? This is used for prevention and treatment of Iron Vitamin and dietary deficiency anemias. Anemias due to blood loss during menstruation, infections, surgery, delivery, intoxications, parasitosis or other causes. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Take one capsule daily, or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? If you are allergic to any of the components in the product. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: - Do not take more than the recommended dose. - Do not use after the expiry date stated on the label. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Generally, if taken with recommended dose, this medicine is well tolerated but in some cases the following may be seen: Ferrous Fumarate- Constipation; dark or green stools, diarrhea; loss of appetite; nausea; stomach cramps, pain, or upset; vomiting. Seek medical attention right away if any of these SEVERE side effects occur: Severe allergic reactions (rash; hives; itching; difficulty breathing; tightness in the chest; swelling of the mouth, face, lips, or tongue); black, tarry stools; blood or streaks of blood in the stool; fever; severe or persistent nausea, stomach pain, or vomiting; vomit that looks like blood or coffee grounds. Niacin- It has a vasodilating action that causes flushing, sensation of heat, faintness and pounding in the head. Riboflavin (Vitamin B2)- Large doses may result to bright yellow discoloration in urine. Folic Acid- Less serious side effects are more likely, but may include: nausea, loss of appetite; bloating, gas; bitter or unpleasant taste in your mouth; sleep problems; depression; or feeling excited or irritable. Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12)- Allergic hypersensitivity reactions have occured rarely that includes rash, itching, and anaphylaxis. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Ferrous Fumarate- Ferrous Fumarate may decrease the effectiveness of doxycycline, mycophenolate, penicillamine or thyroid hormones (eg. Levothyroxine). Ascorbic Acid- Omeprazole Pyridoxine HCI (Vitamin B6)- Pyridoxine reduces the effects of Levodopa and Altretamine. Vitamin B6 decreases concentration of Phenobarbital and Phenytoin. Folic Acid- Tell your doctor about all other medications you use, especially: phenytoin, methotrexate, nitrofurantoin, pyrimethamine, tetracycline, a barbiturate such as butabarbital, secobarbital, pentobarbital; or phenobarbital; or seizure medication such as phenytoin or primidone. Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12)- Neomycin, Aminosalicylic Acid, Histamine H2 Antagonist, Omeprazole, Colchicine reduce the absoption of Vitamin B12. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: The following symptoms might be seen in large doses: Ferrous Fumarate- Symptoms may include black, tarry stools; blood or streaks of blood in the stool; bluish skin or nails; changes in the amount of urine produced; chest pain; coma; dizziness; dry mouth or eyes; fainting; fast or difficult breathing; fast or irregular hearthbeat; flushing; increased thirst or hunger; seizures; severe nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, or stomach pain; severe or unusual tiredness or drowsiness; shortness of breath; sluggishness; unusually pale skin; vomit that looks like blood or coffee grounds. Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C)- Large doses may cause diarrhea, abdominal pain and disturbances. Pyridoxine HCI (Vitamin B6)- Long term use of large doses is associated with the development of severe peripheral neuropathies. Folic Acid- Overdose symptoms may include numbness or tingling, mouth or tongue pain, weakness, tired feeling, confusion, or trouble concentrating. Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12)- gastrointestinal disturbances, fever, chills, hot flushing, dizzines, malaise, acneform, eruptions and tremor. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more that the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How would you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? If any undesirable effect occurs. “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph”. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction