corbic Acid Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and (Vitamin C) 75.0 mg continue with the scheduled dosing. Nicotinamide (Vitamin B3) 18.0 mg Signs and symptoms of overdose: Omega-3-Fatty Acids 5.0 mg The following symptoms might be seen in large doses: Pyridoxine Hydrochloride Retinol Palmitate (Vitamin A)- Intake in excess of 10,000 IU daily or weekly intakes in excess of 25,000 IU (Vitamin B6) 1.6 mg Thiamine Hydrochloride have resulted to hypervitaminosis A (fatigue, irritability, anorexia, loss of weight, vomiting, sedation, dizziness, (Vitamin B1) 1.0 mg confusion and diarrhea). Riboflavin Sodium Phosphate Cholecalciferol (Vitamin D3)- Anorexia, lassitude, nausea, vomiting, constipation, diarrhea, polyuria, nocturia, (Vitamin B2) 1.0 mg Cyanocobalamin sweating, headache, thirst, somnolence and vertigo. Pyridoxine HCI (Vitamin B6)- Long term use of large doses is associated with the development of severe (Vitamin B12) 2.0 mcg peripheral neuropathies. What is this medicine used for? Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12)- gastrointestinal disturbances, fever, chills, hot flushing, dizziness, malaise, Bomvital Forte syrup is used for the treatment and prophylaxis of vitamin deficiencies; nutritional acneform, eruptions and tremor. supplement to stimulate appetite, growth and weight gain, enhances body resistance against stress and Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C)- Large doses may cause diarrhea, abdominal pain and disturbances. infection. It is equally necessary for proper growth, maintenance of health, and proper development of the brain and heart. The body cannot synthesize several vitamins and minerals, thus they must be What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? supplied through diet or dietary supplements. The vitamins function with chemicals called enzymes If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. which are mainly responsible for the oxidation process within the body. Enzymes are also a major factor in biochemical processes such as growth, metabolism, cellular reproduction and digestion. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Children: Protect from direct sunlight. 2-6 years old: 2.5 mL - 5 mL (1/2 to 1 teaspoonful) When should you consult your doctor? 7-12 years old: 5 mL - 10 mL (1-2 teaspoonfuls) If any undesirable effect occurs. To be taken once a day, or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph”. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction If you are allergic to any of the components in the product. Registration number: Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: - DRP-7319 Do not take more than the recommended dose. a Do not use after the expiry date stated on the label. Date of Renewal Authorization: January 21, 2021 Undesirable effects of this medicine: Retinol Palmitate (Vitamin A)- Hypervitaminosis A due to intake of very high doses can cause fatigue, Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet irritability, anorexia, loss of weight, vomiting, sedation, dizziness, confusion and diarrhea. May 06, 2022 Cholecalciferol ( Vitamin D3)- Excessive intake may lead to hypercalcemia or hyperphosphatemia. Riboflavin Sodium Phosphate (Vitamin B2)- Large doses may result to bright yellow discoloration in urine. Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12)- Allergic hypersensitivity reactions have occurred rarely that includes rash, itching and anaphylaxis. Nicotinamide (Vitamin B3)- Side effects are minimal but at high doses, liver problems may occur. Manufactured by the Marketing Authorization Holder: Distributed by: Chlorella- it is possibly safe when taken by mouth, short-term (up to 2 months). The most common side",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,need