PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7383-02,Furosemide,Furowell,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1A5CMTqJzD3THi1Y3WWQ56SqG0ggShJ4B/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7383-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1A5CMTqJzD3THi1Y3WWQ56SqG0ggShJ4B_view_usp_drivesdk_ff769e9408.pdf,page_text/DRP-7383-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1A5CMTqJzD3THi1Y3WWQ56SqG0ggShJ4B_view_usp_drivesdk_ff769e9408.json,137de5fa95958e463b48164b2628b9a99899790bc5427b29d943f32059a15b05,605620,2,digital_text,Furosemide Injection is a clear & colourless solution free from visible particles & fibers and it contains Furosemide BP. Chemical name of Furosemide is 4-Chloro-2-[(furan-2-ylmethyl)amino]- 5-sulfamoylbenzoic acid. Its molecular weight is 330.7gm/mol. Its structural formula is THERAPEUTIC CLASSIFICATION : Diuretic,1,1,DESCRIPTION :,"Furosemide is a diuretic indicated for use when a prompt and effective diuresis is required. The intravenous formulation is appropriate for use in emergencies or when oral therapy is precluded. Indications include cardiac, pulmonary, hepatic and renal edema.",1,1,INDICATIONS :,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:18:58.037514+00:00
