  berylliosis;  fulminating or disseminated tuberculosis (when used concurrently with appropriate antituberculous chemotherapy);  Loeffler's syndrome not manageable by other means;  aspiration pneumonitis;  moderate to severe Pneumocystis jiroveci pneumonia in AIDS patients (as adjunctive therapy when given within the first 72 hours of initial anti-pneumocystis treatment);  exacerbations of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). Hematologic Disorders  acquired (autoimmune) hemolytic anemia;  idiopathic thrombocytopenic purpura in adults;  secondary thrombocytopenia in adults;  erythroblastopenia (RBC anemia);  congenital (erythroid) hypoplastic anemia. Neoplastic Diseases (palliative management)  leukemias and lymphomas in adults;  acute leukemia of childhood;  to improve quality of life in patients with terminal cancer. Edematous States  to induce diuresis or remission of proteinuria in the nephrotic syndrome without uremia. Nervous System  cerebral edema from primary or metastatic tumors or surgical or radiation therapy;  acute exacerbations of multiple sclerosis;  acute spinal cord injury. The treatment should begin within 8 hours of injury.",2,4,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:22:54.938711+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7405,Cetirizine hydrochloride + Phenylephrine hydrochloride,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1swMYKkI5atUt233EpN_RZyOYyiNq8kZA/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7405_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1swMYKkI5atUt233EpN_RZyOYyiNq8kZA_view_usp_drivesdk_c063dea4bf.pdf,page_text/DRP-7405_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1swMYKkI5atUt233EpN_RZyOYyiNq8kZA_view_usp_drivesdk_c063dea4bf.json,cd4e2791327c747e8e3b8e69af1a6079a5ccd9d4de7b2ddc7e94602ffa0187c1,2643014,2,ocr,"Aclear, colorless to yellowish, strawberry-menthol flavoured syrup, free from visible foreign matter. Whatis in the Medicine? Each 5 mL syrup contains 5 mg of Cetirizine HCI and 5 mg of Phenylephrine HCI as the active ingredients. This product also contains Methyl Paraben and Propyl Paraben as preservatives. Cetirizine, an antiallergy, blocks the action of histamine, a substance that causes allergic symptoms. Cetirizine is less likely to cause drowsiness and dizziness than the older class of anti-allergy medicines Phenylephrine HCI, a nasal decongestant, clears obstructed air passages and nasal sinuses due to congestion making breathing easier. Italso reduces postnasal drip. Strength of the Medicine",1,1,Product Description,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T19:23:04.405201+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7406,Metfromin Hydrochloride,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hDtQWdWIn-UGG0KkoPRj5NzeIwHE6X0_/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7406_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hDtQWdWIn-UGG0KkoPRj5NzeIwHE6X0__view_usp_drivesdk_9a22786e43.pdf,page_text/DRP-7406_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hDtQWdWIn-UGG0KkoPRj5NzeIwHE6X0__view_usp_drivesdk_9a22786e43.json,5d095ca2f637f35d49d8dd36d28a55385a76bd21dab0b3ed0d56292e0f8439ad,529431,1,ocr,"All patients should continue their diet with a regular distribution of carbohydrate intake during the Metformin 500 mg Film-Coated Tablet: Overweight patients should continue their energy restricted diet. The usual laboratory tests for White to off-white, oval, biconvex, film coated tablet, plain on both sides. diabetes monitoring should be performed regularly. Metformin alone does not cause hypoglycemia, Metformin 850 mg Film-Coated Tablet: White to off-white, round, biconvex, film-coated tablet, plain on both sides. but caution is advised when it is used in combination with insulin or other oral antidiabetics (e.g., sulfonylureas or meglitinides)",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"taking into account the benefit of breast-feeding and the potential risk to adverse effects on the Treatment of type 2 diabetes mellitus in adults, particularly in overweight patients. Metformin may as monotherapy or in combination with other oral antidiabetic agents, or with insulin. Intensive glucose control with metformin as first line therapy in overweight type 2 diabetic patients",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T19:23:37.783241+00:00
