PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7408,,Dobumine,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1A0uZ31Kn3TPNUhxavCUUGEoIlGgNt03l/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7408_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1A0uZ31Kn3TPNUhxavCUUGEoIlGgNt03l_view_usp_drivesdk_2eb8e7ec3c.pdf,page_text/DRP-7408_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1A0uZ31Kn3TPNUhxavCUUGEoIlGgNt03l_view_usp_drivesdk_2eb8e7ec3c.json,b31fe12cbc42304633a26ff64c2dc7babad4e9bbad9e25a40337dd0177d84373,106955,1,digital_text,"Clear, colorless to pale yellow solution in colorless ampule. PHARMACOKINETICS Dobutamine is inactive when given by mouth, and it is rapidly inactivated in the body by similar processes. It has a half -life of about 2 minutes. Conjugates of dobutamine and its maj or metabolite 3-O-methyldobutamine are excreted primarily in urine, with small amounts eliminated in the faeces.",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Doburan (Dobutamine Hydrochloride Injection) is used to increase the contractility of the heart in acute heart failure, as occurs in cardiogenic shock and myocardial infarction; it is also used in septic shock. Other circumstances in which its inotropic activity may be useful are during cardiac surgery and positive end-expiratory pressure ventilation.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:24:00.236099+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7410-01,,Olik,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1n8GXYkZB2LYkq_dsMZIdYjFc8R1OgtZE/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7410-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1n8GXYkZB2LYkq_dsMZIdYjFc8R1OgtZE_view_usp_drivesdk_2b3aae2c2d.pdf,page_text/DRP-7410-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1n8GXYkZB2LYkq_dsMZIdYjFc8R1OgtZE_view_usp_drivesdk_2b3aae2c2d.json,d19027c487b7b69efd5f2b823d8ed8d84d7e56691d5031a361a2d248a501e0cf,942413,1,ocr,"Folic acid may reduce intestinal absorption of zinc (of particular importance in pregnancy). Folic Acid (Olik) 5 mg Tabletis a yellow, coloured round shaped, biconvex, break line on one side uncoated tablets.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Gastrointestinal disorder: Abdominal distension, flatulence, anorexia and nausea. Indicated for the treatment of megaloblastic anaemia due to folic acid deficiency. Its also used for prophylaxis in chronic haemolytic states, in renal dialysis, and in drug induced folate deficiency. defect: Folic acid is used for the prevention ofr urrence of neural For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T19:24:11.868048+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7416,Irinotecan hydrochloride,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1O2TruHkl969o4JXQniHW52hBxISMohTw/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7416_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1O2TruHkl969o4JXQniHW52hBxISMohTw_view_usp_drivesdk_45453b250e.pdf,page_text/DRP-7416_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1O2TruHkl969o4JXQniHW52hBxISMohTw_view_usp_drivesdk_45453b250e.json,4fe7b6e2316ddb64140e6b2a271032f7a60714ff8a1dc0662f4fb91a40340b88,866607,31,digital_text,"Irinotecan Hydrochloride (Concentrate Solution for Intravenous Infusion) is an antineoplastic agent of the topoisomerase I inhibitor class. Irinotecan Hydrochloride (Concentrate Solution for Intravenous Infusion) is supplied as a sterile, pale yellow, clear, aqueous solution. Each milliliter of solution contains 20 mg of irinotecan hydrochloride (on the basis of the trihydrate salt), 45 mg of sorbitol, NF, and 0.9 mg of lactic acid and Water for Injection. The pH of the solution has been adjusted to 3.5 (range, 3.0 to 3.8) with sodium hydroxide or hydrochloric acid. Irinotecan Hydrochloride, is intended for dilution with 5% Dextrose Injection, USP (D5W), or 0.9% Sodium Chloride Injection, USP, prior to intravenous infusion. The preferred diluent is 5% Dextrose Injection, USP. Irinotecan hydrochloride is a semisynthetic derivative of camptothecin, an alkaloid extract from plants such as Camptotheca acuminata or is chemically synthesized. The chemical name is (S)-4,11-diethyl-3,4,12,14-tetrahydro-4-hydroxy-3,14- dioxo1Hpyrano[3’,4’:6,7]-indolizino[1,2-b]quinolin-9-yl-[1,4’bipiperidine]-1’- carboxylate, monohydrochloride, trihydrate. Its empirical formula is C33H38N4O6•HCl•3H2O and molecular weight is 677.19. It is slightly soluble in water and organic solvents. Its structural formula is as follows .HCl .3H20 N O O N N O O O O H N",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,Irinotecan Hydrochloride Concentrate Solution for Intravenous Infusion is indicated as a component of first-line therapy for patients with metastatic carcinoma of the colon or rectum. Irinotecan Hydrochloride Concentrate Solution for Intravenous Infusion is also indicated for patients with metastatic carcinoma of the colon or rectum whose disease has recurred or progressed following initial therapy.,2,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:24:16.630641+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7419,Rivastigmine,Exelon Patch 10,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uTHzJhfwPVxi2h1Tddgv8ikcECE9Go-N/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7419_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uTHzJhfwPVxi2h1Tddgv8ikcECE9Go-N_view_usp_drivesdk_c0c5ac881c.pdf,page_text/DRP-7419_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1uTHzJhfwPVxi2h1Tddgv8ikcECE9Go-N_view_usp_drivesdk_c0c5ac881c.json,552b19a280d4d546162d194130942967cfc7d2d044baadd5d623a327463d78f8,410897,29,digital_text,"Pharmaceutical form Transdermal patch. Each patch is a thin, matrix-type transdermal patch consisting of three layers. The outside of the backing layer is beige and labelled for each patch dose as follows: - for “Exelon® Patch 5”: “AMCX” - for “Exelon® Patch 10”: “BHDI” - for “Exelon® Patch 15”: “CNFU” Active substance Each patch of 5 cm2 contains 9 mg rivastigmine base, in vivo release rate of 4.6 mg/24 hours. Each patch of 10 cm 2 contains 18 mg rivastigmine base, in vivo release rate of 9.5 mg/24 hours. Each patch of 15 cm 2 contains 27 mg rivastigmine base, in vivo release rate of 13.3 mg/24 hours. Excipients Vitamin E, poly (butylmethacrylate, methyl-methacrylate), acrylic copolymer, silicone oil. Pharmaceutical formulations may vary between countries. [Page 2]",1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,Treatment of patients with:  Mild to moderately severe dementia of the Alzheimer type  Severe dementia of the Alzheimer’s type  Mild to moderately severe dementia associated with Parkinson’s disease,2,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:24:23.314904+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7419,Rivastigmine,Exelon Patch 10,PI_02,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yvELexZYDj2v0pr0_FGrOD_WcRsc4yfK/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7419_PI_02_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1yvELexZYDj2v0pr0_FGrOD_WcRsc4yfK_view_usp_drivesdk_1e055c3173.pdf,page_text/DRP-7419_PI_02_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1yvELexZYDj2v0pr0_FGrOD_WcRsc4yfK_view_usp_drivesdk_1e055c3173.json,86d9eb18c737c78f02181ee15be8ff5da290840cbb9d51132f6c5a355af86545,541340,29,digital_text,"Pharmaceutical form Transdermal patch. Each patch is a thin, matrix-type transdermal patch consisting of three layers. The outside of the backing layer is beige and labelled for each patch dose as follows: - for Rivastigmine (Exelon®) Patch 5: “AMCX” - for Rivastigmine (Exelon®) Patch 10: “BHDI” - for Rivastigmine (Exelon®) Patch 15: “CNFU” Information might differ in some countries. Active substance Each patch of 5 cm2 contains 9 mg rivastigmine base, in vivo release rate of 4.6 mg/24 hours. Each patch of 10 cm 2 contains 18 mg rivastigmine base, in vivo release rate of 9.5 mg/24 hours. Each patch of 15 cm 2 contains 27 mg rivastigmine base, in vivo release rate of 13.3 mg/24 hours. Excipients Acrylic pressure sensitive adhesive, silicone pressure sensitive adhesive, poly (butyl- methacrylate, methyl-methacrylate), polyethylene terephthalate (backing film), fluoropolymer- coated polyethylene terephthalate (release liner), silicone oil, vitamin E. Information might differ in some countries.",1,1,DESCRIPTION AND COMPOSITION,Treatment of patients with: [Page 2]  Mild to moderately severe dementia of the Alzheimer type  Severe dementia of the Alzheimer’s type  Mild to moderately severe dementia associated with Parkinson’s disease,1,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:24:27.783808+00:00
