PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7502,Folium Senna Leaves + Semen Cana Valiae,Kancura,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zDF_NBDEPt6VdUHMAva6U8TdFfXtrf2w/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7502_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zDF_NBDEPt6VdUHMAva6U8TdFfXtrf2w_view_usp_drivesdk_563018aaed.pdf,page_text/DRP-7502_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zDF_NBDEPt6VdUHMAva6U8TdFfXtrf2w_view_usp_drivesdk_563018aaed.json,ef1b0e1ee46067b553a98e9584e7aa28a08462c94278ca4280fa7a555e2f3611,904553,1,ocr,"Senna Pods + Senna Leaves (KANCURA) herbal tea is a mixture of dried black, grayish-green and light brown fragments of senna leaves and senna pods individually packed in a teabag, contained in aluminum foil sachet, box of 4’s and 30’s. What is in the herbal tea? This herbal tea contains Folium Senna Leaves and Semen Cana Valiae (Senna Pods) that is a natural laxative. Senna is used for purging and in weight loss. They appear to act as a local irritant on the colon, which promotes peristalsis and evacuation. Senna may also enhance intestinal fluid accumulation and increase the moisture content of stool by inhibiting electrolyte and water reabsorption from the colon. Strength of the herbal tea: Each teabag contains: Senna Leaves wee eee eee eee cece e eee e eee e teen eee e nena ee ee nee eens eseeenseeeeeateesnentenses 1.04 g SENNA POMS oe. eeeeeeeeeeceeeceeeceeeeeceeeeeeeseeescesaeeeeeeeaeseeeeeeeeeseeseenseess 1.04g What is this herbal tea used for? Senna Pods + Senna Leaves (KANCURA) Herbal Tea is used for constipation and condition in which easy defecation with soft stool is desired. How much and how often should you use this herbal tea? A teabag of Senna Pods + Senna Leaves (KANCURA) Herbal Tea in a cup containing at least 200 mL of hot water. Let it steep for 15 minutes. Add honey or lemon to taste. Do not boil directly in tea pot. For best results, a teabag of Kancura before bedtime daily. Continuous administration will keep you fit and healthy. When should you not take this herbal tea? Kancura Herbal Tea should not be given to patients with nausea or vomiting and if the patient have undiagnosed intestinal obstruction, ulcerative colitis, acute surgical abdomen, appendicitis, Crohn’s disease, abdominal pain or diarrhea. Prolonged use should generally be avoided. Consult your doctor prior to use if you are pregnant or breastfeeding. Care that should be taken when taking this herbal tea: Care should be taken in patients with inflammatory disease. Prolonged use should be avoided. Longer use can cause the bowels to stop functioning normally and might cause dependence on laxatives. Long-term use can also change the amount or and other harmful effects. balance of some chemicals in the blood (electrolytes) that can cause heart function disorders, muscle weakness, liver damage, Undesirable effects of this herbal tea: Kancura Herbal Tea can cause mild abdominal discomfort such as colic or cramps. Some side effects but rare may include diarrhea, brown discoloration of urine and faintness. What other medicine or food should be avoided? Digoxin Stimulant laxatives (SENNA) can decrease potassium levels in the body. Low potassium levels can increase the risk of side Warfarin effects of digoxin. Senna can cause diarrhea; diarrhea can increase the effects of warfarin and increase the risk of bleeding. If you take warfarin do not take excessive amounts of senna. Diuretic drugs such as chlorothiazide, chlorthalidone, ferosemide, hydrochlorothiazide, and others. Some laxatives can decrease potassium in the body. “Water pills” can also decrease potassium in the body. Taking senna along with “water pill” might decrease potassium in the body too much. Signs and symptoms of overdose: Taking an overdose of Kancura Herbal Tea is likely to cause a strong laxative effect. Some of the symptoms that may appear include abdominal pain or cramping, diarrhea, and bloating. Dehydration and electrolyte imbalances can also occur as the result of severe diarrhea. Treatment for an overdose (if necessary) may involve supportive care, which consists of treating the symptoms that occur as a result of the overdose. How should you keep this herbal tea? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. When should you consult your doctor? If you are pregnant and breastfeeding or any undesirable effects occur, consult your doctor. “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph”. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration number: DRP-7502 Date of Renewal Authorization: September 16, 2020 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: September 6, 2024 Manufactured by the 4 Distributed by: Marketing Authorization Holder: _——\ REJ DIAMOND DIAMOND LABORATORIES, INC",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T19:29:33.514138+00:00
