PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7520,Atorvastatin (as Calcium),Atorpro,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1igVbaIq40gQDac6nqlHx_mBJ091O5Wff/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7520_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1igVbaIq40gQDac6nqlHx_mBJ091O5Wff_view_usp_drivesdk_5b412f93f1.pdf,page_text/DRP-7520_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1igVbaIq40gQDac6nqlHx_mBJ091O5Wff_view_usp_drivesdk_5b412f93f1.json,3d57a3f94a81c3c12b4b0802aaf2ca3fa67346ffc069f44d0de735783b9b7f60,582473,3,digital_text,"10 mg : White to off-white film-coated tablet, oval -shaped, biconvex, plain on both sides. 20 mg : White to off -white film -coated tablet, oval-shaped, biconvex, plain on one side and bisected on the other side. 40 mg : White to off -white film -coated tablet, oval-shaped, biconvex, plain on one side and bisected on the other side. Atorvastatin calcium is a synthetic lipid -lowering agent, which is an inhibit or of 3 -hydroxy-3-methylglutaryl-coenzyme A (HMG - CoA) reductase. This enzyme catalyzes the conversion of HMG - CoA to mevalonate, an early and rate -limiting step in cholesterol biosynthesis.",2,2,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Atorvastatin is used to reduce LDL-cholesterol, apolipoprotein B, and triglycerides, and to increase HDL -cholesterol in the treatment of hyperlipidaemias, including hypercholesterolaemias and combined (mixed) hyperlipidaemias (type IIa or IIb hyperlipoproteinaemias), hypertriglyceridaemia (type IV), and dysbetalipoproteinaemia (type III). It is also used for primary and secondary prophylaxis of cardiovascular events in patients with multiple risk factors, including diabetes mellitus.",2,2,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:29:46.903054+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7524,Celecoxib,Celexib,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vCOMT46x0nd349t4F_mz_VxogmHw4f1v/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7524_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vCOMT46x0nd349t4F_mz_VxogmHw4f1v_view_usp_drivesdk_7c5b149928.pdf,page_text/DRP-7524_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vCOMT46x0nd349t4F_mz_VxogmHw4f1v_view_usp_drivesdk_7c5b149928.json,75c523690bfbc91371acc122dbe625570f90635a4805ea6b8a70d9fba69f0f54,371907,1,digital_text,Celecoxib is an NSAID reported to be a selective inhibitor of cyclooxiygenase-2 (COX-2). Celexib 400mg is a white to off-white powder encapsulated in capsule size #0 with white cap and white body. Celexib 200mg is a white to off-white powder encapsulated in capsule size #2 with orange cap and yellow body.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Used in the treatment of rheumatoid arthritis and in the adjunctive treatment of adenomatous colorectal polyps; also used in the management of acute pain and dysmenorrhea.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:29:50.072096+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7534,Paracetamol,Alagesic,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1usOeyn3L8XTKfu8vexUi-xP1d5SYHovS/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7534_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1usOeyn3L8XTKfu8vexUi-xP1d5SYHovS_view_usp_drivesdk_e587ec3011.pdf,page_text/DRP-7534_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1usOeyn3L8XTKfu8vexUi-xP1d5SYHovS_view_usp_drivesdk_e587ec3011.json,d9e940924d23b03d8989f3659990d6c6e8f09876c5ae9c00dec422484790853e,1325676,1,ocr,"Paracetamol (ALAGESIC) is a clear red syrupy with a characteristic of strawberry flavor and aroma contained in a 60 ml amber bottle. What is in the medicine? Paracetamol has analgesic and anti-pyretic properties and weak anti-inflammatory activity. Paracetamol is often the analgesic or anti-pyretic of choice, especially in the elderly and in patients in whom salicylates or other NSAIDs are contraindicated. Such patients include asthmatics, those with a history of peptic ulcer, and children. Strength of the medicine: Each 5 mL of syrup contains 250 mg Paracetamol. What is this medicine used for? ___ Paracetamol (ALAGESIC) is used for relief of painful conditions including headache, migraine, bodyache, earache, toothache, N dysmenorrhea, neuralgia, arthralgia and post operative pain. Also indicated for reduction of fever. ~ = — How much and how often should you use this medicine? Children: — 1 to 5 years old 2.5 - 5 mL (1/2 - 1 teaspoonful) 6 to 12 years old 5-10mL (1-2 teaspoonfuls) To be taken 3 - 4 times a day. Or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? Do not use this medicine if you are allergic to acetaminophen or paracetamol. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: Paracetamol should be given with care to patients with impaired kidney or liver function and to patients with alcohol dependence. Chronic use should be avoided. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Adverse effects of Paracetamol are rare and usually mild, although haematological reaction including thrombocytopenia, leucopenia, pancytopenia, neutropenia, and agranulocytosis have been reported. Skin rashes and other hypersensitivity reaction occurs occasionally. — What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? The risk of Paracetamol toxicity may be increased in patients receiving other potentially hepatotoxic drugs or drugs that induce liver microsomal enzymes. The absorption of paracetamol may be accelerated by drugs such as metoclopramide. — Excretion may be affected and plasma concentrations altered when given with probenicid. Colestyramine reduces the absorption of paracetamol if given within 1 hour of paracetamol. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: Adults taking as little as 10g to 15g of paracetamol within 24 hours may develop severe liver damage and less often, renal tubular necrosis. Early signs of overdosage with paracetamol are nausea, vomiting, and may also include lethargy and sweating usually settle within 24hours. Abdominal pain may be the first indication of liver damage which is not usually apparent for 24 to 48hours and sometime may be delayed for up to 4 to 6 days after ingestion. Activated charcoal may be used to reduce gastrointestinal absorption, if it can be given1 hour of the overdose, and if more than 150 mg/kg or 12 g of paracetamol has been ingested. There is little evidence that gastric lavage is of benefit in those who have overdosed solely in paracetamol. If there is any doubt about the timing or the need to treat, then a patient should be treated with an antidote of choice (Acetylcysteine). What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. a Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? If symptoms persist and any undesirable effect occurs, consult your doctor. ~ “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph”. — Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction DRP-7534 Date of Renewal Authorization: October 14, 2021 Patient Information Leaflet date of revision: November 15, 2021 Manufactured by the Marketing Authorization Holder: Distributed by: I",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T19:29:59.576726+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7535,Dicycloverine Hydrochloride,Diaciel,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/19o2hdDHCmHMEewkUsyvcQCflZfj72rh4/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7535_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19o2hdDHCmHMEewkUsyvcQCflZfj72rh4_view_usp_drivesdk_f5eac777ca.pdf,page_text/DRP-7535_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19o2hdDHCmHMEewkUsyvcQCflZfj72rh4_view_usp_drivesdk_f5eac777ca.json,dc662b083e6bd6ee62b14ef245e5bc217a027f954597e2d345613f20bedd7ce1,1296010,1,ocr,"Dicycloverine Hydrochloride (DIACIEL) is a white, round tablet, scored on one side with company logo on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Functional gastrointestinal tract conditions involving smooth muscle spasm e.g. irritable colon (mucus colitis, spastic colon, irritable bowel syndrome) and spastic constipation. As adjunctive therapy in organic gastrointestinal conditions to relieve associated smooth muscle spasm e.g. in colitis, diverticulitis, regional enteritis, gastritis and peptic ulcer.",1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T19:30:10.771530+00:00
