PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7568,CEFUROXIME (AS AXETIL),XYFROX,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gtr9K86r0808dZXuFGqAOhzthJHiyhpZ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7568_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gtr9K86r0808dZXuFGqAOhzthJHiyhpZ_view_usp_drivesdk_e60cf13090.pdf,page_text/DRP-7568_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gtr9K86r0808dZXuFGqAOhzthJHiyhpZ_view_usp_drivesdk_e60cf13090.json,4e310033676e13afc1944b0e65b96baac1c46d90c79ee7c282cdb5d7ba977a3b,2005708,1,ocr,"cefbuperazone cefmenoxime, cefmetazole, cefonicid cefoperazone. ceforanide, cefotetan, cefpiramide, and latamoxef. The presence of methylthiotriazine ring, as ceftriaxone, might also be White to off-white film coated, oblong shaped biconvex tablet plain on one side and bisected on the associated with such bleeding disorders other side containing 500 mg of Cefuroxime (as axetil). It complies with the USP specifications for Cefuroxime axetil tablets. DOSAGE AND ADMINISTRATION Adults DESCRIPTION Cefuroxime Axetil is a mixture of the diastereoisomers of cefuroxime axetil. A white or almost white Uncomplicated Urinary-Tract Infections: Usual oral doses are 125 mg twice daily. Respiratory-Tract Infections: 250 to 500 mg twice daily. powder. The amorphous form is insoluble in water and in ether; slightly soluble in dehydrated alcohol. For Lyme disease: 500 mg orally twice daily for 20 days. freely soluble in acetone; soluble in chloroform, in ethyl acetate, and in methyl alcohol. The crystalline form is insoluble in water and ether; slightly soluble in dehydrated alcohol; freely soluble in acetone Uncomplicated Gonnorhoea: Single 1 g (1000 mg) oral dose Or as prescribed by the physician sparingly soluble in chloroform, in ethyl acetate, and in methyl alcohol. Store in airtight containers. PREGNANCY AND LACTATION There is no experimental evidence of embryopathic or teratogenic effects attributable to cefuroxime but, as with all drugs, it should be administered with caution during the early months of pregnancy. Cefuroxime is excreted in human milk, and consequently, caution should be exercised when cefuroxime is administered to a nursing mother. OVERDOSE AND TREATMENT Symptoms: Over dosage of cephalosporins can cause cerebral irritation leading to convulsions ANTIMICROBIAL ACTION Treatment: Serum levels of cefuroxime can be reduced by hemodialysis and peritoneal dialysis Cefuroxime is bactericidal and has a similar spectrum of antimicrobial action and pattern of resistance CONTRAINDICATION to those of cefamandole. It is more resistant to hydrolysis by beta-lactamases than cefamandole, and It is contraindicated in patients with known allergy to cephalosporin group of antibiotic. therefore may be more active against beta-lactamase producing strains, Haemophilus influenzae and Neisseria gonnorhea. However, treatment failures have occurred in patients with H. influenzae CAUTION meningitis give cefuroxime and might be associated with a relatively high minimum bactericidal Foods, Drugs, Devices and Cosmetics Act prohibits dispensing without prescription. concentration when compared with the minimum inhibitory concentration or with a significant inoculum effect. Reduced affinity of penicillin-binding proteins for cefuroxime has also been reported to STORAGE CONDITION be responsible for resistance in a beta-lactamase - negative strain of H. influenzae. Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. PHARMACOKINETICS ADR REPORTING STATEMENT Cefuroxime axetil is absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract and is rapidly hydrolyzed in the intestinal mucosa and blood to cefuroxime; absorption is enhanced in the presence of food. Peak plasma “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph”. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction concentrations are reported about 2 to 3 hours after an oral dose. The sodium salt is given by intramus- cular or intravenous injection. Peak plasma concentrations of about 27 tg per mL have been achieved AVAILABILITY 45 minutes after an intramuscular dose of 750 mg with measurable amounts present 8 hours after a Aluminum Strip Foil x 10's (Box of 50's) dose. Up to 50% of cefuroxime in the circulation is bound to plasma proteins. The plasma half-life is about 70 minutes and is prolonged in patients with renal impairment and in neonates. REGISTRATION NUMBER DRP-7568 DRUG INTERACTION Concomitant administration of probenecid with cefuroxime axetil increases the area under the serum DATE OF FIRST AUTHORIZATION/RENEWAL concentration versus time curve by 50%. The peak serum cefuroxime concentration after a 1.5 g single Manufactured by: dose is greater when taken with 1 g of probenecid (mean = 14.8 mcg/mL than without probenecid",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Edison St., cor. Cul de Sac St., Km. 14 Alternative drug for infections due to susceptible organisms such as in otitis media, orbital cellulitis, West Service Road, Parafaque, Metro Manila [Page 2]",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T19:33:04.455748+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7571,Telmisartan + Hydrochlorothiazide,Micardis Plus,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VErHRIPOEyQt5vVfR0fYbiSpmPGvIjgm/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7571_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VErHRIPOEyQt5vVfR0fYbiSpmPGvIjgm_view_usp_drivesdk_43e4883e87.pdf,page_text/DRP-7571_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VErHRIPOEyQt5vVfR0fYbiSpmPGvIjgm_view_usp_drivesdk_43e4883e87.json,bdbe47e3feab8ee4055db614b70c1591b6393184fd803bc43f67d4300faff743,197107,18,digital_text,"Telmisartan/Hydrochlorothiazide layered tablets, 40/12.5 mg are bilayered tablets of oblong, biconvex shape. The two layers have different colors with the Telmisartan layer being white, the Hydrochlorothiazide layer is red. The white layer is marked with the Boehringer Ingelheim company symbol and the code H4. The tablets are for oral administration. Telmisartan / Hydrochlorothiazide layered tablets, 80/12.5 mg are bilayered tablets of oblong, biconvex shape. The two layers have different colors with the Telmisartan layer being white, the Hydrochlorothiazide layer is red. The white layer is marked with the Boehringer Ingelheim company symbol and the code H8. The tablets are for oral administration. Telmisartan / Hydrochlorothiazide layered tablets, 80/25 mg are bilayered tablets of oblong, biconvex shape. The two layers have different colors with the Telmisartan layer being white, the Hydrochlorothiazide layer is yellow. The white layer is marked with the Boehringer Ingelheim company symbol and the code H9. The tablets are for oral administration.",1,1,Product Description,Treatment of essential hypertension. As fixed dose combination Telmisartan + HCTZ (Micardis Plus) is indicated in patients whose blood pressure is not adequately controlled on telmisartan or hydrochlorothiazide alone.,1,1,Indications / Usage,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:33:08.691124+00:00
