PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7602,Paracetamol,Unbranded,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PIEaX_JUEApyCHGasST3THEjOfhHdCis/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7602_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PIEaX_JUEApyCHGasST3THEjOfhHdCis_view_usp_drivesdk_9fe9f50eb8.pdf,page_text/DRP-7602_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PIEaX_JUEApyCHGasST3THEjOfhHdCis_view_usp_drivesdk_9fe9f50eb8.json,38abd6b7404c5377cef94fb06dabbc7a863edc9bf8f1b2222f09b8dec6e74338,150101,1,digital_text,"Paracetamol 500 mg tablet is a peach colored, round, flat, beveled edge tablet and scored on one side. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This product contains paracetamol, a fever and pain reliever. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? For the symptomatic treatment of mild to moderate pain and of fever. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? • If the patient is allergic to paracetamol or any ingredient in the product. • Avoid long-term use of paracetamol in patients with anemia or with heart, lung, kidney, or liver disease. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? • Liver Warning. This product contains paracetamol. Severe liver damage may occur if: > An adult or child 12 years old and above takes more than 4 g of paracetamol in 24 hours, which is the maximum daily amount; > Taken with other medicines containing paracetamol (or acetaminophen); > An adult has 3 or more alcoholic drinks everyday while using this product. • Do not use with any other medicine containing paracetamol (prescription or nonprescription). If you are not sure whether a medicine contains paracetamol, ask a doctor. • Ask a doctor before use if the patient has kidney or liver problems. • Ask a doctor before use if the patient is taking warfarin, a blood thinning medicine. • Do not use after the expiry date on the label",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T19:35:06.087623+00:00
