PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7623,Sildenafil (as citrate),Seregra,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_cPdbeNO6iy2Ol1y_ABHvuudSo2dHR1O/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7623_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_cPdbeNO6iy2Ol1y_ABHvuudSo2dHR1O_view_usp_drivesdk_afe5dc58e1.pdf,page_text/DRP-7623_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_cPdbeNO6iy2Ol1y_ABHvuudSo2dHR1O_view_usp_drivesdk_afe5dc58e1.json,321a9842c3787dc73365ea06f9dd14e873ea6ba065a72994b5871ae16c8009c0,895833,2,digital_text,"Sildenafil citrate is a white to off-white crystalline powder with a solubility of 3.5 mg/mL in water and a molecular weight of 666.7. Sildenafil citrate has the following structural formula: Sildenafil is a selective inhibitor of cyclic guanosine monophosphate (cGMP)-specific phosphodiesterase type 5 (PDE5). Sildenafil tablets are formulated as blue, diamond-shaped film coated tablets equivalent to 50 mg and 100 mg of Sildenafil for oral administration.",2,2,DESCRIPTION:,Sildenafil is indicated for the management of erectile dysfunction .,2,2,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:37:31.188420+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7643,Bortezomib,Dotrex 2,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1QtL102ACbPR6O-MP2gheQLoOuZudBPfs/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7643_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QtL102ACbPR6O-MP2gheQLoOuZudBPfs_view_usp_drivesdk_eaec326384.pdf,page_text/DRP-7643_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1QtL102ACbPR6O-MP2gheQLoOuZudBPfs_view_usp_drivesdk_eaec326384.json,85bd686b152b0ac47b733756d82ca5cb866b9f4780786b825ee9b14481c85924,497016,2,digital_text,"Bortezomib for injection is an antineoplastic agent available for intravenous (Rapid bolus) use only. Bortezomib is a modified dipeptidyl boronic acid which is in the form of mannitol boronic ester, reconstituted form, consists of the mannitol ester in equilibrium with its hydrolysis product, the monomeric boronic acid. The chemical name for bortezomib, the monomeric boronic acid, is [(1R)-3-methyl-1-[[(2S)-1-OXO-3-phenyl-2-[(pyrazinylcabony) amino]propyl]amino]butyl] boronic acid. Bortezomib has the following chemical structure: The molecular weight is 384.24. The molecular formula is C H BN O .The solubility of bortezomib. As the monomeric boronic acid, in water is 3.3-3.8 19 25 4 4 mg /mL in a pH range of 2.0-6.5.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"BORTEZOMIB as monotherapy or in combination with pegylated liposomal doxorubicin or dexamethasone is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with progressive multiple myeloma who have received at least 1 prior therapy and who have already undergone or are unsuitable for haematopoietic stem cell transplantation. BORTEZOMIB in combination with melphalan and prednisone is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with previously untreated multiple myeloma who are not eligible for high-dose chemotherapy with haematopoietic stem cell transplantation. BORTEZOMIB in combination with dexamethasone, or with dexamethasone and thalidomide, is indicated for the induction treatment of adult patients with previously untreated multiple myeloma who are eligible for high-dose chemotherapy with haematopoietic stem cell transplantation.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:37:38.343390+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7643-01,Bortezomib,Tezobort,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1kjYLg9sGQbtdXMIg6YyE7c9jCxUF-0Lz/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7643-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kjYLg9sGQbtdXMIg6YyE7c9jCxUF-0Lz_view_usp_drivesdk_91589d7d21.pdf,page_text/DRP-7643-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kjYLg9sGQbtdXMIg6YyE7c9jCxUF-0Lz_view_usp_drivesdk_91589d7d21.json,c7b8a342badce14389585ae0efaf0923619a494f0bb84b56a9aa30b2aa7327d7,502520,2,digital_text,"Bortezomib for injection is an antineoplastic agent available for intravenous (Rapid bolus) use only. Bortezomib is a modified dipeptidyl boronic acid which is in the form of mannitol boronic ester, reconstituted form, consists of the mannitol ester in equilibrium with its hydrolysis product, the monomeric boronic acid. The chemical name for bortezomib, the monomeric boronic acid, is [(1R)-3-methyl-1-[[(2S)-1-OXO-3-phenyl-2-[(pyrazinylcabony) amino]propyl]amino]butyl] boronic acid. Bortezomib has the following chemical structure: The molecular weight is 384.24. The molecular formula is C H BN O .The solubility of bortezomib. As the monomeric boronic acid, in water is 3.3-3.8 19 25 4 4 mg /mL in a pH range of 2.0-6.5.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"BORTEZOMIB as monotherapy or in combination with pegylated liposomal doxorubicin or dexamethasone is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with progressive multiple myeloma who have received at least 1 prior therapy and who have already undergone or are unsuitable for haematopoietic stem cell transplantation. BORTEZOMIB in combination with melphalan and prednisone is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with previously untreated multiple myeloma who are not eligible for high-dose chemotherapy with haematopoietic stem cell transplantation. BORTEZOMIB in combination with dexamethasone, or with dexamethasone and thalidomide, is indicated for the induction treatment of adult patients with previously untreated multiple myeloma who are eligible for high-dose chemotherapy with haematopoietic stem cell transplantation.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:37:34.623869+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7649,Amoxicillin,None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1O3S9JQzBeWzNUf79elYJJlW8QiPJ7SuZ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7649_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1O3S9JQzBeWzNUf79elYJJlW8QiPJ7SuZ_view_usp_drivesdk_08e0f8f18f.pdf,page_text/DRP-7649_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1O3S9JQzBeWzNUf79elYJJlW8QiPJ7SuZ_view_usp_drivesdk_08e0f8f18f.json,03945eacf76013839d1208cc179f2f9d23dbf7d2eaefab253bf1eacadac7198c,2304131,1,ocr,Penicillins including amoxicillin may decrease renal clearance of methotrexate by inhibiting renal tubular secretion of the drug. Oral probenecids prolongs the half-life of penicillins by Amoxicillin is a white to off white crystalline powder contained in a_blue/white gelatin capsule: 250 mg (EGC #1) competing with it for renal tubular secretion. Concomitant use of penicillins with oral contraceptives may cause breakthrough bleeding.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated in a wide range of infections such as repiratory, genito-urinary, skin and soft tissue Manufactured by the infections, otitis media, tonsillitis, pharyngitis, laryngitis, septicemia, osteomyelitis, Marketing Authorization Holder: meningitis, including venereal infections such as gonorrhea and syphilis.",1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T19:37:56.767409+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7650,Valsartan + Hydrochlorothiazide,Co-Diovan,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FPWBHwRocHc_CdsPk06vofH8nK2rZ36r/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7650_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FPWBHwRocHc_CdsPk06vofH8nK2rZ36r_view_usp_drivesdk_4112ee8160.pdf,page_text/DRP-7650_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1FPWBHwRocHc_CdsPk06vofH8nK2rZ36r_view_usp_drivesdk_4112ee8160.json,ea14f05455698a48f32a06d6b66a53e2a764555130354d40623f4b8fe5b9490f,266701,22,digital_text,"Film-coated tablets (FCT) 80/12.5 mg, 160/12.5 mg, 160/25 mg, 320/12.5 mg, 320/25 mg. Co-Diovan 80/12.5 mg: Ovaloid slightly convex, non -divisible, film -coated tablets measuring approximately 10.2 mm in length and approximately 5.4 mm in width, and weighing approximately 156 mg. The tablets are colored light orange and debossed “HGH” on one side and “CG” on the other side. Co-Diovan 160/12.5 mg: Ovaloid slightly convex, non -divisible, film -coated tablets measuring approximately 15.2 mm in length and approximately 6.2 mm in width, and weighing approximately 312 mg. The tablets are colored dark red and debossed “HHH” on one side and “CG” on the other side. Co-Diovan 160/25 mg: Ovaloid slightly convex, non -divisible, film -coated tablets measuring approximately 14.2 mm in length and approximately 5.7 mm in width, and weighing approximately 310 mg. The tablets are colored brown -orange and debossed “HXH” on one side and “NVR” on the other side. Co-Diovan 320/12.5 mg: Ovaloid slightly convex, non -divisible, film -coated tablets measuring approximately 17.6 mm in length and approximately 8.2 mm in width, and weighing approximately 608 mg. The tablets are colored pink and debossed “HIL” on one side and “NVR” on the other side. Co-Diovan 320/25 mg: Ovaloid slightly convex, non -divisible, film -coated tablets measuring approximately 17.7 mm in length and approximately 8.2 mm in width, and weighing approximately 620 mg. The tablets are colored yellow and debossed “CTI” on one side and “NVR” on the other side. Co-Diovan® FCT cannot be divided into equal doses. Valsartan Hydrochlorothiazide [Page 2] Active substances One tablet contains 80 mg valsartan and 12.5 mg hy drochlorothiazide, or 160 mg valsartan and 12.5 mg hydrochlorothiazide, or 160 mg valsartan and 25 mg hydrochlorothiazide, or 320 mg valsartan and 12.5 mg hydrochlorothiazide, or 320 mg valsartan and 25 mg hydrochlorothiazide. Appearance of tablets may var y between countries. Certain dosage strengths may not be available in all countries. EXCIPIENTS 80/12.5 mg: Colloidal silicon dioxide; crospovidone; hydroxypropyl methylcellulose; magnesium stearate; microcrystalline cellulose; polyethylene glycol; talc; titanium dioxide (E171); red iron oxide (E172); yellow iron oxide (E172). 160/12.5 mg: Colloidal silicon dioxide; crospovidone; hydroxypropyl -methylcellulose; magnesium stearate; microcrystalline cellulose; polyethylene glycol; talc; titanium dioxide (E171); red iron oxide (E172). 160/25 mg: Colloidal silicon dioxide; crospovidone; hydroxypropyl methylcellulose; magnesium stearate; microcrystalline cellulose; polyethylene glycol; talc; titanium dioxide (E171), red iron oxide (E172), yellow iron oxide (E172) , black iron oxide",1,2,Pharmaceutical form,"Treatment of hypertension in adults, 18 years of age and older . Treatment of hypertension in patients whose blood pressure is not adequately controlled by monotherapy. As initial therapy in patients who are likely to need multiple drugs to achieve blood pressure goals. The choice as initial therapy for hypertension should be based on an assessment of potential benefits and risks. [Page 3]",2,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:38:05.504737+00:00
