PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7677,Valsartan + Hydrochlorothiazide,Co-Diovan,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1puE2JMNBpKKB4RuNuYZzKblVzHGVImfs/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7677_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1puE2JMNBpKKB4RuNuYZzKblVzHGVImfs_view_usp_drivesdk_be4c5913cc.pdf,page_text/DRP-7677_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1puE2JMNBpKKB4RuNuYZzKblVzHGVImfs_view_usp_drivesdk_be4c5913cc.json,ea14f05455698a48f32a06d6b66a53e2a764555130354d40623f4b8fe5b9490f,266701,22,digital_text,"Film-coated tablets (FCT) 80/12.5 mg, 160/12.5 mg, 160/25 mg, 320/12.5 mg, 320/25 mg. Co-Diovan 80/12.5 mg: Ovaloid slightly convex, non -divisible, film -coated tablets measuring approximately 10.2 mm in length and approximately 5.4 mm in width, and weighing approximately 156 mg. The tablets are colored light orange and debossed “HGH” on one side and “CG” on the other side. Co-Diovan 160/12.5 mg: Ovaloid slightly convex, non -divisible, film -coated tablets measuring approximately 15.2 mm in length and approximately 6.2 mm in width, and weighing approximately 312 mg. The tablets are colored dark red and debossed “HHH” on one side and “CG” on the other side. Co-Diovan 160/25 mg: Ovaloid slightly convex, non -divisible, film -coated tablets measuring approximately 14.2 mm in length and approximately 5.7 mm in width, and weighing approximately 310 mg. The tablets are colored brown -orange and debossed “HXH” on one side and “NVR” on the other side. Co-Diovan 320/12.5 mg: Ovaloid slightly convex, non -divisible, film -coated tablets measuring approximately 17.6 mm in length and approximately 8.2 mm in width, and weighing approximately 608 mg. The tablets are colored pink and debossed “HIL” on one side and “NVR” on the other side. Co-Diovan 320/25 mg: Ovaloid slightly convex, non -divisible, film -coated tablets measuring approximately 17.7 mm in length and approximately 8.2 mm in width, and weighing approximately 620 mg. The tablets are colored yellow and debossed “CTI” on one side and “NVR” on the other side. Co-Diovan® FCT cannot be divided into equal doses. Valsartan Hydrochlorothiazide [Page 2] Active substances One tablet contains 80 mg valsartan and 12.5 mg hy drochlorothiazide, or 160 mg valsartan and 12.5 mg hydrochlorothiazide, or 160 mg valsartan and 25 mg hydrochlorothiazide, or 320 mg valsartan and 12.5 mg hydrochlorothiazide, or 320 mg valsartan and 25 mg hydrochlorothiazide. Appearance of tablets may var y between countries. Certain dosage strengths may not be available in all countries. EXCIPIENTS 80/12.5 mg: Colloidal silicon dioxide; crospovidone; hydroxypropyl methylcellulose; magnesium stearate; microcrystalline cellulose; polyethylene glycol; talc; titanium dioxide (E171); red iron oxide (E172); yellow iron oxide (E172). 160/12.5 mg: Colloidal silicon dioxide; crospovidone; hydroxypropyl -methylcellulose; magnesium stearate; microcrystalline cellulose; polyethylene glycol; talc; titanium dioxide (E171); red iron oxide (E172). 160/25 mg: Colloidal silicon dioxide; crospovidone; hydroxypropyl methylcellulose; magnesium stearate; microcrystalline cellulose; polyethylene glycol; talc; titanium dioxide (E171), red iron oxide (E172), yellow iron oxide (E172) , black iron oxide",1,2,Pharmaceutical form,"Treatment of hypertension in adults, 18 years of age and older . Treatment of hypertension in patients whose blood pressure is not adequately controlled by monotherapy. As initial therapy in patients who are likely to need multiple drugs to achieve blood pressure goals. The choice as initial therapy for hypertension should be based on an assessment of potential benefits and risks. [Page 3]",2,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:38:25.138528+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7680-03,Sodium Hyaluronate,Hynadin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/13l5knn_Y8oLfo9P0nzIsKoST8JxiazMX/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7680-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13l5knn_Y8oLfo9P0nzIsKoST8JxiazMX_view_usp_drivesdk_03376578c8.pdf,page_text/DRP-7680-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13l5knn_Y8oLfo9P0nzIsKoST8JxiazMX_view_usp_drivesdk_03376578c8.json,bda31c2d876b0f5f27bfb7faab3c553a82a2b5894865d440c2fd18c0f7e1b122,290433,1,digital_text,"Colorless and clear ophthalmic solution. Salcedo Village, Makati City, Metro Manila corner [Page 2]",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T19:38:31.583674+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7687,Diclofenac Potassium,Cataflam,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1aFKCtBZam0r-zm16OzjZhVwYvQQW6LVm/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7687_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1aFKCtBZam0r-zm16OzjZhVwYvQQW6LVm_view_usp_drivesdk_8221ba7610.pdf,page_text/DRP-7687_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1aFKCtBZam0r-zm16OzjZhVwYvQQW6LVm_view_usp_drivesdk_8221ba7610.json,d12e20eecdebedbd013399cb4a5f04c252dcd428cefc16f663c2e023d707dcaf,231175,15,digital_text,Sugar-coated tablets. Active substance The active substance is diclofenac potassium. Each sugar-coated tablet contains 25 mg or 50 mg of diclofenac potassium. Diclofenac potassium (Cataflam®) 25 mg tablet is an over-the-counter (OTC) preparation. Active moiety Diclofenac Excipients Core: Magnesium stearate; povidone; silica colloidal anhydrous; sodium starch glycollate; maize starch; calcium phosphate. Sugar-coat: Microcrystalline cellulose; polyethylene glycol 8000; red iron oxide (E172) and titanium dioxide (E171) (dispersed Anstead); povidone; talc; sucrose. Polish: polyethylene glycol 8000; sucrose. Imprint with printing ink brown for 25 mg and white for 50 mg. Pharmaceutical formulations may vary between countries.,1,1,Pharmaceutical form,"Short-term treatment in the following acute conditions: • Post-traumatic pain, inflammation and swelling, e.g. due to sprains. Diclofenac potassium [Page 2] • Post-operative pain, inflammation and swelling, e.g. following dental or orthopedic surgery. • Painful and/or inflammatory conditions in gynecology, e.g. primary dysmenorrhea or adnexitis. • Migraine attacks. • Painful syndromes of the vertebral column. • Non-articular rheumatism. • As an adjuvant in severe painful inflammatory infections of the ear, nose or throat, e.g. pharyngotonsillitis, otitis. In keeping with general therapeutic principles, the underlying disease should be treated with basic therapy, as appropriate. Fever alone is not an indication.",1,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:38:37.356137+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7692-01,Moxifloxacin (As Hydrochloride),Quinofta,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dLBZ0hcpMD6rROOhcs3UF6dHZ4r144n_/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7692-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dLBZ0hcpMD6rROOhcs3UF6dHZ4r144n__view_usp_drivesdk_172874fb12.pdf,page_text/DRP-7692-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dLBZ0hcpMD6rROOhcs3UF6dHZ4r144n__view_usp_drivesdk_172874fb12.json,8752ff88661e5fe361a828ec17130f14b86abd8446d56cc8349650c19e64f9db,700674,1,digital_text,"Each mL contains: Mechanism of Action: Moxifloxacin Hydrochloride USP Excipients: Boric acid, hydrochloric acid, Sodium chloride, sodium hydroxide, water for injection. Pharmacodynamics In vitro resistance to moxifloxacin develops via multiple-step mutations. Resistance to moxifloxacin -9 -11 occurs in vitro at a general frequency of between 1.8 x 10 to < 1 x 10 for Gram-positive bacteria. Moxifloxacin has been shown to be active against most strains of the following microorganisms: Pharmacotherapeutic group: Ophthalmologicals; anti-infectives, other anti-infective.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Aerobic Gram-negative microorganisms One drop three times a day for 7 days. Or as prescribed by the physician. Hypersensitivity to moxifloxacin, to other quinolones, or to any of the components in this medication. Treatment of bacterial conjunctivitis, corneal epithelial inflammation or corneal ulcer, pre-op & post-op sterilization.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T19:38:40.866784+00:00
