PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7811,Bromhexine Hydrochlrodie,Bisolem,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vm77w3TVWKeHU5p08E1oRf5DsLDYioFh/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7811_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vm77w3TVWKeHU5p08E1oRf5DsLDYioFh_view_usp_drivesdk_53a4c2a26a.pdf,page_text/DRP-7811_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vm77w3TVWKeHU5p08E1oRf5DsLDYioFh_view_usp_drivesdk_53a4c2a26a.json,c5e9859696b252e91bed9eaee607a0574e20df4e7b6da3b8e3aae4d53a3b70be,836239,1,ocr,"The medicine is a clear yellow syrupy cola flavored syrup contained in a 60 mL amber round bottle. What is in the medicine? Bisolem Elixir contains Bromhexine Hydrochloride which is used for conditions where there is a lot of thick mucus in the airways. Bromhexine Hydrochloride belongs to a group of medications called mucolytics. Bromhexine Hydrochloride works by thinning the mucus in the airways, thus making the mucus less sticky and it also facilitates the removal of the mucus. Strength of the medicine: Each 5 milliliter contains 4 mg Bromhexine Hydrochloride. What is this medicine used for? oss — Bromhexine Hydrochloride is used in the treatment of respiratory disorders associated with viscid or excessive mucus. How much and how often should you use this medicine? — 2 to 6 years old 2.5 mL (1/2 teaspoon) — 7 to 12 years old . 5 mL (1 teaspoonful) — ae Adult 10 mL (2 teaspoonfuls) To be taken 3-4 times a day or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? - If the patient is hypersensitive with Bromhexine Hydrochloride. - Before taking this medication, tell your doctor if you have: Symptoms indicative of pneumonia or other lung infections (e.g. breathing difficulty while resting blood-stained mucus, fever with temperature more than 38°C, chest pain), having low immune system due to other health conditions (e.g. HIV) or medications (e.g. chemotherapy, immune system medication) or existing lung conditions such as chronic obstructive lung disorder or severe uncontrolled asthma. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: - Care is advisable in patients with a history of peptic ulcer disease and asthma. acs - Do not use after the expiry date on the label. ae sc - Do not take more than the recommended use. Undesirable effects of this medicine: _ - Gastrointestinal adverse effects may occur occasionally with Bromhexine Hydrochloride and a transient rise in ss serum aminotransferase values has been reported. - Other reported adverse effects include headache, dizziness, sweating, and skin rashes. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? - Inform your doctor if you are taking any antibiotics, as Bromhexine Hydrochloride may increase the absorption of antibiotics. Also if you have recently taken or plan to take other medications, nutritional supplements or herbal products. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Do not double the dose. Signs and symptoms of overdose: No symptoms of overdosage have been reported in man to date. If they occur, symptomatic treatment should be provided. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? - Please seek your doctor’s advice before using this medication if you are pregnant or breastfeeding or likely to become pregnant or breastfeed during the course of medication. - If symptoms persist consult your doctor. cae _ “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph.” _— Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. a DRP-7811 Date of Renewal Authorization: February 14, 2022 Patient Information Leaflet Date of Revision: June 8, 2023 Manufactured by the Marketing Authorization Holder: Distributed by:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T19:47:09.529258+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7812,Chlrophenamine Maleate,Riphen,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Az8sVOl7AhiIXR2iPpOHzribZpiNNl3N/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7812_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Az8sVOl7AhiIXR2iPpOHzribZpiNNl3N_view_usp_drivesdk_c9ccfeb295.pdf,page_text/DRP-7812_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Az8sVOl7AhiIXR2iPpOHzribZpiNNl3N_view_usp_drivesdk_c9ccfeb295.json,924eaeff55436e86b13371bbdb2596f5ee035faf47fb64e339c7bd690fd54712,1650891,1,ocr,"Chlrophenamine Maleate (RIPHEN) is a white, round tablet, scored on one side with company logo on the",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Chlorphenamine Maleate (Riphen) 4 mg Tablet Blister Pack x 20’s (Box of 100’s) For symptomatic relief of allergy such as hay fever, urticaria; emergency treatment of anaphylactic reactions. Chlorphenamine Maleate (Riphen) 2 mg/5 mL Syrup x 60 mL Amber Bottle",1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T19:47:23.110181+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7813-01,Rosuvastatin (As Calcium),Fumicrest,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Sud6K6rHe9U7eXl3L4815VECqKajH8lK/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7813-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Sud6K6rHe9U7eXl3L4815VECqKajH8lK_view_usp_drivesdk_7b83c5cbe4.pdf,page_text/DRP-7813-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Sud6K6rHe9U7eXl3L4815VECqKajH8lK_view_usp_drivesdk_7b83c5cbe4.json,8f13901d36cfa3055a8025a193cb16f8228d156037289d0f56f25d8f2b6d1cc9,441070,1,digital_text,"Yellow coloured, round shaped, biconvex, film-coated tablets. PHARMACOLOGICAL ACTION: Rosuvastatin is a selective and competitive inhibitor of HMG-CoA reductase, the rate-limiting enzyme that converts 3-hydroxy- 3-methylglutaryl coenzyme A to mevalonate, a precursor of cholesterol. Pharmacokinetics: Absorption: In clinical pharmacology studies in man, peak plasma concentrations of rosuvastatin were reached 3 to 5 hours following oral dosing. Both peak concentration (Cmax) and area under the plasma concentration-time curve (AUC) increased in approximate proportion to rosuvastatin dose. The absolute bioavailability of rosuvastatin is approximately 20%. Distribution: Mean volume of distribution at steady-state of rosuvastatin is approximately 134 liters. Rosuvastatin is 88% bound to plasma proteins, mostly albumin. This binding is reversible and independent of plasma concentrations. Metabolism: Rosuvastatin is not extensively metabolized; approximately 10% of a radiolabeled dose is recovered as metabolite. The major metabolite is Ndesmethyl rosuvastatin, which is formed principally by cytochrome P450 2C9, and in vitro studies have demonstrated that N-desmethyl rosuvastatin has approximately one-sixth to one-half the HMG-CoA reductase inhibitory activity of the parent compound. Overall, greater than 90% of active plasma HMG-CoA reductase inhibitory activity is accounted for the parent compound. Excretion: Following oral administration, rosuvastatin and its metabolites are primarily excreted in the feces (90%). The elimination half-life (t1/2) of rosuvastatin is approximately 19 hours. Pharmacodynamics: Rosuvastatin reduces elevated LDL-cholesterol, total cholesterol and triglycerides and increases HDL-cholesterol. It also lowers ApoB, non-HDL-C, VLDL-C, VLDL-TG and increases ApoA-I. Rosuvastatin also lowers the LDL-C/HDL-C, total C/HDL-C and nonHDL-C/HDL-C and the ApoB/ApoA-I ratios.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Hypercholesterolemia Adults Rosuvastatin calcium is indicated as an adjunct to diet, at least equivalent to the Adult Treatment Panel III (ATP III TLC diet), for the reduction of elevated total cholesterol (Total-C), LDL-C, ApoB, the Total-C/HDL-C ratio and triglycerides (TG) and for increasing HDL-C. Pediatrics (10 – 17 years of age) Rosuvastatin is indicated as an adjunct to diet for the reduction of elevated total cholesterol (Total-C), LDL-C and ApoB in boys and girls who are at least one year post-menarche, 10 to 17 years of age with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolemia when response to diet alone has been inadequate. Prevention of Major Cardiovascular Events In adult patients without documented history of cardiovascular or cerebrovascular events, but with at least two conventional risk factors for cardiovascular disease, Rosuvastatin calcium is indicated to: - Reduce the risk of nonfatal myocardial infarction - Reduce the risk of nonfatal stroke - Reduce the risk of coronary artery revascularization",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:32:40.047090+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7814,Paracetamol,Alagesic,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1YGjlsaxCJ0wvRRaKLwXn0jn7FJn2UfdQ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7814_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YGjlsaxCJ0wvRRaKLwXn0jn7FJn2UfdQ_view_usp_drivesdk_5d2462c6d6.pdf,page_text/DRP-7814_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1YGjlsaxCJ0wvRRaKLwXn0jn7FJn2UfdQ_view_usp_drivesdk_5d2462c6d6.json,60992f50b7a357a20dcc3a3fcdeef7a4ec19d8bb1f5ad7ac5ac4e432cb22a920,2221447,1,ocr,"The medicine is a milky orange colored suspension with orange flavor and aroma contained in a 60 mL amber round bottle. What is in the medicine? Paracetamol has analgesic and antipyretic properties and weak anti-inflammatory activity. Paracetamol is often the analgesic or antipyretic of choice, especially in the elderly and in patients in whom salicylates or other NSAIDs are contraindicated. Such patients include asthmatics, those with a history of peptic ulcer and children. Strength of the medicine: Each 5 mL of suspension contains 250 mg Paracetamol. What is this medicine used for? Paracetamol (ALAGESIC) is used for relief of painful conditions including ‘headache, migraine, bodyache, earache, toothache, . nies! eS miele Se eeael “dysmenorrhea, neuralgia, arthralgia and post opérative pain. Also indicated for reduction of fever. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Children: 1 to 5 years old .... .2.5-5 mL (1/2 - 1 teaspoonful) 6 to 12 years old .. . 5-10mL (1-2 teaspoonfuls) To be taken every 4-6 hours, maximum of 4 doses in 24 hours. Or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? Do not use this medicine if you are allergic to acetaminophen or paracetamol. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: Paracetamol should be given with care to patients with impaired kidney or liver function and to patients with alcohol dependence. Chronic use should be avoided. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Adverse effects of Paracetamol are rare and usually mild, although haematological, reaction including thrombocytopenia, i leucopenia, pancytopenia, neutropenia, and agranulocytosis have been reported. Skin rashes and other hypersensitivity reaction occurs occasionally. t What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? The risk of Paracetamol toxicity may be increased in patients receiving other potentially hepatotoxic drugs or drugs that seein induce liver microsomal enzymes. The absorption of paracetamol may be accelerated by drugs such as metoclopramide. sane Seg cavicu Seo mata paeeuiee speee Steere SSeerErT: res Excretion” may “be affected” and “plasma “concentrations ‘aifered when given with probenicid. Colestyramine reduces” the absorption of paracetamol if given within 1 hour of paracetamol. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: Adults taking as little as 10 g to 15 g of paracetamol within 24 hours may develop severe liver damage and less often, renal tubular necrosis. Early signs of overdosage with paracetamol are nausea, vomiting and may also include lethargy and sweating usually settle within 24 hours. Abdominal pain may be the first indication of liver damage which is not usually apparent for 24 to 48 hours and sometime may be delayed for up to 4 to 6 days after ingestion. Activated charcoal may be used to reduce gastrointestinal absorption, if it can be given 1 hour of the overdose and if more than 150 mg/kg or 12 g of paracetamol has been ingested. There is little evidence that gastric lavage is of benefit in those who have overdosed solely in paracetamol. If there is any doubt about the timing or the need to treat, then a patient should be treated with an antidote of choice (Acetylcysteine). What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. iwi When should you consult your doctor? If symptoms persist and any undesirable effect occurs, consult your doctor. “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph”. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. DRP-7814 Date of Authorization: July 17, 2021 Patient Information Leaflet Date of Revision: May 30, 2023 Manufactured by the Marketing Authorization Holder: Distributed by:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T16:32:48.200775+00:00
