PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7925,Amoxicillin (As Trihydrate),Droxyl,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LeA8m0IFnrWho7Cs74aTa0OitqDeCKVM/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7925_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LeA8m0IFnrWho7Cs74aTa0OitqDeCKVM_view_usp_drivesdk_b572e22481.pdf,page_text/DRP-7925_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LeA8m0IFnrWho7Cs74aTa0OitqDeCKVM_view_usp_drivesdk_b572e22481.json,b2184addc8bce75a8789b719c3413f3ecdfa56da03aa307bfbb9286df1f9d79b,458895,1,digital_text,500 mg Capsule - Creamy to yellowish white powder in scarlet cap / white body EGC in size 0,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Indicated for the treatment of genitourinary, respiratory and gastrointestinal tract infections due to susceptible strains of Gram-negative bacteria including Salmonella typhosa and other Salmonella, E. coli, H. influenzae, N. gonorrhea, N. meningitis, Proteus mirabilis, Klebsiella (Aerobacter). Also indicated in infections due to susceptible Gram-positive bacteria such as Streptococcus and Diplococcus and the non-penicillinase producing Staphylococci. Reports of miscellaneous infections treated successfully have included bacterial endocarditis (due to Streptococcus viridans, S. fecales, H. influenzae or D. pneumoniae) and Gram-negative Septicemia (due to E. Coli, Proteus and Aerobacter). Since AMOXICILLIN is a bactericidal antibiotic with a wide spectrum of activity, it may be used as an empiric antimicrobial until the results of in-vitro sensitivity tests have been obtained.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:36:08.260810+00:00
