PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7980,Somatostatin (as acetate),Somaritin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HZxe9h9aCMS9vqugO2fBRsPKQr1yHZ86/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7980_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HZxe9h9aCMS9vqugO2fBRsPKQr1yHZ86_view_usp_drivesdk_e302681cfa.pdf,page_text/DRP-7980_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HZxe9h9aCMS9vqugO2fBRsPKQr1yHZ86_view_usp_drivesdk_e302681cfa.json,419026f348ee5d91b5d923a9ea598df17eba2479789589458938a7c0ef4a23d0,2993384,2,digital_text_and_ocr,White cake with cylinder shape,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"hemorrhage. Furthermore, Somatostatin is capable of reducing remarkably splanchnic blood flow without causing significant variations in the systemic arterial pressure, which proves to be valuable for the management of esophageal variceal hemorrhage. Somatostatin reduces both pancreatic endocrine and exocrine secretion, which makes it effective in the prophylaxis and treatment of postoperative complications of pancreatic surgery. The positive effect of Somatostatin in the management of diabetic ketoacidosis can be ascribed to its suppression activity of glucagon secretion. Pharmacokinetic properties In healthy persons, the plasma level of endogenous Somatostatin is low, generally well <175 ng/L Following IV administration, Somatostatin shows a very short plasma half-life (t7%2) which as measured by radioimmunoassay, lies between 1.1 and 3 min in normal subjects, between 1.2 and 4.8 min in subjects with liver disease, between 2.6 and 4.9 min in subjects with chronic renal failure. Following an IV infusion at a rate of 75 mcg/hr, the plateau level was obtained within 15 min and reached 1250 ng/L. The metabolic clearance rate was around 1 L/min and the t% around 2.7 min. After IV injection of 2 mcg of 125 L-thyrosine Somatostatin urinary excretion contained 0% of the radioactivity after 4 hrs and 70% after 24 hrs. Somatostatin is rapidly metabolized in the liver through the action of endopeptidases and aminopeptidases, resulting in cleavage between the N-terminus and the cyclized portion of the molecule. MECHANISM OF ACTION Somatostatin is a 14-amino acid oligopeptide which was originally isolated from the hypothalamus of animals and, later, found in both epithelial cells and nerve fibers throughout the whole of the digestive system. Somatostatin is thought to act mainly as a local transport substance, thus having a role in both the regulation of endocrine and exocrine secretions and of gastrointestinal motility. When administered at pharmacological doses, Somatostatin will inhibit gastrointestinal function and motility, as well as resorption within the digestive tract.",1,1,indication in the treatment of upper gastrointestinal,medium,needs_human_review,2026-07-01T16:37:03.780232+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-7980-01,Somatostatin (as acetate),Somaset,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zJzxs1opnNfW_Mbq1C_DNxrIA92fNWfm/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-7980-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zJzxs1opnNfW_Mbq1C_DNxrIA92fNWfm_view_usp_drivesdk_8f0a943236.pdf,page_text/DRP-7980-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zJzxs1opnNfW_Mbq1C_DNxrIA92fNWfm_view_usp_drivesdk_8f0a943236.json,0d6dce8f960d6b227f666817b9b2d498de0487f70be47c23000eef62543695d8,9173308,2,ocr,White cake with cylinder shape.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Treatment of acute gastrointestinal hemorrhage, resulting from gastric or duodenal ulcers, hemorrhagic gastritis, and bleeding esophageal varices, whether suspected solely on clinical grounds or proven by endoscopy. Treatment of intestinal and pancreatic fistulae. Symptomatic treatment of excessive secretion from endocrine tumors of the gastrointestinal tract. The prevention of complications after pancreatic surgery or endoscopic retrograde cholangiopancreatography (ERCP).",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-07-01T16:36:52.995425+00:00
