PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8022,Glycerin,Unbranded,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ab281WbNma4TOnTQ3E2kwiEP_lllM4FH/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8022_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ab281WbNma4TOnTQ3E2kwiEP_lllM4FH_view_usp_drivesdk_4e07dc5c3a.pdf,page_text/DRP-8022_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ab281WbNma4TOnTQ3E2kwiEP_lllM4FH_view_usp_drivesdk_4e07dc5c3a.json,fc61cdb0b5e99d9b2690b30478e4171cd6f6d5e62e7d569a716964f2361217be,175005,1,digital_text,"RiteMED ® Glycerin suppositories (1.955 g) for children are white, translucent, pencil-shaped dosage forms intended for rectal insertion. RiteMED® Glycerin suppositories (2.54 g) for adults are white, translucent, bullet-shaped dosage forms intended for rectal insertion. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This product contains a laxative called glycerol (also known as glycerin). Glycerol works by promoting fluid retention in the bowel to keep the stools moist and lubricates the passage of the stool for easy evacuation. Inserted rectally, glycerol suppositories can relieve constipation by producing a mild stimulatory effect on the bowel. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTIONS,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T16:41:19.508741+00:00
