PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8047,Cefalexin (as monohydrate),Fleridine,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1S1Eai1S_2ZUJt-Oj9V5R16JV44h8s_EL/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8047_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1S1Eai1S_2ZUJt-Oj9V5R16JV44h8s_EL_view_usp_drivesdk_206621ed53.pdf,page_text/DRP-8047_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1S1Eai1S_2ZUJt-Oj9V5R16JV44h8s_EL_view_usp_drivesdk_206621ed53.json,f4e9628edadf455203ea59a7b3b2bd5c8ea25ef173e07cb8c35ff8f8562fc8ea,427410,1,digital_text,Cefalexin (Fleridine) 500 mg Capsule is a creamy to light yellow powder in blue cap/ gray body EGC size 0,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Cefalexin is indicated in the treatment of the following infections caused by susceptible strains of the designated microorganisms. Respiratory tract infections caused by S. pneumoniae and group A beta- hemolytic streptococci (Penicillin is the usual drug of choice in the treatment and prevention of streptococcal infections, including the prophylaxis of rheumatic fever. Cefalexin is generally effective in the eradication of Streptococci from the nasopharynx; however, substantial data establishing the efficacy of Cefalexin in the subsequent prevention of rheumatic fever are not available at present.) Bacterial sinusitis caused by streptococci. S. pneumoniae, and S. aureus (methicillin - sensitive only). Otitis media due to S. pneumoniae, H. influenzae, staphylococci, streptococci and N. catarhalis. Skin and soft tissue infections caused by staphylococci, and / or streptococci. Bone and joints infections caused by Staphylococci and /or P. mirabilis. Genito urinary tract infections including acute prostitis, caused by Ecoli, P. mirabilis and klebsiella sp. Dental infection caused by staphylococci and / or streptococci. Note - Appropriate culture and susceptibility tests should be initiated prior to and during therapy. Renal function studies should be informed when indicated.",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:24:48.174467+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8051,Ascorbic Acid (as Sodium Ascorbate) + Zinc (as Zinc Sulfate Monohydrate),Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dE0idGsmzurH0xEuEa5gQlW7ldEXVKit/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8051_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dE0idGsmzurH0xEuEa5gQlW7ldEXVKit_view_usp_drivesdk_e9f3a652dc.pdf,page_text/DRP-8051_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dE0idGsmzurH0xEuEa5gQlW7ldEXVKit_view_usp_drivesdk_e9f3a652dc.json,6c9430fda198a96d3c2b30f33ef309b0588ef850d968163b96689eadf0895008,1386682,1,ocr,"The medicine is a clear yellow to yellow orange syrupy liquid with apple flavor and aroma contained in a 60 mL, 120 mL & 250 mL amber round bottle. What is in the medicine? This medicine contains a combination of Ascorbic Acid and Zinc Sulfate. Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C) is a water soluble vitamin which is essential for the synthesis of collagen and intercellular material. Zinc Sulfate helps regulate the activity of cells involved in immune function. Strength of the medicine: Each 5 milliliter (1 teaspoonful) contains 100 mg Ascorbic Acid (Equivalent to 112.48 mg Sodium Ascorbate) and 10 mg Elemental Zinc (Equivalent to 27.5 mg Zinc Sulfate Monohydrate). What is this medicine used for? It is used for the prevention and treatment of Vitamin C and Zinc deficiencies for normal development and maintenance of the immune system. How much and how often should you use this medicine? 1-3 years old 2.5 mL (1/2 teaspoon) 4-8 years old 5 mL (1 teaspoonful) 9-13 years old 5 to 10 mL (1-2 teaspoonfuls) Once daily or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? If you are allergic to any components of the medicine. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: It should be given care to patients with excessive calcium oxalate kidney stones (hyperoxaluria). Do not take more than the recommended dose. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Vitamin C is usually well tolerated, however when given in high doses greater than 1g or more daily, it causes diarrhea and gastrointestinal disturbances. Zinc may cause gastrointestinal disturbance that includes abdominal pain, dyspepsia, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, gastric irritation, and gastritis. This may be reduced by giving them meals before taking the medicine. What other medicine or food should be avoided? The amount of nutrients in the product is not expected to interact with food or medicine. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: Prolonged intake of Vitamin C greater than 2 g daily may lead to nausea, abdominal cramps, diarrhea and nose bleeding. Prolonged use of high zinc doses (4-8 grams elemental zinc) may cause nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, metallic taste, fever, and lethargy (sleepiness). What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? Treatment with Zinc overdosage includes of giving milk or alkali carbonates and activated charcoal. The use of emetics or gastric lavage should be avoided. Generally, if you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? OEEUF-GORS yt YOU doctor “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph.” Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration number: DRP-805 Date of Renewal Authorization: March 16, 2020 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: October 17, 2022 Manufactured by the: Distributed by: Marketing Authorization Holder:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T21:24:55.752162+00:00
