PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8117-01,Ascorbic Acid,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xaiBBZx_sM3FKgZ5oQMAcIsF8C_oQyAn/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8117-01_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xaiBBZx_sM3FKgZ5oQMAcIsF8C_oQyAn_view_usp_drivesdk_3e5c073855.pdf,page_text/DRP-8117-01_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xaiBBZx_sM3FKgZ5oQMAcIsF8C_oQyAn_view_usp_drivesdk_3e5c073855.json,c87ce114fa15595e9c9aa40048838d5281ece91a27f776f538712e3e378e9b30,46637,1,digital_text,"Rose Pharmacy Ascorbic Acid Chewable Tablet is an orange, round, flat-faced bisected tablet with beveled edge. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This medicine contains Ascorbic acid or Vitamin C. Vitamin C is a water-soluble vitamin that is necessary for normal growth and development. This vitamin is required for the growth and repair of tissues in all parts of the body. It is necessary to form collagen- an important protein used to make skin, scar tissue, tendons, ligaments, and blood vessels. Vitamin C is essential for wound healing and for the repair and maintenance of cartilages, bones and teeth. Vitamin C is also one of the many antioxidants- nutrients that block some of the damage caused by free radicals. Antioxidants also help reduce the damage to the body caused by toxic chemicals and pollutants such as cigarrete smoke, food preservatives, etc. Vitamin C is also a co-factor in many biological processes especially in iron metabolism, resistance to infection, and in cellular respiration. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Each tablet contains 500mg of Ascorbic acid or Vitamin C. WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? Ascorbic acid is used for the prevention and treatment of Vitamin C deficiency. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THE MEDICINE? You may take this medicine following the doses below: For regular Vitamin C supplementation: Take 1 tablet daily. For increased resistance against colds and flu: Take 2-3 tablets daily. Your physician may prescribe a different dose for you according to his assessment. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? You should not take this medicine if you are allergic to Ascorbic acid or to any of the product’s components. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE You should consult your doctor before taking this medicine if you have hyperoxaluria (an excessive excretion of oxalate in your urine) or a condition known as glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase (G6PD) deficiency. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Vitamin C toxicity is very rare, because the body cannot store the vitamin and immediately excretes it in urine. However, if you take amounts greater than 2,000mg/day you may experience stomach upset and diarrhea. The daily use of high doses may lead to the formation of oxalate stones in the kidneys. You may also experience disturbed water and electrolyte balance in your body, increased hemolysis (breaking-up of red blood cells), increased calcium in the kidneys and suppression of cobalamine (Vitamin B 12) activity. If you have a condition called glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase (G6PD) deficiency, taking too much Vitamin C can cause hemolysis which may cause you to feel tired, or dizzy, or even cause you to be anemic. In some rare cases, you may experience painful urination or pink/bloody urine. If any of these effects persist, tell your doctor immediately. For women who take high doses of Vitamin C during pregnancy, your babies may develop a condition known as ‘rebound scurvy’ in which upon delivery, your baby’s intake of Vitamin C drops leading to symptoms of scurvy and requiring immediate Vitamin C supplementation. Ascorbic acid is not compatible in solution with drugs like aminophylline, bleomycin, erythromycin, lactobionate, nafcillin, sodium nitrofurantoin, conjugated estrogens, sodium bicarbonate, sulfafurazole, diethanolamine, chloramphenicol sodium succinate, chlorothiazide sodium and hydrocortisone sodium succinate.Ascorbic acid has also been reported to interfere with blood thinning treatments. You should consult your doctor for advice before taking Ascorbic acid if you are taking any of the above-mentioned medications. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, you may take it as soon as you remember. However, if you remember it at a time that is already close to the next dose, just skip the missed dose and take the next dose as scheduled. Do not take two doses of the medicine at the same time. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE If you take too much Ascorbic acid, you may experience signs and symptoms of toxicity like nausea, vomiting, indigestion, diarrhea, flushing of the face, headache, fatigue and disturbed sleep. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have taken more than the recommended dose of this medicine and you are experiencing adverse symptoms, it would be best to seek medical attention immediately. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? You should keep this medicine at temperatures not exceeding 30°C and protect it from heat and direct sunlight. Keep it out of reach and sight of children. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT A DOCTOR? If your symptoms persist or worsen after a few days of taking this medicine, or if you believe you are experiencing an adverse reaction to this medicine, it would be best to consult your doctor as soon as possible. 12.5 x 17.5 cm 17.5cm 12.5 cm BACK 12.5 x 17.5 cm 17.5cm 12.5 cm FRONT VERSION1 - 6 - 2020 VERSION2 - 6 - 2020",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T21:29:13.018500+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8118-01,Omeprazole,Mepraz,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JLCFGCZZx5JJJ12ptWt6003ClLS72ep7/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8118-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1JLCFGCZZx5JJJ12ptWt6003ClLS72ep7_view_usp_drivesdk_d91e584f30.pdf,page_text/DRP-8118-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1JLCFGCZZx5JJJ12ptWt6003ClLS72ep7_view_usp_drivesdk_d91e584f30.json,10390cf11b2bdb32df0cda7b0c34964876ed02c6be1790656c5d71ed8974803a,3930167,1,ocr,"ADVERSE EFFECTS Omeprazole 20 mg Capsule is a white to off-white enteric coated pellets contained in an ivory body/ ivory cap#2EGC. Omeprazole is generally well tolerated. Adverse effects are generally mild. The most frequent adverse effects of omeprazole and other proton pump inhibitors are headache, diarrhea and skin rashes. Other Omeprazole 40 mg Capsule is a white to off-white enteric coated pellets contained in an ivory body/ adverse effects include pruritus, dizziness, fatigue, constipation, nausea and vomiting, flatulence, orange cap#0EGC. abdominal pain, arthralgia and myalgia, urticaria and dry mouth. Isolated cases of photosensitivity, bullous eruptions, erythema multiforme, angioedema, anaphylaxis, increased liver enzymes, hepatitis, PHARMACODYNAMICS jaundice and hepatic encephalopathy have been reported. Occasional insomnia, somnolence, vertigo, Omeprazole belongs under aclass of drugs called proton pump inhibitors. Omeprazole blocks or inhibits reversible confusional states, agitation, depression and hallucinations have occurred in severely ill gastric acid secretions. It reduces gastric acid secretion by inhibiting the enzyme system of hydrogen - patients. potassium adenosine triphosphate, which is regarded as the acid proton pump of the gastric parietal cells. Also called H+ /K + - Atpase, the enzyme is responsible for the exchange of hydrogen and OVERDOSEAND TREATMENT potassiumions during the formation of hydrochloric acid. Rare reports have been received of overdosage with omeprazole. In the literature doses of up to 560 mg have been described and occasional reports have been received when single oral doses have been PHARMACOKINETICS reached up to 2400 mg omeprazole (120 times the usual recommended clinical dose). Nausea, vomiting, Omeprazole is rapidly but variably absorbed following oral administration. Absorption is not affected by dizziness, abdominal pain, diarrhea and headache have been reported from overdose with omeprazole. food. Omeprazole is acid-labile. The absorption of omeprazole appears to be dose-dependent. Also apathy, depression and confusion have been describedin single cases. Increasing the dosage above 40 mg has been reported to increase the plasma concentrations in a non- linear fashion because of saturable first-pass hepatic metabolism. In addition, absorption is higher after long-term administration. Bioavailability of omeprazole may be increased in elderly patients. In some The symptoms described in connection to omeprazole overdosage have been transient, and no serious outcome due to omeprazole has been reported. The rate of elimination was unchanged (first order ethnic groups such as Chinese, and in patients with impaired hepatic function, but is not markedly kinetics) with increased doses and no specific treatment has been needed. affected in patients with renal impairment. Following absorption, omeprazole is almost completely metabolised in the liver, primarily by the cytochrome P450 isoenzyme CYP2C19 to form CAUTION hydroxyomeprazole, and to a small extent by CYP3A4 to form omeprazole sulfone. The metabolites are Foods, Drugs, Devices, and CosmeticsAct prohibits dispensing without prescription. inactive and are excreted mostly in the urine and to a lesser extent in the bile. The elimination half-life from plasma is reported to be about 0.5 to 3 hours. Omeprazole is highly bound (about 95%) to plasma For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. proteins. Patient should seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reactions",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,1,1,INDICATIONS,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T21:29:33.488703+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8120,"""Lamivudine + Zidovudine
(FOR DOH PROGRAM ONLY)""",None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NgeagFPC0oMPSH5VlRuZ9pJ5iwm5ATKt/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8120_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1NgeagFPC0oMPSH5VlRuZ9pJ5iwm5ATKt_view_usp_drivesdk_9417c4ef97.pdf,page_text/DRP-8120_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1NgeagFPC0oMPSH5VlRuZ9pJ5iwm5ATKt_view_usp_drivesdk_9417c4ef97.json,5c1e46c70524335fd047397c52847016c6819b157272c0bc7277972b52b6ec23,298197,2,digital_text,"Film-coated tablet White to off-white modified capsule shaped, biconvex, film-coated tablets with deep breakline in between ‘C’ and ‘60’ on one side and deep breakline on the other side. 4. Clinical particulars 4.1 Therapeutic indications The fixed combination of Lamivudine and Zidovudine is indicated in antiretroviral combination therapy for the treatment of Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) infection (see section 4.2). 4.2 Posology and method of administration Therapy should be initiated by a physician experienced in the management of HIV infection. Lamivudine and Zidovudine Tablets may be administered with or without food (1). To ensure administration of the entire dose, the tablet(s) should ideally be swallowed without crushing. For patients who are unable to swallow tablets, tablets may be crushed and added to a small amount of semi-solid food or liquid, all of which should be consumed immediately (see section 5.2). Adults and adolescents weighing at least 30 kg: the recommended dose of Lamivudine and Zidovudine is one tablet twice daily Children weighing between 21 kg and 30 kg: the recommended oral dose of Lamivudine and Zidovudine is one-half tablet t aken in the morning and one whole tablet taken in the evening. Children weighing from 14 kg to 21 kg: the recommended oral dose of Lamivudine and Zidovudine is one-half tablet taken twice daily. The dosing regimen for paediatric patients weighing 14-30 kg is based primarily on pharmacokinetic modelling and supported by data from clinical studies using the individual components lamivudine and zidovudine. A pharmacokinetic overexposure of zidovudine can occur, therefore close safety monitoring is warranted in these patients. If gastrointestinal intolerance occurs in patients weighing 21 -30 kg, an alternative dosing schedul e with one-half tablet taken thrice daily can be applied in attempt to improve tolerability. Lamivudine and zidovudine tablets should not be used for children weighing less than 14 kg, since doses cannot be appropriately adjusted for the weight of the child. In these pat ients, lamivudine and zidov udine should be taken as separate fo rmulations according to the p rescribed dosing recommendations for these products. For these patients and for patients, who are unable to swallow tablets, oral solutions of lamivudine and zidovudine are available. For situations where discontinuation of therapy with one of the active substances of Lamivudine and Zidovudine150/300 mg Tablets, or dose reduction is necessary, separate preparations of lamivudine and zidovudine are available in tablets/capsules and oral solution. Renal Impairment: Lamivudine and zidovudine concentrations are increased in patients with renal impairment due to decreased clearance. Therefore as dosage adjustment of these may be necessary it is recommended that separate preparations of lamivudine and zidovudine be administered to patients with reduced renal function (creatinine clearance ≤50 ml/min). Physicians should refer to the individual prescribing information for these medicinal products. Hepatic impairment: Limited data in patients with cirr hosis suggest that accumulation of zidovudine may occur in patients with hepatic impairment be cause of decreased glucuronidation. Data obtained in patients w ith moderate to severe hepatic impairment show that la mivudine pharmacokinetics are no t significantly affected by hepatic dysfunction. Howeve r, as dosage adjustments for zido vudine may be necessary, it is r ecommended that separate prepar ations of lamivudine and zidovudine be administered to patients w ith severe hepatic impairment. Physicians should refer to the individual prescri bing information for these med icinal products Dosage adjustments in patients with haematological adverse reactions: Dosage adjustment of zidovudine may be necessary if the haemoglobin level falls below 9 g/dl or 5.59 mmol/l or the neutroph il count falls below 1.0 x 109 /l (see sections 4.3 and 4.4). As dosa ge adjustment of amivudine and zidovudine is not possible, separate preparations of zidovudine and lamivudine should be used. Physicians should refer to the individual prescribing information for these medicinal products. Dosage in the elderly: No specific data are availab le, however special care is advised in this age group due t o age associated changes such as t he decrease in renal function and alteration of haematological parameters.",1,1,3. Pharmaceutical form,The fixed combination of Lamivudine and Zidovudine is indicated in antiretroviral combination therapy for the treatment of Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) infection (see section 4.2).,1,1,4.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:29:36.881957+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8123,Clindamycin (as phosphate),Blinda,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1r2relKghf-T9ihylnv_ZFiC9aZ4axMYu/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8123_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1r2relKghf-T9ihylnv_ZFiC9aZ4axMYu_view_usp_drivesdk_0fbf65159a.pdf,page_text/DRP-8123_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1r2relKghf-T9ihylnv_ZFiC9aZ4axMYu_view_usp_drivesdk_0fbf65159a.json,83834e9411018f1e532c6765e01bd3700f749470964cf4f7f3c6f579b95b7e16,288270,6,digital_text,,,,,"Clindamycin is antibacterial indicated for the treatment of severe infections caused by susceptible Gram- positive organisms, staphylococci (both penicillinase- and non-penicillinase-producing), streptococci (except Streptococcus faecalis) and pneumococci. It is also indicated in serious infections caused by susceptible anaerobic pathogens such as Bacteroides spp, Fusobacterium spp, Propionibacterium spp, Peptostreptococcus spp. and microaerophilic streptococci. Clindamycin does not penetrate the blood/brain barrier in therapeutically effective quantities.",1,1,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T21:29:40.430675+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8126,dl-Alpha Tocopheryl Acetate,E-Nova,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Ox6yKaoKi_b-7CmUq3TDqFCG36E2gENp/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8126_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Ox6yKaoKi_b-7CmUq3TDqFCG36E2gENp_view_usp_drivesdk_70554970a4.pdf,page_text/DRP-8126_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Ox6yKaoKi_b-7CmUq3TDqFCG36E2gENp_view_usp_drivesdk_70554970a4.json,d8672ece802ff4cd23364c769d5361dfd22125dcdbe6266a707ffadb6ea2abfb,837461,1,digital_text,"Light orange transparent, oblong shaped soft gelatin capsules containing clear oily liquid. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Used in premature infants exposed to high concentration of oxygen, correction of established vitamin E deficiency, in patients at risk of developing vitamin E deficiency, nocturnal muscle cramps, intermittent claudication, fibrocystic breast disease and coronary artery disease. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Take one capsule twice daily with or without food or as directed by the physician.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T21:29:44.249869+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8139,Trimetazidine,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ImYSNk0KtVVkosH1Dckct8mu7m0EpZFT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8139_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ImYSNk0KtVVkosH1Dckct8mu7m0EpZFT_view_usp_drivesdk_a1c5e596ba.pdf,page_text/DRP-8139_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ImYSNk0KtVVkosH1Dckct8mu7m0EpZFT_view_usp_drivesdk_a1c5e596ba.json,9423991eb90e189a01702974dfd37132f8d2e47dd0021766ee5c7023314654aa,953374,1,digital_text,"RiteMED® Pink, round, biconvex, CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY PHARMACODYNAMICS Findings from in vitro and ex vivo of ATP production to glucose oxidation which decreases the consequences of recurrent ischemia and enhances left ventricular performance, (2) protecting endothelial function by increasing endothelial nitric synthase activity and nitric oxide availability, (3) preserving mi- tochondrial function and energy metabolism thus reducing ischemic left ventricular dysfunc- tion, (4) limiting intracellular acidosis, (5) limiting sodium and calcium accumulation, and (6) PHARMACOKINETICS Trimetazidine is rapidly absorbed from the intestinal mucosa after oral administration. In 13 healthy volunteers, the mean peak plasma trimetazidine concentration (Cmax; 53.6 mcg/L) was reached 1.8 hours after a single 20 mg (immediate release) oral dose. After twice daily administration of trimetazidine 20 mg for 15 days, Cmax (84.8 mcg/L) was reached in 1.7 hours. The area under the plasma trimetazidine concentration-time curve (AUC0-∞) was 508.9 mcg·h/L after a single 20 mg dose and 831.4 mcg·h/L after repeated administration. Steady state levels were reached within 24 hours and remained stable for the study duration. Trimetazidine is only weakly protein bound in plasma (~16%) and therefore is widely dis- tributed throughout the body. In 11 healthy volunteers, the volume of distribution (Vd) of trimetazidine was 318.6 L after a 40 mg intravenous dose. The elimination half-life of trimetazidine 20 mg is about 6 hours after single or repeated oral administration. More than 80% of an administered dose of trimetazidine is excreted in urine within 48 hours, with 62% of the drug eliminated unchanged. Eight metabolites have been detected in urine, however, little is known of their properties.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION, Adjunct tr eatment of stable angina pector is inadequately contr olled by or intolerant to  Adjunct treatment of congestive heart failure,1,1,INDICATION,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:29:48.286888+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8146,Warfarin Sodium,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Jpb9nQfaH7IpHkiOu7ewiH6hoWsY8D1H/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8146_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Jpb9nQfaH7IpHkiOu7ewiH6hoWsY8D1H_view_usp_drivesdk_0463cd059a.pdf,page_text/DRP-8146_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Jpb9nQfaH7IpHkiOu7ewiH6hoWsY8D1H_view_usp_drivesdk_0463cd059a.json,804b761d57d45409efb3d241061c704a17b334a0f165419eb462b0d459234279,1626941,1,ocr,"Warfarin sodium 5 mg tablet is a white to off-white, oblong shaped, biconvex, uncoated tablet, bisected on one side and plain on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTIONS:,"Warfarin is a coumarin anticoagulation used for the treatment and prophylaxis of thromboembolic disorders; for the prevention and treatment of venous thromboembolism (deep-vein thrombosis and pulmonary embolism); and for the prevention of systemic thromboembolism and ischemic stroke in some patients with atrial fibrillation, prosthetic heart valves or who have suffered a myocardial infarction.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T21:29:56.885927+00:00
