PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8225,Dextromethorphan Hydrobromide + Guiafenesin,Mucotuss,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1OlIB9RKYnwSe4QJkcHGy8Deyi0KG4PCj/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8225_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OlIB9RKYnwSe4QJkcHGy8Deyi0KG4PCj_view_usp_drivesdk_0db0598a61.pdf,page_text/DRP-8225_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OlIB9RKYnwSe4QJkcHGy8Deyi0KG4PCj_view_usp_drivesdk_0db0598a61.json,c40a8071fd1a29e6bc16d2fc5dc717ee58d616ceaf2bc6a7ce72e5d5de521e60,515492,1,digital_text,"Clear, red liquid w/ cherry flavor. What is in the Medicine? Dextromethorphan Hydrobromide is a cough suppressant. Depresses cough reflex through direct effect on cough center in medulla. Guaifenesin is an expectorant. Exerts vasoconstrictive action that leads to decreased edema congestion. Also increases respiratory secretions and reduces mucus viscosity. Strength of the Medicine",1,1,Product Description:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T21:31:45.369561+00:00
