PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8234,Ascorbic Acid (As Sodium Ascorbate) + Zinc (As Sulfate Monohydrate),C-4 Kids Plus,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1tOvkigaBJkNAbrSXNVjF-TmpjG_0xkHC/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8234_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1tOvkigaBJkNAbrSXNVjF-TmpjG_0xkHC_view_usp_drivesdk_7ca94ab105.pdf,page_text/DRP-8234_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1tOvkigaBJkNAbrSXNVjF-TmpjG_0xkHC_view_usp_drivesdk_7ca94ab105.json,57c8574189c049a5a6a7e3769cfe757a90bc6c1715f90cc0ca444c9ae29d91fc,475752,1,digital_text,"Clear, orange syrup with orange flavor WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Vitamin C, a water-soluble vitamin, is essential for the synthesis of collagen and intercellular material. Zinc is needed for the proper growth and maintenance of the human body. It is needed for the immune function, wound healing, blood clotting, thyroid function, and much more. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Please see formulation WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Sodium ascorbate used to increase body resistance against stress, colds and other infections. Also for the prevention and treatment of scurvy. Zinc is for boosting the immune system, treating the common cold and preventing lower respiratory infections. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Children 9-13 yrs. old: 5-10 mL (1-2 teaspoonful) 4-8 years old: 5 mL (1 teaspoonful) 1-3 years old: 2.5 mL (½ teaspoonful) To be taken once daily for supplementation. Twice or thrice a daily for therapeutic use. Or as prescribed by the physician. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you are allergic to any ingredients. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Large doses may result in hyperoxaluria and the formation of renal calcium oxalate calculi and sodium ascorbate should therefore be given with care to patients with hyperoxaluria. Infants and children: Zinc is possibly unsafe when used in high doses. This product contains FD & C #5 (Tartrazine) which may cause allergic reactions including bronchial asthma in certain susceptible persons. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE? Large doses of sodium ascorbate have resulted in haemolysis in patients with G6PD deficiency. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Sodium Ascorbate may increase the absorption of iron in iron-deficiency states. Taking zinc along with some antibiotics (Quinolones) might decrease the effectiveness of some antibiotics. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, take it as soon as you remember. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T21:31:52.021318+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8237-01,Tamsulosin Hydrochloride,Tamsycare,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gXYNUcSibRcZlarWDXdzCdejd7ghIDsm/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8237-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gXYNUcSibRcZlarWDXdzCdejd7ghIDsm_view_usp_drivesdk_5d0a8664f7.pdf,page_text/DRP-8237-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gXYNUcSibRcZlarWDXdzCdejd7ghIDsm_view_usp_drivesdk_5d0a8664f7.json,62e28a2f166e51b66e6e036cb86a172448bc9e477fd97d51346b1ae15a488c62,466001,1,digital_text,"A purple/purple coloured hard gelatin capsule size “2” containing white to off white spherical pellets. Tamsulosin hydrochloride is an antagonist of alpha adrenoceptors in the prostate. 1A Its structural formula is: Each Tamsulosin Hydrochloride sustained release capsule for oral administration contains Tamsulosin HCl 400 mcg CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY Tamsulosin, an alpha adrenoceptor blocking agent, exhibits selectivity for alpha receptors in the human prostate. At least three 1 1 discrete alpha -adrenoceptor subtypes have been identified: alpha , alpha and alpha ; their distribution differs between human 1 1A 1B 1D organs and tissue. Approximately 70% of the alpha -receptors in human prostate are of the alpha subtype. 1 1A",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Tamsulosin Hydrochloride capsules are indicated for the treatment of the signs and symptoms of benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH). Tamsulosin Hydrochloride capsules are not indicated for the treatment of hypertension.,1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:31:55.225415+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8237-02,Tamsulosin Hydrochloride,Tamzor,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-v8KxGZpGLtIlhew0nLUfqy24gEFCmuZ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8237-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-v8KxGZpGLtIlhew0nLUfqy24gEFCmuZ_view_usp_drivesdk_3e3622456d.pdf,page_text/DRP-8237-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-v8KxGZpGLtIlhew0nLUfqy24gEFCmuZ_view_usp_drivesdk_3e3622456d.json,82b43090531d6b4ae48324c338dd026f15efe7ea90bd6b33319551e0b12e91e9,853335,1,digital_text,"Each Tamsulosin Hydrochloride (Tamzor) sustained release capsule for oral administration contains Tamsulosin HCl 400 mcg. CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY Its structural formula is: Tamsulosin, an alpha adrenoceptor blocking agent, exhibits selectivity for alpha receptors in the human prostate. At least three 1 1 discrete alpha -adrenoceptor subtypes have been identified: alpha , alpha and alpha ; their distribution differs between human 1 1A 1B 1D organs and tissue. Approximately 70% of the alpha -receptors in human prostate are of the alpha subtype. 1 1A",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"The signs and symptoms of orthostasis (postural hypotension, dizziness and vertigo) were detected more frequently in Tamsulosin Hydrochloride (Tamzor) capsule treated patients than in placebo recipients. As with other alpha-adrenergic blocking agents there is a potential risk of syncope. Tamsulosin Hydrochloride (Tamzor) capsules are indicated for the treatment of the signs and symptoms of benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH). Tamsulosin Hydrochloride (Tamzor) capsules are not indicated for the treatment of hypertension. Before therapy with Tamsulosin hydrochloride is initiated, the patient should be examined in order to exclude the presence of other conditions which can cause the same symptoms as benign prostatic hyperplasia. Digital rectal examination and when necessary,",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:31:58.583447+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8248-01,Citicoline (as sodium),Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/11HTpbtYnq-ZG6m7ug6fVE5cIi6-yRmSF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8248-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11HTpbtYnq-ZG6m7ug6fVE5cIi6-yRmSF_view_usp_drivesdk_c1e3537dfd.pdf,page_text/DRP-8248-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11HTpbtYnq-ZG6m7ug6fVE5cIi6-yRmSF_view_usp_drivesdk_c1e3537dfd.json,93a92dc903773b5c211b355d010ac0ebcd4ff340fdb41d7c90b2e3e0d5b5be5f,361088,1,digital_text,"Citicoline is a light purple to purple ﬁlm coated tablet, oval shaped, plain on both sides. Citicoline is a derivative of choline and cytidine that is involved in the biosynthesis of lecithin. It is claimed to increase blood ﬂow and oxygen consumption in the brain and has been given in the treatment of cerebrovascular disorders, Parkinsonism, and head injury. Citicoline is an interneuronal communication enhancer. It increases the neurotransmission levels because it favors the synthesis and production speed of dopamine in the striatum, acting then as a dopaminergic agonist thru the inhibition of tyrosine-hydroxylase. Citicoline acts as a presynaptic cholinergic agent which favors the synthesis of ac etylcholine. It also decreases the release of serotonin. Citicoline makes the neurons more active, causing the astrocytes to loosen their grip on the capillaries, thus improving microcirculation. By virtue of this action, Citicoline has an indirect eﬀect on microcirculation. It has the ability to slightly increase cerebral blood ﬂow and exerts an anti-aggregation eﬀect on platelets.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Used in the treatment of cerebrovascular disorders (including ischaemic stroke), Parkinsonism and head injury.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:32:01.951346+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8252,Paracetamol,Thermodol IV,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1n-IxLgFGxvLnqnMot64e1S4hReuSkVTY/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8252_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1n-IxLgFGxvLnqnMot64e1S4hReuSkVTY_view_usp_drivesdk_b99ba63682.pdf,page_text/DRP-8252_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1n-IxLgFGxvLnqnMot64e1S4hReuSkVTY_view_usp_drivesdk_b99ba63682.json,127992dfed7d70ab6014fe4e8fedec3d9b2ecc58d2216c904f5910faf4bef8d7,1553936,1,digital_text,"Infusion THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS Indicated for the short-term treatment of moderate pain, especially following surgery, and for the short-term treatment of fever, when administration by intravenous route is clinically justified by an urgent need to treat pain or hyperthermia and/or when other routes of administration are not possible. DOSAGE AND ADMINISTRATION Intravenous use. The 100 mL bottle is restricted to adults, adolescents, and children weighing more than 33 kg. Posology: Dosing based on patient weight (please see the dosing table here below. Method of administration The paracetamol solution is administered as a 15-minute intravenous infusion. Patients weighing ≤ 10 kg: l The glass bottle/bag of paracetamol, solution for infusion, should not be hung as an infusion due to the small volume of the medicinal product to be administered in this population l The volume to be administered should be withdrawn from the bottle/bag and diluted in a 0.9% sodium chloride solution or 5% glucose solution up to one tenth (one volume paracetamol, solution for infusion, into nine volumes diluent) and administered over 15 minute l A 5 or 10 ml syringe should be used to measure the dose as appropriate for the weight of the child and the desired volume. However, this should never exceed 7.5ml per dose l The user should be referred to the product information for dosing guidelines. To remove solution, use a 0.8 mm needle (21 gauge needle) and vertically perforate the stopper at the spot specifically indicated. As for all solutions for infusion presented in bottle, it should be remembered that close monitoring is needed notably at the end of the infusion, regardless of administration route. This monitoring at the end of the infusion applies particularly for central route infusions, in order to avoid air embolism",1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,"Indicated for the short-term treatment of moderate pain, especially following surgery, and for the short-term treatment of fever, when administration by intravenous route is clinically justified by an urgent need to treat pain or hyperthermia and/or when other routes of administration are not possible.",1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:32:05.812456+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8266,Vitamin B1 + B6 + B12,Unbranded,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-fEdwdl0Y6VLpOUlYc5ZBfHIJKjmUyLE/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8266_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-fEdwdl0Y6VLpOUlYc5ZBfHIJKjmUyLE_view_usp_drivesdk_9be6f68c03.pdf,page_text/DRP-8266_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-fEdwdl0Y6VLpOUlYc5ZBfHIJKjmUyLE_view_usp_drivesdk_9be6f68c03.json,a6c0987df2720631c25c90c20a7e2e130a94454f9cfb850ba0c21fd945f40acc,2894867,2,digital_text_and_ocr,"Pharex® B-Complex is a pink, round, flat beveled edge tablet, scored on one side and plain on the other side. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This product contains B-complex vitamins (Vitamins B1, B6 and B12). These nutrients are required for the normal function of the nervous system and are used as adjunct in the management of neuromuscular pain. B-complex vitamins also help in the conversion of food to energy to support numerous normal body processes. B-complex vitamins have the following functions/effects: NUTRIENTS NEUROMUSCULAR AND OTHER FUNCTIONS e Involved in the production of acetylcholine, a neurotransmitter required in conveying signals between nerve cells e Assists in the conversion of carbohydrate to Thiamine (B:) ener © Deficiency of Vitamin B1 results in beri-beri manifested as muscle weakness, loss of appetite and nerve degeneration (inability of nerves to function properly) © Required in the formation of neurotransmitters such as serotonin, gamma amino butyric acid (GABA), dopamine, and epinephrine to facilitate normal nervous system function e Assists in the breakdown and utilization of energy from amino acids and protein Pyridoxine (Bs) * Deficiency of Vitamin B6 is manifested as nausea, impaired immune function, skin disorders, mouth sores, weakness, mental depression, and anemia ¢ Required for the synthesis of myelin, the white sheath that surrounds nerve fibers ¢ Essential in the breakdown and utilization of Cyanocobalamin energy from fatty acids (Biz) ° Deficiency of Vitamin B12 is manifested as neuromuscular symptoms such as unsteadiness of the feet, poor muscle coordination and agitation STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Please see formulation WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? eTo prevent and treat deficiencies of Vitamin B1, B6 and B12 eAs an adjunct in the management of neuromuscular pain responsive to Vitamins B1, B6 and B12 which may include neuralgia (nerve pain), neuritis (inflammation of the nerves), and neuropathies (disturbance in the function of the brain and spinal cord that may affect the nerves and muscles of the body). HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THE MEDICINE? Orally, 1 - 2 tablets daily. Or, as prescribed by a doctor. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you are allergic to any component of the product. 93 mm [Page 2] PHX600370IN01 PM00000747 DATE OF REVISION OF PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET April 2023 productsafetyph@pharexhealth.com. ( City [Page 3]",1,2,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T21:32:13.899282+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8269,Meclizine Hydrochloride,none,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZjamapPwd2WSIYwm8E9gYChdY4DUeubC/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8269_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZjamapPwd2WSIYwm8E9gYChdY4DUeubC_view_usp_drivesdk_e851408a93.pdf,page_text/DRP-8269_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZjamapPwd2WSIYwm8E9gYChdY4DUeubC_view_usp_drivesdk_e851408a93.json,b7c02711caadfb92a37cbbe8507ad09387241b70803c7d05f2fd8d4bf4d402f8,604838,1,digital_text,"RiteMED® bisected on one side and plain on the other WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This product contains Meclizine, an antihistamine used as an antiemetic (drug used to stop vomiting). Meclizine works by slowing down the action of the nervous system by blocking the receptors of the brain associated with vomiting. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Please see formulation WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? This medicine is used to prevent or treat the symptoms of nausea, vomiting, or vertigo (dizziness) due to motion sickness. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? This medicine should be taken orally (by mouth), once a day, one hour before travel starts. Dose may be repeated every 24 hours if necessary. Tablets may be chewed then swallowed without water or swallowed whole with water. Age Group Recommended Dose: to be given once a day, one hour before travel Adults and children: 12 years and older 1 to 2 tablets 6 to12 years ½ tablet Or, as prescribed by a doctor. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? • If you are allergic to Meclizine or any ingredient in this product • If you need to perform activities requiring mental alertness of physical coordination (e.g. operating a machine or driving a motor vehicle) since drowsiness may occur with use of Meclizine • If you are pregnant or breastfeeding UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS Drowsiness, fatigue, dry mouth, constipation, headache, stomach upset, and rarely, blurred vision have been reported with the use of Meclizine. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Medicines that depress the nervous system, barbiturates (e.g. Phenobarbital), tranquilizers (e.g., Diazepam), and alcohol should not be taken together with Meclizine because of the potential for increased toxicity. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, just take the next dose as scheduled (i.e., once a day) if still needed to prevent or treat motion sickness. Do not double the dose. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Keep the product out of sight and reach of children. Store at temperatures not exceeding 30 o",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T21:32:17.166069+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8276,Metformin Hydrochloride,Glucosil,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1OweZAxSCadjla9hl2bNQ76gxvlvNuqrZ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8276_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OweZAxSCadjla9hl2bNQ76gxvlvNuqrZ_view_usp_drivesdk_64c894e58b.pdf,page_text/DRP-8276_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OweZAxSCadjla9hl2bNQ76gxvlvNuqrZ_view_usp_drivesdk_64c894e58b.json,0307d15cc650be2c69085aa11c7bff136a8a704c16631f8965cd07796fbb0555,421875,1,digital_text,"Metformin HCl 850 mg Tablet is a creamy white, oval long film coated tablet.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Metformin Hydrochloride is a biguanide derivative which is given by mouth in the treatment of non-insulin dependent diabetes mellitus. The precise mode of action is not clear. Metformin is used only in the treatment of maturity-onset diabetes not responsive to diet plus treatment with a sulphonylurea. It may be used alone or in conjunction with another oral hypoglycemic agent such as sulphonylurea.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:32:20.103370+00:00
