PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8290,Ascorbic acid (as Sodium Ascorbate),Aiyu-Cee,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xvThu4zdm2bJ6cslCbJMHtsD1T63-j0s/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8290_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xvThu4zdm2bJ6cslCbJMHtsD1T63-j0s_view_usp_drivesdk_50de35ddc9.pdf,page_text/DRP-8290_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1xvThu4zdm2bJ6cslCbJMHtsD1T63-j0s_view_usp_drivesdk_50de35ddc9.json,fc2d46d19c26e280aa681808eba1f2f98908091508105fdc3bfc44072989850f,576180,1,digital_text,,,,,"For the prevendon snd featnent ofMtamin C deftdensy. HasEns wound heling and increase body resistane fuom inEclious diseases. For heanhy gums, t€eth, bone$ end other connedive tissue6.",1,1,INDICATION:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T21:32:35.372698+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8297-01,Doxycycline (As Hyclate),Doxed,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J626hvnfnq2FRvepnkYsny-HDg26b1Zw/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8297-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1J626hvnfnq2FRvepnkYsny-HDg26b1Zw_view_usp_drivesdk_c5157e178d.pdf,page_text/DRP-8297-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1J626hvnfnq2FRvepnkYsny-HDg26b1Zw_view_usp_drivesdk_c5157e178d.json,0f4c032415711efe48a32f0539f313339f90a03f58ca7e2070a1ec0f7d4a5e01,297774,6,digital_text,White to almost white crystalline powder filled in size #1 hard gelatin capsule with green cap and white color body.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Indicated in the treatment of infections caused by susceptible strains of the following microorganisms in the condition listed below: • Sexually transmitted disease due to Chlamydia trachomatis, Ureaplasma urealyticum, Hemophilus ducreyi, and Calymmatobacterium granulomatis. • Urinary tract infections due to Enterobacter aerogenes, Klebsiella spp. and Acinetobacter spp. • Respiratory tract infections caused by Microplasma pneumonia, Hemophilus influenza, Streptococcus pneumonia, and Klebsiella spp. • Gastrointestinal infections due to Vibrio cholerae, and Shigella spp. • Systemic infections caused by Rickettsia, Borrelia reccurentis, Yersinia pestis, Francisella tularensis, Bartonella bacilliformis, and Brucella spp. • Infections caused by Escherichia coli, Enterobacter aerogenes, Shigella spp. and Acinetobacter spp. When penicillin is contraindicated, Doxycycline is an alternative drug in the treatment of the following infections: • Uncomplicated gonorrhea caused by Neisseria gonorrhea • Syphilis caused by Treponema pallidum • Yaws caused by Treponema pertenue • Listeriosis due to Listeria monocytogenes • Anthrax due to Bacillus anthracis • Vincent’s infection caused by Fusobacterium fusiforme [Page 2] • Actinomycosis caused by Actinomyces israelii • Infections caused by Clostridium spp. • In acute intestinal amebiasis, Doxycycline may be useful adjunct to amebicides • In severe acne, Doxycycline may be useful adjunctive therapy • In refractory periodontitis and periodontal abscess, Doxycycline may be useful adjunctive therapy. Prophylaxis Doxycycline indicated for the prophylaxis of malaria due to Plasmodium Falciparum in short-term travelers (<4 moths) to areas with Chloroquine and/or pyrimethamine- sulfadoxine resistant strains.",1,2,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:32:38.695303+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8300,Rosuvastatin (as calcium),Roselion-20,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IMjR75PeRBo_D-w6IK53cSavFiqbkXQ4/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8300_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IMjR75PeRBo_D-w6IK53cSavFiqbkXQ4_view_usp_drivesdk_d83d18497d.pdf,page_text/DRP-8300_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IMjR75PeRBo_D-w6IK53cSavFiqbkXQ4_view_usp_drivesdk_d83d18497d.json,b735678931e9b2bd29a0bcb66419a9218c3a7a460c4653b4c8609906c22d45f3,1592366,1,digital_text,,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Rosuvastatin is approximately 90% bound to plasma proteins, mostly albumin. The parent compound, accounts for greater than 90% of the circulating active HMG CoA reductase inhibitor activity. Rosuvastatin undergoes limited metabolism (approximately 10%), mainly to the N-desmethyl form, and 90% is eliminated as unchanged drug in the feces with the remainder being excreted in the urine. Special Populations: Age and sex: There was no clinically relevant effect of age or sex on the pharmacokinetics of Rosuvastatin in adults. The exposure in children and adolescents with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolemia appears to be similar to or lower than that in adult patients with dyslipidemia. Race: Pharmacokinetic studies show an approximate 2-fold elevation in median AUC in Asian subjects compared with Caucasians. A population pharmacokinetic analysis revealed no clinically relevant differences in pharmacokinetics among Caucasian, Hispanic and Black or Afro-Caribbean groups. Renal insufficiency: In a study in subjects with varying degrees of renal impairment, mild to moderate renal disease had little influence on plasma concentrations of Rosuvastatin. However, subjects with severe impairment (CrCl <30 mL/min) had a 3-fold increase in plasma concentration compared to healthy volunteers. Rosuvastatin should be used as an adjunct to diet when the response to diet and exercise is inadequate.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T21:33:00.462884+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8300-01,Rosuvastatin (as Calcium),Gostatin 20,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rKDidmrEF3Y0IMVmmMlsUUjH5t2P9twP/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8300-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rKDidmrEF3Y0IMVmmMlsUUjH5t2P9twP_view_usp_drivesdk_f676cdf693.pdf,page_text/DRP-8300-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rKDidmrEF3Y0IMVmmMlsUUjH5t2P9twP_view_usp_drivesdk_f676cdf693.json,1ab491b70ea74379f2cc6175a2b89d54dc6099a92f2ffd9cc6c343c6703bf090,507058,1,digital_text,"Yellowish coloured, round shaped, biconvex, both side plain film-coated tablet",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Rosuvastatin should be used as an adjunct to diet when the response to diet and exercise is inadequate. Prevention of Cardiovascular Events: In adult patients with an increased risk of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease based on the presence of cardiovascular disease risk markers such as an elevated hsCRP level, age, hypertension, low HDL-C, smoking or a family history of premature coronary heart disease, Rosuvastatin is indicated to reduce total mortality and the risk of major cardiovascular events (cardiovascular death, stroke, MI, unstable angina, or arterial revascularization). In adult patients with hypercholesterolaemia: Rosuvastatin is indicated to: reduce elevated LDL-C, Total Cholesterol, triglycerides and to increase HDL- cholesterol in patients with primary hypercholesterolemia (heterozygous familial and non familial) and mixed dyslipidemia (Fredrickson Types IIa and IIb). Rosuvastatin also lowers ApoB, nonHDL-C, VLDL-C, VLDL-TG, the LDL-C/HDL-C, total C/HDL-C, nonHDL-C/HDL-C, ApoB/ApoA-I ratios and increases ApoA-I in these populations; treat patients with primary dysbetalipoproteinemia (Fredrickson Type III hyper lipoproteinemia); treat isolated hypertriglyceridemia (Fredrickson Type IV hyperlipidemia); reduce Total Cholesterol and LDL-C in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, as an adjunct to diet and other lipid lowering treatments (e.g. LDL apheresis) or alone if such treatments are unavailable; slow or delay the progression of atherosclerosis. Children and adolescents 6 to 17 years of age: Rosuvastatin is indicated to reduce the Total Cholesterol, LDL-C and Apo B in patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia (HeFH).",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:32:42.194779+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8300-02,Rosuvastatin (as calcium),Controld 20,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cllHddVhIoPIonevFFLa0fMRIcaCgfbs/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8300-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cllHddVhIoPIonevFFLa0fMRIcaCgfbs_view_usp_drivesdk_ab8b484052.pdf,page_text/DRP-8300-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cllHddVhIoPIonevFFLa0fMRIcaCgfbs_view_usp_drivesdk_ab8b484052.json,c7e8b0991ec6320e42655bb68e5e397a7e78f4804c3b536bc30ce0c191639aca,504221,1,digital_text,"Yellowish coloured, round shaped, biconvex, both side plain film-coated tablet",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Rosuvastatin should be used as an adjunct to diet when the response to diet and exercise is inadequate. Prevention of Cardiovascular Events: In adult patients with an increased risk of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease based on the presence of cardiovascular disease risk markers such as an elevated hsCRP level, age, hypertension, low HDL-C, smoking or a family history of premature coronary heart disease, Rosuvastatin is indicated to reduce total mortality and the risk of major cardiovascular events (cardiovascular death, stroke, MI, unstable angina, or arterial revascularization). In adult patients with hypercholesterolaemia: Rosuvastatin is indicated to: reduce elevated LDL-C, Total Cholesterol, triglycerides and to increase HDL- cholesterol in patients with primary hypercholesterolemia (heterozygous familial and non familial) and mixed dyslipidemia (Fredrickson Types IIa and IIb). Rosuvastatin also lowers ApoB, nonHDL-C, VLDL-C, VLDL-TG, the LDL-C/HDL-C, total C/HDL-C, nonHDL-C/HDL-C, ApoB/ApoA-I ratios and increases ApoA-I in these populations; treat patients with primary dysbetalipoproteinemia (Fredrickson Type III hyper lipoproteinemia); treat isolated hypertriglyceridemia (Fredrickson Type IV hyperlipidemia); reduce Total Cholesterol and LDL-C in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, as an adjunct to diet and other lipid lowering treatments (e.g. LDL apheresis) or alone if such treatments are unavailable; slow or delay the progression of atherosclerosis. Children and adolescents 6 to 17 years of age: Rosuvastatin is indicated to reduce the Total Cholesterol, LDL-C and Apo B in patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia (HeFH).",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:32:45.354426+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8300-04,Rosuvastatin (as calcium),Rostar,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1AiurtMIB-k52-IqFjinPfhPyfwSMuT1y/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8300-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1AiurtMIB-k52-IqFjinPfhPyfwSMuT1y_view_usp_drivesdk_c569de1d86.pdf,page_text/DRP-8300-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1AiurtMIB-k52-IqFjinPfhPyfwSMuT1y_view_usp_drivesdk_c569de1d86.json,866c3f5752e729dc997678bbd7ebda25238046dff9c647b5bf6ca1f02bc15f0b,1546638,1,digital_text,"Yellowish coloured, round shaped, biconvex, both side plain film-coated tablet. Rosuvastatin produces its lipid-modifying effects in two ways; it increases the number of hepatic LDL receptors on the cell-surface, enhancing uptake and catabolism of LDL and it inhibits the hepatic synthesis of VLDL, thereby reducing the total number of VLDL and LDL particles. Each film-coated tablet contains: Mechanism of action",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Race: Pharmacokinetic studies show an approximate 2-fold elevation in median AUC in Asian subjects compared with Caucasians. A population pharmacokinetic analysis revealed no clinically relevant differences in pharmacokinetics among Caucasian, Hispanic and Black or Afro-Caribbean groups. Toxicology: Preclinical safety data: Preclinical data reveal no special hazards for humans based on conventional studies of safety pharmacology, repeat-dose toxicity, genotoxicity, carcinogenic potential, and reproductive toxicity. In adult patients with an increased risk of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease based on the presence of cardiovascular disease risk markers such as an elevated hsCRP level, age, hypertension, low HDL-C, smoking or a family history of premature coronary heart disease, Rosuvastatin is indicated to reduce total mortality and the risk of major cardiovascular events (cardiovascular death, stroke, MI, unstable angina, or arterial revascularization). The usual dose is 10-40 mg orally once a day. The usual start dose is 10 mg once a day. A 5 mg start dose is available for special patient populations if needed. For patients with severe hypercholesterolemia (including heterozygous familial hypercholesterolemia) or those with aggressive lipid targets, a start dose of 20 mg may be considered.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:32:50.250431+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8300-06,Rosuvastatin (as calcium),Fadztat,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IzWXPifLlxFuSg8Zk7zdfr2LRtS1B0Ny/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8300-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IzWXPifLlxFuSg8Zk7zdfr2LRtS1B0Ny_view_usp_drivesdk_1a8ce5f064.pdf,page_text/DRP-8300-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IzWXPifLlxFuSg8Zk7zdfr2LRtS1B0Ny_view_usp_drivesdk_1a8ce5f064.json,72624640d8f9973d930d314d9899864047a323f3e3dc3f15b951407c5b993fb3,587182,1,digital_text,"Yellowish coloured, round shaped, biconvex, both side plain ﬁlm-coated tablet",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Rosuvastatin should be used as an adjunct to diet when the response to diet and exercise is inadequate. Prevention of Cardiovascular Events: In adult patients with an increased risk of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease based on the presence of cardiovascular disease risk markers such as an elevated hsCRP level, age, hyper tension, low HDL-C, smoking or a family history of premature coronary hear t disease, Rosuvastatin is indicated to reduce total mor tality and the risk of major cardiovascular events (cardiovascular death, stroke, MI, unstable angina, or ar terial revascularization). In adult patients with hypercholesterolaemia: Rosuvastatin is indicated to: reduce elevated LDL-C, Total Cholesterol, triglycerides and to increase HDLcholesterol in patients with primary hypercholesterolemia (heterozygous familial and non familial) and mixed dyslipidemia (Fredrickson Types Iia and Iib). Rosuvastatin also lowers ApoB, nonHDL-C, VLDL-C, VLDL-TG, the LDL-C/HDL-C, total C/HDL-C, nonHDL-C/HDL-C, ApoB/ApoA-I ratios and increases ApoA-I in these populations; treat patients with primary dysbetalipoproteinemia (Fredrickson Type III hyper lipoproteinemia); treat isolated hyper triglyceridemia (Fredrickson Type IV hyperlipidemia); reduce Total Cholesterol and LDL-C in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, as an adjunct to diet and other lipid lowering treatments (e.g. LDL apheresis) or alone if such treatments are unavailable; slow or delay the progression of atherosclerosis. Children and adolescents 6 to 17 years of age: Rosuvastatin is indicated to reduce the Total Cholesterol, LDL-C and Apo B in patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia (HeFH).",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:32:53.944318+00:00
