PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-841-01,Losartan Potassium,Jensar,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dF1QF3WPpK0Z74zKW6O9OYHOaPID5kje/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-841-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dF1QF3WPpK0Z74zKW6O9OYHOaPID5kje_view_usp_drivesdk_abe30e1e5f.pdf,page_text/DRP-841-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dF1QF3WPpK0Z74zKW6O9OYHOaPID5kje_view_usp_drivesdk_abe30e1e5f.json,eccf6ee9d8e81ce583e9382ec83c1938d4f50ef34865f86ceada2fbd99cb9292,437469,1,digital_text,Light orange coloured round flat tablet with an engraved line on one side and the other plain.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Although there is no experience with the use of Losartan potassium in pregnant women, animal studies with Losartan potassium have demonstrated fetal and neonatal injury and death, the mechanism of which is believed to be pharmacologically mediated through effects on the renin-angiotensin system. In humans, fetal renal perfusion, which is dependent upon the development of the renin-angiotensin system, begins in the second trimester; thus, risk to the fetus increases if Losartan potassium is administered during the second or third trimesters of pregnancy. Mechanism of Action",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:37:47.532584+00:00
