rhea. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Syrup: 2 -6years: 5mL(1 teaspoonful) 7-12 years: 10 mL (2 teaspoonfuls) To be taken once a day for supplementation. 2 to 4 times a day for therapeutic use, or as prescribed by the phyisician. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Contraindicated in those persons who have shown hypersensitivity to any component of this preparation. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Do not take more than the recommended dosage. Do not use after the expiry date on the label. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS Ascorbic acid Ascorbic acid is usually well tolerated. However, nausea, vomiting, heartburn, abdominal cramps, fatigue, flushing, insomnia, and sleepiness have been reported with high doses (i.e., 1 g or more daily) Zinc Gastrointestinal side effects such as nausea and vomiting are seen with doses of elemental zinc greater than 30 mg. [Page 2] WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? The amounts of nutrients in the product are not expected to interact with food or medicines. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO WHEN YOU MISS A DOSE? If the child misses the dose for the day just give the next dose and the subsequent doses at the usual recommended schedule, i.e., once a day. Do not double the dose unless recommended by a doctor. WHAT ARE THE SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE? Ascorbic acid Prolonged intake of Ascorbic acid (Vitamin C) in excess of 2 g/day may lead to nausea, abdominal cramps, diarrhea, and nose bleeds. Zinc Rare occurences of acute zinc poisoning have been reported. The toxicity signs observed after ingestion of high zinc doses ( 4 to 8 grams elemental zinc) include nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, fever, metallic taste, and lethargy (sleepiness). WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT A DOCTOR? If any undesirable effect occurs. If the child is taking other vitamin-mineral supplement.",1,2,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T21:50:09.420928+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8627-01,Paracetamol,Neocetamol,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1neQkn0yEX2-hGyCLP3fNpcS_qRbWj19m/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8627-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1neQkn0yEX2-hGyCLP3fNpcS_qRbWj19m_view_usp_drivesdk_104696c0d4.pdf,page_text/DRP-8627-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1neQkn0yEX2-hGyCLP3fNpcS_qRbWj19m_view_usp_drivesdk_104696c0d4.json,7b84d0fb88d801d090255fd2298a226b93fbdebf4c1e436e5907ea90f29d05b2,967100,1,ocr,-Dehydration NEOCETAMOL Intravenous Infusion is clear and slightly yellowish solution. It contains 10mg/ml of paracetamol. Paracetamol is a white crystalline solid or powder chemically described as 4-acetylaminophenol Pregnancy and Lactation: je for Preanane’,1,1,Description,"patients with chronic malnutrition and in patients receiving enzyme inducer. Overdosing may be fatal in these NEOCETAMOL is indicated for the short-term treatment of moderate pain, especially following surgery and for cases. Symptoms generally appear within the first 24 hours and comprise: nausea, vomiting, anorexia, pallor, abdominal pain. Overdose, 7.5g or more of paracetamol in a single administration in adults and 140mg/kg of the short-term treatment of fever, when administration by intravenous route is clinically justified by an urgent need to treat pain or hyperthermia and/or when other route of administration are not possible. body weight in a single administration in children, causes hepatic cytolysis likely to induce complete and irreversible necrosis, resulting in hepatocellular insufficiency, metabolic acidosis and encephalopathy which may",1,1,Indications:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T21:50:23.564509+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8635,Diosmin + Hesperidin,Diosmed,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HqhQa6ZRYmIJnOtsf7F89RFfDzdqG9-D/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8635_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HqhQa6ZRYmIJnOtsf7F89RFfDzdqG9-D_view_usp_drivesdk_2c83d79f98.pdf,page_text/DRP-8635_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HqhQa6ZRYmIJnOtsf7F89RFfDzdqG9-D_view_usp_drivesdk_2c83d79f98.json,dfad433d79c7aa3d605a47488516deceadce1e256da9c4cfb04ade1731ff3954,496655,1,digital_text,"Peach coloured oval shaped film-coated tablet having break line on one side. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? - Pharmacotherapeutic group: Medicinal product acting on the capillaries C: Cardiovascular system - Therapeutic indications: This medicine is a venotonic (it increases venous tone) and a vasculoprotector (it increases resistance in small blood vessels). It is recommended for treating venous circulation disorders (swollen legs, pain, early morning restless legs) and for treating symptoms due to acute haemorrhoidal attack. HOW MUCH & HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Always take this medicine exactly as your doctor or health care provider has told you. Dosage Venous insufficiency: 2 tablets daily, 1 tablet at midday and 1 tablet in the evening, at mealtimes. Haemorrhoidal attack: the dose is 6 tablets per day for 4 days and then 4 tablets per day for the next 3 days, at mealtimes. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Do not take Diosmin + Hesperidin tablet - If you are allergic (hypersensitive) to micronized purified flavonoid fraction or any of the other ingredients.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"This medicine is a venotonic (it increases venous tone) and a vasculoprotector (it increases resistance in small blood vessels). It is recommended for treating venous circulation disorders (swollen legs, pain, early morning restless legs) and for treating symptoms due to acute haemorrhoidal attack. HOW MUCH & HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Always take this medicine exactly as your doctor or health care provider has told you. Dosage Venous insufficiency: 2 tablets daily, 1 tablet at midday and 1 tablet in the evening, at mealtimes. Haemorrhoidal attack: the dose is 6 tablets per day for 4 days and then 4 tablets per day for the next 3 days, at mealtimes. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Do not take Diosmin + Hesperidin tablet - If you are allergic (hypersensitive) to micronized purified flavonoid fraction or any of the other ingredients.",1,1,- Therapeutic indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:50:30.678050+00:00
