W OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Always take this medicine exactly as your doctor or health care provider has told you. Dosage Venous insufficiency: 2 tablets daily, 1 tablet at midday and 1 tablet in the evening, at mealtimes. Haemorrhoidal attack: the dose is 6 tablets per day for 4 days and then 4 tablets per day for the next 3 days, at mealtimes. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Do not take Diosmin + Hesperidin tablet - If you are allergic (hypersensitive) to micronized purified flavonoid fraction or any of the other ingredients.",1,1,- Therapeutic indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:50:26.718377+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8638,Meclizine Hydrochloride,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Mv-B1M8Lr0ljg_4_MQl3GbmUA4YNhKww/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8638_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Mv-B1M8Lr0ljg_4_MQl3GbmUA4YNhKww_view_usp_drivesdk_80faca3ff5.pdf,page_text/DRP-8638_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Mv-B1M8Lr0ljg_4_MQl3GbmUA4YNhKww_view_usp_drivesdk_80faca3ff5.json,e76bb0ab20a7db480da83e7a1ddaa74da32ef84a3833291fea91d08a3c4546ea,166017,1,digital_text,"RiteMED ® Meclizine 25 mg Chewable Tablet is a flat, round, mottled, tutti-frutti flavored chewable tablet that is bisected on both sides WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This product contains meclizine, an antihistamine used as an antiemetic (drug used to stop vomiting). Meclizine works by slowing down the action of the nervous system by blocking the receptors of the brain associated with vomiting. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? This medicine is used to prevent or treat the symptoms of nausea, vomiting or vertigo (dizziness) due to motion sickness. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? This medicine should be taken orally (by mouth), once a day, one hour before travel starts. Dose may be repeated every 24 hours if necessary. Tablets may be chewed then swallowed without water or swallowed whole with water. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? • If you are allergic to meclizine or any ingredient in this product • If you need to perform activities requiring mental alertness or physical coordination (e.g., operating a machine or driving a motor vehicle) since drowsiness may occur with use of meclizine hydrochloride • If you are pregnant or breastfeeding UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS Drowsiness, fatigue, dry mouth, constipation, headache, stomach upset, and rarely, blurred vision have been reported with the use of meclizine hydrochloride. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? • Medicines that depress the nervous system, barbiturates (e.g., phenobarbital), tranquilizers (e.g., diazepam), and alcohol should not be taken together with meclizine because of the potential for increased toxicity WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, just take the next dose as scheduled (i.e., once a day) if still needed to prevent or treat motion sickness. Do not double the dose. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Keep the product out of reach and sight of children. Store at temperatures not exceeding 30ºC. Age Group Recommended Dose: to be given once a day, one hour before travel Adults and children: 1 to 2 tablets 12 years and older 6 to12 years ½ tablet Or, as prescribed by a doctor. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSAGE Symptoms of overdosage with meclizine are similar to atropine overdosage. These include fixed dilated pupils, abnormal eye movements, flushed face, dry mouth, retention of urine in the bladder, drowsiness, fatigue, incoordination, blurred vision, confusion, etc. Central nervous system (CNS) depression with drowsiness or coma which may be followed by excitement, seizures, and finally depression has also been reported. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? • Do not take more than the recommended dose • Do not use after the expiry date on the label WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? • Before taking this medicine, tell your doctor if you have: o Glaucoma (increased eye pressure) o Breathing problem such as asthma, chronic pulmonary disease, emphysema (excessive air in the lungs), or chronic bronchitis o An enlarged prostate gland or difficulty in urinating • If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, consult a doctor before use • If symptoms do not improve or new symptoms appear. ADVERSE DRUG REACTION REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adberse drug reaction, seek medical attention immediately and report to the FDA at www.fda.gov.ph AND RiteMED at (+632) 8-726-0835 or productsafety@ ritemed.com.ph. By reporting undesirable effects, you can help provide more information on the safety of this medicine. AVAILABILITY RiteMED ® Meclizine Hydrochloride 25 mg Chewable Tablet, box of 100’s (in blister pack) Manufactured by Am-Europharma Corporation Brgy. Saimsim, Calamba City, Laguna Distributed by RiteMED Phils., Inc. 56 EDSA, Mandaluyong City, Philippines • RM-MECLIZINE HCl 25 mg Chewable Tablet Product Information Leaflet • F .A. Revision Date: 6 April 2019 • PRINT COLOR Pantone 2756 U V V 140 mm V V V V98 mm 196 mm PAGE 4 Date of First Authorization: Date of Revision: DRP-8638 RTM000000IN01 Reg. IPOPHIL PAGE 2 PAGE 1 PAGE 3 [Page 2]",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T21:50:33.829343+00:00
