PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8649,Pantoprazole (As Sodium Sesquihydrate),None,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/11tKuVpUBPWdAZZq4pz9KhHoxcv3nH9co/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8649_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11tKuVpUBPWdAZZq4pz9KhHoxcv3nH9co_view_usp_drivesdk_8cb439d7fd.pdf,page_text/DRP-8649_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11tKuVpUBPWdAZZq4pz9KhHoxcv3nH9co_view_usp_drivesdk_8cb439d7fd.json,6e4c828cf24aabe3ad52ab21afe8eff184970355f51581a3064b2ba4a42d1325,4077027,2,digital_text_and_ocr,,,,,"Mycophenolate mofetil (MMF): Coadministration of pantoprazole in healthy patients and in transplant patients receiving MMF has been reported to reduce the exposure to the active metabolite, + Patients who are hypersensitive to pantoprazole, other proton pump inhibitors (PPls) or to any mycophenolic acid (MPA), possibly due to a decrease in MMF solubility at an increased gastric pH. component of the product. The clinical relevance of reduced MPA exposure in organ rejection has not been established in trans- + In combination treatment for eradication of H. pylori in patients with moderate to severe renal plant patients receiving pantoprazole and MMF. and hepatic impairment. Drugs Affecting/Metabolized by Hepatic Microsomal Enzymes: Pantoprazole is metabolized in + Patients who are receiving atazanavir. the liver through CYP2C19 and CYP3A4. Drugs known to inhibit CYP2C19 such as fluvoxamine may increase the plasma concentrations of pantoprazole by decreasing the rate of its metabolism. In",2,2,CONTRAINDICATIONS,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T21:50:53.022332+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8651,Ambroxol (As Hydrochloride),Broxamed-30,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1p7D8ARK4axBq24VG2nwSw1Ck2zge9aeT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8651_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1p7D8ARK4axBq24VG2nwSw1Ck2zge9aeT_view_usp_drivesdk_97e2a64e11.pdf,page_text/DRP-8651_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1p7D8ARK4axBq24VG2nwSw1Ck2zge9aeT_view_usp_drivesdk_97e2a64e11.json,d132368224be76579ccf40038d683e73cfd8b20baf17c214c6bc4436d5d99b48,489169,1,digital_text,"White coloured round flat uncoated tablets with beveled edges embossed “ZI” on one side. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Used for the treatment of: Ÿ Acute respiratory tract diseases with impaired formation of secretions, particularly in acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis, asthmatic bronchitis, bronchial asthma and bronchiectasis. Ÿ treatment of respiratory disorders associated with viscid mucus such as: pneumonia, otitis media, sinusitis, nasopharyngitis. Ÿ secretolytic therapy for relieving cough in acute and chronic disorders of the respiratory tract associated with pathologically thickened mucus and impaired mucus transport. HOW MUCH & HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? The tablets should be taken after a meal with adequate fluid. Route of Administration For oral use. Adults one tablet 3 times daily Children The recommended daily dose is 1.2-1.6 mg/kg bodyweight. Children aged 6 to 11 years ½ tablet 3 times daily Elderly There are no relevant data available. Renal impairment In severe renal impairment ambroxol must only be used under medical supervision. In severe renal impairment, maintenance therapy should be reduced or the dosing interval extended. The secretolytic effect of ambroxol is supported by adequate fluid intake. Hepatic impairment In severe hepatic impairment ambroxol must only be used under medical supervision WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Do not take if you are allergic to ambroxol hydrochloride or any of the other ingredients of this medicine.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"Ÿ Dry mouth Ÿ Abdominal pain Rare (may affect less than 1 in 1 000 patients) Ÿ Hypersenzitivity reactions Ÿ Rash Ÿ Urticaria Not known (cannot be estimated from the available data) Ÿ Anaphylactic reactions including anaphylactic shock, angioedema (rapidly developing swelling of the skin, subcutaneous, mucosa or submucosal tissues) and pruritus Ÿ Severe cutaneous adverse reactions (including erythema multiforme, Stevens- Johnson syndrome/toxic epidermal necrolysis and acute generalised exanthematous pustulosis) Ÿ Itching of the skin Ÿ Dry throat WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Do not take with: Antitussives Concomitant administration of antitussives may impair the expectoration of liquefied bronchial mucus due to inhibition of the cough reflex and cause congestion of secretions. Antibiotics After using ambroxol the concentrations of the antibiotics amoxicillin, cefuroxime and erythromycin in bronchial secretions and sputum are increased. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you forget to take a dose, take it as soon as you remember unless it is nearly time for your next dose. If this happens skip the missed dose and take the remaining dose as normal. Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten dose. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE Symptoms and signs In reports of unintentional overdosing and/or medication errors, the symptoms have largely corresponded with the known adverse effects. Treatment If manifestations of poisoning do occur symptomatic treatment is recommended. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you take more than you should, consult your doctor or pharmacist. No specific symptoms of overdose have been reported for humans so far. Based on reports of accidental overdose and/or treatment mistakes observed signs are consistent with known side effects of in recommended doses and may require appropriate symptomatic treatment. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Keep product away from children. For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph Manufactured by: SAGA LIFESCIENCES LIMITED Survey No. 198/2 & 198/3 Chachrawadi, Vasna, Ta. Sanand District, Ahmedabad, Gujarat, 382 210 India Imported and Distributed by:",1,1,Ÿ Indigestion,low,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T21:50:56.136954+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8658,Clomipramine Hydrochloride,Clofranil,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1jyuIqtRmigNll5bb6mvY1jl50inE6w3k/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8658_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jyuIqtRmigNll5bb6mvY1jl50inE6w3k_view_usp_drivesdk_02329c9f5f.pdf,page_text/DRP-8658_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1jyuIqtRmigNll5bb6mvY1jl50inE6w3k_view_usp_drivesdk_02329c9f5f.json,0b3da0f36c7b462afdffc07fbc1f26c753950e4991fab1cea86a2e8cb52738fd,383594,2,digital_text,"A blue colored coated, circulartablet plain on one side and breakline on the other side. Clomipramine is an antiobsessional drug that belongs to the class (dibenzazepine) of pharmacologic agents known as tricyclic antidepressants. Clomipramine hydrochlolide is 3-chloro-5-[3-(dimethylamino)propyl]-10, 11-dihydro5H-dibenz[b,f] azepine monohydrochloride, and its strucrural formula is: yH, /''cH, """"G(p MW=351.31",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION',Clomipramine tablets are indicated for the treatment of • Major depression • Phobias • Obsessive-compulsive disorders • Cataplexy associated with narcolepsy,1,1,"INDICATIONS'·""",high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:50:59.770331+00:00
