PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8666-01,Topiramate,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oAqMLliA3-9KwmtFnV5dCg0rzRgTfZVD/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8666-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oAqMLliA3-9KwmtFnV5dCg0rzRgTfZVD_view_usp_drivesdk_4bb0e0a2c1.pdf,page_text/DRP-8666-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oAqMLliA3-9KwmtFnV5dCg0rzRgTfZVD_view_usp_drivesdk_4bb0e0a2c1.json,03a4ad875badcda9af0b977b3753cb3e7264632208cc689d5935635f3d68025c,340940,2,digital_text,"RiteMED® Topiramate 25 mg is available as a salmon pink colored circular film-coated tablet having a breakline on one side and plain on other side. RiteMED® Topiramate 50 mg is available as a salmon/peach colored circular film-coated tablet having a breakline on one side and plain on other side. RiteMED® Topiramate Tablet is a cytochrome P450 3A4 inducer, and cytochrome P450 2C19 inhibitor. The chemical name for topiramate is [(3aS,5aR,8aR,8bS)- 2,2,7,7-tetramethyl-5,5a,8a,8b-tetrahydrodi[1,3]dioxolo[4,5-a:5’,3’-d]pyran-3a-yl]methyl sulfamate. The empirical formula is C12H21N O8S and molecular weight is 339.359. The structural fomula of topiramate is presented below:",2,2,DESCRIPTION,Epilepsy Topiramate is indicated as monotherapy in patients with newly diagnosed epilepsy or for conversion to monotherapy in patients with epilepsy. Topiramate is indicated as adjunctive therapy for adult and children aged 2 and above with partial onset seizures or generalized tonic-clonic seizures. Topiramate is also indicated in adults and children as adjunctive therapy for the treatment of seizures associated with Lennox Gastaut syndrome. Migraine Topiramate is indicated in adults for the prophylaxis of migraine headache. Topiramate has not been studied in the treatment of acute migraine attacks in other types of headache.,2,2,"INDICATIONS2,3",high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:51:17.329597+00:00
