the eradication of streptococci from the oropharynx; however, data establishing the efficacy of azithromycin and the subsequent prevention of rheumatic fever are not available at present.) In sexually transmitted diseases in men and women, azithromycin is indicated for the treatment of uncomplicated genital infections due to Chlamydia trachomatis. It is also indicated for the treatment of chancroid due to Hemophilus ducreyi and uncomplicated genital infections due to non-multiresistant Neisseria gonorrhoeae; concurrent infection with Treponema pallidum should be excluded. Azithromycin is indicated, either alone or in combination with rifabutin, for prophylaxis against Mycobacterium avium-intracellulare complex (MAC) infection, an opportunistic infection prevalent in patients with advanced human immunodeficiency virus (HIV). Azithromycin is indicated in combination with ethambutol for the treatment of disseminated MAC (DMAC) infection in patients with advanced HIV infection. Azithromycin IV is indicated for the treatment of community-acquired pneumonia (CAP) caused by susceptible organisms, including Legionella pneumophila, in patients who require initial IV therapy. Azithromycin IV is indicated for the treatment of pelvic inflammatory diseases (PID) caused by susceptible organisms (Chlamydia trachomatis, Neisseria gonorrhoea, Mycoplasma hominis) in patients who require initial IV therapy. Viewed on: Tuesday, June 11, 2024 - 2:52:47 AM Eastern Time [Page 3]",2,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:52:22.937535+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-871-02,Diltiazem Hydrochloride,Forzem,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1TU0EH0ZQ_4eyHhgJccwhqafLYKC3JHUi/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-871-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1TU0EH0ZQ_4eyHhgJccwhqafLYKC3JHUi_view_usp_drivesdk_684d99e257.pdf,page_text/DRP-871-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1TU0EH0ZQ_4eyHhgJccwhqafLYKC3JHUi_view_usp_drivesdk_684d99e257.json,6d937cc64563cad9e38ee4e880f7f528ab7048971a81daa2e1d8622eee791848,2337091,2,ocr,"Initial dose of 60mg is given three times daily, increased to 360 mg or u Diltiazem hydrochloride is 1,5-benzothiazepin-4(5H)one,3-(acetyloxy)-5[2-(dimethylamino)-ethyl]-2-3- the physician. p to 480 mg dally or as prescribed by dihydro-2-(4-methoxyphenyl),-monohydrochloride,(+)-cis-. It has an empirical formula of C22H26N204S:HCI and a molecular weight of 450.98. Diltiazem hydrochloride is a white to off-white, round, film-coated tablet, biconvex plain on both sides. HYPERTENSION Initial dose of 60 mg to 120 mg is given twice daily, increased as required to a maximum of 360 mg daily or as",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Each Film-Coated Tablet contains: Used in the management of angina pectoris and hypertension. 30mg Diltiazem Hydrochloride, USP.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T21:52:52.092463+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8715,Levofloxacin (As Hemihydrate),Levoprime,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VpqktTOW7uSYqfgl8aXLF7DVBlrHusHq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8715_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VpqktTOW7uSYqfgl8aXLF7DVBlrHusHq_view_usp_drivesdk_f8f490cd24.pdf,page_text/DRP-8715_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VpqktTOW7uSYqfgl8aXLF7DVBlrHusHq_view_usp_drivesdk_f8f490cd24.json,7cb7221b89e43ece6767c7467aaf20fa682e83cf9f6e29462316f654cc91f1dc,812300,1,digital_text,,,,,"Levofloxacin is used for the treatment of severe infections of the urinary and gastrointestinal tracts including Campylobacter jejuni, Shigella, or Salmonella; for susceptible sexually transmitted diseases; e.g. gonoccocal (including penicillin-resistant) and non-gonoccocal (chlamydial urethritis); for osteomyelitis/septicemia caused by susceptible organisms including bacteria resistant to beta-lactam. It is also used for the treatment of severe infections of the respiratory tract due to susceptible gram-negative infections including Pseudomonas aeruginosa; for multi-drug resistant typhoid fever. It is also used as a post-exposure prophylaxis for meningococcal disease and anthrax in adults.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T21:52:55.274722+00:00
