PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8754,Adapalene,Adrylex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1x_beGRFqCGEsHGOumYokC6Iu6fRk-9eA/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8754_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1x_beGRFqCGEsHGOumYokC6Iu6fRk-9eA_view_usp_drivesdk_eb64452e8f.pdf,page_text/DRP-8754_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1x_beGRFqCGEsHGOumYokC6Iu6fRk-9eA_view_usp_drivesdk_eb64452e8f.json,ae04dfa7408be3bb5f7c3b3db870e29ab6d3b07f129395db1345a5f089d18c2f,3087744,2,digital_text_and_ocr,"Adrylex is a white translucent gel. PHARMACODYNAMICS Topical: The exact mechanism is not known. Adapalene exhibits some retinoic acid-like activity but it also has additional effects. It is thought that adapalene reduces important features of the pathology of acne vulgaris by normalizing the differentiation of follicular epithelial cells and keratinization to prevent microcomedone formation, similar to the mechanism of retinoic acid. Unlike retinoic acid, adapalene selectively binds to some nuclear retinoic acid receptors (RARs) and does not bind to cellular receptors called cytosolic retinoic acid binding proteins (CRABPs). It is hypothesized that by selectively binding to certain nuclear retinoic acid. Also, adapalene may help reduce cell-mediated inflammation, an effect demonstrated by in vitro studies. Adapalene decreases formation of comedones and inflammatory and non-inflammatory acne lesions. PHARMACOKINETICS Absorption Topical bioavailability is low. Elimination Topical: Biliary route is major route of excretion. The elimination half-life is 17.2 + 10.2 hour",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Topical treatment of acne vulgaris.,1,1,INDICATION,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T21:54:12.946962+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8754-01,Adapalene,Adapasenz,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1A8JfFAq6OrQr4YL4wV_SsOHe2xysXx_d/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8754-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1A8JfFAq6OrQr4YL4wV_SsOHe2xysXx_d_view_usp_drivesdk_18dc79a8b1.pdf,page_text/DRP-8754-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1A8JfFAq6OrQr4YL4wV_SsOHe2xysXx_d_view_usp_drivesdk_18dc79a8b1.json,e44c8d8ece7d2abb9596912dfc6571551ca6b4dafe724ef23f7f7d5e3084f703,253302,1,digital_text,"Adapalene (Adapasenz) is a white translucent gel. PHARMACODYNAMICS Topical: The exact mechanism is not known. Adapalene exhibits some retinoic acid-like activity but it also has additional eﬀects. It is thought that Adapalene reduces important features of the pathology of acne vulgaris by normalizing the diﬀerentiation of follicular epithelial cells and keratinization to prevent microcomedone formation, similar to the mechanism of retinoic acid. Unlike retinoic acid, Adapalene selectively binds to some nuclear retinoic acid receptors (RARs) and does not bind to cellular receptor called cystolic retinoic acid binding proteins (CRABPs). It is hypothesized that by selectively binding to certain nuclear retinoic acid. Also, Adapalene may help reduce cell-mediated in/f_lammation, an eﬀect demonstrated by in vitro studies. Adapalene decreases formation of comedones and in/f_lammatory and non-in/f_lammatory acne lesions. PHARMACOKINETICS Absorption Topical bioavailability is low. Elimination Topical: Biliary route is major route of excretion. The elimination half-life is 17.2 ± 10.2 hour.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,Topical treatment of acne vulgaris.,1,1,INDICATION,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T21:54:05.756298+00:00
