PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8757-01,Donepezil hydrochloride,Donepedin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Bx0hlqZpSclnNdjKZ3kLgb0tLV3AbWmU/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8757-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Bx0hlqZpSclnNdjKZ3kLgb0tLV3AbWmU_view_usp_drivesdk_33571a537c.pdf,page_text/DRP-8757-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Bx0hlqZpSclnNdjKZ3kLgb0tLV3AbWmU_view_usp_drivesdk_33571a537c.json,42e28a71cb6faf5cfac79174295074ae190dffb8fd823542b4de5deed8c6a6f1,6120659,1,ocr,"30/5 Donepezil Hydrochloride (Donepedin®) 5 mg is a white, round, film-coated tablets engraved with “WI""on one side and “D5” on the other side. 2) Treatment : As in any case of overdose, general supportive measures should be utilized. Tertiary anticholinergics such as atropine may be used as an Donepezil Hydrochloride (Donepedin®) 10 mg is a yellow, round, film-coated tablets engraved with “W|I”on one side and “D10” on the other side antidote for this drug overdosage. Intravenous atropine sulphate titrated to effect is recommended: an initial dose of 1.0 to 2.0 mg IV with subsequent doses based upon clinical response. Atypical responses in blood pressure and heart rate have been reported with other cholinomimetics when co-administered with 2023.03.21 sH2|At AE AXOA Ho ott sS",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"quaternary anticholinergics such as glycopyrrolate. It is not known whether donepezil hydrochloride and/or its metabolites can be removed by dialysis Symptomatic treatment of mild to moderately severe Alzheimer's dementia. + Haye SEY Ter T ANH AA fms | he (hemodialysis, peritoneal dialysis, or hemofiltration). Treatment of vascular dementia (dementia associated with cerebrovascular disease). > NSSBM",1,1,INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T21:54:42.133882+00:00
