PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8942,Epirubicin Hydrochloride,Carcirub-10,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ExgmSBa1Ru_uGKVKEkvPF15s1FllZ7RR/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8942_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ExgmSBa1Ru_uGKVKEkvPF15s1FllZ7RR_view_usp_drivesdk_900d942a3e.pdf,page_text/DRP-8942_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ExgmSBa1Ru_uGKVKEkvPF15s1FllZ7RR_view_usp_drivesdk_900d942a3e.json,81a52354798795d51541d74031ee0fb382d2f948ee00c41e55e8e93f9f8cd381,5438039,2,digital_text,Orange-red lyophilized powder,1,1,Pharmaceutical forms:,"Epirubicin is used in the treatment of a range of neoplastic conditions including; •Carcinoma of the breast • Gastric cancer When administered intravesically, epirubicin has been shown to be beneficial in the treatment of •Papillary transitional cell carcinoma of the bladder • Carcinoma-in-situ of the bladder. •Prophylaxis of recurrences of superficial bladder carcinoma following transurethral resection",1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T22:08:29.681646+00:00
