PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8993-02,Gliclazide,Glimcose,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UeA9IkUxY9gby0xUJnRm0BAyhhRRa3X_/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8993-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UeA9IkUxY9gby0xUJnRm0BAyhhRRa3X__view_usp_drivesdk_f2e84fa2df.pdf,page_text/DRP-8993-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1UeA9IkUxY9gby0xUJnRm0BAyhhRRa3X__view_usp_drivesdk_f2e84fa2df.json,287256e220904229607ea6bb5e71f59695a07c16b0d0310431b664fea1824dab,495660,1,digital_text,,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Gliclazide (Glimcose) 30 mg can be given in combination with biguanides, alpha glucosidase inhibitors or insulin. Distribution: Special populations: As with any hypoglycemic agent, the dose should be adjusted according to the individual patient's metabolic response (blood glucose, HbA1c). In patients not adequately controlled with Gliclazide (Glimcose) 30 mg, concomitant insulin therapy can be initiated under close medical supervision. Special Populations: Elderly: No clinically significant changes in pharmacokinetic parameters have been observed in elderly patients. Elderly: The maximum recommended daily dose is 120 mg. Gliclazide (Glimcose) 30 mg should be prescribed using the same dosing regimen recommended for patients under 65 years of age. Renal impairment: In patients with mild to moderate renal insufficiency, the same dosing regimen can be used as in patients with normal renal function with careful patient monitoring. These data have been confirmed in clinical trials. Patients at risk of hypoglycemia: -Severe or poorly compensated endocrine disorders (hypopituitarism, hypothyroidism, adrenocorticotrophic insufficiency); -Severe vascular disease (severe coronary heart disease, severe carotid impairment, diffuse vascular disease). It is recommended that the minimum daily starting dose of 30 mg is used. -Withdrawal of prolonged and/or high dose corticosteroid therapy; Pediatric population: Missed Dose: It is important to take the medicine everyday as regular treatment works better. Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten dose. Discontinuation of Treatment: As the treatment for diabetes is usually life long, the patient should discuss with the doctor before stopping this medicinal product. However, if the patient forgets to take a dose of Gliclazide (Glimcose) 30 mg, take the next dose at the usual time. Stopping could cause high blood sugar (hyperglycemia) which increases the risk of developing complications of diabetes. If the patient has any further questions on the use of this product, ask the doctor or pharmacist. The safety and efficacy of Gliclazide (Glimcose) 30 mg in children and adolescents have not been established. No data are available.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T22:09:56.492381+00:00
