PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8994-05,Gliclazide,Glimcose,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dNdu1VNmgDSlHN5ThYpeBZBoSR9i92K2/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8994-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dNdu1VNmgDSlHN5ThYpeBZBoSR9i92K2_view_usp_drivesdk_2a16a0d399.pdf,page_text/DRP-8994-05_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dNdu1VNmgDSlHN5ThYpeBZBoSR9i92K2_view_usp_drivesdk_2a16a0d399.json,e0c194ef605e2bda50480b71a8593053f7a555bd85a393dc5f0bbf9690916ae9,497577,1,digital_text,Gliclazide reduces blood glucose levels by stimulating insulin secretion from the β-cells of the islets of Langerhans. Increase in postprandial insulin and C-peptide secretion persists after two years of treatment.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"If blood glucose is not adequately controlled, the dose may be increased to 60, 90 or 120 mg daily, in successive steps. The interval between each dose increment should be at least 1 month except in patients whose blood glucose has not reduced after two weeks of treatment. In such cases, the dose may be increased at the end of the second week of treatment.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T22:10:10.320311+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8994-06,Gliclazide,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/11Q8PGtCPEaXQOYM74ur04z6Z1JbTyt0S/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8994-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11Q8PGtCPEaXQOYM74ur04z6Z1JbTyt0S_view_usp_drivesdk_ac02a83856.pdf,page_text/DRP-8994-06_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11Q8PGtCPEaXQOYM74ur04z6Z1JbTyt0S_view_usp_drivesdk_ac02a83856.json,5bce53349a804c5cc25829160efea693e1424318a4de106ef23821393cf9520f,8862183,1,digital_text,,,,,,,,,low,needs_human_review_no_sections_found,2026-06-30T22:10:21.002658+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8994-08,Gliclazide,Gliclaphil,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-GZMdl8mTa8amWAHPGWQPrFVjt9KTu2F/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8994-08_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-GZMdl8mTa8amWAHPGWQPrFVjt9KTu2F_view_usp_drivesdk_0f79d51217.pdf,page_text/DRP-8994-08_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-GZMdl8mTa8amWAHPGWQPrFVjt9KTu2F_view_usp_drivesdk_0f79d51217.json,995d4e033db2acb5fc6d8edc83f8d3aff337df5c6b0c95b170c3e7940bbfd9a8,466254,1,digital_text,"White colored, round shaped, flat, uncoated tablet having breakline on one side and plain on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"If a dose is forgotten, there must be no increase in the dose taken the next day. Absorption: As with any hypoglycemic agent, the dose should be adjusted according to the individual patient's metabolic response (blood glucose, HbA1c). In addition to these metabolic properties, gliclazide has hemovascular properties. Initial dose: The recommended starting dose is 30 mg daily half a tablet of Gliclazide 60 mg. If blood glucose is effectively controlled, this dose may be used for maintenance treatment. Elimination: The maximum recommended daily dose is 120 mg. Pharmacodynamic effects: Distribution: Plasma levels increase progressively during the first 6 hours, reaching a plateau which is maintained from the sixth to the twelfth hour after administration. Intra-individual variability is low. Gliclazide is completely absorbed. Food intake does not affect the rate or degree of absorption. In type 2 diabetics, gliclazide restores the first peak of insulin secretion in response to glucose and increases the second phase of insulin secretion. A significant increase in insulin response is seen in response to stimulation induced by a meal or glucose. Mechanism of action: Effects on insulin release: Hemovascular properties: Gliclazide decreases microthrombosis by two mechanisms which may be involved in complications of diabetes: A single daily intake of Gliclazide 60 mg maintains effective gliclazide plasma concentrations over 24 hours. Each modified-release tablet contains: Gliclazide …………………………. 60 mg",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T22:10:24.195598+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8994-09,Gliclazide,Gliget MR,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RN73TMcZgE3F5T0xctUBwZOvIpq6UIBN/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8994-09_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RN73TMcZgE3F5T0xctUBwZOvIpq6UIBN_view_usp_drivesdk_f8e108e84d.pdf,page_text/DRP-8994-09_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1RN73TMcZgE3F5T0xctUBwZOvIpq6UIBN_view_usp_drivesdk_f8e108e84d.json,9e1cf84dea40b4b663c354b84b7f830611daefa0e1ec4492298a8ba7a329e207,842171,1,digital_text,,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Plasma protein binding is approximately 95%. The volume of distribution is around 30 liters. Plasma levels increase progressively during the first 6 hours, reaching a plateau which is maintained from the sixth to the twelfth hour after administration. Intra-individual variability is low. Gliclazide is mainly metabolized in the liver and excreted in the urine: less than 1% of the unchanged form is found in the urine. No active metabolites have been detected in plasma. -Withdrawal of prolonged and/or high dose corticosteroid therapy; -Severe vascular disease (severe coronary heart disease, severe carotid impairment, diffuse vascular disease). Renal impairment: Stopping could cause high blood sugar (hyperglycemia) which increases the risk of developing complications of diabetes. -Severe or poorly compensated endocrine disorders (hypopituitarism, hypothyroidism, adrenocorticotrophic insufficiency); In patients with mild to moderate renal insufficiency, the same dosing regimen can be used as in patients with normal renal function with careful patient monitoring. These data have been confirmed in clinical trials. The safety and efficacy of Gliclazide (Gliget MR) 60 mg in children and adolescents have not been established. No data are available. Discontinuation of Treatment: As the treatment for diabetes is usually life long, the patient should discuss with the doctor before stopping this medicinal product. Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten dose. Patients at risk of hypoglycemia: Missed Dose: It is important to take the medicine everyday as regular treatment works better. -Undernourished or malnourished; However, if the patient forgets to take a dose of Gliclazide (Gliget MR) 60 mg, take the next dose at the usual time. It is recommended that the minimum daily starting dose of 30 mg is used. Pediatric population: In type 2 diabetics, Gliclazide restores the first peak of insulin secretion in response to glucose and increases the second phase of insulin secretion. A significant increase in insulin response is seen in response to stimulation induced by a meal or glucose. Hemovascular properties: Gliclazide decreases microthrombosis by two mechanisms which may be involved in complications of diabetes: -A partial inhibition of platelet aggregation and adhesion, with a decrease in the markers of platelet activation (beta thromboglobulin, thromboxane B2) -An action on the vascular endothelium fibrinolytic activity with an increase in tPA activity. Gliclazide reduces blood glucose levels by stimulating insulin secretion from the β-cells of the islets of Langerhans. Increase in postprandial insulin and C-peptide secretion persists after two years of treatment. Each modified-release tablet contains: In addition to these metabolic properties, Gliclazide has hemovascular properties. Pharmacodynamic effects:",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T22:10:27.472839+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8994-11,Gliclazide,Xbloc-60 MR,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rfl8U0fM2paBX8B7Dh5wYBkdkPsM5xbX/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8994-11_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rfl8U0fM2paBX8B7Dh5wYBkdkPsM5xbX_view_usp_drivesdk_54b9ae4ec0.pdf,page_text/DRP-8994-11_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1rfl8U0fM2paBX8B7Dh5wYBkdkPsM5xbX_view_usp_drivesdk_54b9ae4ec0.json,75b2dd1938fd13e996baa8b942cdc70461e60e228ec756dffa48dd6bd070ce36,5639036,1,ocr,food intake (including breakfast). It is important to have a regular carbohydrate,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"monitoring may also be useful. Moderate symptoms of hypoglycemia, without any loss of consciousness or For non-insulin-dependent diabetes (type 2) in adults, in association with dietary Treatment of patients with G6PD-deficiency with sulfonylurea agents can lead to neurological signs, must be corrected by carbohydrate intake, dose adjustment measures and with exercise, when these measures alone are not sufficient. hemolytic anemia. Since gliclazide belongs to the chemical class of sulfonylurea and/or change of diet. Strict monitoring should be continued until the doctor is drugs, caution should be used in patients with G6PD-deficiency and a non- sure that the patient is out of danger.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T22:10:55.124387+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8994-12,Gliclazide,Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LfBMdEl9UArtviaG-8T4Gsa8B-nwJHJz/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8994-12_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LfBMdEl9UArtviaG-8T4Gsa8B-nwJHJz_view_usp_drivesdk_3d64e5251f.pdf,page_text/DRP-8994-12_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1LfBMdEl9UArtviaG-8T4Gsa8B-nwJHJz_view_usp_drivesdk_3d64e5251f.json,2340a9c8896e4b06d245de845ae79236496a337b85ad9c697ed75498719f877a,569324,1,digital_text,"-Diabetic pre-coma and coma, diabetic keto-acidosis; -Patient refuses or (particularly in elderly subjects) is unable to cooperate; Hypoglycemia: Hospitalization may be necessary and glucose administration may need to be continued for several days. -Hypersensitivity to Gliclazide or to any of the excipients, other sulfonylurea, sulfonamides; -Type 1 diabetes; -Treatment with miconazole; -Lactation.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"If a dose is forgotten, there must be no increase in the dose taken the next day. Initial dose: The recommended starting dose is 30 mg daily [half a tablet of Gliclazide 60 mg. If blood glucose is effectively controlled, this dose may be used for maintenance treatment. The maximum recommended daily dose is 120 mg. The dosage and the half-life of the previous antidiabetic agent should be taken into account when switching to Gliclazide 60 mg. Gliclazide 60 mg can be given in combination with biguanides, alpha glucosidase inhibitors or insulin.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T22:10:58.268243+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-8994-13,Gliclazide,Glik-S,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_uO-ijfzX8lRN0_QdThEvlkVMDuBeMCv/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-8994-13_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_uO-ijfzX8lRN0_QdThEvlkVMDuBeMCv_view_usp_drivesdk_1c26392611.pdf,page_text/DRP-8994-13_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_uO-ijfzX8lRN0_QdThEvlkVMDuBeMCv_view_usp_drivesdk_1c26392611.json,1a49bd9ba3575f602a3eb26e4c8cf8f4153726bfc9cdf8de4252094d02a19f6c,1013113,1,digital_text,"White colored, round shaped, flat, uncoated tablet having breakline on one side and plain on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"For non-insulin-dependent diabetes (type 2) in adults, in association with dietary measures and with exercise, when these measures alone are not sufficient.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T22:11:01.587088+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9007,Terbinafine (as Hydrochloride),Tenafine,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/15TL7qZ8x6gBqVF_M1cbuw1ujg9_mB9GH/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9007_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15TL7qZ8x6gBqVF_M1cbuw1ujg9_mB9GH_view_usp_drivesdk_a1770e7bd7.pdf,page_text/DRP-9007_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_15TL7qZ8x6gBqVF_M1cbuw1ujg9_mB9GH_view_usp_drivesdk_a1770e7bd7.json,70cc5ad7ba0288435494c25780fd96858990c21f3fc6d452f3d712bd2c49864c,76722,1,digital_text,"White homegenous cream. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Tenafine (as hydrochloride) STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE? 10 mg/g (1% w/w) WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Terbinafine hydrochloride cream is used to treat patients with fungal and certain yeast infections of the skin. It attacks and kills the fungus or yeast which is causing your infection. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Adults Your doctor will decide the right amount of Terbinafine hydrochloride cream for you to use and will tell you for how long to use your medication. Apply the cream once or twice a day, for one to two weeks, but this will depend upon the type and area of infection. Infections usually appear to improve within a few days of starting to use Terbinafine hydrochloride cream, but may reappear if the cream is not applied regularly or is stopped too early. Directions for use: ɾCleanse and dry the affected areas thoroughly and wash your hands. Treatment can be helped by keeping the affected areas clean by regular washing and careful drying with your own clean towels and clothes, and not rubbing or scratching the skin. ɾUnscrew the cap then gently squeeze out a small amount of the cream onto your finger. ɾApply just enough cream to form a thin layer on the affected skin and surrounding areas. ɾRub in gently. When used between the toes, buttocks or on the groin, the treated area may be covered with a light, fresh gauze strip, especially at night. ɾReplace the cap on the tube and wash your hands. Even though you will not be using Terbinafine hydrochloride cream during the second week for athlete's foot, full skin healing after the infection has cleared will continue for up to 4 weeks. If you have not noticed any signs of improvement within 2 weeks of first starting treatment, please seek advice from your doctor or pharmacist. Children Use in children is not recommended, since there are no data to support use in this population. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Do not use Terbinafine hydrochloride cream if you are allergic (hypersensitive) to any of the ingredients in the product. The cream is not recommended for use on children. Pregnancy and Lactation Do not use the cream if you are pregnant or breastfeeding, unless advised to by your doctor. Ask your doctor or pharmacist for advice before taking any medicine. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? The cream is for external use only. Do not use on the face. Avoid contact with eyes. In case of accidental contact with eyes, rinse thoroughly with running water. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE? Like all medicines, Terbinafine hydrochloride cream can cause side effects, although not everybody gets them. Stop using the cream and seek medical help immediately if you have any of the following very rare allergic reactions: •difficulty breathing or swallowing, swelling of the mouth, face, lips, tongue or throat(severe allergic reaction). •severe itching of the skin, with a red rash or raised lumps, hives or blisters. Common: (may affect up to 1 in 10 people): skin peeling, itching. Uncommon: (may affect up to 1 in 100 people): skin lesions, scab, skin colour changes, redness, burning, pain and irritation at the site of application. These common and uncommon side effects are usually harmless and you can carry on using the cream. Rare: (may affect up to 1 in 1000 people): eye irritation, dry skin, contact dermatitis, eczema, worsening of symptoms. If you stop using Lamisil 1% w/w Cream Infections may come back if you do not use the cream regularly, or if you stop the treatment too early. If you have any further questions on the use of this product, ask your doctor or pharmacist",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT :,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T22:11:05.543399+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9008,Calcium Carbonate,UCAL,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/19Ku189XPqp-amPW7-4Ve7PCNCOL-7KpR/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9008_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19Ku189XPqp-amPW7-4Ve7PCNCOL-7KpR_view_usp_drivesdk_093f6e32e4.pdf,page_text/DRP-9008_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_19Ku189XPqp-amPW7-4Ve7PCNCOL-7KpR_view_usp_drivesdk_093f6e32e4.json,a209ae71029694562b58610ac3172ca388122f1596bdafe823e40853060bd9ad,358192,1,ocr,"Blue-colored, elongated-shaped biconvex scored on one side film-coated arrhythmias.Extreme hypercalcemia may result in coma and death. Persistently tablets. high calcium levels may lead to irreversible renal damage and soft tissue calcification. Milk-alkali syndrome may occur in patients who ingest large amounts of calcium WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? and absorbable alkali. Calcium carbonate Treatment of hypercalcemia: The treatment with calcium must be discontinued. Treatment with thiazide diuretics, lithium, vitamin A, vitamin D and cardiac",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T22:11:15.881701+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9021,Multivitamins + Iron,Siderfol,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1nl-_a_RqnCplCLdIZlxNOjFzUOye-rsm/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9021_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1nl-_a_RqnCplCLdIZlxNOjFzUOye-rsm_view_usp_drivesdk_6e9bbe47b2.pdf,page_text/DRP-9021_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1nl-_a_RqnCplCLdIZlxNOjFzUOye-rsm_view_usp_drivesdk_6e9bbe47b2.json,5f4583056cb0bcb250f7b0f308bf5a7ab58836db2e4cc3983093ee7e0d89a795,2897221,1,ocr,1 capsule daily or as advised by the physician. Hard Gelatin capsules of Size 0 with red body & red cap with SIDERFOL printed on both body and,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Pyridoxine Hydrochloride B.P. (Vitamin Be) 1.5 mg Prevention and treatment of iron deficiency anemia. In cases of increase iron requirement e.g. Copper Sulphate B.P. 5.0 mg pregnancy, lactation, menstrual period, post operative cases, hemorrhage, ankylostomosis, Permitted colours used in capsule shell. convalescence period of severe diseases, vegetarian diets, etc.",1,1,INDICATION:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T22:11:31.381525+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9031-01,Sitagliptin (as phosphate monohydrate),Sitagligo,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/18KiYIm1HcC3OPvvnWQS1tEf6OKLjk6B9/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9031-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18KiYIm1HcC3OPvvnWQS1tEf6OKLjk6B9_view_usp_drivesdk_846ad4c551.pdf,page_text/DRP-9031-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_18KiYIm1HcC3OPvvnWQS1tEf6OKLjk6B9_view_usp_drivesdk_846ad4c551.json,3eb0bcb37b3a0242c3b6a0f0ccbeeb2d00c7eaed51b0b5cf4c0a1c967e375462,1567435,1,digital_text,"White to off white coloured, round shaped, biconvex, film coated tablet, plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Hypoglycemic Sitagliptin tablets is also indicated as add-on to insulin (with or without metformin) when diet and exercise plus stable dose of insulin do not provide adequate glycaemic control.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T22:11:37.556076+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9033-01,Levetiracetam,Ivetra-100,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1P6zi5ZvbC46W_5YrrfbqpEOlsU25Es2d/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9033-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1P6zi5ZvbC46W_5YrrfbqpEOlsU25Es2d_view_usp_drivesdk_a9dd13607f.pdf,page_text/DRP-9033-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1P6zi5ZvbC46W_5YrrfbqpEOlsU25Es2d_view_usp_drivesdk_a9dd13607f.json,32397acef3d3ebf0a10db3775ad3479cd957877fdb7671cfaf465c3a2a18e040,1971790,2,digital_text,"Levetiracetam is an antiepileptic drug available as grape-flavored liquid (100 mg/mL) for oral administration. The chemical name of levetiracetam, a single enantiomer, is (-)-(S)-␀-ethyl-2-oxo-1- pyrrolidine acetamide, its molecular formula is C H N O and its molecular weight is 8 14 2 2 170.21. Levetiracetam is chemically unrelated to existing antiepileptic drugs (AEDs). It has the following structural formula: Levetiracetam is a white to off-white crystalline powder with a faint odor and a bitter taste. It is very soluble in water (104.0 g/100 mL). It is freely soluble in chloroform (65.3 g/100 mL) and in methanol (53.6 g/100 mL), soluble in ethanol (16.5 g/100 mL), sparingly soluble in acetonitrile (5.7 g/100 mL) and practically insoluble in n-hexane. (Solubility limits are expressed as g/100 mL solvent.) Levetiracetam Oral Solution contains the labeled amount of levetiracetam. Inactive ingredients: sodium citrate, citric acid monohydrate, methyl parahydroxybenzoate, propyl parahydroxybenzoate, ammonium glycyrrhizate, glycerol, maltitol liquid, acesulfame potassium, ART grape flavour, purified water. INDICATION AND USAGE Levetiracetam Oral Solution is indicated as monotherapy in the treatment of partial onset seizures with or without secondary generalisation in patients from 16 years of age with newly diagnosed epilepsy. Levetiracetam Oral Solution is indicated as adjunctive therapy • In the treatment of partial onset seizures with or without secondary generalisation in adults and children from 1 month of age with epilepsy. • In the treatment of myoclonic seizures in adults and adolescents from 12 years of age with Juvenile Myoclonic Epilepsy. • In the treatment of primary generalised tonic-clonic seizures in adults and adolescents from 12 years of age with Idiopathic Generalised Epilepsy. Levetiracetam Oral Solution concentrate is an alternative for patients (adults and children from 4 years of age) when oral administration is temporarily not feasible. DOSAGE AND ADMINISTRATION Monotherapy for adults and adolescents from 16 years of age The recommended starting dose is 250 mg twice daily which should be increased to an initial therapeutic dose of 500 mg twice daily after two weeks. The dose can be further increased by 250 mg twice daily every two weeks depending upon the clinical response. The maximum dose is 1500 mg twice daily. Add-on therapy for adults (18 years) and adolescents (12 to 17 years) weighing 50 kg or more The initial therapeutic dose is 500 mg twice daily. This dose can be started on the first day of treatment. Depending upon the clinical response and tolerability, the daily dose can be increased up to 1,500 mg twice daily. Dose changes can be made in 500 mg twice daily increases or decreases every two to four weeks. Hepatic impairment No dose adjustment is needed in patients with mild to moderate hepatic impairment. In patients with severe hepatic impairment, the creatinine clearance may underestimate the renal insufficiency. Therefore a 50 % reduction of the daily maintenance dose is 2 recommended when the creatinine clearance is < 60 ml/min/1.73 m . Paediatric population The physician should prescribe the most appropriate pharmaceutical form, presentation and strength according to weight and dose. The safety and efficacy of Levetiracetam Oral Solution concentrate for solution for infusion in infants and children less than 4 years have not been established. Monotherapy The safety and efficacy of Levetiracetam Oral Solution in children and adolescents below 16 years as monotherapy treatment have not been established. There are no data available. Add-on therapy for infants aged from 6 to 23 months, children (2 to 11 years) and adolescents (12 to 17 years) weighing less than 50 kg The initial therapeutic dose is 10 mg/kg twice daily. Depending upon the clinical response and tolerability, the dose can be increased up to 30 mg/kg twice daily. Dose changes should not exceed increases or decreases of 10 mg/kg twice daily every two weeks. The lowest effective dose should be used. Dose in children 50 kg or greater is the same as in adults. Dose recommendations for infants from 6 months of age, children and adolescents: Weight Starting dose: Maximum dose: 10 mg/kg twice daily 30 mg/kg twice daily (1) 6 kg 60 mg (0.6 ml) twice daily 180 mg (1.8 ml) twice daily (1) 10 kg 100 mg (1 ml) twice daily 300 mg (3 ml) twice daily (1) 15 kg 150 mg (1.5 ml) twice daily 450 mg (4.5 ml)twice daily (1) 20 kg 200 mg (2 ml) twice daily 600 mg (6 ml) twice daily 25 kg 250 mg twice daily 750 mg twice daily (2) From 50 kg 500 mg twice daily 1,500 mg twice daily (1) Children 20 kg or less should preferably start the treatment with Levetiracetam Oral Solution 100 mg/ml oral solution. (2) Dose in children and adolescents 50 kg or more is the same as in adults. Add-on therapy for infants from 1 month to less than 6 months The tablet formulation is not adapted for use in infants under the age of 6 months. The oral solution is the formulation to use in infants. The initial therapeutic dose is 7 mg/kg twice daily. Depending upon the clinical response and tolerability, the dose can be increased up to 21 mg/kg twice daily. Dose changes should not exceed increases or decreases of 7 mg/kg twice daily every two weeks. The lowest effective dose should be used. Infants should start the treatment with Levetiracetam Oral Solution 100 mg/ml oral solution. Dose recommendations for infants less than 6 months: This presentation should be prescribed for children older than 4 years, adolescents and adults. - A 150 ml bottle with graduated oral syringe containing up to 300 mg levetiracetam (corresponding to 3 ml) with a graduation every 0.1 ml (corresponding to10 mg). In order to ensure the accuracy of the dosing, the smaller bottle (150 ml) and syringe graduated from 0.1 to 3 ml per graduation of 0.1 ml should be prescribed for infants older than 6 months and young children. - A 150 ml bottle with graduated oral syringe containing up to 100 mg levetiracetam (corresponding to 1 ml) with a graduation every 0.05 ml (corresponding to 5 mg). In order to ensure the accuracy of the dosing, the smaller bottle (150 ml) and syringe graduated from 0.05 to 1 ml per graduation of 0.05 ml should be prescribed for infants less than 6 months. Method of administration oral solution The oral solution may be diluted in a glass of water and may be taken with or without food. A graduated oral syringe, an adaptor for the syringe and instructions for use in the package leaflet are provided with Levetiracetam Oral Solution 100mg/mL. The daily dose is administered in two equally divided doses.",1,1,DESCRIPTION,Levetiracetam Oral Solution is indicated as monotherapy in the treatment of partial onset seizures with or without secondary generalisation in patients from 16 years of age with newly diagnosed epilepsy. Levetiracetam Oral Solution is indicated as adjunctive therapy • In the treatment of partial onset seizures with or without secondary generalisation in adults and children from 1 month of age with epilepsy. • In the treatment of myoclonic seizures in adults and adolescents from 12 years of age with Juvenile Myoclonic Epilepsy. • In the treatment of primary generalised tonic-clonic seizures in adults and adolescents from 12 years of age with Idiopathic Generalised Epilepsy. Levetiracetam Oral Solution concentrate is an alternative for patients (adults and children from 4 years of age) when oral administration is temporarily not feasible.,1,1,INDICATION AND USAGE,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T22:11:41.713532+00:00
