ge, proctitis, tenesmus, pruritus, erythema and bleeding. Diosmin + Hesperidin also significantly reduces the frequency, severity and duration of acute hemorrhoidal attacks and bleeding by chronic treatment. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Each film-coated tablet contains: 500 mg micronized purified flavonoid fraction of rutaceae equivalent to Diosmin …… 450 mg Hesperidin…….50 mg WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? This medicine is used for the treatment of the symptoms and signs of organic and idiopathic chronic venous disease of the lower limbs e.g., heavy legs, pain, heat sensation, edema, functional impairment and nocturnal cramps. Treatment of the symptoms of acute hemorrhoidal attacks and chronic hemorrhoidal treatment. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Always take Diosmin + Hesperidin exactly as your doctor or health care provider has told you. Dosage: Usual Dose: Chronic Venous Disease: 2 tablets daily with meals Chronic Hemorrhoidal Disease: 2 tablets daily with meals Acute Hemorrhoidal Attack: 6 tablets daily (in 2 divided doses) for 4 days, then 4 tablets daily (in 2 divided doses) for 3 days, 2 tablets thereafter. Should be taken with food: Take at mealtime. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Do not take this medicine if you are hypersensitive to the active substance or to any of the excipients of Diosmin + Hesperidin. WHAT SHOULD I TAKE NOTE OF WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINES? Let your doctor know if you are pregnant and breastfeeding. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINES Diosmin + Hesperidin may cause any of the following side effects: headache, dizziness, diarrhea, indigestion, stomach pain, nausea, vomiting, constipation and skin itching. If you develop rashes, breathlessness, swollen mouth, lips, tongue or eyes, stop taking this medicine and inform your doctor immediately. These could be sign of an allergic reaction. WHAT OTHER MEDICINES OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Inform your doctor and pharmacist if you are taking any of these medicines: -diclofenac (NSAID or medicine for pain and inflammation) -chlorzoxazone (medicines used for muscle spasm pain) -fexofenadine (medicines for cold and allergy) This list does not include all medicines that may interact with Diosmin + Hesperidin Always notify your doctor and pharmacist if you are taking any other medicines, including herbal tonics such as traditional Chinese medicines, supplements and medicines that you buy without a prescription. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Take the missed dose as soon as you remember. If it is almost time for your next dose, skip the missed dose and return to your normal dosing schedule. Do not double a dose under any circumstances. If you often forget to take your medicines, let your doctor and pharmacist know. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE The most frequently reported adverse events in overdose cases were gastrointestinal events (such as diarrhea, nausea, abdominal pain) and skin events (such as pruritus, rash). WHAT TO DO IF YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage of this medicine and you are experiencing adverse symptoms, seek medical attention immediately. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If you are experiencing an adverse reaction to this medicine, it would be best to consult your doctor as soon as possible. HOW SHOULD I STORE THIS MEDICINE? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T22:21:50.744926+00:00
