of these medicines: -diclofenac (NSAID or medicine for pain and inflammation) -chlorzoxazone (medicines used for muscle spasm pain) -fexofenadine (medicines for cold and allergy) This list does not include all medicines that may interact with Diosmin + Hesperidin Always notify your doctor and pharmacist if you are taking any other medicines, including herbal tonics such as traditional Chinese medicines, supplements and medicines that you buy without a prescription. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Take the missed dose as soon as you remember. If it is almost time for your next dose, skip the missed dose and return to your normal dosing schedule. Do not double a dose under any circumstances. If you often forget to take your medicines, let your doctor and pharmacist know. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE The most frequently reported adverse events in overdose cases were gastrointestinal events (such as diarrhea, nausea, abdominal pain) and skin events (such as pruritus, rash). WHAT TO DO IF YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage of this medicine and you are experiencing adverse symptoms, seek medical attention immediately. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If you are experiencing an adverse reaction to this medicine, it would be best to consult your doctor as soon as possible. HOW SHOULD I STORE THIS MEDICINE? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T22:21:59.701671+00:00
