ny of these medicines: -diclofenac (NSAID or medicine for pain and inflammation) -chlorzoxazone (medicines used for muscle spasm pain) -fexofenadine (medicines for cold and allergy) This list does not include all medicines that may interact with Diosmin + Hesperidin Always notify your doctor and pharmacist if you are taking any other medicines, including herbal tonics such as traditional Chinese medicines, supplements and medicines that you buy without a prescription. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Take the missed dose as soon as you remember. If it is almost time for your next dose, skip the missed dose and return to your normal dosing schedule. Do not double a dose under any circumstances. If you often forget to take your medicines, let your doctor and pharmacist know. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE The most frequently reported adverse events in overdose cases were gastrointestinal events (such as diarrhea, nausea, abdominal pain) and skin events (such as pruritus, rash). WHAT TO DO IF YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage of this medicine and you are experiencing adverse symptoms, seek medical attention immediately. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If you are experiencing an adverse reaction to this medicine, it would be best to consult your doctor as soon as possible. HOW SHOULD I STORE THIS MEDICINE? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T22:22:05.850427+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9166,Clopidogrel (as bisulfate),Clopinova,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1h6KfIKDwqXuX7DEIuMyOshrIyXfdtiNl/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9166_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1h6KfIKDwqXuX7DEIuMyOshrIyXfdtiNl_view_usp_drivesdk_3f49374202.pdf,page_text/DRP-9166_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1h6KfIKDwqXuX7DEIuMyOshrIyXfdtiNl_view_usp_drivesdk_3f49374202.json,fcb4f979bc9656dd0e47a4dd8cb1dbe962005f4668720d9d1c7094124d476905,527494,3,digital_text,,,,,"Prevention of atherothrombotic events Clopidogrel is indicated in: - Adult patients suffering from myocardial infarction (from a few days until less than 35 days), ischaemic stroke (from 7 days until less than 6 months) or established peripheral arterial disease. - Adult patients suffering from acute coronary syndrome: - Non-ST segment elevation acute coronary syndrome (unstable angina or non-Q-wave myocardial infarction), including patients undergoing a stent placement following percutaneous coronary intervention, in combination with acetylsalicylic acid (ASA). - ST segment elevation acute myocardial infarction, in combination with ASA in medically treated patients eligible for thrombolytic therapy.Prevention of atherothrombotic and thromboembolic events in atrial fibrillation In adult patients with atrial fibrillation who have at least one risk factor for vascular events, are not suitable for treatment with Vitamin K antagonists (VKA) and who have a low bleeding risk, clopidogrel is indicated in combination with ASA for the prevention of atherothrombotic and thromboembolic events, including stroke.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-06-30T22:22:15.617048+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9166-03,Clopidogrel (As Bisulfate),Clopitreve,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1F6XY4jRvqBAHg1Ktog47qqPmr8zrcbPm/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9166-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1F6XY4jRvqBAHg1Ktog47qqPmr8zrcbPm_view_usp_drivesdk_7e4a78e562.pdf,page_text/DRP-9166-03_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1F6XY4jRvqBAHg1Ktog47qqPmr8zrcbPm_view_usp_drivesdk_7e4a78e562.json,1c78bf2fbf8c2e28814ae5dfd4239a95685f5a703176ade8fc73bc95bcf99944,486577,3,digital_text,"Light brown, circular, slightly biconvex film-coated tablets, plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Prevention of atherothrombotic events Clopidogrel is indicated in: - Adult patients suffering from myocardial infarction (from a few days until less than 35 days), ischaemic stroke (from 7 days until less than 6 months) or established peripheral arterial disease. - Adult patients suffering from acute coronary syndrome: - Non-ST segment elevation acute coronary syndrome (unstable angina or non-Q-wave myocardial infarction), including patients undergoing a stent placement following percutaneous coronary intervention, in combination with acetylsalicylic acid (ASA). - ST segment elevation acute myocardial infarction, in combination with ASA in medically treated patients eligible for thrombolytic therapy.Prevention of atherothrombotic and thromboembolic events in atrial fibrillation In adult patients with atrial fibrillation who have at least one risk factor for vascular events, are not suitable for treatment with Vitamin K antagonists (VKA) and who have a low bleeding risk, clopidogrel is indicated in combination with ASA for the prevention of atherothrombotic and thromboembolic events, including stroke.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-06-30T22:22:12.093451+00:00
