PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9232-04,Levetiracetam,Levecare,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/12IzkcZaofY_BZIqXPp_RqOGELeyB5k6Z/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9232-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_12IzkcZaofY_BZIqXPp_RqOGELeyB5k6Z_view_usp_drivesdk_efddc15085.pdf,page_text/DRP-9232-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_12IzkcZaofY_BZIqXPp_RqOGELeyB5k6Z_view_usp_drivesdk_efddc15085.json,3c7a8c283ccdd8b19af7be9305579b761750c4e05bcbb3fdbe83bb705dc89c1e,7787815,2,ocr,"Table 5 lists adverse reactions from the pooled pediatric controlled studies (4 to 16 years of age) that occurred Dosage Adjustments in Adult Renal Impairment 12 CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY in at least 2% of pediatric Levetiracetam-treated patients and were numerically more common than in pediatric 2.8 Compatibility and Stability patients treated with placebo. In these studies, either Levetiracetam or placebo was added to concurrent AED DOSAGE FORMS AND STRENGTHS 12.1 Mechanism of Action therapy. 12.2 Pharmacodynamics",1,1,11 DESCRIPTION,0/2014 DOSAGE FORMS AND STRENGTHS Somnolence 15 8 0/2014 Injection: 500 mg/5 mL single-use vial (3),1,1,"Indications and Usage (1.1, 1.2, 1.3)",medium,needs_human_review,2026-06-30T22:26:34.229362+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9236,Amlodipine (as besilate),Azovas,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Wv4xE5H4yqJ233t_37ejltSlMDV8_EOT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9236_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Wv4xE5H4yqJ233t_37ejltSlMDV8_EOT_view_usp_drivesdk_a6e35adc52.pdf,page_text/DRP-9236_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Wv4xE5H4yqJ233t_37ejltSlMDV8_EOT_view_usp_drivesdk_a6e35adc52.json,bbd14a327662c4a048ee0faa14cce54a85404e7925e1c37d7b48351da8f91d71,455126,2,digital_text,"White to off white round flat faced, bevel edged uncoated tablet with break line on one side and plain on other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Hypertension Amlodipine is indicated for the treatment of hypertension, to lower blood pressure. Lowering blood pressure reduces the risk of fatal and nonfatal cardiovascular events, primarily strokes and myocardial infarctions. These benefits have been seen in controlled trials of antihypertensive drugs from a wide variety of pharmacologic classes including amlodipine. Elevated systolic or diastolic pressure causes increased cardiovascular risk, and the absolute risk increase per mmHg is greater at higher blood pressures, so that even modest reductions of severe hypertension can provide substantial benefit. Relative risk reduction from blood pressure reduction is similar across populations with varying absolute risk, so the absolute benefit is greater in patients who are at higher risk independent of their hypertension (for example, patients with diabetes or hyperlipidemia), and such patients would be expected to benefit from more aggressive treatment to a lower blood pressure goal. Some antihypertensive drugs have smaller blood pressure effects (as monotherapy) in black patients, and many antihypertensive drugs have additional approved indications and effects (e.g., on angina, heart failure, or diabetic kidney disease). These considerations may guide selection of therapy. Amlodipine may be used alone or in combination with other antihypertensive agents. Coronary Artery Disease (CAD) Chronic Stable Angina Amlodipine is indicated for the symptomatic treatment of chronic stable angina. Amlodipine may be used alone or in combination with other antianginal agents. Vasospastic Angina (Prinzmetal’s or Variant Angina) Amlodipine is indicated for the treatment of confirmed or suspected vasospastic angina. Amlodipine may be used as monotherapy or in combination with other antianginal agents. Angiographically Documented CAD. In patients with recently documented CAD by angiography and without heart failure or an ejection fraction <40%, Amlodipine is indicated to reduce the risk of hospitalization due to angina and to reduce the risk of a coronary revascularization procedure.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:41:46.138489+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9244,Salbutamol (as sulfate),Oppul,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1aISlR4j6QR3aTUQxswM9GzJpQY1sfcuu/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9244_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1aISlR4j6QR3aTUQxswM9GzJpQY1sfcuu_view_usp_drivesdk_9c4f6f2486.pdf,page_text/DRP-9244_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1aISlR4j6QR3aTUQxswM9GzJpQY1sfcuu_view_usp_drivesdk_9c4f6f2486.json,9eff9921079f953b6ca141bbfd9810e34c93869aae4a2b7a2e03590853bea100,3098375,1,ocr,"A clear colorless, odourless solution.",1,1,DESCRIPTION :,"Salbutamol is used as bronchodilators in the management of reversible airways obstruction, as in asthma and in some patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-07-01T16:41:59.600339+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9251,Ascorbic Acid,Unbranded,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/17a_VcfCPfEmvDz-moxD2oPEdlUntgKPD/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9251_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17a_VcfCPfEmvDz-moxD2oPEdlUntgKPD_view_usp_drivesdk_879984b50f.pdf,page_text/DRP-9251_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17a_VcfCPfEmvDz-moxD2oPEdlUntgKPD_view_usp_drivesdk_879984b50f.json,f1e073f86fda81d8f21e35a6b8951133b4290d2809704eb6863a0201ad6928bc,1126675,1,ocr,"Ascorbic Acid is a white to off-white fine powder; contained in EGC Brown/Brown size #0 by 10’s blister pack, box of 100 capsules. What is in the medicine? The medicine contains Ascorbic Acid, a water soluble vitamin which is essential for the synthesis of collagen and intercellular material. Strength of the medicine Each capsule contains: Ascorbic Acid 500 mg (eq. to 562.4 mg Sodium Ascorbate). What is this medicine used for? It is used for prevention and treatment of Vitamin C deficiency or scurvy and also used to increase body resistance against stress, colds and other infections. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Take 1-2 capsule/s a day or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? -If you are allergic to Ascorbic acid or vitamin C. -Patients with G6PD deficiency. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: It should be given care to patients with excessive urinary excretion of calcium oxalate or hyperoxaluria. Large doses of ascorbic acid have resulted in haemolysis in patients with G6PD deficiency. Tolerance may induce in patients taking high doses. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Ascorbic acid is usually well tolerated. Large doses are reported to cause diarrhea, hyperoxaluria and other gastrointestinal disturbances. Prolonged or excessive use of chewable vitamin C preparations may cause erosion of tooth enamel. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Omeprazole may affect the bioavailability of dietary vitamin C. Ascorbic acid should not be given for the first month after starting desferrioxamine treatment because when there is excess tissue iron there is some evidence that Vitamin C may worsen the iron toxicity. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: Ascorbic acid is usually well tolerated. Large doses are reported to cause diarrhea, hyperoxaluria and other gastrointestinal disturbances. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? If symptoms persist and any undesirable effect occurs, consult your doctor. “For suspected adverse drug reaction report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. ” Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction DRP-9251 DATE OF AUTHORIZATION: October 26, 2020 PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET DATE OF REVISION: November 27, 2020 Manufactured by the Marketing Authorization Holder:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T16:42:07.078879+00:00
