PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-945,Omeprazole,Wilom,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qZ_OdyKh1z3Y4rq7YHOxC7WnPCwRJgfB/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-945_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qZ_OdyKh1z3Y4rq7YHOxC7WnPCwRJgfB_view_usp_drivesdk_ef52df346c.pdf,page_text/DRP-945_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1qZ_OdyKh1z3Y4rq7YHOxC7WnPCwRJgfB_view_usp_drivesdk_ef52df346c.json,13d3a82c402b248d0c74455f3ce8cf0c8272003bbc643b5025830bf260c02d93,1610923,2,ocr,Omeprazole (Wilom) 40 mg Capsule is a white to off-white enteric-coated pellets contained in a white body/white cap #0 EGC.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Omeprazole is a proton pump inhibitor. It inhibits secretions of gastric acid by irreversibly blocking the enzyme system of hydrogen / potassium adenosine triphosphatase, the proton pump of gastric parietal cell. It is used in conditions where inhibition of gastric acid secretion may be beneficial including aspiration syndromes, dyspepsia, gastro-esophageal reflux disease, peptic ulcer disease, and the Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-07-01T16:48:17.811070+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-946,Omeprazole,Wilom,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dw6FWQstZpQR22s5zq7iT7oekwZVaHE4/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-946_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dw6FWQstZpQR22s5zq7iT7oekwZVaHE4_view_usp_drivesdk_8c14304485.pdf,page_text/DRP-946_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dw6FWQstZpQR22s5zq7iT7oekwZVaHE4_view_usp_drivesdk_8c14304485.json,7d4170bbc56ee0bc1a4f8088f733ef6ac26b45ae305d0762db3a349a177fb32c,1478492,2,ocr,Omeprazole 20 mg Capsule is a white to off-white enteric-coated pellets contained in a white body / light gray cap #2 EGC.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Omeprazole is a proton pump inhibitor. It inhibits secretions of gastric acid by irreversibly blocking the enzyme system of hydrogen/potassium adenosine triphosphatase, the proton pump of the gastric parietal cell. It is used in conditions where inhibition of gastric acid secretion may be beneficial, including aspiration syndromes, dyspepsia, gastro-esophageal reflux disease, peptic ulcer disease, and the Zollinger-Ellison syndrome.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,medium,needs_human_review,2026-07-01T16:48:26.051670+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-948,Clopidogrel (As Bisulfate),Plagerine,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_ANHdz2Vlzo6TGfRnDejLNDE_3Je9WVq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-948_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_ANHdz2Vlzo6TGfRnDejLNDE_3Je9WVq_view_usp_drivesdk_831bb58861.pdf,page_text/DRP-948_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_ANHdz2Vlzo6TGfRnDejLNDE_3Je9WVq_view_usp_drivesdk_831bb58861.json,18a4057190a1217e24c24850365f077c98d2ce8f086b92120c76669ef23b9e11,11129807,3,digital_text,,,,,"Clopidogrel is an analogue of ticlopedine with similar actions. It is given prophylactically as an alternative to aspirin in patients at risk of thromboembolic disorders such as myocardial infarction, peripheral arterial disease and stroke.",1,1,INDICATION :,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T16:48:38.279144+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9548,Ascorbic Acid,Excel C,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/14zq31RyeRZ-hReWhviWg3ruPMaLZsWm3/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9548_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14zq31RyeRZ-hReWhviWg3ruPMaLZsWm3_view_usp_drivesdk_6aa84503eb.pdf,page_text/DRP-9548_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_14zq31RyeRZ-hReWhviWg3ruPMaLZsWm3_view_usp_drivesdk_6aa84503eb.json,c842cadefe3dfadb9052a07e2fb7154e9aa07fba6cdfd565653945d39e895638,4335017,2,digital_text,"The product is encapsulated in scarlet cap and body gelatin capsule size #0 and it is white to very faintly yellow crystalline powder. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? It contains Vitamin C. Excel C is an Ascorbic Acid (as Sodium Ascorbate) (Vitamin C) capsule that boosts the body’s immune system. It protects against Vitamin C de/f_iciency and enhances the body’s resistance to stress, the common cold and some types of infections. It meets the increased Vitamin C requirements needed by smokers, athletes, pregnant women, the elderly, and those who suffer from infectious diseases and chronic illness. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Please see formulation. WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? For prevention of Vitamin C de/f_iciency and hastens wound healing and increase body resistance from infectious diseases and for the healthy gums, teeth, bones and other connective tissues. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? For daily maintenance take 1-2 capsule/s. For cold symptoms, take 3-4 capsules daily. Can be given as is or dissolve in fruit juices, water or beverages of choice. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you are allergic on the component of the product. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE Sodium Ascorbate should be given with care to patients with hyperoxaluria. Tolerance may be induced in patients taking high doses. Do not use after the expiry date stated on the label. Ask a doctor before use, if you are on sodium restricted diet. Do not take more than the recommended dose. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Vitamin C is usually well tolerated, but diarrhea, nausea, vomiting and nose bleed if taken with high dose. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? The amount of Vitamin C in the product is not expected to interact with food or medicines. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Take the missed dose and subsequent doses. Do not take extra medicine to make up the missed dose. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE Prolonged intake of Vitamin C in excess of 2g/day may lead to nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, /f_lushing and nose bleeds. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have taken the recommended dosage, consult your doctor. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Keep away from direct sunlight. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If undesirable effect occurs. ADVERSE DRUG REACTION REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adverse drug reaction, seek medical attention immediately and report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph AVAILABILITY In blister pack x 10’s (Box of 30’s & 100’s) 500 mg Capsule VITAMIN",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T16:48:43.018361+00:00
