PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9598,Telmisartan + Hydrochlorothiazide,Micardis Plus,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DTFAD-LLsDsfcoeBFY0v7NwWLsefagjL/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9598_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1DTFAD-LLsDsfcoeBFY0v7NwWLsefagjL_view_usp_drivesdk_f82683d168.pdf,page_text/DRP-9598_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1DTFAD-LLsDsfcoeBFY0v7NwWLsefagjL_view_usp_drivesdk_f82683d168.json,33879850e9721721a143dfa953fd0b62d7e53412fa08d781eb0e1d361af4a061,187818,21,digital_text_and_ocr,"Telmisartan/Hydrochlorothiazide layered tablets, 40/12.5 mg are bilayered tablets of oblong, biconvex shape. The two layers have different colors with the Telmisartan layer being white, the Hydrochlorothiazide layer is red. The white layer is marked with the Boehringer Ingelheim company symbol and the code H4. The tablets are for oral administration. Telmisartan / Hydrochlorothiazide layered tablets, 80/12.5 mg are bilayered tablets of oblong, biconvex shape. The two layers have different colors with the Telmisartan layer being white, the Hydrochlorothiazide layer is red. The white layer is marked with the Boehringer Ingelheim company symbol and the code H8. The tablets are for oral administration. Telmisartan / Hydrochlorothiazide layered tablets, 80/25 mg are bilayered tablets of oblong, biconvex shape. The two layers have different colors with the Telmisartan layer being white, the Hydrochlorothiazide layer is yellow. The white layer is marked with the Boehringer Ingelheim company symbol and the code H9. T he tablets are for oral administration.",1,1,Product Description,Treatment of essential hypertension. As fixed dose combination Telmisartan + HCTZ (Micardis Plus) is indicated in patients whose blood pressure is not adequately controlled on telmisartan or hydrochlorothiazide alone.,1,1,Indications / Usage,medium,needs_human_review,2026-07-01T16:49:09.627238+00:00
