PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9619,,,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/178IRA1G2mOShV16IRsafQdYjj_m9ZExx/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9619_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_178IRA1G2mOShV16IRsafQdYjj_m9ZExx_view_usp_drivesdk_8fd86ec260.pdf,page_text/DRP-9619_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_178IRA1G2mOShV16IRsafQdYjj_m9ZExx_view_usp_drivesdk_8fd86ec260.json,373c7de3454e04f75df7256262ff3e6de30b21a7871a15cb2ab955bcac83f532,964040,1,digital_text,"Bed wetting, pain when passing urine Other side effects (frequency cannot be estimated from the available data) Increased appetite Vertigo (spinning sensation) Inflammation of the liver Urinary retention (difficulty passing urine) (see “Urinary retention”) Suicidal thoughts (see “Suicidal thoughts” earlier in this section), nightmare Amnesia, memory impairment Joint pain Rash with blisters containing pus Intense itching (pruritus) upon discontinuation → Tell your doctor or pharmacist if any of the side effects listed become severe or troublesome, or if you notice side effects not listed in this leaflet. 5. How to store Cetirizine (Allertin): Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Store in original packaging. Do not dispose of medicines in wastewater or household waste. Ask your pharmacist how to dispose of medicines no longer required. This will help to protect the environment. Keep out of reach of children. Do not use this medicine beyond the expiry date shown on the pack. 6. What Cetirizine (Allertin) contains Cetirizine (Allertin) Film-Coated Tablet Each tablet of Cetirizine (Allertin) contains cetirizine dihydrochloride 10 mg. Excipients: lactose monohydrate, starch (maize), P.V.P.K. 30, isopropyl alcohol, colloidal silicon dioxide, magnesium stearate, purified talc, methylene chloride, hydroxy propyl methyl cellulose, titanium dioxide, diethyl phthalate. What Cetirizine (Allertin) looks like and contents of the pack Cetirizine (Allertin) Tablets are white coloured oblong biconvex film-coated tablets having a break line mark on one side and other side plain of each tablet. Availability: Alu/ PVC Blister Pack x 10's (Box of 100's) ADR Reporting Statement: For suspected adverse drug reactions, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration Number: DRP-9619 Date of First Authorization: October 26, 2021 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet: Noveber 5, 2024 Cetirizine Hydrochloride 10 mg Film-Coated Tablet ANTIHISTAMINE Allertin Imported and Distributed by: Ambicare Pharmaceuticals Inc. Amsterdam Extn., Merville Park2F Ambica Building, Subd., Parañaque , Metro Manila Manufactured by: Umedica Laboratories Pvt. Ltd. Plot No. 221, G.I.D.C., II Phase, Vapi, Gujarat, 396195, India [Page 2]",1,1,eruption.,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T16:49:26.569493+00:00
