PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9659,Phenylephrine Hydrochloride + Chlorphenamine Maleate,Neozep,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vE-fhhSmN1TYMjx3dZvVXrhdwVPaWkMi/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9659_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vE-fhhSmN1TYMjx3dZvVXrhdwVPaWkMi_view_usp_drivesdk_b0f06e9f63.pdf,page_text/DRP-9659_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1vE-fhhSmN1TYMjx3dZvVXrhdwVPaWkMi_view_usp_drivesdk_b0f06e9f63.json,ca00b0f7ba54a9c635e3abd519b708d53a9063aa3b036df7412b1dcef926b9a4,584317,1,digital_text,"Phenylephrine HCl + Chlorphenamine maleate (Neozep) Syrup (Oral Drops) is a red, clear syrup with fruity strawberry odor, and candy strawberry taste. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? This medicine contains Phenylephrine HCl and Chlorphenamine maleate. Phenylephrine HCl, a nasal decongestant, clears obstructed air passages and nasal sinuses due to congestion making breathing easier. It also reduces postnasal drip. Chlorphenamine maleate, an anti-allergy, relieves symptoms of allergy such as runny nose, sneezing, and itchy, watery eyes. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T16:49:55.429455+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9664,Piperacillin (as Sodium) + Tazobactam (as Sodium),Pitanic,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dsw1xxK5-3f6VR61xsG_UMQxCOXg3LpB/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9664_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dsw1xxK5-3f6VR61xsG_UMQxCOXg3LpB_view_usp_drivesdk_83bfea5cfa.pdf,page_text/DRP-9664_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dsw1xxK5-3f6VR61xsG_UMQxCOXg3LpB_view_usp_drivesdk_83bfea5cfa.json,898d82f03a0fa48796f5625102de50a388a35880a5efd3b37db6502e8383479c,499463,2,digital_text,A white to oﬀ white crystalline powder ﬁlled in 30 mL USP Type III ﬂint vial with ﬂip oﬀ seal.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION :,"For documented multidrug resistant Gram-negative infections due to organisms proven or suspected to be susceptible to piperacillin + tazobactam except CNS infections; polymicrobial infections (e.g., mixed aerobic and anaerobic infections) in which other agents have insuﬃcient activity or are contraindicated due to toxic potential.",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:49:58.828634+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9666,Olanzapine,Olan ODT,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1nyevKiwyqpRUKHp2igKuHq6xWgYAJm9W/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9666_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1nyevKiwyqpRUKHp2igKuHq6xWgYAJm9W_view_usp_drivesdk_f8ae7df98e.pdf,page_text/DRP-9666_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1nyevKiwyqpRUKHp2igKuHq6xWgYAJm9W_view_usp_drivesdk_f8ae7df98e.json,4d6fe27705554e780c53a0d3bbd216acaa70c4969db6b230c115059eb9b7e2a6,4840090,3,digital_text,"Pale yellow to yellow colored, circular shaped, flat faced beveled edge, Orodispersible tablet, with breakline on one face and plain on other face. Tablet may contain few yellow colored specks of active pharmaceutical ingredient.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Adults Olanzapine is indicated for the treatment of schizophrenia. Olanzapine is effective in maintaining the clinical improvement during continuation therapy in patients who have shown an initial treatment response. Olanzapine is indicated for the treatment of moderate to severe manic episode. In patients whose manic episode has responded to olanzapine treatment, olanzapine is indicated for the prevention of recurrence in patients with bipolar disorder.",1,1,INDICATION:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:50:03.457502+00:00
