PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9761,Eplerenone,Inspra,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/13RKeU6UkrLZwSkEoLMYgGRPzbXvFgA-A/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9761_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13RKeU6UkrLZwSkEoLMYgGRPzbXvFgA-A_view_usp_drivesdk_d23ef5d361.pdf,page_text/DRP-9761_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13RKeU6UkrLZwSkEoLMYgGRPzbXvFgA-A_view_usp_drivesdk_d23ef5d361.json,6795acae07d0f037954076f0651a785f3fee961b16b51978894a27898e7bc222,253229,2,digital_text,"Eplerenone is chemically described as Pregn-4-ene-7 ,21- dicarboxylic acid, 9,11-epoxy-17 -hydroxy-3-oxo-, γ-lactone, methyl ester, (7α,11α,17α)-. Its empirical formula is C24H30O6 and it has a molecular weight of 414.50. The structural formula of eplerenone is represented below: Eplerenone Eplerenone (Inspra) is a yellow, arc diamond film-coated tablet containing eplerenone. Eplerenone is an aldosterone receptor antagonist.",1,1,2.0 DESCRIPTION,"Hypertension Eplerenone is indicated for the treatment of hypertension. In these patients, eplerenone may be used alone or in combination with other antihypertensive agents. Heart Failure – Post Myocardial Infarction (MI) Eplerenone is indicated, in addition to standard therapy, to reduce the risk of cardiovascular mortality and morbidity in stable patients with left ventricular dysfunction (left ventricular ejection fraction [LVEF] ≤40%) and clinical evidence of heart failure after recent MI. New York Heart Association (NYHA) Class II (Chronic) Heart Failure Eplerenone is indicated in addition to standard optimal therapy to reduce the risk of cardiovascular mortality and morbidity in adult patients with NYHA class II (chronic) heart failure and left ventricular systolic dysfunction (LVEF ≤35%).",1,1,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:51:14.020705+00:00
