PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9777,Lidocaine + Prilocaine,Skinumb,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1pwEPRyaqVOap52iQaP1N6b350GHnokgZ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9777_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1pwEPRyaqVOap52iQaP1N6b350GHnokgZ_view_usp_drivesdk_5c16c43f88.pdf,page_text/DRP-9777_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1pwEPRyaqVOap52iQaP1N6b350GHnokgZ_view_usp_drivesdk_5c16c43f88.json,92a18ef896c1d48772f87ac3c7a0c82dc2a64e0886a6f207a9741f5143c1bf54,695639,1,digital_text,White to almost white homogenous cream free from grittiness,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Adults: Topical anaesthesia of the skin in connection with: - intact skin prior to minor dermatological procedures (e.g. needle insertion and surgical treatment of localised lesions) and prior to dermal procedures on larger areas e.g. split skin grafting. - dermal procedures on newly shaven skin of large body areas e.g. laser hair removal - Topical anaesthesia of the genital mucosa, e.g. prior to superficial surgical procedures or prior to infiltration anaesthesia of mucosa. - Topical anaesthesia of leg ulcers to facilitate mechanical cleansing/debridement. Paediatric: (Skinumb) Cream is indicated in the following age groups: neonates 0-2 months, infants 3-11 months and children 1-11 years, Lidocaine + Prilocaine for topical anaesthesia of the skin in connection with needle insertion e.g. iv catheters or blood sampling and in superficial surgical procedure. Lidocaine + Prilocaine (Skinumb) Cream is also indicated in children with atopic dermatitis prior to curettage of mollusca. Studies have failed to demonstrate efficacy of (Skinumb) Cream for heel lancing in newborn infants. Lidocaine + Prilocaine",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:51:41.890586+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9781,Carbocisteine,Diacof,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Tt1WLMLUq4bsgX4dKdBpwb8UaNFtaSD1/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9781_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Tt1WLMLUq4bsgX4dKdBpwb8UaNFtaSD1_view_usp_drivesdk_1683886f8f.pdf,page_text/DRP-9781_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Tt1WLMLUq4bsgX4dKdBpwb8UaNFtaSD1_view_usp_drivesdk_1683886f8f.json,f3b6650f22928000c34a92c86194e668fcd337cdb74b79f4d3751b3db631b5e2,500108,1,ocr,"The medicine is a white crystalline powder contained in green opaque/white opaque capsule size #0, blister pack by 10’s, box of 100 capsules. What is in the medicine? Diacof capsule contains Carbocisteine that reduces the viscosity of sputum and so can be used to help relieve cough and allows bringing up sputum more easily. Strength of the medicine: Each capsule contains 500 mg Carbocisteine. What is this medicine used for? Diacof capsule (Carbocisteine) is a mucolytic agent for the adjunctive therapy of respiratory tract disorders characterized by excessive or viscous mucus where it is advised to promote fluidification and facilitate expectoration. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Take one capsule three times a day or every eight hours, or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? -Caution in patients with a history of peptic ulcer disease because of the risk that mucolytics may disrupt the gastric mucosal barrier. -Not recommended during the first trimester of pregnancy. -If you are allergic to any ingredient in the medicine. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: - When taking this medicine, care is necessary in patients with a history of stomach or intestinal ulcer and gastrointestinal bleeding. - Do not use after the expiry date stated on the label. - Do not take more than the recommended dose. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Nausea and gastric discomfort, and gastrointestinal bleeding have occasionally occurred with Carbocisteine. Skin rashes have also been reported. Carbocisteine rarely causes dizziness, insomnia, headache, palpitations, mid lowering of blood glucose, dryness of mouth, abnormal heart rhythm (atrial fibrillation), and gassiness. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? It has an excellent safety profile and rarely causes side effects. There are no known drug interactions for Carbocisteine. However, this does not necessarily mean no interactions exist. Always consult your doctor if you are taking other medicines What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember, but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: The most common symptoms of an overdose include gastrointestinal disorders. There is no specific antidote for Carbocisteine poisoning. If patient took a higher dose than recommended, gastric lavage can be applied. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, particularly exceeds 4 to 5 times the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct sunlight . When should you consult your doctor? -Consult your doctor first if you are pregnant or breastfeeding before taking Carbocisteine. -If hypersensitivity reaction occur (skin rashes, stomach or intestinal bleeding) consult your doctor. -If symptoms persist and any undesirable effect occurs, consult your doctor. “For suspected adverse drug reaction report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph”. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. DRP-9781 Date of Renewal Authorization: June 03, 2021 Patient Information Leaflet date of revision: July 04, 2021 Manufactured by the Marketing Authorization Holder: Distributed by:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T16:51:50.702637+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9782,Finasteride,Atepros,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1StXCuuHzH3rsJaveh6V6fk40cFvD16rz/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9782_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1StXCuuHzH3rsJaveh6V6fk40cFvD16rz_view_usp_drivesdk_5d5949d0dd.pdf,page_text/DRP-9782_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1StXCuuHzH3rsJaveh6V6fk40cFvD16rz_view_usp_drivesdk_5d5949d0dd.json,620b9ad999ed07e88fdfd4fa3a37a1970a1c3b90c269f39e420dc32b41dc4931,503041,1,digital_text,"Finasteride 5 mg is a biconvex film-coated, blue tablet, 5/16” in diameter, plain on both sides. CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY Pharmacodynamics Finasteride is a member of the 4-azasteroid family of compounds. It is a competitive and specific inhibitor of Type II 5α-reductase. Type II 5α-reductase is an intracellular enzyme which converts testosterone into the more potent androgen 5-dihydrotestosterone (DHT), the principal androgen responsible for stimulation of prostatic growth. Benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH), the abnormal enlargement of the prostate gland dependent upon the conversion of testosterone to DHT within the prostate, produces manifestations such as weak urinary stream, difficulty in initiating urination, urinary frequency and urgency. Inhibition of the conversion of testosterone to DHT by finasteride leads to reduced prostatic size and improvement of urinary flow and associated manifestations of urinary obstruction. Finasteride has no androgenic, antiandrogenic, or other steroid hormone-related properties. Pharmacokinetics Finasteride is rapidly and almost completely absorbed after oral administration. Peak plasma concentrations (Cmax) are attained two hours after an oral dose of 5 mg finasteride and absorption is complete after 6 to 8 hours. There is slow accumulation of the drug during chronic administration. Steady state concentrations of finasteride 5 mg daily are 8 to 10 µg/L. Oral bioavailability is 80%. Food does not affect absorption or bioavailability of finasteride. Finasteride is extensively bound to plasma proteins (~93%); its volume of distribution is 76 liters. Small amounts of finasteride are excreted in seminal fluid in subjects receiving finasteride 5 mg daily but the amount of finasteride in ejaculate is only 1 to 2% of the minimum daily oral dose needed to produce a measurable reduction in circulating DHT levels. Finasteride crosses the blood-brain barrier. The extent to which finasteride is excreted in breast milk is unknown. Finasteride is eliminated relatively rapidly from plasma and its terminal elimination half-life is 6 hours. Finasteride is metabolized extensively in the liver primarily through the cytochrome P450 3A4 enzyme subfamily. Its metabolites, t-butyl side chain monohydroxylated and monocarboxylic acid metabolites, possess < 20% the 5α-reductase inhibitory activity of finasteride. These metabolites are excreted in both the urine (39%) and feces (57%) with only trace amounts of finasteride excreted unchanged in urine (0.04%) or feces. Finasteride's total body clearance is 165 mL/min. No dosage adjustment in the elderly (≥ 70 years old) is required although finasteride's elimination rate in these patients increases to 8 hours compared with 6 hours in younger subjects (45-60 years old).",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"• Treatment and control of benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH) in men with enlarged prostate to: - Cause regression of the enlarged prostate, improve urinary flow and alleviate symptoms associated with BPH - Reduce the risk of acute urinary retention - Reduce the need for surgery including transurethral resection of the prostate (TURP) and prostatectomy Note: Finasteride is not indicated in the following: • Patients who are candidates for immediate surgery • To reduce the risk of developing prostate cancer in healthy men.",1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:51:53.724399+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9783,Potassium Citrate (as monohydrate),Tascit,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1405d5xjOqeey2zAu3l6ihypi8b--JDHO/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9783_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1405d5xjOqeey2zAu3l6ihypi8b--JDHO_view_usp_drivesdk_baeac85682.pdf,page_text/DRP-9783_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1405d5xjOqeey2zAu3l6ihypi8b--JDHO_view_usp_drivesdk_baeac85682.json,d6e48a01ca512d2d1b1a181a1f31475ed36742856c697b2a0b91f08bd98a89ac,931843,1,digital_text,"Potassium Citrate (Tascit ) 1080 mg (10 mEq) Extended-Release Tablet: Cream-mottled, elliptical tablet, plain on both sides ® Potassium Citrate (Tascit BID) 1620 mg (15 mEq) Extended-Release Tablet: Cream-mottled, modified oval tablet, plain on both sides PHARMACODYNAMICS Metabolism of absorbed potassium citrate produces an alkaline load, raising urinary pH and increasing urinary citrate by augmenting citrate clearance. Thus, potassium citrate therapy appears to increase urinary citrate mainly by changing the renal handling of citrate, and, to a smaller extent, by increasing the filterable load of citrate. Increased urinary citrate and pH decrease calcium ion activity by increasing calcium complexation to dissociated anions and thus decreasing the saturation of calcium oxalate. Potassium citrate also inhibits the crystallization and spontaneous nucleation of calcium oxalate and calcium phosphate in hypocitraturic calcium nephrolithiasis. However, potassium citrate does not alter the urinary saturation of calcium phosphate, because the effect of increased citrate complexation of calcium is antagonized by the rise in pH-dependent dissociation of phosphate. Calcium phosphate stones are more stable in alkaline urine. PHARMACOKINETICS Potassium citrate is oxidized in the body to form potassium bicarbonate. Oxidation is virtually complete. Less than 5% of the citrate is excreted unchanged in the urine.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTIONS®,• For the management of:  Renal tubular acidosis (RTA) with calcium stones  Hypocitraturic calcium oxalate nephrolithiasis of any etiology  Uric acid lithiasis with or without calcium stones • For the prevention of stone relapse after extracorporeal shock wave lithotripsy (ESWL),1,1,INDICATIONS,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:51:56.852525+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9784,Risperidone,Risdin,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZhWaJmHs5Hx4trkwSn54dDb_d9w609JW/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9784_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZhWaJmHs5Hx4trkwSn54dDb_d9w609JW_view_usp_drivesdk_2971c7d866.pdf,page_text/DRP-9784_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ZhWaJmHs5Hx4trkwSn54dDb_d9w609JW_view_usp_drivesdk_2971c7d866.json,7795db1255bd89ce85f32724a788337aac8880b1cbbac2d353b7b275ebbd2e93,7257131,1,ocr,"Risperidone (Risdin) 2 mg is a white, oval-shaped biconvex tablet, plain on one side and scored on the other side. H2-Receptor Antagonists (Cimetidine and Ranitidine): These drugs increase the bioavailability of risperidone Risperidone (Risdin) 4 mg is a mottled, green, oval-shaped tablet, plain on one side and scored on the other side. Clozapine: May decrease the clearance of risperidone. Valproate: Risperidone may increase peak plasma concentration of this drug",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,"Drugs that Inhibit CYP2D6 and Other CYP Isozymes: Drug interactions that reduce the metabolism of risperidone to its Risperidone is used for the treatment of schizophrenia and other psychoses active metabolite, 9-hydroxyrisperidone, would increase the plasma concentrations of risperidone and lower the concentrations of 9-hydroxyrisperidone. Selective Serotonin Reuptake Inhibitors (Fluoxetine and Paroxetine): Increase plasma concentrations of risperidone",1,1,INDICATION,medium,needs_human_review,2026-07-01T16:52:21.521088+00:00
