PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9804-02,Nicardipine Hydrochloride,Kardian,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ouUxheD75QT8x7jfRquC23M-1b5dMnYm/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9804-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ouUxheD75QT8x7jfRquC23M-1b5dMnYm_view_usp_drivesdk_978c9e07d3.pdf,page_text/DRP-9804-02_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1ouUxheD75QT8x7jfRquC23M-1b5dMnYm_view_usp_drivesdk_978c9e07d3.json,2e1e21127f27adec97c7b79b09713bd319c562d4c299f1718992d26890d2dfcc,1965791,1,digital_text,Yellow colored clear solution.,1,1,Product Description:,"Nicardipine solution for injection is indicated for the treatment of acute life- threatening hypertension, particularly in the event of: • Malignant arterial hypertension/Hypertensive encephalopathy • Aortic dissection, when short acting beta-blocker therapy is not suitable, or in combination with a beta-blocker when beta-blocker alone is not effective. • Severe pre-eclampsia, when other intravenous antihypertensive agents are not recommended or are contraindicated • Nicardipine is also indicated for the treatment of post-operative hypertension",1,1,Indications:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:53:03.614056+00:00
