PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9891,Felodipine,Plendil ER,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HWg-uYac6E0QYfgsQ2IByNViLNmMvdHL/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9891_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HWg-uYac6E0QYfgsQ2IByNViLNmMvdHL_view_usp_drivesdk_ab17bb71e7.pdf,page_text/DRP-9891_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1HWg-uYac6E0QYfgsQ2IByNViLNmMvdHL_view_usp_drivesdk_ab17bb71e7.json,36d126ca64e7ca8e61d2149c9152b6c6dd90a2f1ceda492a2dc314a42636aa95,123418,11,digital_text,"Film-coated extended-release tablets based on the hydrophilic gel matrix principle. The Felodipine (PLENDIL ER) 2.5 mg tablet is yellow, circular, biconvex, engraved A/FL on one side and 2.5 on the other side, with a diameter of 8.5 mm. The Felodipine (PLENDIL ER) 5 mg tablet is pink, circular, biconvex, engraved A/Fm on one side and 5 on the other side, with a diameter of 9 mm. The Felodipine (PLENDIL ER) 10 mg tablet is reddish-brown, circular, biconvex, engraved A/FE on one side and 10 on the other side, with a diameter of 9 mm.",1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,Hypertension Angina pectoris [Page 2],1,1,Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:54:49.470814+00:00
