PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9896-04,Budesonide,Breecort,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1OUeZK0tCv1r1Dm9Fc68oQ-JjahW2tOMK/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9896-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OUeZK0tCv1r1Dm9Fc68oQ-JjahW2tOMK_view_usp_drivesdk_fc0af91034.pdf,page_text/DRP-9896-04_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1OUeZK0tCv1r1Dm9Fc68oQ-JjahW2tOMK_view_usp_drivesdk_fc0af91034.json,f1ea6722ec29457f09900d0a0f40592dc7c2afa1efef98d791e2348093184ff7,846567,2,ocr,"Children 3 months to 12 years: 0.5-1 mg twice daily. White suspension free from extraneous particles. Maintenance The maintenance dose should be individualised and be the lowest dose which keeps the patient symptom-free. O- Adults (including the elderly and children 12 years and older): 0.5- 1 mg twice daily. HO, Oo Paediatric population Children 3 months to 12 years: 0.25 -0.5 mg twice daily. Patients maintained on oral glucocorticosteroids budesonide nebuliser suspension may permit replacement or significant reduction in dosage of oral glucocorticosteroids while maintaining asthma control. When transfer from oral steroids to budesonide nebuliser suspension is started, the patient should be in a relatively stable phase. A high dose of CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY budesonide nebuliser suspension is then given in combination with the previously used oral",1,1,DESCRIPTION,"Patients who have required high dose emergency corticosteroid therapy or prolonged Treatment of persistent bronchial asthma in patients where use of a pressurised inhaler or treatment at the highest recommended dose of inhaled corticosteroids, may also be at risk dry powder formulation is unsatisfactory or inappropriate. of impaired adrenal function. These patients may exhibit signs and symptoms of adrenal Very serious pseudocroup (laryngitis subglottica) in which hospitalisation is indicated. insufficiency when exposed to severe stress. Additional systemic corticosteroid treatment should be considered during periods of stress or elective surgery. Systemic effects may occur with any inhaled corticosteroid, particularly at high doses",1,1,THERAPEUTIC INDICATIONS,medium,needs_human_review,2026-07-01T16:55:58.862895+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9897,,,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PXsqeEJ6DCNVBnsTeXSniyZNwTQ2gZzG/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9897_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PXsqeEJ6DCNVBnsTeXSniyZNwTQ2gZzG_view_usp_drivesdk_959a62a441.pdf,page_text/DRP-9897_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1PXsqeEJ6DCNVBnsTeXSniyZNwTQ2gZzG_view_usp_drivesdk_959a62a441.json,4c50e7a15182a0911c007b3f784d4909ec6bb874100b6a69787b4b001083f395,1739568,1,digital_text,"Tadah Forte is a light yellow to yellow circular film-coated tablet, biconvex, quadrisect on one side and plain on the other side.",1,1,PROUCT DESCRIPTION:,It is used in the management of erectile dysfunction.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:56:02.545143+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9898,Simeticone,Restime,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VV2RdrDcqItuJ60uqwd1LHoxVEauKMNn/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9898_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VV2RdrDcqItuJ60uqwd1LHoxVEauKMNn_view_usp_drivesdk_c9e703afb8.pdf,page_text/DRP-9898_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VV2RdrDcqItuJ60uqwd1LHoxVEauKMNn_view_usp_drivesdk_c9e703afb8.json,fe5c96ba8c0310b959dde7a5f97e96ae20521f5f0b40f1faafb0494b15cbf3ee,1437519,1,ocr,"Simeticone (Restime®) Suspension (Oral Drops) is a pink suspension, strawberry odor and CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? strawberry flavor. © Take the medicine after meals and at bedtime for best results. © Do not take more than the recommended dose. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? © Do not use after the expiry date on the label. This product contains simeticone, a water-repellant that relieves bloating and gassiness by lowering surface tension of gas bubbles in the gastrointestinal (Gl) tract leading them to coalesce and be expelled. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE ¢ If any undesirable effect occurs. Please see formulation. ¢ If symptoms persist. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? AVAILABILITY ¢ This medicine is used to relieve discomfort due to the accumulation of gas in the stomach and Simeticone (Restime®) Suspension (Oral Drops) in amber bottle of 10 mL. intestines including sensations of bloating, pressure, fullness or stuffed feeling which can be caused by certain food (e.g., carbonated drinks, legumes, potatoes, infant formula, etc.), air swallowing, and dyspepsia. ADVERSE DRUG REACTION REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adverse drug reaction, seek medical attention immediately and report to the FDA at ¢ For the relief of symptoms of excess gas associated with colic. www.fda.gov.ph AND Unilab at +632-8-UNILAB-1 (+632-8-864522-1) for Metro Manila or toll-free HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? +1-800-10-UNILAB-1 for provinces, or e-mail productsafety@unilab.com.ph. By reporting undesirable ¢ This medicine should be taken orally (by mouth) 4 times a day after meals and at bedtime. effects, you can help provide more information on the safety of this medicine. ¢ Fill enclosed dropper to recommended dosage level and dispense slowly into the baby's mouth.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T16:56:10.979315+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9909,Imipenem + Cilastatin Sodium,BDIMI-C 250,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1j2Xop8P5xHRNf6SM1cFLaCWBH4cvF5w-/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9909_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1j2Xop8P5xHRNf6SM1cFLaCWBH4cvF5w-_view_usp_drivesdk_d9c14e33af.pdf,page_text/DRP-9909_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1j2Xop8P5xHRNf6SM1cFLaCWBH4cvF5w-_view_usp_drivesdk_d9c14e33af.json,97abf7a652084bb1a7225e1fee7adaf2a5852c1a11cbabf7430835b431e99bfb,500273,1,digital_text,A white or light yellow powder sealed in 20 mL tubular glass vial USP type I.,1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,"Imipenem and Cilastatin for Injection is indicated for the treatment of serious infections caused by susceptible strains of microorganisms in the conditions listed below: 1) Lower respiratory tract infections 2) Urinary tract infections 3) Intra-abdominal infections 4) Gynecological infections 5) Bacterial Septicemia 6) Bone and joint infections 7) Skin and skin structure infections 8) Endocarditis 9) Polymicrobic infections ANTIMICROBIAL SPECTRUM Imipenem has in vitro activity against a wide range of gram-positive and gram-negative organisms. Imipenem has been shown to be active against most strains of the following microorganisms both in vitro and in clinical infections treated with Imipenem Cilastatin Sodium intravenous formulation. Gram-positive aerobes: (Enterococcus faecalis) (formerly S. faecalis) (Imipenem is inactive in vitro against Enterococcus faecium (formerly S. faecium), Staphylococcus aureus including penicillinase-producing stains (Methicillin-resistant staphylococci should be reported as resistant to Imipenem), Streptococcus pneumoniae, Streptococcus pyogenes. Gram-positive anaerobes: Bifidobacterium spp., Clostridium spp., Eubacterium spp., Peptococcus spp., Peptostreptococcus spp., Propionibacterium spp. Gram-positive aerobes: Bacillus spp., Listeria monocytogenes, Nocardia spp., Staphylococcus saprophyticus, Group C streptococci, Group G streptococci, Viridans group streptococci. The following in vitro data are available, but their clinical significance is unknown: Imipenem exhibits in vitro minimum inhibitory concentrations (MICs) of 4 µg/mL or less against most (90%) strains of the following. microorganisms; however, the safety and effectiveness of Imipenem in treating clinical infestations due to these microorganisms have not been established in adequate and well-controlled clinical trials. Gram-negative aerobes: Acinetobacter spp., Citrobacter spp., Enterobacter spp., Escherichia coli, Gardnerella vaginalis, , , spp., , Haemophilus influenzae Haemophilus parainfluenzae Klebsiella Morganella morganii Proteus vulgaris Providencia rattgeri Pseudomonas aeruginosa Xanthomonas , , (Imipenem is inactive in vitro againt (Pseudomonas) maltophilia and some strains of P. cepacia.), Serratia spp. including S. marcescens. Gram-negative anaerobes: Bacteroides spp. including B. fragilis, Fusobacterium spp. Gram-negative aerobes: Aeromonas hydrophila, Alcaligenes spp., Capnocytophaga spp., Haemophilus ducreyi, Neisseria gonorrhoeae including penicillinase producing strains, Pasteurella spp., Providencia stuartii. Gram-negative anaerobes: Prevotella bivia, Prevotella disiens, Prevotella melaninogenica, Veillonella spp. In vitro tests shows Imipenem to act synergistically with aminoglycoside antibiotics against some isolates of Pseudomonas aeruginosa.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:56:13.958686+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9912,Olanzapine,Olanzapro,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Uan--CjqKdOh-L-3jec9dqgZfKeNMHWT/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9912_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Uan--CjqKdOh-L-3jec9dqgZfKeNMHWT_view_usp_drivesdk_60a27fdba5.pdf,page_text/DRP-9912_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Uan--CjqKdOh-L-3jec9dqgZfKeNMHWT_view_usp_drivesdk_60a27fdba5.json,1305d5172243f6eebea9d57069fd54482c7109bb83eb3e388c2b5ffc63a694c9,330588,1,digital_text,"Olanzapro is an off-white to yellowish-white film-coated tablet, round, biconvex, deep scored on one side and plain on the other side.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Used for the management of schizophrenia and for the short-term treatment of mania associated with bipolar disorder.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:56:16.872676+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9913,Quetiapine Fumarate,Quetiapro,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bPTqNsnSLBCtzgrljviVVsSobvWbGrk2/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9913_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bPTqNsnSLBCtzgrljviVVsSobvWbGrk2_view_usp_drivesdk_93cc262ed8.pdf,page_text/DRP-9913_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bPTqNsnSLBCtzgrljviVVsSobvWbGrk2_view_usp_drivesdk_93cc262ed8.json,567c8d81e584884cf18fb21bdff7f662ff6fa553183f69901e276c07efeb47b7,349332,1,digital_text,"Quetiapro 200 is a white to off-white film coated tablet, round, biconvex and plain on both sides. Quetiapro 100 is a cream yellow to light yellow to yellow film coated tablet, round, biconvex, plain on both sides.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,Quetiapine is used for the treatment of schizophrenia and of mania associated with bipolar disorder.,1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:56:20.707443+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9916,Dapagliflozin (as propanediol monohydrate),ForxigaÂ®,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1K3OmXNVKjWzNMAJq88x5ywZ29xn5Qfir/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9916_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1K3OmXNVKjWzNMAJq88x5ywZ29xn5Qfir_view_usp_drivesdk_ddeea03f84.pdf,page_text/DRP-9916_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1K3OmXNVKjWzNMAJq88x5ywZ29xn5Qfir_view_usp_drivesdk_ddeea03f84.json,fe5cbfc3ea62050b084423b320389f8daea771ab79b8513fa33d6c7be6a5420d,3079244,75,digital_text,"Dapagliflozin ( FORXIGA) 5 mg tablets are yellow, biconvex, round, film coated tablets with “5” debossed on one side and “1427” debossed on the other side. Dapagliflozin (FORXIGA) 10 mg tablets are yellow, biconvex, diamond -shaped, film-coated tablets with “10” debossed on one side and “1428” debossed on the other side. For excipients, see section 6.1 List of Excipients. Dapagliflozin propanediol is described chemically as D-glucitol, 1,5 -anhydro-1-C-[4-chloro-3-[(4- ethoxyphenyl)methyl]phenyl]-, (1 S)-, compounded with (2 S)-1,2-propanediol, hydrate (1:1:1). The empirical formula is C21H25ClO6•C3H8O2•H2O and the molecular weight is 502.98. The structural",1,1,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,Type 2 diabetes mellitus Dapagliflozin (FORXIGA) is indicated in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus for: - the treatment of diabetes as an adjunct to diet and exercise. Dapagliflozin (FORXIGA) can be given as monotherapy or in combination with other medicinal products indicated for the treatment of type 2 diabetes mellitus (see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). - the prevention of new or worsening heart failure or cardiovascular death (see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). - the prevention of new or worsening nephropathy (see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). [Page 2] Heart failure Dapagliflozin (FORXIGA) is indicated in adults for the treatment of heart failure (see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). Chronic kidney disease Dapagliflozin (FORXIGA) is indicated in adults for the treatment of chronic kidney disease (see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). Limitations of Use Dapagliflozin (FORXIGA) is not indicated for use in patients with type 1 diabetes. Dapagliflozin (FORXIGA) should not be used for the treatment of diabetic ketoacidosis.,1,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:56:33.196500+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9916-01,Dapagliflozin (as propanediol monohydrate),Unbranded,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1euMYIcyoDWg-veBavo5fIURuviyzRQnv/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9916-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1euMYIcyoDWg-veBavo5fIURuviyzRQnv_view_usp_drivesdk_c51cc6874a.pdf,page_text/DRP-9916-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1euMYIcyoDWg-veBavo5fIURuviyzRQnv_view_usp_drivesdk_c51cc6874a.json,a18787aad871d4968e6738fbea262937557c4aaf2269de27fc45576ea48e1ea1,2619848,66,digital_text,"Dapagliflozin 10 mg tablets are yellow, biconvex, diamond, film coated tablets with “10” debossed on one side and “1428” debossed on the other side. For excipients, see section 6.1 List of Excipients. Dapagliflozin propanediol is described chemically as D-glucitol, 1,5 -anhydro-1-C-[4-chloro-3-[(4- ethoxyphenyl)methyl]phenyl]-, (1 S)-, compounded with (2 S)-1,2-propanediol, hyd rate (1:1:1). The empirical formula is C21H25ClO6•C3H8O2•H2O and the molecular weight is 502.98. The structural",1,1,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,Type 2 diabetes mellitus Dapagliflozin is indicated in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus for: - the treatment of diabetes as an adjunct to diet and exercise. Dapagliflozin can be given as monotherapy or in combination with other medicinal products indicated for the treatment of type 2 diabetes mellitus (see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). - the prevention of new or worsening heart failure or cardiovascular death (see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). - the prevention of new or worsening nephropathy (see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). Heart failure [Page 2] Dapagliflozin is indicated in adults for the treatment of heart failure with reduced ejection fraction (see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). Chronic kidney disease Dapagliflozin is indicated in adults for the treatment of chronic kidney disease (see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). Limitations of Use Dapagliflozin is not indicated for use in patients with type 1 diabetes. Dapagliflozin should not be used for the treatment of diabetic ketoacidosis.,1,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:56:26.379299+00:00
