PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9927,Anastrozole,Arimidex,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-_qDyI9z16pSY5x6vRanntP0kc9rYg9a/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9927_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-_qDyI9z16pSY5x6vRanntP0kc9rYg9a_view_usp_drivesdk_f911b279cc.pdf,page_text/DRP-9927_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-_qDyI9z16pSY5x6vRanntP0kc9rYg9a_view_usp_drivesdk_f911b279cc.json,6019d4ea214c59a16570b538ce2aeec716091c5d3193987553fb9a011e61d2a1,221186,12,digital_text,"Film-coated tablet. White, round, biconvex tablet with logo on one side and strength on the other. 4. CLINICAL PARTICULARS 4.1 Therapeutic indications Adjuvant treatment of post-menopausal women with hormone receptor positive early invasive breast cancer. Adjuvant treatment of early breast cancer in hormone receptor positive post-menopausal women who have received 2 to 3 years of adjuvant tamoxifen. Treatment of a dvanced breast cancer in post-menopausal w omen. Efficacy has not been demonstrated in estrogen receptor negative patients unless they had a previous positive clinical response to tamoxifen. 4.2 Dosage and method of administration Adults including elderly: One 1 mg tablet to be taken orally once a day. Anastrozole [Page 2] Children: The use of Anastrozole (ARIMIDEX) is not recommended in children, as efficacy has not been established (see sections 5.1 Pharmacodynamic Properties and 5.2 Pharmacokinetic Properties). Renal impairment: No dose change is recommended. Hepatic impairment: No dose change is recommended.",1,2,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,Adjuvant treatment of post-menopausal women with hormone receptor positive early invasive breast cancer. Adjuvant treatment of early breast cancer in hormone receptor positive post-menopausal women who have received 2 to 3 years of adjuvant tamoxifen. Treatment of a dvanced breast cancer in post-menopausal w omen. Efficacy has not been demonstrated in estrogen receptor negative patients unless they had a previous positive clinical response to tamoxifen.,1,1,4.1 Therapeutic indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:57:26.969458+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9928,Felodipine,Plendil ER,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1tLpi1fObj9_gMVzoBQIBYWUlppl4ORqm/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9928_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1tLpi1fObj9_gMVzoBQIBYWUlppl4ORqm_view_usp_drivesdk_4de4b2eef2.pdf,page_text/DRP-9928_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1tLpi1fObj9_gMVzoBQIBYWUlppl4ORqm_view_usp_drivesdk_4de4b2eef2.json,36d126ca64e7ca8e61d2149c9152b6c6dd90a2f1ceda492a2dc314a42636aa95,123418,11,digital_text,"Film-coated extended-release tablets based on the hydrophilic gel matrix principle. The Felodipine (PLENDIL ER) 2.5 mg tablet is yellow, circular, biconvex, engraved A/FL on one side and 2.5 on the other side, with a diameter of 8.5 mm. The Felodipine (PLENDIL ER) 5 mg tablet is pink, circular, biconvex, engraved A/Fm on one side and 5 on the other side, with a diameter of 9 mm. The Felodipine (PLENDIL ER) 10 mg tablet is reddish-brown, circular, biconvex, engraved A/FE on one side and 10 on the other side, with a diameter of 9 mm.",1,1,PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,Hypertension Angina pectoris [Page 2],1,1,Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:57:30.110717+00:00
