PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9942,Dapagliflozin (as propanediol monohydrate),Forxiga,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1_DySBQ8tdCPQmgGGS-Zxkk4VGENcOxK0/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9942_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_DySBQ8tdCPQmgGGS-Zxkk4VGENcOxK0_view_usp_drivesdk_a53d5682d5.pdf,page_text/DRP-9942_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1_DySBQ8tdCPQmgGGS-Zxkk4VGENcOxK0_view_usp_drivesdk_a53d5682d5.json,fe5cbfc3ea62050b084423b320389f8daea771ab79b8513fa33d6c7be6a5420d,3079244,75,digital_text,"Dapagliflozin ( FORXIGA) 5 mg tablets are yellow, biconvex, round, film coated tablets with “5” debossed on one side and “1427” debossed on the other side. Dapagliflozin (FORXIGA) 10 mg tablets are yellow, biconvex, diamond -shaped, film-coated tablets with “10” debossed on one side and “1428” debossed on the other side. For excipients, see section 6.1 List of Excipients. Dapagliflozin propanediol is described chemically as D-glucitol, 1,5 -anhydro-1-C-[4-chloro-3-[(4- ethoxyphenyl)methyl]phenyl]-, (1 S)-, compounded with (2 S)-1,2-propanediol, hydrate (1:1:1). The empirical formula is C21H25ClO6•C3H8O2•H2O and the molecular weight is 502.98. The structural",1,1,3. PHARMACEUTICAL FORM,Type 2 diabetes mellitus Dapagliflozin (FORXIGA) is indicated in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus for: - the treatment of diabetes as an adjunct to diet and exercise. Dapagliflozin (FORXIGA) can be given as monotherapy or in combination with other medicinal products indicated for the treatment of type 2 diabetes mellitus (see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). - the prevention of new or worsening heart failure or cardiovascular death (see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). - the prevention of new or worsening nephropathy (see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). [Page 2] Heart failure Dapagliflozin (FORXIGA) is indicated in adults for the treatment of heart failure (see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). Chronic kidney disease Dapagliflozin (FORXIGA) is indicated in adults for the treatment of chronic kidney disease (see section 5.1 Pharmacodynamic properties). Limitations of Use Dapagliflozin (FORXIGA) is not indicated for use in patients with type 1 diabetes. Dapagliflozin (FORXIGA) should not be used for the treatment of diabetic ketoacidosis.,1,2,4.1 Therapeutic Indications,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:58:13.802419+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9955-01,Citicoline (as sodium),Citinerve,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1dBy1a8Ha4QG5MPmEwVZ-IL7dWmHm7sw4/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9955-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dBy1a8Ha4QG5MPmEwVZ-IL7dWmHm7sw4_view_usp_drivesdk_5885f43920.pdf,page_text/DRP-9955-01_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1dBy1a8Ha4QG5MPmEwVZ-IL7dWmHm7sw4_view_usp_drivesdk_5885f43920.json,9e756a0e5cbde4362713ce26de3192f3832b66c130cc9843dc13ff9f5dd5ecbb,498254,1,digital_text,"Citicoline is a derivative of choline and cytidine that is involved in the biosynthesis of lecithin. It is claimed to increase blood flow and oxygen consumption in the brain and has been given in the treatment of cerebrovascular disorders, Parkinsonism, and head injury. Citicoline is an interneuronal communication enhancer. It increases the neurotransmission levels because it favors the synthesis and production speed of dopamine in the striatum, acting then as a dopaminergic agonist thru the inhibition of tyrosine-hydroxylase. Citicoline acts as a presynaptic cholinergic agent which favors the synthesis of acetylcholine. It also decreases the release of serotonin. Citicoline makes the neurons more active, causing the astrocytes to loosen their grip on the capillaries, thus improving microcirculation. By virtue of this action, Citicoline has an indirect effect on microcirculation. It has the ability to slightly increase cerebral blood flow and exerts an anti-aggregation effect on platelets.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,"Used in the treatment of cerebrovascular disorders (including ischaemic stroke), Parkinsonism, and head injury.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,high,machine_extracted_review_recommended,2026-07-01T16:58:16.422145+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,DRP-9960,,FUDION,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1H_9qyr_QMEV5uVEB-erdEXTSMil4nPte/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/DRP-9960_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1H_9qyr_QMEV5uVEB-erdEXTSMil4nPte_view_usp_drivesdk_51d5f093d3.pdf,page_text/DRP-9960_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1H_9qyr_QMEV5uVEB-erdEXTSMil4nPte_view_usp_drivesdk_51d5f093d3.json,5f5b358019a8f254dd459fa4e630a23ddbd5d5900636fe1a110b3c39af7e1988,171632,1,digital_text,,,,,"Fusidic Acid is indicated for treatment of skin infections caused by staphylococci, streptococci, Propionbacterium acnes, Corynebacterium minutissimum and other Fusidic acid sensitive organisms. The most important indications being: Impetigo, Carbuncles, Infected wounds, Hidradentis, Folliculitis, Boils, Paronychia, Sycosis barbae, Erythrasma, Acne Vulgaris. Fusidic acid is an invisible, non-straining preparation, which is cosmetically acceptable for the treatment of face and scalp infections.",1,1,INDICATIONS:,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T16:58:19.516331+00:00
