PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HMR-112,Vitex Negundo L. (Lagundi Leaf),Negacof,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oJYQIH52AQZ4O9DBuyQi3Q4xiVy-o95_/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HMR-112_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oJYQIH52AQZ4O9DBuyQi3Q4xiVy-o95__view_usp_drivesdk_1f66012aff.pdf,page_text/HMR-112_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1oJYQIH52AQZ4O9DBuyQi3Q4xiVy-o95__view_usp_drivesdk_1f66012aff.json,fef3ad9842787ebf46b8d95a5f3817f814e84acbf1e77d2d6c33c6b251934c9d,240887,1,ocr,"Negacof tablet is a greenish brown to brown mottied white, capsule shaped tablet (oblongated flat) with distinctly perceptible Lagundi odor. . WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? f tablet contains Lagundi (Vitex negundo |. Fam Verbenaceae), cried leaves. It is the only extensively researched and clinically proven natural medicine for cough and asthma in the Philippines. Lagundi (Vitex negundo L.) leaves is the main component of the Negacof . Itts a large native shrub that grows in the Philippines. WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? This product is used for the relief of mild to moderate cough _ to common colds and flu. For cough of bacterial origin. For the relief of mild to moderate reversible bronchospasm in adults. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THE MEDICINE? Adult: 300 — 600 mg three to four times a day. Or as prescribed by the physician WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you are allergic to any ingredient of the product. Safety among pregnant and lactating women has not been studied. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS? Some patients experience itch, nausea, vomiting and diarrhea without a predominating complaint. No known contraindications. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOODS SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? It may be taken with or without food. Take before or after meal WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, just give the next dose and the subsequent doses at the usual recommended schedule. Do not double the dose unless recommended by a doctor. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THE MEDICINE? + Keep the product out of reach and sight of children, * Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C » Protect from light SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE “There is no known signs and symptoms of overdose” WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE USED MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? In case of an overdose, consult a doctor or pharmacist immediately. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE * Do not use after the expiry date on the label. * Do not give more than the recommended dose WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? if any undesirable effect occurs and if symptoms persist. AVAILABILITY ; Aluminum Strip Foil x 10’s (Box of 100’s) DATE OF PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET (PIL): August 2018 Negacof Tablet Registration no.: HMR-112 ADR Reporting Statement “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA:.www.fda.gov.ph” Patient must seek medica! attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Manufactured by: LA CROESUS PHARMA INC, Brgy. Sto. Tomas Bifian, Laguna Manufactured for: MEDILYN DRUG 4 Dominga St. Mendez Rd., Baesa Quezon City Under License from: University of the Philippines Manila (UPM, National Integrated Research Program on Medicinal Plants (NIRPROMP) —— — [Page 2]",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T16:59:55.388650+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HMR-113,Vitex Negundo L. (Lagundi Leaf),Negacof,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/17_HqLRcAbSal2AwPNIPdkAnujWdlmyp_/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HMR-113_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17_HqLRcAbSal2AwPNIPdkAnujWdlmyp__view_usp_drivesdk_705a33b15a.pdf,page_text/HMR-113_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_17_HqLRcAbSal2AwPNIPdkAnujWdlmyp__view_usp_drivesdk_705a33b15a.json,01a67da1fb3d3085744e225161575cb93d25f7ab43b9742d6a571ce077f59a18,292376,1,ocr,"h brown homogenous liquid having a distinct odor of Lagundi, with grapes flavor Negacof syrup is a dark green to greenis| and characteristic Lagundi taste WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? It is the only extensively Negacof syrup contains Lagundi ( Vitex negundo L. Fam Ve rbenaceae) di ried leaves researched and clinically proven n atural m edicine for cough and a: sthma in the Philippin es. Lagundi (Vitex negundo L.) leaves is the main component of the Negacof . It is a large native s hrub that grows in the Philippines. WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? This product is used for the relie f of mild to moderate cough due to comm on colds, flu and mild to moderate acute bronchitis. For relief of mild to mo derate reversible bronchospasm in adults and children over 2 years with obstructive airway disease such as asthma and chronic bronchitis. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOUL D YOU USE THE MEDICINE? Adults: 10 mL (2 teaspoonful) 3 to 4t imes daily. Dose may be increased as needed. Children: 15 mg/kg/dose (or 0.25 mL/ kg/dose) administered 3 times daily. 3 times daily. (10 to 15.5 kgs.) 2-4 years: ¥ teaspoon to 1 teaspoon daily. (15.5 to 20 kgs.) 4-6 years: 1 teaspoon 3 times 6 — 12 years: 1 2 teaspoonful — 2 teaspoonful 3 times daily Children over 40 kgs body weight: 2 teaspoonful 3 times daily. Or as prescribed by the physician. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? among pregnant and lactating women has not been studied. If you are allergic to any ingredient of the product. Safety UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS There are undesirable effects on the tablet WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOODS SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? it may be taken with or without food. Take before or after meal. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? if you miss a dose, just give the next dose and the subs equent doses at the usual recommended schedule. Do not double the dose unless recommended by a doctor. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THE MEDICINE? + Keep the product out of reach and sight of children + Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C * Protect from light + Always keep container tightly closed. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE There is no known signs and symptoms of overdose WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE USED MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? In case of an overdose, consult a doctor or pharmacist immediately. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE + Do not use after the expiry date on the label. * Do not give more than the recommended dose WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If any undesirable effect occurs and if symptoms persist.",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:00:03.431314+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HMR-127,Vitex negundo L. (Lagundi Leaf),Flumexal,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VzIGjRiedn5er_zz7PlpcRV9vNRrpc4Y/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HMR-127_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VzIGjRiedn5er_zz7PlpcRV9vNRrpc4Y_view_usp_drivesdk_35db26e9b2.pdf,page_text/HMR-127_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1VzIGjRiedn5er_zz7PlpcRV9vNRrpc4Y_view_usp_drivesdk_35db26e9b2.json,5c25da0b6ea23a202f07e5cd27763df3be16213e38d0ac310cd7df618ed22ede,322821,1,ocr,THIS MEDICINE? There are no known contraindications. For: Lagundi is erect branched shrub that grows up to 5 meters high and is found throughout,1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:00:09.485511+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HMR-128,Vitex negundo L. (Lagundi Leaf),Negacof,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hmX0dY6mz7mFZ7oKINqYwralGnvyXg3b/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HMR-128_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hmX0dY6mz7mFZ7oKINqYwralGnvyXg3b_view_usp_drivesdk_3a7798c528.pdf,page_text/HMR-128_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1hmX0dY6mz7mFZ7oKINqYwralGnvyXg3b_view_usp_drivesdk_3a7798c528.json,60ff74df2b22f184decf8771c7c7faf9df802422b893a6ecc7ee535f63bcb278,437212,1,ocr,"Negacof 300 mg tablet is a greenish brown to brown round shaped biconvex tablet plain on both sides with characterisitic Lagundi odor. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Negacof tablet contains Lagundi (Vitex negundo L. Fam Verbenaceae) dried leaves . It is the only extensively researched and clinically proven natural medicine for cough and asthma in the Philippines. Lagundi (Vitex negundo L) leaves is the main component of the Negacof . It is a large native shrub that grows in the Philippines. STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE 300 mg per tablet WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? This product is used for the relief of cough due to the common colds, flu and mild to moderate acute bronchitis. For the relief of reversible mild to moderate bronchospasm in adults and children 2 years of age and older with obstructive airway disease such as asthma and bronchitis. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THE MEDICINE? Adult: 1 tablet three to four times a day. Or as prescribed by the physician. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you are allergic to any ingredient of this product. Safety among pregnant and lactating women has not been studied. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS? Some patients experience itch, nausea, vomiting and diarrhea without a predominating complaint. No known contraindications. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOODS SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? It may be taken with or without food. Take before or after meal. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, just give the next dose and the subsequent doses at the usual recommended schedule. Do not double the dose unless recommended by a doctor. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THE MEDICINE? + Keep the product out of reach and sight of children. + Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C + Protect from light SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE There is no known signs and symptoms of overdose. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE USED MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? In case of an overdose, consult a doctor or pharmacist immediately. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE Do not use after the expiry date on the label. + Do not give more than the recommended dose. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? if any undesirable effect occurs and if symptoms persist. AVAILABILITY Aluminum Strip Foil x 10's (Box of 100's) DATE OF OF PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET (PIL): February 2021 Negacof Tablet Registration no.: HMR-128 ADR Reporting Statement “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA:.www.fda.gov.ph” Patient must seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Manufactured by:",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:00:15.576570+00:00
