PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HMR-167,Radix baptisiae tinctoriae (Wild Indigo Root) + Radix echinaceae purpureae (Purple Coneflower Root) + Radix echinaceae pallidae (Pale Coneflower Root) + Herba thujae occidentalis (White Cedar Leaf),Esberitox Compact,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQV7Ot6_NCxDmtvHa4sVghZVqCkTNCyP/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HMR-167_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1DQV7Ot6_NCxDmtvHa4sVghZVqCkTNCyP_view_usp_drivesdk_ab361d02c7.pdf,page_text/HMR-167_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1DQV7Ot6_NCxDmtvHa4sVghZVqCkTNCyP_view_usp_drivesdk_ab361d02c7.json,c7f5fb663be1e568e2c14b19d15a6e31d7038b1e448e9833a8fec6d48ab28d5e,101477,2,digital_text,"Beige to brownish, round, marbled, slightly bi-convexed tablet with a diameter of 12 mm.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,"WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? In case of known hypersensitivity to one of the ac- tive or inactive ingredients or against composites. GI_Esberitox_COMPACT_RP_0000-099-00.indd 1 23.09.21 11:44 [Page 2] 0000/099/00 For principle reasons, do not use in case of • progressive systemic diseases such as tuberculo- sis and a rare inﬂammatory disease (sarcoidosis); • diseases directing the immune system against the own body (auto-immune diseases) like inﬂamma- tory connective-tissue diseases (collagenoses), multiple sclerosis; • acquired immunodeﬁciency like AIDS-diseases, HIV-infections; • an immunosuppressive therapy e.g. after trans- plantations or by chemotherapy for treatment of cancer (cytostatic therapy); • systemic diseases of the white blood cell sys- tem like leukaemia and a reduction of particular white blood cells (agranulocytosis).",1,2,CONTRAINDICATIONS,low,needs_human_review,2026-07-01T17:00:21.862808+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HMR-169,Pelargonium sidoides DC,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1B01wYiVZAzNrHozFrxQqjNGeCiP4PHjD/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HMR-169_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1B01wYiVZAzNrHozFrxQqjNGeCiP4PHjD_view_usp_drivesdk_32ebf04d96.pdf,page_text/HMR-169_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1B01wYiVZAzNrHozFrxQqjNGeCiP4PHjD_view_usp_drivesdk_32ebf04d96.json,45f3ef44847a4e48bc4cdb30448dd5fe77ee04b37e3933b5ea65ad51aea36fb5,469029,1,digital_text,"Pelargonium sidoides 20 mg/5 mL Syrup: a clear, light to reddish brown syrup with a characteristic grape odor and ﬂavor. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Pelargonium sidoides Syrup contains EFLA ®956, a proprietary standardized powder extract from the dried root of Pelargonium sidoides DC (3-7:1). Preparations from the roots of Pelargonium sidoides DC have been traditionally used as herbal treatment for relief of upper respiratory tract infections. Several clinical studies have shown that pelargonium root extract reduced the severity and shortened the duration of throat, nose and bronchial irritations. WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? Pelargonium sidoides Syrup may be effective in alleviating symptoms of acute rhinosinusitis and the common cold. It may be effective in relieving symptoms of chronic cough and sore throat in adults and children. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Adults and children over 12 years............................. take 5 mL 3 times daily After relief of symptoms, continuation of treatment is recommended for a further 2-3 days to prevent a relapse. Treatment duration should not exceed 2 weeks. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you suffer from increased tendency to bleeding and/or taking blood-thinning medication such as warfarin. If you are allergic to any component of the product. If you suffer from severe liver or kidney disease. If you are pregnant or breastfeeding. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS Uncommon side effects (affecting more than 1 in 1,000 but fewer than 1 in 100 people)  Gastrointestinal complaints – stomach pain, heartburn, nausea, diarrhea Rare side effects (affecting more than 1 in 10,000 but fewer than 1 in 1,000)  Mild bleeding from gums and nose  Hypersensitivity reactions – skin rash, itching of skin and mucous membranes Very rare side effects (affecting 1 or fewer in 10,000 people)  Serious hypersensitivity reactions with swelling of face, breathlessness and drop in blood pressure Single cases  Signs indicating changes in liver function have been reported, however causal relationship between these effects and use of the product has not been demonstrated INSERT Pelargonium sidoides DC Pelargonium root extract SPACE FOR Reg IPOPHIL",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:00:25.289193+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HMR-170,Pelargonium sidoides DC. Root,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/11ZjLcloDLlEz4sFwFb1EY9s8MpGXCu9y/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HMR-170_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11ZjLcloDLlEz4sFwFb1EY9s8MpGXCu9y_view_usp_drivesdk_611dac561b.pdf,page_text/HMR-170_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11ZjLcloDLlEz4sFwFb1EY9s8MpGXCu9y_view_usp_drivesdk_611dac561b.json,5a55e726e5a7077767f11395bba091f1d9629ebc647daa535989eb57588a1b00,496099,1,digital_text,"Pelargonium sidoides DC is one-piece, dark brown to black opaque, oval-shaped soft gelatin capsule. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Pelargonium sidoides DC Softgel Capsule contains EFLA ® 956, a proprietary standardized powder extract from the dried root of Pelargonium sidoides DC (3-7:1). Preparations from the roots of Pelargonium sidoides DC have been traditionally used as herbal treatment for relief of upper respiratory tract infections. Several clinical studies have shown that pelargonium root extract reduced the severity and shortened the duration of throat, nose and bronchial irritations. WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? Pelargonium sidoides DC Softgel Capsule may be effective in alleviating symptoms of the common cold. It may be effective in relieving symptoms of chronic cough and sore throat in adults and children. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Adults and children over 12 years: 1 Capsule 3 times daily After relief of symptoms, continuation of treatment is recommended for a further 2-3 days to prevent a relapse. Treatment duration should not exceed 2 weeks. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you suffer from increased tendency to bleeding and/or taking blood-thinning medication such as warfarin. If you are allergic to any component of the product. If you suffer from severe liver or kidney disease. If you are pregnant or breastfeeding. Pelargonium sidoides DC Pelargonium root extract 20 mg Softgel Capsule Cough and Cold Relief INSERT UNILAB UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS Uncommon side effects (affecting more than 1 in 1,000 but fewer than 1 in 100 people)  Gastrointestinal complaints – stomach pain, heartburn, nausea, diarrhea Rare side effects (affecting more than 1 in 10,000 but fewer than 1 in 1,000)  Mild bleeding from gums and nose  Hypersensitivity reactions – skin rash, itching of skin and mucous membranes Very rare side effects (affecting 1 or fewer in 10,000 people)  Serious hypersensitivity reactions with swelling of face, breathlessness and drop in blood pressure Single cases  Signs indicating changes in liver function have been reported, however causal relationship between these effects and use of the product has not been demonstrated",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:00:28.771032+00:00
