ed by the physici an Astrol tablet: Adult: 300 — 600 mg three to four times a day. Or as prescribed by the physician, WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you are allergic to any ingredient women has not been studied. of the product. Safety among pregnant and lactating UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS None where reported in the clinical tr vomiting and diarrhea without a pred ials for Astrol Syrup. For Astrol tablet itch, nausea, ominating complaint. No known contraindications. — — [Page 2] WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOODS SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? It may be taken with or without food. Take before or after meal. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, just give the next dose and the subsequent doses at the usual recommended schedule. Do not double the dose unless recommended by a doctor. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THE MEDICINE? « Keep the product out of reach and sight of children. * Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C * Protect from light + Always keep container tightly closed. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE There is no risk of overdose. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE USED MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? As per clinical studies, there is no risk of overdose. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE * Do not use after the expiry date on the label. « Do not give more than the recommended dose. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If any undesirabie effect occurs and if symptoms persist. AVAILABILITY Astrol Syrup: Amber glass bottle x 60 mL and 120 mL Astrol Tablet: Foil strip x 10’s (Box of 100’s) DATE OF OF PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET (PIL): July 2018 Astrol Syrup Registration no. : HMR-47 Astrol Tablet Registration no.: HMR-48 ADR Reporting Statement “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA:.www.fda.gov.ph” Patient must seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction Under License from: University of the Philippines Manila (UPM) National Integrated Research Program on Medicinal Plants