PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HMR-69,Blumea balsamifera L. (Sambong Leaf),URISAM,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gqAqh1BJhO_LDdkldoXmG1II1nHLDIe6/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HMR-69_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gqAqh1BJhO_LDdkldoXmG1II1nHLDIe6_view_usp_drivesdk_a67b032a43.pdf,page_text/HMR-69_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1gqAqh1BJhO_LDdkldoXmG1II1nHLDIe6_view_usp_drivesdk_a67b032a43.json,14bdf8771e2513b29984ffd076dc2205d6dd39163127945af9bc26bac4d48ed2,301138,1,ocr,"Urisam tablet is a greenish to grayish brown 8 mm oblong tablet, plain on one side bisected on the other. WHATIS IN THE MEDICINE? Urisam tablet is a herbal medicine approved by Department of Health and Food and Drug Administration . It contains Sambong {Blumea balsamifera L_) leaf powder. WHAT IS THE MEDICINE USED FOR? This product is used as an anti-urolithiasis in patients with urinary tract stones with normal kidney function and as a diuretic in patients with mild to moderate congestive heart failure and edema. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU. USE THE MEDICINE? Anti-urolithiasis: 2 tablets three times a cay. Diuretic. 1 tablet three times a day. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you are allergic to any ingredient of the product. Special precaution needed for patients with excretory urogram showing signs of tenal obstruction, Not enough is known about the use of sambong during pregnancy and breast-feeding. Stay on the safe side and avoid use. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS? Sambong can cause allergic reaction for people sensitive to ragweed plants and its relatives. Side effect may include itching and skin irritation WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOODS SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? It may be taken with or without food. Take before or after meal. There is no known contraindications for this product. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, just give the next dose and the subsequent doses at the usual recommended schedule. Do not double the dose unless recommended by a doctor. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THE MEDICINE? * Keep the product out of reach and sight of children. » Store at ternperatures not exceeding 30°C * Protect from light SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE There is no known signs and symptoms of overdose. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE USED MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? As per clinical studies, there is no risk of overdose. In case of an overdose, consult a doctor or pharmacist immediately. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE - Do not use after the expiry date on the label. + Do not give more than the recommended dose. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If any undesirable effect occurs and if symptoms persist. AVAILABILITY Alu/Green PVC Blister Pack x 10's (Box of 100's) DATE OF PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET (PIL): August 2018 Urisam Tablet Registration no.; HMR-69 ADR Reporting Statement “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA:.www.fda.gov.ph.” Patient must seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Manufactured by:",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:01:38.901789+00:00
