PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-006-03,Carbocisteine,United Home Broncho,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wMwcybwYT9NOW9iJbTo6k4Q59-7ZrUYU/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-006-03_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wMwcybwYT9NOW9iJbTo6k4Q59-7ZrUYU_view_usp_drivesdk_ea5cc43aaf.pdf,page_text/HRP-006-03_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1wMwcybwYT9NOW9iJbTo6k4Q59-7ZrUYU_view_usp_drivesdk_ea5cc43aaf.json,d2fdcfafc9586808925e4221d179957e786351c085889836d10be8106c43fb4a,2012296,1,ocr,,,,,"For the treatment of disorders of the respiratory tract associated with excessive mucus PRECAUTION Active peptic ulcer, concomitant administration of antitussive. ADVERSE EFFECTS Nausea, headache, gastric discomfort, diarrhea, gastrointestinal bleeding, and skin rash occasionally occurred with Carbocisteine. DOSAGE CAPSULE 500 mg Adult: 1 capsule every 8 hours or as prescribed by the physician. STORAGE CONDITION Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from light. For suspected adverse drug reaction, seek medical attention immediately and report to the FDA at www.fda.gov.ph AND Unilab at (+632) 858-1000 or productsafety@uni- lab.com.ph. By reporting undesirable effects, you can help provide more information on the safety of this medicine. AVAILABILITY Carbocisteine 500 mg Capsule Blister pack by 10’s (Box of 100’s) DATE OF REVISION: June 2005 DATE OF FIRST AUTHORIZATION: June 2017 Manufactured by Am-Europharma Corporation Brgy. Saimsim, Calamba City, Laguna, Philippines Distributed by UNILAB, Inc. No. 66 United Street, Mandaluyong City Metro Manila, Philippines HRP-006-03 Reg. IPOPHIL ULC157646INO2 Trusted Quality Healthcare Vv a 93.00 mm COLOR GUIDE Pantone 072C [Page 2]",1,1,INDICATION,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:02:16.350672+00:00
