PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-069,Carbocisteine,Abluent,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1adKSPPOPwQuobP_rDFaB3ksBWraMg2zr/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-069_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1adKSPPOPwQuobP_rDFaB3ksBWraMg2zr_view_usp_drivesdk_cbc39dc104.pdf,page_text/HRP-069_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1adKSPPOPwQuobP_rDFaB3ksBWraMg2zr_view_usp_drivesdk_cbc39dc104.json,c316a4791e092cc4518337d39c9525b3010f9fc4f27978ae86e411b020ea1053,528734,1,digital_text,"Slightly sweet, bland and sour, Tutti-Frutti Flavored Pinkish-red Suspension Oral Drops. What is in the Medicine? These medicine contain the active ingredient Carbocisteine, a mucolytic agent. Strength of the medicine Capsule :Each capsule contains: CARBOCISTEINE, PP1…........................................................................................500 mg Suspension :Each 5 mL contains: CARBOCISTEINE, PP1…….…..............................................……...........................250 mg Syrup :Each 5 mL contains: CARBOCISTEINE, PP1……………...............................................….......................100 mg Suspension (Oral Drops) :Each mL contains CARBOCISTEINE, PP1……..….................................................................................50 mg What is this Medicine used for? Carbocisteine is used in the treatment of disorder of the respiratory tract associated with excessive mucus. How much and how often should you use this Medicine? 500 mg Capsule Adult One (1) capsule (500 mg) 250 mg/5 mLSuspension Adults 15 mL (750 mg) Children 6 - 12 years old 5 mL (250 mg) 2 - 5 years old 1.25 mL- 2.5 mL (62.5 mg - 125 mg) 100 mg/5 mL Syrup Children 6 - 12 years old 10 mL (2 teaspoonfuls) 2 - 5 years old 2.5 mL - 5 mL (½ - 1 teaspoonful) 50 mg/mL Suspension (Oral Drops) Infants 12 - 24 months old 1.25 mL 9 - 11 months old 1.00 mL 6 - 8 months old 0.75 mL 3 - 5 months old 0.50 mL < 3 months old 0.25 mL All doses to be taken three (3) to four (4) times a day. Or as prescribed by a physician. When should you not take this Medicine? Active peptic ulcer and known hypersensitivity to Carbocisteine. Care that should be taken when taking this Medicine? It is recommended that Carbocisteine be used with caution in patients with a history of peptic ulcer and be avoided in patients with active ulceration. Undesirable Effects of this Medicine Nausea, headache, gastric discomfort, diarrhea, gastrointestinal bleeding and skin rash have occasionally occurred with Carbocisteine. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this Medicine? Dilution with syrups containing pholcodine will cause precipitation. The use of concomitant antitussive agents is not recommended. In human studies, no interaction has been found between carbocisteine and antibiotics , antihistamines or corticosteroids. Signs and Symptoms of Overdose Reports of overdosage with Carbocisteine do not provide consistent data regarding the signs and symptoms of overdose. There is no known antidote for overdosage. Treatment is symptomatic and supportive. If vomiting has not occured it should be induced by conventional means or gastric lavage may be instituted. In case of accidental overdose or at the first sign of any adverse reaction, discontinue use and seek professional assistance immediately. How should you keep this Medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Availability Capsule - Alu/Clear PVC Blister Pack x 10’s (Box of 100's) Suspension - 60 mLAmber Glass Bottle (Box of 1’s) Syrup -Amber Glass Bottle x 60 mL Suspension (Oral Drops) - Amber Glass Bottle x 15 mL with Dropper (Box of 1’s) ADR REPORTING STATEMENT “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA:www.fda.gov.ph” Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration Number HRP-069 Date of First Authorization/ Renewal August 19, 2008 Date of Revison of Patient Information Leaflet JUNE 2022 If you miss a dose, just take the next dose if still needed for the condition being treated, and the subsequent doses at the recommended time or schedule, i.e., every 8 hours (for adults and children 2 years and older) or every 6 hours (for children 1 to 2 years old). Do not double the dose. What should you do if you miss a dose? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor or contact a poison control center right away. What to do if you have taken more than the recommended dosage? 500 mg Capsule 250 mg/5 mL Suspension 100 mg/5 mL Syrup 50 mg/mL Suspension (Oral Drops) MUCOLYTIC CARBOCISTEINE ABLUENT ® Manufactured by: JM TOLMANN",1,1,Description of the Product,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:02:28.741957+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-071,Carbocisteine,Unbranded,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1n6knxYt3ljYFs5ObNzNiJ9f-JBfpkcX5/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-071_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1n6knxYt3ljYFs5ObNzNiJ9f-JBfpkcX5_view_usp_drivesdk_3ff0cae10e.pdf,page_text/HRP-071_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1n6knxYt3ljYFs5ObNzNiJ9f-JBfpkcX5_view_usp_drivesdk_3ff0cae10e.json,70f71bfa6a2ed7cb9e9d7e86dba40a6893d369bcf173804fcabca0c971ab5913,521766,1,digital_text,"Carbocisteine a medicine that causes phlegm to be less thick and sticky sputum and thus easier to cough up and expel. Carbocisteine, in an in vitro study (outside the living organism), was shown to have signiﬁcantly reduced the ability of bacteria to adhere to human pharyngeal cells. AVAILABILITY White to off-white crystalline powder with dark green cap and light green body hard gelatin capsule. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? STRENGTH OF THE MEDICINE Each capsule contains: CARBOCISTEINE, PP1...................................................................500 mg WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Carbocisteine is used in the treatment of disorder of the respiratory tract associated with excessive mucus. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Adult Dose: 500 mg, one (1) capsule three (3) times daily Or as prescribed by a physician. To be taken orally with food. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Ÿ If you are allergic to any ingredient in the products. Ÿ Avoid carbocisteine in patients with active stomach or intestinal ulcer. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Ÿ These medicines should be given with care in patients with a history of stomach or intestinal ulcer and gastrointestinal bleeding. Ÿ Do not take more than the recommended dose. Ÿ Do not use after the expiry date on the label. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Ÿ Carbocisteine is generally safe. Ÿ Nausea, stomach discomfort, diarrhea, and skin rashes are the most common undesirable effects. Ÿ Carbocisteine rarely causes dizziness, insomnia, headache, palpitations, mild lowering of blood glucose, dryness of mouth, abnormal heart rhythm (atrial ﬁbrillation), and “gasiness”. Ÿ WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Always tell your doctor if you are taking other medicines, including herbal medicines and food supplements. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you mis a dose, just take the next dose if still needed for the condition being treated, and the subsequent doses at the recommended time or schedule, i.e., every 8 hours (for adults and children 2 years and older) or every 6 hours (for children 1 to 2 years old). Do not double the dose. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE Carbocisteine overdose is usually associated with stomach or intestinal discomfort. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor or contact a poison control center right away. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE?o Store at temperatures not exceeding 30 C. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? Ÿ If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, consult your doctor before using this product. Ÿ Stop taking the medicines and consult your doctor immediately if you develop any of the following: *Skin rashes *Stomach or intestinal bleeding Ÿ If symptoms do not improve or new symptoms appear. Clear PVC/Alu Blister Pack x 10’s (Box of 100’s) ADR REPORTING STATEMENT “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.go.ph”, Seek medical attention immediately at the ﬁrst sign of any adverse drug reaction. REGISTRATION NUMBER HRP-071 DATE OF FIRST AUTHORIZATION/ RENEWAL OF THE AUTHORIZATION October 2023 170 mm [Page 2]",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:02:34.787076+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-079,Ascorbic Acid (as Sodium Ascorbate),MaxC,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Zhl9MarNOQ8cIAAEsMW72GkfXe3c4Xz0/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-079_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Zhl9MarNOQ8cIAAEsMW72GkfXe3c4Xz0_view_usp_drivesdk_273a4db80b.pdf,page_text/HRP-079_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1Zhl9MarNOQ8cIAAEsMW72GkfXe3c4Xz0_view_usp_drivesdk_273a4db80b.json,9363d9ca66fc626ad711140b91575a57dac03da6e72968bf4bb1db9285836829,711124,2,ocr,"This product is white to yellowish crystalline powder contained in a yellow/yellow #0 EGC. Whatis in the Medicine? This product contains Ascorbic Acid 500 mg (equivalent to Sodium Ascorbate 562.5 mg), a water-soluble vitamin, essential for the synthesis of collagen and intercellular material. Strength of the Medicine: 500 mg (equivalent to 562.5 mg Sodium Ascorbate) Capsule Whatis this Medicine used for? For the treatment and prevention of ascorbic acid deficiency and scurvy. How much and how often should you use this Medicine? Adults: Orally, 1 capsule daily or as prescribed bya physician. When should you not take this Medicine? If you are allergic (hypersensitive) to any component of the product. Care that should be taken when taking this Medicine? Swallow the capsule whole; do not crush or chew. [Page 2] Undesirable Effects of this Medicine: Large doses may lead to diarrhea, other gastrointestinal disturbances, hyperoxaluria, formation of renal calcium oxalate calculi and haemolysis in patients with G6PD deficiency. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this Medicine? It should not be given for the first month after starting desferrioxamine treatment. What should you do if you miss a dose? Just take the next dose if you miss a dose. Do not take a double dose to make up the missed dose. Signs and Symptoms of Overdose: Ascorbic acid is usually well tolerated. There is no information regarding overdosage. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you take more than the recommended dose, consult a doctor. How should you keep this Medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from light. When should you consult your doctor? If you experience any undesirable effect, talk to a doctor. ADR Reporting: For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph Patient should seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration Number: HRP-079 Availability Alu/PVC/PVDC Blister Pack x 10's (Box of 30's, 50's, and 100's) Date of First Authorization: 15 May 2009 Manufactured by: Hizon Laboratories, Inc. Assumption Road, Sumulong Highway, Antipolo City Revision date: April 2021 [Page 3]",1,2,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:02:43.614448+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-079-05,Ascorbic Acid (as Sodium Ascorbate),Boie-C,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/13JImCRiAfk9GEBfXCqsb24R5_h3JT9BN/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-079-05_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13JImCRiAfk9GEBfXCqsb24R5_h3JT9BN_view_usp_drivesdk_f8eb5fedfa.pdf,page_text/HRP-079-05_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13JImCRiAfk9GEBfXCqsb24R5_h3JT9BN_view_usp_drivesdk_f8eb5fedfa.json,374f838c9ef210ea3933fdaf12f1628097d2bf6b0f064950d1761cdcaec49da3,877007,1,digital_text,"What is in the Medicine? Registration Number: HRP-079-05 500 mg CAPSULE When should you not take this Medicine? If you are allergic (hypersensitive) to any component of the product. Care that should be taken when taking this Medicine? Swallow the capsule whole; do not crush or chew. Large doses may lead to diarrhea, other gastrointestinal disturbances, hyperoxaluria, formation of renal calcium oxalate calculi and haemolysis in patients with G6PD deficiency. . Undesirable Eﬀects of this Medicine: What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this Medicine? It should not be given for the first month after starting desferrioxamine treatment. Just take the next dose if you miss a dose. Do not take a double dose to make up the missed dose. Ascorbic acid is usually well tolerated. There is no information regarding overdosage. If you take more than the recommended dose, consult a doctor. Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from light. What should you do if you miss a dose? Signs and Symptoms of Overdose: What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? How should you keep this Medicine? When should you consult your doctor? If you experience any undesirable e ﬀect, talk to a doctor. Patient should seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Dimension: 9.5cm x 22.5cm BOIPIN0007102 [Page 2]",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:02:38.410686+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-097,ASCORBIC ACID,ASCOR-Kid,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CoBymDeNThpOcxr1v0SCZpfN1K_8ROR6/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-097_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1CoBymDeNThpOcxr1v0SCZpfN1K_8ROR6_view_usp_drivesdk_d863a2390b.pdf,page_text/HRP-097_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1CoBymDeNThpOcxr1v0SCZpfN1K_8ROR6_view_usp_drivesdk_d863a2390b.json,871fd71d65d7e13560f84c9af8984c3c73a4f3a027af8ff31cd519194e455f07,216892,1,ocr,"Clear yellow to orange colored, orange flavored syrup with sweet and If the child has taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a sour taste containing 100 mg of Ascorbic Acid in each 5 mL. It complies doctor. with the USP specifications for Ascorbic Acid Oral Solution. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine Whatis in the medicine? Y Donotgive more than the recommended dose. These nutritional supplements contain Vitamin C. Y Donotuse after the expiry date on the label. Vitamin C helps the body’s natural defense against damaging free radicals. Free radicals are highly reactive and unstable chemicals How should you keep this medicine? generated during normal body activities that require oxygen (e.g. Y Keep the product out of reach and sight of children. respiration, digestion, blood circulation, immune system response, etc.) Y Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. and after exposure to UV light, cigarette smoke and various pollutants, Vitamin C forms part of the body’s natural immune system and Y Protect from light. stimulates the activity of specialized white blood cells which inhibit Y Keep away from direct heat and sunlight. harmful bacteria and viruses. Vitamin C is also needed for the formation ADR REPORTING STATEMENT of the protein, collagen. Collagen is important in the formation of bones, teeth, cartilage, and skin and helps promote faster wound healing. “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph” Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Strength of the medicine Each 5 mLcontains: Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C), USP. 100 mg Availability Amber Glass Bottle x 60 mL (Box of 1’s) Whatis this medicine used for? Amber Glass Bottle x 120 mL (Box of 1’s) For the prevention and treatment of Vitamin C deficiency. Registration Number HRP-097 How much and how often should you use this medicine? One teaspoonful (5 mL) once daily or as prescribed by the physician. Date of First Authorization/ Renewal April 21, 2021 When should you not take this medicine? If the child is allergic to any ingredient in the product. Date of Revision of PIL Undesirable Effects May 2021 Prolonged intake of Vitamin C in excess of 2g/day may lead to nausea, abdominal cramps, diarrhea and nose bleeds. Manufactured by: OLMANN What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this Py # 95 North Zuzuarregui St., Diliman, @. C.",1,1,Description of Product,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:02:50.099091+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-122,Carbocisteine,Diacof,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IcVq4zxbazHpt_efCWDxGO_aqNQ8BKMv/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-122_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IcVq4zxbazHpt_efCWDxGO_aqNQ8BKMv_view_usp_drivesdk_89da1a276c.pdf,page_text/HRP-122_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1IcVq4zxbazHpt_efCWDxGO_aqNQ8BKMv_view_usp_drivesdk_89da1a276c.json,60fc2a430224253951a7c5460ea5597a87a16c073f9da509e2e820216621d03e,767308,1,ocr,"The medicine is a clear orange colored syrup with orange flavor and aroma contained in a 60 mL amber bottle What is in the medicine? Diacof Syrup contains Carbocisteine that reduces the viscosity of sputum and so can be used to help relieve cough and brings up sputum more easily. Strength of the medicine: Each 5 milliliter (1 teaspoonful) of the syrup contains: Carbocisteine .... mg Ethyl Alcohol eis 3.7% What is this medicine used for? Diacof Syrup is a mucolytic agent for the adjunctive therapy of respiratory tract infections, characterized by excessive or viscid mucus where it is advised to promote fluidification and facilitate expectoration. _— How much and how often should you use this medicine? soe — Children: 2-5 years old auevel 1.25-2.5 mL four times a day 6-12 years old. 5 mL (1 teaspoonful) three times a day Or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? -Caution in patients with a history of peptic ulcer disease because of the risk that mucolytics may disrupt the gastric mucosal barrier. -If you are allergic to any ingredient in the medicine. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: -When taking this medicine, care is necessary in patients with a history of stomach or intestinal ulcer and gastrointestinal bleeding. -Not recommended during the first trimester of pregnancy. -Do not use after the expiry date stated on the label. —_ -Do not take more than the recommended dose. — Undesirable effects of this medicine: — Nausea, gastric discomfort and gastrointestinal bleeding have occasionally occurred with carbocisteine. Skin rashes have also been reported, Carbocisteine rarely causes dizziness, insomnia, headache, palpitations, mid lowering of blood glucose. ee dryness of mouth, abnormal heart rhythm (atrial fibrillation) and gassiness. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? There are no known drug interactions for Carbocisteine. However, this does not necessarily mean no interactions exist. Always consult your doctor if you are taking other medicines. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember, but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: The most common symptoms of an overdose include gastrointestinal disorders. There is no specific antidote for Carbocisteine poisoning. If patient took a higher dose than recommended then gastric lavage can be applied. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, particularly exceeds 4 to 5 times the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? -Consult your doctor first if you are pregnant or breastfeeding before taking Carbocisteine. hy | -If hypersensitivity reaction occur (skin rashes, stomach or intestinal bleeding) consult your doctor. — -If symptoms persist and any undesirable effect occurs, consult your doctor. = — ”For suspected adverse drug reaction report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph”. — Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. — — HRP-122 Date of Renewal Authorization: March 19, 2020 Patient Information Leaflet date of revision: March 21, 2023 Manufactured by the Distributed by: Marketing Authorization Holder: li",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:02:57.630801+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-155-02,Fulvit-Cee,Ascorbic Acid,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1nIB87i6LC1u4SXuYLtNFdNv3E5E7ZFtj/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-155-02_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1nIB87i6LC1u4SXuYLtNFdNv3E5E7ZFtj_view_usp_drivesdk_72a1cca188.pdf,page_text/HRP-155-02_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1nIB87i6LC1u4SXuYLtNFdNv3E5E7ZFtj_view_usp_drivesdk_72a1cca188.json,78f8f158116470461e6df814f761f77b8702110f1c218bcd2123e29a88a885c0,1321061,1,ocr,"Ascorbic acid (FULVIT-CEE) is a clear, yellow colored syrup with lemon flavor and odor , contained in a 60 mL/120 mL amber round bottle. What is in the medicine? Fulvit-cee contains Ascorbic acid, a water soluble vitamin which is essential for the synthesis of collagen and intercellular material. Strength of the medicine:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:03:04.257281+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-178,Carbocisteine,Diacof,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cpa7PF0sh_QOFQyXGa8HSlSk7C1QAi2C/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-178_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cpa7PF0sh_QOFQyXGa8HSlSk7C1QAi2C_view_usp_drivesdk_26e9dffa84.pdf,page_text/HRP-178_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cpa7PF0sh_QOFQyXGa8HSlSk7C1QAi2C_view_usp_drivesdk_26e9dffa84.json,9ae1993e9c6315b8a62ed8a495d90914e9621b0e72628f283280965b5ee7dcf4,807114,1,ocr,"The medicine is a clear yellow syrup with tutti frutti vanilla flavor contained in a 15 mL amber bottle. What is in the medicine? Diacof Drops contains Carbocisteine that reduces the viscosity of sputum and so can be used to help relieve cough and to bring up sputum more easily. Le Strength of the medicine: Each milliliter of the syrup contains: Carbocisteine eee eeeenaeeensaeecceees daceeeeees Areerrr rene eecccecessceecee rene ececcccsccscccevesenns cases 50mg FD &C Yellow #5 (Tartrazine). iPRSRNIERS 7.2mcg Ethyl Alcohol pone cccccccccnevscsenee deceeeee tececeecevene Prerryry 1.4% What is this medicine used for? Ul Ve or viscous mucus where it is advised to promote fluidification and facilitate expectoration. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Infants under 2 months old aYSTSTSISTSreiete nen LOS yerm STEKO EGRENeISLesS 0.3 mL 3-6 months old ATER Fata TaPSNS arnt aaa bale tv oleate a fatal een aenatene aera, 0.6 mL 7-12 months old... 0.9 mL 13-24 months old SoS Cerne oonD canny SonnCnnooeooaonT 1-2mL To be taken four times daily or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? -Caution in patients with a history of peptic ulcer disease because of the risk that mucolytics may disrupt the gastric mucosal barrier. -If you are allergic to any ingredient in the medicine. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: - When taking this medicine, care is necessary in patients with a history of stomach or intestinal ulcer and gastrointestinal bleeding. - Do not use after the expiry date stated on the label. - Do not take more than the recommended dose. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Nausea, gastric discomfort and gastrointestinal bleeding have occasionally occurred with Carbocisteine. Skin rashes have also been reported. Carbocisteine rarely causes dizziness, insomnia, headache, palpitations, mid lowering of blood glucose, dryness of mouth, abnormal heart rhythm (atrial fibrillation) and gassiness. ad h dd, What other or food Id be d while taking this medicine? It has an excellent safety profile and rarely causes side effects, There are no known drug interactions for Carbocisteine. — However, this does not necessarily mean no interactions exist. Always consult your doctor if you are taking other medicines. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember, but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: The most common symptoms of an overdose include gastrointestinal disorders. There is no specific antidote for Carbocisteine poisoning. If patient took a higher dose than recommended gastric lavage can be applied. Whatto dowhen you havetaken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, particularly exceeds 4 to 5 times the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or yourdoctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? -Consult your doctor first if you are pregnant or breastfeeding before taking Carbocisteine. -If hypersensitivity reaction occur (skin rashes, stomach or intestinal bleeding) consult your doctor. -If symptoms persist and any undesirable effect occurs, consult your doctor. — “For suspected a rug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph”. Seek di 1 att, +3 dverse d 1 pe y at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. HRP-178 Date of Renewal Authorization: January 17,2022 Patient Information Leaflet Date of Revision: September 12, 2022 2 | Manufactured by the Marketing Authorization Holder: Distributed by:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:03:11.978315+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-195-01,Ascorbic Acid,None,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zXv4ljIE-hrJ6yCtNos_UeH74Cu9PUdV/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-195-01_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zXv4ljIE-hrJ6yCtNos_UeH74Cu9PUdV_view_usp_drivesdk_8c88eb9765.pdf,page_text/HRP-195-01_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1zXv4ljIE-hrJ6yCtNos_UeH74Cu9PUdV_view_usp_drivesdk_8c88eb9765.json,f47377240a4d2bf12b853a59d096fb020edb96033c521dc98434cfdaa99b1379,399627,2,digital_text,"PHAREX® Ascorbic Acid 500 mg Capsule, is a very faintly yellow crystalline powder, in vegetable capsule of HPMC dark green cap and body size #0. STRENGTH OF MEDICINE Each capsule contains 500 mg Ascorbic Acid equivalent to 568.18 mg Sodium Ascorbate. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? • Prevention and treatment of scurvy (Vitamin C deficiency) • Increases the body’s resistance from infectious diseases HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? For daily maintenance: take 1-2 capsules For cold symptoms: take 3-4 capsules daily Or, as prescribed by the physician. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? If you are allergic to any ingredient of the product. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS Like any other medicines, Ascorbic Acid, may occasionally cause side effects in some patients, which may include nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, stomach cramps, flushing or redness of the skin, headache and a mild increase in urination. WHAT OTHER MEDICINES OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Tell your doctor or pharmacist if you are taking Vitamin C for a long time. You may need to stop taking it slowly as Sodium Ascorbate may alter your kidney function, and if you are taking antacids for indigestion remedies which contain aluminum. Aspirin can interfere with the absorption of Sodium Ascorbate. Desferioxamine should also not be taken together with Sodium Ascorbate, it is used to treat excessive absorption and storage of iron and some abnormalities. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? If you miss a dose, take another dose as soon as you remember it and then your next dose at the usual recommended schedule. Never take two doses at the same time. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Keep this product out of reach and sight of children. Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct sunlight SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSAGE There is no information regarding overdosage of Ascorbic Acid. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSE? If you have taken more than the recommended dosage, consult a doctor or a Poison Control Center right away. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE Tell a doctor if you are pregnant, or are breastfeeding before taking this medicine. Should be given with care to patients with hyperoxaluria. Do not take more than the recommended dose. Do not use after the expiry date. Keep out of reach and sight of children. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT A DOCTOR? If any undesirable effects occur. ADVERSE DRUG REACTION REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adverse drug reaction, seek medical attention immediately and report to the FDA at www.fda.gov.ph AND PHAREX HEALTH CORPORATION at (+632) 7-971-3333 or productsafety@pharexhealth.com.ph. By reporting undesirable effects, you can help provide more information on the safety of this medicine. AVAILABILITY PHAREX® Ascorbic Acid 500 mg Capsule, in blister pack x 10’s (box x 100’s) PHAREX® Ascorbic Acid 500 mg Capsule, in blister pack x 10’s (box x 30’s) Manufactured by Am-Europharma Corporation Brgy. Saimsim, Calamba City Laguna, Philippines Distributed by Pharex Health Corporation Unit 12A North Tower Rockwell Business Center Sheridan Street corner United Street Mandaluyong City Metro Manila, Philippines HRP-195-01 Date of First Authorization: 23 April 2015 Date of revision of Patient Information Leaflet: January 4, 2022 Reg. IPOPHIL 93mm 216mm Pantone Black [Page 2]",1,1,PRODUCT DESCRIPTION,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:03:14.927470+00:00
