PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-254,Ascorbic Acid,Vitcee,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/13D31WxJMAUZ8t83fWCmDqqo2OWWDB-vH/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-254_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13D31WxJMAUZ8t83fWCmDqqo2OWWDB-vH_view_usp_drivesdk_a4ccc89fe2.pdf,page_text/HRP-254_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_13D31WxJMAUZ8t83fWCmDqqo2OWWDB-vH_view_usp_drivesdk_a4ccc89fe2.json,d369927babb1954d1f0fc1eefaf1bb95a64a2ebf13a5328fdb21bd8fd366b125,566102,1,ocr,"Ascorbic acid (VITCEE) is a clear , pale yellow colored syrup with lemon flavor and odor ina15mL amber round bottle. What is in the medicine: Vitcee contains Ascorbic acid, a water soluble vitamin which is essential for the synthesis of collagen and intercellular material. Strength of the medicine: Each milliliter of the syrup in drops contains 100 mg Ascorbic Acid (Vitamin C), USP. What is this medicine used for? It is used to treat Vitamin C deficiency or scurvy and also used to increase body resistance against stress, colds and other infections. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Infants: 0.3 mL - 0.6 mL once daily or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? If you are allergic to ascorbic acid or vitamin C. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: It should be given care to patients with excessive calcium oxalate kidney stones (hyperoxaluria). Tolerance may induced in patients taking high doses. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Diarrhea and gastrointestinal disturbances. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Omeprazole What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: Hemolysis in patients with G6PD deficiency. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? If symptoms persist or any undesirable effects occur, consult your doctor. “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph”. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. Registration number : HRP-254 Date of Renewal Authorization : December 28, 2020 Date of Revision of Patient Information Leaflet : January 29, 2021 Manufactured by the Distributed by: Marketing Authorization Holder:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:03:32.146170+00:00
