PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-313,Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol + Amylmetacresol,Trosoothe,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-1TGuekMjplQhfp4mxfFbEN50qe-ZETq/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-313_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-1TGuekMjplQhfp4mxfFbEN50qe-ZETq_view_usp_drivesdk_5994e6ecd1.pdf,page_text/HRP-313_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1-1TGuekMjplQhfp4mxfFbEN50qe-ZETq_view_usp_drivesdk_5994e6ecd1.json,277e0533c772cde4567f49a516e2b0f9703c9a90945b3714c36084aba922742a,418673,1,digital_text,"Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol and Amylmetacresol Lozenges contains 2,4-Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol and Amylmetacresol. It comes in Blister of 12 Lozenges. Available in different ␀avors. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol and Amylmetacresol Lozenges contains two antiseptic ingredients 2,4 dichlorobenzyl alcohol and amylmetacresol, for use in throat medications. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol and Amylmetacresol Lozenges are used for the symptomatic relief of mouth and throat infections. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? This product is for short term use only. You should take the lowest dose for the shor test time necessary to relieve your symptoms. Dissolve one lozenge slowly in the mouth every 2- 3 hours. W H E N S H O U L D Y O U N O T T A K E T H I S MEDICINE? Do not take this product if you are allergic (hypersensitive) to 2, 4-dichlorobenzyl alcohol, amylmetacresol, or any of the other ingredients. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Do not wear dentures, take them out while sucking the lozenge. If symptoms persist for more than two days, consult your doctor. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Like all medicines, Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol and Amylmetacresol Lozenges can cause side effects, although not everybody gets them. If you experience any hypersensitivity to this product stop taking this product and consult your doctor or pharmacist. Soreness of the tongue is a possibility after consuming Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol and Amylmetacresol Lozenges. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Not known food or drug integrations with Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol and Amylmetacresol Lozenges. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten lozenge. Continue to use this product normally. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE? You may experience stomach discomfort. Do not take any more of this product and consult your doctor or pharmacist. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? Do not take any more of this product and consult your doctor or pharmacist. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Keep out of the sight and reach of children. Do not use this product after the expiry date which is stated on the carton. The expiry date refers to the last day of that month and the year. Store at a temperature not exceeding 30°C in a dry place. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If symptoms persist for more than two days, consult your doctor. ADR REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:03:45.864738+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-314,Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol + Amylmetacresol,Trosoothe,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BXSEG_E5KErqnePbg_xVay7fpdWx1c0E/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-314_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1BXSEG_E5KErqnePbg_xVay7fpdWx1c0E_view_usp_drivesdk_f5b91c647f.pdf,page_text/HRP-314_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1BXSEG_E5KErqnePbg_xVay7fpdWx1c0E_view_usp_drivesdk_f5b91c647f.json,a399cb80a3673c239f1ff5ada2cdd0270cf0f0005ddc904d7de28e206a1b3c6e,417823,1,digital_text,"Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol and Amylmetacresol Lozenges contains 2,4-Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol and Amylmetacresol. It comes in Blister of 12 Lozenges. Available in different ␀avors. WHAT IS IN THE MEDICINE? Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol and Amylmetacresol Lozenges contains two antiseptic ingredients 2,4 dichlorobenzyl alcohol and amylmetacresol, for use in throat medications. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol and Amylmetacresol Lozenges are used for the symptomatic relief of mouth and throat infections. HOW MUCH AND HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? This product is for short term use only. You should take the lowest dose for the shor test time necessary to relieve your symptoms. Dissolve one lozenge slowly in the mouth every 2- 3 hours. W H E N S H O U L D Y O U N O T T A K E T H I S MEDICINE? Do not take this product if you are allergic (hypersensitive) to 2, 4-dichlorobenzyl alcohol, amylmetacresol, or any of the other ingredients. CARE THAT SHOULD BE TAKEN WHEN TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Do not wear dentures, take them out while sucking the lozenge. If symptoms persist for more than two days, consult your doctor. UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS OF THIS MEDICINE Like all medicines, Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol and Amylmetacresol Lozenges can cause side effects, although not everybody gets them. If you experience any hypersensitivity to this product stop taking this product and consult your doctor or pharmacist. Soreness of the tongue is a possibility after consuming Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol and Amylmetacresol Lozenges. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Not known food or drug integrations with Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol and Amylmetacresol Lozenges. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten lozenge. Continue to use this product normally. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE? You may experience stomach discomfort. Do not take any more of this product and consult your doctor or pharmacist. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? Do not take any more of this product and consult your doctor or pharmacist. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Keep out of the sight and reach of children. Do not use this product after the expiry date which is stated on the carton. The expiry date refers to the last day of that month and the year. Store at a temperature not exceeding 30°C in a dry place. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If symptoms persist for more than two days, consult your doctor. ADR REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:03:48.908883+00:00
