cist. Soreness of the tongue is a possibility after consuming Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol and Amylmetacresol Lozenges. WHAT OTHER MEDICINE OR FOOD SHOULD BE AVOIDED WHILE TAKING THIS MEDICINE? Not known food or drug integrations with Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol and Amylmetacresol Lozenges. WHAT SHOULD YOU DO IF YOU MISS A DOSE? Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten lozenge. Continue to use this product normally. SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS OF OVERDOSE? You may experience stomach discomfort. Do not take any more of this product and consult your doctor or pharmacist. WHAT TO DO WHEN YOU HAVE TAKEN MORE THAN THE RECOMMENDED DOSAGE? Do not take any more of this product and consult your doctor or pharmacist. HOW SHOULD YOU KEEP THIS MEDICINE? Keep out of the sight and reach of children. Do not use this product after the expiry date which is stated on the carton. The expiry date refers to the last day of that month and the year. Store at a temperature not exceeding 30°C in a dry place. WHEN SHOULD YOU CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR? If symptoms persist for more than two days, consult your doctor. ADR REPORTING STATEMENT For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction.",1,1,DESCRIPTION OF THE PRODUCT,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:03:51.900170+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-319,Ascorbic Acid,Unbranded,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1iQ1s5UxeKEzu9fW_JG2b8ClE3mqwKwGF/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-319_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1iQ1s5UxeKEzu9fW_JG2b8ClE3mqwKwGF_view_usp_drivesdk_8c8d9a0172.pdf,page_text/HRP-319_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1iQ1s5UxeKEzu9fW_JG2b8ClE3mqwKwGF_view_usp_drivesdk_8c8d9a0172.json,fff8dee3a6d44d19254e168000824a8972f2b754b15a5d7085bec1673965f6a8,522348,1,ocr,"Ascorbic Acid is a white to off-white fine powder, contained in EGC: Orange/Orange size #0. 50 capsules in a 100 mL HDPE bottle with cap. What is in the medicine? This medicine contains Ascorbic acid , a water soluble vitamin which is essential for the synthesis of collagen and intercellular material. Strength of the medicine: Each capsule contains 500mg Ascorbic Acid. What is this medicine used for? It is used for prevention and treatment of Vitamin C deficiency or scurvy and also used to increase body resistance against stress, colds and other infections. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Take 1-2 capsule/s a day or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? -If you are allergic to Ascorbic acid or vitamin C. -Patients with G6PD deficiency. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: It should be given care to patients with excessive urinary excretion of calcium oxalate or hyperoxaluria. Large doses of ascorbic acid have resulted in haemolysis in patients with G6PD deficiency. Tolerance may induce in patients taking high doses. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Ascorbic acid is usually well tolerated. Large doses are reported to cause diarrhea, hyperoxaluria and other gastrointestinal disturbances. Prolonged or excessive use of chewable vitamin C preparations may cause erosion of tooth enamel. What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? Omeprazole may affect the bioavailability of dietary vitamin C. Ascorbic acid should not be given for the first month after starting desferrioxamine treatment because when there is excess tissue iron there is some evidence that Vitamin C may worsen the iron toxicity. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: Ascorbic acid is usually well tolerated. Large doses are reported to cause diarrhea, hyperoxaluria and other gastrointestinal disturbances. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C Protect from direct sunlight When should you consult your doctor? If symptoms persist and any undesirable effect occurs, consult your doctor. “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph.” Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. HRP-319 DATE OF RENEWAL AUTHORIZATION: October 29, 2020 PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET DATE OF REVISION: November 30, 2020 Manufactured by the Marketing Authorization Holder:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:03:59.827741+00:00
