prazole may affect the bioavailability of dietary vitamin C. Ascorbic acid should not be given for the first month after starting desferrioxamine treatment because when there is excess tissue iron there is some evidence that Vitamin C may worsen the iron toxicity. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: Ascorbic acid is usually well tolerated. Large doses are reported to cause diarrhea, hyperoxaluria and other gastrointestinal disturbances. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C Protect from direct sunlight When should you consult your doctor? If symptoms persist and any undesirable effect occurs, consult your doctor. “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph.” Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. HRP-319 DATE OF RENEWAL AUTHORIZATION: October 29, 2020 PATIENT INFORMATION LEAFLET DATE OF REVISION: November 30, 2020 Manufactured by the Marketing Authorization Holder:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:04:07.887270+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-321,Carbocisteine,DIACOF,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1kpqpB97Tqd9qzEguy-qXjcgJxd03CUv9/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-321_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kpqpB97Tqd9qzEguy-qXjcgJxd03CUv9_view_usp_drivesdk_88978f6379.pdf,page_text/HRP-321_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1kpqpB97Tqd9qzEguy-qXjcgJxd03CUv9_view_usp_drivesdk_88978f6379.json,8d871efaf469a0cb55ccfd4c267075b6af1e12d3e89bc0eb3c5fb454187cc4ea,1938460,1,ocr,"The medicine is a clear orange colored syrup with orange flavor and aroma contained in a 60 mL amber bottle. What is in the medicine? Diacof Syrup contains Carbocisteine that reduces the viscosity of sputum and so can be used to help relieve cough and brings up sputum more easily. Strength of the medicine: Each 5 milliliter of the syrup contains: Carbocisteine. ..100 mg EtYAIGON 22 ccnweevsensrnneacsecwremceaneed 1.7% - 7 = - = 7 -“ = 7 = = = 7 7 . 7 = = = - = - eo - oe - - = = = = = = = 7 ‘What is this medicine used for?” “~"" ""~~ Diacof Syrup is a mucolytic agent for the adjunctive therapy of respiratory tract infections, characterized by excessive or viscid mucus where it is advised to promote fluidification and facilitate expectoration. How much and how often should you use this medicine? 1-3 years old 5-7.5 mL (1-1 % teaspoonfuls) 4-7 years old... 7.5-10 mL (1% - 2 teaspoonfuls) 8-12 years old... ..10-15 mL (2-3 teaspoonfuls) Every 8 hours, or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? -Caution in patients with a history of peptic ulcer disease because of the risk that mucolytics may disrupt the gastric mucosal barrier. -If you are allergic to any ingredient in the medicine. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: - When taking this medicine, care is necessary in patients with a history of stomach or intestinal ulcer and gastrointestinal bleeding - Do not use after the expiry date stated on the label. - Do not take more than the recommended dose. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Nausea, gastric discomfort and gastrointestinal bleeding have occasionally occurred with carbocisteine. Skin rashes have also been reported. Carbocisteine rarely causes dizziness, insomnia, headache, palpitations, mid lowering of blood glucose, dryness of mouth, abnormal heart rhythm (atrial fibrillation) and gassiness. - - - - - oe — _— ——— What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this fiedicine? There are no known drug interactions for Carbocisteine. However, this does not necessarily mean no interactions exist. Always consult your doctor if you are taking other medicines. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember, but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: The most common symptoms of an overdose include gastrointestinal disorders. There is no specific antidote for Carbocisteine poisoning. If patient took a higher dose than recommended then gastric lavage can be applied. What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, particularly exceeds 4 to 5 times the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? o -Consult your doctor first if you are pregnant or bi 1g before taking C: 1e. -lf hypersensitivity reaction occur (skin rashes, stomach or intestinal bleeding) consult your doctor. = a =llisymptoms persist and,any_undesirablejeffect occurs ;consulfiyour decior.. ey a ai = a i ane o rasie aie “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph”. Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. HRP-321 Date of Renewal Authorization: March 21, 2022 Patient Information Leaflet date of revision: September 12, 2022 Manufactured by the Marketing Authorization Holder: Distributed by:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:04:15.686895+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-322,Paracetamol,Alagesic,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/11sWbf-151HCzb45LJ8xo7G2JiLpeamj_/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-322_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11sWbf-151HCzb45LJ8xo7G2JiLpeamj__view_usp_drivesdk_4c86de4df6.pdf,page_text/HRP-322_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_11sWbf-151HCzb45LJ8xo7G2JiLpeamj__view_usp_drivesdk_4c86de4df6.json,ba17047ea13ddba607cd32f999a89ae89de9d9d2e655bdf65a1a4a684c73eb8c,840323,1,ocr,"The medicine is a milky orange colored suspension with orange flavor and aroma contained in a 60 mL amber round bottle. What is in the medicine? Paracetamol has analgesic and anti-pyretic properties and weak anti-inflammatory activity. Paracetamol is often the analgesic or anti-pyretic of choice, especially in the elderly and in patients in whom salicylates or other NSAIDs are contraindicated. Such patients include asthmatics, those with a history of peptic ulcer and children. Strength of the medicine: Each 5 mL of suspension contains 125 mg Paracetamol. What is this medicine used for? Paracetamol (ALAGESIC) is used for relief of painful conditions including headache, migraine, bodyache, earache, toothache, eo dysmenorrhea, neuralgia, arthralgia and post operative pain. Also indicated for reduction of fever. How much and how often should you use this medicine? Children: 1 to 5 years old 5-10 mL (1 - 2 teaspoonfuls) poe 6 to 12 years old 10 - 20 mL (2-4 teaspoonfuls) To be taken every 4-6 hours, maximum of 4 doses in 24 hours. Or as prescribed by the physician. When should you not take this medicine? Do not use this medicine if you are allergic to acetaminophen or paracetamol. Care that should be taken when taking this medicine: Paracetamol should be given with care to patients with impaired kidney or liver function and to patients with alcohol dependence. Chronic use should be avoided. Undesirable effects of this medicine: Adverse effects of Paracetamol are rare and usually mild, although haematological reaction including thrombocytopenia, leucopenia, pancytopenia, neutropenia and agranulocytosis have been reported. Skin rashes and other hypersensitivity reaction occur occasionally. = What other medicine or food should be avoided while taking this medicine? se The risk of Paracetamol toxicity may be increased in patients receiving other potentially hepatotoxic drugs or drugs that =. induce liver microsomal enzymes. The absorption of paracetamol may be accelerated by drugs such as metoclopramide. Excretion may be affected and plasma concentrations altered when given with probenecid. Colestyramine reduces the — rt absorption of paracetamol if given within 1 hour of paracetamol. What should you do if you miss a dose? Take the dose as soon as you remember but if the missed dose is near the next dose skip the missed dose and continue with the scheduled dosing. Signs and symptoms of overdose: Adults taking as little as 10 g to 15 g of paracetamol within 24 hours may develop severe liver damage and less often, renal tubular necrosis. Early signs of overdosage with paracetamol are nausea, vomiting, and may also include lethargy and sweating usually settles within 24 hours. Abdominal pain may be the first indication of liver damage which is not usually apparent for 24 to 48 hours and sometime may be delayed for up to 4 to 6 days after ingestion. Activated charcoal may be used to reduce gastrointestinal absorption, if it can be given within 1 hour of the overdose, and if more than 150 mg/kg or 12g of paracetamol has been ingested. There is little evidence that gastric lavage is of benefit in those who have been overdosed solely in paracetamol. If there is any doubt about the timing or the need to treat, then a patient should be treated with an antidote of choice (Acetylcysteine). What to do when you have taken more than the recommended dosage? If you ingested more than the recommended dose, contact the nearest hospital or your doctor immediately. How should you keep this medicine? Store at temperatures not exceeding 30°C. Protect from direct sunlight. When should you consult your doctor? If symptoms persist and any undesirable effect occurs, consult your doctor. “For suspected adverse drug reaction, report to the FDA: www.fda.gov.ph”. —~— Seek medical attention immediately at the first sign of any adverse drug reaction. HRP-322 Date of Authorization: January 06, 2020 Patient Information Leaflet Date of Revision: April 11, 2023 Manufactured by the Marketing Authorization Holder: Distributed by:",1,1,Description of the product:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:04:23.283815+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-328,"2,4-Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol + Amylmetacresol",Lozemed Plain,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1TziIxez7RPPgGH_gysiBlnu830A4FrQx/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-328_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1TziIxez7RPPgGH_gysiBlnu830A4FrQx_view_usp_drivesdk_8997da3e7b.pdf,page_text/HRP-328_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1TziIxez7RPPgGH_gysiBlnu830A4FrQx_view_usp_drivesdk_8997da3e7b.json,41d299764550b2e4250cccd46d6beeb13b82ed3c67350c22e5dad564949473cb,1122409,1,digital_text,"Brownish yellow coloured, round, biconvex lozenges having honey lemon flavour with sweet taste. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Lozemed is an antiseptic lozenge used for prevention and treatment of local infections in mouth and throat area. HOW MUCH & HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Adults and Children: Dissolve one lozenge in the mouth every 2 to 3 hours or as prescribed by the physician. If symptoms persist, consult your doctor. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Do not take this product if you are allergic to any of the ingredients. Do not take this product if under 6 years old.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:04:26.761394+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-329,"2,4-Dichlorobenzyl Alcohol Â + Amylmetacresol",Lozemed Plain,PIL_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bn0lrkYKtTvA5-BhyPS5qMEiAeADLUcV/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-329_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bn0lrkYKtTvA5-BhyPS5qMEiAeADLUcV_view_usp_drivesdk_468751c2ba.pdf,page_text/HRP-329_PIL_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1bn0lrkYKtTvA5-BhyPS5qMEiAeADLUcV_view_usp_drivesdk_468751c2ba.json,0d9c47a7f8172853f85e2e1e11dd753bce1041f52aa84d0ee71e8c385fe177af,944412,1,digital_text,"Brownish yellow coloured, round, biconvex lozenges having honey lemon flavour with sweet taste. WHAT IS THIS MEDICINE USED FOR? Lozemed is an antiseptic lozenge used for prevention and treatment of local infections in mouth and throat area. HOW MUCH & HOW OFTEN SHOULD YOU USE THIS MEDICINE? Adults and Children: Dissolve one lozenge in the mouth every 2 to 3 hours or as prescribed by the physician. If symptoms persist, consult your doctor. WHEN SHOULD YOU NOT TAKE THIS MEDICINE? Do not take this product if you are allergic to any of the ingredients. Do not take this product if under 6 years old.",1,1,DESCRIPTION:,,,,,low,needs_human_review_missing_section,2026-07-01T17:04:30.268806+00:00
PH_FDA_VERIFICATION_PORTAL,HRP-408,Zinc Oxide,Caloderm,PI_01,"Package Insert, Patient Information Leaflet, PI/PIL, Indication, SmPC, SPC",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cVDp6yFMlJzJvo9fwbWP0T0gEVq0VAOZ/view?usp=drivesdk,pdf/HRP-408_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cVDp6yFMlJzJvo9fwbWP0T0gEVq0VAOZ_view_usp_drivesdk_0f42c5943a.pdf,page_text/HRP-408_PI_01_https_drive.google.com_file_d_1cVDp6yFMlJzJvo9fwbWP0T0gEVq0VAOZ_view_usp_drivesdk_0f42c5943a.json,47dc259cda503a411f63099faf0d765c6ef616155f82cd4f3309b1256675499e,1538669,12,digital_text_and_ocr,Zinc Oxide (Caloderm) is a white to off-white smooth paste. Pharmacodynamics Zinc oxide has a mild antiseptic action and is useful for relieving the symptoms of nappy rash and other minor skin irritations. The formulation acts to provide a mildly antiseptic water resistant emollient barrier for dry skin conditions and nappy rash.,11,11,Product Description,Helps treat and prevent diaper rash. It is used to protect skin from other irritation.,11,11,Indications,medium,needs_human_review,2026-07-01T17:04:48.755990+00:00
